    <node id="SEEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SEEN, or Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n, is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This organization plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders, contributing significantly to the development of clinical guidelines and evidence-based practices. SEEN is involved in various aspects of clinical nutrition, including the publication of texts and resources that support professionals in the field. 

The society is particularly focused on issues related to obesity and diabetes, engaging in clinical trials and research that enhance understanding and treatment of these conditions. SEEN also provides educational resources, including materials related to dysphagia, and endorses scientific literature, such as the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia. With a commitment to advancing knowledge and practice in endocrinology and nutrition, SEEN supports education and research initiatives, making it a vital organization in the health landscape of Spain.</data>
