      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">20</data>
      <data key="d7">a27287579b8a4bc9a35bb51ca577bc43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADORES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">CUIDADORES, or caregivers, are individuals who play a crucial role in providing care to patients, particularly those with health conditions such as disfagia orofar&#237;ngea (oropharyngeal dysphagia) and chronic illnesses. Often family members, caregivers support patients receiving nutritional therapy at home and help manage their daily care needs. They also address the psychological and emotional challenges faced by these patients, especially the elderly who may be frail. The involvement of caregivers significantly impacts the overall well-being of the individuals they assist, highlighting their importance in the healthcare system.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d083c309fb6f4d0d16c0e2b23ea5c8b,123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721,669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593,7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39,e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b</data>
