    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES NEUROL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDADES NEUROL&#211;GICAS" refers to a range of disorders that significantly impact the nervous system and are a major health concern in developed countries. These diseases can lead to various complications, including altered consciousness and difficulties with swallowing, known as dysphagia. As a result, many patients suffering from neurological diseases may require artificial nutritional support, specifically enteral nutrition, to meet their dietary needs. Conditions such as Parkinson's disease, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and Alzheimer's disease are notable examples of neurological disorders that can severely impair the ability to eat normally, necessitating this form of nutritional intervention. Overall, neurological diseases present complex challenges that often require specialized care and support for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
