      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">23</data>
      <data key="d7">3c089ece6ed74ef19a3e5c2360ecab0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUIMIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">QUIMIOTERAPIA, or chemotherapy, is an aggressive treatment method for cancer that employs powerful drugs to kill cancer cells. It is commonly used in various contexts, including before hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and in the management of specific cancers such as pancreatic cancer. While effective in targeting cancer, chemotherapy often leads to significant side effects that can adversely affect a patient's nutritional status and overall quality of life. 

Patients undergoing chemotherapy may experience complications such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, hyperglycemia, cachexia, nausea, vomiting, and mucositis, which can hinder normal food intake and may necessitate enteral nutrition. The treatment can also result in nutritional deficiencies and weight changes, including loss of appetite. As a result, careful management of the patient's nutritional needs is crucial during chemotherapy to mitigate these adverse effects and support recovery. 

In summary, QUIMIOTERAPIA is a vital but challenging component of cancer treatment, requiring close attention to the patient's health and nutritional status throughout the process.</data>
      <data key="d2">084639519c323a72fcf1322c38efd173,0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,16887bf1589e9515213d2e392bbc8c69,2bbe847617971cacfe15b2c970de2d21,4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4,61890d3cb54fb752b95a4dfad8db8bb6,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,7c0d1f274b31d130e4feb8e46fbeb764,9c3716c3860855ce045a1e5d9d30b9d1,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408,b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db,b2b9da64e886eb0b5a8b332d2ba9c7fb,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513,f0d279ccc92a98dc953edafb1080630b</data>
