    <node id="DESHIDRATACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DESHIDRATACI&#211;N" refers to dehydration, a condition that occurs when the body loses more fluids than it takes in, which can significantly affect overall health and performance. It is a common consequence of various medical conditions, including watery diarrhea, particularly in patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase. Dehydration can also arise from oropharyngeal dysphagia, which complicates the clinical situation for affected patients, as well as from difficulties in swallowing and eating, especially in individuals with head and neck tumors. Additionally, patients undergoing enteral nutrition may experience dehydration due to negative fluid balance, leading to symptoms such as dryness of the skin and mucous membranes. Proper hydration is crucial, particularly during exercise, to prevent dehydration and its associated health risks. Overall, dehydration is a serious condition that can lead to significant health issues if not properly managed.</data>
      <data key="d2">364aa13581a973c2e55c25191bad27cc,58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,a079902e52676a05df746098c930a0e7,cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9,ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
