    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DESNUTRICI&#211;N" refers to a medical condition characterized by a deficiency of essential nutrients, which can significantly impact health and recovery across various patient populations. This condition is particularly concerning for frail elderly individuals, children with chronic illnesses, and critically ill patients. It often arises from inadequate nutrient intake, malabsorption, or increased metabolic demands due to conditions such as cancer, severe burns, and chronic diseases like cystic fibrosis and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease).

In hospitalized patients, "DESNUTRICI&#211;N" can complicate recovery and is often assessed through nutritional screening tools. It is prevalent among surgical patients, those with dysphagia, and individuals undergoing aggressive treatments, as inadequate nutrition can lead to weakened immune function, muscle wasting, and prolonged hospital stays. The condition can also affect the effectiveness of medications and is associated with various health issues, including complications like quilothorax and ascitic chylous.

"DESNUTRICI&#211;N" is recognized as a significant public health issue affecting both developing and developed countries, necessitating dietary assessment and intervention to prevent and treat malnutrition. Nutritional support, including enteral or parenteral nutrition, may be required for patients unable to meet their caloric needs through oral intake alone. The healthcare system aims to identify, prevent, and treat this condition to improve patient outcomes and quality of life.</data>
