      <data key="d1">Manuel Rodr&#237;guez Paradinas is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, serving as a co-author and contributor to clinical guidelines related to dysphagia. He is recognized as an expert in otolaryngology and plays a vital role in the multidisciplinary team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar&#237;ngea. His research interests include studying the impact of digital technology on health and dysphagia, highlighting his commitment to advancing knowledge in this area. Additionally, he specializes in the Otolaryngology Service and is responsible for overseeing the Oropharyngeal Dysphagia Functional Unit at the Hospital Universitario Pr&#237;ncipe de Asturias. Through his work, Manuel Rodr&#237;guez Paradinas focuses on the treatment and evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to the understanding and management of this condition.</data>
