    <node id="MAR&#205;A DOLORES VALVERDE CARRILLO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mar&#237;a Dolores Valverde Carrillo is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to both research and clinical practice. She is a member of the team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar&#237;ngea, where she focuses on patient care and rehabilitation. As the head of the Rehabilitation Service and an associate professor of Health Sciences at the University of Alcal&#225; (UAH), she plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.

Her contributions include authoring a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia solutions, which emphasizes exercises for orofacial structures essential for swallowing. Additionally, she is involved in research that examines the effects of internet and digital technology on health and dysphagia, further expanding the understanding of this condition and its impact on quality of life. Through her work, Mar&#237;a Dolores Valverde Carrillo is dedicated to advancing the knowledge and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, making her a key contributor to the field.</data>
