      <data key="d6">49</data>
      <data key="d7">33c0ac45c52d42e99f0afd14ccc3718c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MADRID">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Madrid is the capital city of Spain and serves as a significant political, economic, and cultural center. It is home to various important institutions, including the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n, which is dedicated to research and publications in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This society has published numerous significant works, including the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n" and the "Tratado de Nutrici&#243;n," as well as the 3rd edition of the pediatric gastroenterology, hepatology, and nutrition treatment guidelines.

In addition to its role in medical publishing, Madrid is also noted for its healthcare infrastructure, housing several prominent hospitals such as the Hospital General Universitario Gregorio Mara&#241;&#243;n and Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre. The city is involved in various healthcare initiatives, including the requirement for patients to submit justification reports to primary care centers for continued treatment related to nutritional needs.

Madrid is recognized as a key location for medical literature, with significant contributions from publishing houses like Editorial M&#233;dica Panamericana, S.A., which focuses on clinical nutrition. The city has also been a site for research related to oropharyngeal dysphagia and has reported on health issues such as the mortality rate for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).

Overall, Madrid stands out as a central hub for advancements in nutrition and endocrinology, contributing to both national and international medical knowledge and practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">193f43446f6311107c8a73b6111fa25a,1e6677459719ee2aa18d6d2ffbe46330,2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,2def4be9506db96f8bdfe9e3ba6f9b6f,2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,2f5d9123a78d23b1bc3d9f06d7a53d78,3f46d79bcfab2143f045659e11be171b,42f51d76ff4164f7e731f1af04780490,47ba8105b81c59f81a9038446898d200,49279a0184d5222e806637f084f42c50,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,593ae586183f02d2611966f8a1603e5d,5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,5c69bb68f0d23a5aa15fa31301aa13c2,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0,6dfb109dac53e054fd015f6d8adf48ac,742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1,746fad557197bebe72763efd23a9e0e2,7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445,7ea112a550fd775a80c3eda15663fba5,80793c857399f9e6e22c76392e96ac8b,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,916ad020bd9c528e55001071b4d9530b,9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,a76f25b0b56092f8125f49ec456f78df,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe,b7465350e74a3bada96615deb0d7b031,c3a9acd26c8b8bbe2144d4fe53046439,c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf,c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27,cca60bfbb1e73ceda513fbcaf0866a8f,e0102bb655b6476ce3296726e3aceb4a,e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f,e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2,e9bb1d3d1af940dd655e0cca9bbb5c02,ed97532e0b848baf08ee24448e340f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1479</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">50</data>
      <data key="d7">36a8d21e53804c2aa7ea9ce5f16f2618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISIOLOG&#205;A DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The study of the physiological processes involved in swallowing, including the coordination of muscles and nerves.</data>
      <data key="d2">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">51</data>
      <data key="d7">72c572a0c6d647da941c3b02bb6e24f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LANCASTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">An author who has defined dysphagia and contributed to the understanding of swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">52</data>
      <data key="d7">2576960a13ca4204ab587bf5a5a47bdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVIDENCIA CIENT&#205;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EVIDENCIA CIENT&#205;FICA refers to the quality and strength of evidence in scientific studies, which is classified into different levels. This concept encompasses a broad range of information that supports various fields, including the understanding and treatment of dysphagia, as well as clinical practices in nutrition. Overall, EVIDENCIA CIENT&#205;FICA serves as a critical foundation for informed decision-making in scientific research and clinical applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e07cfac64a6162c745f1c392de1bff4,4cbb124f28ea6f426c4aa7bc0edbb742,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">53</data>
      <data key="d7">cc31b4e70a3542238bb28a6cee24ce1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORBIMORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MORBIMORTALIDAD refers to the frequency and incidence of diseases and deaths within a population, particularly in relation to various health conditions and factors such as malnutrition, surgical procedures, and specific patient demographics. It is a significant public health issue, especially concerning the impact of malnutrition on morbidity and mortality rates among vulnerable groups, including the elderly and critically ill patients. 

The term encompasses the complications and mortality associated with medical conditions, including but not limited to oropharyngeal dysphagia, chronic respiratory diseases, and conditions like hyponatremia and cystic fibrosis. It is also relevant in evaluating health outcomes in patients undergoing surgical interventions, where it can be influenced by factors such as glycemic control. 

MORBIMORTALIDAD is particularly important in the context of cancer treatment, where it serves as a critical measure of patient outcomes. Overall, it highlights the interconnectedness of nutritional status and health, emphasizing the need for early detection and treatment of underlying health issues to mitigate the risks associated with morbidity and mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b61e2d4f840772c76a05502aa4f171,21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a,3159307e5633698722f72fde1e82702f,4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f,70a9e916b8c55784c53828958c76eb09,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74,d2f16314e7098030a6780411d2e03023,d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">28</data>
      <data key="d6">54</data>
      <data key="d7">0ac7b51bb4b849c7b07f0f226002130b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS DEL &#193;NIMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mood disorders are psychological impacts that can arise from the challenges faced by individuals with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">55</data>
      <data key="d7">4ec0155c2deb4cf08aacfd3f80324fff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AISLAMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AISLAMIENTO refers to the phenomenon of isolation, which is a prevalent issue particularly among the elderly population. This isolation can have detrimental effects on their nutritional habits, as social interactions are often linked to eating and meal preparation. Additionally, isolation serves as a social consequence that can significantly impact patients suffering from dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulties in swallowing. For these individuals, the challenges associated with eating can be exacerbated by a lack of social support and interaction, further complicating their nutritional intake and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">56</data>
      <data key="d7">f532ac1fbec74f889b5ff6bf2ffba00c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alimentaci&#243;n" encompasses a broad range of dietary management strategies and practices essential for maintaining health and nutritional status across various patient populations. It refers to the act of eating, which is closely linked to swallowing processes that can be impacted by conditions such as dysphagia. In the context of healthcare, alimentaci&#243;n involves dietary aspects and nutritional care provided to patients during hospitalization, ensuring that their dietary intake is adequate, whether it is normal or deteriorated.

For patients with specific health conditions, such as pancreatitis or head and neck cancers, alimentaci&#243;n plays a critical role in alleviating symptoms and providing necessary nutritional support. It also includes the assessment of eating habits through tools like the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which evaluates nutritional intake and overall health.

Furthermore, alimentaci&#243;n addresses the feeding practices and nutritional strategies vital for the health and growth of infants, particularly those who are preterm. It emphasizes the importance of hydration and nutrient intake, which are crucial for maintaining physical performance and overall well-being.

In summary, alimentaci&#243;n is a multifaceted concept that involves the careful planning, preparation, and provision of food and hydration tailored to meet the needs of individuals, particularly those facing health challenges, ensuring their safety and promoting optimal health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6,1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b,29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,364aa13581a973c2e55c25191bad27cc,4fbc9ba7c1f3ff190b594c75e7eac015,54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d,67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,67f60ae11335cf41da4f96400b69e67b,6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a,6d174de24d62997808908333da591120,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3,905bf2bbef1716cece7bd2f1f62c204e,91131751d701592a597bae807e00c1dc,aacbc2a88a21cd749df3c22de5daea04,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">57</data>
      <data key="d7">f997fd0b4bbc47ba9c5eb0b3eadf80ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">"DEGLUCI&#211;n" refers to the process of swallowing, which involves the formation and movement of a food bolus through the digestive system. This act, known as deglutition, is critical for individuals, particularly those with swallowing difficulties, such as patients with head and neck cancers, multiple sclerosis, or those who have experienced a stroke. Swallowing can be impaired by various medical conditions, necessitating regular assessments and specific exercises to improve the function. In the context of dysphagia, the act of swallowing is actively engaged in during treatment, and it can be enhanced through the use of thickeners to ensure safety for individuals facing these challenges. The process of degluci&#243;n encompasses multiple phases and mechanisms, highlighting its complexity and the importance of understanding its implications for affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d5d152382113aa1b8faab4e554c88cd,28e2e3a92ef4dd76af0898ae3e3df522,4ae09eb472a346b355bc66df2fea519f,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,63bd8dcdc323614f5359e4978e154e90,665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad,bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4,c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959,db12fd42641d2de0cee5f33601bfb6dc</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">31</data>
      <data key="d6">58</data>
      <data key="d7">3591d4a82eb74aaba96700b888e57c97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NERVIO VAGO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El nervio vago es un nervio craneal que proporciona inervaci&#243;n sensorial y motora a los m&#250;sculos involucrados en la degluci&#243;n y el tracto respiratorio superior.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">59</data>
      <data key="d7">903d023fcdf84959a888d45b5b330b73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#211;RTEX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El c&#243;rtex es la parte del cerebro que participa en el control neural de la degluci&#243;n, coordinando los procesos motores necesarios para este evento.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">60</data>
      <data key="d7">0e949fffeadb44a8b734e5024cf39f94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOLLO ALIMENTICIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "BOLLO ALIMENTICIO" refers to the mass of food that is formed in the mouth during the process of swallowing. This mass is created as food is chewed and mixed with saliva, and it is then transferred to the esophagus. The bolo alimenticio plays a crucial role in the digestive process, facilitating the movement of food from the mouth to the esophagus for further digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25,d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">61</data>
      <data key="d7">88773576bf644d65a562c7464cda3d29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#218;SCULOS INFRAHIOIDEOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los m&#250;sculos infrahioideos ayudan a la recuperaci&#243;n de la configuraci&#243;n respiratoria despu&#233;s de la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">62</data>
      <data key="d7">73be8372331b484990d979152e6757d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIG&#201;MINO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El nervio trig&#233;mino es un nervio craneal que participa en la masticaci&#243;n y en la motilidad de labios y mejillas durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">63</data>
      <data key="d7">f64e980f69b24539a17621ca94563079</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACIAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El nervio facial es un nervio craneal que tambi&#233;n participa en la motilidad de labios y mejillas durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">64</data>
      <data key="d7">5566248d68e44eb7a038604324f724f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLOSOFAR&#205;NGEO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El nervio glosofar&#237;ngeo es un nervio craneal que participa en la degluci&#243;n, proporcionando inervaci&#243;n a la faringe.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">65</data>
      <data key="d7">d85f9f6de321458383653f622a03f8d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGLOSO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El nervio hipogloso es un nervio craneal que inerva la lengua, facilitando su movimiento durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">66</data>
      <data key="d7">734bf5a6a4f44e3e8144adcd8ccb4651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ES&#211;FAGO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The es&#243;fago, or esophagus, is a muscular tube that plays a crucial role in the digestive system by transporting the bolus of food from the pharynx to the stomach during the process of swallowing. It is essential for the proper movement of food, and its function can be impacted by various swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">936</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">67</data>
      <data key="d7">35d658f3886d40e889d17a79a88e9fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LARINGE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La laringe es una parte fundamental del tracto respiratorio que desempe&#241;a un papel crucial durante la degluci&#243;n, ya que se cierra para evitar que el bolo alimenticio ingrese a las v&#237;as respiratorias. Adem&#225;s, la laringe es una estructura anat&#243;mica que se eval&#250;a durante la evaluaci&#243;n de la degluci&#243;n (VED) debido a su importancia en este proceso. Su funci&#243;n en la degluci&#243;n puede verse afectada por diversas condiciones que pueden llevar a la disfagia, un trastorno que dificulta la capacidad de tragar.</data>
      <data key="d2">23e28a69f275d88d0a56a430dde4b568,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">68</data>
      <data key="d7">a8147cf5e0da41ed94395438445e35c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPIGLOTIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La epiglotis es una estructura que bloquea la laringe durante la degluci&#243;n, asegurando que el bolo alimenticio se dirija al es&#243;fago.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">69</data>
      <data key="d7">80560de4603d4098b35354fe2cf3349e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PALADAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El paladar es la parte superior de la boca que ayuda a cerrar la cavidad nasal durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">70</data>
      <data key="d7">d4c5bcf737924ea784fe89d1643f128f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NERVIOS CRANEALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los nervios craneales son un grupo de nervios que proporcionan la inervaci&#243;n necesaria para los m&#250;sculos involucrados en la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">71</data>
      <data key="d7">6feaa6ec14fc418a91c41853a3596eac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARINGE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The entity "FARINGE," also known as the pharynx, is a critical anatomical structure involved in the swallowing process. It is a muscular tube that connects the mouth and nasal passages to the esophagus, playing a vital role in the act of swallowing. The pharynx is assessed during procedures such as video fluoroscopy and VED (Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing), highlighting its importance in evaluating swallowing function. Overall, the pharynx is an essential part of the throat that facilitates the transition of food and air, underscoring its significance in both respiratory and digestive systems.</data>
      <data key="d2">23e28a69f275d88d0a56a430dde4b568,63bd8dcdc323614f5359e4978e154e90,b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d3">936</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">72</data>
      <data key="d7">18e3e4cc536d4281ae6d45504acaebf6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#218;CLEO DEL TRACTO SOLITARIO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El n&#250;cleo del tracto solitario es una estructura en el sistema nervioso central que juega un papel crucial en la degluci&#243;n y la integraci&#243;n de informaci&#243;n sensorial relacionada con este proceso.</data>
      <data key="d2">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">73</data>
      <data key="d7">9a34af488602420aa32f19f8b85359f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREBRO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">CEREBRO refers to the brain, a central organ of the nervous system that plays a crucial role in regulating various functions, including swallowing and respiration. It is significantly impacted in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy due to inflammatory responses. Additionally, the brain is involved in various biochemical processes, including those related to copper metabolism. In the context of Wilson's disease, the brain is another critical organ affected, as copper accumulation can lead to neurological symptoms. Overall, CEREBRO encompasses the complex functions and vulnerabilities of the brain in relation to different medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b,f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">74</data>
      <data key="d7">2b5ef3fb4d5148f38987dc065a9d9a1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACCIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A cerebrovascular accident (commonly known as a stroke) is a medical event that can significantly impact a person's ability to swallow, a condition known as dysphagia. This occurs due to damage to the brain areas responsible for swallowing, which is a direct result of interrupted blood flow to the brain. As a consequence of dysphagia, patients who have experienced a cerebrovascular accident are at an increased risk of developing aspiration pneumonia, a serious complication that arises when food or liquid enters the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">75</data>
      <data key="d7">bdd5e2b6c7094461be904cead3cc14ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESONANCIA MAGN&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Resonancia Magn&#233;tica, or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), is a non-invasive diagnostic technique utilized for various medical purposes. It is primarily known for its application in studying brain activity and its relationship with functions such as swallowing and other neurological processes. Additionally, MRI serves as an important tool for quantifying liver iron concentration and assessing liver damage, particularly in patients suffering from hereditary hemochromatosis. This versatility highlights the significance of Resonancia Magn&#233;tica in both neurological and hepatic evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c,f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">76</data>
      <data key="d7">72dc44b1be1c41d2ba7defc2700f147e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTIMULACI&#211;N MAGN&#201;TICA TRANSCRANEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La estimulaci&#243;n magn&#233;tica transcraneal es una t&#233;cnica que permite investigar la funci&#243;n cerebral y su implicaci&#243;n en procesos como la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">77</data>
      <data key="d7">ecea8d91932e4bad989c82d6c7b9d2a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMACI&#211;N RETICULAR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">La formaci&#243;n reticular es una estructura en el tronco del enc&#233;falo que juega un papel importante en la regulaci&#243;n de la degluci&#243;n y la respiraci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">78</data>
      <data key="d7">901e38e394904b1186f49071351fb3de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GANGLIOS BASALES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Los ganglios basales son un grupo de n&#250;cleos en el cerebro que est&#225;n implicados en el control motor y pueden influir en la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">79</data>
      <data key="d7">417c16ab34fa4330be0c70e27e7a83ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#193;LAMO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El t&#225;lamo es una estructura cerebral que forma parte del sistema nervioso central y act&#250;a como un centro de relevo para la informaci&#243;n sensorial. Adem&#225;s de su funci&#243;n en el procesamiento sensorial, el t&#225;lamo est&#225; involucrado en la regulaci&#243;n de la alimentaci&#243;n y la degluci&#243;n, especialmente en los ni&#241;os. Su papel es crucial en la integraci&#243;n de diversas se&#241;ales que afectan estas funciones vitales.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">80</data>
      <data key="d7">72b4ef4c9f794f819a037f4811b23394</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREBELO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El cerebelo es una parte del cerebro que coordina el movimiento y puede influir en la funci&#243;n de degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">81</data>
      <data key="d7">bd73cc97a14147b48bef32e0ab8d1fdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTEX CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">La corteza cerebral es una parte fundamental del sistema nervioso central, responsable de diversas funciones cognitivas y motoras. Estas funciones son cruciales para el desarrollo conductual en los ni&#241;os, as&#237; como para procesos relacionados con la alimentaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">82</data>
      <data key="d7">54b19cbd0d4b46c4a13c015d82fe5032</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El accidente cerebrovascular es un evento m&#233;dico que afecta la funci&#243;n neurol&#243;gica y puede causar disfagia debido a la p&#233;rdida de conectividad funcional en la red de degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d3">957</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">83</data>
      <data key="d7">e3a6b23862534459b8b45b018b87406c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON," or Parkinson's disease, is a neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects motor control, leading to difficulties in movement and coordination. This condition can significantly impact various bodily functions, including the ability to interrupt the vagal tone of the esophagus, which is crucial for swallowing. As a result, individuals with Parkinson's disease often experience a high prevalence of swallowing disorders, known as dysphagia, which can increase the risk of malnutrition. Due to these challenges, patients may require nutritional support and specific screening and treatment recommendations to manage their symptoms effectively. Overall, Parkinson's disease is characterized by its profound effects on motor functions and the associated risks of complications related to swallowing and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0482404f71667592ce2b0f771153ece8,59a97e6bf8748a66eb335bec2852ce38,665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">912</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">84</data>
      <data key="d7">ce715ce8d49e4f3f905f300440c4db79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P. CLAV&#201;">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">P. Clav&#233; is a researcher who has focused on the study of swallowing and has developed methods for evaluating the propulsion forces of the tongue.</data>
      <data key="d2">4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b,665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d3">901</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">85</data>
      <data key="d7">f1901c2dc8ad4ea89309d4aea4a8bd69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCLEROSIS LATERAL AMIOTR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esclerosis lateral amiotr&#243;fica (ELA), also known as amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that primarily affects motor neurons. This degeneration leads to significant muscle weakness and can result in dysphagia, or swallowing difficulties, which occur in approximately 60% of patients. As the disease progresses, individuals may experience increased risks of malnutrition due to these swallowing challenges, necessitating specific nutritional interventions and targeted care strategies. The condition is characterized by the gradual loss of motor function, which can ultimately lead to paralysis. Overall, ELA is a complex disease that requires comprehensive management to address both its neurological and nutritional implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,1adf391b13598f3ffe28ae596ff49438,59a97e6bf8748a66eb335bec2852ce38,665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">912</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">86</data>
      <data key="d7">2aadb9b9b8da436ca1570bd3453c4aae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA MUSCULAR BULBOESPINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La atrofia muscular bulboespinal es una condici&#243;n que causa lesiones en las motoneuronas y afecta la funci&#243;n de degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">87</data>
      <data key="d7">d66a0fa36e5e4bd2ae00b987afd572b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLASTICIDAD NEURONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La plasticidad neuronal se refiere a la capacidad del cerebro para reorganizarse y adaptarse, lo que es crucial para la recuperaci&#243;n funcional despu&#233;s de un accidente cerebrovascular.</data>
      <data key="d2">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d3">957</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">88</data>
      <data key="d7">68729e00ce534a70879511e6c833eb9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROANATOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">89</data>
      <data key="d7">c58e69662d0f4d36a21438f2c545e8f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The upper esophageal sphincter (EES) is a crucial muscular structure that facilitates the opening during the swallowing process, allowing food to pass from the pharynx to the esophagus. It plays a significant role in the swallowing mechanism and can be impacted by various medical conditions, particularly in cases of dysphagia oropharyngeal. The EES is essential for proper swallowing function, and any dysfunction in this area can lead to swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">90</data>
      <data key="d7">010b137cf1ca4c01a302569d051d210f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P. CALV&#201;">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">P. Calv&#233; es un autor que ha defendido el uso de videofluoroscopia para analizar la respuesta motora orofar&#237;ngea y la apertura del EES.</data>
      <data key="d2">cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">91</data>
      <data key="d7">fa03e92867994d5db15aa81c9a78565a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVERT&#205;CULO DE ZENKER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Divert&#237;culo de Zenker" is a structural issue characterized by the formation of a pharyngeal pouch, which can lead to various swallowing symptoms that are influenced by the size of the diverticulum. This condition is associated with fibrosis of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), which can affect its distensibility. As a result, individuals with Zenker's diverticulum may experience difficulties in swallowing, making it an important esophageal condition to recognize and address.</data>
      <data key="d2">63bd8dcdc323614f5359e4978e154e90,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">92</data>
      <data key="d7">524dd49b4e9641bab9b7b4dc01bc43b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad de Crohn, tambi&#233;n conocida como Crohn's disease (CD), es un tipo de enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal (EII) que puede afectar cualquier segmento del tracto gastrointestinal, desde la boca hasta el ano. Esta enfermedad se caracteriza por una inflamaci&#243;n discontinua que afecta todas las capas de la pared intestinal, lo que puede llevar a una variedad de s&#237;ntomas, incluyendo dolor abdominal, diarrea severa, fatiga, p&#233;rdida de peso y malnutrici&#243;n. 

La enfermedad de Crohn es cr&#243;nica y puede presentar complicaciones como malabsorci&#243;n de nutrientes, incluyendo la vitamina E, y dificultades para tragar. Adem&#225;s, puede causar problemas en la apertura del esf&#237;nter esof&#225;gico superior (EES) y tr&#225;nsito intestinal lento, a menudo asociado con el s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto. Debido a la naturaleza de la enfermedad, muchos pacientes, especialmente en la poblaci&#243;n pedi&#225;trica, pueden requerir nutrici&#243;n enteral como parte de su manejo para controlar los s&#237;ntomas y prevenir la desnutrici&#243;n. 

En resumen, la enfermedad de Crohn es un trastorno inflamatorio intestinal que provoca una serie de s&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales y puede tener un impacto significativo en la calidad de vida de quienes la padecen.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,4ec3e8cb1f21808e70bbc71cb26d7396,5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,a519216aaee7bf8a1317f5d6b522c4b6,ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8,cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">93</data>
      <data key="d7">6367267424cc4cb6aca7b3dd2849b6a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOPAT&#205;A POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La miopat&#237;a por cuerpos de inclusi&#243;n es una condici&#243;n que puede estar relacionada con la disfunci&#243;n del EES.</data>
      <data key="d2">cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">94</data>
      <data key="d7">0ec6f011ec7a43d187e2918fee9e19f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANOMETR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MANOMETR&#205;A is a functional diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the pressure and distensibility of the esophageal sphincter (EES) during the act of swallowing. This technique is particularly important for assessing esophageal motility disorders and swallowing function in patients experiencing oropharyngeal dysphagia. By measuring the pressure and patterns of muscle contractions in the esophagus, manometr&#237;a provides critical insights into the underlying neural or muscular mechanisms, helping to differentiate between primary esophageal obstruction and mechanical obstruction. Often, this procedure is performed alongside impedance testing to enhance diagnostic accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,b58b0258891d9207b27237bab6a03946,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698,dbe1af2b277e06c9d447af56351e496f</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">95</data>
      <data key="d7">d9b0c852bb31451ea50738e6e35db8ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESIDUOS POSTDEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los residuos postdegluci&#243;n son restos de alimento que pueden quedar en la faringe despu&#233;s de tragar, lo que puede indicar problemas en la apertura del EES.</data>
      <data key="d2">cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">96</data>
      <data key="d7">5faec755eabf4712af0190dea7f112dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aspiration, referred to as "ASPIRACI&#211;N," occurs when material enters the airway below the vocal cords, which poses a significant risk of respiratory complications. This condition is particularly associated with an abnormal opening of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES), where food can inadvertently enter the respiratory tract, increasing the likelihood of respiratory issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698,eff38537223691079c4930d76cbb7427</data>
      <data key="d3">964</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">97</data>
      <data key="d7">e6601e62cbed4ed3aeb8daf7bbb06b7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#218;SCULOS SUPRAHIOIDEOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">cad4abc24b98ed3e82ec4c199dd49698</data>
      <data key="d3">962</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">98</data>
      <data key="d7">9581525f73e54bcbac5c1d713c0335e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOSITIS POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inclusion body myositis is a muscle disorder that can lead to swallowing difficulties due to muscle weakness.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">99</data>
      <data key="d7">be4d5ad95d0c4b11baef8b8d942ae2e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJERCICIO SHAKER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Shaker exercise is a rehabilitation technique aimed at improving swallowing function by strengthening the suprahyoid muscles.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">100</data>
      <data key="d7">d3ff638f46ab4662a32d496a24b55701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN," also known as the Mendelsohn maneuver, is a specialized technique designed to enhance the swallowing process. This maneuver focuses on prolonging the elevation of the larynx during swallowing, which serves to improve airway protection and minimize pharyngeal residue. Additionally, it aims to improve the coordination of swallowing and the function of the upper esophageal sphincter (EES). Overall, the Mendelsohn maneuver is an effective strategy for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties, contributing to safer and more efficient swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2b8f7ec7ed3d06b96620951376b640a,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">101</data>
      <data key="d7">7e4b00b253c343d0a61c639bcf59be47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LESIONES POSTQUIR&#218;RGICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Post-surgical injuries can lead to complications affecting swallowing, resulting in oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">102</data>
      <data key="d7">0c4c2892acd745beb9097e106711446c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRAUMATISMOS CRANEOENCEF&#193;LICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Head injuries can disrupt the neural pathways involved in swallowing, leading to dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">103</data>
      <data key="d7">dce1741a467c4628a1876e6c61f574b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dementia is a cognitive disorder that primarily affects cognitive functions, often associated with aging and cognitive frailty. It can lead to various complications, one of which is oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that impairs the ability to swallow. This impairment is particularly significant in older adults, as dementia can contribute to the development of dysphagia, further complicating their health and care needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bff3417518c19ae80d20de8150be58b,b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">919</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">104</data>
      <data key="d7">07b4df1cb21d4e1a9087fe399352dabd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCLEROSIS M&#218;LTIPLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esclerosis m&#250;ltiple, or multiple sclerosis (MS), is a chronic neurological disease that affects the central nervous system, leading to a variety of neurological symptoms. It is characterized by its impact on muscle control, which can result in dysphagia (swallowing difficulties) in approximately 60% of patients. This condition not only contributes to challenges in swallowing but also increases the risk of malnutrition among affected individuals. As a result, managing esclerosis m&#250;ltiple requires specific nutritional guidelines to enhance the well-being of patients. Additionally, esclerosis m&#250;ltiple is recognized as one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, emphasizing its significance in ongoing medical research and treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,4ae09eb472a346b355bc66df2fea519f,5173ac9bd92d5f238acade41f8c65ebf,59a97e6bf8748a66eb335bec2852ce38,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">961</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">105</data>
      <data key="d7">02cfac84db7e4a888cdb1d0358faa09f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIOMIELITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Poliomyelitis is a viral disease that can cause paralysis and affect swallowing muscles, leading to dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">106</data>
      <data key="d7">6bfc7ff6daf04222adb474b58ee96f3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAR&#193;LISIS CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cerebral palsy, known as "PAR&#193;LISIS CEREBRAL," is a group of disorders that primarily affect movement and muscle tone. Individuals with cerebral palsy may experience a range of challenges, including severe difficulties with swallowing. These swallowing difficulties can be significant enough to necessitate enteral nutrition for those affected, highlighting the impact of the condition on daily functioning and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">107</data>
      <data key="d7">9f4aa280930c438eac90a616c0c7aef0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE GUILLAIN-BARR&#201;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Guillain-Barr&#233; syndrome is a neurological autoimmune disorder characterized by muscle weakness and can significantly impact various bodily functions, including swallowing. In some cases, the severity of the condition may require patients to rely on enteral nutrition to meet their dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">108</data>
      <data key="d7">1f5cd38394cc4df2acb6e06d509afb28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COREA DE HUNTINGTON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Huntington's disease is a genetic disorder that can lead to movement and cognitive issues, including difficulties with swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">109</data>
      <data key="d7">ce764d395c344aac9ffd466ba2b29319</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS CONG&#201;NITOS O DEGENERATIVOS CEREBRALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Congenital or degenerative brain disorders can impact swallowing function, leading to dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">b04b84e34f404f9b800fded78143c4d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar levels due to the body's inability to effectively process glucose. This condition can arise from insulin resistance or insufficient insulin production and is associated with various health complications if not managed properly. Diabetes Mellitus is prevalent in different populations, including those with specific health conditions such as cancer, chronic pancreatitis, and MELAS syndrome, and it often coexists with other clinical issues, complicating their management.

The management of Diabetes Mellitus requires careful dietary considerations, lifestyle changes, and sometimes medication, including insulin therapy. Nutritional support is particularly important for hospitalized patients and those with comorbidities, as diabetes can influence dietary management and nutritional needs. For instance, dietary fat intake, glycemic index, and the consumption of fruits and vegetables can significantly impact blood sugar control. Additionally, diabetes is a significant risk factor for malnutrition, especially in elderly patients and those with chronic illnesses.

Diabetes Mellitus can lead to serious complications, including hypoglycemia, diabetic ketoacidosis, chronic kidney disease, and cognitive decline, including dementia. It is also linked to conditions such as sarcopenia and can complicate medical procedures. The condition is increasingly recognized as a public health issue, necessitating coordinated efforts for prevention and control due to its rising prevalence and associated health complications globally.

In summary, Diabetes Mellitus is a complex chronic condition that requires comprehensive management strategies, including dietary management, lifestyle modifications, and medical interventions, to maintain health and prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,148443357888793655b663333268775a,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,1f2b31f5a0bba00ecee5e3a8fb2c83ea,201f8e6a0d6c49396cf9c81f5da4520f,21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436,234b514a40a64bc02f1346cb62cf3f97,27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,36c1edffe986e2f70996b6e440e11213,3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d,3b21a011b73cb6fe2bb548f624a8c45c,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230,40253f8b49d61452dbc56454cd1a07e0,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc,53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,5b487245068b8e8b87ffcc04970aaff4,5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448,62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,70715c061c27ab1993ef057601f5489d,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,8d1eb00b23450a2f2cb1243ea32aa36f,95ef1473677a26ea6ad77c7db0c55e5e,9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733,ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707,b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,c55f34a09dbf07224c85384f08173e27,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15,cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b,ce43a9a4cdf2497b2f984547a2787fff,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,e5b6965b2fc3b73112c8bd3bdb58738f,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e,eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4,f558c372d16630f14b614e232fc151de,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5,fc8df7c3d7a0d2286c55493077ed3937</data>
