    <node id="ALCOHOLISMO CR&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic alcoholism, referred to as "ALCOHOLISMO CR&#211;NICO," is a serious condition that can lead to various health complications. It is known to cause neurological damage, which can impair an individual's ability to swallow. Additionally, chronic alcoholism is a major contributor to liver disease; however, it is noteworthy that only 15% of individuals suffering from chronic alcoholism progress to advanced liver disease. Furthermore, chronic alcoholism is identified as the most prevalent cause of chronic pancreatitis in adults, significantly heightening the risk of developing this condition. Overall, chronic alcoholism poses substantial health risks, affecting multiple organ systems and leading to severe medical issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">198</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">112</data>
      <data key="d7">824ae48c886e42a5953c08a0b6650f77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAR&#193;LISIS DEL NERVIO LAR&#205;NGEO RECURRENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Recurrent laryngeal nerve paralysis can affect the muscles involved in swallowing, leading to dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">113</data>
      <data key="d7">ea74fa0d81a24776ba3089c28f721517</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEOPLASIAS refer to abnormal growths of tissue that can manifest in various forms and lead to a range of medical complications. These growths can cause significant issues such as intestinal obstruction and malnutrition, often necessitating nutritional support through parenteral nutrition. Additionally, neoplasias can result in conditions like ascitis quilosa and quilot&#243;rax, which are associated with fluid accumulation in the body. Tumors located in the throat or esophagus can obstruct swallowing, leading to dysphagia, and may require interventions such as gastrostomy for nutritional support. Furthermore, dietary factors can influence the development of neoplasms, which are recognized as a significant cause of mortality worldwide. Overall, neoplasias represent a serious health concern due to their potential to disrupt normal bodily functions and contribute to severe health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1796</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">114</data>
      <data key="d7">a57531e34f874c248ffafea47af04001</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE TAGLE">
