    </node>
    <node id="MEMBRANAS ESOF&#193;GICAS CERVICALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cervical esophageal membranes can obstruct swallowing and lead to dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">132</data>
      <data key="d7">43a06934191b4622be26c13b76917be7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE PLUMMER-VINSON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plummer-Vinson syndrome, also known as Sindrome de Plummer-Vinson, is a rare medical condition primarily associated with severe iron deficiency anemia. This syndrome is characterized by the formation of esophageal webs, which can lead to significant swallowing difficulties. The presence of these webs in the esophagus contributes to the challenges individuals face when consuming food, making it a notable aspect of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">133</data>
      <data key="d7">7a77be1aa38b4239aa93bf0835a3c27a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOCIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bocio, also known as goiter, is an enlargement of the thyroid gland that can arise from various thyroid disorders, including congenital hypothyroidism. This condition can lead to complications such as pressure on the esophagus, resulting in difficulties with swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d3">1670</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
