    <node id="CAVIDAD ORAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">CAVIDAD ORAL, or the oral cavity, is the anatomical space within the mouth that encompasses the tongue, teeth, and gums. This area plays a crucial role in oral hygiene and health, making it significant in discussions related to these topics. The oral cavity is particularly important for hygiene practices, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition, as it can influence their overall health and well-being. Additionally, the oral cavity serves as the initial part of the digestive system, where the process of swallowing begins. It is also a region where various sensory stimuli can be applied, which can modify aspects of swallowing, highlighting its functional importance in both digestion and sensory perception.</data>
      <data key="d2">04fc50226ccbf87e5833a09d52275757,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf,c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
