      <data key="d6">159</data>
      <data key="d7">c4030ad3f8dc47a4a1b1d93750e9f7df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMA IGNORADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term refers to conditions like dysphagia that are often overlooked in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bff3417518c19ae80d20de8150be58b</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">160</data>
      <data key="d7">71b21d8385cd4b39aefe2d24cee8a885</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREVALENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prevalencia refers to the commonness of a condition, such as dysphagia, within a specific population. It encompasses the total number of cases of a disease present in a population at a given point in time. This concept is crucial for understanding the extent of health issues within communities and aids in public health planning and resource allocation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bff3417518c19ae80d20de8150be58b,cf8a6f1b6d59546ed7bd297d032f6b30</data>
      <data key="d3">1167</data>
