    <node id="SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sistema Nacional de Salud (SNS) is the public healthcare system in Spain that provides a wide range of health services to the population. It is responsible for the funding, regulation, and delivery of healthcare services, ensuring health promotion and equity in access to care, as governed by the General Health Law of 1986. The SNS includes various provisions in its portfolio, such as home parenteral nutrition, dietary products, and medical services, and it plays a crucial role in the management and treatment of conditions like diabetes. Additionally, the SNS oversees health services and research, regulating both healthcare delivery and nutrition-related provisions. Overall, the Sistema Nacional de Salud is integral to the health and well-being of the Spanish population, encompassing a comprehensive array of healthcare services and organizations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748,123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,4cbb124f28ea6f426c4aa7bc0edbb742,5bda98c244ed300cfc07192e54c7eb88,6d174de24d62997808908333da591120,7c815eb3ecbf3e8cb61d3f9e27d9e061,9dc17f7051b7301e9568b97f4f8dfaa5,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
      <data key="d3">1918</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">163</data>
      <data key="d7">12fefccd8e114d9c9c371b3c490f9d84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE ALZHEIMER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alzheimer's disease, known as "enfermedad de Alzheimer" in Spanish, is the most common form of dementia, primarily affecting the elderly population. It is characterized by a complex pathophysiology and is significantly influenced by age, which is the main risk factor. This neurodegenerative condition leads to severe cognitive decline, including memory loss and behavioral changes. Additionally, it can result in significant swallowing difficulties, impacting up to 80% of patients. Research suggests that Alzheimer's disease may also be influenced by diet and other modifiable risk factors, highlighting the importance of lifestyle choices in its management and prevention.</data>
      <data key="d2">035d53a7f46fdb72c0a939265667044b,76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">164</data>
      <data key="d7">ed78e870ccc0458798671f017dc06b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACCIDENTES CEREBROVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cerebrovascular accidents, commonly known as strokes, can significantly impact patients' health, particularly affecting their ability to swallow. Research indicates that approximately 47% of individuals who experience cerebrovascular accidents may develop dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This impairment can further complicate their nutritional intake, often requiring enteral nutrition support to ensure adequate nourishment and digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">165</data>
      <data key="d7">cf513d69aa9149e88237a32b440a2eef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMON&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUMON&#205;A is an infection characterized by the inflammation of the air sacs in one or both lungs, which can fill with fluid or pus, leading to severe respiratory issues. This condition can arise as a complication in patients with various underlying health issues, including muscular diseases such as the s&#237;ndrome de Kennedy, where it can significantly affect respiratory function. Additionally, pneumonia is a notable risk for individuals suffering from dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia, as it can lead to aspiration pneumonia. The infection can also induce conditions like SIADH and typically requires a specific duration of treatment. Overall, pneumonia poses a serious health risk, especially for patients with chronic respiratory conditions like EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease).</data>
      <data key="d2">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,a76f25b0b56092f8125f49ec456f78df,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">166</data>
      <data key="d7">a768afc524ae4d2196b2df7eee7f97ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PA&#205;SES DESARROLLADOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Developed countries are experiencing an increase in the elderly population, which is projected to reach 20% of the population over 65 years old in the near future.</data>
      <data key="d2">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
