      <data key="d6">174</data>
      <data key="d7">3d0e028fdc824622bade819a8fc0df03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMON&#205;A POR ASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUMON&#205;A POR ASPIRACI&#211;N, also known as aspiration pneumonia, is a lung infection that arises from the inhalation of saliva, food, liquid, or vomit into the lungs. This condition is often linked to dysphagia, which is difficulty swallowing, and can occur as a potential complication in patients receiving nasogastric feeding. The infection is characterized by the introduction of contaminated substances into the respiratory tract, leading to inflammation and infection in the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">175</data>
      <data key="d7">ff3718f9e40d4c1cadfb6e1713f12491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HAEMOPHILUS INFLUENZAE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Haemophilus influenzae is a bacterium commonly associated with aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">176</data>
      <data key="d7">267ada807e584ac1aea1be36a2340a57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STREPTOCOCCUS PNEUMONIAE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Streptococcus pneumoniae is another bacterium linked to aspiration pneumonia, often found in patients with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">177</data>
      <data key="d7">2d1208adbf1346efa250e8538a7109b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterium belonging to the Enterobacteriaceae family, known for its association with various infections, particularly catheter-related infections. This pathogen is also capable of causing aspiration pneumonia, especially in vulnerable populations such as the elderly or those with compromised immune systems. Its ability to thrive in hospital settings makes it a significant concern in healthcare-associated infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">178</data>
      <data key="d7">183c08d690de483c81009abab29b89b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCHERICHIA COLI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Escherichia coli, commonly known as E. coli, is a type of bacterium that is widely recognized for its role in various infections and gastrointestinal diseases. One notable strain, enterohemorrhagic E. coli, is particularly concerning as it can lead to severe gastrointestinal illness, characterized by diarrhea and abdominal pain. E. coli is also known to cause infections in patients with urinary catheters and other invasive medical devices, making it a significant concern in healthcare settings. Additionally, this bacterium can be implicated in infections related to surgical sites and has been associated with inflammatory bowel disease. In certain cases, E. coli may even contribute to the development of aspiration pneumonia. Overall, E. coli is a versatile bacterium that poses various health risks, particularly in vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40,3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">179</data>
      <data key="d7">f7929a3cf25941ea9c32d7c75c067e2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOMONAS AERUGINOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium known for its role in various infections, particularly in individuals with compromised health. It is notably associated with aspiration pneumonia, where it can contribute to respiratory complications. Additionally, Pseudomonas aeruginosa is recognized for its potential to cause infections in patients who have central venous catheters, highlighting its significance in healthcare settings, especially among vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a</data>
      <data key="d3">1201</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">180</data>
      <data key="d7">696ca5d099c943e793e9460f1d68de37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES NEURODEGENERATIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDADES NEURODEGENERATIVAS" refers to a group of disorders characterized by the progressive degeneration of the structure and function of the nervous system, which includes conditions such as dementia and Parkinson's disease. These diseases can significantly impact patients' quality of life, often leading to complications such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, which increases the risk of aspiration pneumonia. Specialized nutritional support may be required for individuals suffering from these conditions.

In Spain, CIBERned is a dedicated research center focused on neurodegenerative diseases, contributing to the understanding and treatment of these disorders. Additionally, neurodegenerative diseases present unique ethical and legal challenges in healthcare decision-making, particularly concerning patients' rights to medical treatment. Overall, the implications of neurodegenerative diseases extend beyond medical concerns, affecting various aspects of patients' lives and the healthcare system.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8ce52208981fd781dcf23f690f6c3c,3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f,574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,7d929a0137a287c5c96416fa5fc36239,8bf23d86ceb6dc396acc52c92878463d,ce0de74f95e1a41a930b2df09da1f887</data>
      <data key="d3">1936</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">181</data>
      <data key="d7">7afece1737374b4d94ba7808f4979f97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIBIOTICOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Antibiotic therapy, also known as "ANTIBIOTICOTERAPIA," involves the use of antibiotics to treat bacterial infections. This treatment is essential for managing infections that may arise from medical devices such as catheters. However, antibiotic therapy can also have significant effects on the oral flora, potentially increasing the risk of aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients who experience dysphagia. Thus, while antibiotic therapy plays a critical role in combating bacterial infections, it is important to consider its implications on oral health and the associated risks in vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,e5313f692c0a8259c93be803a704413c</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">182</data>
      <data key="d7">3ceaacb0fb8e429ab8a6224882b80395</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGIENE DENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dental hygiene is a factor that can affect the risk of aspiration pneumonia, particularly in patients with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d3">100</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">183</data>
      <data key="d7">a12ba0b455be41668d582b238f112d2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSORIALIDAD LAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Laryngeal sensitivity is crucial for preventing aspiration; its impairment can lead to increased risk of aspiration pneumonia.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">184</data>
      <data key="d7">dfb6e941474b470e81dc1ebabc562f06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REFLEJO TUSIGENO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The cough reflex is an important defense mechanism against aspiration; its dysfunction can lead to aspiration pneumonia.</data>
      <data key="d2">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">185</data>
      <data key="d7">e883941b9485440a86ace21deddf3f48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" is a medical device designed for enteral feeding, particularly beneficial for patients suffering from severe dysphagia who are unable to swallow safely. This flexible tube is inserted through the nose and extends into the stomach, allowing for the administration of nutrition and medications. It is primarily utilized in hospital settings, managed by nursing staff, and serves as a temporary solution for hydration and nutritional support.

The nasogastric tube is indicated for patients with intact gastric function and is used for short to medium-term nutritional support. It facilitates the delivery of hyperosmolar diets and can be employed for continuous or intermittent infusion flows. Additionally, the device is instrumental in assessing the tolerance of infusions and monitoring for significant reflux prior to medical interventions.

While the nasogastric tube provides essential nutritional support, its use can also impact a patient's relationship with their environment and self. Furthermore, it may alter the oropharyngeal ecosystem, potentially increasing the risk of aspiration pneumonia. Overall, the "SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" is a critical tool in managing the nutritional needs of patients who cannot eat by mouth, ensuring they receive necessary sustenance directly into their stomachs.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a,0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,4fbc9ba7c1f3ff190b594c75e7eac015,60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac,7c43869fff0960219e47d176597b35b8,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,aa99de2530170165c9ac9333021210e3,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca,c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36,e569eda9506ef1e77080a8120e388963,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835,fcc886f826047ced8783c4abfe3bf4a3</data>
