    <node id="PREDYCES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PREDYCES is a comprehensive multicenter study conducted in hospitals across Spain, focusing on the nutritional status and prevalence of malnutrition among oncology patients and other hospitalized individuals. The study reveals significant rates of malnutrition both upon admission and discharge, highlighting the critical issue of disease-related malnutrition in this vulnerable population. 

PREDYCES specifically assesses the prevalence and impact of malnutrition, including its costs in hospitalized patients, and has analyzed groups such as those with oropharyngeal dysphagia. The research included a sample of 352 patients with dysphagia, demonstrating high rates of malnutrition and emphasizing the detrimental effects of oropharyngeal dysphagia on patients' health and associated hospital costs. Additionally, the study involved the nutritional assessment of diabetic patients across 50 hospitals, further underscoring the widespread issue of malnutrition in various patient groups.

Overall, PREDYCES provides valuable data on the prevalence and consequences of malnutrition in hospitalized patients, aiming to raise awareness and improve nutritional care in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b61e2d4f840772c76a05502aa4f171,02c3924fac2660b8531f61207f3b04bb,3ed179f6e734d9fe4921fb0be0b018e4,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,73fd366244763cef4b13c058330147b1,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff,f093c7e72a5015556281394111990625,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831</data>
