    <node id="DEHYDRATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dehydration is a condition characterized by a significant loss of body fluids, which can lead to various health complications. It is particularly common among elderly patients, where it can exacerbate malnutrition and contribute to a decline in overall health. Additionally, dehydration can occur in patients with dysphagia, a condition that impairs the ability to swallow liquids effectively, resulting in inadequate fluid intake. This highlights the importance of monitoring fluid consumption in vulnerable populations to prevent dehydration and its associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">73fd366244763cef4b13c058330147b1,f093c7e72a5015556281394111990625</data>
