    <node id="PATIENTS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Patients are individuals undergoing treatment for various health conditions, including dysphagia, cystic fibrosis, and those preparing for bariatric surgery. Specifically, patients with dysphagia often require multidisciplinary approaches for effective rehabilitation, as their condition can lead to increased healthcare costs and longer hospital stays. Additionally, patients undergoing bariatric surgery may face complications such as dumping syndrome and changes in bone density. Furthermore, patients with cystic fibrosis necessitate dietary management and supplementation to enhance their health outcomes. Overall, the care and management of these patients involve addressing complex medical needs and potential complications associated with their conditions.</data>
