    <node id="PACIENTES GERI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Geriatric patients, referred to as "PACIENTES GERI&#193;TRICOS," are a specific group of older adults who face unique health challenges, particularly related to disease-related malnutrition, as emphasized in the PREDYCES study. This demographic is more susceptible to dysphagia, a condition that complicates their ability to eat and drink, leading to increased healthcare costs. Additionally, geriatric patients often require specialized nutritional care due to their health conditions and specific dietary needs. Overall, this group necessitates careful attention to their nutritional and healthcare requirements to improve their quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">1835e55766e759ce3b8acec75f4b6875,2ad1c3591301bd2ea6f99c3782714d69,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
