    <node id="SARCOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sarcoma is a type of malignant tumor that can affect the selar region and originates in connective tissues. It is important to note that sarcoma is distinct from sarcopenia, which is a condition that can accompany oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in older adults, impacting their health and quality of life. While both terms relate to health issues, sarcoma specifically refers to a cancerous growth, whereas sarcopenia pertains to muscle loss and its associated complications.</data>
