    <node id="MORBIMORTALITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Morbimortality refers to the combined incidence of morbidity and mortality, encompassing various health risks associated with different conditions. It is particularly relevant in the context of preterm newborns, where the risks of disease and death are heightened. Additionally, morbimortality is significant in relation to oropharyngeal dysphagia, which can lead to serious complications such as aspiration pneumonia and malnutrition. Furthermore, it also pertains to the incidence of disease and death linked to health conditions, especially concerning nutritional deficiencies in chronic patients. Overall, morbimortality serves as a critical measure of health outcomes across diverse populations and medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">02c3924fac2660b8531f61207f3b04bb,c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f</data>
