    <node id="GASTROENTEROLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastroenterology is a specialized branch of medicine that focuses on the digestive system and its disorders. This field encompasses the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions affecting the digestive tract, including but not limited to pancreatitis, Crohn's disease, and liver diseases. Gastroenterology also involves nutritional management, particularly in cases requiring parenteral nutrition.

In addition to its clinical aspects, Gastroenterology is represented by a leading peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes significant research and guidelines related to digestive health. This journal covers a wide range of topics, including studies on swallowing, dysphagia, dietary factors, cancer risk, and complications associated with liver cirrhosis. Notably, the journal published a study in 1997 that examined the coordination of deglutitive glottal function and pharyngeal bolus transit.

Overall, Gastroenterology plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and treatment of digestive system disorders, contributing to both clinical practice and academic research in the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">17593b5969d4126aef1c56a7d32dc922,1d3c30089c42a02917c7625774aa29f2,384e13475cc83e77e160fd6be9a88e73,581527a14dedf97c7a839eff5c40cbc2,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,719fff2d16bc334d3d4b53f070373a10,7a389f3625ba13c74ce52213197b01ae,9ea9816b490492ba0030e6ba4bc3bb9f,a265c943c66b9cb5d09f89d40ddb995f,a3d355dd6da93691c892691f873338aa,bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c,c84372864fd2ee7b7ed425b2d597efdb,cdb6aae3097a018e194a3fa9452146af,dce680808e039e852dc0f2639835db32,e376d9f50b7608f5b6d1f88877fde59e,ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29,f5175f0c433eb4e10840a41d8052c8e0,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
