    <node id="PLOS ONE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PLOS ONE is a multidisciplinary peer-reviewed open-access journal that publishes research across all areas of science and medicine. Established to facilitate the dissemination of scientific knowledge, PLOS ONE covers a wide range of topics, including nutrition, cancer, and dietary factors. The journal is known for its commitment to open access, allowing researchers and the public to access its articles freely.

In 2011, PLOS ONE published a significant study on the cortical processing of swallowing in patients with Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), highlighting its role in advancing medical research. Additionally, the journal has featured systematic reviews and meta-analyses, such as those examining the impact of fruit and vegetable consumption on anthropometric changes and the relationship between red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk.

Overall, PLOS ONE serves as a vital platform for the publication of diverse scientific research, contributing to the advancement of knowledge across various fields.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f465485ab8858e532f511401e7558f9,3af2658fd59065a71bfee00d2bd27b1b,6533cbcb76873caf6fd68eb95d313d24,97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,bb2e69a0ff4c25a21149882162922c8d,cdb6aae3097a018e194a3fa9452146af,cf833689453c8ce13d3650766a8b47a7,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
