    <node id="MARTINO R">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">MARTINO R is a notable figure in the field of dysphagia research, recognized for his contributions to the understanding and assessment of swallowing disorders in older adults. He co-authored a review on oropharyngeal dysphagia in older persons, which was published in the journal Clinical Interventions in Aging in 2016. Additionally, Martino R is credited with the development and validation of the Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST), a tool specifically designed for evaluating swallowing function in patients who have experienced a stroke. His work has significantly advanced the knowledge and clinical practices related to swallowing difficulties in vulnerable populations.</data>
