      <data key="d7">9e90c46377ee4d8c826ca40b82f52161</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYSFAGIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dysfagia, also known as dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This condition can significantly impact patients' health and quality of life, leading to serious complications such as aspiration, malnutrition, and dehydration, particularly in patients with conditions like ELA (Early Life Autism) and those who have suffered strokes. Various organizations provide resources related to dysphagia, and it can be assessed using a range of screening methods, scales, and tools designed to improve nutritional recommendations and enhance patient independence. Additionally, technological interventions, including virtual reality, have been explored as potential solutions to address the challenges associated with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cd8f3cd1703aeede881bef67e072607,5aef6ccb162a04d926beeb343ceea252,6716f78f148d9f4f2a622919eee02554,7a685dfeed939ab716eb2f6e86a6cc04,7ff388a8f346ea7b1ceece48ed64b1a2,806361fc4a48aa9718a93e11a04170d2,cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c,f0c6cfeca2bb2f42209798eccceb4ac5,f12947896819ee4ab30d1fa3f3c9995d</data>
      <data key="d3">1896</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">271</data>
      <data key="d7">0e451c3184724e18944a0d917132af8f</data>
    </node>
