    <node id="ENFERMERAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermeras, or nurses, are healthcare professionals who play a crucial role in the assessment and care of patients, particularly in the area of enteral nutrition. They are trained to utilize the SSA (Swallowing Screening Assessment) for detecting dysphagia, demonstrating specific sensitivity and specificity rates in its application. Additionally, nurses are fundamental in identifying signs of swallowing disorders and providing necessary care to patients who are at risk of dysphagia. Their expertise is essential in ensuring the well-being of patients requiring specialized nutritional support and monitoring for swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">06484c3fe8af6e4c44bbfc3ac2fa2590,13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b,754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462</data>
