    <node id="CALIDAD DE VIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calidad de vida" refers to the general well-being and life satisfaction of individuals and societies, encompassing various factors that can influence this state. It is particularly relevant in the context of health conditions and interventions, such as in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), chronic gastrointestinal symptoms, and neurological diseases. The quality of life can be negatively affected by these health issues, but it can also be improved through adequate nutritional treatment and medical care.

In healthcare, quality of life is often measured through cost-utility analyses and questionnaires, which assess how various factors, including nutrition and underlying health conditions, impact an individual's overall well-being. For instance, patients suffering from dysphagia experience significant challenges that affect their social and emotional well-being, but early intervention and treatment can lead to improvements in their quality of life.

Moreover, the impact of cancer and its treatment on quality of life underscores the importance of nutritional support, as it can significantly enhance the overall well-being of patients. Thus, "calidad de vida" encompasses a holistic view of health, emphasizing the interplay between medical treatments, caregiving responsibilities, and the nutritional status of individuals, ultimately highlighting the importance of tailored interventions to improve life satisfaction and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">0482404f71667592ce2b0f771153ece8,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8,29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721,2ad1c3591301bd2ea6f99c3782714d69,3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,a6ccbda174f6599eeeb2e4cdb00db5f2,a76f25b0b56092f8125f49ec456f78df,c1fce1d059978d0a9ee9e63f75c8ca98,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,e510500bd5a5f16a0bf0353cfdb79c13</data>
