    <node id="DR. P. CLAV&#201; CIVIT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dr. P. Clav&#233; Civit is a medical professional who designed the clinical exploration method for assessing swallowing disorders, known as MECV-V or V-VST.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d3">1532</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">281</data>
      <data key="d7">d2fbf2a8871845d7ad7de695e59be4b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#201;TODO DE EXPLORACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The M&#233;todo de Exploraci&#243;n Cl&#237;nica Volumen-Viscosidad (MECV-V) is a non-invasive clinical assessment method specifically designed to evaluate dysphagia, which is a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This method involves administering food at varying volumes and viscosities to assess the safety and efficacy of swallowing. By utilizing different bolus characteristics, the MECV-V aims to provide a comprehensive evaluation of an individual's swallowing capabilities, ensuring a thorough understanding of their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">42cc35e2edb450d48bb31f7c51b7a02f,89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d3">1532</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">282</data>
      <data key="d7">381b445e8060460ea9f8a9fa4c7e2b3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR AGUDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute cerebrovascular accident (ACVA) refers to a medical emergency that can lead to swallowing difficulties, necessitating specific screening methods for dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">283</data>
      <data key="d7">f932092496dc42a6bc407f332b62fcec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOLUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">BOLUS refers to a mass of substance, typically food or liquid, that is swallowed. It plays a crucial role in the assessment of swallowing disorders, as it is the material that is evaluated during such assessments. Specifically, the bolus is the mass of food that is prepared in the oral cavity for swallowing, making it an essential component in understanding and diagnosing swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">371e848e9da77bf71f58614d1265aff8,89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268,a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1533</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">284</data>
      <data key="d7">644164bf6bb44017b30eaf6ef115bb4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PULSOX&#205;METRO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A pulse oximeter is a medical device used to monitor the oxygen saturation of a patient's blood, often used during swallowing assessments to detect silent aspirations.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d3">1532</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">285</data>
      <data key="d7">e604fee13ec349fea2d04ac26dd5f807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOVILIDAD DE LA MAND&#205;BULA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Jaw mobility involves the movement of the jaw in various directions, which is crucial for effective chewing and swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">286</data>
      <data key="d7">baf76720740f4a2797be7dbffaa02fe3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSIBILIDAD OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Oropharyngeal sensitivity refers to the ability to feel sensations in the oral and pharyngeal areas, which is important for triggering the swallowing reflex.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">287</data>
      <data key="d7">2f589a749ead419a925cf2f66a4fde70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAPACIDAD DE LIMPIEZA DE LOS SURCOS GINGIVOLABIALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ability to clean the gingivolabial sulcus is important for maintaining oral hygiene and preventing swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">288</data>
      <data key="d7">6d50a593259e499a89aa38b51cb377e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAPACIDAD DE REALIZAR EL TIPPEER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ability to perform the Tippeer involves specific tongue movements that are important for swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">289</data>
      <data key="d7">7c994590f9f4484eadae7538b5430cba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALIDAD VOCAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vocal quality refers to the characteristics of a person's voice, which can indicate issues related to swallowing and airway protection.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">290</data>
      <data key="d7">c05ff4ff2614492da73dfa6f70a6fae4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETARDO DEL DISPARO DEGLUTORIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Swallowing delay refers to the time taken for the swallowing reflex to initiate after food or liquid is presented, which is critical in assessing swallowing function.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">291</data>
      <data key="d7">b1d024268653482a85966dd71e37fb0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIGNOS DE SEGURIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Safety signs are indicators observed during swallowing assessments that help determine if the swallowing process is safe.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">292</data>
      <data key="d7">2d9b2f57a5f6478896d31f39a143d264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIGNOS DE EFICACIA DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Efficacy signs refer to the indicators that show how effectively a person can swallow without residue or aspiration.</data>
      <data key="d2">89b6a28e230890818d938efa74cd1268</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">293</data>
      <data key="d7">e781793ba74b4b5d9a0b11921a979283</data>
    </node>
