    <node id="MECV-V">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MECV-V is a clinical exploration method designed to assess the volume-viscosity needs of patients with dysphagia, particularly those who have experienced a stroke. This bedside exploration method involves a structured protocol that outlines a step-by-step process for testing swallowing with various viscosities and volumes. The MECV-V serves as a valuable tool for evaluating swallowing safety and efficiency, helping to diagnose the specific swallowing difficulties faced by patients suspected of having oropharyngeal dysphagia. Overall, MECV-V is instrumental in the clinical follow-up and management of dysphagia in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b,7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,806140d9fadd08a1e72238d53c829eb2,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,c30b47b534824f4d1b74f3c0bb00ffd9,d8fa59c6af96b4ebb96f2c6b4ddb5473</data>
      <data key="d3">901</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">295</data>
      <data key="d7">139d6251e0bb48e091e234a9b9d772e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAVID G SMITHARD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">David G Smithard is a professional who co-designed the Standardized Bedside Swallowing Assessment (SSA) for detecting dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b</data>
      <data key="d3">157</data>
