    </node>
    <node id="OXIMETR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Oximetr&#237;a is a method utilized to evaluate swallowing safety, often in conjunction with water tests. It serves as a screening tool for dysphagia, which involves monitoring symptoms that may arise after a patient is given liquids. This approach helps in assessing the patient's ability to swallow safely and effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b,7ff388a8f346ea7b1ceece48ed64b1a2</data>
      <data key="d3">540</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">302</data>
      <data key="d7">ba1e983e8b9e47c4b4971e4a6e70be1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGUA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AGUA refers to water, an essential fluid required for hydration and various bodily functions. It plays a critical role in cooking and baking, including the preparation of desserts. In healthcare settings, AGUA is vital for the hydration needs of hospitalized patients, with daily requirements typically ranging from 30 to 40 mL/kg. It is also used to dilute medications for proper delivery through enteral feeding tubes and is a key component in clinical nutrition products, affecting the hydration and stability of ingredients.

The recommended daily intake of AGUA varies based on body weight, age, and activity level, and it is crucial for maintaining hydration, especially during physical exercise, where it aids in cooling, nutrient delivery, and waste elimination. In patients undergoing hematopoietic transplants, monitoring the balance of AGUA is essential for their dietary needs. Additionally, AGUA is important for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in enteral nutrition.

AGUA is a gluten-free beverage and is often assessed in nutritional evaluations for its critical role in overall health. It is also used for cleaning feeding tubes and ensuring patient oral hygiene. While AGUA can contain sodium, particularly in mineral waters, it is generally recommended that its consumption does not correlate with weight variations. Overall, AGUA is a vital nutrient necessary for life, contributing significantly to hydration and health, particularly in children.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,056067ecde43f31b356fc39e056221ee,0bc48d0666e895b990c211acf7cbcf23,0e014859b304da60c29590e36c9cbc85,173bd6d0dd53c58c39f748b3c60c08bd,1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108,2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9,3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58,3d73ef14929e7391e915f739189e4dfa,451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61,4befdcd21a98898cec30bbac7b402d4b,51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,700a4472a23342b891a5685b622437d2,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,767d564db2dbf0182707caaf1b0a52d2,8178ba40e7ef08e569845c1f3f1621cc,81bb0be389c10331fb2a5568b6c379dc,93ddfb3a9423ac76f9303638f6465d25,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,b8fd422921866f53cdaa6c24db528ee5,d9e4179f945ec9152199511522d70159,f713611b23199b8a9eb9c28377b9f128</data>
