    <node id="TORONTO BEDSIDE SWALLOWING SCREENING TEST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Toronto Bedside Swallowing Screening Test (TOR-BSST) is a validated tool for early detection of oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e83f9d1f09d1d6b2eb82c16a15f1928</data>
      <data key="d3">1222</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">314</data>
      <data key="d7">20b365fda02949a3b76377d62a4d5f9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIC EVALUATION OF SWALLOWING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (VFES) is a diagnostic procedure that uses X-ray technology to assess swallowing function.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e83f9d1f09d1d6b2eb82c16a15f1928</data>
      <data key="d3">1222</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">315</data>
      <data key="d7">2df094b1c35e466093b506b074e9f9c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBEROPTIC ENDOSCOPIC EVALUATION OF SWALLOWING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fiberoptic Endoscopic Evaluation of Swallowing (FEES) is an instrumental assessment method recommended for evaluating swallowing function in patients with dysphagia. This procedure utilizes an endoscope to visualize the swallowing process, allowing for a detailed assessment of any swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e83f9d1f09d1d6b2eb82c16a15f1928,59a97e6bf8748a66eb335bec2852ce38,e2aeed1cae3c67005a57b0695a907fbf</data>
      <data key="d3">912</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">316</data>
      <data key="d7">36e3282437e540399fed35ad82846e92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACVA refers to Accidente Cerebrovascular, the Spanish term for stroke, which is medically known as an acute cerebrovascular accident. This condition is a medical emergency that affects blood flow to the brain and can result in significant health complications. One of the potential consequences of an ACVA is dysphagia, or swallowing difficulties, which necessitates careful management to address these challenges. Overall, ACVA encompasses the critical nature of strokes and their impact on patients' health, particularly regarding swallowing functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e83f9d1f09d1d6b2eb82c16a15f1928,5dd39815651d2d44f18c16e69696c0cf,6716f78f148d9f4f2a622919eee02554,76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac</data>
      <data key="d3">915</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">317</data>
      <data key="d7">dfb46fd6919e43caa29af840760d01c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYSPHAGIA DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dysphagia diet refers to dietary modifications made for individuals with swallowing difficulties, including pureed and soft foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e83f9d1f09d1d6b2eb82c16a15f1928</data>
      <data key="d3">1221</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
