    </node>
    <node id="DYSHPHAGIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dysphagia refers to difficulty in swallowing, which is the primary focus of the assessments described in the document.</data>
      <data key="d2">db12fd42641d2de0cee5f33601bfb6dc</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">330</data>
      <data key="d7">778b366665754d5b997b8a32d9efa7e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARCHIVES OF NEUROLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Archives of Neurology" is a scholarly publication that focuses on studies related to various neurological conditions, including dementia and cognitive decline. Additionally, it serves as a platform for research on swallowing and dysphagia, as evidenced by a publication from DePippo. This journal encompasses a wide range of topics within the field of neurology, contributing to the understanding and treatment of neurological disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e,db12fd42641d2de0cee5f33601bfb6dc</data>
      <data key="d3">919</data>
