      <data key="d6">334</data>
      <data key="d7">73807ad0b60943aebe138bde2be1423f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DRA. R. BURGOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dra. R. Burgos is a researcher who translated the EAT-10 into Spanish and contributed to its validation.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136</data>
      <data key="d3">959</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">335</data>
      <data key="d7">a63c70d1593645389a2a49c816ede11d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EAT-10">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The EAT-10, or Eating Assessment Tool-10, is a validated self-assessment questionnaire designed to evaluate the severity of swallowing problems, specifically dysphagia, experienced by patients. It serves as a screening tool to assess specific symptoms related to swallowing difficulties. The EAT-10 is recognized for its effectiveness in identifying dysphagia and is utilized in clinical settings to help healthcare professionals understand the extent of a patient's swallowing issues. This comprehensive tool is available in multiple languages, including Spanish, where it is referred to as "test de cribado utilizado para evaluar la disfagia en el paciente." Overall, the EAT-10 is an essential instrument for evaluating and managing dysphagia in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,806140d9fadd08a1e72238d53c829eb2,8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378,d590f931bbeb2d87392c751f2746e4da,d96ab48565912e67fdb51ccdf5a100ac</data>
      <data key="d3">959</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">336</data>
      <data key="d7">03559095e78842d6b3b23b99c5a0ce89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSIDAD DE SE&#218;L">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Universidad de Se&#250;l conducted a comprehensive study that reviewed various screening methods for dysphagia, significantly contributing to clinical practice. This review specifically examined 31 different screening methods for dysphagia that were developed and utilized between 1992 and 2011.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378</data>
      <data key="d3">157</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">337</data>
      <data key="d7">f1044986302d414596b8332d976106f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUSS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gugging Swallowing Assessment (GUSS) is a test that offers scientific rigor for detecting dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136</data>
      <data key="d3">157</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">338</data>
      <data key="d7">158482b5235e4f84a7799fb373bccf55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTR HOSP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTR HOSP is a specialized journal dedicated to the publication of articles and studies focused on nutrition within hospital settings. It encompasses a wide range of topics related to clinical nutrition research, including home artificial nutrition, enteral nutrition, and dietary requirements for older adults. The journal addresses various nutritional issues, such as the effectiveness of hypocaloric diets and the management of dysphagia, evidenced by its publication of the translation and validation of the EAT-10 scale for dysphagia screening.

NUTR HOSP also explores the impact of nutrition on health, particularly concerning cardiovascular disease and obesity management. It publishes research that examines dietary modifications for patients and the overall effects of nutrition on health outcomes in hospital care. Through its comprehensive approach, NUTR HOSP serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals interested in the intersection of nutrition and clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">0381a11415dca4cfeda74f1de745d6ae,1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,1e6677459719ee2aa18d6d2ffbe46330,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,28503044e98192e03a043b0103f37a9b,2f5d9123a78d23b1bc3d9f06d7a53d78,3534154ea7562c7d4abe51bf29546109,62cb70a5fd28a7c444f52a64ce2a7f75,6907c82f1f024ed1b75f6aea88c47b3e,7e3e2024996e402fc0ab62933ab9417b,8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136,987613571ae90d73ce7a875f3ddc41bf,d6a596828c4ca22ce0a49c5ba26b33e8,d96ab48565912e67fdb51ccdf5a100ac,ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4,dea403b707c5339329451aa7494d9ca5,e271766bdc88e84209e5cdac4adc0724,fa36086a4b64a662e6e1752ee6e589aa</data>
      <data key="d3">1579</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">23</data>
      <data key="d6">339</data>
      <data key="d7">e295ea5872514f3380a06933cadc5d00</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) is a prominent organization dedicated to advancing the field of clinical nutrition and metabolism across Europe. It supports healthcare professionals by providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations that are grounded in current research. ESPEN focuses on various aspects of clinical nutrition, including nutritional support in critical care settings, neurological pathologies, and specific patient populations such as those with dementia and liver disease.

ESPEN publishes guidelines that address nutritional assessment tools and practices, emphasizing the importance of enteral nutrition in clinical settings. The organization is committed to promoting best practices in clinical nutrition and metabolism, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the latest evidence-based information to enhance patient care. Through its efforts, ESPEN plays a crucial role in shaping the standards and definitions related to nutritional support, thereby contributing significantly to the field of clinical nutrition and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92,59a97e6bf8748a66eb335bec2852ce38,7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3,73fd366244763cef4b13c058330147b1,8c1c8ef18f5c90fe936a3ca920768ee2,aae3f23f674724518bcb311a99d764d6,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835,f7d56bac9cc29e47690669e812094c99,fb0c6cd346ca91e15f8ff1cc07570d9d,fbeb9736ced2a2a020bdb39bdd10de0d</data>
      <data key="d3">911</data>
