    <node id="ESPEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPEN, which stands for the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is a prominent organization dedicated to advancing the study and practice of clinical nutrition and metabolism across Europe. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for various aspects of clinical nutrition, including enteral and parenteral nutrition, aimed at improving patient care in diverse medical settings.

ESPEN develops and disseminates clinical guidelines for nutritional support tailored to specific patient populations, including critically ill patients, those undergoing surgery, oncology patients, and individuals with conditions such as liver disease, pancreatitis, and renal insufficiency. The organization emphasizes the importance of nutritional screening and assessment, recommending tools like the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) and the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) for identifying malnutrition risk, particularly in elderly and frail individuals.

In addition to its focus on clinical guidelines, ESPEN supports projects addressing hospital malnutrition and offers scholarships to enhance nutritional practices in healthcare settings. The organization also provides recommendations for nutritional interventions in patients with special needs, such as those with dementia, and promotes the use of immunomodulatory formulas for patients undergoing cancer surgery.

ESPEN's guidelines cover a wide range of topics, including preoperative nutritional support, management of acute intestinal failure, and hydration relevant to diabetes management. The organization is committed to evidence-based practices and regularly publishes consensus papers and research findings to inform healthcare professionals about the latest developments in clinical nutrition.

Overall, ESPEN plays a crucial role in shaping the standards of nutritional care in Europe, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the latest evidence and recommendations to support their patients' nutritional needs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">0379ef9e3f56ccd30c572884eb5bd723,07a16ed299a7f8bafcaa44a54495a9c3,07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb,0b02ff4978fb09a0b2a360ae8c661337,125acd19edb76fa23986de56fc2517e8,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973,14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,202e4fa915a698c9d9164c3fcc61534e,242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,2ec23f85b858abc42196ef48260e8cb0,3159307e5633698722f72fde1e82702f,36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,396dda5c9597828f0749f963f42142b4,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,3f1d1c7c7c62b83f62f6fa31c25f65b2,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,477da86aa038212a1e2b555b5a854cba,4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe,4cf0c8d0f4e711be85d16ee71317aa4e,54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,61890d3cb54fb752b95a4dfad8db8bb6,61eea56f443c7bb2509edd6f42af2643,62cb70a5fd28a7c444f52a64ce2a7f75,687a74f539aea483b8c6611f3b062931,76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,8c198f866d8fb49a782cb57139b30d76,90fe1d34782402a1896d33ad5bb47614,91b470ee527a45d8e81a821eeb9ce259,969bdfc6cc15b9089e96000addd87561,97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,aae3f23f674724518bcb311a99d764d6,b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,c07baf818737d704c290ca0f5eefd30f,c3182f51249513a920db6b935632fead,c84372864fd2ee7b7ed425b2d597efdb,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce,ce8f5f24dbbf8624e49a6f85c2ad0d04,d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,dd15aaae6791a32f0adb78cc25cb70c3,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb,eae8ddef005974a2ffe71cf7c61b0634