    <node id="VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "VIDEOENDOSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N" is a diagnostic procedure that allows for the observation of the swallowing phase in patients, which is crucial for diagnosing oropharyngeal dysphagia. This technique involves both static and dynamic assessments of the anatomical structures involved in the swallowing process. It was first described by Dr. Susan Langmore in 1988 and is utilized to evaluate swallowing function and anatomy in patients experiencing difficulties with swallowing. The procedure is conducted in specialized units, such as the UFDOF unit, ensuring a comprehensive evaluation of the patient's swallowing capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">67cdbb6902307ad33e10fe5e37096083,a3444da30e339275da1056c3e13bcae5,be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c,dae3d2cddf63b2af4067a27d8b9d7ab5,eb2f276d3dc4e4a9e53923d9d80fec1a</data>
