    </node>
    <node id="EDITORIAL M&#201;DICA PANAMERICANA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Editorial M&#233;dica Panamericana is a publishing house known for its contributions to medical literature. It is particularly recognized for publishing the "Tratado de Nutrici&#243;n," a comprehensive medical textbook that discusses oligomonomeric formulas among other topics related to nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b02ff4978fb09a0b2a360ae8c661337,2def4be9506db96f8bdfe9e3ba6f9b6f,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,6dfb109dac53e054fd015f6d8adf48ac,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,dae3d2cddf63b2af4067a27d8b9d7ab5</data>
      <data key="d3">1479</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">388</data>
      <data key="d7">19a2e642d34048b0956971e0e775a83c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR SWALLOWING DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Society for Swallowing Disorders (ESSD) is an organization dedicated to advancing research and education concerning swallowing disorders, particularly dysphagia. In 2012, the ESSD played a pivotal role by hosting a meeting that initiated the International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI), aimed at standardizing practices related to dysphagia management. Additionally, the ESSD is committed to providing guidelines and standards for the diagnosis and treatment of swallowing disorders, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the most current and effective practices in the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">90aa696a6e48637e06acfcd7213699da,be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c,c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">946</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">389</data>
      <data key="d7">7db0297a0b1047f892d8fdccff1c435d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUSAN LANGMORE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dr. Susan Langmore is a physician known for her contributions to the evaluation of swallowing disorders and for publishing a key reference book on the subject in 2001.</data>
      <data key="d2">be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">945</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">390</data>
      <data key="d7">509f66e56b274d9c8901bf2eb3321f67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VFS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VFS, or Videofluoroscopic Swallowing Study, is a diagnostic procedure utilized to analyze the swallowing process and the movement of anatomical structures involved in bolus formation and propulsion. It is specifically designed to observe the oral phase of swallowing and is regarded as the gold standard in diagnosing swallowing disorders. The procedure involves a radiological examination that provides detailed insights into the mechanics of swallowing, making it an essential tool for healthcare professionals in assessing and treating patients with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">371e848e9da77bf71f58614d1265aff8,38a83c2ae0b0c378bfcaba5d18866dc0,be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">945</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">391</data>
      <data key="d7">e37e63ae56a24e9e94324bb1ea32c690</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VED, or Videofluoroscopic Esophageal Dysphagia, is a diagnostic test utilized to evaluate the swallowing process, particularly focusing on the pharyngeal phase of swallowing. This test assesses both the oral phase and the function of the upper esophageal sphincter. VED serves as an exploration process in a medical context, specifically aimed at assessing swallowing and the anatomical structures involved. Additionally, it is often performed in conjunction with videoendoscopy (VFS) to provide a comprehensive evaluation of swallowing function.</data>
      <data key="d2">071141fe8f0a45f56522de2f52ddcb46,23e28a69f275d88d0a56a430dde4b568,371e848e9da77bf71f58614d1265aff8,be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">392</data>
      <data key="d7">abea6f4e775c4a788d6d0e53ee773dfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROSCOPIOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibroscopes are medical instruments used by otolaryngologists for endoscopic examinations, including the evaluation of swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">945</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">393</data>
      <data key="d7">d8f539ed770147bea881d86ee29ba144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANOMETR&#205;A ESOF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MANOMETR&#205;A ESOF&#193;GICA is a diagnostic test that measures the pressure and coordination of muscle contractions in the esophagus. This procedure is essential for assessing swallowing disorders and diagnosing esophageal motility disorders. By evaluating the pressure patterns and muscle activity within the esophagus, MANOMETR&#205;A ESOF&#193;GICA provides critical insights into the functioning of this vital organ.</data>
      <data key="d2">be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c,cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">394</data>
      <data key="d7">01b129ed4154414c8e95215696d9b710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PH-METR&#205;A DE 24 HORAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">24-hour pH monitoring is a diagnostic test used to measure acid levels in the esophagus, which can help identify issues related to swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">395</data>
      <data key="d7">668f5d0320e343cb82a68ccf53a923a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMPEDANCIOMETR&#205;A INTRALUMINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intraluminal impedance is a diagnostic test that measures the flow of liquids and solids in the esophagus, aiding in the evaluation of swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">396</data>
      <data key="d7">4c6fc62363ad410bb0ca9fb70766ecad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OTORRINOLARING&#211;LOGOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">OTORRINOLARING&#211;LOGOS, also known as otolaryngologists, are medical specialists dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders associated with the head and neck. Their expertise encompasses a range of conditions related to the ear, nose, and throat, including specific issues such as oropharyngeal dysphagia, which refers to swallowing disorders. These professionals play a crucial role in evaluating and managing various ailments affecting the throat and surrounding areas, ensuring comprehensive care for patients with related health concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3444da30e339275da1056c3e13bcae5,be410757354948d16ee86e49a852101c,dfc3b0905ab9fc1fca9fc64473ebed80</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">397</data>
      <data key="d7">4947d91ddf844cd4b6389930cd2309bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LANGMORE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">LANGMORE refers to both Dr. Langmore, a medical professional recognized for her expertise in swallowing disorders, and a scale developed for assessing the risk of aspiration in patients. Dr. Langmore is particularly noted for her contributions to the field, including the publication of a reference manual on swallowing disorders in 2001. The Langmore scale serves as a tool for evaluating the risk of aspiration by analyzing the occupation of pharyngeal-laryngeal areas by secretions, thereby aiding in the clinical assessment of patients with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">071141fe8f0a45f56522de2f52ddcb46,a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1535</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">398</data>
      <data key="d7">c262b1e2d27545f5bbee6d90d0f77bd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOSCOPIC EVALUATION AND TREATMENT OF SWALLOWING DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A book published by Dr. Langmore in 2001 that serves as a reference for diagnosing and treating swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1535</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">399</data>
      <data key="d7">a19ab6f2f9264e2ea12c4d28db5c40a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIDEOENDOSCOPIC EXPLORATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A procedure similar to that proposed by Dr. Langmore, used to evaluate swallowing by observing anatomy and swallowing mechanics.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1534</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">400</data>
      <data key="d7">d870b4a45e654ef4a0147c322af0d84c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METHEMOGLOBINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A medical condition that can occur due to the use of certain dyes, such as methylene blue, during swallowing evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1535</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">401</data>
      <data key="d7">54e807523b51470caa34dd0e6fb495cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIDEOENDOSCOPE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A medical device used in the videoendoscopic exploration to visualize the anatomy and assess swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1534</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">402</data>
      <data key="d7">d44ba0fe0b184a54bc95e62daa3b8506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGH DEFINITION SCREEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A display device used in conjunction with a videoendoscope to provide clear images during swallowing evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1534</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">403</data>
      <data key="d7">ed5107d501a1403bab2f6e734538183a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSENT FORM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A document that patients must sign to acknowledge understanding of the risks associated with swallowing evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">404</data>
      <data key="d7">778e616cc51e40c9b711f783ed4e87f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THICKENING AGENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A substance used to modify the consistency of liquids for swallowing evaluations, ensuring safety for patients with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1534</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">405</data>
      <data key="d7">90bc99d6f3714934a9b17cb52af164a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWALLOWING DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">a76f6268d6065b1baabb9e13ef7f098c</data>
      <data key="d3">1534</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">406</data>
      <data key="d7">41c3c260f80243ccba5ec64ea87eabf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "PACIENTE" refers to individuals receiving medical care, particularly those with specific health conditions that necessitate various forms of treatment and nutritional support. In the context of oropharyngeal dysphagia, a patient is someone who experiences difficulties with swallowing and may require assistance during meals to prevent choking and ensure proper nutrition. This includes individuals undergoing evaluation and treatment for swallowing disorders, who receive care from a multidisciplinary team at specialized units.

Patients may also be those receiving medical treatment for complications related to catheter use, nutritional risks associated with surgery, or conditions such as cancer, diabetes, and other critical illnesses. They often require tailored dietary modifications due to challenges in chewing or swallowing, and their nutritional needs are assessed to determine appropriate enteral or parenteral nutrition.

Specific cases include patients diagnosed with conditions such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, severe caloric malnutrition, and various eating disorders, who may experience significant weight loss and require specialized interventions. For instance, individuals with diabetes, including type 1 and type 2, may face challenges in managing their insulin intake and dietary habits, while those with cystic fibrosis or Crohn's disease may undergo multiple nutritional therapies and surgeries.

Additionally, patients may be monitored for complications arising from their conditions, such as diarrhea or fluctuations in glucose levels, and they have rights regarding their medical information and consent for treatment. The importance of patient collaboration during procedures, such as the placement of a nasogastric tube, is also emphasized.

Overall, "PACIENTE" encompasses a diverse group of individuals who are actively engaged in their healthcare, receiving various forms of nutritional support and medical treatment tailored to their unique health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375,09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada,0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,1130db2843c569042990b711cf15d8ee,13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,140611dbb8a68fc40712c946de92b73f,1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,1719a8d20788e3b25240980cad2b6c5d,17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce,1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,22dcdc62dcda2e81a8707024945a4b01,23e28a69f275d88d0a56a430dde4b568,27c75984e62c5adcac1ac33cbdc520dc,28e2e3a92ef4dd76af0898ae3e3df522,2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,2ebe12524f7750215eee73b328b601ee,306519cca8810e0ff1c973128a75200a,362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,3f685a05a9682db6dcde958d1918cc77,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe,4b4f297dec86d7f65e362ad688bbb28f,4fbc9ba7c1f3ff190b594c75e7eac015,5099515cbc35bc6330fb794c4f1d715d,514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,544f7d3afd9f7def46c357525e55cabf,574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,593ae586183f02d2611966f8a1603e5d,59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5,5c11ed246e1a48261910b9b71b65014c,5cf1703fd601b27dd0ebda9f20cb3259,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,61eea56f443c7bb2509edd6f42af2643,64417661dbb019f8f4ceb9fcc2fbdaa6,67cdbb6902307ad33e10fe5e37096083,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,7b13bde26d33b4316c3183dd027ed909,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,7c842769e1890739769789ed10a08005,7dbb13ddc40e2f4d060338cabf9ecea7,7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241