      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">071141fe8f0a45f56522de2f52ddcb46</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">435</data>
      <data key="d7">f236a22d44714f1094443100df79ca69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIDEOFLUOROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A radiographic procedure designed to define the anatomy and physiology of swallowing in patients and to examine the effectiveness of rehabilitation strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d3">1078</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">436</data>
      <data key="d7">39f9e9929b064fbdb05f572275dcb142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOGOPEDA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A logopeda, also known as a logopedist or speech therapist, is a specialized professional dedicated to improving oral and swallowing functions in patients. They conduct various exercises and therapies aimed at enhancing speech and language abilities, as well as addressing swallowing disorders such as dysphagia. In particular, logopedas play a crucial role in the rehabilitation process for individuals experiencing swallowing difficulties. They also work with children to rehabilitate swallowing and feeding behaviors, helping to normalize oral stimulation. Overall, the logopeda's expertise encompasses a wide range of speech and language therapy, making them essential in the treatment and support of patients with communication and swallowing challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,2bd5c03d0aa542ef4a7b0380e30e84c3,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d3">937</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">437</data>
      <data key="d7">d77cb875036844239b2d1c66f0bb6242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EQUIPAMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The basic fluoroscopic unit required for conducting swallowing assessments, including a constant radiation source and a radiography detector.</data>
      <data key="d2">b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d3">1078</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">438</data>
      <data key="d7">a0a9b172b56d4bdba464adbd22462368</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANATOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The study of the structure of the body, particularly relevant in understanding the swallowing process in patients with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">439</data>
      <data key="d7">bf0a2714da0b436d97f762c35c33ca63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISIOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fisiolog&#237;a refers to the study of bodily functions and processes, encompassing various aspects of human health and performance. It is particularly relevant in the context of nutrition and exercise performance, as it helps to understand how the body responds to different dietary and physical activities. Additionally, Fisiolog&#237;a includes the examination of specific functions such as swallowing and dysphagia, highlighting its importance in understanding both general bodily functions and specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
