    <node id="SENSIBILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SENSIBILIDAD refers to the assessment of sensitivity in various medical contexts. In the realm of swallowing disorders, it pertains to the evaluation of sensitivity as outlined in relevant manuals. Additionally, SENSIBILIDAD is associated with the ability of diagnostic tests to accurately identify patients with pheochromocytomas, a type of tumor that can affect the adrenal glands. This sensitivity can vary depending on the imaging techniques employed. Specifically, tests such as 18F-FDG and MIBG are noted for their sensitivity in detecting the presence of disease, including metastatic pheochromocytomas. Overall, SENSIBILIDAD encompasses both the evaluation of swallowing disorders and the effectiveness of imaging tests in identifying specific medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">0096a43decd2fc51a199ad13832cca8a,94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
