    <node id="REFLUJO GASTROESOF&#193;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El reflujo gastroesof&#225;gico (RGE) es una afecci&#243;n multifactorial que se caracteriza por la exposici&#243;n del es&#243;fago distal al &#225;cido, lo que puede provocar molestias y complicaciones. Esta condici&#243;n, tambi&#233;n conocida como enfermedad por reflujo gastroesof&#225;gico (GERD), es un trastorno digestivo cr&#243;nico en el que el &#225;cido del est&#243;mago o la bilis irritan el revestimiento del es&#243;fago. El RGE es prevalente entre los pacientes con fibrosis qu&#237;stica, donde un porcentaje significativo experimenta s&#237;ntomas relacionados. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado que el reflujo gastroesof&#225;gico puede empeorar o ser inducido por procedimientos de gastrostom&#237;a. En resumen, el REFLUJO GASTROESOF&#193;GICO es una condici&#243;n que genera altos costes sanitarios y requiere atenci&#243;n m&#233;dica adecuada para su manejo.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,6d116bdd48d75e9e6c33844db5816915,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9</data>
      <data key="d3">963</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">493</data>
      <data key="d7">d7bebb97260a454d8edc98a589635aec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ES&#211;FAGO DE BARRETT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El es&#243;fago de Barrett es una condici&#243;n precancerosa asociada al reflujo gastroesof&#225;gico que requiere diagn&#243;stico y tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d116bdd48d75e9e6c33844db5816915</data>
      <data key="d3">963</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">494</data>
      <data key="d7">f9576fb7583c4806b52376d875a0ddb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PH-METR&#205;A ESOF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La pH-metr&#237;a esof&#225;gica es una prueba diagn&#243;stica que cuantifica el reflujo &#225;cido y es la prueba de referencia para el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad por reflujo gastroesof&#225;gico.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d116bdd48d75e9e6c33844db5816915</data>
      <data key="d3">963</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">495</data>
      <data key="d7">546f8f7f9bfe4b999a93657e9a72e275</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IBP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">IBP, or Inhibitors of Proton Pump, is a class of medications utilized to treat acid-related conditions, particularly gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) and esophagitis. These medications are effective in alleviating symptoms associated with gastroesophageal reflux, making them a common choice for managing these conditions. In summary, IBP medications play a crucial role in the treatment of GERD and related disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d116bdd48d75e9e6c33844db5816915,b58b0258891d9207b27237bab6a03946,f7c941bced546a7d607c30a9a5e9d887</data>
      <data key="d3">965</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">496</data>
      <data key="d7">6cf34026c76248e580f4a584b749d6da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia is a common medical condition characterized by a deficiency of red blood cells or hemoglobin in the blood, leading to symptoms such as fatigue and weakness. It is often associated with various underlying health issues, including Wilson's disease, where it may result from hemolysis and liver dysfunction. Anemia can arise from multiple causes, including iron deficiency, chronic diseases, malabsorption, and nutrient deficiencies, particularly in conditions like inflammatory bowel diseases and celiac disease. In celiac patients, iron deficiency anemia is frequently observed due to malabsorption of nutrients, including iron and folic acid.

The condition can also be prevalent among malnourished elderly individuals and cancer patients. In chronic kidney disease, anemia may occur due to a lack of erythropoietin, a hormone essential for red blood cell production. Additionally, anemia can be linked to disorders of iron metabolism, such as hereditary hemochromatosis, and can be managed through dietary control of iron intake.

Anemia is not only a sign of potential nutritional deficiencies but can also indicate more serious underlying conditions, necessitating further evaluation, especially in patients presenting atypical symptoms. Overall, anemia is a multifaceted condition that requires careful assessment and management based on its diverse causes and implications for health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,4e8b65ec9939ccf2152e68fa7f8b12c4,5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c,66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de,68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2,6d116bdd48d75e9e6c33844db5816915,7ba4a7e7b4c409f6d4c6979a7de6c832,7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,83b82871866963bb43f901dd9ca09fcb,a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74,b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b,cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
