    <node id="ANILLO DE SCHATZKI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El anillo de Schatzki es una condici&#243;n que puede causar disfagia, caracterizada por un estrechamiento del es&#243;fago que puede ser resultado de inflamaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">524</data>
      <data key="d7">a94a935b2f2c410a80b8d6a0ac44ea48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La endoscopia es un procedimiento diagn&#243;stico m&#233;dico que permite la visualizaci&#243;n directa del interior del tracto digestivo. Este procedimiento es fundamental para investigar diversas condiciones, como la disfagia, y puede incluir la toma de biopsias para evaluar reacciones al&#233;rgicas o descartar hemorragias, especialmente en pacientes con deficiencia de hierro. Durante la endoscopia, se pueden observar alteraciones en la mucosa, como atrofia parcheada y linfangiectasias, lo que contribuye significativamente al diagn&#243;stico del paciente. En resumen, la endoscopia es una herramienta clave en la evaluaci&#243;n y diagn&#243;stico de diversas patolog&#237;as del tracto digestivo.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,4e38cc524978e9eb248721d211c4574b,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d3">954</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">525</data>
      <data key="d7">c1b3101572304252ac4bffe84a34a921</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESOFAGITIS EOSINOF&#205;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esofagitis eosinof&#237;lica is an allergic condition that primarily affects the esophagus, often associated with food allergies. This disease typically manifests in childhood or adolescence and is characterized by the presence of eosinophilic infiltration in the esophageal walls. Symptoms commonly include dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and reflux. Diagnosis is achieved through endoscopy and biopsies, which help confirm the inflammation of the esophagus.</data>
      <data key="d2">693b5721c7fc52c8165c48b580777840,9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1,cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d3">1531</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">526</data>
      <data key="d7">53fde18432494c05aff95c72af8a8a29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TUMORES refer to abnormal growths of cells that can be either benign or malignant. They are associated with various medical conditions and complications. For instance, gastric or colon tumors may indicate the need for parenteral nutrition, particularly in patients suffering from malnutrition. Additionally, tumors can lead to hypopituitarism, which affects hormone production in the pituitary gland. They are also a significant consideration in patients presenting with dysphagia, as tumors can impair esophageal function. Furthermore, tumors can be a contributing factor to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), especially in cases involving pulmonary and non-thoracic tumors. In some instances, tumors may necessitate a hematopoietic cell transplant due to their impact on the body&#8217;s cellular functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">084639519c323a72fcf1322c38efd173,2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740,4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32,addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce,cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d3">1130</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">527</data>
      <data key="d7">2f5f7f3ff66143dc9790085cc09634ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVERT&#205;CULOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los divert&#237;culos son sacos que pueden formarse en el es&#243;fago y son una de las causas menos frecuentes de disfagia que deben ser consideradas.</data>
      <data key="d2">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
