    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL TREATMENT">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Nutritional treatment encompasses a range of dietary interventions aimed at maintaining normal blood glucose levels and ensuring adequate nutrition for growth and development, particularly in patients with metabolic disorders. It includes specific dietary recommendations for diabetes management, which focus on controlling blood sugar levels and preventing complications associated with the condition. Additionally, nutritional treatment involves adjustments and interventions tailored to manage symptoms of various metabolic disorders and improve the overall nutritional status of individuals, especially those experiencing dysphagia. Furthermore, it is essential for addressing malnutrition in patients with disorders of feeding (DOF), emphasizing the importance of meeting energy, protein, and hydration needs. Overall, nutritional treatment plays a critical role in enhancing health outcomes for individuals with diverse nutritional challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">28cd3f60e1ccd9129a7d4d386e241a93,67f60ae11335cf41da4f96400b69e67b,73fd366244763cef4b13c058330147b1,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,ccd3c800d2985d4ad5e2c8d6e88b1b68,e2304aa7e992d9e26558aab3c807b51d</data>
      <data key="d3">1221</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
