    <node id="NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING 2002">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional Risk Screening 2002 (NRS 2002) is a validated screening tool designed to assess nutritional risk in patients, particularly in hospital settings. Developed by a Danish group associated with the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN), NRS 2002 is specifically aimed at identifying patients at risk of malnutrition, including those with conditions such as gastric carcinoma prior to surgery. The tool requires specific training for proper execution, ensuring accurate assessments of nutritional risk among hospitalized patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185,687a74f539aea483b8c6611f3b062931,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a,aae3f23f674724518bcb311a99d764d6,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
