      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">551</data>
      <data key="d7">b976c10eb52f43b0b5bbaa5e2e0cc2e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ALIMENTOS refers to a broad category of food products that are essential for clinical nutrition and dietary management, focusing on specific dietary needs and health outcomes. These food items are formulated to meet various nutritional requirements and are subject to safety regulations and standards to prevent contamination and ensure public health. 

In the context of children's nutrition, ALIMENTOS includes various food items that children may initially reject but can learn to accept through repeated exposure. Additionally, ALIMENTOS encompasses food products that can influence health, particularly concerning cardiovascular risk, and those that are evaluated for their nutritional value and impact on health.

ALIMENTOS also includes food administered during assessments, such as the MECV-V, to evaluate swallowing efficacy and safety. Foods in this category can vary in their nutritional content, including phosphorus levels based on processing and additives, and may contain nutritional information and health claims. 

Moreover, ALIMENTOS consists of various food groups, including dairy, cereals, legumes, tubers, fruits, fats, proteins, and vegetables, which are integral to dietary recommendations. These foods can also contain high levels of FODMAPs, potentially triggering symptoms in sensitive individuals. 

For patients with specific health conditions, such as dysphagia, ALIMENTOS refers to food items that may need to be modified in consistency for safety and ease of swallowing. This includes foods that can be thickened for better texture and those that must meet specific hygiene and safety standards to prevent infections. 

ALIMENTOS plays a crucial role in patient recovery, providing nutritional support that may need to be adjusted for individuals with eating disorders, cancer, or those on controlled diets, such as ketogenic or low-sodium diets. Furthermore, these food items can interact with medications, affecting their efficacy and safety, and may cause allergic reactions in sensitive individuals. 

Overall, ALIMENTOS encompasses a wide range of food items that are vital for health management, dietary planning, and nutritional support across various populations and health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,03b047c49cda5e7bb642efcc9109ccc6,058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375,072912695b1cff9f390d4ead3b9ad742,085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f,0a43b350a248173236a96a64e266b744,11662a6f83b8217976d8c9c5d33fe7fd,17fc469cf1ddbb8fa68bad4446bd65e6,186a95fdfe908123ad6f42d43b52ee1d,1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b,1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108,232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a,2d07762e6db07c2587caceac3427a1c7,2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb,36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,3dbf07634cee8d4d443f59ed50f98b54,42cc35e2edb450d48bb31f7c51b7a02f,544f7d3afd9f7def46c357525e55cabf,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,701eb4c24e94839def8d18882a2dda63,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,7f0ee0bea2b1dfd09e75026d4c027291,89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d,8a7b2d5e0440750e36603c8d3f93a68a,8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950,ae1766e8ae855b3c79ad6d5fdefab1b0,bc394d70461777b6300d5449185a7859,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4,caeec333a833f2df895a80c4047485cb,caf1d075a295b93dcd3c6f5cf72b028d,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978,d10e6c00bbb982bda449b9cb815691a3,da965f79110bd8915deff461d0d91187,dc38a37c30b175667931b84a9c9103bb,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
