    <node id="MALNUTRITION UNIVERSAL SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) is a comprehensive clinical method developed to assess the risk of malnutrition among various populations, particularly focusing on adults. Initially designed for community use, it has been validated for application in institutionalized settings, such as nursing homes and hospitals. MUST analyzes key factors including Body Mass Index (BMI), weight loss, and the impact of acute illness on food intake to identify individuals who are malnourished or at risk of malnutrition.

This standardized screening tool is widely utilized in clinical environments and has been specifically noted for its effectiveness in predicting clinical outcomes, including mortality and length of hospital stay, particularly in elderly patients. MUST is recognized for its role in identifying individuals who may require nutritional intervention, especially those preparing for medical procedures like transplants. Developed by the British Association for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN), MUST serves as an essential resource for healthcare professionals aiming to address malnutrition and improve patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,084639519c323a72fcf1322c38efd173,17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,628cd3e2664561301cbe6679f48c4bd3,7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff,f764c1a74fbbce262e79b50639acb7bd</data>
