    <node id="MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) is a structured and practical questionnaire designed for the early detection of malnutrition or risk of malnutrition in elderly individuals, both in outpatient settings and institutionalized environments. This tool is particularly valuable in geriatric evaluations, as it includes a dietary questionnaire and is recognized for its high sensitivity in assessing nutritional status. The MNA is validated specifically for elderly populations and is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in both institutionalized and non-institutionalized individuals.

The MNA serves to classify patients based on their nutritional risk, helping healthcare providers identify those at risk of malnutrition. It evaluates various aspects of nutritional status and is linked to criteria of frailty, making it an essential component of comprehensive geriatric assessments. Overall, the Mini Nutritional Assessment is a non-invasive tool that plays a crucial role in identifying and addressing malnutrition in the elderly.</data>
      <data key="d2">242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,687a74f539aea483b8c6611f3b062931,83d00bec042a3fe8b69d68316d8569ff,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39,c639615d7681ffeb945a996d231bb7aa,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4,f764c1a74fbbce262e79b50639acb7bd</data>
      <data key="d3">729</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">560</data>
      <data key="d7">ad69106330b84548bddfb4439f353cc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRITION SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Malnutrition Screening Tool (MST) is an Australian-origin method specifically designed to assess the risk of malnutrition in patients, particularly those with swallowing difficulties and oncology patients. It is validated for use in clinical settings and focuses on recent appetite changes and weight loss to identify malnutrition risk. The MST serves as a comprehensive screening tool that aids healthcare professionals in recognizing malnutrition in patients, ensuring timely intervention and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,28cd3f60e1ccd9129a7d4d386e241a93,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04,f764c1a74fbbce262e79b50639acb7bd</data>
