    </node>
    <node id="ESPANA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Spain, known as "Espa&#241;a" in Spanish, is a country located in Southern Europe that has made significant advancements in various health and nutritional initiatives. It is the site where the Multidisciplinary Consensus on Hospital Malnutrition Management was developed, particularly focusing on the approach to malnutrition in the elderly population. Spain has conducted numerous studies on the prevalence of obesity and its complications, as well as diabetes, highlighting the socio-economic impacts of these health issues. The country has seen a general decrease in diabetes mortality rates, although this trend contrasts with the situation in the region of Castilla y Le&#243;n.

In the realm of nutritional care, Spain is actively discussing guidelines for nutritional interventions tailored for frail elderly patients and is implementing specific food fortification programs to combat iron deficiency, especially in breakfast cereals and infant formulas. The country adheres to specific guidelines for gluten labeling in accordance with the Codex Alimentarius and is involved in the discussion and application of nutritional assessment tools relevant to elderly care.

Spain also plays a role in health and biomedical research, with various initiatives aimed at understanding and addressing health conditions such as bronquiectasias and McArdle disease, which has a reported prevalence of 1 in 170,000 individuals. The Sistema Nacional de Salud operates within Spain to regulate health services, ensuring that medical treatments, including iron carboxymaltose and pancreatic enzyme preparations for cystic fibrosis patients, are available and recommended.

Furthermore, Spain is noted for its studies on population weight and ideal weight tables, as well as the indirect method for measuring sodium levels in patients with altered protein levels. The country is committed to discussing and applying nutritional standards and assessments, including the recommended daily dosage of calcium for the elderly, thereby contributing to the overall health and well-being of its population.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,028c43c3f0f3d1f8085eed8518636f97,17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,1d8aa686c6377246fee05010ef969018,201f8e6a0d6c49396cf9c81f5da4520f,4464b0da291e94ba7b7f5b51134b4a75,6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a,6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0,7c815eb3ecbf3e8cb61d3f9e27d9e061,7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd,86d733befbaaebe4eccbc45db498a0b0,a25b0f84bc321cad942a2e33f681a5e4,a2675f78609440ca1162c24997360929,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4,cc6ee3d7bc9bfaf4a06f3f02c4907eb0,ce0de74f95e1a41a930b2df09da1f887,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831,f764c1a74fbbce262e79b50639acb7bd</data>
