    <node id="NESTL&#201; NUTRITION INSTITUTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nestl&#233; Nutrition Institute is an organization dedicated to nutritional research, assessment, and education. It focuses on evaluating and treating nutritional status, offering tools such as the Mini Nutritional Assessment to help healthcare professionals assess patients' nutritional needs. The institute aims to enhance understanding and awareness of nutrition, particularly in the context of malnutrition, by providing resources and support for effective nutritional screening and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,83d00bec042a3fe8b69d68316d8569ff</data>
      <data key="d3">729</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">568</data>
      <data key="d7">59d290db289f4089a2b9e913a4ef897b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERDIDA DE PESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">P&#233;rdida de peso, or weight loss, is a significant factor evaluated in the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which is used to classify patients' nutritional risk. This condition is particularly relevant in various medical contexts, including inflammatory bowel diseases, where weight loss can occur due to malabsorption, diarrhea, and decreased appetite. Additionally, weight loss is a common issue among cancer patients, often necessitating the implementation of nutritional support strategies to address the challenges associated with maintaining adequate nutrition during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">569</data>
      <data key="d7">a0a8b99d4c1c48a798b29bd0c4ab019d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOVILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Movilidad refers to the assessment of a patient's ability to move independently, which is an important factor in evaluating their nutritional status. This assessment is conducted as part of the Mini Nutritional Assessment, where understanding a patient's mobility is crucial, as it can significantly impact their overall nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,8e8aac45bfe71fa006f622690dfdbbb8</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
