    <node id="&#205;NDICE DE MASA CORPORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#205;ndice de Masa Corporal (IMC), known as Body Mass Index (BMI) in English, is a widely utilized measure that assesses body weight relative to height. It serves as a simple index for classifying individuals based on their weight and height, making it an important tool for monitoring health, particularly in various patient populations, including those with genetic disorders such as Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI) and chronic conditions like Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD).

BMI is crucial for evaluating nutritional status, as it helps identify obesity and malnutrition. It is often employed in nutritional screening and is a key measure in the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which evaluates a patient's weight in relation to their height. Additionally, research has indicated a correlation between BMI and the consumption of sugary beverages among children and adolescents.

However, it is important to note that BMI may not be a reliable indicator for all patients, particularly those with liver disease, due to potential fluid retention that can skew results. Overall, the &#205;ndice de Masa Corporal is a significant metric in health assessments, providing insights into an individual's nutritional health and aiding in the diagnosis and severity classification of eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,8e8aac45bfe71fa006f622690dfdbbb8,9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210,ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e,bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,cb8368db73f739b1f11f2a202c776e6d,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682,f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af</data>
