    <node id="AUTONOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Autonom&#237;a encompasses the concept of a patient's ability to perform daily activities independently, which is influenced by their nutritional status. It also signifies the right of patients to make informed decisions regarding their health care, a principle that holds particular importance in Anglo-Saxon culture. Furthermore, Autonom&#237;a is evaluated through tools such as the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which assesses a patient's capacity to live independently. Overall, Autonom&#237;a integrates both the practical aspects of daily living and the ethical dimensions of patient rights in health care decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bc48d0666e895b990c211acf7cbcf23,46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d,67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161</data>
