    <node id="SPAIN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Spain is a country located in Southern Europe, known for its diverse population and significant public health research initiatives. It has been the site of various studies, including the EPIRCE study on the prevalence of chronic renal disease and the PREDYCES study, which estimated the costs associated with disease-related malnutrition. Spain faces a considerable public health challenge due to the increasing prevalence of diabetes mellitus, ranking fourth in Europe for the number of affected individuals. The country has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, estimated at 35-50%, and has seen a rise in obesity rates and food allergies over the years.

In addition to diabetes, Spain conducts extensive research on other health issues, including the prevalence and management of diseases such as EPOC (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) and Cystic Fibrosis, as well as iron deficiency and iron deficiency anemia. The country is also involved in studying hypopituitarism, particularly among the adult Caucasian population. 

Spain has established a multidisciplinary consensus on hospital malnutrition, emphasizing the importance of early screening and intervention. This consensus has led to the development of guidelines for addressing malnutrition in hospitals and has been supported by groups such as NADYA and NADYA-SENPE, which focus on home parenteral and enteral nutrition. Furthermore, Spain is responsible for implementing EU regulations, including those related to organic product certification and gluten-free product certification through FACE.

Overall, Spain is a key player in public health research and the management of various chronic diseases, with ongoing studies and initiatives aimed at improving health outcomes for its population.</data>
      <data key="d2">018644ab78da6f804c57546f08ff6a65,07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,28cd3f60e1ccd9129a7d4d386e241a93,3defb74705676a025b15398e300eb230,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,4cf0c8d0f4e711be85d16ee71317aa4e,4e8b65ec9939ccf2152e68fa7f8b12c4,594e6f43e0098791036927da2623b2f5,5a591aa1c68fac4ef889974f6a57c73a,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b,bd8df34b86026d71089bcf062570b70f,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,d3ffabc46da9b238994a7769ffc8f6b7,d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f,da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,f9951c9666473dd8daea6c3f2bcf9a8e,fa4851ce095f27e98350dcb826e5b09c,fa557ef3cae0faa594a71dc7e2d84cdc,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f,fff76d1cd0e64233a5727a707d80e2b9</data>
