    <node id="NUTRITIONAL STATUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional status is a comprehensive measure of an individual's health that is closely linked to their dietary intake and nutritional needs. It is particularly critical for patients with chronic diseases, as it can significantly impact health outcomes. Nutritional status is assessed in hospitalized patients using various tools, including the Global Subjective Assessment (VGS) and the Nutritional Risk Screening 2002 (NRS-2002), as well as other methods like the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA).

The condition of nutritional status reflects how well the body utilizes nutrients, which is essential for overall health. This assessment is especially important in managing specific health conditions, such as liver disease and MELAS syndrome, where nutritional intake can play a pivotal role in treatment and recovery. Additionally, nutritional status is a significant focus in cancer research, as it can influence postoperative outcomes, particularly in surgeries related to gastric cancer.

Overall, nutritional status encompasses the health condition of individuals based on their dietary habits and nutrient intake, making it a vital aspect of healthcare and patient management.</data>
