    <node id="ANTHROPOMETRY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anthropometry is a method that involves measuring body dimensions and proportions to evaluate nutritional status and growth in both children and adults. It serves as a crucial tool in assessing health and nutritional status, often utilized in various nutritional assessments. Additionally, anthropometry can be specifically applied to assess the nutritional status of patients with liver disease, highlighting its importance in clinical settings. Overall, anthropometry provides valuable insights into the physical characteristics of individuals, aiding in the understanding of their health and nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">28cd3f60e1ccd9129a7d4d386e241a93,4c07b8e0a5058216ff9f2f748bde2ada,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
