    <node id="DOLOR ABDOMINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DOLOR ABDOMINAL" refers to abdominal pain, a symptom that can manifest in various gastrointestinal conditions. It is commonly associated with diseases such as colitis ulcerosa and enfermedad de Crohn, where the intensity and location of the pain can vary significantly. Additionally, patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase may experience abdominal pain when consuming sucrose. This symptom can also complicate the administration of enteral nutrition. 

Furthermore, "dolor abdominal" is frequently linked to acute pancreatitis, indicating inflammation in the pancreas, and is a general indicator of discomfort in the abdominal area. It can also arise from malabsorci&#243;n de fructosa, particularly after the intake of high fructose foods. Overall, abdominal pain is a prevalent symptom that may be associated with a range of conditions, including food allergies and gastrointestinal reactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,2ae5ac5b335a00d15c090777da386817,67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d,693b5721c7fc52c8165c48b580777840,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,a079902e52676a05df746098c930a0e7,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e</data>
