    <node id="ANTROPOMETR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANTROPOMETR&#205;A, or anthropometry, refers to the measurement of the human body to assess nutritional status. This method involves measuring various physical dimensions and body composition, including weight, height, and body mass index, to evaluate health and nutritional needs. It is particularly important in assessing the nutritional status of individuals, including children and patients with specific health conditions such as liver diseases or cirrhosis. The study of anthropometry is crucial for understanding the proportions and measurements of the human body, which aids in determining nutritional requirements based on individual health conditions. Overall, ANTROPOMETR&#205;A serves as a vital tool in nutritional assessment and health evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,2ae5ac5b335a00d15c090777da386817,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,4681d149c863ed06c99b19443f841abd,4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,a9b588c70518bc2aa91325853898b7c0,c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b,cb8368db73f739b1f11f2a202c776e6d,d0fb942f9036630b4cf0727dea808fd2,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
