      <data key="d6">598</data>
      <data key="d7">0a6f8d80ff8f465994ac5eb779b1976b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "ENFERMEDAD" encompasses a broad range of conditions that disrupt normal bodily functions, often necessitating medical evaluation and treatment. It refers to any ailment that impairs normal functioning, which can significantly impact a patient's nutritional requirements and status. This is particularly important in assessments of health, especially for vulnerable populations such as children. 

In the context of nutritional support, "enfermedad" includes conditions that may affect how drugs interact with diet, highlighting the need for careful consideration of dietary factors in treatment plans. Additionally, it pertains to diseases being studied in relation to nutritional factors and risk exposures, indicating a focus on the interplay between health conditions and nutrition.

The term also encompasses diseases that are the subject of epidemiological research, reflecting the influence of genetic and environmental factors on health. Specific examples include metabolic diseases like galactosemia, which can lead to various complications if not managed properly. Furthermore, "enfermedad" is discussed in relation to dyslipidemias and their treatment, illustrating its relevance in the medical field. Overall, "enfermedad" represents a critical concept in understanding health, nutrition, and the complexities of disease management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bc48d0666e895b990c211acf7cbcf23,2ae5ac5b335a00d15c090777da386817,39a7166ca777be46a1613c54a746e2b8,3f379d10d8c57694a1c646c072f7ed84,6799d5deb7130f888605e5e2d58c9de5,916ad020bd9c528e55001071b4d9530b,c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa,cd63370bdd798f0b060b047dc29056ae,cf8a6f1b6d59546ed7bd297d032f6b30,fa5c0208b983c59b247a65e6bb166f2a</data>
