    <node id="ENFERMEDADES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">ENFERMEDADES refer to various health conditions that can significantly impact an individual's nutritional needs and treatment. These diseases may coexist with diabetes, influencing the management of the condition and the patient's overall health. Additionally, ENFERMEDADES can affect athletes, often linked to inadequate nutritional practices, which can compromise their health and performance. In children requiring parenteral nutrition, underlying diseases can alter their metabolism and energy requirements, further complicating their nutritional needs. Overall, ENFERMEDADES encompass medical conditions that can adversely affect a patient's nutritional status, highlighting the importance of tailored nutritional interventions in managing these health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d,ab9a942f3aa9ca3eb88bcd26fcd60ddb,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">604</data>
      <data key="d7">b8864a2f7ede4b0eb98c7e476736b307</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO ONCOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El tratamiento oncol&#243;gico se refiere a las diversas terapias aplicadas a pacientes con c&#225;ncer, incluyendo modalidades como radioterapia, quimioterapia y cirug&#237;a. Estas intervenciones son fundamentales en la lucha contra el c&#225;ncer, pero tambi&#233;n pueden tener un impacto significativo en el estado nutricional del paciente. Es importante considerar c&#243;mo estas terapias pueden influir en la nutrici&#243;n, ya que el estado nutricional puede afectar la eficacia del tratamiento y la recuperaci&#243;n del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f379d10d8c57694a1c646c072f7ed84,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">699</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">605</data>
      <data key="d7">1caf85261abd49b886736dc4500cac12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXPLORACI&#211;N F&#205;SICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"EXPLORACI&#211;N F&#205;SICA" refers to a medical examination that plays a crucial role in identifying signs of malnutrition and diseases, particularly in patients with cirrhosis. This examination is a key method used in nutritional assessment to evaluate the overall health status of patients. It involves a thorough evaluation of the patient's physical condition, which is essential for determining nutritional status and general health, especially in critically ill patients, such as those undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. The process includes careful observation of physical signs related to the patient's nutritional state. Additionally, physical examination is a daily requirement for monitoring patients on parenteral nutrition, as it helps to check for potential issues such as dehydration or fluid overload. Overall, "EXPLORACI&#211;N F&#205;SICA" is an integral part of patient care, particularly for those with complex health needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">2bd5549759c6a0d8393bb93fdccb747b,c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674,f333e5a9af59dd8504607b2559ac35dd,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1125</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">606</data>
      <data key="d7">aa15a9676ab4425594c2ea373effab5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Edema, also known as swelling, is a condition characterized by the accumulation of excess fluid in the body's tissues. It can manifest as a potential side effect of growth hormone treatment, indicating fluid retention within the body. Additionally, edema is a common complication associated with venous access, where fluid may accumulate due to various factors. In patients, edema may be observed as swelling resulting from this fluid retention. Furthermore, it can also be a sign of underlying health issues, such as malnutrition or other medical problems. Overall, edema represents a significant clinical concern that can arise from multiple causes, including medical treatments and health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">607</data>
      <data key="d7">b6145858ebdf4005a9c2e541057c0a47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASCITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ASCITIS is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fluid in the abdominal cavity. This condition is often associated with liver diseases, particularly cirrhosis, and can complicate nutritional assessments and dietary restrictions for affected patients. In individuals with liver disease, ascites can lead to challenges in nutrient intake and overall nutritional status. Additionally, ascites may be indicative of other underlying issues, such as hypervolemic hyponatremia or complications related to conditions like celiac disease, particularly in the context of hypoalbuminemia. Overall, ASCITIS is a significant health concern that requires careful management and monitoring, especially in patients with chronic liver conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c,20491afa9a4770e93e6cff9034f8b0f0,3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854,c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682,fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">608</data>
      <data key="d7">f990efc53c784a479d2722f68922a0ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;RDIDA DE TEJIDO ADIPOSO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La p&#233;rdida de tejido adiposo es un signo de desnutrici&#243;n que se eval&#250;a durante la valoraci&#243;n nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">609</data>
      <data key="d7">b6760fe3e5de484fa06c16283949b3a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;RDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">P&#201;RDIDA DE MASA MUSCULAR, or loss of muscle mass, is a significant indicator of severe malnutrition and is assessed during the global subjective evaluation. This condition can arise from malnutrition and is frequently worsened by dysphagia, particularly in patients suffering from neurological diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1099</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">610</data>
      <data key="d7">75211e5ac5884ab8afdb16501bf3bec5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA NORMAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta normal se refiere a un r&#233;gimen alimenticio que incluye una variedad de alimentos y es considerado adecuado para la salud general.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">611</data>
      <data key="d7">3ad78bce069447369c7f551b41712880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POCOS S&#211;LIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La categor&#237;a de pocos s&#243;lidos se refiere a una dieta que limita la ingesta de alimentos s&#243;lidos, a menudo utilizada en pacientes con dificultades para tragar.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">612</data>
      <data key="d7">0bc3f5ac341344d6828f88fa668bf9c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLO L&#205;QUIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta de solo l&#237;quidos implica la ingesta exclusiva de l&#237;quidos, utilizada en situaciones donde la masticaci&#243;n o la degluci&#243;n son problem&#225;ticas.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">613</data>
      <data key="d7">e93e482943e7402e8801c00107395e4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLO PREPARADOS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta de solo preparados nutricionales se refiere a la ingesta de productos dise&#241;ados espec&#237;ficamente para proporcionar nutrientes esenciales, a menudo utilizada en pacientes con necesidades diet&#233;ticas especiales.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">614</data>
      <data key="d7">bfea2b28dd92407d9003bbc80e1cdb75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUY POCO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La categor&#237;a de muy poco se refiere a una ingesta alimentaria extremadamente limitada, que puede ser un signo de desnutrici&#243;n o problemas de salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">615</data>
      <data key="d7">e6cbeaf38c824a528593c35b5633490c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIFICULTAD PARA ALIMENTARSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dificultad para alimentarse se refiere a los problemas que un paciente puede experimentar al intentar comer, lo que puede afectar su estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">616</data>
      <data key="d7">9c6e272e66a34f309ff9291aea485aff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALTA DE APETITO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La falta de apetito es un s&#237;ntoma que puede llevar a una disminuci&#243;n en la ingesta de alimentos y, por ende, a la desnutrici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">617</data>
      <data key="d7">bb5bbf0fd6684c4386c2d08b9d795060</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTRE&#209;IMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estre&#241;imiento," or constipation, is a common digestive issue characterized by infrequent bowel movements or difficulty in passing stools, typically defined as having fewer than three bowel movements per week. This condition can significantly impact an individual's quality of life and is a frequent reason for clinical consultation, affecting a substantial percentage of the population. 

Constipation can arise in various patient populations, including those with diabetes, cancer, and anorexia nerviosa. In diabetic patients, it may necessitate dietary adjustments and the use of osmotic laxatives. For patients receiving enteral nutrition, constipation is a prevalent gastrointestinal complication, often requiring specific nutritional formulas and dietary interventions to alleviate symptoms. Additionally, individuals undergoing chemotherapy may experience constipation, which can complicate their nutritional status.

The condition is not only a symptom of underlying health issues but also poses challenges to health and nutrition, particularly in chronic cases. Effective management of estre&#241;imiento often involves dietary modifications and may include the use of laxatives to improve bowel function. Overall, estre&#241;imiento is a significant gastrointestinal concern that can affect health outcomes and necessitate careful management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada,0bdc356a46149def2545e7939372c20d,0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,2bbe847617971cacfe15b2c970de2d21,42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,90f122c65fbb08f52e052d0e22714849,beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1404</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">26</data>
      <data key="d6">618</data>
      <data key="d7">183750d858084f0fa5535f57a1fc86f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLORES DESAGRADABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los olores desagradables pueden afectar la experiencia de comer y contribuir a la falta de apetito.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">619</data>
      <data key="d7">ae9015c7731142feb4d87935fd68b2af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SABORES DESAGRADABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los sabores desagradables en los alimentos pueden llevar a la aversi&#243;n a comer y afectar la ingesta nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">620</data>
      <data key="d7">2166b753b23347bfb4ce52b53582db3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS SIN SABOR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La percepci&#243;n de que los alimentos no tienen sabor puede contribuir a la falta de apetito y a la disminuci&#243;n de la ingesta alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">621</data>
      <data key="d7">fc610c515e0d4ccb8f831d3874cd945b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENTIRSE LLENO ENSEGUIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La sensaci&#243;n de saciedad r&#225;pida puede limitar la cantidad de alimentos que un paciente puede consumir, afectando su nutrici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">622</data>
      <data key="d7">b1d76d275f1a4ee0a3d68a44fca74d23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROBLEMAS DENTALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los problemas dentales pueden interferir con la capacidad de un paciente para comer adecuadamente, afectando su nutrici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">623</data>
      <data key="d7">8f709983854840b4a797daec00b3a8dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOLOR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DOLOR refers to pain, which can significantly impact a patient's well-being and health. It is known to trigger the release of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), potentially leading to conditions such as Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH) and hyponatremia. Additionally, pain can adversely affect a patient's food intake and nutritional status, making it difficult for them to eat adequately. To manage the pain experienced by patients, medications such as pregabalin and acetyl salicylic acid are commonly used. Overall, DOLOR encompasses both the physiological and nutritional implications of pain on patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,9562f39f9e78644164daeff3177a2f84,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1197</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">624</data>
      <data key="d7">f5a41dd99f594fb1a990ded7f538e4e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEPRESI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Depresi&#243;n, o depresi&#243;n, es un trastorno del estado de &#225;nimo que se caracteriza por una sensaci&#243;n persistente de tristeza y p&#233;rdida de inter&#233;s, afectando la forma en que una persona se siente, piensa y maneja las actividades diarias. Esta condici&#243;n es com&#250;nmente observada como una comorbilidad psiqui&#225;trica en pacientes con trastornos de la alimentaci&#243;n, donde a menudo se relaciona con alteraciones en los niveles de serotonina. Adem&#225;s, la depresi&#243;n puede presentarse en pacientes con disfagia, debido al estr&#233;s y las complicaciones asociadas con esta condici&#243;n.

La depresi&#243;n tambi&#233;n tiene un impacto significativo en la ingesta de alimentos y el estado nutricional, especialmente en pacientes con insuficiencia renal, donde puede influir negativamente en su alimentaci&#243;n. Asimismo, puede afectar el apetito y la ingesta de alimentos, contribuyendo a problemas nutricionales. En algunos casos, la depresi&#243;n puede provocar alteraciones hormonales que son similares a las del s&#237;ndrome de Cushing, aunque estas alteraciones son reversibles con el tratamiento adecuado. En resumen, la depresi&#243;n no solo afecta el bienestar emocional, sino que tambi&#233;n tiene implicaciones importantes en la salud f&#237;sica y nutricional de los individuos.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,a87e8e113488b153c5b4b2d2fca712c0,e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d3">1122</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">625</data>
      <data key="d7">a9c504bd9ec548cea3e0748bcdc4310c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROBLEMAS ECON&#211;MICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los problemas econ&#243;micos pueden limitar el acceso a alimentos nutritivos, afectando el estado nutricional de un paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d3">1126</data>
