    <node id="ALB&#218;MINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alb&#250;mina is a protein that is measured to assess the nutritional status of patients prior to treatment, particularly in the context of oncology. This measurement serves as an important indicator of liver function and overall nutritional health. In summary, Alb&#250;mina plays a crucial role in evaluating a patient's condition before undergoing treatment, providing insights into their nutritional well-being and liver performance.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f379d10d8c57694a1c646c072f7ed84,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,67f60ae11335cf41da4f96400b69e67b</data>
      <data key="d3">699</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">636</data>
      <data key="d7">b8e088158c9048338bd6427fb6016b7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREALB&#218;MINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prealbumin, also known as prealb&#250;mina, is a protein that plays a crucial role in assessing nutritional status. It is particularly sensitive to acute changes in nutrition and can respond quickly to nutritional interventions, making it an important marker for evaluating a patient's nutritional condition. Prealbumin is measured both before and after treatment to monitor the effectiveness of nutritional support, especially in patients undergoing oncological treatment. This protein serves as an indicator of inflammation and infection, highlighting its relevance in clinical settings where rapid changes in nutritional status may occur. Overall, prealbumin is a valuable tool for healthcare professionals in managing and assessing the nutritional health of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f379d10d8c57694a1c646c072f7ed84,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,67f60ae11335cf41da4f96400b69e67b,a6ed8551aad722adcaf8fced4ac8685b,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">637</data>
      <data key="d7">ba9df2adbfd64f09961a45b6440d580e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Body Mass Index (IMC), or &#205;ndice de Masa Corporal, is a widely used measure that assesses body weight relative to height. It plays a crucial role in evaluating nutritional status, particularly in patients undergoing surgery, and is instrumental in identifying individuals at risk of malnutrition. IMC is utilized to classify individuals into categories such as healthy weight, overweight, and obesity, making it an important tool in obesity assessments and nutritional evaluations.

In clinical settings, IMC is particularly significant for patients with specific health conditions, such as cancer, where it can indicate nutritional status and potential risks associated with low body weight. For instance, an IMC value below 20 kg/m&#178; suggests a risk of malnutrition, while values above 35 kg/m&#178; may indicate eligibility for bariatric surgery, especially when accompanied by significant comorbidities.

The IMC is calculated using a person's weight and height, and it is essential for diagnosing various health issues, including the severity of eating disorders and the overall health of patients. It is also relevant in pediatric assessments, where it helps classify nutritional status in children. Overall, the IMC serves as a vital indicator of health, guiding interventions and treatment plans across different medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,285343ba92b89a1761b72d9d789ba8f6,2ad1c3591301bd2ea6f99c3782714d69,34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21,5664277128c865feb0e93f9fd56a3d05,5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5,5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49,67f60ae11335cf41da4f96400b69e67b,6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,7c0d1f274b31d130e4feb8e46fbeb764,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,cc6ee3d7bc9bfaf4a06f3f02c4907eb0,d6469f98d2161058fb7b214a1a800441,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3,f5660be03d70d5dd506c197283dd79ae,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c</data>
