      <data key="d7">6c448a427b2c4450b3266f533dbc8c2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE REALIMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome de Realimentaci&#243;n" (Refeeding Syndrome) is a serious clinical condition that can arise in patients who have experienced severe malnutrition and are subsequently reintroduced to nutritional support. This syndrome is characterized by a range of metabolic complications that can occur when nutrients, particularly carbohydrates, are administered too quickly. It poses significant health risks, including severe electrolyte imbalances, arrhythmias, and even coma, making careful monitoring and management essential.

Patients at risk for this condition include those who are malnourished, especially after periods of fasting or following surgical procedures. The reintroduction of feeding must be approached with caution, as the sudden influx of calories can lead to dangerous metabolic disturbances. The condition is particularly associated with thiamine deficiency and can manifest as a potentially fatal complication if not properly identified and managed.

In summary, the S&#237;ndrome de Realimentaci&#243;n is a critical medical condition that necessitates vigilant oversight during the refeeding process in malnourished individuals to prevent severe health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,140611dbb8a68fc40712c946de92b73f,241d358b60724c07a75223b79c9e5f41,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,6bd3e5b773cab27e91a4a150de700918,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf,cff2f16dff598dbf0bff544091c77837,d6469f98d2161058fb7b214a1a800441,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379,da6937e21690cfcb43a43b3438ec7586,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
