    <node id="DINAMARCA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Denmark, also referred to as Dinamarca, is a country noted for its significant contributions to various fields, including public health and nutrition. It is mentioned in the epidemiological study of NED, highlighting its relevance in health-related research. Denmark has also established specific descriptors for food textures and liquid viscosities, which are incorporated into clinical guidelines, demonstrating its commitment to improving dietary standards and patient care. Furthermore, Denmark holds the distinction of being the first country to legislate Nutritional Product Development (NPD) in 1975, showcasing its pioneering role in the regulation and advancement of nutritional products.</data>
      <data key="d2">398be32cb0a16895225a8b29c9d118df,eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">649</data>
      <data key="d7">4164a343df83499da5edd5bd331bc476</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUSTRIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Austria is a country known for its healthcare policies, where patients are required to cover all costs associated with NED (New and Emerging Drugs) treatment. Additionally, Austria has established specific descriptors for food textures and liquid viscosities that are utilized in clinical guidelines, reflecting its commitment to patient care and dietary management. Furthermore, Austria is notable for being home to a mutation in the GALT gene, which is responsible for causing classic galactosemia, a genetic disorder that affects the metabolism of galactose.</data>
      <data key="d2">398be32cb0a16895225a8b29c9d118df,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">650</data>
      <data key="d7">3b75f2ac9cb44beca99bec77bf1dd3d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTADOS UNIDOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Estados Unidos es un pa&#237;s donde casi 15 millones de personas consumieron suplementos de vitaminas en el &#250;ltimo a&#241;o, buscando beneficios para la salud cognitiva. Adem&#225;s, proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y la nutrici&#243;n en el contexto de la Organizaci&#243;n Mundial de la Salud (OMS). Sin embargo, se ha observado que Estados Unidos tiene ingestas estimadas de DHA y EPA m&#225;s bajas, que oscilan entre 0.1 y 0.2 g/d&#237;a. En el &#225;mbito de la regulaci&#243;n alimentaria, el pa&#237;s actualmente carece de una normativa federal para el etiquetado de gluten. A pesar de esto, Estados Unidos ha establecido ingestas diet&#233;ticas de referencia a trav&#233;s de su Junta de Alimentos y Nutrici&#243;n. Tambi&#233;n se ha llevado a cabo un estudio en el pa&#237;s que mostr&#243; una mayor mortalidad en el grupo de inmunonutrici&#243;n. Por &#250;ltimo, Estados Unidos cuenta con su propio conjunto de descriptores para las texturas de los alimentos y las viscosidades l&#237;quidas en las gu&#237;as cl&#237;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d8aa686c6377246fee05010ef969018,21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,398be32cb0a16895225a8b29c9d118df,4198768cfbdf9c226ffba9074adf628f,9e4c5851293c18ef6b304ff6293b0be5,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d3">1567</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">651</data>
      <data key="d7">0d449fea63554f18b2bc4241a87f32a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CARNES refers to meats in general, which serve as a significant source of various nutrients and can vary in their purine and sodium content, potentially affecting uric acid levels. They are recognized as one of the primary sources of vitamin B12, and inadequate intake of meats can lead to deficiencies in this essential vitamin. Additionally, CARNES provide a recommended source of protein in the diet, particularly when they are fresh and unprocessed, free from gluten. They are also important for their contribution of several B vitamins, including B&#8323;, B&#8325;, B&#8326;, and B&#8321;&#8322;. Furthermore, meats are a major source of long-chain saturated fatty acids, which are associated with the development of cardiovascular diseases (ECV). Daily consumption of meats is encouraged, especially in the form of pur&#233;es and creams, to enhance protein content. While most meats are generally safe for individuals with celiac disease, they must be prepared without gluten-containing ingredients to ensure safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,08edfb59071449728499ca59eb51ac84,1aab735899b0c557ec11da0558bcfc15,26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,398be32cb0a16895225a8b29c9d118df,70b2393fa61e51fc3e772479a9792c98,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e</data>
      <data key="d3">1888</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">652</data>
      <data key="d7">a9006af5a5b94eba82495ad3cb02de82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PESCADOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PESCADOS, or fish, encompasses all fish and fish products, which are recognized as potential allergens according to food safety guidelines. The consumption of fish has been extensively studied for its positive impact on cardiovascular health, with recommendations suggesting at least two servings per week. Dietary guidelines advocate for fish consumption due to its numerous health benefits, including its high protein content and essential nutrients such as vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; and B&#8326;, which are vital for human health.

Fish is particularly encouraged as part of children's diets, with suggestions for its inclusion in pur&#233;es and creams. However, certain types of fish should be avoided prior to specific medical tests to prevent false positives. It is important to note that fish should be fresh and not battered or preserved in sauces containing gluten to maximize health benefits. Additionally, while fish is a good source of omega-3 fatty acids, it can vary in purine content, with some varieties potentially leading to elevated uric acid levels. Processed fish products may also differ in sodium content, which is a consideration for those monitoring their salt intake. Overall, PESCADOS is a nutritious food group that plays a significant role in a balanced diet.</data>
