    <node id="IDDSI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI) is an organization dedicated to unifying concepts and terminology related to dietary modifications for individuals with dysphagia. IDDSI develops standardized terminology and definitions for modified texture foods and thickened beverages, ensuring consistency and clarity in the dietary guidelines for those affected by this condition. The initiative provides comprehensive guidelines aimed at the standardization of dysphagia diets, facilitating better communication and understanding among healthcare professionals, caregivers, and patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">25dd6d6eeff00cc5f1d10dd686c46ad4,362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319,c30b47b534824f4d1b74f3c0bb00ffd9</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">662</data>
      <data key="d7">9a2f5bbcf42840a8be29c0cdc9c0e2b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NIVEL 1 refers to a specific dietary consistency level designed for individuals with dysphagia. It describes a slightly thickened liquid that flows through a straw but requires more effort to swallow compared to thin liquids. Additionally, NIVEL 1 encompasses the first level of dietary consistency, which includes pureed foods that do not require chewing. This level is crucial for ensuring safe and manageable eating for those with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319,c30b47b534824f4d1b74f3c0bb00ffd9</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">663</data>
      <data key="d7">e882c74f8a394cd6a3cfa35f5dcd5caf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIVEL 2" refers to a specific level of food texture designed for individuals experiencing mild swallowing difficulties, commonly known as dysphagia. This level indicates that the liquid is mildly thickened, flowing more slowly than a thin liquid, and requires some effort to consume. Additionally, NIVEL 2 encompasses the second level of dietary consistency, which includes mechanically altered soft foods, making it suitable for those who need a modified diet to ensure safe and effective swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319,c30b47b534824f4d1b74f3c0bb00ffd9</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">664</data>
      <data key="d7">1c0f2439dfd141acb3e042652441baa3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIVEL 3" refers to a specific level of food texture designed for individuals with dysphagia, characterized by a moderately thick consistency. This level is suitable for those who have slight lingual control issues and consists of soft foods that require gentle chewing. NIVEL 3 foods can be consumed with a straw, although they necessitate more effort to manage compared to levels 1 and 2. Overall, this dietary consistency aims to provide safe and manageable options for individuals facing challenges with swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319,c30b47b534824f4d1b74f3c0bb00ffd9</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">665</data>
      <data key="d7">b0edd74d8384472d9760378197ea1619</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NIVEL 4 refers to a specific level of food texture characterized as an extremely thick puree that requires no chewing. This texture is designed for individuals who have significant lingual control issues and those experiencing considerable swallowing difficulties. The food can be shaped, making it suitable for individuals who need a pureed diet for safe consumption.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">666</data>
      <data key="d7">308ad15d3cb94d6b8836ca17ff6661ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 5">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NIVEL 5 refers to a specific level of food texture characterized by being minced and moist. This texture is designed to require minimal chewing, making it particularly suitable for individuals who have dental issues or experience fatigue while chewing. Additionally, NIVEL 5 is beneficial for those with dysphagia, as it provides an easier-to-swallow option, ensuring that individuals with swallowing difficulties can consume food safely and comfortably.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319</data>
      <data key="d3">1859</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">667</data>
      <data key="d7">64c95b8457f14c7f8cee9bccfa4a9e39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL 6">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NIVEL 6 refers to a specific level of food texture characterized by being soft and bite-sized. This texture requires some chewing but can be easily manipulated with utensils, making it suitable for individuals with mild swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">85615e916e16fc7d0e49d66102bfedec,adb71bc02844276a2ecb4c4302938319,c7cd7add413c00d9d6eb40d934ba10af</data>
