    <node id="GOMA GUAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GOMA GUAR, also known as guar gum, is a natural polysaccharide derived from the endosperm of guar beans. It serves as a stabilizing agent and thickening agent in various food products, enhancing texture and viscosity. In addition to its role in the food industry, GOMA GUAR is also utilized in the pharmaceutical sector as a water-binding agent. Its dietary fiber content makes it a valuable ingredient in food formulations, contributing to both the functional and nutritional aspects of the products in which it is used.</data>
      <data key="d2">5367d7f3e598922a050de5ed400cd0c4,751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1,c7cd7add413c00d9d6eb40d934ba10af,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a</data>
