    </node>
    <node id="GOMA XANTANA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GOMA XANTANA is a polysaccharide produced through the fermentation of sugars and carbohydrates, specifically by microbial processes. It serves as a thickening agent, emulsion stabilizer, and is widely utilized in the food industry to enhance texture and stability. GOMA XANTANA is particularly prevalent in gluten-free products, where it helps to improve the consistency and quality of food items.</data>
      <data key="d2">5367d7f3e598922a050de5ed400cd0c4,767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1,c7cd7add413c00d9d6eb40d934ba10af</data>
