      <data key="d6">704</data>
      <data key="d7">0810d8c0726b407ea99d7dd9ce909aab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANA CANT&#211;N BLANCO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ana Cant&#243;n Blanco is an author of the nutritional support guide for the diagnosis and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">705</data>
      <data key="d7">a0113e68ff4c4ae298cdb8a4969853da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N B&#193;SICA ADAPTADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALIMENTACI&#211;N B&#193;SICA ADAPTADA" refers to the practice of modifying food textures and consistencies to accommodate patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This concept includes the use of modified texture foods that are designed to be high in caloric density and rich in protein, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition while managing their swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca</data>
      <data key="d3">1188</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">706</data>
      <data key="d7">ebfe2f919ffd4317b46478fc3d40461e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADOR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The "CUIDADOR," or caregiver, is a vital figure in the healthcare setting, particularly for patients experiencing dysphagia, which is a condition that affects swallowing. This individual is responsible for assisting patients during meals to ensure their safety and proper feeding techniques are followed. The caregiver plays a crucial role in supervising patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, ensuring they are positioned correctly and adhering to safety protocols throughout the feeding process. This responsibility is especially important for elderly patients or those with cognitive decline, as they may require additional support in managing their dietary needs. Overall, the caregiver's role is essential in promoting safe and effective feeding practices for individuals with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,28e2e3a92ef4dd76af0898ae3e3df522,2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,7c842769e1890739769789ed10a08005</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">707</data>
      <data key="d7">c1a686d2bfbf45bea7525be173ea7d73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPRIMIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tablets that need to be crushed for patients with dysphagia to facilitate safe swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d3">1070</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">708</data>
      <data key="d7">8cc0b1253bdd4cf8acfe946a75f7bb91</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMULAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Formulas are specialized nutritional products designed to provide essential nutrients to patients, particularly those with specific dietary needs. Additionally, the term "formulas" also refers to liquid medications that require thickening to ensure safe consumption by patients with dysphagia. This dual definition highlights the importance of formulas in both nutritional support and medical treatment for individuals with particular health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,abd9a4b801dbdaca1708f0e22331a829</data>
      <data key="d3">1216</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">709</data>
      <data key="d7">318beb6cccdb4bd2b35c44944bc3e182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JERINGAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Syringes are tools that should not be used for oral administration of liquids in dysphagic patients to prevent aspiration.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">710</data>
      <data key="d7">cfb0d1c3e4d64ec1a284edf6810a61eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAJITAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PAJITAS refers to bending straws or drinking tubes that are advised against for individuals with swallowing difficulties, particularly those with dysphagia. These straws can facilitate aspiration during drinking, making them unsuitable for patients who may struggle with safe swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,1380487b18595e66eb8e203f2c0ebcfd</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">711</data>
      <data key="d7">f49dd23b8e8c4951817bdcc6f6453e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VASOS DE BOCA ANCHA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wide-mouth cups are recommended for patients with dysphagia to aid in safe drinking practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">712</data>
      <data key="d7">29dc7abc0c4b4b7495791ca2efaca687</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIANZA M&#193;S NUTRIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alianza m&#225;s nutridos is an organization focused on nutritional efficacy and combating malnutrition in various settings, including hospitals and communities.</data>
      <data key="d2">b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">727</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">713</data>
      <data key="d7">38f5d07d0a4b4f4196795ad9747318c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIETY ESPA&#209;OLA DE NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral y Enteral (SENPE) promotes multidisciplinary consensus on the approach to hospital malnutrition in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">727</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">714</data>
      <data key="d7">d5411b3455fc4a16a4906d433bd114b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JENSEN GL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Jensen GL is a prominent researcher and author in the field of nutritional assessment and malnutrition. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of malnutrition syndromes and their implications in clinical practice. Additionally, Jensen GL has been actively involved in the development of clinical practice guidelines for diagnosing malnutrition, further establishing his expertise and influence in this critical area of healthcare.</data>
      <data key="d2">242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,628cd3e2664561301cbe6679f48c4bd3,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
