    <node id="COMPHER C">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Compher C is a prominent figure in the field of clinical nutrition, recognized for their significant contributions to various guidelines and proposals aimed at improving patient care. They are a co-author of a proposal focused on etiology-based diagnosis in clinical practice concerning malnutrition, highlighting their commitment to addressing nutritional deficiencies in clinical settings. Additionally, Compher C has contributed to clinical guidelines for nutrition support specifically tailored for hyperglycemic patients, demonstrating their expertise in managing complex nutritional needs. They are also an author of clinical guidelines related to nutrition support in renal failure, further showcasing their involvement in critical areas of patient nutrition management. Furthermore, Compher C has played a key role in authoring the ASPEN clinical guidelines for nutrition screening, which are essential for identifying patients at risk of malnutrition. Lastly, they are one of the authors discussing treatment outcomes of early enteral versus early parenteral nutrition, contributing to the ongoing discourse on optimal nutritional strategies in clinical practice. Overall, Compher C's work reflects a deep commitment to enhancing nutritional support across various patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,a700a2e14ec1a75902455bcb005e1434,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39,ceb66a898fed371e013171c43a87e1d1,e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d3">728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">717</data>
      <data key="d7">aa5c3aec55804a9a9de12706ce723958</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHALIWAL R">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dhaliwal R is an author who is actively engaged in the systematic review of nutrition support in acute pancreatitis. Additionally, Dhaliwal R contributes to the development of guidelines concerning the diagnosis of malnutrition. Through these efforts, Dhaliwal R plays a significant role in advancing knowledge and practices related to nutrition in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">718</data>
      <data key="d7">421579e7c8b646cbbee6829e02fdcb3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORBES A">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Forbes A is a prominent author of the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition in inflammatory bowel diseases. Additionally, Forbes A plays a significant role in the international consensus on the diagnosis of malnutrition, contributing to the advancement of nutritional standards and practices in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb,b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">719</data>
      <data key="d7">e2e196f1631745cfb7c36918183d01fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIGUEREDO GRIJALBA R">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Figueredo Grijalba R is a contributor to the guidelines for diagnosing malnutrition in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">720</data>
      <data key="d7">d5c80423d6dc4a1e84b6c62956539d83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING (NRS2002)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS2002) is a method developed for assessing nutritional risk based on clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d2">b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">721</data>
      <data key="d7">da1ba20fb77a4f79a4556441d3377e7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOULOUSE FRAILTY PLATFORM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Toulouse Frailty Platform is a research initiative focused on frailty and nutritional assessment in elderly populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">b422a0b87e2f7205a53dc0a5f1c0ab39</data>
      <data key="d3">729</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">722</data>
      <data key="d7">487a2e9e6aaa47d4b7aefaa46dac1b6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GU&#205;A DE DIAGN&#211;STICO Y TRATAMIENTO NUTRICIONAL Y REHABILITADOR DE LA DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A comprehensive guide focused on the diagnosis and nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, edited by Clav&#233; Civit P and Garc&#237;a Peris P.</data>
      <data key="d2">25dd6d6eeff00cc5f1d10dd686c46ad4</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">723</data>
      <data key="d7">c10a8580d7ab4bb690179b0388468b22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA Y DIET&#201;TICA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A journal that publishes research and articles related to clinical nutrition and dietary practices in hospital settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">25dd6d6eeff00cc5f1d10dd686c46ad4</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">724</data>
      <data key="d7">a2a65ffc317641359c455a4536a728c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"NUTRICI&#211;N HOSPITALARIA" is a comprehensive journal dedicated to the field of hospital nutrition, emphasizing various aspects of nutritional management and dietary practices in clinical settings. It addresses the nutritional needs of patients, focusing on both enteral and parenteral nutrition. The journal publishes research and articles that explore a wide range of topics, including the prevalence and incidence of hyponatremia in patients receiving parenteral nutrition, the role of proteins and peptides in enteral nutrition, and balanced nutrition strategies for diabetic patients.

In addition to these specific studies, "NUTRICI&#211;N HOSPITALARIA" has also published a consensus on the approach to hospital malnutrition in Spain, highlighting the importance of nutritional support in hospital environments. The journal serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals involved in the nutritional care of hospitalized patients, providing insights into effective dietary interventions and rehabilitation strategies. Overall, "NUTRICI&#211;N HOSPITALARIA" plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and practice of clinical nutrition within hospital settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ed0218136adceb16e9f246f3072e6dd,19e153f7c5e2fcd13d3bf7a99298834e,25dd6d6eeff00cc5f1d10dd686c46ad4,28503044e98192e03a043b0103f37a9b,820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b,8778654a17a48b8ea7b1cec378d52346,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,b96414a52f13cac336436d9e8173baef,c3182f51249513a920db6b935632fead,cd56385abb6f8c594bf532666bdf1860,ce6821fbd8f78047e06917383f25f037,e5542485c64706310c70513397de07f9</data>
      <data key="d3">518</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">725</data>
      <data key="d7">945705c139264d6a8c8442ed599fecc3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUGENE BINGHAM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Eugene Bingham was a physicist who introduced the term "rheology" in 1929, which studies the flow and deformation of materials.</data>
      <data key="d2">362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2</data>
      <data key="d3">906</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">726</data>
      <data key="d7">b524a1d15b8b4e299b30ad6f23b9c2c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GU&#205;AS CL&#205;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GU&#205;AS CL&#205;NICAS are systematically developed statements designed to assist both practitioners and patients in making informed decisions regarding appropriate healthcare for specific clinical circumstances. These guidelines encompass a range of recommendations, including those focused on dietary modifications aimed at minimizing complications in patients suffering from dysphagia. Additionally, GU&#205;AS CL&#205;NICAS provide recommendations based on clinical experience for the refeeding of patients with eating disorders, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to evidence-based practices tailored to these specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa</data>
      <data key="d3">1140</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">727</data>
      <data key="d7">036136edee8248c09007db7f1b70910e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VISCOCIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Viscosidad, or viscosity, is a rheological property that describes a fluid's resistance to flow. It plays a crucial role in the behavior of food boluses, influencing how they move and interact within the digestive system. Additionally, viscosity is a key factor in modifying the texture of liquids, particularly for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This modification is essential for ensuring that such patients can safely consume liquids without the risk of aspiration or choking.</data>
      <data key="d2">362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">728</data>
      <data key="d7">05e994a9104a4b59898318dcfc6a7628</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERNATIONAL DYSPHAGIA DIET STANDARDISATION INITIATIVE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Dysphagia Diet Standardisation Initiative (IDDSI) is an organization dedicated to standardizing the terminology and descriptors associated with food textures and viscosities specifically for patients suffering from dysphagia. This initiative aims to create a unified framework for the values and nomenclature used in nutritional treatments for dysphagia on a global scale, ensuring consistency and clarity in dietary recommendations for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">929b14ae2554caeaab2a010ad94222eb,c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">946</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">729</data>
      <data key="d7">2879f3d9ba4d46f2ac6a28fcf080aa09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CENTIPOISE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Centipoise is a unit used in healthcare to measure viscosity, equivalent to 10 Pa&#183;s.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">916</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">730</data>
      <data key="d7">f0fdf789150648dea2a201979c5870d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEXTURE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Texture refers to the set of rheological properties and structure of a product that can be perceived by various sensory receptors.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">731</data>
      <data key="d7">a504ab801007440096357241bd7cfacb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VISCOSITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Viscosity is a crucial physical property of fluids that describes their resistance to flow, which is primarily influenced by particle collisions. This characteristic plays a significant role in the design of products intended for individuals with dysphagia, as it directly impacts the safety and efficacy of swallowing. Understanding viscosity is essential for creating formulations that ensure safe consumption for those with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412,da965f79110bd8915deff461d0d91187</data>
      <data key="d3">916</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">732</data>
      <data key="d7">d8360aa0302144119b16dac84b934931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GELIFICATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gelification is the process of thickening and stabilizing liquid solutions, emulsions, and suspensions.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">733</data>
      <data key="d7">91530488603a4f8c8ff6d46c3b34ea27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GELATINS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gelatins are food products that are primarily liquid but have a solid appearance due to gelification.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">734</data>
      <data key="d7">bb6bac3bad48403ca6724b7c1bb08bd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALGINATES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alginates are compounds derived from brown algae that can form irreversible gels in cold water in the presence of calcium ions.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">735</data>
      <data key="d7">eac633ea589d473a9726019c2190109e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUM AGAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gum agar is a gel-forming agent obtained from red algae, known for its strong gelification properties at specific temperatures.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">736</data>
      <data key="d7">6211041fc5c746dba0f8f2c8df9af8e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDROCOLOIDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hidrocoloides are natural polymeric substances that are soluble or dispersible in water, often used in food products for their thickening and gelling properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">737</data>
      <data key="d7">580afd7dad2d4d1494563408ac5483b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GOMAS are high molecular weight molecules characterized by their hydrophilic or hydrophobic properties, which enable them to form gels when mixed with suitable solvents. These substances, commonly referred to as gums, serve as stabilizers that enhance the viscosity of mixtures, particularly in clinical nutrition, thereby influencing the hydration and stability of the final product. In the food industry, gums are utilized to modify texture and viscosity, making them essential thickeners for managing dysphagia. They can function independently or in conjunction with starch to achieve the desired viscosity in various food products.</data>
      <data key="d2">4aeca0ee5f2663f449cfd017d3e3bbfb,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4,c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412,d9e4179f945ec9152199511522d70159</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">738</data>
      <data key="d7">347d3ed798c34d05acd2cf84bf7c1f72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PECTINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PECTINA is an acidic polysaccharide found in fruits and vegetables, widely utilized as a thickening and stabilizing agent in the food industry. It is particularly important in the production of jams and jellies, where it serves as a common gelling agent.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd,c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">949</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">739</data>
      <data key="d7">a9bcf4a3444b4f10a1840c71e0bc21c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARRAGENINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carragenina is a gelling agent extracted from red algae, widely used in the food industry for its thickening and stabilizing properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">740</data>
      <data key="d7">37aaa680142543488e20ccd70f217d44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGENTS GELIFICANTES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">c77a5a4f92d7d5509acc676d31f68412</data>
      <data key="d3">925</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">741</data>
      <data key="d7">53e8b493b48c43b9b3204e5dafd7f642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA AR&#193;BIGA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma ar&#225;biga, also known as gum arabic, is a natural polysaccharide extracted from the resin of sub-Saharan trees. It is widely utilized in the food industry for its properties as a stabilizer and thickener, helping to fix aromas and stabilize emulsions in various food products.</data>
      <data key="d2">751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a</data>
      <data key="d3">115</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">742</data>
      <data key="d7">3e996ca064b94355a8d7ee18089d13ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA GAROF&#205;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma garrof&#237;n, tambi&#233;n conocida como goma de algarrobo, es un agente espesante y gelificante extra&#237;do de las semillas del algarrobo, utilizado en la tecnolog&#237;a de alimentos.</data>
      <data key="d2">767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1</data>
      <data key="d3">115</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">743</data>
      <data key="d7">7d191db6eacb4b8b830b7eb050240f7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA CARRAGENINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma carragenina es un pol&#237;mero sulfatado extra&#237;do de algas rojas, conocido por sus propiedades como gelificante, espesante, estabilizante y emulsionante. Se utiliza principalmente en la industria de los productos l&#225;cteos y se clasifica en tres grupos principales: iota, kappa y lambda. Su versatilidad en la elaboraci&#243;n de alimentos la convierte en un aditivo esencial para mejorar la textura y estabilidad de diversos productos.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd,767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1</data>
      <data key="d3">951</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">744</data>
      <data key="d7">8bee3bb980fd4d87acb1b12a443bd7c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARRAGHEEN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Carragheen es un municipio donde se ha utilizado la carragenina durante casi 600 a&#241;os, conocido por su producci&#243;n de algas rojas.</data>
      <data key="d2">767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1</data>
      <data key="d3">951</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">745</data>
      <data key="d7">7378b7348bd3485294bf3760e080c989</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHONDRUS CRISPUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Chondrus crispus, tambi&#233;n conocido como musgo irland&#233;s, es una alga roja de la cual se extrae la carragenina, utilizada en la elaboraci&#243;n de alimentos.</data>
      <data key="d2">767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1</data>
      <data key="d3">951</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">746</data>
      <data key="d7">3d6b1b5975b64315b6be7e4ab1a9b2e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACACIA SENEGAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">767c2489bbb49e4b253ae54565c7a4f1</data>
      <data key="d3">115</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">747</data>
      <data key="d7">113f26cdb3244938b3fab98ce29e7d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA LOCUSTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma locuste es un polisac&#225;rido neutro extra&#237;do de las semillas de Ceratonia siliqua, utilizado como espesante y estabilizante en diversos productos alimenticios.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">951</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">748</data>
      <data key="d7">3f7fb971d42a4d20bb6c6e063a470326</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA GHATTI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma ghatti es un exudado del &#225;rbol Anogeissus latifolia, utilizado como emulsionante y soluble en agua, originaria de la India.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">952</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">749</data>
      <data key="d7">629bbd050f684cfa9ffd89b8c54796c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA KARAYA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma karaya es un polisac&#225;rido complejo de baja solubilidad, utilizado para prevenir la formaci&#243;n de cristales de hielo en helados, originaria del norte y centro de la India.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">950</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">750</data>
      <data key="d7">8d87977a15894a1480a969b505fff3c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOMA TRAGACANTO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Goma tragacanto es una mezcla de polisac&#225;ridos obtenida de un arbusto del g&#233;nero Astragalus, utilizada como emulsionante y estabilizante en la industria alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">950</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">751</data>
      <data key="d7">91e7531ace654bdfa2db51c0af5c4639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOGEISSUS LATIFOLIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Anogeissus latifolia es un &#225;rbol de la familia Combretaceae, originario de la India, del cual se extrae la goma ghatti.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">952</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">752</data>
      <data key="d7">516fe1983bba4df3b993530cd6407063</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASTRAGALUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Astragalus es un g&#233;nero de plantas leguminosas de donde se obtiene la goma tragacanto, originario de Asia menor y regiones monta&#241;osas de Ir&#225;n, Siria y Turqu&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">950</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">753</data>
      <data key="d7">eaa622044e5a4248b4ebe1f0cd67b6f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANZANAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Las manzanas son frutas que contienen pectina, un polisac&#225;rido utilizado en la industria alimentaria para la elaboraci&#243;n de gelatinas y mermeladas.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">949</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">754</data>
      <data key="d7">d77ada2158de434a93ba760f051c1b53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEMBRILLOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Los membrillos son frutas que contienen pectina, utilizada como agente espesante en la industria alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">949</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">755</data>
      <data key="d7">451fd88f29694a5b91c34a07db290317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NARANJAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Las naranjas son frutas que contienen pectina, utilizada en la elaboraci&#243;n de productos alimentarios como gelatinas y salsas.</data>
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">949</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">756</data>
      <data key="d7">80aff473beb242bd8999aebd2f39bf7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CERATONIA SILIQUA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">16da5930da05ae4c3744357a7d6e67cd</data>
      <data key="d3">951</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">757</data>
      <data key="d7">c84604e9a8ee4c03a7be504e53e5ac24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMID&#211;N MODIFICADO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El almid&#243;n modificado es un polisac&#225;rido vegetal que se utiliza en la industria alimentaria, aportando beneficios nutricionales y funcionales a los productos alimenticios.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d3">129</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">758</data>
      <data key="d7">a83d273a28654392947de20a409a8658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALTODEXITRINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las maltodextrinas son productos derivados de la hidr&#243;lisis controlada del almid&#243;n, utilizados en la industria alimentaria por sus propiedades fisicoqu&#237;micas.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d3">129</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">759</data>
      <data key="d7">5099ea6251f046ab89385859e996632d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARBOXIMETILCELULOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La carboximetilcelulosa es un derivado de la celulosa natural, utilizado como agente dispersante y para retener humedad en productos alimenticios como helados.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d3">129</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">760</data>
      <data key="d7">a8a0fb6f7f8a47bca959fa0c474f6a21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GILCKSMAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gilcksman es un autor que clasifica los hidrocoloides en su obra, proporcionando informaci&#243;n sobre sus compuestos y aplicaciones en la industria alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">761</data>
      <data key="d7">4c7f8f13fe6940519f42697f463afc1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">REOLOG&#205;A es el estudio del flujo y la deformaci&#243;n de los alimentos, lo que resulta fundamental para comprender la degluci&#243;n y las propiedades de los bolos alimenticios. Esta ciencia tambi&#233;n se centra en el comportamiento de los l&#237;quidos y su flujo, lo que la hace relevante en la formulaci&#243;n de espesantes, especialmente para pacientes que padecen disfagia. En resumen, la reolog&#237;a juega un papel crucial tanto en la alimentaci&#243;n como en la salud, al facilitar la comprensi&#243;n de c&#243;mo los alimentos se comportan en el sistema digestivo y al ayudar en la creaci&#243;n de productos que mejoren la ingesta de aquellos con dificultades para tragar.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932,a3444da30e339275da1056c3e13bcae5</data>
      <data key="d3">924</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">762</data>
      <data key="d7">4af01a7eb0d446619d08420f0dd87eeb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMULSIFICANTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El emulsificante es un compuesto que ayuda a mezclar ingredientes que normalmente no se combinar&#237;an, como el agua y el aceite, en productos alimentarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d3">818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">763</data>
      <data key="d7">e9bb025614c14ff08c6bc3427bb49599</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTABILIZANTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El estabilizante es un aditivo que ayuda a mantener la uniformidad y la textura de los productos alimentarios, evitando la separaci&#243;n de ingredientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">764</data>
      <data key="d7">08542743d97e40748687751c992cab61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MERMELEDAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MERMELEDAS are food products made from fruits and sugar, often incorporating thickening agents to enhance their consistency. They are commonly used as spreads and are known for their sweet and fruity flavors.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">765</data>
      <data key="d7">e21beee1b9a945899719c61c9a097f47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GELATINAS DE FRUTAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las gelatinas de frutas son postres que utilizan gelificantes para obtener una textura firme y son populares en la industria alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">766</data>
      <data key="d7">df1a0a48295f48509469749357dd57ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SORBETES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SORBETES are frozen desserts made primarily from fruit puree and sugar. They may also include thickening agents to enhance their texture. These delightful treats are characterized by their refreshing flavors and smooth consistency, making them a popular choice for dessert.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">767</data>
      <data key="d7">eb3625356a2746dbb4f83d43b9b5be71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HELADOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HELADOS are frozen dairy products commonly known as ice creams. They are included in food frequency questionnaires and can contain gluten, which necessitates caution for individuals with celiac disease. Typically, HELADOS are made using stabilizers and emulsifiers to achieve a creamy texture, enhancing their overall quality and mouthfeel.</data>
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932,7d2050a2481adc105bdebbcf2af1a173,bbb1a87c3287956d3da7d37a9b24e8f3</data>
      <data key="d3">818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">768</data>
      <data key="d7">33d5abd16a5e4e6cbb6bf44101823c94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGENTE ESPESANTE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">306c653730f336c5553a6d1acf1f0932</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">769</data>
      <data key="d7">bb337be00e9243dc8ed2533077c62004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREBRO HUMANO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El cerebro humano se activa por la percepci&#243;n oral de la viscosidad y otras propiedades reol&#243;gicas durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">770</data>
      <data key="d7">9762b1deabfc4256afb92cb8caeaea19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROPIEDADES REOL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las propiedades reol&#243;gicas son caracter&#237;sticas de los alimentos que afectan su textura y consistencia, influyendo en la percepci&#243;n sensorial durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">771</data>
      <data key="d7">524eef838e84442596d45facc9235fb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IM&#193;GENES CEREBRALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los estudios funcionales cerebrales con im&#225;genes indican que la sensaci&#243;n del gusto activa m&#250;ltiples &#225;reas cerebrales durante la degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">772</data>
      <data key="d7">f1cc023a1ee34241b0a4b41c2a3ea62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS DE PERFIL DE TEXTURA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El an&#225;lisis de perfil de textura in vitro es una t&#233;cnica experimental utilizada para evaluar el comportamiento del bolo alimenticio y su relaci&#243;n con las dimensiones sensoriales.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">933</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">773</data>
      <data key="d7">51ce49320ad140fda831d380d1e318a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#201;TODOS PSICOF&#205;SICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los m&#233;todos psicof&#237;sicos son t&#233;cnicas de evaluaci&#243;n que pueden ser utilizadas para estudiar la degluci&#243;n y las propiedades sensoriales de los alimentos.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">774</data>
      <data key="d7">1746d5e82bfa44af8987705de780ba5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELECTROENCEFALOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">bc20bf64107d944924272321bba4ab25</data>
      <data key="d3">935</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">775</data>
      <data key="d7">e187b531140f4b908dc70143a8caadd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRUPO NACIONAL DE TRABAJO SOBRE LA DIETA PARA LA DISFAGIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Working Group on Diet for Dysphagia is an organization that establishes dietary recommendations for patients with dysphagia, focusing on the rheological properties of food boluses.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f</data>
      <data key="d3">920</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">776</data>
      <data key="d7">511700e6cdb0422081e8ac2963d0f716</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALLEGOS ET AL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gallegos et al. refers to authors who have recently questioned the established conditions regarding dysphagia and its dietary recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f</data>
      <data key="d3">920</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">777</data>
      <data key="d7">73b4efd99ce84f8fa6472ed59fc95b9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPESANTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPESANTES are substances, also known as thickeners, that are utilized to modify the viscosity of liquids and stabilize certain solid foods. They play a crucial role in aiding hydration and nutrition for individuals with swallowing difficulties, particularly those suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia. These macromolecules are added to liquids to enhance their consistency, ensuring safety during swallowing for patients with dysphagia. By increasing the viscosity of liquids and foods, ESPESANTES provide essential support for individuals who require assistance in managing their dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f,4aeca0ee5f2663f449cfd017d3e3bbfb,a3444da30e339275da1056c3e13bcae5,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4,da965f79110bd8915deff461d0d91187,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
      <data key="d3">924</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">778</data>
      <data key="d7">b86bc66293bb41079bbb5c138aa5c7ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LIQUIDOS are fluids that can be thickened to assist individuals, particularly patients with dysphagia, in swallowing safely. These substances can be modified using thickeners to enhance their consistency, making it easier for those with swallowing difficulties to consume them.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
      <data key="d3">924</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">779</data>
      <data key="d7">6a1f42e8e522486e847f051286529256</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VELOCIDAD DE CORTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cutting speed refers to the rate at which food boluses are processed during swallowing, which is critical for patients with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">780</data>
      <data key="d7">8c503a0318734acfb1cb5294a883cbbf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VISCOSIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VISCOSIDAD refers to the thickness of a mixture, which plays a crucial role in the mixing and stability of clinical nutrition products. It is a measure of a fluid's resistance to flow, making it an important factor in determining the safety of swallowing for patients with dysphagia. Additionally, viscosity is a physical property of clinical nutrition products that can be influenced by factors such as protein stability and thermal treatment. These aspects are significant as they impact the administration of these products via feeding tubes, highlighting the importance of managing viscosity in clinical nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f,62f527b38024e8807d3e63a0cf488046,d9e4179f945ec9152199511522d70159</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">781</data>
      <data key="d7">4cdb0f370de04702abec80a5d264b67d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMENDACIONES DE MODIFICACI&#211;N DE LA DIETA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Diet modification recommendations are guidelines established to assist patients with dysphagia in safe eating practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">782</data>
      <data key="d7">0a7d4ec31a074ff7a864439b52407307</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ESTUDIOS CL&#205;NICOS" refers to clinical studies that are research efforts focused on understanding the effects of dietary modifications on patients suffering from dysphagia. These studies also encompass investigations aimed at evaluating the efficacy and safety of clinical nutrition products. Through these research initiatives, "ESTUDIOS CL&#205;NICOS" seeks to enhance knowledge and improve treatment options for individuals with specific dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">085d1e3702bc42fa47418095d541867f,4cbb124f28ea6f426c4aa7bc0edbb742</data>
      <data key="d3">1919</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">783</data>
      <data key="d7">cddbf6e73a654ded9afe3c5d8d346b66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INDUSTRIA ALIMENTARIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The INDUSTRIA ALIMENTARIA, or food industry, has made significant advancements in addressing nutritional deficiencies and improving food quality. It has developed fortified foods, particularly focusing on products such as milk, juices, cereals, and various milk substitutes to combat calcium deficiency among consumers. Additionally, the industry employs thickeners to enhance the texture and stability of a wide range of food products and recipes, ensuring a better culinary experience and product consistency.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
      <data key="d3">924</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">784</data>
      <data key="d7">d7efc8cc508249afa37e74da78cd6746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SALIVA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Saliva is a complex bodily fluid that plays a crucial role in the digestion process. It contains various enzymes, including &#945;-amylase, which aids in the digestion of starches. Additionally, saliva influences the viscosity of thickened liquids, contributing to the overall digestive function.</data>
      <data key="d2">4aeca0ee5f2663f449cfd017d3e3bbfb,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
      <data key="d3">927</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">785</data>
      <data key="d7">bd82926557bc41dba1d53e4ce9fe2b36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMID&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Almid&#243;n, also known as starch, is a carbohydrate that serves multiple purposes in food products. It is commonly used as a thickening agent and an energy source, making it a vital ingredient in various nutritional products. Almid&#243;n can be included in optional nutritional information and is often present in infant formulas. Its versatility allows it to be utilized in the preparation of thickened liquids and foods, contributing to both texture and energy provision in dietary applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">056e169253fe046c2922537bb79ba187,16e694ae79763a00ceb974feca8e733d,4aeca0ee5f2663f449cfd017d3e3bbfb,751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,a079902e52676a05df746098c930a0e7,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a</data>
      <data key="d3">926</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">786</data>
      <data key="d7">3d7329aa86574f3686bcba8cf92855e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEBIDAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BEBIDAS refers to drinks, encompassing a wide range of beverages such as water, tea, coffee, and various other liquids. These beverages can include options that contain aspartame, a sweetener that is a phenylalanine analog, which should be avoided by individuals with phenylketonuria due to health concerns. Additionally, BEBIDAS can be modified in viscosity using thickeners, making them suitable for safe consumption by individuals with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Overall, BEBIDAS represents a diverse category of drinks that cater to different dietary needs and preferences.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944,c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
      <data key="d3">924</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">787</data>
      <data key="d7">e7f07c5c62cc4870a04d67048fc40b58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROPIEDADES INTR&#205;NSECAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Intrinsic properties refer to the inherent characteristics of thickeners that can affect the consistency of thickened liquids.</data>
      <data key="d2">c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
