    <node id="AMERICAN DIETETIC ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Dietetic Association (ADA) is a professional organization of dietitians and nutritionists in the United States. It plays a crucial role in the field of nutrition and dietetics by providing evidence analysis manuals and guidelines that inform dietary practices. The ADA offers comprehensive guidelines and positions on various aspects of nutrition, including dietary practices for older adults in long-term care settings, nutrition interventions for the treatment of eating disorders, and resources for managing specific conditions such as dysphagia. Additionally, the organization addresses the nutritional needs of patients with specific health conditions, including those with dementia, ensuring that dietitians and nutritionists have access to the necessary tools and information to support their clients effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">0692eb750371d46b9fff71ec305df6ce,28503044e98192e03a043b0103f37a9b,4aeca0ee5f2663f449cfd017d3e3bbfb,770e8796aac9c96d967ef99d1f307e06,9303a85464d02f1cc012aaca21edf9bb,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,f5d0adafea7d8fe8216c624188ddad04</data>
