    <node id="APPCC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">APPCC, which stands for An&#225;lisis de Peligros y Puntos de Control Cr&#237;tico, is a comprehensive food safety management system designed to ensure food safety and hygiene across various food operations. This system focuses on analyzing hazards and controlling risks at all stages of the manufacturing process, making it essential for maintaining high safety standards. APPCC employs a systematic preventive approach to food safety, which is particularly crucial in sensitive environments such as hospitals. By identifying and controlling potential hazards throughout the food production process, APPCC plays a vital role in safeguarding public health and ensuring the integrity of food products.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb,31f8f2c83d12928b56228d8b3f9d081c,440978f75b135fa97eb7b99ca379e9a4,90aa696a6e48637e06acfcd7213699da</data>
