    </node>
    <node id="SERVICIO DE COCINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SERVICIO DE COCINA" is the kitchen service within hospitals that plays a crucial role in the nutritional care of patients. It is responsible for preparing and serving meals that meet the specific dietary needs of patients, including those with dysphagia. The Servicio de Cocina collaborates closely with the dysphagia unit to develop modified texture menus tailored to the requirements of these patients. Overall, the kitchen service ensures that all meals provided to patients are not only nutritious but also aligned with their individual dietary restrictions and health needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">06484c3fe8af6e4c44bbfc3ac2fa2590,544f7d3afd9f7def46c357525e55cabf,929b14ae2554caeaab2a010ad94222eb,aacbc2a88a21cd749df3c22de5daea04</data>
      <data key="d3">1269</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">841</data>
      <data key="d7">7e9af170674b4e0595c37f9eb47fa7c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CALIDAD refers to the quality of nutrients, emphasizing that not all food sources offer the same benefits for growth and health. It encompasses the overall attributes of clinical nutrition products, which include sensory, physical-chemical, and nutritional aspects that must be maintained to ensure efficacy. Additionally, CALIDAD pertains to the standards and certifications that guarantee products meet specified requirements, ensuring their reliability and safety. Furthermore, it includes the standards of food preparation and service in hospitals, which are essential for patient satisfaction and health. Overall, CALIDAD represents a comprehensive approach to ensuring high-quality nutrition and food services across various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">440978f75b135fa97eb7b99ca379e9a4,544f7d3afd9f7def46c357525e55cabf,62f527b38024e8807d3e63a0cf488046,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d3">1444</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">842</data>
      <data key="d7">66c2cadd89a4402ca7c9636076ba0cc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DRE, or disease-related malnutrition, is a condition that can significantly impact patients' health and is influenced by the quality of food provided in hospitals. In particular, DRE is identified and evaluated in patients with Alzheimer&#8217;s disease to tailor their nutritional treatment effectively. This highlights the importance of addressing nutritional needs in the management of various health conditions, ensuring that patients receive appropriate dietary support to improve their overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,b4d5429d9b553438d3404c57e35c5c56</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
