      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">862</data>
      <data key="d7">d5d92cfdcb894cc99ed0a32a38d0629b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARLAMENTO EUROPEO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Parlamento Europeo, or European Parliament, is a key legislative institution within the European Union responsible for defining and regulating food hygiene standards across the region. It establishes necessary measures to ensure the safety of food products, thereby protecting consumer health. Additionally, the European Parliament has adopted regulations concerning food labeling, which aim to provide consumers with essential information about the products they purchase. Furthermore, the Parlamento Europeo has engaged with reports from the Comisi&#243;n Europea, specifically regarding foods targeted at athletes, highlighting its role in addressing various aspects of food regulation and consumer protection within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d2">4de75db0e24f0f89d890287e2a3f3dcc,54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074</data>
      <data key="d3">1561</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">863</data>
      <data key="d7">e8f6972354be459198d925ccd4a3753b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNI&#211;N EUROPEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Uni&#243;n Europea (European Union, EU) is a political and economic union comprising 27 member states located primarily in Europe. It aims to promote integration and cooperation among its members while establishing a comprehensive framework of regulations and directives that cover various aspects of health, nutrition, and food safety. The EU is responsible for setting guidelines related to health and nutrition, including dietary reference intakes and nutritional guidelines for its member states. 

In addition to health and nutrition, the Uni&#243;n Europea regulates food safety through the establishment of norms concerning food quality, safety, and the use of food additives. It oversees legislation that impacts health law and patient rights across its member states, ensuring that standards are maintained, including those for infant formulas. The EU has also emphasized the importance of defining frailty, particularly in relation to healthcare resources and elderly care.

Furthermore, the Uni&#243;n Europea has incorporated the Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP) system into its food safety legislation, reinforcing its commitment to ensuring the safety and quality of food products. Overall, the Uni&#243;n Europea plays a crucial role in shaping health and nutrition policies, as well as food safety regulations, across its member states.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,285343ba92b89a1761b72d9d789ba8f6,2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb,4198768cfbdf9c226ffba9074adf628f,42f51d76ff4164f7e731f1af04780490,4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a,4de75db0e24f0f89d890287e2a3f3dcc,574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,65e1359e381a0ac66f53b3a6eeba408b,8255943be503f6709a8e63d7d33b79d1,91131751d701592a597bae807e00c1dc,a4b56b993221a7065a59bca622c02953,cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1556</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">864</data>
      <data key="d7">e9e04b5737ed4fb78fdc55b62cca8c08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORGANIZACI&#211;N MUNDIAL DE LA SALUD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Organizaci&#243;n Mundial de la Salud (OMS), known in English as the World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations established in 1948. It is responsible for coordinating international public health efforts and defining health as a state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being. The OMS plays a crucial role in setting guidelines and recommendations on various health-related issues, including nutrition, hygiene, and disease prevention.

The organization has established diagnostic criteria for conditions such as osteoporosis and has set recommendations regarding the consumption of sodium and salt on a global scale. Additionally, the OMS provides guidance on dietary needs, recommending daily intake levels for essential nutrients like DHA, EPA, and iron supplementation for pregnant women to help reduce the prevalence of maternal anemia during childbirth.

Overall, the Organizaci&#243;n Mundial de la Salud is pivotal in shaping health policies and practices worldwide, ensuring that public health standards are met and maintained across different nations.</data>
      <data key="d2">22dcdc62dcda2e81a8707024945a4b01,285343ba92b89a1761b72d9d789ba8f6,4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a,4c07ceea84c09e222ce1317604be3e55,4de75db0e24f0f89d890287e2a3f3dcc,84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4,868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd,9df735d7829302712be068a5d1b1540b,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,d0a687d823ff2f3d5cb0f20b01d8530e,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">1612</data>
