    <node id="COMISI&#211;N DEL CODEX ALIMENTARIUS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Comisi&#243;n del Codex Alimentarius is a body of the FAO that standardizes food safety protocols, including the APPCC system for food safety management.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d3">1549</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">874</data>
      <data key="d7">9489ce5dd11c49cfbb723378bbf6f173</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to leading international efforts to combat hunger and enhance nutrition and food security. Established to address global food challenges, the FAO plays a crucial role in providing dietary guidelines, including recommendations for dietary protein intake, which were notably published in 2010. Additionally, the organization is responsible for creating international food composition tables that serve as essential resources for understanding nutritional values. Through its various initiatives, the FAO aims to improve nutrition and ensure that food security is achieved worldwide.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb,4198768cfbdf9c226ffba9074adf628f,42f51d76ff4164f7e731f1af04780490,60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,6907c82f1f024ed1b75f6aea88c47b3e,767d564db2dbf0182707caaf1b0a52d2,8778654a17a48b8ea7b1cec378d52346,87cb06eed8a8c92c589d25ea2d5cfaec,9303a85464d02f1cc012aaca21edf9bb,a4b56b993221a7065a59bca622c02953,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1549</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">875</data>
      <data key="d7">3fa20fb8fb5344c39f794bc59d462cbf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRCUITO ADECUADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The adecuado circuito refers to the proper flow and handling of food products to prevent contamination in the food supply chain.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d3">1523</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">876</data>
      <data key="d7">3a168882a5bf4ea3801e7026a88b4491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROORGANISMOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Microorganismos are tiny living organisms, such as bacteria and viruses, that can contaminate food and cause foodborne illnesses.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">877</data>
      <data key="d7">8bfd632eb2234fdeba8b4e5d9897d52a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGIENE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIGIENE refers to the practices and conditions that help maintain health and prevent the spread of diseases, particularly in food handling.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb,aacbc2a88a21cd749df3c22de5daea04</data>
      <data key="d3">1270</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">878</data>
      <data key="d7">522187868eba4671834823c917a3db42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANIPULADORES DE ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Manipuladores de alimentos are individuals involved in the food supply chain who handle food products and must adhere to hygiene standards to prevent contamination.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d3">1270</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">879</data>
      <data key="d7">d98d09ec73654c74957cbf20993c2bcd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSTALACIONES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Instalaciones refer to the facilities and environments where food is processed and handled, which must be designed to prevent contamination.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d3">1270</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">880</data>
      <data key="d7">67f7bcb6f1a542788a1a85679dc84ade</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO CERO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Riesgo cero refers to the concept that there is no absolute safety in food handling, and risks of contamination can never be completely eliminated.</data>
      <data key="d2">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d3">1524</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">881</data>
      <data key="d7">31759dc0340449a484f91dc22982ed93</data>
    </node>
