      <data key="d7">f5d3fecc1aeb4eca8744cfe7fa74d3df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRINCIPIO 7">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Principio 7 focuses on the documentation of procedures and records related to food safety principles and their application.</data>
      <data key="d2">4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">885</data>
      <data key="d7">5054090c92ed460a8ea148c697524ffc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AL&#201;RGENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AL&#201;RGENOS refers to allergens present in food, which are critical for dietary considerations, especially in the context of meal preparations, such as those in hospitals. These allergens include a variety of substances that can trigger allergic reactions in some individuals, such as dairy, fruits, fish, blue fish, nickel, and various spices. It is essential to identify and clearly indicate these allergens in recipes and on food product labels to ensure the safety of those with food sensitivities. The management of allergens has become a fundamental aspect of food safety protocols, necessitating the identification and control of these substances in food production.</data>
      <data key="d2">23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8,3d1d32234cefc2cce659d3f08feb0c80,4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a,569c8eafa9f82b2becef8d37416316a8,5bda98c244ed300cfc07192e54c7eb88,69fe73731693a5e2e639f646aaefaeec,8255943be503f6709a8e63d7d33b79d1,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,ec9e9b1519699c4c01b955945ea892d5,fa95290726c6f8f7c5947019c98a3e1d,ffb492629e13ca96c1fcee1496522f12</data>
      <data key="d3">1875</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">886</data>
      <data key="d7">9619011a67e1400ba78326e87b26a7b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRUST&#193;CEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Crust&#225;ceos refers to crustaceans, a diverse group of aquatic animals that includes species such as shrimp and crabs. These animals are significant in various culinary contexts, but it is important to note that products containing crustaceans are recognized as common allergens in food safety protocols. As such, awareness and caution are advised when consuming or handling foods that may include these ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d2">4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">887</data>
      <data key="d7">e67271aea157406786f6e325d0014a3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CACAHUETES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cacahuetes, commonly known as peanuts, are widely consumed as snacks and are also used in a variety of dishes. They are recognized not only for their culinary versatility but also as a significant source of essential nutrients, including vitamin B&#8323;. Additionally, it is important to note that peanuts are classified as a major allergen in food safety protocols, which means that products containing peanuts must be clearly labeled to inform consumers of potential allergy risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d3">1888</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">888</data>
      <data key="d7">c7c2365c053744b5a28e5a7a05fa09c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOJA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SOJA, commonly known as soybean, is a legume that serves as a major source of protein and is widely utilized in various food products. It is recognized for its nutritional value, being a plant source of omega-3 fatty acids and often recommended as a dietary supplement. SOJA is included in enteral formulas due to its high protein content, making it beneficial for individuals requiring specialized nutrition.

In culinary applications, SOJA is used as an emulsifier in products like Galleta Maria, where it helps blend ingredients and improve texture. However, it is important to note that soy and its derivatives are high in phenylalanine, which necessitates dietary restrictions for individuals with phenylketonuria.

Additionally, soy protein is acknowledged for its health benefits, including potential positive effects on lipid metabolism. Research suggests that soybeans may also offer protective effects against certain types of cancer, such as lung and breast cancer, attributed to their isoflavones. Furthermore, soy and soy-based products are significant allergens and are included in allergen management protocols. Overall, SOJA is a versatile legume with numerous health benefits and applications in both nutrition and food production.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc,ede4d21db7723c6b72e8493236b217ad,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
