    <node id="APIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">APIO refers to a vegetable that is characterized by its low galactose content, specifically containing less than 5 mg of galactose per 100 g. While the term "APIO" is often associated with celery, it is important to note that celery itself contains oxalate, a compound that can contribute to the formation of kidney stones. Additionally, celery has hard fibers, which may pose a risk for individuals with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Furthermore, celery is recognized as a potential allergen, and products that may contain celery should be approached with caution by those with allergies.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,4431bc1a109798ef648c103ac4eb321a,bd22bf95ac5fc6dc95539efb99c5b11a,e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
