    <node id="COCINA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cocina Hospitalaria is a culinary organization and institution dedicated to developing recipes and culinary practices specifically designed for hospital settings. Its primary focus is on meeting the nutritional needs of patients, including those with specific dietary requirements such as dysphagia. The organization emphasizes the importance of creating suitable meals that cater to the diverse dietary needs of patients, ensuring that their nutritional solutions are both safe and palatable. Cocina Hospitalaria encompasses the practices and recipes utilized in hospital kitchens, which are equipped to prepare meals tailored to the unique health conditions of patients. Overall, Cocina Hospitalaria plays a crucial role in enhancing the dietary care provided in healthcare facilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">0af5605f96545f73fc229a30e2aa34bd,18b4ac5d9393f776e63cac226bb6b12b,3d1d32234cefc2cce659d3f08feb0c80,65a32ea8f3ddb1c9b8e875c393d63151,7ce7a74ee3898be3e3f6d500d73afefd,80220ae2bbcfeda884776e0ed9103390,c1ec1ae8298c71442c08a75a2e629469,d01787532282add470408550197035c8</data>
