    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA Y DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA Y DIET&#201;TICA" refers to a specialized field and unit within healthcare that emphasizes the importance of dietary management and nutritional care for patients. This unit serves as a crucial component of hospitals, focusing on clinical nutrition and diet planning tailored to meet the specific needs of patients with various medical conditions. 

The unit is responsible for developing dietary menus in collaboration with the kitchen service, ensuring that meals are not only nutritious but also aligned with the dietary requirements of individual patients. Additionally, it creates dietary codes and guidelines that help maintain proper nutrition standards within the hospital setting. 

Overall, "NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA Y DIET&#201;TICA" encompasses both a field of study and a practical application aimed at improving patient health through effective nutritional strategies and management. It serves as a basic manual for healthcare professionals, providing essential nutritional guidelines that cater to a wide range of medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375,66c092d222e72c03a1f36507ce355cd4,6dfb109dac53e054fd015f6d8adf48ac,9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f,9df735d7829302712be068a5d1b1540b,aacbc2a88a21cd749df3c22de5daea04,aaef63df030ff97e66b358358491e6a5</data>
