    <node id="MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD, SERVICIOS SOCIALES E IGUALDAD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Ministerio de Sanidad, Servicios Sociales e Igualdad" is a governmental body in Spain responsible for the formulation and implementation of health and social services policies. This ministry oversees public health initiatives and is tasked with developing health-related strategies, including those focused on nutrition and clinical practice guidelines. Its role encompasses a broad spectrum of responsibilities aimed at promoting health and well-being within the Spanish population, ensuring that effective health policies and social services are in place to support the community.</data>
      <data key="d2">135d72a9407315b8bbf5b1ac13d72abf,1e6677459719ee2aa18d6d2ffbe46330,42f51d76ff4164f7e731f1af04780490,4c07ceea84c09e222ce1317604be3e55,66c092d222e72c03a1f36507ce355cd4</data>
