    <node id="COMISI&#211;N EUROPEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Comisi&#243;n Europea, also known as the European Commission, is the executive body of the European Union. It plays a crucial role in proposing legislation and implementing decisions within the EU framework. Recently, the Comisi&#243;n Europea presented a report to the European Parliament and Council concerning foods intended for athletes. Additionally, it is responsible for ensuring that food labeling regulations are updated and enforced, highlighting its commitment to maintaining food safety and transparency in the market.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c07ceea84c09e222ce1317604be3e55,54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1</data>
