    <node id="AGENCIA DE CALIDAD SANITARIA DE ANDALUC&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The AGENCIA DE CALIDAD SANITARIA DE ANDALUC&#205;A, also known as the Agency for Health Quality in Andalusia (ACSA), is an institution dedicated to ensuring the quality of health services within the Andalusian region of Spain. In addition to its primary role in overseeing health service quality, the agency is also responsible for reviewing and accrediting health-related web content in Spain, thereby contributing to the overall improvement and reliability of health information available to the public.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c07ceea84c09e222ce1317604be3e55,6d628d186db6cb708d96ec523f3e35c8</data>
