    </node>
    <node id="PLAN DE TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The treatment plan is a comprehensive strategy designed to address the needs of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, incorporating various therapeutic measures.</data>
      <data key="d2">e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b</data>
      <data key="d3">1172</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">969</data>
      <data key="d7">c7428146e92b4e6fad564934ba6bdf15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMILIARES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "FAMILIARES" refers to family members who play a crucial role in the care and support of patients. They are individuals related to the patient and can provide both emotional and practical assistance, particularly during the rehabilitation process for conditions such as oropharyngeal dysphagia. In cases involving specific disorders like galactosemia, family members may have a history of the condition, which can significantly influence screening and treatment decisions. Additionally, family members are often consulted for consent in situations where the patient is unable to make decisions for themselves. Their proximity to the patient allows them to have a substantial impact on treatment choices and consent processes, especially in instances of the patient's incapacity. Overall, family members are integral to the patient's healthcare journey, providing support and facilitating important decisions regarding treatment and consent.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,9934fdd98a0d66fb3ff7ac1b56b18460,e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b,e475fe60f9aab6773eddfe8bad25eef6,eaa675a346becd53a4fcfacbb99def88</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">970</data>
      <data key="d7">63b860f9c6d84e8585595e7f155dbe7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical evaluation is a comprehensive assessment of the patient's medical history, cognitive abilities, and swallowing function to inform treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d2">e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b</data>
      <data key="d3">1172</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">971</data>
      <data key="d7">2990b069da49418cbeea86c78e75da67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTE CON DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El paciente con disfagia orofar&#237;ngea es una persona que presenta dificultades para deglutir, lo que puede afectar su nutrici&#243;n y calidad de vida.</data>
      <data key="d2">8bf23d86ceb6dc396acc52c92878463d</data>
      <data key="d3">528</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">972</data>
      <data key="d7">0804aa39bea94f27bc54c2c9c2d86832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICAS COMPENSADORAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las t&#233;cnicas compensadoras son m&#233;todos que permiten al paciente comer algunos alimentos por v&#237;a oral, mejorando los s&#237;ntomas de la disfagia de manera inmediata.</data>
      <data key="d2">8bf23d86ceb6dc396acc52c92878463d</data>
      <data key="d3">528</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">973</data>
      <data key="d7">2334390fb193440892bb3164e10c30c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA E INSTRUMENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La evaluaci&#243;n cl&#237;nica e instrumental es un proceso necesario para determinar las caracter&#237;sticas adecuadas del bolo alimenticio para el paciente con disfagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">8bf23d86ceb6dc396acc52c92878463d</data>
      <data key="d3">528</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">974</data>
      <data key="d7">bdd3d16d3eb444b48074a70087c92863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODIFICACIONES EN EL VOLUMEN, TEXTURA Y VISCOSIDAD DEL BOLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las modificaciones en el volumen, textura y viscosidad del bolo son t&#233;cnicas utilizadas para facilitar la degluci&#243;n en pacientes con disfagia orofar&#237;ngea.</data>
      <data key="d2">8bf23d86ceb6dc396acc52c92878463d</data>
      <data key="d3">528</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">975</data>
      <data key="d7">93f43ce4aba247268da2a70a37112d26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLEXI&#211;N CERVICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A recommended posture for patients to protect the airway during swallowing by lowering the chin or tucking it in.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">976</data>
      <data key="d7">a48e716f54ce431cbd80686c063d87d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXTENSI&#211;N CERVICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A posture where the patient raises the chin to facilitate the passage of food from the mouth to the pharynx.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">977</data>
      <data key="d7">d16d80b105644c63a3118c4e27de0e17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROTACI&#211;N DE LA CABEZA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A technique where the patient rotates the head towards the affected side to direct the food bolus towards the healthy side.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">978</data>
      <data key="d7">3a3748d2c65d4d7d8effc3a6a5dd2827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INCLINACI&#211;N LATERAL DE LA CABEZA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A posture where the patient tilts the head towards the stronger side to assist in swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">979</data>
      <data key="d7">18d08f49d3c14dc2b3e0e699ea98cf27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CERVICOARTROSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition that may limit the ability of patients to perform certain postural techniques due to pain and mobility restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">980</data>
      <data key="d7">153e5408e17f4adfb17aa72a68d25cf7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REFLEJO DEGLUTORIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The swallowing reflex that is crucial for the safe passage of food from the mouth to the esophagus.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6fc88c88f73b50820517647aa8f4959</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">981</data>
      <data key="d7">862f95659d434021b349be20c832ddbe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROFES ET AL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Rofes et al are researchers who studied the effects of capsaicinoids on elderly patients with dysphagia oropharyngeal.</data>
      <data key="d2">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">982</data>
      <data key="d7">a1e706245ef94d8da935ac9763e19b31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCULATURA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The oropharyngeal musculature is involved in the swallowing process and can be trained through various exercises.</data>
      <data key="d2">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf</data>
      <data key="d3">162</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">983</data>
      <data key="d7">e80d88959d854f5680f729cec9510bce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANIOBRAS DEGLUTORIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Swallowing maneuvers are exercises that involve active swallowing to improve control and strength of the swallowing process.</data>
      <data key="d2">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf</data>
      <data key="d3">162</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">984</data>
      <data key="d7">0472491f7f4844fab056f823c6356c84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTIMULACI&#211;N T&#193;CTIL Y T&#201;RMICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tactile and thermal stimulation are techniques used to modify swallowing in patients with dysphagia oropharyngeal.</data>
      <data key="d2">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf</data>
      <data key="d3">914</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">985</data>
      <data key="d7">4f9c997ce3cd45188d315f9e3967f4ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASAKO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A specific swallowing maneuver that involves holding the tongue between the teeth or lips while swallowing to improve pharyngeal wall movement.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2b8f7ec7ed3d06b96620951376b640a</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">986</data>
      <data key="d7">3495aaf136684eec8db4b51c9ad1fc26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEGLUCI&#211;N FORZADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A swallowing technique that involves tightening all throat and tongue muscles while swallowing to enhance pressure and movement during the act of swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2b8f7ec7ed3d06b96620951376b640a</data>
      <data key="d3">1857</data>
