    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de cabeza y cuello refers to a type of cancer that affects the head and neck region, specifically characterized by conditions such as carcinoma epidermoide of the hemilangue. This medical condition often leads to swallowing difficulties, known as disfagia, which can significantly impact the patient's nutritional intake. As a result, patients may require specific rehabilitation exercises and nutritional support during their treatment. Additionally, this type of cancer can lead to complications such as hypercalcemia. Current evaluations are being conducted to explore specific nutritional treatments for patients undergoing surgery related to c&#225;ncer de cabeza y cuello.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,0d5d152382113aa1b8faab4e554c88cd,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,40dcfaa6144c6424068ba46fdf288dd2,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,d77e49d1dba3a67fbc9cf58911dc2478</data>
