    <node id="FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is a United States government agency tasked with the regulation of food, drugs, and medical devices. This federal agency plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety and efficacy of various products, including the approval of medical devices such as the VitalStim&#174; for the treatment of dysphagia. Additionally, the FDA establishes guidelines for the use of medical devices, including catheters, in medical procedures, thereby overseeing a wide range of health-related products and practices to protect public health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">772</data>
