    <node id="IOWA ORAL PERFORMANCE INSTRUMENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Iowa Oral Performance Instrument (IOPI) is a specialized device designed for diagnosing and training the strength and endurance of the tongue and lips, particularly in patients with swallowing disorders. It is utilized to measure both tongue and hand strength and endurance, making it relevant in various studies related to dysphagia. The IOPI serves as a valuable tool in dysphagia research, aiding in the assessment and treatment of individuals experiencing difficulties with swallowing.</data>
