    <node id="ENFERMER&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermer&#237;a (Nursing) provides essential support in the care of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow. The nursing staff plays a crucial role in assessing patients and implementing dietary modifications as part of the treatment for swallowing disorders. Specifically, the nursing team is instrumental in the assessment and care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia within the hospital setting. Their expertise and interventions are vital for ensuring the well-being and recovery of these patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">1719a8d20788e3b25240980cad2b6c5d,a3fd9c0d942a044ac2490f16d4ecc520,dfc3b0905ab9fc1fca9fc64473ebed80,fcc886f826047ced8783c4abfe3bf4a3</data>
