      <data key="d6">1185</data>
      <data key="d7">5a013d38abac4a4a83a23a926c414682</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATALU&#209;A">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Catalu&#241;a is an autonomous community in Spain known for its comprehensive approach to public health and nutrition. In this region, administrative tools are available for hiring dietitians within the public health system, ensuring that nutritional needs are adequately addressed. Additionally, Catalu&#241;a has been the site of significant research, including studies on iron deficiency and overload among the adult population, highlighting its commitment to understanding and improving health outcomes. For patients requiring ongoing nutritional treatment, it is necessary to submit a justification report to the relevant primary care center, which underscores the region's structured approach to healthcare management. Furthermore, the dispensing of nutritional and dietary products, referred to as NED products, is facilitated through hospital pharmacies, and there are established agreements with the pharmaceutical industry to enable home delivery, enhancing accessibility for patients in need.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,1f06578cbfda22ce8c7d322ba35a93a1,298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,eb2f276d3dc4e4a9e53923d9d80fec1a</data>
      <data key="d3">1369</data>
