    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL TOTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a medical treatment that provides 100% of a patient's nutritional requirements through intravenous administration. This method is utilized when enteral nutrition is contraindicated or not tolerated, allowing nutrients to be delivered directly into the bloodstream, thereby bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. TPN is particularly important for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, ensuring they receive essential nutrients for their health and recovery.

In specific cases, such as when a patient loses their nasoenteric tube, TPN may be initiated to support their nutritional needs until they can resume oral feeding. This treatment serves as a critical intervention during hospitalization, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not viable. Overall, NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL TOTAL is a vital component of patient care for those requiring specialized nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,488affd4bfc1b1b4b9f5b6a054c97d80,6886c5b652319bea0ba2427a3fdbf701,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,a9b588c70518bc2aa91325853898b7c0,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
      <data key="d3">1077</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
