    <node id="NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional Risk Screening refers to a systematic approach aimed at assessing the risk of malnutrition, particularly among older adults and patients in various healthcare settings. The Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS 2002) is a specific tool designed for this purpose, which helps identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, guiding healthcare professionals in implementing appropriate interventions to improve patient outcomes. This tool is especially relevant in hospitalized environments and is recommended for use in patients entering the Intensive Care Unit (ICU). A systematic review of nutritional screening tools highlights the importance of these assessments in predicting mortality and functional decline in older adults, underscoring the critical role of Nutritional Risk Screening in enhancing patient care and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,a9b588c70518bc2aa91325853898b7c0,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
