    <node id="ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS" refers to foods that pose significant risks for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. These dangerous foods include sticky items and those that can easily fragment, which may lead to choking or aspiration. Specifically, the foods identified as hazardous for individuals undergoing dysphagia assessment encompass orange, noodle soup, croquettes, meatballs in sauce, toasted bread, and cookies. It is crucial for caregivers and healthcare providers to be aware of these foods to ensure the safety and well-being of patients with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3,bd22bf95ac5fc6dc95539efb99c5b11a</data>
      <data key="d3">1445</data>
