    <node id="ALZHEIMER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alzheimer's disease is a progressive neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects memory and cognitive function, leading to significant cognitive decline. It is characterized by the presence of beta-amyloid plaques in the brain and the degeneration of brain cells. This condition not only impacts the patient's ability to perform daily activities but also contributes to complications such as dysphagia and malnutrition. Various risk factors are associated with Alzheimer's disease, including cardiovascular disease, diabetes mellitus, and elevated levels of homocysteine. Additionally, dietary habits may influence the progression of the disease. Overall, Alzheimer's disease represents a serious neurological condition that poses challenges for both patients and caregivers.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,5dd39815651d2d44f18c16e69696c0cf,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
