    </node>
    <node id="UNI&#211;N INTERNACIONAL DE TELECOMUNICACIONES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Uni&#243;n Internacional de Telecomunicaciones (UIT) is a specialized agency of the United Nations that plays a crucial role in coordinating global telecommunication standards and policies. It is responsible for managing the global use of the radio-frequency spectrum and satellite orbits, ensuring that these resources are utilized efficiently and effectively. Additionally, the UIT develops technical standards for telecommunications, including significant recommendations such as UIT-T Y.3600, which pertains to big data. Through its various functions, the UIT aims to facilitate international cooperation in the field of telecommunications and promote the development of communication technologies worldwide.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d64634b55389cb5d01f78b185bada8d,b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d</data>
      <data key="d3">1017</data>
