    <node id="OMS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The OMS (Organizaci&#243;n Mundial de la Salud), known in English as the World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for coordinating international public health efforts. The OMS plays a crucial role in establishing health standards, providing guidelines, and conducting research on various health-related topics. It is involved in the classification of diseases, including specific conditions such as craniofaringiomas and neuroendocrine tumors, and has updated its classifications, notably in 2017 for pituitary tumors.

The OMS provides comprehensive guidelines on a wide range of health issues, including the management of acute diarrhea, nutritional needs, and dietary recommendations. It emphasizes the importance of proper nutrition for children, pregnant women, and lactating mothers, advocating for a varied diet that meets all necessary nutrient requirements. The organization also offers formulas for estimating energy expenditure and dietary needs, which are essential for understanding the nutritional status of different populations.

In addition to its focus on nutrition, the OMS addresses broader health topics such as active aging, telemedicine, and the use of information and communication technologies in healthcare. It provides guidelines for rehydration solutions and has developed international reference patterns for child growth, contributing to global health initiatives aimed at improving the quality of life.

The OMS is recognized for its leadership in global health matters, shaping the health research agenda, and providing critical data on health issues such as diabetes prevalence and obesity management. Through its extensive guidelines and recommendations, the OMS aims to optimize health opportunities and enhance the overall well-being of populations worldwide.</data>
      <data key="d2">018644ab78da6f804c57546f08ff6a65,12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6,135d72a9407315b8bbf5b1ac13d72abf,148443357888793655b663333268775a,21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,2d14f6773b107ec9a872245c32ae0a94,3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,4198768cfbdf9c226ffba9074adf628f,48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,6da89a24c60015649c1d669e4e23fb2d,767d564db2dbf0182707caaf1b0a52d2,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7,7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,89b0bde0358432506a0e03d4691dd2ab,8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,91131751d701592a597bae807e00c1dc,a2675f78609440ca1162c24997360929,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,a4b56b993221a7065a59bca622c02953,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,a6ed8551aad722adcaf8fced4ac8685b,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c,bd31c6face847551241359e37e4baa2e,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052,cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c,d10d3648e8642657567d9a619f210ca6,d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f,d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f,d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6,e0102bb655b6476ce3296726e3aceb4a,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
