    <node id="SOCIEDAD ESPA&#209;OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n" (SEEN) is a prominent professional organization based in Spain, dedicated to the study, research, and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders. It plays a crucial role in the dissemination of knowledge in these fields, having published various guidelines, manuals, and educational resources, including the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n." 

SEEN is involved in the research and education of endocrinology and nutrition, providing valuable resources for the evaluation and management of various conditions, such as dislipemias, metabolic bone disease associated with home parenteral nutrition, hyperprolactinemia, and multiple endocrine neoplasia. The organization also offers online video courses and other educational materials to support training in these areas.

As a scientific society, SEEN is committed to promoting the advancement of endocrinology and nutrition in Spain, and it supports the professional development of its members, including notable figures such as Nuria Valdes Gallego, who has been actively involved in the Neuroendocrinology and Thyroid Area and served on the board from 2008 to 2011. Overall, the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n is a vital institution for healthcare professionals in Spain, fostering research, education, and best practices in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition.</data>
