    <node id="TABACO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TABACO refers to tobacco, a substance that is widely recognized for its negative health impacts. It is strongly advised to avoid tobacco consumption for at least 12 hours prior to medical tests to ensure accurate results, particularly in imaging procedures. The use of tobacco is discouraged due to its detrimental effects on bone health, as it is a known risk factor for osteoporosis. This is especially critical for patients with obesity and those undergoing bariatric surgery, as tobacco can exacerbate health complications in these groups. Furthermore, tobacco smoking has been established as a significant risk factor for the development of Graves' disease, with studies indicating an odds ratio of 3.5. Overall, tobacco consumption is a major public health concern, and health promotion programs often focus on reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,108b158c33fead285203903273758748,1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,6d174de24d62997808908333da591120,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
