    <node id="ANDALUC&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Andaluc&#237;a is an autonomous community located in the southern part of Spain, recognized for its rich cultural heritage and significant healthcare initiatives. It is home to the Agencia de Evaluaci&#243;n de Tecnolog&#237;as Sanitarias, which plays a vital role in contributing to public health. The region faces challenges related to health, notably high obesity prevalence rates, which have prompted specific healthcare policies. For instance, patients in Andaluc&#237;a are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs. Overall, Andaluc&#237;a combines a deep cultural legacy with ongoing efforts to address public health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">135d72a9407315b8bbf5b1ac13d72abf,298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,f12947896819ee4ab30d1fa3f3c9995d</data>
