    </node>
    <node id="HIGIENE BUCODENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Higiene bucodental refers to the practices and protocols aimed at maintaining oral health and preventing infections, particularly in patients with limited autonomy and those with swallowing difficulties. These oral hygiene practices are critical for ensuring cleanliness and preventing complications during feeding, especially for patients with dysphagia. Maintaining proper oral hygiene is essential for overall health and well-being, as it helps to mitigate the risk of infections and other oral health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">04fc50226ccbf87e5833a09d52275757,1719a8d20788e3b25240980cad2b6c5d,7c842769e1890739769789ed10a08005,bfc7f52d9f15519c092dee53ea9dcc33</data>
      <data key="d3">1064</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">1345</data>
      <data key="d7">e312e3877aff480682038c345bcf65b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMERA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The enfermera, or nurse, is a vital healthcare professional dedicated to providing comprehensive patient care. Their responsibilities encompass monitoring patients' nutritional status and implementing postural techniques for those suffering from dysphagia. Additionally, the enfermera plays a crucial role in oral care, which includes assessing the mucosa and educating patients on the significance of maintaining good oral hygiene. Furthermore, the nurse is tasked with administering medications and overseeing patient care related to the functionality of catheters, ensuring that all aspects of patient health are effectively managed.</data>
      <data key="d2">1c3eeb30a49c70f750b79e7bc1dfef52,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,bfc7f52d9f15519c092dee53ea9dcc33</data>
      <data key="d3">159</data>
