    <node id="LAUREL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Laurel, commonly known as bay leaf, is a versatile herb used for seasoning in a variety of culinary applications. It is particularly noted for its role in enhancing the flavor of dishes, including soups, stews, and sauces. Laurel is also utilized in specific recipes, such as hake medallions and gnocchi, where it contributes to the overall taste profile. Additionally, it is recognized for its use in managing dysphagia, as it can be incorporated into recipes designed for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Overall, laurel serves as a flavorful addition to many recipes, including those for boiled vegetables, making it a valuable herb in both everyday cooking and specialized dietary preparations.</data>
