    <node id="PATATA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Patata, commonly known as potato, is a starchy root vegetable that is widely utilized in cooking across various cuisines around the world. It is characterized by its versatility as an ingredient, appearing in numerous recipes such as Ralladura de huevo con tomate, Bacalao al cava, and Menudillo de Cocido, where it provides essential texture and substance. Patata is also a key component in dishes like gnocchi and is used to create pur&#233;es, such as in the hake medallions recipe.

In terms of nutritional content, Patata contains a small amount of dietary fiber and has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 g. The glycemic index of potatoes varies depending on the cooking method, with boiled potatoes having a high glycemic index of 121 and baked potatoes reaching 144. Overall, Patata is a significant food source that plays an important role in many culinary traditions, particularly for individuals with dysphagia, as it is featured in multiple recipes tailored for this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0af5605f96545f73fc229a30e2aa34bd,160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,5116416429465894c102d9fb93d6a8fc,53ab21b47d6304cc0eba5a45de3e8b53,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,b8fd422921866f53cdaa6c24db528ee5,cddf59ae158cab9962605b9e7d903544,ffb492629e13ca96c1fcee1496522f12</data>
