    <node id="ZANAHORIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Zanahoria, commonly known as carrot, is a versatile root vegetable celebrated for its sweetness, color, and nutritional value. It is frequently utilized in a variety of dishes, including sauces, soups, and salads, where it contributes both flavor and texture. Zanahoria is particularly noted for its role in dysphagia-friendly recipes, making it a suitable ingredient for individuals with swallowing difficulties. 

In culinary applications, zanahoria is featured in traditional recipes such as Menudillo de Cocido and is an essential component in dishes like Milhojas de Calabaza y Emperador and hake medallions. It is also used in vegetable pies and as a base for purees, especially recommended during the semisolid diet phase following bariatric surgery.

Nutritionally, zanahoria is high in fiber and contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5-10 mg per 100 g. It has a low glycemic index of 23 when raw and a higher index of 70 when cooked, making it a healthy choice for various diets. Overall, zanahoria is a nutritious and flavorful vegetable that enhances a wide array of culinary creations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0af5605f96545f73fc229a30e2aa34bd,160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,3d1d32234cefc2cce659d3f08feb0c80,5116416429465894c102d9fb93d6a8fc,569c8eafa9f82b2becef8d37416316a8,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,b8fd422921866f53cdaa6c24db528ee5,c1ec1ae8298c71442c08a75a2e629469,cddf59ae158cab9962605b9e7d903544,d01787532282add470408550197035c8,fa95290726c6f8f7c5947019c98a3e1d</data>
