    <node id="MAYONESA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mayonesa, commonly known as mayonnaise, is a condiment made from emulsified egg yolks and oil. It is widely used in various recipes, including the traditional Spanish dish ensaladilla rusa. Depending on the recipe, mayonesa may contain lactose. However, it is important to note that mayonnaise is not permitted in modified diets. In culinary applications, mayonnaise is utilized in recipes such as cold salmon cake, where it contributes creaminess and flavor.</data>
