    <node id="CEBOLLA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cebolla, commonly known as onion, is a bulb vegetable renowned for its strong flavor and aroma, making it an essential ingredient in a wide variety of culinary dishes. It is frequently saut&#233;ed or cooked to enhance its natural sweetness, contributing significantly to the flavor profile of many recipes. Cebolla is utilized in the preparation of numerous dishes, including Crema Fr&#237;a de Mel&#243;n con Jam&#243;n, pur&#233; calabaza, pea sauce for boiled vegetables, cold salmon cake, hake medallions, vegetable pie, and gnocchi, among others.

In addition to its culinary uses, cebolla contains varying levels of fructans, which may affect individuals with FODMAP sensitivity. It also has a moderate amount of galactose, ranging between 5-10 mg per 100 grams. Overall, cebolla serves as a foundational ingredient in cooking, valued for its ability to enhance flavor and aroma across a diverse array of recipes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0af5605f96545f73fc229a30e2aa34bd,160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,3d1d32234cefc2cce659d3f08feb0c80,53ab21b47d6304cc0eba5a45de3e8b53,569c8eafa9f82b2becef8d37416316a8,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,7ce7a74ee3898be3e3f6d500d73afefd,9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,b8fd422921866f53cdaa6c24db528ee5,c1ec1ae8298c71442c08a75a2e629469,cddf59ae158cab9962605b9e7d903544,d01787532282add470408550197035c8,fa95290726c6f8f7c5947019c98a3e1d</data>
