    <node id="PUERRO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Puerro, commonly known as leek, is a vegetable that resembles an onion and is valued in cooking for its mild flavor. It is frequently used in the preparation of various culinary dishes, particularly soups and sauces, where it enhances the overall flavor profile. Puerro is an essential ingredient in several recipes, including pea sauce for boiled vegetables, hake medallions, and vegetable pie, showcasing its versatility in the kitchen. Additionally, it is a component in pur&#233; calabaza, further highlighting its culinary applications. However, it is important to note that puerro contains fructans, which may pose challenges for individuals with FODMAP intolerance. Overall, puerro is a flavorful and widely used vegetable in various cooking contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">0af5605f96545f73fc229a30e2aa34bd,3d1d32234cefc2cce659d3f08feb0c80,53ab21b47d6304cc0eba5a45de3e8b53,569c8eafa9f82b2becef8d37416316a8,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,b8fd422921866f53cdaa6c24db528ee5,c1ec1ae8298c71442c08a75a2e629469,cddf59ae158cab9962605b9e7d903544,d01787532282add470408550197035c8</data>
