    <node id="CALABAC&#205;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Calabac&#237;n, commonly known as zucchini, is a versatile summer squash celebrated for its mild flavor and nutritional benefits. It is a gluten-free vegetable that is featured in various dietary plans, making it suitable for those with gluten sensitivities. Calabac&#237;n contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams, which adds to its appeal for health-conscious individuals.

This vegetable is widely used in a variety of recipes, including lasagna, where it is often layered with meat and sauce, as well as in salads and vegetable pies. Its adaptability in cooking allows it to be incorporated into numerous dishes, enhancing both flavor and nutrition. Overall, Calabac&#237;n is a popular ingredient in many culinary applications, appreciated for its health benefits and culinary versatility.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,1cdda2c6d946ce6e48baae4230be531d,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe,8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84,a8a688d676adb0ffde17c9f1d729aea3,c1ec1ae8298c71442c08a75a2e629469</data>
