    <node id="HARINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HARINA is a versatile powder made from grinding raw grains, commonly used as a primary ingredient in a variety of recipes, including the masa for croquetas. It is recognized as part of the cereal group and is allowed in modified diets. In culinary applications, HARINA serves multiple purposes, such as a thickening agent in recipes like hake medallions and Br&#243;coli con Salsa Aurora. Additionally, it is frequently utilized in cooking for breading and in the preparation of sauces and other dishes, making it an essential ingredient in both cooking and baking.</data>
