    <node id="PATATAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Patatas, commonly known as potatoes, are a versatile tuber that serves as a staple food item in many diets around the world. They are rich in vitamin B&#8323; and are considered an essential component of a balanced diet. It is recommended to consume patatas fresh or in homemade preparations, as opposed to fried versions typically found in bars and restaurants, which may be less healthy. 

Patatas can be utilized in a variety of culinary applications, functioning both as a main course and a side dish. They provide carbohydrates and energy, making them a significant source of nutrition. Specific weight measurements are often provided for different serving sizes, highlighting their importance in meal planning. Additionally, patatas are commonly used in recipes for pur&#233;e or as a filling in various dishes, showcasing their adaptability in the kitchen.</data>
      <data key="d2">08edfb59071449728499ca59eb51ac84,26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,e0208971287419e734607191646ae36d,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4,fa95290726c6f8f7c5947019c98a3e1d</data>
