    <node id="POLLO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pollo, which translates to chicken, is a versatile ingredient commonly used in various culinary applications, including the Menudillo de Cocido recipe, where it contributes both protein and flavor. In terms of serving sizes, pollo is often measured by specific weight, allowing for precise portioning in meals. Additionally, pollo has a varying purine content, generally regarded as moderate, which can influence uric acid levels in the body. This makes pollo a popular choice in many diets, balancing nutritional benefits with considerations for health.</data>
