      <data key="d1">Perejil, commonly known as parsley, is an herb that serves multiple culinary purposes. It is particularly noted for its role as a garnish and flavor enhancer in various dishes, including hake medallions. Additionally, perejil is characterized by its low galactose content, containing less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This makes it a suitable option for individuals who are mindful of their galactose intake.</data>
