    <node id="NARANJA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">NARANJA, commonly known as orange, is a citrus fruit that is widely consumed for its juice and high vitamin C content. It contains a fructose level of 2 g per 100 g and has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 g. In addition to its nutritional benefits, NARANJA is also an ingredient used in the preparation of dishes such as 'Sufl&#233; de Salm&#243;n en Salsa de Naranja'. Importantly, oranges do not contain tiocianates, which means they do not affect the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells. However, it is worth noting that oranges can release liquids when chewed, which may pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Overall, NARANJA is a versatile fruit that provides dietary fiber and is enjoyed in various culinary applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040,569c8eafa9f82b2becef8d37416316a8,9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,bd22bf95ac5fc6dc95539efb99c5b11a</data>
