    <node id="CALABAZA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Calabaza, also known as pumpkin, is a type of squash recognized for its sweet flavor and versatility in culinary applications. It is commonly used in various dishes, including soups and pies. In particular, calabaza serves as a key ingredient in the preparation of 'Milhojas de Calabaza y Emperador'. Nutritionally, calabaza contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams.</data>
