    <node id="SACARINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Saccharin, also known by its E number E954, is one of the oldest artificial sweeteners, recognized for its ability to provide sweetness without contributing calories. It is commonly utilized as a sugar substitute in various recipes, including the Cremoso de Manzana, where it serves to enhance flavor while reducing caloric content.</data>
