    <node id="PARES CRANEALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pares craneales, or cranial nerves, play a crucial role in the swallowing process. This group includes the trigeminal, facial, glossopharyngeal, vagus, accessory, and hypoglossal nerves. In patients with bulbar onset amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ELA), these cranial nerves can be significantly affected, leading to difficulties in swallowing. The involvement of pares craneales in this context highlights their importance in the neurological function related to swallowing and the challenges faced by individuals with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8</data>
      <data key="d3">473</data>
