    <node id="FRUTAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">FRUTAS, or fruits, are essential components of a balanced diet, providing a wide array of nutrients including vitamins, minerals, fiber, potassium, and magnesium. They are particularly encouraged for their health benefits, such as reducing the risk of cardiovascular events and preventing kidney stones due to their hydrating properties. Dietary guidelines recommend consuming fruits at least three times a day, with specific intake suggestions of two servings per day, focusing on those with lower potassium content for certain individuals.

Fruits are also recognized for their protective effects against cancer, especially when consumed in large quantities. They are an important part of the Mediterranean diet, known for their rich nutrient profile, including antioxidants. However, certain fruits may contain small amounts of galactose, which should be consumed with caution by individuals with galactosemia. Additionally, fresh fruits or juices may need to be eliminated from the diet prior to specific medical tests to avoid false positives.

It is advised to prefer fresh fruits over commercial jams, which may contain gluten. Overall, FRUTAS are a vital aspect of dietary recommendations for both children and adults, promoting overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,08edfb59071449728499ca59eb51ac84,23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,72ed1fffc10ea163a92b5f1a7b972732,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c,b5db5210dfb726bf3f6d3fae82598596,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
