    <node id="PANCREATITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"PANCREATITIS AGUDA" refers to acute pancreatitis, a medical condition characterized by sudden inflammation of the pancreas. This condition can lead to severe abdominal pain and requires immediate medical attention. It is often associated with complications such as hyperglycemia and can necessitate careful nutritional management, particularly in diabetic patients. 

Acute pancreatitis may require nutritional support, which can include enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition, especially during the initial days of treatment. The severity of the condition can vary, being classified as mild, moderate, or severe, depending on the presence of complications and organ failure. Symptoms typically manifest between 24 to 36 hours after the peak production of cytokines, and the condition is marked by elevated levels of pancreatic enzymes such as amylase and lipase in the blood.

Acute pancreatitis is a common reason for emergency consultations, with a presentation rate of 0.1% to 1.5% in large hospitals. It is crucial for patients experiencing this condition to receive intensive treatment and monitoring to manage the potential complications effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,b1464c57df2eaa651a10c1522ab7db68,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83,be7eb01a6daf673db6a127f66c79c96c,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e,dbfd111867924ed831f05d8fff01888b,dce680808e039e852dc0f2639835db32,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
