      <data key="d6">1641</data>
      <data key="d7">d954d65a51e745619d3774bc045227d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatopathies refer to diseases affecting the liver, which can lead to nutritional alterations and complications. These liver diseases are significant enough to be considered a contraindication for the use of lorcaserin, a medication that may not be suitable for individuals with such conditions. Additionally, hepatopathies may necessitate specialized nutritional care to address the unique dietary needs and complications associated with liver dysfunction.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,82adde9844cf0b1ccd052f91b304fb6e,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613</data>
      <data key="d3">1819</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">1642</data>
      <data key="d7">3ba54bf98aef44c1a4f5ad93dd1fb34c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">**S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO (Short Bowel Syndrome)** is a medical condition characterized by a significant reduction in the absorptive capacity of the small intestine, often resulting from the surgical removal of a large portion of the intestine, congenital defects, or various medical conditions such as Crohn's disease and mesenteric ischemia. This condition leads to malabsorption of nutrients and can cause nutritional deficiencies, diarrhea, and other complications.

Patients with S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO may require specialized nutritional management, including enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition (NPT), particularly when there is a substantial loss of intestinal length. The condition can necessitate long-term nutritional support due to the reduced ability to absorb essential nutrients, making it a significant concern in clinical settings. In fact, S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO is one of the most frequent indications for NPT, accounting for approximately 32.2% of cases.

Overall, S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO is a complex condition that requires careful management to address the challenges of nutrient absorption and to prevent complications associated with malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,41dee7570059d609c99074f155d4f927,4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe,538970e30e9d0e758546ca1a3cf5a205,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,6dfb109dac53e054fd015f6d8adf48ac,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d,bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9,cd63370bdd798f0b060b047dc29056ae,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5,efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613,f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
