    <node id="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" is a medical procedure that involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are blood-forming stem cells, to treat a variety of diseases, including cancers and blood disorders. This procedure may require nutritional support for recovery, as patients often experience malnutrition during the treatment of neoplastic diseases. Additionally, the transplantation can lead to complications, such as hepatic veno-occlusive disease. Overall, hematopoietic cell transplantation is a critical intervention for managing serious health conditions, necessitating careful monitoring and support throughout the recovery process.</data>
