    <node id="TRASPLANTE HEP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TRASPLANTE HEP&#193;TICO" refers to the surgical procedure of liver transplantation, which involves replacing a diseased liver with a healthy liver from a donor. This procedure is considered a definitive treatment for chronic liver disease, aimed at curing the condition. It is particularly indicated for patients with severe liver disease, including those with severe OTC and CPS deficiencies who experience recurrent hyperammonemia.

The liver transplant for the patient in question was performed in September 2003 at the Hepatic Transplant Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc&#237;o and was completed without complications. The procedure has a survival rate of approximately 90% at one year and 70% at five years post-transplant. It is important to note that the nutritional status of patients, especially those with chronic liver disease, can impact the outcomes of liver transplantation.

Additionally, while liver transplantation was evaluated as a treatment option for the patient with MNGIE, it was ultimately deemed unsuitable. Overall, liver transplantation is a critical surgical intervention for patients suffering from severe liver conditions, providing a potential cure and significantly improving quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c,2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f,94a9c497b06553e1f7643ff25e4b464f,b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa,d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7,fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d3">611</data>
