    <node id="PLIEGUE TRICIPITAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Pliegue Tricipital" is a measurement utilized to estimate body fat in the body by assessing the thickness of skinfolds, specifically taken from the non-dominant arm. This measurement serves as an important tool for evaluating body fat percentage, which in turn offers valuable insights into an individual's nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">1132</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1681</data>
      <data key="d7">99a789157c1942a7bbb60be5697aa7a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PER&#205;METRO MUSCULAR DEL BRAZO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Per&#237;metro Muscular del Brazo" is a measurement that estimates lean body mass by utilizing the Circunferencia Braquial (brachial circumference) and the Pliegue Tricipital (triceps skinfold). This calculation serves as an important tool for assessing muscle mass, providing valuable insights into an individual's body composition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b6ad83080610bbf1789d7db4c8d40ba,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">1075</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1682</data>
      <data key="d7">b2bd8fce6ce74d7ca50b80daa2ed5808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M. ARGENTE PLA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">M. Argente Pla is a medical doctor and a prominent contributor to various chapters related to nutrition in medical contexts. He has authored and co-authored several significant works, including a chapter on nutrition and diabetes in relation to cystic fibrosis, and has collaborated with M.D. Hig&#243;n Ballester on this topic. Additionally, M. Argente Pla has written a chapter on artificial nutrition in acute pancreatitis and has contributed to discussions on artificial nutrition in liver diseases. His expertise extends to inflammatory bowel disease, where he has co-authored research on nutrition. 

M. Argente Pla is also involved in educational initiatives, having contributed to chapters on enteral nutrition, parenteral nutrition, nutritional requirements, and nutritional screening in hospitals. Furthermore, he has played a role in the nutritional assessment chapter, showcasing his comprehensive involvement in the field of nutrition within medical literature.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb,3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58,3fa37a80a7ecb21c1bdd4838ed9abf2e,61ece3be5a1146d0a386ccd0a379c88b,820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b,82adde9844cf0b1ccd052f91b304fb6e,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,bfe875ea294b9a390193b5de532ff71b,c67141db7734dcc583e60c351c2e0772,ce8f5f24dbbf8624e49a6f85c2ad0d04</data>
