    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N MODERADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DESNUTRICI&#211;N MODERADA" refers to a classification of malnutrition characterized by a Body Mass Index (BMI) ranging from 16 to 16.9. It is a condition diagnosed in patients who exhibit significant deficiencies in nutritional intake, which can adversely affect their health and recovery. According to the GLIM criteria, patients diagnosed with moderate malnutrition experience notable weight loss and nutrient depletion, necessitating the implementation of a nutritional treatment plan to address their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,c92ceeeeae88c8288176cbfd00c75e17,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206</data>
