    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS GASTROINTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "S&#237;ntomas Gastrointestinales" encompasses a range of gastrointestinal symptoms that are commonly observed in individuals with various conditions, including celiac disease, gluten sensitivity, and lactose intolerance. These symptoms include bloating, diarrhea, nausea, and vomiting, which can significantly impair a patient's ability to maintain proper nutrition. In patients with celiac disease, clinical manifestations may include chronic diarrhea and abdominal distension. Additionally, gastrointestinal symptoms are also noted in patients with MELAS, where they contribute to an increased risk of malnutrition. Overall, these symptoms are critical factors that are assessed during evaluations to understand their impact on nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bc48d0666e895b990c211acf7cbcf23,281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
