    <node id="MARCADORES NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los Marcadores Nutricionales son indicadores que ayudan a completar la valoraci&#243;n nutricional y a monitorizar el tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">671</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">1727</data>
      <data key="d7">914e848a15a84cb79261f272ab7bf671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GLUCOSA, also known as glucose, is a simple sugar and a primary source of energy for the body's cells. It plays a crucial role in various metabolic processes and is essential for living organisms. GLUCOSA is produced during the digestion of carbohydrates and is commonly found in many foods. It is particularly important in medical nutrition, especially for patients with specific dietary needs, such as those receiving parenteral nutrition.

In parenteral nutrition, GLUCOSA is administered in various concentrations, often as dextrose, and constitutes a significant portion of caloric intake, typically representing 60-75% of non-protein caloric contributions. It is vital for energy supply in patients, including newborns with low birth weight, and is the primary source of calories recommended for burned patients, accounting for about 50% of their total caloric needs. However, the administration of GLUCOSA must be carefully monitored to avoid complications such as hyperglycemia, with a recommended maximum rate of 3.5 g/kg/day.

GLUCOSA also serves as a marker for nutritional assessment and is involved in the management of blood sugar levels in patients with diabetes and metabolic disorders. It can interfere with the uptake of radiotracers during medical tests and is crucial for energy production during physical activities, particularly in prolonged exercises. Overall, GLUCOSA is a fundamental carbohydrate that must be consumed in moderation to maintain health and energy balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb,01704aec4089b2f0f24dd0f0841b5ecf,033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,056067ecde43f31b356fc39e056221ee,06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,202e4fa915a698c9d9164c3fcc61534e,2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced,439efa4d64a3de0b12975ea727c939f4,449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,490f5e3c6dbf3754eee50c52154da09a,4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd,507eeea555c496a467930836fc4c1a39,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead,7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f,880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162,8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544,9baa05f21f51764ac1d0537294bdc7db,ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e,b3bff0edc314389f2ac432a753fec9f7,c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4,cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2,d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b,e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a,f0bfe278aa9f43f4bc9d056de67a5b96,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
