    </node>
    <node id="TRANSFERRINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Transferrina, also known as transferrin, is a crucial protein that plays a significant role in the transport of iron in the blood. It is commonly measured to evaluate nutritional status and liver function, particularly in patients with conditions such as inflammatory bowel disease and malnutrition. Transferrina is sensitive to changes in nutritional status, making it a valuable diagnostic parameter. Additionally, it can indicate iron depletion in dialysis patients, often in relation to the administration of recombinant erythropoietin (EPO). Overall, transferrina serves as an important marker for assessing both nutritional and health status in various clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8,541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292,a6ed8551aad722adcaf8fced4ac8685b,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395</data>
      <data key="d3">671</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1731</data>
      <data key="d7">e3d71db15f1945bf8bb524887cdf570b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREALBUMINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PREALBUMINA is a protein that plays a crucial role in evaluating nutritional status and serves as a prognostic marker. It is particularly significant in assessing malnutrition, as its levels can be indicative of a patient's nutritional condition throughout treatment. PREALBUMINA is commonly measured in patients, including those with inflammatory bowel disease, where it helps to reflect their nutritional status. Overall, PREALBUMINA is recognized as an important protein for monitoring nutritional health, especially in cases of malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f,45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8,61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">1155</data>
