      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1732</data>
      <data key="d7">343dabea578340149894ba2f55e0613b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NA LIGADORA DE RETINOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La Prote&#237;na Ligadora de Retinol es un marcador nutricional que se mide para evaluar el estado nutricional del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">671</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1733</data>
      <data key="d7">3b73c88064234fe18d02488a8d5c1a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;NDICE CREATININA-ALTURA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#205;ndice Creatinina-Altura is an important indicator of muscle mass that is derived from the excretion of creatinina. This parameter is utilized in nutritional assessments to evaluate both kidney function and nutritional status. By measuring the creatinina levels in relation to height, it provides valuable insights into an individual's overall health, particularly in assessing muscle mass and renal performance.</data>
      <data key="d2">86d733befbaaebe4eccbc45db498a0b0,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1734</data>
      <data key="d7">f68b3d60e54143a6ba4149e69f1dfe63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BALANCE NITROGENADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Balance nitrogenado" is a crucial measure used in nutritional assessments to evaluate protein intake and metabolism. It reflects the protein metabolism in the body and is calculated based on the difference between nitrogen ingested and nitrogen excreted. This balance serves as an important indicator of nutritional status, with a positive nitrogen balance being desirable in healthy individuals and in patients who are malnourished or under metabolic stress. The measurement of nitrogen balance is particularly significant during parenteral nutrition, as it helps assess the intake and elimination of nitrogen in patients. Additionally, it is important to note that nitrogen balance can be negatively affected in conditions such as primary hypothyroidism, highlighting its role in understanding protein needs and overall metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d2">5cf1703fd601b27dd0ebda9f20cb3259,60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,838d1ef59dfea4cab2a724bc85b02632,86d733befbaaebe4eccbc45db498a0b0,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1735</data>
      <data key="d7">cf2135af9e2d4d79b427e1a1aea589e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD ABDOMINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La obesidad abdominal es un componente del s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico que representa un riesgo significativo en pacientes que reciben tratamiento con testosterona. Se define como un per&#237;metro abdominal superior a 102 cm en hombres y 88 cm en mujeres, lo que indica un aumento en el riesgo vascular.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1736</data>
      <data key="d7">4dca0007f4754931b309618ed2cfdd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME NEFR&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome nefr&#243;tico," or nephrotic syndrome, is a significant kidney disorder characterized by the excessive loss of proteins in the urine, known as proteinuria. This condition arises from damage to the glomerular membrane, which impairs the kidneys' ability to filter proteins effectively. As a result, patients often experience low levels of albumin in the blood, leading to hipoalbuminemia, and may develop edema due to fluid retention.

The syndrome not only affects protein levels but also has implications for the patient's nutritional status, necessitating specific nutritional management to prevent complications. It can lead to various metabolic disturbances, including alterations in SHBG (sex hormone-binding globulin) levels and hormonal balance, as well as hypervolemic hyponatremia, which is an excess of fluid in the body that dilutes sodium levels.

Additionally, the condition may be associated with low levels of copper and ceruloplasmin, further complicating the patient's health. Overall, the s&#237;ndrome nefr&#243;tico requires careful monitoring and management to address both the renal and nutritional challenges it presents.</data>
      <data key="d2">232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,2c60ced31055ac58d76da9c1e90c8e9d,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181,94a9c497b06553e1f7643ff25e4b464f,9562f39f9e78644164daeff3177a2f84,9f77fc213da2123b013166c181a60323,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4,d1e7cd9fdc3093bc5902030d654d0763,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">1737</data>
      <data key="d7">f22b55e32b354b74b32fc3b160756e73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUEMADURAS EXTENSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">QUEMADURAS EXTENSAS se refiere a una condici&#243;n que puede resultar en niveles bajos de cobre en el organismo. Adem&#225;s, las quemaduras extensas pueden influir en los niveles de prote&#237;nas circulantes y en la evaluaci&#243;n del estado nutricional del individuo afectado. Esto sugiere que las quemaduras extensas no solo tienen un impacto f&#237;sico directo, sino que tambi&#233;n pueden alterar el equilibrio nutricional y los niveles de minerales esenciales en el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d2">232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1738</data>
      <data key="d7">e5590f724d284f0fa61588bafbc9a84b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES PLASM&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los niveles plasm&#225;ticos se refieren a la concentraci&#243;n de sustancias en la sangre, que se utilizan para evaluar el estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1739</data>
      <data key="d7">68852c3a5f7444b9b6d048e64823a3be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCION HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La funci&#243;n hep&#225;tica se refiere a la capacidad del h&#237;gado para realizar sus funciones, que puede influir en el estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1740</data>
      <data key="d7">ec77ec0825bc4668920353be7795095e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCION RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La funci&#243;n renal se refiere a la capacidad de los ri&#241;ones para filtrar y excretar desechos, que puede afectar el estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1741</data>
      <data key="d7">916d6be8e0e14e488805f213fcb24fd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALOR PRON&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El valor pron&#243;stico se refiere a la capacidad de un marcador o medici&#243;n para predecir el estado de salud o la evoluci&#243;n de una enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1742</data>
      <data key="d7">b56183eb9c58459ca822eb37fd1ab69a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#201;TODOS DE VALORACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los m&#233;todos de valoraci&#243;n son t&#233;cnicas utilizadas para evaluar el estado nutricional y la composici&#243;n corporal de un individuo.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1743</data>
      <data key="d7">a92f6d34b4a6421ea4716c0c223b2a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAMBIOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los cambios cl&#237;nicos se refieren a alteraciones en el estado de salud de un paciente que pueden requerir una reevaluaci&#243;n nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1744</data>
      <data key="d7">2168b58b93dd427eb1930a7fa2820e51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N POR EXCESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La malnutrici&#243;n por exceso se refiere a la ingesta excesiva de nutrientes, que puede llevar a la obesidad y otros problemas de salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1745</data>
      <data key="d7">5084b406bde5405daddd8f4b67875f8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N POR DEFECTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La malnutrici&#243;n por defecto se refiere a la ingesta insuficiente de nutrientes, que puede afectar la salud y el bienestar general.</data>
      <data key="d2">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1746</data>
      <data key="d7">2a2c13f828f84a629889dfd0793bf571</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIEDAD ESPA&#209;OLA PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LA OBESIDAD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad Espa&#241;ola para el Estudio de la Obesidad (SEEDO) is an organization dedicated to the study and evaluation of obesity. It provides established criteria for assessing the outcomes of metabolic surgery and for classifying obesity based on body mass index (IMC). Additionally, Nuria Valdes Gallego has been a board member of SEEDO since 2015, contributing to its mission and activities in the field of obesity research and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d3">1368</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1747</data>
      <data key="d7">e93149d6475e4f558a8318e8342220e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"PROTE&#205;NAS" are essential macromolecules that play a critical role in the functioning of the body. They are vital for growth, repair of tissues, and maintaining overall health. Proteins are macronutrients that should comprise a significant portion of the diet, with recommendations suggesting they should account for 12-15% of total caloric intake for the general population, and 20-30% for patients with specific health conditions, such as liver disease. 

In clinical nutrition, proteins are particularly important for various patient populations, including the elderly, those with chronic kidney disease, cancer patients, and individuals with inflammatory bowel disease (EII). For elderly patients, high biological value proteins are necessary to maintain functional capacity and autonomy. In patients with EII, protein intake must be adequate to support health and recovery, as these individuals may experience nutrient loss through inflamed intestinal mucosa.

Proteins are also crucial in managing metabolic stress, with specific intake recommendations ranging from 1.5 to 2 g/kg/day to minimize catabolic responses. In the context of renal failure, careful management of protein intake is essential to prevent malnutrition and disease progression. Similarly, in patients with respiratory failure and those recovering from surgery or transplants, proteins play a significant role in recovery and healing.

Athletes, particularly those engaged in strength sports, require specific amounts of protein to support muscle formation and energy metabolism. The sources of protein can vary, with animal proteins generally providing higher biological value compared to plant-based options. However, excessive intake of animal proteins may increase the risk of kidney stones due to their effects on urinary pH and calcium excretion.

Proteins are also integral to pediatric nutrition, especially for children involved in sports, and are included in parenteral nutrition formulations tailored to individual health needs. Overall, proteins are essential nutrients that contribute to various bodily functions, including muscle repair, immune function, and metabolic processes, and their intake must be carefully managed based on individual health conditions and dietary requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">043ed163c427b880fe39884076cae7ea,056067ecde43f31b356fc39e056221ee,06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,1130db2843c569042990b711cf15d8ee,1592143354d1ef792f8618ec03a32a16,20491afa9a4770e93e6cff9034f8b0f0,281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,2c60ced31055ac58d76da9c1e90c8e9d,2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9,30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b,3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab,39da0855b83941d97766254aa36ed2fd,3dbf07634cee8d4d443f59ed50f98b54,43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd,45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186,622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817,62f527b38024e8807d3e63a0cf488046,64417661dbb019f8f4ceb9fcc2fbdaa6,658ee56030a35ceeeec05d15cfa49842,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,7e539a13a598e4ff2d2d4d6641a044d5,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,91c1a9b0c0d7cb718d7711ef7384a142,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,aea37ea74c52c952285b3ae7db228572,b3bff0edc314389f2ac432a753fec9f7,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,bb9a5c32408b601f9ecedc2a2b82d6b6,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,d1e7cd9fdc3093bc5902030d654d0763,dc38a37c30b175667931b84a9c9103bb,dcb97f7ffdb0aea3051bdf53e04bcc29,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b,e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9,f558c372d16630f14b614e232fc151de,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef,f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af,fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
