    <node id="ANAMNESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANAMNESIS is a comprehensive assessment process that involves gathering detailed information about a patient's medical history, dietary habits, and psychological factors, particularly in relation to eating disorders. This process is crucial in nutritional assessment as it evaluates changes in weight, appetite, and dietary habits, among other relevant factors. Additionally, ANAMNESIS plays a significant role in understanding the context of various health issues, such as diarrhea, by obtaining a thorough medical history from the patient. Overall, ANAMNESIS serves as an essential tool in the evaluation and management of patients' health and nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
