    </node>
    <node id="BALANCE NITROGENADO (BN)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Balance nitrogenado (BN) is a clinical measure that reflects the difference between nitrogen intake and excretion, indicating protein metabolism status.</data>
      <data key="d2">30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b</data>
      <data key="d3">591</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1751</data>
      <data key="d7">bd11281e31b246d28418be24b00bd62b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">UREA is a chemical compound that plays a significant role in assessing renal function and hydration status in patients. It is a waste product formed from the breakdown of proteins and is commonly measured in both blood and urine. In blood tests, urea levels are evaluated to determine kidney function and overall metabolic health, while in urine tests, it is used to calculate nitrogen balance. Additionally, urea is utilized in medical treatments to enhance the renal elimination of free water and reduce natriuresis, although it is noted for its poor palatability and issues with patient adherence.</data>
      <data key="d2">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7,30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">1752</data>
      <data key="d7">42c3fe6dd6dc4bd997b05002fd924104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCIONES INMUNITARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Immune functions are biological processes that can be affected by malnutrition and are assessed through various nutritional markers.</data>
      <data key="d2">30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b</data>
      <data key="d3">1102</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
