      <data key="d6">1756</data>
      <data key="d7">d7528e1115664e5081fe451ad9a45a56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUJERES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "MUJERES" refers to a demographic group of females categorized by various age groups for health and demographic statistics. This group includes female individuals from different age ranges, specifically those aged 9 years and older, with particular focus on adolescents aged 9-18 years. The data encompasses various aspects of health, including body measurements, nutritional status, and dietary recommendations.

Mujeres are studied in relation to their body mass index (IMC) and are assessed for potential malnutrition, especially among those who are pregnant or lactating. Specific dietary guidelines are provided for females aged 9-18 years, addressing their unique nutritional needs. Additionally, women aged 10 years and older are categorized for dietary intake recommendations, with further breakdowns into age groups: 9-13 years, 14-18 years, 19-30 years, 31-50 years, 51-70 years, and those over 70 years.

The data also highlights that women aged 60-69 and older have specific dietary recommendations, particularly concerning Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; and other essential nutrients. Furthermore, it is noted that women are more frequently affected by certain health conditions, such as adrenal carcinoma, and are at a higher risk for iron deficiency, particularly during adolescence, especially in cases of heavy menstrual bleeding.

Overall, the descriptions collectively emphasize the importance of understanding the health and nutritional needs of mujeres across different life stages, as well as the specific health risks they may face.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7,4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,51b86280e7cb04c3479a556d4028df28,5378bfd93e0d839bd2292cf3a82ecff6,6c65beaf6ed5575b0945052270630136,72ed1fffc10ea163a92b5f1a7b972732,8eb2b7021402eb440fe88889b78c2785,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,a2675f78609440ca1162c24997360929,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,dad52b0e2f29edbe1c7e7e1fdee1d7cc,efbbfb33c127e16f4f9013683aff2c5f,f96dd2fbe3cd9aa6516522de8ed33145</data>
