      <data key="d6">1772</data>
      <data key="d7">9f1927d96b5b4180aebb9055df2ea560</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACRONUTRIENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Macronutrients are essential nutrients required in large amounts for energy and bodily functions, encompassing carbohydrates, proteins, and fats. They play a crucial role in dietary planning for various health conditions, including cystic fibrosis and diabetes management. For patients with cystic fibrosis, specific recommendations regarding macronutrient intake are vital to support their unique nutritional needs. In the context of diabetes, careful management of macronutrients is necessary to maintain optimal health, as their balance can significantly impact blood sugar levels. Additionally, macronutrients are important for energy and growth, particularly in discussions surrounding frailty, where their distribution in the diet is critical. Overall, macronutrients are modified in various diets to achieve specific health goals, highlighting their significance in nutritional planning and management across different health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6,1f2b31f5a0bba00ecee5e3a8fb2c83ea,27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2,bfe875ea294b9a390193b5de532ff71b,e2304aa7e992d9e26558aab3c807b51d,f6135205f57ce2216ab62038ac34a2bb</data>
      <data key="d3">870</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">1773</data>
      <data key="d7">98f45a5eee9b41f7ab31af401913938b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WATER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Water needs are discussed as a critical component of nutritional requirements for hospitalized patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">bfe875ea294b9a390193b5de532ff71b</data>
