      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">1781</data>
      <data key="d7">ab19cadebcd64542a1c174b60e42c1b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA ORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DIETA ORAL refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after undergoing metabolic surgery, although some individuals may encounter complications that hinder this process. It is recognized as the preferred method of nutritional support for hospitalized patients, as it aims to fulfill their energy and nutrient requirements through food intake. Additionally, an oral diet is essential for patients with liver diseases, helping them maintain adequate nutrition. However, it is important to note that the intake of food and drink by mouth can also trigger the onset of ascitis quilosa in certain patients. Overall, DIETA ORAL encompasses the dietary practices that are vital for recovery and health maintenance in various patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,93ddfb3a9423ac76f9303638f6465d25,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
