    <node id="GASTO ENERG&#201;TICO TOTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "GASTO ENERG&#201;TICO TOTAL" (Total Energy Expenditure, TEE) refers to the total amount of energy that an individual uses in a day. This includes several components: the basal metabolic rate (the energy required for basic physiological functions at rest), the thermic effect of food (the energy expended during digestion and absorption of food), and energy used during physical activity. 

For instance, it has been specifically noted that a 75-year-old male requires approximately 1628 kcal per day to meet his total energy needs. In clinical settings, the total energy expenditure is particularly important for dietary planning, especially for patients with specific health conditions such as cystic fibrosis and cancer. In these cases, the total energy expenditure may be lower than expected due to the unique metabolic demands and stress factors associated with their conditions. 

Overall, the calculation of total energy expenditure is essential for determining the energy requirements of various individuals, including hospitalized patients, as it helps tailor dietary plans to their specific activity levels and health needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21,79dc467f42c611bc9f285c95a6c6ff62,93ddfb3a9423ac76f9303638f6465d25,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56</data>
