    <node id="KONDRUP J">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kondrup J is a prominent researcher specializing in nutrition, particularly in the context of end-stage liver disease. He is recognized for his significant contributions to the field, including the development of nutritional risk screening methods. Kondrup J is notably associated with the ESPEN (European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism) guidelines, having authored several key documents related to nutrition screening and support for liver disease. His work includes contributions to the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in liver disease and the NRS 2002 method, which is a widely used tool for assessing nutritional risk. Through his research and guidelines, Kondrup J has played a crucial role in advancing the understanding and management of nutritional needs in patients with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,2f5d9123a78d23b1bc3d9f06d7a53d78,7d1eed82db6d0ad62418f3f965316c39,a700a2e14ec1a75902455bcb005e1434,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
