    </node>
    <node id="APARATO DIGESTIVO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The digestive system is the anatomical structure involved in the process of digestion and nutrient absorption, which is relevant in the context of enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1858</data>
      <data key="d7">d2a24c350d624dca8e24c822b35855ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPORESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiporexia refers to a reduced appetite, which can lead to the need for enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1859</data>
      <data key="d7">2150363ef7ad46aeb0abf30f3ed62772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAQUEXIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cachexia is a complex metabolic syndrome associated with various underlying diseases, particularly cancer. It is characterized by significant involuntary weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and, in some cases, fat loss. This syndrome is not fully reversible through nutritional supplementation, making it a critical concern in the management of patients with chronic illnesses, especially in older adults and those with advanced cancer, such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas.

Cachexia often leads to malnutrition and can severely impact the quality of life of affected individuals. It is frequently observed in patients with conditions like MNGIE, cirrhosis, and respiratory diseases, where severe digestive symptoms or chronic illness contribute to the syndrome. The condition is marked by symptoms such as anorexia and fatigue, and it may necessitate enteral nutrition to address the nutritional deficiencies caused by the ongoing muscle and weight loss.

In summary, cachexia is a serious syndrome that combines the involuntary loss of weight and muscle mass, significantly affecting patients' health and prognosis, particularly in advanced stages of cancer and other chronic diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f,b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83,cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1,ce62d279f86b3364fed4e121ad2d5e1f,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91,f0d279ccc92a98dc953edafb1080630b</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">1860</data>
      <data key="d7">1555da7df3e040ffa48c5ed7a0bca37a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#237;stulas are abnormal connections between organs that can lead to complications in nutrition, potentially causing nutrient loss and affecting the patient's overall nutritional status. These abnormal connections may necessitate enteral feeding to ensure adequate nutrient intake. In certain cases, f&#237;stulas can benefit from enteral feeding if the access route is appropriately adjusted to accommodate the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1861</data>
      <data key="d7">606e3ffad470423fba8970b1ba4e973c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VENTILACI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VENTILACI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA is a medical intervention that provides mechanical support for breathing in patients who are unable to breathe adequately on their own. This method is particularly important for individuals experiencing respiratory failure, as it assists or replaces spontaneous breathing. In certain cases, patients undergoing mechanical ventilation may also require enteral nutrition due to their inability to eat orally. This is especially relevant for premature newborns, who may be affected by their reliance on mechanical ventilation, impacting their capacity to receive enteral nutrition. Overall, VENTILACI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA serves as a critical support system for both respiration and nutritional needs in vulnerable patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1862</data>
      <data key="d7">5e1fb973111a4da0b35ba9261ec44eca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPEREMESIS GRAVIDICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperemesis gravidarum is a severe form of nausea and vomiting during pregnancy that can lead to the need for enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1863</data>
      <data key="d7">cc84b18a1bb5456f98df87895854d728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESECCIONES PARCIALES DE INTESTINO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Partial resections of the intestine can affect nutrient absorption and may require enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1864</data>
      <data key="d7">a2533d87b296445583773e31589a4bc7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROMES DE MALABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malabsorption syndromes are conditions that hinder the absorption of nutrients from food, which can lead to deficiencies in essential vitamins, including vitamin E. These syndromes often necessitate enteral nutrition to ensure that individuals receive adequate nutrients despite their impaired absorption capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83,c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1865</data>
      <data key="d7">8a3e40ac3bd54b018d399a0dc68ec59b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL GRAVE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL GRAVE," or severe inflammatory bowel disease, is a condition that can necessitate enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake in patients experiencing severe symptoms. This disease can result in significant nutritional deficiencies, highlighting the importance of enteral nutrition as a critical intervention for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1866</data>
      <data key="d7">b732e32e67cb4bb7a7ddeae111a99987</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"OBSTRUCCI&#211;N INTESTINAL" refers to a medical condition characterized by a blockage that prevents food or liquid from passing through the small or large intestine. This blockage complicates nutritional treatment and can hinder normal food intake, often necessitating enteral nutrition. However, in some cases, intestinal obstruction may contraindicate enteral nutrition, requiring alternative approaches such as parenteral nutrition. This condition is particularly relevant in patients with cancer, as it can significantly impede their ability to consume adequate food. Intestinal obstruction is noted to be the second most frequent indication for nutritional support, accounting for 25.6% of cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83,efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1867</data>
      <data key="d7">042cd2394b20456cb95e3385ed44ae53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERFORACI&#211;N GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrointestinal perforation is a serious condition that can complicate nutrition and may require enteral feeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1868</data>
      <data key="d7">abf1c7c739ef415ebaf88be5b2d40b99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMORRAGIA GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrointestinal bleeding is a condition that can lead to the need for enteral nutrition due to the inability to eat.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1869</data>
      <data key="d7">0053c9f9d5684b1d99358b4d39f11a90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISQUEMIA MESENT&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mesenteric ischemia is a condition that can affect blood flow to the intestines, complicating nutrition and potentially requiring enteral feeding.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">bd297992bd38c0b110dd5f0cae141f83</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1870</data>
      <data key="d7">e50d5fbc9e7c4ac19e2abd9f3418202a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDAS NASOENTERALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las sondas nasoenterales son dispositivos m&#233;dicos utilizados en pacientes con enfermedades que afectan al est&#243;mago y requieren soporte nutricional a largo plazo.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa99de2530170165c9ac9333021210e3</data>
      <data key="d3">1193</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1871</data>
      <data key="d7">c4a8db15b9a247c49ae6680807bc8616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTROSTOM&#205;A ENDOSC&#211;PICA PERCUT&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrostom&#237;a Endosc&#243;pica Percut&#225;nea (GEP), also known as Percutaneous Endoscopic Gastrostomy (PEG), is a medical procedure designed to create an opening in the stomach to facilitate nutritional support for patients who are unable to eat normally. This procedure is particularly indicated for long-term enteral nutrition, especially when nutritional support is required for more than 4-6 weeks. It allows for the placement of a feeding tube directly into the stomach, enabling patients to receive necessary nutrients at home. The impact of gastrostomy on quality of life has been evaluated, highlighting its importance in providing essential care for individuals with feeding difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721,59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,60a2803170af3c20448ef70091bdfadd,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,aa99de2530170165c9ac9333021210e3,e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87,f087e20586f6b263059597e194a04993</data>
      <data key="d3">1194</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">1872</data>
      <data key="d7">bb97d6b63e7449b1b233cafad87dd8ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A, also known as jejunostomy, is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the jejunum for the purpose of enteral feeding. This procedure is typically employed when oral intake is not possible or when access through the stomach is not feasible, such as in cases of severe gastroesophageal reflux or gastroparesis that cannot be controlled. The jejunostomy allows for the placement of a feeding tube directly into the jejunum, providing nutritional support to patients who require enteral nutrition. It is particularly useful in situations where the stomach is not functional or when gastrostomy is not a viable option. Overall, YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A serves as a critical intervention for patients needing nutritional assistance when traditional feeding methods are inadequate.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9,0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,395385fad73fd5b7ed9eda114b482624,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,7c43869fff0960219e47d176597b35b8,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,aa99de2530170165c9ac9333021210e3,c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1149</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">1873</data>
      <data key="d7">4a42e936edd5480b9ccd8acd0f3cb1f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SILICONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La silicona es otro material utilizado en la fabricaci&#243;n de sondas de nutrici&#243;n, apreciado por su resistencia y durabilidad.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa99de2530170165c9ac9333021210e3</data>
