    <node id="ENCEFALOPAT&#205;A HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ENCEFALOPAT&#205;A HEP&#193;TICA, or hepatic encephalopathy, is a serious liver condition characterized by a decline in brain function due to severe liver disease. This neuropsychiatric syndrome manifests as cognitive dysfunction and altered mental status, significantly impacting the patient's overall health. The condition often necessitates specific dietary interventions and nutritional support, as nutrition can play a crucial role in its management. Hepatic encephalopathy can develop in patients with liver disease, highlighting the importance of monitoring and addressing nutritional needs to mitigate its effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,aea37ea74c52c952285b3ae7db228572,c55f34a09dbf07224c85384f08173e27,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">1880</data>
      <data key="d7">d782ddd7ec9b4fbfba5db2cb02b7d0fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISTR&#201;S RESPIRATORIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DISTR&#201;S RESPIRATORIO refers to a respiratory condition that often necessitates specialized nutritional support. This condition is frequently observed in critically ill patients, where respiratory distress can complicate their overall health status. Additionally, in preterm infants, respiratory distress is a significant concern as it can lead to increased energy expenditure and heightened nutritional requirements. Thus, managing DISTR&#201;S RESPIRATORIO involves addressing both the respiratory challenges and the associated nutritional needs of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f965e7f43fe2ea0144b4b16715a04ba,aea37ea74c52c952285b3ae7db228572,e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
