    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N CONTINUA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Continuous feeding method used in enteral nutrition where the patient receives a steady infusion of nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1893</data>
      <data key="d7">3812591b7c50428abe4add922bfea9c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADMINISTRACI&#211;N EN BOLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bolus feeding method in enteral nutrition where a larger amount of nutrients is given at once.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1894</data>
      <data key="d7">4181b478aae54e1298fcfc4efccd1f34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"VALORACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" refers to the comprehensive clinical assessment process that involves evaluating a patient's neurological and volume status, particularly to guide the treatment of hyponatremia. Additionally, this assessment also encompasses the evaluation of the patient's nutritional status. Thus, "VALORACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" serves as a critical tool in understanding both the neurological and nutritional needs of patients, ensuring appropriate and effective treatment strategies are implemented.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec,3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
