    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"COMPLICACIONES" refers to the potential adverse effects and issues that can arise from various medical treatments and conditions. These complications can manifest in several contexts, including the use of feeding tubes, surgical procedures for obesity treatment, and the management of chronic conditions such as diabetes.

In the context of enteral nutrition, complications may include mechanical, gastrointestinal, and metabolic problems, particularly affecting pediatric patients. Specific adverse effects associated with enteral nutrition can involve increased gastric residue and diarrhea. Additionally, complications can arise from parenteral nutrition, such as thrombophlebitis and issues related to an excess of macronutrients.

Surgical procedures, especially those related to obesity treatment, carry their own set of risks, including complications that must be prevented and managed during the postoperative period. Patients with cancer may also experience adverse effects during or after surgical interventions. Furthermore, complications may arise from inadequate nutrition in critically ill patients, necessitating nutritional interventions to address these health issues.

Overall, "COMPLICACIONES" encompasses a wide range of potential health issues that can arise during treatment, highlighting the importance of monitoring and addressing these risks to ensure patient safety and effective care.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,3c6db755168f2fea94b2535a81ce6f58,40fbc53467b8460d1d2d6bcd0d6dbf2a,5c69bb68f0d23a5aa15fa31301aa13c2,6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a,79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,89c28a4a0410d8f4cbbbc0fbdf4b1c40,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,a7baff5fb024c516ea6ae8c236dc945d,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c,c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247,ff844169c2b512733f5bde26e6f1ed32</data>
      <data key="d3">1156</data>
