    <node id="PERFORACI&#211;N ESOF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esophageal perforation is a serious condition where there is a hole in the esophagus, which can lead to severe complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1903</data>
      <data key="d7">fb688be478554f88bbb7540af772c25f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDRONEUMOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hydropneumothorax is a condition where both air and fluid accumulate in the pleural space, often due to injury or disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1904</data>
      <data key="d7">804f41d95ca34e76ae8b1010e80549e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMPIEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Empyema is a collection of pus in the pleural cavity, typically due to infection.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1905</data>
      <data key="d7">d31c6974ed734bf68f8fbabf95415182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULA BRONCOPLEURAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bronchopleural fistula is an abnormal connection between the bronchial tubes and the pleural space, often resulting from disease or injury.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1906</data>
      <data key="d7">5b4c60ab165846fd9b3b7b5a908c2ff8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATON&#205;A G&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ATON&#205;A G&#193;STRICA refers to a condition characterized by the stomach's loss of ability to contract and empty properly. This condition can significantly impact digestion and the intake of food. It is particularly noted to occur in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, where it complicates the digestive process.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1907</data>
      <data key="d7">cbd760f071af453291a4ec311330214d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ILEO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ileus is a condition characterized by a lack of movement in the intestines, leading to a blockage.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1908</data>
      <data key="d7">423306963222457a8e57e507281290be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERGUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERGUCEMIA refers to a condition characterized by elevated blood glucose levels. It can occur in some patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0) and is often associated with diabetes. Hyperglycemia signifies an excess of glucose in the bloodstream, which can lead to various health complications if not managed properly.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d3">1712</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1909</data>
      <data key="d7">a15133d10a7e4dc8a428d9b90ba732eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypoglycemia is a condition where blood sugar levels drop too low, which can be dangerous.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1910</data>
      <data key="d7">9ddcd0e480d04c539f1ac507bba68843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOFOSFATEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipofosfatemia, also known as hypophosphatemia, is a medical condition defined by a serum phosphorus concentration below 2.5 mg/dl. This condition can occur in hospitalized patients and is often asymptomatic; however, it can lead to severe health issues if phosphorus levels drop below 1 mg/dl. Hypophosphatemia is characterized by low phosphate levels in the blood and can arise from various causes, including patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The condition is significant in clinical settings due to its potential complications and the need for appropriate management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,5bb504bf68288cc0ba6a8f0dd9e4c245,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d3">1157</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">1911</data>
      <data key="d7">9703799133ae4f4580e46b2dd34a33a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPOTASEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERPOTASEMIA, also known as hyperkalemia, is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of potassium in the blood. This condition can be particularly critical for patients who are receiving nutritional support, as it poses significant health risks. Hyperkalemia can lead to serious complications, especially affecting heart function, as excess potassium in the bloodstream can disrupt normal cardiac rhythms and potentially result in life-threatening situations.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,814d394c907e59b29a5f0d9e82aed423</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1912</data>
      <data key="d7">3519fd826bc84dfe872c7013b3b29fab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERNATREMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypernatremia is a condition characterized by high sodium levels in the blood, often due to dehydration.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1913</data>
      <data key="d7">d1fb851a4fee4debace9370e03b56092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyponatremia is a medical condition characterized by low sodium concentration in the serum, specifically defined as low sodium levels in the blood. This condition is commonly observed in hospitalized patients, particularly those receiving artificial nutrition, and can also occur in individuals with eating disorders due to fluid imbalances. Hyponatremia can arise from various underlying causes, including medications, hormonal imbalances, heart failure, liver cirrhosis, and excessive water retention often related to antidiuretic hormone (ADH) activity.

The condition can lead to serious health complications, including increased mortality and morbidity, as well as neurological symptoms such as confusion, seizures, and even coma. It is crucial for healthcare providers to manage hyponatremia carefully, as it requires specific treatment strategies. In some cases, it is treated with medications like tolvapt&#225;n. Hyponatremia can be classified into different types based on volume status: hypovolemic, euvolemic, and hypervolemic. Additionally, it may be a potential adverse effect of following a low-sodium diet, and it can also indicate an imbalance in sodium levels in cases of adrenal insufficiency. Overall, hyponatremia is a significant clinical concern that necessitates thorough evaluation and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec,1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108,214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141,2206bb4d5efe2dcf644ee48468ea112c,3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">66</data>
      <data key="d6">1914</data>
      <data key="d7">a546c9cf183f4e28bf56753eb58eb29e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE DUMPING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dumping syndrome, known in Spanish as "s&#237;ndrome de dumping," is a medical condition that can occur following gastric surgery, particularly bariatric procedures. It is characterized by rapid gastric emptying, where food moves too quickly from the stomach into the small intestine. This condition can lead to a variety of symptoms, including gastrointestinal issues such as nausea and diarrhea, as well as hypoglycemia after food intake. The symptoms arise due to the body's inability to properly manage the sudden influx of food into the intestines, resulting in discomfort and other related health effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681d149c863ed06c99b19443f841abd,58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,65e3dfcb7a0c5a2a09a98342c597c020,d10d3648e8642657567d9a619f210ca6,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d,e569eda9506ef1e77080a8120e388963</data>
      <data key="d3">1417</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">1915</data>
      <data key="d7">8874e5c8dd064d56a9b73f0286976d6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SINUSITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sinusitis is an inflammation of the sinuses, commonly resulting from an infection. This condition is characterized by symptoms such as nasal congestion and pain. Additionally, sinusitis can be a potential complication in patients who are undergoing nasogastric feeding, highlighting the importance of monitoring for this condition in such individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1916</data>
      <data key="d7">53ce11a62c2c4a5e88ed7b871fd0eccd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OTITIS MEDIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Otitis media is a common ear infection or inflammation of the middle ear, particularly prevalent in children. It is characterized by symptoms such as ear pain and fever. This condition can often be prevented through breastfeeding, which is believed to provide protective factors that help reduce the risk of developing ear infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,d0a687d823ff2f3d5cb0f20b01d8530e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1917</data>
      <data key="d7">c68de192f55d48418a92895693f59ec8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERITONITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Peritonitis is an inflammation of the peritoneum, the tissue lining the abdominal cavity, which often arises due to infection or injury. This serious condition can complicate surgical procedures and requires urgent medical care. It may develop as a complication from various procedures, such as gastrointestinal endoscopic procedures (GEP), particularly if infections are not detected early. Overall, peritonitis is a critical condition that necessitates prompt attention to prevent severe complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,58e7286e0ab9d6d52b4c70dadb8b001f,b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707</data>
      <data key="d3">1217</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1918</data>
      <data key="d7">53aaf70511d149379711e174415caa55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUP LA FE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HUP La Fe is a hospital that provides guidelines for the administration of medications via enteral feeding tubes.</data>
      <data key="d2">52a0434694f8face489cdb4c8d206a9e,bb6ff0a9ac5248b96f246a39919aa779</data>
