      <data key="d7">3eebc9d6a36c46d38e2a0ce66d6ee832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="B. BALERDI P&#201;REZ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">B. Balerdi P&#233;rez is a medical professional with significant contributions to the field of nutrition and trauma care. He co-authored a chapter on polytraumatism and traumatic brain injury, showcasing his expertise in critical medical conditions. Additionally, he has authored several chapters related to parenteral nutrition, including topics on access routes, nutrition for burn patients, and nutrition in cases of renal insufficiency. His work emphasizes the importance of tailored nutritional strategies in various medical scenarios, particularly in critical care settings. Overall, B. Balerdi P&#233;rez's contributions reflect a deep commitment to advancing knowledge in medical nutrition and trauma management.</data>
      <data key="d2">36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd,cd16cc82ca1357af8c9c1ab73ea55c5a,d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">1928</data>
      <data key="d7">2f357e4f30ee4682b1e0f5ff65e21bbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADMINISTRACI&#211;N DE MEDICAMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The administration of medications in patients with enteral nutrition involves careful management to ensure proper nutrient absorption and patient safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
