    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPERCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n Hipercal&#243;rica is a type of nutritional support that provides a high caloric intake, often used for patients with increased energy needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1930</data>
      <data key="d7">416106c1e2fc4daeac97cefd5a46bb2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N NORMOCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n Normocal&#243;rica refers to a balanced nutritional support that meets the standard caloric needs of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1931</data>
      <data key="d7">51445d12772b4bd8ab7eba28e890adf6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOCAL&#211;RICA refers to a dietary approach characterized by a lower caloric intake, primarily aimed at managing obesity and supporting critically ill patients. This type of nutritional support is specifically designed to prevent negative outcomes associated with overfeeding, such as hyperglycemia and increased infection rates. By providing a controlled caloric intake, NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOCAL&#211;RICA plays a crucial role in weight management and the overall health of individuals requiring dietary intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1932</data>
      <data key="d7">0089eb3196e54739a9a9ac2cdbc55bf3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N HIPERPROTEICA refers to a dietary strategy that emphasizes high protein intake, particularly beneficial for critically ill patients. This approach is recommended for individuals who do not have severe liver or kidney dysfunction, as it aims to avoid the negative consequences associated with overfeeding. Overall, Nutrici&#243;n Hiperproteica serves as a nutritional intervention that can be advantageous for certain medical conditions, focusing on the importance of adequate protein consumption in the management of health.</data>
      <data key="d2">195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1933</data>
      <data key="d7">7cf295be5a524bb79357fb552215b8c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N NORMOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n Normoproteica refers to a standard protein intake that meets the average dietary requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1934</data>
      <data key="d7">36abe7bd49984925be5fb21e3644ef5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n Hipoproteica is a nutritional strategy that limits protein intake, often necessary for patients with specific health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1935</data>
      <data key="d7">63a9bc9a8c1241b4824dcffbbaa439df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP V&#205;A CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NP v&#237;a central is a method of administering nutrition parenteral through a central vein, suitable for patients requiring high osmolarity solutions.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1936</data>
      <data key="d7">b9b94266cb5b4359bd9e12e28b594282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NP v&#237;a perif&#233;rica is a method of administering nutrition parenteral through peripheral veins, with lower osmolarity and limited caloric intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1937</data>
      <data key="d7">7991a9a51f3a4bf58ea02283e149c6a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL HIPOCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral Hipocal&#243;rica is a type of parenteral nutrition that provides fewer calories than required, typically used in short-term treatments or post-operative care.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1938</data>
      <data key="d7">f352cd256ba24522af3f142dda3ddf44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NP Domiciliaria refers to the administration of parenteral nutrition at the patient's home, requiring a suitable family and social environment for proper management.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1939</data>
      <data key="d7">cf86a8db339c48e4ad152a7755ab24c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP CONTINUA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NP Continua is a method of administering parenteral nutrition continuously over 24 hours, often used in hospital settings or for home care patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1940</data>
      <data key="d7">6fdbde59c921498295d116b5f5ac9288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NP C&#205;CLICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NP C&#237;clica is a method of administering parenteral nutrition for less than 24 hours, typically 12-16 hours, used for home care patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1941</data>
      <data key="d7">5ed1d565af1242b7b911a3dbf5453eef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOFLEBITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trombo-flebitis is a medical condition characterized by the inflammation of a vein due to the formation of a blood clot. This condition can arise as a complication during the maintenance of a central venous catheter and is particularly associated with intravenous access, especially in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. It is a common complication linked to the use of peripheral nutrition as well. The presence of a blood clot leads to inflammation in the affected vein, making trombo-flebitis a significant concern in clinical settings where intravenous therapies are employed.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,4ce6342fdfe4419826c1ab2f84c56247,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,f79f02438413f5accef9ac5fbd96f6df</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1942</data>
      <data key="d7">5ced47e5de874ca3aef4136d9fb84c4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTO ESTR&#201;S METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alto estr&#233;s metab&#243;lico refers to a condition where the body's metabolic demands are significantly increased, often necessitating the use of parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1943</data>
      <data key="d7">81fffdc29fe64f0087eea253e74c67f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULAS YEYUNALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#237;stulas yeyunales are abnormal connections in the jejunum that may indicate a relative indication for parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1944</data>
      <data key="d7">9b7c1d73b4314680982e6520649a608a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad inflamatoria refers to a group of conditions characterized by inflammation that may necessitate parenteral nutrition during acute phases, particularly when the digestive tract is not functional. These inflammatory diseases can lead to intestinal malabsorption, which in turn contributes to hypomagnesemia, a condition marked by low levels of magnesium in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1945</data>
      <data key="d7">c4fd2337fcfc46a8bfe339b3387012e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENTERITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enteritis aguda is an acute inflammation of the intestine that may lead to the need for parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1946</data>
      <data key="d7">357132bd2a9c4f53971f1a948c79a5f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;LEO NO QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#237;leo no quir&#250;rgico es una condici&#243;n que puede requerir nutrici&#243;n parenteral si el paciente no puede alimentarse adecuadamente.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1947</data>
      <data key="d7">8bb1287cbe1648709c9c4ad739e0e2b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMOS TERMINALES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los enfermos terminales son pacientes con un pron&#243;stico de vida limitado que pueden no beneficiarse de la nutrici&#243;n parenteral agresiva.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1948</data>
      <data key="d7">58a3bc99df9843ab8dd0ff8dc4685038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#205;A DIGESTIVA NORMOFUNCIONANTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Se refiere a pacientes que tienen un sistema digestivo que funciona correctamente y que no necesitan nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1949</data>
      <data key="d7">4bcbffd282da4a1c9fdc910169bba6ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AYUNO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AYUNO refers to the practice of fasting, which is commonly undertaken by patients before and after surgery to ensure accurate results in diagnostic tests and surgical procedures. This practice of abstaining from food and liquids is crucial for patients undergoing various medical evaluations, including those related to conditions such as hepatic disease and chylothorax, particularly in malnourished individuals. Additionally, AYUNO is associated with dietary strategies, such as the ketogenic diet, where fasting may enhance its effectiveness. Prolonged fasting, whether pre-operative or post-operative, may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to maintain adequate nutrient intake. Furthermore, fasting is recognized as a physiological factor that can influence energy expenditure, especially in pediatric patients, and it is known to stimulate the secretion of growth hormone. Overall, AYUNO encompasses a range of medical and dietary implications, highlighting its significance in both clinical and nutritional contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ebd0c517a3d578a6823dc39797e4da1,1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d3">1028</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">1950</data>
      <data key="d7">12c452e4b353482aac464d1f01fb8d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTR&#201;S METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El estr&#233;s metab&#243;lico puede afectar la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar nutrientes, lo que puede hacer necesaria la nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1951</data>
      <data key="d7">bc49ce50f54247e79741e72a812e1059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECHAZO DE INTERVENCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El rechazo de la intervenci&#243;n por parte del paciente o su representante legal puede influir en la decisi&#243;n de administrar nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1952</data>
      <data key="d7">1b67eb0003ff47f0a7cba55f6c7a1288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMULSIONES LIP&#205;DICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Emulsiones lip&#237;dicas are lipid emulsions utilized in parenteral nutrition to deliver essential fatty acids and calories, thereby preventing complications that may arise from glucose-only nutrition. These emulsions serve as energy substrates without increasing osmolarity, making them suitable for incorporation into parenteral nutrition regimens. Composed of triglycerides, oils, and emulsifiers, emulsiones lip&#237;dicas provide a vital source of energy and essential fatty acids for patients. Their varying compositions can lead to different effects on patients, highlighting the importance of tailored nutritional support in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">40fbc53467b8460d1d2d6bcd0d6dbf2a,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544,c70d301baddcdcdefbba9b024ad4f3c5</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">18</data>
      <data key="d6">1953</data>
      <data key="d7">a7f74842f123472fab5a5f3dd652ea99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA LARGA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA LARGA, or long-chain triglycerides, are a type of fat that plays a significant role in early lipid emulsions used for parenteral nutrition. These triglycerides are derived from soybean oil and are rich in essential fatty acids, making them an important source of nutrition in medical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1954</data>
      <data key="d7">350f409df6804b24bb7dc78ef8d2b9db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS ESENCIALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cidos Grasos Esenciales are vital nutrients that the body cannot synthesize on its own, necessitating their acquisition through diet or supplementation. These essential fatty acids, such as linoleic acid and alpha-linolenic acid, play a crucial role in various bodily functions, including modulating inflammatory responses and improving health outcomes, particularly for individuals with conditions like cystic fibrosis. Their importance in maintaining overall health underscores the need for adequate dietary intake of these necessary fats.</data>
      <data key="d2">0090177678aee58d08471d09d24d2842,60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,c70d301baddcdcdefbba9b024ad4f3c5,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d3">1613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">1955</data>
      <data key="d7">361c037495dc4e2ba034d128407839f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO LINOL&#201;ICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#225;cido linoleico es un &#225;cido graso esencial que debe ser aportado en la dieta y es importante para la salud metab&#243;lica.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">1613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1956</data>
      <data key="d7">e89055534e634202aa3d75906b4d8c9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO ALFA-LINOL&#201;NICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#225;cido alfa-linol&#233;nico es un &#225;cido graso omega-3 esencial que debe ser incluido en la dieta para mantener la salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">1613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1957</data>
      <data key="d7">ae02acfd2ecc4f2a8156dfa62d87a3d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALFA TOCOFEROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alfa tocopherol is a form of Vitamin E that serves as an important antioxidant. It is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition and is also found in lipid emulsions, where it plays a crucial role in preventing peroxidation. This compound is essential for maintaining cellular health and protecting against oxidative stress.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1958</data>
      <data key="d7">d72bacc5a18d4402a3a82e70d671860f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can lead to severe abdominal pain, digestive issues, and nutritional deficiencies. This inflammation can significantly affect digestion, often necessitating enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutritional support for patients. In pediatric patients, pancreatitis can notably increase energy expenditure, presenting additional metabolic challenges. The condition can be acute or chronic and may require medical intervention due to its potential complications, including malnutrition and the need for specialized treatment.

Furthermore, pancreatitis can arise as a serious complication in patients with severe metabolic disorders and has been reported in individuals following a ketogenic diet. It is important to exercise caution in drug use for patients with this condition, as it can lead to further complications. In certain cases, the use of lipid emulsions may be indicated to support nutritional needs. Overall, pancreatitis is a severe condition that demands careful management and monitoring by healthcare professionals.</data>
      <data key="d2">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,75a4b2d504de480eaef247aa682bfd05,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,86aa5f95aae53ab120c5c63eda5486bc,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,bf7fc15e1aac41553dc6586efe68b8cb,c84372864fd2ee7b7ed425b2d597efdb,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d3">1198</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">56</data>
      <data key="d6">1959</data>
      <data key="d7">632844e474264b4295ce177f03c1a825</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITE DE SOJA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El "ACEITE DE SOJA" es un aceite que se deriva de las semillas de soja y se caracteriza por ser una fuente de triglic&#233;ridos de cadena larga, lo que lo hace &#250;til en emulsiones lip&#237;dicas. Adem&#225;s, el aceite de soja es rico en &#225;cidos grasos esenciales, lo que lo convierte en un componente recomendado en la dieta de personas que padecen trastornos de la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n. Sin embargo, en el contexto de la nutrici&#243;n en cuidados cr&#237;ticos, se menciona que el aceite de soja, como fuente de &#225;cidos grasos omega-6, deber&#237;a ser reducido. A pesar de esta recomendaci&#243;n, el aceite de soja sigue siendo utilizado como fuente de l&#237;pidos en la nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">1960</data>
      <data key="d7">6c7da03aea8a4c7d83fdc5fa624fc956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITE DE COCO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El "ACEITE DE COCO" es un tipo de grasa que se caracteriza por su contenido en triglic&#233;ridos de cadena media (TCM), los cuales se metabolizan r&#225;pidamente y son utilizados en emulsiones lip&#237;dicas. Este aceite contiene proporciones significativas de &#225;cidos grasos saturados de cadena media, que tienen un efecto diferente en el organismo en comparaci&#243;n con los &#225;cidos grasos de cadena larga. Adem&#225;s, el aceite de coco puede ser beneficioso en la dieta de personas que padecen trastornos de la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n, ya que su composici&#243;n permite una utilizaci&#243;n m&#225;s eficiente de los l&#237;pidos.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e</data>
      <data key="d3">648</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">1961</data>
      <data key="d7">4d0331986caa4fac89dd7a99a6690f04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LECITINA DE HUEVO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La lecitina de huevo es un emulgente utilizado para estabilizar emulsiones lip&#237;dicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1962</data>
      <data key="d7">0b6b7e56ac624f89835ad7aa25cccfed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLICEROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glicerol, also known as glycerin, is a three-carbon molecule that plays a significant role in various biological and chemical processes. It is commonly used as an isotonizing agent in the formulation of lipid emulsions, where it helps maintain the appropriate osmolarity. Additionally, glicerol can be converted into glucose through the process of gluconeogenesis, highlighting its importance in energy metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">1963</data>
      <data key="d7">f7477be4821446c78ff48479aacf8388</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLEATO S&#211;DICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El oleato s&#243;dico es un estabilizante que se utiliza en emulsiones lip&#237;dicas para mejorar su estabilidad.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1964</data>
      <data key="d7">9841bc70922d4b1b92dc48231bca65ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINAS K">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las vitaminas K son nutrientes que se encuentran en las emulsiones lip&#237;dicas y son esenciales para la coagulaci&#243;n sangu&#237;nea.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1965</data>
      <data key="d7">7250d4ac7b364b6cb36ad007c41122c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINAS E">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las vitaminas E son antioxidantes que se encuentran en las emulsiones lip&#237;dicas y ayudan a proteger las c&#233;lulas del da&#241;o oxidativo.</data>
      <data key="d2">86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842</data>
      <data key="d3">649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1966</data>
      <data key="d7">891a5fa5cad9467fbd310e5d77aa14f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;SFORO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#243;sforo, or phosphorus, is an essential mineral that plays a critical role in various biological functions, representing approximately 1% of the body's weight. It is vital for the formation of bones and teeth, energy production, and overall metabolism. F&#243;sforo is particularly important in dietary recommendations for children and is included in parenteral nutrition, where its levels must be adjusted based on individual patient needs.

In the context of health, f&#243;sforo is crucial for bone health and cellular function, but its intake must be carefully controlled, especially in patients with chronic kidney disease or those undergoing dialysis, as excessive phosphorus can lead to complications such as decreased calcium absorption and cardiovascular risks. Additionally, f&#243;sforo levels can be affected by vitamin D deficiency and the action of parathyroid hormone (PTH).

F&#243;sforo can also be deficient in specific diets, such as the ketogenic diet, where supplementation may be necessary to optimize bone mineralization. In pediatric patients, phosphorus supplementation is often recommended, with dosages tailored to their age. Furthermore, elevated phosphorus levels in the blood can pose significant health risks, particularly in individuals with chronic kidney disease.

Overall, f&#243;sforo is a vital mineral that must be included in nutritional plans, with careful monitoring and adjustment to ensure optimal health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,1592143354d1ef792f8618ec03a32a16,1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,afe0f4f37815c175f0faff06eb24a256,b789dfd7a5aa36fac33c5c881a1a4981,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">1967</data>
      <data key="d7">88d30f1f1fbc4a14a06e31ddd5ee9061</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINO ACIDS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Amino acids are essential nutrients that serve as the building blocks of proteins, playing a crucial role in protein synthesis and overall health. They are vital for various bodily functions, including muscle synthesis, particularly in patients requiring nutritional support. Additionally, amino acids are important in the nutritional management of liver disease and can be released from muscle during metabolic processes, contributing to the body's energy supply. Their potential benefits in metabolic conditions have been explored, although results for Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI) have not been satisfactory. Overall, amino acids are integral to maintaining health and supporting various physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">24cc40d6e3b225945cd4d8c2484632e4,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,a66b01654a2f495559fd1a24efc0e64e,cf34fdea5374cdee9a8be8f93c63e830,ec94449c6ffff75664588262301de0a6</data>
      <data key="d3">1230</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">1968</data>
      <data key="d7">b6d729c820b24b0fa1046adcc625afb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NITROGEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen is a key component in amino acids and is essential for maintaining a proper balance in protein intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">cf34fdea5374cdee9a8be8f93c63e830</data>
      <data key="d3">1230</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">1969</data>
      <data key="d7">a87ce5487bbb4ccfa97ae6e712b93d01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTAMINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glutamine is a conditionally essential amino acid that plays a critical role in various metabolic processes, particularly during catabolic states such as critical illness, surgery, and trauma. It serves as a primary energy source for various cells, including intestinal epithelial cells, and is frequently used in nutritional support for patients undergoing surgery or suffering from trauma. 

In clinical settings, glutamine is often supplemented in both parenteral and enteral nutrition to support recovery, immune function, and gut health, especially in critically ill patients, burn victims, and those undergoing chemotherapy or transplantation. It is also being studied for its potential benefits in patients with severe pancreatitis and is considered for supplementation in the nutritional management of patients with brain injuries and trauma.

Despite its widespread use, the efficacy of glutamine supplementation in critically ill patients remains debated, with current guidelines not recommending its addition due to a lack of demonstrated benefits. However, it is noted that glutamine may improve nutritional status and response in patients with severe pancreatic diseases and can help reduce infections and complications in surgical patients, particularly those undergoing abdominal surgeries. 

Overall, glutamine is recognized for its importance in supporting recovery and metabolic needs in various clinical contexts, although its use should be carefully considered based on individual patient circumstances and current clinical guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,29cd22ec41c1cb5160d9987958d6ae16,396dda5c9597828f0749f963f42142b4,3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3,6efaddddefe1cf5ab78825e1d8c53cab,7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97,8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a,cf34fdea5374cdee9a8be8f93c63e830,eadd983c9f28c11a1c279e4b923351cd,ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29,fb24bf4c9fcf60bbc1dd56cd60ba0a47</data>
      <data key="d3">1234</data>
