    <node id="FLUIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FLUIDOS refers to essential liquids provided to patients to maintain hydration and electrolyte balance, particularly for those receiving nutritional support. In the context of pediatric nutrition, especially for infants, fluid intake is crucial for proper hydration. Recommendations for fluid intake vary based on age and weight, highlighting the importance of adjusting fluid requirements to ensure effective minimum nutritional support. Overall, FLUIDOS encompasses the necessary liquid intake that is vital for maintaining health and well-being in various patient populations.</data>
