    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL (NP)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL (NP) is a method of nutritional support that involves the intravenous administration of nutrients, including electrolytes and vitamins, to patients who are unable to eat or absorb food through their digestive tract. This approach is utilized when enteral nutrition is either insufficient or contraindicated, particularly in cases such as abdominal injuries or other medical complications. NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is essential for providing adequate nutrition to patients who cannot be nourished through traditional oral means.</data>
      <data key="d2">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,6feef8e192d7b29998dea0f23077a021,d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
