    <node id="OLIGOELEMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">OLIGOELEMENTOS refers to trace elements that are essential minerals required in small quantities for the growth and development of pediatric patients, particularly those receiving parenteral nutrition. These trace elements, which include important nutrients like zinc and selenium, play a crucial role in various bodily functions, including brain metabolism and cognitive function. The administration of oligoelementos is recommended by the American Medical Association, and their levels must be carefully controlled to prevent deficiencies, especially in vulnerable populations such as preterm infants and patients with renal failure. Oligoelementos are typically included in medical formulations and nutritional products to support the health of these patients, with a standard contribution of 1 ml in nutritional solutions. Overall, oligoelementos are vital for maintaining health and preventing complications in pediatric patients requiring specialized nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817,64417661dbb019f8f4ceb9fcc2fbdaa6,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,a6e7937ce59bfc2b38e9ed2acf3e991c,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,fa356397bc52582bdbbd1868639feec9</data>
