    <node id="FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fosfato, or phosphate, is a vital mineral that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes, particularly in bone health and energy production. It is essential for the mineralization of bones, contributing to the formation and crystallization of bone tissue. A deficiency in phosphate can lead to conditions such as osteomalacia and rickets, highlighting its importance in maintaining skeletal integrity.

In the context of nutrition, phosphate is a key component of parenteral nutrition solutions, which are used to provide essential nutrients to individuals who cannot consume food orally. It is necessary for energy transfer within the body and must be administered in daily amounts ranging from 20 to 40 mmol, according to recommended dietary guidelines. However, careful management of phosphate levels is crucial, as it is an essential electrolyte that supports both energy production and overall bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c,cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2,d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
