    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA K">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VITAMINA K, also known as Vitamin K, is an essential fat-soluble nutrient crucial for various bodily functions, particularly blood clotting and bone metabolism. It is produced by intestinal bacteria and is found in various foods, especially green leafy vegetables and some animal products. This vitamin plays a key role in the activation of several blood coagulation factors, making it vital for preventing hemorrhagic diseases, particularly in newborns, for whom it is recommended to be administered intramuscularly at birth to prevent transient deficiencies in coagulation factors.

In patients with celiac disease, Vitamin K deficiency can occur, leading to increased risk of hemorrhagic conditions. Additionally, certain medications can affect Vitamin K levels, resulting in increased requirements for this nutrient. It is important to note that there are no established upper limits for Vitamin K due to a lack of data on adverse effects. However, it can antagonize the therapeutic action of oral anticoagulants when present in enteral nutrition.

Vitamin K is also recommended for patients with coagulation issues to improve blood clotting before medical procedures. In cases of cholestasis, specific recommendations for supplementation are made to ensure adequate levels. Regular administration of Vitamin K is advised, typically 1-2 times a week, as it is not included in most commercial preparations. Overall, Vitamin K is a critical nutrient for maintaining health, particularly in relation to blood coagulation and bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d9c11c44c3cf4e1e3148949cc0a4096,20491afa9a4770e93e6cff9034f8b0f0,2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,5eb14e2cbec104d89ad73e2ac968b7fd,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233,b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa,bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
