    <node id="VITAMINA B1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VITAMINA B1, also known as Thiamine, is an essential water-soluble nutrient that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism. It is particularly important for converting carbohydrates into energy, making it a vital component of nutritional recommendations for various populations, including patients on nutritional support and infants. The recommended daily intake of Vitamin B1 is 3 mg, and it is available in various forms, such as Benerva 100 mg/ml and Benerva 300 mg. Due to its significance in maintaining health, Vitamin B1 is advised for administration to enhance overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,3202b451a4ece0fc376bd2899a412bef,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,e510500bd5a5f16a0bf0353cfdb79c13,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
      <data key="d3">610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">1999</data>
      <data key="d7">c8e8e583cb054e819a431c3990f30ac4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B2, also known as Riboflavin, is an essential water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy production and cellular function. It is particularly important in the dietary recommendations for infants, where it is advised to be administered in quantities of 3.6 mg according to daily vitamin recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
