      <data key="d6">2000</data>
      <data key="d7">5c909ecb0d76492f8850bce4f343de3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIACINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NIACINA, tambi&#233;n conocida como vitamina B&#8323;, es un nutriente esencial que desempe&#241;a un papel crucial como coenzima en diversos procesos metab&#243;licos. Esta vitamina soluble en agua es fundamental para la conversi&#243;n de los alimentos en energ&#237;a y se incluye com&#250;nmente en la composici&#243;n de multivitaminas para la nutrici&#243;n parenteral. La niacina es importante no solo para el metabolismo energ&#233;tico, sino tambi&#233;n para la reparaci&#243;n del ADN. Se encuentra en alimentos como la carne, las patatas y el pan. La deficiencia de niacina puede provocar s&#237;ntomas que se asemejan a los del s&#237;ndrome carcinoide. Seg&#250;n las recomendaciones diarias de vitaminas, se sugiere una ingesta de 40 mg de niacina.</data>
      <data key="d2">26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d3">608</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2001</data>
      <data key="d7">4308b81c5b5c4f529365e50e0c07e246</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B6">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VITAMINA B6, also known as Pyridoxine, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It is essential for protein metabolism, amino acid metabolism, and neurotransmitter synthesis, making it vital for brain development and function. The vitamin is included in nutritional guidelines for infants, highlighting its importance during early growth stages. 

Deficiency in Vitamin B6 can lead to health issues, such as hypomagnesemia, as it influences magnesium metabolism. Additionally, certain medications, like isoniazid, can contribute to Vitamin B6 deficiency. The recommended daily intake of Vitamin B6 is approximately 4 mg, and it is commonly found in foods such as meats, fish, eggs, and whole grains. For supplementation, Vitamin B6 is available in various forms, including Benad&#243;n 300 mg, which can be administered in both tablet and injectable forms.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,3202b451a4ece0fc376bd2899a412bef,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
