      <data key="d6">2007</data>
      <data key="d7">7ce73be80f864813b852aaf1846b7856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZINC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Zinc is an essential trace element and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, including immune response, protein synthesis, wound healing, and cognitive development. It is particularly important for the growth and development of children and is often included in infant formulas to support immune function and overall health. The recommended daily intake of zinc varies by age and gender, with general guidelines suggesting a daily intake of 10-20 mg for adults and specific recommendations for pediatric patients.

Zinc deficiency is frequently observed in various health conditions, including chronic liver disease, cirrhosis, inflammatory bowel disease, and after biliopancreatic diversion surgeries. It is also common in patients with eating disorders, cystic fibrosis, and those undergoing parenteral nutrition. Deficiencies can lead to significant health issues, such as impaired wound healing, immune dysfunction, and alterations in taste perception. In critically ill patients, zinc supplementation is recommended to support recovery, and it is also suggested for children experiencing acute diarrhea, as per WHO and UNICEF guidelines.

Zinc is involved in numerous biological processes, including DNA replication and transcription, and it helps reduce infections, particularly in older adults. While zinc is crucial for health, excessive levels can contribute to oxidative stress and neurodegeneration. Therefore, monitoring zinc levels is important, especially in patients with specific health conditions or those at risk of deficiency. Zinc supplements are available in various forms, including capsules and tablets, to help individuals meet their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">125acd19edb76fa23986de56fc2517e8,12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7,2e4409d82bf1cb293a2df7fc1a8cc9e7,2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1,3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92,46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,86a4647fb1fa580f7b72aa4833965ecb,89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,8f2e38ed25a683975b314e8e56721ad6,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1,a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,b1d4c144806ac7875725e152251868f3,bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2,bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9,c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b,c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119,cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2,d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723,d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550,d77e49d1dba3a67fbc9cf58911dc2478,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a,ea920d08266b329db73fb7b804bbb9ce,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef,fa356397bc52582bdbbd1868639feec9</data>
