    <node id="MANGANESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Manganeso, o mangan&#233;s, es un micronutriente esencial y un oligoelemento que desempe&#241;a un papel crucial en el metabolismo, la formaci&#243;n de huesos, la coagulaci&#243;n sangu&#237;nea y la reducci&#243;n de la inflamaci&#243;n. Su deficiencia, aunque poco com&#250;n, puede tener implicaciones cl&#237;nicas significativas, especialmente en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Este mineral se encuentra en alimentos como el arroz y los frutos secos, y est&#225; vinculado a la acci&#243;n antioxidante.

Es importante tener en cuenta que, aunque el manganeso es esencial para la salud, su administraci&#243;n en dosis elevadas puede resultar t&#243;xica, afectando negativamente al h&#237;gado y al sistema nervioso central. Por lo tanto, se recomienda un consumo controlado, con niveles de ingesta diaria sugeridos que oscilan entre 0.15 y 0.8 mg, especialmente en pacientes pedi&#225;tricos y en ciertas condiciones m&#233;dicas. En resumen, el manganeso es un mineral vital que contribuye a diversas funciones biol&#243;gicas, pero debe ser consumido con precauci&#243;n para evitar efectos adversos.</data>
      <data key="d2">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,f43e3958f11ed24b0a02f60a2993309a</data>
      <data key="d3">599</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">2011</data>
      <data key="d7">46139aff78b642ed93f332dbe0997924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COBALTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cobalto, also known as cobalt, is a trace element that plays a crucial role in the formation of vitamin B12, which is essential for the production of red blood cells. It is important to administer cobalt in specific dosages, typically ranging from 0.002 to 0.005 mg, in accordance with daily recommendations for trace elements.</data>
      <data key="d2">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2012</data>
      <data key="d7">718492166a414bf9b0076512f06e2a12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SODIO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Sodio, or sodium, is an essential electrolyte that plays a critical role in maintaining fluid balance and is vital for proper muscle and nerve function. It is necessary for various bodily functions, including hydration, especially during exercise, and is crucial in the nutrition of newborns to prevent complications. In pediatric nutrition, specific daily requirements for sodium must be adhered to, particularly for patients receiving parenteral nutrition, where sodium levels need to be monitored and supplemented appropriately.

Sodio is also significant in dietary contexts, as it helps regulate the balance of fluids in the body and can affect the reabsorption of lithium in the kidneys. However, excessive sodium intake is associated with health issues such as hypertension and cardiovascular problems, leading to recommendations for limiting sodium consumption. Dietary guidelines suggest that sodium intake should be restricted to below 3.5 g/day to reduce the risk of kidney stones and manage blood pressure, particularly in individuals with diabetes or fluid retention.

Sodio is present in various foods, including Galleta Maria, where it contributes to flavor and preservation. It is important to note that sodium levels can be affected in patients with conditions like renal insufficiency, cor pulmonale, and respiratory failure, necessitating careful management of sodium intake. Normal sodium levels in the body typically range between 135 and 145 mEq/l, and its interaction with other minerals, such as magnesium, further underscores the need for balanced dietary intake. Overall, while sodium is a crucial nutrient, its consumption must be carefully managed to promote health and prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,11662a6f83b8217976d8c9c5d33fe7fd,15ffbfba2decfecb69a26bcb1e4bd898,29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a,3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab,364aa13581a973c2e55c25191bad27cc,3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb,633a3a90a82e02d05096b361ddba3ad7,66b7c4d336056f832579dc20ffb92992,66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6,b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce,cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2,cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723,d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194,f1635e39e27702010af8222ea31360d6,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
