    <node id="SELENIO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SELENIO, or selenium, is an essential trace mineral and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, particularly in antioxidant defense and thyroid function. It is recommended as a supplement for patients, with a suggested daily intake of 100 mg, although specific dosage recommendations may vary based on factors such as age and gender. Selenium is known for its antioxidant properties, which help protect against free radicals, and it is a cofactor for the enzyme glutathione peroxidase, crucial for maintaining cellular health.

Deficiency in selenium has been associated with several health issues, including coronary pathology, immunosuppression, and certain neoplasias. In particular, its deficiency can lead to reversible myocardiopathy and irreversible encephalitis in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, selenium deficiency is linked to the development of goiter due to its role in thyroid hormone synthesis. While selenium is generally rare in deficiency, it can be particularly low in patients with chronic liver disease, those undergoing prolonged dialysis, and individuals who have had certain surgeries.

Selenium supplementation is advised with caution, especially in patients with renal insufficiency, and its use in oncology is not sufficiently supported by evidence. It has been suggested as a protective factor against cardiovascular diseases and cancer due to its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties. Regular monitoring of selenium levels in the blood is recommended for individuals on restricted diets or those not supplementing regularly. Overall, selenium is a vital micronutrient that contributes significantly to metabolic processes and immune health.</data>
      <data key="d2">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,14299e85574ef5c76c7164e2c4d20a53,2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9,3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02,5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,b1d4c144806ac7875725e152251868f3,bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9,d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09,f43e3958f11ed24b0a02f60a2993309a</data>
