      <data key="d7">53af1e297f614ac1a4771184e9e0705b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insuficiencia hep&#225;tica, or hepatic insufficiency, is a severe medical condition characterized by the liver's inability to perform its normal functions. This condition necessitates urgent medical care and careful management of various dietary factors. Specifically, individuals with hepatic insufficiency require specific dietary adjustments, including limited intake of copper and manganese, as well as careful management of lipid intake, particularly in cases involving parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, this condition can significantly impact the metabolism of nutrients, especially in newborns, highlighting the critical nature of liver function in overall nutritional status and metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,82adde9844cf0b1ccd052f91b304fb6e,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">659</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2020</data>
      <data key="d7">e0392d0c12b24cd093d1dace9763c963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLSTASIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COLSTASIS is a medical condition characterized by reduced bile flow, which can lead to various complications. This condition necessitates dietary modifications, specifically limiting the intake of copper and manganese to manage its effects. Additionally, cholestasis can occur in patients who are receiving prolonged parenteral nutrition, where the flow of bile is either reduced or completely blocked.</data>
      <data key="d2">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155</data>
      <data key="d3">586</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2021</data>
      <data key="d7">0c51522c3e014978a4fa81545f32ef39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TIAMINA, also known as Thiamine or Vitamin B1, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism, particularly in the conversion of carbohydrates into energy. It is included in parenteral nutrition formulations, such as Infuvite Pedi&#225;trico, to support metabolic processes and prevent complications in patients at risk during the first week of nutritional therapy. Thiamine is essential for nerve function and is found in various food sources, including cereals, potatoes, and pork.

Deficiency in Thiamine can lead to serious health issues, such as Wernicke's encephalopathy, particularly in patients who have undergone certain surgeries or those with alcohol-related liver disease. Additionally, patients on dialysis may require increased intake of Thiamine. While it is sometimes considered for supplementation in patients with cognitive decline, the benefits of such supplementation remain debated. Thiamine is also recommended as a supplement for all forms of Maple Syrup Urine Disease to improve patient outcomes. Notably, there are no established upper limits for Thiamine intake due to a lack of data on adverse effects. Overall, Thiamine is a vital nutrient that is part of the B-complex vitamins and is critical for maintaining energy metabolism and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,91c1a9b0c0d7cb718d7711ef7384a142,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">2022</data>
      <data key="d7">0cffd564a2034f498e72465fd16681c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" refers to long-term health conditions that significantly impact an individual's nutritional status and overall health. These chronic diseases, which include diabetes, obesity, cardiovascular diseases, and cancer, are major contributors to mortality and disability on a global scale. They are often associated with lifestyle and dietary factors, highlighting the importance of nutrition in their management. In particular, chronic diseases can lead to complications such as chronic kidney disease and phosphorus imbalance. Additionally, pediatric patients with chronic diseases may require specialized nutritional support and management to address their unique health needs. Overall, "ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" encompasses a range of health issues that necessitate careful consideration of dietary habits and nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074,b6c8d5ff1536806d6512fb9d1af1e6db,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1164</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">2023</data>
      <data key="d7">cc1a19c3fe784764a1e78b2bfdf7814c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCOHOLISMO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcoholism, known as "alcoholismo" in Spanish, is a chronic disease characterized by an inability to control or stop drinking despite experiencing negative consequences. This condition can lead to various health issues, including nutritional deficiencies and liver diseases such as cirrhosis. Additionally, alcoholism can result in decreased magnesium absorption, contributing to hypomagnesemia, and may cause physiological hypercortisolism. It is also noted that alcoholism can be a contraindication for the use of very low-calorie diets (VLCD). The biochemical alterations associated with alcoholism can improve with abstinence from alcohol, highlighting the potential for recovery and health restoration.</data>
      <data key="d2">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9,863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2024</data>
      <data key="d7">d7ec18b54fd241cb9f77f9bd406e1fb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DROGADICCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Drogadicci&#243;n refers to the compulsive use of drugs, which can severely impact a person's nutritional health and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
