      <data key="d7">a346a8a6c9a747afa8fa74f222256371</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CER-NEVIT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CER-NEVIT is a multivitamin composition used in parenteral nutrition for adults, containing various vitamins and excipients.</data>
      <data key="d2">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">2044</data>
      <data key="d7">f4c66e340a554599888708681172f19d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="A. NAVARRO EDUARDO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A. Navarro Eduardo is an author contributing to the chapter on access routes in parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2045</data>
      <data key="d7">750f2b758ccc4d11bb4f4aaa06d6933d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA refers to a method of venous access utilized in parenteral nutrition, specifically designed for situations where the osmolarity of the nutritional solution is below 800 mOsm/l. This method involves administering nutrition through peripheral veins, making it a suitable option when central venous access is not available.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2046</data>
      <data key="d7">f2a62503962143dbbe276b0785b82cfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA D3">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin D3, also known as Cholecalciferol or colecalciferol, is a fat-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium and phosphate levels in the body. It is essential for maintaining bone health and supporting immune function. Vitamin D3 is produced in the skin in response to sunlight and is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition. It is recognized as a more effective form of vitamin D compared to D2 in raising vitamin D levels in the body. Additionally, it is noted that some patients may be deficient in Vitamin D3, highlighting its importance for overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2047</data>
      <data key="d7">c7b284d28cda46289028009c0e7d2749</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIBOFLAVINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Riboflavin, also known as Vitamin B2, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in energy production and cellular function. It is an essential component of the B-complex vitamins and is included in parenteral nutrition formulations, such as Infuvite Pedi&#225;trico, to support overall health. Riboflavin is recognized for its importance in energy metabolism, and it is included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition. Notably, there are currently no established upper limits for riboflavin intake due to insufficient data on potential adverse effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2048</data>
      <data key="d7">aaaddff90dbf426688f3fed69b8d974f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PIRIDOXINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pyridoxina, commonly known as Vitamin B6, is a water-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It is involved in amino acid metabolism and neurotransmitter synthesis, making it important for cognitive development and overall brain health. While there is some discussion regarding its potential benefits for cognitive health and dementia, the evidence supporting its effectiveness in these areas is limited.

Pyridoxina is also included in parenteral nutrition formulations, highlighting its significance in protein metabolism. It is a key component of multivitamin compositions used in parenteral nutrition, such as Infuvite Pedi&#225;trico, ensuring that individuals receiving this form of nutrition obtain essential nutrients for their health. Overall, Pyridoxina is recognized for its vital contributions to metabolic processes and its inclusion in nutritional support therapies.</data>
      <data key="d2">49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2049</data>
      <data key="d7">98a0db6f75fb41408be55df36942dbae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AC. F&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Folic acid is a B-vitamin important for cell division and the production of DNA, included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2050</data>
      <data key="d7">6dd9a3eda52f467db1ffd253cc5c41a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AC. DEXPANTOT&#201;NICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dexpanthenol (Vitamin B5) is a water-soluble vitamin involved in the synthesis of coenzyme A, included in the multivitamin composition for parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d3">609</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2051</data>
      <data key="d7">30adac4f386741dc93fa377dd3682edc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HICKMAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hickman is a type of tunneled central venous catheter designed for accessing the venous system, particularly beneficial for patients requiring long-term intravenous therapy, such as those undergoing oncology treatments and other medical interventions. This catheter is known for its lower infection rates compared to non-tunneled catheters, making it a preferred choice for sustained venous access.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826,781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">772</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2052</data>
      <data key="d7">1e3450bb355043e0a34f9ec77e3b76ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PORT-A-CATH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Port-a-Cath is a brand of totally implanted catheter designed for long-term access to the vascular system, primarily for patients who require frequent blood draws or infusions. It is classified as a type of central venous catheter, which necessitates regular maintenance, including sealing every 1 to 6 months to prevent thrombotic obstruction. This device provides a reliable solution for patients needing ongoing vascular access.</data>
      <data key="d2">20a97c2641138578710a84f5040c86ef,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">772</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2053</data>
      <data key="d7">550e0640bfcf442e80536fab9df02f4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLDINGHER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Seldingher is a technique used for the puncture of large veins, such as the internal jugular or subclavian veins, for catheter insertion.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2054</data>
      <data key="d7">8075a56b72d94c5eb7b2f1cfd23d03ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UCIS ESPA&#209;OLAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UCIs Espa&#241;olas refers to Intensive Care Units in Spain, which follow specific protocols for preventing infections related to catheter use.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2055</data>
      <data key="d7">009624b72e444ba8a4fc23f56312285a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VENAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Veins are blood vessels that are accessed for catheter insertion, including antecubital, jugular, subclavian, and femoral veins.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">759</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2056</data>
      <data key="d7">3c0c790970d947cf958e78e9a3bf98c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ALIMENTACI&#211;N PARENTERAL es un m&#233;todo de nutrici&#243;n que se administra por v&#237;a intravenosa. Este tratamiento se utiliza en pacientes que no pueden recibir alimentos por v&#237;a oral o enteral, proporcionando as&#237; la nutrici&#243;n necesaria de manera efectiva.</data>
      <data key="d2">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">590</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2057</data>
      <data key="d7">13191f9147cb44f8907fab6facd63405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATAETERES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Catheters are medical devices used to deliver fluids or medications directly into the bloodstream or to drain fluids from the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d3">759</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2058</data>
      <data key="d7">3844292c89ca44f2a4dc06e7002f7a74</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUMOT&#211;RAX is a medical condition characterized by the presence of air in the pleural space, which is the area between the lung and the chest wall. This condition can arise as a complication during various medical procedures, particularly during the insertion of a central venous catheter. The risk of developing a pneumothorax is notably associated with central parenteral nutrition and other venous access procedures, where improper technique or accidental puncture of the pleura may lead to air leakage. Overall, pneumothorax is a significant concern in clinical settings, as it can complicate patient care and necessitate further medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826,67344d72dff60fcb903b258fbca95de5,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855</data>
      <data key="d3">759</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2059</data>
      <data key="d7">ea2894cddf394c8fa4cb8e38f4001c9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemot&#243;rax is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of blood in the pleural cavity. This condition can arise as a complication during the insertion of a catheter, particularly due to arterial puncture. Hemot&#243;rax represents a significant risk associated with catheter procedures, highlighting the importance of careful technique to prevent such complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">759</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2060</data>
      <data key="d7">0e396de6708347a9bdd574dfb49a0f2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" (NPD) refers to home parenteral nutrition, a medical treatment designed for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through oral intake. This form of home nutritional therapy involves the intravenous delivery of essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, making it a vital option for individuals with conditions such as intestinal failure or other gastrointestinal disorders that prevent normal food consumption.

NPD allows stable patients to receive nutritional support in the comfort of their own homes, significantly improving their quality of life while reducing the risk of hospital-related complications. It is particularly beneficial for those requiring long-term nutritional therapy, as it provides a means to maintain nutritional status outside of a clinical setting.

The method has been analyzed for its cost-effectiveness compared to traditional hospital-based nutrition, and it is documented annually by the NADYA group, which tracks the health implications and associated costs of home parenteral nutrition. Overall, "NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" serves as a crucial intervention for patients who cannot meet their nutritional needs through natural food sources, facilitating their rehabilitation and enhancing their overall well-being.</data>
