    <node id="KLEBSIELLA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Klebsiella is a type of gram-negative bacteria known to cause infections, particularly in patients who have catheters or those who are immunocompromised. This bacterium poses a significant risk in healthcare settings, where it can lead to serious infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a,c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
