    <node id="CANDIDA ALBICANS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Candida albicans is a type of fungus that can lead to infections, particularly in patients with catheters and those who are immunocompromised. It is known to cause various infections and has been mentioned as a potential cause of diarrhea in certain patients. This opportunistic pathogen poses a significant risk, especially in vulnerable populations, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing infections associated with this fungus.</data>
