      <data key="d7">e3620224778248f6a47801391fdd1b97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD METAB&#211;LICA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDAD METAB&#211;LICA &#211;SEA" refers to a condition affecting bone metabolism, particularly prevalent in patients receiving long-term parenteral nutrition. This condition is characterized by osteoporosis and osteomalacia, leading to symptoms such as bone pain and an increased risk of fractures due to nutrient deficiencies. It encompasses various bone metabolic disorders that arise as a result of prolonged nutritional support via parenteral means.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
