      <data key="d7">fc41933f20af48d49233526034e337c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional supplementation encompasses the provision of additional nutrients to individuals, particularly in clinical settings, to enhance their nutritional status and meet dietary requirements. This practice is especially crucial for malnourished patients and those with specific health conditions, such as chronic diseases like Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), liver disease, and during treatments like chemotherapy. 

Nutritional supplementation can be administered either parenterally or enterally and is often employed to prepare patients for surgery, such as those undergoing procedures for gastric cancer. It plays a significant role in improving health outcomes, particularly in elderly individuals, by enhancing the effects of exercise, preventing frailty, and potentially improving cognitive function. 

The use of dietary supplements, which may include vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients, is vital for supporting health in various patient populations, including those with conditions like dementia and cancer. Overall, nutritional supplementation is a critical component of patient care aimed at optimizing health and recovery in individuals with diverse nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,3ec3efbe130c20d623681e00e3d784f7,4b0d0238a19e23ffee592c9d0817e226,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b,97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,bf2e1510b4d6b43da85e8086d93e5602,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,d23c564df025cf16e37f2ef2be83ec34,ea8be3e3b3d7195ddc85512be460b6f8,eadd983c9f28c11a1c279e4b923351cd,f6135205f57ce2216ab62038ac34a2bb</data>
