      <data key="d7">9df192270b214059974ea2fb17c0c006</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SNG, or Sonda Nasog&#225;strica, is a medical device known as a nasogastric tube that is primarily used to provide nutritional support to patients who are unable to eat by mouth. This tube is utilized for enteral feeding, allowing for the administration of nutrition and medications directly to the stomach. It is particularly beneficial for patients with swallowing difficulties or those in poor general health who cannot undergo more invasive feeding interventions. The SNG serves as a critical tool in medical procedures, facilitating the delivery of air or water to the stomach as needed. Overall, SNG is an essential method for ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrition when oral intake is not possible or safe.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9,140611dbb8a68fc40712c946de92b73f,1adf391b13598f3ffe28ae596ff49438,242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,395385fad73fd5b7ed9eda114b482624,40dcfaa6144c6424068ba46fdf288dd2,417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,cae7bf8d7b8c9d1f34a87ef41ff39a17,e7df0ed14559db764d393fb9411fec33</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
