      <data key="d7">303d76d9fde44665adf9f5097f6723ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES DESNUTRIDOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pacientes Desnutridos" refers to individuals suffering from malnutrition, who are at an increased risk of developing complications such as S&#237;ndrome de Realimentaci&#243;n when receiving nutritional support. These patients may require enteral nutrition before major surgeries or transplants, as well as parenteral or enteral nutrition both before and after surgical procedures. Malnourished patients are particularly vulnerable to health issues like hypophosphatemia, which can arise from their nutritional deficiencies. Often, this state of malnutrition is a consequence of eating disorders, highlighting the complex interplay between nutritional health and psychological factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,241d358b60724c07a75223b79c9e5f41,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd,969bdfc6cc15b9089e96000addd87561,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d3">748</data>
