    </node>
    <node id="TRAUMATIC BRAIN INJURY (TCE)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Traumatic brain injury (TCE) refers to the brain damage resulting from trauma, which significantly affects the metabolic response and nutritional needs of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c</data>
      <data key="d3">608</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2111</data>
      <data key="d7">340a32f37f8244668130700abd8bde93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLYTRAUMATISMOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polytraumatism refers to the condition of having multiple traumatic injuries, which can affect a wide range of patients and requires specialized nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c</data>
      <data key="d3">608</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2112</data>
      <data key="d7">d66588e105994f8fbe996bd24ea5c32c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARRIS-BENEDICT EQUATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Harris-Benedict equation is a formula utilized to estimate an individual's energy requirements, taking into account their weight and activity level. This equation is particularly important for calculating caloric needs, which is essential for determining the nutritional support necessary for patients, especially those experiencing a hypermetabolic state.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c</data>
      <data key="d3">608</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2113</data>
      <data key="d7">953d723ff82f43b68114d8f967f3474f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL (NE)">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL (NE) refers to nutritional support provided through the gastrointestinal tract. This form of nutrition is particularly essential for patients suffering from severe acute pancreatitis, as it helps meet their dietary needs when they are unable to consume food orally.</data>
      <data key="d2">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,d2110ea1623a52d24b22d1a18f66010c</data>
      <data key="d3">608</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2114</data>
      <data key="d7">02c0bbe5987f400f870f7ab9a2486566</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEMICYUC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Spanish Society of Intensive Care Medicine (SEMICYUC) is a medical society dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for critical care nutrition and metabolic support, particularly for patients who are neurocritical and polytraumatized. The organization has developed specialized recommendations for nutritional approaches in clinical settings, focusing on the management of nutritional needs in critically ill patients, including those with severe burns. SEMICYUC plays a crucial role in collaborating on guidelines that enhance the nutritional support provided to critically ill patients, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the best practices in critical care nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">125acd19edb76fa23986de56fc2517e8,195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,2ec23f85b858abc42196ef48260e8cb0,4c4d1882f0ac14b7c55941ec1c17b650,51ccbecf506101052f08de7cbbaa6b62,762a80a4c9f24d778b79fdd596f343e3,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da</data>
