    <node id="LIPIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LIPIDOS, or lipids, are a group of organic compounds that are insoluble in water, including fats and oils. They play crucial roles in biological functions and are essential for nutritional support. Lipids provide essential fatty acids and serve as an important non-protein energy source, particularly in infant nutrition. In the context of dietary recommendations, it is noted that lipids should be adjusted in the diet of patients with renal insufficiency, typically comprising 30% of total caloric intake. Overall, lipids are vital for providing energy and maintaining cell membrane structure, highlighting their importance in both health and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">33815f13a51d2a716356eaca97176390,7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce,e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
      <data key="d3">1389</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">2131</data>
      <data key="d7">0b8d81c30db84ea6b37a29c7a4b1c686</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Proteins are crucial for daily intake and are catabolized for energy during metabolic stress.</data>
      <data key="d2">33815f13a51d2a716356eaca97176390</data>
      <data key="d3">1389</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
