    <node id="CORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Corticosteroids, commonly referred to as corticoides, are a class of steroid hormones utilized in the treatment of a variety of medical conditions. They are particularly effective in managing acute adrenal insufficiency and serve as anti-inflammatory medications for inflammatory bowel diseases (IBD), often used alongside nutritional support. Key corticosteroids such as dexamethasone, prednisolone, and methylprednisolone are employed to enhance appetite and alleviate nausea in cancer patients, although they are associated with several side effects.

In the context of IBD, corticosteroids like prednisolone and budesonide play a crucial role in significantly suppressing inflammation during acute episodes. They are also used in high doses to treat conditions such as graft-versus-host disease (GVHD), where they help inhibit the activity of pro-inflammatory prostaglandins and cytokines. However, their use can exacerbate the adverse effects of chemotherapy, including nausea and vomiting.

Corticosteroids are known to impact carbohydrate metabolism, particularly in transplant patients, and may lead to nutritional issues in individuals with chronic respiratory diseases. Additionally, they can cause high potassium loss and are linked to muscle loss and an increased risk of infections in critically ill patients. Despite their effectiveness, the use of corticosteroids in treating symptoms of IBD can be controversial, highlighting the need for careful consideration in their application. They are also utilized in the treatment of conditions such as Graves' ophthalmopathy, where they are administered in intravenous pulses for optimal results.</data>
      <data key="d2">42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,4c18507e3d98242cdbcddd1a1997b92f,4ec3e8cb1f21808e70bbc71cb26d7396,5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807,5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972,5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d,89c28a4a0410d8f4cbbbc0fbdf4b1c40,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,df0e6695be23c07606ca5b9accc62df2,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,f333e5a9af59dd8504607b2559ac35dd,fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
