      <data key="d6">2149</data>
      <data key="d7">2f0a5e04abe244d69264db34679be366</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUCOSA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MUCOSA INTESTINAL" serves as a crucial barrier in the gastrointestinal tract, particularly in the early months of life when it may be compromised, allowing the passage of antigens and potentially leading to food allergies. This intestinal lining can exhibit atrophy and linfangiectasias, conditions that are observable during endoscopic examinations and are significant for patient diagnosis. Furthermore, the integrity of the mucosa intestinal is maintained through enteral nutrition, which plays a vital role in reducing the risk of infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">89c28a4a0410d8f4cbbbc0fbdf4b1c40,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,d10e6c00bbb982bda449b9cb815691a3</data>
