    <node id="ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA" refers to the duration of time a patient spends in the hospital. This period is significant as it can be influenced by various factors, including nutritional status, complications arising during surgery, and specific medical conditions such as hyponatremia. Efforts are often made to reduce the length of hospital stay through appropriate nutritional interventions, such as enteral nutrition, which is designed to be immunomodulatory. The goal of these nutritional strategies is to enhance patient recovery and minimize the time spent in the hospital, thereby improving overall health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b02ff4978fb09a0b2a360ae8c661337,27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,70a9e916b8c55784c53828958c76eb09,7184072817ac284bebfea449e3eaac8b,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,89c28a4a0410d8f4cbbbc0fbdf4b1c40,a7baff5fb024c516ea6ae8c236dc945d,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d3">1156</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2154</data>
      <data key="d7">ae3831e8c3454b9a803a004e771cda32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE DISTR&#201;S RESPIRATORIO AGUDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome de Distr&#233;s Respiratorio Agudo" (SDRA) is a critical medical condition characterized by acute respiratory failure, which significantly impacts a patient's ability to breathe. This severe syndrome often necessitates the use of mechanical ventilation to support respiratory function. In addition to respiratory support, patients with SDRA may require specialized nutritional attention and the administration of immunomodulatory formulas to aid in their recovery. Overall, SDRA represents a serious health challenge that demands comprehensive medical management and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,d77e49d1dba3a67fbc9cf58911dc2478,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d3">623</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2155</data>
      <data key="d7">aad2f21793944973972c26518f3a0875</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;CIDOS GRASOS, or fatty acids, are essential components of dietary lipids that are classified based on their structure, specifically their chain length and degree of saturation. They play a significant role in nutrition and health, particularly concerning cardiovascular diseases. These nutrients are crucial for energy storage and cellular function, serving as the building blocks of lipids. Fatty acids are also important for the absorption of water and electrolytes, and they contribute to energy support for the lungs, including the synthesis of pulmonary surfactant.

In nutritional contexts, fatty acids such as ALA (alpha-linolenic acid), EPA (eicosapentaenoic acid), and DHA (docosahexaenoic acid) are recognized for their positive influence on cardiovascular health. They are included in various nutritional formulas due to their vital roles in maintaining overall health and supporting cellular functions. Additionally, fatty acids are produced during the metabolism of triglycerides, further underscoring their importance in energy metabolism and physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a43b350a248173236a96a64e266b744,3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d3">486</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2156</data>
      <data key="d7">efcf8d09545743458465aa6e0d7e54a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITES DE PESCADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aceites de pescado, or fish oils, are recognized for their high content of omega-3 fatty acids, which are beneficial for enhancing the nutritional status of patients experiencing respiratory distress. These oils are frequently utilized in clinical nutrition products, where they can influence both taste and odor. Additionally, fish oils have been extensively researched for their potential effects on blood pressure, further highlighting their significance in dietary and health-related applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a,62f527b38024e8807d3e63a0cf488046,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
