    </node>
    <node id="COPD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is a common and progressive lung disease characterized by breathing difficulties due to blocked airflow. It is often associated with long-term exposure to harmful substances, such as irritating gases or particulate matter, which can lead to significant morbidity and mortality. COPD encompasses a group of lung diseases that not only affect respiratory function but also require nutritional support for management. This condition is a significant health issue in various regions, including Spain, where it contributes notably to the overall burden of disease in the population. Additionally, COPD is sometimes studied in relation to other respiratory conditions, such as cystic fibrosis, highlighting its relevance in the broader context of lung health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68,6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0,c3e74ddf9529482684f4b62e713df49b,ea8be3e3b3d7195ddc85512be460b6f8</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">36</data>
      <data key="d6">2161</data>
      <data key="d7">4abf5a77a59d4be490305ce79219fbff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTENSIVE CARE UNIT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Intensive Care Unit (ICU) is a specialized department within hospitals dedicated to the intensive treatment and monitoring of critically ill patients. It is designed to provide advanced medical care and support for individuals who require close observation and complex interventions due to severe health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826</data>
      <data key="d3">765</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2162</data>
      <data key="d7">a32e45a927f04654ac035a869e56dfd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SDRA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SDRA, or Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome, is a severe medical condition characterized by respiratory failure. Management of SDRA often necessitates the use of specialized nutritional formulas to support the patient's recovery and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,428ea9c156fe3f0571b20d5d81648868</data>
      <data key="d3">765</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2163</data>
      <data key="d7">d79e5028844f4c45bbcaf4a64b90f75e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL, or artificial nutrition, refers to the provision of nutrients through means other than oral intake, commonly utilized in critically ill patients. This treatment modality is particularly important for patients with conditions such as inflammatory bowel disease, where it aims to enhance nutritional intake and assist in the remission of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,d66daca6ec5ffce0fc73bce55a3c0ff0</data>
      <data key="d3">765</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">2164</data>
      <data key="d7">df99b970ab434b95817e13e8a0c6638b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARGININE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arginine is a conditionally essential amino acid that plays a significant role in various clinical settings, particularly in immunonutrition. It is known for its immunomodulatory effects, notably in stimulating T lymphocyte activity and reducing pro-inflammatory cytokines. This amino acid is often included in formulas designed for patients with specific deficiencies, such as CPS (carbamoyl phosphate synthetase) and OTC (ornithine transcarbamylase) deficiencies. Additionally, arginine serves as a precursor for nitric oxide, making it a consideration for patients suffering from acute lung injury. Furthermore, it is utilized in the chronic treatment of patients with MELAS (mitochondrial encephalomyopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes) to help manage associated symptoms. Overall, arginine's diverse applications highlight its importance in both immunological and metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5,eadd983c9f28c11a1c279e4b923351cd,ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29</data>
      <data key="d3">1138</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">2165</data>
      <data key="d7">d82e7b94bcfb4e6bbd2c6c6bbd8a3ba5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICRONUTRIENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Micronutrients are essential dietary components, including vitamins and minerals, that play a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are vital for modulating inflammation, supporting cardiovascular health, and reducing oxidative stress, which is particularly important for brain health. Micronutrients are also critical in maintaining cognitive function and preventing cognitive decline, especially in older adults. 

Certain populations, such as patients post-bariatric surgery, may experience deficiencies in these essential nutrients due to dietary restrictions. Similarly, individuals with Phenylketonuria may require supplementation of specific micronutrients. Additionally, micronutrients are important for patients with respiratory issues and those suffering from conditions like pancreatitis, where deficiencies in nutrients such as thiamine, folic acid, and zinc can occur.

Furthermore, micronutrients like copper, selenium, and zinc are essential for immune modulation and wound healing, particularly in burned patients. The significance of micronutrient intake and its implications for public health are emphasized, highlighting their role in preventing frailty and maintaining overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">396dda5c9597828f0749f963f42142b4,3bfd2ce2b4408f718fd35e43c03965c7,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b,680ff2c9e67ec29c5952df66bd83c984,6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2,75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8,7ff62e1dc423be2f4b2fe08546751d0d,8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2,f2b8b21255397ebbaf2b5d66ff6bde88</data>
