      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The New England Journal of Medicine is a prestigious peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes original research articles and reviews across all areas of medicine. It is known for disseminating significant findings, including research on the risks associated with MEN1 and studies on the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease through the Mediterranean diet. The journal plays a crucial role in advancing medical knowledge and informing clinical practice through its rigorous publication standards.</data>
