      <data key="d7">bcda0b21f3a74b8fad89b31a14240bc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA," or chronic kidney failure, is a long-term medical condition characterized by the gradual loss of kidney function over time. This condition significantly impacts the kidneys' ability to effectively remove waste and maintain fluid balance, leading to various complications. As kidney function declines, patients may experience issues such as malnutrition, caquexia, and growth problems in children. 

Chronic renal failure often requires careful management, including dietary restrictions, particularly in protein intake, and supplementation of vitamins and minerals to address nutritional deficiencies. The condition is also associated with cardiovascular risks and can lead to severe complications, necessitating interventions such as dialysis or kidney transplantation in advanced stages. 

Additionally, chronic kidney failure can result in limitations in renal potassium excretion and may manifest as hypervolemic hyponatremia. It is important to note that ongoing kidney damage is a primary factor in the progression of this disease, which can be linked to underlying conditions such as diabetes. Overall, "INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA" represents a serious health challenge that requires comprehensive management and monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,2c60ced31055ac58d76da9c1e90c8e9d,31b61ae47905168ef430433c9eb5237a,61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181,64417661dbb019f8f4ceb9fcc2fbdaa6,665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,7ba4a7e7b4c409f6d4c6979a7de6c832,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce,ce43a9a4cdf2497b2f984547a2787fff,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
