    <node id="ENERG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "ENERG&#205;A" encompasses various aspects of energy intake and expenditure, which are crucial for dietary management across different populations, particularly in patients with specific health conditions. Energy intake is vital for individuals with renal failure, necessitating tailored caloric recommendations to support their unique dietary needs. In the context of infants receiving parenteral nutrition, energy is defined as the caloric intake essential for their growth and maintenance. Furthermore, energy is recognized as the capacity to perform work, which is fundamental for all bodily functions and activities, especially in children where it plays a significant role in growth and development.

Additionally, the concept of energ&#237;a includes the assessment of energy expenditure and requirements, which is particularly important for critically ill patients. Accurate calculations of energy expenditure are also critical for dietary planning in diabetes management. Overall, energ&#237;a is an essential nutritional requirement that varies among individuals and is vital for maintaining vital functions and supporting growth, especially in pediatric patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">490f5e3c6dbf3754eee50c52154da09a,64417661dbb019f8f4ceb9fcc2fbdaa6,767d564db2dbf0182707caaf1b0a52d2,79dc467f42c611bc9f285c95a6c6ff62,a0b6196d53d4eb1c8ca5b1a3a78e8fc7,abf638322cfb1c522bfbee1852e28a19,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02,c567251c335f000303144ce3d7e1d638,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,d92f4ecdee41ca35485c997a95642c5b</data>
      <data key="d3">675</data>
