    <node id="AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (A.S.P.E.N.) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the science and practice of clinical nutrition. It provides comprehensive guidelines and education on parenteral and enteral nutrition practices in the United States, catering to both adult and pediatric patients. A.S.P.E.N. develops clinical guidelines for nutrition support therapy, particularly during adult anticancer treatment, hematopoietic cell transplantation, and in critical care settings.

The organization emphasizes the importance of nutrition screening, assessment, and intervention in adults, including those with acute and chronic renal failure, neurological diseases, and other conditions requiring nutritional support. A.S.P.E.N. also offers recommendations for nutritional support in hospitalized patients, ensuring that healthcare providers have the necessary resources to address malnutrition effectively.

Overall, A.S.P.E.N. plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and support for nutrition therapy, focusing on the needs of patients requiring enteral and parenteral nutrition across various healthcare settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,29cd22ec41c1cb5160d9987958d6ae16,2d14f6773b107ec9a872245c32ae0a94,36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,38547636a4ef9fd045b438047fb629fc,396dda5c9597828f0749f963f42142b4,477da86aa038212a1e2b555b5a854cba,4ce6342fdfe4419826c1ab2f84c56247,62cb70a5fd28a7c444f52a64ce2a7f75,7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97,916d4d35de887923f4ea5b05928f13e3,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,aae3f23f674724518bcb311a99d764d6,d26aec24f3f8c930c1c4b1d464bacd6b,e3203d9f5bd82749de9eee35c52c67ce</data>
