    <node id="HEMODIALISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemodialysis is a medical procedure to remove waste products and excess fluid from the blood when the kidneys are not functioning properly.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2199</data>
      <data key="d7">d743a9effb5a44c6947de057fd1a8402</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL is a type of dialysis that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood, serving as an alternative to hemodialysis for patients with renal failure. This treatment method is specifically designed for individuals with chronic kidney disease, allowing for the removal of bodily waste. It is important to note that peritoneal dialysis requires patients to increase their caloric intake due to the presence of glucose in the dialysis fluid. Overall, DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL provides a viable option for those suffering from kidney insufficiency, leveraging the body's own abdominal lining to facilitate the filtration process.</data>
      <data key="d2">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448,169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,2c60ced31055ac58d76da9c1e90c8e9d,532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0,541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292,9f77fc213da2123b013166c181a60323,a87e8e113488b153c5b4b2d2fca712c0</data>
