    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE RESPUESTA INFLAMATORIA SIST&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome de Respuesta Inflamatoria Sist&#233;mica" (Systemic Inflammatory Response Syndrome, SIRS) is a clinical condition that can arise from various severe clinical insults, including acute pancreatitis. It is characterized by a systemic inflammatory response, which may manifest through various clinical signs. In severe cases of pancreatitis, SIRS can lead to a hypermetabolic state, necessitating careful nutritional management to support the affected individual. Additionally, it has been noted that the condition can be mitigated through immunonutrition, particularly in post-surgical patients. Overall, SIRS represents a significant clinical challenge that requires comprehensive management strategies to address its inflammatory and metabolic implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,e34642244b0c7f309ab1c1be1e81da31,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
