    <node id="ENZIMAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENZIMAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS" refers to digestive enzymes produced by the pancreas that play a crucial role in the digestion of food. These enzymes are particularly important for patients suffering from conditions such as pancreatitis, where their levels may be elevated and used to assess the severity of the condition. In cases of pancreatitis, supplementation of pancreatic enzymes may be necessary to aid digestion and improve nutrient absorption due to pancreatic insufficiency. Additionally, pancreatic enzymes are also prescribed to patients with cystic fibrosis to help prevent malnutrition by facilitating proper digestion. Overall, these enzymes are vital for individuals experiencing malabsorption issues, ensuring that they receive adequate nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">028c43c3f0f3d1f8085eed8518636f97,17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56,67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,95ef1473677a26ea6ad77c7db0c55e5e,c926a8237fba5d5bc497ac2165bbb039,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
