    <node id="DIETA ABSOLUTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA ABSOLUTA" refers to a medical dietary restriction characterized by the complete cessation of food intake. This absolute diet is often implemented in various medical contexts, particularly in cases of suspected lymphatic injuries and as a preparatory measure for medical procedures. Additionally, it is commonly prescribed for patients experiencing acute pancreatitis during the initial treatment phase. The primary purpose of the dieta absoluta is to ensure that no food is consumed, allowing for necessary medical interventions and recovery processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
