    <node id="CREATININA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatinina, also known as creatinine, is a chemical waste product found in the blood that is primarily used to assess kidney function. It is produced from muscle metabolism and is an important marker in blood tests for evaluating renal health. The measurement of creatinine levels can also provide insights into a person's nutritional status and may influence vitamin D metabolism. Additionally, creatinine levels can be affected in patients with liver disease, highlighting its relevance in broader health assessments. In summary, creatinina is a crucial indicator in blood analyses for evaluating renal function and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
