    <node id="ESPEN GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The ESPEN Guidelines, established by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, offer comprehensive, evidence-based recommendations for nutritional support across a variety of clinical conditions. These guidelines specifically address enteral nutrition for non-surgical oncology patients, patients with dementia, and individuals suffering from liver disease, with the goal of improving patient outcomes. By providing targeted nutritional strategies, the ESPEN Guidelines aim to enhance the overall care and recovery of patients in these diverse medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dfb109dac53e054fd015f6d8adf48ac,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3,ce6821fbd8f78047e06917383f25f037,f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
