      <data key="d6">2243</data>
      <data key="d7">1af988a82b32470997a70dd3a677a9dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS LACTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidosis l&#225;ctica, or lactic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lactic acid in the body, which can occur due to various metabolic disturbances. This condition is particularly relevant in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI), where abnormal glucose metabolism can lead to increased lactate levels in the blood. The buildup of lactic acid is often associated with inadequate oxygen supply to tissues, which exacerbates the condition. 

In addition to GSDI, lactic acidosis can also arise from other metabolic derangements, such as fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency. Furthermore, it can be worsened by the fermentation of unabsorbed carbohydrates in the colon, contributing to malabsorption issues. However, there are potential interventions, such as medium-chain triglyceride (MCT) supplementation, that may help improve the condition. Overall, acidosis l&#225;ctica is a complex clinical manifestation that requires careful management, especially in individuals with specific metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,704cfd179507a977ecc0691a5bd2861e,948f7e888e5bb06b347a80a3fbf87ae7,9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce,a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853,d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2244</data>
      <data key="d7">24111d19bb3046b1b2f593713d680342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERSECRECI&#211;N &#193;CIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acid hypersecretion is an increase in gastric acid secretion that contributes to malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246</data>
