    <node id="MALABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">MALABSORCI&#211;N is a medical condition characterized by the impaired absorption of nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition can lead to malnutrition and is commonly observed in individuals with various underlying health issues, including inflammatory bowel disease (EII), celiac disease, pancreatic disorders, and liver disease. 

Patients with MALABSORCI&#211;N may experience difficulties in absorbing essential nutrients, which can necessitate dietary adjustments to ensure proper nutrient intake. The condition can also arise as a result of certain medical treatments, such as chemotherapy with cyclophosphamide and radiation therapy, which may further compromise nutritional status. 

In individuals with celiac disease, for instance, the small intestine's inability to absorb nutrients adequately is a significant concern. Similarly, patients with cancer may face challenges related to nutrient absorption, impacting their overall health and recovery. Additionally, medications can influence nutrient absorption, potentially leading to complications such as hypophosphatemia.

Overall, MALABSORCI&#211;N is a complex condition that requires careful management and dietary planning to address the specific needs of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,5bb504bf68288cc0ba6a8f0dd9e4c245,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,af40d7a664dbfc9c14307a26f52b9bff,c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa,d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246,d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7,ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91,e569eda9506ef1e77080a8120e388963,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
