    </node>
    <node id="CROHN'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Crohn's disease is a type of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) that causes chronic inflammation of the gastrointestinal tract, affecting various parts of the digestive system. This condition can lead to significant complications, including malabsorption of essential nutrients such as calcium, which can adversely impact bone health. Nutritional management is a critical aspect of addressing Crohn's disease, as it requires specific dietary considerations to help manage symptoms and maintain overall health. The disease is recognized in both English and Spanish, with the Spanish description emphasizing its nature as a form of inflammatory bowel disease that necessitates targeted management.</data>
      <data key="d2">7a389f3625ba13c74ce52213197b01ae,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,b3ddc7e512f6a789fa4cef18e7b18fab,b4580c82418cd4df97f400e183702858,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">756</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2250</data>
      <data key="d7">d2685030d45f4b74aea915b171847e93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ULCERATIVE COLITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ulcerative colitis is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease that causes inflammation and ulcers in the digestive tract.</data>
      <data key="d2">9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,b3ddc7e512f6a789fa4cef18e7b18fab</data>
      <data key="d3">756</data>
