      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2251</data>
      <data key="d7">cb81b78daba74453958608d8374d1980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BICARBONATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bicarbonate, also known as bicarbonato, is a chemical compound that plays a crucial role in maintaining the pH balance in the body, with normal levels typically ranging between 22 and 29 mmol/l. It acts as a buffer, helping to regulate acidity and alkalinity in various physiological processes. Bicarbonate is particularly significant in medical contexts, as it is often measured in patients with diabetic ketoacidosis to assess their metabolic status and is used in treatments to correct acidosis. Additionally, it is recognized as an electrolyte that can be affected in patients experiencing secretory diarrhea, potentially leading to electrolyte imbalances.

Research has also explored the potential effects of bicarbonate on exercise performance and muscle function, indicating its broader relevance beyond just metabolic health. Overall, bicarbonate is an essential substance in both clinical and physiological settings, contributing to the body's homeostasis and being utilized in various medical treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e,86a4647fb1fa580f7b72aa4833965ecb,8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a,a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853</data>
      <data key="d3">624</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2252</data>
      <data key="d7">0f67620506a34408ba154659b37ce1ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLECALCIFEROL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Colecalciferol, also known as vitamin D3, is a form of vitamin D that is primarily used to correct vitamin D deficiency. It is recommended as a supplement for patients undergoing steroid treatment to prevent osteopenia and osteoporosis. This highlights its importance in maintaining bone health, particularly in individuals at risk due to medication-related side effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,d66daca6ec5ffce0fc73bce55a3c0ff0</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2253</data>
      <data key="d7">5b4fdd1a67174f97bb73b75dd21a3034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los esteroides son medicamentos que se utilizan en diversas aplicaciones m&#233;dicas, incluyendo el tratamiento de pacientes trasplantados y la enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Sin embargo, su uso puede conllevar efectos secundarios significativos. Entre estos efectos secundarios se incluyen la diarrea y la hiperglucemia, lo que resalta la importancia de un monitoreo cuidadoso durante su administraci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,81bb0be389c10331fb2a5568b6c379dc,d66daca6ec5ffce0fc73bce55a3c0ff0</data>
