    </node>
    <node id="FISTULAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fistulas are abnormal connections between organs or vessels that can result in high-output drainage, which may significantly impact an individual's nutritional status and treatment. These conditions often necessitate specific nutritional management strategies to address the complications arising from the abnormal connections.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d3">656</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2264</data>
      <data key="d7">c7f25ae02fcf4b9986cc860ef6811019</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEGACOLON T&#211;XICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A severe complication of inflammatory bowel disease characterized by extreme dilation of the colon, often requiring surgical intervention and nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2265</data>
      <data key="d7">504b776f7bb846d0b144211cfd96d5c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMOR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue that can be either benign or malignant, often associated with cancer. Tumors can lead to various health issues, including weight loss, depending on their location and type. In the case of a 72-year-old woman, a tumor located in her right lung is likely causing paraneoplastic syndrome and is associated with Cushing's syndrome. Additionally, tumors related to acromegaly can result in increased secretion of growth hormone, which contributes to the symptoms of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608,85eef7ed9c9b92d86939a6687ea2acfd,b1ce0d940909277d321ee55bffcc69b3,b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d3">1316</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">21</data>
      <data key="d6">2266</data>
      <data key="d7">9341dff478c2483a903173c363016c78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">G&#225;strico refers to gastric tumors which are known to cause significant weight loss in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db</data>
      <data key="d3">1316</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2267</data>
      <data key="d7">c7ea3814b0c345b2933560c9d0f1fcd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The pancreas is a vital organ involved in digestion and metabolism, playing a crucial role in the secretion of digestive enzymes and fluids containing electrolytes into the small intestine. It can be adversely affected by various conditions, including cancer, which may lead to malabsorption issues and weight loss due to its impact on digestion. Additionally, the pancreas is susceptible to iron accumulation in conditions such as hemochromatosis. It is also a site where carcinoid tumors can develop, contributing to the secretion of serotonin, and where VIPomas and other neuroendocrine tumors may originate. Recently, a 3 cm nodule was identified in the pancreas during an urgent ultrasound examination, highlighting the importance of monitoring this organ for potential abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db,cba5d81f1acff7cbf84e85ef35420521,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260</data>
      <data key="d3">1124</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
