    <node id="COLON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The colon, also known as the large intestine, is a crucial component of the digestive system. It plays a significant role in various metabolic functions, including the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates, which results in the production of short-chain fatty acids and gases. The colon is home to a vast number of intestinal bacteria that contribute to these metabolic processes. Additionally, it is responsible for the reabsorption of water and electrolytes, which is essential for maintaining fluid balance in the body.

However, the colon can be affected by health issues such as colorectal cancer, which can lead to symptoms like diarrhea, malabsorption of nutrients, and weight loss. These complications may arise due to factors such as obstruction and the inability to properly absorb nutrients. Overall, the colon is vital for digestion and nutrient absorption, while also being susceptible to various diseases that can impact its function.</data>
      <data key="d2">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1004</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2272</data>
      <data key="d7">59a56d9f7903415f913227ae34377726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFOMA ALTO GRADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Linfoma alto grado refers to high-grade lymphoma, a type of cancer that can lead to significant weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db</data>
      <data key="d3">1316</data>
