    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tratamientos refers to the various medical interventions, such as surgery, radiotherapy, and chemotherapy, that can affect the nutritional status and weight of cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db</data>
      <data key="d3">1139</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2278</data>
      <data key="d7">e4efbe8e50fd405ab8d64056703a16f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETATO DE MEGESTROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetato de Megestrol is a medication primarily used as an appetite stimulant, particularly in patients experiencing malnutrition, such as those with cancer. It was prescribed to a patient in 2011, resulting in positive effects on appetite in the subsequent years. The medication is known to improve appetite and increase weight in cancer patients; however, it does not contribute to an increase in lean mass or survival rates. Clinical trials have demonstrated its effectiveness in enhancing appetite and weight gain among this patient population.</data>
      <data key="d2">16887bf1589e9515213d2e392bbc8c69,42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da</data>
      <data key="d3">1117</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">2279</data>
      <data key="d7">661385940af24db1afa4f3b15fdc3151</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREDNISONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Prednisona is a corticosteroid medication that plays a significant role in the treatment of various medical conditions. It is primarily utilized in the management of inflammatory bowel disease, providing rapid relief of symptoms during acute flare-ups. Additionally, Prednisona is effective in reducing inflammation and suppressing the immune system, making it suitable for treating autoimmune conditions. The medication also serves as an antiemetic, helping to alleviate nausea, although its exact mechanism of action in this regard is not well understood. Furthermore, Prednisona can stimulate appetite in patients suffering from cancer-related malnutrition. While it is beneficial for many conditions, long-term use of Prednisona may lead to secondary osteoporosis. Overall, Prednisona is a versatile glucocorticoid that addresses a range of inflammatory and autoimmune disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d3">603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2280</data>
      <data key="d7">c12b22484cac48819350ccf490a2d811</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METILFENIDATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Metilfenidato is a psycho-stimulant used to help increase appetite in patients suffering from malnutrition due to cancer treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2281</data>
      <data key="d7">4fd2d9114ca24561af281f27ba372e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METOCLOPRAMIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Metoclopramida is a medication that has been tested in patients as part of their treatment for regurgitation. It is primarily used to facilitate the passage of feeding tubes through the digestive system and to improve gastric emptying. As a procin&#233;tico agent, Metoclopramida promotes gastric emptying and stimulates intestinal motility, which can be beneficial in enhancing enteral nutrition tolerance. It is particularly effective in alleviating nausea, a common symptom in cancer patients that can significantly impact their nutritional intake. The medication is often administered in critical care settings and is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. However, it is important to note that Metoclopramida may be associated with the production of diarrhea. Overall, it is a commonly used medication in oncology for managing nausea and vomiting, as well as for treating gastroparesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,5eb14e2cbec104d89ad73e2ac968b7fd,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,fc664efd4e1c463dc21857e596b68b46</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2282</data>
      <data key="d7">3c2c988553814333a890d74f83e7d0d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PILOCARPINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pilocarpina is a medication primarily used to treat xerostomia, or dry mouth, which is often a side effect of cancer treatments and can significantly affect a patient's ability to eat. When administered at doses of 5-10 mg every 8 hours orally, Pilocarpina can have systemic effects, including potential side effects such as sweating and abdominal pain.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60</data>
      <data key="d3">1069</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2283</data>
      <data key="d7">6548f04f876d4dcdb0ccce0555852dca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NISTATINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nistatina is an antifungal medication that is primarily used to treat fungal infections. It is often administered in mouthwash form, which has demonstrated effective results in managing these infections. Additionally, Nistatina can be swallowed, providing versatility in its application. This medication is particularly beneficial for patients experiencing xerostomia, a condition that can occur in cancer patients, as it helps address the fungal infections associated with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d3">1069</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2284</data>
      <data key="d7">48a5c97d5dd7413f9ee9c88aab1ee7d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUCONAZOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fluconazol is an antifungal medication that is primarily used to treat fungal infections, particularly in cases of systemic infections. It is recommended for use in cancer patients, as these individuals may be more susceptible to infections that can lead to nutritional issues. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, it is advised that Fluconazol be taken with meals. Overall, Fluconazol serves as an important therapeutic option for managing various fungal infections when systemic treatment is necessary.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d3">1110</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2285</data>
      <data key="d7">acfcf2d245c14a93bc0b4936203a53a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ITRACONAZOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Itraconazol is an antifungal medication utilized to treat a range of fungal infections, especially in immunocompromised patients, such as those with cancer. It plays a significant role in managing infections that can impact the nutritional status of these patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d3">1110</data>
