    </node>
    <node id="INTESTINO DELGADO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The "intestino delgado," or small intestine, is a crucial component of the human digestive system, primarily responsible for the absorption of various micronutrients and macronutrients. It plays a significant role in nutrient absorption, where enzymes such as &#946;-galactosidase aid in the digestion of specific sugars like galactose. While the intestino delgado contributes to the production of uric acid, its role in this process is relatively minor compared to other organs. Additionally, the intestino delgado can be adversely affected by conditions such as celiac disease, cancer, and malnutrition, highlighting its importance in overall digestive health and nutrient assimilation.</data>
      <data key="d2">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60</data>
      <data key="d3">671</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">2288</data>
      <data key="d7">3d0226f25b8e4f80aa7db33b6d9c71c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTOMAGO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Est&#243;mago is the organ where food is digested, and its function can be impaired by cancer, leading to symptoms like early satiety and malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ce201472321f20b339146bb6b452f60</data>
