    <node id="BROWN JK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Brown JK is an author of a guide by the American Cancer Society regarding nutrition and physical activity during and after cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537</data>
      <data key="d3">1839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2300</data>
      <data key="d7">0eceb49825094b42879ac20c947d7820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUIMIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">QUIMIO refers to chemotherapy, a type of cancer treatment that utilizes drugs to target and kill cancer cells. This treatment method is known to present nutritional challenges for patients undergoing therapy, as the side effects of the drugs can impact their ability to maintain a healthy diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2301</data>
      <data key="d7">2e30a9a7d28d481fb1f85644d3f7df4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL, or nutritional support, is a vital intervention aimed at enhancing the tolerance to treatment and improving the quality of life for patients suffering from malnutrition. It is particularly crucial for individuals who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially those experiencing complications. Nutritional support plays a significant role in the management of various health conditions, including cancer and dementia, as it helps to improve overall health outcomes.

This support is designed to meet the dietary needs of patients who are unable to eat normally, including those with intestinal failure and critically ill patients. It encompasses a range of methods and practices to provide nutrition, especially for patients who cannot consume food orally. Nutritional support is also essential in clinical settings for individuals with eating disorders and is particularly important for children who require assistance in meeting their dietary needs.

Overall, SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL is a comprehensive approach to ensuring that patients receive the necessary dietary assistance to enhance their clinical outcomes and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,2a387a0f62fd64b31ecf55b1538932c2,36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,89e0e7fac6984f367ae1649e9eaab7d7,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,af40d7a664dbfc9c14307a26f52b9bff,afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc,dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d,ec4fd77add427ab49ea4b8687b94b263,f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">1103</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">2302</data>
      <data key="d7">78c02775b76749c19070dc03f03a8b70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES QUEMADOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">"PACIENTES QUEMADOS" refers to individuals who have suffered from burns and require specialized nutritional management due to their hypermetabolic and catabolic responses following the injury. These patients are particularly vulnerable, as they often experience critical burn injuries that place them at a high risk of malnutrition. Their condition is characterized by hypermetabolism, hypercatabolism, and inflammation, necessitating careful dietary interventions to support their recovery and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,2ec23f85b858abc42196ef48260e8cb0,b3bff0edc314389f2ac432a753fec9f7,f999ed498214f69427e629a05ea8ce4a</data>
      <data key="d3">1143</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">25</data>
      <data key="d6">2303</data>
      <data key="d7">9ca9b9c5a23e401c9742f2bb0e18035f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CICATRIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CICATRIZACI&#211;N refers to the process of wound healing, which is particularly crucial for patients who have suffered burns. This healing process necessitates adequate protein intake to support recovery. Additionally, wound healing is essential for patients undergoing surgical procedures, especially those related to head and neck tumors. The effectiveness of cicatrizaci&#243;n is significantly influenced by nutritional support, highlighting the importance of proper dietary management in promoting recovery for these patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02,b3bff0edc314389f2ac432a753fec9f7</data>
      <data key="d3">1113</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2304</data>
      <data key="d7">3b3570d68b5642a5b7aa065a0a9e46ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINAS A, C Y D">
      <data key="d0">NUTRIENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Suplementos recomendados para pacientes quemados, importantes para la funci&#243;n inmune y la reparaci&#243;n de heridas</data>
      <data key="d2">b3bff0edc314389f2ac432a753fec9f7</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
