    <node id="NPT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NPT, which stands for Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral Total or Nutritional Parenteral Therapy, is a method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to eat or absorb nutrients through their gastrointestinal tract. This nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients during their hospital stay and is also utilized for infants who cannot receive adequate nutrition through oral feeding. NPT is specifically indicated for individuals with conditions such as severe pancreatitis, where oral intake is not possible or tolerated. Overall, NPT serves as a vital intervention for those requiring nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d2">319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,acd36e6dbcd98757c4cf33ff090764ee,b2b9da64e886eb0b5a8b332d2ba9c7fb,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb,e98937544f56006f5d327136c593c969</data>
      <data key="d3">1086</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">2326</data>
      <data key="d7">5c2ffdba90c9430b802c8100258da6c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE AUT&#211;LOGO">
