    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS MONOINSATURADOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;CIDOS GRASOS MONOINSATURADOS, or monounsaturated fatty acids, are a type of fat recognized for their favorable impact on cardiovascular health. These fats, including notable examples like oleic acid, are integral components of the Mediterranean diet, which is associated with improved cardiovascular outcomes. They are also included in enteral nutrition formulas, highlighting their role in managing diabetes effectively. 

The health benefits of monounsaturated fatty acids can vary based on their dietary sources; for instance, fats derived from virgin olive oil are particularly noted for their positive effects. Overall, these healthy fats are encouraged in dietary recommendations aimed at enhancing lipid profiles and are considered beneficial or neutral concerning cardiovascular risk. Furthermore, they can be consumed without restriction in children's diets, emphasizing their importance for overall health and well-being. Thus, incorporating &#225;cidos grasos monoinsaturados into daily nutrition is advocated for better cardiovascular health and effective dietary management of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,8d1eb00b23450a2f2cb1243ea32aa36f,c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27,d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061</data>
