    <node id="ENTERAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enteral nutrition is a medical practice that involves the delivery of nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract. This method is particularly beneficial for patients who are unable to eat normally due to various health conditions. It is commonly used in individuals with liver disease, diabetes, and those who have experienced burns. Additionally, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the care of critically ill patients and is often utilized in postoperative care. By delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines, enteral nutrition ensures that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their recovery and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">36c1edffe986e2f70996b6e440e11213,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,762a80a4c9f24d778b79fdd596f343e3,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97,9ec3bf4d23f9f4fca8984c81d95aac41,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,9f0dc667db1447b9e51420cc6ba091c9,abd9a4b801dbdaca1708f0e22331a829,ceb66a898fed371e013171c43a87e1d1,d26aec24f3f8c930c1c4b1d464bacd6b,f902ee3930fcc849fa131b58d6e4933d,fb24bf4c9fcf60bbc1dd56cd60ba0a47</data>
      <data key="d3">1232</data>
