    </node>
    <node id="PARENTERAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parenteral Nutrition is a medical method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to obtain nutrition through eating or absorb food through their digestive tract. This approach is particularly crucial for preterm infants and critically ill patients who cannot feed normally. By bypassing the gastrointestinal tract, Parenteral Nutrition delivers essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, making it an essential intervention for individuals with severe health conditions, such as acute pancreatitis or those who have specific medical needs that prevent oral consumption of food.

This method is employed in various medical settings when enteral feeding is not possible or sufficient, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrition to support their recovery and overall health. Parenteral Nutrition is also relevant for certain diabetes patients who may struggle to consume food orally. Overall, it serves as a vital nutritional support system for individuals facing significant health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">33900ea313cbdf466c2bebc1f587e2bf,52d93d6adba464a2397ddec01d152840,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,6efaddddefe1cf5ab78825e1d8c53cab,719fff2d16bc334d3d4b53f070373a10,762a80a4c9f24d778b79fdd596f343e3,7c60735b2451e2d314fe6c5377b7a79d,9ec3bf4d23f9f4fca8984c81d95aac41,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,ceb66a898fed371e013171c43a87e1d1,d26aec24f3f8c930c1c4b1d464bacd6b,deb3afabda4adf3c61e4b9e1545103cc,fb24bf4c9fcf60bbc1dd56cd60ba0a47,fbeb9736ced2a2a020bdb39bdd10de0d</data>
