      <data key="d6">2403</data>
      <data key="d7">ca9c55ad73334ce6a5efe22bdf6ea416</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIFARMACIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polifarmacia, also known as polypharmacy, is characterized by the concurrent use of five or more medications by an individual, particularly among the elderly population. This practice can significantly impact nutrient absorption and metabolism, potentially leading to adverse health outcomes. Additionally, the use of multiple medications can contribute to frailty in older adults, highlighting the importance of careful management and monitoring of medication regimens in this demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">1052683f23a0c9825af9c5c1d39ceb2c,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2404</data>
      <data key="d7">3c1d4e6c31b847dd99b8ea9474111306</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POBREZA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Poverty is a cause of nutritional deficits and associated diseases in the elderly.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2405</data>
      <data key="d7">e64480d76a464d7b92953c0edf782afb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES" refers to a set of dietary guidelines designed to promote health and prevent chronic diseases through proper dietary practices. These recommendations encompass various age groups, including specific guidelines for the elderly, which address their unique energy requirements, water needs, and macronutrient distribution. Additionally, "RECOMENDACIONES NUTRICIONALES" includes dietary guidelines aimed at children, focusing on fostering health and nutrition from a young age. Furthermore, these recommendations also target the prevention and management of specific health conditions, such as kidney stones and hyperuricemia, highlighting their comprehensive approach to nutrition and health management across different populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1382</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2406</data>
      <data key="d7">02f35e3287d448eca0dba720666a0728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMENDACIONES ENERG&#201;TICAS EN EL ANCIANO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Energy recommendations for the elderly based on age and gender, detailing daily caloric needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1382</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2407</data>
      <data key="d7">56c0498e0a344d478af9df4cafd2a590</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMILIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "familia" encompasses the group of individuals who provide essential support to children and elderly individuals in various healthcare contexts. In the case of children, the family is instrumental in the process of enteral nutrition, where their education and training in managing this technique are vital for the child's well-being. For patients requiring home parenteral nutrition, the family plays a crucial role in overseeing the treatment and ensuring adherence to the prescribed regimen. Overall, the family serves as a fundamental support system, actively involved in the care and assistance of both children and elderly individuals in their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1382</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2408</data>
      <data key="d7">8090335d3b7044e4bb8102e95e863d15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROMES GERI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#205;NDROMES GERI&#193;TRICOS refers to a group of clinical conditions that commonly affect the elderly population. These syndromes include delirium, falls, immobility, incontinence, and pressure ulcers, all of which are associated with frailty in older adults. Geriatric syndromes are often interrelated with malnutrition and other health issues, highlighting the complex health challenges faced by this demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2409</data>
      <data key="d7">e50bc7a56fd648c8b35675149b246d83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DETERIORO COGNITIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cognitive decline is a common issue in the elderly that can be exacerbated by malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6180d67d6fdf45ff73aa2a63a8e3f74</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
