    <node id="DENSIDAD MINERAL &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DENSIDAD MINERAL &#211;SEA" refers to bone mineral density (DMO), a crucial measure used to assess bone strength and predict fracture risk, particularly in patients with osteoporosis. It is an important factor in evaluating the risk of osteoporosis and fractures in older adults. Additionally, DMO is often assessed in patients with Anorexia Nervosa to evaluate their bone health. The term also encompasses the amount of mineral matter per square centimeter of bones, which can be influenced by nutritional interventions in various patient populations, including those with respiratory diseases and celiac disease. Furthermore, DMO can improve in children with glycogen storage diseases when dietary recommendations are adhered to. Overall, "densidad mineral &#243;sea" serves as an indicator of bone health, with adequate nutrition playing a significant role in enhancing bone density, especially in geriatric patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98,2ad1c3591301bd2ea6f99c3782714d69,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
