      <data key="d7">a175d802f06e42d890657e510c8b68d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERVENCI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"INTERVENCI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL" refers to the process of evaluating and modifying a patient's diet to enhance their nutritional status, particularly in individuals with specific health challenges such as cancer. This intervention encompasses a range of actions designed to improve nutritional intake and overall health, with a focus on preventing and reversing nutritional deficiencies. It is especially critical for patients at risk of malnutrition, including those who are frail elderly or suffering from obesity and metabolic diseases. Nutritional intervention strategies may also include dietary changes aimed at managing conditions like hypertension, exemplified by approaches such as the DASH diet. Overall, the goal of "INTERVENCI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL" is to improve health outcomes and quality of life for patients through tailored dietary modifications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2689c33de87eab465f004fff5f0530b8,3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">1633</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">2434</data>
      <data key="d7">172c7f931fc04620b3d4faddf44eef17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSEJO DIET&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "CONSEJO DIET&#201;TICO" refers to dietary advice aimed at enhancing nutritional intake for patients, particularly those dealing with specific health challenges. This intervention includes recommendations on meal frequency, food preparation, and hydration. It is especially beneficial for patients with esophageal cancer, as it assists them in managing symptoms such as dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) and anorexia by making necessary adjustments to their food intake. Overall, the consejo diet&#233;tico serves as a crucial support system for improving the dietary habits and overall well-being of patients facing these health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">397cb82cce268866351c44a5b38ccb8b,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1140</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2435</data>
      <data key="d7">d7319965e42341b1be2751f84ee7d54a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONTROL FARMACOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pharmacological control involves using medications to stimulate appetite and manage symptoms related to malnutrition in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1082</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2436</data>
      <data key="d7">7eb0b7e532ab4e4eb3e8f8f79524db83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COTICOSTEROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Corticosteroids like Prednisone and Dexamethasone are used to stimulate appetite in patients with a life expectancy of more than four weeks.</data>
      <data key="d2">d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1082</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2437</data>
      <data key="d7">2c958eb696114a43868a1b6c32bbec33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSICOESTIMULANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Psychostimulants such as Methylphenidate are used to enhance appetite but may cause side effects like sleep disturbances and anxiety.</data>
      <data key="d2">d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1082</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2438</data>
      <data key="d7">d042a284b64d4fbfb7038019f2c632f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROGEST&#193;GENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Progestogens, including compounds such as Megestrol acetate and levonorgestrel, are a class of hormones that play significant roles in various physiological processes. Megestrol acetate is particularly noted for its effectiveness in increasing appetite and weight in patients, especially those with a life expectancy of more than three months. On the other hand, levonorgestrel, another type of progestogen, can influence androgen levels and has been associated with conditions such as hirsutism. Additionally, progestogens are known to affect sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels and are integral to the regulation of the menstrual cycle. Overall, progestogens are versatile hormones with important implications for health and medical treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1356</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2439</data>
      <data key="d7">9211fcad60064babaa0efa1cac193eab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIPROHEPTADINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ciproheptadina is a potent antagonist of histamine and serotonin, primarily recognized for its role as an antihistamine. It has been evaluated for its potential to increase appetite and caloric intake, particularly in patients suffering from malnutrition and advanced cancer. While Ciproheptadina has demonstrated some effectiveness in slightly increasing appetite among patients, its overall impact on weight gain is limited. As an antiserotonergic agent, it has been observed to have a modest effect on appetite enhancement, making it a consideration in the management of appetite-related issues in specific patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da</data>
      <data key="d3">1119</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2440</data>
      <data key="d7">f61b20b0085a49839a6523517f3a84d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFATO DE HIDRACINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfato de Hidracina, also known as hydrazine sulfate, is primarily utilized as an appetite stimulant in patients with cancer, although its effectiveness can vary among individuals. Additionally, it functions as an inhibitor of phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase, the initial enzyme involved in gluconeogenesis, which may enhance carbohydrate metabolism. This dual role highlights its potential therapeutic applications in managing symptoms related to cancer and metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,d3f53b7b7352e8ba2fd9dc8be977648c</data>
      <data key="d3">1119</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2441</data>
      <data key="d7">37296d45a392469598aa7e1d601c9096</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HALOPERIDOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Haloperidol is a butyrophenone used for vomiting, especially effective in cases related to opioid use.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2442</data>
      <data key="d7">14fc5b63ecc34fe8b0e26c12622ad28e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCOPOLAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Escopolamina is an anticholinergic medication that acts on the vomiting center and gastrointestinal tract.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">1112</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2443</data>
      <data key="d7">27eb2783e963412990880bd83d78e69c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OCTE&#211;TRIDO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Octe&#243;trido is an antisecretory medication effective in providing symptomatic relief for abdominal obstruction.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2444</data>
      <data key="d7">1d8d327385cc40c1a50e1882816e2af3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDAS ENTERALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sondas enterales are tubes used for enteral nutrition when oral intake is insufficient.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">1194</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2445</data>
      <data key="d7">b0dabc43a1b649cd9cbb5029bc51a8ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA ESTANDAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dieta estandar is a standard diet designed to meet patient needs while avoiding excessive lactose content.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2446</data>
      <data key="d7">735c0ac1d0ad4beaa019f1a78861048e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NAUSEAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NAUSEAS are a symptom characterized by a sensation of unease and discomfort in the stomach, often leading to the urge to vomit. They can manifest in various medical contexts, including as a symptom in patients with acute pancreatitis, where they contribute to a reduction in oral intake. Additionally, NAUSEAS can occur as a gastrointestinal complication in patients receiving enteral nutrition, negatively impacting their overall well-being and the effectiveness of their treatment. They may also indicate underlying issues such as dehydration or physical overexertion. Furthermore, NAUSEAS are recognized as moderate neurological symptoms in patients with hyponatremia, highlighting their significance in a broader range of health concerns. Overall, NAUSEAS are a common symptom that can exacerbate existing health issues and complicate patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">364aa13581a973c2e55c25191bad27cc,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d3">1092</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2447</data>
      <data key="d7">b78f019a306a41e589c392d31f773abe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECCI&#211;N F&#218;NGICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Infecci&#243;n f&#250;ngica refers to infections caused by fungi, which can lead to various health issues including xerostom&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654</data>
      <data key="d3">1121</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2448</data>
      <data key="d7">34c65830174f402485c0070d143f96d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECCIONES VIRALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Infecciones virales are infections caused by viruses that can lead to a variety of symptoms, including nausea and vomiting. Additionally, these viral infections have been implicated as potential environmental triggers for the onset of Type 1 Diabetes, suggesting a broader impact on health beyond immediate symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,ed9fbb82a9162d601f8370ef97810e54</data>
      <data key="d3">1121</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2449</data>
      <data key="d7">1bb76c38689544adb116a070e6dfafdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XEROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">XEROSTOM&#205;A refers to the condition of dry mouth, which is characterized by a lack of saliva. This condition can significantly impact the ability of individuals, particularly cancer patients, to eat and drink comfortably. Xerostom&#237;a is often a side effect experienced by those undergoing cancer treatment, leading to difficulties in maintaining proper nutrition and hydration.</data>
      <data key="d2">42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9562f39f9e78644164daeff3177a2f84</data>
      <data key="d3">1121</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2450</data>
      <data key="d7">11b26e4227224719bc69d8ae17e47bf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPODERMOCLISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A method of subcutaneous rehydration that is preferred when oral intake is restricted, requiring changes every 4-5 days due to absorption issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
