    <node id="DEXTROSA-EQUIVALENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dextrose equivalent (DE) is a measure used to determine the length of dextrin maltose chains in nutritional formulas, impacting digestibility and osmolarity.</data>
      <data key="d2">7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae</data>
      <data key="d3">1735</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2473</data>
      <data key="d7">3052b0cd2da245a999433477632c1214</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS POLIM&#201;RICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;RMULAS POLIM&#201;RICAS are complete nutritional formulas designed for both pediatric and adult patients, often flavored to enhance palatability. These formulas are specifically formulated for individuals who do not have alterations in intestinal absorption or digestion. They consist of whole proteins and are indicated for patients with minimally affected gastrointestinal function. F&#211;RMULAS POLIM&#201;RICAS are utilized in enteral nutrition, containing non-hydrolyzed macronutrients that are suitable for patients with adequate intestinal function. These nutritional products are generally well tolerated and are commonly used in critical care settings, making them a standard choice in enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb,2def4be9506db96f8bdfe9e3ba6f9b6f,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b,7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae,7b13bde26d33b4316c3183dd027ed909,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87</data>
      <data key="d3">1183</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">2474</data>
      <data key="d7">a87eaa6a76a74f418e28481322224f4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS OLIGOM&#201;RICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;RMULAS OLIGOM&#201;RICAS son preparaciones nutricionales que contienen prote&#237;nas hidrolizadas, dise&#241;adas espec&#237;ficamente para pacientes con funci&#243;n digestiva alterada. Estas f&#243;rmulas son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay alteraciones en la digesti&#243;n o absorci&#243;n intestinal, lo que las hace adecuadas para individuos con necesidades diet&#233;ticas espec&#237;ficas. En particular, las f&#243;rmulas oligom&#233;ricas, tambi&#233;n conocidas como f&#243;rmulas de p&#233;ptidos, son especialmente beneficiosas para ni&#241;os que requieren un soporte nutricional adaptado a sus necesidades digestivas particulares.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b,7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1183</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2475</data>
      <data key="d7">78ff31cdbdd44748bb2cb9714dac22ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS ELEMENTALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;RMULAS ELEMENTALES are highly processed nutritional products primarily composed of synthetic amino acids. They are specifically designed for infants and children who suffer from severe allergies or malabsorption issues, particularly in cases where traditional hydrolyzed formulas are ineffective. These formulas are indicated for digestive conditions that do not respond to oligomeric formulas. However, it is important to note that elemental formulas are characterized by their high osmolarity and cost, which raises concerns about their use and suggests that they should be avoided when possible.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,a562e90891c11da0293bc7de511acc8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1183</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2476</data>
      <data key="d7">3cf7b9ac8c734ad3a1dde1f791b509d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS HIPERPROTEICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperproteic formulas contain a higher protein content, indicated for specific medical conditions in older children.</data>
      <data key="d2">7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae</data>
      <data key="d3">1183</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2477</data>
      <data key="d7">5adcbef18b304beda4e914e37d922f5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENSIDAD CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DENSIDAD CAL&#211;RICA refers to the amount of energy provided per volume of formula, which is essential for meeting the dietary needs of children. It is defined as the quantity of calories per milliliter of formula and is classified into three categories: hypocaloric, normocaloric, and hypercaloric. This classification helps in determining the appropriate formula to ensure that children receive the necessary caloric intake for their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb,7796f48230d374753b744d8e5fb1e8ae</data>
      <data key="d3">1183</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2478</data>
      <data key="d7">382b250468f24fb9be7f65aa2beeb3a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PEDIATR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La pediatr&#237;a es la rama de la medicina que se ocupa de la salud y las enfermedades de los ni&#241;os. Esta especialidad m&#233;dica abarca el tratamiento de diversas condiciones, incluyendo trastornos alimentarios y nutricionales, asegurando as&#237; un enfoque integral en el cuidado de la salud infantil.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2479</data>
      <data key="d7">acb50d70c22344788c41ce8d5f711ade</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS COMPLETAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las f&#243;rmulas completas son preparaciones alimenticias dise&#241;adas para proporcionar todos los nutrientes necesarios a los pacientes, especialmente en pediatr&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2480</data>
      <data key="d7">125f86b26dc04974a00cefcdf6463ca2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TABLA 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TABLA 1 is a comprehensive resource that encompasses various aspects of nutritional management and assessment. It serves as a record tracking the evolution of a patient's weight, height, BMI, and glycemic control over time, which is crucial for monitoring health progress. Additionally, TABLA 1 includes a list of foods that are discouraged in a broad low-sodium diet, emphasizing dietary restrictions for better health outcomes. 

In the context of pediatric care, TABLA 1 presents the main clinical indications for enteral nutrition, highlighting its importance in managing nutritional needs in children. Furthermore, it details various nitrogen solutions used for parenteral nutrition, providing information on their composition and nutritional values, which is essential for healthcare providers in administering appropriate nutritional support.

Moreover, TABLA 1 provides mandatory nutritional information per 100 g/100 ml, ensuring that users have access to standardized data for dietary planning. Lastly, it outlines the Mini Nutritional Assessment-Short Form (MNA-SF) criteria, which are used to evaluate nutritional status, thereby aiding in the identification of individuals at risk of malnutrition. Overall, TABLA 1 serves as a vital tool in the fields of nutrition and dietetics, offering a multifaceted approach to dietary management and assessment.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f,630fa9125532edf1c291507de8298869,79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
      <data key="d3">1576</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">2481</data>
      <data key="d7">8b69514e10ce41fea0b35594697fbe2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N ORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alimentaci&#243;n oral refers to the process of consuming food by mouth. This method may be transitioned to after enteral nutrition in stable patients. It is particularly significant in the management of patients with intestinal failure, as it plays a crucial role in their nutritional care. However, the ability to engage in alimentaci&#243;n oral can be affected in patients experiencing malnutrition or gastrointestinal issues. Therefore, the safety of oral feeding is often evaluated in patients who have been receiving enteral nutrition to ensure that they can safely consume food through the mouth.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2482</data>
      <data key="d7">d7876f19b35f4a8b9f0f36f621cf37f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA" refers to a range of psychological conditions that significantly impact eating behaviors and the relationship individuals have with food. These disorders, which include anorexia nerviosa (AN) among others, are characterized by abnormal or disturbed eating habits. They can complicate the management of obesity and necessitate specialized treatment approaches. Additionally, eating disorders can develop in children who are subjected to prolonged enteral nutrition, further affecting their relationship with food. Overall, "TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA" encompasses various psychological disorders that require careful attention and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">2483</data>
      <data key="d7">c6ff26b5bcbf4f52977b5bf1da675ae1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS HIPOCAL&#211;RICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las f&#243;rmulas hipocal&#243;ricas son preparaciones alimenticias que no tienen indicaciones pedi&#225;tricas espec&#237;ficas.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2484</data>
      <data key="d7">a923f27d46f84632a6f4380c7b41036c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS NORMOCAL&#211;RICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las f&#243;rmulas normocal&#243;ricas son indicadas en la mayor&#237;a de los pacientes pedi&#225;tricos, proporcionando un aporte cal&#243;rico adecuado.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2485</data>
      <data key="d7">8581539650084bd99e706b0d8eef42b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS HIPERCAL&#211;RICAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;RMULAS HIPERCAL&#211;RICAS son preparaciones nutricionales espec&#237;ficamente dise&#241;adas para ofrecer un alto contenido cal&#243;rico. Estas f&#243;rmulas son especialmente &#250;tiles para pacientes que presentan descompensaci&#243;n hidr&#243;pica y son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay un aumento de las necesidades cal&#243;ricas, como en el caso de pacientes con desnutrici&#243;n. Su objetivo principal es proporcionar la energ&#237;a necesaria para apoyar la recuperaci&#243;n y el bienestar de estos pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">029b25f481d41458f45f1711f98c970f,169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088</data>
      <data key="d3">1114</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2486</data>
      <data key="d7">8edb4e57802b432696e865d12f583eff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDAS G&#193;STRICAS Y YEYUNALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las sondas g&#225;stricas y yeyunales son dispositivos utilizados para la administraci&#243;n de nutrici&#243;n enteral, adapt&#225;ndose a las necesidades del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2487</data>
      <data key="d7">1d36432d253541e99eb3352b47b95ba5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;LEO G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#237;leo g&#225;strico es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica caracterizada por el retraso en el vaciamiento del est&#243;mago, frecuentemente observado en el periodo postoperatorio inmediato. Esta condici&#243;n implica una obstrucci&#243;n en el proceso de vaciamiento g&#225;strico, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici&#243;n enteral para asegurar la adecuada ingesta de nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2488</data>
      <data key="d7">15ec10bc432148e39dfaf22265f20f0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las f&#237;stulas pancre&#225;ticas son conexiones anormales que pueden formarse entre el p&#225;ncreas y otros &#243;rganos, a menudo requiriendo nutrici&#243;n enteral para evitar la estimulaci&#243;n de la secreci&#243;n pancre&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
