    <node id="PICA PERCUT&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pica percut&#225;nea is a medical procedure used for gastrostomy in patients, except those with severe thoracic and spinal deformities, malrotation, previous abdominal surgery, obstructions, and esophageal stenosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2491</data>
      <data key="d7">7adbed332c604f87956126eef7f59a42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDAS DE GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrostomy tubes are medical devices used for feeding patients who cannot eat by mouth, which can be replaced after three months once the gastrocutaneous fistula is formed.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2492</data>
      <data key="d7">ff75dcfb43274d148a8fa3bc9f755b20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMAS DE INFUSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Infusion systems are methods used to deliver nutrients to patients, including gravity drip and pump systems, with specific applications in pediatric and critical care.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d9237f72732f1f51141fa79be271c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1149</data>
