    <node id="SEGHNP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SEGHNP, the Spanish Society of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition, is an organization dedicated to advancing pediatric nutrition standards. It collaborates with SENPE to develop and enhance guidelines related to pediatric nutrition, ensuring that best practices are established and followed in the field. Through its efforts, SEGHNP plays a crucial role in shaping the nutritional care and guidelines for children.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036</data>
      <data key="d3">1843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2506</data>
      <data key="d7">c7b6886bc61f4ea8a92b475cb022c4a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANECIPN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ANECIPN is the National Association of Pediatric Nutrition Specialists in Spain, dedicated to the field of pediatric enteral nutrition. The organization collaborates with SENPE and SEGHNP to establish and promote standards for enteral nutrition, ensuring that best practices are followed in the care of pediatric patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036</data>
      <data key="d3">1843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2507</data>
      <data key="d7">32dfc9aee0c5453d80708a4c8ee25561</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SECP, or Spanish Society of Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is an organization that plays a significant role in the consensus on pediatric enteral nutrition, collaborating closely with SENPE. It is dedicated to establishing and promoting standards for pediatric nutrition, ensuring that best practices are followed in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036</data>
      <data key="d3">1843</data>
