      <data key="d7">9b9efd829bee44088f50ed8a9f5d8b0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EDAD, which stands for "Elderly Demographic Age Data," plays a crucial role in understanding age-related health considerations. It provides recommendations for catheter sizes and fluid intake tailored to the needs of older patients. Furthermore, EDAD is identified as a significant predictor of the necessity for enteral nutrition, especially in individuals aged 80 years and older. This highlights the importance of age in influencing surgical outcomes and underscores the need for age-specific medical strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b,781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff,b0ffa7260c4fc20462ad4c9bedcbfae7</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2535</data>
      <data key="d7">442d7966795844e39f2f1babd3e7ee68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLORHEXIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Chlorhexidine is a versatile antiseptic widely utilized for various disinfection purposes. It is employed for skin disinfection prior to surgical procedures and for sterilizing surgical instruments, ensuring a sterile environment in medical settings. Additionally, chlorhexidine is used for disinfection before venipuncture, making it essential in clinical practices. Furthermore, it serves an important role in oral hygiene, particularly for patients in critical care settings, helping to maintain oral health and prevent infections. Overall, chlorhexidine is a crucial antiseptic in both surgical and healthcare environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,61eea56f443c7bb2509edd6f42af2643,781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff</data>
      <data key="d3">642</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2536</data>
      <data key="d7">e58b563ab18a4bcc830a83ca91033181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFLAMACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inflammation is a physiological response that serves as a common complication associated with venous access. It can significantly impact the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with chronic kidney disease. This response plays a crucial role in the body's healing processes but can also lead to adverse effects in certain medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2537</data>
      <data key="d7">1366ce459de84607bd35dc313c79f1ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLEBITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phlebitis is a common complication associated with venous access</data>
      <data key="d2">781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff</data>
