    <node id="FIEBRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FIEBRE, or fever, is a clinical condition characterized by an increase in body temperature. This condition can lead to heightened energy expenditure, particularly in pediatric patients, which may subsequently elevate their nutritional requirements. Fever often accompanies acute diarrhea and serves as an important indicator for conducting stool cultures in specific situations. In hospitalized children, fever can significantly impact their nutritional treatment by increasing both energy and fluid needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">1027</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">2543</data>
      <data key="d7">270d835a0de747e489842b95445395ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insuficiencia cardiaca is a medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood sufficiently to meet the body's needs. This condition often leads to fluid retention and various complications. It is commonly associated with heart disease and may necessitate adjustments in fluid and nutrient administration, particularly in the context of parenteral nutrition for children.</data>
      <data key="d2">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c</data>
      <data key="d3">1423</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2544</data>
      <data key="d7">1beeaf2a9034470daa5edfba6567ecf6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EDMAS refers to the presence of edema, a condition that can complicate the assessment of nutritional status in patients. Edema can influence the fluid and electrolyte needs in children, thereby affecting their nutritional treatment. It is also a clinical manifestation of congestive heart failure, which is associated with sodium and water retention. Additionally, edema can be a sign of malnutrition, particularly in patients with celiac disease if not properly managed.</data>
      <data key="d2">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2545</data>
      <data key="d7">87329b14e3644b5094e0a9333dac4b4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINOSTERIL-N HEPA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A specialized amino acid solution used for patients with liver failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
