      <data key="d6">2547</data>
      <data key="d7">8eff659097d04aae9cc222c096d06710</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLORO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CLORO, also known as chloride, is a vital mineral and electrolyte that plays a crucial role in maintaining the body's electrolyte balance and fluid regulation. It is typically found in the body at levels ranging from 98 to 106 mEq/l. The recommended daily intake of chloride varies by age, with specific dietary reference intake levels outlined in health guidelines for different age groups, including pediatric patients.

Chloride is particularly important in the care of neonates, where it is managed alongside sodium and potassium levels. It is an essential component of parenteral nutrition solutions, which are critical for maintaining acid-base balance and fluid balance in patients who cannot receive nutrition through traditional means. In pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, chloride is required in specific amounts to support their growth and development.

Additionally, CLORO is utilized in medical treatments, especially in cases of metabolic alkalosis, highlighting its significance in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, chloride is an indispensable electrolyte necessary for numerous bodily functions, including the maintenance of acid-base balance and fluid homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">15ffbfba2decfecb69a26bcb1e4bd898,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6,cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">583</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">2548</data>
      <data key="d7">61f55ce44c044d55aec9ee096ecf565f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPOFUNDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LIPOFUNDINA is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for use in parenteral nutrition. It is a 20% fat emulsion that combines soybean oil and medium-chain triglycerides, which enhances tolerance, particularly in newborns. This mixed lipid preparation, introduced in the late 1980s, consists of a balanced formulation of 50% medium-chain triglycerides and 50% long-chain triglycerides derived from soybean oil. LIPOFUNDINA serves to meet the lipid requirements in pediatric nutrition, making it a vital component in intravenous nutrition therapies.</data>
      <data key="d2">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">659</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">2549</data>
      <data key="d7">a34b37e6b65c4836afaf36a75e8380ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMOFLIPID">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SMOFLIPID is a brand of lipid emulsion specifically designed for parenteral nutrition. It is formulated as a 20% lipid emulsion that combines soybean oil, medium-chain triglycerides, olive oil, and fish oil, creating a balanced mixture aimed at providing a more physiological composition for nutritional support. This fat emulsion is particularly beneficial for intravenous nutrition in newborns, as it supplies essential fatty acids and calories necessary for their growth and development. Notably, SMOFLIPID is recognized for its high concentration of alpha-tocopherol and is rich in docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) and eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA), which are important components for overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd,87da0f3b46604498629565db45667b3b,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">659</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">2550</data>
      <data key="d7">8626c56f94d843059f350cbdc8524135</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLICEROFOSFATO S&#211;DICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sodium glycerophosphate is a compound used to prevent precipitation of calcium-phosphate salts in parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d2">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2551</data>
      <data key="d7">cbbb9425610e46b1af7cd537c90923c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOLIBDENO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MOLIBDENO, or molybdenum, is a trace element that serves as a cofactor for various enzymes involved in the metabolism of pyrimidines and purines. It is found in foods such as milk and legumes. Molybdenum is essential for health, but deficiencies can occur, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease, where it may contribute to health complications. Additionally, in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, the intake of molybdenum should be limited in cases of renal insufficiency. Overall, molybdenum plays a significant role in enzyme function, and specific dietary recommendations are advised to ensure adequate intake while avoiding potential excesses in vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d,eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">583</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2552</data>
      <data key="d7">99bd6092499344db88e516676af9a1e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IODO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Iodine is a trace element essential for thyroid hormone production, with specific dosage recommendations for pediatric patients</data>
      <data key="d2">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2553</data>
      <data key="d7">518bc32fb1fd46d6ab3125919fb3a8a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINOVEN INFANT&#174;">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Aminoven Infant&#174; is a pediatric amino acid solution specifically designed for the nutritional therapy of infants. It contains a carefully formulated blend of amino acids that supports the nutritional needs of infants up to 1 year old. This product is essential for providing the necessary nutrients to promote healthy growth and development in young children.</data>
      <data key="d2">a6e7937ce59bfc2b38e9ed2acf3e991c,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc</data>
