    <node id="HEPARINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Heparina is an anticoagulant medication primarily used to prevent and treat blood clots, particularly in patients at risk of thromboembolic events such as deep vein thrombosis. It is often utilized in medical settings, especially in conjunction with intravenous nutrition administration. Heparina is sometimes included in parenteral nutrition solutions, although its use is not routine due to potential risks associated with mixing. 

In particular, Heparina is employed to prolong the use of catheters and to mitigate complications related to catheter obstruction and sepsis. It may also be used alongside taurolidine in parenteral nutrition to prevent clotting. Specifically, Heparina can be administered via central lines at a concentration of 0.5 UI/ml, highlighting its importance in managing catheter-related complications. Overall, Heparina plays a crucial role in enhancing patient safety and efficacy in various medical treatments involving intravenous and parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,222519e556047fafecd61c2964aaaeed,622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
