    <node id="HIPERTENSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERTENSI&#211;N is a medical condition characterized by consistently elevated blood pressure, which can lead to various health complications. It is defined as a condition in which the force of the blood against the artery walls is too high. This chronic condition is often associated with several health issues, including kidney stones and cardiometabolic disorders, and may also be linked to renal insufficiency. 

There are different types of hypertension, including hipertensi&#243;n de origen endocrinol&#243;gico, which refers to hypertension caused by endocrine disorders. The condition can be influenced by dietary factors, particularly sodium intake, as increased salt consumption has been linked to elevated blood pressure levels. 

In some cases, hypertension can be severe and resistant to treatment, necessitating specific dietary considerations. Additionally, it has been noted that breastfeeding may be associated with a lower risk of developing hypertension. Overall, HIPERTENSI&#211;N is a significant health concern that requires careful management and monitoring in patients, as it is often part of their medical history.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3,261db9bb173f461ca4f26fd087d3da2a,319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d,47ba8105b81c59f81a9038446898d200,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3,d0a687d823ff2f3d5cb0f20b01d8530e,e321db63d9b561eb98a4f01853b141ad,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
