    <node id="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enfermedad cardiovascular" refers to a group of medical conditions that affect the heart and blood vessels. This term encompasses a wide range of disorders, including those linked to dyslipidemia, obesity, diabetes, metabolic syndrome, and hypertension. The European Society of Cardiology emphasizes the importance of managing risk factors associated with cardiovascular disease, which is a significant health issue globally.

Cardiovascular disease is often influenced by dietary habits, particularly the intake of trans fatty acids and saturated fats, as well as lifestyle factors. It is also associated with metabolic disorders such as hyperuricemia and can contribute to complications in patients with diabetes, leading to increased morbidity and mortality. Additionally, there is evidence suggesting that breastfeeding may reduce the prevalence of certain cardiovascular conditions.

The condition is also linked to renal issues, such as kidney stones, and is a risk factor for familial combined hyperlipidemia. Overall, "enfermedad cardiovascular" represents a critical area of concern in public health, necessitating careful monitoring and management to mitigate its impact on individuals' health.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,5c11ed246e1a48261910b9b71b65014c,62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8,64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,7e1b90e2c8714b39e283be229f6d5de3,7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,ce43a9a4cdf2497b2f984547a2787fff,cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c,d0a687d823ff2f3d5cb0f20b01d8530e,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e,e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc,ed97532e0b848baf08ee24448e340f98,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
      <data key="d3">1399</data>
