    <node id="UNICEF">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The United Nations Children's Fund (UNICEF), also known as the United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund, is an agency dedicated to providing humanitarian and developmental aid to children around the globe. UNICEF focuses on improving the lives of children and their families, addressing critical issues such as child mortality, particularly in relation to health challenges like diarrhea. The agency advocates for interventions such as zinc supplementation in cases of acute diarrhea, highlighting its commitment to enhancing child health and well-being. Through its various initiatives, UNICEF aims to ensure that every child has the opportunity to thrive and reach their full potential.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
