    </node>
    <node id="DIGITAL EDUCATIONAL PUBLISHING, INC.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Digital Educational Publishing, INC. is the publisher of the book that contains information on human milk and infant nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">537</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2596</data>
      <data key="d7">47c2d11b0d72420ab100388955bb740d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRETERM INFANT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A preterm infant is a baby born before the 37th week of pregnancy, who may require special nutritional considerations, including the composition of human milk.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">538</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2597</data>
      <data key="d7">2151682b61f349f19f30c79d99dc3cd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPOSICI&#211;N DE LA LECHE MATERNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Composici&#243;n de la leche materna refers to the detailed analysis of the nutritional components of breast milk, including energy, proteins, fats, and carbohydrates.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">537</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2598</data>
      <data key="d7">de3e0e993b9f493aa88250e46228edfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS Y VITAMINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Suplementos y vitaminas refers to the guidelines and recommendations for administering supplements and vitamins to infants, particularly in cases of excessive weight loss or dehydration.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">538</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2599</data>
      <data key="d7">3fc17316147e4ed4bb8e82c5335c9472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ingesta refers to the intake of food or nutrients by the infant, which is monitored to ensure adequate nutrition and growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">538</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2600</data>
      <data key="d7">e09d96dec2c744a0a27d385b22a359fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;RDIDA PONDERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">P&#233;rdida ponderal refers to the weight loss experienced by infants after birth, which is a critical factor in assessing their health and nutritional needs. Additionally, weight loss is a primary goal in the treatment of obesity, often requiring individualized strategies based on patient needs. This highlights the importance of understanding weight loss in different contexts, such as in newborns for health assessment and in adults for obesity management.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
      <data key="d3">538</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2601</data>
      <data key="d7">37e9ff105f364b6687c8676b6a55c0b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LECHE DE MADRES DE PRET&#201;RMINO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">ea5e972294754a47333efb4c580cf15c</data>
      <data key="d3">537</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2602</data>
      <data key="d7">3e835868934e45c983a721895d69fa88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMIT&#201; DE NUTRICI&#211;N DE LA AEP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Committee on Nutrition of the AEP provides recommendations for infant nutrition and supplementation, particularly regarding vitamin K and vitamin D for newborns.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2603</data>
      <data key="d7">9cc40d309d0346289e20258ad325ba42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPGHAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPGHAN, the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition, is an organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations on pediatric nutrition, particularly focusing on infants and children. It plays a crucial role in developing guidelines for pediatric parenteral nutrition, especially for vulnerable populations such as infants and newborns. Additionally, ESPGHAN is recognized for its contributions to the field through the publication of position papers, including those addressing intestinal failure and transplantation. The organization has also published specific recommendations regarding the composition of infant formulas, with notable guidelines released in 2005. Overall, ESPGHAN serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals involved in the nutritional care of children, ensuring that best practices are followed in pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,52d93d6adba464a2397ddec01d152840,89855c293083756b0ff7a0081f67e9fd,a0b6196d53d4eb1c8ca5b1a3a78e8fc7,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">2604</data>
      <data key="d7">399f45f6b314402a991d736fe1370bc3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTANCIA ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Artificial lactation refers to the use of industrially prepared formulas for infants when breastfeeding is not an option.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d3">378</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2605</data>
      <data key="d7">9e6a8ef2540e44f9ad545245fef5b15c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS ADAPTADAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;RMULAS ADAPTADAS are specialized nutritional products designed for infants who have allergies to cow's milk proteins. These adapted formulas serve as specially prepared milk substitutes for infants when breastfeeding is not possible or is contraindicated. They provide essential nutrients tailored to meet the dietary needs of sensitive infants, ensuring their health and growth in situations where traditional milk options are unsuitable.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,a562e90891c11da0293bc7de511acc8f</data>
      <data key="d3">378</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2606</data>
      <data key="d7">6730573b0fd6451f80dc13f7059ebaf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN REGULATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European regulation oversees the preparation of infant formulas, ensuring they meet nutritional needs for infants during their first six months of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1727</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2607</data>
      <data key="d7">42896367563c425ba0b1365a8228b434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOSE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactose is a sugar found in milk and dairy products, serving as the primary carbohydrate in infant formulas, which is essential for energy and growth in infants. While it is allowed in the diets of patients with certain glycogen storage diseases, it can also cause intolerance in some individuals, particularly those with celiac disease. For patients with lactose intolerance, lactose may need to be substituted with lactose-free options, and it is often excluded from formulas designed for infants with specific allergies or intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf,e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d3">454</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">2608</data>
      <data key="d7">3ad6e0167ec84928855a2421d9774a5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRETERM NEWBORN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Preterm newborns have increased nutritional needs compared to term newborns and are at risk of extrauterine malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1726</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2609</data>
      <data key="d7">1daf8d979978454e9aac9c8adf841ba9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOTHER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mothers play a crucial role in the early stages of a child's life, as they are advised to receive information on the proper preparation of infant formulas and the nutritional needs of their newborns. During pregnancy, mothers undergo significant physiological changes to support fetal development, ensuring the health and well-being of their unborn child. Additionally, in specific cases, such as that of a patient with a genetic condition, the mother may also be a carrier of genetic mutations, like the A243G mutation, and may face her own health challenges, including diabetes and hearing loss. This highlights the multifaceted responsibilities and health considerations that mothers navigate throughout pregnancy and beyond.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">2610</data>
      <data key="d7">02a51ca151d7448da5d44adcb990213a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NECROTIZING ENTEROCOLITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC) is a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect preterm newborns, with a relationship to feeding practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1726</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2611</data>
      <data key="d7">9165e89a937c4820973976a146275d67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BREAST MILK">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Breast milk provides numerous benefits to preterm newborns, including reduced mortality and lower rates of infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1726</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2612</data>
      <data key="d7">8d50f0ac0cd54d00a0c31937328c3f27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional guidelines are comprehensive recommendations designed to assist individuals and healthcare professionals in making informed dietary choices to promote health and prevent chronic diseases. These guidelines are particularly important in managing dietary intake for specific populations, such as renal patients and individuals with liver disease, ensuring that their unique nutritional needs are met. Additionally, nutritional guidelines aim to prevent nutritional deficiencies and support health outcomes in vulnerable populations, including preterm newborns who require adequate nutrition for growth. Overall, these guidelines serve as a crucial tool in both clinical settings and general health promotion, advocating for proper dietary practices that contribute to overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc,594e6f43e0098791036927da2623b2f5,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,70e4538100be270d06e7a3cdc254ba28,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,a826c03dcc41919d172b2e1ae8eeceb2,bb209dcfffac9c89dae0ad4ed2908d85,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3,c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf,da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127</data>
      <data key="d3">1725</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">2613</data>
      <data key="d7">fb58b760ce0a430486e9e7339dfda1aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFANT FORMULAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Infant formulas are specialized food products designed to meet the nutritional needs of infants, especially those who are not breastfed.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1727</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2614</data>
      <data key="d7">60d1bd4d694f423b80fe2ae47df86550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL EMERGENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional emergency refers to the critical situation where preterm newborns require immediate nutritional support to prevent malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1726</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2615</data>
      <data key="d7">9938dc8760634dff91248c4431546f40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL NEEDS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Nutritional needs encompass the dietary requirements essential for maintaining health across various populations. This includes the specific needs of older adults, who require adequate trace elements and vitamins to support their well-being. Additionally, nutritional needs vary significantly for preterm infants, whose dietary requirements differ from those of full-term newborns, necessitating careful consideration and tailored nutrition plans. Furthermore, for patients undergoing nutritional support, particularly in critical care settings, it is crucial to calculate and meet their specific dietary requirements to ensure optimal recovery and health outcomes. Overall, nutritional needs are diverse and must be addressed according to the unique requirements of different groups.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,c9bfa7bc5a1f4d1862e69908d6325dcf</data>
      <data key="d3">1726</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2616</data>
      <data key="d7">0d69e9e37bcc459290a396ebcb587031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LECHE MATERNA DONADA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Donated human milk (LMD) is recognized as a second option when maternal milk is unavailable, used under specific medical indications.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2617</data>
      <data key="d7">653fa6a3916249ee90cee6161678f81b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS DE PREMATUROS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Formulas designed for premature infants to meet their nutritional needs, providing higher calories, proteins, and minerals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1899</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2618</data>
      <data key="d7">de0425cde8a54514990de80387748df7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALPREM CLINIC 1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A hospital-use formula specifically designed for premature newborns weighing less than 1,800 grams, with higher protein content.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2619</data>
      <data key="d7">923341eb3e4b476e8206e9fca9d5b439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPGHAN 2010">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ESPGHAN 2010 guidelines provide nutritional recommendations for the enteral feeding of premature newborns.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1899</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2620</data>
      <data key="d7">f056f48cbb504c78b0c3c8f15a8d5849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECI&#201;N NACIDOS PRET&#201;RMINO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reci&#233;n nacidos pret&#233;rmino" refers to premature newborns who are born before the completion of 37 weeks of gestation. These infants often have low birth weight and specific developmental needs, which necessitate specialized nutritional support. Due to their early arrival, preterm newborns may require immediate nutritional intervention to prevent adverse effects associated with fasting and to support their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca,cd63370bdd798f0b060b047dc29056ae,fa356397bc52582bdbbd1868639feec9</data>
      <data key="d3">1898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2621</data>
      <data key="d7">8279d377400a4432ada3be5e34fdd0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACANTIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactation is the process of feeding infants with breast milk, which is particularly important for premature infants to receive essential nutrients and antibodies.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2622</data>
      <data key="d7">1a255d84becc4b35a906186d11d3f422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MATERIALES DE LA LECHE MATERNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The composition of human milk varies significantly, impacting the nutritional intake of premature infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2623</data>
      <data key="d7">b7849099dc01488786b318f3bf0b75e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIFICULTADES EN LA ALIMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Feeding difficulties in premature infants can arise from various factors, including the availability of maternal milk and the infant's ability to tolerate feeding volumes.</data>
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2624</data>
      <data key="d7">2bc56d8342a14b009a87f55cc8f87753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETINOPAT&#205;A DE LA PREMATURIDAD">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">a00805212febe78884955ddd3476f6ca</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2625</data>
      <data key="d7">218b39e66a59472282ac9acf2f44241b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JOURNAL OF PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY AND NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research and commentary focused on pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. It serves as a platform for disseminating research findings and guidelines that pertain to pediatric nutrition and gastrointestinal health, contributing to the advancement of knowledge in these critical areas of child health.</data>
      <data key="d2">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2626</data>
      <data key="d7">0d0c41c183e84cfeb9aebd47b0f3098c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRETERM INFANTS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Preterm infants are defined as babies born before the completion of 37 weeks of gestation. Due to their early birth, they often require specialized medical care and have specific nutritional needs that differ from those of full-term infants. These infants necessitate specialized nutritional guidelines and formulas to support their development and ensure they receive the appropriate care for their unique circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,7c60735b2451e2d314fe6c5377b7a79d,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467,fa356397bc52582bdbbd1868639feec9</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">26</data>
      <data key="d6">2627</data>
      <data key="d7">2986d87246be45f58616b3d83a4f60b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL M&#205;NIMA O TR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A feeding protocol aimed at stimulating and nourishing the immature intestines of preterm infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2628</data>
      <data key="d7">7d97af25b3ea4e8baceb9ecddf8ee7ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEC refers to necrotizing enterocolitis, a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect premature infants. This clinical guideline or protocol is focused on the dietary needs and management of these vulnerable infants, emphasizing the importance of proper nutrition to mitigate the risks associated with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2629</data>
      <data key="d7">9ea60bb8f4664fcda238777f263cc421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RCIU">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RCIU, or Retraso de Crecimiento Intrauterino, refers to a condition characterized by intrauterine growth restriction, where a fetus fails to achieve normal weight during pregnancy. This condition is defined as being small for gestational age at birth and indicates that the fetus does not reach its genetic growth potential while in utero.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">639</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">2630</data>
      <data key="d7">7e34215628d9426ab539566c9056bf81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DHA, or Docosahexaenoic Acid, is an essential omega-3 fatty acid that plays a critical role in human health, particularly in brain and heart function. It is vital for cognitive development and is a significant component of the brain's structure, contributing to brain health and cognitive function. DHA is also important for cardiovascular health and may help prevent progressive atrophy of the cerebral cortex, thereby reducing the risk of Alzheimer's disease.

In addition to its neurological benefits, DHA is proposed for dietary supplementation in conditions such as cystic fibrosis to help modulate inflammatory responses and improve immune function. It is derived from alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) and is crucial for eye function as well. Furthermore, recent European legislation emphasizes the necessity of including DHA in infant formulas, highlighting its importance for brain development in preterm infants. Overall, DHA is recognized as a vital nutrient for maintaining overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">056e169253fe046c2922537bb79ba187,0a43b350a248173236a96a64e266b744,680ff2c9e67ec29c5952df66bd83c984,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467,d2f16314e7098030a6780411d2e03023,dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">2631</data>
      <data key="d7">68f0739443be4e3094c0e76af23d8f47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arachidonic acid, an essential fatty acid important for growth and development in preterm infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2632</data>
      <data key="d7">4cd7194d4bb148e4b37698ea612a18e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcium, an essential mineral for bone development in preterm infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2633</data>
      <data key="d7">c06175844b394b7dae250f20bc468e24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phosphorus (P) is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in bone health and energy metabolism, particularly in preterm infants. It is important to monitor phosphorus levels in patients at risk of refeeding syndrome to prevent metabolic complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467,d6469f98d2161058fb7b214a1a800441</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2634</data>
      <data key="d7">7db713f3d14e42558ad6aa7f6e04ba2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RATIO CA/P">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ratio of calcium to phosphorus, which is important for the nutritional balance in preterm infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2635</data>
      <data key="d7">3aa59809e0fb4ace8fad0456ffbc9fac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IBUPROFENO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ibuprofen is a medication mentioned in the context of treatment for certain conditions in premature infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2636</data>
      <data key="d7">e935ae1e4d6c4d86a8b85a798fbda7cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">RN refers to a registered nurse who plays a crucial role in the care and management of premature infants. This specialized nursing professional is involved in providing essential support to neonatal patients, particularly those who require specialized nutritional assistance through parenteral nutrition due to their inability to feed orally. The RN's expertise is vital in ensuring the health and well-being of these vulnerable infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2637</data>
      <data key="d7">d5aadd8bd7994d978231ded8bd40f92c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RNPT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">RNPT refers to "Reci&#233;n Nacidos Prematuros" or "Premature Newborns," a specific group of patients that includes preterm newborns who require specialized nutritional support due to their unique health needs. This group encompasses newborns with low birth weight and very low birth weight, who are particularly susceptible to conditions such as hypoglycemia and hyperglycemia. As a result, they require careful nutritional management, including elevated glucose intake to prevent hypoglycemia and adherence to specific nutritional guidelines when receiving parenteral nutrition. Additionally, RNPT can also refer to a registered nurse specializing in the care of these premature infants, ensuring they receive the necessary attention and support for optimal growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">507eeea555c496a467930836fc4c1a39,52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715,a0b6196d53d4eb1c8ca5b1a3a78e8fc7,aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5,e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194,f5175f0c433eb4e10840a41d8052c8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">631</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">2638</data>
      <data key="d7">3b57280bfa6b46aaaf79321a18a6d57d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORTIFICACI&#211;N DE LA LECHE MATERNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fortification of breast milk is a process designed to enhance the nutritional content of breast milk for premature infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">638</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2639</data>
      <data key="d7">48b574e700dc46d5b1bdf249dbd2064d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ECN refers to enterocolitis necrotizing, a serious gastrointestinal condition that can affect premature infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">638</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2640</data>
      <data key="d7">d98811bd27104d1488e5d0eaa288b0ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alimentaci&#243;n enteral is a method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract, primarily utilized when patients are stabilized. This approach is particularly significant for infants, especially those who are premature, as it ensures they receive essential nutrients directly through their digestive system. Alimentaci&#243;n enteral serves as an alternative to parenteral nutrition, offering a means to deliver nutrition effectively through the digestive tract.</data>
      <data key="d2">61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296,aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d3">660</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">2641</data>
      <data key="d7">632f56f2ae89453dae8d6f8ead57e6e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SOG refers to the method of administration for feeding, specifically through a gastric tube.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2642</data>
      <data key="d7">6b824ebfdf2d4f86969ed6ae59a597fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GCI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GCI refers to a method of feeding that involves administering nutrition over a set period, typically used for infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">2643</data>
      <data key="d7">bcca68932797417db2206ae19da62640</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISTENSI&#211;N ABDOMINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Distensi&#243;n abdominal is a clinical sign that may indicate feeding intolerance in infants. It is also recognized as a gastrointestinal symptom that can arise from the use of certain medications in conjunction with enteral nutrition. This condition highlights the importance of monitoring abdominal distension, particularly in vulnerable populations such as infants, as it may signal underlying issues related to their nutritional intake and medication effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4,fc664efd4e1c463dc21857e596b68b46</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2644</data>
      <data key="d7">7dfdb875d12d450fb8753ca49ad53773</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOLOR A LA PALPACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dolor a la palpaci&#243;n is a clinical sign that may suggest gastrointestinal issues in infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">660</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2645</data>
      <data key="d7">14a72d19aee34ce5b032686cd996f2f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERISTALTISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Peristaltismo refers to the movement of the intestines, which can be assessed to evaluate feeding tolerance in infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">660</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2646</data>
      <data key="d7">6b06d1616d66484a8c0393bb1003e979</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECI&#201;N NACIDOS PREMATUROS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">"RECI&#201;N NACIDOS PREMATUROS" refers to newborns who are born before 37 weeks of gestation. These infants require special attention in terms of their feeding and care due to their physiological immaturity. They are at risk of undernutrition and therefore need specific nutritional support to ensure their health and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3,aacaabd084b7839bdedf5fbebfd7dcf4</data>
      <data key="d3">659</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">2647</data>
      <data key="d7">da40d888e00e43e3937a92c355faae9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEAD-JOHNSON">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mead-Johnson is a company that specializes in pediatric nutrition, focusing on the development and production of products designed for infant feeding. One of their notable products is Enfalac HMF, which is specifically formulated to meet the nutritional needs of infants.</data>
      <data key="d2">4351677d6166c9c88ab941dc8dcecb82,919ff63f7f48a238e717f60361d8dbd1</data>
      <data key="d3">801</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2648</data>
      <data key="d7">f44b434bb0634436ac20ddd78ef3841c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDROPOLIVIT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hidropolivit is a liquid multivitamin supplement designed to enhance hydration and nutrient intake. It is particularly recommended for premature infants to ensure they receive adequate vitamin D, which is crucial for their development. Additionally, Hidropolivit serves as a polivitaminic supplement that provides essential vitamins and minerals necessary for the growth and health of infants and children.</data>
      <data key="d2">8366a6776a090c4e13b4746a1b23e96f,919ff63f7f48a238e717f60361d8dbd1,acfde2ff93b969353912836034d74242</data>
      <data key="d3">1627</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">2649</data>
      <data key="d7">797fd9bb55984b03ad2403a6b229b7b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHA VIT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">DHA Vit is a nutritional supplement designed to support the health and nutritional needs of infants. It contains DHA, along with vitamins A, D, and E, which are essential for the proper development and well-being of young children.</data>
      <data key="d2">8366a6776a090c4e13b4746a1b23e96f,919ff63f7f48a238e717f60361d8dbd1</data>
