      <data key="d7">38ae4a4e37d643358b20c11eac64d348</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TABLE 5">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Table 5 serves multiple purposes related to dietary management in a pediatric hospital setting. It presents dietary recommendations for liquid intake based on the age of pediatric patients, ensuring that their hydration needs are appropriately met. Additionally, Table 5 details the composition of available milk fortifiers within the hospital, providing essential information about their nutritional content to support the dietary needs of infants and children. Furthermore, it includes information on dietary restrictions for patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD), specifically focusing on the limitations regarding leucine content to manage this metabolic condition effectively. Overall, Table 5 is a comprehensive resource for dietary guidelines and nutritional support for pediatric patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a351a5c3cb70af0293c0897583049cc,919ff63f7f48a238e717f60361d8dbd1,91c1a9b0c0d7cb718d7711ef7384a142</data>
