    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N OPTIMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrici&#243;n &#243;ptima refers to the ideal nutritional practices for infants, emphasizing the importance of breast milk.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">638</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2674</data>
      <data key="d7">874b2b20b7b74cb492081f0598faef94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N AL ALTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alimentaci&#243;n al alta refers to the nutritional options available for premature infants upon discharge from the hospital.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">639</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2675</data>
      <data key="d7">498fb9557ec842fe9cb834f4b24a7681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REALIMENTACI&#211;N TRAS CIRUG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Realimentaci&#243;n tras cirug&#237;a refers to the process of reintroducing nutrition after surgical procedures, with specific guidelines based on the type of surgery performed.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">1200</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">2676</data>
      <data key="d7">aa8157f4e9eb469c9ff73a92fcdd0967</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXIA FETAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxia fetal cr&#243;nica is a condition associated with RCIU, indicating chronic low oxygen levels affecting fetal growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">639</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2677</data>
      <data key="d7">0f96ab282f744c9db0bc756a69aa8f08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PER&#205;METRO CEF&#193;LICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Per&#237;metro cef&#225;lico is a measurement used to assess head size in newborns, important for evaluating growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">639</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2678</data>
      <data key="d7">61417fa4ec4845a088aaf8bd35e77f92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARCADORES BIOQU&#205;MICOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MARCADORES BIOQU&#205;MICOS, or biochemical markers, are utilized to evaluate nutritional status and metabolism in patients. While they serve an important role in assessing these aspects, their reliability can be compromised, particularly in critically ill patients. This highlights the need for careful interpretation of biochemical markers in such contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">638</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2679</data>
      <data key="d7">092b51818b6e4fd0908e524103dae9af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEPOSICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deposici&#243;n refers to the act of defecation, which is an important factor in assessing gastrointestinal function post-surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">1200</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2680</data>
      <data key="d7">2f103495eb5846318422803653e46331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TR&#193;NSITO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tr&#225;nsito refers to the movement of food through the digestive system, which is monitored post-surgery to determine when to resume feeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a251705839547c8dcd0e9ddc5bb4066</data>
      <data key="d3">1200</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2681</data>
      <data key="d7">62d8508fad4746dd80384d3bcb890b2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL MANAGEMENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional management encompasses a range of dietary strategies and interventions designed to address the unique needs of patients with various medical conditions. In the context of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), nutritional management focuses on dietary strategies tailored to the specific challenges faced by individuals suffering from this neurodegenerative disease. Additionally, it involves continuous assessment of growth and development to ensure optimal outcomes for patients requiring nutritional support, such as those with renal needs (RNPT).

Furthermore, nutritional management plays a critical role in preventing malnutrition associated with rumination syndrome and is essential for improving health outcomes in patients with pancreatitis. It also includes dietary strategies aimed at treating conditions like chylothorax and chylous effusions, as well as supporting patients with chyle leaks and related disorders. Overall, nutritional management is vital for enhancing the quality of life and health outcomes for patients across a spectrum of medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">37182848d30a82f99b7a617859ac6e0d,44d6374ee887ebef4cba5ec2a31f0673,52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715,5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2,a35fdf8cbbb5fe4783572ea6e86f7776,a3d355dd6da93691c892691f873338aa,fba8cc8092875a542f3b63663ce5c8d9</data>
      <data key="d3">1195</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">2682</data>
      <data key="d7">13a253bfd97d4576862cab826b08fa7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROWTH ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Growth assessment is the process of evaluating the growth of RNPT after hospital discharge using corrected age.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d3">1196</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2683</data>
      <data key="d7">6ab74cd43ef94ba390b3a54c1d7e26cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOCHEMICAL MARKERS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Periodic determinations of biochemical markers are tools used in the nutritional management of RNPT.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d3">1195</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2684</data>
      <data key="d7">56c508c1bd274af88096a3e0399c9633</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROWTH VELOCITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Growth velocity is used to monitor the growth of RNPT and assess dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d3">1195</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2685</data>
      <data key="d7">d3f76a9c34644152826cd32930bef336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATTERNS OF GROWTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Patterns of growth classification for RNPT at discharge help identify their growth status and needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d3">1195</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2686</data>
      <data key="d7">da90586bb35a4dcf9251e80876bd0ff8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EBPN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EBPN refers to a group of extremely low birth weight newborns who have specific nutritional needs and face significant challenges in growth and development. This group is similar to RNMBPN, indicating that both entities share common characteristics related to the nutritional and developmental requirements of newborns with low birth weight.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715,89855c293083756b0ff7a0081f67e9fd</data>
      <data key="d3">631</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2687</data>
      <data key="d7">151457aabf5d4dfc852e46dbc2736344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL DISCHARGE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital discharge is the process of releasing RNPT from medical care, requiring careful assessment of their growth patterns.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d3">1196</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2688</data>
      <data key="d7">1816800946c5412eb0489ccd01a07cd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EARLY POSTNATAL CATCH-UP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Early postnatal catch-up refers to the rapid growth that some RNPT experience after birth, which is crucial for their development.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2689</data>
      <data key="d7">f6ae5e33a0c242de9adbec5f36b0ff47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROWTH COMPENSATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Growth compensation is the process by which RNPT may catch up in growth after experiencing delays.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2690</data>
      <data key="d7">57615d7b77054cafbf953ea6a7f24ffa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RNMBPN">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">RNMBPN refers to a group of newborns with specific nutritional needs, particularly those receiving mixed parenteral nutrition, which is a method of providing nutrition intravenously. Although it is not a widely recognized organization, RNMBPN highlights the importance of addressing the unique dietary requirements of these newborns to ensure their health and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bb736eec60ff1b81771029cc43f715,89855c293083756b0ff7a0081f67e9fd,a0b6196d53d4eb1c8ca5b1a3a78e8fc7</data>
      <data key="d3">631</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2691</data>
      <data key="d7">8d9d5984cea24240a8e5bc251754f666</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N INFANTIL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N INFANTIL encompasses the field of pediatric nutrition, which is dedicated to ensuring that children receive balanced diets that supply the essential nutrients required for their growth and development. This area of study also includes specific recommendations regarding infant nutrition, with a particular emphasis on the needs of preterm infants. The focus is on promoting healthy dietary practices that support the overall well-being of children from infancy through their developmental stages.</data>
      <data key="d2">89855c293083756b0ff7a0081f67e9fd,a4b56b993221a7065a59bca622c02953</data>
      <data key="d3">637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2692</data>
      <data key="d7">f810a407c66941dfa540ccbe47801fd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LCPUFA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LCPUFA stands for Long-Chain Polyunsaturated Fatty Acids, which are essential nutrients for infant growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">89855c293083756b0ff7a0081f67e9fd</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2693</data>
      <data key="d7">d85e0a6cc99e4333aebd608c2617c56c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULA DE INICIO">
