      <data key="d6">2708</data>
      <data key="d7">d662fb869f374faaa51a9c9da7555a04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATABOLISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CATABOLISMO, or catabolism, is a crucial metabolic process that involves the breakdown of molecules to obtain energy. This process can be influenced by various factors, including medications and health conditions. In particular, catabolism tends to increase during illness, which can pose significant challenges for patients. For instance, in burn patients, catabolism is difficult to halt, leading to muscle loss and nutritional difficulties. Additionally, in cases of acute pancreatitis, catabolism accelerates, resulting in a deterioration of nutritional status. This metabolic process is also a concern for premature infants, as their energy needs and nutritional requirements are critical for their development. Overall, catabolism plays a vital role in energy production but can lead to serious health implications under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02</data>
      <data key="d3">1091</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">2709</data>
      <data key="d7">c328cdbf3a234343ad2223c88f7fa6f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANABOLISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The metabolic process that builds up molecules, crucial for growth and development in premature infants</data>
      <data key="d2">61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296</data>
      <data key="d3">1091</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2710</data>
      <data key="d7">b5e2bb81e1c54109b6189f559b4fc163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREMATUROS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
