      <data key="d6">2711</data>
      <data key="d7">0eefd75a71aa457cbbe81e568cf7ced3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECI&#201;N NACIDO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "reci&#233;n nacido" refers to newborns, particularly in the context of their medical care and nutritional needs during the early days of life. Newborns are individuals whose gastrointestinal tracts are exposed to a variety of microorganisms at the time of birth, which plays a significant role in the development of their microbiota. This exposure is crucial for establishing a healthy gut flora, which can impact their overall health and development in the subsequent days and weeks.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d3">661</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">2712</data>
      <data key="d7">386e83da39344e259c3c2e05eec1b2b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fluids and electrolytes are crucial components for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in patients, particularly those receiving nutritional support. The management of these elements is especially important in vulnerable populations, such as newborns, where careful monitoring is necessary to prevent complications. Ensuring an appropriate balance of fluids and electrolytes is essential for overall health and recovery in these patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">661</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2713</data>
      <data key="d7">b3d6ed1408dd40578e7b67fac0a67409</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADOS NEONATALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Refers to the specialized medical care provided to newborns, especially those who are premature or have health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2714</data>
      <data key="d7">73f8fab3864541c8a1ff21b9411d0c18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APORTE PROTEICO-CAL&#211;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Refers to the ideal nutritional intake of proteins and calories necessary for weight gain in newborns.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29</data>
      <data key="d3">661</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2715</data>
      <data key="d7">f4c2c92703af445d9d78683f011d0de6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#205;A DE ADMINISTRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Refers to the method of delivering nutrition, either through peripheral or central routes, particularly in newborns.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2716</data>
      <data key="d7">7b4934771b7545db86ec9ded8b614ca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAT&#201;TER VENOSO UMBILICAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A central venous catheter used in newborns for administering nutrition and medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
