    <node id="RNT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RNT refers to "reci&#233;n nacido a t&#233;rmino," which translates to term newborns. These infants have distinct glucose and nutritional requirements compared to preterm infants. RNT specifically encompasses term newborns who may be receiving parenteral nutrition, adhering to specific nutritional guidelines to meet their needs. Additionally, RNT highlights the importance of nutritional attention for this group of pediatric patients, emphasizing that they require tailored care to support their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">a0b6196d53d4eb1c8ca5b1a3a78e8fc7,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
