      <data key="d6">2828</data>
      <data key="d7">b1c66ff0e11a4aeb8920bdc4aa5c22f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPARINIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Heparinization refers to the administration of low molecular weight heparins for the treatment and prophylaxis of thrombotic events.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b</data>
      <data key="d3">751</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2829</data>
      <data key="d7">2b0a0fda5dee4dc6a00b32de854dac69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICOAGULACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anticoagulation is a treatment method that involves the use of anticoagulant medications to prevent blood clots from forming or growing.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b</data>
      <data key="d3">764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2830</data>
      <data key="d7">1bf2e90c27ea4704bdb5f29b8c54df4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOL&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trombolytic therapy involves the use of drugs to dissolve blood clots that are obstructing blood flow to vital organs.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b</data>
      <data key="d3">764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2831</data>
      <data key="d7">212bcc03a3d048eda2c78e959ed37988</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPARINAS DE BAJO PESO MOLECULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Low molecular weight heparins (LMWH) are anticoagulant medications used for the prevention and treatment of thromboembolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b</data>
      <data key="d3">764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2832</data>
      <data key="d7">1047442e4c424047b1e0b6703490be55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#205;MEROS D">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">D-dimer is a fibrin degradation product that is typically elevated in the presence of a blood clot, used as a diagnostic marker in thrombotic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b</data>
      <data key="d3">764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2833</data>
      <data key="d7">1d67ba1a7be24e8787a71ba71fe2d977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRIN&#211;GENO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrinogen is a crucial blood plasma protein that plays a vital role in blood clot formation and wound healing. It is essential for the coagulation process, helping to prevent excessive bleeding when injuries occur. Additionally, fibrinogen levels are closely monitored in patients undergoing anticoagulation therapy and those with thrombotic conditions, as these levels can indicate the body's ability to form clots effectively. Overall, fibrinogen is integral to maintaining hemostasis and is a key factor in the management of various blood-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">5ad53a3f16964261ae37b64f7c3cb688,6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d3">1798</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2834</data>
      <data key="d7">4bcf59f8746c4338bff4f4ff58857d3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOSIS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Thrombosis is a medical condition characterized by the formation of a blood clot within a blood vessel. This condition can lead to significant complications, particularly during venous access procedures. It is also noted as a potential complication associated with central parenteral nutrition. The presence of thrombosis can complicate medical interventions and may pose risks to patient health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826,67344d72dff60fcb903b258fbca95de5,6b73aed941007771a7f23462cdb4470b,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855</data>
