      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2839</data>
      <data key="d7">60e7f13fa46d4cacaec34a8f5fa63d01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENTEROCOCO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterococcus, also referred to as Enterococo, is a genus of bacteria that is commonly found as part of the normal intestinal flora. However, it has the potential to cause infections, particularly in patients with weakened immune systems or those with central venous catheters (CVC). These infections can be serious and are more likely to occur in individuals who are already vulnerable due to underlying health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5ad53a3f16964261ae37b64f7c3cb688,f79f02438413f5accef9ac5fbd96f6df</data>
      <data key="d3">767</data>
