    <node id="ANTIBIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Antibioterapia refers to the treatment of infections through the use of antibiotics. This therapy may be tailored according to culture results to ensure effective management of the infection. Additionally, antibiotic therapy is essential in addressing complications that may arise from intestinal failure, highlighting its critical role in both infection management and the treatment of related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,f79f02438413f5accef9ac5fbd96f6df</data>
      <data key="d3">766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2857</data>
      <data key="d7">df9baffc016b4332ba145369c6d19f03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOMIELITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteomyelitis is an infection in the bone that can occur as a complication of severe infections related to central venous catheters.</data>
      <data key="d2">f79f02438413f5accef9ac5fbd96f6df</data>
      <data key="d3">766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2858</data>
      <data key="d7">079b814cfc104ee28d9f1723160166b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUTROPENIA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Neutropenia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of neutrophils, a type of white blood cell essential for fighting off infections. This condition leads to an increased susceptibility to infections, particularly in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type Ib (GSDIb). Additionally, the low neutrophil count associated with neutropenia can influence dietary choices due to the heightened risk of infections. Neutropenia can occur in individuals with GSDIb, further complicating their health management.</data>
      <data key="d2">42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc,f79f02438413f5accef9ac5fbd96f6df</data>
