    </node>
    <node id="ORL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ORL refers to the Otolaryngology department, also known as Otorrinolaringolog&#237;a, which specializes in the evaluation and treatment of conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat. This department is involved in the patient's treatment and follow-up care, particularly in cases such as laryngeal carcinoma. Additionally, ORL encompasses hospital wards where dysphagia screening is protocolized for patients, highlighting its role in managing conditions that may lead to swallowing difficulties. Overall, ORL plays a crucial role in the comprehensive care of patients with various otolaryngological issues, including those that may cause dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,d590f931bbeb2d87392c751f2746e4da</data>
