    <node id="ESPESANTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPESANTE is a thickening agent designed to modify the texture of liquids and foods for individuals with swallowing difficulties. It ensures safe consumption by altering the consistency of these substances, making them easier to swallow. The product is particularly beneficial for patients who require dietary modifications to prevent choking or aspiration. Nutilis is another name associated with this thickening agent, emphasizing its role in enhancing the safety and comfort of those with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,806140d9fadd08a1e72238d53c829eb2,9b853d8ac0d48f1111932f52fb0749db</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">2911</data>
      <data key="d7">7dcd556a2a9945c0a7cdbed15f065c2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "NUTRICIONAL" encompasses a range of nutritional attributes and requirements essential for various patient populations. It highlights the importance of nutritional assessment as a dynamic process, particularly for burn patients, to ensure they receive adequate support for recovery. Additionally, it is crucial for patients undergoing bariatric surgery, as proper nutritional evaluation helps facilitate weight loss and prevent potential complications. Nutritional education plays a significant role in this context, aiming to alter patients' beliefs and behaviors regarding food to encourage healthier eating habits. Furthermore, "NUTRICIONAL" also pertains to dietary interventions and management strategies for patients, especially those in oncology, as well as the nutritional assessment and management aspects of the dysphagia protocol. Overall, the concept of "NUTRICIONAL" is integral to promoting optimal health outcomes across various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,3ed179f6e734d9fe4921fb0be0b018e4,806140d9fadd08a1e72238d53c829eb2,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d3">902</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">2912</data>
      <data key="d7">b3702fc7364743bead861628fa250506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ALTA refers to the discharge or release of a patient from medical care, marking the conclusion of treatment or monitoring for various medical conditions. This term is often discussed in the context of recovery from conditions such as diabetic ketoacidosis (cetoacidosis diab&#233;tica) and is also relevant in the discharge process for patients with dysphagia. In both cases, ALTA signifies that the patient has reached a stage where they no longer require ongoing medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">806140d9fadd08a1e72238d53c829eb2,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d3">902</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">2913</data>
      <data key="d7">34482d79da05426b8226251c3d966ca4</data>
    </node>
