    <node id="ESTUDIO OCTABAIX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESTUDIO OCTABAIX is a longitudinal research study conducted in Barcelona that focuses on aging and frailty among older adults. The study examines various factors related to fragility in this demographic, aiming to enhance understanding of the challenges faced by the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d2">65e1359e381a0ac66f53b3a6eeba408b,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1777</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3000</data>
      <data key="d7">38e25b970b31494187e7c14f76da7961</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIOS PE&#209;AGRANDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESTUDIOS PE&#209;AGRANDE refers to a series of research studies conducted in Madrid that investigate frailty in the elderly population. These studies focus specifically on the fragility of older individuals, aiming to understand the various factors that contribute to their vulnerability.</data>
      <data key="d2">65e1359e381a0ac66f53b3a6eeba408b,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1778</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3001</data>
      <data key="d7">7582355f389f4c5384ebcde6d423f238</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO FRALLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESTUDIO FRALLE is a longitudinal study conducted in Lleida that focuses on frailty and its implications for elderly care. The study investigates the concept of fragility in aging individuals, aiming to understand how this condition affects their overall well-being and the care they require. Through its comprehensive approach, ESTUDIO FRALLE seeks to provide valuable insights into the challenges faced by the elderly population in relation to frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">65e1359e381a0ac66f53b3a6eeba408b,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">475</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3002</data>
      <data key="d7">58a83666635247eeb210b7099ff41b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAILTY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Frailty is a clinical syndrome primarily affecting older adults, characterized by decreased physiological reserve and resistance to stressors. This condition often manifests through a combination of symptoms, including weight loss, weakness, slow walking speed, and decreased physical activity, which collectively increase vulnerability to adverse health events. Frailty is frequently associated with sarcopenia, a condition involving the loss of muscle mass and strength, and it encompasses physical, psychological, and social dimensions. The syndrome results from cumulative declines across multiple physiological systems, leading to heightened health risks and complications for frail elderly individuals. In summary, frailty represents a significant geriatric syndrome that underscores the complex interplay of various health issues in older adults, making them more susceptible to stressors and adverse outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,0903b40c7774225e89c5e798f9feef9b,1052683f23a0c9825af9c5c1d39ceb2c,4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,65e1359e381a0ac66f53b3a6eeba408b,6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2,72bafac70ee8322d8f303cf94612b461,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642,e155d9b2d1858daab734fd68a45d0c0a</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">31</data>
      <data key="d6">3003</data>
      <data key="d7">be97c0d272434ebab986210e277c4481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO DE ENVEJECIMIENTO SALUDABLE EN TOLEDO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A longitudinal study focused on healthy aging in Toledo, contributing to research on fragility in the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3004</data>
      <data key="d7">cb47b687454d41d58d0854f85ecf8ba3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ONON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">An author who published an article in 1968 linking aging and fragility in the British Medical Journal.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3005</data>
      <data key="d7">eb0a5b85fe0444ffa64e3a647a8ac8ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VAUPEL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who, in 1979, described fragility as a characteristic of individuals that influences longevity.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1776</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3006</data>
      <data key="d7">15c9b8954f64434eb78a908861670521</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOODHOUSE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who defined the frail elderly as those over 65 who depend on others for daily activities in 1988.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1777</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3007</data>
      <data key="d7">11d3c473b29b4dc3b05426a7cbda75e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GILLICK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who characterized frail elderly individuals as those who require substantial help from others.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1778</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3008</data>
      <data key="d7">f50749df92164ff3b5f27d546e0253d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLAYMAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who defined frail elderly individuals as neither too well nor too disabled.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">475</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3009</data>
      <data key="d7">31f682a3024e470092c5db811340ebfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WINOGRAD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who classified hospitalized patients into subgroups of independent, frail, and too disabled elderly.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3010</data>
      <data key="d7">d37dd9e52966402ba5d7babc4e715588</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPIRDUSO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who related the concept of fragility in the elderly to the human condition as inherently fragile.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3011</data>
      <data key="d7">1a50c227962b434191a58be9ab5bb964</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BORTZ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who characterized the human condition as necessarily fragile, including illness and disuse.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3012</data>
      <data key="d7">82ee28ee2cbd4d5382b2be00aae528ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BUCHNER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who reviewed the concept of fragility and defined it as losses in physiological reserve increasing disability risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3013</data>
      <data key="d7">d308adf27a634112b064417808d7f4d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WAGNER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who contributed to the understanding of fragility as a precursor to disability and dependence.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3014</data>
      <data key="d7">3d90b52da6ac4e3abda38b1393411639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROCKLEHURST">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A researcher who developed a dynamic model of fragility balancing psychosocial and biomedical components.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1100</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
