      <data key="d7">03a62f629da94233bdd12f5fa2e03af2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROWN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">BROWN is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of fragility, suggesting that it is dependent on motor function and can be identified through physical function tests. Additionally, BROWN is the author of a study that investigates the administration of glutamine in adults undergoing hematopoietic transplantation.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e6ae05671fed21e332ee155332df21e,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1100</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3016</data>
      <data key="d7">a93f3ea0b3624250bd4c3b75de0abed1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"FRAGILIDAD" refers to a syndrome primarily affecting older adults, characterized by a significant reduction in physiological reserve and an increased vulnerability to stressors. This condition manifests as a decline in strength, endurance, and overall physiological function, which heightens the risk of developing dependency or mortality. The syndrome is marked by multisystem deterioration, leading to adverse health outcomes and a greater likelihood of requiring medical attention.

Fragility is defined by the presence of three or more specific criteria, indicating a higher risk of negative health consequences in the elderly population. It is closely associated with sarcopenia, which contributes to the loss of muscle mass and strength. Additionally, factors such as adherence to a Mediterranean diet and nutritional supplementation can influence the severity of fragility, suggesting that these interventions may help improve the health status of frail individuals.

Overall, fragility represents a critical health concern in geriatric medicine, emphasizing the need for awareness and management strategies to mitigate its effects and enhance the quality of life for older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972,5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b,5f15452403a4c9b4b3c7a48bac634a04,6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32,7e1b90e2c8714b39e283be229f6d5de3,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,b7465350e74a3bada96615deb0d7b031,bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">45</data>
      <data key="d6">3017</data>
      <data key="d7">44b1f31baef24af2acc79f19e57c16c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VULNERABILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VULNERABILIDAD refers to the increased susceptibility to adverse outcomes that frail elderly individuals experience. It is a concept closely related to fragility, indicating a heightened risk of negative health events. This understanding of vulnerabilidad highlights the challenges faced by older adults, emphasizing the need for targeted interventions to mitigate these risks and improve their overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3018</data>
      <data key="d7">d5dd7e2b73ad4d429ebc5876b0bafdde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESERVA FISIOL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Physiological reserves that are diminished in frail elderly individuals, increasing their risk of disability.</data>
      <data key="d2">e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3019</data>
      <data key="d7">66c6c860f42d406ba8a5b81eaa0d860f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEPENDENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "Dependencia" encompasses the concept of dependence, which is characterized by an increased need for assistance in daily activities, particularly due to the effects of sarcopenia. This condition is prevalent among older adults who often require support due to various health issues, making it a significant concern in geriatric care. Dependencia reflects the state of relying on others for help in daily tasks, a situation commonly observed in frail elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b,d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f,e09463a0b899f9cd54a1daefc265ca39</data>
      <data key="d3">1784</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3020</data>
      <data key="d7">deae32228bf64469bfd74e9da4112c1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORLANDO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Orlando es la ciudad en EE.UU. donde se gest&#243; el &#250;ltimo documento de consenso sobre fragilidad en diciembre de 2012.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3021</data>
      <data key="d7">a8ffee2faeea41348ce6adf01620167f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASOCIACI&#211;N INTERNACIONAL DE GERIATR&#205;A Y GERONTOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La Asociaci&#243;n Internacional de Geriatr&#237;a y Gerontolog&#237;a es la organizaci&#243;n que auspicia la conferencia donde se defini&#243; el s&#237;ndrome geri&#225;trico de fragilidad f&#237;sica.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3022</data>
      <data key="d7">ba478f6dd432494ba02eb2bea1ff77ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINDA P. FRIED">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Linda P. Fried is a prominent researcher and physician recognized for her significant contributions to the field of gerontology. She developed the frailty phenotype model based on a prospective cohort study, which has been instrumental in defining criteria for frailty in elderly populations. Her work has greatly enhanced the understanding of health and aging, providing valuable insights into the challenges faced by older individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1770</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3023</data>
      <data key="d7">5baa34c0a0cf4454bcda250105ef7a04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOVASCULAR HEALTH STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cardiovascular Health Study is a prospective cohort study that serves as a foundational model for understanding the phenotype of frailty. This research initiative examines the health and risk factors associated with cardiovascular disease specifically in older adults. Additionally, the study focuses on understanding frailty and its relationship to inflammation and coagulation systems within this demographic. Through its comprehensive approach, the Cardiovascular Health Study aims to provide valuable insights into the interplay between cardiovascular health and frailty in aging populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,0903b40c7774225e89c5e798f9feef9b,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d3">1770</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3024</data>
      <data key="d7">6b962e3a3f6d453fb22744144a7362e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODELO DE D&#201;FICITS ACUMULATIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El modelo de d&#233;ficits acumulativos es uno de los principales modelos de fragilidad f&#237;sica que se utiliza en la evaluaci&#243;n cl&#237;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
