    </node>
    <node id="CANADIAN STUDY OF HEALTH AND AGING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Canadian Study of Health and Aging is a prospective cohort study designed to investigate the epidemiology and impact of dementia in the elderly population of Canada.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1769</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3031</data>
      <data key="d7">91f8ffeca7f84cc7a50e2fd3b0bf7354</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KEN ROCKWOOD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ken Rockwood is a researcher who developed the Frailty Index as part of the Canadian Study of Health and Aging, focusing on the cumulative deficits model of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1769</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3032</data>
      <data key="d7">97f306cad0044c26b09249f405536239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREFRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PREFRAGILIDAD refers to a condition characterized by the presence of one or two frailty criteria, indicating an intermediate risk of adverse health outcomes in elderly individuals. This state of pre-frailty suggests that those affected may be more vulnerable to health complications compared to those who do not meet any frailty criteria.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1770</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3033</data>
      <data key="d7">003a672d6e3d42d39cf3f46fb12f78dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NO FR&#193;GILES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NO FR&#193;GILES refers to non-frail or robust individuals who do not meet any of the frailty criteria. This classification indicates that they have a lower risk of adverse health outcomes and health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3034</data>
      <data key="d7">868d139da4de4dec8864f57eac8b3c9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;NDICE DE FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#205;ndice de Fragilidad is a model designed to evaluate the fragility of patients through a set of criteria and accumulated deficits. It serves as a measure to assess the cumulative effects of various deficits, particularly in elderly populations. This index is crucial for understanding the overall health and vulnerability of older adults, allowing for better management and care strategies tailored to their needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223,5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3035</data>
      <data key="d7">6b40c47f3bb34bb7a8874a45b8aecb2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COHORTA PROSPECTIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A prospective cohort study is a research design that follows a group of individuals over time to assess outcomes related to health and aging.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a503efaa0ae32d36050a36646f1e01b</data>
      <data key="d3">1769</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3036</data>
      <data key="d7">89c70a60948040a5bca4a5e5db702e21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENOTIPO DE FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El Fenotipo de Fragilidad es un modelo que clasifica la fragilidad en tres niveles: robusto, prefr&#225;gil y fr&#225;gil, basado en signos y s&#237;ntomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3037</data>
      <data key="d7">85961d04d63c4afba58ee7c52c49b5f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES FR&#193;GILES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los pacientes fr&#225;giles son aquellos que presentan un alto riesgo de mortalidad y requieren intervenciones preventivas o terap&#233;uticas.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3038</data>
      <data key="d7">7005be2d39ba4a629e6baabeebd36d2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HERRAMIENTAS DE IDENTIFICACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las herramientas de identificaci&#243;n son instrumentos dise&#241;ados para detectar la fragilidad en pacientes, como cuestionarios estandarizados.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3039</data>
      <data key="d7">ea7490816dd44d6793f87b1583039de1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROENINGEN FRAILTY INDEX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El Groningen Frailty Index es una herramienta utilizada para identificar pacientes fr&#225;giles, destacando su validez y sensibilidad al cambio.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3040</data>
      <data key="d7">af36521dd4314bee98e61afa35ae4437</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VULNERABLE ELDERS' SURVEY-12">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Vulnerable Elders' Survey-12 is a screening tool designed to identify vulnerable elderly individuals and assess their risk of fragility. This questionnaire aids in recognizing those seniors who may require additional health assessments, ensuring that their specific needs are addressed effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223,f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3041</data>
      <data key="d7">ccc71d0e860b48dcb8315cb1c8989e7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TILLBURG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tillburg es una herramienta sencilla de identificaci&#243;n de pacientes fr&#225;giles, utilizada en la evaluaci&#243;n geri&#225;trica.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3042</data>
      <data key="d7">4d8b5efce1e14cbdb379f9be790a2ed5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEBATE ACERCA DE LA FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El debate acerca de la fragilidad se centra en la definici&#243;n de fragilidad como un s&#237;ndrome cl&#237;nico y su evaluaci&#243;n en pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3043</data>
      <data key="d7">f466616b8a9f43de88577d60b9e5b3dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA INTEGRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La valoraci&#243;n cl&#237;nica integral es un proceso necesario para evaluar la fragilidad y determinar el perfil de riesgo de un paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3044</data>
      <data key="d7">6887b8779d794c59a9f6c196e83d3719</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUESTIONARIOS ESTANDARIZADOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los cuestionarios estandarizados son m&#233;todos utilizados para identificar la fragilidad en pacientes, basados en diferentes modelos.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3045</data>
      <data key="d7">0a19714fb2c64c72b9936990d8929e70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REVISI&#211;N SISTEM&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"REVISI&#211;N SISTEM&#193;TICA" refers to a systematic review, which is a method of summarizing and evaluating evidence from multiple studies on a specific topic. This process involves an exhaustive analysis of the methods used to identify fragility in selected populations. Through this comprehensive approach, "REVISI&#211;N SISTEM&#193;TICA" aims to provide a thorough understanding of the available evidence and its implications for the topic at hand.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223,4261c82c43dac1a06d46f91f46f6d510</data>
      <data key="d3">1276</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3046</data>
      <data key="d7">c64c4215cc1640f2aa552d6d177faa9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS refers to individuals diagnosed with cancer who may require tailored dietary plans and specialized nutritional support during their treatment. This group of patients is particularly vulnerable to malnutrition, with prevalence rates that can reach up to 50%. The need for nutritional interventions is critical as these patients often face challenges that can impact their health and quality of life. Additionally, the evaluation of fragility in oncological patients can be beneficial for predicting treatment outcomes. Overall, PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS represent a specific population that necessitates careful nutritional assessment and support to enhance their overall well-being during the course of their illness.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b61e2d4f840772c76a05502aa4f171,28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c,c6406ac5c0c7b03d4ee61ca311fd783f,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">1099</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">3047</data>
      <data key="d7">ab69bac80a0c41c89772d052c1619018</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N GERI&#193;TRICA INTEGRAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "VALORACI&#211;N GERI&#193;TRICA INTEGRAL" refers to a comprehensive geriatric assessment, which is a multidimensional evaluation essential for determining the baseline situation of frail elderly patients. This method of assessment is particularly utilized to predict outcomes in fragile patients, especially among the elderly population. It serves as a critical tool in understanding the health and needs of older adults, facilitating better care and management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223,6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3048</data>
      <data key="d7">b2b13dbf850840db973ed3372239d737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERNATIONAL ACADEMY ON NUTRITION AND AGEING">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Academy on Nutrition and Ageing (IANA) is an organization that focuses on the nutritional needs and assessments of the elderly, particularly in relation to frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3049</data>
      <data key="d7">d4064607a0154f599fc76e29f65aaa71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL OF LEICESTER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The University Hospital of Leicester is a medical institution that provides healthcare services and conducts assessments related to elderly patients, including frailty evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3050</data>
      <data key="d7">dcc54ff0a19644e1a9ff6a2dd8595738</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRONINGEN FRAILTY INDICATOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Groningen Frailty Indicator is a tool used to assess frailty in elderly patients, focusing on their ability to perform daily activities and their overall health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3051</data>
      <data key="d7">976a3af79e8c462194d89e2f4bb5caba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TILBURG FRAILTY INDICATOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tilburg Frailty Indicator is a scale designed to evaluate frailty in older adults, assessing various physical and mental health aspects.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3052</data>
      <data key="d7">85d82566245243df8f38b88a918bd5a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Edmonton Frailty Scale is a comprehensive and multidimensional assessment tool designed to identify frailty in elderly patients. It evaluates frailty in older adults through a series of health-related questions and tests, which include the Timed-up-and-go test and assessments for cognitive impairment. This tool aims to provide a thorough evaluation of the health status of older individuals, helping to inform care and intervention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4,f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3053</data>
      <data key="d7">855c9511b1de46b085a6d717c495fd8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAIL SCALE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The FRAIL Scale is a simple tool used to assess frailty in older adults based on their energy levels and physical capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3054</data>
      <data key="d7">eeb7aa7bd4ce49f493e89f39be62d9f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "Anciano Fr&#225;gil" refers to an elderly person who is experiencing frailty, characterized by decreased physiological reserve and increased vulnerability to stressors. This condition is particularly significant as frail elderly individuals often require specific nutritional intervention guidelines due to their heightened risk of malnutrition. As such, the "Anciano Fr&#225;gil" represents a group of patients whose nutritional needs must be carefully managed to support their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a,79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,cc6ee3d7bc9bfaf4a06f3f02c4907eb0,f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">706</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">3055</data>
      <data key="d7">906d6d98d288477fb68e4b835245761e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABBREVIATED COMPREHENSIVE GERIATRIC ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Abbreviated Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment is a streamlined evaluation method used to assess the health and functional status of elderly patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3056</data>
      <data key="d7">5b196b7a5dbd4f9bbc371135e837c499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GERIATRIC 8">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Geriatric 8 is a screening tool that helps identify frailty and functional decline in older adults, facilitating timely interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3057</data>
      <data key="d7">5eb08b80f1004cfc961b380fac1fb34d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIAGE RISK SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Triage Risk Screening Tool is used to assess the risk of adverse events in elderly patients, aiding in the identification of those who may need further evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3058</data>
      <data key="d7">b7071b1e231e41fba3b4950b618f80ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROENING FRAILTY INDEX">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d3">483</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3059</data>
      <data key="d7">5f4ceb52316244f18591ce9b0fea628a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TWO-STEP OLDER PERSONS SCREENING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Two-step Older Persons Screening (EASY-Care TOS) is a tool designed to identify frailty in elderly individuals, providing a simple screening method for healthcare providers.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3060</data>
      <data key="d7">00775e509d5b409bac0416ca9b708d6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GERONTOPOLE FRAILTY SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gerontopole Frailty Screening Tool is a diagnostic tool developed in collaboration with primary care physicians to screen for frailty in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3061</data>
      <data key="d7">ef76978970b94c5bbdb0fac2cf0f9629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAILTY TRAIT SCALE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Frailty Trait Scale is a recently developed tool that identifies seven dimensions of frailty, including nutritional balance, physical activity, and cognitive function.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3062</data>
      <data key="d7">b03a3ee25c7c4d8b992b2e65efe868ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORLEY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Morley is a prominent researcher known for significant contributions to the field of gerontology, particularly in understanding physical frailty in the elderly. In 2013, Morley co-authored a consensus on frailty, which has enhanced the comprehension of this critical health issue. Additionally, Morley proposed four main mechanisms that are responsible for the origin of frailty: atherosclerosis, cognitive decline, malnutrition, and sarcopenia. These insights have been instrumental in advancing the knowledge and management of frailty among older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3063</data>
      <data key="d7">65b14b044eb9453e893744737bdd1809</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHYSICAL ACTIVITY SCALE FOR THE ELDERLY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Physical Activity Scale for the Elderly is a tool used to assess physical activity levels in older adults, which is one of the dimensions of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3064</data>
      <data key="d7">884c9acb0f264c20a7ea18706b116cd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHORT PHYSICAL PERFORMANCE BATTERY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Short Physical Performance Battery (SPPB) is a test used to measure physical performance in older adults, contributing to the assessment of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">479</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3065</data>
      <data key="d7">e7eb22e1a71542379f8bb51fdbc91adc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEPRESSION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Depression is a mental health condition that can significantly impact individuals, particularly the elderly, and is recognized as a background condition relevant to frailty assessment. It is characterized by persistent feelings of sadness, loss of interest, and various emotional and physical problems. In severe cases, depression can contraindicate the use of certain treatments, such as BN (a specific therapeutic intervention), highlighting the importance of careful assessment and management of this condition in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4,f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
      <data key="d3">248</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3066</data>
      <data key="d7">ce51297693bf413aa6d6b15109b936d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANGINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Angina is a type of chest pain caused by reduced blood flow to the heart, mentioned as a background condition in the context of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3067</data>
      <data key="d7">57bd8f13120a4dbda5f6d075b3c6d960</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEART ATTACK">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Heart attack is a medical emergency that occurs when blood flow to the heart is blocked, included as a background condition in frailty assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3068</data>
      <data key="d7">55967690b4b44cd3a2646dcc02f4e9d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARTHRITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arthritis is a condition characterized by inflammation of the joints, which is significant in the context of frailty. It is also recognized as a complication that may arise in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis, potentially linked to the deposition of iron in the joints.</data>
      <data key="d2">83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">1645</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3069</data>
      <data key="d7">1937fe768d9243c4ab70eb1cbc04f627</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASTHMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Asthma is a chronic respiratory condition that can impact the health of elderly individuals, listed as a background condition in frailty assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3070</data>
      <data key="d7">8de36bb088fa43e5bde2fc385ac8fcdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRONCHITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bronchitis is an inflammation of the lining of the bronchial tubes, mentioned as a background condition in the context of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3071</data>
      <data key="d7">7f4acd47543847a1b653d5c7e71430cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMPHYSEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Emphysema is a lung condition characterized by shortness of breath, and it is recognized as a background condition relevant to frailty. This pulmonary disease poses an increased risk for individuals with Klinefelter syndrome, highlighting the importance of monitoring respiratory health in this population.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3072</data>
      <data key="d7">49cde38c52084351bf55aeab01ba94b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertension (HTA) is a chronic medical condition characterized by persistently elevated blood pressure in the arteries. It requires careful management and lifestyle changes to mitigate its effects. Hypertension is commonly associated with various health issues, including obesity, diabetes, and metabolic syndrome, particularly in specific populations such as those with Klinefelter syndrome. It is also a significant risk factor for cardiovascular diseases, kidney disease, and complications related to diabetic nephropathy.

The condition can develop as a secondary effect of renal impairment and is often exacerbated by dietary factors, particularly high sodium intake. Hypertension is prevalent among the elderly and is considered a background condition in frailty assessments. It can complicate the management of diabetes and is linked to an increased risk of cognitive decline, including Alzheimer's disease and vascular dementia.

In some cases, hypertension may arise as a complication following liver transplantation, necessitating ongoing monitoring and management. Additionally, there are contraindications for certain treatments in patients with hypertension, highlighting the need for tailored approaches in their care. Overall, hypertension is a multifaceted condition that poses serious health risks and requires comprehensive management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">20863ac06779722abc2cbc2dd023777e,265fcc321b2c0bbf0bf8200d0489e1a1,3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,49279a0184d5222e806637f084f42c50,4a59488a9440b38afba989ca88d49ca3,53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,63593ac5546e44eaddb37a2f257bfa80,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83,b49f181ca7099fc110f35ccc27e7fafc,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4,dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7,f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a,fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1633</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">39</data>
      <data key="d6">3073</data>
      <data key="d7">98127fc1c5964498ad2d865fd536b16f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteoporosis is a medical condition characterized by weakened and brittle bones, leading to an increased risk of fractures. It is often linked to various factors, including vitamin D deficiency, calcium deficiency, and hormonal imbalances. The condition is prevalent among older adults, particularly postmenopausal women, and can be exacerbated by long-term corticosteroid use, eating disorders such as Anorexia Nervosa, and certain metabolic bone diseases.

Osteoporosis can develop due to insufficient dietary intake of calcium and vitamin D, lack of exercise, and malnutrition, which may occur in patients with conditions like celiac disease or those receiving prolonged parenteral nutrition. It is also observed in patients with specific genetic conditions, such as Turner syndrome and Klinefelter syndrome, as well as in individuals with chronic illnesses like Wilson's disease, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), and cystic fibrosis.

The disease is more severe than osteopenia, involving significant bone loss and deterioration of bone microarchitecture. It is often described as a silent disease, as it can lead to spontaneous fractures or fractures from minimal trauma, resulting in long-term consequences such as chronic pain or deformities. Treatment options typically include bisphosphonates, dietary changes, and calcium supplementation, aimed at improving bone density and reducing fracture risk.

Overall, osteoporosis is a complex condition influenced by genetic, nutritional, and lifestyle factors, and it poses a significant public health concern due to its impact on bone health and associated healthcare costs.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98,17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b,18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,4a59488a9440b38afba989ca88d49ca3,5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1,68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2,700a4472a23342b891a5685b622437d2,770e8796aac9c96d967ef99d1f307e06,7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90,bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb,d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
