      <data key="d6">3076</data>
      <data key="d7">5e7f344a98724077bb517b105f07eccf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REV ESP GERIATR GERONTOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Rev Esp Geriatr Gerontol, also known as Revista Espa&#241;ola de Geriatr&#237;a y Gerontolog&#237;a, is a journal dedicated to the field of geriatrics and gerontology. It publishes a variety of research and reviews focused on the geriatric population, including studies on nutritional assessment, frailty, and the aging process. The journal serves as a significant resource for advancing knowledge and understanding in these areas, contributing to the overall discourse on elderly care and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">caab2e12a2bce3c947d663cf8b71cb67,cb8368db73f739b1f11f2a202c776e6d</data>
      <data key="d3">1760</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3077</data>
      <data key="d7">ec1afdc82a8a486ca2006851c0ee41e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IL-1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Interleukin-1 (IL-1) is a cytokine that plays a significant role in inflammatory responses. It is associated with the aging process and is linked to conditions such as frailty, particularly in the elderly population. The cytokine's involvement in inflammation highlights its importance in various physiological and pathological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000,caab2e12a2bce3c947d663cf8b71cb67</data>
      <data key="d3">469</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3078</data>
      <data key="d7">597258a148c9487997515369217ccafe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NA C REACTIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C-reactive protein (CRP), known in Spanish as "Prote&#237;na C Reactiva," is a substance synthesized in the liver that serves as a marker of general inflammation. It reflects the body's nutritional status and is particularly relevant in assessing inflammatory conditions. Elevated levels of CRP are commonly observed in frail elderly individuals, indicating a potential risk of fragility in this population. Additionally, CRP is utilized in the nutritional assessment of burn patients, highlighting its importance in various clinical contexts related to inflammation and nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">241d358b60724c07a75223b79c9e5f41,a6ed8551aad722adcaf8fced4ac8685b,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02,bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c,caab2e12a2bce3c947d663cf8b71cb67,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3079</data>
      <data key="d7">a95d695f837c4dcdb8764cdd65037d3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTOR VIII">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Factor VIII is a blood coagulation factor that can be elevated in frail elderly individuals, indicating a potential link to inflammation and frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">caab2e12a2bce3c947d663cf8b71cb67</data>
      <data key="d3">469</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
