    <node id="DISABILITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Disability in elderly individuals is a significant concern that intersects with frailty and has a profound impact on their quality of life. In older adults, disability can arise from various conditions, including sarcopenia, which leads to difficulties in performing daily tasks and increased dependence on others for assistance. This highlights the importance of addressing disability in the aging population to enhance their overall well-being and independence.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,72bafac70ee8322d8f303cf94612b461</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3096</data>
      <data key="d7">3def5d9face64da59ed6c47c4209ac11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aging is a complex process that primarily affects the elderly population, resulting in increased vulnerability and a heightened need for interventions related to frailty. This process involves not only the physical aspects of becoming older but also encompasses cognitive decline, which can lead to an increased risk of diseases such as dementia and Alzheimer's. As individuals age, they may experience various challenges that necessitate support and care to maintain their quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">680ff2c9e67ec29c5952df66bd83c984,72bafac70ee8322d8f303cf94612b461</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
