      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3097</data>
      <data key="d7">83d4171645ba4ac39be19504621fa051</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRIED">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Fried is a prominent figure in the field of gerontology, recognized for co-authoring the recent consensus on frailty published in 2013. This work significantly contributed to the understanding of physical frailty in the elderly population. Additionally, Fried refers to a set of diagnostic criteria for frailty that was developed by a researcher in this area, further establishing its importance in assessing and addressing frailty among older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972,6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3098</data>
      <data key="d7">22b35e71b1d945b3913cc3e31b1d2dee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROCKWOOD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Rockwood is a classification system designed to evaluate the physical capacity and fragility of elderly individuals. It categorizes these individuals based on their physical condition and levels of dependency, providing a structured approach to understanding their health status. Additionally, Rockwood is recognized as a co-author of the recent consensus on frailty published in 2013, which has significantly contributed to the understanding of physical frailty in the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49,6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3099</data>
      <data key="d7">e1d1021de09d42f0a61f306eef93194f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIX SOCIEDADES CIENT&#205;FICAS INTERNACIONALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A collaboration of six international scientific societies that participated in the recent consensus on frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3100</data>
      <data key="d7">0fdd77f93df546d194726a0d7d862bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The S&#237;ndrome de Fragilidad, or frailty syndrome, is a clinical condition primarily affecting the elderly, characterized by a notable decrease in functionality and an increased vulnerability to adverse health events. This syndrome manifests through a specific group of signs and symptoms that indicate an abnormality in the health and functional independence of older adults. Importantly, the frailty syndrome is treatable and reversible, highlighting the potential for intervention before significant functional deterioration occurs.</data>
      <data key="d2">1052683f23a0c9825af9c5c1d39ceb2c,4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58,6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">3101</data>
      <data key="d7">b2eb40938d754e2da0202d7fb83a4d96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEPENDENCIA FUNCIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Functional dependence refers to the inability to perform basic daily activities independently, often associated with frailty in the elderly.</data>
      <data key="d2">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3102</data>
      <data key="d7">c2117282e7d541759416ddcf17c54609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISCAPACIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DISCAPACIDAD refers to a condition characterized by reduced physical capabilities, which can arise from various factors, including sarcopenia. Additionally, disability is often a severe consequence of the frailty syndrome, highlighting the necessity for assistance in daily activities. This underscores the impact of disability on individuals' ability to perform everyday tasks and the importance of support systems for those affected.</data>
      <data key="d2">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3103</data>
      <data key="d7">e85090eacb4347d2840bf9d83e977dd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTORES NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"FACTORES NUTRICIONALES" refers to the nutritional elements that significantly influence the fragility and overall health of elderly individuals. These factors are crucial in both the development and management of frailty among the aging population, highlighting their importance in promoting better health outcomes for seniors.</data>
      <data key="d2">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32,bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3104</data>
      <data key="d7">f37d485883894ec281655598567da558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRITERIOS DE FRIED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los criterios de Fried son un conjunto de par&#225;metros utilizados para diagnosticar la fragilidad en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3105</data>
      <data key="d7">479f53bfbf6e4ceabc7efd6f6750e625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N MULTIDIMENSIONAL DE ROCKWOOD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La valoraci&#243;n multidimensional de Rockwood es una herramienta para evaluar la fragilidad en personas mayores.</data>
      <data key="d2">bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
