    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL FRAILTY SCALE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Clinical Frailty Scale is a diagnostic tool used to evaluate the level of frailty in elderly patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3114</data>
      <data key="d7">2a25defe5ce24f90a0de567d7a9b3b0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="G&#201;RONTOP&#212;LE FRAILTY SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The G&#233;rontop&#244;le Frailty Screening Tool is a comprehensive assessment tool for identifying frailty in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3115</data>
      <data key="d7">0ab3a7cbe1564632a3fed55de4b28953</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GERIATRIC INTEGRAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Geriatric Integral Assessment is a multidimensional evaluation process for assessing the medical, functional, psychological, and social status of frail elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3116</data>
      <data key="d7">90867538d96244a0914e5574056189ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELDERLY POPULATION">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The elderly population refers to individuals aged 70 and above who may be at risk of frailty and adverse health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">471</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3117</data>
      <data key="d7">aff50e14d4e14e8f939680bda25b5a03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTIMORBIDITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Multimorbidity refers to the presence of multiple chronic conditions in an individual, which can increase the risk of frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">471</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3118</data>
      <data key="d7">2479796c61774fce83bce7f57d139bf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPECIALIZED CARE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Specialized Care refers to healthcare services that deliver advanced treatment and management for specific health conditions, often involving a multidisciplinary team of healthcare professionals. This type of care is particularly important for patients with unique medical needs, such as those experiencing specific complications following bariatric surgery. By focusing on tailored approaches to treatment, Specialized Care aims to improve patient outcomes and ensure comprehensive management of complex health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870,db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3119</data>
      <data key="d7">d6308175e5d94024912d407a55799c6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEART FAILURE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Heart failure is a chronic medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood effectively, which can lead to various health complications. Its progression can be positively influenced by lifestyle choices, such as adherence to the Mediterranean diet. Heart failure is frequently discussed in clinical guidelines and studies, highlighting its significance in medical research and practice. 

In older adults, heart failure can exacerbate sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, and it can also increase the risk of frailty due to its detrimental effects on physical health and functional capacity. Additionally, heart failure is a serious condition that can be complicated by iron overload, particularly in patients with hemochromatosis, making it a critical consideration in their management. Overall, heart failure presents a multifaceted challenge that requires careful attention to both dietary and medical management to improve patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271,97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,eb275fa50517d86a71589fd318784a5b</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3120</data>
      <data key="d7">2207df70d5a445eaa6dfb92f96143b97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHRONIC KIDNEY DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic kidney disease (CKD) is a long-term condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to function effectively, which can significantly impact overall health and bodily functions. This condition often necessitates dietary management, particularly concerning phosphorus and calcium, as imbalances in these minerals can adversely affect bone health. Additionally, CKD is associated with muscle wasting and is frequently linked to sarcopenia, especially in older populations. The effects of chronic kidney disease can lead to frailty in the elderly, further complicating their health status and quality of life. Nutritional support and careful management are essential components in addressing the challenges posed by this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,08bc4a83d18482b48f5bbef4fbf316f3,5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2,8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8,97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">1650</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3121</data>
      <data key="d7">4ff7186825f240ea9bc04eedd66f27b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIV INFECTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIV infection is a chronic condition that can lead to frailty in elderly individuals, affecting their immune system and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">471</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3122</data>
      <data key="d7">7fbbf888673946feb70415acf1c51635</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SURGICAL INTERVENTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Surgical intervention refers to medical procedures that can impact the health status of elderly individuals, potentially leading to frailty post-operation.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">471</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3123</data>
      <data key="d7">f4337eb0c81c4729b8b989bb016d9ab5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATTENTION PRIMARY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3124</data>
      <data key="d7">b03dbc1050894f36a374085b126395b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COCHRANE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cochrane is a global independent organization that conducts systematic reviews on the effectiveness of health interventions, including strength training for the elderly. It comprises a network of researchers, professionals, patients, and individuals interested in health. Cochrane is dedicated to producing high-quality, relevant, and accessible systematic reviews and other synthesized research evidence to inform health decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d2">4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58,61eea56f443c7bb2509edd6f42af2643</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3125</data>
      <data key="d7">8e19a68363e1409091f8837b28003b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTACI&#211;N PROTEICO-CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La suplementaci&#243;n proteico-cal&#243;rica se refiere a la ingesta adicional de prote&#237;nas y calor&#237;as para mejorar la salud y combatir la desnutrici&#243;n en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3126</data>
      <data key="d7">ae8c6dfa96ff43ef9ac52f0d86599697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BATER&#205;A BREVE DE RENDIMIENTO F&#205;SICO (SPPB)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La bater&#237;a breve de rendimiento f&#237;sico (SPPB) eval&#250;a el equilibrio, marcha, fuerza y resistencia en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3127</data>
      <data key="d7">7e67322399cc4af5a89138651675aa2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VELOCIDAD DE LA MARCHA HABITUAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La velocidad de la marcha habitual es una prueba que mide la capacidad funcional y predictiva de limitaci&#243;n en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3128</data>
      <data key="d7">d2cd6a3da0d54c47b2720a6664ae5e68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRUEBA CRONOMETRADA DE LEV&#193;NTATE Y ANDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La prueba cronometrada de lev&#225;ntate y anda mide el rendimiento f&#237;sico y el equilibrio en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58</data>
      <data key="d3">1783</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3129</data>
      <data key="d7">ba6f1b0927cc4676bfaf3fda5dbff9fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEXA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DEXA, or Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry, is a medical imaging technique widely recognized for its ability to measure bone density and body composition. This method is particularly useful in assessing various health conditions, including chronic respiratory diseases and sarcopenia, as it provides critical insights into muscle mass and fat distribution. DEXA scans are recommended for patients with certain conditions, such as cystic fibrosis, starting from the age of 8 to 10, and are also employed to evaluate nutritional status in patients with cirrhosis.

The technique is considered the gold standard for measuring muscle mass, especially in the diagnosis of sarcopenia, and is effective in calculating both fat and lean mass. However, it is important to note that DEXA may underestimate bone density in patients of shorter stature. Overall, DEXA serves as a vital tool in the clinical assessment of bone health and body composition, providing essential data for managing various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b,18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8,4913cc391a44397e2e1ea12979e1fd58,76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281,f5660be03d70d5dd506c197283dd79ae,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
