    <node id="EUROPEAN WORKING GROUP ON SARCOPENIA IN OLDER PEOPLE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Working Group on Sarcopenia in Older People is a consortium dedicated to the definition and diagnosis of sarcopenia in older adults. This group has developed a consensus on the criteria for identifying sarcopenia, aiming to provide clear guidelines and recommendations for clinical practice. By focusing on older individuals, the European Working Group seeks to enhance understanding and management of this condition, which is characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff,ea432f742f5cd2b4840a984ae35a9d09</data>
