    </node>
    <node id="BMJ">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The British Medical Journal (BMJ) is a leading peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes a wide range of research articles, reviews, and meta-analyses across various health topics. It is known for its contributions to the medical field, including systematic reviews and meta-analyses on subjects such as fruit and vegetable intake and its relationship with type 2 diabetes, as well as obesity and its treatments. BMJ also provides valuable resources for practitioners, such as guides on understanding medical literature, exemplified by its publication "How to read a paper: the basics of evidence-based medicine." The journal covers diverse areas of medicine, including geriatrics, and is published weekly, making it a significant source of information for healthcare professionals and researchers alike.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,36823f72c2a40918b243d0c6f175c0e4,3af2658fd59065a71bfee00d2bd27b1b,3ec3efbe130c20d623681e00e3d784f7,56fede71b721264441e35be77e3ed1d1,9ec3bf4d23f9f4fca8984c81d95aac41,b2549791b62afc5e1244c2c610af55e6,cf833689453c8ce13d3650766a8b47a7,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,dd05b76341cb3efe3f7a515a4ed1a030,e376d9f50b7608f5b6d1f88877fde59e,ea432f742f5cd2b4840a984ae35a9d09,eb275fa50517d86a71589fd318784a5b,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
