    </node>
    <node id="HEALTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Health in elderly individuals is influenced by various factors, including nutrition, physical activity, and cognitive function.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3160</data>
      <data key="d7">bc84f0ea2881423cb08c20e2377c6f11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRCULO VICIOSO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The vicious cycle refers to the interrelationship between physical decline, cognitive decline, frailty, and sarcopenia in the elderly.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3161</data>
      <data key="d7">2c6d2656ceae4306b7631e8e4d30d7ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIFICULTADES PARA CAMINAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Walking difficulties in elderly individuals are associated with higher risks of cognitive decline and dementia.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3162</data>
      <data key="d7">d7c3e3212e384ee5b53ebebcd1c63d7d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEST COGNITIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cognitive tests are used to assess cognitive function and identify potential declines in elderly patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3163</data>
      <data key="d7">77867dee07f04b7e8e2a306ad863844e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N Y FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The relationship between nutrition and frailty is crucial in understanding how dietary interventions can impact elderly health.</data>
      <data key="d2">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3164</data>
      <data key="d7">472b54beeb744c1b93e7cb972a98ec3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MCI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) is a condition that often precedes Alzheimer's disease. It is characterized by noticeable memory and cognitive difficulties, which are significant enough to be recognized but not severe enough to interfere significantly with daily life.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1642</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3165</data>
      <data key="d7">93a322dfa5dd4bff95409268aa7f253c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CVD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiovascular disease (CVD) encompasses a variety of conditions that impact the heart and blood vessels. These diseases have been associated with an elevated risk of developing Alzheimer's disease and other forms of dementia. Additionally, research suggests that omega-3 fatty acids may play a role in preventing CVD. Furthermore, CVD can be influenced by dietary choices and the consumption of fats, highlighting the importance of nutrition in managing cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061</data>
      <data key="d3">1648</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3166</data>
      <data key="d7">22319cfb1cd6498bb1e01e9545c436d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vascular dementia (VaD) is a type of dementia caused by reduced blood flow to the brain, often associated with cardiovascular issues and risk factors similar to those of Alzheimer's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132</data>
      <data key="d3">1642</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3167</data>
      <data key="d7">61a1f08a3b9c44289cef3e9433ca78b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APOE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Apolipoprotein E (APOE) is a gene that has been identified as a significant genetic risk factor for Alzheimer's disease, particularly the &#949;4 allele which increases the likelihood of developing the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3168</data>
      <data key="d7">56f9a9e5da1748ce854c38640245c284</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHRONIC DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic diseases are long-lasting conditions that can significantly impact an individual's health, particularly cognitive health, and are associated with an increased risk of developing dementia, including Alzheimer's disease. These conditions can be managed and controlled through various means, often linked to dietary intake, but they cannot be cured.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95</data>
      <data key="d3">1565</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3169</data>
      <data key="d7">c3efc29b7d5c41cba1802e012165bdf3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES METAB&#211;LICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ENFERMEDADES METAB&#211;LICAS refer to a group of disorders that impact the body's metabolism. These diseases are associated with various metabolic processes and have been linked to an increased risk of cognitive decline and dementia.</data>
      <data key="d2">01eb4b96cd8e6a886ebc313171922a77,53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132</data>
      <data key="d3">1391</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3170</data>
      <data key="d7">0e3ceac883b44a97b5e72b0bcd2ce922</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES RESPIRATORIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ENFERMEDADES RESPIRATORIAS refers to respiratory diseases, which are a significant area of research in Spain, particularly through the CIBERes center dedicated to this field. CIBERes is a CIBER center focused on advancing the understanding and treatment of respiratory diseases. These conditions not only affect overall health but have also been linked to cognitive decline, which may increase the risk of developing dementia.</data>
      <data key="d2">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,ce0de74f95e1a41a930b2df09da1f887</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3171</data>
      <data key="d7">a649a9842c8b4d198f9d00ea2d6eedc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES" refers to a group of disorders that affect the heart and blood vessels, encompassing a wide range of health conditions. These diseases are significantly influenced by various factors, including dietary choices, lifestyle habits, and nutritional intake. Key dietary influences include vitamin D levels, the consumption of salt, dairy products, trans fats, and sugary beverages, as well as the balance of fats and carbohydrates in the diet. 

Cardiovascular diseases are particularly concerning for patients with chronic kidney disease, where phosphorus levels play a critical role. They are also major complications associated with diabetes, which can increase mortality risk. Furthermore, these diseases are linked to other serious health issues, such as Alzheimer's disease and other dementias, highlighting their broad impact on overall health.

In Western countries, cardiovascular diseases are the leading cause of death and disability, often associated with modifiable risk factors like hypertension and type 2 diabetes. As such, they represent one of the primary health threats in the 21st century. Preventative measures through improved nutrition and lifestyle changes are essential in mitigating the risks associated with these conditions.

Additionally, "ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES" is a focus area within one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, emphasizing the importance of ongoing research and intervention strategies in addressing cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0090177678aee58d08471d09d24d2842,035d53a7f46fdb72c0a939265667044b,05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a,5173ac9bd92d5f238acade41f8c65ebf,53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074,c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
