    </node>
    <node id="TEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TEA, particularly black and green tea, is recognized for its potential health benefits, including the prevention of cognitive decline and dementia, attributed to its active ingredients such as catechins. Additionally, green tea is emphasized as a significant source of flavonoids and antioxidants, which may contribute to reducing the risk of cardiovascular disease. Overall, TEA is associated with various health-promoting properties that support both cognitive and cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1642</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3177</data>
      <data key="d7">08a50a8a8d5347e4ba9d0faaed26ecf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATECHINS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Catechins are antioxidants found in tea that may help protect brain cells and reduce cognitive decline.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1642</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3178</data>
      <data key="d7">6c62246af2414afb8030e67947cff4bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXERCISE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Exercise is a vital form of physical activity that plays a significant role in enhancing the health and well-being of individuals, particularly older adults. It is recommended to be combined with protein intake to prevent muscle loss in the elderly, making it an essential intervention for improving muscle function and physical capability, especially for those at risk of sarcopenia and frailty. Regular physical activity is crucial for managing various health conditions, including diabetes and hypertension, and is beneficial for overall health.

In addition to its physical benefits, exercise is known to enhance cognitive function and may contribute to cognitive health, potentially helping to prevent dementia. It is also important for improving strength, balance, and overall functional capacity, which are critical for maintaining independence in older adults. Furthermore, regular physical exercise is important for preventing osteoporosis and maintaining bone health. Overall, exercise is a comprehensive approach to improving both physical and cognitive health in the elderly, promoting a better quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f194bef97e28167f81acc7a66ac56ab,3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1,680ff2c9e67ec29c5952df66bd83c984,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,a4b144210b0a4b654a260ebc394de0af,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
