      <data key="d6">3180</data>
      <data key="d7">60d79df3d51d4954b336e8d8dc8ae4f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREALS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cereals are a diverse group of grains that encompass wheat, barley, rye, and oats. These grains are significant in various diets, including the Mediterranean diet, where they serve as a staple food. While cereals are important for cognitive health, it is essential to note that they contain gluten, which can be problematic for individuals with celiac disease. Overall, cereals play a crucial role in nutrition and dietary practices across different cultures.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3181</data>
      <data key="d7">1fede505c7af4a1a8eda7b7eba15a711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VEGETABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vegetables are a vital food group that plays a significant role in human nutrition and health. They are known to provide essential nutrients, including calcium, particularly from leafy greens; however, the absorption rates of calcium from vegetables may be lower compared to dairy sources. Research has indicated that vegetables can impact cancer risk, highlighting their importance in disease prevention. Additionally, for patients with potassium restrictions, the consumption of vegetables may need to be limited, as they can contribute to overall potassium intake.

In the context of dietary patterns, vegetables are a cornerstone of the Mediterranean diet, which is recognized for its health benefits. They are nutrient-dense foods that not only support cardiovascular health but also help reduce risk factors associated with chronic diseases, including cardiovascular disease and cancer. Furthermore, vegetables are linked to improved cognitive health, underscoring their importance in a balanced and healthy diet. Overall, vegetables are essential components of a nutritious diet, contributing to overall well-being and disease prevention.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b79601d85087d62f0d4890761776c04,5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363,581527a14dedf97c7a839eff5c40cbc2,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3182</data>
      <data key="d7">0b79df6a90d84137afb6985e4f26bbfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUITS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fruits are a vital food group recognized for their potential impact on cancer risk and are a significant component of the Mediterranean diet, which recommends their daily consumption. They are natural foods that provide essential vitamins and antioxidants, contributing to overall health and supporting cognitive function. However, it is important to note that fruits may be limited in the diets of patients undergoing certain dietary restrictions, particularly those with potassium limitations.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b79601d85087d62f0d4890761776c04,5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363,581527a14dedf97c7a839eff5c40cbc2,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3183</data>
      <data key="d7">e0dc4050428a499483c822786bd202c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fish is a highly regarded dietary source of omega-3 fatty acids, which are essential for various aspects of health. It is particularly recommended for improving cardiovascular health and is noted for its role in the prevention and treatment of cardiovascular disease. Fatty fish, especially blue fish, are highlighted for their rich content of these beneficial omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, fish is recognized for its positive effects on brain health, making it a valuable component of a balanced diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">41d7db510fc74d3763959481cc15ea20,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">1636</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3184</data>
      <data key="d7">df3b4473e3df467e9c2279896fc66ebb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED MEAT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Red meat is a type of meat that is consumed in moderation within the Mediterranean diet. Its consumption can have an impact on health outcomes, suggesting that while it can be part of a balanced diet, attention to portion sizes and frequency of intake is important for overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1620</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3185</data>
      <data key="d7">cb290209e8db4cf4af2d32600cc23487</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAIRY PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dairy products, such as butter and cream, are included in the Mediterranean diet in small amounts and can influence health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3186</data>
      <data key="d7">968de8d0125347b79b1c5dc4bc1ae461</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcohol is a substance that can have a wide range of effects on health, particularly when consumed in excess. It interacts with various medications, leading to pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic interactions that can modify drug metabolism and enhance or diminish their effects. This can result in significant health implications, especially for individuals on medication.

In terms of metabolic effects, alcohol consumption can influence triglyceride levels in the blood, impacting lipid metabolism. It also has implications for blood sugar control and weight management in diabetic patients, with recommendations for moderate intake. Furthermore, alcohol is a frequent cause of acute pancreatitis, particularly in Scandinavian countries and urban areas of the United States, contributing to up to 75% of cases in some regions.

Dietary guidelines address alcohol consumption, recommending moderation to reduce health risks. For instance, it is linked to hypertension, with suggestions to limit intake to manage blood pressure effectively. Additionally, alcohol consumption is associated with higher uric acid levels, increasing the risk of developing gout, especially with certain types of alcoholic beverages.

In specific populations, such as those who have undergone bariatric surgery or individuals with obesity, alcohol consumption is advised to be restricted to avoid complications and negative health effects. Chronic alcohol consumption can lead to decreased bone mineral density (BMD) and hypomagnesemia due to direct tubular toxicity and other metabolic effects. It is also noted that excessive alcohol intake can contribute to various diseases, including cancer and cardiovascular diseases, and can negatively affect the absorption of essential nutrients like calcium and phosphorus.

Moderate consumption of alcohol, particularly red wine, is sometimes included in dietary patterns like the Mediterranean diet, which may offer certain health benefits. However, it is crucial to avoid alcohol for at least 12 hours prior to medical tests to ensure accurate results. Additionally, the alcohol content in beverages must be indicated on labels if it exceeds 1.2%.

Overall, while alcohol can have some health benefits when consumed in moderation, excessive intake poses significant health risks and should be approached with caution.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,108b158c33fead285203903273758748,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1,71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,7ff62e1dc423be2f4b2fe08546751d0d,8255943be503f6709a8e63d7d33b79d1,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5,b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,b9342cecd69cdc0e9936df041657f5f5,c4f12f866dc714cdbb2323a920f524c2,ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e,e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
