      <data key="d7">3f2f891ac3d94145acf539e65b1d9b71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESOLVINA D1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Resolvin D1 is a lipid mediator synthesized from DHA that enhances immune cell activity against beta-amyloid plaques.</data>
      <data key="d2">dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3196</data>
      <data key="d7">ce450f930cca4a91bc2e313e3b5d8376</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OMEGA-3 FATTY ACIDS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Omega-3 fatty acids are a group of essential polyunsaturated fatty acids that play a significant role in promoting cardiovascular health. They are commonly found in fish and other dietary sources and have been the subject of extensive research, particularly in clinical trials, to explore their potential health benefits. These fatty acids are recognized for their ability to reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease and may also have a positive impact on cancer risk. Additionally, Omega-3 fatty acids are believed to support cognitive health and may contribute to maintaining muscle mass and function, especially in older adults. Furthermore, they are considered beneficial in the nutritional support of patients suffering from pancreatitis. Overall, Omega-3 fatty acids are vital nutrients that offer a range of health advantages.</data>
      <data key="d2">69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3,6a95bf35e698b03ca552f2c75d5d60ef,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,bb2e69a0ff4c25a21149882162922c8d,cf833689453c8ce13d3650766a8b47a7,dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34,e271766bdc88e84209e5cdac4adc0724</data>
      <data key="d3">1620</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">3197</data>
      <data key="d7">a6558536aa7446bba3a14de3caeef941</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMENTIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dementia is a progressive neurological condition characterized by a decline in cognitive function that significantly impacts memory, thinking, and social abilities, ultimately interfering with daily life. It is often associated with Alzheimer's disease and can complicate the management of enteral nutrition, particularly in elderly patients. The condition necessitates tailored nutritional support to improve patient outcomes, with studies indicating that dietary factors, such as omega-3 fatty acids, may play a role in its management. Additionally, dementia can lead to complications like dysphagia, further complicating nutritional considerations for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,91b470ee527a45d8e81a821eeb9ce259,b3760fcb9c0421b66d37c20b1dc68577,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34,dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d3">1655</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">3198</data>
      <data key="d7">59f4072820ab4647a29767e9575a18fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIGLYCERIDES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Triglycerides (TG) are a type of fat found in the blood that play a crucial role in various health contexts. They are essential to monitor in patients with pancreatitis to prevent complications, as elevated levels can pose significant health risks. High triglyceride levels are associated with an increased risk of heart disease, making them a critical component of lipid panels used in routine health assessments. 

The levels of triglycerides can be influenced by dietary intake, particularly in individuals with diabetes, highlighting the importance of nutrition in managing lipid levels. Additionally, triglycerides are significant in ketogenic diets, where they can induce ketosis, a metabolic state that some individuals seek for weight loss or other health benefits. In clinical settings, triglycerides can also be administered as part of lipid emulsions to provide energy for critically ill patients, underscoring their importance in medical nutrition therapy.

The introduction of Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) in 1950 marked a significant advancement in the treatment of lipid absorption and metabolism disorders, further emphasizing the evolving understanding and management of triglycerides in health and disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc,55b85a76a2c3d515bd3fe6137255abac,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,a66b01654a2f495559fd1a24efc0e64e,dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34</data>
      <data key="d3">1648</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3199</data>
      <data key="d7">6051685010a449f5a889192cae54b14b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LDL CHOLESTEROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol is often referred to as "bad" cholesterol, which can lead to atherosclerosis and cardiovascular issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34</data>
      <data key="d3">1648</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3200</data>
      <data key="d7">771ec3cf962f4854b6a152dceac34882</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACROPHAGES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Macrophages are immune cells that play a role in the body's defense and can help dissolve beta-amyloid plaques in the brain.</data>
      <data key="d2">dd8c7ee9ef48992cebb11e84fbb0fe34</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3201</data>
      <data key="d7">435990f8f59647269b425f890f8bd79d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETA-CAROTENE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Beta-carotene is a precursor to vitamin A and has antioxidant properties that may protect against oxidative stress in the brain.</data>
      <data key="d2">75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3202</data>
      <data key="d7">2067a1521b0f4d908199eb9fe613687e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLAVONOIDS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Flavonoids are water-soluble plant pigments found in a variety of foods, including tea, onions, soy, and wine. These compounds serve as potent inhibitors of various cytochrome P450 enzymes, which play a crucial role in drug metabolism. In addition to their enzymatic inhibition, flavonoids possess significant antioxidant properties, which may help reduce inflammation and oxidative stress in the body. Their contribution to the antioxidant capacity of the diet is noteworthy, as they are associated with a reduced risk of cardiovascular disease. Overall, flavonoids are important plant metabolites that offer various health benefits through their biochemical activities.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8</data>
      <data key="d3">1644</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3203</data>
      <data key="d7">b89b945b767f4d69909d665cbe5716e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXIDATIVE STRESS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxidative stress refers to an imbalance between free radicals and antioxidants in the body, which can contribute to various chronic diseases. This condition is characterized by damage caused by free radicals, which are unstable molecules that can harm cellular structures. The implications of oxidative stress are significant, as it is linked to the development of neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3204</data>
      <data key="d7">9cbf73a9113b4586a031c38a55a2745a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEURODEGENERATIVE DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurodegenerative diseases are conditions characterized by the progressive degeneration of the structure and function of the nervous system.</data>
      <data key="d2">75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8</data>
      <data key="d3">1626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3205</data>
      <data key="d7">ac4c1919c33741cd9213c71c664be3bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMOCYSTEINE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Homocysteine is an amino acid found in the blood that plays a significant role in various health conditions. Elevated levels of homocysteine are associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular issues and cognitive decline, as well as neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer's. Additionally, high levels of homocysteine are considered neurotoxic. The concentration of homocysteine in the blood is influenced by the levels of essential vitamins, specifically vitamin B6, B12, and folate. Furthermore, homocysteine is linked to various metabolic disorders, highlighting its importance in overall health and disease risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">75457662a196b78b5738344c4dbd89a8,7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1,b3760fcb9c0421b66d37c20b1dc68577</data>
      <data key="d3">1658</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">3206</data>
      <data key="d7">27b4f6915afe4d8593f4c51f7e754ce2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIOXIDANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Antioxidantes are compounds that play a significant role in health and wellness, particularly in the context of chronic kidney disease, where they may improve patient outcomes through dietary interventions. These substances are known for their ability to protect cells from damage caused by free radicals, which are unstable molecules that can lead to oxidative stress. This protective function is associated with various health benefits, including support for muscle health and cognitive function. Additionally, antioxidants are utilized in food preservation to prevent oxidation, with examples including citric acid and butylated hydroxyanisole. Overall, antioxidants are vital for maintaining cellular integrity and promoting overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc,ee7fb587e5ab0f265d2036071b632b36</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3207</data>
      <data key="d7">f3de3fc82e9f4cb8b1ebac2e4b95be2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMOCISTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Homociste&#237;na is an amino acid that is produced during the metabolism of methionine and is formed from protein metabolism. It is known to accumulate in the body due to various metabolic disorders, which can lead to significant health issues. Elevated levels of homociste&#237;na are associated with several problems, including cardiovascular diseases and cognitive decline, such as dementia. Additionally, high levels of this amino acid can damage blood vessels, further increasing the risk of cardiovascular complications. A deficiency in Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; can also lead to increased homociste&#237;na levels, highlighting the importance of proper nutritional intake for maintaining healthy levels of this amino acid. Overall, monitoring and managing homociste&#237;na levels is crucial for preventing associated health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7,499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,b1d588e0c9c4cef32da41373afbd1901,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">1640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">3208</data>
      <data key="d7">a59645cb60974523b0d09a8d03150a47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES DE ALZHEIMER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients with Alzheimer's disease often exhibit low levels of vitamin D and may benefit from nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f</data>
