      <data key="d6">3211</data>
      <data key="d7">eaa070c412cd4305b9e0c12ab1f974b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENSAYOS CONTROLADOS ALEATORIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Randomized controlled trials are studies that randomly assign participants to different interventions to compare outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3212</data>
      <data key="d7">9153d98abb374d5a81fd01105efe2e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIENCIA DE VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La deficiencia de vitamina D es una condici&#243;n que puede provocar hipocalcemia y est&#225; asociada con una serie de problemas de salud. Esta deficiencia puede resultar en un aumento de la hormona paratiroidea (PTH) y est&#225; relacionada con un mayor riesgo de fracturas y otras enfermedades. Adem&#225;s, se ha vinculado a un deterioro cognitivo y puede aumentar el riesgo de demencia. En conjunto, estos efectos destacan la importancia de mantener niveles adecuados de vitamina D para la salud general y el bienestar.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">617</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3213</data>
      <data key="d7">2b844b3936cf44ffa7e455d936b1fd79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE SELENIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Selenium levels in the blood are associated with cognitive health, with low levels indicating a higher risk of cognitive decline.</data>
      <data key="d2">7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3214</data>
      <data key="d7">a24a5ddbfb8041ebbb7497dbd3868604</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLAVONOIDES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Flavonoids are compounds known for their role as inhibitors or inducers of hepatic enzyme systems, which can modify drug bioavailability. Additionally, they are recognized as antioxidant compounds that may have beneficial effects on cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e</data>
      <data key="d3">1641</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3215</data>
      <data key="d7">c3b8afcbda9048738fa552f288026b1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las vitaminas B, incluyendo B&#8326;, B&#8329; y B&#8321;&#8322;, son nutrientes esenciales que pueden ayudar a reducir los niveles de homociste&#237;na y el riesgo de enfermedades cognitivas.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d3">1640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3216</data>
      <data key="d7">1ab41b5fb2714fcdbc0eb8910c7cdc2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">EUROPA, or Europe, is a continent characterized by a variety of health-related issues and dietary habits. It has a notable prevalence of celiac disease, with an incidence ranging from 1 in 85 to 1 in 540 individuals. The continent's dietary patterns reveal that saturated fat consumption primarily comes from meats and dairy products, which contributes to mortality rates associated with cardiovascular diseases (ECV). 

In terms of nutritional health, Europe has seen an increase in the consumption of vitamin B supplements, particularly among individuals facing cognitive challenges. Additionally, it is estimated that between 10,000 and 15,000 people with short bowel syndrome in Europe rely on parenteral nutrition for more than 90 days. The region also has established guidelines for the refeeding of malnourished patients, recommending a caloric intake of 10-15 kcal/kg.

Regulatory frameworks concerning nutritional information for food products are set and enforced across Europe, although there is significant variation in regulations regarding nutritional education and dietary (NED) practices among different countries. The continent also faces health challenges such as cystic fibrosis, with an incidence of 1 in every 3,500 births and a mean prevalence of 0.8 per 10,000 inhabitants. Healthcare spending on diabetes is a major concern, with a substantial portion of health budgets dedicated to managing this condition. Furthermore, Tolvapt&#225;n is available in Europe for the treatment of SIADH-related hyponatremia, and Southern Europe has a higher frequency of the IVS10 mutation linked to phenylketonuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,da6937e21690cfcb43a43b3438ec7586,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">3217</data>
      <data key="d7">224f74e199904a85be6fa7b4938ac63d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8326;">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La vitamina B&#8326;, tambi&#233;n conocida como piridoxina, es un nutriente esencial que desempe&#241;a un papel fundamental en el metabolismo de amino&#225;cidos. Se encuentra en una variedad de alimentos, incluyendo cereales y carnes. Adem&#225;s, la vitamina B&#8326; puede ayudar a reducir los niveles de homociste&#237;na en el organismo, lo que est&#225; asociado con un menor riesgo de desarrollar demencia de Alzheimer.</data>
      <data key="d2">26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d3">1640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3218</data>
      <data key="d7">225dbf64d5564d279a3823203f25b148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8329;">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La vitamina B&#8329;, tambi&#233;n conocida como &#225;cido f&#243;lico, es importante para la salud cognitiva y puede ayudar a disminuir los niveles de homociste&#237;na.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
