      <data key="d7">10835dd854f84137b92cc1aaa6a10fc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTICENTER STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MULTICENTER STUDY" refers to a research initiative conducted across various locations, specifically in Spain, aimed at investigating the prevalence of malnutrition among elderly patients. This type of study is characterized by its execution at multiple institutions, which allows for the collection of broader data and enhances the validity of the results. Additionally, multicenter studies can also encompass clinical research focused on evaluating the effectiveness of treatments for specific conditions, such as medullary thyroid carcinoma. Overall, the multicenter study serves as a vital approach in clinical research, facilitating comprehensive data collection and analysis across diverse populations and settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,c879347903aabeef630597c99cff2275</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
