      <data key="d6">3224</data>
      <data key="d7">56a327e76ed74fedaf04e938ccd04571</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cognitive impairment refers to a decline in mental function that can affect memory, thinking, and social abilities, often studied in relation to nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b</data>
      <data key="d3">259</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3225</data>
      <data key="d7">36bc2038c58c4de5b8f99d6c28f403ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional intervention encompasses a range of dietary strategies designed to meet the energy, fluid, vitamin, and mineral needs of various patient populations, particularly those who are vulnerable, such as the elderly and individuals with specific health conditions. It aims to improve health outcomes by addressing the nutritional status of patients, thereby slowing disease progression and preventing complications.

In the context of elderly patients, nutritional intervention focuses on preventing or managing sarcopenia and fragility, ensuring that their dietary intake supports overall health. For patients with liver disease, nutritional intervention is critical, involving the assessment and addressing of their dietary needs to enhance health outcomes. Similarly, for individuals with Anorexia Nervosa, the intervention emphasizes restoring healthy eating patterns and preventing refeeding syndrome.

Nutritional intervention is also vital for patients with cystic fibrosis, cancer, and those undergoing cancer treatment, as it involves personalized dietary strategies tailored to individual risk factors and health conditions. Overall, nutritional intervention plays a significant role in improving the nutritional status of patients across various medical contexts, ensuring that their dietary needs are met throughout their treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">11cbdce47eee11a80ab609f3b786bcc1,5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49,65143afbc494705be9ccc4e48bee296b,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,770e8796aac9c96d967ef99d1f307e06,c3e74ddf9529482684f4b62e713df49b,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3,cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c,e33729f8eea62e59507c132b7c2437df,ea8be3e3b3d7195ddc85512be460b6f8,f5660be03d70d5dd506c197283dd79ae,fb7b0d121f195e2a472f3d47e28ccff9</data>
      <data key="d3">1235</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">3226</data>
      <data key="d7">5fb4a940e32b4b87a272b764635ed25f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITALIZATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospitalization refers to the process of admitting a patient to a hospital for medical care and treatment. This process is particularly significant for older adults, especially those with sarcopenia, as hospitalization can lead to a further decline in muscle mass and functional status. During hospitalization, a patient's nutritional status plays a crucial role in their recovery, making it essential to evaluate and address any malnutrition. It is recommended that malnutrition screening be conducted within the first 24-48 hours of admission. Additionally, hospitalization is a key context in which the benefits of oral nutritional supplements are assessed, and it is a critical concern in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) programs, which aim to reduce costs and length of stay.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,628cd3e2664561301cbe6679f48c4bd3,980d6217f6ec073bf1673f14542ebbf0,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d3">1241</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3227</data>
      <data key="d7">b23e953e5d9b4762bcc90ddf19bf0dbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANCIANOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ancianos refers to elderly individuals, particularly those who are at risk of malnutrition, especially the frail. This group has specific dietary recommendations aimed at managing diabetes, highlighting the importance of tailored nutrition to support their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
