    <node id="NRS 2002">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NRS 2002 is a nutritional risk screening tool designed to evaluate both the nutritional status of individuals and the severity of any underlying diseases they may have. It is based on clinical trials and serves as a method for assessing nutritional risk. NRS 2002 is particularly useful in situations where the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) is not applicable, providing a questionnaire format to effectively identify individuals at risk of malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,7d1eed82db6d0ad62418f3f965316c39,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
      <data key="d3">706</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3233</data>
      <data key="d7">161f6e62a432448bb1ec17a866b39a9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TABLA 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TABLA 2 is a comprehensive resource that encompasses a variety of dietary and nutritional information. It includes a table listing foods that are permitted in a broad low-sodium diet, as well as a reference to the composition of copper in different food groups. Additionally, TABLA 2 outlines steps proposed by Diego Gracia for a deliberative process in clinical nutrition.

The table also details foods that are restricted and allowed for individuals with phenylketonuria, providing essential guidance for dietary management in this condition. Furthermore, it presents various lipid solutions used for parenteral nutrition, including their composition and nutritional values, along with optional nutritional information per 100 g/100 ml.

In a broader context, TABLA 2 showcases data from a population study on body mass index (IMC) for men and women under 45 years of age. It also presents characteristics of different dietary assessment methods, clinical characteristics of various types of Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young (MODY), including mutations, clinical features, and treatment options.

Moreover, TABLA 2 provides an example recipe for enteral nutrition, detailing ingredient quantities necessary for formulation, and outlines the criteria for the Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS 2002) process. Overall, TABLA 2 serves as a multifaceted tool for understanding dietary needs and nutritional assessment across various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f,3d73ef14929e7391e915f739189e4dfa,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,630fa9125532edf1c291507de8298869,79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,a4d8922d5e65304a84f8a61999f77933,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
