      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A tool designed to predict clinical outcomes in hospitalized adults and elderly, categorizing nutritional risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0061877457bb078516d0e43dd6d8131</data>
      <data key="d3">710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3238</data>
      <data key="d7">80870a8647d3442fa7352e9e3e53db84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELDERLY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The elderly population, particularly individuals aged 70 years and older, is characterized by a higher risk of developing diabetes and other health issues, necessitating tailored dietary needs that align with their health status and life expectancy. This demographic is often the focus of nutritional screening tools such as SNAQ, MNA, and NRS 2002, which are designed to address their specific nutritional requirements. Given their increased fragility, elderly individuals require careful consideration in nutritional assessments to ensure their well-being and health management.</data>
      <data key="d2">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,d0061877457bb078516d0e43dd6d8131,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
      <data key="d3">710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3239</data>
      <data key="d7">e51c5f4aa73b40518dc0da557378ab46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BODY MASS INDEX (BMI)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A measurement that compares weight and height to assess body fat and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">d0061877457bb078516d0e43dd6d8131</data>
      <data key="d3">710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3240</data>
      <data key="d7">ea1e80f6d69c489db910c1b9e5cd6a86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL RISK">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Nutritional risk refers to the potential for malnutrition and is assessed based on various criteria, including serum albumin levels and body mass index (BMI). To determine the need for nutritional support, various screening tools are utilized in the assessment process.</data>
      <data key="d2">58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,7d1eed82db6d0ad62418f3f965316c39,d0061877457bb078516d0e43dd6d8131</data>
      <data key="d3">1174</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3241</data>
      <data key="d7">9eca1f84e4214f149060dc4cc8e85e18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GERIATRIC NUTRITIONAL RISK INDEX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Geriatric Nutritional Risk Index (GNRI) is a specialized index utilized to assess the nutritional status of elderly patients and to predict various clinical outcomes. It is particularly designed to evaluate the prognosis of hospitalized elderly individuals, focusing on their nutritional needs. The GNRI serves as a critical tool in predicting morbidity and mortality among elderly patients who are receiving nutritional support, thereby aiding healthcare providers in making informed decisions regarding patient care and intervention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff</data>
      <data key="d3">734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3242</data>
      <data key="d7">ca4264383f0548d8972fe5325db7bea3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL RISK INDEX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nutritional Risk Index (NRI) is a tool designed to assess nutritional risk, particularly in elderly patients. It has been associated with perioperative mortality, highlighting its importance in evaluating the nutritional status of individuals who may be at risk during surgical procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3243</data>
      <data key="d7">5db4606ebd184960ad675d5d6e50611b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUFFE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NUFFE, or Nutritional Form For The Elderly, is a specialized tool created to evaluate and assess the nutritional status and needs of elderly patients. It serves as an important resource in understanding the dietary requirements of this demographic, ensuring that their nutritional health is adequately monitored and addressed.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">708</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3244</data>
      <data key="d7">dbd331a1e9104b16a022d09a292c0019</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SKIPER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Skiper is a researcher who has established a grading system for nutritional screening tools based on the quality of studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3245</data>
      <data key="d7">176ab4f366a44653a49c23ce906d1ef7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Elia is a researcher who discusses the effectiveness of age as a predictor of mortality and hospital stay compared to nutritional screening tools.</data>
      <data key="d2">8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3246</data>
      <data key="d7">3bc690b5f12141d7a2d5beb67cebbdd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STRATTON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Stratton is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly concerning elderly patients. He analyzed various studies on supplementation in older adults and concluded that such interventions have positive effects on nutritional evolution and mortality rates. Additionally, Stratton has contributed to the discourse on the effectiveness of nutritional screening tools for elderly patients, emphasizing the importance of proper assessment in this demographic. He is also the author of a systematic review and meta-analysis published in 2013, which focused on the use of oral supplements following hospital discharge, further highlighting his commitment to improving nutritional outcomes for older individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f15452403a4c9b4b3c7a48bac634a04,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04,c10cd7b5fa3f7e4428da8371caba4087</data>
      <data key="d3">1782</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3247</data>
      <data key="d7">4443d9412c1945b7b53587bb0c071fb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHANDRA NUTRITION SCREEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Chandra Nutrition Screen is a tool specifically designed to assess nutritional risk in elderly patients and populations. It aims to identify individuals who may be at risk of malnutrition, thereby facilitating timely interventions to improve their nutritional status and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3248</data>
      <data key="d7">66a6b838e4de40ed823c6fd40798dfcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VAN BOKHORST-DE VAN DER SCHUEREN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Van Bokhorst-de van der Schueren is a researcher and author who has published a review on nutritional assessment tools specifically designed for hospitalized elderly patients. This work contributes to the understanding and improvement of nutritional care for this vulnerable population.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3249</data>
      <data key="d7">ab48a35bd91d49e0b0f2f992ce40b15d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION SCREENING INITIATIVE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The Nutrition Screening Initiative is a program designed to enhance the nutritional health of older adults by implementing screening and intervention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d3">734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3250</data>
      <data key="d7">dbcc5a80113b47dea61ba16833098abb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VGS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The VGS, or Global Subjective Assessment, is a comprehensive tool designed to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly in hospital settings. Developed by Baker in the 1980s, it is recognized as a classic method for assessing the nutritional needs of patients undergoing gastrointestinal surgery. The VGS has been shown to have a high level of agreement with other nutritional assessment tools, making it a reliable choice for healthcare professionals. Additionally, the Visual Geriatric Scale, which is also referred to as VGS, specifically targets the nutritional assessment of hospitalized elderly patients. The VGS is recommended by the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) as a valuable nutritional screening tool, further emphasizing its importance in clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,e596bbb9231cc72bade554b3d67804b8,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">705</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3251</data>
      <data key="d7">dbc8b4841158488bb279e5e073f73c9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PCR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PCR, or C-reactive protein, is a significant marker of inflammation that plays a crucial role in evaluating the health status of patients, particularly in surgical contexts. It is commonly used in hospitals to assess the inflammatory status of patients while also considering nutritional parameters. Elevated levels of PCR in laboratory results can indicate a heightened inflammatory response, which may suggest nutritional risk among surgical patients. As a blood test, PCR measures inflammation in the body and is utilized to assess various health conditions, making it an important tool in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">1174</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3252</data>
      <data key="d7">988d42697a71483f951f6abae191fe52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARAMETROS ANTROPOMETRICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PARAMETROS ANTROPOMETRICOS refer to anthropometric parameters, which are measurements utilized to assess the body composition and nutritional status of patients. These parameters play a crucial role in evaluating an individual's health and can provide valuable insights into their physical condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a,cc6ee3d7bc9bfaf4a06f3f02c4907eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3253</data>
      <data key="d7">6a7a2cb010584e6cb433dd709ac38c7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARAMETROS BIOQUIMICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biochemical parameters are laboratory tests used to evaluate the nutritional status and health of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a</data>
      <data key="d3">762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3254</data>
      <data key="d7">3b739a61feb94d23818319e43da9a5fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN CONSENSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Consensus is a comprehensive framework that outlines definitions and classifications of sarcopenia, distinguishing between its primary and secondary causes. It provides essential guidelines for diagnosing sarcopenia, particularly in frail patients, with a strong emphasis on the measurement of handgrip strength as a key diagnostic tool. The Consensus highlights the association of sarcopenia with frailty in older adults and underscores the importance of assessing muscle mass and strength in the diagnosis and management of this condition. Additionally, the European Consensus offers guidelines for dietary assessments and monitoring in patients suffering from chronic respiratory diseases, such as cystic fibrosis, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), and bronchiectasis (BQ). It serves as a valuable resource for a group of experts who provide recommendations for managing various health conditions, including osteoporosis in patients with cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b,a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4</data>
      <data key="d3">1766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">3255</data>
      <data key="d7">8a7fa2c4c391418cb635a602bcad419a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BIA, or Bioelectrical Impedance Analysis, is a method utilized to assess body composition, specifically focusing on the evaluation of muscle mass and fat distribution in individuals. This technique estimates body composition parameters, including fat mass and lean mass, and is particularly relevant in clinical settings for diagnosing conditions such as sarcopenia. BIA serves as a valuable tool for understanding an individual's body composition, providing insights into both muscle and fat distribution.</data>
      <data key="d2">1033f1626ca6ac2b3bab298805a17aec,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1176</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3256</data>
      <data key="d7">e1e5cace11714ad68de23e3b99a9bbe5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHARLSON COMORBIDITY INDEX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Charlson Comorbidity Index is a method of classifying prognostic comorbidity in longitudinal studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">704</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3257</data>
      <data key="d7">b84d27901c764208b88b7945707bd958</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTROINTESTINAL SYMPTOMS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrointestinal symptoms encompass a variety of issues that can significantly impact an individual's health and nutritional status. These symptoms include diarrhea, abdominal pain, bloating, nausea, and vomiting. They can arise from various conditions, such as lactose intolerance, and can lead to challenges in maintaining adequate nutritional intake. Overall, gastrointestinal symptoms represent a complex interplay of factors that can affect both physical well-being and dietary habits.</data>
      <data key="d2">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">704</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3258</data>
      <data key="d7">2e85fee076084d2faec148fa968b201e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORTALITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mortality refers to the incidence of death within a population and is a critical measure in various health studies, including those focused on diabetes and cardiovascular diseases. It encompasses the state of being subject to death and is often quantified through mortality rates, which can be influenced by factors such as nutritional status and overall health, particularly in hospitalized patients. Researchers utilize mortality data to assess the long-term effects of medical treatments and interventions on patient survival rates, as well as to identify risk factors associated with different diseases. Overall, mortality serves as an essential metric for understanding health outcomes and the effectiveness of healthcare strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,9f0dc667db1447b9e51420cc6ba091c9,dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833,ecd0e2cc6ed4a480591f4ac32cd7f691</data>
      <data key="d3">704</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3259</data>
      <data key="d7">6ebf3e326a8f4e5eb8d1022f235213c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOIMPEDANCE VECTORIAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bioimpedance Vectorial (BIVA) is a method used to standardize results in body composition assessment, particularly in acute patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">1176</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3260</data>
      <data key="d7">511456cfa6cb4d0594163faad58848f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUTE PATIENTS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute patients are individuals who are hospitalized and may experience rapid changes in their health status, affecting their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">704</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3261</data>
      <data key="d7">89456e74e7e44853af006fd06b25793e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTION GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional intervention guidelines provide recommendations for managing the nutritional needs of frail elderly patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3262</data>
      <data key="d7">c25378dc9a2d44289bdf289a2ab13e9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCTIONAL CAPACITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Functional capacity refers to the ability of individuals, particularly older adults, to perform activities of daily living. This capacity can be enhanced through exercise and proper nutrition. It is influenced by a patient's overall health conditions and nutritional status, which can, in turn, affect their ability to carry out daily activities. Therefore, maintaining and improving functional capacity is crucial for ensuring that individuals can meet their daily needs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">83</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3263</data>
      <data key="d7">3aafe714f2f348a98a206cf52de49639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HANDGRIP STRENGTH">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Handgrip strength is a specific measure of muscle strength that is often utilized as a diagnostic criterion for sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3264</data>
      <data key="d7">3300e1f8838b4d83ab1ddb647d8445e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEDOM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SEDOM, or the Spanish Society of Medical Documentation, is an organization dedicated to the collaboration and development of nutritional documentation and guidelines. It plays a significant role in the field of medical nutrition, contributing to the establishment of standards and practices that enhance the quality of medical documentation related to nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d3">1842</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3265</data>
      <data key="d7">f88f62b667654fe6a05419b9fdc92126</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NA LIGADA A RETINOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prote&#237;na ligada a retinol is a protein that indicates vitamin A status and is used in nutritional assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3266</data>
      <data key="d7">4cb0701fb4634bee8afe5ef8eea3db8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFOCITOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Linfocitos, or lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a crucial role in the immune system. They are found in the chyle and are essential for immune function. The count of lymphocytes is an important parameter used in diagnosing malnutrition and assessing nutritional health. Specifically, lymphocyte levels are included in the Nutritional Index of Pinato, which helps evaluate an individual's nutritional status. Overall, lymphocytes serve as indicators of both immune function and nutritional well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395</data>
      <data key="d3">1797</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3267</data>
      <data key="d7">53ca54e24cde4b779145a26590f98e5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLESTEROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cholesterol is a type of lipid that plays a crucial role in the formation of cell membranes and the production of certain hormones. It is a waxy substance found in the blood and is essential for building cells, being transported by lipoproteins. However, when cholesterol levels are too high, it can contribute to various health issues, particularly cardiovascular problems. For optimal cardiovascular health, it is recommended that cholesterol intake be kept below 300 mg per day.

Cholesterol levels can be influenced by various health conditions. For instance, elevated cholesterol levels are commonly observed in individuals with primary hypothyroidism, which is associated with reduced metabolism and clearance of cholesterol from the body. Additionally, cholesterol levels are measured through blood tests and serve as an important parameter in assessing malnutrition. In cases of malnutrition, cholesterol levels may be low, which can adversely affect overall health. 

In summary, cholesterol is a vital lipid necessary for bodily functions, but maintaining appropriate levels is essential for preventing health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,838d1ef59dfea4cab2a724bc85b02632,bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a,c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27,e9734d049699822c67b55a2a56aee7b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1377</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3268</data>
      <data key="d7">7d3b50b905b44aaeb9b6caad60d1d8af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARAMETROS DIAGNOSTICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parameters for diagnosing malnutrition in hospital settings, including various clinical measurements.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3269</data>
      <data key="d7">b21c06470aba4c36a897d1cfbdbee2e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Caloric malnutrition refers to a deficiency in caloric intake, impacting overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3270</data>
      <data key="d7">1cbd057c5b6c45b1be8bd7f39c596c93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N PROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Protein malnutrition refers to a deficiency in protein intake, affecting bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3271</data>
      <data key="d7">757b69d57f7d44acad6727e844d6432b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N MIXTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mixed malnutrition refers to a combination of caloric and protein deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3272</data>
      <data key="d7">3d73b92f85e847dabbb52d468acb0afa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLIEGUES Y ANTROPOMETR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Skinfold thickness and anthropometric measurements are used to assess body composition and nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf0cc16dc61df5b90a5a1e961322391a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3273</data>
      <data key="d7">b98702a691f94671b3662f937769cc64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATAULU&#209;A">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">A region in Spain where studies on the prevalence of malnutrition in the community have been conducted.</data>
      <data key="d2">17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b</data>
