      <data key="d7">5c39d51c8eb04e2ea040b6b12dc59c53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GERMANY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Germany is a country that exhibits varying prevalence rates of malnutrition in residential settings, indicating a complex relationship with nutritional health among its population. Additionally, Germany is recognized as one of the European countries with high obesity rates, highlighting a significant public health concern related to both undernutrition and overnutrition within its demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">996</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3275</data>
      <data key="d7">32abd7065e49465d92dc6cecbf356172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIE 10">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Classification of Diseases, 10th Revision, used for coding various health conditions, including malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b</data>
      <data key="d3">703</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3276</data>
      <data key="d7">bb4731a88b61493c839917829c34642b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRUPOS RELACIONADOS DE DIAGN&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"GRUPOS RELACIONADOS DE DIAGN&#211;STICO" refers to Diagnosis-related groups (DRGs), which are a classification system used to categorize hospital cases for payment purposes. This system organizes cases based on the diagnosis and treatment provided, ensuring that hospitals receive appropriate compensation for the services rendered. Additionally, DRGs encompass a variety of conditions, including those related to malnutrition, highlighting their broad application in the healthcare payment framework.</data>
      <data key="d2">17444b83ec19bdcc65ff0722869e7b4b,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff</data>
      <data key="d3">703</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
