    <node id="SNAQ">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SNAQ, or the Simplified Nutritional Appetite Questionnaire, is a brief and effective tool designed for assessing nutritional risk and appetite, particularly among elderly populations. It serves as a simplified version of appetite assessment tools, specifically tailored for elderly patients, and is utilized in various healthcare settings, including hospitals. SNAQ is recognized for its rapid and straightforward approach to nutritional screening, aiding in the evaluation of malnutrition and nutritional status.

Since its implementation in the Netherlands in 2006, SNAQ has been employed to assess nutritional risk in hospitalized patients and those in elderly care settings. The questionnaire is available in multiple languages, making it accessible for diverse populations. Scores obtained from the SNAQ can indicate a higher risk of postoperative mortality, highlighting its importance in clinical assessments. Overall, SNAQ is a valuable tool in nutritional assessment, particularly for institutionalized elderly individuals, and is derived from the more comprehensive CNAQ.</data>
      <data key="d2">005b22fc9dae5f9b135f0c8ba729819f,17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,2ebe12524f7750215eee73b328b601ee,969bdfc6cc15b9089e96000addd87561,bd8df34b86026d71089bcf062570b70f,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c,fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">723</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
