    <node id="AHSP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AHSP, or The Appetite, Hunger and Sensory Perception Questionnaire, is a specialized scale designed to evaluate appetite in elderly individuals. This tool comprises 29 items that specifically examine various aspects of eating habits among older adults. By focusing on appetite and sensory perception, AHSP aims to provide insights into the dietary behaviors and needs of this demographic, facilitating better understanding and management of their nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6</data>
      <data key="d3">723</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3291</data>
      <data key="d7">781f3d11f87e478b914e53acd366bef6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CNAQ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CNAQ, or the Council of Nutrition Questionnaire, is a tool designed to evaluate appetite and assess nutritional status in elderly patients. It specifically targets older adults, providing a means to understand their nutritional needs and appetite levels effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6</data>
      <data key="d3">723</data>
