    </node>
    <node id="CLASIFICACI&#211;N INTERNACIONAL DE ENFERMEDADES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Clasificaci&#243;n Internacional de Enfermedades (CIE), known in English as the International Classification of Diseases (ICD), is an international instrument developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) to identify health trends and statistics worldwide. This system is utilized for coding and classifying diseases and health conditions, providing a standardized framework for health data collection and analysis across different countries and healthcare systems.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,d80f1e55925e0ce0cd958e35ad2e49ff</data>
