    <node id="EUR J CLIN NUTR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EUR J CLIN NUTR is a journal dedicated to publishing clinical nutrition research, with a particular focus on studies related to enteral nutrition and its effects on patient outcomes. The journal has featured research on various topics, including the relationship between fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes, as well as studies examining postsurgery enteral nutrition specifically in head and neck cancer patients. Overall, EUR J CLIN NUTR serves as a significant platform for disseminating research on clinical nutrition within Europe.</data>
      <data key="d2">3af2658fd59065a71bfee00d2bd27b1b,8c198f866d8fb49a782cb57139b30d76,b9a7e8e8fec7968cf56017bf41f92bb4,bd8df34b86026d71089bcf062570b70f</data>
      <data key="d3">559</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3308</data>
      <data key="d7">656ff0c419a94d6cb7dd6467bb26dcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="J AM MED DIR ASSOC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "J AM MED DIR ASSOC," also known as the Journal of the American Medical Directors Association, is a scholarly journal dedicated to the publication of articles focused on the management and medical care of older adults in various medical settings. It serves as a platform for disseminating research, consensus statements, and reviews that address issues related to geriatric care, frailty, and aging. The journal aims to provide valuable insights and guidance for medical professionals involved in the care of older populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">3be9d646c354d76527755d79a77c916b,bd8df34b86026d71089bcf062570b70f,c10cd7b5fa3f7e4428da8371caba4087,e155d9b2d1858daab734fd68a45d0c0a</data>
      <data key="d3">1497</data>
