    </node>
    <node id="NUTRIGENOMICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrigenomics is a field of study that investigates the interaction between nutrition and genes, particularly how food affects gene expression.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3313</data>
      <data key="d7">8ba7adf3a43f426ab622e1aaf9af612a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPIGENETICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Epigenetics is a branch of genetics that studies changes in gene expression that do not involve alterations to the underlying DNA sequence, often influenced by environmental factors such as diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3314</data>
      <data key="d7">d5817ec25db243448b66f08b4b8082b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEALTH, AGING AND BODY COMPOSITION STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Health, Aging and Body Composition Study (Health ABC) investigates the relationship between health, aging, and body composition in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3315</data>
      <data key="d7">2e8d1050b8c54acf9ff5de2ed000212d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOMEN'S HEALTH INITIATIVE OBSERVATIONAL STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Women's Health Initiative Observational Study (WHI-OS) is a long-term research initiative focused on understanding the health of women, particularly postmenopausal women. This study aims to investigate various health issues affecting women, with a specific emphasis on the impact of diet and lifestyle on their overall health. One of the key areas of investigation within the WHI-OS is the effect of protein intake on fragility, highlighting the study's commitment to exploring how nutritional factors influence women's health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49,6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d3">1764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3316</data>
      <data key="d7">734c0fd8253846bf8a7702272a22ddfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAROTENOIDS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Carotenoids are pigments found in plants that have health benefits, including potential protective effects against frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3317</data>
      <data key="d7">72453ae08ea6438c8d05bee089f521b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ITALIAN INCHIANTI STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Italian inCHIANTI study investigates the aging process and its impact on health, including the relationship between nutrition and frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3318</data>
      <data key="d7">e8fa17ee80af466fb7073357e65b40bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KIM HK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kim HK is a researcher who has conducted significant studies on the effects of exercise and nutritional supplementation in elderly populations, particularly focusing on elderly women with sarcopenia. Their research includes investigations into the impact of both protein and amino acid supplementation alongside exercise, highlighting the importance of these interventions in improving health outcomes for older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f194bef97e28167f81acc7a66ac56ab,3ec3efbe130c20d623681e00e3d784f7</data>
      <data key="d3">1781</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3319</data>
      <data key="d7">8f333c899bc64a37a6103baf32edbe6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROT-AGE STUDY GROUP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The PROT-AGE Study Group is a collective of experts dedicated to establishing evidence-based recommendations for dietary protein intake specifically tailored for older adults. This group has reached a consensus on the protein requirements for healthy elderly individuals, as well as those who may be ill. Their focus is on providing optimal protein intake guidelines that enhance the health and well-being of elderly individuals, emphasizing the importance of nutrition and exercise strategies to improve strength and functional capacity. Overall, the PROT-AGE Study Group plays a crucial role in guiding dietary practices for older adults to ensure they receive adequate protein for their health needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f194bef97e28167f81acc7a66ac56ab,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,c10cd7b5fa3f7e4428da8371caba4087,e155d9b2d1858daab734fd68a45d0c0a</data>
      <data key="d3">1781</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3320</data>
      <data key="d7">8c59b68e67af4fee8c38bdf88220c8c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JAPANESE WOMEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Japanese women over 75 years old who participated in a study on sarcopenia and protein intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f194bef97e28167f81acc7a66ac56ab</data>
