    <node id="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Dieta Mediterr&#225;nea" is a model of healthy eating that emphasizes a dietary pattern traditionally consumed by populations near the Mediterranean Sea. It is characterized by a low intake of saturated fats and a high intake of monounsaturated fats, particularly from sources like olive oil. This diet is rich in antioxidants and polyphenols, derived from a high consumption of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, legumes, and moderate amounts of fish and white meat.

The Mediterranean diet is associated with numerous health benefits, including a reduction in inflammation, weight management, and a lower risk of cardiovascular diseases and certain types of cancer. It promotes a protective effect against cognitive decline and is linked to improved metabolic health and lower prevalence of frailty among the elderly. Additionally, the diet encourages moderate alcohol consumption, particularly red wine, which is also associated with positive health outcomes.

Overall, the Mediterranean diet reflects traditional eating habits of Mediterranean countries and is recognized for its potential to enhance overall health and longevity, making it a widely recommended dietary pattern in various health guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63,035d53a7f46fdb72c0a939265667044b,05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,633a3a90a82e02d05096b361ddba3ad7,64347a9be918a67f786cbdf9f9db9c8a,72d0be9d03c79097f867a8af2e3e89e4,7852af9e2886d0d889fbc056d0a75f21,7e1b90e2c8714b39e283be229f6d5de3,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119,c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">59</data>
      <data key="d6">3327</data>
      <data key="d7">5984c88ae16b4acba2722962e5c3c4ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CREATINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatine is a supplement that has garnered attention for its potential benefits in enhancing muscle strength and performance across various populations, particularly among athletes. It is a metabolite derived from amino acids, primarily found in skeletal muscle, and is known to stimulate muscle anabolism. Creatine has been shown to be effective in muscle regeneration, especially during rehabilitation phases, and is recognized for its ability to increase anaerobic capacity and lean mass during training. Additionally, creatine may be utilized in the treatment of metabolic disorders to improve muscular and energetic function, making it a versatile supplement for both performance enhancement and therapeutic applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079,3e8ab018917854d76a0137102e0392bd,3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1749</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3328</data>
      <data key="d7">cd9e3492b99f4037982b82111261b7d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS OMEGA-3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 son nutrientes esenciales que han sido objeto de numerosos estudios debido a sus m&#250;ltiples beneficios para la salud. Estos compuestos, que incluyen el EPA (&#225;cido eicosapentaenoico) y el DHA (&#225;cido docosahexaenoico), son poliinsaturados y se obtienen principalmente del aceite de pescado. Se ha demostrado que los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 tienen un papel protector en el desarrollo del deterioro cognitivo y la demencia, as&#237; como efectos antiinflamatorios significativos en pacientes con enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales (EII).

Adem&#225;s, se recomienda la administraci&#243;n de omega-3 a pacientes cr&#237;ticos, ya que su actividad antiinflamatoria puede ayudar a reducir las respuestas inflamatorias y mejorar los resultados de salud. Estos &#225;cidos grasos tambi&#233;n son beneficiosos para la salud muscular, especialmente cuando se combinan con amino&#225;cidos, lo que potencia la respuesta anab&#243;lica muscular. En el contexto de la salud cardiovascular, los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 est&#225;n asociados con la reducci&#243;n de triglic&#233;ridos y la prevenci&#243;n de enfermedades card&#237;acas, siendo particularmente beneficiosos para pacientes renales.

Los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 tambi&#233;n se han vinculado a efectos positivos en la salud inmunol&#243;gica, especialmente en condiciones como la pancreatitis cr&#243;nica. Adem&#225;s, se ha sugerido que estos nutrientes pueden tener efectos protectores contra ciertos tipos de c&#225;ncer. En resumen, los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 son compuestos esenciales que ofrecen una amplia gama de beneficios para la salud, incluyendo la regulaci&#243;n de la inflamaci&#243;n y la prevenci&#243;n de diversas enfermedades.</data>
      <data key="d2">01704aec4089b2f0f24dd0f0841b5ecf,111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d,c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119,df0e6695be23c07606ca5b9accc62df2</data>
      <data key="d3">981</data>
