    <node id="PIRLICH M">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Pirlich M is a researcher and author who specializes in nutritional interventions for older populations. In addition to this focus, Pirlich M has conducted significant research on bioelectrical impedance analysis specifically in cirrhotic patients. Furthermore, Pirlich M has explored the creatinine approach as a method to estimate skeletal muscle mass in individuals with cirrhosis. Through these studies, Pirlich M contributes valuable insights into the nutritional and physiological challenges faced by older adults and patients with liver conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">22f9164844b9778cfef429e45de95060,3ec3efbe130c20d623681e00e3d784f7,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
