    </node>
    <node id="ARCHIVES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Archives of Internal Medicine" is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research articles related to various aspects of internal medicine. It covers a wide range of topics, including studies on diabetes and its complications, frailty, and vitamin D deficiency in older Americans. The journal aims to disseminate significant findings in the field, particularly those that explore the effects of vitamin D and other critical health issues affecting the population.</data>
      <data key="d2">0903b40c7774225e89c5e798f9feef9b,d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f,d93c7f9ea61d85e6be22df63c4b67d4d</data>
