    <node id="RESIDENCIA DE MAYORES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Residencia de Mayores is a senior residence in Almer&#237;a where Dr. Nicol&#225;s Maturana Navarrete practices as a geriatrician.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3fea62b02f75fe3cf6e469e624ac7f9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3421</data>
      <data key="d7">98071097dc6547f28304111ff440a955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D. MIGUEL DE CERVANTES SAAVEDRA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">D. Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra is a renowned Spanish writer, known for his literary works, including the famous novel "Don Quixote," which includes wisdom applicable to healthy aging.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">1784</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3422</data>
      <data key="d7">e601b902cbcc4a8799f9e4866a86f8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VECENAT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Vegenat is a company committed to the nutrition and dietary needs of older adults, sponsoring the series "Envejecimiento y Nutrici&#243;n."</data>
      <data key="d2">d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">1784</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3423</data>
      <data key="d7">f4aa35437a344638958d80efe8503cd5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN COUNTRIES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">European countries are currently confronting significant challenges associated with an aging population. In response, they are implementing various programs aimed at promoting healthy aging and fostering independence among older adults. Additionally, these countries are involved in research studies that focus on elderly patients, particularly in relation to diabetes, which underscores the geographical scope of health-related issues affecting the aging demographic in Europe.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">1784</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3424</data>
      <data key="d7">e1635565d37c4043ac2d811bffb0c4ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA IDEAL PARA LOS MAYORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA IDEAL PARA LOS MAYORES" refers to a comprehensive set of nutritional recommendations designed to maintain health in the elderly population. This concept underscores the significance of tailored nutrition that addresses the specific needs of older adults. The ideal diet emphasizes balanced nutrition, focusing on the appropriate balance of macronutrients, as well as the inclusion of fiber and healthy fats. It aims to improve health outcomes for seniors, particularly in combating age-related health issues such as the loss of muscle mass and diminished immune function. Additionally, this dietary guideline is encapsulated in the document titled "Dieta ideal para los mayores," published by VEGENAT in 2014, which serves as a resource for understanding the optimal dietary practices for older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,bd228b54354e751399b62683662e2b56,c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a,d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">473</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">3425</data>
      <data key="d7">906529719929414a9dc7fa333b795e30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJERCICIO F&#205;SICO REGULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"EJERCICIO F&#205;SICO REGULAR" refers to the practice of engaging in consistent physical activity, which is linked to numerous health benefits. It is particularly noted for its role in reducing the incidence of osteoporosis, a condition that weakens bones and increases the risk of fractures. Additionally, regular physical exercise is emphasized as a vital component for maintaining overall health and preventing diseases, especially in older adults. This highlights the importance of incorporating regular exercise into daily routines to promote longevity and enhance quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3426</data>
      <data key="d7">a7d23913bc7840cd93e698fd3c1f23db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACTIVIDAD INTELECTUAL Y RELACIONES SOCIALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intellectual activity and social relationships are recognized as important factors for cognitive health and well-being in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">473</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3427</data>
      <data key="d7">d9887910209547fc8475f8d3b3801ad8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N ADECUADA Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adequate feeding and nutrition are essential for the health and quality of life of older adults, as discussed in the context of aging.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">473</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3428</data>
      <data key="d7">4648971e7a4d4fdf91a27248c4a803f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORBILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MORBILIDAD refers to the incidence of disease or health complications that can arise from various conditions, including malnutrition, hereditary hemochromatosis, and sarcopenia. It is a significant consequence of renal lithiasis, which may manifest as pain, hematuria, or infection. Additionally, morbidity encompasses the health issues that affect the aging population, contributing to a decreased quality of life and various health complications. Overall, morbidity is a critical factor in health management, highlighting the importance of addressing these issues to improve patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb,d6c8f8036af0c4f0b6f7938c4bab491f</data>
      <data key="d3">1821</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3429</data>
      <data key="d7">49397432d48d44148204f9cc963d88f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUEBEC LONGITUDINAL STUDY NUAGE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Quebec Longitudinal Study NuAge is a research project aimed at analyzing the role of nutrition in the aging process.</data>
      <data key="d2">12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3430</data>
      <data key="d7">4d8577080c924f29909fe3d4f1472fc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARRIS AND BENEDICT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Harris and Benedict equations are formulas used to calculate basal energy expenditure based on various factors such as weight, height, age, and gender.</data>
      <data key="d2">12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3431</data>
      <data key="d7">b7d8350f5faf44eb985a1e79124cc9ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESTRICCI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Restricci&#243;n cal&#243;rica" is a dietary approach that involves reducing calorie intake, which may have significant effects on aging and health outcomes. This regimen has been shown to influence microbiota composition and obesity, suggesting that it plays a role in overall health and longevity.</data>
      <data key="d2">05360f0d7332f748b436b98d64e4eeb7,12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6</data>
      <data key="d3">1007</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3432</data>
      <data key="d7">f65cad368e744e2797be7aaabdd26930</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMBRE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HOMBRE es un g&#233;nero que se refiere a los varones humanos. En este contexto, se menciona en relaci&#243;n con el gasto energ&#233;tico basal, que es la cantidad m&#237;nima de energ&#237;a que el cuerpo necesita para mantener sus funciones vitales en reposo.</data>
      <data key="d2">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">1139</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3433</data>
      <data key="d7">81394983bca348ba9bd56975fef380b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUJER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "MUJER" refers to a female individual, specifically in the context of energy expenditure, which is calculated using specific formulas. The term "mujer" also denotes the gender that pertains to human females, particularly in relation to basal energy expenditure. Additionally, women have increasingly participated in the labor market, which has influenced their food purchasing habits and the time allocated for food preparation. This multifaceted description highlights the biological, social, and economic aspects associated with women.</data>
      <data key="d2">148443357888793655b663333268775a,24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074</data>
      <data key="d3">676</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3434</data>
      <data key="d7">323d8b6f7546437881bdfc2ed61075e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTO ENERG&#201;TICO BASAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gasto energ&#233;tico basal (GEB) refers to the amount of energy expended by the body while at rest in a neutrally temperate environment and in the post-absorptive state. It represents the energy required to maintain vital functions while the body is not engaged in any physical activity. This expenditure is crucial for sustaining essential physiological processes, ensuring that the body can perform necessary functions even when at rest.</data>
      <data key="d2">148443357888793655b663333268775a,24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,79dc467f42c611bc9f285c95a6c6ff62,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">676</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3435</data>
      <data key="d7">1ed50a3dc10749f99374a9100ae0b910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTO ENERG&#201;TICO DIARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El gasto energ&#233;tico diario es la cantidad total de energ&#237;a que una persona utiliza en un d&#237;a, incluyendo actividad f&#237;sica y metabolismo basal.</data>
      <data key="d2">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3436</data>
      <data key="d7">f04742e8c20043de8c9bd4667768fc95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDRATOS DE CARBONO GLUC&#201;MICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los hidratos de carbono gluc&#233;micos son aquellos que se convierten en glucosa y afectan los niveles de az&#250;car en sangre.</data>
      <data key="d2">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3437</data>
      <data key="d7">dc992308f2bb436896d7401a05e934eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDRATOS DE CARBONO NO GLIC&#201;MICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los hidratos de carbono no glic&#233;micos, como la fibra, no se digieren y tienen un impacto diferente en la salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3438</data>
      <data key="d7">1dd0b0add4da44c6a7f8a362e5f4aef0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Heart Association (AHA) is a prominent non-profit organization based in the United States dedicated to reducing the incidence of heart disease and stroke. Through a combination of education, research, and advocacy, the AHA aims to mitigate the impact of cardiovascular diseases on public health. The organization focuses on promoting cardiovascular health by publishing studies and guidelines that address various aspects of heart health, including dietary recommendations.

The AHA has conducted extensive research on dietary fats, specifically providing guidelines for fat intake to help prevent cardiovascular risks. It recommends that individuals limit their saturated fat intake to less than 7% of total daily calories and offers insights into the effects of dietary cholesterol on heart health. Additionally, the AHA has published studies regarding the consumption of omega-6 and omega-3 fatty acids, emphasizing their importance in a heart-healthy diet.

Overall, the American Heart Association plays a crucial role in funding cardiovascular medical research and educating the public about healthy living practices to combat heart disease and stroke effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,59a6475dbe0ccafda60f2647dea78371,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,a739523b87def5cdfa8fe97cdf423fe7,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a,e032cf926bee7048e207a0e28604f60e,e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">1544</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">3439</data>
      <data key="d7">7d659ec26d97416b8bacc89db8b9f92c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE COLON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#193;NCER DE COLON, or colon cancer, is a type of cancer that can be influenced by various dietary factors. Research indicates that a diet rich in fiber, vitamin E, and vitamin C may play a significant role in the prevention of this disease. Specifically, an intake of 60 mg of vitamin C per day has been associated with a reduced risk of developing colon cancer, as highlighted by epidemiological studies. Additionally, the effects of omega-3 fatty acids on the development of colon cancer have also been a subject of research. Overall, colon cancer is a health risk that is closely linked to dietary intake, and it is a concern that is addressed in nutritional guidelines and recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a,c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3440</data>
      <data key="d7">978db19ce70048f28906b6455f0a18d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSIBILIDAD PERIF&#201;RICA A LA INSULINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Peripheral insulin sensitivity is a metabolic condition that can be improved through dietary choices, particularly those high in fiber and complex carbohydrates.</data>
      <data key="d2">c7af1c950a6caab8be5d180a2889a25a</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3441</data>
      <data key="d7">345066fdc2144ae6bcdcdbf132744c84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASOCIACI&#211;N INTERNACIONAL PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LOS &#193;CIDOS GRASOS Y L&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ASOCIACI&#211;N INTERNACIONAL PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LOS &#193;CIDOS GRASOS Y L&#205;PIDOS," also known as the International Society for the Study of Fatty Acids and Lipids (ISSFAL), is an international organization dedicated to providing guidance on the intake of fatty acids, particularly focusing on the essential fatty acids DHA (docosahexaenoic acid) and EPA (eicosapentaenoic acid). ISSFAL offers recommendations regarding the daily intake levels of these important nutrients, emphasizing their significance for health and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d3">1614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3442</data>
      <data key="d7">e2565eadc6fd4583a3798def73cbcbac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGENCIA FRANCESA PARA LA SEGURIDAD SANITARIA DE LOS ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The AGENCIA FRANCESA PARA LA SEGURIDAD SANITARIA DE LOS ALIMENTOS, known as AFSSA, is a French agency dedicated to ensuring food safety. It plays a crucial role in establishing dietary recommendations related to food safety, particularly focusing on the intake of fatty acids. Specifically, AFSSA provides guidelines for omega-3 fatty acids, emphasizing their importance in a balanced diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d3">1614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3443</data>
      <data key="d7">02d164ffceaf4cceaef060acc062f1d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNDACI&#211;N BRIT&#193;NICA PARA LA NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fundaci&#243;n Brit&#225;nica para la Nutrici&#243;n (BNF) is a British foundation dedicated to promoting healthy dietary practices. It offers comprehensive guidance on nutritional intake, including specific recommendations for fatty acid consumption. Among its key suggestions, the foundation emphasizes the importance of omega-3 fatty acids, providing evidence-based dietary guidelines to help individuals make informed choices about their nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">60577bdc0f4979d10ba7385bf483c344,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d3">1614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3444</data>
      <data key="d7">0a2409d164ca467d91dba6208feefff0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRASAS SATURADAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GRASAS SATURADAS, or saturated fats, are dietary fats that are associated with increased cardiovascular risk. Health recommendations advise limiting the intake of saturated fats to reduce this risk and improve overall health. Specifically, minimizing saturated fats in a healthy diet is suggested to enhance lipid profiles and decrease the likelihood of coronary disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">59a6475dbe0ccafda60f2647dea78371,633a3a90a82e02d05096b361ddba3ad7,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d3">1649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3445</data>
      <data key="d7">134de3a4ef324c7380da9cb1aafaabe7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRASAS HIDROGENADAS &quot;TRANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trans fats are a type of unhealthy fat that can worsen lipid profiles and increase the risk of coronary disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3446</data>
      <data key="d7">f4c58a1d04474e7cb7fc07489e819513</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA," or coronary disease, is a medical condition characterized by the reduction of blood flow to the heart, primarily due to the buildup of plaque in the coronary arteries. This condition is often associated with obesity and metabolic health issues. Dietary factors play a significant role in the development and management of coronary disease, particularly the intake of dietary fats. The balance of omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids, as well as the consumption of alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) and fish rich in omega-3 fatty acids, can influence the risk of developing this condition. Overall, coronary disease is linked to various cardiovascular risk factors and can be mitigated through dietary choices.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a43b350a248173236a96a64e266b744,25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507,e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3447</data>
      <data key="d7">669759b2e2074d128b946f8c16dd6c6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE DHA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DHA deficiency refers to the insufficient intake of docosahexaenoic acid, which is crucial for various bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3448</data>
      <data key="d7">1d46ad71412c4c19a92cb1253a76bce7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE EPA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EPA deficiency indicates a lack of eicosapentaenoic acid in the diet, which is important for reducing inflammation and supporting heart health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3449</data>
      <data key="d7">f1754f03b7b046d68f4a41e4a4b67301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROPORCI&#211;N &#937;-6/&#937;-3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The omega-6 to omega-3 ratio is a critical dietary consideration that affects health outcomes, particularly in relation to cardiovascular disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3450</data>
      <data key="d7">28dacc3068794290b69513e676af0ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de pr&#243;stata, or prostate cancer, is a type of cancer that occurs in the prostate gland. Research has indicated several dietary factors that may influence the risk of developing this condition. Notably, excessive consumption of dairy products, specifically more than three servings per day, has been associated with an increased risk of prostate cancer. In contrast, studies regarding the relationship between red meat consumption and prostate cancer have yielded inconclusive results, although there is a weak positive correlation with processed meats.

Additionally, prostate cancer has been examined in relation to fish consumption, with some studies suggesting potential benefits from omega-3 fatty acids in cancer suppression. Furthermore, recent findings indicate that a higher intake of cruciferous vegetables and tomatoes may help reduce the risk of developing prostate cancer.

It is also important to note that prostate cancer should be closely monitored in men undergoing testosterone treatment, as this therapy may elevate the risk of the disease. Interestingly, studies have shown no significant relationship between prostate cancer and fiber consumption. Overall, while certain dietary factors may influence the risk of prostate cancer, the evidence remains mixed for some food groups, necessitating further research.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">983</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3451</data>
      <data key="d7">41585e06f3014ce18add4ea41b4991f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de h&#237;gado, or liver cancer, is a type of cancer that has been linked to dietary habits, especially the consumption of certain meats. This form of cancer is also included in research studies that investigate the role of omega-3 fatty acids in cancer development. Additionally, it is a disease that often necessitates surgical resection and has been the subject of studies examining the effects of immunomodulatory enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">7184072817ac284bebfea449e3eaac8b,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d3">579</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3452</data>
      <data key="d7">460a675b41494f7389901ed65a9e2758</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas, or pancreatic cancer, is a serious and aggressive form of cancer that affects the pancreas. It is recognized as the second most common cause of digestive neoplasia in the United States and is associated with a high mortality rate. The disease often presents late due to a lack of symptoms, which contributes to its low survival rate. 

Patients diagnosed with c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas frequently experience malnutrition, necessitating careful nutritional management and specialized treatment. Research has indicated a link between obesity and an increased risk of developing this type of cancer, as well as a positive association between the consumption of processed meats and the likelihood of diagnosis. Conversely, no relationship has been found between fish consumption and the risk of pancreatic cancer.

In terms of treatment, surgical intervention may be required, and there is ongoing research into the potential benefits of omega-3 fatty acids in cancer prevention. Overall, c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas poses significant health challenges and requires a multifaceted approach to management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">0977493109f1215441cf1927961d21ee,2754a719b063eed550046e5b405be3d5,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,7c0d1f274b31d130e4feb8e46fbeb764,a13a13b249ba729ec581f7a16ec5eae5,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,a960ccbf15a28151d1461c4203408408,b110392fc91bc3d7875124ec3fa07c46,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1083</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
