    </node>
    <node id="AMINO&#193;CIDOS ESENCIALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Essential amino acids are vital nutrients that play a significant role in various bodily functions, including muscle synthesis and immune response, especially in older adults. They are particularly important for individuals with low protein intake, as they can be supplemented to help mitigate issues such as uremia in renal patients. Additionally, essential amino acids are recommended for supplementation in patients experiencing severe protein restriction, ensuring that their nutritional needs are adequately met.</data>
      <data key="d2">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce</data>
      <data key="d3">1746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">3457</data>
      <data key="d7">343caef2aea9458c98ec011a4888e62c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINO&#193;CIDOS NO ESENCIALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Non-essential amino acids are produced by the body and are important for various metabolic processes, but are not required from dietary sources.</data>
      <data key="d2">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d3">1746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3458</data>
      <data key="d7">0c592474117746469ad6e6e44a61553b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEUCINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LEUCINA is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in stimulating muscle protein synthesis, particularly after meals. It is known to contribute to increasing muscle mass and function, especially in the elderly, making it significant for maintaining muscle health in this demographic. Additionally, leucina is classified as a branched-chain amino acid; however, it can be neurotoxic in high concentrations and is involved in metabolic pathways related to Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD). Overall, leucina is vital for muscle health and metabolic processes, but care must be taken regarding its concentration in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,a25b0f84bc321cad942a2e33f681a5e4,dcb97f7ffdb0aea3051bdf53e04bcc29</data>
      <data key="d3">1744</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3459</data>
      <data key="d7">245d847219a24af796835d0db1ecec53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISOLEUCINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Isoleucine is a branched-chain amino acid that plays a crucial role in various metabolic pathways, particularly those affected in Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD). As an essential amino acid, isoleucine is vital for muscle metabolism and supports immune function, highlighting its importance in overall health and physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d3">1743</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3460</data>
      <data key="d7">90ee797f776a42f782b6cbe34a8b24f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Valina is an essential branched-chain amino acid that plays a significant role in various metabolic processes. It provides nitrogen, which favors the production of glutamine from &#945;-ketoglutarate, thereby contributing to nitrogen balance in the body. Additionally, Valina is involved in the metabolic pathways related to Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD), highlighting its importance in specific metabolic conditions. Furthermore, Valina is crucial for muscle growth and tissue repair, making it an important nutrient for athletes and individuals engaged in physical training.</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d3">1746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3461</data>
      <data key="d7">6ec5ae16459a4476ac61a671cde9cf97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LISINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lisina, also known as lysine, is an essential amino acid that plays a critical role in protein synthesis. It is important for growth and development, as well as for various metabolic functions. This amino acid is necessary for the body to produce proteins, which are vital for numerous physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d3">1746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3462</data>
      <data key="d7">3bac6a3a635c41b49819aa093324bf7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Histidine is an essential amino acid that is important for the production of histamine and plays a role in immune response.</data>
      <data key="d2">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d3">1746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3463</data>
      <data key="d7">697206bb13144a41be9e2b60b42abc23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METIONINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Metionina, also known as methionine, is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in various metabolic processes within the body. It is particularly involved in the metabolism of homocysteine, a significant compound in amino acid metabolism. While Metionina is vital for health, it can be toxic in high amounts, highlighting the importance of maintaining balanced levels. Additionally, it is often found to be limited in plant-based proteins, making it a critical nutrient for individuals following vegetarian or vegan diets. Overall, Metionina is essential for numerous metabolic functions, underscoring its importance in nutrition and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35,b1d588e0c9c4cef32da41373afbd1901,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d3">1640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3464</data>
      <data key="d7">f2eff6213c614a2a9806a1cfcf5ce822</data>
    </node>
