      <data key="d7">fc65362d425d4554a7e6b26e8ffd52ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO DE 1993">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A study in 1993 evaluated supplementation with multiple vitamins and minerals in non-institutionalized older adults, finding no benefits in infection incidence.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3468</data>
      <data key="d7">bde63bd216d849d09512a2ed179b3544</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO DE 1997">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A 1997 study assessed the effectiveness of specific antioxidant micronutrient supplementation over two years, showing reduced respiratory and urinary infections in non-institutionalized older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3469</data>
      <data key="d7">8fbe5cc46d93491f82a56fe321a2be1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENSAYO CL&#205;NICO 2003">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A clinical trial in 2003 evaluated the impact of mineral and vitamin supplementation on well-being and infection presence, showing the best results in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3470</data>
      <data key="d7">588cf601f1404a0dbee546b1b5c22a24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO DE 2005">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A 2005 study found no significant benefits in infectious morbidity, drug consumption, or quality of life in healthy community-dwelling older adults supplemented for one year with vitamins, minerals, and trace elements.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3471</data>
      <data key="d7">ffe131b874be465abdec6d4140434f20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICITS DE MICRONUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Micronutrient deficiencies are a significant health concern for older adults, particularly for calcium, folic acid, vitamin A, and vitamin D.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d3">646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3472</data>
      <data key="d7">aad76e04cd3348acbf166430e94814e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTR&#211;GENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Estrogens are a group of hormones that play a crucial role in the development and regulation of the female reproductive system, as well as in the establishment of secondary sexual characteristics. These hormones are also significant for maintaining bone health; their reduction with age is linked to an increased risk of osteoporosis. In addition to their natural functions, estrogens are utilized in medical treatments, particularly for transgender women, to help align their physical characteristics with their gender identity. Furthermore, estrogens influence the regulation of gonadotropin secretion, including hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone) and LH (luteinizing hormone). They also have an impact on prolactin levels and are associated with conditions like hyperprolactinemia. Overall, estrogens are vital for various physiological processes and health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3473</data>
      <data key="d7">27b2a1f4bf924f37bb18f808012c7588</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MINERALES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">MINERALES are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in various bodily functions, including bone health, fluid balance, and muscle function. They are inorganic nutrients found in foods such as cereals and are vital for overall health. In particular, certain minerals like selenium, zinc, magnesium, and copper are important for optimizing recovery after exercise. Additionally, minerals can be consumed in greater quantities through a Mediterranean diet, which is known to enhance general health. It is also noteworthy that patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation may experience deficiencies in these essential nutrients, highlighting the importance of adequate mineral intake for recovery and well-being. Overall, MINERALES are integral to maintaining health and supporting various physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63,281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,86a4647fb1fa580f7b72aa4833965ecb,aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d3">647</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3474</data>
      <data key="d7">8f73a55053914dbaad070e1c8017fc5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSTITUTO DE MEDICINA NORTEAMERICANO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Institute of Medicine in North America provides guidelines and recommendations regarding health and nutrition, including vitamin D levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3475</data>
      <data key="d7">774249c3027a4e27ba45dafdd63bc501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BISCHOFF-FERRARI">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Bischoff-Ferrari is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the effects of vitamin D supplementation on fracture reduction.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3476</data>
      <data key="d7">7ac9ff1ec53a42ec81dcc8cf39d06874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA D2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin D2, also known as Ergocalciferol, is a form of vitamin D that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium and phosphate levels in the body. It is commonly used to treat deficiencies and to help maintain adequate calcium levels. However, studies have indicated that Vitamin D2 does not show significant effects on mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3477</data>
      <data key="d7">17883e47ca194da98ce1a3e30fcbe7f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALFACALCIDOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alfacalcidol is an active form of vitamin D that is used in the treatment of certain conditions but did not show significant effects on mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3478</data>
      <data key="d7">029dfa6f247140efa2073bf02d24f74a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCITRIOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcitriol is a biologically active form of vitamin D that plays a crucial role in calcium metabolism and bone health. It is a metabolite of vitamin D that is particularly important for enhancing calcium absorption in the intestines, making it beneficial for patients with conditions that lead to hypocalcemia, especially those with abnormal vitamin D metabolism or hypoparathyroidism. Additionally, calcitriol has been noted to enhance magnesium absorption in the intestines, further supporting its role in mineral metabolism. As a supplement, calcitriol is utilized to improve calcium absorption in patients, thereby contributing to overall bone health and metabolic function.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3479</data>
      <data key="d7">e000be5202a04fbf818f7f76fce3564c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOPENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteopenia is a condition characterized by lower than normal bone density, which can be a significant health concern for various patient populations. It is often detected in individuals with metabolic disorders, including those with Glycogen Storage Disease (GSD) types III and 0, where it can develop as a long-term complication. Additionally, osteopenia is prevalent among patients receiving prolonged parenteral nutrition, indicating reduced bone mass due to nutritional deficiencies. 

This condition can also arise in patients suffering from chronic diseases such as EPOC (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) and Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica (Cystic Fibrosis), particularly in those who are malnourished. Furthermore, individuals with Anorexia Nerviosa may experience osteopenia due to elevated cortisol levels, which negatively impact bone density. 

Preventive measures, such as adequate vitamin D intake, are crucial in mitigating the risk of developing osteopenia. The condition is often seen as a precursor to osteoporosis, highlighting the importance of monitoring bone health in at-risk populations, including those with hyperparathyroidism. Overall, osteopenia represents a multifaceted health issue that requires attention across various medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8,cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">1037</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">3480</data>
      <data key="d7">93f797cf25cd4cb49227cbafdf2348d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Autoimmune diseases, referred to as "ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNES," are conditions characterized by the immune system erroneously attacking the body's own tissues. Research suggests that vitamin D may have a role in the prevention of these diseases. Additionally, autoimmune diseases can be a potential cause of pancreatitis, which highlights the importance of excluding them during the diagnostic process.</data>
      <data key="d2">71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3481</data>
      <data key="d7">990ee2a0dbf94abd81f93decbb6e2ae0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES INFECCIOSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDADES INFECCIOSAS" refers to infectious diseases, which are illnesses caused by pathogens. Research has indicated that vitamin D may play a potential role in the prevention of these diseases. Additionally, "ENFERMEDADES INFECCIOSAS" is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing specifically on the study and management of infectious diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">5173ac9bd92d5f238acade41f8c65ebf,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d3">568</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3482</data>
      <data key="d7">40a662d392514d1d93fffcee4cbe0e5b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDODEMENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudodementia is a condition that mimics dementia but is caused by other factors, often linked to folate deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3483</data>
      <data key="d7">cd81adbebcdd4d2cb0fe1bad8d2ada31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMENCIA SECUNDARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Secondary dementia is a type of dementia that is caused by other medical conditions, which can be influenced by nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3484</data>
      <data key="d7">eaa4d78f00e241f09a5bef2ebf0be588</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PIRIDOXAL-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pyridoxal phosphate is the active form of vitamin B6, which is involved in the metabolism of homocysteine.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3485</data>
      <data key="d7">965faa69377f476781dc0f42948910fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES S&#201;RICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serum levels refer to the concentration of substances in the blood, such as vitamin D, which are important for health assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3486</data>
      <data key="d7">c29272363d48487983cb9df2e22d3e94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA MEGALOBL&#193;STICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia megalobl&#225;stica is a medical condition characterized by the presence of large, abnormal red blood cells. This type of anemia can arise from deficiencies in essential nutrients, specifically Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; and folate. A deficiency in Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; can lead to the development of anemia megalobl&#225;stica, while a lack of folate is also a significant cause of megaloblastic anemia. Both deficiencies result in impaired red blood cell production, contributing to the overall condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7,fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3487</data>
      <data key="d7">005fa24d89784c768601476779475143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMOCISTE&#205;NA ELEVADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Elevated homocysteine levels are a risk factor for cardiovascular diseases and can be reduced by adequate folate intake.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3488</data>
      <data key="d7">c59caa161d8a4b8381e06ee04c7fcce8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIOXIDANTE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">ANTIOXIDANTE refers to substances that help protect cells from damage caused by free radicals. One notable example is vitamin C, which functions as an antioxidant, playing a crucial role in safeguarding cellular integrity and promoting overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a,c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3489</data>
      <data key="d7">2698df650c6a4730a92f59a8e73d2954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCORBUTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El escorbuto es una enfermedad causada por la deficiencia de vitamina C, que se ha estudiado en relaci&#243;n con la ingesta de esta vitamina.</data>
      <data key="d2">499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3490</data>
      <data key="d7">3fb52a9f8b0b41d9b208fcbc1954eced</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESFRIADO COM&#218;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El resfriado com&#250;n es una enfermedad que ha sido objeto de investigaci&#243;n en relaci&#243;n con la vitamina C y su potencial para prevenirla.</data>
      <data key="d2">499d173ee93b4176f90d9ebe4ad8dd9a</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3491</data>
      <data key="d7">a3f56d1159544938ab5670aa44d17783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRAAT JM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Graat JM is a researcher who analyzed the effects of vitamin E on infections, finding paradoxical results in a study published in JAMA 2002.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3492</data>
      <data key="d7">3215b0795d04493d9377620b2d5cb4ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER DE PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CANCER DE PULM&#211;N, or lung cancer, is a serious disease that can metastasize to the pituitary gland, potentially impacting its function. Research suggests that there is a probable association between lung cancer and selenium deficiency. Additionally, dietary deficiencies in vitamin E, especially in men, may also influence the development of lung cancer. This highlights the importance of nutrition in the context of lung cancer risk and progression.</data>
      <data key="d2">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f,c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8,f43e3958f11ed24b0a02f60a2993309a</data>
      <data key="d3">611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3493</data>
      <data key="d7">c276afbf81944f25b792a020e92a360d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRROSIS BILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biliary cirrhosis is a condition that can lead to severe vitamin E deficiency and associated health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3494</data>
      <data key="d7">a89903f36b634110835c4c53046efab6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PEROXIDACI&#211;N LIP&#205;DICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lipid peroxidation is a biochemical process characterized by the reaction of free radicals with lipids in cell membranes, resulting in the theft of electrons from these lipids. This process can lead to significant cell damage. However, antioxidants such as vitamins C and E play a crucial role in inhibiting lipid peroxidation, thereby protecting cells from oxidative stress and maintaining cellular integrity.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3495</data>
      <data key="d7">65ec5a3ed9f84ff0b2490ff2ff66ecb5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATRESIA BILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biliary atresia is a condition that affects the bile ducts and can lead to malabsorption of nutrients, including vitamin E.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3496</data>
      <data key="d7">951eab01568e4f9997d8ef038649b4b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGREGACI&#211;N PLAQUETARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Platelet aggregation is the clumping together of platelets in the blood, which can be inhibited by vitamin E.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3497</data>
      <data key="d7">1e18728ee56646578b114e77cfe0bfda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A AT&#193;XICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ataxic neuropathy is a condition that can result from severe vitamin E deficiency, leading to coordination problems.</data>
      <data key="d2">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3498</data>
      <data key="d7">fdfc081cde3a43f0962e6be7c7948752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8321;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B&#8321;, also known as thiamine, is important for neurological health and is found in various foods including bread, legumes, and pork.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">3499</data>
      <data key="d7">e540ee2a572544d59de9eae6b6c8702a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8322;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B&#8322;, or riboflavin, acts as a cofactor in Red-Ox reactions and is found in dairy products and green vegetables.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3500</data>
      <data key="d7">720bd37ce9ee43a8bf5de30217adf371</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8323;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B&#8323;, also known as niacin, is an essential vitamin that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is found in organ meats and several other foods. Additionally, niacin is utilized therapeutically to address deficiencies in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f,bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">1888</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">3501</data>
      <data key="d7">139f454751eb4dc9b55c0a328dbc0295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XEROFTALMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Xerophthalmia is a condition caused by vitamin A deficiency, leading to dryness of the cornea and potential blindness.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3502</data>
      <data key="d7">2c49866b6c4e45018fc3f3f1ba3a32d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEGENERACI&#211;N MACULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Age-related macular degeneration is an eye condition that can be influenced by vitamin deficiencies, particularly vitamin A.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3503</data>
      <data key="d7">b53a013030554683b9b2cfe312ed33df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMORRAGIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemorragias refer to bleeding that can occur within adrenal masses, which may be discovered incidentally during medical examinations. Additionally, hemorrhages can arise from a significant deficiency of vitamin K, a crucial nutrient necessary for proper blood clotting. This highlights the importance of both anatomical factors, such as adrenal masses, and nutritional deficiencies in the occurrence of hemorragias.</data>
      <data key="d2">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3504</data>
      <data key="d7">343a55fe5022413a9d3ce3f817daf203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEURITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neuritis is an inflammation of the nerves that can be treated with vitamin B&#8321;, highlighting its therapeutic utility.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3505</data>
      <data key="d7">be7defdcf65c4b1a83deb920016bca5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLINEURITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyneuritis is a condition that can be treated with vitamin B&#8321;, which is important for nerve health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3506</data>
      <data key="d7">77325e64083447689488f0353074b2c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAJO NIVEL SOCIOECON&#211;MICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Low socioeconomic status can lead to nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin B&#8321;, particularly in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3507</data>
      <data key="d7">82b089d0950849a58ddb0344e12bf6a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROTOXICOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thyrotoxicosis is a clinical syndrome characterized by elevated levels of thyroid hormones in the body, which can arise from various causes. This condition is not only significant for its hormonal implications but can also be associated with vitamin B&#8321; deficiency, which may impact neurological health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3508</data>
      <data key="d7">1bb71ca9862e4947a6206c31a7069a7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AYUNO PROLONGADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prolonged fasting can result in deficiencies of vitamins, particularly vitamin K.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3509</data>
      <data key="d7">a75937951c644144a3be253602dfb2ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMENDACIONES DIARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Daily recommendations for vitamins A, K, B&#8321;, B&#8322;, and B&#8323; are essential for maintaining health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d3">613</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3510</data>
      <data key="d7">bdf6c49d4f99466b8699e7857c207876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINA B&#8325;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#225;cido pantot&#233;nico, conocido como vitamina B&#8325;, es importante en la s&#237;ntesis de &#225;cidos grasos y se encuentra en abundancia en alimentos como carnes y legumbres.</data>
      <data key="d2">26629a423810543625be19deea4cc35f</data>
      <data key="d3">1890</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
