    </node>
    <node id="PROTECTORES G&#193;STRICOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Protectores g&#225;stricos, such as omeprazol, are medications that may reduce Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; absorption when used long-term.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3521</data>
      <data key="d7">b398769df66e4b7ab92cf4f1e93fc82d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO CARDIOVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Riesgo cardiovascular, or cardiovascular risk, encompasses the likelihood of developing heart-related conditions and is influenced by various factors, including lifestyle and dietary choices. It is a significant concern in the context of hormone replacement therapy, where its potential effects on heart health are closely monitored. Additionally, cardiovascular risk is a critical area of study in relation to diabetes, which is part of Samuel Namara's research focus. 

The risk can also be heightened in patients with EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease) and is associated with Vitamin B&#8321;&#8322; deficiency. Furthermore, the long-term health risks linked to the use of certain medications, such as fentermina, have been noted by the European Medicines Agency (EMA). Overall, understanding and managing cardiovascular risk is essential for preventing heart-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">2cff1005fe34ac994249b78b4ca112c7,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,920badd1fd76f2c279282a4a20295a55,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6,ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
