    <node id="HORMONAS TIROIDEAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">HORMONAS TIROIDEAS, or thyroid hormones, are hormones produced by the thyroid gland, primarily including T3 (triiodothyronine) and T4 (thyroxine). These hormones are essential for regulating various metabolic processes in the body, including lipid metabolism and overall metabolic function. The production of thyroid hormones is dependent on the availability of iodine, and their synthesis can be affected by factors such as iodine deficiency.

Thyroid hormones are regulated by thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) and play a crucial role not only in metabolism but also in influencing sodium levels and fluid and electrolyte balance within the body. They are vital for normal development and function, and their levels are often assessed in the initial evaluation of patients, particularly those with eating disorders, to understand their metabolic status.

Additionally, thyroid hormones are involved in conditions such as hyperthyroidism, highlighting their significance in both health and disease. Overall, HORMONAS TIROIDEAS are critical for maintaining metabolic homeostasis and overall physiological balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7,08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,10cd1db13dc50a14adab6e4c215bb3b0,1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,14299e85574ef5c76c7164e2c4d20a53,3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,4c18507e3d98242cdbcddd1a1997b92f,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d,92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f,f43e3958f11ed24b0a02f60a2993309a,f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
