    </node>
    <node id="ACIDO FOLICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acido F&#243;lico, also known as folic acid, is a B vitamin produced by intestinal bacteria and plays a crucial role in DNA synthesis and repair. It is essential for cell division and overall health, with a recommended daily intake of 200-400 &#956;g for adults. Additionally, Acido F&#243;lico is important for brain health, as it has been linked to cognitive function and the prevention of cognitive decline. In certain medical situations, such as hyper-homocysteinemia in patients undergoing dialysis, higher doses of 1-5 mg per day may be recommended. Folic acid levels are also measured in blood tests to assess a patient's health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d9c11c44c3cf4e1e3148949cc0a4096,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1,b3760fcb9c0421b66d37c20b1dc68577</data>
