    <node id="HELICOBACTER PYLORI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Helicobacter pylori is a type of bacteria that resides in the human stomach and is associated with various gastrointestinal diseases. It can cause infections that lead to conditions such as gastritis and peptic ulcer disease. Additionally, Helicobacter pylori is linked to atrophic gastritis, which may contribute to vitamin B12 deficiency. The presence of this bacterium can also result in iron deficiency due to malabsorption. Overall, Helicobacter pylori plays a significant role in gastrointestinal health and disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5,6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc,70b2393fa61e51fc3e772479a9792c98,90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021,b602544ec2048878e40226cd2c0b29d4</data>
      <data key="d3">1810</data>
