    <node id="MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Myocardial infarction, commonly known as a heart attack, is a critical health event characterized by the blockage of blood flow to the heart, resulting in a medical emergency. This serious condition is influenced by various risk factors, including dietary intake. Research has shown that factors such as vitamin D and calcium intake, as well as omega-3 fatty acids, can play a significant role in the risk of experiencing a myocardial infarction. Understanding these dietary impacts is essential for managing and potentially reducing the risk of this life-threatening event.</data>
      <data key="d2">d93c7f9ea61d85e6be22df63c4b67d4d,dbdb3cd3b9065e8846fd2eb15b9d5879,e271766bdc88e84209e5cdac4adc0724</data>
