    <node id="N ENGL J MED">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The New England Journal of Medicine (N Engl J Med) is a prestigious peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes a wide range of research articles, reviews, and case reports across various medical disciplines. Established as a leading source of medical knowledge, it has published significant studies on topics such as urinary sodium and potassium excretion and their relationship to cardiovascular events, as well as the causes, pathogenesis, and treatment of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis. The journal also focuses on the impacts of diet on health, including research related to obesity and its treatments, and cardiovascular health. Overall, N Engl J Med serves as a vital resource for medical professionals and researchers seeking comprehensive insights into contemporary medical issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,7e4178b0d21cc5424b4c54bc5de42471,8cdedff25a6a366c17615073d05a5aa2,91c73a1de38742d1b6c4e803ec1717a3,b2549791b62afc5e1244c2c610af55e6,b96414a52f13cac336436d9e8173baef,ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4,e271766bdc88e84209e5cdac4adc0724,e376d9f50b7608f5b6d1f88877fde59e,fa36086a4b64a662e6e1752ee6e589aa</data>
