    <node id="TIROIDES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TIROIDES," or thyroid gland, is an essential endocrine gland located in the neck that plays a critical role in regulating metabolism, growth, and development. It produces several hormones, including thyroid hormones such as T3 (triiodothyronine) and T4 (thyroxine), as well as calcitonin, which is involved in calcium metabolism. The gland captures iodine, which is necessary for the synthesis of these hormones.

The thyroid is also significant in the context of various medical conditions. Its dysfunction can lead to disorders such as hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism, which are characterized by an underactive or overactive thyroid, respectively. Additionally, the thyroid gland can be the site of serious health issues, including the development of medullary carcinomas and other forms of thyroid cancer.

In the field of endocrinology, the TIROIDES is a focal point for diagnostic studies and treatments, particularly concerning the differential diagnosis of conditions like TSH-producing pituitary tumors and thyroid hormone resistance. Overall, the thyroid gland is vital for maintaining metabolic balance and overall health in the human body.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7,072912695b1cff9f390d4ead3b9ad742,10cd1db13dc50a14adab6e4c215bb3b0,171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040,39cdf983b8de558536d2d829978daba1,4138cb85d4afff56555b4a536340ca90,4c18507e3d98242cdbcddd1a1997b92f,7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415,bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56,fc81f645a5600b374c960fd8739a0503</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
