    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DIFERENCIADO DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer diferenciado de tiroides is a type of thyroid cancer that is addressed in clinical practice guidelines. This form of cancer is characterized by its ability to concentrate iodine in a manner similar to healthy thyroid tissue, which necessitates specific diagnostic follow-up. C&#225;ncer diferenciado de tiroides generally includes papillary and follicular thyroid cancers and is associated with a better prognosis compared to other types of thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a,f4a7e9b010f4062fc8a4ad57c51de506,fc81f645a5600b374c960fd8739a0503</data>
