    <node id="MISCELEANEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "MISCELEANEA" encompasses a diverse range of subjects. It includes a variety of substances that can induce the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), such as opiates and other medications. Additionally, "MISCELEANEA" covers various miscellaneous topics related to nutrition that do not fit into other specific categories. This broad scope highlights the entity's multifaceted nature, addressing both pharmacological aspects and nutritional themes.</data>
      <data key="d2">476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3618</data>
      <data key="d7">027c2819286f4d2f8da5c0719e197e5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CASOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"CASOS CL&#205;NICOS" refers to clinical case studies that serve to illustrate specific medical and nutritional conditions and their management. These case studies provide detailed examples that highlight various medical issues as well as nutritional challenges and treatments. They are utilized to enhance understanding of both medical and nutritional practices through specific clinical examples.</data>
      <data key="d2">476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d3">1291</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
