      <data key="d6">3619</data>
      <data key="d7">8f8518762fd54266965f4b053df92d25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL" is a medical condition characterized by the inadequate production of hormones by the adrenal glands, specifically steroid hormones such as cortisol and aldosterone. This insufficiency affects the body's fluid and electrolyte balance and can lead to various health issues, including symptoms like hypoglycemia and fatigue. In summary, "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL" occurs when the adrenal glands fail to produce sufficient amounts of essential hormones, resulting in significant physiological consequences.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,4eb5a5cd6147917dd1380d49c613a78b,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
      <data key="d3">1491</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">20</data>
      <data key="d6">3620</data>
      <data key="d7">fcdf62a0ef8d471faff771122565a550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE CUSHING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cushing's syndrome, known as "s&#237;ndrome de Cushing" in Spanish, is a hormonal disorder characterized by prolonged exposure to high levels of cortisol, a glucocorticoid hormone. This condition can arise from various causes, including tumors and the administration of medications. It is associated with specific clinical features and can manifest in different forms, either dependent or independent of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). 

In particular, Cushing's syndrome can occur in approximately 30% of cases related to micronodular adrenal disease, which is linked to the Carney complex. Symptoms of the syndrome may include hirsutism, among other manifestations. Overall, Cushing's syndrome represents a significant medical condition that necessitates careful diagnosis and treatment due to its complex nature and the various underlying causes that can lead to excessive cortisol production.</data>
      <data key="d2">1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1329</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">21</data>
      <data key="d6">3621</data>
      <data key="d7">4d476de45d134be8a84c57eaad9d634c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERALDOSTERONISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperaldosteronism, also known as Hiperaldosteronismo, is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of the hormone aldosterone. This condition is often associated with adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal tumors during imaging studies. Hyperaldosteronism is primarily related to excessive sodium retention in the body, leading to various health complications. The condition is discussed in detail in the Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n, highlighting its significance in endocrinology and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3</data>
      <data key="d3">1492</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3622</data>
      <data key="d7">caeedcc18df344b1b880a461cf936585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEOCROMOCITOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FEOCROMOCITOMA, also known as pheochromocytoma, is a rare tumor that originates from chromaffin cells in the adrenal glands. This tumor is characterized by the excessive production of catecholamines, which can lead to various clinical symptoms, including hypertension and hypertensive crises. It is often diagnosed through biochemical profiling and is important to rule out before surgical procedures, such as those for medullary thyroid carcinoma.

Patients with FEOCROMOCITOMA may experience a range of symptoms due to the overproduction of catecholamines, and the condition is associated with certain genetic syndromes, including Cowden syndrome. Screening for this tumor is recommended starting at the age of 11 for individuals at risk. Treatment typically involves surgical intervention, which is necessary after proper medical preparation to manage the symptoms and potential complications, such as hypercalcemia due to excess PTHrP secretion.

Overall, FEOCROMOCITOMA requires specific diagnostic and therapeutic approaches due to its potential malignancy and the serious health implications associated with its symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,4433d2fdc6ba080efa0cf63e8603172a,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,a0b43d4a377fca32f55f83fd79e3d9e1,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3,de6e1d8ac9f422acb17fd26b77b485da</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">46</data>
      <data key="d6">3623</data>
      <data key="d7">9f5cc04375d048d8875bbdd61b2101b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" refers to an adrenal incidentaloma, which is a mass found in the adrenal gland that is typically benign and non-functioning. These masses are often discovered incidentally during imaging studies conducted for unrelated medical conditions. Upon discovery, further evaluation may be necessary to assess the hormonal activity of the mass and to rule out the possibility of malignancy. The term "incidentaloma suprarrenal" specifically denotes an adrenal mass that requires careful assessment to determine its functionality and whether surgical removal (ex&#233;resis) is needed.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">25</data>
      <data key="d6">3624</data>
      <data key="d7">504b118d43dd4de09844d90be84ae876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinoma suprarrenal is a rare primary malignant tumor that originates in the adrenal glands, with an incidence of approximately 1 in 1,000,000 inhabitants per year. This type of cancer is more commonly diagnosed in women and typically occurs in individuals between the ages of 40 to 50. Carcinoma suprarrenal may be suspected in cases of adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal masses during imaging studies. Overall, carcinoma suprarrenal represents a significant concern in the context of adrenal cancer, highlighting the need for awareness and careful evaluation of adrenal masses.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3625</data>
      <data key="d7">ada1e85a16c94b33b5ba67609eb07996</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita, also known as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, is a genetic disorder that significantly impacts the production of hormones in the adrenal glands. This condition is primarily caused by a deficiency of the enzyme 21-hydroxylase, which leads to an overproduction of androgens. As a result, individuals with this disorder may experience symptoms such as hirsutism and other hormonal imbalances. The disorder affects adrenal gland function, resulting in various health implications related to adrenal hormone production.</data>
      <data key="d2">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,476274b4d401aba4307379ed0f5387ac,b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d3">1288</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">3626</data>
      <data key="d7">b23103e49068420380cd90c45bf4e6df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE, also known as autoimmune polyglandular syndrome, is a medical condition characterized by the presence of multiple autoimmune disorders that affect the endocrine system. This syndrome may involve the association of two or more endocrine disorders mediated by an immune mechanism, which can include conditions such as diabetes mellitus and Addison's disease. Specifically, autoimmune polyglandular syndrome type 1 is noted for the destruction of the parathyroid glands, resulting in hypoparathyroidism and related complications. Additionally, this syndrome may be connected to other endocrine disorders discussed in the context of POEMS syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d3">680</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">3627</data>
      <data key="d7">f6670e79b0f043b6abb9b2dfdd6aaabf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLISMO FOSFOC&#193;LCICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolismo fosfoc&#225;lcico refers to the metabolic processes involving calcium and phosphate in the body, crucial for bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
