    <node id="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS, or neuroendocrine tumors, are a group of neoplasias that can arise from neuroendocrine cells, which are responsible for hormone production and regulation. These tumors can occur in various parts of the body, including the digestive system, and may lead to symptoms such as chronic diarrhea. They are also associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes, specifically MEN1 and MEN2. Research on neuroendocrine tumors is being conducted by Nuria Valdes Gallego, with a particular focus on paragangliomas and pheochromocytomas. Additionally, these tumors can have significant implications for hormone production, which may affect bone health and contribute to conditions like osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2,7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3,7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc,9851218c3244d6f4279055a04d219044,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d3">1310</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3629</data>
      <data key="d7">97ce0f63d53c42eab1dfe762953456c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia, is a group of disorders that impact the endocrine glands, resulting in the formation of tumors and hormonal imbalances. Additionally, the term "men" refers to a demographic group that is often considered in dietary guidelines, which include specific nutritional recommendations tailored to their needs. This dual context highlights both the medical implications of MEN as a health condition and the nutritional considerations relevant to the male demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a,e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2</data>
      <data key="d3">1310</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3630</data>
      <data key="d7">358ef208a3b74cf3922129b6cb019ccf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PUBERTAD PRECOZ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La pubertad precoz es un desarrollo sexual anormalmente temprano en ni&#241;os, caracterizado por la aparici&#243;n de caracter&#237;sticas sexuales secundarias antes de la edad normal, que se establece como antes de los 9 a&#241;os para los ni&#241;os y antes de los 7 a&#241;os para las ni&#241;as. Esta condici&#243;n puede ser clasificada como central o perif&#233;rica y puede estar asociada a diversas condiciones m&#233;dicas. Aunque no es la causa m&#225;s frecuente, la pubertad precoz puede manifestarse como un s&#237;ntoma relacionado con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal. En resumen, la pubertad precoz es una manifestaci&#243;n cl&#237;nica que conlleva importantes implicaciones m&#233;dicas y requiere atenci&#243;n adecuada.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">3631</data>
      <data key="d7">986532654adf44e18db71e85471eb1ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETRASO PUBERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Retraso puberal is a condition characterized by delayed onset of puberty, which may require medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
