    <node id="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">G&#211;NADAS are the organs responsible for producing gametes, which are the reproductive cells necessary for sexual reproduction. In humans, the gonads are represented by the testes in males and the ovaries in females. Additionally, in the context of hormone therapy, gonads may undergo surgical alteration or removal, impacting their function in gamete production.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415,bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d3">1365</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
