      <data key="d6">3638</data>
      <data key="d7">4f34c4e8cd6c413ba551cafa6b39444b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERCALCEMIA is a medical condition characterized by abnormally high levels of calcium in the blood, typically defined as serum calcium levels exceeding 10.5 mg/dl. This condition is often associated with various medical issues, including hyperparathyroidism, which is a common cause, as well as malignancies such as certain tumors. The elevated calcium levels can lead to a range of health complications, potentially affecting kidney function and altering a patient's nutritional needs. Treatment is often required to lower calcium levels and manage the associated health risks. Hipercalcemia can occur in a small percentage of the population and is an important condition to consider in the context of parathyroid hormone and its implications for patient health.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335,7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">3639</data>
      <data key="d7">534e6c5c0c8542c1aaebec6603142e3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOCALCEMIA is a medical condition characterized by low calcium levels in the blood, defined as a serum calcium level below 8.5 mg/dl. This condition can lead to various health issues, including muscle spasms and complications in patients with conditions such as pancreatitis. Hypocalcemia can also occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition and is commonly observed in hospitalized patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,86aa5f95aae53ab120c5c63eda5486bc,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
