      <data key="d6">3681</data>
      <data key="d7">7c8a8e98c2224222aec06e6394a3369f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GH, or Growth Hormone, is a crucial hormone that plays a significant role in growth, metabolism, and body composition in humans and other animals. Its secretion is episodic and regulated by various physiological factors, exhibiting a diurnal rhythm. GH stimulates growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration, making it essential for development and overall health. In the context of patient diagnosis and treatment, GH deficiency is a critical concern, as it can impact growth and metabolic functions. Additionally, while GH is sometimes considered for nutritional support, there is insufficient evidence to support its effectiveness in this area. In certain cases, such as hypophysitis, GH levels may remain normal despite deficiencies in other hormones. Overall, GH is vital for maintaining proper physiological functions related to growth and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,2261671ccad439da1ed9ea5a27857dc8,4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,593ae586183f02d2611966f8a1603e5d,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32,9d100ca2bc5b797561fe3b3a4bb61586,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">3682</data>
      <data key="d7">2753a32dedc04b74b2326634339e86c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FSH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FSH, or Follicle-Stimulating Hormone, is a crucial gonadotropin produced by the adenohypophysis (anterior pituitary gland) that plays a significant role in regulating reproductive processes. It is essential for the development of eggs in the ovaries of females and the production of sperm in the testes of males. FSH is involved in the regulation of the menstrual cycle and is also relevant in diagnosing conditions such as pubertal delays and endocrine function through hormonal studies.

In addition to its primary functions, FSH can be present at normal levels in certain medical conditions, such as hypophysitis, which distinguishes it from other hormones like ACTH and TSH. The hormone stimulates the growth of ovarian follicles in women and activates Sertoli cells in the testes to facilitate sperm production. Overall, FSH is vital for sexual development and reproductive health in both genders.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,592d424edaa447a54ab4489d82495db6,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1292</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3683</data>
      <data key="d7">966ac4ee87274aa4b184fd648bf46d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LH, or luteinizing hormone, is a crucial gonadotropin that plays a significant role in the regulation of the menstrual cycle and ovulation in females. It is responsible for triggering ovulation and stimulating the production of testosterone in males by acting on the Leydig cells in the testes. LH can be present at normal levels in cases of hypophysitis, which distinguishes it from other hormones such as ACTH and TSH. In summary, LH is essential for reproductive health, influencing both female ovulation and male testosterone production, and is often measured in hormonal studies to assess hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,592d424edaa447a54ab4489d82495db6,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
