    <node id="DOPAMINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dopamina, also known as dopamine, is a crucial neurotransmitter synthesized in the brain that plays a significant role in various physiological functions. It is involved in mood regulation, motor control, and the inhibition of prolactin secretion in the adenohypophysis. Additionally, dopamine is mentioned in the context of tesofensina's mechanism of action, highlighting its importance in pharmacological processes. Overall, dopamine serves as an essential regulator of hormonal activity and contributes to numerous neurological functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
