      <data key="d7">283cd6fea4e348c88f1b8ac5a6f80d2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VASOPRESINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VASOPRESINA, also known as antidiuretic hormone (ADH), is a hormone produced in the hypothalamus and released by the neurohypophysis. It plays a crucial role in regulating water retention in the kidneys, thereby helping to maintain the body's fluid balance. In addition to its primary function in water regulation, vasopresina is also implicated in the regulation of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) and has been studied in relation to thyroid function. Overall, vasopresina is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body through its various regulatory roles.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
