    <node id="GHRH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GHRH, or growth hormone-releasing hormone, is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating the release of growth hormone (GH) from the pituitary gland. Additionally, GHRH is involved in the regulation of luteinizing hormone (LH) and follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH). This hormone is essential for various physiological processes, including growth and metabolism, by promoting the secretion of growth hormone.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3691</data>
      <data key="d7">3092b8f6d16445f2ad4e26cd48d7154d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOMATOSTATINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SOMATOSTATINA is a hormone produced by pancreatic delta cells that plays a crucial role in inhibiting the secretion of several other hormones, including growth hormone (GH), thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH), prolactin (PRL), and adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) in the pituitary gland. This inhibitory function makes somatostatin significant in various medical treatments. 

Somatostatin is utilized in the treatment of pituitary tumors and is effective in managing complications following surgery, such as anastomotic dehiscence. Additionally, it is employed in the treatment of specific conditions like chylothorax and lymphatic fistulas, where it helps reduce gastrointestinal secretions and lymphatic flow. 

Moreover, somatostatin analogs are medications derived from this hormone that can be administered in parenteral nutrition under specific circumstances. These analogs are particularly useful in treating VIPoma, a type of tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide, by inhibiting its secretion. They are also used in managing acromegaly, a condition characterized by excessive growth hormone, and are often combined with dietary modifications to enhance treatment efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,200447233341122a47f0010251600608,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,3ee948dc4ddfdc75daa8fe7db9bb471e,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d3">1795</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3692</data>
      <data key="d7">cd610ea059c94753b654d08564a86771</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACTH, or Adrenocorticotropic Hormone, is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that plays a crucial role in stimulating the adrenal glands to release cortisol. This hormone is significant in the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions, particularly Cushing's disease and adrenal insufficiency. ACTH is involved in the regulation of cortisol production and can also influence the secretion of other hormones, such as aldosterone and ADH, under certain conditions.

The secretion of ACTH follows a circadian rhythm and is regulated by hypothalamic corticotropin-releasing hormone (CRH) and other factors. It is often measured in the evaluation of adrenal function and is essential for diagnosing conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia and pituitary disorders such as hypophysitis, which can lead to hormonal deficiencies.

In summary, ACTH is a vital hormone that not only stimulates cortisol production in the adrenal glands but also plays a key role in various diagnostic processes related to adrenal health and hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,172da539e648a8f72cc1576d16e35f46,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,55a9e6e8ff365dac34555c938dd3c244,6083387b51909347a13ed5aa1c92bb26,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,7f3df1437755b60344fdffd2ef3b8a9e,85eef7ed9c9b92d86939a6687ea2acfd,88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,8eb2b7021402eb440fe88889b78c2785,9d100ca2bc5b797561fe3b3a4bb61586,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0,bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6,dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb,dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14,fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
