    </node>
    <node id="CRH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">CRH, or corticotropin-releasing hormone, is a hormone released by the hypothalamus that plays a crucial role in the body's stress response. It stimulates the release of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) from the pituitary gland, which is essential for regulating various physiological processes related to stress. Overall, CRH is integral to the endocrine system's response to stressors, facilitating the communication between the hypothalamus and the pituitary gland.</data>
      <data key="d2">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
