    <node id="KRONENBERG HM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kronenberg HM is a prominent figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized as both a co-author and editor of the "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology." His contributions to this comprehensive work encompass a wide range of topics within endocrinology, including hormonal influences on bone health, calcium metabolism, and parathyroid function. Additionally, he has provided insights into the treatment of hypercalcemia and the study of neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Kronenberg HM has played a significant role in advancing endocrine research and education, particularly in relation to conditions such as pheochromocytoma and insulinoma. His extensive involvement in the textbook underscores his expertise and commitment to the field of endocrinology.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
