    <node id="MELMED S">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Melmed S is a prominent researcher and author in the field of endocrinology, particularly known for his contributions to the understanding and treatment of various endocrine disorders. He has made significant contributions to the literature on the adenohypophysis and the treatment of disorders related to prolactin. Melmed S is notably recognized for his work on acromegaly, having authored clinical practice guidelines for this condition.

He is one of the authors and editors of the "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology," a comprehensive resource that covers a wide range of topics within endocrinology, including the treatment of osteoporosis and the management of neuroendocrine tumors. His contributions to this textbook have provided valuable insights into various endocrine disorders, including insulinoma and pheochromocytoma. Through his extensive work, Melmed S has established himself as a key figure in the field of endocrinology, influencing both clinical practice and academic research.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,200447233341122a47f0010251600608,2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
