    <node id="POLONSKY KS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Polonsky KS is a prominent figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized for his significant contributions as both a co-author and editor of the "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology." His work has greatly enhanced the understanding of various hormonal regulations and disorders, including conditions such as insulinoma, osteoporosis, hypercalcemia, and neuroendocrine tumors. As an editor, Polonsky KS has played a crucial role in shaping the content of the textbook, providing insights into endocrine functions and specific conditions like pheochromocytoma. His contributions have established him as a key authority in the field, making the "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology" a vital resource for understanding complex endocrine issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
