    <node id="GNRH">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH) is a vital hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of the reproductive system. It is responsible for stimulating the release of gonadotropins, specifically follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH), from the pituitary gland. This release is essential for reproductive health and is involved in the onset of puberty. Additionally, GnRH is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as cryptorchidism, where it stimulates testosterone production. Overall, GnRH is integral to the functioning of the reproductive system and the regulation of sexual hormone production.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1299</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3709</data>
      <data key="d7">8c89fefc2e8b40fca1d1cb02932d1c2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IGFBP3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">IGFBP3 is the main binding protein for IGF-1, abundant in plasma, and plays a crucial role in regulating the availability of IGF-1 in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa</data>
