    </node>
    <node id="SNYDER PJ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Snyder PJ is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the areas of hyperprolactinemia and hypopituitarism. He has written extensively on the causes and management of hyperprolactinemia, detailing its clinical manifestations and implications. Additionally, Snyder PJ is referenced in the context of male hypogonadism, focusing on its clinical features and diagnosis. His work also encompasses research related to growth hormone, further establishing his expertise in endocrinological disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">172da539e648a8f72cc1576d16e35f46,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51,94acece2df038421a302ca1fa53d5275,9d100ca2bc5b797561fe3b3a4bb61586,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,b344a34a623d4ade6b3ed6e1adae0016</data>
