    </node>
    <node id="HESX1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HESX1 is a transcription factor associated with early activation cascades and linked to septo-optic dysplasia when mutated.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3716</data>
      <data key="d7">a4cbdd70acf849cab2dc3faad9c6bc93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LHX3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">LHX3 is a transcription factor that, when mutated, can cause neurological anomalies due to its expression in the central nervous system.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3717</data>
      <data key="d7">8d0bf15bb1fc49c989b8ece610e0cb7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LHX4">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">LHX4 is a transcription factor involved in the early differentiation of pituitary cells.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
