      <data key="d7">3efd53f81462462183ef7e999a822397</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MUTACIONES refers to genetic mutations that can have significant implications for various health conditions. Notably, mutations in the CYP21A2 gene are responsible for the majority of cases of congenital adrenal hyperplasia and can occur either de novo or be inherited. Additionally, mutations in the PTEN gene are crucial for the diagnosis and management of Cowden syndrome and other related neoplastic syndromes. These genetic alterations can also lead to conditions such as hypopituitarism, which affects hormone production and regulation. Furthermore, mutations can be associated with hereditary conditions, including feochromocitomas and paragangliomas. The PAH gene is another critical area, where over 400 mutations have been identified, leading to various forms of phenylketonuria. Specific mutations in the RTFQ gene have been documented, particularly within the Spanish population. Lastly, mutations in the X-ALD gene are responsible for adrenoleukodystrophy, a condition that impacts the metabolism of very long-chain fatty acids. Overall, the study of MUTACIONES encompasses a wide range of genetic changes that can lead to diverse and significant health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,4eb5a5cd6147917dd1380d49c613a78b,94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558,fa557ef3cae0faa594a71dc7e2d84cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1501</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3730</data>
      <data key="d7">97acd67ed43b4184a10e75f5305d2045</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMAS HIPOFISARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenomas hipofisarios are the most common type of pituitary tumors, characterized as benign growths that affect the pituitary gland. These tumors can lead to various hormonal imbalances and conditions, such as hypopituitarism, which is a deficiency in one or more of the hormones produced by the pituitary gland. Additionally, adenomas hipofisarios can cause hyperprolactinemia, a condition resulting from the overproduction of prolactin. Overall, these tumors can significantly impact hormonal function and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626,fa557ef3cae0faa594a71dc7e2d84cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1321</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">3731</data>
      <data key="d7">c26ede4db1d24fa3817bb50644659cc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipofisitis is an inflammatory condition of the pituitary gland, also known as the hypophysis. This inflammation can lead to various symptoms, including headaches and diabetes insipidus. Additionally, it may result in hypopituitarism, which is a deficiency in hormone production due to damage to the hormone-producing cells of the gland. The condition can be caused by infections or autoimmune processes. Characteristic findings of hipofisitis can be observed through magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).</data>
      <data key="d2">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14,fa557ef3cae0faa594a71dc7e2d84cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">3732</data>
      <data key="d7">8019d24ea63c4bac8b7cc6d3d325fb05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE SHEEHAN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#237;ndrome de Sheehan is a condition that occurs due to pituitary gland damage during childbirth, leading to hypopituitarism.</data>
      <data key="d2">fa557ef3cae0faa594a71dc7e2d84cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1345</data>
