    <node id="UPTODATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UpToDate is a comprehensive online clinical decision support resource that offers evidence-based information for healthcare professionals across a wide range of medical topics. It provides up-to-date literature reviews, clinical guidelines, and detailed information on various conditions, including adrenal incidentalomas, primary aldosteronism, Cushing's syndrome, hyperparathyroidism, hypercalcemia, delayed puberty, primary adrenal insufficiency, hypopituitarism, pheochromocytoma, and acromegaly. 

The platform is designed to assist healthcare providers by delivering current and relevant medical knowledge, including epidemiology, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, and treatment options for numerous conditions. UpToDate is recognized for its role in enhancing clinical decision-making and improving patient care through its extensive database of medical information. Additionally, it includes resources on dietary therapy and obesity in adults, further broadening its scope of support for healthcare professionals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,14ad20b4ac1105ca21faf20e4978fb5a,151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,89b0bde0358432506a0e03d4691dd2ab,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,9d100ca2bc5b797561fe3b3a4bb61586,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,bb2f48277736ce24d1ff0310a682376d,bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">3746</data>
      <data key="d7">11e4f188736f4e4ab98764a54cdb22e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANUAL DE ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n" is a comprehensive guide published by the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n. It serves as a valuable reference for various aspects of endocrinology and nutrition, including the treatment and management of endocrine disorders. The manual discusses lipid metabolism and provides dietary recommendations for managing lipid levels, specifically addressing dyslipidemias. It includes detailed information on the epidemiology, diagnosis, and classification of dyslipidemias, as well as treatment guidelines.

Additionally, the manual covers a range of endocrine disorders, such as Cushing's syndrome, primary adrenal insufficiency, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, and primary hyperaldosteronism. It also provides insights into hypopituitarism and includes guidelines on enteral and parenteral nutrition. Overall, the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n" is an essential resource for healthcare professionals seeking to understand and manage various endocrine and nutritional issues effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">03b7a89c9bb1dfd115acef377b491808,095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,593ae586183f02d2611966f8a1603e5d,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c,6083387b51909347a13ed5aa1c92bb26,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,746fad557197bebe72763efd23a9e0e2,8938669dda86a6eafe0882ea036408c1,9312fdfba5d3f79b95c5e6af38ced009,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,9d100ca2bc5b797561fe3b3a4bb61586,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3,bb2f48277736ce24d1ff0310a682376d,c3a9acd26c8b8bbe2144d4fe53046439,ce43a9a4cdf2497b2f984547a2787fff,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
