    <node id="ADENOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenomas are non-functioning tumors that primarily occur in the pituitary gland, necessitating close observation due to the potential for complications. Additionally, adenomas can also develop in the liver, particularly in patients with hepatic glycogenosis type I, where there is a risk that these tumors may become malignant.</data>
      <data key="d2">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">1345</data>
