      <data key="d6">3771</data>
      <data key="d7">a64190a7a8a8415db94b342c99502ef4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING," also known as Cushing's disease, is an endocrine disorder characterized by elevated levels of cortisol in the body. This condition can arise from various causes, most commonly due to pituitary tumors, specifically corticotropinomas, which produce excess adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). The elevated cortisol levels can lead to secondary hypertension and potassium loss, highlighting the importance of dietary management in affected individuals. Treatment for Cushing's disease may be necessary to control the symptoms and manage the hormonal imbalance effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51,6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb</data>
      <data key="d3">1328</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">3772</data>
      <data key="d7">c6a7cc285b524608bec6a74410fa55f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES PINEALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TUMORES PINEALES, or pineal tumors, are rare tumors that can affect the pineal gland. These tumors are classified into several types, including germ cell tumors and others.</data>
      <data key="d2">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef,4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51</data>
      <data key="d3">1342</data>
