    </node>
    <node id="SUBTIPOS DE RECEPTORES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los subtipos de receptores de somatostatina, como SSTR2 y SSTR5, influyen en la respuesta tumoral a los an&#225;logos de somatostatina.</data>
      <data key="d2">b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626</data>
      <data key="d3">1344</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3814</data>
      <data key="d7">b8efd31f43864afbadee9ee1a718ab64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acromegalia is a chronic hormonal disorder caused by the hypersecretion of growth hormone (GH), often due to pituitary adenomas. This condition leads to abnormal growth of bones and tissues, resulting in various clinical changes and health risks. Individuals with acromegalia may experience somatic growth, which can contribute to multiple comorbidities and an increased risk of premature mortality. The disorder can also affect sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels, further complicating the health profile of those affected. Overall, acromegalia is characterized by significant physical changes and a range of associated health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608,2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32,b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">27</data>
      <data key="d6">3815</data>
      <data key="d7">f3ecacff830248f6b20e9ec8bd2929e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTICOTROPINOMA SILENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El corticotropinoma silente es un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que no presenta s&#237;ntomas evidentes y se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci&#243;n de la OMS.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3816</data>
      <data key="d7">294e8524ab514dcca6f291be1a8f4507</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenoma hipofisario is a benign tumor of the pituitary gland that can lead to various health issues due to its potential to produce excess hormones. This type of tumor originates in the pituitary gland and can cause significant hormonal and clinical alterations. Specifically, adenoma hipofisario may result in the overproduction of growth hormone, which can lead to conditions such as acromegaly, as well as excess adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), which is associated with Cushing's syndrome. These tumors are classified based on their cellular type and hormonal characteristics, highlighting the diversity in their presentation and effects on the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f,8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">28</data>
      <data key="d6">3817</data>
      <data key="d7">d45afebed21b4d0a98448e64d20e291c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA SOMATOTROPO ESCASAMENTE GRANULADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se caracteriza por una baja granulaci&#243;n y se ha reconocido por su agresividad cl&#237;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3818</data>
      <data key="d7">5d1f0ee80521400d989a22cfe96faf21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACROADENOMA LACTOTROPO EN VARONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un adenoma hipofisario que afecta a los varones y se clasifica como macroadenoma, mostrando caracter&#237;sticas cl&#237;nicas espec&#237;ficas.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3819</data>
      <data key="d7">16cba2987ffe400c96e18e0d5fed49cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA DE C&#201;LULAS DE CROOKE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci&#243;n de la OMS y se asocia con caracter&#237;sticas histol&#243;gicas particulares.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3820</data>
      <data key="d7">c91f6a7373624ff5a6228b3a6386d4de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA PLURIHORMONAL PIT-1 POSITIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un adenoma hipofisario que produce m&#250;ltiples hormonas y se clasifica como Pit-1 positivo, anteriormente conocido como adenoma hipofisario silente subtipo III.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3821</data>
      <data key="d7">b9209444ff194b0a9c2122dcaf3f69db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PITUICITOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumores de bajo grado de origen glial que se originan en la hip&#243;fisis posterior y son infrecuentes, a menudo diagnosticados en adultos.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3822</data>
      <data key="d7">be24695503ae480283fd3040770f4a01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRANEOPARINGIOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CRANEOPARINGIOMAS son tumores que afectan la hip&#243;fisis y se clasifican en dos grupos seg&#250;n su histolog&#237;a y alteraciones moleculares. Estos tumores son benignos y se originan de los restos de la bolsa de Rathke. Pueden causar s&#237;ntomas compresivos en la infancia o adolescencia, lo que resalta su impacto en el desarrollo y la salud de los pacientes j&#243;venes.</data>
      <data key="d2">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1346</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3823</data>
      <data key="d7">0a29c4f071eb46ad98a4e1511f6f94dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUISTE DE RATHKE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un tipo de quiste que se forma a partir de restos de la bolsa de Rathke, que puede encontrarse en la regi&#243;n selar.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3824</data>
      <data key="d7">a9d667d46c194a8b9d5cb8b96a3b1b19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEURISMAS CAROT&#205;DEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dilataciones anormales de las arterias carot&#237;deas que pueden afectar la regi&#243;n selar y causar complicaciones.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3825</data>
      <data key="d7">ec5c8edbba3c4aa78c5f03e4d2dac00a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULAS CAROT&#205;DEAS ARTERIOVENOSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Conexiones anormales entre las arterias y venas carot&#237;deas que pueden tener implicaciones cl&#237;nicas en la regi&#243;n selar.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3826</data>
      <data key="d7">8388c2295870416aba0b8bf3191a8cab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASAS SELARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las masas selares son lesiones que pueden encontrarse en la regi&#243;n de la silla turca, donde se localiza la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria, e incluyen tumores, quistes y otros procesos.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1344</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3827</data>
      <data key="d7">8dbac36594424decaa75e851364ebe6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE C&#201;LULAS GERMINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores de c&#233;lulas germinales son neoplasias que pueden aparecer en la regi&#243;n selar y son considerados malignos.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1344</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3828</data>
      <data key="d7">f282f237a2fd4b8ba5b7b750f645d27a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORDOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El cordoma es un tumor maligno que puede localizarse en la regi&#243;n selar y se origina de restos de la notocorda.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1344</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3829</data>
      <data key="d7">8bded11741d0459a96f90acdbc7f5b7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El carcinoma hipofisario es un tipo de tumor maligno que afecta la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria y es menos com&#250;n que los adenomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1344</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3830</data>
      <data key="d7">787176c377f74b23a25ebfc493177b8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LINFOMAS are a type of cancer characterized by malignant tumors that can metastasize to the pituitary gland, potentially affecting its function. Additionally, LINFOMAS can lead to adrenal insufficiency, highlighting their serious impact on the body's endocrine system.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
      <data key="d3">1491</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3831</data>
      <data key="d7">9db548cb5b2d493796ce40ed2c86e827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS ADENOHIPOFISARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las hormonas adenohipofisarias son producidas por la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria anterior y son cruciales para diversas funciones endocrinas.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3832</data>
      <data key="d7">167a531005dc4118890deef8223a4182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTORES DE TRANSCRIPCI&#211;N HIPOFISARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los factores de transcripci&#243;n hipofisarios son prote&#237;nas que regulan la expresi&#243;n de genes en las c&#233;lulas de la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3833</data>
      <data key="d7">becb96660ea2427094ad1b5c644760d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;NDICE KI67">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#237;ndice Ki67 es un marcador utilizado para evaluar la proliferaci&#243;n celular en tumores, incluyendo adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3834</data>
      <data key="d7">5f060d721db0412b9a419226ea548462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECUENTO DE MITOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El recuento de mitosis es una t&#233;cnica utilizada para evaluar la actividad proliferativa de los tumores, incluyendo los adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3835</data>
      <data key="d7">9b00adb3edb84290b373ae50c0086ba8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INVASI&#211;N TUMORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La invasi&#243;n tumoral se refiere a la capacidad de un tumor para infiltrarse en tejidos adyacentes, un aspecto importante en la evaluaci&#243;n de la agresividad de los adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3836</data>
      <data key="d7">fe4ef08b02144cf1ba09e8130e6692d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome MEN 1 es una neoplasia endocrina m&#250;ltiple que se asocia con adenomas hipofisarios y otros tumores endocrinos.</data>
      <data key="d2">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3837</data>
      <data key="d7">17eeaa74da1b4d24abd09115b67a93be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER DE MAMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El c&#225;ncer de mama puede dar met&#225;stasis en la hip&#243;fisis, afectando su funci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3838</data>
      <data key="d7">257641e4cbcf41c9a7e00daaf52fbce3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FGF-4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El FGF-4 es un receptor del factor de crecimiento que puede estar alterado en algunos adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3839</data>
      <data key="d7">36e7789f8c004af3a420f55bd41ee719</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERTENSI&#211;N INTRACRANEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipertensi&#243;n intracraneal puede ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado a tumores en el &#225;rea selar, como los adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d3">1341</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3840</data>
      <data key="d7">96e50be2d1664af6a6409062495445c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormonas refers to a group of various hormones tested in patients, including insulin, glucagon, and serotonin. These hormones are chemical messengers produced by glands in the body that play a crucial role in regulating a wide array of physiological processes, such as growth, metabolism, reproduction, mood, and the body's response to stress. They are essential for coordinating activities like lipid metabolism and maintaining cardiovascular health, as well as regulating water and electrolyte balance.

Hormones can be significantly affected by conditions such as pituitary adenomas, which may lead to clinical alterations. Additionally, they are involved in treatments for gender affirmation, including the use of estrogen and anti-androgens. Specific hormones, such as testosterone, are vital in treating conditions like hypogonadism, while others, like estrogens and androgens, are important for bone mass regulation and can influence the risk of osteoporosis. Overall, hormones are regulatory substances that are integral to maintaining homeostasis and overall health in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,473502714ce73073f93b598ca0edcc21,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f,764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">3841</data>
      <data key="d7">09fd04f2046c46db879f7f215beb26ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLEJO DE CARNEY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El complejo de Carney es un s&#237;ndrome raro de endoplasia endocrina m&#250;ltiple que se hereda de forma autos&#243;mica dominante, asociado a mutaciones en el gen PRKAR1A y caracterizado por lesiones pigmentadas cut&#225;neas y tumores mixomatosos.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1325</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3842</data>
      <data key="d7">df3e4181f72649b38056815b71552bda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRKAR1A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El gen PRKAR1A codifica para una subunidad reguladora de la prote&#237;na cinasa A y est&#225; relacionado con el complejo de Carney.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1325</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3843</data>
      <data key="d7">0127ad43ec1140be98eb42222294b335</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CTNNB1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El gen CTNNB1 codifica la &#946;-catenina y puede estar relacionado con la formaci&#243;n de craneofaringiomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1346</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3844</data>
      <data key="d7">71b74e367a1047008de12e622049d33b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRAF">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BRAF is a gene that can be associated with the formation of craniopharyngiomas through V600E mutations. This oncogene is frequently mutated in papillary craniopharyngiomas, which predominantly occur in adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab,640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d3">1346</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3845</data>
      <data key="d7">433c211658c84b5b808f828d50fe3f57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPLASIA HIPOFISARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hiperplasia hipofisaria se define como un aumento en el volumen y contenido celular de la hip&#243;fisis, que puede ocurrir en situaciones como el embarazo y el hipotiroidismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3846</data>
      <data key="d7">ceb8e482b1a442c9b228f2889f635666</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEVUS AZUL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El nevus azul es una lesi&#243;n pigmentada cut&#225;nea asociada con el complejo de Carney.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3847</data>
      <data key="d7">2c86e1437cd74ff590f41747cfd0eff8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LENTIGOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los lentigos son lesiones pigmentadas cut&#225;neas que tambi&#233;n se asocian con el complejo de Carney.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3848</data>
      <data key="d7">694a2566e3aa47e79236e20ab34e785b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES MIXOMATOSOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores mixomatosos son un tipo de tumor que puede aparecer en el contexto del complejo de Carney, afectando el coraz&#243;n, la piel o la mama.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3849</data>
      <data key="d7">c35f9296614741428ddf9d6f621b2f69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE C&#201;LULAS DE SERTOLI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores de c&#233;lulas de Sertoli son un tipo de tumor endocrino que puede estar relacionado con el complejo de Carney.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3850</data>
      <data key="d7">6e5e3f04ff1b4a0395f0e215875b30e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE C&#201;LULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores de c&#233;lulas de Leydig son otro tipo de tumor endocrino que puede estar relacionado con el complejo de Carney.</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3851</data>
      <data key="d7">6d85ba584a3c4bb1822d7ccb723853f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES TIROIDEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores tiroideos son alteraciones endocrinol&#243;gicas que pueden asociarse con el complejo de Carney.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">39838811d935b8d580e419ac87ef32ab</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3852</data>
      <data key="d7">39282c5e9c094b21ba6203dbe5d4bbaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CASTA&#209;O I ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Casta&#241;o I es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci&#243;n sobre adenomas hipofisarios y sus hallazgos moleculares.</data>
      <data key="d2">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d3">1346</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3853</data>
      <data key="d7">6afa9d31e6614a3ca98c07b5b897d6bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARSH GR ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Harsh GR es un autor que ha escrito sobre craneofaringiomas y su tratamiento en la literatura m&#233;dica.</data>
      <data key="d2">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d3">1346</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3854</data>
      <data key="d7">c398e587c37048ba85446ef85d47837e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOFISITIS LINFOC&#205;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipofisitis linfoc&#237;tica es la forma m&#225;s frecuente de hipofisitis primaria, asociada a una etiolog&#237;a autoinmunitaria y que puede causar d&#233;ficits hormonales.</data>
      <data key="d2">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3855</data>
      <data key="d7">d35a00874c4e4b3f98c8655cbb5aafec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROADENOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MICROADENOMA refers to a small tumor of the pituitary gland, typically measuring less than 1 cm. It is often associated with the production of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) and is relevant in the context of thyroid hormone resistance. Microadenomas are more common in women and are frequently treated with surgical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">2261671ccad439da1ed9ea5a27857dc8,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3856</data>
      <data key="d7">bdef8d1bcda3455b9f535062884f43f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AULINAS A">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Aulinas A es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n que aborda la hipofisitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3857</data>
      <data key="d7">54ba9cec4ca24e13a7b1d9f363f73883</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WEBB S">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Webb S es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n que aborda la hipofisitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3858</data>
      <data key="d7">1f00cdfe3259404c942220a68375fb94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESMINI E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Resmini E es uno de los autores del Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n que aborda la hipofisitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3859</data>
      <data key="d7">7330898fbedc4f96960c68e36014fb14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEFAL&#201;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La cefalea es un s&#237;ntoma que puede presentarse de forma aguda en pacientes con hipofisitis, a menudo asociado con s&#237;ntomas compresivos.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3860</data>
      <data key="d7">024559e53d3b4172ae70ee057fbaeae3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS AUTOINMUNITARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las hormonas autoinmunitarias son marcadores que pueden estar presentes en pacientes con hipofisitis, indicando un proceso autoinmunitario.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3861</data>
      <data key="d7">e33286c290dc4e16b8fb4a5b420fbd05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RMN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RMN, or resonancia magn&#233;tica nuclear (magnetic resonance imaging), is a non-invasive medical imaging technique widely utilized for diagnostic purposes. It is particularly effective in evaluating various conditions, including pituitary disorders such as hipofisitis and pituitary tumors. Additionally, RMN is relevant in the assessment of adrenal tumors, as it provides detailed images that help characterize adrenal nodules and lesions. The technique has also been employed to suggest the presence of mucinous tumors and to detect metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma. Overall, RMN serves as a crucial tool in the diagnosis and characterization of a range of medical conditions, particularly those related to the endocrine system.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf,d6bea02011329ebf0fa64f4d6792d101,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3862</data>
      <data key="d7">f4cfa50f7b3d4314bef309e389493b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HALLAZGOS RADIOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los hallazgos radiol&#243;gicos son observaciones en im&#225;genes que pueden ayudar a diferenciar entre hipofisitis y adenomas hipofisarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3863</data>
      <data key="d7">a78d8fe4c06e4d8db5c7c18b4989270c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA HIPOFISARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La atrofia hipofisaria es una posible consecuencia evolutiva de la hipofisitis, donde el tejido normal es reemplazado por fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3864</data>
      <data key="d7">6db62b918b3d473fa2ba5b391332eeb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrosis is a pathological process characterized by the formation of scar tissue in various organs, which can significantly impair their function. In the context of the heart, fibrosis leads to alterations that affect its performance. Additionally, fibrosis can occur in conditions such as hypophysitis, where normal tissue is replaced by fibrous tissue, further illustrating the diverse implications of this process across different bodily systems.</data>
      <data key="d2">884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d3">1293</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3865</data>
      <data key="d7">e0894e641765482fa728a1ea7db2682e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROLACTINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prolactinoma is a type of pituitary tumor that produces an excessive amount of prolactin, leading to a condition known as hyperprolactinemia. This overproduction of prolactin can result in various clinical symptoms, including hypogonadism. The management of hyperprolactinemia is a central focus in addressing the effects of prolactinoma, highlighting its significance in both diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3866</data>
      <data key="d7">778dba3b30054d0e9ebc87c302a11cda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTORREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactorrea is defined as the abnormal flow of milk from the breast, which can occur in both men and women. This condition is often associated with elevated levels of prolactin, a hormone that can be indicative of various underlying health issues, such as Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). In medical terms, galactorrea is linked to hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by excessive prolactin in the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3867</data>
      <data key="d7">70a3dccbc3cf48c58c37127927779eb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPROLACTINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperprolactinemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. This condition can lead to various symptoms and health issues, including decreased libido, impotence, and infertility. Hyperprolactinemia may be caused by pituitary tumors or certain medications. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish, with the Spanish description emphasizing the same key points regarding its causes and symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">592f69a8890825d710e132d8e60f6d24,94acece2df038421a302ca1fa53d5275,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">18</data>
      <data key="d6">3868</data>
      <data key="d7">7012bb7c294f4db294cd008b0e8604e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA BRONCOG&#201;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El carcinoma broncog&#233;nico es un tipo de c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n que puede producir prolactina de manera ect&#243;pica, contribuyendo a la hiperprolactinemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3869</data>
      <data key="d7">48f868979fdc49cbb772259be6ab388a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIDEPRESIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los antidepresivos, que incluyen clases como los tric&#237;clicos y los inhibidores de la recaptaci&#243;n de serotonina, son medicamentos utilizados para tratar la depresi&#243;n y otros trastornos del estado de &#225;nimo. Sin embargo, uno de los efectos secundarios asociados con su uso es la hiperprolactinemia, una condici&#243;n caracterizada por niveles elevados de prolactina en la sangre.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3870</data>
      <data key="d7">e5b72f59c9a840ac8a62ac86fcd67f8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIPSIC&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los antipsic&#243;ticos, especialmente los de primera generaci&#243;n, son conocidos por inducir hiperprolactinemia debido a su efecto sobre la dopamina.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3871</data>
      <data key="d7">e18f967534934111bc7c39675acd5010</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGONISTAS DOPAMIN&#201;RGICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los agonistas dopamin&#233;rgicos son medicamentos utilizados en el tratamiento de los prolactinomas, ya que ayudan a reducir los niveles de prolactina.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3872</data>
      <data key="d7">7fc46af71fe648158b7bd6929d7df9da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIMETIDINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La cimetidina es un medicamento que puede causar hiperprolactinemia como efecto secundario, afectando la secreci&#243;n de prolactina.</data>
      <data key="d2">b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3873</data>
      <data key="d7">4468c89242f847cc80e2987b2824e54f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICONCEPTIVOS ORALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anticonceptivos orales are oral contraceptives that can have complex interactions with vitamin metabolism. Their use may lead to increased plasma concentrations of ceruloplasmin and copper in the body. Additionally, anticonceptivos orales can cause elevated levels of prolactin, which may contribute to hyperprolactinemia in some women.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,b157600f59e67793829a144ddaff24df,d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849</data>
      <data key="d3">27</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3874</data>
      <data key="d7">72270de56cb349efb66b16cdf972cd92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPROLACTINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperprolactinemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. This condition can arise from various causes, including pituitary tumors, certain medications, and other physiological conditions. It is noted that the patient's mother also has a history of hiperprolactinemia, which is associated with her health issues. Overall, hiperprolactinemia is a multifactorial condition that requires careful evaluation to determine its underlying causes and appropriate management.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740,b344a34a623d4ade6b3ed6e1adae0016,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1318</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">3875</data>
      <data key="d7">31437d1b87c74dfa9dbd433dc2d53e85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARMACOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Farmacos refers to drugs that are currently being tested for the treatment of obesity. Additionally, these medications are known to be a common cause of hyperprolactinemia, as they act on central aminergic pathways. Furthermore, Farmacos can also influence the outcomes of medical tests, particularly those related to blood detection in feces.</data>
      <data key="d2">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740</data>
      <data key="d3">1317</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3876</data>
      <data key="d7">4df6e2db022640f18316de4eeb1d5992</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES INFILTRATIVAS DEL HIPOT&#193;LAMO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades infiltrativas del hipot&#225;lamo, como la tuberculosis y la sarcoidosis, pueden afectar la producci&#243;n de prolactina.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740</data>
      <data key="d3">1318</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3877</data>
      <data key="d7">5537095cc2a146fd85fbbb40a4a458e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOTIROIDISMO PRIMARIO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El hipotiroidismo primario puede estar asociado con hiperprolactinemia y galactorrea.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740</data>
      <data key="d3">1318</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3878</data>
      <data key="d7">f9ca26bd3ad74d1d8580b6d399a5fc88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA ADRENAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenal insufficiency, known as "insuficiencia adrenal" in Spanish, is a medical condition characterized by the inadequate production of steroid hormones by the adrenal glands. This condition can also be associated with hyperprolactinemia, which is an elevated level of prolactin in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">984</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3879</data>
      <data key="d7">0df4538235184dc7960b784af076dc6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE OVARIO POLIQU&#205;STICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The S&#237;ndrome de Ovario Poliqu&#237;stico, commonly known as Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS), is a hormonal disorder prevalent among women of reproductive age, affecting approximately 6-15% of this population. This condition is characterized by a range of symptoms, including irregular menstrual periods, amenorrhea (the absence of menstruation), and hyperandrogenism, which can manifest as excess hair growth. 

PCOS is also associated with enlarged ovaries that contain small cysts on their outer edges. It is recognized as an endocrinopathy that can lead to anovulation, which is the failure to ovulate. Additionally, the syndrome can result in hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood.

Furthermore, women with PCOS are at an increased risk of developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2, highlighting the metabolic implications of the disorder. The syndrome is often discussed in the context of various hormonal and reproductive health issues, making it a significant concern in women's health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,401a6af689562ae0b9d7fe627eb56d0f,70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58,a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">18</data>
      <data key="d6">3880</data>
      <data key="d7">2abd041e972c4131bd390363d2a65350</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TORRES VELA E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Torres Vela E is a notable author in the field of endocrinology, recognized for their contributions to medical literature. They have authored a practical guide focused on the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly, a condition characterized by excessive growth hormone. Additionally, Torres Vela E is a contributor to the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n," a comprehensive resource that addresses various topics within endocrinology, including hyperprolactinemia and its treatment. Through these works, Torres Vela E has made significant strides in enhancing the understanding and management of endocrine disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
