    </node>
    <node id="CABERGOLINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cabergolina is a medication primarily used to treat hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of prolactin in the blood. It is particularly effective for patients with prolactinomas, which are benign tumors of the pituitary gland that produce excess prolactin. Additionally, Cabergolina functions as a dopamine agonist, which means it can stimulate dopamine receptors in the brain. This action allows it to inhibit the secretion of growth hormone, making it useful in cases where there is a mild elevation of insulin-like growth factor 1 (IGF-1). Overall, Cabergolina plays a significant role in managing hormonal imbalances related to prolactin and growth hormone levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608,a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1319</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3883</data>
      <data key="d7">22eb0279872a44c6a4c5b98176e02733</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACROPROLACTINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Macroprolactinoma is a larger type of prolactinoma, which is a specific kind of pituitary tumor that produces elevated levels of prolactin. This overproduction of prolactin can result in hyperprolactinemia, a condition characterized by various hormonal imbalances and associated symptoms. Due to the significant health issues that can arise from macroprolactinomas, they may necessitate surgical intervention to manage the condition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,592f69a8890825d710e132d8e60f6d24,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1318</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3884</data>
      <data key="d7">61464da814fc4426b970ee9da6f13e1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROPROLACTINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microprolactinoma is a small tumor of the pituitary gland that produces excess prolactin, which can significantly impact the patient's treatment options. It is a smaller variant of prolactinoma, a type of tumor that is more common and typically managed with medication.</data>
      <data key="d2">a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,b530539793a70d1223f3307aa47777fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1362</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">3885</data>
      <data key="d7">7017eac8db2842f79358c23e6a922328</data>
    </node>
    <node id="L&#211;PEZ MEZQUITA TORRES E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">L&#243;pez Mezquita Torres E is an author of the Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n, contributing to the field of endocrinology.</data>
      <data key="d2">a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3886</data>
      <data key="d7">da22fa68ef1d44ad94ba3f4c8891660c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IPILIMUMAB">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ipilimumab is a monoclonal antibody utilized in immunotherapy for the treatment of various tumors, notably melanoma and renal cell carcinoma. As an immune checkpoint inhibitor, it enhances the immune response against cancer cells. However, ipilimumab is associated with several adverse effects, the most common being hypophysitis, which can disrupt hormone levels, including prolactin. This condition may lead to secondary adrenal insufficiency due to its impact on the pituitary gland. Overall, ipilimumab plays a significant role in cancer treatment while also presenting risks of autoimmune reactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">40253f8b49d61452dbc56454cd1a07e0,592f69a8890825d710e132d8e60f6d24,84ebd4f784ceacfe0744f6bb9cd9a5a3,a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">1355</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3887</data>
      <data key="d7">e81f4fe7f31643b8b344eb6debd0c642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VERAPAMILO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Verapamil, also known as Verapamilo, is a calcium antagonist and calcium channel blocker primarily used in the treatment of high blood pressure and angina. It is recognized for its potential side effect of causing hyperprolactinemia, which can occur in up to 8.5% of users. Additionally, Verapamil is utilized in managing symptoms associated with late dumping syndrome. Overall, it serves multiple therapeutic purposes while also being linked to elevated prolactin levels in some patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,b344a34a623d4ade6b3ed6e1adae0016,d10d3648e8642657567d9a619f210ca6</data>
      <data key="d3">1418</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">3888</data>
      <data key="d7">f75a22acc88944a0b5fc061b05deea66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTANCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LACTANCIA refers to the process of breastfeeding, which involves feeding a baby with breast milk and has specific nutritional requirements for the mother. It encompasses various aspects, including dietary reference intakes tailored for the Spanish population, particularly focusing on infants and children. The term also highlights the importance of breastfeeding for individuals aged 14-18 years, who have unique dietary recommendations.

Breastfeeding is a critical concern for patients diagnosed with conditions such as microprolactinoma, as it can influence their nutritional needs and health. During the lactation period, which is when a mother produces milk for her infant, specific dietary recommendations are established for different age groups, including infants. These recommendations include defined nutrient intake levels and metrics for females under 18 years.

Additionally, lactation is evaluated for its impact on energy requirements, particularly during the first and second semesters of breastfeeding. It is important to note that lactation can be affected by certain medications, such as tiamazol and PTU, which are used to treat hyperthyroidism. Overall, LACTANCIA encompasses the multifaceted nature of breastfeeding, its nutritional implications, and the specific dietary guidelines that support both mothers and their children during this crucial period.</data>
      <data key="d2">135d72a9407315b8bbf5b1ac13d72abf,4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2,a1403e657780088123382f4725789e67,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6,b46fefa9f55d92c74acad101fc4f812e,bd31c6face847551241359e37e4baa2e,dad52b0e2f29edbe1c7e7e1fdee1d7cc</data>
