    <node id="PROLACTIN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Prolactin is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating milk production in mammals. Its levels can be influenced by various factors, including certain medications such as risperidone, which can lead to a condition known as hyperprolactinemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">592f69a8890825d710e132d8e60f6d24,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3892</data>
      <data key="d7">0f5ece0dcedd4cc1ba2294778f5344cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RISPERIDONE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Risperidone is an antipsychotic medication that can cause elevated prolactin levels, leading to hyperprolactinemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">592f69a8890825d710e132d8e60f6d24</data>
