    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO CON GH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El tratamiento con GH (hormona de crecimiento) es un enfoque terap&#233;utico para la talla baja y otras condiciones relacionadas con el crecimiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1359</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3933</data>
      <data key="d7">f80dd20143e5439aa0adf28c189f56b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE TURNER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El S&#237;ndrome de Turner es una alteraci&#243;n sexual cromos&#243;mica que afecta a las mujeres, caracterizada por la p&#233;rdida total o parcial del cromosoma X. Esta condici&#243;n gen&#233;tica se manifiesta con s&#237;ntomas como talla baja, insuficiencia gonadal, amenorrea primaria y diversas anomal&#237;as f&#237;sicas y hormonales. La prevalencia del s&#237;ndrome es de aproximadamente 1 por cada 2,000 a 2,500 reci&#233;n nacidas vivas. Adem&#225;s, el S&#237;ndrome de Turner puede estar asociado con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar enfermedades como la enfermedad cel&#237;aca. Es importante destacar que esta condici&#243;n puede requerir tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento (GH) para abordar algunas de sus complicaciones.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">23</data>
      <data key="d6">3934</data>
      <data key="d7">5392da3018f347f48cff76dc376e38c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE PRADER-WILLI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sindrome de Prader-Willi is a genetic disorder that affects growth and is also an approved indication for GH treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1359</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3935</data>
      <data key="d7">38425e69ca6d4e6d8716f565a09cc880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE NOONAN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sindrome de Noonan is a genetic disorder that can cause growth issues, but is not approved for GH treatment in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1359</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3936</data>
      <data key="d7">78328d5a703d442ba0d93300bdfd8417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALLA BAJA IDIOP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Talla baja idiop&#225;tica is a condition of short stature with no known cause, which is treated with GH in the United States but not in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1359</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3937</data>
      <data key="d7">a9f49d6acdb6415f9045f0a7b466584e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN SHOX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El gen SHOX est&#225; relacionado con el crecimiento y su alteraci&#243;n puede causar deficiencia de crecimiento, lo que puede ser tratado con GH.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1359</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3938</data>
      <data key="d7">f5906dbb7f2e49678ca82bfc7b1d6ca5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICRO-ADENOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Micro-adenomas are small tumors of the pituitary gland that can affect hormone production, relevant in the context of Cushing's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3939</data>
      <data key="d7">f560c1206117449a9f0aebbf9bc2ab97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACRO-ADENOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Macro-adenomas are larger tumors of the pituitary gland that can lead to excessive hormone production, significant in the context of Cushing's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3940</data>
      <data key="d7">8279c51aec574fef987842ba5c529206</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO," or Growth Hormone, is a hormone that plays a crucial role in stimulating growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration. It is utilized in various medical treatments, particularly for patients with growth deficiencies. In the context of critical care, growth hormone is mentioned as a potential treatment option for patients, including pediatric patients with extensive burns, to aid in their recovery. 

Research indicates that growth hormone can enhance magnesium absorption in the body. Additionally, while growth hormone treatment has been shown to increase muscle mass, the results regarding strength improvements have been inconsistent across different clinical trials. Overall, growth hormone is a significant therapeutic agent in both pediatric and critical care settings, aimed at promoting recovery and addressing growth-related issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,125acd19edb76fa23986de56fc2517e8,200447233341122a47f0010251600608,3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e,863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3941</data>
      <data key="d7">511880d0aafa4abfbcfd9d74c5e6f105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARTRALGIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Artralgias (Joint pain) are a common side effect associated with growth hormone treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3942</data>
      <data key="d7">fb4ce7da9a9c410d9596f041ddbb965d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GINECOMASTIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ginecomastia, also known as gynecomastia, is a medical condition characterized by the enlargement of breast tissue in males. This condition can arise due to various factors, including hormonal imbalances, and is often noted as a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment. Ginecomastia can occur in individuals with specific genetic conditions, such as Klinefelter syndrome and Wilson's disease, where hormonal imbalances are prevalent. Additionally, it can manifest during puberty as a natural developmental change. The condition may also be a side effect of testosterone therapy, leading to an increase in breast tissue. Overall, ginecomastia is a multifaceted condition that can result from a variety of hormonal influences and medical treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1,592d424edaa447a54ab4489d82495db6,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0,b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1298</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">3943</data>
      <data key="d7">9b505e469a514d07bf5815841da4a7f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERTENSI&#211;N INTRACRANEAL BENIGNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipertensi&#243;n intracraneal benigna (Benign Intracranial Hypertension) is a rare side effect of growth hormone treatment that can lead to increased pressure in the skull.</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3944</data>
      <data key="d7">2434f264734946cc91df6148fb1b3315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEVUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nevus (Mole) refers to a pigmented skin lesion that may increase in number, size, and pigmentation as a side effect of growth hormone treatment.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">b11e575be155e186717a992a9d641577</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3945</data>
      <data key="d7">44fcbf276e4146c7ba8132634dc256c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PEIN&#211; R.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Pein&#243; R. is the author of the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n," a comprehensive work that addresses growth hormone deficiency and its treatment. The manual covers this condition in both children and adults, providing valuable insights into its implications and management across different age groups.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3946</data>
      <data key="d7">9c1dfa5775094a4b86c22c0c767a9a7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GH RECOMBINANTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GH recombinante refers to the recombinant growth hormone used in medical treatments, which can have various side effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3947</data>
      <data key="d7">553bb489e333414cbaaf6dab4538651d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIT DE GH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deficit de GH refers to growth hormone deficiency, a medical condition that impacts growth and development in both children and adults. This condition is significant in the context of treatment and evaluation, as it can lead to various health issues if not addressed.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">3948</data>
      <data key="d7">2c9960b4d2a646c69495047a5e69a405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALLA BAJA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Talla Baja is a condition characterized by short stature, defined as height significantly below the average for a child's age and sex. This condition can occur as a long-term consequence in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0). Additionally, Talla Baja can manifest in patients with Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes (MELAS) due to hormonal deficiencies. Overall, Talla Baja encompasses various underlying causes and is an important consideration in the assessment of growth and development in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">3949</data>
      <data key="d7">8580121abf3843eab632dc53295ff4fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOMATOTROPINA HUMANA RECOMBINANTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Somatotropina humana recombinante is a synthetic form of human growth hormone used in medical treatments for growth hormone deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3950</data>
      <data key="d7">7a42128f425749868a0ce296863b26cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOMAL&#205;AS ESTRUCTURALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anomal&#237;as estructurales refer to structural anomalies that can accompany severe growth hormone deficiency in children.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3951</data>
      <data key="d7">16ddf712970f47a283a3e064fe5a0fe1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENSIDAD &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Densidad &#243;sea refers to the measure of bone strength and health, specifically indicating the amount of mineral content within a given volume of bone. This measurement can be influenced by various factors, including growth hormone levels. Techniques such as quantitative computed tomography are commonly used to evaluate densidad &#243;sea, providing insights into the overall condition of the bones.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3952</data>
      <data key="d7">480a250a9e6a4631911ce8811fee23b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASA MAGRA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Masa Magra refers to lean body mass, which is a critical factor in evaluating nutritional status and health outcomes in chronic diseases. It encompasses the amount of muscle and tissue in the body, and this composition can be influenced by various factors, including growth hormone treatment. Understanding Masa Magra is essential for assessing overall health and managing chronic conditions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f30de565a9a9acf7ac0930483276bbb,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3953</data>
      <data key="d7">1ce20ef5231641af9a04caba9394bb0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VELOCIDAD DE CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Velocidad de crecimiento is a measure of how quickly a child grows, which is important for assessing growth hormone deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3954</data>
      <data key="d7">2c2fa9d9bd634f52a708c2cd65464f3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALLA MEDIA PARENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Talla media parental is a reference height based on the average height of parents, used in assessing children's growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1</data>
      <data key="d3">1326</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3955</data>
      <data key="d7">065871fdeae74e0287e6f903826ea4fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFINICI&#211;N DE CRITERIOS AUXOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Definici&#243;n de criterios auxol&#243;gicos refers to the established guidelines for assessing growth and diagnosing growth disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">742d2991389effe376f335dad6fbafa1</data>
      <data key="d3">1345</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3956</data>
      <data key="d7">f55ea375b2534d4dbf4646083c7fbdac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE INTERRUPCI&#211;N DEL TALLA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de interrupci&#243;n del tallo hipofisario es una condici&#243;n que afecta la funci&#243;n de la hip&#243;fisis, a menudo resultando en deficiencias hormonales.</data>
      <data key="d2">9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3957</data>
      <data key="d7">4cdcbef1a8d74a9c99db182e60b002ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFARTO HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El infarto hipofisario es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que implica la muerte del tejido hipofisario, lo que puede resultar en deficiencias hormonales.</data>
      <data key="d2">9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3958</data>
      <data key="d7">21140a9bdc99423b9e7ab14ead3755df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMOCROMATOSIS HEREDITARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemochromatosis hereditaria is a genetic condition characterized by excessive iron absorption and accumulation in the body. This disorder can lead to various complications, including diabetes, which is commonly observed in symptomatic patients. Additionally, hereditary hemochromatosis may result in iron deposits in the pituitary gland, potentially affecting its function.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec,4885c129837f58f091d24d2cbc8aae66,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1519</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">3959</data>
      <data key="d7">cda0fab3e8b3460fa1ecc1d0b9c82e44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES NASOFAR&#205;NGEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores nasofar&#237;ngeos son crecimientos anormales en la nasofaringe que pueden afectar la hip&#243;fisis y causar deficiencias hormonales.</data>
      <data key="d2">9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3960</data>
      <data key="d7">fb007269bee54b5691503db21b3c764d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRAUMA CRANEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El trauma craneal puede da&#241;ar la hip&#243;fisis, resultando en problemas hormonales como el hipopituitarismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3961</data>
      <data key="d7">bbcb23efa87649bc93f028f955166dd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES CEREBRALES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">TUMORES CEREBRALES, or brain tumors, can significantly impact various bodily functions, including swallowing and digestion. This impairment may necessitate the use of enteral nutrition to ensure that affected individuals receive adequate nourishment.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32</data>
      <data key="d3">1323</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3962</data>
      <data key="d7">2712c3d2367d4882b5d5ee69474b3eb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PEGVISOMANT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pegvisomant is a growth hormone receptor antagonist used in the treatment of acromegaly, preventing the action of growth hormone but not its secretion.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3963</data>
      <data key="d7">fb53c74dbdab4b5ca4c8d9a6a4d86e04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KATZNELSON L">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Katznelson L is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding and treatment of acromegaly. He has played a vital role in developing clinical practice guidelines for the management of this condition, further establishing his expertise in the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295</data>
      <data key="d3">885</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">3964</data>
      <data key="d7">78da2fc585fa475295e2da5f1d2f4da9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LOGOS DE SOMATOSTATINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Somatostatin analogs are medications that inhibit the secretion of growth hormone and are used in the treatment of acromegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3965</data>
      <data key="d7">e6f266ce6c4d4ea9ac85f21dc9609c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORDIDO F ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cordido F et al. authored a practical guide for the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly published in Endocrinol Nutr in 2013.</data>
      <data key="d2">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">885</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3966</data>
      <data key="d7">d81be1af2c6144d0934e76e7322b1155</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIETY ESPA&#209;OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This professional organization plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and recommendations for the management of various conditions, including diabetes and acromegaly. In 2005, the society published a monograph that outlined evidence-based nutritional recommendations, further emphasizing its commitment to advancing knowledge in these areas. Overall, the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n focuses on the study and treatment of endocrine disorders, contributing significantly to the healthcare landscape in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">07a16ed299a7f8bafcaa44a54495a9c3,a4b144210b0a4b654a260ebc394de0af,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">885</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">3967</data>
      <data key="d7">1c51d648511b4c26ba24fe8141a6c22b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HO PJ ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ho PJ et al. conducted research on the regulation of pulsatile growth hormone secretion in normal subjects and patients with acromegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3968</data>
      <data key="d7">d96e9a8fe60546f49a60629b51eae688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KATZNELSON L ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Katznelson L et al. provided clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly published in J Clin Endocrinol Metab in 2014.</data>
      <data key="d2">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3969</data>
      <data key="d7">2826d412e9a44d1ab16879e86681c991</data>
    </node>
    <node id="X-LAG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">X-linked acrogigantism syndrome (X-LAG) is a condition characterized by early-onset gigantism due to genetic mutations.</data>
      <data key="d2">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3970</data>
      <data key="d7">c58abafe021045fd870a54394ce3187b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO SOMATOTROPO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3971</data>
      <data key="d7">0efb5730b5d44bfb8eb59c0242173063</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiovascular disease refers to a group of disorders affecting the heart and blood vessels. This condition encompasses a range of ailments that can be influenced by various factors, particularly dietary and lifestyle choices. Key dietary factors linked to cardiovascular disease include fat and sodium intake, as well as fiber and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, obesity and diabetes are significant risk factors associated with the prevalence of cardiovascular disease.

The condition can be exacerbated by testosterone treatment and is often discussed in relation to metabolic health. It is also noted that cardiovascular disease is associated with increased mortality in patients with acromegaly. Preventative measures for cardiovascular disease can include dietary modifications, such as adopting low-fat diets like the Ornish and Pritikin diets.

Overall, cardiovascular disease is a complex health issue that is influenced by a combination of dietary habits, lifestyle factors, and underlying health conditions, making it a critical area of study and intervention in public health.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6,06dcefb711cbd9fdb958145cca571b83,1566fcfef74295869c46405aaca05b32,25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda,2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,41d7db510fc74d3763959481cc15ea20,428616513e9e654c21ede19bd544ffbc,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,6a95bf35e698b03ca552f2c75d5d60ef,6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,bb2e69a0ff4c25a21149882162922c8d,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,dbdb3cd3b9065e8846fd2eb15b9d5879,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7,e271766bdc88e84209e5cdac4adc0724,ecd0e2cc6ed4a480591f4ac32cd7f691,f2b8b21255397ebbaf2b5d66ff6bde88,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de,fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">74</data>
      <data key="d6">3972</data>
      <data key="d7">a9be1224649845fd8b7a7e43e24dcae6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAL DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormonal disorders refer to conditions that result from an imbalance in hormone levels, which can lead to various health issues, including acromegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3973</data>
      <data key="d7">9d0dee816a3742c0a49c2bd27ba93ebe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACIONES ACTIVANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Activating mutations are genetic changes that lead to increased activity of certain proteins, such as those involved in hormone production, and are often implicated in conditions like acromegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">3974</data>
      <data key="d7">bd3a5dba5516439fb7fe6c594e4ceae4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperplasia refers to the increase in the number of cells in an organ or tissue, which can lead to overproduction of hormones, including growth hormone in the context of acromegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">3975</data>
      <data key="d7">ec75e49925734081afb48a0edc60743b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">McCune-Albright syndrome is a genetic disorder characterized by fibrous dysplasia of bone, skin pigmentation, and precocious puberty, often associated with hormonal imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d2">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d3">1322</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
