    <node id="MURAD MH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Murad MH is a multifaceted professional engaged in various aspects of medical research and clinical practice. He is notably involved in the development of clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma, as well as acromegaly. Additionally, Murad MH has contributed to the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline concerning the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric individuals, demonstrating his commitment to advancing care in this area.

In the realm of obesity research, Murad MH has conducted systematic reviews of obesity treatments and has studied the effects of pharmacological interventions for obesity. His work reflects a dedication to improving treatment options and outcomes for patients dealing with obesity and related endocrine disorders. Overall, Murad MH's contributions span both clinical guidelines and research, highlighting his significant role in the field of endocrinology.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295</data>
