    <node id="DESMOPRESINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Desmopresina is a synthetic medication that serves multiple purposes in the medical field. Primarily, it is used in the treatment of diabetes insipidus, especially in its central form, where there is a deficiency of the antidiuretic hormone (ADH). Additionally, Desmopresina plays a role in managing sodium levels, particularly in conjunction with tolvapt&#225;n, when sodium levels rise too quickly. It is also utilized in the diagnosis and treatment of conditions related to ADH deficiency and is effective in managing hyponatremia. Overall, Desmopresina is a versatile medication that addresses both the symptoms of diabetes insipidus and the complications associated with sodium imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4000</data>
      <data key="d7">66ee59dcc1d04042944a83436de6eb26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEST DE LA SED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The test of the sed is a diagnostic procedure used to differentiate types of diabetes ins&#237;pida based on urine concentration responses.</data>
      <data key="d2">afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4001</data>
      <data key="d7">fd9eaf8bb38e4b2699a057cbd5de65d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA ANTIDIUR&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "HORMONA ANTIDIUR&#201;TICA," also known as antidiuretic hormone (ADH) or vasopressin, is a crucial hormone that regulates water retention and balance in the body. Its levels can be influenced by various conditions, including adrenal insufficiency. ADH plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of diabetes ins&#237;pida, a condition characterized by excessive thirst and urination due to insufficient levels of this hormone. Additionally, it is involved in the pathophysiology of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), where excessive release of ADH leads to water retention and dilutional hyponatremia.

The hormone is particularly relevant in the context of patients undergoing nutritional support, as it affects water balance and can influence electrolyte levels, including magnesium. Overall, the "HORMONA ANTIDIUR&#201;TICA" is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body's water levels and is a key factor in various medical conditions related to fluid regulation.</data>
      <data key="d2">473502714ce73073f93b598ca0edcc21,addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce,afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da,cff2f16dff598dbf0bff544091c77837,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4002</data>
      <data key="d7">93a1cc0c949149aaba9934a10478b715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">POLIURIA is a medical condition characterized by excessive urination, which involves the production of abnormally large volumes of dilute urine. This condition can be a symptom of various underlying health issues, most notably uncontrolled diabetes due to high blood sugar levels. Additionally, POLIURIA is often associated with diabetes ins&#237;pida, a specific type of diabetes that affects the body's ability to regulate water balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d3">899</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4003</data>
      <data key="d7">c8374c1ae2334d248ef224d58e6b8e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIDIPSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polydipsia is a condition characterized by excessive thirst, which is commonly observed in individuals experiencing hyperglycemia. This condition typically arises in response to dehydration or elevated blood sugar levels, and it is often associated with diabetes insipidus. In essence, polydipsia occurs as the body attempts to compensate for fluid loss resulting from high blood sugar levels, particularly in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582,cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d3">899</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4004</data>
      <data key="d7">188d778b9819455ba46db65df66d1c18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSMOLARIDAD URINARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urinary osmolarity is a measure of the concentration of solutes in urine, used in the diagnosis of diabetes ins&#237;pida.</data>
      <data key="d2">afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4005</data>
      <data key="d7">9f273c3b1e8e4d51a244effe01dcda24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSMOLALIDAD PLASM&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osmolalidad plasm&#225;tica refers to the concentration of solutes in the blood plasma, which is crucial for diagnosing various types of hyponatremia. It serves as a measure of the body's electrolyte-water balance and plays a significant role in diagnosing conditions such as diabetes ins&#237;pida.</data>
      <data key="d2">afb4fa63fc94607d1545407e79240295,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
