    </node>
    <node id="POLIDIPSIA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polidipsia primaria es un trastorno que se caracteriza por la sed excesiva y la ingesta de grandes cantidades de agua. Esta condici&#243;n puede resultar en una diluci&#243;n de la orina, lo que implica que el cuerpo est&#225; consumiendo m&#225;s l&#237;quidos de lo que necesita, afectando as&#237; el equilibrio h&#237;drico del organismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37,d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1424</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4009</data>
      <data key="d7">2dce774fa429494c9353edad9fad9046</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La diabetes ins&#237;pida central es un tipo de diabetes ins&#237;pida que resulta de la falta de producci&#243;n de ADH por la hip&#243;fisis, lo que lleva a una incapacidad para concentrar la orina.</data>
      <data key="d2">67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4010</data>
      <data key="d7">b590a25fb99140108dddd7ae899c89c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA NEFROG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La diabetes ins&#237;pida nefrog&#233;nica es un tipo de diabetes ins&#237;pida que ocurre cuando los ri&#241;ones no responden adecuadamente a la ADH, resultando en una incapacidad para concentrar la orina.</data>
      <data key="d2">67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4011</data>
      <data key="d7">b7a860f89316487f82c74dad1aaa68db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADH">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">ADH, or Antidiuretic Hormone, is a nonapeptide hormone synthesized in the hypothalamus that plays a crucial role in regulating water balance and sodium levels in the body. It helps control the amount of water reabsorbed by the kidneys, thereby regulating water retention. ADH is particularly significant in the context of conditions such as hyponatremia and the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), where its levels can be altered. Additionally, the secretion of ADH can be affected in individuals with eating disorders, highlighting its importance in various physiological and pathological states. Overall, ADH is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body's water balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">4012</data>
      <data key="d7">63d6f2b0739040f6ac4d6d387aa22009</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUERTE CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Muerte cerebral refers to a state of irreversible loss of all brain functions, often leading to complications such as diabetes ins&#237;pida neurog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4013</data>
      <data key="d7">30b75e1624d14377a0e453bd07647086</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOFISITIS IGG4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipofisitis IgG4 is a rare autoimmune condition affecting the pituitary gland, characterized by inflammation and often presenting with diabetes ins&#237;pida and other symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">321</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4014</data>
      <data key="d7">1886b832e9bc4a7f851afe4b5ea4b7ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD RELACIONADA CON LA IGG4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad relacionada con la IgG4 is a systemic autoimmune disease that can manifest with various symptoms, including those affecting the pituitary gland.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">321</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4015</data>
      <data key="d7">012bcef38c6b4eec8ad7eff879f92b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGLICEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOGLICEMIA refers to a condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels, known as hypoglycemia. This condition can arise in various medical situations and is particularly noted as a potential complication in patients with pituitary disorders. Hypoglycemia can occur in a range of medical conditions, highlighting its significance in clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1,c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1091</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4016</data>
      <data key="d7">44e8d6fbe69d41c694265e7d7b5714bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIADH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH) is a medical condition characterized by the excessive release of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) without an appropriate physiological stimulus. This abnormal secretion leads to water retention in the body, resulting in euvolemic hyponatremia, a condition where sodium levels in the blood become dangerously low despite normal blood volume. SIADH is responsible for approximately 95% of hyponatremia cases in hospitalized patients.

The condition can manifest in various forms, including ectopic or eutopic secretion, and is often associated with several diseases and conditions that affect the hypothalamic-pituitary axis. It may also occur following pituitary surgery. Management of SIADH is crucial, as it requires careful monitoring and regulation of sodium levels to prevent complications associated with hyponatremia. The syndrome is discussed in medical literature, including the "Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n," highlighting its significance in clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ceaa92ed88d3f829122e1554f2e7277,22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7,2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86,c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf,d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">62</data>
      <data key="d6">4017</data>
      <data key="d7">1a3e46983aed49dc8436cdfb4dac91ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULA DE FURST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#243;rmula de Furst is a calculation used to assess a patient's ability to excrete free water, guiding fluid restriction in conditions like SIADH.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4018</data>
      <data key="d7">00ceec6ed40b490180092cc7355c8fbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iones refer to charged particles that are monitored in patients with diabetes ins&#237;pida and SIADH to manage electrolyte balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4019</data>
      <data key="d7">7de61035413a4dd29c32b413e267cc31</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PITUITARIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Pituitaria refers to the pituitary gland, which is central to the discussion of conditions like hipofisitis and diabetes ins&#237;pida.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d3">321</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4020</data>
      <data key="d7">512e358865a240c6a98655e6716898c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAHERA VARGAS M.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Lahera Vargas M. is an author of a chapter in the Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n regarding primary hyperaldosteronism.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4021</data>
      <data key="d7">7de9f6fb5ccf4c638e98e3b8d7cb5b8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VILLABONA C.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Villabona C. is an author of a chapter in the Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n regarding the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH).</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1457</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4022</data>
      <data key="d7">9928886157b7483ab0b17598e3faa8f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOLVAPT&#193;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tolvapt&#225;n is a medication primarily used to treat hyponatremia, particularly in patients with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). It functions by blocking the action of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) in the kidneys, specifically targeting the V2 receptor, which promotes water excretion and induces aquaresis. This mechanism helps to manage sodium levels in patients by facilitating the elimination of excess water from the body.

Tolvapt&#225;n can be administered in specific dosages, either orally or via nasogastric tube, depending on the patient's nutritional status. It is particularly beneficial for patients experiencing low sodium levels in the blood, including those with heart failure. Overall, tolvapt&#225;n serves as a selective vasopressin receptor antagonist that effectively addresses euvolemic hyponatremia by promoting water excretion and helping to restore normal sodium levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd,306519cca8810e0ff1c973128a75200a,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">4023</data>
      <data key="d7">11e270936a9245bc9d491901d0d8abb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">T&#237;a refers to thiazide diuretics, which are mentioned as part of the treatment for nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
