    </node>
    <node id="AINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AINE refers to non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, which are mentioned in the context of treating hyperaldosteronism.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1492</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4026</data>
      <data key="d7">ca624703dd784f5fabb63034e2b62f90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUOXETINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fluoxetina, also known as fluoxetine, is a medication primarily used as an antidepressant. It is prescribed as part of treatment plans for various conditions, including depression and eating disorders. Fluoxetina has been studied for its effectiveness in reducing binge eating and purging behaviors in patients with eating disorders. Additionally, it is noted that fluoxetine can increase appetite in some individuals. However, it is important to be aware that fluoxetine may lead to the development of Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), particularly in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4027</data>
      <data key="d7">18b2c8c8873d4d9185d65f56b7a79a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLORPROPAMIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Clorpropamida is a medication that can cause SIADH</data>
      <data key="d2">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4028</data>
      <data key="d7">38b30f3364d743f1a32b05fb5a268f49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARBAMACEPINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Carbamacepina, also known as carbamazepine, is an anticonvulsant medication primarily used to manage seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia. In addition to its anticonvulsant properties, carbamazepine can influence the metabolism of thyroid hormones, which requires monitoring of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels in patients who are hypothyroid. Furthermore, carbamazepine has been associated with the development of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), which can impact the duration of treatment. Overall, carbamazepine is a critical medication in seizure management, but it necessitates careful monitoring due to its effects on thyroid function and potential to induce SIADH.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,be2de576112f22070e8ef8a5cb9e1017</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4029</data>
      <data key="d7">70d1340701174183831fce6ca666dcac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER PULMONAR DE C&#201;LULAS PEQUE&#209;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Small cell lung cancer is a type of cancer that can cause ectopic production of vasopressin leading to SIADH</data>
      <data key="d2">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4030</data>
      <data key="d7">7b206ca7089f4a538ea6524572e1036f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR OBSTRUCTIVA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (EPOC), known in Spanish as Enfermedad Pulmonar Obstructiva Cr&#243;nica, is a progressive lung condition that encompasses diseases such as emphysema and chronic bronchitis. This condition is characterized by obstructed airflow, which leads to difficulties in breathing. EPOC can also be associated with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it is a chronic respiratory illness that requires tailored nutritional interventions, as it can lead to malnutrition and other health complications. Overall, EPOC significantly impacts respiratory function and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6,7e539a13a598e4ff2d2d4d6641a044d5,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977</data>
      <data key="d3">1037</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4031</data>
      <data key="d7">26745b1d425b4a07a188cd34467cfe90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUERO HIPERT&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertonic saline is a treatment used to rapidly increase sodium levels in patients with severe hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d2">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
