    <node id="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipertensi&#243;n Arterial, or high blood pressure, is a medical condition characterized by a systolic blood pressure (PAS) of 140 mmHg or higher, or a diastolic blood pressure (PAD) of 90 mmHg or higher. It is a chronic condition that can develop due to poor nutrition and lifestyle choices, particularly in children. The condition is associated with elevated blood pressure levels, which can be influenced by sodium intake and is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular diseases.

Management of Hipertensi&#243;n Arterial often involves dietary controls, particularly regarding sodium and potassium consumption. It is also recognized as a risk factor for chronic kidney disease and can complicate the management of phosphorus levels. Furthermore, hypertension is linked to the development of Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 and is often addressed through dietary interventions aimed at reducing cardiovascular risk.

While some studies have explored the relationship between fish consumption and the incidence of hypertension, findings have been contradictory, indicating that more research is needed to clarify this association. Overall, Hipertensi&#243;n Arterial is a critical health concern that requires attention to diet and lifestyle to mitigate its risks and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb,66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,b6c8d5ff1536806d6512fb9d1af1e6db,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d3">626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">4102</data>
      <data key="d7">4b578d09b0714e07ba0b59c057ad2533</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal levels of lipids in the blood. This condition can manifest in various forms, including mild cases in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0) and more pronounced forms such as hypertriglyceridemia in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII). Dyslipidemia is commonly observed in individuals undergoing dietary treatment and is influenced by diet and lifestyle choices.

The condition is significant as it increases the risk of cardiovascular diseases, which are responsible for millions of deaths annually. Dyslipidemia is often associated with obesity and is prevalent among patients with diabetes, contributing to the overall risk of developing cardiovascular disease and Diabetes Mellitus Type 2. Effective management of dyslipidemia typically requires tailored dietary interventions and treatment strategies aimed at controlling cholesterol levels to mitigate these health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141,34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,55aabc274c460459322072406f17d52c,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8,ecd0e2cc6ed4a480591f4ac32cd7f691,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">1487</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">21</data>
      <data key="d6">4103</data>
      <data key="d7">879a93e7063e4be5bcf10571d2777c84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEDENTARISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sedentarismo, or physical inactivity, is identified as a significant risk factor for various health issues, including cardiovascular disease and the development of Diabetes Mellitus Type 2. To mitigate these risks, regular physical activity is strongly recommended. Engaging in consistent exercise can help counteract the negative effects associated with a sedentary lifestyle, promoting overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d3">1604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4104</data>
      <data key="d7">7c356c5a43d843d681082bee7aee4efe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTORIA PREVIA DE DIABETES GESTACIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A previous history of gestational diabetes is a significant risk factor for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad</data>
      <data key="d3">1602</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4105</data>
      <data key="d7">89c2067fe46445beaed1968cf0893c9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFROAMERICANOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Afroamericans are a demographic group characterized by a higher prevalence of hypertension, which occurs more frequently and at an earlier age compared to Caucasians. Additionally, they have a lower prevalence of hereditary fructose intolerance, with an estimated occurrence of 1 in 200,000 individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">34d62296f09da1a452febcc9ab8c18ad,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950</data>
      <data key="d3">626</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4106</data>
      <data key="d7">c21a20ab3f8a4a1cb77383d620d29efe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MODY (Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young) is a form of diabetes caused by genetic mutations affecting insulin production, characterized by different subtypes with varying clinical features and treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">989</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4107</data>
      <data key="d7">7920e72474ad4bb69b506552f45bd2b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HAPO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HAPO (Hyperglycemia and Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes) is a study that established criteria for diagnosing gestational diabetes based on glucose levels during an oral glucose tolerance test.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">883</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4108</data>
      <data key="d7">e5ad70054e0b420291433077d9181484</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINAGLIPTINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Linagliptina is a medication specifically designed for the treatment of type 2 diabetes. It functions by increasing insulin production and decreasing glucose production in the liver, thereby helping to manage blood sugar levels effectively. Notably, Linagliptina does not require dose adjustment in patients with severe renal impairment, making it a suitable option for individuals with compromised kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d2">630ac8fefe27e4b893831674a67dcc82,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4109</data>
      <data key="d7">731f6a89ee384a119a24d1003caa256e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFONILUREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfonylureas are a class of medications that serve dual purposes in diabetes management. They are primarily used to treat Type 2 diabetes by stimulating insulin release from the pancreas, thereby helping to lower blood sugar levels. Additionally, sulfonylureas are also utilized in the treatment of certain cases of neonatal diabetes, where they target ATP-dependent potassium channels to regulate insulin secretion. This versatility makes sulfonylureas an important option in the pharmacological management of diabetes across different age groups and types of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac89fcaa7dcce835c0d5b9ed9ce94cea,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4110</data>
      <data key="d7">da2df214d7c9405c8062729ccb65238e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS DE EMPRESA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Company analysis refers to the evaluation of blood glucose levels and other health metrics to diagnose diabetes or prediabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">1600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4111</data>
      <data key="d7">279b5369c4544297a205c20fce05fa71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CURVA CON 75 G DE GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The 75g glucose curve test is a diagnostic procedure used to confirm diabetes by measuring blood glucose levels at intervals after consuming a glucose solution.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">883</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4112</data>
      <data key="d7">03ae1d3057784358b1c4a64b4b597536</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES GESTACIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes gestacional is a specific type of diabetes that develops during pregnancy, typically characterized by elevated blood sugar levels. This condition necessitates careful monitoring and management to safeguard the health of both the mother and the baby. Diagnosis usually involves specific screening conducted between the 24th and 28th weeks of gestation. Women with obesity are particularly at risk for developing gestational diabetes. Overall, effective management is crucial to mitigate potential complications associated with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4,4c37affdd97e7772d1ea27aee34533b8,6a2d5ced0ad16871fec539845797e0ac,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">883</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">4113</data>
      <data key="d7">a0d83501511b4d25b28cc3c65878abe4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HNF-4&#913;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HNF-4&#945; (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 4 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY type 1, which affects insulin secretion.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">989</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4114</data>
      <data key="d7">7f37396123e942d28d223ce6c31c87ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOKINASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucokinase is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism, particularly within the &#946;-cells of the pancreas, where it stimulates insulin secretion. Additionally, glucokinase is associated with maturity onset diabetes of the young (MODY) type 2, highlighting its importance in both normal metabolic processes and in certain genetic forms of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89,fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">989</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4115</data>
      <data key="d7">9e585f6e5fe94f6ba22dbb8f85a39ee5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HNF-1&#914;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HNF-1&#946; (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Beta) is a gene that plays a significant role in the development of MODY type 5 (Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young type 5). This genetic condition is associated with complications affecting both the kidneys and the pancreas. HNF-1&#946; is particularly important in the regulation and secretion of insulin, which is crucial for maintaining normal glucose levels in the body. Thus, mutations or dysfunctions in the HNF-1&#946; gene can lead to diabetes and related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4116</data>
      <data key="d7">99607c138d75404d9677667433d96438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HNF-1&#913;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HNF-1&#945; (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY type 3, which is linked to microvascular complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">989</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4117</data>
      <data key="d7">5e2b330558b7495c98fcd006824b632c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IPF-1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">IPF-1 (Insulin Promoter Factor 1) is a gene associated with MODY type 4, which can lead to pancreatic agenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">989</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4118</data>
      <data key="d7">3fedacdc967240a88ccbde24a67faf88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes tipo 2 is a chronic medical condition that has affected the patient for 12 years, primarily associated with obesity and challenges in glucose control. This condition significantly impacts how the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and is characterized by insulin resistance and elevated blood sugar levels. It is often linked to various lifestyle factors, including dietary habits such as the consumption of sugary beverages and trans fats, as well as the intake of fiber and whole grains, which may help reduce the risk of developing the disease.

Diabetes tipo 2 is prevalent in Spain and poses a considerable burden on healthcare resources and costs. It is also associated with an increased risk of complications, including cardiovascular disease and uric acid stone formation. The condition can be treated with medications such as liraglutide and may require insulin in some cases. Additionally, diabetes tipo 2 is related to metabolic syndrome and has shown an inverse association with vitamin D levels.

The rising prevalence of diabetes tipo 2, particularly among older populations, highlights the importance of addressing lifestyle factors and dietary choices to manage and potentially prevent this condition. Furthermore, it is considered in the context of metabolic surgery for obese patients and is often discussed in relation to low-carbohydrate diets and very low-calorie diets (VLCD). Overall, diabetes tipo 2 is a complex metabolic disorder that necessitates a comprehensive approach to treatment and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">201f8e6a0d6c49396cf9c81f5da4520f,3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4,445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce,65e3dfcb7a0c5a2a09a98342c597c020,72d0be9d03c79097f867a8af2e3e89e4,7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0,880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831,f558c372d16630f14b614e232fc151de,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">23</data>
      <data key="d6">4119</data>
      <data key="d7">9abf4708bc624c19aaf250d299c262ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AN&#193;LISIS refers to a comprehensive medical evaluation process that encompasses various assessments related to health metrics. This includes the analysis of blood glucose levels and other health indicators to diagnose conditions such as diabetes or prediabetes. Additionally, AN&#193;LISIS involves conducting medical tests to evaluate hormone levels and other physiological parameters, particularly in the context of precocious puberty. Furthermore, it encompasses the analytical monitoring of patients with chronic diseases, which is recommended to be performed annually or as clinically indicated. Overall, AN&#193;LISIS plays a crucial role in the diagnosis and management of various health conditions through systematic evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d2">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,cf8a6f1b6d59546ed7bd297d032f6b30,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
