      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4120</data>
      <data key="d7">5f8e133bbacb47138018d0134cf5de32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRCUITO DE GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The glucose circuit refers to the metabolic pathway through which glucose is processed in the body, crucial for understanding diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4121</data>
      <data key="d7">6c791623c8554b55ac610196b8bfda3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES MICROVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microvascular complications are health issues that arise from damage to small blood vessels, commonly associated with poorly managed diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4122</data>
      <data key="d7">e8db9eaef63442f3ba698b172ffc5dc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "TRATAMIENTO" encompasses a variety of medical interventions aimed at improving patient health across different conditions. In the case of classical galactosemia, treatment involves the strict elimination of galactose from the diet starting from the first days of life. For oncology patients, treatment may include a combination of radiotherapy, chemotherapy, and surgery, all of which can significantly impact nutritional status. Additionally, treatment for allergies and food intolerances often requires the removal of specific foods from the diet and the management of associated symptoms. 

Furthermore, treatment is a broad term that refers to the medical care provided to patients, which necessitates informed consent. It also includes various methods to manage and alleviate symptoms of inflammatory bowel disease, as well as medical interventions for conditions such as hyponatremia. In the context of diabetes management, treatment involves lifestyle modifications, medications, and insulin therapy. Overall, "TRATAMIENTO" signifies a comprehensive approach to healthcare that addresses a wide range of medical conditions through tailored interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,9934fdd98a0d66fb3ff7ac1b56b18460,a519216aaee7bf8a1317f5d6b522c4b6,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4123</data>
      <data key="d7">36ba1b5a0e2540a09e2988971812b462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MODY 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes MODY 1 is a form of monogenic diabetes that is not usually associated with macrovascular complications but has an increased risk of microvascular complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">865</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4124</data>
      <data key="d7">e7e768c1c2524969b7cd736784969858</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MODY 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes MODY 2 is characterized by mild and stable hyperglycemia, often manageable with diet, and typically does not present symptoms of hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">865</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4125</data>
      <data key="d7">96cbedffb20a4d26a219bf0124d5a195</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MODY 3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes MODY 3 is characterized by a progressive secretory defect, typically presenting hyperglycemia in childhood or adolescence, and may require insulin treatment as the defect progresses.</data>
      <data key="d2">f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">879</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4126</data>
      <data key="d7">c3dcf96c5fa949b395e0d07409c3e849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MODY 5">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes MODY 5 can be associated with renal dysplasia, cysts, and renal failure, and may require insulin treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">867</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4127</data>
      <data key="d7">b87eba5b55fe4f34bf76d64ab0f97894</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFONYLUREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfonylureas are a class of oral medications primarily used in the treatment of Type 2 diabetes. They function by stimulating insulin secretion from the pancreatic beta cells, thereby increasing insulin production from the pancreas. This mechanism helps to manage blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">06fe3811ad957d6841997b2a0e9be50f,265fcc321b2c0bbf0bf8200d0489e1a1,f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">879</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4128</data>
      <data key="d7">fefd6962d1254fc39e1b028cd399459d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULIN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulin is a vital hormone produced by the pancreas that plays a crucial role in regulating glucose levels in the blood. It is primarily used in the treatment of diabetes, particularly for managing blood glucose levels and addressing hyperglycemic crises. Insulin lowers blood sugar levels and is essential for glucose metabolism, as well as the metabolism of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins.

In diabetes management, insulin is often administered to maintain glycemic control, especially in cases of severe hyperglycemia or progressive secretory defects. The dosage and administration of insulin are typically adjusted based on the individual patient's needs. Additionally, it is important to note that insulin's hypoglycemic effects can be potentiated by alcohol consumption.

In specific populations, such as patients with Anorexia Nervosa, insulin levels may be appropriately low, and their sensitivity to insulin remains normal. Furthermore, insulin may be administered as necessary during dietary management for patients with various metabolic disorders. Overall, insulin is a critical component in the effective management of diabetes and related metabolic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">06fe3811ad957d6841997b2a0e9be50f,1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,4351677d6166c9c88ab941dc8dcecb82,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc,50fafa000d5f2830cbf66f3201657396,5b487245068b8e8b87ffcc04970aaff4,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,7a6970183393c5ef1adc99851ef3eada,7b084f7afc5f3c66a528475ae4fa76b1,bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582,c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82,cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034,eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381,f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d,fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1713</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">4129</data>
      <data key="d7">0cdff859d3b3477189bb609018e62de5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RENAL DYSPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Renal dysplasia is a developmental disorder of the kidneys that can be associated with diabetes MODY 5, leading to complications such as renal failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">867</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4130</data>
      <data key="d7">8e40c2e2d84c4e8792438bb7f2761669</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KCNJ11">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">KCNJ11 is a gene that encodes a potassium channel that plays a crucial role in the regulation of insulin secretion. Mutations in this gene can lead to conditions such as hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia and neonatal diabetes. Additionally, KCNJ11 is associated with various types of diabetes, particularly those that involve the functioning of potassium channels.</data>
      <data key="d2">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b,f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4131</data>
      <data key="d7">6fa59a2d16a642259c3bb07e28f6fdcf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABCC8">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">ABCC8 is a gene that encodes a protein crucial for the regulation of insulin secretion. It is associated with various types of diabetes, particularly those that affect ATP-sensitive potassium channels. Specifically, ABCC8 encodes a subunit of these channels, and mutations in this gene can lead to conditions such as neonatal diabetes and hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b,f836064d1a0fd1b13c5a6084a44deb7d</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4132</data>
      <data key="d7">478fa36d2e864d8caedebc4a8078d5f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TIPO MODY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes tipo MODY is a genetic form of diabetes characterized by specific mutations affecting insulin production and secretion, often presenting in childhood or early adulthood.</data>
      <data key="d2">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4133</data>
      <data key="d7">ab6774b5b11247cfa283128beb7510df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROD1">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUROD1 is a gene associated with MODY 6 diabetes, playing a role in pancreatic beta-cell function.</data>
      <data key="d2">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b</data>
      <data key="d3">184</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4134</data>
      <data key="d7">a7875e68628d4775ac0cc7da0c763f4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IPF1">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">IPF1 is a gene that encodes a transcription factor important for insulin production, associated with MODY 4 diabetes.</data>
