    <node id="SAMUEL NAMARA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Samuel Namara is a multifaceted individual recognized for his contributions in both the medical and business fields. He is primarily a researcher and educator specializing in endocrinology, with a focus on diabetes and nutrition. In addition to his work in endocrinology, he has also engaged in research concerning cardiovascular health and the impact of dietary factors. His involvement extends to studies on dietary fiber and its health outcomes, highlighting his commitment to understanding the relationship between diet and health.

While there is a fictional aspect to the name Samuel Namara, including references to a character in a hostage scenario and a hypothetical child with precocious puberty, these elements are not pertinent to his professional contributions. Instead, the emphasis remains on his significant role in dietary studies and his influence in the fields of endocrinology and cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">4885c129837f58f091d24d2cbc8aae66,920badd1fd76f2c279282a4a20295a55,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2,cf833689453c8ce13d3650766a8b47a7,e032cf926bee7048e207a0e28604f60e,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
      <data key="d3">1297</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">21</data>
      <data key="d6">4151</data>
      <data key="d7">fd6fdeb8c05b4ed4952f7fbf1c2b4df1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 (DM2) is a prevalent and chronic metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, significantly affecting how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). It is particularly common in Spain, with a prevalence rate of 13.8% in the general population and an incidence of 11.58 cases per 1,000 people per year. The condition is often associated with obesity, lifestyle factors, and can lead to serious health complications, including cardiovascular disease and diabetic retinopathy.

Patients with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 may experience varying degrees of control over their condition; some have managed it effectively for many years, while others may face challenges, particularly if it is insulin-dependent and poorly controlled. The condition has been linked to the use of statins, especially in individuals with pre-existing risk factors, indicating a complex relationship between medication and diabetes management.

Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is also recognized as a comorbidity that can significantly improve following interventions such as bariatric surgery. Dietary habits and lifestyle choices play a crucial role in managing the disease, with evidence suggesting that adherence to a Mediterranean diet may help prevent its onset. Additionally, the condition has familial links, as indicated by a family history of diabetes in some patients.

Overall, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a significant health issue that requires ongoing management and intervention to mitigate its risks and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">035d53a7f46fdb72c0a939265667044b,0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,1f2b31f5a0bba00ecee5e3a8fb2c83ea,2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,410fab643c125e0f8944ebae5dba5ec0,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,4885c129837f58f091d24d2cbc8aae66,488970234520652b063db88e8346031c,4b4f297dec86d7f65e362ad688bbb28f,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b,6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa,7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5,9312fdfba5d3f79b95c5e6af38ced009,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,da2707b26ddb548995a6d0e2a3eeddb0,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
      <data key="d3">1372</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
