    </node>
    <node id="SALINE SOLUTION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Saline solution is a treatment method that involves the infusion of isotonic saline to correct fluid and electrolyte imbalances in patients experiencing hyperglycemic crises. This therapeutic approach is essential for restoring proper hydration and electrolyte levels in individuals facing such medical emergencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41,d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1852</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4202</data>
      <data key="d7">75c435d96e3c45ee9cd132c9e7f11828</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LETARGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A state of sluggishness or lack of energy, which can occur in patients with severe hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4203</data>
      <data key="d7">06ca5c6bc4404803b603e0c3f8c5d295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMIPARESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition characterized by weakness on one side of the body, which can be a neurological symptom of severe hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4204</data>
      <data key="d7">e5d45d01fc7b4b968e848b4eacb8731e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMIANOPSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A visual field defect that can occur in patients with neurological symptoms due to hyperglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4205</data>
      <data key="d7">82057e062dc246e38e9452a9ef4d335b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COMA refers to a state of deep unconsciousness that can arise from various severe medical conditions. Specifically, it can result from severe hyperglycemic conditions, where high blood sugar levels lead to a loss of consciousness. Additionally, coma can also occur due to severe hyponatremia, a condition characterized by dangerously low sodium levels in the blood. This serious medical state indicates a critical impairment of brain function, necessitating immediate medical attention.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4206</data>
      <data key="d7">0077d70224ec4cb2aeb3d33c78ef902f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPEROSMOLALITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition of increased osmolality in the blood, which is a key factor in hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4207</data>
      <data key="d7">d28faa1815614c09b4632ffbdb250197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERVENTILATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition of rapid or deep breathing that can occur in response to metabolic disturbances, including those seen in diabetic crises.</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4208</data>
      <data key="d7">766d4e18c486469ebc08a2b381679be8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Infection refers to the invasion of the body by harmful pathogens, including pathogenic microorganisms, which can lead to disease and complicate recovery in various medical contexts. It is particularly relevant for patients undergoing nutritional support, especially in hematological settings, where the risk of infection is heightened. Additionally, infection can be a precipitating factor for hyperglycemic crises, necessitating prompt identification and treatment in affected individuals. In patients with pancreatitis, infection can arise as a complication, potentially leading to further health issues. Furthermore, the use of non-tunneled catheters for venous access is associated with an increased risk of infection. Overall, infection poses significant challenges in the management and recovery of patients, particularly those undergoing treatments such as bone marrow transplantation.</data>
      <data key="d2">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826,73d47e377c2910da3393d7bb65f80e8e,b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707,be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a,cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d3">1201</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">4209</data>
      <data key="d7">78fbfae05bc247f6ae1f705e60a9f477</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SGLT2 INHIBITORS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A class of medications that can precipitate diabetic ketoacidosis and should be suspended in patients experiencing hyperglycemic crises.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">cda0904fd9d29455ee008c43bc9f7b41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4210</data>
      <data key="d7">26d3fc6d6b80448396dae4d3948473fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JOHN WILEY &amp; SONS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">John Wiley &amp; Sons is a publishing company that published the work on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hypersmolar state in 2004.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4211</data>
      <data key="d7">4de12b010f93441ca334c1cee641cfc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERGLYCEMIC HYPERSMOLAR STATE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperglycemic hypersmolar state is a severe condition associated with uncontrolled diabetes, leading to high blood sugar and dehydration.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4212</data>
      <data key="d7">33b5c4b67c604c068ff658f67bf015ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEFROPAT&#205;A DIAB&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic nephropathy is a kidney-related complication associated with diabetes, which can ultimately lead to kidney failure. It is a significant area of research for Samuel Namara, highlighting its importance in understanding and addressing the health challenges posed by diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1,920badd1fd76f2c279282a4a20295a55</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">4213</data>
      <data key="d7">8d3ed9ac0ab34d319e6e8eb243f4eebf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIONAL KIDNEY FOUNDATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Kidney Foundation is an organization dedicated to promoting kidney health and managing kidney diseases. It provides comprehensive guidelines and resources for various aspects of kidney health, including the evaluation, classification, and management of chronic kidney disease. Additionally, the foundation offers specific guidelines for diabetic nephropathy and addresses bone metabolism and disease in the context of chronic kidney disease. Through its efforts, the National Kidney Foundation aims to enhance understanding and treatment of kidney-related conditions, ensuring that both healthcare professionals and patients have access to essential information and support.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc4a83d18482b48f5bbef4fbf316f3,08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1,1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d3">745</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4214</data>
      <data key="d7">4c5ed1741bfa4fcea08a9882587301d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOTOXICIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucotoxicity refers to the toxic effects of high glucose levels on cells, particularly in the context of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4215</data>
      <data key="d7">9cc54345720d4fd9a14a36eb000b79fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALBUMINURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Albuminuria is the presence of albumin in the urine, which serves as a significant marker for kidney damage, particularly in individuals with diabetic nephropathy. This condition indicates that the kidneys are not functioning properly, and it is especially relevant for diabetic patients, as it can signal the onset of kidney-related complications associated with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1,8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d3">1632</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4216</data>
      <data key="d7">d7d3758eb867477ab0cad11c935cf582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEINURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Proteinuria is the presence of excess proteins in the urine, indicating kidney damage, particularly in diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4217</data>
      <data key="d7">67aa840300c64c668eab995ac884334d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA TUBULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tubular atrophy is a condition where the kidney tubules shrink, often associated with chronic kidney disease, including diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4218</data>
      <data key="d7">bc32bfdc943948e4b4274dd44ffed104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROSIS INTERSTICIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Interstitial fibrosis is the accumulation of fibrous tissue in the kidney, which can occur in diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4219</data>
      <data key="d7">ed767ac881d84a2aab87539d336f12eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertension Arterial, commonly referred to as hypertension, is a chronic condition characterized by elevated blood pressure. This condition plays a significant role in the overall health profile of affected individuals. It is particularly noteworthy as a common comorbidity in patients with diabetes, where it can exacerbate health complications. Additionally, hypertension is recognized as a significant risk factor for the development and progression of diabetic nephropathy, highlighting its critical impact on kidney health in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4220</data>
      <data key="d7">32b8f81dd97d4d1c8fc18b39595305c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERFILTRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperfiltration is an increase in the glomerular filtration rate, often seen in the early stages of diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4221</data>
      <data key="d7">5f9ab1e1be79413f90ccd1096ad87903</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROHEMATURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microhematuria is the presence of small amounts of blood in the urine, which can indicate kidney issues unrelated to diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4222</data>
      <data key="d7">121afde5e1b047118ea572a28213d05f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PODOCITOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Podocytes are specialized cells in the kidney that play a crucial role in filtering blood; their damage is an early sign of diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4223</data>
      <data key="d7">da0f7294ce084e8bbaa62c0d8e3659bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MATRIZ MESANGIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mesangial matrix refers to the connective tissue in the kidney glomeruli, which can expand in diabetic nephropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1</data>
      <data key="d3">514</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4224</data>
      <data key="d7">59ac6f0b5a874d35a3d92c3210138502</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic kidney disease (enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica, ERC) is a long-term medical condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to function effectively, often associated with diabetes. It is defined by a glomerular filtration rate (GFR) below 60 ml/min for at least three months, which can lead to various health complications. The disease is classified into different stages, with stage 3 considered to be of high cardiovascular risk, and stages 4-5 or those requiring dialysis classified as very high risk.

Management of chronic kidney disease necessitates dietary restrictions and specialized nutritional formulas, particularly in advanced stages. It requires careful monitoring of phosphorus intake to prevent further complications. Additionally, chronic kidney disease can invalidate the results of catecholamine and metanephrine tests used in diagnosing pheochromocytoma. The condition also complicates the management of acute diarrhea, necessitating special attention in treatment. Overall, chronic kidney disease is a serious condition that demands comprehensive medical and nutritional care.</data>
      <data key="d2">08f89bb92750950761f8f59bffa402c1,14b7a8c27778bb8821d74790cd2da5ea,169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,a0b43d4a377fca32f55f83fd79e3d9e1,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d3">1157</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">4225</data>
      <data key="d7">967169b4dd884766a3477869fc29984a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETIC NEPHROPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic nephropathy is a kidney disease that results from diabetes, characterized by the presence of albuminuria and reduced glomerular filtration rate.</data>
      <data key="d2">8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d3">1632</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4226</data>
      <data key="d7">505e8d628a774f029f62cb3f397bce8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETINOPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Retinopathy is a diabetes-related eye condition that can lead to vision loss, often requiring treatment to prevent progression.</data>
      <data key="d2">8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d3">1603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4227</data>
      <data key="d7">ffba7ed4a7124306b564ce19359a593e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VEGF">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor (VEGF) is a signal protein that plays a crucial role in the formation of blood vessels. It is particularly significant in the context of various medical conditions, including diabetic retinopathy, where it has been linked to the disease's pathogenesis. VEGF promotes the growth of blood vessels, making it a key target in treatments for diabetic retinopathy. Additionally, it is mentioned in relation to POEMS syndrome, highlighting its broader implications in vascular biology and disease. Overall, VEGF is an important protein in both the development of certain diseases and the therapeutic strategies employed to manage them.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d3">1603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4228</data>
      <data key="d7">e42e181b7acd4b7794296776cbac99cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANRETINAL LASER COAGULATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Panretinal laser coagulation is a treatment method used to reduce the risk of vision loss in patients with proliferative diabetic retinopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d3">1603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4229</data>
      <data key="d7">d2c54872312b4894ad025750ccfee3cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES-2019">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes-2019 refers to a publication or event related to diabetes care and research, specifically focusing on diabetic retinopathy and its classifications.</data>
      <data key="d2">784f8d7f49cdce2d0611be585eda7e2c</data>
      <data key="d3">145</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4230</data>
      <data key="d7">9472cc7adff2427487c5e09ee59f4e6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WILKINSON C">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Wilkinson C is an author who contributed to the proposed international clinical diabetic retinopathy and diabetic macular edema disease severity scales.</data>
      <data key="d2">784f8d7f49cdce2d0611be585eda7e2c</data>
      <data key="d3">145</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
