    <node id="DIABETIC RETINOPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic retinopathy is a complication of diabetes that significantly impacts the eyes. It is characterized by damage to the retina, which occurs as a result of prolonged high blood sugar levels. This condition can lead to vision impairment and, if left untreated, may result in blindness. Additionally, diabetic retinopathy can worsen with rapid improvements in glycemic control, highlighting the importance of careful management of blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b,aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83,dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">4237</data>
      <data key="d7">044671b6358e4502b48d9d137c9d2c55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDEMA MACULAR DIAB&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic macular edema (DME) is a condition characterized by retinal thickening and swelling affecting the macula, which can lead to decreased visual acuity and blindness.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4238</data>
      <data key="d7">c4e851d698a947e69267c12c1be2b9a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTONETTI DA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Antonetti DA is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of diabetic retinopathy and its complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
