    <node id="DIABETES CONTROL AND COMPLICATIONS TRIAL RESEARCH GROUP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial Research Group is a collaborative entity that conducted the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT). This research group focused on studying the effects of strict glycemic control on various complications associated with diabetes, particularly diabetic retinopathy. Their work aimed to understand how effective diabetes management can influence the development and progression of complications, thereby contributing valuable insights to the field of diabetes care.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b,dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4240</data>
      <data key="d7">67bddca391e8441081fd98e1ac25fde3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMBARAZO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EMBARAZO, or pregnancy, is a physiological condition that significantly influences various health aspects, including the progression of retinopathy diab&#233;tica in some patients. It is characterized by specific dietary recommendations tailored to different age groups, particularly focusing on pregnant individuals aged 14-18 years. These recommendations include defined nutrient intake levels that vary according to the age of the pregnant individual, with metrics established for those under 18 years, 19-30 years, and 31-50 years.

During pregnancy, there is a notable impact on nutritional needs and energy requirements, which fluctuate throughout the different trimesters. Additionally, pregnancy affects thyroid function and hormone levels, necessitating careful management of any thyroid-related issues. Overall, EMBARAZO encompasses a range of health and demographic considerations, highlighting the importance of tailored dietary and health management strategies for pregnant individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,4f445fb2c039daae07b71341057c9b9b,4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,6c65beaf6ed5575b0945052270630136,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2,b46fefa9f55d92c74acad101fc4f812e,bd31c6face847551241359e37e4baa2e,dad52b0e2f29edbe1c7e7e1fdee1d7cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1541</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">4241</data>
      <data key="d7">b6aad2e1bc7f4a2cb85c127db8b2f02b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETIC MACULAR EDEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic macular edema is a condition that involves the swelling of the retina and affects the macula, often resulting from diabetic retinopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
