      <data key="d7">07111790b1ad4d9da92dfb7562327ba0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEURISMA DE LA ARTERIA COMUNICANTE POSTERIOR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aneurisma de la arteria comunicante posterior is a type of aneurysm that can occur in the brain, potentially affecting vision and other neurological functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4245</data>
      <data key="d7">4e5ae3d7d5ad4421a46449397a5109e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMORRAGIA V&#205;TREO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemorragia v&#237;treo is a condition characterized by bleeding into the vitreous humor of the eye, often associated with diabetic retinopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d3">400</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4246</data>
      <data key="d7">c662f136f3974ba7a6ef7fc98e6354c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neoplasia refers to the abnormal growth of tissue, which can manifest as either benign or malignant forms. This condition can occur in various parts of the body, including the eyes and the larynx, as evidenced by findings from a CT scan of a patient. In this particular case, neoplasia is associated with the presence of a tumor that impacts the patient's medical condition, specifically affecting their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d3">1162</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4247</data>
      <data key="d7">9f7f1bcb4318420588b8cb7c3d84427a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIPLOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diplopia, or double vision, is a visual disturbance that can occur due to various conditions, including diabetic complications affecting the eye muscles.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4248</data>
      <data key="d7">c13281379f2846338030a4196d06fc7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ptosis is a condition characterized by the drooping of one or both eyelids, which can be associated with neurological issues in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4249</data>
      <data key="d7">75c4356ede8f4faf91eefa35064d4d50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETIC NEUROPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic neuropathy is a heterogeneous group of disorders that result from nerve damage due to diabetes, leading to various clinical manifestations.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1601</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4250</data>
      <data key="d7">44df24d949a64ce694e15dcd6bd5a452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLYNEUROPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyneuropathy is a condition that affects multiple peripheral nerves, often seen in diabetic patients as a complication of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1601</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4251</data>
      <data key="d7">909b6bb6d0f04645b466aa06fd5d320f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOSE CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucose control refers to the management of blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes to prevent complications such as neuropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1713</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4252</data>
      <data key="d7">575c3344cb5a4d369664b4203a575bfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOOT CARE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Foot care is an essential aspect of diabetes management to prevent complications such as foot injuries and infections, particularly in patients with neuropathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4253</data>
      <data key="d7">bd7188ef703641e4a119eab801d24cfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEART DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Heart disease encompasses various cardiovascular conditions that are more prevalent in individuals with diabetes, leading to increased mortality risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1601</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4254</data>
      <data key="d7">cce24db01f0040e2b38985167e84e5dc</data>
    </node>
