      <data key="d6">4255</data>
      <data key="d7">1ea181cf547443978e6396d47690b9de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUTE MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute myocardial infarction (AMI) is a medical emergency where blood flow to the heart is blocked, leading to heart damage, particularly prevalent among diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4256</data>
      <data key="d7">aa93048a737049049fd68b5ed8530267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN COLLEGE OF CARDIOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American College of Cardiology (ACC) is a prominent professional organization based in the USA dedicated to enhancing cardiovascular health through a multifaceted approach that includes education, research, and advocacy. The ACC plays a crucial role in providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of cardiovascular health and diseases, particularly focusing on the care of patients with acute coronary syndromes. Additionally, the organization addresses broader health concerns by publishing guidelines for the management of overweight and obesity in adults, thereby contributing to disease prevention efforts. Through its initiatives, the ACC aims to improve patient outcomes and promote best practices in cardiovascular care.</data>
      <data key="d2">22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,e032cf926bee7048e207a0e28604f60e,e33729f8eea62e59507c132b7c2437df,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">1544</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4257</data>
      <data key="d7">19cab235365a44688a0be10210870c89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DCCT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) is a landmark and pivotal study that demonstrated the significant benefits of intensive diabetes management in reducing microvascular complications among patients with Type 1 Diabetes. This groundbreaking research established the importance of rigorous control of blood glucose levels to improve health outcomes for individuals living with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4258</data>
      <data key="d7">33db7827ee424543aeb601bfd6f73820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDIC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The EDIC, or Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications, is a long-term follow-up study of patients with Type 1 Diabetes who were initially included in the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT). This study tracks the health outcomes of these patients over a period of 27 years, assessing the long-term effects of diabetes management interventions. The EDIC study aims to provide valuable insights into the complications and management of Type 1 Diabetes, building on the foundational data gathered during the DCCT.</data>
      <data key="d2">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4259</data>
      <data key="d7">4c33e6ca802644a89a7e3002062d4d59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME CORONARIO AGUDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS) refers to a group of conditions characterized by a sudden decrease in blood flow to the heart, which can lead to serious cardiovascular events. This syndrome is often associated with underlying health issues such as diabetes. Research suggests that the risk of developing acute coronary syndrome may be mitigated by dietary changes, specifically by increasing the weekly intake of fish.</data>
      <data key="d2">3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4260</data>
      <data key="d7">87d0f5d83302483ba913978e8eb4b238</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETABLOQUEANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Beta-blockers, known as "BETABLOQUEANTES," are a class of medications primarily used to manage various heart conditions, including acute coronary syndrome. They are particularly recommended for diabetic patients due to their beneficial effects on cardiovascular health. In critical care settings, these drugs are considered essential for managing patients' conditions effectively. Additionally, specific beta-blockers, such as propranolol and metoprolol, are utilized in burn patients to reduce muscle catabolism and enhance immune response, highlighting their versatility in treating different medical scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,2ec23f85b858abc42196ef48260e8cb0,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">1143</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4261</data>
      <data key="d7">f4f44e5078ec498890328f1785c20303</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA CARD&#205;ACA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Insuficiencia card&#237;aca, or heart failure, is a medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood sufficiently to meet the body's needs. This chronic condition can lead to various complications, including fluid accumulation in the abdomen, which may be associated with ascitis quilosa. The incidence of heart failure has been found to be inversely related to fish consumption, suggesting dietary factors may play a role in its management. 

In pediatric patients, heart failure significantly affects energy expenditure and may necessitate nutritional management, including adjustments in fluid and nutrient intake. Additionally, it is noted that heart failure is a precautionary consideration when using certain medications, such as lorcaserin. Furthermore, this condition can lead to hypervolemic hyponatremia, highlighting the importance of careful monitoring and management in affected individuals. Overall, insuficiencia card&#237;aca is a complex condition that requires comprehensive care and dietary considerations, particularly in vulnerable populations like children.</data>
      <data key="d2">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,79dc467f42c611bc9f285c95a6c6ff62,8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4262</data>
      <data key="d7">01dec5f89a0e4c1bab5d1d7289cfb4fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DM1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DM1 refers to Type 1 Diabetes, a chronic condition characterized by the pancreas producing little or no insulin. It is a high-risk condition that is often associated with celiac disease. Additionally, individuals with Type 1 Diabetes may also manage other health issues, such as eating disorders, which can complicate the management of their diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f685a05a9682db6dcde958d1918cc77,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4263</data>
      <data key="d7">1f4ec42532434b70928ff72417728d0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUBITOSI-KLUG RA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gubitosi-Klug RA is a researcher associated with the DCCT/EDIC Research Group, contributing to studies on diabetes management and outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4264</data>
      <data key="d7">66267353e39d4e22b46be9c2e413b834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACHIN JM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Lachin JM is a researcher involved in the DCCT/EDIC Research Group, focusing on long-term diabetes outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
