    </node>
    <node id="SITAGLIPTINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Sitagliptina is an oral antidiabetic medication primarily used in the treatment of type 2 diabetes. It functions by increasing insulin release and decreasing glucose production in the liver, thereby helping to control blood sugar levels. In addition to its general use for type 2 diabetes, Sitagliptina has also been utilized in the treatment regimen for patients with MNGIE (Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy), indicating its versatility in managing blood sugar levels in different patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,630ac8fefe27e4b893831674a67dcc82,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9</data>
