    </node>
    <node id="GLP-1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GLP-1, or Glucagon-like peptide-1, is an incretin hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of insulin secretion and blood sugar levels. It is a gastrointestinal hormone produced by intestinal L cells in the distal intestine, released after eating. GLP-1 enhances insulin secretion, lowers blood sugar levels, and is involved in various physiological processes, including gastric emptying and appetite regulation. 

This peptide hormone exerts anorexigenic effects, meaning it helps reduce appetite, and it inhibits signals from neuropeptide Y, which is associated with hunger. GLP-1's functions are influenced by dietary factors such as fiber intake and short-chain fatty acids. It is particularly relevant in the context of obesity treatment, as it regulates glucose metabolism and energy expenditure. Additionally, GLP-1 is the target of medications like liraglutide, which are designed to leverage its effects for therapeutic purposes. Overall, GLP-1 is integral to maintaining glucose homeostasis and managing appetite.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a78cb1d502baf0116e4326e7fbcae41,50fafa000d5f2830cbf66f3201657396,51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d,630ac8fefe27e4b893831674a67dcc82,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872,a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360,e189588f51b4bb84b3621a1f846d07bc,e83d288a4f420cdc975112d3a63bd522,f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
      <data key="d3">999</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">4313</data>
      <data key="d7">5ad5fdf9cd5641f7a7e7126d4655e6ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GIP">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GIP, or Gastric Inhibitory Polypeptide, is an incretin hormone that plays a significant role in the regulation of insulin.</data>
      <data key="d2">50fafa000d5f2830cbf66f3201657396,630ac8fefe27e4b893831674a67dcc82</data>
      <data key="d3">999</data>
