    <node id="SISTEMA RENINA-ANGIOTENSINA-ALDOSTERONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SISTEMA RENINA-ANGIOTENSINA-ALDOSTERONA" is a crucial hormonal system that plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and maintaining fluid balance in the body. This system is activated during pregnancy, highlighting its importance in physiological changes that occur during this period. Additionally, it can be affected in patients with eating disorders, indicating its relevance in various health conditions. Furthermore, the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system may interact with the effects of GLP-1, suggesting a complex interplay between different hormonal systems in the regulation of blood pressure. Overall, the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system is essential for cardiovascular health and fluid homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">50fafa000d5f2830cbf66f3201657396,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
