      <data key="d7">4687a5006c154826a953fa2ed3fae61b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINA BASAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulina basal refers to a type of insulin used to control blood sugar levels in patients with diabetes. It is typically administered once or twice daily to help maintain stable glucose levels throughout the day and night.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,e83d288a4f420cdc975112d3a63bd522</data>
      <data key="d3">1072</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4326</data>
      <data key="d7">93ba3950730b4eeaae46db27f50f8859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINA R&#193;PIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulina r&#225;pida is a type of fast-acting insulin utilized in the management of blood sugar levels for diabetic patients. It is specifically designed to address blood sugar spikes that occur during meals, making it an essential component of diabetes treatment. This insulin is administered subcutaneously to patients every six hours to effectively control their glycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">514518b96e32b025815b45cc2a504f0d,e83d288a4f420cdc975112d3a63bd522,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5</data>
      <data key="d3">1072</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4327</data>
      <data key="d7">d14722c8a80c4e57916be4d329578651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINA GLARGINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulina Glargina is a long-acting insulin utilized by patients for the management of diabetes. It is administered at night to help control blood sugar levels effectively. This insulin formulation is particularly beneficial for maintaining steady insulin levels in the body, which is crucial for managing blood glucose levels in diabetic patients. Insulina Glargina is also noted for its role in diabetes management post-surgery and is used in the context of nutritional therapy, including in patients with Alzheimer's disease. It is specifically indicated for patients with type 2 diabetes, highlighting its importance in comprehensive diabetes care. Overall, Insulina Glargina serves as a vital medication for individuals seeking to regulate their blood sugar levels and improve their overall diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86,84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d,aeb399b3f90c6a50eed8adfa8a140451,bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b,e7df0ed14559db764d393fb9411fec33,e83d288a4f420cdc975112d3a63bd522</data>
      <data key="d3">1072</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4328</data>
      <data key="d7">d1cbbabf7fd94e489224e8970ee321f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINA REGULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulina regular is a transparent solution of zinc insulin crystals, primarily utilized in the treatment of diabetes. It is classified as a short-acting insulin, which is typically administered before meals to effectively manage blood sugar levels. This type of insulin is particularly important for individuals with diabetes, as it helps control blood sugar levels not only during meals but also before exercise. Additionally, insulina regular is used in the context of parenteral nutrition, highlighting its versatility in various treatment scenarios for patients requiring insulin therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,e1f3aed8f37691759547d488b926a79f,e83d288a4f420cdc975112d3a63bd522</data>
      <data key="d3">1072</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
