    <node id="TYPE 2 DIABETES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 2 diabetes is a chronic condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to process blood sugar (glucose). It is often associated with obesity and various lifestyle factors, including diet. This form of diabetes can arise when the body becomes resistant to insulin or when the pancreas fails to produce sufficient insulin. Research has indicated that dietary influences play a crucial role in managing this condition, with studies suggesting that higher dietary fiber intake may lower the risk of developing Type 2 diabetes. Management of the condition can sometimes be achieved through lifestyle changes and the use of oral medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">a4b144210b0a4b654a260ebc394de0af,bb2e69a0ff4c25a21149882162922c8d,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
      <data key="d3">1622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">4345</data>
      <data key="d7">439b376a45684f6ab9dc019e78f4815e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLYCEMIC CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, which is essential for preventing complications associated with the condition. This management often involves dietary adjustments and the use of medication to maintain optimal blood sugar levels. By effectively controlling glycemic levels, diabetic patients can reduce the risk of serious health issues and improve their overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15,dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034,e2304aa7e992d9e26558aab3c807b51d</data>
      <data key="d3">1718</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">4346</data>
      <data key="d7">a3f17356582141cf9f88c74357321b3e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPOHYPERTROPHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition that can occur in diabetes patients due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to erratic insulin absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">dda50550d881b4487154c85b2f279034</data>
      <data key="d3">1713</data>
