    <node id="NICE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) is an organization that provides comprehensive guidelines related to healthcare. It focuses on various aspects of medical care, including the management of specific health conditions and the improvement of patient outcomes. NICE offers directives on the care of malnourished patients, ensuring that their nutritional needs are addressed effectively. Additionally, it provides guidelines for the prevention and management of diabetic foot problems, highlighting its commitment to addressing critical health issues and enhancing the quality of care across different patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6,da6937e21690cfcb43a43b3438ec7586</data>
      <data key="d3">1930</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4366</data>
      <data key="d7">b5c6e5b8bc244cd4a4d127beee01067f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KAMEL KS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kamel KS is a researcher focused on the pathophysiology of low urine pH in patients with uric acid stones. In addition to this area of study, Kamel KS has also made significant contributions to the understanding of acid-base problems associated with diabetic ketoacidosis. Through his research, Kamel KS aims to enhance the knowledge surrounding these critical health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a,f757219e84dba985f7c8d66ac951b9f2</data>
      <data key="d3">899</data>
