    </node>
    <node id="WOLFSDORF JI">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Wolfsdorf JI is a distinguished medical professional known for significant contributions to pediatric and adolescent diabetes management. He has played a vital role in the development of the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines, specifically addressing diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state. As a member of the International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes, Wolfsdorf has actively participated in shaping clinical practice consensus on diabetes management. In addition to his work in diabetes, he has authored research on cornstarch regimens for glycogen storage disease and has investigated the relationship between metabolic control and renal dysfunction in type 1 glycogen storage disease. Through his research and clinical guidelines, Wolfsdorf JI has made substantial contributions to the understanding and management of these complex medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">37124cb23ee078d1ff25425727336ae5,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a,ed9e6da7ef23d47467822d2a1e461195,f713611b23199b8a9eb9c28377b9f128</data>
      <data key="d3">897</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4369</data>
      <data key="d7">7f1ae7c2fe924dacad0ea38eb0009204</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY FOR PEDIATRIC AND ADOLESCENT DIABETES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes is a global organization dedicated to enhancing the care and management of diabetes in children and adolescents. It provides comprehensive guidelines and support aimed at improving the health outcomes of young individuals affected by diabetes. The organization emphasizes the importance of research and education in its mission to advance the understanding and treatment of diabetes in this specific age group.</data>
      <data key="d2">9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a,ed9e6da7ef23d47467822d2a1e461195</data>
      <data key="d3">897</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">4370</data>
      <data key="d7">7cae013bf11a4efbb90d2c79dbadb866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUIDOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FLUIDOTERAPIA, or fluid therapy, is a vital medical treatment that involves the administration of fluids to patients to maintain hydration and electrolyte balance. It is particularly crucial for burn patients, where it focuses on hydration to ensure vital organ perfusion and manage shock. Additionally, fluid therapy plays an important role in managing diabetic ketoacidosis (cetoacidosis diab&#233;tica). The practice is also commonly utilized in surgical contexts to support patients' hydration needs and overall stability during and after procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,916d4d35de887923f4ea5b05928f13e3,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d3">1113</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4371</data>
      <data key="d7">bc5a62e49b9b4ed3bb6c3e02f5aadbf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRISTALOIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cristaloides are a type of intravenous fluid used in medical treatment, particularly for hydration in conditions like cetoacidosis diab&#233;tica.</data>
      <data key="d2">9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4372</data>
      <data key="d7">3ac8293f3521429099407951b7572613</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;SFOROS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#243;sforos are phosphates, which may be relevant in the context of electrolyte management in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4373</data>
      <data key="d7">b791c9f651bb4e2b965791c3fac5f5a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS L&#193;CTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidosis l&#225;ctica, or lactic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lactic acid in the body. This condition can arise in various medical situations, including metabolic disturbances such as those seen in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0) and in individuals with Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes (MELAS). In GSD0, the diversion of excess glucose and intermediates towards lactic acid production can lead to this condition. In MELAS patients, lactic acidosis is a common occurrence resulting from mitochondrial dysfunction and is considered a diagnostic criterion for the syndrome. Additionally, lactic acidosis must be ruled out in children presenting symptoms before initiating a ketogenic diet, as it can indicate underlying metabolic issues. Overall, acidosis l&#225;ctica is a significant metabolic disturbance that reflects a buildup of lactic acid in the body, often necessitating careful monitoring and management in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a9b42ff082f2d0bb036ec3365d9a6e9,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a,9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4374</data>
      <data key="d7">97a81d54606642368e5d307866f66db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RABDOMI&#211;LISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rabdomi&#243;lisis, also known as rhabdomyolysis, is a serious medical condition characterized by the breakdown of muscle tissue. This condition can complicate the management of diabetes and may arise as a severe side effect of statin medications, which are commonly prescribed to lower cholesterol levels. The breakdown of muscle tissue in rabdomi&#243;lisis can lead to significant health issues, including the risk of kidney failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">9312fdfba5d3f79b95c5e6af38ced009,9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4375</data>
      <data key="d7">04f696a912fd474890fe3b4637ab8126</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#237;ndrome refers to a group of symptoms that occur together, which can be relevant in the context of diabetes and its complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">9889a9000d5a82ffba9e0f6c92da918a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4376</data>
      <data key="d7">5f161cb9d3ee40739ac5846468704f90</data>
    </node>
