    <node id="ESTATINAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Estatinas, also known as statins, are a class of medications primarily used to lower cholesterol levels in the blood. They are effective hypolipemiant drugs that help manage dyslipidemia, particularly by reducing LDL cholesterol levels. Estatinas are often prescribed to patients to mitigate cardiovascular risk, especially in individuals with conditions such as diabetes or chronic kidney disease, although their use may depend on the patient's overall health status.

In addition to their cholesterol-lowering effects, estatinas can also be utilized in the treatment of severe hypertriglyceridemia, although they are generally considered a second-line option due to their moderate impact on triglyceride levels. It is important to note that the effects of estatinas can be potentiated by alcohol consumption, which may influence their efficacy and safety profile.

Overall, estatinas are widely recognized for their role in cardiovascular health and are a common choice in the management of lipid disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">14b7a8c27778bb8821d74790cd2da5ea,2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,41d7db510fc74d3763959481cc15ea20,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,5c11ed246e1a48261910b9b71b65014c,746fad557197bebe72763efd23a9e0e2,75a4b2d504de480eaef247aa682bfd05,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7,9312fdfba5d3f79b95c5e6af38ced009,a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6,c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27</data>
