    </node>
    <node id="SEDYNE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad de Endocrinolog&#237;a, Diabetes y Nutrici&#243;n de Euskadi (SEDyNE) is a professional society that Fco. Javier Santamar&#237;a Sandi presided over from March 2011 to March 2016.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1450</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4408</data>
      <data key="d7">a28ccb59f66b4c32a83026fb43e2f592</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de tiroides, or thyroid cancer, is a condition characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the thyroid gland. This type of cancer has been associated with obesity, although the exact mechanisms remain unclear. Treatment for thyroid cancer may involve specific therapies, such as radioiodine therapy. 

Research has suggested that there is no significant association between the consumption of fish and the development of thyroid cancer. However, the relationship between thyroid cancer and the intake of fruits and vegetables is more controversial, particularly due to the presence of thiocyanates in cruciferous vegetables, which may influence thyroid health.

Additionally, thyroid cancer can be a potential complication for patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), although the connection between thyroid cancer and the MEN1 gene is not well established. 

The Thyroid Cancer Working Group, a committee within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition, has been involved in addressing issues related to thyroid cancer, with Fco. Javier Santamar&#237;a Sandi serving as secretary from 2012 to 2016.</data>
      <data key="d2">072912695b1cff9f390d4ead3b9ad742,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5,b110392fc91bc3d7875124ec3fa07c46</data>
      <data key="d3">1350</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">4409</data>
      <data key="d7">e268b6eaa15b41fab850b78d707ce62c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOTIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOTIROIDISMO, or hypothyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by the insufficient production of thyroid hormones by the thyroid gland. This deficiency leads to a slow metabolism and can result in various health problems, including decreased energy levels. Additionally, hypothyroidism may contribute to low levels of copper in the body and can influence sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels, which in turn affects testosterone levels. It is also noted that hypothyroidism can be a common adverse effect associated with certain immune checkpoint inhibitors, such as ipilimumab and nivolumab. The condition encompasses various forms, including congenital hypothyroidism, which has specific implications for affected individuals. Overall, hypothyroidism is a significant health concern that impacts metabolic function and hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,40253f8b49d61452dbc56454cd1a07e0,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5,cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
      <data key="d3">1355</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4410</data>
      <data key="d7">df446965d37249e087cd74d523a5cf16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROSIGLITAZONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rosiglitazone is a medication that has shown to improve &#946;-cell function and insulin sensitivity in patients with type 2 diabetes, as highlighted in the ADOPT study.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4411</data>
      <data key="d7">2a4d585238094a41bed3baf2adee20f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METFORMINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metformina, or metformin, is a medication primarily used for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus. It works by improving insulin sensitivity, which helps manage blood sugar levels in patients with this condition. However, in some cases, such as when a patient has low glomerular filtration rates, metformin may be suspended due to potential risks. Additionally, it is recommended that metformin be withdrawn two days prior to any studies if gastrointestinal tumors are suspected.

While metformin is effective in managing diabetes, it can be associated with side effects, including diarrhea and a reduction in vitamin B12 concentrations. In clinical studies, such as the ADOPT study, metformin has been compared to other medications like rosiglitazone, particularly in terms of glycemic durability. Overall, metformin remains a widely used and important medication in the management of type 2 diabetes, although careful consideration of patient-specific factors is necessary for its use.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,70b2393fa61e51fc3e772479a9792c98,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5,9c43759c41fe226a2702de300b9e580a,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d3">674</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4412</data>
      <data key="d7">e86c92260ed74d44b6559329c299b844</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLIBURIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gliburide is another alternative medication for type 2 diabetes that is compared to rosiglitazone in the ADOPT study.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4413</data>
