    </node>
    <node id="ANTICUERPOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANTICUERPOS are proteins produced by the immune system in response to various stimuli, including allergens and specific proteins such as gluten in individuals with celiac disease. They play a crucial role in the immune response, with different types of antibodies serving distinct functions. For instance, antibodies against the thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) receptor can be present in newborns with congenital hypothyroidism, affecting thyroid function. Additionally, antibodies such as IgE are produced in response to allergens, contributing to allergic reactions. Furthermore, these antibodies are utilized in diagnostic tests for conditions like celiac disease, highlighting their importance in both immune response and medical diagnostics.</data>
      <data key="d2">1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30,bc394d70461777b6300d5449185a7859</data>
      <data key="d3">1353</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4414</data>
      <data key="d7">d57da0c32203443485e94ea9021d2fc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRIBADO NEONATAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neonatal screening is a process that helps identify congenital hypothyroidism in newborns, with varying incidence rates depending on the country and screening practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4415</data>
      <data key="d7">f92eb0a2731a4610a81573748e899fa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISGENESIA TIROIDEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Disgenesia tiroidea, also known as thyroid dysgenesis, is recognized as the primary cause of congenital hypothyroidism, accounting for approximately 85% of cases. This condition plays a significant role in the overall incidence of congenital hypothyroidism, highlighting its importance in the field of endocrinology and pediatric health.</data>
      <data key="d2">838d1ef59dfea4cab2a724bc85b02632,8ddb42b0859e58bd2f937125505ed9d5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4416</data>
      <data key="d7">6f78ac791c754d1cb733afba3bf88960</data>
    </node>
