    <node id="J CLIN ENDOCRINOL METAB">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism (J Clin Endocrinol Metab) is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research and clinical practice guidelines related to endocrinology and metabolism. It features a wide range of studies, including those focused on adrenal insufficiency, hyponatremia, congenital hypothyroidism, thyroid disease, and conditions such as pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma. The journal has also published significant clinical practice guidelines on endocrine treatment for gender-dysphoric individuals, as well as research on the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIAD) and glucocorticoid deficiency. Overall, J Clin Endocrinol Metab serves as a vital resource for advancements in the field of endocrinology.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,152aeb8f10c2f4548114403c05af6b55,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,1dc3bddf85e4bb26e46f373169e43b14,4937d8f482fff897409bb1d7a094151a,70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58,838d1ef59dfea4cab2a724bc85b02632,b96414a52f13cac336436d9e8173baef</data>
