    <node id="AMPC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AMPC, or cyclic AMP (adenosine monophosphate cyclic), is a crucial secondary messenger involved in various biological processes. It plays a significant role in cellular signaling pathways, particularly those influenced by thyroid hormones. Additionally, AMPC is affected by the Gs&#945; protein, which is integral to its function in cellular signaling. This highlights the importance of AMPC in mediating responses within the cell and its involvement in complex regulatory mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">4138cb85d4afff56555b4a536340ca90,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b</data>
      <data key="d3">285</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4448</data>
      <data key="d7">24050cde0c9642f4a995c3853ceb09fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESYODASAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deiodinases are enzymes that convert thyroid hormones into their active or inactive forms, playing a key role in thyroid hormone metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">4138cb85d4afff56555b4a536340ca90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4449</data>
      <data key="d7">9eb6984ec2e74891adfab613d6d5e811</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD GRAVE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Severe illness can lead to changes in thyroid function, affecting hormone levels and metabolism.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">4138cb85d4afff56555b4a536340ca90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4450</data>
      <data key="d7">5ee6b5c924d643359e3fab5cf0a43ab6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMANGIOMAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los hemangiomas son tumores vasculares que pueden estar asociados con hipotiroidismo debido a la expresi&#243;n elevada de la enzima yodotironina desyodasa tipo 3, que afecta la producci&#243;n de hormonas tiroideas.</data>
      <data key="d2">f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
      <data key="d3">1350</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4451</data>
      <data key="d7">a4641bba2afd43ac947612368a2840ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROIDITIS DE HASHIMOTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La tiroiditis de Hashimoto es una enfermedad autoinmune que afecta la tiroides, caracterizada por la inflamaci&#243;n de esta gl&#225;ndula. Esta condici&#243;n a menudo se asocia con el uso de interfer&#243;n &#945;, que puede inducir su aparici&#243;n. La tiroiditis de Hashimoto se manifiesta frecuentemente con la presencia de bocio y niveles elevados de anticuerpos antitiroideos, lo que indica una respuesta inmune anormal contra el tejido tiroideo.</data>
      <data key="d2">3491690ff2b417d00598f7df8e68f4d6,f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
      <data key="d3">1675</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4452</data>
      <data key="d7">dc3d52500eb94b39ae778fe3e38fc90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEVOTIROXINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Levotiroxina is a medication that serves as a synthetic form of the thyroid hormone, primarily utilized in the treatment of hypothyroidism. It is particularly important in managing congenital hypothyroidism, where it acts as the primary treatment option. However, the absorption of levotiroxina can be influenced by other medications, such as carbamazepine, which may affect its efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7,be2de576112f22070e8ef8a5cb9e1017,f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
      <data key="d3">1671</data>
