    <node id="HORMONA TIROIDEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HORMONA TIROIDEA, or thyroid hormone, is produced with the assistance of iodine and plays a crucial role in metabolic processes and development in humans. The primary thyroid hormones, T4 (thyroxine) and T3 (triiodothyronine), are essential for regulating metabolism. Their production and function can be influenced by various factors, including pH levels and interactions with medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">be2de576112f22070e8ef8a5cb9e1017,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b,efbbfb33c127e16f4f9013683aff2c5f</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
