    <node id="ANTICUERPOS ANTILEVOTIROXINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anticuerpos antilevotiroxina are antibodies that may be present in patients with certain thyroid disorders, including Graves' disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4486</data>
      <data key="d7">4ac3151111cb4c858faad41e7ee3ddca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE GRAVES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Graves' disease, known as "enfermedad de Graves" in Spanish, is an autoimmune disorder that leads to hyperactivity of the thyroid gland, resulting in hyperthyroidism. This condition is characterized by the presence of antibodies that bind to the thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) receptor, which stimulates the thyroid gland's overproduction of hormones. Graves' disease can also be associated with other autoimmune disorders and may lead to complications such as hypoparathyroidism and goiter. Overall, it is a significant health condition that affects the endocrine system and requires careful management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7,1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1353</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">4487</data>
      <data key="d7">b69f5a9418a4486bbf2a58072e1b39ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAQUICARDIA SINUSAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Taquicardia sinusal is a common cardiovascular manifestation associated with hyperthyroidism, including in patients with Graves' disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d3">1353</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4488</data>
      <data key="d7">3f5a276907314566a41c5f1ccbf3a5fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEDICINA NUCLEAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Medicina nuclear refers to a medical specialty that uses radioactive substances for diagnosis and treatment, often used in evaluating thyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d3">1670</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4489</data>
      <data key="d7">b5cabd26201b4b5fb8d36f5abd0d3946</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESHALOGENAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Deshalogenas are enzymes involved in the metabolism of thyroid hormones, and defects in these enzymes can lead to congenital hypothyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d3">1350</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4490</data>
      <data key="d7">38ff86bd34614f92926a26aaf6dfbe61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NA TRANSPORTADORA DE YODO NIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La prote&#237;na transportadora de yodo NIS (Na/I symporter) is essential for iodine uptake in the thyroid gland, and its dysfunction can lead to thyroid disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d3">1670</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4491</data>
      <data key="d7">135bd816ecaf4a538ed47d29ce4b875c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIXEDEMA PRETIBIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El mixedema pretibial es una manifestaci&#243;n cl&#237;nica infrecuente de la enfermedad de Graves, con una prevalencia de alrededor del 5%.</data>
      <data key="d2">1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63</data>
      <data key="d3">1353</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4492</data>
      <data key="d7">d1139d069ddf4d8fabe21b148e9b58f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTR&#201;S">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESTR&#201;S, aunque ha sido relacionado con la aparici&#243;n de la enfermedad de Graves, carece de evidencias s&#243;lidas que respalden esta conexi&#243;n. Adem&#225;s, el estr&#233;s se manifiesta como una respuesta fisiol&#243;gica que puede aumentar los requerimientos nutricionales y afectar la recuperaci&#243;n despu&#233;s de una cirug&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866</data>
      <data key="d3">1353</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4493</data>
      <data key="d7">19e36cebf31b4d8fa0a889a5fb92536c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRILACI&#211;N AURICULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrilaci&#243;n auricular, or atrial fibrillation, is a heart condition characterized by an irregular and often rapid heart rate. This condition was present in the patient and significantly contributed to his risk of stroke. Atrial fibrillation is classified as a type of cardiac arrhythmia, which can be influenced by various factors, including obesity. Additionally, there is some evidence suggesting that the use of fish oil may help manage atrial fibrillation, although further research is needed to confirm these potential benefits. Furthermore, atrial fibrillation can also be a cardiovascular complication associated with hyperthyroidism, particularly in individuals over the age of 60.</data>
      <data key="d2">1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c</data>
      <data key="d3">1397</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">4494</data>
      <data key="d7">a75889bc9ea6499cb703508ed5e80b03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOELAERT K">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Boelaert K is a notable author involved in significant research and guidelines related to thyroid health. He has contributed to a study focusing on hyperthyroidism in older individuals, highlighting the importance of understanding this condition in the aging population. Additionally, Boelaert K is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer, which were published in the journal Clinical Endocrinology. This work underscores his expertise and influence in the field of endocrinology, particularly concerning thyroid disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1263bbcd20f6e54800e1c9361466bc63,a4e97817eb89c3941a890d94f5359369</data>
