    <node id="GRAVES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Graves is an autoimmune disorder that affects the thyroid gland, resulting in hyperthyroidism. This condition is characterized by the overactivity of the thyroid, which can lead to various symptoms associated with excessive thyroid hormone production. Additionally, Graves' disease is often linked with Graves' ophthalmopathy, a condition that affects the eyes and can cause symptoms such as bulging eyes and vision problems.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c18507e3d98242cdbcddd1a1997b92f,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b,cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
      <data key="d3">1352</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4508</data>
      <data key="d7">e969f879c14e4347b954ca3d5ce3f9d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMIODARONE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Amiodarone is a medication primarily used to treat serious irregular heartbeats, functioning as an antiarrhythmic agent. It is widely recognized for its effectiveness in managing various cardiac conditions. Notably, amiodarone has a high iodine content, which can significantly impact thyroid function, potentially leading to conditions such as type 2 thyrotoxicosis. This dual effect on both cardiac rhythm and thyroid health underscores the importance of monitoring thyroid function in patients undergoing treatment with amiodarone.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed,45213238a7d4c834b6db62ef71dcda43,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">173</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4509</data>
      <data key="d7">7cecd3cf098d4dadb57d065a96419bac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOCALCINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteocalcina is a protein that plays a crucial role in evaluating bone health, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. It is produced by osteoblasts and functions as a hormone involved in bone formation. Additionally, osteocalcin levels can be elevated in conditions such as hyperthyroidism, indicating its significance in various metabolic processes related to bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4510</data>
      <data key="d7">c66ba9bcde274757b9148432cec56afd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHBG">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SHBG (Sex Hormone-Binding Globulin) is a protein that plays a crucial role in binding sex hormones, thereby regulating their availability and influencing hormone levels in the body, particularly testosterone. It serves as an important marker in diagnosing conditions such as thyroid hormone resistance and TSHomas. Additionally, SHBG levels are influenced by thyroid hormones, highlighting its interconnectedness with the endocrine system. Overall, SHBG is essential for maintaining hormonal balance and is significant in various clinical assessments related to hormone-related disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">10cd1db13dc50a14adab6e4c215bb3b0,39cdf983b8de558536d2d829978daba1,4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1356</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">4511</data>
      <data key="d7">404c664756cb4ae1b1d9f167fc5172a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FERRITINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ferritina, also known as ferritin, is a crucial protein that stores iron in the body, playing a vital role in maintaining iron homeostasis and preventing anemia. It functions by releasing iron when needed, thus regulating iron levels within cells. Ferritin levels are commonly measured to evaluate the body's iron stores, which is particularly important for patients with eating disorders and those suffering from conditions such as hemochromatosis. Elevated ferritin levels can occur in various medical conditions, including hyperthyroidism and inflammatory bowel disease, even in cases of iron deficiency. Additionally, ferritin serves as a significant biomarker for assessing iron levels in the blood, making it an essential component in diagnosing and managing various health conditions related to iron metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0,c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">4512</data>
      <data key="d7">74801a1665a4426e88f483b97d53c785</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#211;DULO T&#211;XICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Toxic nodules are hyperfunctioning thyroid nodules that can cause hyperthyroidism by producing excess thyroid hormones.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4f0f024f16be34d17dbbbae57042b2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4513</data>
      <data key="d7">04565b7cb79447a593d3a081bf58af6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROIDITIS DESTRUCTIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tiroiditis destructiva is a type of thyroiditis that leads to the release of stored hormones rather than an increase in hormone synthesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
      <data key="d3">1355</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4514</data>
      <data key="d7">b9e5e4c27e864f23b2a2ca88184e29b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERTALENA L">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Bertalena L is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of Graves' orbitopathy and its management.</data>
      <data key="d2">cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
      <data key="d3">1352</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4515</data>
