    </node>
    <node id="FIBROSIS DE LA MUSCULATURA OCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrosis de la musculatura ocular is a condition that can occur in the later stages of Graves' ophthalmopathy, characterized by scarring of the eye muscles.</data>
      <data key="d2">cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
      <data key="d3">1352</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4516</data>
      <data key="d7">66b18e89f822474683f7c8f21e8889db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H&#193;BITO TAB&#193;QUICO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">H&#225;bito tab&#225;quico, or the practice of smoking, is a significant factor that influences various health outcomes. It is particularly noted for its role in the progression of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and other respiratory diseases, making it a critical prognostic factor. In Spain, tobacco habits are a key determinant of the prevalence of COPD across different demographics. Additionally, smoking has been linked to an increased risk and severity of Graves' ophthalmopathy, highlighting its detrimental effects on overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0,bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,cca243547034544596d9409f2643eac0</data>
