    <node id="THYROID">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The thyroid is a gland located in the neck that plays a crucial role in the body's metabolism by producing hormones. It can develop nodules, which may be either benign or malignant. Diseases of the thyroid are often classified and staged according to the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) guidelines. Additionally, "Thyroid" is a medical journal dedicated to publishing research related to thyroid diseases and disorders. This journal covers a wide range of topics, including guidelines and studies on specific conditions such as medullary thyroid carcinoma and Graves' disease, along with their complications and treatments. Overall, the thyroid is a vital gland with significant implications for health, and ongoing research in the field is essential for understanding and managing thyroid-related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">17db9c3996d806c3332ba2796ab7736f,39cdf983b8de558536d2d829978daba1,3c8b29df4105e84d4766d8d632de8535,673c86b4e90c81d1c4bc78cdd08e9be0,b1ce0d940909277d321ee55bffcc69b3,e775708e66a97968834f7476479a21b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1212</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">4526</data>
      <data key="d7">1ec295545d894f1b813d78cab346be6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRAVES' DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Graves' disease is an autoimmune disorder that is recognized as the most common cause of hyperthyroidism, particularly in adults. This condition affects the thyroid gland, resulting in an overproduction of thyroid hormones. In addition to hyperthyroidism, Graves' disease can lead to various complications, one of the most notable being Graves' orbitopathy, which affects the eyes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dc3bddf85e4bb26e46f373169e43b14,3c8b29df4105e84d4766d8d632de8535</data>
      <data key="d3">1516</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4527</data>
      <data key="d7">2fecd72a89a24b5a88ca572af2603348</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METHYLPREDNISOLONE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Methylprednisolone is a corticosteroid medication used in the treatment of Graves' orbitopathy to reduce inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c8b29df4105e84d4766d8d632de8535</data>
      <data key="d3">1517</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4528</data>
      <data key="d7">9c5b2f92c6d049a39e83fbc685bab546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIVER DAMAGE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Liver damage is a potential side effect associated with the use of intravenous glucocorticoid pulse therapy in patients with Graves' orbitopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c8b29df4105e84d4766d8d632de8535</data>
      <data key="d3">1517</data>
