    </node>
    <node id="IODINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">IODINE is a mineral that plays a crucial role in thyroid function, and its dietary intake is subject to specific recommendations. It is essential for the production of thyroid hormones, which regulate various metabolic processes in the body. The dietary reference intake for iodine, also referred to as "Yodo," varies across different age groups, as outlined in dietary guidelines. However, it is important to note that excessive iodine consumption has been linked to the development of Graves' disease, an autoimmune disorder that affects the thyroid. Therefore, while iodine is vital for health, maintaining an appropriate balance in dietary intake is essential to prevent potential health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c8b29df4105e84d4766d8d632de8535,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
