    </node>
    <node id="TIAMAZOL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tiamazol is a medication utilized for the treatment of hyperthyroidism, primarily by inhibiting the production of thyroid hormones. It is classified as an antithyroid medication and is noted for its potential teratogenic effects, which are important considerations in the context of thyroid treatment. In particular situations, such as during pregnancy, Tiamazol may be switched to another medication known as PTU to mitigate risks associated with its use.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed,45213238a7d4c834b6db62ef71dcda43,92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2</data>
      <data key="d3">174</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4551</data>
      <data key="d7">7bbad96d04ff4fb0a55a6328b8cb63b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROPYLTHIOURACIL (PTU)">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Propylthiouracil (PTU) is a medication used to manage hyperthyroidism, particularly during the first trimester of pregnancy due to its lower teratogenic risk compared to tiamazol.</data>
      <data key="d2">92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2</data>
      <data key="d3">174</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
