    <node id="THYROID DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thyroid disease refers to various conditions affecting the thyroid gland, including hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism, which can be influenced by medications like amiodarone.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed</data>
      <data key="d3">173</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4554</data>
      <data key="d7">6a1b5e5aa8b04066ad6f63c80d7b60a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTIROIDISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperthyroidism is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of thyroid hormones by an overactive thyroid gland. This condition can manifest in various forms, including subclinical hyperthyroidism, which may necessitate treatment depending on specific patient factors, particularly in older adults. Additionally, hyperthyroidism can be associated with other endocrine disorders. It is important to note that hyperthyroidism can also be induced as a side effect of certain medications, such as amiodarone, which can significantly affect thyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed,45213238a7d4c834b6db62ef71dcda43,4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">172</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">4555</data>
      <data key="d7">db897691035b466282f025c84e00ea5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROCYTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tirocytes are the cells of the thyroid gland that can be affected by drugs like amiodarone, leading to cytotoxic effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed</data>
      <data key="d3">173</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4556</data>
      <data key="d7">fbfc4a5d5ac94c2a90de01823d6bc29c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN THYROID ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Thyroid Association (ATA) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and management of thyroid diseases. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the diagnosis and treatment of various thyroid conditions, including thyroid nodules, differentiated thyroid cancer, and medullary thyroid carcinoma. The ATA's guidelines also encompass the management of thyroid disease during pregnancy and the postpartum period, ensuring that both patients and healthcare providers have access to the latest research and best practices in thyroid health. Through its efforts, the American Thyroid Association plays a crucial role in improving patient outcomes and promoting awareness of thyroid-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">02db15b9ad7bc5655e1907ad3fa4e8ad,0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce,0d78e460e4fb4a82bb6e11496f7d5aed,17db9c3996d806c3332ba2796ab7736f,1dc3bddf85e4bb26e46f373169e43b14,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,a4e97817eb89c3941a890d94f5359369,bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f,cb3b93a50040c892ecf439582ebb6ac0,de6e1d8ac9f422acb17fd26b77b485da,e2091cc12f3e5cfae8cc2c1358cddc65,e775708e66a97968834f7476479a21b2</data>
