    <node id="ENDOCRINOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Endocrinology is a specialized branch of medicine that focuses on the endocrine system, its diseases, and the hormones it produces. This field plays a crucial role in the management of various health conditions, particularly diabetes, and is also involved in nutrition management. Endocrinology encompasses the study of specific secretions known as hormones, which are vital for numerous bodily functions. Additionally, the field includes research published in medical journals, such as studies on the cytotoxic effects of amiodarone and discussions on related disorders, including those concerning carcinoid tumors as noted by &#214;berg KE. Overall, endocrinology is essential for understanding and treating hormonal imbalances and related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">04b13f0ccbff81f5f7e92e7bd239cd92,45213238a7d4c834b6db62ef71dcda43,4937d8f482fff897409bb1d7a094151a,54bdd3faa067cdbb44671453ffaf4be5,a7672b877f024a5e716c48c18cd14f54</data>
