    <node id="TSHOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TSHoma refers to a type of pituitary tumor characterized by its production and secretion of excess thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH). This condition is the focus of various studies and clinical evaluations, highlighting its significance in understanding pituitary tumors and their effects on hormone regulation.</data>
      <data key="d2">39cdf983b8de558536d2d829978daba1,d6bea02011329ebf0fa64f4d6792d101</data>
      <data key="d3">1669</data>
