    <node id="TIROIDITIS DE RIEDEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tiroiditis de Riedel is a rare and chronic inflammatory disease of the thyroid gland, characterized by the presence of fibrosis within the thyroid tissue. This condition can lead to progressive local symptoms and may result in complications, including hypoparathyroidism. The fibrosis associated with Tiroiditis de Riedel can significantly affect thyroid function and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3491690ff2b417d00598f7df8e68f4d6,4937d8f482fff897409bb1d7a094151a</data>
      <data key="d3">1674</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">4613</data>
      <data key="d7">9b3990c0fbf348a081d962ab53f79eee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HASHIMOTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hashimoto's thyroiditis is an autoimmune disorder that causes chronic inflammation of the thyroid gland, differing from Riedel's in that it does not involve fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">4937d8f482fff897409bb1d7a094151a</data>
      <data key="d3">1674</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
