    <node id="CLINICAL GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical guidelines are systematically developed statements designed to assist both practitioners and patients in making informed decisions regarding appropriate healthcare for specific clinical circumstances. These guidelines encompass a wide range of medical conditions and provide evidence-based recommendations tailored for healthcare professionals. For instance, clinical guidelines for the management of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis offer targeted recommendations to improve patient care. Additionally, they include protocols for the diagnosis and treatment of conditions such as incidental pituitary adenomas, as well as management strategies for hyponatremia, addressing various severity levels. Overall, clinical guidelines serve as a crucial resource in ensuring effective and standardized healthcare practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">37182848d30a82f99b7a617859ac6e0d,4937d8f482fff897409bb1d7a094151a,d26aec24f3f8c930c1c4b1d464bacd6b,d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055,f5d0adafea7d8fe8216c624188ddad04</data>
