    <node id="THYROID NODULES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thyroid nodules are abnormal growths that occur in the thyroid gland, which can be either benign or malignant. The characteristics of these nodules are assessed to evaluate the risk of cancer. Their management is guided by the American Thyroid Association, ensuring that appropriate monitoring or treatment is provided based on the specific circumstances of each case. Overall, thyroid nodules may require careful observation or intervention depending on their nature and associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">02db15b9ad7bc5655e1907ad3fa4e8ad,0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce,673c86b4e90c81d1c4bc78cdd08e9be0,bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f,e2091cc12f3e5cfae8cc2c1358cddc65</data>
      <data key="d3">1211</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">4633</data>
      <data key="d7">65ac7d1914574a048e3a65ebec01b9d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THYROID CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the thyroid gland, which can be predicted through ultrasound features of thyroid nodules.</data>
      <data key="d2">673c86b4e90c81d1c4bc78cdd08e9be0</data>
      <data key="d3">1213</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
