    <node id="PAAF">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PAAF, or Punci&#243;n Aspiraci&#243;n con Aguja Fina, is a medical procedure utilized for diagnostic purposes. It is primarily employed to evaluate thyroid nodules and assess the potential for malignancy. Additionally, PAAF is also performed to obtain tissue samples from liver lesions, aiding in the diagnosis of various conditions. This technique is significant in the medical field for its role in determining the nature of suspicious lesions in both the thyroid and liver.</data>
      <data key="d2">171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040,b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
