      <data key="d6">4643</data>
      <data key="d7">b9613646ebe641029e4d42c5ce2cff44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NABO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">NABO, known as "nabo" in Spanish, is a vegetable that possesses certain properties relevant to health. It contains substances that may interfere with the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells, which is an important consideration for individuals concerned about thyroid function. Additionally, NABO has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 grams, making it a suitable option for those monitoring their galactose intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4644</data>
      <data key="d7">9e4d8106aa6448e8b26d700e23a35918</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BR&#211;COLI">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Br&#243;coli is a vegetable that is notable for its nutritional content. It contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams. Additionally, br&#243;coli is known to contain thiocyanates, which have the potential to inhibit the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells. This dual aspect of br&#243;coli highlights both its nutritional benefits and its possible effects on thyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4645</data>
      <data key="d7">810aa9da584a4e06831a6fc475427bf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMENDRAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Almendras, or almonds, are a type of nut recognized for their numerous health benefits and versatility in culinary applications. They are particularly noted for being a significant source of magnesium, which is essential for various bodily functions. Additionally, almonds are classified as a type of dried fruit that does not contain thiocyanates, meaning they do not interfere with iodine uptake by the thyroid gland. This makes them a healthy choice for those concerned about thyroid function. Overall, almendras are valued for their nutritional properties and their role in a balanced diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d3">1351</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4646</data>
      <data key="d7">2937d6c73af04bff8466add9b10c9c7d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AR&#193;NDANOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">AR&#193;NDANOS, commonly known as blueberries, are fruits that are notable for their nutritional properties. They contain oxalate, a compound that can contribute to the risk of kidney stone formation. However, it is important to note that blueberries do not contain thiocyanates, which means they do not affect the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells (tirocitos). This makes them a safe choice for individuals concerned about iodine absorption while still providing the health benefits associated with their consumption.</data>
      <data key="d2">171bf5a205ba13cbab91aab05e088040,e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4647</data>
      <data key="d7">bf36387e5e054881a6d1b526ebe3431a</data>
