      <data key="d7">0d8db232d62b4903bcd7902cebee4191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NODULO TIROIDEO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">NODULO TIROIDEO refers to a thyroid nodule, which is a growth that occurs within the thyroid gland. These nodules can be assessed for the potential presence of malignancy by examining their characteristics through ultrasound imaging.</data>
      <data key="d2">17db9c3996d806c3332ba2796ab7736f,cb3b93a50040c892ecf439582ebb6ac0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4656</data>
      <data key="d7">48580cc9c56b44d4aec5b80fdcd42f53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN ASSOCIATION OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGISTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists (AACE) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the field of endocrinology. AACE plays a crucial role in developing comprehensive clinical practice guidelines that assist healthcare professionals in the diagnosis and management of various endocrine disorders. This includes providing guidelines for the diagnosis and management of thyroid nodules and related conditions, as well as offering consensus statements on diabetes management. Additionally, AACE focuses on the medical care of patients with obesity, ensuring that practitioners have access to the latest recommendations and best practices in this area. Through these efforts, AACE aims to enhance the quality of care for patients with endocrine-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">0381a11415dca4cfeda74f1de745d6ae,1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0,d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f,e2091cc12f3e5cfae8cc2c1358cddc65</data>
      <data key="d3">1580</data>
