    </node>
    <node id="CANCER TREAT REVIEWS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer Treat Reviews is a journal that publishes critical reviews on cancer treatment, including syndromes like Cowden syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1662</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4706</data>
      <data key="d7">5891a9ee519449c0b930421404dcb109</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JOURNAL OF GENETIC COUNSELING">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Journal of Genetic Counseling publishes research and reviews related to genetic counseling, including studies on Cowden syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4707</data>
      <data key="d7">8c10a92faa2943b4ba2c6acd614034d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COWDEN SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cowden syndrome is a genetic condition associated with mutations in the PTEN gene, leading to an increased risk of various cancers.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d3">682</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4708</data>
      <data key="d7">360c8c151e3045568dd77e1ae3bff807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN2B">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN2B is a genetic syndrome characterized by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene, leading to multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2B. This condition significantly increases the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma, pheochromocytoma, and mucosal neuromas. MEN2B is recognized as the rarest and most aggressive form of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2), with medullary thyroid carcinoma often manifesting in the first or second decade of life. Due to the high risk of these malignancies, early surgical intervention, specifically prophylactic thyroidectomy, is typically required for affected individuals. The syndrome is associated with distinct phenotypic features that further characterize its presentation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce,2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">971</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">4709</data>
      <data key="d7">b539b149bdf8455d9d836b475f641f76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">PTEN is a tumor suppressor gene that plays a crucial role in regulating cell growth and apoptosis. It is particularly significant in the context of Cowden syndrome, a genetic disorder characterized by multiple benign tumors and an increased risk of certain cancers. Mutations in the PTEN gene are identified in approximately 80% of cases involving germline mutations associated with Cowden syndrome. This highlights the importance of PTEN in both the diagnosis and understanding of this syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce,6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">682</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4710</data>
      <data key="d7">29136d5f0b48495782b2d2da9112d551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACINI ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Pacini et al. is a reference cited in the context of the frequency of familial cases of medullary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1662</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4711</data>
      <data key="d7">b407144193e04eab980bb9f35d554c21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a specific type of thyroid cancer that originates from the parafollicular C cells of the thyroid gland. This cancer is notable for its association with elevated levels of calcitonin, which can be used for diagnosis and monitoring of the disease. Medullary thyroid carcinoma is also linked to certain genetic syndromes, including Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2B (MEN2B) and Cowden syndrome. The disease has the potential to metastasize, making careful monitoring and treatment essential. It is the subject of various studies and clinical trials aimed at improving understanding and management of the condition. At the time of diagnosis, patients may already present with metastases, highlighting the aggressive nature of this cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce,53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,de6e1d8ac9f422acb17fd26b77b485da</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">4712</data>
      <data key="d7">60515de32f1b48468dc66bfd0f8a1e28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUIDELINES TASK FORCE ON THYROID NODULES AND DIFFERENTIATED THYROID CANCER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">This task force is part of the American Thyroid Association and is responsible for developing management guidelines for thyroid conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1662</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4713</data>
      <data key="d7">8c7b2d31dde24041af93fe5c35c4c31e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE COWDEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Cowden es un s&#237;ndrome raro de tumores asociado a mutaciones en el gen PTEN. Se caracteriza por la formaci&#243;n de hamartomas en m&#250;ltiples tejidos y un riesgo aumentado de desarrollar varios tipos de c&#225;ncer. Entre los tipos de neoplasias m&#225;s comunes asociadas con este s&#237;ndrome se encuentran el c&#225;ncer de mama, tiroides y endometrio. Adem&#225;s, el s&#237;ndrome puede provocar un crecimiento hamartomatoso en tejidos como el colon y la piel.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">682</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4714</data>
      <data key="d7">3b02afd5d6f64ff1af7dbfa409fef67c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tiroidectom&#237;a is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of all or part of the thyroid gland. It is particularly recommended for patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma, especially in cases where specific mutations, such as those associated with MEN2B, are present. This procedure can have implications for parathyroid hormone levels, potentially affecting the patient's overall hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4715</data>
      <data key="d7">0d7307bd20c04ca2af575718b1e5dded</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFADENECTOM&#205;A CERVICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La linfadenectom&#237;a cervical es un procedimiento que se debe realizar junto con la tiroidectom&#237;a total en el tratamiento del carcinoma medular de tiroides.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4716</data>
      <data key="d7">be691319c9a041dd924ec4f77df5038f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M918T MEN2B">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La mutaci&#243;n M918T MEN2B es una mutaci&#243;n gen&#233;tica asociada con un alto riesgo de carcinoma medular de tiroides y requiere cirug&#237;a profil&#225;ctica antes del primer a&#241;o de vida.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">679</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4717</data>
      <data key="d7">724e40c618b34d7bbeb4e41c2d50bfde</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GU&#205;A DE CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES DE LA ATA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La Gu&#237;a de carcinoma medular de tiroides de la ATA proporciona recomendaciones sobre el manejo y tratamiento de las mutaciones que pueden causar carcinoma medular de tiroides.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4718</data>
      <data key="d7">227747edc45543bdba936173192bebf2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HAMPARTOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los hamartomas son crecimientos benignos que pueden presentarse en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Cowden, afectando tejidos como colon y piel.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d3">679</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4719</data>
      <data key="d7">727935c9170d4b15ad74011a8f0b6939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCITONINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcitonin, or "calcitonina" in Spanish, is a hormone produced by the C cells of the thyroid gland. It plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body by inhibiting osteoclastic bone resorption, which helps to decrease bone loss. Calcitonin is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as osteoporosis, although its effectiveness in reducing fractures remains a topic of debate. Additionally, it is employed in managing severe hypercalcemia.

The hormone is also important in the context of medullary thyroid carcinoma, particularly in patients with potential RET mutations. In these cases, calcitonin levels are monitored to assess the risk of developing this type of cancer, as well as to evaluate the progression of the disease and the necessity for surgical intervention. Overall, calcitonin serves both therapeutic and diagnostic purposes in various medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">4720</data>
      <data key="d7">73b8fc08fcfa45a7a89c55dd810f2f8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOPARATIROIDISMO, or hypoparathyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone, which results in low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise as a complication following total thyroidectomy and should be considered in surgical management. Additionally, hypoparathyroidism can lead to various complications, including hypomagnesemia and osteoporosis, due to its impact on calcium and phosphate metabolism. The condition may occur due to several factors, including the treatment of thyroid disease and infiltrative diseases that affect the parathyroid glands.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">4721</data>
      <data key="d7">d08ae88b2d2f491c90996cc03be06c32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
