      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">e775708e66a97968834f7476479a21b2</data>
      <data key="d3">427</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4732</data>
      <data key="d7">852a48f57cde468894d93ee79863c884</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN2A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN2A, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 2A, is a genetic condition characterized by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This autosomal dominant disorder is primarily associated with a high risk of developing specific tumors, including medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC), which occurs in 100% of patients, bilateral pheochromocytomas in approximately 50% of cases, and hyperparathyroidism in 20-30% of individuals. The syndrome necessitates early preventive treatment due to its association with these malignancies, particularly medullary thyroid carcinoma and pheochromocytoma. Overall, MEN2A is a significant health concern that requires careful monitoring and management to mitigate the risks of these endocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,4433d2fdc6ba080efa0cf63e8603172a,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">4733</data>
      <data key="d7">e704d7d7d18b4d95bc772c37b34298e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Thyroid Association (ATA) is an organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of thyroid diseases. Among its key contributions, the ATA offers specific guidance for the diagnosis and management of medullary thyroid carcinoma, including risk stratification associated with various genetic mutations. The ATA's resources are essential for healthcare professionals in effectively addressing thyroid-related conditions and ensuring optimal patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140,b1ce0d940909277d321ee55bffcc69b3</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
