      <data key="d7">a065f5a266ec4763a808d3499e3cddff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PET 18F-FDG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PET 18F-FDG is a type of positron emission tomography (PET) that is utilized primarily for staging and evaluating treatment responses in patients with thyroid cancer. It plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of various cancers, particularly differentiated thyroid cancer. PET 18F-FDG detects metabolic activity in tumors, providing valuable insights into cancer progression and treatment efficacy. However, it is important to note that this imaging method has low sensitivity for detecting medullary thyroid carcinoma, which may limit its effectiveness in certain cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f</data>
      <data key="d3">181</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4745</data>
      <data key="d7">872f5bf252614a43900c1b099f7c7552</data>
    </node>
    <node id="I-131">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">I-131 is a radioactive isotope used in the treatment of thyroid cancer.</data>
