    <node id="CERVICAL ULTRASOUND">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cervical ultrasound is a diagnostic imaging technique that plays a crucial role in the management of patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. It is recommended for all such patients to assess for lymph node metastases, providing essential information for treatment planning. Additionally, cervical ultrasound serves as a key imaging method to evaluate the outcomes of surgical interventions in these patients, helping to monitor their post-operative status and detect any potential complications or recurrences.</data>
      <data key="d2">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
