      <data key="d6">4768</data>
      <data key="d7">8a100bcea2ab4cb68cb9c285693e8d1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MRI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) is a sophisticated medical imaging technique that provides detailed visualization of internal structures within the body. It is particularly effective in identifying tumors and assessing various conditions, including the evaluation of hepatic iron stores. Additionally, MRI plays a crucial role in detecting bone metastases, especially in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. This versatility makes MRI an invaluable tool in modern medical diagnostics.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,e376d9f50b7608f5b6d1f88877fde59e</data>
      <data key="d3">365</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4769</data>
      <data key="d7">4577fe4ba0ac475ba9c0a297ee80024b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BONE SCINTIGRAPHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone scintigraphy is an imaging technique used to detect bone metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d2">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4770</data>
      <data key="d7">d5a8939d70c14240b7dbf905c0f14cfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE CALCITONINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Niveles de calcitonina are used as a biomarker to assess the presence and extent of medullary thyroid carcinoma, with higher levels indicating more advanced disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d3">1337</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4771</data>
      <data key="d7">28f02704c36b414b819480be23992eb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAMMAGRAF&#205;A &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gammagraf&#237;a &#243;sea is an imaging technique used to assess bone metastases in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d2">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d3">1337</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4772</data>
      <data key="d7">0329bf138041421694d05d7ca605cd11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER MEDULAR DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">CANCER MEDULAR DE TIROIDES, also known as medullary thyroid carcinoma (CMT), is a type of cancer that can arise in patients who have mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This condition is particularly associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2).</data>
      <data key="d2">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d3">1337</data>
