    <node id="CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a tumor marker utilized in the medical field, particularly in the assessment of various cancers, including medullary thyroid carcinoma. It is often used in conjunction with calcitonin to evaluate the prognosis of patients diagnosed with this specific type of cancer. CEA serves as an important indicator in monitoring disease progression and treatment response in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d3">967</data>
