    <node id="BRITISH JOURNAL OF CANCER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The British Journal of Cancer is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of cancer. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including clinical studies, meta-analyses, treatment, prevention, and epidemiology. Notably, the journal also features studies focused on specific types of cancer, such as medullary thyroid carcinoma outcomes. Through its comprehensive coverage, the British Journal of Cancer serves as a significant resource for researchers and healthcare professionals in the field of oncology.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,bef1f848ac9b922f7361b740210a8314</data>
