    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD M&#211;RBIDA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">"OBESIDAD M&#211;RBIDA," or morbid obesity, is a severe medical condition characterized by excessive body weight that significantly increases the risk of various health complications. This condition has been discussed in clinical cases, highlighting its impact on patients who often experience multiple attempts at weight loss and may ultimately require surgical intervention, such as bariatric surgery. Morbid obesity is resistant to conventional treatment methods and is associated with serious health issues, including diabetes and an increased risk of pancreatic cancer. Management of morbid obesity often necessitates specific nutritional strategies, particularly for critically ill patients, to address the complex health challenges it presents. Overall, morbid obesity is a critical health concern that demands comprehensive medical attention and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f,195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
