      <data key="d7">eb117c1124014ea1b507bc712d0bae06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA refers to dietary fiber, a crucial component of nutrition that plays a significant role in promoting digestive health. It is found in various food sources, including whole grains, legumes, vegetables, and fruits. Dietary fiber aids in digestion, helps stabilize blood sugar levels, and contributes to the reduction of energy density in foods, which can promote feelings of fullness and assist in weight control.

Research indicates that dietary fiber is particularly beneficial for the elderly, as it is linked to improved overall health. Additionally, it is essential for children's diets, supporting their digestive health. As a type of carbohydrate that the body cannot digest, dietary fiber is important for gut health and is associated with various health benefits, including the potential to inhibit the absorption of adenine, which may lower uric acid levels.

FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA is recognized in dietary recommendations and guidelines, such as those from the World Health Organization (WHO), emphasizing its importance in maintaining a balanced and healthy diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,2689c33de87eab465f004fff5f0530b8,51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,91131751d701592a597bae807e00c1dc,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
