    <node id="INSTITUTE OF MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Institute of Medicine (IOM) is a nonprofit organization that operates as part of the National Academy of Sciences. It is dedicated to providing expert advice on health and medicine to decision-makers and the public. The IOM offers a wide range of services, including the development of clinical guidelines, nutritional guidelines, and dietary reference intakes for various nutrients. It focuses on delivering evidence-based information regarding health and nutrition, which encompasses dietary recommendations and requirements. Additionally, the IOM defines adequate fiber intake during pregnancy and lactation, ensuring that its health recommendations and guidelines are grounded in scientific evidence. Overall, the Institute of Medicine plays a crucial role in shaping health policy and providing comprehensive health recommendations, including those related to dietary intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">03b7a89c9bb1dfd115acef377b491808,561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,6907c82f1f024ed1b75f6aea88c47b3e,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,7ff62e1dc423be2f4b2fe08546751d0d,88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95,9303a85464d02f1cc012aaca21edf9bb,b46fefa9f55d92c74acad101fc4f812e,b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,f5d0adafea7d8fe8216c624188ddad04</data>
