      <data key="d1">Madrigal refers to multiple contexts, primarily associated with the capital city of Spain, Madrid, where a relevant manual was published. Additionally, Madrigal is a fictional character used in clinical nutrition discussions, representing a patient scenario that aids in understanding nutritional guidelines. Furthermore, Madrigal is also recognized as an author who has contributed to the analysis of quality indicators in nutritional support, highlighting the importance of effective nutritional practices in clinical settings.</data>
