    <node id="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Obstrucci&#243;n Mec&#225;nica Intestinal is a medical condition characterized by a blockage in the intestine that prevents the normal passage of contents. This blockage can lead to complications that may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition, particularly when oral feeding is not feasible. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish, highlighting its significance in medical discussions across different languages.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4898</data>
      <data key="d7">5c18b227f94143c3b2ee052954b510fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALTERACIONES DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL" refers to disorders that impact the normal movement of the intestines. These conditions can significantly disrupt gastrointestinal function, potentially resulting in severe cases that necessitate parenteral nutrition. The term encompasses various issues that hinder the intestines' ability to move food and waste effectively, highlighting the critical nature of these disorders in relation to nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4899</data>
      <data key="d7">9572bb28de6a411f8570e1ba999e0917</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFECTACI&#211;N EXTENSA DE LA MUCOSA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition where extensive damage to the intestinal lining occurs, leading to malabsorption and the potential requirement for parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4900</data>
      <data key="d7">f9bd96ab1ca04ccfa8c5827e66d055af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS &#937;-3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cidos Grasos &#969;-3, commonly known as omega-3 fatty acids, are essential fats recognized for their numerous health benefits. They play a significant role in optimizing post-exercise recovery and are often utilized in conjunction with other medications to lower triglyceride levels. Omega-3 fatty acids are included in fourth-generation lipid emulsions for parenteral nutrition, where they are valued for their anti-inflammatory properties and potential to improve nutritional outcomes in patients. They are particularly noted as a first-choice treatment for individuals with severe hypertriglyceridemia, especially those who cannot use fibrates due to contraindications. The primary components of omega-3 fatty acids, such as EPA and DHA, are derived from fish oil and are administered in high doses to effectively manage hypertriglyceridemia. Overall, omega-3 fatty acids are essential for maintaining health and are integral to various therapeutic applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f46d79bcfab2143f045659e11be171b,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,746fad557197bebe72763efd23a9e0e2,75a4b2d504de480eaef247aa682bfd05,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d3">597</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4901</data>
      <data key="d7">a16c616a877147519645b9909f7437f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINO&#193;CIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Amino&#225;cidos are organic compounds that serve as the fundamental building blocks of proteins, playing a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are essential nutrients included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the protein needs of patients, particularly those undergoing dialysis or requiring nutritional support. Amino acids are vital for maintaining lean body mass, supporting protein synthesis, and facilitating muscle synthesis and energy production. Additionally, they are important for growth and development, especially in pediatric nutrition. It is noted that specific requirements for amino acids may increase during physical exercise, highlighting their significance in both health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,bb9a5c32408b601f9ecedc2a2b82d6b6,dcb97f7ffdb0aea3051bdf53e04bcc29,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">4902</data>
      <data key="d7">0730296b8f604120b5de28c701cb4bc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCONATO C&#193;LCICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcium gluconate is a form of calcium used in parenteral nutrition to avoid calculation errors associated with calcium chloride.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
