      <data key="d6">4903</data>
      <data key="d7">c405b3af3ee04a1cb5636a935962059b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">F&#237;stula intestinal refers to an abnormal connection between the intestine and another organ or the skin. This condition can arise from various medical issues, including diseases such as cancer or complications following surgical procedures. The presence of an intestinal fistula may lead to significant health implications, including the potential for intestinal failure. In some cases, patients with this condition may require parenteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient delivery, as the abnormal connection can disrupt normal digestive processes. Overall, intestinal fistulas represent a serious medical concern that necessitates careful management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">41dee7570059d609c99074f155d4f927,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
