    <node id="ESTEATOSIS HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ESTEATOSIS HEP&#193;TICA, also known as hepatic steatosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fat in the liver. This condition is commonly observed in patients receiving parenteral nutrition, particularly after the initiation of such treatment. Additionally, hepatic steatosis can occur in patients with cystic fibrosis, where it is often associated with severe malnutrition. The condition highlights the importance of monitoring liver health in individuals undergoing parenteral nutrition and those with specific health challenges like cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
