      <data key="d7">070d55e346a8458d8c308c66dd82e6d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFOL&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">FOSFOL&#205;PIDOS, or phospholipids, are a class of lipids that serve as a major component of all cell membranes, playing a crucial role in maintaining cellular structure and function. They are essential for various cellular processes, including those that require copper for their synthesis. Additionally, phospholipids are included in some nutritional products, highlighting their importance not only in cellular biology but also in nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">242f6cf03a4c50245e71fee58de41d18,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
