      <data key="d6">4918</data>
      <data key="d7">b9508e67923945d9a7c0361bf2fd2132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STAPHYLOCOCCUS AUREUS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Staphylococcus aureus is a common bacterium known for its role in causing various infections, particularly in patients with medical devices such as catheters. It is recognized as a significant pathogen in catheter-related infections and can lead to severe conditions, including sepsis, especially in individuals with central venous catheters. Additionally, Staphylococcus aureus has been proposed to act as a trigger for low-grade inflammation, which is associated with weight gain. This dual role highlights its importance not only as a cause of infections but also in potential metabolic implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">959173b0e9d9c5ea2edabff579240462,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">1200</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4919</data>
      <data key="d7">074dff45198247f5aad19d45ccf7fa42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAT&#201;TER VENOSO CENTRAL TUNELIZADO TIPO HICKMAN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Hickman catheter is a type of central venous catheter used for long-term intravenous access, often in patients requiring parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704</data>
      <data key="d3">1200</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4920</data>
      <data key="d7">903464293f934ce683be5af4b49f098f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CULTIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cultivos refer to microbiological tests performed to identify infections, such as those caused by Staphylococcus aureus in patients with catheters.</data>
      <data key="d2">9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">4921</data>
      <data key="d7">9e7b2719ed3b49db8ed2a07a320f4190</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ETANOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ETANOL, also known as ethanol, is a chemical compound with diverse applications and implications in both medical and recreational contexts. In medical settings, ETANOL is utilized for sealing catheters to prevent infections, highlighting its importance in maintaining sterile conditions in healthcare. However, it is also associated with potential health risks; studies have indicated that ethanol may be linked to an increased risk of thrombosis in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. Beyond its medical uses, ethanol is widely recognized as a type of alcohol found in beverages, characterized by its high energy density and consumption in various forms. This dual nature of ETANOL underscores its significance in both health-related applications and social practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d,7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d3">1922</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4922</data>
      <data key="d7">56c8c0b956f548c087d705fd7a91167a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAUROLIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TAUROLIDINA is a compound utilized in medical settings primarily for its prophylactic properties in catheter sealing, aimed at reducing infection rates. It is particularly recommended for use in parenteral nutrition to prevent infections and complications associated with central venous catheters. Overall, TAUROLIDINA serves as an important measure in the prevention of infections linked to catheter use.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf,e5313f692c0a8259c93be803a704413c</data>
      <data key="d3">766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">4923</data>
      <data key="d7">8022b900ce30409cafbc419b46c53fdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEDUGLUTIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TEDUGLUTIDE is a medication currently under investigation for the treatment of intestinal failure, specifically targeting conditions such as Short Bowel Syndrome. It works by promoting intestinal adaptation, which enhances the absorption of nutrients in the intestines. This mechanism helps to reduce the reliance on parenteral nutrition in patients suffering from intestinal failure, thereby improving their overall nutritional status and quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe</data>
