    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA" (NAD) refers to a medical intervention that provides nutritional support to patients in their own homes. This approach encompasses the administration of nutrition through enteral (NED) or parenteral (NPD) methods, aimed at improving or maintaining the nutritional status of patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. NAD is recognized as a significant advancement in the care of chronic patients, allowing them to receive necessary nutritional support without the need for hospitalization. 

By enabling patients to remain in their familiar social and family environments, NAD not only enhances their nutritional status but also helps reduce potential complications associated with inadequate nutrition. The provision of nutritional support at home is documented by the Grupo NADYA-SENPE and is essential for those who cannot meet their dietary needs through natural foods. Overall, "NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA" plays a crucial role in the management of patients requiring specialized nutritional therapy in a home setting.</data>
      <data key="d2">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2,123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,4cf0c8d0f4e711be85d16ee71317aa4e,4e86ca77481672995a03989d321652bc,7e3e2024996e402fc0ab62933ab9417b,9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,a6ccbda174f6599eeeb2e4cdb00db5f2,ed9b8701ef76cf4813eccfc58d6be998,efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1924</data>
