      <data key="d5">40</data>
      <data key="d6">4945</data>
      <data key="d7">3ec455d29c23460681ffed3d06f6d12a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIC">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The Short Bowel Syndrome (SIC) is a medical condition characterized by the loss of a significant portion of the small intestine, resulting in the preservation of less than 115 cm of intestinal length. This condition severely impacts the absorption of nutrients, leading to nutritional deficiencies and various complications. Patients with SIC may require parenteral nutrition to maintain their health due to the insufficient intestinal length for adequate nutrient absorption. The syndrome often arises following surgical resections of the intestine, which can further exacerbate the challenges in nutrient uptake. Additionally, SIC is associated with the evaluation of intestinal anatomy and complications such as abscesses, highlighting the importance of medical organizations focused on the diagnosis and treatment of intestinal conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368,5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
