    <node id="MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD Y CONSUMO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD Y CONSUMO" is the governmental body in Spain tasked with regulating and ensuring public health. This ministry is responsible for the creation of the National Registry of Advance Directives and oversees public health policies and guidelines, which encompass various areas including mental health and eating disorders. Additionally, the ministry plays a role in consumer protection and provides access to Cochrane reviews in Spanish, further supporting its commitment to public health and informed consumer choices.</data>
      <data key="d2">14ad20b4ac1105ca21faf20e4978fb5a,70e6c476cce381861896b5a6be2f39ad,8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239,9934fdd98a0d66fb3ff7ac1b56b18460,9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210</data>
