    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE WERNICKE-KORSAKOFF">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is a neurological disorder caused by thiamine deficiency, often associated with chronic alcoholism and malnutrition, leading to confusion and memory issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239</data>
      <data key="d3">1099</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4968</data>
      <data key="d7">1d0bb99d3702436b9e51ce488dc386cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDUCACI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Educaci&#243;n nutricional" refers to the process of educating patients about proper dietary practices to manage their health conditions, particularly diabetes. It encompasses teaching individuals about healthy eating habits and the significance of nutrition in maintaining overall health and preventing diseases. Additionally, nutritional education plays a crucial role in the treatment of patients with eating disorders, as it helps them understand and adopt healthy eating patterns. Overall, educaci&#243;n nutricional is essential for promoting better health outcomes through informed dietary choices.</data>
      <data key="d2">46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239,dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
      <data key="d3">1109</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">4969</data>
      <data key="d7">8266e2ab487a4d2e8ff6d2ce631ab56c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BULIMIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bulimia Nervosa (BN) is an eating disorder characterized by recurrent episodes of binge eating, during which individuals consume large quantities of food in a short period. This behavior is typically followed by inappropriate compensatory actions aimed at preventing weight gain, such as self-induced vomiting, excessive exercise, or the misuse of laxatives. The disorder can lead to a range of serious health complications and often goes unnoticed by those around the affected individual. Treatment for Bulimia Nervosa generally requires a multifaceted approach that includes psychotherapy and medication to address both the psychological and physical aspects of the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457,3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c,ecf27310ce7cbfc335117dafa5d4eefb</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">4970</data>
      <data key="d7">97dc3b6db3e64fbb97056e3796d82e16</data>
    </node>
