    <node id="TOPIRAMATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Topiramate, also known as Topiramato, is a versatile medication primarily used for the prevention of seizures and migraine management. In addition to its neurological applications, Topiramate has demonstrated effectiveness in addressing uncontrolled eating and related psychological issues in patients with eating disorders. It is particularly noted for its appetite-suppressing properties. When combined with fentermina, Topiramate is indicated for weight loss in patients who have not met their weight loss goals with lower doses. This combination therapy has received approval from the FDA for the treatment of obesity, although it has not been approved by the EMA. Furthermore, there are considerations regarding Topiramate's potential effects on kidney stone formation, which is an important aspect to monitor during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1415</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">4975</data>
      <data key="d7">3b0695d1efe240b595845ee3de135931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METOTREXATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Methotrexate, known as Metotrexato, is a medication that serves as a chemotherapy agent and immune system suppressant, primarily used in the treatment of cancer and autoimmune diseases. Its mechanism of action involves the inhibition of folate reductase, which can lead to a deficiency of folic acid and may contribute to anemia, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, Methotrexate is classified as a cytotoxic agent that interacts pharmacokinetically with glutamine, potentially enhancing its intratumoral concentrations and therapeutic effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6,88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25</data>
      <data key="d3">644</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">4976</data>
      <data key="d7">2941ed17917d4028bf650ac64ecb0b72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISONIACIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Isoniazid is a medication that can cause a deficiency of vitamin B6 due to malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25</data>
      <data key="d3">610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4977</data>
      <data key="d7">28c9eee59b9348a9a26ec66079d552f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLESTIRAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Colestiramina, also known as Cholestyramine, is a medication that is primarily used to help control cholesterol levels in patients. However, it is important to note that the use of Colestiramina can lead to malabsorption of fat-soluble vitamins and other nutrients, which may have implications for the patient's overall nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2,8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
