    <node id="SEH-LELHA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SEH-LELHA is an organization dedicated to promoting health and wellness through various initiatives. It offers a food table and nutritional composition calculator as part of its comprehensive nutrition program, which aids individuals in understanding their dietary intake. Additionally, SEH-LELHA provides guidelines for physical exercise prescription specifically tailored for patients with cardiovascular risk, emphasizing the importance of physical activity in managing health. As a scientific society, the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Hipertensi&#243;n Arterial (SEH-LELHA) also offers online tools for dietary intake calculations and nutritional analysis, further supporting individuals in making informed dietary choices.</data>
      <data key="d2">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,6da89a24c60015649c1d669e4e23fb2d,91ec0cc70cd70254acbbebc425f84163</data>
      <data key="d3">858</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">4993</data>
      <data key="d7">5a94f347e08d45e280ca4f59d65cfe49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENILCETONURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fenilcetonuria, also known as phenylketonuria (PKU), is a metabolic disorder characterized by high levels of phenylalanine in the blood due to a deficiency in the enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH). This condition requires lifelong dietary management to control phenylalanine levels in the body, as excessive accumulation can lead to serious health issues, including intellectual disability and malformations in fetuses of mothers with elevated phenylalanine levels during pregnancy. Fenilcetonuria is recognized as the most common inherited metabolic disorder resulting from this enzymatic deficiency, necessitating careful monitoring and dietary restrictions to prevent toxic effects associated with phenylalanine accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38,3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">30</data>
      <data key="d6">4994</data>
      <data key="d7">41a92ddaede0478ba1017035c001b21a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA, also known as tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4), is a crucial cofactor for the hydroxylases of phenylalanine, tyrosine, and tryptophan. It plays a significant role in the treatment of mild phenylketonuria, a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process phenylalanine. Tetrahydrobiopterin can enhance tolerance to phenylalanine in patients suffering from this condition, thereby aiding in the management of their dietary restrictions and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4995</data>
      <data key="d7">634d940be9ec4228917285b6a482318a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FENILALANINA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Foods high in phenylalanine include meats, fish, eggs, cheese, nuts, soy, and aspartame, which must be restricted in the diet of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4996</data>
      <data key="d7">717f38c1bce74121acc7276e50273742</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" refers to the complex community of microorganisms residing in the human digestive tract, which plays a vital role in health and disease. This intestinal microbiota is crucial for various metabolic processes, including energy absorption, appetite regulation, and the maintenance of the immune system. It has been identified as a key factor in the development of metabolic disorders such as obesity and diabetes.

Research indicates that the composition and variations of the intestinal microbiota can significantly differ between Western and Eastern populations, influenced by dietary patterns. Diets rich in animal protein can alter the microbiota's composition, highlighting the relationship between diet and microbial communities in the gut. Additionally, the microbiota undergoes significant changes during early life, influenced by factors such as the method of birth and dietary intake.

Overall, the intestinal microbiota is essential for energy homeostasis and has profound implications for human health, particularly in relation to metabolic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">01eb4b96cd8e6a886ebc313171922a77,0a78cb1d502baf0116e4326e7fbcae41,0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7,1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,341d121c4c1cc1e4fb942e4b23f6931b,5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,89e0e7fac6984f367ae1649e9eaab7d7,90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021,9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872,b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,e189588f51b4bb84b3621a1f846d07bc,ffdc08ec09899ab7dfa255af4cecac1c</data>
      <data key="d3">1002</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">44</data>
      <data key="d6">4997</data>
      <data key="d7">eed1ba615a1c43f69a5be0f8d17c544f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPHENYLALANINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperphenylalaninemia is a clinical condition characterized by elevated levels of phenylalanine in the blood, often due to a metabolic defect.</data>
      <data key="d2">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4998</data>
      <data key="d7">45a69b1ee09847a29e2272eee90fb82f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINO&#193;CIDOS EXENTOS DE FENILALANINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Commercial preparations of amino acids free of phenylalanine are used for supplementation in patients with phenylketonuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">4999</data>
      <data key="d7">ddb4d685f48a49ba905b6062b8563fbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Short-chain fatty acids (SCFA) are fermentation products derived from dietary fiber, playing significant roles in energy metabolism and the reduction of inflammation. They are produced during the fermentation process of dietary fiber by the intestinal microbiota, highlighting their importance in gut health and overall metabolic functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d3">1002</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5000</data>
      <data key="d7">1b51b5c5eb404849a2d537457e532ee4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCUDERO &#193;LVAREZ E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Escudero &#193;lvarez E is an author who contributed to the research on dietary fiber and its implications in clinical nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33</data>
      <data key="d3">518</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5001</data>
      <data key="d7">5410325963b24a07a83bbebf68150ef1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUARNER AGUILAR F">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Guarner Aguilar F is an author who contributed to the research on probiotics, prebiotics, and symbiotics in clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33</data>
      <data key="d3">518</data>
