      <data key="d6">5002</data>
      <data key="d7">d134d0f2c34740e6974df8e353839c46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fallo intestinal, or intestinal failure, is defined as a condition characterized by a significant reduction in intestinal function, falling below the minimum threshold necessary for the adequate absorption of macronutrients, water, and electrolytes. This impairment necessitates intravenous supplementation to maintain health and support growth. In essence, individuals with intestinal failure are unable to absorb sufficient nutrients through their intestines, which leads to the requirement for nutritional support to ensure their well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed,f7d56bac9cc29e47690669e812094c99</data>
      <data key="d3">657</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">20</data>
      <data key="d6">5003</data>
      <data key="d7">2a85c4c754d24a2dbb9b14a7cee6adfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A ASOCIADA A NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Liver damage associated with home parenteral nutrition, which can occur due to various factors related to intestinal failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
