    </node>
    <node id="ILEOSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A surgical procedure that creates an opening in the abdominal wall for waste to exit the body, often leading to significant fluid loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5005</data>
      <data key="d7">aa9de8c5111d4d31aac11ab13d145658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIDAL CASARIEGO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Vidal Casariego is a medical professional who co-authored the guidelines on short bowel syndrome and its management.</data>
      <data key="d2">4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5006</data>
      <data key="d7">e265a3d03d6446009fa5e31e9067290c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCLACEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypocalcemia is a condition characterized by low calcium levels in the blood. It can be associated with vitamin D deficiency, which is essential for calcium absorption. Additionally, hypocalcemia may occur in patients with chronic kidney disease, where it is often related to phosphorus levels. This condition highlights the interconnectedness of calcium, vitamin D, and kidney function in maintaining overall mineral balance in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5007</data>
      <data key="d7">5167d94cf2d740ac9fa4e0f1c2f5dd64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENSITOMETR&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DENSITOMETR&#205;AS refers to the practice of conducting bone density tests periodically to assess the health of bones, particularly in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. These tests are essential for monitoring the effects of parenteral nutrition on bone health, ensuring that any potential issues can be identified and addressed in a timely manner.</data>
      <data key="d2">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5008</data>
      <data key="d7">d987cadd041f49d2b24dec50c2db8df4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T-SCORE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">T-SCORE is a measurement utilized in bone density tests to evaluate bone health. It serves as a comparative metric, assessing an individual's bone density against that of a healthy 30-year-old. Lower T-scores indicate a higher risk of osteoporosis, making it a crucial tool in diagnosing osteoporosis, particularly in patients with specific conditions such as FQ (cystic fibrosis).</data>
      <data key="d2">d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5009</data>
      <data key="d7">378735e7f9674342a582da4d0ad2d482</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTHI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parathyroid hormone levels that can indicate calcium metabolism issues, often monitored in patients with vitamin D deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5010</data>
      <data key="d7">4a8d03d290d24c62a1b489c492a857c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The level of calcium in the blood, which is crucial for diagnosing conditions related to bone health and vitamin D status.</data>
      <data key="d2">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5011</data>
      <data key="d7">473991fbf5bc450d879b09ae933af85a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOMALACIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">OSTEOMALACIA is a condition characterized by the softening of bones, primarily due to a prolonged deficiency of vitamin D, which affects calcium absorption and leads to weakened bones. This condition can manifest in various contexts, including in patients with Wilson's disease and those receiving home parenteral nutrition. Osteomalacia results in symptoms such as bone pain and overall weakness, and it involves the deterioration of bone matrix mineralization, contributing to the fragility of the skeletal structure.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d3">617</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5012</data>
      <data key="d7">26e4e80419c04e739b99fd8e31ad709d</data>
    </node>
