      <data key="d7">ecb2694ed9214d1182862275303089d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEHISCENCIA DE ANASTOMOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DEHISCENCIA DE ANASTOMOSIS refers to anastomotic dehiscence, which is a complication that occurs post-surgery. This condition indicates a failure of the surgical connection between two segments of the intestine, leading to a separation of the anastomosis. It is a significant concern in surgical procedures involving intestinal reconnections, as it can result in serious complications for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ee948dc4ddfdc75daa8fe7db9bb471e,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d</data>
