    <node id="ANEMIA PERNICIOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia perniciosa is an autoimmune condition characterized by impaired absorption of vitamin B12. This disorder can be associated with various other autoimmune diseases, including autoimmune thyroid diseases and type 1 diabetes mellitus. Additionally, it is frequently linked to primary adrenal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,4eb5a5cd6147917dd1380d49c613a78b,71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1491</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5041</data>
      <data key="d7">1782413d322145d393c6ec512232c0e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN X-ALD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The GEN X-ALD gene is responsible for encoding a protein that functions as a peroxisomal membrane transporter, specifically involved in the transport of fatty acids within cells. Mutations in the X-ALD gene result in a condition known as adrenoleukodystrophy, which is characterized by the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids due to impaired transport. This genetic alteration can lead to severe neurological and adrenal dysfunction, highlighting the critical role of the X-ALD gene in cellular fatty acid metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,4eb5a5cd6147917dd1380d49c613a78b</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5042</data>
      <data key="d7">a0bc3c58ca6b4e6b8aa45cbe284edeb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME PLURIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2 es una condici&#243;n gen&#233;tica que se caracteriza por la presencia de m&#250;ltiples enfermedades autoinmunitarias, incluyendo insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0</data>
      <data key="d3">1491</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5043</data>
      <data key="d7">81f7d62c78e54afab282aa74e69035fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HLA-DR3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HLA-DR3 is a genetic region that is associated with type 2 autoimmune polyglandular syndrome, as well as other autoimmune diseases. It is classified as a histocompatibility antigen, playing a significant role in the immune system's response.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1106</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5044</data>
      <data key="d7">e3887a881ea545b6bf3e900f9cdcbc53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes tipo 1 es una enfermedad cr&#243;nica que afecta la forma en que el cuerpo metaboliza la glucosa, resultando en niveles elevados de glucosa en sangre. Esta condici&#243;n es una enfermedad autoinmunitaria, en la cual el sistema inmunol&#243;gico ataca las c&#233;lulas productoras de insulina en el p&#225;ncreas, lo que lleva a la incapacidad del cuerpo para producir insulina. Como resultado, los pacientes con diabetes tipo 1 requieren un manejo y tratamiento de por vida para controlar sus niveles de glucosa en sangre.

Adem&#225;s, la diabetes tipo 1 es un &#225;rea principal de investigaci&#243;n para Mart&#237;n Cuesta Hern&#225;ndez, quien se enfoca en su tratamiento y gesti&#243;n. Tambi&#233;n se ha observado que la diabetes tipo 1 puede tener una mayor prevalencia entre pacientes con trastornos alimentarios, como la Anorexia Nerviosa. Aunque menos frecuentemente, esta enfermedad puede estar asociada con el s&#237;ndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,75a4b2d504de480eaef247aa682bfd05,a549bdc3929c5dd7a613c6900a0fe90e,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831</data>
      <data key="d3">1048</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5045</data>
      <data key="d7">c5490f783bcc420db1511b788a76b25e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO OV&#193;RICO PRECOZ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El fallo ov&#225;rico precoz es una condici&#243;n que puede estar asociada con el s&#237;ndrome pluriglandular autoinmune tipo 2, afectando la funci&#243;n reproductiva en mujeres j&#243;venes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0</data>
      <data key="d3">1491</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5046</data>
      <data key="d7">ece2f155d8734001ac7d6db344acfb28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna" is a comprehensive medical textbook edited by a team of experts including Kasper DL, Hauser SL, Jameson JL, Fauci AS, Longo DL, and Loscazo J. This authoritative reference provides extensive information on various aspects of internal medicine, covering a wide range of medical conditions and treatments. Notably, it includes detailed discussions on adrenal disorders, such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia and pheochromocytoma, as well as other endocrine disorders. The textbook is widely recognized and utilized in the medical field for its thorough guidelines and insights into internal medicine, making it an essential resource for healthcare professionals.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,41b6e4025d59564d7881f459e230639d,4433d2fdc6ba080efa0cf63e8603172a,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3,bb2f48277736ce24d1ff0310a682376d,bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d3">1283</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">30</data>
      <data key="d6">5047</data>
      <data key="d7">218053756ae34948a75b7abf62a49e10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOCRINE SOCIETY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Endocrine Society is a professional organization dedicated to advancing research and education in the field of endocrinology. It plays a crucial role in establishing clinical practice guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of various endocrine disorders. These guidelines encompass a wide range of conditions, including adrenal insufficiency, primary aldosteronism, congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, pheochromocytoma, paraganglioma, and hypoglycemic disorders. 

Additionally, the Endocrine Society provides specific guidelines for the treatment and management of gender-dysphoric individuals, as well as for conditions such as hirsutism. The organization is committed to ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest evidence-based practices for the effective management of endocrine disorders, thereby improving patient care and outcomes. 

In summary, the Endocrine Society serves as a vital resource for clinicians, offering comprehensive guidelines that address a broad spectrum of endocrine conditions, thereby enhancing the quality of care in this specialized field.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,4433d2fdc6ba080efa0cf63e8603172a,46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5,4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58,7f3df1437755b60344fdffd2ef3b8a9e,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0,bb2f48277736ce24d1ff0310a682376d,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">5048</data>
      <data key="d7">0782d8b01839401883310e0db34a959b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOX3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A gene associated with certain rare causes of adrenal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
