    </node>
    <node id="ALDOSTERONA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Aldosterona, also known as aldosterone, is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium and potassium levels in the body. It is particularly relevant in the context of adrenal disorders and is involved in the evaluation of adrenal masses. Aldosterona functions by increasing sodium retention, which in turn helps to regulate blood pressure and maintain fluid balance. Its secretion is often elevated in conditions such as obesity, highlighting its impact on blood pressure regulation. Additionally, a deficiency in aldosterone is linked to primary adrenal insufficiency, underscoring its importance in overall electrolyte balance and cardiovascular health. The hormone activates mineralocorticoid receptors, further contributing to its role in sodium retention and blood pressure management.</data>
      <data key="d2">261db9bb173f461ca4f26fd087d3da2a,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,8eb2b7021402eb440fe88889b78c2785,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">1330</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5050</data>
      <data key="d7">b1a9189e19ad4e7ea47c2e9e172e9831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POMC">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Proopiomelanocortin (POMC) is a precursor polypeptide that plays a crucial role in the production of several important hormones. When mutated, POMC can lead to isolated adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) deficiency, which can have significant physiological implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
      <data key="d3">997</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5051</data>
      <data key="d7">09cefda7fdda4078be7b6d9c89eb8184</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TBX19">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A gene that, when mutated, can cause isolated ACTH deficiency, affecting adrenal function.</data>
      <data key="d2">c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
