    <node id="WILLIAMS TEXTBOOK OF ENDOCRINOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology" is a comprehensive medical textbook edited by Melmed S, Polonsky KS, Larsen PR, and Kronenberg HM. It serves as a key reference in the field of endocrinology, providing detailed information on a wide range of endocrine disorders and their treatments. The textbook covers various aspects of endocrinology, including physiological processes and specific disorders such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, Cushing's syndrome, pheochromocytoma, and osteoporosis. Additionally, it addresses pediatric disorders of sex development and the role of vitamin D in health. The "Williams Textbook of Endocrinology" is recognized for its thorough exploration of hormonal disorders, making it an essential resource for medical professionals and students in the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,1de72f0ea3a981289854857b691b52af,313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,41b6e4025d59564d7881f459e230639d,5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c,7f3df1437755b60344fdffd2ef3b8a9e,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638,fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
