    </node>
    <node id="KASPER DL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kasper DL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, particularly noted for his contributions to the medical textbook "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine." This comprehensive work includes extensive information on various adrenal disorders, such as Cushing's syndrome, hyperaldosteronism, and congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Kasper DL's expertise is highlighted in the context of disorders of the adrenal cortex, making significant contributions to the understanding and treatment of these conditions. His role as an editor and contributor to this influential textbook underscores his importance in the medical community, particularly in the study and management of adrenal disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,85eef7ed9c9b92d86939a6687ea2acfd,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf,dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb</data>
