    <node id="ADENOMA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ADENOMA refers to a benign tumor of glandular origin that can occur in various glands, including the adrenal glands, parathyroid glands, and pituitary gland. In the adrenal glands, adenomas are characterized by their lipid content and are often detected through imaging techniques. These tumors may be associated with incidental findings during imaging studies. In the parathyroid glands, adenomas can lead to primary hyperparathyroidism, resulting in elevated calcium levels in the blood (hypercalcemia). Additionally, adenomas in the pituitary gland can cause conditions such as Cushing's syndrome due to excessive production of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). Overall, adenomas are benign tumors that can have significant clinical implications depending on their location and the hormones they may affect.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5071</data>
      <data key="d7">6a53dff0a1114c0f894fb903e139e6b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPRARENAL GLANDS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The adrenal glands are responsible for producing hormones like cortisol and androgens, and can be affected in cases of Cushing's syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b</data>
