      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Longo DL is a prominent author and editor in the field of internal medicine, recognized for his contributions to the esteemed medical textbook "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine." This comprehensive work addresses a wide range of medical conditions, including disorders related to the adrenal cortex, such as Cushing's syndrome and congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Longo DL's expertise is reflected in his editorial role, where he collaborates with other experts to provide in-depth information on various medical topics, including pheochromocytoma. His involvement in this influential reference underscores his significant impact on the field of internal medicine.</data>
