      <data key="d6">5113</data>
      <data key="d7">885ce32d231c429fb68c9ac641c65639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL (HTA)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertension Arterial (HTA) is a medical condition characterized by consistently high blood pressure, which can lead to various health complications. It may be associated with adrenal disorders and is often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas. This condition requires careful monitoring and management to prevent potential health risks associated with elevated blood pressure levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1339</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5114</data>
      <data key="d7">2efdc3750d164c55bec534f88dc03fd6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION RESISTANT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Resistant hypertension refers to high blood pressure that remains above target levels despite the use of multiple antihypertensive medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1339</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5115</data>
      <data key="d7">93f4347ec7f14450a3022ba08a0397e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIMARY ALDOSTERONISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary aldosteronism is a medical condition characterized by excessive secretion of aldosterone, which is a common cause of secondary hypertension. This condition results in elevated blood pressure and can lead to electrolyte imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,41b6e4025d59564d7881f459e230639d</data>
      <data key="d3">1339</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5116</data>
      <data key="d7">01863c9c8ffe4b9f8386844d6a1e2508</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#201;XICO DF">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Mexico City (DF) is the capital of Mexico, known for being a significant hub for medical publications and guidelines. It is notable for the publication of the Spanish edition of Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, which underscores its importance in the medical field.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,41b6e4025d59564d7881f459e230639d,8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3</data>
