      <data key="d6">5117</data>
      <data key="d7">3b7034629bfc4d71bc9459a6dc65f21a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertension arterial (HTA) is a specific type of hypertension that affects the arteries, resulting in an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases. It is recognized as a significant risk factor associated with diabetes, further elevating the likelihood of developing cardiovascular complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e</data>
      <data key="d3">1372</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5118</data>
      <data key="d7">5cbd9b8f941d4a1cbefd444091b906a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALDOSTERONE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aldosterone is a steroid hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium and potassium levels in the blood. This regulation is significant as it influences blood pressure. The secretion of aldosterone is suppressed when there are high levels of deoxycorticosterone acetate (DOCA) present in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0,1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c</data>
      <data key="d3">1330</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5119</data>
      <data key="d7">63347b79e3bc45b48733c78e98a06e95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTENSION RESISTENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Resistant hypertension refers to high blood pressure that remains above target levels despite the use of multiple antihypertensive medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5120</data>
      <data key="d7">af829dd8bdd24ed08264db841782a8fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE APNEA-HIPOXIA DEL SUE&#209;O">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sleep apnea-hypopnea syndrome is a disorder characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep, which can contribute to hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d2">05edb31ec01c621a00d71bd5868784e0</data>
