    </node>
    <node id="HIPOPOTASEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOPOTASEMIA, also known as hypokalemia, is a medical condition characterized by low levels of potassium in the blood. This electrolyte disturbance can significantly affect muscle function and heart rhythm, leading to symptoms such as muscle weakness and potential cardiac issues. It is particularly common in patients receiving enteral nutrition, where low potassium levels can result in various health complications. Management of hipopotasemia may involve dietary adjustments, specifically a high potassium diet, in certain medical situations. Overall, hipopotasemia is often associated with nutritional deficiencies and requires careful monitoring and treatment to prevent serious health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,814d394c907e59b29a5f0d9e82aed423,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3,cff2f16dff598dbf0bff544091c77837,d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1492</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5131</data>
      <data key="d7">c8c6729b4fe6479ebb16d66c3b549d82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERALDOSTERONISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperaldosteronismo es un trastorno endocrino en el que hay una producci&#243;n excesiva de aldosterona, lo que puede resultar en hipertensi&#243;n y desequilibrios electrol&#237;ticos.</data>
      <data key="d2">b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5132</data>
      <data key="d7">2eb55c14a4d045cfaa110431ef45cb74</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPIRONOLACTONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Espironolactona, also known as spironolactone, is a potassium-sparing diuretic that plays a crucial role in managing various medical conditions. It is primarily used to help the body eliminate excess fluid, making it effective in treating heart failure and hypertension. Additionally, espironolactona is utilized in the management of hyperaldosteronism, a condition characterized by excessive production of the hormone aldosterone.

Beyond its diuretic properties, spironolactone functions as an aldosterone antagonist, which means it blocks the effects of aldosterone, a hormone that can lead to fluid retention and increased blood pressure. This mechanism is particularly important when assessing the aldosterone/renin plasma activity ratio, as the medication must be withdrawn prior to testing to ensure accurate results.

Moreover, spironolactone has applications in hormone therapy, particularly for transgender women, as it blocks androgen receptors, contributing to the desired hormonal effects in this population. Overall, espironolactona is a versatile medication with significant implications in both cardiovascular health and hormone therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3,3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,b9bf0b94c01d3dfa9ef4cbce09dd7ec3</data>
      <data key="d3">1340</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5133</data>
      <data key="d7">c6fbad6df5074b66a04787f69e7098d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YOUNG WF, JR.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Young WF, Jr. is a distinguished medical expert recognized for his significant contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the diagnosis and management of primary aldosteronism and endocrine hypertension. He has authored numerous works that enhance the understanding of these conditions. Additionally, Young WF, Jr. has made substantial contributions to the literature regarding pheochromocytoma, focusing on its clinical presentation, diagnosis, and treatment. His expertise is reflected in his involvement in various medical guidelines and publications, establishing him as a prominent figure in the medical community.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3,41b6e4025d59564d7881f459e230639d,973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9,a0b43d4a377fca32f55f83fd79e3d9e1</data>
