    <node id="MET&#193;STASIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MET&#193;STASIS refers to the process by which cancer cells spread from the original tumor site to other parts of the body. This phenomenon can involve various organs, including the liver, bones, and adrenal glands. Additionally, metastasis may be associated with the carcinoid syndrome, which is a group of symptoms that can occur in patients with certain types of cancer. Overall, MET&#193;STASIS signifies a critical aspect of cancer progression, highlighting the ability of cancer cells to invade and affect multiple areas beyond their initial location.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5187</data>
      <data key="d7">2d04db774dc64d358fd3002864f5322c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIELOLIPOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mielolipoma is a rare benign tumor of the adrenal gland composed of adipose tissue and hematopoietic elements.</data>
      <data key="d2">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5188</data>
      <data key="d7">e36a959d9ea24aaf8d2e5e0a194dc344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUISTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Quistes are fluid-filled sacs that can occur in the adrenal glands and may be discovered incidentally.</data>
      <data key="d2">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5189</data>
      <data key="d7">ca08c292868845e9a3c973dbe190a6a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Society of Endocrinology is a professional organization dedicated to providing clinical practice guidelines for the management of endocrine disorders. This includes specific guidelines for the management of adrenal incidentalomas, which are incidental findings of adrenal tumors that may or may not be clinically significant. The organization plays a crucial role in standardizing care and improving outcomes for patients with various endocrine conditions, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest evidence-based practices in the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,1bfdc8a3b2272265ee6fd132fcf3a8ce,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf</data>
      <data key="d3">1334</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">5190</data>
      <data key="d7">43cfe4f61dba4c97bddad8315272d16d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUSHING SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A hormonal disorder caused by prolonged exposure to high levels of cortisol, which can be detected through various tests.</data>
      <data key="d2">8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7</data>
      <data key="d3">1332</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5191</data>
      <data key="d7">b74787b363a24259993e43776aff2364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FASSNACHT M">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Fassnacht M is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. He is actively involved in the management guidelines for these conditions and participates in endocrinology research. Additionally, Fassnacht M is recognized as one of the authors of the article addressing the management of adrenal incidentalomas within the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf</data>
