    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE CUSHING SUBCL&#205;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Cushing subcl&#237;nico es un estado transitorio que puede revertir y que puede progresar a un s&#237;ndrome de Cushing manifiesto, aunque su evoluci&#243;n no est&#225; clara y es poco frecuente.</data>
      <data key="d2">a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d3">1283</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5196</data>
      <data key="d7">31b32b3714a146b58f41d5e0cc04208b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HORMONAS SEXUALES, or sex hormones, are crucial hormones that regulate the development and functioning of reproductive organs. This group includes hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone), LH (luteinizing hormone), and testosterone, as well as androgens and estrogens. The measurement of sex hormones is particularly important in clinical scenarios where there is a suspicion of adrenal carcinoma, as their secretion by a benign adenoma is quite rare. In cases of adrenal incidentalomas, where there is a clinical suspicion of malignancy, it is essential to evaluate the potential secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors. Thus, the assessment of these hormones plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of conditions related to the adrenal glands and reproductive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,209bcca22090a109f52e26657bf3c999,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5197</data>
      <data key="d7">b38d25109d87415b855d167a607e2087</data>
    </node>
