      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition characterized by excessive production of aldosterone, often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d3">1330</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5212</data>
      <data key="d7">852d1424e3c240859e3815a369ec3e04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIUR&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Diur&#233;ticos, or diuretics, are medications that promote the excretion of water and salts from the body through urine. They are commonly used in the treatment of conditions such as hypertension and edema, as they help to alleviate fluid retention. Diuretics can significantly affect sodium levels and are relevant in the context of diagnosing conditions like SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion). Additionally, they may influence the evaluation of adrenal function in patients with adrenal incidentalomas and can impact electrolyte balance, particularly in individuals with adrenal insufficiency.

These medications can also affect magnesium reabsorption in the kidneys, potentially leading to changes in magnesium levels and causing conditions such as hypomagnesemia or hypermagnesiuria. Furthermore, diuretics are known to promote the loss of potassium, which is an important consideration in their use. Overall, diur&#233;ticos play a crucial role in managing fluid balance and electrolyte levels in various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a,addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508,fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5213</data>
      <data key="d7">5c42317f08194dd8b83750dda3fa739b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTAGONISTAS DE LA ALDOSTERONA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A class of medications that block the effects of aldosterone, relevant in the context of hyperaldosteronism and adrenal incidentalomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d3">1492</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5214</data>
      <data key="d7">2598950158f649e8800a86005750abe3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS ADRENALINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormones produced by the adrenal glands that are involved in the body's stress response, relevant in the context of adrenal tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5215</data>
      <data key="d7">cfbd0882ee154e32a5b1c81821f75fc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMA BENIGNO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A benign tumor of the adrenal gland that rarely secretes sex hormones.</data>
      <data key="d2">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5216</data>
      <data key="d7">1307986e9438498c9b8143792083af3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDROXIPROGESTERONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">17-hidroxiprogesterona is a hormone that should be measured in cases of bilateral adrenal incidentalomas to rule out congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1333</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5217</data>
      <data key="d7">ccfbe0b10f894a1c8a5cd581f0b872ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "suprarrenal" refers to the adrenal glands, which are located above the kidneys. These glands play a crucial role in the endocrine system, producing important hormones such as cortisol and adrenaline. In the context of medical conditions, suprarrenal glands are often discussed in relation to incidentalomas and disorders associated with them. Additionally, they are known to be the site where tumors such as feochromocitomas and paragangliomas can develop. Overall, the suprarrenal glands are vital components of the body's hormonal regulation and are involved in various health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">984</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5218</data>
      <data key="d7">0759e3a97e2b45b0bb44fafcf92f8033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAASSNACHT M">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Fassnacht M is an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1334</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5219</data>
