    <node id="ELSEVIER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Elsevier is a global information analytics business that specializes in scientific, technical, and medical content. It is recognized for its extensive portfolio in scientific publishing, which includes a variety of medical textbooks and journals. Among its notable publications is the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology. While some of its operations are based in Madrid, Elsevier's influence and reach extend worldwide, making it a prominent entity in the field of medical and scientific literature.</data>
      <data key="d2">47ba8105b81c59f81a9038446898d200,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664,ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
      <data key="d3">1300</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5238</data>
      <data key="d7">d62b14a69a0c4c4e85ae15367f98456c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMOR PRODUCTOR DE CATECOLAMINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumors that produce catecholamines can lead to various clinical symptoms and are significant in the context of adrenal disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5239</data>
      <data key="d7">ea18c61a31ab4716b2a905463d18552c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN RET">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The RET gene is associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia and is significant in the context of genetic testing for patients with feochromocytomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5240</data>
      <data key="d7">b540b3a4dbcf48478df67378c9283834</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN VHL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GEN VHL refers to the VHL gene, which is a crucial tumor suppressor gene. When mutated, it is associated with various neoplasms, including feocromocitoma. The VHL gene is also linked to von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, a genetic condition that can lead to the development of multiple tumors. This gene plays a significant role in the genetic assessment of patients with adrenal tumors, highlighting its importance in both cancer predisposition and clinical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2,5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5241</data>
      <data key="d7">e324ab14d2d647a4a256b184fc495260</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN SDHB">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SDHB gene is involved in the development of certain tumors, including paragangliomas and is relevant for genetic testing in affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5242</data>
      <data key="d7">e1bc031330f1445ab17ce39c8b861a4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN SDHC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SDHC gene is associated with hereditary paraganglioma and is important for genetic counseling in families with a history of these tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">5fd3de876d776b591d7dfd812aa2873c</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5243</data>
      <data key="d7">f1bc44bdd9924979851cb08fac23ab6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE VON HIPPEL-LINDAU">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome is a genetic disorder characterized by an increased risk of developing various tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors and pheochromocytomas. This condition is inherited in an autosomal dominant manner, meaning that it can be passed down from one generation to the next. Individuals with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome may experience a range of tumor types due to the genetic mutations associated with the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5244</data>
      <data key="d7">a840619947c54448b569338fcfe467f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIA ENDOCRINA M&#218;LTIPLE TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 2 (MEN 2) is a genetic syndrome characterized by a hereditary predisposition to the development of tumors in endocrine glands. This condition significantly increases the risk of developing various endocrine tumors, including feocromocitomas, which are tumors of the adrenal glands. MEN 2 encompasses a range of endocrine neoplasms, highlighting the importance of genetic screening and monitoring for individuals affected by this syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5245</data>
      <data key="d7">2fae44d1a75f4d1a969a2e5ba9b96ce3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROFIBROMATOSIS DE TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurofibromatosis type 1 is a genetic disorder that can be associated with feocromocitomas, although less commonly than the other syndromes mentioned.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5246</data>
      <data key="d7">d72e16a9bf744bf783e7e98243c9e06f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SDHC">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SDHC is a gene that is associated with the development of hereditary pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, which are types of tumors that arise from adrenal gland tissue and nerve tissue, respectively. This gene plays a significant role in the cellular response to hypoxia, which is a condition characterized by insufficient oxygen levels. Additionally, SDHC is involved in mitochondrial function, indicating its importance in energy production and cellular metabolism. Overall, SDHC is crucial in the pathogenesis of these tumors and in maintaining normal cellular functions under varying oxygen conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5247</data>
      <data key="d7">ca97d2e52a704d9c9b7952cf26ab65f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VHL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The VHL gene, located on chromosome 3p25-26, encodes a protein that plays a crucial role in regulating hypoxia-induced proteins. Mutations in the VHL gene are associated with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome, a genetic condition that significantly increases the risk of developing pheochromocytomas, as well as other tumors. This syndrome highlights the importance of the VHL gene in tumorigenesis and its role in the body's response to low oxygen levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">5248</data>
      <data key="d7">9a1ed364efff47eaaff21678a5753a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SDHD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SDHD is a gene that is significant in the development of paragangliomas and pheochromocytomas, particularly in the context of hypoxia. It is one of the key genes associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, and it plays a crucial role in mitochondrial function.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5249</data>
      <data key="d7">79c8a3abe7e1411b80522cd72c30bd1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARAGANGLIOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Paragangliomas are tumors that can occur alongside feocromocitomas and are associated with the secretion of catecholamines, affecting patients with certain genetic syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5250</data>
      <data key="d7">dd4a8587267b41a7b388f209d65acaef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GENES DE SUSCEPTIBILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Genes of susceptibility are genetic factors that increase the risk of developing feocromocitomas and paragangliomas, including SDHB, SDHC, and others.</data>
      <data key="d2">c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5251</data>
      <data key="d7">7b94120374a54ddabfea53cd85a5e498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANATOMOPATOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anatomopathological report refers to the examination of tissues to diagnose diseases, including tumors like feocromocitomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5252</data>
      <data key="d7">8f5d2d0008c84bc3bce4a034f6c14a68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Genetic study refers to the analysis of genes to identify mutations associated with feocromocitomas and paragangliomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5253</data>
      <data key="d7">78347ca977f54b879aec18cda9352842</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurofibromatosis Type 1 is a genetic disorder that can also be associated with feocromocitomas, although less frequently than other syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5254</data>
      <data key="d7">b97a91c4d3d446ec8eea9121a582e866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATOVASTATINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Atorvastatin is a medication that can cause false positives in the measurement of catecholamines and metanephrines.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">976</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5255</data>
      <data key="d7">7d92cb596ca34ed7b41d403ee6b2b0df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANFETAMINAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">ANFETAMINAS, also known as amphetamines, are a class of stimulant drugs that can elevate catecholamine levels in the body. This elevation can lead to false positives in laboratory tests, particularly in the assessment of catecholamines in patients suspected of having pheochromocytomas. The elimination of anfetaminas can be enhanced through dietary acidification. Historically, anfetaminas were utilized starting in 1936 for weight loss purposes; however, their use was discontinued due to concerns over dependence, abuse, and potential cardiovascular effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1413</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5256</data>
      <data key="d7">8aabf76fb255457c8375d0cfae41ee4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COCA&#205;NA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cocaine, known as "coca&#237;na" in Spanish, is a drug that can cause elevated levels of catecholamines and metanephrines in the body. This elevation can result in false positives during medical tests, particularly complicating the diagnosis of pheochromocytomas, which are tumors that can affect catecholamine levels. The presence of cocaine in the system can therefore interfere with accurate medical assessments and diagnoses.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606,c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">976</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5257</data>
      <data key="d7">75402b3878b6466bbe0badf3c6e0536a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPRARRENALCTOM&#205;A BILATERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bilateral adrenalectomy is a surgical procedure performed to remove both adrenal glands, often due to the presence of feocromocitomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5258</data>
      <data key="d7">99c6bce63d29403c95438c2afc943853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HALLAZGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Findings refer to the results obtained from imaging studies or tests that indicate the presence of feocromocitomas or paragangliomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d3">975</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5259</data>
      <data key="d7">c587bbf95b8044c794e324f30ef72d5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RET">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">RET is a proto-oncogene that plays a significant role in multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2). Mutations in the RET gene are linked to various endocrine disorders, particularly MEN2A and MEN2B, which increase the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and pheochromocytoma. The gene's involvement in these conditions highlights its importance in endocrine tumorigenesis, making it a critical focus for understanding and managing these syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab,c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">971</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5260</data>
      <data key="d7">bb8aae1db5ae441c81405ecaaf859cf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NF1">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">The NF1 gene is associated with neurofibromatosis type 1 and can lead to the development of pheochromocytomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5261</data>
      <data key="d7">d97b279c9f88422dac5190336a0ca9c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAX">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">The MAX gene is involved in the regulation of cell growth and is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5262</data>
      <data key="d7">bc1756186ad84328a4f98b5aa8058aa6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TMEM127">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">The TMEM127 gene is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas and is involved in cellular signaling.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d3">985</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5263</data>
      <data key="d7">08f44af08db8433196eb3615a47654b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAC CON CONTRASTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TAC con contraste is a specific imaging test used to detect tumors, particularly pheochromocytomas, due to its high spatial resolution.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5264</data>
      <data key="d7">c186d2c794724083b96ef94cacbfae55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAMMAGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gammagraf&#237;a is a functional imaging test used to detect pheochromocytomas and paragangliomas, providing information about tumor activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5265</data>
      <data key="d7">46cfc92de0fc4197b5d76f651e749402</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUORODESOXIGLUCOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fluorodesoxiglucosa is a radiotracer used in PET scans, considered more sensitive for detecting metastases of malignant paragangliomas compared to MIBG.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5266</data>
      <data key="d7">96c4d4050fe3410db6b20abfc6031df7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LABETALOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Labetalol is a medication that can interfere with catecholamine testing, leading to false positives in patients suspected of having pheochromocytomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5267</data>
      <data key="d7">dbaa87084fe948aba532dc72206e9d9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTOQU&#205;MICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inmunohistoqu&#237;mica is a technique used to analyze tissue samples for the presence of specific proteins, which can help identify mutations in genes related to pheochromocytomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5268</data>
      <data key="d7">bb00ecd27dd742d0be3b846734298e5b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPECIFICIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Especificidad refers to the ability of a test to correctly identify patients without pheochromocytomas, which is crucial for accurate diagnosis.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5269</data>
      <data key="d7">1efeae405de84b4183f5a4eddcd0e2a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MART&#205;N L&#211;PEZ DE LA TORRE CASARES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mart&#237;n L&#243;pez de la Torre Casares is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, with a Doctorate in Medicine from the University of Bologna and currently serves as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at the Hospital Universitario Virgen de las Nieves in Granada.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1452</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5270</data>
      <data key="d7">083ecb002ee94c798a9bdbb9c0d06e49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSIDAD DE BOLONIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The University of Bologna is where Mart&#237;n L&#243;pez de la Torre Casares obtained his Doctorate in Medicine in 1990.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1452</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5271</data>
      <data key="d7">d78ce916519545ca8607cd82fb03c172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSIDAD INTERNACIONAL MEN&#201;NDEZ PELAYO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Universidad Internacional Men&#233;ndez Pelayo is where Mart&#237;n L&#243;pez de la Torre Casares completed his Master's in Clinical Management of Endocrinology and Nutrition in 2018.</data>
      <data key="d2">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1452</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5272</data>
      <data key="d7">abd90fa8e646448bb360fd5fe2744ff6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Central precocious puberty, known in Spanish as "pubertad precoz central," is a condition characterized by the early activation of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis. This condition leads to the development of secondary sexual characteristics before the age of 8 in girls and before the age of 9 in boys. The early onset of puberty in this manner signifies a significant deviation from the typical developmental timeline, prompting further medical evaluation and potential intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5273</data>
      <data key="d7">11833e0ffa5f47ae822a5506a0b34e34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STYNE DM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Styne DM es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la fisiolog&#237;a y los trastornos de la pubertad.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d3">1300</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5274</data>
      <data key="d7">cbd770da76b74072b0c9e681a25d27be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRUMBACH MM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grumbach MM es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la fisiolog&#237;a y los trastornos de la pubertad.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d3">1300</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5275</data>
      <data key="d7">c8c2d939e17143b0a28b00f52c2d2c87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LOGOS DE LA GNRH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los an&#225;logos de la GnRH son tratamientos utilizados para estabilizar la progresi&#243;n puberal en casos de pubertad precoz central.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5276</data>
      <data key="d7">97c813f50bf047bfa49bc3c75650b859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJE HIPOT&#193;LAMO-HIP&#211;FISO-GONADAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El eje hipot&#225;lamo-hip&#243;fiso-gonadal es un sistema hormonal que regula la funci&#243;n reproductiva y se activa durante la pubertad.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5277</data>
      <data key="d7">54ccb3ac6bde408ba6f334340f94d24c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDAD &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La edad &#243;sea es un indicador del desarrollo f&#237;sico de un ni&#241;o y se utiliza para evaluar la pubertad precoz al compararla con la edad cronol&#243;gica.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5278</data>
      <data key="d7">7b44918c912e4098aec13609d8a19aff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIPTORELINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Triptorelina, also known as triptorelin, is a synthetic analog of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH). It is primarily utilized in the treatment of central precocious puberty, a condition characterized by the early onset of puberty. In addition to its use in managing this specific condition, triptorelina is also employed in various medical treatments related to hormone-related disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5279</data>
      <data key="d7">8903a3e68d054ae6828720affaf8b4aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEURPORELINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LEURPORELINA is an analog of Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone (GnRH) that is primarily utilized in the treatment of central precocious puberty. It is known for its effectiveness in managing hormone-sensitive conditions, similar to another synthetic analog of GnRH, leuprolide. Both compounds serve important roles in regulating hormonal activity and are used in various medical treatments related to hormonal imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d2">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5280</data>
      <data key="d7">d3bd56f03d2f4fecb0a77e2e61490d9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GONADOTROFINAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">GONADOTROFINAS son hormonas que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n del sistema reproductivo. Estas hormonas, que incluyen la LH (hormona luteinizante) y la FSH (hormona foliculoestimulante), estimulan las g&#243;nadas y son fundamentales para la producci&#243;n de testosterona y esperma. En pacientes con insuficiencia gonadal, como aquellos que padecen el s&#237;ndrome de Turner, los niveles de gonadotrofinas tienden a aumentar, lo que indica su importancia en la funci&#243;n reproductiva y el desarrollo sexual.</data>
      <data key="d2">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df,a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1292</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5281</data>
      <data key="d7">4491220d98fa41f1815da173f78c9973</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LUFORAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Luforan is a medication used in tests to assess the function of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis.</data>
      <data key="d2">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5282</data>
      <data key="d7">cdf066586e8d464fa988e761ae0b70dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TANNER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tanner stages are a scale of physical development in children, adolescents, and adults, used to assess sexual maturity.</data>
      <data key="d2">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5283</data>
      <data key="d7">7dcecf67ad16404988e0a8aff4e4b5fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PUBERTAD PRECOZ PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Peripheral precocious puberty is a type of precocious puberty that occurs independently of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis.</data>
      <data key="d2">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5284</data>
      <data key="d7">148f21cd948e44edad41fd3450338e2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GONADOTROPINAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">GONADOTROPINAS son hormonas que pueden ser administradas en el tratamiento del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, con el objetivo de estimular la producci&#243;n de testosterona.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1297</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5285</data>
      <data key="d7">1f5e53fa232c4e85a2b0cdfb5817ad43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TESTOTOCICOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La testotoxicosis es una condici&#243;n que causa la maduraci&#243;n precoz de las c&#233;lulas de Leydig, resultando en un aumento de testosterona y desarrollo sexual temprano en varones.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5286</data>
      <data key="d7">0d0003da9e974a2f8859b68558c75f68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MCUNE-ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de McCune-Albright es un trastorno gen&#233;tico que se asocia con pubertad precoz, displasia fibrosa y manchas caf&#233; con leche en la piel.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1363</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5287</data>
      <data key="d7">708a49b2865446fb9d8aaf407458b29a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CELULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las c&#233;lulas de Leydig son c&#233;lulas en los test&#237;culos que producen testosterona, y su maduraci&#243;n puede ser prematura en casos de testotoxicosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5288</data>
      <data key="d7">ba67166c622b44068133d7bc4416dee0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIO MATERNO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El t&#237;o materno del paciente es mencionado como alguien que tambi&#233;n experiment&#243; pubertad precoz, sugiriendo un posible patr&#243;n hereditario en la familia.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5289</data>
      <data key="d7">3a0ad95fee874ab9ac8d85607e890871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE TESTOSTERONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los niveles de testosterona son cruciales para determinar el desarrollo sexual en varones y se miden para diagnosticar condiciones como la pubertad precoz.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5290</data>
      <data key="d7">0319b70458174c198eaf9cea80e11e7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECOGRAF&#205;A TESTICULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La ecograf&#237;a testicular es un procedimiento diagn&#243;stico utilizado para evaluar el tama&#241;o y la salud de los test&#237;culos en el contexto de la pubertad precoz.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5291</data>
      <data key="d7">9c1b69839501490a985eadb0890aec84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAC DE SUPRARRENALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La tomograf&#237;a axial computarizada (TAC) de suprarrenales es un estudio que se realiza para descartar patolog&#237;as tumorales en pacientes con pubertad precoz.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5292</data>
      <data key="d7">da5cd3092e4e4497abae7604d3958161</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RNM CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RNM CEREBRAL, or resonancia magn&#233;tica cerebral, is a medical imaging procedure utilized to assess the brain and identify abnormalities. This imaging technique is particularly effective in detecting conditions such as the absence of the olfactory bulb, which is associated with Kallman syndrome. Additionally, RNM CEREBRAL serves as an examination to evaluate potential neurological causes of precocious puberty. Through its advanced imaging capabilities, RNM CEREBRAL plays a crucial role in diagnosing various neurological conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5293</data>
      <data key="d7">b56ec3cdf4ad4cb4b515fcf534aedec2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANDROSTENDIONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Androstendiona is a steroid hormone that is less potent than some of its counterparts but has the ability to activate steroid receptors. It can be elevated in cases of precocious puberty and is measured to assess hormonal function.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5294</data>
      <data key="d7">ef591b2321814deaa750899ca66d5fe8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="17-OH-PROGESTERONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">17-OH-Progesterona is a hormone that plays a crucial role in assessing adrenal function. It is particularly relevant in diagnosing conditions associated with sexual differentiation and puberty. Additionally, 17-OH-Progesterona is measured to evaluate hormonal disorders in children experiencing precocious puberty. This hormone's levels can provide important insights into various endocrine disorders and developmental issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5295</data>
      <data key="d7">9df07384249141189821e71bd8d1fe62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">McCune-Albright syndrome is a condition characterized by fibrous dysplasia, caf&#233;-au-lait spots on the skin, and/or precocious puberty, affecting mostly females before the age of 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1295</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5296</data>
      <data key="d7">944e437e4edb47e99c1aa7daa2fcc09a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADRENARQUIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenarche is the period of maturation of the adrenal glands that leads to the production of androgens, which can cause early sexual development.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5297</data>
      <data key="d7">92da31c0b19745798a6c2932727201f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERANDROGENISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperandrogenism is a medical condition characterized by excessive levels of androgens in the body, particularly in females. This condition is often associated with disorders such as Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS). The elevated androgen levels can lead to a variety of symptoms, including hirsutism (excessive hair growth), irregular menstrual cycles, and virilization (development of male physical characteristics). Overall, hyperandrogenism manifests through various clinical symptoms that can significantly impact the health and well-being of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">5298</data>
      <data key="d7">fab7bc8232414640a975f0117415ac32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLITOROMEGALY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clitoromegaly is an abnormal enlargement of the clitoris, often associated with elevated androgen levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5299</data>
      <data key="d7">d779649d6a784d50b219518c870b8b42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPOTHALAMIC PULSE GENERATOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The hypothalamic pulse generator is a mechanism in the hypothalamus that regulates the release of GnRH in a pulsatile manner, influencing puberty onset.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1299</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5300</data>
      <data key="d7">16e7783eda6c495099ea52402eb717a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEMALE PATIENT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A 15-year-old female patient referred for consultation due to delayed onset of puberty, with a family history of early puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1299</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5301</data>
      <data key="d7">174f02ceae36448399444c84072e1125</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRECOCIOUS PUBERTY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Precocious puberty is the onset of secondary sexual characteristics before the typical age, often seen in females with McCune-Albright syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1295</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5302</data>
      <data key="d7">4a02f66a0fe5418e819967a5b4ec6a44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEMALE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Refers to individuals of the female sex, particularly in the context of the discussed conditions affecting puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1295</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5303</data>
      <data key="d7">e21c5cabdb264c42b8a0531d4ae5b1e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Refers to individuals of the male sex, particularly in the context of the discussed conditions affecting puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1295</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5304</data>
      <data key="d7">c007312703ea477ba1b2128502555004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROUS DYSPLASIA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1295</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5305</data>
      <data key="d7">0c70e512314e45b984aced9c667d8e9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROWLEY WF, JR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Crowley WF, Jr is a medical professional who contributed to the literature on the approach to patients with delayed puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5306</data>
      <data key="d7">4954f0c173584f1b9b1918ee0379106e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROTAN GE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Trotman GE is a medical professional who has written about delayed puberty in female patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5307</data>
      <data key="d7">9c042590e35d44718e87bab5298b0563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMENORREA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary amenorrhea is the medical term for the absence of menstruation in a girl by age 15, which can be caused by various conditions affecting the gonadal axis.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">5308</data>
      <data key="d7">2eb38c9405284ea488c9eaf7d71031df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HAMARTOMA HIPOTAL&#193;MICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypothalamic hamartoma is a benign tumor that can affect hormonal regulation and may be related to primary amenorrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5309</data>
      <data key="d7">927c6ebf7c7b48469ea3d7287b89775d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTRADIOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Estradiol is a form of estrogen that plays a crucial role in the regulation of the female reproductive system. It is essential for the development of female secondary sexual characteristics and is commonly measured to evaluate the onset of puberty. In individuals with aromatase deficiency, estradiol levels are typically low, which can lead to various developmental issues. Overall, estradiol is a vital hormone in female health and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5310</data>
      <data key="d7">a1196fdbc2094839bf4ccd7cbc63e62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO, or hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of sex hormones resulting from inadequate stimulation by the pituitary gland. This condition can be either congenital or acquired and often leads to delayed puberty due to the low levels of sex hormones.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266,4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">5311</data>
      <data key="d7">ce7bd184cfab4c4abfb8a58386085633</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETRASO CONSTITUCIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Constitutional delay is a temporary condition in which a child grows and develops more slowly than peers but eventually catches up, often affecting the timing of puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5312</data>
      <data key="d7">de7b7441596b4cb6ace841a0417b134d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARIOTIPO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Karyotype is a test that examines the number and structure of chromosomes, used to identify genetic abnormalities that may affect puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d3">1357</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5313</data>
      <data key="d7">220723dac3da4ae3865ac03f92391566</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE KALLMAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Kallman es un trastorno gen&#233;tico que causa hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo y anosmia, resultando en retraso puberal y amenorrea primaria en varones y mujeres.</data>
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5314</data>
      <data key="d7">69aa95f98581482bb2f8b887ed3f4afa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE KLINEFELTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Klinefelter es una condici&#243;n gen&#233;tica que afecta a hombres, caracterizada por la presencia de un cromosoma X adicional. Esta anomal&#237;a cromos&#243;mica puede resultar en hipogonadismo, que se manifiesta como una disminuci&#243;n en la producci&#243;n de hormonas sexuales, as&#237; como en un retraso en el desarrollo puberal. Adem&#225;s, el s&#237;ndrome puede influir en el desarrollo f&#237;sico y cognitivo de los varones, generando diversos problemas de salud. En resumen, el s&#237;ndrome de Klinefelter es una condici&#243;n que impacta tanto el desarrollo f&#237;sico como el cognitivo en los hombres debido a la presencia de un cromosoma X extra.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5315</data>
      <data key="d7">2d10707b82824533871e3e66b6758af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOSMIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La anosmia es la p&#233;rdida del sentido del olfato, que puede ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado con el s&#237;ndrome de Kallman.</data>
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5316</data>
      <data key="d7">878004246b464546bbb86b18725b0a0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRIPTORQUIDIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cryptorchidism, also known as "criptorquidia" in Spanish, is a medical condition characterized by the failure of one or both testicles to descend into the scrotum. This condition can have implications for hormonal and pubertal development in males.</data>
      <data key="d2">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5317</data>
      <data key="d7">3c2f0431eb564c738696f6372e5b28a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORQUIDOPEXIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ORQUIDOPEXIA, also known as orchidopexy, is a surgical procedure designed to correct cryptorchidism, a condition where one or both testicles fail to descend into the scrotum. The procedure involves placing the undescended testicle into the scrotum, allowing for proper positioning and function. This intervention is crucial for the health and development of the testicles, as it helps prevent potential complications associated with cryptorchidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5318</data>
      <data key="d7">e0b7c972d74a4f9badc4f2ae21d8bd1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETARDO PUBERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El retraso puberal es una condici&#243;n en la que el desarrollo f&#237;sico y hormonal de un adolescente se retrasa en comparaci&#243;n con sus pares.</data>
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">5319</data>
      <data key="d7">111a6e67616c4ed3bcdc4bb04d513ff6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOMAL&#205;AS M&#220;LLERIANAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Las anomal&#237;as m&#252;llerianas son malformaciones cong&#233;nitas del tracto reproductivo femenino que pueden resultar en amenorrea primaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5320</data>
      <data key="d7">da6c8d84d52c42c4ba9f21165b975bb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;RDIDA DE PESO/ANOREXIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La p&#233;rdida de peso significativa o la anorexia nerviosa pueden llevar a la amenorrea primaria debido a la alteraci&#243;n del equilibrio hormonal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5321</data>
      <data key="d7">4145c30125b041799d2901ac6dd4f6fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISGENESIA GONADAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d3">1361</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5322</data>
      <data key="d7">d1c006c54ec343b9a84b9be0c055b6bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE MAESTRE DE SAN JUAN-KALLMAN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Maestre de San Juan-Kallman es un trastorno gen&#233;tico que se caracteriza por hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo cong&#233;nito asociado a defectos olfativos, como anosmia o hiposmia.</data>
      <data key="d2">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5323</data>
      <data key="d7">a5f16695b2b04f139bf80a089ad38017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RNM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RNM, or Resonancia Magn&#233;tica, is an advanced imaging technique utilized to visualize internal structures of the body. This method is particularly valuable in diagnosing various medical conditions, including the Maestre de San Juan-Kallman syndrome. Additionally, RNM, which stands for Resonancia Magn&#233;tica Nuclear, plays a crucial role in assessing a patient's condition, especially in the detection of metastasis. Through its detailed imaging capabilities, RNM aids healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient care and treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d2">b00c312f46e790b32fe99743480f9e47,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5324</data>
      <data key="d7">ec835fade4254c428d96b10830b86bfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INHIBINA B">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La inhibina B es una prote&#237;na producida por las c&#233;lulas de Sertoli en los test&#237;culos, que regula la producci&#243;n de hormonas sexuales y se utiliza en el diagn&#243;stico de hipogonadismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5325</data>
      <data key="d7">338509a6d460435ea6e81ef3032f06b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA ANTIM&#220;LLERIANA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hormona antim&#252;lleriana es una hormona que se mide para evaluar la funci&#243;n ov&#225;rica y testicular, y puede ser un indicador en el diagn&#243;stico de hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo.</data>
      <data key="d2">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5326</data>
      <data key="d7">fe8989c979c244cf9604ab625519bb23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETARDO CONSTITUCIONAL DEL CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El retraso constitucional del crecimiento es una condici&#243;n en la que un ni&#241;o presenta un crecimiento m&#225;s lento de lo normal, pero eventualmente alcanza su altura esperada, a diferencia del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo.</data>
      <data key="d2">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5327</data>
      <data key="d7">34a097909a1244b5a38d1455c5a5104a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PALADAR HENDIDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Paladar Hendido, also known as cleft palate, is a congenital condition characterized by a malformation in the structure of the palate. This condition can significantly impact feeding, often necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate intake. Additionally, it has been noted that paladar hendido may occur in patients with hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, indicating a potential association with this hormonal condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5328</data>
      <data key="d7">f4caade83501445295427eec949398a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SORDERA NEUROL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La sordera neurol&#243;gica es una posible anomal&#237;a fenot&#237;pica asociada con el hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, que puede afectar la audici&#243;n de los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5329</data>
      <data key="d7">ebbbff4f69a2465395a72c539e99d59c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Klinefelter Syndrome is a genetic condition that affects males, characterized by the presence of an extra X chromosome. This chromosomal anomaly leads to a range of physical and reproductive abnormalities, including hypogonadism, which is a condition of reduced hormone production. Additionally, individuals with Klinefelter Syndrome may experience cognitive challenges and have an increased risk of certain health issues, including specific types of cancer. It is recognized as the most common chromosomal sexual pathology in males, highlighting its significance in genetic and medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,766fec9f74738cf0af53aee77d58dc78,81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0,bc241ef500af250c0f0e0253bf5ae0f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">5330</data>
      <data key="d7">d1fd461fe68a448d8f128d3c5059eb45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOEHM U">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Boehm U is one of the authors referenced in the European Consensus Statement on congenital hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5331</data>
      <data key="d7">957669c6306042c3bf2a72417c399948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROWLEY WF">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Crowley WF is referenced in the context of approaches to patients with delayed puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5332</data>
      <data key="d7">735b598cae1e494999743ab1e4ada746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADDISON'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Addison's disease is an autoimmune disorder that is frequently seen in patients with Klinefelter syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5333</data>
      <data key="d7">4e6012da56ec4a7982a5937acc6b0ffe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOEMBOLISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tromboembolism is a risk associated with Klinefelter syndrome due to thrombophilia.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5334</data>
      <data key="d7">58b8d06145e54e04b138a95088686fd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER OF THE PROSTATE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer of the prostate is a condition that individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at increased risk for compared to the general male population.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5335</data>
      <data key="d7">239707e5ee184fca80e9b20519fca927</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRONCHITIS CHRONIC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic bronchitis is a pulmonary disease that individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at higher risk of developing.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d3">1610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5336</data>
      <data key="d7">74374313b4854a3f82cf823277d0de6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRONCHIECTASIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bronchiectasis is a condition characterized by the permanent enlargement of parts of the airways in the lungs. This condition often results from infections or other factors that damage the airways. It is particularly relevant in patients with cystic fibrosis, as they may experience significant respiratory health issues due to this condition. Additionally, individuals with Klinefelter syndrome may also be predisposed to developing bronchiectasis, highlighting its association with various underlying health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4eb41f33f9aba3b8ecd3906de91a1345,5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68,cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
      <data key="d3">1044</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">5337</data>
      <data key="d7">67793491c15646feb8bedce43e55bed8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLIC SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic syndrome is a cluster of conditions that significantly increase the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes. This syndrome is often associated with various factors, including dietary habits, obesity, and insulin resistance. It is particularly prevalent in certain populations, such as patients with Klinefelter syndrome and individuals who have undergone liver transplantation. Management of metabolic syndrome can be achieved through dietary changes, with the Mediterranean diet being one effective approach. Overall, metabolic syndrome represents a serious health concern that requires attention to lifestyle and dietary factors to mitigate its associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,b602544ec2048878e40226cd2c0b29d4,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7,e2f9ec03a9b71e608bdd14455b0595a6,e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3,ea920d08266b329db73fb7b804bbb9ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">5338</data>
      <data key="d7">d81c6de96df144a09a80f73acce11de9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYSPLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal lipid levels in the body. It is often observed in patients with Klinefelter syndrome, a genetic disorder that affects male physical and cognitive development. Management of dyslipidemia typically involves both treatment and dietary modifications to help regulate lipid levels and reduce associated health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1646</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5339</data>
      <data key="d7">8c7729b92d7f4a6081f6781207cf8e5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANCER OF THE BREAST">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Breast cancer is a type of cancer that develops from breast tissue. Research suggests that adherence to the Mediterranean diet may help reduce the risk of developing this disease. Additionally, the risk of breast cancer is associated with hormone replacement therapy, especially when progestogens are included in estrogen treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5340</data>
      <data key="d7">accc0e94005a48febdd39b7f004b581b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGRESIVIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La agresividad es un posible efecto secundario del tratamiento con testosterona que debe ser monitoreado durante la terapia.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5341</data>
      <data key="d7">1f69fd2eebfe4dbe9748ee4c1fd12be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#201;LULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las c&#233;lulas de Leydig son c&#233;lulas ubicadas en los test&#237;culos que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en la producci&#243;n de testosterona. Estas c&#233;lulas son estimuladas por la hormona luteinizante (LH) y tambi&#233;n pueden ser activadas por gonadotropinas. Su funci&#243;n principal es la s&#237;ntesis de testosterona, una hormona esencial para el desarrollo y mantenimiento de caracter&#237;sticas sexuales masculinas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4</data>
      <data key="d3">1292</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5342</data>
      <data key="d7">aa3c4757deec455a92a783c7a7f3f3d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome Metab&#243;lico" is a complex cluster of conditions that significantly increases the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes. This syndrome encompasses several interrelated factors, including hypertension, hyperglycemia, excess abdominal fat, and abnormal cholesterol levels. It is often associated with insulin resistance, obesity, and poor nutrition, and can be exacerbated by lifestyle choices such as high salt consumption and the intake of sugar-sweetened beverages and trans fats.

Additionally, the syndrome may be influenced by dietary factors, including protein and dairy consumption, although evidence regarding the protective effects of dairy is inconsistent. There is also a noted association between the syndrome and conditions such as dislipidemia, hyperuricemia, and kidney stone formation. Furthermore, treatment with testosterone has been identified as a potential exacerbating factor for the syndrome.

Overall, the "S&#237;ndrome Metab&#243;lico" represents a significant health concern, necessitating careful dietary management and lifestyle modifications to mitigate its associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">035d53a7f46fdb72c0a939265667044b,05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448,72d0be9d03c79097f867a8af2e3e89e4,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,7d5f6bf9cedae48d8c4054344fea60b4,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313,b6c8d5ff1536806d6512fb9d1af1e6db,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">21</data>
      <data key="d6">5343</data>
      <data key="d7">1d932fa38cf7463cb6ef1e13200d787e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHOX">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The SHOX gene is located on the X chromosome and plays a crucial role in determining height. It is particularly significant in patients with Turner syndrome, where its deficiency is commonly associated with the characteristic short stature observed in these individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b,a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5344</data>
      <data key="d7">ebc48a74c85b45acb0eedc168997fca7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOPAT&#205;A ISQU&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La cardiopat&#237;a isqu&#233;mica es un riesgo aumentado en mujeres con s&#237;ndrome de Turner debido a problemas metab&#243;licos.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5345</data>
      <data key="d7">55b3e94e455f45aa8a983186ee4ad4ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNITARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades autoinmunitarias como la tiroiditis linfoc&#237;tica cr&#243;nica y la enfermedad cel&#237;aca son m&#225;s frecuentes en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5346</data>
      <data key="d7">d670c3f5164c490caa63bf753089b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO OV&#193;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El fallo ov&#225;rico es una condici&#243;n com&#250;n en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner, caracterizada por gonadotrofinas elevadas y estradiol bajo.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5347</data>
      <data key="d7">06357cd00e5049e79ce7997434a4fcf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENOPAUSIA PRECOZ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La menopausia precoz es una posible evoluci&#243;n en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner, especialmente en aquellas que inician la pubertad.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5348</data>
      <data key="d7">1d82e1577da544078cae11fe2a53b80e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOMAL&#205;AS CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las anomal&#237;as cardiovasculares son comunes en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner, incluyendo defectos card&#237;acos cong&#233;nitos.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5349</data>
      <data key="d7">4acc286647d046eda14303fcefc4c0c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISECCI&#211;N DE AORTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La disecci&#243;n de aorta es una complicaci&#243;n grave que puede ocurrir en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner, requiriendo vigilancia estrecha.</data>
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5350</data>
      <data key="d7">6eacf93b955540d6bed50e6dff223c3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENOTIPO FEMENINO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">17de78bfa13b95801265f7abb14d3e2b</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5351</data>
      <data key="d7">323478d7c8564d15b8761de94b46df1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GONADOBLASTOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El gonadoblastoma es un tumor mixto de los cordones sexuales-estroma que puede inducir signos de virilizaci&#243;n en pacientes j&#243;venes fenot&#237;picamente femeninas, especialmente en aquellos con material del cromosoma Y.</data>
      <data key="d2">a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5352</data>
      <data key="d7">e3e23dd85c6a41c69dc4ebc3812afb08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="E2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">E2 es una forma de estr&#243;geno que se encuentra en niveles bajos en pacientes con insuficiencia gonadal, como en el s&#237;ndrome de Turner.</data>
      <data key="d2">a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1360</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5353</data>
      <data key="d7">ea18d326cd79484388fc79fdecad4921</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXANDROLONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">OXANDROLONA es un f&#225;rmaco que se utiliza en el contexto del tratamiento de pacientes cr&#237;ticos. Se trata de un derivado sint&#233;tico de la testosterona, que se emplea especialmente en adultos que sufren de quemaduras severas, con el objetivo de aumentar la masa magra y acelerar la cicatrizaci&#243;n de heridas. Adem&#225;s, la oxandrolona es un tratamiento recomendado para pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Turner que han comenzado el tratamiento con hormona de crecimiento de manera tard&#237;a y que presentan un pron&#243;stico de talla final insatisfactorio.</data>
      <data key="d2">111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5,2ec23f85b858abc42196ef48260e8cb0,a2ccbbd76866c4f88a82e64c95764b04</data>
      <data key="d3">1143</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5354</data>
      <data key="d7">860b29c28d17418c9159223262b3aa4d</data>
    </node>
