    </node>
    <node id="ARCH ENDOCRINOL METAB">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Archives of Endocrinology and Metabolism is a journal that published a review on Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">bc241ef500af250c0f0e0253bf5ae0f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5397</data>
      <data key="d7">fd67d295e153415d809d4507eed9423c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LANCET DIABETES ENDOCRINOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lancet Diabetes &amp; Endocrinology is a specialized medical journal dedicated to research in the fields of diabetes and endocrine health. It publishes a wide range of studies, including those focused on non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, exploring its causes and treatment strategies. The journal also addresses topics related to differences in sex development and has published significant research on cardiovascular disease and mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes following bariatric surgery. Through its diverse array of articles, Lancet Diabetes &amp; Endocrinology contributes to the advancement of knowledge and understanding in these critical areas of health.</data>
      <data key="d2">1388342730ee9177144f78f9e9d7816e,7e4178b0d21cc5424b4c54bc5de42471,b0a60df651e774a77b1969babdf3b21a,bc241ef500af250c0f0e0253bf5ae0f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5398</data>
      <data key="d7">01c4f661742f4208aec5594339a4f2d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN PEDIATR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Anales de Pediatr&#237;a is a journal that published guidelines on anomalies of sexual differentiation.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">bc241ef500af250c0f0e0253bf5ae0f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5399</data>
      <data key="d7">fa78b1aad4844010969abd8974ae5fe8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE DENYS-DRASH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Denys-Drash es un s&#237;ndrome raro que incluye enfermedad renal progresiva, trastorno de la diferenciaci&#243;n sexual y tumor de Wilms, asociado a mutaciones en el gen WT1.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d3">683</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5400</data>
      <data key="d7">da724a5839814323bdae61bf2f74825f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE SMITH-LEMLI-OPITZ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Smith-Lemli-Opitz es un trastorno autos&#243;mico recesivo que causa discapacidad intelectual y diversas anomal&#237;as fenot&#237;picas debido a una anomal&#237;a en la s&#237;ntesis del colesterol.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d3">678</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5401</data>
      <data key="d7">2a24cda3f5524385a5eab0aff39b413c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE ANTLEY-BIXLER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Antley-Bixler es un trastorno que puede derivar de un d&#233;ficit de lanosterol desmetilasa, causando genitales ambiguos y malformaciones esquel&#233;ticas en algunos casos.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d3">683</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5402</data>
      <data key="d7">0dd5c8305bec43e8bc32bc2d50125a10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WT1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">WT1 es un gen que, cuando presenta mutaciones, est&#225; asociado al s&#237;ndrome de Denys-Drash y a problemas de diferenciaci&#243;n sexual.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d3">683</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5403</data>
      <data key="d7">1a420a20e2834ee981e3ba2ea5db22d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CYP19A1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">CYP19A1 is a gene located on chromosome 15q21.2 that encodes the aromatase enzyme, which plays a crucial role in converting androgens into estrogens. Mutations in the CYP19A1 gene can lead to a deficiency of aromatase, a condition that is associated with the Smith-Lemli-Opitz syndrome. This gene's function is essential for the proper balance of sex hormones in the body, and its impairment can have significant implications for hormonal health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab,88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">678</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5404</data>
      <data key="d7">4ea80bb0e8ea455683b70c9d7c3203ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CYP51A1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">CYP51A1 es un gen que est&#225; implicado en el s&#237;ndrome de Antley-Bixler, relacionado con la esteroidog&#233;nesis y genitales ambiguos.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d3">683</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5405</data>
      <data key="d7">ded01a34c3684c41853f5690e36d14af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AROMATASE">
      <data key="d0">ENZYME</data>
      <data key="d1">Aromatase is a cytochrome P450 enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of androgens (C21 steroids) into estrogens (C18 steroids).</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">678</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5406</data>
      <data key="d7">50e4a9749c7b44a8bac4bcbdaa428bc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="46,XX">
      <data key="d0">GENOTYPE</data>
      <data key="d1">46,XX refers to the typical chromosomal pattern for females, which can be affected by aromatase deficiency leading to sexual differentiation disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5407</data>
      <data key="d7">05020363891d4f24ba6b07a01a70f1d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="46,XY">
      <data key="d0">GENOTYPE</data>
      <data key="d1">46,XY refers to the typical chromosomal pattern for males, who may also experience symptoms related to aromatase deficiency during puberty.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5408</data>
      <data key="d7">eb769411f9f5488cb3046b79c7a0d993</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FETOPLACENTARY UNIT">
      <data key="d0">SYSTEM</data>
      <data key="d1">The fetoplacental unit refers to the interaction between the fetus and the placenta, where aromatase plays a crucial role in protecting the fetus from androgens.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">678</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5409</data>
      <data key="d7">ce9d60aeea4e42a88b4306f86afdccb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERGONADOTROPIC HYPOGONADISM">
      <data key="d0">CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism is a condition characterized by elevated gonadotropins and low sex steroid levels, often observed in individuals with aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5410</data>
      <data key="d7">7c1c959f66e44e1da4b72f7cfedaccb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPOSPADIAS">
      <data key="d0">CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypospadias is a condition that can occur in males with aromatase deficiency, affecting the development of the penis.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5411</data>
      <data key="d7">9fdd587691f04e2b9cbbc2d81a59d22e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIRSUTISM">
      <data key="d0">CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hirsutism is characterized by the abnormal growth of terminal hair in women, which is often associated with hormonal imbalances, such as those resulting from aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5412</data>
      <data key="d7">7cd7a6b077914f3c82dc6a71f66c2832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACNE">
      <data key="d0">CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acne is a skin condition that can be exacerbated by hormonal changes, including those seen in women with aromatase deficiency during pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5413</data>
      <data key="d7">7ac86406e359494cbf8b9cd052609b06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANDROSTENDIONE">
      <data key="d0">HORMONE</data>
      <data key="d1">Androstendione is an androgen that can accumulate in individuals with aromatase deficiency, contributing to virilization.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">1336</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5414</data>
      <data key="d7">812c256c64ab4bdfa3b2613e60962309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTRICHOSIS">
      <data key="d0">CONDITION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertrichosis is a condition characterized by excessive hair growth that is not androgen-dependent, unlike hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5415</data>
      <data key="d7">4345912cae4b49909f97d67c75883f91</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIEDLICH SU">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Miedlich SU is an author referenced in the context of aromatase deficiency in a male patient in the literature.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5416</data>
      <data key="d7">74a13e6ebaf34f0ca4a900137869d608</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BONE">
      <data key="d0">JOURNAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone is a scientific journal that published a case report and review of the literature on aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5417</data>
      <data key="d7">278b4b141c5b4b29b5ff57fd198472a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACHERMANN JC">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d3">1300</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5418</data>
      <data key="d7">09ed6596dc27412e90d43f16c1aac944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERANDROGENISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperandrogenism is a condition marked by excessive levels of androgens in the body, which can lead to symptoms such as hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">5419</data>
      <data key="d7">8a86babc990645c0b2dd21fdb0eac95e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE OVARIOS POLIQU&#205;STICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a common cause of hyperandrogenism in women, associated with chronic anovulation and various metabolic issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5420</data>
      <data key="d7">2d4455c7f88d4159936ac880de3b3b0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMOR OV&#193;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ovarian tumors can secrete androgens, contributing to hyperandrogenism and resulting in hirsutism in women.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5421</data>
      <data key="d7">5938edbcc7fa4d58b868f9c721da3f0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA DE SUPRARENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenal carcinoma is a rare cancer that can produce androgens, leading to symptoms such as hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5422</data>
      <data key="d7">1cf28b971d644cfd8bc4de2cc22d3f6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE 21-HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">21-Hydroxylase deficiency is a genetic disorder that affects adrenal steroid production, leading to excess androgens and symptoms like hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5423</data>
      <data key="d7">0caca2c32dc54dc8a9ed49d018b3b3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEROIDES ANABOLIZANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anabolic steroids are synthetic derivatives of testosterone that can lead to increased androgen levels and are associated with hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1289</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5424</data>
      <data key="d7">bd0767786b574712b5aa01c87a1a0bf9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE HIPOANDROGENISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypoandrogenism syndrome refers to conditions with low androgen levels, which can also be relevant in the context of hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d2">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5425</data>
      <data key="d7">20a53eece92241df82265b3951037492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FERRIMAN-GALLWEY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ferriman-Gallwey scale is a clinical tool designed to assess hirsutism in women, providing a systematic method to quantify excessive hair growth. This scale utilizes specific cut-off points to indicate pathological levels of androgenization, allowing healthcare professionals to evaluate the severity of hirsutism based on the amount of hair growth in designated areas of the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5426</data>
      <data key="d7">5af027cdaf8548dcac08544288a24be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPRARENAL GLAND">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The suprarenal glands are endocrine glands located above the kidneys that produce hormones including cortisol and androgens.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d3">1336</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5427</data>
      <data key="d7">2b67682f6ce14eaab50b88fd84f77743</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OVARIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The ovaries are female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones, including estrogen and testosterone.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5428</data>
      <data key="d7">e22f66aaed604d55b5ba7406e6a0b3b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="17-OH-PROGESTERONE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">17-OH-Progesterone is a steroid hormone involved in the menstrual cycle and is used as a marker in diagnosing conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5429</data>
      <data key="d7">17df99de33f84c7ba1f17408d9ff0ba2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPLASIA SUPRARENAL CONG&#201;NITA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Congenital adrenal hyperplasia is a genetic disorder affecting adrenal hormone production, often leading to hyperandrogenism in females.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5430</data>
      <data key="d7">aba581a24ed74e259a98604a7dc74000</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENARCHE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Menarche is the first occurrence of menstruation in females, marking the onset of reproductive capability.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5431</data>
      <data key="d7">b55cff8beb45429784e2cf42be882c3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIRILIZATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Virilization refers to the development of male physical characteristics in females, often due to elevated androgen levels, and can be a symptom of hyperandrogenism.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5432</data>
      <data key="d7">36a60c4252374da0b003d69850975b4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANDROGENS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Androgens are male hormones, including testosterone, that are found in both males and females. Elevated levels of androgens can lead to various health conditions, such as hirsutism, which is characterized by excessive hair growth, and virilization, which refers to the development of male physical characteristics in females.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5433</data>
      <data key="d7">4e18afb59222486f9379de063633b0ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMILY HISTORY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Family history of congenital adrenal hyperplasia can provide important genetic information for diagnosing hyperandrogenism in women.</data>
      <data key="d2">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d3">1306</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5434</data>
      <data key="d7">5e6372b00c1d4bb08fd5f2904e9cdc84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La DHT es un metabolito activo de la testosterona que tiene una mayor afinidad por el receptor androg&#233;nico y es crucial en el desarrollo del hirsutismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">401a6af689562ae0b9d7fe627eb56d0f</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5435</data>
      <data key="d7">56cc15ea0dff492285108f1de26efae1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE C&#201;LULAS DE SERTOLI-LEYDIG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores de c&#233;lulas de Sertoli-Leydig son tumores ov&#225;ricos que pueden causar hiperandrogenismo y hirsutismo.</data>
      <data key="d2">401a6af689562ae0b9d7fe627eb56d0f</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5436</data>
      <data key="d7">5348242adaec42c2813e4a8f37d0ad47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOVULACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La anovulaci&#243;n es la ausencia de ovulaci&#243;n, que es una de las principales consecuencias del s&#237;ndrome de ovario poliqu&#237;stico.</data>
      <data key="d2">401a6af689562ae0b9d7fe627eb56d0f</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5437</data>
      <data key="d7">feadee24576e46f390c37bff4ff47983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MDTEXT.COM, INC.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MDText.com, Inc. is a publisher based in South Dartmouth, MA, known for providing medical information and guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5438</data>
      <data key="d7">59b22054a1e6414d91fff0529d075ede</data>
    </node>
    <node id="28-YEAR-OLD PATIENT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A 28-year-old female patient presenting with slowly progressive hirsutism and irregular menstrual cycles, suspected to have PCOS.</data>
      <data key="d2">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5439</data>
      <data key="d7">bb45dd6ccf2e4b4ca740e3f34d0a6753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIONAL CENTER FOR BIOTECHNOLOGY INFORMATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is a branch of the National Institutes of Health that provides access to biomedical and genomic information.</data>
      <data key="d2">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5440</data>
      <data key="d7">99ad8fea2723487e89f6c2ac3116fc35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLYCYSTIC OVARY SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a prevalent endocrine disorder that primarily affects women. It is characterized by irregular menstrual cycles, elevated levels of androgens, and the presence of polycystic ovaries, which are enlarged ovaries containing small cysts on their outer edges. This hormonal disorder can lead to a range of metabolic and clinical consequences, impacting women's overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5441</data>
      <data key="d7">d5a8e94a9c25434cb9975573976bc4bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOUTH DARTMOUTH">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5442</data>
      <data key="d7">70530cc025bf48e9a60c8943d7bd583f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMA INDEX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The HOMA index is a method used to estimate insulin resistance and beta-cell function, often elevated in patients with Polycystic Ovary Syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1305</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5443</data>
      <data key="d7">81990cbe208c44d4b7cebc3102570197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME, specifically obstructive sleep apnea syndrome, is a condition characterized by repeated interruptions in breathing during sleep. This disorder can be exacerbated by obesity, which may worsen the severity of the condition. Additionally, sleep apnea syndrome has implications for patients undergoing testosterone treatment, highlighting the need for careful management in individuals affected by this disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">996</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5444</data>
      <data key="d7">4db7e87674a44f78b1c378dea8249338</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERYTHROCYTOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Erythrocytosis is a condition where there is an increase in red blood cells, which can be a potential adverse effect of testosterone treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1307</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5445</data>
      <data key="d7">440aee6d569043089d224b8ed8e2efae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOMETRIAL ATROPHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Endometrial atrophy is the thinning of the endometrial lining, which can occur as a result of testosterone treatment in transsexual men.</data>
      <data key="d2">dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d3">1307</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5446</data>
      <data key="d7">774a3d4f157d43cc8122f1c5979ee7df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMBREE WC">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Hembree WC is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals regarding the appropriate endocrine interventions for individuals experiencing gender dysphoria.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5447</data>
      <data key="d7">e2dc732e321c4e6787a8ca04f0d4d5e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COHEN-KETTENIS PT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cohen-Kettenis PT is recognized as an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline concerning the endocrine treatment of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria. This guideline serves as a critical resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of gender-dysphoric persons, providing evidence-based recommendations for their treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5448</data>
      <data key="d7">a16777015f26422290c6bcca13836519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOOREN L">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gooren L is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, outlining best practices and recommendations for endocrine treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5449</data>
      <data key="d7">cb5798ff3968427d90d727020e144232</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HANNEMA SE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Hannema SE is recognized as an author of the Clinical Practice Guideline on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons, published by the Endocrine Society. This guideline provides essential recommendations for the endocrine treatment of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, reflecting Hannema SE's expertise and contribution to this important area of healthcare.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5450</data>
      <data key="d7">4b74e39a4ae54642b89b0fd1876c84b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEYER WJ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Meyer WJ is an author of the Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline focused on the endocrine treatment of gender-dysphoric persons. This guideline serves as a comprehensive resource for the clinical management of individuals experiencing gender dysphoria, outlining best practices and recommendations for endocrine treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5451</data>
      <data key="d7">1025b07ea374408c992daec5b33fc20b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIPROTERONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ciproterona is a medication that is primarily used in hormone therapy for transgender individuals, noted for its antiandrogenic effects. It is recommended that Ciproterona be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d3">1285</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5452</data>
      <data key="d7">f2b1ff3a992d4e669587e22e603b3a02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMATOCRITO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hematocrit is a measure of the proportion of blood volume that is occupied by red blood cells, important in assessing cardiovascular risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5453</data>
      <data key="d7">813139d4520e44c1b6b4e4fd7e849419</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APNEAS DEL SUE&#209;O">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sleep apnea is a sleep disorder characterized by pauses in breathing or periods of shallow breathing during sleep, often associated with obesity and metabolic syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5454</data>
      <data key="d7">21bb0191fc524f4699ca5b5a9b1c8fc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE &#218;TERO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Uterine cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lining of the uterus, with risk factors that may be influenced by hormonal treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5455</data>
      <data key="d7">1aa81fa5c6304ffda04a7d76f50c44fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAMOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mammography is a diagnostic tool used to screen for breast cancer, important for monitoring health in individuals undergoing hormone therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5456</data>
      <data key="d7">0c856e1d8ff843c98ae870aea12c73b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTERECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, which may be relevant for individuals undergoing gender-affirming surgeries.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5457</data>
      <data key="d7">87a8024fa5484358b3eeaaf6c53b77b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO HORMONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormone therapy refers to the use of hormones in medical treatment, particularly for transgender individuals to align physical characteristics with gender identity.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5458</data>
      <data key="d7">b9da31857272440ab9cde459a55e7ba3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIE-11">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The CIE-11, or Clasificaci&#243;n Internacional de Enfermedades (International Classification of Diseases), is the 11th revision of a comprehensive classification system designed to categorize diseases and health conditions. It was presented at the World Health Assembly in May 2019 for adoption by Member States. This classification system includes parameters specifically for the evaluation of nutritional status, highlighting its role in assessing various health aspects beyond just diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1553</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5459</data>
      <data key="d7">8f5a5132a0c248639f221a179765e522</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIE-10">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The CIE-10, or Clasificaci&#243;n Internacional de Enfermedades, 10&#170; revisi&#243;n, is a comprehensive coding system utilized for the classification of medical diagnoses and procedures. This system plays a crucial role in categorizing diseases and health-related issues, thereby facilitating data collection and clinical management. The CIE-10 is the 10th revision of the International Classification of Diseases and remains in use until the implementation of the CIE-11. Additionally, the CIE-10 provides updated guidelines for the classification of various conditions, including eating disorders, ensuring a standardized approach to health data across different medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430,b6336e61e2a290a5c471fd72297d6093,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c,f53d37f60efeb5d6cdba204bf8f2bd9b</data>
      <data key="d3">1279</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5460</data>
      <data key="d7">ba359889198843c1af71db5cf30f76e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE LA IDENTIDAD SEXUAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Trastorno de la identidad sexual refers to disorders of sexual identity classified in the CIE-10.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1279</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5461</data>
      <data key="d7">26e58195bf7e400bbb10a8941f299d68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETATO DE CIPROTERONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetato de ciproterona is a progestin with anti-androgenic properties commonly used in Europe for transgender women.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5462</data>
      <data key="d7">991d60d721774197ad727a28162e2809</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTOS CON HORMONAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormone treatments are medical procedures that transgender individuals may undergo to align their physical characteristics with their gender identity.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1280</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5463</data>
      <data key="d7">cc3b37c04dc24b359b31ffe08db7f5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IDENTIDAD DE G&#201;NERO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gender identity refers to a person's deeply felt internal experience of gender, which may or may not correspond with the sex assigned at birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1280</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5464</data>
      <data key="d7">2a8cce8eb7ff4040b5fa966a4314c4dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INCONGRUENCIA DE G&#201;NERO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gender incongruence is a condition where a person's gender identity does not align with their assigned sex at birth, often leading to distress.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1279</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5465</data>
      <data key="d7">effcb16522524b4888f3b6282a4a5823</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE LA IDENTIDAD SEXUAL DE LA INFANCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">This refers to a condition in children where there is a marked incongruence between the child's experienced/expressed gender and the gender assigned at birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1279</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5466</data>
      <data key="d7">95eaa1e4bb2c4b4cbfab8a05182b87fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRANSEXUAL MUJER">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">3779506e9a987b6bdf5da381df675430</data>
      <data key="d3">1280</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5467</data>
      <data key="d7">ca30037da842404cb6a39ddc3b5844f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HMG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HMG (human menopausal gonadotropin) is a hormone that can be used in conjunction with hCG for treating cryptorchidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1299</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5468</data>
      <data key="d7">b2d70ca1f78243078361e3b0ce363aff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TESTICULOS CRIPTORQU&#205;DICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cryptorchid testicles are those that have not descended into the scrotum and may require medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1204</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5469</data>
      <data key="d7">494268544e0a4b6aa54cee8860feb724</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ATROFIA refers to the condition characterized by the reduction in size or wasting away of body tissues or organs. In the context of neuropathy, atrophy in the feet and hands can be a symptom associated with disorders that affect copper metabolism. Additionally, atrophy can also pertain to the reduction in size of the testicles, which may occur in cases of cryptorchidism. Thus, ATROFIA encompasses both peripheral atrophy related to neurological conditions and testicular atrophy linked to developmental issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d3">1208</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5470</data>
      <data key="d7">c99da3bdc14c4ca79bfbab0133c3e99e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TORSI&#211;N TESTICULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Testicular torsion is a medical emergency that can occur in undescended testicles, leading to severe complications if not treated promptly.</data>
      <data key="d2">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
