    </node>
    <node id="MENOPAUSIA TEMPRANA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Menopausia temprana (early menopause) is a condition that can occur in women with HIV and is associated with hormonal changes.</data>
      <data key="d2">4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55</data>
      <data key="d3">1356</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5491</data>
      <data key="d7">6a82dd1651bd438ea000439138d4238f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GENE SRY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SRY gene is crucial for male sex determination and is often translocated in individuals with atypical chromosomal patterns.</data>
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5492</data>
      <data key="d7">5ac31fe543974f7abbf8caacbd68b54a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUDIOLOGICAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Audiological assessments are recommended for patients with 46,XX karyotype due to the frequent occurrence of sensorineural hearing loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5493</data>
      <data key="d7">eaaad3fc683048da86385b2b7bb10589</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZOOSPERMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Azoospermia is a medical condition characterized by the absence of sperm in the semen, commonly found in individuals with Klinefelter syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5494</data>
      <data key="d7">bb63d9d179c84b8ab31e10484250a65f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROCEFALIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microcefalia is a condition where a person's head is significantly smaller than expected, which can be associated with genetic syndromes including Klinefelter syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5495</data>
      <data key="d7">373220d0e3a547ca9fbceb846a580e05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOPAT&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiopat&#237;as refer to heart diseases that may be present in individuals with certain genetic conditions, including Klinefelter syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5496</data>
      <data key="d7">65f07b043ad54352ad367af7ee511b72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENOPAUSE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">81491129b1fbfcc2e010109419cde1f0</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5497</data>
      <data key="d7">3aefff423d8143d2b97c5c096e822677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN SRY">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">The SRY gene is involved in the differentiation of Sertoli cells and the development of testicles, crucial for male sexual development.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1358</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5498</data>
      <data key="d7">a92917ade59047a884cc190f962dd4aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZF">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">The AZF region is a genetic factor associated with azoospermia, which is the absence of sperm in semen, affecting male fertility.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1296</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5499</data>
      <data key="d7">4856ccf695ee45458a4c51d53dc37664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSA">
      <data key="d0">PROTEIN</data>
      <data key="d1">Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by prostate cells, commonly measured to assess prostate health. It serves as a crucial marker for evaluating prostate health, particularly in the context of testosterone therapy, where monitoring PSA levels can provide important insights into the condition of the prostate.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1298</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5500</data>
      <data key="d7">013562c345ed41e8af75b8778310f850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACIONES DEL GEN RSPO1">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">Mutations in the RSPO1 gene are associated with conditions like hyperkeratosis palmoplantar and squamous cell carcinoma, affecting sexual development.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1298</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5501</data>
      <data key="d7">b11bf689c00b48c1b629c5acd28f119d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VARONES 46,XX">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1296</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5502</data>
      <data key="d7">29d9e5e02e12479f98d983153d0d3d7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE ADDISON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Addison's disease, known as "enfermedad de Addison," is an autoimmune condition characterized by the insufficient production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This disorder can occur in patients who have other autoimmune disorders, such as type 1 diabetes mellitus. It is classified as an adrenal insufficiency and is one of the endocrine abnormalities that may manifest in autoimmune polyglandular syndromes. Management of Addison's disease often requires dietary adjustments, particularly in sodium and potassium intake, to help regulate the body's hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046,9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b</data>
      <data key="d3">1105</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">5503</data>
      <data key="d7">a8293e17c1574b26ab8cb8c0227dd23d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN AIRE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El gen AIRE es un gen regulador autoinmune que, cuando presenta mutaciones, est&#225; asociado con el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d3">680</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5504</data>
      <data key="d7">f4d9995c8e67439285228ad6565ad252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANDIDIASIS MUCOCUT&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La candidiasis mucocut&#225;nea es una infecci&#243;n f&#250;ngica que puede presentarse en la piel, u&#241;as y mucosas, y es una manifestaci&#243;n com&#250;n en el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d3">680</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5505</data>
      <data key="d7">89283f47862e46f983fac2d91c4ba676</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES DE TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La diabetes de tipo 1 es una enfermedad autoinmunitaria que puede asociarse con el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d3">680</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5506</data>
      <data key="d7">db1ca48fcb9a48cda015936a6989edb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROIDITIS AUTOINMUNE CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic autoimmune thyroiditis, known as "tiroiditis autoinmune cr&#243;nica," is a condition that can manifest in patients with autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome, impacting thyroid function. Additionally, it is associated with adrenal insufficiency in individuals diagnosed with POEMS syndrome. This highlights the condition's relevance in the context of broader autoimmune disorders and its potential complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d3">1107</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5507</data>
      <data key="d7">f4cf3b9f063a4e649644b6eaa9156748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome Poliglandular Autoinmune Tipo 1" is a rare autoimmune disorder characterized by a combination of several autoimmune conditions. It includes mucocutaneous candidiasis, which affects the skin and mucous membranes, hypoparathyroidism, a condition where the parathyroid glands produce insufficient hormones, and Addison's disease, which is characterized by insufficient production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This syndrome may also involve other autoimmune disorders, highlighting its complex nature and the interplay of various immune system dysfunctions.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1105</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5508</data>
      <data key="d7">4e35880429c341de98e4d806fd1e2859</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome Poliglandular Autoinmune Tipo 2" is a condition characterized by the presence of multiple autoimmune disorders. It includes Addison's disease, autoimmune thyroid disease, type 1 diabetes mellitus, and other autoimmune conditions. This syndrome is more prevalent than type 1 autoimmune polyglandular syndrome and is linked to genetic factors, particularly the HLA-DR3 allele.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1106</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5509</data>
      <data key="d7">5b555c5d2ab745eba90977e89f0458a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune tipo 3 es m&#225;s heterog&#233;neo y asocia endocrinopat&#237;as autoinmunes sin enfermedad de Addison, incluyendo tiroidopat&#237;a autoinmune y diabetes mellitus tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1073</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5510</data>
      <data key="d7">9db34c1177214539842d806d3e8e9188</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROIDITIS CR&#211;NICA AUTOINMUNE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La tiroiditis cr&#243;nica autoinmune es una enfermedad que afecta la tiroides y puede asociarse con otros trastornos autoinmunes.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1073</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5511</data>
      <data key="d7">4542afd883e7493b9d56b4be3ec2dcec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OOFORITIS AUTOINMUNE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">OOFORITIS AUTOINMUNE, or autoimmune oophoritis, is a condition characterized by lymphocytic infiltration of ovarian follicles. This infiltration leads to primary ovarian insufficiency, which is a significant consequence of the disorder. Additionally, autoimmune oophoritis is associated with other autoimmune disorders, indicating a broader context of autoimmune activity in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee,806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1108</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5512</data>
      <data key="d7">a3b535d884d54f4096d06a29a4227a7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AUTOINMUNITARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La insuficiencia suprarrenal autoinmunitaria es una condici&#243;n en la que las gl&#225;ndulas suprarrenales no producen suficientes hormonas, a menudo asociada con autoanticuerpos antiadrenales.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1106</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5513</data>
      <data key="d7">d0d908c791ae44a184babb001fb4f031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIT&#205;LIGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El vit&#237;ligo es una enfermedad autoinmune que causa la p&#233;rdida de pigmento en la piel y puede asociarse con otros trastornos autoinmunes.</data>
      <data key="d2">71a67838e4fbd705b0fb3b14b20664ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1073</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5514</data>
      <data key="d7">ede595787ef64c3fbfc3c2725f4cdfd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA OV&#193;RICA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary ovarian insufficiency is defined by primary hypogonadism before the age of 40 in women and is associated with autoimmune conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1108</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5515</data>
      <data key="d7">b3dd40ff95f74000b476cd2af4a6c5c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUTOANTICUERPOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Autoantibodies are markers that can indicate autoimmune conditions, including those related to ovarian insufficiency and Addison's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1105</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5516</data>
      <data key="d7">c6cf9a2343b84da5adc89eb37fef9504</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICUERPOS ANTIADRENALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anti-adrenal antibodies are markers that may indicate the risk of developing Addison's disease in patients with autoimmune conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1105</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5517</data>
      <data key="d7">f403d35e8bd54e0c971de2b6b7ec8211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICUERPOS ANTI-21 HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anti-21 hydroxylase antibodies are associated with adrenal insufficiency and can precede the onset of Addison's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">806e7b517eea737f1b254b699db60046</data>
      <data key="d3">1105</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5518</data>
      <data key="d7">4e38b51c79bc4199968bf8c99d8b88e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POEMS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">POEMS is a rare paraneoplastic syndrome characterized by polyneuropathy, organomegaly, endocrinopathy, monoclonal plasma cell disorder, and skin changes.</data>
      <data key="d2">77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d3">1107</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">5519</data>
      <data key="d7">d4660177471a436f9f76f0191c630e41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenal insufficiency, also known as "insuficiencia suprarrenal," is a condition characterized by the inadequate production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This condition can arise in patients undergoing treatment with immune checkpoint inhibitors, necessitating careful management to address the hormonal deficiencies. Additionally, adrenal insufficiency is recognized as a less common endocrinopathy associated with POEMS syndrome, a rare disorder that affects multiple systems in the body. In patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy, the diagnosis of insuficiencia suprarrenal can be confirmed through MRI findings, highlighting the importance of imaging in the assessment of this condition. Overall, adrenal insufficiency presents a significant clinical challenge that requires thorough evaluation and management in various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">40253f8b49d61452dbc56454cd1a07e0,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a,c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d3">1355</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5520</data>
      <data key="d7">3a6bd2c675524cc393831f85977f7ee7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALHAMBRA PRISON">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Alhambra Prison is a facility that is referenced in the context of the treatment of patients with adrenal insufficiency. Additionally, it serves as a type of institution where patients with diabetes may receive treatment for related health issues. While the text does not explicitly detail its role in diabetes care, the mention of Alhambra Prison highlights its relevance in the broader context of healthcare for individuals with endocrine disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5521</data>
      <data key="d7">95e8d3b32a55414e9abed50efd75ceb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CTLA-4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CTLA-4 is a gene involved in immune regulation, referenced in relation to the genetic factors associated with SPA type 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d3">1107</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5522</data>
      <data key="d7">391dca1cb8c44862bb5f3f479315b4f0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTPN22">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PTPN22 is a gene that plays a role in immune system regulation, mentioned in the context of genetic associations with SPA type 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d3">1107</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5523</data>
      <data key="d7">b41d181903fb4c8e81f2452a6fc4f05f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLEC16A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CLEC16A is a gene associated with immune regulation, noted in the discussion of genetic factors related to SPA type 2.</data>
      <data key="d2">77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d3">1107</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5524</data>
      <data key="d7">c758bcdde3fa451292ea5df4e2fce1c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PTH, or parathyroid hormone, is a crucial hormone that regulates calcium and phosphorus levels in the body. It plays a significant role in maintaining calcium homeostasis by influencing the absorption and reabsorption of calcium, as well as decreasing the tubular reabsorption of phosphorus. PTH is particularly important in the context of vitamin D deficiency, as its levels may become elevated in such cases. Additionally, PTH is involved in the pathophysiology of hypocalcemia and is essential for bone metabolism. Overall, PTH is vital for ensuring proper calcium levels in the blood and supporting various physiological processes related to bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5525</data>
      <data key="d7">ec054d0edd1845a6a44e7e2996b5be44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANGIOTENSIN II">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Angiotensin II is a hormone that increases blood pressure and stimulates the release of aldosterone.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1330</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5526</data>
      <data key="d7">f1ad0904d82945beb7f05340b80e8447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATRIURETIC PEPTIDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atrial natriuretic peptide is a hormone that helps regulate blood pressure and fluid balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5527</data>
      <data key="d7">48c909a63cd6441aafe7beb6938a9235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NITRIC OXIDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitric oxide is a signaling molecule that plays a role in various physiological processes, including vasodilation.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5528</data>
      <data key="d7">b91e2bb6a8cb44fcbcbea6e781236cd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROGESTERONE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Progesterone is a hormone that plays a crucial role in preparing the uterus for pregnancy and regulating the menstrual cycle. Additionally, when administered cyclically, progesterone has been shown to increase bone mass in adolescents suffering from Anorexia Nervosa. This dual function highlights its importance not only in reproductive health but also in supporting bone density in vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5529</data>
      <data key="d7">98203a53e8bc410ebd9ca4f4fee0ed8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THYROID HORMONES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1299</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5530</data>
      <data key="d7">3f1e3f1e36294a5aae9ac35f81781684</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KIDNEYS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The kidneys are vital organs in the human body that play a crucial role in various physiological processes. In addition to their primary function of filtering blood and producing urine, the kidneys also participate in gluconeogenesis, although to a lesser extent than the liver. This metabolic process is essential for maintaining blood glucose levels, particularly during periods of fasting or intense exercise.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d,fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5531</data>
      <data key="d7">5bb3a67a55484ada8bffe41328b22db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECEPTORES INTRACELULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intracellular receptors are proteins that bind to lipophilic hormones and mediate their effects by regulating gene transcription.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5532</data>
      <data key="d7">8ff6ac07fa4a4eceba21a0c6f05dcba0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CICLOPENTANO-PERHIDROFENANTRENO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ciclopentano-perhidrofenantreno is a chemical structure from which steroid hormones are derived, synthesized from cholesterol.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5533</data>
      <data key="d7">284cdbe265724893938c671eaa52a944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Steroid Response Elements (SRE) are specific DNA sequences that steroid hormone-receptor complexes bind to, regulating gene transcription.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1597</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5534</data>
      <data key="d7">045a4d21abe740fe969f8958882afdcd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5'-YODINASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">5'-iodinase is an enzyme that converts T4 to T3 in target cells, activating the thyroid hormone's effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d3">1597</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5535</data>
      <data key="d7">2e5a8c45162946c1962e324319711462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS ESTEROIDEAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Steroid hormones are lipid-derived hormones that regulate various physiological processes through intracellular receptors.</data>
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5536</data>
      <data key="d7">e896cd08453441bbadc23c7f8a0c6b2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS LIPOF&#205;LICAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
