      <data key="d6">5537</data>
      <data key="d7">2bbb40a4010d417e9c7d78dcf8be4c9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PPAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PPAR (Peroxisome Proliferator Activated Receptor) is a nuclear receptor that acts as a transcription factor in response to metabolic stimuli.</data>
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">1488</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5538</data>
      <data key="d7">12b0029b187841dc855c4efb34e935da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRATOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrates are a class of medications that target PPAR (peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor) receptors to regulate lipid levels in the body. They are primarily used to treat dyslipidemia, particularly in patients with metabolic disorders. Fibrates are effective in managing hypertriglyceridemia, functioning as agonists of the PPAR-&#945; receptor, which plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism. However, it is important to note that fibrates can have gastrointestinal side effects and are contraindicated in individuals with advanced liver and kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63,746fad557197bebe72763efd23a9e0e2,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">1488</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5539</data>
      <data key="d7">3017656202274e90ad168883e44b4c16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLACENTA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The placenta is an organ that provides nutrients and oxygen to the fetus and secretes hormones during pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">1142</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5540</data>
      <data key="d7">546818b0754c4be69439ecf23b1f2cc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FETO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The fetus is the developing offspring in the womb that relies on the mother for nutrients and energy.</data>
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5541</data>
      <data key="d7">c4a9e07b44314343a7205498d49fdefd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA" es una condici&#243;n metab&#243;lica que se caracteriza por una disminuci&#243;n en la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la insulina de manera efectiva. Esta condici&#243;n puede aumentar durante el embarazo, lo que afecta la captaci&#243;n de glucosa y el metabolismo de la madre. Adem&#225;s, la resistencia a la insulina tambi&#233;n puede presentarse en pacientes cr&#237;ticamente enfermos, impactando negativamente su metabolismo. Asimismo, se ha observado que este trastorno metab&#243;lico puede ocurrir en pacientes con c&#225;ncer, lo que repercute en su nutrici&#243;n y salud general. En resumen, la resistencia a la insulina es un fen&#243;meno que puede afectar a diferentes grupos de pacientes, incluyendo a mujeres embarazadas y aquellos con enfermedades graves, como el c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5542</data>
      <data key="d7">a25af186ac254b86b3551b736f543be8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VOLUMEN PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cantidad de plasma en la sangre que aumenta significativamente durante el embarazo.</data>
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5543</data>
      <data key="d7">b4e7460067ed4015859450c1b29f4eb5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIURIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Calciuria refers to the presence of calcium in the urine, a condition that can influence calcium availability for fetal development. It is characterized by the excretion of calcium in the urine, which tends to increase during pregnancy. This heightened excretion may have implications for both maternal and fetal health, particularly in ensuring adequate calcium levels for the developing fetus.</data>
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5544</data>
      <data key="d7">dd49daf168104e23bf6dbbf19237bc4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS DIABETOG&#201;NICAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5545</data>
      <data key="d7">aa46439fedec43fd86f83ee3743c1f42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOMEN'S HEALTH INITIATIVE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Women's Health Initiative is a long-term national health study focused on addressing the most common causes of death, disability, and poor quality of life in postmenopausal women. This initiative investigates various health issues pertinent to this demographic, including the relationship between protein intake and frailty. Through its comprehensive approach, the Women's Health Initiative aims to enhance the understanding of health challenges faced by postmenopausal women and improve their overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">3be9d646c354d76527755d79a77c916b,a739523b87def5cdfa8fe97cdf423fe7,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5546</data>
      <data key="d7">418c9bbddba745eb964884d97b6156b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormone replacement therapy with estrogens is used in postmenopausal women to seek cardiovascular benefits but has associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5547</data>
      <data key="d7">30272fc5a9634e85b3a76008a4a3663b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TESTOSTERONE THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Testosterone therapy is administered to men and requires evaluation of prostate size, PSA levels, and hematocrit before and during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1298</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5548</data>
      <data key="d7">dd07ba31b2654af4baf522404b5e299c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BASEDOW'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Basedow's disease is an autoimmune disorder that can cause hyperthyroidism and may lead to spontaneous remission after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">172</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5549</data>
      <data key="d7">2031aa1f883f4057a4b49846ae837b73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTINODULAR GOITER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Multinodular goiter is a condition that often requires early treatment with I-131 due to low incidence of hypothyroidism and low probability of spontaneous remission.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">172</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5550</data>
      <data key="d7">2a203b7523d54ff5b64d34202156b15b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIAC DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiac disease is a condition that may necessitate treatment for subclinical hyperthyroidism in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">172</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5551</data>
      <data key="d7">2888922e71fd4bd28164d8b861f24926</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRILLATION AURICULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atrial fibrillation is a potential complication associated with untreated subclinical hyperthyroidism in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">172</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5552</data>
      <data key="d7">dfc01e1a55864d65bec9e39a09507560</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREGNANCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pregnancy is a physiological condition characterized by various metabolic adaptations in the mother that are essential for supporting fetal development. It necessitates careful nutritional management, particularly for women with diabetes, to ensure both proper fetal growth and the health of the mother.</data>
      <data key="d2">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5553</data>
      <data key="d7">c790aae5505744c28a7946f43e60acb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTIROIDISMO SUBCL&#205;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Subclinical hyperthyroidism is a condition characterized by low TSH levels with normal FT4 levels, which may require treatment in certain populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">398</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5554</data>
      <data key="d7">278ac96209ae49d3b95475a6717afbf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENOPAUSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Menopause is a natural biological process marking the end of a woman's reproductive years, often associated with hormonal changes and health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">1611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5555</data>
      <data key="d7">34bc853363324fb18841374d237a4d35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DEL T&#218;NEL CARPIANO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carpal tunnel syndrome is a condition that may be associated with the use of growth hormone in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d3">398</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5556</data>
      <data key="d7">1c3b15f78c5b47deb06c8a44d03c6523</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAL RESISTANCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormonal resistance is a condition where an organ does not respond adequately to a biologically active hormone, often due to genetic alterations affecting hormone receptors.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ebd4f784ceacfe0744f6bb9cd9a5a3</data>
      <data key="d3">1308</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5557</data>
      <data key="d7">d786e79c265f400cb0eabf811a07bc81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CYTOCHROME CYP3A4">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cytochrome CYP3A4 is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of many drugs, affecting their efficacy and safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ebd4f784ceacfe0744f6bb9cd9a5a3</data>
      <data key="d3">1327</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5558</data>
      <data key="d7">4a43ec3be54d42379681c32a501730ba</data>
    </node>
