    </node>
    <node id="YERVOY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Yervoy is a medication with the active ingredient ipilimumab, used in cancer immunotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">1355</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5591</data>
      <data key="d7">744a86fcf32044938c106424da29c919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MITOTANE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mitotane is a drug used to treat adrenal cancer by inhibiting adrenal cortex function.</data>
      <data key="d2">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">1416</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5592</data>
      <data key="d7">e8a95b3cc2c2431fa3639def7213062c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZARZUELO A">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Zarzuelo A is an author who contributed to the book on pharmacological interactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">1424</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5593</data>
      <data key="d7">215556a0f79143ceb28c48883150fd7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUDROCORTISONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fludrocortisona, also known as fludrocortisone, is a synthetic corticosteroid medication primarily used in the treatment of isolated aldosterone deficiency and adrenal insufficiency. It plays a crucial role in managing conditions related to insufficient production of aldosterone, helping to regulate sodium and potassium levels in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d3">1424</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5594</data>
      <data key="d7">b27fdf7e0ce64e6fb3610c7fb023989d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperuricemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of uric acid in the blood. This condition can lead to various health issues, most notably gout, and is often influenced by dietary factors, including purine intake and alcohol consumption. Hyperuricemia is relevant in the context of dietary management for conditions such as nephrolithiasis and can frequently occur in patients. It may also be a complication associated with Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI). Treatment for hyperuricemia typically involves dietary modifications and medical intervention to manage uric acid levels effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,6533cbcb76873caf6fd68eb95d313d24,704cfd179507a977ecc0691a5bd2861e,9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce,a0162312192878417ef2c4ef8f9cffba,af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">1384</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">19</data>
      <data key="d6">5595</data>
      <data key="d7">2f741ae18b90450497b3b2e4ab01cdf4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alterations refer to changes in normal physiological functions, often leading to medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d3">52</data>
