    </node>
    <node id="SAPROPTERINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sapropterina is a synthetic preparation of tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4) that is utilized in the treatment of mild phenylketonuria (PKU). It is often administered alongside dietary management to enhance the patient's ability to tolerate phenylalanine (Phe). As a commercial preparation, Sapropterina plays a crucial role in managing PKU by increasing the tolerance to this amino acid, thereby aiding in the overall treatment strategy for individuals affected by this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5609</data>
      <data key="d7">a7124aa4ef6e4afdbd49fff7c3320105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The FDA, or Food and Drug Administration, is the U.S. government agency responsible for regulating food, pharmaceuticals, and medical devices. It plays a crucial role in overseeing the safety and efficacy of various products, including clinical nutrition items and obesity treatments such as lorcaserin and the combination of phentermine and topiramate. Additionally, the FDA approved teduglutide for use in patients with intestinal failure in December 2012. The agency categorizes drugs and treatments based on their safety and efficacy, ensuring that medications, including those for conditions like osteoporosis, meet the necessary standards before they can be made available to the public.</data>
      <data key="d2">3159307e5633698722f72fde1e82702f,35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219,e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772,f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">5610</data>
      <data key="d7">e29b8e56573d42b89c158e32280628ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypercalcemia is a medical condition characterized by an abnormally high level of calcium in the blood. This condition is often associated with various underlying medical issues, including hyperparathyroidism, certain cancers such as lymphomas, and parathyroid tumors, particularly in cases of Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). Additionally, hypercalcemia can be linked to hypomagnesemia and familial hypocalciuric hypercalcemia. Overall, hypercalcemia can arise from a range of conditions, highlighting its complexity and the need for careful diagnosis and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906,b9342cecd69cdc0e9936df041657f5f5,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">31</data>
      <data key="d6">5611</data>
      <data key="d7">a00dc99c0e854e66aba06a285b77d3d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperparathyroidism is a medical condition characterized by an excess production of parathyroid hormone (PTH) by the parathyroid glands. This overproduction leads to elevated levels of calcium in the blood, which can result in various health complications. The condition is often associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes, particularly MEN1 and MEN2A. Additionally, hyperparathyroidism can arise from prolonged elevated levels of phosphorus in the blood, especially in patients with chronic kidney disease. Overall, hyperparathyroidism is marked by its impact on calcium metabolism and its potential links to genetic syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab,ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">5612</data>
      <data key="d7">c3d32a6ef57e4b94a883288613b7e0f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EL-HAJJ FULEIHAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El-Hajj Fuleihan is a medical professional and researcher who has made significant contributions to the understanding and management of primary hyperparathyroidism. His work has enhanced the knowledge surrounding the diagnosis and treatment of this condition, highlighting his role in advancing medical research in this area.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">1286</data>
