      <data key="d6">5614</data>
      <data key="d7">7d6e1210e68d48e7b016891c0f7655f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YIP">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Yip is a medical professional involved in the preoperative localization for parathyroid surgery in patients with primary hyperparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5615</data>
      <data key="d7">8f8acbbfdf4f490ab5c0cafd31607cb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPARATIROIDISMO SECUNDARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperparatiroidismo secundario es una condici&#243;n que se presenta como respuesta a niveles bajos de calcio en el organismo, frecuentemente asociada con la insuficiencia renal. Esta afecci&#243;n se caracteriza por una producci&#243;n excesiva de hormona paratiroidea por parte de las gl&#225;ndulas paratiroides, que ocurre como resultado de la hipocalcemia. Es com&#250;nmente observada en pacientes con enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica, donde la incapacidad de los ri&#241;ones para mantener niveles adecuados de calcio contribuye al desarrollo de esta condici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba4a7e7b4c409f6d4c6979a7de6c832,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5616</data>
      <data key="d7">cc803ba351a44b2ab345164785e4230f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hormona paratiroidea (PTH) is a polypeptide hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium levels in the blood. It functions to increase serum calcium levels and is influenced by the use of glucocorticoids. PTH is essential for maintaining calcium homeostasis in the body, ensuring that calcium levels remain within a healthy range.</data>
      <data key="d2">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5617</data>
      <data key="d7">50a507d9b1ba4d86b01b2a7c0c1dc9ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE RI&#209;&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El c&#225;ncer de ri&#241;&#243;n es otro tipo de c&#225;ncer que puede estar asociado con hipercalcemia, a menudo a trav&#233;s de mecanismos tumorales.</data>
      <data key="d2">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">1208</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5618</data>
      <data key="d7">3a2cab44f66c4f1f95d20bbb1b3e0cba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N, o c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n, es una enfermedad que se ha relacionado con diversos factores diet&#233;ticos y de salud. Se ha observado que el consumo elevado de carne roja incrementa el riesgo de desarrollar esta neoplasia, mientras que la ingesta de carne de aves de corral parece tener un efecto protector, disminuyendo dicho riesgo. Adem&#225;s, el c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n puede causar hipercalcemia en pacientes, lo cual a menudo est&#225; relacionado con met&#225;stasis.

La influencia de la dieta en el c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n tambi&#233;n se extiende a los &#225;cidos grasos omega-3, cuya ingesta podr&#237;a tener un impacto, especialmente en mujeres, aunque los resultados de los estudios no son estad&#237;sticamente significativos. Por otro lado, el consumo de frutas y verduras se ha asociado con una disminuci&#243;n en el riesgo de incidencia de c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n, sugiriendo que una dieta rica en estos alimentos puede ser beneficiosa. Asimismo, se ha planteado que el consumo de soja podr&#237;a reducir el riesgo de c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n, aunque la evidencia al respecto es limitada.

En resumen, el c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n es una enfermedad compleja influenciada por h&#225;bitos diet&#233;ticos, donde el consumo de carne roja aumenta el riesgo, mientras que el consumo de aves de corral, frutas, verduras y posiblemente soja podr&#237;a ayudar a reducirlo.</data>
      <data key="d2">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">981</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5619</data>
      <data key="d7">365820e8be2d4092a333674503f2930a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIELOMA M&#218;LTIPLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mieloma m&#250;ltiple es un tipo de c&#225;ncer de la sangre que se caracteriza por la proliferaci&#243;n anormal de c&#233;lulas plasm&#225;ticas en la m&#233;dula &#243;sea. Esta enfermedad puede provocar hipercalcemia, que es un aumento de los niveles de calcio en la sangre, debido a la destrucci&#243;n &#243;sea asociada con el mieloma. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado una posible asociaci&#243;n entre el mieloma m&#250;ltiple y el consumo elevado de pescado. En general, el mieloma m&#250;ltiple puede afectar los niveles de calcio en la sangre, lo que se relaciona con anormalidades en la concentraci&#243;n de este mineral.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">980</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5620</data>
      <data key="d7">4873c3a3655342bb9de2d2b73224a059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALCEMIA MALIGNA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5621</data>
      <data key="d7">d20dc5d3c47749c380ccb15e7308f31a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPARATHYROIDISM SECUNDARY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5622</data>
      <data key="d7">a021ce197d274aab873bbdc9cf890eef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HODGKIN'S LYMPHOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hodgkin's lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the lymphatic system and is associated with hypercalcemia due to tumor production of 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5623</data>
      <data key="d7">2b607cfcb19a40a9b6cb7658410868ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NON-HODGKIN'S LYMPHOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma is a group of blood cancers that includes all types of lymphoma except Hodgkin's lymphoma, also linked to hypercalcemia in some cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5624</data>
      <data key="d7">8fda87b3a1324c8ea2c26fb7402699a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARATHYROID HORMONE (PTH)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Parathyroid hormone is a hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium levels in the blood and is involved in the pathophysiology of hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5625</data>
      <data key="d7">cf7eaf25fee847cdbc0d287d99f93dfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinoma refers to a type of cancer that starts in the skin or in tissues that line or cover internal organs, which can lead to ectopic PTH secretion and hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5626</data>
      <data key="d7">d07e225418e6491ea14f4e4615378c4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIMARY HYPERPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary hyperparathyroidism is a specific type of hyperparathyroidism that occurs due to an issue within the parathyroid glands themselves, often leading to elevated calcium levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5627</data>
      <data key="d7">852d4019a02b46ae8c7b82000872ed92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEPHROCALCINOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nephrocalcinosis is a condition characterized by the deposition of calcium in the renal parenchyma, often associated with hypercalcemia and hyperparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5628</data>
      <data key="d7">fb4a97e5859b49afbf01271d91187601</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CREATININE CLEARANCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatinine clearance is a measure of kidney function that can be affected by hyperparathyroidism, particularly when levels fall below 60 ml/min.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5629</data>
      <data key="d7">f34974440d3045c98cf1541e83ad9d76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARATHYROIDECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parathyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove one or more parathyroid glands, often indicated in cases of symptomatic hyperparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5630</data>
      <data key="d7">d1025d9df9f74512b21bd7cceb4f62ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WORKSHOP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fourth International Workshop refers to a conference focused on guidelines for the management of hyperparathyroidism, providing recommendations for treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae9d1fec31d651598e2db7436382c906</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5631</data>
      <data key="d7">5c0b2008482d4cfba895fb9a2d822e72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERCALCEMIA HIPOCALCI&#218;RICA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipercalcemia hipocalci&#250;rica familiar (HHF) es un trastorno hereditario autos&#243;mico dominante que afecta la regulaci&#243;n del calcio en el cuerpo, causado por mutaciones en el gen receptor sensor del calcio (CASR).</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d3">180</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5632</data>
      <data key="d7">45a799f0cade4e2194a0a4b9640a7e37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARATIROIDECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La paratiroidectom&#237;a es una intervenci&#243;n quir&#250;rgica que puede beneficiar a pacientes con hiperparatiroidismo primario leve y hipercalcemia hipocalci&#250;rica familiar.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d3">180</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5633</data>
      <data key="d7">f8c7c32811914ff7b247718617aad22f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CASR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El gen receptor sensor del calcio (CASR) es responsable de la regulaci&#243;n del calcio en el cuerpo y su mutaci&#243;n puede causar hipercalcemia hipocalci&#250;rica familiar.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d3">180</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5634</data>
      <data key="d7">aafeb2c7b8584c95baaae69f8e01a735</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTHRP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PTHRP, or parathyroid hormone-related peptide, is a protein that plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body. It is particularly noted for its association with malignancies, as it can lead to hypercalcemia, a condition characterized by elevated calcium levels in the blood. This effect is especially observed in patients with solid tumors that are not metastatic. PTHrP's ability to induce hypercalcemia highlights its importance in the context of certain cancers and underscores its relevance in medical discussions surrounding tumor-related calcium dysregulation.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">974</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5635</data>
      <data key="d7">d5c542f76f394fa38091017e5795ccb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALCEMIA RELACIONADA CON PTHRP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipercalcemia relacionada con PTHrP elevada es una condici&#243;n que representa hasta el 80% de los pacientes con hipercalcemia de malignidad.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d3">974</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5636</data>
      <data key="d7">34ed209fd07d48668417281414a51dec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALCEMIA DE MALIGNIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipercalcemia de malignidad es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que se presenta en pacientes con c&#225;ncer, donde la hipercalcemia es causada por mecanismos relacionados con tumores.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d3">974</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5637</data>
      <data key="d7">d00851799b42415d9d5719de0b40cdd5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPECT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SPECT, which stands for Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography, is a nuclear imaging technique that generates three-dimensional images of the body. This advanced imaging modality is often utilized in conjunction with other imaging techniques to enhance diagnostic accuracy. SPECT is particularly valuable in improving the detection of parathyroid glands, among other applications, making it a crucial tool in medical imaging.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">1320</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5638</data>
      <data key="d7">11d2f66378a24204a32bf6d628149266</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAMMAGRAF&#205;A CON SESTAMIBI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gammagraf&#237;a con sestamibi is a type of imaging test used to locate parathyroid adenomas in patients suspected of having hyperparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5639</data>
      <data key="d7">a6f9f80942da4f579224d261cd3f71e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER ESOF&#193;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico es una enfermedad maligna que afecta el es&#243;fago, un &#243;rgano crucial en el sistema digestivo. Esta condici&#243;n puede tener efectos significativos sobre el estado nutricional de los pacientes, ya que puede llevar a complicaciones que afectan la ingesta y absorci&#243;n de nutrientes. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado que el c&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico puede estar asociado con la hipercalcemia, una condici&#243;n caracterizada por niveles elevados de calcio en la sangre. Los estudios tambi&#233;n indican que el consumo de carne roja y procesada est&#225; relacionado con un aumento en el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, un tipo espec&#237;fico de c&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico. En resumen, el c&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico no solo representa un desaf&#237;o m&#233;dico en t&#233;rminos de tratamiento y manejo, sino que tambi&#233;n plantea preocupaciones nutricionales significativas para quienes lo padecen.</data>
      <data key="d2">397cb82cce268866351c44a5b38ccb8b,40dcfaa6144c6424068ba46fdf288dd2,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">955</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5640</data>
      <data key="d7">3eafed4e138b4dbb97d142e43f129399</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE CUELLO UTERINO BULBAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de cuello uterino bulbar is a type of cancer that can cause hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5641</data>
      <data key="d7">3a358ab25bd34d7896e60a2cede1b530</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer renal is a type of kidney cancer that is often associated with hypercalcemia. It has been linked to obesity, which significantly increases the mortality risk for those affected. Research has also explored the relationship between c&#225;ncer renal and dietary factors, particularly the consumption of fish and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, studies indicate that a diet rich in plant fiber and legumes may reduce the risk of developing this type of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,b110392fc91bc3d7875124ec3fa07c46</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5642</data>
      <data key="d7">a5d24f0829154ca992a69724ff5eb23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER VESICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer vesical, or bladder cancer, is a type of malignancy that can be influenced by various dietary factors. Research suggests that the antioxidant properties found in fruits and vegetables may play a role in reducing the risk of developing bladder cancer, particularly among smokers. Additionally, this type of cancer is associated with certain health complications, such as hypercalcemia. Furthermore, there is an increased risk of bladder cancer linked to the consumption of processed meats. Overall, dietary choices, particularly the intake of antioxidants from fruits and vegetables, are significant factors in the risk profile for c&#225;ncer vesical.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
      <data key="d3">983</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5643</data>
      <data key="d7">5ff69fdb26244ca18038791adbad8015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE C&#201;LULAS DE LOS ISLOTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumores de c&#233;lulas de los islotes can also produce excess PTHrP, contributing to hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5644</data>
      <data key="d7">fcdb164764e14e36a373a5feb6d0b933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinoides are tumors that may lead to hypercalcemia through the production of PTHrP.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5645</data>
      <data key="d7">b58c516a267a4d798b73ddb77fb43838</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFOMA DE LINFOCITOS T AGRESIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Linfoma de linfocitos T agresivo is a hematological cancer associated with excessive PTHrP production and hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5646</data>
      <data key="d7">94c4502a57834ee6a06558fd67147b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER EPIDERMICO PULMONAR">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5647</data>
      <data key="d7">97bb9375e26544b89d9c2afb9c3576d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HPP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HPP refers to Hyperparathyroidism, a medical condition characterized by the overproduction of parathyroid hormone, which can lead to elevated levels of calcium in the blood. This condition necessitates careful diagnosis and management primarily based on biochemical findings rather than imaging studies. Additionally, hyperparathyroidism can be associated with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), a genetic disorder that affects the endocrine glands.</data>
      <data key="d2">de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d3">1320</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5648</data>
      <data key="d7">66d0f7ee1c2b48478583567da70fed03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIBI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MIBI refers to Methoxyisobutylisonitrile, a radiopharmaceutical used in imaging studies for localizing parathyroid adenomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">1320</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5649</data>
      <data key="d7">ada744ad969c40d392386683fbdb529a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REED LARSEN P">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Reed Larsen P is a prominent co-author and contributor to the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, a comprehensive resource that delves into various aspects of endocrine physiology and pathology. His work focuses on providing valuable insights into endocrine disorders, their management, and specific conditions such as insulinoma and hypercalcemia. Additionally, Reed Larsen P is recognized for his contributions related to neuroendocrine tumors within the context of the textbook. Overall, his expertise and authorship play a significant role in enhancing the understanding of endocrinology through this essential medical reference.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">1300</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5650</data>
      <data key="d7">3df46028974c40e2a06978cc0877acf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BISPHOSPHONATES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bisphosphonates are a class of medications that play a crucial role in the management of bone health. They are primarily known for their ability to inhibit bone resorption, making them effective in treating conditions such as hypercalcemia that arises from osteoclastic activity. Additionally, bisphosphonates are beneficial in preventing bone loss and may be indicated for certain patients with Anorexia Nervosa, especially those who are at risk of developing osteoporosis. This dual functionality highlights their importance in both general bone health management and specific clinical scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb,de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5651</data>
      <data key="d7">9a50685379f64b5b8b7680da61dd5625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUROSEMIDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Furosemide is a loop diuretic that can be used to promote calcium excretion but may worsen volume depletion if not used carefully.</data>
      <data key="d2">de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5652</data>
      <data key="d7">b8d782f0e60740c8a68989713b5b20ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SERUM PHYSIOLOGICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serum physiological refers to saline solution used for rehydration in patients with hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5653</data>
      <data key="d7">001bb121037f4adebdcac50526b02645</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPLASIA PARATIROIDEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperplasia paratiroidea refers to the enlargement of the parathyroid glands, which can lead to increased calcium levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">de7d109afad1dbd144cb8e76c49ed638</data>
      <data key="d3">973</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5654</data>
      <data key="d7">c0d719c6060f4acbbbcade675d914ee4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARMACOS ANTIRRESORTIVOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Antiresorptive drugs are medications used to prevent the loss of bone mass and are often used in conjunction with calcitonin for treating severe hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5655</data>
      <data key="d7">a3ed66769dd945b28288844f0948497d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAMIDRONATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pamidronate is a bisphosphonate medication used to treat high calcium levels in the blood, particularly in cases of malignancy-related hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5656</data>
      <data key="d7">e11e2d2bfed748f1a38d425fa771f6f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUROSEMIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Furosemida, also known as furosemide, is a diuretic medication primarily used to treat fluid build-up associated with conditions such as heart failure, liver scarring, and kidney disease. It is effective in managing fluid retention and high blood pressure, and it can also assist in the treatment of hypercalcemia and hyponatremia by promoting the elimination of excess water from the body. 

To maximize its effectiveness, furosemida should be taken on an empty stomach, as food can alter gastrointestinal motility and reduce its bioavailability. Additionally, it is often used in conjunction with other treatments for conditions like the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Overall, furosemida plays a crucial role in managing fluid balance and sodium levels in patients with various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1423</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5657</data>
      <data key="d7">fe1ac45a9fdf4addbc92d4b834ecbc2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUERO SALINO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Saline solution is often used in medical treatments to help hydrate patients and can be part of the management strategy for hypercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5658</data>
      <data key="d7">f21312c7fa7346cf9650a48db6ca5cdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHANE E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Shane E is an author referenced in the context of hypercalcemia treatment in UpToDate.</data>
      <data key="d2">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5659</data>
      <data key="d7">e87385c226044e4a9803d379e49017fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERENSON JR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Berenson JR is an author referenced in the context of hypercalcemia treatment in UpToDate.</data>
      <data key="d2">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d3">1284</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5660</data>
      <data key="d7">70197ca1994d4a0086071b168f78d4aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EASTELL R">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Eastell R is an author of clinical practice guidelines focused on the pharmacological management of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5661</data>
      <data key="d7">72d34b3f4da64affb7c192a9e33c46f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOLTZMAN D">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Goltzman D is an author recognized for his contributions to the understanding of hypocalcemia, particularly focusing on its diagnostic approaches and etiology in adults. His work emphasizes the importance of accurately diagnosing hypocalcemia and exploring its underlying causes, providing valuable insights into this medical condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5662</data>
      <data key="d7">099d91f1f8ea4cba8e515ea4ae54fb15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOHYPOPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudohypoparathyroidism is a condition characterized by resistance to parathyroid hormone (PTH) action, leading to hypocalcemia and hyperphosphatemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5663</data>
      <data key="d7">35c29f0b809c451d8b3d9ecabad81267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISECCI&#211;N CERVICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Disecci&#243;n cervical is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of lymph nodes in the neck, often performed in cancer treatment, which can impact parathyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d2">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5664</data>
      <data key="d7">3a18e73a74e144a99b5d2c86f55480e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEODISTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteodistrofia hereditaria de Albright is a genetic disorder characterized by bone abnormalities and resistance to parathyroid hormone.</data>
      <data key="d2">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5665</data>
      <data key="d7">1f8f51ff811b4ea39835b469388efa8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GNAS1">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">GNAS1 is a gene that encodes the alpha subunit of the G protein that binds to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, playing a crucial role in signal transduction for parathyroid hormone responses.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5666</data>
      <data key="d7">644dd20add444ccfa1578c02fc3e4e99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEODYSTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteodystrophy is a condition characterized by round faces, short stature, short fourth metacarpal bones, obesity, subcutaneous calcifications, and developmental delay, associated with mutations in GNAS1.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5667</data>
      <data key="d7">49355775303f40f28a83dcff66e14cf3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOPSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudopseudohypoparathyroidism is a condition where individuals have the phenotype of osteodystrophy but normal serum calcium, phosphate, and PTH levels due to the normal maternal allele.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5668</data>
      <data key="d7">46ff2e0657c047b5b45797e19eff25f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 1a pseudohypoparathyroidism is an autosomal dominant condition requiring maternal transmission of the mutation, leading to resistance to hormones coupled with G proteins.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5669</data>
      <data key="d7">f4fea5a76a9942048fd6489296a296d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1B">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 1b pseudohypoparathyroidism is characterized by hypocalcemia without the phenotypic anomalies of osteodystrophy, with resistance to PTH confined to the kidney.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5670</data>
      <data key="d7">4f28f49d015a4c25a955117fb0292e4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1C">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 1c pseudohypoparathyroidism involves mutations affecting G protein coupling to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, leading to resistance to other hormones while maintaining the ability to stimulate adenyl cyclase.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5671</data>
      <data key="d7">815088076f9a40a986fb57046fc8c330</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism shows normal AMPc response to PTH but abnormal phosphaturia, lacking the osteodystrophy phenotype and familial characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5672</data>
      <data key="d7">41d7e83f7eec43679ac1a60c79b31608</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIAG&#201;ORGE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">DiGeorge syndrome is a genetic disorder that can lead to various health issues, including hypoparathyroidism and calcium metabolism disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">73</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5673</data>
      <data key="d7">bd4b537d9ae949df9140e12f53707cfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium levels in the blood and bone metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5674</data>
      <data key="d7">55063a91d172452ca52bbad98db49362</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA LUTEINIZANTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La hormona luteinizante, conocida como LH (luteinizing hormone en ingl&#233;s), es una hormona producida por la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria. Esta hormona desempe&#241;a un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n del ciclo menstrual y la ovulaci&#243;n, siendo fundamental para el funcionamiento del sistema reproductivo.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5675</data>
      <data key="d7">2ddb791c3a414da19a79750e65e01d55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA ESTIMULANTE DEL FOL&#205;CULO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) is a hormone involved in the regulation of reproductive processes, including the development of eggs in ovaries and sperm in testes.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5676</data>
      <data key="d7">4258c83821da4e2682eec7e04761baa3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA LIBERADORA DE GONADOTROPINA (GNRH)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) is a hormone responsible for the release of FSH and LH from the pituitary gland, playing a crucial role in reproductive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">1364</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5677</data>
      <data key="d7">8728fe01290045929b3f2c0dd52df914</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECEPTOR PTH/PTHRP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The PTH/PTHrP receptor is a receptor that binds parathyroid hormone and parathyroid hormone-related peptide, mediating their effects on calcium and phosphate metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5678</data>
      <data key="d7">3dbffb7ce87048e893712bebbed74210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENIL-CICLASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenyl cyclase is an enzyme that converts ATP to cyclic AMP, playing a key role in signal transduction pathways, including those activated by hormones like PTH.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d3">625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5679</data>
      <data key="d7">e7ce85ea90624d06bf6c30019f800985</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS ACOPLADAS A PROTE&#205;NA G">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">G protein-coupled hormones are a class of hormones that exert their effects through G protein-coupled receptors, influencing various physiological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5680</data>
      <data key="d7">4ce1da6bc42944229263e2e8f56d2396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE DIGEORGE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de DiGeorge es un trastorno cong&#233;nito que se asocia con la ausencia de gl&#225;ndulas paratiroides y otras anomal&#237;as cong&#233;nitas.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5681</data>
      <data key="d7">79c29498590e4d88a119e0bde6a6ecfa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCALINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las fosfatasas alcalinas son enzimas que pueden elevarse en la deficiencia de vitamina D, indicando problemas en el metabolismo &#243;seo.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5682</data>
      <data key="d7">0a37c5216f66411d9e76c6790b4de2ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RAQUITISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RAQUITISMO, tambi&#233;n conocido como raquitismo, es una enfermedad metab&#243;lica &#243;sea que afecta principalmente a los ni&#241;os y resulta de la deficiencia de vitamina D. Esta condici&#243;n se caracteriza por un desarrollo &#243;seo inadecuado, lo que provoca la desmineralizaci&#243;n en la placa de crecimiento y, como consecuencia, deformidades &#243;seas. Adem&#225;s, el raquitismo puede desarrollarse en pacientes cel&#237;acos debido a la malabsorci&#243;n de calcio y vitamina D, y tambi&#233;n puede ser una complicaci&#243;n de la enfermedad de Wilson. En resumen, el raquitismo es una enfermedad que lleva a la formaci&#243;n de huesos blandos y d&#233;biles, afectando gravemente el crecimiento y desarrollo de los ni&#241;os.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6,bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5683</data>
      <data key="d7">8a444e51a9ba41a69bf1f0c5804ded61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFATASA ALCALINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that is often elevated in cases of bone disease and is used as a marker in diagnosing conditions related to bone metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d3">617</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5684</data>
      <data key="d7">16cae6a6e606466b8a22078243be9d15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="25(OH)D">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">25-hydroxyvitamin D is a form of vitamin D that is measured in the blood to assess vitamin D status.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5685</data>
      <data key="d7">406d826b7b044d1b9ddfb26e811ec4da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1,25(OH)&#8322;D&#8323;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 is the active form of vitamin D that regulates calcium and phosphate metabolism in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5686</data>
      <data key="d7">3a7df486fe6a4b20968fb98709bdd038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDROXILACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hydroxylation is a biochemical process that activates vitamin D in the liver and kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d2">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1067</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5687</data>
      <data key="d7">966663d9da9147fb85fe209d49651b65</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAWSON-HUGHES B.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dawson-Hughes B. is an author who has contributed to the understanding of vitamin D deficiency in adults, focusing on its definition, clinical manifestations, and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">1286</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5688</data>
      <data key="d7">5fbf45324cb94a109e1aa9116171f20d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DREZNER MK.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Drezner MK. is an author who has explored the causes of vitamin D deficiency and resistance, contributing to the medical literature on the subject.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">1286</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5689</data>
      <data key="d7">44fb2d91d60a4ceaab39b236b75bc0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERGOCALCIFEROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ergocalciferol, also known as vitamin D2, is a form of vitamin D that is utilized to treat vitamin D deficiency and associated conditions. It plays a crucial role in maintaining healthy levels of vitamin D in the body, which is essential for various physiological functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5690</data>
      <data key="d7">ab6bffb983ba4365ae2ed1925c5054f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIFEDIOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcifediol is a metabolite of vitamin D that is used in the treatment of vitamin D deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5691</data>
      <data key="d7">0d3e63cfeb8040f8babba801f3925a7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypocalcemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise from various factors, including vitamin D deficiency. Additionally, hypocalcemia is commonly observed in a significant percentage of patients suffering from pancreatitis, where it is often associated with metabolic disturbances.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf</data>
      <data key="d3">1653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5692</data>
      <data key="d7">a10e051fa3b048f5b879dac125a15275</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPOPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypoparathyroidism is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone by the parathyroid glands. This deficiency results in low levels of calcium in the blood, which can lead to various complications, including potential bone issues. Patients with hypoparathyroidism often require treatment with vitamin D to help manage their calcium levels effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">1653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5693</data>
      <data key="d7">ac919518c17d4d17966989743e5be9a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RADIATION ULTRAVIOLETA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ultraviolet radiation is a type of light that helps the skin synthesize vitamin D when exposed, playing a crucial role in preventing vitamin D deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5694</data>
      <data key="d7">0c3fb5a7e79a470fb10e88af7a4db387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALABSORPTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malabsorption is a medical condition characterized by the intestine's inability to properly absorb nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition is often observed in patients with celiac disease and can result in various nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin D deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6,3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5695</data>
      <data key="d7">5b79c4f53f1240a0ac1f7c67b2e6278f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIEPILEPTIC MEDICATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Antiepileptic medications can affect the metabolism of vitamin D, potentially leading to deficiencies in patients taking these drugs.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5696</data>
      <data key="d7">f493201492204e239bd6ca47d43f6219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUBERCULOSTATIC MEDICATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tuberculostatic medications are used to treat tuberculosis and can also impact vitamin D metabolism, contributing to deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5697</data>
      <data key="d7">c6568283dc404c54807da4e8cbc8ca03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIHIDROTAQUISTEROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dihidrotaquisterol is a metabolite of vitamin D that can be used in specific medical conditions related to vitamin D metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5698</data>
      <data key="d7">bfcd17964ca64f9e95880f69263dc449</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIDIOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcidiol is a vitamin D metabolite that does not require hepatic 25-hydroxylation and is useful in patients with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3</data>
      <data key="d3">621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5699</data>
      <data key="d7">08654904e8b040c58707f7130bda15e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALASEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thalassemia is a blood disorder that can lead to complications requiring multiple blood transfusions, potentially affecting parathyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d2">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3</data>
      <data key="d3">681</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5700</data>
      <data key="d7">bc405eb8cc084535b2f2e70e33714214</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASOCIACI&#211;N AMERICANA DE REUMATOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Rheumatology Association suggests guidelines for patients taking glucocorticoids to maintain calcium and vitamin D intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1290</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5701</data>
      <data key="d7">b290434e00234c7eb6cbfa3642871a24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALENDRONATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alendronato, also known as Alendronate, is a bisphosphonate medication primarily used to treat osteoporosis. It is effective in reducing bone resorption and increasing bone mineral density, which helps to lower the risk of fractures in individuals with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5702</data>
      <data key="d7">428bb1ac6c1d4761ba790b78512fc345</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RISEDRONATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Risedronate is a bisphosphonate medication that helps reduce the risk of vertebral and hip fractures in osteoporosis patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5703</data>
      <data key="d7">72dff54746f14108b400ac6185932af9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IBANDRONATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ibandronate is a bisphosphonate that suppresses bone resorption and significantly reduces the rate of vertebral fractures.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5704</data>
      <data key="d7">fcb247452b0943a8bb76708a6fc19552</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRATURAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fractures are breaks in bones that can occur more frequently in individuals with osteoporosis, especially when treated with glucocorticoids.</data>
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1290</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5705</data>
      <data key="d7">d493444fc2234e5298b80c4f8136926c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DREZNER MK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Drezner MK is a prominent figure in the field of medicine, particularly known for his contributions to clinical studies on osteoporosis, with a specific focus on diagnosis and evaluation in postmenopausal women. In addition to his research work, Drezner MK serves as an editor for UpToDate, a reputable resource that provides comprehensive medical information, including topics related to endocrine neoplasia. His dual roles in research and editorial work highlight his commitment to advancing medical knowledge and improving patient care in these important areas.</data>
      <data key="d2">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1310</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5706</data>
      <data key="d7">2bc50d70cf9a499c80c9c38f25709b48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROSE HN">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">15cc53e1fcf2a1afd24bf25a2b059f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1286</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5707</data>
      <data key="d7">f5ffd0fe530c43d9bf2c8d2574c119d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIZEDRONATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Risedronato is a bisphosphonate medication that helps in the treatment of osteoporosis by reducing bone resorption and increasing bone mineral density.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5708</data>
      <data key="d7">619cfa27a9554daeb311f1a976286999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENOSUMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Denosumab is a fully human monoclonal antibody that functions by inhibiting RANKL, a key factor in the regulation of bone resorption. This mechanism leads to a reduction in bone resorption and an increase in bone mineral density, making it an effective treatment for osteoporosis. Additionally, Denosumab has been utilized in patients suffering from chronic anorexia nervosa who also have osteoporosis, highlighting its versatility in addressing bone health in various clinical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">606</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5709</data>
      <data key="d7">194bc6e5782d4f0eb156bdfef272dbb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RALOXIFENO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Raloxifene is a selective estrogen receptor modulator that reduces the risk of vertebral and hip fractures in postmenopausal women with osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5710</data>
      <data key="d7">0f4bf52eabc14edea606b25c751eae09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROSEN CJ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Rosen CJ is a prominent figure in the field of osteoporosis management, recognized for his contributions to clinical guidelines and research. He has authored several studies that enhance the understanding and treatment of osteoporosis. Additionally, Rosen CJ serves as an editor and contributor to UpToDate, where he focuses on the clinical features and evaluation of glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis, further solidifying his expertise and influence in this area of medicine.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d3">1286</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5711</data>
      <data key="d7">d34f1e6aa13145f8aa94a25a02f73fc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK DM">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Black DM is a researcher actively engaged in the field of osteoporosis, focusing on studies and the development of clinical guidelines for its management. In addition to this work, Black DM is also investigating intestinal calcium absorption, particularly in the context of gastric bypass surgery. This dual focus highlights Black DM's commitment to advancing knowledge in both osteoporosis and the nutritional implications of surgical weight loss procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5712</data>
      <data key="d7">5e4fc0f2305447a4944cc5b360cbf230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOCLASTO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteoclasts are cells that break down bone tissue, and their activity is inhibited by treatments like denosumab and bisphosphonates.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">606</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5713</data>
      <data key="d7">800a0e88aee74fe29c0ed04aecab81c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RANELATO DE ESTRONCIO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ranelato de estroncio, also known as strontium ranelate, is a medication specifically designed for the treatment of osteoporosis, particularly in postmenopausal women. It functions through a dual mechanism: it stimulates the absorption of calcium in the bones while simultaneously inhibiting the resorption of bone tissue. This unique action helps to reduce the risk of fractures and supports overall bone health in individuals suffering from osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5714</data>
      <data key="d7">198da5ce47e14db1935afd4ec00ded13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAMOXIFENO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tamoxifen, also known as Tamoxifeno, is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that is primarily used in the treatment and prevention of breast cancer. In addition to its role in oncology, Tamoxifen has been noted for its effects on bone density, making it a multifaceted medication in the management of breast cancer and related health concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d3">644</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5715</data>
      <data key="d7">c8413ee79aeb4f50af656f403a982e6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BISFOSFONATOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">BISFOSFONATOS are medications used as an adjunct treatment for patients with celiac disease to prevent the loss of bone mineral density.</data>
      <data key="d2">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5716</data>
      <data key="d7">bb7b727bd6fa44d68c5b0138f04f8381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOCLASTOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteoclasts are cells that break down bone tissue, playing a crucial role in bone remodeling and the pathophysiology of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5717</data>
      <data key="d7">9f22fb0e12134868a227ffeb7e07189c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUESO TRABECULAR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Trabecular bone is the spongy tissue inside bones that is most affected by osteoporosis, particularly in postmenopausal women.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5718</data>
      <data key="d7">7ae8664a689b44b6a01d2ac0779b7a22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DMO VERTEBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DMO vertebral refers to vertebral bone mineral density, which is a crucial indicator of bone health and plays a significant role in assessing bone loss, particularly in cases of glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis. It is sensitive to changes in osteoporosis, making it an important measure for monitoring bone density and overall skeletal health.</data>
      <data key="d2">08bc93c6dcf6df5ebf660f30b1f1ef2d,9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d3">603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5719</data>
      <data key="d7">e71fec6126ef419ca73efd6ea30c0f5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis is a medical condition resulting from the use of glucocorticoids, leading to bone density loss and increased fracture risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d3">603</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5720</data>
      <data key="d7">859b88e09d984fb08d73192e20dfd776</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOMALACIA ONCOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica es un s&#237;ndrome paraneopl&#225;sico adquirido poco frecuente que se caracteriza por anomal&#237;as bioqu&#237;micas y de mineralizaci&#243;n &#243;sea similares a las del raquitismo hipofosfat&#233;mico.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5721</data>
      <data key="d7">37c4265a5b394a6d8ead4df1a3f3d530</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FGF23">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El factor de crecimiento de fibroblastos 23 (FGF23) es una prote&#237;na fosfat&#250;rica que se expresa y secreta ect&#243;picamente en tumores mesenquimatosos asociados con la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica. Adem&#225;s, FGF23 act&#250;a como un nuevo regulador del metabolismo fosfoc&#225;lcico, influyendo en la eliminaci&#243;n urinaria de f&#243;sforo. Esta prote&#237;na desempe&#241;a un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n de los niveles de f&#243;sforo en el organismo, lo que la convierte en un elemento importante en el estudio de trastornos relacionados con el metabolismo mineral.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5722</data>
      <data key="d7">be07a3f4d6134263a39d17a9ce56ae3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores mesenquimatosos son neoplasias polimorfas peque&#241;as de crecimiento lento que pueden causar osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica al secretar FGF23 y otras prote&#237;nas fosfat&#250;ricas.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5723</data>
      <data key="d7">558f5148e4cf45639c6daef285bcde18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUESOS LARGOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Los huesos largos son una de las localizaciones donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5724</data>
      <data key="d7">e10eea4f916d4e19b12671b1f0852a04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXTREMIDADES DISTALES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Las extremidades distales son otra localizaci&#243;n donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5725</data>
      <data key="d7">f1835bfb764a49ea8a0bc55425c4e7d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NASOFARINGE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">La nasofaringe es una de las &#225;reas anat&#243;micas donde pueden localizarse tumores mesenquimatosos responsables de la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5726</data>
      <data key="d7">483a714c67cb4a3eb2197d916160d40e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENOS NASALES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Los senos nasales son otra localizaci&#243;n donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5727</data>
      <data key="d7">ecbae35932d04fd7bb796c56f5df4d78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">La ingle es una de las &#225;reas donde se pueden localizar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5728</data>
      <data key="d7">8b23f101b4e24e4b9a950676f1f2a21d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1&#913;-HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">1&#945;-hidroxilasa is an enzyme crucial for the activation of vitamin D, affecting calcium and phosphate metabolism</data>
      <data key="d2">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d3">615</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5729</data>
      <data key="d7">f22b035904c146e99ab706a98881837b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CYP27B1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CYP27B1 is a gene that encodes the enzyme 1&#945;-hidroxilasa, mutations of which can lead to vitamin D deficiency disorders</data>
      <data key="d2">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d3">615</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5730</data>
      <data key="d7">4cb7b24cb9ea472a8fc7494dd766edd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS NEUROGLUCOP&#201;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#237;ntomas neuroglucop&#233;nicos are symptoms resulting from low glucose levels affecting the brain, often seen in patients with insulinoma</data>
      <data key="d2">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5731</data>
      <data key="d7">9651560487224259b3804a37b518b127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS SIMP&#193;TICOS ADRENALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S&#237;ntomas simp&#225;ticos adrenales are autonomic symptoms that can occur during hypoglycemic episodes</data>
      <data key="d2">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5732</data>
      <data key="d7">193171f6c18c47afab5055138c2e97b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES ENDOCRINOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumores endocrinos are tumors that arise from endocrine glands, including insulinomas</data>
      <data key="d2">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5733</data>
      <data key="d7">7ecb066ae58c49c78b2d6349b82b88de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Insulinoma is a type of tumor that leads to hyperinsulinism, a condition characterized by excessive levels of insulin in the blood. This often results in hypoglycemia, which is a dangerously low level of glucose in the bloodstream. The diagnosis of insulinoma typically involves specific biochemical tests that help identify the presence of the tumor and assess its impact on insulin production.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">5734</data>
      <data key="d7">d154e35f4bb341679706a33dd39cb305</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRYER PE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cryer PE is one of the authors of the guidelines for the evaluation and management of adult hypoglycemic disorders, contributing to the understanding of insulinoma.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5735</data>
      <data key="d7">860c3aac99d442aaa87a78d0a5cb1c8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AXELROD L">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Axelrod L is a co-author of the guidelines for the evaluation and management of adult hypoglycemic disorders, providing insights into insulinoma diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5736</data>
      <data key="d7">7b3ba5c8f9d94608b013ee728f720c26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROSSMAN AB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grossman AB is a contributor to the clinical practice guidelines for managing hypoglycemic disorders, including insulinoma.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d3">1313</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5737</data>
      <data key="d7">c29757dfceba4173bb37b5789d9154c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The pancreas is a vital organ in the body that plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism and hormone production. It is involved in the secretion of important hormones, including insulin, and is a site where various tumors, such as insulinomas and somatostatinomas, can develop. Additionally, the pancreas is the focus of research published in the journal "Pancreas," which covers studies related to pancreatic diseases, including investigations into nutrition in acute pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,60d24674009cc67523f1ecdc63975fdc,69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3</data>
      <data key="d3">1312</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5738</data>
      <data key="d7">88d43b041c1345b5b24896ab206ca49b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IGF-2">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">IGF-2 is a growth factor that can be overproduced in certain tumors, leading to hypoglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5</data>
      <data key="d3">1711</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5739</data>
      <data key="d7">15bdbb8d326d4bb78097f6628e5115ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOID SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinoid syndrome is a condition that occurs when vasoactive substances escape hepatic degradation, often associated with neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5</data>
      <data key="d3">1711</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5740</data>
      <data key="d7">6b6622dae70a4f528890a3c741e66eb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROSARCOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrosarcoma is a type of mesenchymal tumor that can be associated with hypoglycemia due to the overproduction of IGF-2.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5</data>
      <data key="d3">1711</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5741</data>
      <data key="d7">9808d1c99c564f03afd10668c1f7e575</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMANGIOPERICITOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemangiopericytoma is a vascular tumor that can also lead to hypoglycemia through similar mechanisms as other tumors producing IGF-2.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5</data>
      <data key="d3">1711</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5742</data>
      <data key="d7">f40fbebf25bc47349fb84062c494ae6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOCARCINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatocarcinoma is a type of liver cancer characterized by its association with various factors, including dietary influences, particularly the consumption of vegetables. It is noted to occur in less than 10% of patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII), making it a relatively rare complication in this population. Hepatocarcinoma is recognized as the most common epithelial tumor that can lead to hypoglycemia, primarily due to the overproduction of Insulin-like Growth Factor 2 (IGF-2). Additionally, hepatocellular carcinoma, which is another form of liver cancer, can also manifest in patients with GSDIII, although it is considered rare.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5,4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d3">1714</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5743</data>
      <data key="d7">d7e95f16c33f4f6193581ebe3117cd98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GROWTH HORMONE (GH)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Growth hormone is a hormone that can be suppressed in cases of hypoglycemia, affecting glucose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">46466da830644a88f74108645c668fd5</data>
      <data key="d3">1711</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5744</data>
      <data key="d7">5a105869b87949ecb45cc590256d7816</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome carcinoide es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica caracterizada por rubefacci&#243;n, diarrea, y otros s&#237;ntomas debido a la liberaci&#243;n de sustancias vasoactivas en la circulaci&#243;n sist&#233;mica.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5745</data>
      <data key="d7">c380c441458e45be8215ffeac55f8a5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIPT&#211;FANO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tript&#243;fano is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions, including the production of serotonin, a neurotransmitter that regulates mood, sleep, and appetite. In the body, tript&#243;fano is converted into serotonin, highlighting its importance in maintaining mental health and overall well-being. However, the metabolism of tript&#243;fano can be disrupted in patients with carcinoid syndrome, a condition that affects the body's ability to process this amino acid effectively. This alteration in metabolism can have significant implications for individuals suffering from this syndrome, emphasizing the need for understanding the role of tript&#243;fano in both health and disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5746</data>
      <data key="d7">a48d04820d8c489595802a1ec34d42ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEROTONINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Serotonina, or serotonin, is a neurotransmitter that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is produced from the amino acid tryptophan and is primarily known for its involvement in regulating mood, intestinal permeability, weight control, and satiety. Additionally, serotonin has vasoconstrictive properties and is secreted by carcinoid tumors, which are a type of neuroendocrine tumor. In the liver, serotonin is metabolized to form 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). Furthermore, serotonin is mentioned in relation to the effects of tesofensina, a drug associated with weight loss. Overall, serotonin is a multifaceted substance that influences both psychological and physiological processes in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a,9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1122</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">5747</data>
      <data key="d7">de29f4464502451dae6c30fd963e9406</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TNE PANCRE&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los tumores neuroendocrinos pancre&#225;ticos son un tipo de tumor que afecta al p&#225;ncreas y se clasifican seg&#250;n el &#237;ndice Ki-67 y otros factores.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1553</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5748</data>
      <data key="d7">aea69569c53f44c49bbfb1a9d9f70789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECOCARDIOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ECOCARDIOGRAF&#205;A es un procedimiento diagn&#243;stico m&#233;dico que utiliza ultrasonido para evaluar tanto la estructura como la funci&#243;n del coraz&#243;n. Este m&#233;todo es especialmente &#250;til para detectar lesiones en pacientes que presentan s&#237;ndrome carcinoide, lo que resalta su importancia en la identificaci&#243;n de condiciones card&#237;acas espec&#237;ficas.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5749</data>
      <data key="d7">fec7068bef934482b6b5df68c3e03bbb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los carcinomas son un tipo de c&#225;ncer que puede incluir componentes no neuroendocrinos y se relacionan con los tumores neuroendocrinos.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5750</data>
      <data key="d7">97f836703ca145edabd13c975127fc7d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASA TUMORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La masa tumoral se refiere al tama&#241;o y extensi&#243;n del tumor, que influye en la aparici&#243;n del s&#237;ndrome carcinoide.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5751</data>
      <data key="d7">67e7d715971f43b8bee50fe995773a35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE NIACINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El d&#233;ficit de niacina es una condici&#243;n que puede causar s&#237;ntomas como lesiones cut&#225;neas, relacionados con el s&#237;ndrome carcinoide.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5752</data>
      <data key="d7">6434cc8d20ef42ea90d4c3cfc9952ec0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES CARCINOIDES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">TUMORES CARCINOIDES are tumors that can be diagnosed through the measurement of 5-Hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). These tumors are derived from enterchromaffin cells, which are specialized cells found in the gastrointestinal tract that produce serotonin.</data>
      <data key="d2">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,47ba8105b81c59f81a9038446898d200,7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a,eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d3">1123</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5753</data>
      <data key="d7">f7a7c42dc1e64550967979c5145a2d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WHO CLASSIFICATION OF TUMOURS OF ENDOCRINE ORGANS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The WHO Classification of Tumours of Endocrine Organs is a publication that provides guidelines and classifications for endocrine tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors, as of the 4th edition published in 2017.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1310</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5754</data>
      <data key="d7">a1fe62d3084443b49b10375d051f329b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTRINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrinomas are neuroendocrine tumors that secrete gastrin, often associated with the condition MEN1, and typically found in the duodenum.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5755</data>
      <data key="d7">84f66fd2aee34f719f7a3e9e4b46a2a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIPOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VIPOMA is a syndrome and a type of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor characterized by the secretion of vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP). This condition leads to severe, intermittent watery diarrhea, hypokalemia (low potassium levels), and achlorhydria (absence of hydrochloric acid in gastric secretions). VIPomas are specifically neuroendocrine tumors that primarily originate in the pancreas and are known for causing chronic diarrhea due to the excessive release of VIP.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d3">1312</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5756</data>
      <data key="d7">df6b31ff43d44dc38577fac7ae48ec67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCAGONOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucagonomas are rare neuroendocrine tumors that secrete glucagon, leading to a specific syndrome characterized by weight loss and diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5757</data>
      <data key="d7">611d196f70f64b348e58954bbcb21c4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOMATOSTATINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Somatostatinomas are very rare neuroendocrine tumors that secrete somatostatin, often found in the pancreas and duodenum.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5758</data>
      <data key="d7">b6676109afca4bfe9fe22a23076be7b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLINSTRA DS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Klimstra DS is a researcher known for contributions to the pathology and classification of neuroendocrine neoplasms in the digestive system.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1304</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5759</data>
      <data key="d7">c586e49bf0b6407daa85376e0b99d514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors are a specific type of neuroendocrine tumor that occurs in the pancreas, which can be functional or non-functional and vary in their clinical behavior.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5760</data>
      <data key="d7">bc38a136ba53484c8559f09b8cbb7472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOCARCINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenocarcinoma is a type of cancer that forms in mucus-secreting glands and can be a component of neuroendocrine tumors, particularly in mixed neoplasms.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5761</data>
      <data key="d7">4a249e8094a04cda9f801af1f59dfc8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA DE C&#201;LULAS EN ANILLO DE SELLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ring cell carcinoma is a rare type of cancer characterized by ring-shaped cells and can be associated with neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5762</data>
      <data key="d7">b21418e2c921459580f0e75e6ac44506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE C&#201;LULAS ESCAMOSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that arises from squamous cells and can also be a component of mixed neuroendocrine neoplasms.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5763</data>
      <data key="d7">106a86db72d44bd3b927645444a32a8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;NDICE DE PROLIFERACI&#211;N KI-67">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ki-67 proliferation index is a marker used to determine the growth fraction of a given cell population, particularly in the context of neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5764</data>
      <data key="d7">241935b1fd5345a19be921ae4b7a918d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;NDICE MIT&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The mitotic index is a measure of the number of cells undergoing mitosis in a given population, which is important for assessing the aggressiveness of tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5765</data>
      <data key="d7">08131c9d448d4ad3818c2bc2cd3bca78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d3">1309</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5766</data>
      <data key="d7">428ad421020d42058051f223bd233fb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOMATOSTATINOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Somatostatinomas are rare tumors that occur in the pancreas and duodenum, often associated with various syndromes and conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">5767</data>
      <data key="d7">15d9cd82f3184f35a6574fd1af696d2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUODENUM">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine where somatostatinomas can also occur.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5768</data>
      <data key="d7">12fcb4f148cf440ea7d132ac1ebbe2cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TYPE 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurofibromatosis type 1 is a genetic disorder that can be associated with duodenal tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5769</data>
      <data key="d7">555e58612d3442d8b0e63f348c090644</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VON HIPPEL-LINDAU SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome is a genetic condition that can be associated with duodenal tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5770</data>
      <data key="d7">4d94cf033ff0425ab68028597e2e1347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN1 SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN1 syndrome is a hereditary condition that can lead to the development of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1312</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5771</data>
      <data key="d7">5bb8ffd7caef4078bbd8d993e0343e5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROMOGRANINS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cromogranins are substances secreted by neuroendocrine tumors, often used as tumor markers.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5772</data>
      <data key="d7">85c5b79c05fc4c40946b0391c4272812</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENOLASA NEUROESPEC&#205;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enolase neuroespec&#237;fica is another marker associated with neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5773</data>
      <data key="d7">fd0f0024568249b48d202f9d319a89f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIP&#201;PTIDO PANCRE&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone secreted by pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d3">1303</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5774</data>
      <data key="d7">9cbf7490707d43fea614352bc22dc94e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GHRELINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ghrelin, also known as "GHRELINA," is a hormone primarily released in the gastric fundus. It is recognized as a potent orexigenic hormone, meaning it stimulates appetite by activating neuropeptide Y pathways in the brain. Additionally, ghrelin can be secreted by neuroendocrine tumors, which can further influence appetite and metabolism. This dual role highlights its significance in both normal physiological processes and potential pathological conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5775</data>
      <data key="d7">ec087ef7978b462d8e83defc09a91a60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERITEMA NECROL&#205;TICO MIGRATORIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Eritema necrol&#237;tico migratorio is a skin condition that can be associated with somatostatinomas and other neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5776</data>
      <data key="d7">7d5dc3fa0a644769bc8d33334681136f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIARREA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic diarrhea, known as "diarrea cr&#243;nica," is a medical condition characterized by the persistent presence of diarrhea over an extended period. This condition is often associated with dehydration and malnutrition. It can manifest in infants, particularly when lactose is introduced, as seen in cases of glucose-galactose malabsorption. Additionally, chronic diarrhea can arise from various underlying conditions, including VIPoma, which is a type of neuroendocrine tumor. The prolonged nature of chronic diarrhea can lead to malabsorption issues, potentially resulting in complications such as hypophosphatemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,5bb504bf68288cc0ba6a8f0dd9e4c245,e329b5d4c64709889680df357bd1cc09</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">5777</data>
      <data key="d7">6c2c19015fa142c692dbb8c6912407cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATECTOM&#205;A DISTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Distal pancreatectomy is a surgical procedure aimed at treating tumors located in the tail of the pancreas. This operation involves the removal of a portion of the pancreas and is often performed alongside duodenotomy, particularly in cases involving gastrinomas.</data>
      <data key="d2">11fcae49d6b540a5ad5cdfe74ed269a9,3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5778</data>
      <data key="d7">24b18155436f4971bef5a42648cbb3ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMAS NEUROENDOCRINOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neuroendocrine carcinomas are poorly differentiated tumors that often have a high proliferation index and can metastasize quickly.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5779</data>
      <data key="d7">d674e7bddd314c62aca2b621168d22d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE MEN1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN1 syndrome is a hereditary condition that predisposes individuals to multiple endocrine tumors, including pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5780</data>
      <data key="d7">9d1bfc6204d3467d92314f7403cdf359</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROFIBROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurofibromatosis is a genetic disorder that can be associated with the development of neuroendocrine tumors, particularly in the duodenum.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5781</data>
      <data key="d7">0ba4490bb1f849c689f18c8caf65a01e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES DE LAS C&#201;LULAS DE LOS ISLOTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumors of the islet cells are a type of neuroendocrine tumor that arises in the pancreas and can secrete hormones like insulin and glucagon.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5782</data>
      <data key="d7">63051799816c4c25b4751a7f53216554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEOCHROMOCITOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pheochromocytoma is a tumor of the adrenal gland that is more frequent in patients with specific mutations in the RET proto-oncogene.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d3">971</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5783</data>
      <data key="d7">df8d8a467bf04997b675c00337560c84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGADO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Higado, commonly known as the liver, is a vital organ that plays a crucial role in processing and metabolizing nutrients absorbed from the digestive tract. It provides 8 mg of iron per 100 g, highlighting its nutritional significance. The liver is also responsible for synthesizing very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL) and is integral to lipid metabolism. Additionally, it is the primary site for fructose metabolism, where enzyme deficiencies can impact energy production. However, the liver can be adversely affected by metastases from malignant pancreatic tumors, indicating its susceptibility to cancer spread in patients with such conditions. Overall, Higado is essential for various metabolic processes and is a key organ in maintaining overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728,e9734d049699822c67b55a2a56aee7b2</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5784</data>
      <data key="d7">f5bcedc9907740788818d0080c4915fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE VERNE-MORRISON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Verner-Morrison syndrome is another name for VIPoma, characterized by severe diarrhea, hypokalemia, and achlorhydria.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5785</data>
      <data key="d7">843edc53597f4114aa734bed4a2a2401</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIARREA ACUOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diarrea acuosa is a common condition frequently caused by viral or bacterial infections, and it is characterized by the presence of watery stools. This clinical symptom can also manifest in patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase, particularly upon the intake of sucrose. Additionally, watery diarrhea is a significant symptom associated with VIPoma, a type of tumor that can lead to considerable fluid loss and subsequent metabolic complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,a079902e52676a05df746098c930a0e7,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1753</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">5786</data>
      <data key="d7">eb6bb4dd06824a94b55ea3b045df591f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMOR PANCRE&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TUMOR PANCRE&#193;TICO refers to a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, which is a vital organ involved in digestion and blood sugar regulation. This condition often leads to complications such as hyperglycemia, a condition characterized by elevated blood sugar levels, and malnutrition due to the pancreas's impaired ability to produce digestive enzymes. Additionally, pancreatic tumors can be neuroendocrine in nature, which may result in specific syndromes such as VIPoma, a rare tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP) and can cause severe diarrhea and electrolyte imbalances. Overall, TUMOR PANCRE&#193;TICO encompasses a range of tumor types and associated complications that significantly impact the health and well-being of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe,c55f34a09dbf07224c85384f08173e27</data>
      <data key="d3">874</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5787</data>
      <data key="d7">870736330f7249b899d2bc5cd7d0c257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOPOATASEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypokalemia is a condition characterized by low potassium levels, often seen in patients with VIPoma due to excessive diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5788</data>
      <data key="d7">eb62b4c4d99340b186359c9ea9d4502a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDIFICACI&#211;N METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic acidosis is a condition that can arise from the severe fluid and electrolyte loss in VIPoma patients.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5789</data>
      <data key="d7">2b2e6305f26b44a58a9599290e236a4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CMT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CMT refers to medullary thyroid carcinoma, a type of cancer that arises from the parafollicular C cells of the thyroid gland.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">971</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5790</data>
      <data key="d7">85793f5276124460916f803701df18af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FEO refers to pheochromocytoma, a tumor of the adrenal gland that can cause excessive production of catecholamines, often associated with MEN2 syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5791</data>
      <data key="d7">cf254e5fc0df4d7e9bb19b58120a6e53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="E805K">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">E805K is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene that is associated with the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma and is included in the risk stratification for MEN2A.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5792</data>
      <data key="d7">d16ec82a0ed642019e4b34780cefa13d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Y806C">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Y806C is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene linked to the risk of medullary thyroid carcinoma and is part of the recommendations for surgical intervention in MEN2A.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5793</data>
      <data key="d7">c1e1372e5ae4468bb376c36c17527027</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S904C">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">S904C is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene that is associated with MEN2A and influences the clinical management of patients with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5794</data>
      <data key="d7">38ccfeaec2934b158cd773b7a882b6d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE RIESGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Niveles de riesgo refers to the classification of RET mutations into different risk categories for developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and other associated conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">970</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5795</data>
      <data key="d7">d96f7b6f15624c3b96d460b46bcd3ef7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRIBADO BIOQU&#205;MICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cribado bioqu&#237;mico refers to biochemical screening for conditions such as pheochromocytoma and hyperparathyroidism in patients with MEN syndromes.</data>
      <data key="d2">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d3">972</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5796</data>
      <data key="d7">af3482248b7b440e931e130717fcf179</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M918T">
      <data key="d0" />
