    </node>
    <node id="THOMPSON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Thompson is referenced as the developer of a surgical technique for treating gastrinomas, specifically duodenotomy plus distal pancreatectomy.</data>
      <data key="d2">11fcae49d6b540a5ad5cdfe74ed269a9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5838</data>
      <data key="d7">bd71e4f996a941d7bc4feb80b54baa50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATODUODENECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatoduodenectomy is a surgical technique recommended for treating gastrinomas, which involves the removal of the pancreas and duodenum.</data>
      <data key="d2">11fcae49d6b540a5ad5cdfe74ed269a9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5839</data>
      <data key="d7">ed5700798c924f55a70b30585ca9cf14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMORES PANCRE&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic tumors are a significant concern in the context of gastrinomas and are discussed in relation to surgical treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d2">11fcae49d6b540a5ad5cdfe74ed269a9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5840</data>
      <data key="d7">c05351f5c2c24cd6b901de5e38acb9b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MET&#193;STASIS HEP&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatic metastases are a potential complication of gastrinomas, occurring in a percentage of patients and influencing treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d2">11fcae49d6b540a5ad5cdfe74ed269a9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5841</data>
      <data key="d7">6b0625e876394d59ab36e68c344361d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MET&#193;STASIS GANGLIONARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lymph node metastases are a common issue in patients with gastrinomas, complicating treatment and prognosis.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
