    </node>
    <node id="ENRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ENRICA study is a research project conducted between 2008-2010 to assess obesity prevalence in Spain, involving a representative sample of the population.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1370</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5844</data>
      <data key="d7">6005284066654245a7c617c3f187118b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENPE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ENPE is an organization dedicated to studying obesity prevalence and its impact on public health. One of its significant initiatives is the ENPE study, a research project conducted between 2014 and 2015, which aimed to evaluate obesity prevalence within a specific age group in Spain. Through its research efforts, ENPE seeks to contribute valuable insights into the public health challenges posed by obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1373</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5845</data>
      <data key="d7">a0aced1703fc4974b89bd10e83bf5d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASTURIAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Asturias is an autonomous community located in northern Spain, distinguished by several notable characteristics. It is recognized for a higher occurrence of RTFQ gene mutations and has high rates of obesity among its population. The region is also known for its aging demographic, which significantly influences diabetes statistics in neighboring areas. In terms of healthcare, Asturias is home to prominent institutions, including the Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias and the University Hospital Central of Asturias, which provide essential medical services to the community. Additionally, patients in Asturias are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, highlighting the region's approach to healthcare management.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,16d282094937dc2b58bfd40e13934fd2,298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1,fc8df7c3d7a0d2286c55493077ed3937</data>
      <data key="d3">1373</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5846</data>
      <data key="d7">4d2dc996d07b4fa1885e5b2d282cc0cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXTREMADURA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Extremadura is an autonomous community in Spain known for its unique healthcare policies and demographic health statistics. In this region, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, highlighting the community's structured approach to healthcare management. Additionally, Extremadura boasts lower obesity prevalence rates compared to other regions in Spain, indicating a potentially healthier population in terms of weight-related issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1370</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5847</data>
      <data key="d7">f0dd9e28b2d147b1ad53aef53ffb5905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANARIAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Canarias is an autonomous community in Spain known for its significant health challenges, particularly related to diabetes and obesity. The region has been noted for having higher mortality rates associated with diabetes, which is a critical public health concern. Additionally, Canarias has a high prevalence of obesity, further complicating the health landscape of the community. In response to these issues, patients in Canarias are required to submit a justification report to the Patient Care Service of the hospitals within the Canarian Health Service in order to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs. This requirement highlights the region's efforts to manage and address the health complications arising from obesity and diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e</data>
      <data key="d3">1370</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5848</data>
      <data key="d7">27e181af80ba4b5fa6ac8de7c04f9f41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNITED STATES OF AMERICA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The United States has one of the highest obesity prevalence rates in the world, ranging between 31% and 35%.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1370</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5849</data>
      <data key="d7">d25bd2ef339647c3857ae64e8db31238</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEXICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Mexico is one of the countries with the highest obesity prevalence rates globally, with rates ranging between 31% and 35%. This significant prevalence highlights Mexico's status as a nation facing serious public health challenges related to obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">996</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5850</data>
      <data key="d7">413ec4a663f949b58d34b1020dff72f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EGYPT">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Egypt is noted for having high obesity prevalence rates, similar to the United States and Mexico.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1370</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5851</data>
      <data key="d7">f207f68ed61844ce8606a9cba5489a60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SAUDI ARABIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Saudi Arabia is a country characterized by a high prevalence of obesity, with rates estimated to be between 31% and 35%. This places it among the nations with the highest obesity prevalence rates globally.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa</data>
      <data key="d3">996</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5852</data>
      <data key="d7">e30eac7d7e3f456aa8978b9adb66e448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS ELECTROL&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TRASTORNOS ELECTROL&#205;TICOS refer to electrolyte imbalances in the body, which are significant in the context of health and nutrition. These disorders are often associated with obesity and various metabolic disorders, highlighting their relevance in dietary considerations and overall health management.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,89b0bde0358432506a0e03d4691dd2ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5853</data>
      <data key="d7">7211508e8f6d43709078566caafa278c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEURONAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurons that modulate appetite, including those expressing neuropeptide Y and agouti-related protein, which have orexigenic properties, and melanocortin pathways that are anorexigenic.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5854</data>
      <data key="d7">3bb488b59a36490188958e62ee617142</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#218;CLEO ARCUATO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The arcuate nucleus is a part of the hypothalamus involved in appetite regulation, communicating with other hypothalamic nuclei.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">5855</data>
      <data key="d7">a921832a9e224ef0bd1eeb8644928cad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#218;CLEOS DORSOMEDIAL, PARAVENTRICULAR, HIPOT&#193;LAMO LATERAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">These nuclei in the hypothalamus activate the sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous systems in response to appetite signals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">5856</data>
      <data key="d7">727cf9ad71a943a99dd11ac98286487e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEPTINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Leptina es una hormona producida por los adipocitos que desempe&#241;a un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n del apetito y el gasto metab&#243;lico. Sus niveles est&#225;n directamente relacionados con la masa grasa corporal, y se ha observado que pueden disminuir en pacientes caqu&#233;cticos, como aquellos con c&#225;ncer de es&#243;fago. Esta hormona no solo ayuda a regular el equilibrio energ&#233;tico y suprime el hambre, sino que tambi&#233;n est&#225; vinculada a los &#225;cidos grasos de cadena corta. En el contexto de la obesidad, los niveles de leptina tienden a estar elevados, lo que contribuye a un aumento del tono simp&#225;tico y a la inflamaci&#243;n. Adem&#225;s, la leptina ejerce efectos anorexig&#233;nicos al estimular las v&#237;as melanocortinas y al inhibir las v&#237;as orexig&#233;nicas, lo que refuerza su papel en la regulaci&#243;n del peso corporal.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a78cb1d502baf0116e4326e7fbcae41,1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360,c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221,e189588f51b4bb84b3621a1f846d07bc,f0d279ccc92a98dc953edafb1080630b</data>
      <data key="d3">1806</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">5857</data>
      <data key="d7">37f61d4192b04c3e85d410da676db3f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;PTIDO YY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Peptide YY is secreted in the distal intestine and primarily has anorexigenic effects, interacting with neuropeptide Y neurons.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5858</data>
      <data key="d7">8dff78a5d3a74b498d162916b0472e6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD METAB&#211;LICAMENTE SANA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"OBESIDAD METAB&#211;LICAMENTE SANA" refers to a condition characterized by individuals who are classified as obese yet do not display metabolic complications typically associated with obesity. These individuals tend to have a lower percentage of visceral fat and exhibit cardiovascular risk levels comparable to those of healthy individuals with normal weight.</data>
      <data key="d2">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5859</data>
      <data key="d7">02544ebd2a934dcd96f3320aeb8cb2cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NORMOPESO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">NORMOPESO refers to individuals who maintain a normal weight and do not experience metabolic complications. This term is associated with achieving a healthy weight, which is particularly important in the nutritional management of patients with chronic kidney disease. Maintaining a normoweight is considered a key goal for promoting overall health and preventing potential health issues related to weight and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5860</data>
      <data key="d7">140391f85e754549adfd982f5df08031</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMA NERVIOSO SIMP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The sympathetic nervous system is part of the autonomic nervous system that can influence appetite regulation and energy expenditure.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5861</data>
      <data key="d7">033fdbc5c59f4a9980e073b4c4e28ef3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMA NERVIOSO PARASIMP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The parasympathetic nervous system is part of the autonomic nervous system that can also affect appetite and digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5862</data>
      <data key="d7">a6f5d5608f0d407b834294064cbae0c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#218;CLEO ACCUMBENS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The nucleus accumbens is a brain region involved in reward and addiction, influencing eating behavior and appetite.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5863</data>
      <data key="d7">065c94b7a9fa4763af5f8a433a493292</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AM&#205;GDALA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The amygdala is a brain region associated with memory and emotions, which can impact appetite and food-related behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5864</data>
      <data key="d7">a335e663b3a340ae9fc240a9b2b7d7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#211;RTEX PREFRONTAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The prefrontal cortex is involved in executive functions and decision-making, including choices related to food intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d3">1805</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5865</data>
      <data key="d7">c32f6aa4b29f422d9ebf4aeadf425017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NURSES' HEALTH STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nurses' Health Study is a long-term epidemiological study that investigates the health effects of diet, lifestyle, and other factors among nurses, with a particular focus on women's health issues. This extensive study has been following over 90,000 women for more than 30 years, providing valuable insights into the association between food consumption, obesity, and various health outcomes. Over its 32-year duration, the Nurses' Health Study has contributed significantly to understanding how diet and lifestyle choices impact women's health.</data>
      <data key="d2">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,428616513e9e654c21ede19bd544ffbc,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc,eb275fa50517d86a71589fd318784a5b</data>
      <data key="d3">1638</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">5866</data>
      <data key="d7">09a4f8454b98406c8461ce5ccb769de2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE INVESTIGATION INTO CANCER AND NUTRITION STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The EPIC study is a large-scale research project that investigates the relationships between diet, lifestyle, and health outcomes, including cardiovascular disease, across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d2">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5867</data>
      <data key="d7">5eca809c796e4d859ca5850eaf6e7ae9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EHGNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EHGNA, or Non-Alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease, is a condition characterized by excessive fat accumulation in the liver without the influence of alcohol consumption. It is closely associated with obesity and various metabolic disorders, impacting a significant percentage of obese individuals. This condition affects a notable portion of the adult population, highlighting its relevance in discussions surrounding obesity and liver health.</data>
      <data key="d2">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,7e4178b0d21cc5424b4c54bc5de42471</data>
      <data key="d3">305</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">5868</data>
      <data key="d7">435c7cbdf8434a018d07de73e9a7fbfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD METAB&#211;LICAMENTE ENFERMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolically unhealthy obesity is characterized by the presence of metabolic complications in individuals who are obese, significantly increasing their risk for cardiovascular disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
