    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOFIT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CARDIOFIT is a study that investigates the effects of aerobic exercise on the recurrence of atrial fibrillation (AF) in individuals who have experienced weight loss. The research aims to understand how engaging in aerobic activities can influence the frequency of AF episodes in this specific population. The study highlights the significance of exercise as a potential intervention for managing atrial fibrillation, particularly in those who have successfully lost weight.</data>
      <data key="d2">884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c,ea79efb65695c260a301f5c42237e2cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1397</data>
