    <node id="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA, or bariatric surgery, is a medical procedure designed to treat severe obesity through various surgical techniques. It is primarily aimed at facilitating weight loss for individuals suffering from obesity, particularly those with related health issues such as diabetes. The procedure is increasingly utilized, especially among diabetic patients, and is associated with low complication rates; however, the risks may increase with more complex interventions.

Bariatric surgery is an elective surgical procedure performed on patients with morbid obesity, often involving techniques such as simplified gastric bypass. This surgery not only aids in significant weight loss but also contributes to the improvement of comorbidities, including better management of type 2 diabetes and potential positive effects on conditions like atrial fibrillation.

Before and after the surgery, patients are required to adhere to specific dietary management protocols to optimize outcomes. Overall, bariatric surgery serves as an effective treatment option for severe obesity, helping individuals achieve substantial weight loss and enhance their overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,64347a9be918a67f786cbdf9f9db9c8a,67f96f3e5c366f82de31f1bf189aa71f,6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa,884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
