    <node id="PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Pulm&#243;n refers to the lungs, which are vital organs in the respiratory system. Obesity is associated with a higher risk of lung cancer, highlighting the impact of body weight on lung health. Additionally, the lungs can be a site for carcinoid tumors, which primarily originate in the digestive system but can also manifest in the pulmonary region. This underscores the importance of understanding the various health risks associated with the lungs, particularly in relation to obesity and tumor development.</data>
