    </node>
    <node id="BYPASS G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">BYPASS G&#193;STRICO is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves altering the digestive system to assist patients in losing weight. This mixed surgical technique reduces the size of the stomach and modifies the digestive process, creating a small pouch from the stomach that is directly connected to the small intestine. While effective for weight loss, bypass g&#225;strico can lead to complications similar to those associated with biliopancreatic diversion, particularly when performed distally or using pure restrictive techniques. Additionally, it is often linked with the dumping syndrome, a condition that can occur after the surgery. Overall, bypass g&#225;strico is recognized as a bariatric surgery aimed at promoting significant weight loss through these surgical modifications.</data>
      <data key="d2">65e3dfcb7a0c5a2a09a98342c597c020,70b2393fa61e51fc3e772479a9792c98,7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0,8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18,b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c,bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2,e70fa2e099766154321f13c0112d436a</data>
      <data key="d3">1393</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">5930</data>
      <data key="d7">dd19c1ba7b414a0ca61db555ac30cfc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRUCE DUODENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cruce duodenal is a malabsorptive surgical technique designed to assist in weight loss, particularly for individuals suffering from severe obesity. The procedure involves a two-step process that includes a longitudinal gastrectomy, which is performed while preserving the pylorus. This approach aims to reduce the stomach's capacity and alter the digestive process, thereby promoting weight loss and improving overall health outcomes for patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0,b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
