    </node>
    <node id="GASTRECTOM&#205;A VERTICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrectom&#237;a vertical, also known as vertical gastrectomy, is a surgical procedure designed primarily for weight loss, particularly in patients suffering from severe obesity. This procedure involves the vertical removal of a portion of the stomach, which effectively reduces its size and aids in weight management. By decreasing the stomach's capacity, gastrectom&#237;a vertical helps patients achieve significant weight loss and addresses obesity-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">65e3dfcb7a0c5a2a09a98342c597c020,8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18,b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
