    <node id="BMI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">BMI, or Body Mass Index, is a widely used measure that assesses an individual's body weight in relation to their height. This calculation helps categorize individuals into different classifications: underweight, normal weight, overweight, or obese. BMI serves as an important tool in evaluating nutritional status and can influence the nutritional support needs of patients. It is commonly utilized in obesity and health assessments to provide insights into an individual's weight status, thereby aiding in the identification of potential health risks associated with being underweight or overweight.</data>
      <data key="d2">20863ac06779722abc2cbc2dd023777e,58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,7855ffa74481ba85f44e9700279250e7,cba5d81f1acff7cbf84e85ef35420521,cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
