      <data key="d7">b5ab812e878b4e64a7831c5239bb6cdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUSTAIN TRIALS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The SUSTAIN trials are a series of clinical studies evaluating the efficacy and safety of semaglutide in the treatment of type 2 diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18</data>
      <data key="d3">1398</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">5977</data>
      <data key="d7">522ebdae736f4333b412fea3626c2cfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEMAGLUTIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Semaglutide is a medication used for the treatment of type 2 diabetes, showing significant improvements in HbA1c and weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18</data>
      <data key="d3">1398</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">5978</data>
      <data key="d7">49b9179c2a754928b64f683f7e741591</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIRAGLUTIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Liraglutide is a human glucagon-like peptide-1 analog that has been extensively studied for its efficacy and safety in the management of weight and the treatment of diabetes. It is commonly used as an injectable medication for controlling type 2 diabetes. In clinical studies, liraglutide is often compared with another medication, semaglutide, highlighting its role in diabetes treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">39ea441f219d949e8bc3c6f430970689,3eddab8e3e55bbd7e6cbcd3776fecb29,8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18</data>
      <data key="d3">1398</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">5979</data>
      <data key="d7">a53bf51ac918434786eb099b2a52ffac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DERIVACI&#211;N BILIOPANCRE&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Derivaci&#243;n biliopancre&#225;tica, also known as biliopancreatic diversion, is a surgical technique designed for weight loss that significantly alters the digestive system to assist patients in achieving substantial weight reduction. This procedure has demonstrated high success rates, particularly among individuals classified as superobese. It combines elements of gastric bypass with biliopancreatic diversion to enhance malabsorption, thereby promoting effective weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d2d57471630a504ffa4a39c259d9b18,b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1393</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">5980</data>
      <data key="d7">8e07f4f2ff254125bfc969101cb7705f</data>
    </node>
