      <data key="d7">490803081fd44c9abadb534d2adcd11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTRECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of part or all of the stomach. This procedure is often performed as a treatment for obesity and is mentioned in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols. Following gastrectomy, specific nutritional protocols are necessary to support recovery, highlighting the importance of tailored post-operative care for patients undergoing this surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef,980d6217f6ec073bf1673f14542ebbf0,fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6002</data>
      <data key="d7">048f5cd82ffc4f1bb399108cad1f51e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALLIED HEALTH SCIENCES SECTION AD HOC NUTRITION COMMITTEE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">This committee provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional practices in surgical weight loss patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6003</data>
      <data key="d7">6403a6370e344e8d978ab5a6aa20cc26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASMBS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Society for Metabolic and Bariatric Surgery (ASMBS) is an organization that focuses on the treatment of obesity and related conditions through surgical methods.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6004</data>
      <data key="d7">0511e6f7c751410f8b7a49f8b0ac6efa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Laparoscopic surgery is a minimally invasive surgical technique that uses small incisions and specialized instruments, often resulting in quicker recovery times.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6005</data>
      <data key="d7">2fef57e7962e4599a453d4f4d00d58a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VERY LOW CALORIE DIET (VLCD)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VLCD is a dietary regimen that provides very low caloric intake, often used in conjunction with bariatric surgery to promote weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6006</data>
      <data key="d7">aee98005621e4c23b98fa20f5d2c9b2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POSTOPERATIVE CARE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Postoperative care involves the management and monitoring of patients after surgery to ensure proper recovery and address any complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6007</data>
      <data key="d7">81882ce2d0044dbd8a2f2f6dbe746d17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIEETARY MANAGEMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary management refers to the planning and implementation of a diet tailored to meet the specific needs of patients, especially after surgical procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6008</data>
      <data key="d7">253ab65cf60847ee98a3612fd56ad75f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY MANAGEMENT">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Dietary management involves adjusting food intake to effectively manage symptoms associated with metabolic disorders, including conditions such as galactosaemia and lactose intolerance. This approach focuses on tailoring dietary choices to alleviate the impact of these disorders on an individual's health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef,ccd3c800d2985d4ad5e2c8d6e88b1b68</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6009</data>
      <data key="d7">4043bc8b9edd456d94bf7716401b43ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">POSE (Primary Obesity Surgery Endolumenal) is a procedure suggested for treating obesity before considering bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6010</data>
      <data key="d7">3dc7ea85a6eb4f4b9209e80963763990</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAL&#211;N INTRAG&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The intragastric balloon (BIG) is a temporary therapeutic strategy for significant weight loss before bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5</data>
      <data key="d3">1062</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6011</data>
      <data key="d7">173421b64a444c40830f08e656c14b43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTRECTOM&#205;A ENDOSC&#211;PICA (APOLLO)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The endoscopic vertical gastrectomy (Apollo) aims to mimic surgical gastrectomy by suturing the stomach internally.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5</data>
      <data key="d3">1062</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6012</data>
      <data key="d7">d3735a3301774c9a8c2825ad2ea0585f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOBARRIER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EndoBarrier is a medical device designed for the treatment of obesity and type 2 diabetes, primarily by regulating gastrointestinal hormones. This innovative device, also known as the endoluminal bypass or endobarrier, is strategically placed in the duodenum to inhibit food absorption, thereby enhancing glycemic control in individuals with diabetes. Through its mechanism of action, EndoBarrier aims to provide a non-surgical option for managing these conditions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5,ecd0e2cc6ed4a480591f4ac32cd7f691</data>
      <data key="d3">521</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">6013</data>
      <data key="d7">b354cff2e03e4714aef44e37d5ea624a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2 (DM2)">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Type 2 diabetes (DM2) is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and can be improved through weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6014</data>
      <data key="d7">a851f9338c294d25aab882c16561cd11</data>
    </node>
