    <node id="HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipercolesterolemia Familiar is a genetic disorder characterized by significantly elevated cholesterol levels, particularly high levels of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol. This condition is primarily caused by mutations in the LDL receptor, which results in high cholesterol levels from birth. The disorder occurs with a frequency of approximately one individual per million and is associated with plasma cholesterol levels exceeding 500 mg/dl. Due to its implications for cardiovascular health, Hipercolesterolemia Familiar is a major focus of research within the field of endocrinology, as it often leads to serious cardiovascular events.</data>
      <data key="d2">916ad020bd9c528e55001071b4d9530b,920badd1fd76f2c279282a4a20295a55,a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6,e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a</data>
      <data key="d3">1458</data>
