      <data key="d7">cab8297f22054ac8b82508061e8a0e50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipertrigliceridemia familiar is a genetic disorder characterized by elevated triglyceride levels in the blood. This condition is transmitted as an autosomal dominant trait, meaning that it can be inherited from just one affected parent.</data>
      <data key="d2">a9ee55a5371c88622e278b2543fa7317,e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a</data>
      <data key="d3">1800</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6068</data>
      <data key="d7">f9c3826a63f04e7c824af3db9bbb0a73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERLIPIDEMIA FAMILIAR COMBINADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hiperlipidemia familiar combinada" es un trastorno gen&#233;tico que afecta entre el 0,5% y el 1% de la poblaci&#243;n norteamericana. Se caracteriza por una captaci&#243;n reducida de &#225;cidos grasos libres y una sobreproducci&#243;n de apolipoprote&#237;na B y triglic&#233;ridos, manifest&#225;ndose en forma de lipoprote&#237;nas de muy baja densidad. Esta condici&#243;n se hereda de manera autos&#243;mica dominante y se asocia con niveles elevados de l&#237;pidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y colesterol elevado. Adem&#225;s, puede presentarse como una hiperlipidemia mixta, que puede incluir hipertrigliceridemia aislada o niveles elevados de colesterol. La hiperlipidemia familiar combinada est&#225; relacionada con un alto riesgo cardiovascular, lo que la convierte en una preocupaci&#243;n significativa para la salud de quienes la padecen.</data>
      <data key="d2">14b7a8c27778bb8821d74790cd2da5ea,e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a,e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2,ed97532e0b848baf08ee24448e340f98</data>
      <data key="d3">1801</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">6069</data>
      <data key="d7">1d6b892b3aae4ae3876ad707e3d5f4d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XANTOMAS TENDINOSOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Xantomas tendinosos are cholesterol deposits that can occur in tendons, often associated with certain types of hyperlipidemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a</data>
      <data key="d3">1458</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6070</data>
      <data key="d7">34a6e03e0fb0402eaae2ee7422c77f5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARCO CORNEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arco corneal refers to a ring around the cornea that can indicate high cholesterol levels, often seen in hyperlipidemia conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0db2f1e2ec0f05e24ec079563d8952a</data>
      <data key="d3">1458</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6071</data>
      <data key="d7">3af9032e9c534f7382de9e2621602417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APOLIPOPROTE&#205;NA E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La apolipoprote&#237;na E es una prote&#237;na crucial en el catabolismo de los quilomicrones y restos de VLDL, con diferentes genotipos que afectan la dislipidemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d3">493</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6072</data>
      <data key="d7">ec7655c384fa42e6a3fa1c9217e9e3b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISBETALIPOPROTEINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Disbetalipoproteinemia is a rare lipid disorder primarily caused by homozygosity in the apolipoprotein E (apo E) gene. This condition is characterized by a mutation in the apo E gene, which significantly affects the metabolism of lipoproteins. As a result, individuals with disbetalipoproteinemia exhibit elevated levels of triglycerides and very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL) cholesterol, as well as the presence of chylomicrons in fasting states.</data>
      <data key="d2">14b7a8c27778bb8821d74790cd2da5ea,c3a9acd26c8b8bbe2144d4fe53046439,e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d3">493</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">6073</data>
      <data key="d7">fe75a3a3b2aa49628f5db4cc8063bd70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XANTOMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Xantomas are fatty deposits that can form on the skin and are indicative of lipid disorders, such as hypertriglyceridemia and dyslipidemia. These deposits are often associated with metabolic disorders and can occur in individuals with high cholesterol levels, particularly in cases of familial hypercholesterolemia and dysbetalipoproteinemia. Overall, xantomas serve as a manifestation of underlying lipid abnormalities in affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">8938669dda86a6eafe0882ea036408c1,916ad020bd9c528e55001071b4d9530b,a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98,a9ee55a5371c88622e278b2543fa7317,e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d3">493</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">6074</data>
      <data key="d7">96df5cb7d92d44fabf4a33a0b03aa639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPOPROTE&#205;NAS DE MUY BAJA DENSIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las lipoprote&#237;nas de muy baja densidad (VLDL) son un tipo de lipoprote&#237;na que se produce en el h&#237;gado y est&#225; asociada con el transporte de triglic&#233;ridos en la sangre.</data>
      <data key="d2">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d3">1804</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6075</data>
      <data key="d7">a847f86631fd46968a6146957755fa23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APOLIPOPROTE&#205;NA B">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La apolipoprote&#237;na B es una prote&#237;na que se asocia con lipoprote&#237;nas y es un marcador importante en el diagn&#243;stico de dislipidemias.</data>
      <data key="d2">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d3">1804</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6076</data>
      <data key="d7">01be78e22d19442daa37fed5268455fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPID DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lipid disorders refer to abnormalities in lipid metabolism, which can result in conditions such as hyperlipidemia and are often managed through dietary changes and medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91</data>
      <data key="d3">1621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6077</data>
      <data key="d7">bcd5ff29fd6d49ba85b7ef549e22eb34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHOLESTEROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cholesterol is a lipid that serves as an important indicator of nutritional status and overall health. It is a waxy substance found in the blood, essential for building cells. However, while cholesterol is necessary for various bodily functions, high levels can lead to significant health issues, including heart disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6078</data>
      <data key="d7">592978f4bd7644a5b7f15fa62030d80c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Hyperlipidemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of lipids in the blood. This condition poses significant health risks, particularly increasing the likelihood of cardiovascular diseases. It is especially concerning for patients receiving intravenous lipids and those who have undergone liver transplantation. Management of hyperlipidemia can often be achieved through dietary changes, as supported by various studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,6a95bf35e698b03ca552f2c75d5d60ef,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29,f2b8b21255397ebbaf2b5d66ff6bde88</data>
      <data key="d3">1621</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">6079</data>
      <data key="d7">821875b2c44148178fe7b537c1e7e654</data>
    </node>
