    </node>
    <node id="CETOACIDOSIS DIABETICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cetoacidosis diab&#233;tica is a serious complication of diabetes characterized by high levels of ketones in the blood, leading to metabolic acidosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853</data>
      <data key="d3">628</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6183</data>
      <data key="d7">476550eef51f467e874dfab9b090730f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS TUBULAR RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La acidosis tubular renal es un cuadro caracterizado por acidosis metab&#243;lica hiperclor&#233;mica debido a la incapacidad renal de reabsorber o generar bicarbonato.</data>
      <data key="d2">473502714ce73073f93b598ca0edcc21</data>
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6184</data>
      <data key="d7">6910867bee5e432c8eb716f5687551df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AVP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Arginine-vasopressin (AVP) is a hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating water retention and osmolarity in the human body. It is particularly significant in the mechanism of nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, a condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to concentrate urine, leading to excessive urination and thirst. AVP helps maintain the balance of water in the body, ensuring proper hydration and physiological function.</data>
      <data key="d2">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f,473502714ce73073f93b598ca0edcc21</data>
      <data key="d3">1573</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6185</data>
      <data key="d7">95c3d4d3e37448f6848d830e882ca319</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA, or hypophyseal radiotherapy, is a specialized treatment method designed to target pituitary adenomas while minimizing radiation exposure to the surrounding brain structures. This approach is particularly effective in treating these types of tumors without causing adverse effects such as hyponatremia or diabetes insipidus.</data>
      <data key="d2">473502714ce73073f93b598ca0edcc21,773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6186</data>
      <data key="d7">4c0d635c5f414ef485d6492e71215ede</data>
    </node>
