    <node id="ORLISTAT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Orlistat is a weight loss medication that has been marketed in Europe since 1998. It functions by inhibiting fat absorption from the diet, making it a popular choice for individuals seeking to lose weight. However, it has been noted that Orlistat has the least effect on body weight compared to other weight loss medications. In clinical trials, Orlistat, also known by its brand name Xenical, has been compared with another weight loss drug, cetilistat. Additionally, it is important to note that Orlistat can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, a potential side effect associated with its use.</data>
      <data key="d2">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,488970234520652b063db88e8346031c,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">324</data>
