    <node id="RUNKLE I">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Runkle I is an author known for contributions to the field of clinical gerontology, particularly in the study of hyponatremia. In 2015, Runkle I co-authored a study published in Reviews in Clinical Gerontology that focused on the clinical aspects of hyponatremia. Additionally, Runkle I reported on the use of tolvaptan as a treatment for hyponatremia secondary to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). This work highlights Runkle I's involvement in addressing the complexities of hyponatremia and its management in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ceaa92ed88d3f829122e1554f2e7277,d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4</data>
