    </node>
    <node id="HYPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyponatremia is a medical condition characterized by abnormally low sodium levels in the blood. This electrolyte imbalance can lead to various health issues, affecting the body's overall function and potentially resulting in serious complications if not addressed.</data>
      <data key="d2">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7,62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,814d394c907e59b29a5f0d9e82aed423,d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">6225</data>
      <data key="d7">28d1481f1a3542d79f65b466c99ff296</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERTONIC SALINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertonic saline is a concentrated saline solution used to treat severe hyponatremia and reduce cerebral edema.</data>
      <data key="d2">d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6226</data>
      <data key="d7">6265bc5e2dfd4934b251ca4e3582e11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREBRAL EDEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cerebral edema is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of excess fluid in the brain. This condition can be induced by hyponatremia, a state of low sodium levels in the blood. The presence of excess fluid can lead to increased intracranial pressure and may require medical intervention to manage the associated risks and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6227</data>
      <data key="d7">994b9318f2914661b24aee4ca616fff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYNDROME OF DESMYELINATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The syndrome of desmyelination is a potential risk associated with rapid correction of hyponatremia, leading to neurological complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6228</data>
      <data key="d7">de897382392a41c8bca0f27dc7b2d71a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELECTROLYTE DISORDERS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Electrolyte disorders refer to imbalances in the body's electrolytes, which can include conditions like hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">d7880a3661021454f32e78a000064055</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
