    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN JOURNAL OF MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Journal of Medicine (Am J Med) is a reputable journal that focuses on publishing research across a diverse array of medical topics. It is particularly noted for its contributions to the understanding and management of hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. The journal not only features original research articles but also expert panel recommendations that guide the diagnosis, evaluation, and treatment of hyponatremia. Through its comprehensive coverage, the American Journal of Medicine serves as a valuable resource for medical professionals seeking insights into various health issues, including the complexities surrounding hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">152aeb8f10c2f4548114403c05af6b55,38547636a4ef9fd045b438047fb629fc,b9342cecd69cdc0e9936df041657f5f5</data>
      <data key="d3">1826</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">6232</data>
      <data key="d7">2cdce21decdf4a4a89ed163b97b4e7b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPASOVSKI G">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Spasovski G is a contributor to the clinical practice guidelines on hyponatremia diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">b9342cecd69cdc0e9936df041657f5f5</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6233</data>
