    </node>
    <node id="VERBALIS JG">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Verbalis JG is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of hyponatremia and its implications for both diagnosis and therapy. He has conducted extensive research on disorders of body water homeostasis, focusing particularly on the efficacy and safety of conivaptan in patients with euvolemic hyponatremia. Additionally, Verbalis JG has studied the association between moderate hyponatremia and an increased risk of mortality. His expertise has also led him to contribute to the development of recommendations for the diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia, solidifying his role as a key figure in this field of medical research.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ceaa92ed88d3f829122e1554f2e7277,38547636a4ef9fd045b438047fb629fc,91c73a1de38742d1b6c4e803ec1717a3,b9342cecd69cdc0e9936df041657f5f5</data>
