    </node>
    <node id="ALCALOSIS RESPIRATORIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcalosis respiratoria is a condition that can influence phosphate levels, particularly in the context of hypophosphatemia. Additionally, it is characterized by an increase in the binding of calcium to albumin, which affects the levels of ionized calcium in the body. This disorder highlights the interconnectedness of electrolyte imbalances and their physiological implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,5bb504bf68288cc0ba6a8f0dd9e4c245</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
