    </node>
    <node id="ANTI&#193;CIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anti&#225;cidos are medications that play a significant role in managing gastrointestinal issues. They can affect phosphate absorption, which is particularly relevant in the context of hypophosphatemia, a condition characterized by low phosphate levels in the blood. Additionally, anti&#225;cidos can interact with enteral nutrition, potentially leading to gastrointestinal complications. Furthermore, these medications may have interactions with certain nutrients, impacting their absorption. Overall, while anti&#225;cidos are commonly used to alleviate symptoms related to acidity, their effects on nutrient absorption and gastrointestinal health warrant careful consideration.</data>
      <data key="d2">5bb504bf68288cc0ba6a8f0dd9e4c245,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94,fc664efd4e1c463dc21857e596b68b46</data>
