    <node id="HEMOGLOBINA GLICOSILADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HEMOGLOBINA GLICOSILADA, also known as glycated hemoglobin, is a form of hemoglobin that is chemically linked to glucose. It serves as a crucial blood test that reflects average blood sugar levels over the past three months, making it an important tool for managing diabetes. This measure is used to assess long-term glucose control in individuals with diabetes, and it can be positively influenced by dietary choices, such as the Mediterranean diet. Overall, HEMOGLOBINA GLICOSILADA is a key marker in diabetes management, providing valuable insights into a patient's blood sugar levels over an extended period.</data>
      <data key="d2">72d0be9d03c79097f867a8af2e3e89e4,79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458,a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6384</data>
      <data key="d7">007fe32f04ec452db2efb8dc320e5205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRADUADOS EN NUTRICI&#211;N HUMANA Y DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Graduates in Human Nutrition and Dietetics are professionals trained to provide dietary advice and nutritional therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6385</data>
      <data key="d7">7c540bf93d874cfe8a1475d8584ca23e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPECIALISTAS EN ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Specialists in Endocrinology and Nutrition are healthcare professionals with expertise in hormonal and nutritional management of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6386</data>
      <data key="d7">27d5f794e999487292d2330e2b44522f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBJETIVOS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "OBJETIVOS NUTRICIONALES" refer to specific dietary goals established to enhance the health and nutritional status of patients. These objectives are particularly important for individuals with inflammatory bowel disease, as they aim to improve their overall health and nutritional well-being. Additionally, these nutritional goals are also tailored for patients managing diabetes, focusing on improving their health outcomes through targeted dietary interventions. Overall, the "OBJETIVOS NUTRICIONALES" encompass a range of specific targets designed to address the unique dietary needs of patients with various health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">a519216aaee7bf8a1317f5d6b522c4b6,a5ee3f91f8571820c338a8db4d3db09d</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
