    </node>
    <node id="EUROPE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Europe is a diverse continent characterized by a wide range of legislation and funding related to home artificial nutrition, reflecting the varying health policies of its countries. It serves as a focal point for nutritional guidelines and legal standards concerning food products, which are essential for public health. The continent is also a significant area of study for cardiovascular disease, with ongoing epidemiological updates and initiatives like the SCORE project aimed at estimating cardiovascular disease risk.

Diabetes prevalence is a major health concern in Europe, affecting millions of individuals, while hemochromatosis is notably more common in northern regions. The rates of obesity vary across Europe, with some countries experiencing higher prevalence than others. Additionally, the population exhibits differing levels of lactase persistence, particularly in northern and western areas, which influences dietary habits and health outcomes.

Regulations regarding the production and labeling of organic products, including gluten-free certifications, are established within Europe, ensuring consumer safety and product integrity. The continent has also seen significant variations in the prevalence of non-communicable diseases (NPD) among countries, as noted in studies from 1993. Disease-related malnutrition remains a pressing public health issue, prompting various studies and surveys, including those focused on cystic fibrosis.

Overall, Europe is a continent marked by its complex health landscape, diverse nutritional challenges, and regulatory frameworks that aim to address these issues effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03,19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699,35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,7e3e2024996e402fc0ab62933ab9417b,b49f181ca7099fc110f35ccc27e7fafc,d3ffabc46da9b238994a7769ffc8f6b7,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,dfb6e1826ded0b8ca7cf3304d1b75d1a,efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608</data>
