    <node id="CASTILLA Y LE&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Castilla y Le&#243;n is an autonomous community in Spain that is currently facing a significant increase in the prevalence of diabetes and related mortality rates. This region is characterized by an aging population, which contributes to the growing health concern surrounding diabetes. In response to this issue, clinical case conferences have been held in Castilla y Le&#243;n to address the challenges posed by this condition. Additionally, patients in the region are required to submit a justification report from a hospital specialist in order to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, highlighting the structured approach to managing diabetes and its complications within the community.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396,d2e2009d967ecd49af312dba4e2ed4fd,dec6b3fc008edd47758cfc00106d077b,fc8df7c3d7a0d2286c55493077ed3937</data>
