    <node id="HOSPITALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospitals are healthcare institutions dedicated to providing treatment and care for patients, including those who require specialized services such as parenteral nutrition and catheter insertion. They often operate under management contracts to deliver a range of medical services. In addition to medical care, hospitals also serve food products, such as Galleta Maria, and must provide allergen information to ensure patient safety. In Spain, hospitals are involved in research studies focusing on diabetes and malnutrition among patients, highlighting their role in evaluating and addressing nutritional needs through initiatives like Nutrition Day. Overall, hospitals are essential institutions that not only deliver health services but also prioritize the nutritional well-being of their patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,26765fd0d663c8708d7bd6a545de3e2c,61eea56f443c7bb2509edd6f42af2643,969bdfc6cc15b9089e96000addd87561,ed7bd985e5e4a3d5642e4b401b8e3e17,f2846d08229fda837153207946e29831</data>
