    <node id="DISLIPEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal lipid levels in the blood, which is part of the patient's medical history. This condition is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease and can be influenced by various factors, including diet and obesity. Dyslipidemia is also associated with diabetes, contributing to potential cardiovascular complications. It is important to note that dyslipidemia can complicate the treatment of patients, particularly those who are obese. Overall, dyslipidemia represents a disorder of lipid metabolism that requires careful management to mitigate its associated health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">3356667d6f35de6a8587ece00f8c6580,3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d,ac8c5a07bd415723c0410ec34b9d7c5e,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
