    <node id="H&#193;BITOS ALIMENTARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"H&#193;BITOS ALIMENTARIOS" refers to the dietary practices and consumption behaviors of individuals, which play a significant role in health management and the risk of chronic diseases. These eating habits are patterns of food consumption that can influence the risk and management of conditions such as diabetes. The assessment of "h&#225;bitos alimentarios" is crucial for understanding nutritional patterns and their associations with health outcomes. In recent years, there has been a dramatic shift in eating habits, characterized by an increase in high-fat diets, which contribute to the development of metabolic diseases. Overall, "h&#225;bitos alimentarios" encompass the dietary patterns and practices that are essential for nutritional assessments and health management.</data>
      <data key="d2">01eb4b96cd8e6a886ebc313171922a77,55aabc274c460459322072406f17d52c,caf1d075a295b93dcd3c6f5cf72b028d,da2707b26ddb548995a6d0e2a3eeddb0,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c,f14ec70726a24a574ae5d437903fddb8</data>
