    <node id="ENFERMEDAD RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ENFERMEDAD RENAL es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que afecta la funci&#243;n de los ri&#241;ones, lo que puede llevar a complicaciones significativas en la salud de los pacientes. Esta enfermedad es especialmente relevante para aquellos que padecen diabetes, ya que puede ser una complicaci&#243;n asociada a esta condici&#243;n. La enfermedad renal se caracteriza por un aumento del volumen de agua y sodio en el organismo, lo que a su vez requiere la implementaci&#243;n de dietas espec&#237;ficas, incluyendo una restricci&#243;n diet&#233;tica de sodio, para controlar la hipertensi&#243;n arterial y manejar adecuadamente la enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448,7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0,84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4</data>
      <data key="d3">832</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6545</data>
      <data key="d7">b349849fd1804aaa9ab92a1827b38257</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INERCIA TERAP&#201;UTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inercia terap&#233;utica refers to the therapeutic inertia in diabetes treatment, highlighting the delay in prescribing optimal treatments for patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6546</data>
      <data key="d7">bcb197691e66444681ee2157d671d9bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMPA-REG STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The EMPA-REG Study is a clinical trial that investigated the cardiovascular safety of a diabetes medication, influencing treatment guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6547</data>
      <data key="d7">46dd1b67d10541febf4fd7b2f1e1d890</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEADER STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The LEADER Study is a long-term clinical trial designed to assess the cardiovascular outcomes and safety of liraglutide, a medication used in the treatment of diabetes. This study has significant implications for treatment practices, as it evaluates how liraglutide affects cardiovascular health in patients with diabetes. Through its findings, the LEADER Study aims to provide valuable insights into the management of diabetes and its associated cardiovascular risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0,90c684dca4542bbe1177afd26e78581e</data>
      <data key="d3">997</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6548</data>
      <data key="d7">d0d90d8571504895ab1caa3cee40b8f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROASPIRE V">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EUROASPIRE V is a study that evaluates the management of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Europe, providing insights into treatment practices.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">7f3fb444fd8d5532fb968747a3b176c0</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6549</data>
      <data key="d7">490d6a5b70894c7e84ca7276b7baac97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS" is a round table event focused on discussing clinical cases within the medical community. It features various medical professionals who present and analyze different cases. The event has taken place in the Comunidad Valenciana, where a diverse group of specialists share their insights. Additionally, there is a specific iteration of this event that addresses clinical cases related to diabetes and nutrition, which was held in Granada, also involving various specialists. Overall, the MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL&#205;NICOS serves as a platform for collaboration and knowledge exchange among healthcare professionals across different regions and specialties.</data>
      <data key="d2">234b514a40a64bc02f1346cb62cf3f97,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d3">1908</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">6550</data>
      <data key="d7">e3d65106a23d49109964e4c72ed3113d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME MELAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A rare genetic disorder discussed in one of the clinical cases, characterized by mitochondrial dysfunction and associated with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6551</data>
      <data key="d7">a8be8a7814c1484d8cafba30bedc3147</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOPLASIA INTRADUCTAL PAPILAR MUCINOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neoplasia intraductal papilar mucinosa is a specific type of pancreatic tumor that has been discussed in clinical cases. It is associated with malnutrition and diabetes, highlighting its potential impact on the patient's overall health. The patient in the case was diagnosed with this type of tumor, indicating its clinical significance and the need for careful management of related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,a86e44ac34c096cea172895339d5f733</data>
      <data key="d3">1095</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">6552</data>
      <data key="d7">368f6b5eb5444fab989845b0c5b1aeb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO SANTA LUC&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital General Universitario Santa Luc&#237;a is a healthcare institution in Cartagena where specialized medical care is provided, including for patients with endocrine and nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">140</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6553</data>
      <data key="d7">4387921934914cda83cde06a342483b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE MELAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MELAS is a mitochondrial disease characterized by encephalomyopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes, significantly affecting muscle and nervous system function, often leading to complications such as diabetes mellitus.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">140</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6554</data>
      <data key="d7">7b44ea70594146cc89cbdc4a493589bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES MITOCONDRIALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mitochondrial diseases are a group of disorders caused by dysfunctional mitochondria, which can lead to a variety of health issues, including metabolic and neurological problems.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6555</data>
      <data key="d7">8cc7bea856df4d2f9912769cb2ea5bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICA SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Severe caloric malnutrition is a condition resulting from inadequate intake of calories, leading to significant health issues, particularly in patients with complex medical conditions like MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6556</data>
      <data key="d7">a5b423db7de7421e90fe058c6b059630</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO-MOTORA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO-MOTORA, also known as sensory-motor polyneuropathy, is a medical condition that impacts the peripheral nerves. This condition is characterized by both sensory loss and motor weakness, which can significantly affect a patient's quality of life. It is often observed in individuals with mitochondrial diseases, highlighting a potential link between these two health issues. Overall, sensory-motor polyneuropathy represents a serious neurological disorder that requires careful management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6557</data>
      <data key="d7">bbaff96176c54309b24b0db49fa2dc23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOMA MUCINOSO DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mucinous pancreatic carcinoma is a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, characterized by the production of mucin, and may require surgical intervention like duodenopancreatectomy.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
      <data key="d3">225</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6558</data>
      <data key="d7">ca3a6745bcdc43f8aa3e2bff7bb6cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MELAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">MELAS, which stands for Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes, is the most common mitochondrial disease. It is characterized by a heterogeneous phenotypic expression that includes a variety of symptoms affecting multiple systems in the body. Individuals with MELAS often experience neurological impairments, such as migraines, seizures, and episodes resembling strokes. Additionally, the disorder can lead to muscular weakness and various gastrointestinal issues, which frequently result in malnutrition. Other systemic manifestations may include diabetes mellitus. The complexity of MELAS symptoms can vary significantly among affected individuals, making diagnosis and management challenging. One patient was diagnosed with MELAS in 2008, highlighting the ongoing recognition and understanding of this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">59fd1772b0c4b6c23c975977be6a60fe,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">26</data>
      <data key="d6">6559</data>
      <data key="d7">470c5ce89f3e40a5a30442565c253d42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITRULINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrulina is a non-essential amino acid that plays a significant role in evaluating intestinal health, particularly in determining the need for long-term nutritional support. It serves as a biochemical marker in this context. Additionally, Citrulina is recognized as a supplement that enhances the production of nitric oxide (NO), which is crucial for various physiological functions. It is noted for potentially having better absorption and bioavailability compared to arginine. While Citrulina is relevant in the context of MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), particularly for patients with low levels of nitric oxide, its specific effects on this condition have not been extensively studied. Overall, Citrulina is an important amino acid with implications for both intestinal health and nitric oxide production.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6560</data>
      <data key="d7">a130fb9f81ee4e6f9626bb94870f03f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOCROMO C">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citocromo C is an enzyme that has a high affinity for nitric oxide and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS due to its interaction with nitric oxide synthase.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6561</data>
      <data key="d7">794277990fe44d55a0d3519e5ba85c89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPILESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Epilepsy is a neurological manifestation observed in a significant percentage of MELAS patients, contributing to the overall clinical picture of the syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6562</data>
      <data key="d7">9d356c13b9d2448dba12b551dc2f20bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neuropat&#237;a perif&#233;rica is a condition affecting the peripheral nerves, noted in MELAS patients, contributing to their neurological symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6563</data>
      <data key="d7">fe4d65cd9072426787ff08aa9efbe502</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#211;XIDO N&#205;TRICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#211;xido n&#237;trico is a crucial signaling molecule that plays a significant role in vascular relaxation and is involved in the pathophysiology of MELAS, particularly through its interaction with endothelial cells. It functions as an endogenous vasodilator, regulating blood pressure and organ perfusion. &#211;xido n&#237;trico is produced from the amino acid arginine, highlighting its importance in cardiovascular health and disease mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8,6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">1945</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6564</data>
      <data key="d7">92625ee846f0460c86d59f5458972ada</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOCROMO C OXIDASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citocromo C oxidasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the electron transport chain, which is essential for cellular respiration. This enzyme is particularly noted for its increased activity in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), a condition that can impact the availability of nitric oxide in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6565</data>
      <data key="d7">ea63830c505742f2bc9275f850751015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOACUSIA NEUROSENSORIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoacusia neurosensorial is a type of hearing loss that is commonly observed in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). This auditory manifestation significantly contributes to the overall neurological symptoms associated with the syndrome, thereby affecting the quality of life of those affected. Additionally, it is noted that hipoacusia neurosensorial can also be experienced by family members, such as the patient's mother, indicating a potential genetic link related to the underlying mutation.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6566</data>
      <data key="d7">f1f5374f8ec14635a29ae22cd7b6d9e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMANDA DE INSULINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Demanda de insulina refers to the requirement for insulin treatment in MELAS patients, particularly in those developing diabetes mellitus.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6567</data>
      <data key="d7">83a85d604ba243ceb1a2ced66c479317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEW CASTLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">New Castle is associated with the scale of severity for adult mitochondrial diseases, specifically the NMDAS used to assess patients with MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6568</data>
      <data key="d7">008b3b3bc3c44aceac15ff37257dcd1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COENZIMA Q10">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Coenzima Q10 is a compound known for its role in stabilizing the electron transport chain and exhibiting antioxidant properties. It is particularly noted for its potential benefits for patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). Additionally, Coenzima Q10 is utilized as an antioxidant to enhance recovery following exercise, highlighting its versatility in both medical and athletic contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d3">578</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6569</data>
      <data key="d7">ff65cd1e77264fdeb2b3c57848a61f20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Dieta cetog&#233;nica" (ketogenic diet) is a dietary approach characterized by a high intake of fats and a significant reduction in carbohydrates. It is primarily utilized for the treatment of refractory epilepsy, particularly in children, and has shown effectiveness in reducing epileptic seizures, including in patients with MELAS syndrome. While the diet provides an alternative energy substrate for the brain, its long-term safety and effectiveness remain uncertain.

The ketogenic diet is often implemented as a treatment for patients who do not respond to conventional medication, and it may have implications for growth, as well as potential digestive and cardiac complications. The diet is typically maintained as long as it continues to be beneficial, with a gradual adjustment process when discontinuing treatment. Various forms and protocols of the ketogenic diet exist, tailored to meet the specific needs of patients, particularly those with intractable epilepsy and other metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">06adf563f18feaa5629f0e368a72d227,0a9b42ff082f2d0bb036ec3365d9a6e9,0ebd0c517a3d578a6823dc39797e4da1,1592143354d1ef792f8618ec03a32a16,2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e,2d07762e6db07c2587caceac3427a1c7,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02,a8929d6c031b44205ed738ec0a0cd435,bf7fc15e1aac41553dc6586efe68b8cb,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1940</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">90</data>
      <data key="d6">6570</data>
      <data key="d7">4fb363a53ebb4a469b7c9bbd4087dd46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMANCIAS PSIQUI&#193;TRICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Demanias psiqui&#225;tricas refer to psychiatric manifestations that may arise in patients with MELAS, impacting their mental health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6571</data>
      <data key="d7">5ba6b5a2d21f41b0b6b937e2ff595d9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOTOP&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Miopat&#237;a is a cardinal manifestation of MELAS, characterized by muscle weakness and intolerance to exercise.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6572</data>
      <data key="d7">70b2676249d94178af13074e036d2951</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOCARDIOPAT&#205;A HIPERTR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Miocardiopat&#237;a hipertr&#243;fica is a cardiac manifestation that can occur in MELAS patients, affecting heart function.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6573</data>
      <data key="d7">f87dd604c8de4af5975622fd20e16f71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO DE MEDRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fallo de medro is a condition of poor growth that can occur in MELAS patients, often linked to nutritional issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1944</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6574</data>
      <data key="d7">fc90622617ce4d6597614600380d8dbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="L-CARNITINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">L-Carnitine is a supplement that plays a crucial role in fatty acid metabolism and is included in treatment regimens to potentially enhance mitochondrial function. It is particularly suggested for patients with primary systemic carnitine deficiency, where it is recognized for its safety and effectiveness in correcting underlying carnitine deficits.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc,e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6575</data>
      <data key="d7">02d30cb0c65343e9a249e9210a05c9c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COENZYME Q10">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Coenzyme Q10 is a compound involved in energy production in cells, used in the patient's treatment to address complications related to MELAS.</data>
      <data key="d2">e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6576</data>
      <data key="d7">bf52e8a21008449c8515a5406a1e4bf3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLOPIDOGREL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Clopidogrel is a medication used in the patient's treatment, likely for its antiplatelet effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">e279d3a0da085b47528c08f486afe0a5</data>
