    <node id="CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICILE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Clostridium difficile is a bacterium known for causing infections in the intestines, which often lead to severe diarrhea and colitis. This condition is particularly prevalent in patients who have recently undergone antibiotic treatment, as the bacterium can proliferate in the gut following the disruption of normal flora. Testing for the toxin produced by Clostridium difficile is commonly performed in patients presenting with gastrointestinal symptoms, especially diarrhea. The bacterium remains a significant focus of ongoing research aimed at developing effective treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bdc356a46149def2545e7939372c20d,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b,d3e1df90991ea82fcccbd02589473ead,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
