    <node id="TABLA 4">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TABLA 4 is a comprehensive table that encompasses a variety of important characteristics related to dietary assessment methods and nutritional guidelines. It presents strategies aimed at reducing the risk of aspiration in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Additionally, TABLA 4 outlines commercial preparations of parenteral nutrition, specifically focusing on ternary mixtures. The table details the energy requirements for girls at three levels of physical activity, providing insights into caloric intake based on age and weight. It also includes reference intake values for an average adult and offers estimations of weight and height derived from other anthropometric parameters. Furthermore, TABLA 4 displays data from a population study concerning body mass index (IMC) for men and women over the age of 60. Lastly, it contains laboratory results from a patient's hospitalization, detailing various blood parameters, and outlines the analytical parameters necessary for monitoring patients receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c83fbbd4b26fbfe03a1df6d36025796,13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,2bd5549759c6a0d8393bb93fdccb747b,3dbf07634cee8d4d443f59ed50f98b54,45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,c567251c335f000303144ce3d7e1d638,cb8368db73f739b1f11f2a202c776e6d</data>
