      <data key="d6">6616</data>
      <data key="d7">f4b5ff12c36e40f8b3f2ecb9edced7cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTIC ACIDOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactic acidosis is a condition characterized by the buildup of lactic acid in the body, often seen in mitochondrial disorders like MELAS syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6617</data>
      <data key="d7">89719be6962b451a940825b3b5a54718</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STROKE-LIKE EPISODES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Stroke-like episodes are neurological events that can occur in patients with MELAS syndrome, leading to various symptoms and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6618</data>
      <data key="d7">e52e5c1ca595498ba3ad111a75d8569a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MITOCHONDRIAL DNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mitochondrial DNA is the DNA located in mitochondria, which can harbor mutations leading to mitochondrial diseases, including MELAS syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6619</data>
      <data key="d7">8e83dd6f66cc464a92ced2a935334840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL PHENOTYPE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical phenotype refers to the observable characteristics and symptoms of a disease, which in the case of MELAS syndrome can vary widely among patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6620</data>
      <data key="d7">830f3eb36c9c4bd395a768461a475837</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TREATMENT OPTIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Treatment options for MELAS syndrome may include dietary management, exercise, and specific therapies aimed at managing symptoms and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6621</data>
      <data key="d7">2c39c8f6071c48c7bc2cfa38c491d4af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYSFUNCTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dysfunction refers to impaired or abnormal functioning, which can occur in various systems of the body in patients with mitochondrial diseases like MELAS syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2</data>
      <data key="d3">192</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6622</data>
      <data key="d7">c4e06d4376ee404e92821cc4d637dbf3</data>
    </node>
