    </node>
    <node id="DOBRATZ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dobratz is a researcher who evaluated predictive equations for measuring basal metabolic expenditure in obese women.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6652</data>
      <data key="d7">70efea491a304195915bf9656638bd78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRUG&#205;A METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic surgery is a medical procedure recommended for treating type 2 diabetes in patients with obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1366</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6653</data>
      <data key="d7">cf3a41ed7d1c46d387ae4820760a7b30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUGA ANASTOM&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fuga anastom&#243;tica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6654</data>
      <data key="d7">ccf4e201b99e4772a5c2f7adbc9ac5ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NA&#218;SEAS Y V&#211;MITOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nauseas y v&#243;mitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6655</data>
      <data key="d7">de6ca466a2e34e98967ecd8a95969ba4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALABSORCI&#211;N SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malabsorci&#243;n severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6656</data>
      <data key="d7">7433570d8d5e43c6ba75684d0c711883</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">445e6aeaae0e8edb3faf2d36be2073ce</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6657</data>
      <data key="d7">3972289a8bc246af85c0c1002ab0182c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL" (ASPEN) is an organization dedicated to advancing the field of nutritional support. It provides clinical guidelines for artificial nutritional support specifically for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Additionally, ASPEN offers guidelines for nutritional support tailored to hospitalized adult obese patients, with a particular focus on those undergoing bariatric surgery. Through these initiatives, ASPEN aims to enhance the quality of care and outcomes for patients requiring specialized nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">27c75984e62c5adcac1ac33cbdc520dc,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">1185</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6658</data>
      <data key="d7">9064c3e953904d80a8fd3160c5d78dc7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIDAD DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Intensive Care Unit (UCI) is a specialized department in hospitals where patients receive close monitoring and care, particularly for nutritional adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6659</data>
      <data key="d7">b362dd13114145609bce291471d4c363</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE RECOMENDACI&#211;N BAJO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A low level of recommendation indicates that the evidence supporting a particular nutritional approach is not strong, as seen in the guidelines for nutritional support in bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6660</data>
      <data key="d7">c2966a1fb89a41078c3dde187397208a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE CUIDADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Levels of care refer to the different intensities of medical care provided, particularly in the context of monitoring nutritional intake in critical patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6661</data>
      <data key="d7">3949f341cd3a487fad753a472a3bec15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAR&#193;METROS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical parameters are metrics used to assess a patient's health status, including wound healing and early mobilization in the context of nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6662</data>
      <data key="d7">cc772d42993c4100819e9bbd23902deb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIENCIAS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional deficiencies are conditions that arise when the body does not get enough nutrients, which can be a risk for patients undergoing bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6663</data>
      <data key="d7">18d9e2c103774922bdf7f6844afd4f8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Blood glucose levels are monitored to manage the metabolic state of patients, particularly those undergoing bariatric surgery.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6664</data>
      <data key="d7">aa2f3b06b9884f5db6ff2bb0c0e7dd4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO MORALES MESEGUER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is a healthcare institution located in Murcia, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6665</data>
      <data key="d7">ee6677134f72432c8d6a8edc5d0ef4d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YAMINA SULEIMAN MARTOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dra. Yamina Suleiman Martos is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, involved in the clinical management of diabetes and related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">6666</data>
      <data key="d7">1038529cc35f4502986ef073cebd371c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MURCIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Murcia is an autonomous community in Spain known for its diverse healthcare and educational initiatives. It is home to the Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer, which serves the local population's medical needs. In 2003, Murcia hosted the National Congress on Pediatric Nutrition, highlighting its commitment to addressing nutritional issues within the community. Additionally, in this region, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, reflecting the structured approach to healthcare management in Murcia.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,7ea112a550fd775a80c3eda15663fba5</data>
      <data key="d3">892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6667</data>
      <data key="d7">6f944af1a4b74a928e87b13d998f43d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MNGIE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MNGIE, or mitochondrial neurogastrointestinal encephalomyopathy, is a rare genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in thymidine phosphorylase, which is caused by mutations in the TYMP gene. This disorder primarily affects the gastrointestinal and nervous systems, resulting in a range of metabolic issues and complications, including diabetes. Due to the complexity of the symptoms and the interplay between the affected systems, MNGIE requires intricate treatment approaches to manage its severe manifestations.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc,cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">6668</data>
      <data key="d7">146a58bdca224ddcabdaba272492536f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICIONAL SUPPLEMENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional supplements are products taken to enhance dietary intake, often used in clinical settings to support patients with specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6669</data>
      <data key="d7">1d53d87c80da4b59a8b64224472ab71a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS VITAM&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Suplementos vitam&#237;nicos are dietary products designed to provide essential vitamins that may be lacking in an individual's diet. These supplements are particularly beneficial for cancer patients, as they help to address specific vitamin deficiencies that may arise due to their health condition. Overall, vitamin supplements serve as a valuable resource for individuals seeking to enhance their nutritional intake and support their health.</data>
      <data key="d2">043ed163c427b880fe39884076cae7ea,16887bf1589e9515213d2e392bbc8c69,58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88</data>
      <data key="d3">1602</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6670</data>
      <data key="d7">f768d4839ddf4caeb9968ea76af4e0f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A &#211;PTICA BILATERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La neuropat&#237;a &#243;ptica bilateral es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 10-12 a&#241;os, caracterizado por la disminuci&#243;n progresiva de la agudeza visual y la atrofia &#243;ptica observada en el fondo de ojo.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6671</data>
      <data key="d7">a8161ae1314341d0a08fa488af97ff58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLINEUROPAT&#205;A SENSITIVO MOTORA AXONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La polineuropat&#237;a sensitivo motora axonal es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 16 a&#241;os, caracterizado por debilidad progresiva en miembros y amiotrofia distal.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6672</data>
      <data key="d7">61d4d13c61444c4e862e49a13f18b970</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOACUSIA PROFUNDA BILATERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipoacusia profunda bilateral neurosensorial es un diagn&#243;stico que se presenta a los 30 a&#241;os, que requiere la colocaci&#243;n de un implante coclear debido a la severidad de la p&#233;rdida auditiva.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">896</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6673</data>
      <data key="d7">49aabc5ccfa743c38dd358a8c8ce74d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEUCOENCEFALOPAT&#205;A SUPRATENTORIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La leucoencefalopat&#237;a supratentorial periventricular difusa es un hallazgo observado en la resonancia magn&#233;tica nuclear cerebral, indicando cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">896</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6674</data>
      <data key="d7">eefebdc87aaf4819abe949312e884b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS DIGESTIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los s&#237;ntomas digestivos incluyen p&#233;rdida de peso, deposiciones blandas y episodios diarreicos, que se presentan en el paciente a lo largo del tiempo.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">954</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6675</data>
      <data key="d7">c2931850a715438581939c93aa0ea471</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS DE SANGRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "AN&#193;LISIS DE SANGRE" refers to blood tests conducted on patients to assess various health indicators. These tests are essential for monitoring glucose levels, renal function, and other critical health parameters. The blood analysis reveals several important metrics, including blood sugar (glucemia), cholesterol levels, and vitamin concentrations, all of which are relevant for diagnosing the patient's health status. Overall, blood tests serve as a vital tool in evaluating the patient's overall health and nutritional parameters.</data>
      <data key="d2">17b7995dcf275c50629c7e3d4723882e,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,c3975fe03d2af26b95b09795c7769e8b</data>
      <data key="d3">870</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6676</data>
      <data key="d7">7a9eb2c52bf04a63ac531b37f39d8fe4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;PSULA ENDOSC&#211;PICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La c&#225;psula endosc&#243;pica visualiza linfangiectasias y edema en el yeyuno proximal, proporcionando informaci&#243;n adicional sobre la condici&#243;n del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">954</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6677</data>
      <data key="d7">468b0e18f8dd4d7eb2fabe5b9425f907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA &#211;PTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La atrofia &#243;ptica es un hallazgo observado en el fondo de ojo del paciente, indicando da&#241;o severo en la v&#237;a visual.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6678</data>
      <data key="d7">7b0c0d69b0c14538ba1e233a193e4a14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEBILIDAD PROGRESIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La debilidad progresiva es un s&#237;ntoma que se presenta a los 16 a&#241;os, afectando principalmente a los miembros inferiores y superiores.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6679</data>
      <data key="d7">9aa1fc3e38f141e6a0934d75ddc7252f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOGLICEMIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las hipoglucemias son episodios que ocurren debido a la suspensi&#243;n irregular del tratamiento antidiab&#233;tico, afectando la salud del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">870</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6680</data>
      <data key="d7">8c452731142148f3861ca0fbfe9f8c0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSACI&#211;N DE PLENITUD POSTPRANDIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La sensaci&#243;n de plenitud postprandial es un s&#237;ntoma que el paciente experimenta despu&#233;s de las comidas, indicando problemas digestivos.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">954</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6681</data>
      <data key="d7">200c95870ae84257a3b2ac82bbb78eff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMAGEN DE RMN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La imagen de resonancia magn&#233;tica nuclear (RMN) muestra cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro, lo que es relevante para el diagn&#243;stico del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d</data>
      <data key="d3">896</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6682</data>
      <data key="d7">ae4907de80524d42903e0106a738c649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATOLOG&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">PATOLOG&#205;AS refer to diseases or disorders that can impact carbohydrate digestion and absorption. These health conditions necessitate nutritional support and dietary management, especially concerning FODMAP intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">21dc8cb1a5078e23dae18b9c62b05625,8b6f748cffc65b1521a9ee4b11f2273d,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">895</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">6683</data>
      <data key="d7">1b8aa8d06c3e41979561f0e6f76357f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TYMP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The TYMP gene is located on chromosome 22q13.33 and encodes a protein involved in the phosphorylation of thymidine, mutations in which cause MNGIE.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6684</data>
      <data key="d7">863bbbf8dcc14eddbee6a9b7d8afbf69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GARONE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Garone is a researcher who reviewed 102 cases of MNGIE between 1988 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6685</data>
      <data key="d7">f052b83f8af24ac89db889d92a90b0f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIMIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6686</data>
      <data key="d7">9f2de0835ca5497f9600799747cf42a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEOXIURIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6687</data>
      <data key="d7">9db900f46c2b4be7ae856da87c942d45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurological symptoms associated with MNGIE include peripheral neuropathy, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and leukoencephalopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6688</data>
      <data key="d7">960dff018901411c838132075a22844f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIGESTIVE SYMPTOMS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Digestive symptoms of MNGIE include gastrointestinal dysmotility, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb3d17a78ad2d9342ebe0fd2aac8e9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
