    </node>
    <node id="CREATINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatine is a substance known for its ability to enhance muscle strength and performance, especially when used in conjunction with regular strength training. It has been the subject of research for its potential benefits in improving muscle strength in patients with mitochondrial diseases. Additionally, creatine has been studied for its effects on exercise tolerance in individuals with metabolic disorders, such as Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI), although the results of these studies have been mixed. Overall, creatine is recognized for its role in supporting muscle function and performance across various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">06a75d9ed2fc1cdca5b08759d3df04d4,24cc40d6e3b225945cd4d8c2484632e4,b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">6695</data>
      <data key="d7">f24ffcf5c2bc4941ba8e79dc311fdbb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THYMIDINE PHOSPHORYLASE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Thymidine phosphorylase is an enzyme whose activity is crucial for the metabolism of thymidine, and its deficiency is linked to MNGIE.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d3">228</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6696</data>
      <data key="d7">c1aa376ad85042bba1e77adb4e6122ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplant (HSCT) is a medical procedure that involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells to treat a variety of diseases, particularly hematological malignancies and solid tumors. Additionally, HSCT is being investigated as a potential treatment option to address the enzymatic deficiency associated with Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE). This procedure represents a significant therapeutic approach in the field of regenerative medicine and offers hope for patients with challenging medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">408288a47065e62d79bbc9b19df87c61,b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d3">503</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
