    <node id="HEPATITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the liver, which can be caused by various factors including viral infections, alcohol use, or autoimmune diseases. It is important to note that hepatitis can also manifest as a rare complication in the early weeks of treatment with the ketogenic diet. In the context of specific medical conditions, hepatic transplantation is considered a viable treatment option for patients with Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), due to the liver's essential role in producing thymidine phosphorylase.</data>
      <data key="d2">125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973,1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,bf2e1510b4d6b43da85e8086d93e5602,bf7fc15e1aac41553dc6586efe68b8cb</data>
