    </node>
    <node id="L-CARNITINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">L-CARNITINA, also known as L-carnitine, is an amino acid that plays a crucial role in energy metabolism. It is often included in infant formulas to support the energy needs of infants. Additionally, L-carnitine is utilized as a dietary supplement to assist in managing symptoms associated with mitochondrial diseases, such as MNGIE. In cancer patients, L-carnitine may help increase body weight and enhance overall quality of life. Furthermore, it is recognized for its benefits in optimizing weight and body composition among athletes. L-carnitine is also important in the treatment of &#946;-oxidation disorders, as it aids in the transport of fatty acids into the mitochondria for energy production.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079,763c8ac63b4c91616bcea6f1f4aa38c9,8f2e38ed25a683975b314e8e56721ad6,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
