    <node id="UCI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos (UCI), also known as the Intensive Care Unit, is a specialized area within a hospital dedicated to providing intensive medical care to critically ill patients. This unit is equipped to handle a variety of severe medical conditions, including but not limited to severe pancreatitis and acute renal failure. Patients in the UCI receive close monitoring and specialized treatment tailored to their critical health needs. The UCI plays a crucial role in managing complications and ensuring that patients in critical condition receive the necessary care to stabilize their health.</data>
      <data key="d2">21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3,9f77fc213da2123b013166c181a60323,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944,c07baf818737d704c290ca0f5eefd30f</data>
