    <node id="BIOPSIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">BIOPSIA refers to a medical procedure involving the extraction of tissue for diagnostic purposes. In one instance, a biopsy was performed via endoscopic ultrasound to confirm the diagnosis of a pancreatic mucinous tumor. Additionally, the term encompasses intestinal biopsy, which is a diagnostic procedure that involves the removal of tissue from the small intestine to assess damage caused by celiac disease. Thus, BIOPSIA encompasses various types of biopsies used to diagnose different conditions, including pancreatic tumors and intestinal disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,a633c156fb0077e3f669d8eb258be944</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
