    <node id="DIABETES TECHNOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes technology refers to the tools and methods used to manage diabetes, including enteral formulas and monitoring devices.</data>
      <data key="d2">7949b821c1ca2e4adc524e7775626396</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6782</data>
      <data key="d7">3e42d61559964a81906d829866b2887b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN PSYCHIATRIC ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Psychiatric Association (APA) is a professional organization dedicated to the advancement of mental health care. It provides comprehensive guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of various mental disorders, including eating disorders such as anorexia nerviosa. The APA publishes essential resources, including the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5), which outlines the criteria for diagnosing these conditions. Additionally, the organization offers specific recommendations regarding the nutritional care of patients suffering from anorexia nerviosa, ensuring that practitioners have the necessary tools to provide effective treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">770e8796aac9c96d967ef99d1f307e06,bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c,da6937e21690cfcb43a43b3438ec7586</data>
      <data key="d3">1590</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6783</data>
      <data key="d7">5d6da114b8d74dfe983187ad5fb35889</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNDACI&#211;N SED">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fundaci&#243;n SED is an organization in Spain that provides data and support for individuals with diabetes, including statistics on the prevalence of diabetes in minors.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">1594</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6784</data>
      <data key="d7">c0c2b707a9274dcbafdba625c98072f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE EVITACI&#211;N/RESTRICCI&#211;N DE ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Avoidant/Restrictive Food Intake Disorder is characterized by a lack of interest in eating or avoidance of certain foods, which can lead to nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">1593</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6785</data>
      <data key="d7">7634dec93d7e4f968a82d097a1968105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE ATRACONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Binge Eating Disorder involves recurrent episodes of eating large quantities of food, often to the point of discomfort, and is associated with feelings of loss of control.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">1593</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6786</data>
      <data key="d7">6bba8fc049784c139264320f3a0d584c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pica is an eating disorder characterized by the persistent consumption of non-nutritive, non-food substances, which can lead to serious health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">1593</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6787</data>
      <data key="d7">e803596191a7495788d8aa66c39f65a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNO DE RUMIACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rumination Disorder involves the repeated regurgitation of food, which may be re-chewed, re-swallowed, or spit out, and can have significant health implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d3">1593</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6788</data>
      <data key="d7">9da2e3a8c444484c95f137fa5925c9ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIE-9">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Classification of Diseases, 9th Revision (ICD-9) is a system used for coding and classifying diseases, including eating disorders.</data>
