    <node id="CETONURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cetonuria refers to the presence of ketones in the urine, which serves as an important indicator of metabolic processes in the body. This condition often signifies a lack of insulin, raising concerns about the potential for cetoacidosis, particularly in diabetic patients. Additionally, ketonuria highlights poor control of diabetes, suggesting that the patient's blood sugar levels are not being effectively managed. Overall, cetonuria is a critical marker for assessing the health and metabolic status of individuals with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436,933d6526b2d313c95c9f4aaa950a62a3</data>
