    <node id="HIPOGLUCEMIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOGLUCEMIAS refer to episodes of low blood sugar that can occur in various medical conditions. Specifically, they are commonly observed in patients with glycogen storage diseases, particularly during the early years of life. Additionally, hypoglycemia can also occur in patients with diabetes when blood sugar levels fall too low, necessitating immediate intervention. This condition highlights the importance of monitoring blood sugar levels in affected individuals to prevent potential complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">48f1fe343d54cd0f353be34b736a352c,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
