    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL TOTAL (NPT)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NPT es un tipo de nutrici&#243;n administrada intravenosamente que el paciente ha estado recibiendo para mantener su estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6844</data>
      <data key="d7">8b0d904d63474671a83adb9e99792ebd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDA NASOENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SONDA NASOENTERAL" refers to a medical procedure involving the use of a nasoenteral tube, which is a type of feeding tube designed for providing enteral nutrition to patients who are unable to eat by mouth. This device is particularly indicated for short-term use and is beneficial for patients with issues such as delayed gastric emptying or a risk of aspiration. 

The nasoenteral tube can be categorized into specific types, including the nasoduodenal (SND) and nasoyeyunal (SNY) tubes, which allow for the infusion of nutrition beyond the pylorus, directly into the stomach or intestines. While effective for delivering nutrition, the use of nasoenteral tubes can lead to complications and may cause agitation in patients with decreased consciousness. Overall, the SONDA NASOENTERAL serves as a critical tool in the management of patients requiring enteral feeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,4fbc9ba7c1f3ff190b594c75e7eac015,7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">6845</data>
      <data key="d7">a41b767aff154b4aaf1f33a2ef85d89c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TC (TOMOGRAF&#205;A COMPUTARIZADA)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La TC es un procedimiento de imagen que se realiz&#243; para evaluar la evoluci&#243;n del paciente con pancreatitis aguda.</data>
      <data key="d2">7c10030e29c1434df3b10b1533710486</data>
