    </node>
    <node id="REPOSO PANCRE&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El reposo pancre&#225;tico es una estrategia terap&#233;utica que se ha utilizado en el tratamiento de la pancreatitis, aunque su eficacia ha sido cuestionada.</data>
      <data key="d2">88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6850</data>
      <data key="d7">e726c17a54c44cf6b68432ace94851ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO ORG&#193;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FALLO ORG&#193;NICO refers to a serious condition characterized by the failure of one or more organs, which may require the use of specialized nutritional formulas to support the affected individual. This condition is particularly critical in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, where it can manifest as a severe complication. The presence of organ failure in these patients can extend beyond 48 hours and is associated with an increased mortality rate, especially in severe cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,b3dfcfd0255d51aaff0c01a236bce881,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e</data>
      <data key="d3">1096</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6851</data>
      <data key="d7">7f1f6febc9854d888b6cfd80e70ddf56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LITIASIS BILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LITIASIS BILIAR, also known as biliary lithiasis or gallstones, is a significant medical condition characterized by the formation of stones in the bile ducts. It is recognized as the most common cause of acute pancreatitis in various countries, accounting for approximately 35% of episodes. This condition can arise as a complication of obesity, which negatively impacts digestive health and necessitates appropriate management. In particular, biliary lithiasis is one of the most prevalent etiologies of acute pancreatitis, as the presence of gallstones can obstruct the pancreatic duct, leading to inflammation and other serious complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,f9aab8a2d805b64afaa1c261f3947869</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6852</data>
      <data key="d7">9521ab1054a34239b7f592e0de314f13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSUMO EXCESIVO DE ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El consumo excesivo de alcohol es una de las principales causas de pancreatitis aguda, contribuyendo al da&#241;o del tejido pancre&#225;tico.</data>
      <data key="d2">88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6853</data>
