    </node>
    <node id="HEYLAND DK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Heyland DK is a prominent researcher recognized for significant contributions to clinical practice guidelines regarding nutrition support in critically ill patients. His work encompasses a broad understanding of nutritional management, particularly for vulnerable groups such as burn victims. Additionally, Heyland DK has played a key role as an author in the recommendations stemming from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit. He has also contributed to the systematic review focused on nutrition support in cases of acute pancreatitis, further underscoring his expertise and influence in the field of nutritional care for critically ill individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5af63a33abe5094b25a96394f69969,3f1d1c7c7c62b83f62f6fa31c25f65b2,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97</data>
