    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCALORIC JEJUNAL FEEDING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypocaloric jejunal feeding is a nutritional strategy that provides fewer calories than the body needs, delivered through the jejunum, often used in patients with acute pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6912</data>
      <data key="d7">8f4a959d72e84ea686f3edab632508a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED TRIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A randomized controlled trial is a study design that randomly assigns participants to different interventions to compare outcomes and assess the effects of those interventions. This methodology is often employed in clinical research to evaluate the effectiveness of various treatments. Specifically, randomized controlled trials are utilized to test the efficacy of nutritional interventions in patients, including those with gastric cancer. Additionally, this type of scientific experiment is used to examine the efficacy of treatments for conditions such as obesity, with examples including the testing of drugs like cetilistat and beloranib. Overall, randomized controlled trials are a crucial tool in determining the effectiveness of medical and nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,3534154ea7562c7d4abe51bf29546109,3d5af63a33abe5094b25a96394f69969,64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d3">324</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">6913</data>
      <data key="d7">64c68a68b1b14d0b9ec3cb22eaee7980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYSTEMATIC REVIEW">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A systematic review is a methodical and comprehensive analysis of research studies focused on a specific topic. It serves as a crucial research method that summarizes the results of available studies, providing a thorough understanding of the evidence related to various subjects, particularly in health and nutritional research. Systematic reviews are essential for developing clinical practice guidelines and often address specific research questions. They can cover a wide range of topics, including but not limited to parenteral nutrition-associated cholestasis, dietary advice for women with gestational diabetes, nutrient deficiencies after bariatric surgery, the effects of diet on cognitive performance, and the impact of iron-fortified foods. By compiling and analyzing multiple studies, systematic reviews contribute significantly to the body of knowledge in their respective fields.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f06578cbfda22ce8c7d322ba35a93a1,35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,384e13475cc83e77e160fd6be9a88e73,60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,91b470ee527a45d8e81a821eeb9ce259,cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b,dbdb3cd3b9065e8846fd2eb15b9d5879,faa6d27a781e64a98fe101236a44dc16</data>
      <data key="d3">689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6914</data>
      <data key="d7">13ee14bffa794d83b92cade9a596f1da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="META-ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">META-ANALYSIS refers to a statistical technique that integrates the results of multiple studies to identify patterns, differences, or overall effects. This method is frequently utilized in dietary and health research to derive comprehensive conclusions from various research findings. By synthesizing data from different studies, meta-analysis helps to enhance the understanding of specific research questions and provides a more robust evidence base for decision-making in these fields.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,dbdb3cd3b9065e8846fd2eb15b9d5879</data>
      <data key="d3">689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6915</data>
      <data key="d7">112480c9856f426091108371bbec1a54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROSPECTIVE STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A prospective study is a research design that follows participants over time to observe outcomes, often used in clinical research to assess the effects of interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6916</data>
      <data key="d7">ba5b0255c4164917891906e31a2f4e2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEALTH TECHNOLOGY ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Health technology assessment is a systematic evaluation of the properties and effects of health technology, including its direct and intended effects, as well as its indirect effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6917</data>
      <data key="d7">2e9856787edf46f4881ce79055824066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL TRIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A clinical trial is a research study conducted with human participants to evaluate the effects and efficacy of medical interventions. It tests how well new medical approaches, including new drugs, devices, or treatment strategies, work in people. Additionally, clinical trials can also focus on specific nutritional interventions to assess their impact on patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">33900ea313cbdf466c2bebc1f587e2bf,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29</data>
      <data key="d3">1252</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">6918</data>
      <data key="d7">476fb183f66d4541ba6b023396a149f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFLAMMATORY RESPONSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The inflammatory response is a biological reaction that occurs in the body as a response to injury or infection. It can be particularly heightened in patients with esophageal cancer, where it contributes to conditions such as cachexia and weight loss. Additionally, the inflammatory response can be influenced by nutritional support, especially in cases of acute pancreatitis, highlighting the complex interplay between inflammation and nutritional status in various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6919</data>
      <data key="d7">c6195571acf9435dbafbfdbe6db89d0a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APACHE II SCORE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The APACHE II score is a severity-of-disease classification system that is used to assess the prognosis of patients in intensive care, particularly in cases like acute pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6920</data>
      <data key="d7">4c902a0a024146a1ab9ab033dadaf60b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN ACUTE PANCREATITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional support in acute pancreatitis refers to the strategies and methods used to provide adequate nutrition to patients suffering from this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6921</data>
      <data key="d7">1d8171f6207f4267a20593a0ac9d4d4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEVERE ACUTE PANCREATITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Severe acute pancreatitis is a serious condition characterized by significant inflammation of the pancreas. This more severe form of acute pancreatitis can lead to various complications and necessitates intensive medical management. Patients with severe acute pancreatitis often require nutritional support to aid in their recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5af63a33abe5094b25a96394f69969,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d3">204</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">6922</data>
      <data key="d7">98bf0c4aba2247bb9076283d87ef2ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional interventions are essential strategies designed to enhance dietary intake and improve nutritional status across various medical conditions. They are particularly recommended for patients with liver disease to help improve their nutritional status and prevent complications. These interventions are also crucial for individuals with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, where they aim to enhance overall health and dietary intake. Additionally, nutritional interventions play a significant role in the management of patients with acute pancreatitis, focusing on improving their nutritional status. Furthermore, these interventions often incorporate food education to promote better treatment adherence and healthier dietary patterns. Overall, nutritional interventions are vital in clinical settings to support patients' health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">37182848d30a82f99b7a617859ac6e0d,55aabc274c460459322072406f17d52c,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d3">240</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">6923</data>
      <data key="d7">ba279a1786f643149bf0714d74d5c3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RANDOMIZED COMPARATIVE STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A randomized comparative study is a type of research that compares two or more interventions in a randomized manner to determine their effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6924</data>
      <data key="d7">92ef83eb5def4220a5b61b66e740193b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROGNOSTIC INDICES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prognostic indices are tools used to predict the outcome of a disease or condition, often based on clinical and laboratory data.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6925</data>
      <data key="d7">7b14cfe1d3914e3d9f3ccf374babd439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL OUTCOMES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional outcomes refer to the results of nutritional interventions and assessments in patients with liver disease. These outcomes encompass improvements in health status, recovery times, and overall well-being, highlighting the significance of nutrition in the management and treatment of liver conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6926</data>
      <data key="d7">528f34c88eea4aef9c6a4d8e616d0be6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical Nutrition is a multifaceted field of study and practice that emphasizes the critical role of nutrition in clinical settings, particularly for patients with various health conditions, including cancer, diabetes, and acute pancreatitis. It encompasses the dietary management of patients to enhance health outcomes and improve disease management. 

In addition to being a specialized area of nutrition, Clinical Nutrition is also the title of a journal that publishes a wide range of research and reviews related to clinical nutrition practices. This journal covers topics such as home artificial nutrition, nutritional interventions in clinical settings, and the effects of nutrition on health outcomes. It includes studies on specific patient populations, such as those with stroke, pancreatitis, and burn care, as well as research on body mass index, malnutrition, and the prognostic significance of sarcopenia in hospitalized patients.

Overall, Clinical Nutrition serves as both a vital field of study and a key resource for practitioners, providing guidelines and evidence-based research to inform dietary management strategies in clinical practice.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,12b6478763cfb60ad144be6b81778e03,14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,22f9164844b9778cfef429e45de95060,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,499132ff7f7da81d7effbadf776c5b54,4c4d1882f0ac14b7c55941ec1c17b650,54bdd3faa067cdbb44671453ffaf4be5,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,723cbca2d5cfbf8cf05a923c52569641,7e3e2024996e402fc0ab62933ab9417b,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97,933cfaece6287ed7626c5216a1e5c54d,a3d355dd6da93691c892691f873338aa,aae3f23f674724518bcb311a99d764d6,c3182f51249513a920db6b935632fead,e5542485c64706310c70513397de07f9</data>
      <data key="d3">712</data>
