      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">6927</data>
      <data key="d7">3c93e97e0d7646fdb7e875f51439cf5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENTERAL FEEDING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enteral feeding is a method of delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines, primarily utilized for patients who are unable to eat by mouth or cannot consume food normally. This approach ensures that individuals receive the necessary nutrients to maintain their health and support recovery when oral intake is not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5af63a33abe5094b25a96394f69969,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,6f500b6f65f41f4fc89abcf53a4e409e</data>
      <data key="d3">204</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">6928</data>
      <data key="d7">44ea49f91acb4e4eb0bb888ea40b9a1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOTAL PARENTERAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Total parenteral nutrition (TPN) is a medical method of feeding that delivers nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This approach is often utilized for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, including those with chylous conditions or severe cases of pancreatitis. TPN provides all nutritional requirements intravenously, making it a critical option for individuals who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through traditional means.</data>
      <data key="d2">64378df2be6b08b39bd652c0a2d3789c,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,73d47e377c2910da3393d7bb65f80e8e,a265c943c66b9cb5d09f89d40ddb995f,a35fdf8cbbb5fe4783572ea6e86f7776,f5175f0c433eb4e10840a41d8052c8e0</data>
      <data key="d3">1723</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">6929</data>
      <data key="d7">339b6d964bf84515962ff9775841df7d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY INTERVENTIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary interventions refer to changes made to a patient's diet aimed at improving health outcomes. These interventions are particularly significant in the management of various diseases, including acute pancreatitis and chronic conditions such as Alzheimer's disease. By implementing strategies to modify dietary habits, dietary interventions seek to enhance overall health and well-being, addressing both acute and chronic health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,91b470ee527a45d8e81a821eeb9ce259</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">6930</data>
      <data key="d7">4d350f05ebd1432f8f8a96de06128570</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional therapy is a comprehensive treatment approach that utilizes dietary interventions to enhance the quality of life and health outcomes for patients across various medical conditions. This therapy is particularly beneficial for individuals with cancer, liver disease, chronic kidney disease, and liver cirrhosis, as it involves tailored dietary practices aimed at managing these specific health issues. 

In addition to these conditions, nutritional therapy plays a crucial role in the recovery of patients with burns and is essential for managing diabetes by focusing on dietary adjustments to regulate blood sugar levels and minimize complications. It is also employed in the treatment of critically ill patients, addressing their unique nutritional needs to improve their clinical course.

Furthermore, nutritional therapy encompasses dietary management for patients with inflammatory bowel diseases, such as Crohn's disease, and is utilized in cases of acute pancreatitis. Overall, this therapy involves the provision of dietary prescriptions based on individual nutritional requirements, which may include various types of diets and nutritional support, making it a vital component of patient care in numerous health contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">03b047c49cda5e7bb642efcc9109ccc6,10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,2e4409d82bf1cb293a2df7fc1a8cc9e7,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,7a389f3625ba13c74ce52213197b01ae,7f3e164582a504c9fe6bdbc56e1a8e97,8c198f866d8fb49a782cb57139b30d76,97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4,a7672b877f024a5e716c48c18cd14f54,afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc,b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
      <data key="d3">1231</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">27</data>
      <data key="d6">6931</data>
      <data key="d7">9702f5bad8204f3097632bce4fcad685</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL EVALUATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional evaluation is a critical process that involves assessing the dietary intake and nutritional status of patients across various demographics, including neonates, pediatric patients, and individuals with specific health conditions such as liver cirrhosis and diabetes. This evaluation is particularly significant in vulnerable populations, such as infants, where proper nutritional assessment can inform treatment plans and dietary interventions. The literature highlights the importance of nutritional evaluation in optimizing health outcomes, especially for those with liver disease and other chronic conditions. By understanding a patient's dietary needs and health status, healthcare providers can tailor interventions to improve overall nutritional health and support effective management of various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">52d93d6adba464a2397ddec01d152840,6935432f69970131a6485f38e3f06003,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,bb209dcfffac9c89dae0ad4ed2908d85,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
