    <node id="GASTROSTOM&#205;A QUIR&#218;RGICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GASTROSTOM&#205;A QUIR&#218;RGICA is a surgical procedure designed to create an opening into the stomach, primarily for the purpose of providing nutritional support to patients who experience difficulties with swallowing. This procedure involves the placement of a feeding tube directly into the stomach, which is particularly beneficial for individuals suffering from esophageal obstruction or other medical conditions that hinder the use of endoscopic techniques for feeding. Overall, GASTROSTOM&#205;A QUIR&#218;RGICA serves as a critical intervention for patients requiring alternative methods of nutrition delivery.</data>
      <data key="d2">234b514a40a64bc02f1346cb62cf3f97,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
