      <data key="d7">50b25a78898045a394d6e268ff1e5e93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CFTR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CFTR (Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator) is the gene responsible for cystic fibrosis, coding for a chloride channel protein.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7005</data>
      <data key="d7">64b7cb3081454afba148fe9e7f431b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACI&#211;N F508DEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F508del is the most common mutation associated with cystic fibrosis, affecting the CFTR gene.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7006</data>
      <data key="d7">8709bf68626e407b97f2c4ebc2ec6fb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA EXOCRINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency (EPI) is a medical condition characterized by the pancreas's inability to produce sufficient digestive enzymes, which can lead to difficulties in digesting food properly. This condition is commonly associated with cystic fibrosis, where it significantly impacts the patient's ability to absorb nutrients effectively. Management of EPI often requires specific dietary adjustments to help mitigate the effects of the insufficient enzyme production and improve overall nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7007</data>
      <data key="d7">2deff7ddf43340ada2744dee61367d22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA ENDOCRINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Endocrine pancreatic insufficiency is another complication of cystic fibrosis that can lead to diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7008</data>
      <data key="d7">86367422bdb9441185c40be853525a4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSULTAS EXTERNAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"CONSULTAS EXTERNAS" refers to medical services that enable patients to receive care without the need for hospitalization. This includes medical follow-ups and assessments specifically for patients with cystic fibrosis, ensuring they receive the necessary attention and support in an outpatient setting.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
