      <data key="d6">7022</data>
      <data key="d7">54c44da76bb04ff7b342539dca18af46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A RELACIONADA CON LA FQ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatopathy related to cystic fibrosis refers to liver disease that can occur as a complication of cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699</data>
      <data key="d3">1042</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7023</data>
      <data key="d7">a6061a050a0747408af61b21c39a55b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA, or pancreatic insufficiency, is a medical condition characterized by the pancreas's inability to produce sufficient digestive enzymes. This deficiency can lead to impaired nutritional absorption and is commonly associated with several underlying health issues. It is frequently observed in patients with cystic fibrosis, chronic pancreatitis, and liver disease. The lack of adequate enzyme production can significantly affect digestion and overall health, necessitating medical intervention to manage the condition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699,32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
      <data key="d3">1042</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7024</data>
      <data key="d7">5b4b2ab7ce0e4447a292becd5602b5c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR" refers to a range of conditions that impact the lungs, including Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), which is recognized as a significant health concern. Additionally, pulmonary disease is a critical component of cystic fibrosis, characterized by chronic inflammation and infection within the lungs. This pulmonary involvement is a common complication in cystic fibrosis, influencing both the management strategies and dietary requirements of affected patients. Overall, pulmonary disease plays a central role in the health challenges faced by individuals with these conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699,6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7025</data>
      <data key="d7">2d08b9e20084487bb7a3ae2a9b939651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE OBSTRUCCI&#211;N INTESTINAL DISTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Distal Intestinal Obstruction Syndrome (DIOS), also known as "S&#237;ndrome de Obstrucci&#243;n Intestinal Distal," is a significant complication that occurs in patients with cystic fibrosis. This condition is characterized by partial bowel obstruction, which can severely limit oral consumption and overall nutritional intake for affected individuals. DIOS is specifically associated with the complications arising from cystic fibrosis, leading to challenges in managing bowel health and dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d3">1042</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
