    <node id="SEPSIS GRAVE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sepsis Grave, or severe sepsis, is a life-threatening condition that occurs when the body's response to an infection leads to significant injury to its own tissues and organs. This serious medical condition can develop as a result of various infections, including peritonitis, which is an inflammation of the peritoneum often caused by bacterial infection. In such cases, the body's overwhelming response to the infection can result in severe complications, making timely medical intervention critical for patient survival.</data>
      <data key="d2">449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,bc381304b682e075c7356c6edbfb0c2d</data>
