    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES ORALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Suplementos nutricionales orales son productos dise&#241;ados para complementar la dieta y proporcionar nutrientes adicionales, utilizados en pacientes con deficiencias nutricionales.</data>
      <data key="d2">e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7070</data>
      <data key="d7">831c5a39241e4bbd81ff6d6e9ed39b27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CCEE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CCEE, or Consultas Externas Especializadas, refers to specialized medical services that provide care to patients who do not require continuous hospitalization. These services focus on offering specialized follow-up and treatment, ensuring that patients receive the necessary medical attention without the need for an inpatient stay.</data>
      <data key="d2">4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,e474ebdcd3e5392e4b2bed8434293849</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7071</data>
      <data key="d7">5ef1159c979f445294f6ac74ca7c1503</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The UN, in this context, refers to a medical unit that plays a crucial role in the nutritional assessment and treatment of patients, especially in complex cases. Additionally, the UN encompasses the nursing unit responsible for the overall care of the patient, which includes daily wound care and dietary recommendations. This dual focus highlights the UN's commitment to providing comprehensive medical support and specialized nursing care to enhance patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7072</data>
      <data key="d7">a34c40ac872d4cfe8d4fe76e956275c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GRP refers to a prophylactic gastrostomy placement that was requested for the patient, serving as a medical intervention to provide nutritional support. This type of feeding tube is utilized for patients who are unable to take food orally, indicating its importance in ensuring adequate nutrition. The gastrostomy route through which the patient received this nutritional support is critical for their recovery post-surgery, highlighting the essential role of GRP in the patient's overall treatment plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b901814a09392d24880be465dcbce6f,4681f41ebd69a732f7a8be6c2ed0f51a,49d3f1ca700a7974db89e684f3744a40,5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c</data>
      <data key="d3">1111</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7073</data>
      <data key="d7">d9c8b9ed1b0b4e00a6dd9c519ef89109</data>
    </node>
