    <node id="CIPROFLOXACINO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ciprofloxacino is a specific quinolone antibiotic primarily used to treat various bacterial infections, including urinary tract infections and acute diarrhea. It is recognized as a basic medication, and its absorption can be enhanced in higher pH conditions, which may be influenced by food intake. Ciprofloxacino is primarily absorbed in the upper digestive tract; however, its absorption can be compromised when administered through a jejunostomy. Additionally, it is utilized in severe cases of inflammatory bowel disease to improve prognosis in situations such as perforation.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f,850572c4d004fc52f65ced939eda06bf,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b,cba5d81f1acff7cbf84e85ef35420521</data>
