    <node id="BILIRRUBINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bilirrubina is a substance produced from the breakdown of red blood cells. It plays a crucial role in assessing liver function and hemolysis, as its levels are indicative of these processes. Total bilirubin levels are routinely monitored as part of liver function tests to evaluate the health of the liver and detect any potential issues related to red blood cell breakdown.</data>
