    <node id="HEPATITIS B">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatitis B is a viral infection that primarily affects the liver and can lead to serious health complications. A patient was diagnosed with hepatitis B in March-April of 2005, which complicated their overall health condition. This infection is particularly concerning for individuals with hemochromatosis, as it poses additional risks and can exacerbate liver-related issues. Hepatitis B is known to cause chronic liver disease and is associated with iron overload, making it a significant concern for patients suffering from conditions that affect iron metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
