    <node id="FERROPENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FERROPENIA refers to iron deficiency, a condition characterized by a lack of iron in the body, which can lead to anemia. This condition is particularly prevalent among women in developing countries and is also common during adolescence, especially in females who experience heavy menstrual losses. The presence of ferropenia was identified during developmental assessments of patients, indicating a significant deficiency of iron.</data>
      <data key="d2">0c6c9eb4aba5c4642a75d76bd7ea08ba,62bb1dedc96b7530649f4c9762faab9d,868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd,efbbfb33c127e16f4f9013683aff2c5f</data>
