      <data key="d6">7139</data>
      <data key="d7">e4b88559a8b6446483900791eae9d0b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENCEFALOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Encefalopat&#237;a is a neurological condition characterized by brain dysfunction, which can manifest in patients suffering from urea cycle disorders and severe liver disease. This condition is often a result of hyperammonemia, a buildup of ammonia in the blood, which can significantly impact the overall health and level of consciousness of affected individuals. Encefalopat&#237;a encompasses a wide range of brain dysfunctions, highlighting its complexity and the various underlying causes associated with liver disease and metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a,6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7140</data>
      <data key="d7">2a6b7fa31023477b95830df06a83205e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERKALEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperkalemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated potassium levels in the blood, which can pose significant health risks. In the patient's case, hyperkalemia was noted as a concerning condition. Additionally, hyperkalemia can occur in conjunction with other conditions such as hypoaldosteronism and hyponatremia, indicating a potential interplay between these disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">6edff59a3b151e946e7664f13bcb0931,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
