    <node id="BENZODIAZEPINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Benzodiazepinas are a class of medications known for their ability to produce sedative, anxiolytic, and muscle relaxant effects. These medications can have their effects potentiated by alcohol consumption, which may increase the risk of sedation and respiratory depression. Additionally, benzodiazepinas are utilized in the treatment of seizures, particularly in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, a rare genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. Furthermore, benzodiazepinas have been tested in patients as part of their treatment regimen for conditions such as regurgitation, indicating their diverse therapeutic applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,ce4c057e0a625bc9e64301a0cca1e206</data>
