    <node id="GASTROSTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrostomy is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the stomach to provide nutritional support. This procedure entails placing a feeding tube directly into the stomach, allowing for the delivery of food and medications to individuals who may have difficulty eating by mouth. It is primarily used for patients requiring long-term nutritional assistance.</data>
      <data key="d2">3a5d7e4dc412f1d4701672c3af3cb4ed,cae7bf8d7b8c9d1f34a87ef41ff39a17,f902ee3930fcc849fa131b58d6e4933d</data>
