    <node id="HOSPITALARIO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HOSPITALARIO refers to the hospital setting, particularly focusing on the role of the hospital pharmacist. The hospital pharmacist is a professional who plays a crucial role in managing the interactions between medications and nutrients for patients receiving enteral nutrition. Additionally, within this hospital context, the prevalence of malnutrition among patients is assessed, highlighting the importance of nutritional management in healthcare settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ed179f6e734d9fe4921fb0be0b018e4,7f0ee0bea2b1dfd09e75026d4c027291</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7241</data>
      <data key="d7">ef1c21a9104443e9acecfa9ab67cdf75</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANCREATIC CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the tissues of the pancreas. It is known for its aggressive nature and poor prognosis, often being diagnosed at an advanced stage. This cancer is frequently associated with cachexia, a syndrome characterized by significant weight loss and muscle wasting, which poses considerable health challenges for affected individuals. Treatment for pancreatic cancer often requires surgical intervention and nutritional support to manage the symptoms and complications associated with the disease. Additionally, studies have explored the relationship between pancreatic cancer and dietary habits, including the potential protective effects of dietary fiber intake. Overall, pancreatic cancer presents a serious health concern with a high mortality rate, necessitating ongoing research and comprehensive treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">6216a2d06144ebde48b78330f488c603,758bc764453f49b9097073c5175470cc,9f0dc667db1447b9e51420cc6ba091c9,a496bf37d4cc9b6246f5eb6b66b03d8a,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,daed781ebc502b854582efdef23e9dde,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
      <data key="d3">1207</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">7242</data>
      <data key="d7">3ba06b08509a4c419be6db1ccfcc43ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA, also known as cancer cachexia, is a syndrome that manifests as severe body weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and fat loss, frequently observed in patients suffering from advanced cancer. This condition can also arise from chronic enteritis, which may be a consequence of chemotherapy and/or radiotherapy, resulting in significant malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3</data>
      <data key="d3">1207</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7243</data>
      <data key="d7">f4e34194ed0b4c37bf3e1bc9b2ed8750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOCARCINOMA DE P&#193;NCREAS DUCTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adenocarcinoma de p&#225;ncreas ductal is a type of cancer that is frequently associated with cachexia, affecting 70-80% of patients and linked to decreased survival and quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7244</data>
      <data key="d7">318a988c4a0f4eb7b55aaf4496bf7733</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NE NORMOCAL&#211;RICA Y NORMOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Normocaloric and normoproteic nutritional support with soluble fiber was administered to the patient to normalize weight and regulate intestinal rhythm.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7245</data>
      <data key="d7">eec15a92603e451ab839b8766842266c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a condition that worsened the patient's metabolic control, leading to elevated blood glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7246</data>
      <data key="d7">85ef610d1be04963b426ab26fd815140</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA, also known as medroxyprogesterone acetate, is a medication that serves multiple therapeutic purposes. It is primarily recognized for its ability to improve appetite and reduce weight loss, particularly in patients suffering from conditions such as cancer. Additionally, this medication may antagonize the catabolic effects of cytokines, which are often elevated in such patients, thereby helping to mitigate the adverse effects associated with these inflammatory markers. Overall, ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA plays a significant role in enhancing the quality of life for individuals experiencing appetite loss and weight reduction due to various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7247</data>
      <data key="d7">df272de41cb344f6ad15f87496cd238e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNO INMUNOMODULADORA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Immunomodulatory nutritional support was not chosen for the patient, focusing instead on specific nutritional support for diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7248</data>
      <data key="d7">1128131cd9384c5da54ba107c0a8c4b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNO ESPEC&#205;FICA DE DM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Specific nutritional support for diabetes management was recommended, which does not contain omega-3 or nucleotides.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7249</data>
      <data key="d7">2bb02cf0d7a44bc6af015fd014e70373</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HMB">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HMB, or &#946;-hydroxy-&#946;-methylbutyrate, is a metabolite of the amino acid leucine. It is commonly used as a dietary supplement aimed at improving muscle mass and strength. Research indicates that HMB may help mitigate muscle loss and promote muscle gain, particularly in elderly individuals and patients with various conditions, including those experiencing excessive post-exercise oxygen consumption (EPOC). While HMB has been studied for its potential benefits in enhancing muscle mass and strength, the clarity of its positive effects for generating specific recommendations remains uncertain. Overall, HMB is recognized for its role in influencing muscle mass, especially in the context of resistance training.</data>
      <data key="d2">54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,da58ef987e74d508eb95395230f21cdc,eadd983c9f28c11a1c279e4b923351cd</data>
      <data key="d3">1041</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7250</data>
      <data key="d7">29bdfac5134145b3bb1f64d0ec1f4fb6</data>
    </node>
