    </node>
    <node id="CRUCIFEROUS VEGETABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cruciferous vegetables are a group of vegetables known for their health benefits, particularly in reducing the risk of cardiovascular disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7293</data>
      <data key="d7">509b37e8e0194764838223d49af7b2d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYSLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal levels of lipids in the blood, which poses a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease. This condition is often associated with obesity, highlighting the relationship between lipid levels and body weight.</data>
      <data key="d2">20863ac06779722abc2cbc2dd023777e,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7294</data>
      <data key="d7">dbf6822fcc014517aa32ad56c6574d62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad cerebrovascular se refiere a un grupo de condiciones que afectan el flujo sangu&#237;neo al cerebro, lo que puede resultar en un accidente cerebrovascular o ictus.</data>
      <data key="d2">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7295</data>
      <data key="d7">7a7d5037542b4f32836d85ec1b9cd777</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUTAS Y VERDURAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Frutas y verduras son alimentos de origen vegetal que se asocian con m&#250;ltiples beneficios para la salud, incluyendo la reducci&#243;n del riesgo de enfermedades cr&#243;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">7296</data>
      <data key="d7">7cb1158051024d9fbe6e11305a1e159a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETA-CAROTENOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los beta-carotenos son compuestos que se encuentran en frutas y verduras de color naranja y verde, y se asocian con beneficios para la salud, incluyendo la reducci&#243;n del riesgo de enfermedades cr&#243;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7297</data>
      <data key="d7">c3b2ba02ef18475cb6b23de6529db40a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VERDURAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">VERDURAS, or vegetables, are essential components of a balanced diet, providing a wealth of vitamins, minerals, and fiber that contribute to overall health. They are generally low in calories and sodium, making them a healthy choice for various dietary needs. Regular consumption of vegetables is associated with a reduced risk of cancer and plays a crucial role in dietary guidelines, particularly for children and heart health, as emphasized in the DASH and Mediterranean diets. 

Certain vegetables may contain small amounts of galactose, which should be consumed with caution by individuals with galactosemia. Additionally, vegetables are recommended for their role in preventing kidney stones and promoting hydration and nutrient intake. Leafy greens, in particular, are highlighted for their high calcium content and are encouraged for daily intake.

Vegetables are categorized with specific weight measurements for main and side dishes, and they are noted for their low purine content, which can influence uric acid levels. Some vegetables have been linked to lower serum uric acid levels and a decreased risk of hyperuricemia. However, it is advised to eliminate certain vegetables from the diet prior to specific medical tests to avoid false positives.

Overall, VERDURAS are fundamental in the Mediterranean diet and are emphasized in dietary recommendations for their numerous health benefits, including their contributions to cardiovascular health and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,633a3a90a82e02d05096b361ddba3ad7,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,b5db5210dfb726bf3f6d3fae82598596,e0208971287419e734607191646ae36d,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
      <data key="d3">1401</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">7298</data>
      <data key="d7">3ff68cf2045644cf9c69ae1b7ba29752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRUC&#205;FERAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las verduras cruc&#237;feras son un grupo de vegetales que han sido objeto de investigaci&#243;n por sus potenciales efectos protectores frente al c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7299</data>
      <data key="d7">ac76d6f9571d4e0797f825bb41b2d6af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA RICA EN FRUTAS Y VERDURAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Una dieta que incluye un alto consumo de frutas y verduras se asocia con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de varios tipos de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">7300</data>
      <data key="d7">dd8b365025b04536a65ff0f5b95672c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE ES&#211;FAGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de es&#243;fago es una enfermedad que afecta el es&#243;fago, caracterizada por la formaci&#243;n de c&#233;lulas malignas en sus tejidos. Esta neoplasia se asocia con una alta incidencia de malnutrici&#243;n y p&#233;rdida de peso en los pacientes, lo que puede llevar a complicaciones graves como la caquexia. A menudo, el c&#225;ncer de es&#243;fago es diagnosticado en estadios avanzados y presenta s&#237;ntomas como disfagia, que es la dificultad para tragar. El tratamiento de esta enfermedad generalmente requiere un enfoque quir&#250;rgico, como la esofagectom&#237;a, as&#237; como un manejo nutricional especializado para abordar las complicaciones relacionadas con la malnutrici&#243;n. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado que un mayor consumo de frutas y verduras puede reducir el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, una de las formas m&#225;s comunes de c&#225;ncer de es&#243;fago. En resumen, el c&#225;ncer de es&#243;fago es una condici&#243;n grave que no solo afecta la salud f&#237;sica del paciente, sino que tambi&#233;n requiere un enfoque integral en su tratamiento y manejo nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,27b65be3bda292c9c26dfd7a87e74752,5664277128c865feb0e93f9fd56a3d05,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,7c0d1f274b31d130e4feb8e46fbeb764,a7baff5fb024c516ea6ae8c236dc945d,acba2f4838c3e73b321d9dcc6ba6fe55,f0d279ccc92a98dc953edafb1080630b</data>
      <data key="d3">1139</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">7301</data>
      <data key="d7">7c4eeec4b60c4ea5b45f361faab36d68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer g&#225;strico, tambi&#233;n conocido como c&#225;ncer de est&#243;mago, es una enfermedad que afecta el est&#243;mago y se caracteriza por un pron&#243;stico desfavorable, especialmente en estadios avanzados. Esta enfermedad puede causar p&#233;rdida de peso y otros s&#237;ntomas relacionados con la inflamaci&#243;n sist&#233;mica. El c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico es un problema de salud significativo, siendo el quinto tipo de c&#225;ncer m&#225;s com&#250;n a nivel mundial y la tercera causa principal de mortalidad por c&#225;ncer, a menudo diagnosticado en etapas tard&#237;as debido a s&#237;ntomas no espec&#237;ficos.

El tratamiento del c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico puede requerir cirug&#237;a y un tratamiento nutricional espec&#237;fico, incluyendo cuidados postoperatorios para mejorar la recuperaci&#243;n y reducir complicaciones. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado que el c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico puede afectar el gasto energ&#233;tico en reposo de los pacientes, lo que resalta la importancia de la nutrici&#243;n en su manejo.

Existen factores diet&#233;ticos que pueden influir en el riesgo de desarrollar c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico. Se ha sugerido que una mayor ingesta de fibra diet&#233;tica puede actuar como un eliminador potencial de nitritos, lo que podr&#237;a ayudar a prevenir esta enfermedad. Por otro lado, un alto consumo de nitritos provenientes de la carne roja o procesada se ha relacionado con un mayor riesgo de c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico. Asimismo, el consumo de frutas parece estar asociado con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de esta enfermedad, lo que sugiere que una dieta equilibrada puede desempe&#241;ar un papel protector.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,70a9e916b8c55784c53828958c76eb09,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,a7baff5fb024c516ea6ae8c236dc945d,d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56,e34642244b0c7f309ab1c1be1e81da31,f0d279ccc92a98dc953edafb1080630b,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1087</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">7302</data>
      <data key="d7">d5517bc438ef4c068d258fbe319ae58f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER HEP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer hep&#225;tico is a type of liver cancer that has been the subject of various studies, particularly concerning its relationship with dietary factors. Research indicates that a high intake of omega-3 fatty acids may have implications for the risk of developing this cancer. Additionally, a significant inverse association has been observed between fish consumption and the risk of c&#225;ncer hep&#225;tico, suggesting that higher fish intake may lower the likelihood of this disease. Furthermore, the consumption of white meat has been noted to potentially reduce the risk of c&#225;ncer hep&#225;tico. In contrast, an increase in the intake of vegetables has also been linked to a decreased risk of developing this type of cancer. Overall, dietary choices, including the consumption of fish, white meat, and vegetables, play a crucial role in influencing the risk of c&#225;ncer hep&#225;tico.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7303</data>
      <data key="d7">5e801b66b16840519f5f09523fdc00c6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER OV&#193;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#193;NCER OV&#193;RICO, or ovarian cancer, is a type of cancer that may be influenced by dietary factors, particularly the consumption of cruciferous vegetables. While some evidence suggests that these vegetables could play a role in reducing the risk of ovarian cancer, the findings are inconsistent, indicating that further research is needed to fully understand the relationship between cruciferous vegetable intake and ovarian cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d3">981</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7304</data>
      <data key="d7">f76ff455e8c24c18834e08133901d658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LINFOMA NO HODGKIN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Linfoma no Hodgkin, also known as Non-Hodgkin lymphoma, is a type of cancer characterized by the abnormal growth of lymphatic cells. Research indicates that the risk of developing Linfoma no Hodgkin may be influenced by dietary factors. Specifically, several meta-analyses have found an association between the consumption of red and processed meats and an increased risk of this type of lymphoma. Conversely, the risk of Linfoma no Hodgkin may be inversely associated with the consumption of fruits and vegetables, suggesting that a diet rich in these foods could potentially lower the risk of developing this cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
      <data key="d3">983</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7305</data>
      <data key="d7">4b180f6c577546638d3f4ca6fbc7c0b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CARNE refers to meat, which plays a significant role in dietary practices. While meat consumption, especially red and processed meat, is associated with various health risks, including chronic diseases, it is also recognized as a vital component of dietary recommendations for children. These recommendations highlight the importance of meat in providing essential protein and maintaining nutritional balance in their diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7306</data>
      <data key="d7">381e719a05114fd981ed5dbd9995bef8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNE ROJA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La carne roja se asocia con un aumento del riesgo de varios tipos de c&#225;ncer, incluyendo c&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico, g&#225;strico y colorrectal.</data>
      <data key="d2">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7307</data>
      <data key="d7">896bc6a84348419eb9d9f863db6e9aaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNE PROCESADA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La carne procesada se relaciona con un incremento del riesgo de c&#225;ncer colorrectal, p&#225;ncreas, y otros tipos de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d2">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7308</data>
      <data key="d7">432ac246ec014e7da2fbb34802af0019</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NITRITOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los nitritos presentes en la carne est&#225;n asociados con un mayor riesgo de c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico y de vejiga.</data>
      <data key="d2">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7309</data>
      <data key="d7">c6335fe62c1c4bdc96e7b18467f0ddce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE VEJIGA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de vejiga is a type of bladder cancer that has been studied for its associations with dietary factors, particularly omega-3 intake. Research indicates that higher consumption of red and processed meats, as well as nitrites, is linked to an increased risk of developing c&#225;ncer de vejiga.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7310</data>
      <data key="d7">03a1aca5cb0d432e8fc5899ac8bb662a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREALES INTEGRALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cereales integrales, or whole grains, are a vital source of dietary fiber, vitamins, minerals, and phytochemicals, which contribute to improved health and a reduced risk of various diseases. Their consumption has been linked to a lower risk of colorectal cancer and type 2 diabetes, highlighting their anticancer properties. Whole grains are particularly beneficial for cardiovascular health, as they are associated with a decreased risk of cardiovascular disease and related events. They are also a good source of magnesium, especially when the bran is included.

However, it is important to note that some whole grain cereals can fragment easily, which may pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Additionally, there are concerns regarding the high phosphorus content in certain whole grains, such as brown rice, which can reach up to 40 mg/g. Despite these considerations, the overall health benefits of consuming whole grains are widely recognized, making them a recommended component of a balanced diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164,bd22bf95ac5fc6dc95539efb99c5b11a</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">7311</data>
      <data key="d7">d655ef0a8b424481ae85cf81822a4b05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE VES&#205;CULA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer de ves&#237;cula is a type of cancer that has been associated with dietary habits, including meat consumption.</data>
      <data key="d2">a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
      <data key="d3">1087</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7312</data>
      <data key="d7">be71c2dcc6dc49cdbe625f3412d283f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUECES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nueces, commonly known as walnuts, are a type of nut that is recognized for their numerous health benefits, particularly for cardiovascular health. They are rich in omega-3 fatty acids, magnesium, and iron, containing 2.3 mg of iron per 100 grams. Regular consumption of nueces has been associated with lower blood pressure and a reduced risk of coronary disease. Despite their health benefits, it is important to consume nueces in moderation due to their high caloric content. These nuts are versatile and often used in snacks and various cooking applications, making them a popular choice for those looking to enhance their diet with nutritious options.</data>
      <data key="d2">3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,5e5296bf59e1f2b0fbeace9cc0e62ef5,846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d3">870</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7313</data>
      <data key="d7">3c9190983c8c4f7f8d33cd97b9f27408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER PANCRE&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;ncer pancre&#225;tico, or pancreatic cancer, is a serious type of cancer that has been the subject of various studies exploring its potential links to dietary factors. Research has investigated the relationship between fish consumption and the incidence of pancreatic cancer, although findings may vary. Additionally, the connection between pancreatic cancer and dietary fiber intake, particularly from whole grains, remains inconsistent according to existing studies. This type of cancer is also noted for its impact on patients' metabolic rates, as it can increase resting energy expenditure. Furthermore, it is crucial to consider pancreatic cancer as a possible diagnosis in patients presenting with pancreatitis, especially when the underlying cause is not clearly identified.</data>
      <data key="d2">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417,8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692,d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56</data>
      <data key="d3">1090</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7314</data>
      <data key="d7">79b4c64cb4a64e95bc455cd1951219b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PISTACHOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pistachios are a type of nut that are recognized for their health benefits and nutritional value. They are often recommended as part of a hypocaloric diet due to their low sodium content. Research has shown that pistachios are strongly associated with lower blood pressure, making them a heart-healthy snack option. In terms of nutrition, pistachios provide 7.3 mg of iron per 100 grams, contributing to their status as a nutritious food choice. Additionally, they are commonly consumed as a snack, enjoyed for their unique flavor and texture.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d3">370</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7315</data>
      <data key="d7">909f05b27f3b4b5ca8f64beff743315e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PESCADO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PESCADO refers to fish and seafood, which are highly recommended in dietary guidelines due to their numerous health benefits, particularly in relation to cardiovascular health. Fish is recognized as a significant source of omega-3 fatty acids, essential for overall health and particularly beneficial in children's diets. The consumption of PESCADO has been studied for its positive impacts on various health conditions, including cancer and diabetes. Additionally, PESCADO is permitted in diets prior to medical tests, making it a versatile food choice. It is also important to note that while PESCADO is rich in omega-3 fatty acids and protein, it contains phenylalanine, which should be avoided by individuals with phenylketonuria. Furthermore, PESCADO is utilized in some enteral nutrition products, highlighting its role in dietary formulations aimed at providing essential nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,108b158c33fead285203903273758748,11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a,ede4d21db7723c6b72e8493236b217ad</data>
      <data key="d3">980</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">7316</data>
      <data key="d7">1d1f765468b74a4e835e26b80457a407</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARRITMIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arritmias, or arrhythmias, are irregular heartbeats that can arise as a complication during procedures such as catheter insertion. These conditions represent alterations in the heart's rhythm and can be caused by various issues, including heart problems like cardiopathy related to iron overload. Additionally, it has been suggested that regular consumption of fish oil may help maintain a normal heart rhythm, particularly in cases of atrial fibrillation.</data>
      <data key="d2">3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">980</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7317</data>
      <data key="d7">730455656bd34f9e9a715565695625de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO EICOSAPENTAENOICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA), also known as &#225;CIDO EICOSAPENTAENOICO, is an essential omega-3 fatty acid that offers significant health benefits, particularly for cardiovascular health. It is recognized for its role in reducing inflammation and is often included in various nutritional solutions to support overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7</data>
      <data key="d3">980</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7318</data>
      <data key="d7">c243334db65c48d1962d16c3cf0a089a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO DOCOSAHEXAENOICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cido Docosahexaenoico, commonly known as docosahexaenoic acid (DHA), is an omega-3 fatty acid that plays a crucial role in promoting brain and heart health. It is particularly significant for brain development and function, making it a vital component often included in various nutritional formulations.</data>
      <data key="d2">3dd309c324107af87b7988bd0284892e,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7</data>
      <data key="d3">980</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7319</data>
      <data key="d7">3e86c8cca0974d38b6e2cda53fab05dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTACI&#211;N DE OMEGA-3">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La suplementaci&#243;n de omega-3 se refiere a la ingesta de &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 a trav&#233;s de suplementos, que ha mostrado beneficios modestos en la prevenci&#243;n de arritmias y otros problemas de salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d3">1397</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7320</data>
      <data key="d7">7ff0f8460a0144398b53a902113f84f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARITMIAS VENTRICULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que no parece verse afectada por la suplementaci&#243;n de omega-3, aunque se observa una tendencia beneficiosa en algunos casos.</data>
      <data key="d2">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">7321</data>
      <data key="d7">99791f74c5954126aa31a43a5370ab05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "SUPLEMENTACI&#211;N" encompasses the practice of adding essential nutrients to the diet to enhance health and prevent diseases, particularly for individuals at risk of deficiencies. This process is especially important for patients with specific health conditions, such as those in a chronic state of acidosis, who may benefit from calcium and vitamin D supplementation as part of a ketogenic diet. Additionally, supplementation is crucial for patients with dietary restrictions due to conditions like inflammatory bowel disease (EII) and cystic fibrosis, where tailored nutrient additions, including omega-3 fatty acids, sodium, and fatty acids, are necessary to meet their unique dietary needs. Overall, supplementation plays a vital role in supporting the health of individuals with various medical conditions by ensuring they receive adequate nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d2">06adf563f18feaa5629f0e368a72d227,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728</data>
      <data key="d3">1036</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7322</data>
      <data key="d7">962ad6d0ccc9492caa702f7d917550fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N EN MUJERES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tipo espec&#237;fico de c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n que puede verse influenciado por el consumo de &#225;cidos grasos omega-3, con un posible efecto protector en mujeres.</data>
      <data key="d2">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7323</data>
      <data key="d7">58913dafa6844c93b111331d9f2cb4c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA EN MUJERES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tipo de c&#225;ncer que afecta a las mujeres y que puede ser influenciado por la ingesta de &#225;cidos grasos omega-3, mostrando una reducci&#243;n en el riesgo con la suplementaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
