    </node>
    <node id="BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS, or sugary drinks, are beverages that contain added sugars. They are associated with an increased risk of metabolic and cardiovascular diseases. Dietary recommendations discourage the consumption of sugary drinks to promote better health outcomes. Furthermore, these drinks are highlighted in dietary guidelines, which advise limiting their intake for health reasons.</data>
      <data key="d2">73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">7330</data>
      <data key="d7">9ce2fd9b3bb94dd589de00358151dc47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOCINAS PROINFLAMATORIAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las citocinas proinflamatorias son prote&#237;nas que se producen en respuesta a la inflamaci&#243;n, y su incremento se ha asociado con el consumo de bebidas edulcoradas artificialmente.</data>
      <data key="d2">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7331</data>
      <data key="d7">b079e9983da447cc87fd0c9df7df5718</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORTALIDAD CARDIOVASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MORTALIDAD CARDIOVASCULAR refers to deaths caused by cardiovascular diseases, which encompass a range of heart-related conditions. This type of mortality has been linked to dietary factors, particularly the consumption of salt and trans fats. The relationship between these dietary components and cardiovascular health highlights the significant impact of nutrition on the risk of heart disease and related fatalities.</data>
      <data key="d2">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d3">1881</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7332</data>
      <data key="d7">872ab5b20aa245d1bddb5fc6a5f9d310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRODUCTOS L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PRODUCTOS L&#193;CTEOS refer to a category of food items derived from milk, which includes products such as milk, cheese, yogurt, and butter. These dairy products are recognized as a primary source of essential nutrients, particularly calcium and vitamin D, which are crucial for children's dietary needs and overall health. They play a significant role in helping individuals meet their recommended intakes of these nutrients.

In addition to their nutritional benefits, dairy products have been studied for their effects on blood pressure and are associated with dietary quality and cardiovascular risk reduction. However, it is important to note that dairy products, especially in the European diet, can also be significant sources of saturated fat. Overall, while dairy products offer important health benefits, moderation and balance in consumption are key to maintaining a healthy diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a,62bb1dedc96b7530649f4c9762faab9d,a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,b68dc7398a80c0b67d28b1d9f73ff885,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7333</data>
      <data key="d7">cd7426768bd24d6eb5dea05c4e552a12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA" is a dietary regimen that restricts sodium intake, primarily recommended for patients with specific health conditions such as hypertension. This low-sodium diet aims to control sodium levels in the body, thereby reducing cardiovascular risks and improving arterial health. It is utilized to treat various health conditions by limiting the consumption of sodium, making it an essential dietary approach for individuals needing to manage their sodium intake for better health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b,a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7</data>
      <data key="d3">1575</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">7334</data>
      <data key="d7">637033d18c6a4d339a10694134bf928b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOFERRINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactoferrin is a component of milk that exhibits antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties, potentially inhibiting cell proliferation.</data>
      <data key="d2">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1</data>
      <data key="d3">1081</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7335</data>
      <data key="d7">5ba0a079cbff4669b6b787d017deb58b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNESCO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La UNESCO es la organizaci&#243;n de las Naciones Unidas encargada de promover la educaci&#243;n, la ciencia y la cultura a nivel mundial. En 2010, la UNESCO inscribi&#243; la dieta mediterr&#225;nea en la Lista Representativa del Patrimonio Cultural Inmaterial de la Humanidad, reconociendo su importancia cultural y su contribuci&#243;n a la diversidad cultural global.</data>
      <data key="d2">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7336</data>
      <data key="d7">fe59aeaf986241068ad004ba642a2436</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOSA PLASM&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La glucosa plasm&#225;tica es el nivel de az&#250;car en la sangre, que se ve influenciado por la insulina y la vitamina D, y est&#225; relacionado con el s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico.</data>
      <data key="d2">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7337</data>
      <data key="d7">19c2be810fad42f1b89844f02e259643</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNDACI&#211;N DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fundaci&#243;n Dieta Mediterr&#225;nea is an organization focused on promoting the Mediterranean diet and its health benefits, including cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7338</data>
      <data key="d7">851235a35e784fd08caec30081095c97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO PREDIMED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ESTUDIO PREDIMED" is a multicenter, randomized clinical trial that investigated the effects of the Mediterranean diet on various health outcomes, particularly focusing on cardiovascular health. The study involved over 7,000 adults who were at high risk for cardiovascular disease. It aimed to analyze not only the impact of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular events but also its effects on adiposity and cognitive function. The findings from the study suggest that adherence to the Mediterranean diet is associated with a reduction in cardiovascular events, which may also influence the development of dementia. Overall, the ESTUDIO PREDIMED provides significant insights into the health benefits of the Mediterranean diet, particularly in relation to cardiovascular complications and cognitive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49,c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7339</data>
      <data key="d7">6dfdaf3106ef473094beb08cacfe9670</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMBRES Y MUJERES DE EDAD AVANZADA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Older men and women aged 55 to 80 years with type 2 diabetes and/or multiple cardiovascular risk factors participated in the study.</data>
      <data key="d2">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7340</data>
      <data key="d7">dd8aca34c255488e868279f1146bac37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiovascular complications refer to serious health issues related to the heart and blood vessels, which the Mediterranean diet aims to prevent.</data>
      <data key="d2">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d3">1604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">7341</data>
      <data key="d7">37cd80f36fba4bffb1fadc0eb25639c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXCESO DE PESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Exceso de peso, or overweight, is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease, often linked to dietary habits.</data>
      <data key="d2">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d3">1604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7342</data>
      <data key="d7">5c583d8faaa24d699d966dd33241353a</data>
    </node>
