    <node id="CANCER CAUSES CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer Causes &amp; Control is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to the epidemiology and prevention of cancer. It examines the causes of cancer and the various factors that influence cancer risk. The journal has published significant research, including a meta-analysis on the relationship between red and processed meat intake and the risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma, as well as meta-analyses focusing on colorectal cancer risk factors. Through its publications, Cancer Causes &amp; Control contributes valuable insights into understanding and mitigating cancer risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">3af2658fd59065a71bfee00d2bd27b1b,581527a14dedf97c7a839eff5c40cbc2,cf833689453c8ce13d3650766a8b47a7</data>
