    <node id="ZHANG D">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Zhang D is a prominent researcher who has contributed significantly to the field of nutrition and cancer research. They are a co-author of a meta-analysis examining the relationship between vegetable intake and liver cancer, highlighting the potential protective effects of vegetables against this type of cancer. Additionally, Zhang D has been involved in studying the effects of glutamine on cytokine levels in patients undergoing hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, which is crucial for understanding immune responses in these patients. Furthermore, Zhang D has also conducted a meta-analysis focused on the risks associated with red meat consumption and stomach cancer, providing valuable insights into dietary factors that may influence cancer risk. Through these diverse research efforts, Zhang D has made important contributions to the understanding of dietary impacts on cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">3af2658fd59065a71bfee00d2bd27b1b,42b1be887a83da3e796a9cec7a082b11,581527a14dedf97c7a839eff5c40cbc2</data>
