    <node id="INT J CANCER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "International Journal of Cancer" (Int J Cancer) is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to cancer and its treatment. Among its notable contributions, the journal has published a meta-analysis examining the relationship between the consumption of fruits and vegetables and the risk of developing non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. This highlights the journal's commitment to disseminating significant findings in the field of oncology and public health.</data>
