    <node id="ZHU H">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Zhu H is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of health and nutrition. They examined the antidepressant-like effects of sodium butyrate in combination with estrogen, exploring potential therapeutic avenues for mental health. Additionally, Zhu H conducted a meta-analysis on the relationship between red and processed meat intake and gastric cancer risk, providing valuable insights into dietary impacts on cancer development. Through these studies, Zhu H has contributed significantly to understanding both mental health treatments and dietary influences on cancer risk.</data>
