    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOCELLULAR CARCINOMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatocellular carcinoma is a primary malignancy of the liver and is recognized as a type of liver cancer that frequently arises in patients with liver cirrhosis. This condition is often linked to various dietary and lifestyle factors, which can contribute to its development. Hepatocellular carcinoma is significant in the context of liver diseases, accounting for approximately 30% of deaths related to these conditions, particularly among individuals suffering from liver cirrhosis. Additionally, it is important to consider nutritional support during the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma, as patients may experience increased energy expenditure due to the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271,9ea9816b490492ba0030e6ba4bc3bb9f,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe</data>
      <data key="d3">1513</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7544</data>
      <data key="d7">3fbc973b0cd84b49bc89b7611f0dc13b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LUNG CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lung cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lungs, with research exploring its links to meat consumption.</data>
