    </node>
    <node id="BREAST CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Breast cancer is a type of cancer that develops from breast tissue. It is a significant area of study, particularly concerning its risk factors, which include various dietary intakes. Numerous studies have been conducted to examine the relationship between dietary factors and the risk of developing breast cancer, highlighting the importance of nutrition in understanding this disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
      <data key="d3">1652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7546</data>
      <data key="d7">7c2ec10474504c369093a748b6329753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OVARIAN CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ovarian cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the ovaries. Research has been conducted to explore various dietary factors that may influence the risk of developing this disease. Specifically, studies have examined the association between meat consumption and ovarian cancer, as well as the impact of fish intake on its risk. These investigations aim to better understand how different dietary habits may contribute to the development of ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe</data>
      <data key="d3">364</data>
