    <node id="COLORECTAL CANCER">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the colon or rectum. Research has indicated a potential link between dietary factors and the risk of developing this disease. Specifically, studies suggest that higher intake of dietary fiber may reduce the risk of colorectal cancer. Additionally, various studies have explored the relationship between fish consumption and the risk of this type of cancer, highlighting the importance of diet in influencing colorectal cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,d0b74d75847bdd3e0d4962e7cc2ca5fe,f8c0a9f795e94be1048ffba0007831de</data>
