    <node id="NUTRITION CANCER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition Cancer is a journal dedicated to exploring the intricate relationship between nutrition and cancer. It publishes a wide range of research, including studies that examine the impact of dietary factors, such as dairy products, on cancer risk. The journal also focuses on dietary interventions specifically designed for cancer patients, providing insights into how nutrition can influence cancer outcomes. Additionally, Nutrition Cancer features meta-analyses that synthesize existing research on dietary factors and their association with cancer risk, contributing to a deeper understanding of how nutrition can affect cancer prevention and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7,e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
