    <node id="EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Journal of Clinical Nutrition (Eur J Clin Nutr) is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of nutrition and its impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including inter-observer variability in body composition measurement, cancer risk studies, and the implications of clinical nutrition for health and disease. The journal also focuses on specific issues such as sarcopenia and its effects on the elderly, as well as studies and guidelines related to the management of eating disorders. Through its comprehensive research publications, the European Journal of Clinical Nutrition aims to advance the understanding of nutrition and its critical role in health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0692eb750371d46b9fff71ec305df6ce,22f9164844b9778cfef429e45de95060,933cfaece6287ed7626c5216a1e5c54d,97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4</data>
