    <node id="GASTRIC CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastric cancer is a type of cancer that affects the stomach and is the focus of extensive research and clinical studies. It is associated with various complications, including chyloperitoneum, and often necessitates nutritional assessment and support for affected patients. The journal "Gastric Cancer" publishes research specifically dedicated to this disease, covering a wide range of topics such as surgical outcomes, treatment strategies, and nutritional guidelines for patient care. Additionally, studies have explored the influence of dietary factors, including salt intake and fish consumption, on the risk of developing gastric cancer. Overall, gastric cancer remains a significant area of study, with ongoing research aimed at improving patient outcomes and understanding the disease's complexities.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,3f1d1c7c7c62b83f62f6fa31c25f65b2,6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,c3c8c4edabc77ed1f0a834676de2939c,fba8cc8092875a542f3b63663ce5c8d9</data>
