    <node id="ESOPHAGEAL CANCER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer that affects the esophagus, the tube responsible for carrying food from the throat to the stomach. This condition is the focus of numerous studies that investigate various aspects, including nutritional support, treatment options, and surgical outcomes. Research has highlighted the significant weight loss and nutritional challenges faced by patients with esophageal cancer, prompting investigations into dietary influences, such as the impact of fish consumption on the disease. Overall, esophageal cancer presents complex challenges that are being actively studied to improve patient care and outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">758bc764453f49b9097073c5175470cc,97c27548ceb554d425303875efc5f9b4,bef1f848ac9b922f7361b740210a8314,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7</data>
