    <node id="BRITISH JOURNAL OF NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The British Journal of Nutrition is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on nutrition and its significant impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including the effects of dietary fats on health, the relationship between nutrition and various health conditions, and the implications of nutritional status for health outcomes. The journal features studies on specific populations, such as stroke patients and individuals with liver cirrhosis, as well as broader research on energy expenditure and other nutritional factors. Overall, the British Journal of Nutrition serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge in the field of nutrition and its effects on health.</data>
