    <node id="DASH DIET">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The DASH diet, or Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension, is a comprehensive dietary plan designed to help treat and prevent high blood pressure (hypertension). It emphasizes the consumption of fruits, vegetables, and low saturated fat intake, promoting specific food patterns and nutrient intake that contribute to improved cardiovascular health. The diet has been studied for its effects on urine composition and the risk of kidney stones, highlighting its focus on magnesium-rich foods, which can help reduce the saturation of calcium oxalate. Overall, the DASH diet aims to reduce hypertension and its associated health risks while also decreasing the incidence of kidney stones through its nutrient-rich food recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b79601d85087d62f0d4890761776c04,550574bce077f34348bd11c78dc814a1,57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7,f757219e84dba985f7c8d66ac951b9f2</data>
      <data key="d3">1634</data>
