    <node id="NATIONAL INSTITUTES OF HEALTH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Institutes of Health (NIH) is a key agency within the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, serving as the primary entity for conducting and supporting medical research. It is responsible for advancing biomedical and public health research, and it also sponsors various projects related to dietary evaluation technology. As the nation's medical research agency, the NIH plays a crucial role in improving health outcomes through its extensive research initiatives and funding programs.</data>
