      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An organization that represents health product manufacturers in Europe, involved in setting nutritional standards.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1556</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7779</data>
      <data key="d7">17cce0eec83e4ebdb253a7eef179ceeb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN RESPONSIBLE NUTRITION ALLIANCE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An alliance focused on promoting responsible nutrition practices in Europe.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1556</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7780</data>
      <data key="d7">e9e6722372574c70b9104838afea7584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NAP.EDU">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A website that provides access to research and publications related to nutrition and health.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1556</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7781</data>
      <data key="d7">ff9f6caf178441f8836287bdd231491f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RIESGO refers to the risk associated with inadequate or excessive nutrient intake as defined in dietary guidelines. Additionally, it encompasses risk management in healthcare, which involves identifying, analyzing, and mitigating potential risks to patient health. This dual focus highlights the importance of both nutritional balance and proactive healthcare strategies in minimizing health-related risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">07e45dae0f017eba9ef9f48439de5c59,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">43</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7782</data>
      <data key="d7">c57c9aec7713406d822f6fd4744326ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA &#211;PTIMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The optimal intake levels of nutrients as recommended by health organizations.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">43</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7783</data>
      <data key="d7">56562eebe4c1447d9bdda3d0d65f95cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE INGESTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The level of nutrient intake that is considered safe or adequate according to dietary guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">43</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7784</data>
      <data key="d7">5e5c026eb50344ceab348fac13dcb56b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DRI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary Reference Intakes (DRI) are a set of reference values designed to plan and assess nutrient intakes for healthy individuals. These guidelines encompass recommendations for nutrient intake aimed at promoting health and preventing chronic diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7785</data>
      <data key="d7">012b5c41457246a29ac35133e3b79c06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">RDA, which stands for Recommended Dietary Allowance, refers to the daily intake levels of essential nutrients that are recommended to maintain health. The RDA represents the average daily level of intake sufficient to meet the nutrient requirements of nearly all (97-98%) healthy individuals. These guidelines are established to prevent nutrient deficiencies and ensure that individuals consume adequate amounts of nutrients necessary for optimal health. In Spanish, RDA is referred to as "Recomendaciones Diarias de Ingesta," emphasizing the importance of these recommendations in daily dietary practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912,d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">7786</data>
      <data key="d7">4bb395d5e57349fb99473d124219d4e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL) refers to the maximum daily intake of a nutrient that is unlikely to cause adverse health effects in the general population. This concept is crucial for understanding safe consumption levels of various nutrients, as exceeding the UL may lead to negative health outcomes. The term UL is consistently used to denote these maximum intake levels, emphasizing the importance of adhering to these guidelines to maintain health and prevent toxicity.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7787</data>
      <data key="d7">aa565d09d8da4a829e4d0cc63d444f43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "EAR" stands for Estimated Average Requirement, which is a key measure used in dietary guidelines. It refers to the daily intake value that is estimated to meet the nutritional requirements of half the healthy individuals within a specific life stage and gender group. The Estimated Average Requirements (EAR) represent the average daily nutrient intake levels that are calculated to satisfy the needs of this demographic, ensuring that dietary recommendations are tailored to support the health of various populations effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7788</data>
      <data key="d7">244f8d6c95794a1d88f0c3a8506704f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NOAEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">No Observed Adverse Effect Level (NOAEL) is the highest experimental dose that does not cause a significant increase in adverse effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7789</data>
      <data key="d7">fc82c04aa57149f5b273342fee4eadff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOAEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lowest Observed Adverse Effect Level (LOAEL) is the lowest experimental dose that causes a significant increase in adverse effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7790</data>
      <data key="d7">f6877c1009fb43768eb40f74cae8563e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA INSUFICIENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insufficient intake refers to the consumption of nutrients below the recommended levels, leading to potential health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">7791</data>
      <data key="d7">c40830656fd54e65b6f8e9216664e44a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA EXCESIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Excessive intake refers to the consumption of nutrients above the recommended levels, which can lead to adverse health effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">7792</data>
      <data key="d7">ad26b287cbc94ccea376c07feb7ba27a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EFECTOS ADVERSOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adverse effects are negative health outcomes resulting from inadequate or excessive nutrient intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">d091ddf14a273c8981b300afdea77912</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7793</data>
      <data key="d7">d7251e96dc7f4c21a40f61e96dc39422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union of member states primarily located in Europe. It plays a significant role in regulating food standards, including those specifically for athlete-targeted products. Additionally, the EU provides dietary recommendations for sodium intake and is actively working on harmonizing food labeling legislation across its member states.</data>
      <data key="d2">54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,7ff62e1dc423be2f4b2fe08546751d0d,88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95</data>
      <data key="d3">1561</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7794</data>
      <data key="d7">9dd3ed36765b45198e94ba7fb71f57ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adequate Intake (AI) is a recommended intake level based on observed or experimentally determined estimates of nutrient intake by a group of healthy people.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95</data>
      <data key="d3">1558</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7795</data>
      <data key="d7">f5eaf0bd5b66471dad99bebb14b29722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRIENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrients are substances that provide nourishment essential for the maintenance of life and for growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95</data>
      <data key="d3">1565</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7796</data>
      <data key="d7">c8038e9451504816807f06fe5c2d0b90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOOD LABELING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Food labeling refers to the information provided on food packaging that informs consumers about the nutritional content and ingredients.</data>
      <data key="d2">88d6f98c356e5a49db38ab5aa960bb95</data>
      <data key="d3">1581</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7797</data>
      <data key="d7">914148b2bbbd444fa656dcba128d5679</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SENC, or the Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Nutrici&#243;n Comunitaria, is a scientific organization dedicated to the development of nutritional recommendations and dietary guidelines for the general population. From 2000 to 2016, SENC focused on creating comprehensive nutritional advice, which includes the adaptation of the healthy eating pyramid in 2015. Additionally, SENC places a particular emphasis on providing dietary recommendations for pediatric patients, ensuring that nutritional guidance is tailored to the needs of younger demographics. Overall, SENC plays a crucial role in promoting community nutrition in Spain through its evidence-based guidelines and recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">6907c82f1f024ed1b75f6aea88c47b3e,72ed1fffc10ea163a92b5f1a7b972732,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,f96dd2fbe3cd9aa6516522de8ed33145</data>
      <data key="d3">1552</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7798</data>
      <data key="d7">5117e7d530ad4cf7a1c0929af3f156c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EURODIET">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">EURODIET is a dietary guideline initiative established in 2000 that aims to provide comprehensive recommendations on nutrition across Europe. The project focuses on creating dietary guidelines that incorporate proposals from various European countries, ensuring that the recommendations are relevant and applicable to diverse populations within the region. Through its efforts, EURODIET seeks to promote better nutritional practices and improve public health across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1552</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7799</data>
      <data key="d7">00cbb2b6377a4b0baec06bd6c79f5545</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The NAS, or National Academy of Sciences, is a private, nonprofit institution comprised of distinguished scholars dedicated to scientific and engineering research. Established to provide expert advice on various scientific and technical issues, the NAS plays a significant role in formulating dietary guidelines. In 2002, the NAS published dietary recommendations that include the definition of the Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) for carbohydrates. Additionally, the NAS proposes formulas for calculating estimated energy requirements tailored to different age groups, further contributing to the understanding of nutritional needs across the lifespan.</data>
      <data key="d2">018644ab78da6f804c57546f08ff6a65,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,7ff62e1dc423be2f4b2fe08546751d0d,bd31c6face847551241359e37e4baa2e,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">619</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">7800</data>
      <data key="d7">7a7c26a70f14413bbe171b77991def65</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POBLACI&#211;N GENERAL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The general population refers to the collective group of individuals for whom the nutritional recommendations are intended.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1552</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">7801</data>
      <data key="d7">e4d563b8cd0b45ce90b3293f3b2c16d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJERCICIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EJERCICIO refers to any bodily movement that consumes energy, which is essential for health and the performance of athletes. It encompasses physical activity that is planned, structured, and repetitive, aimed at improving or maintaining physical fitness. This dual perspective highlights the importance of exercise not only as a means of enhancing athletic performance but also as a crucial component of overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab9a942f3aa9ca3eb88bcd26fcd60ddb,c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1742</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7802</data>
      <data key="d7">1b1215eef48b44a2a180dec3389f93f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REQUERIMIENTOS ENERG&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"REQUERIMIENTOS ENERG&#201;TICOS" refers to the dietary intake of energy necessary to maintain energy balance in healthy individuals. This concept encompasses the caloric needs for both adults and children, with specific guidelines tailored to different age groups and activity levels. For adults, energy requirements are focused on maintaining overall health, while for children, these requirements are adjusted according to their developmental needs and physical activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d3">675</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7803</data>
      <data key="d7">6cc23eca18e0401683ac17f9b007138a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EFECTO TERMOG&#201;NICO DE LOS ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The thermic effect of food refers to the increase in metabolic rate after ingestion of a meal, accounting for approximately 10% of total energy consumed.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">676</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7804</data>
      <data key="d7">2ab25eafd5f9441fb7499e5b0fdb608b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE ACTIVIDAD F&#205;SICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Physical activity levels are defined as the ratio of total energy expenditure to basal energy expenditure, indicating the level of physical activity of an individual.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1537</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7805</data>
      <data key="d7">d4138be43582436bbbb9b7185a291622</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PAL, which stands for Physical Activity Level, is a measure utilized to categorize energy requirements based on the intensity of physical activity. It serves as an assessment tool for evaluating an individual's energy expenditure in relation to their activity level.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2a8dd9d28d1992a73de2834131b69c9,c567251c335f000303144ce3d7e1d638</data>
      <data key="d3">1537</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7806</data>
      <data key="d7">b44385374e9e48059c1be62f83fd45f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Academy of Sciences (NAS) is a United States nonprofit organization dedicated to providing expert advice on scientific and technical issues. It serves as a private, non-profit society composed of distinguished scholars who are actively engaged in scientific and engineering research. In addition to offering guidance on a wide range of scientific matters, the NAS conducts studies specifically related to health and nutrition, further emphasizing its commitment to addressing critical scientific challenges and informing public policy.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2</data>
      <data key="d3">1545</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7807</data>
      <data key="d7">e9b399ceb9f449e4b81f0afe31ba353e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOMEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Women are a demographic group referenced in dietary guidelines, which often include specific nutritional recommendations tailored to their needs. Additionally, in a particular study involving women, some participants faced challenges in performing the grip strength test due to difficulties with the dynamometer. This highlights the importance of considering the unique circumstances and requirements of women in both nutritional and physical assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2,f9951c9666473dd8daea6c3f2bcf9a8e</data>
      <data key="d3">1538</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7808</data>
      <data key="d7">350784a85d0b47c4a76fbf57d84cfc37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUGARS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sugars are a type of carbohydrate that should be limited in the diet according to health guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2</data>
      <data key="d3">1248</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7809</data>
      <data key="d7">2989d31a48a94bd9a973fcdabf304ab4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHYSICAL ACTIVITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Physical activity refers to bodily movement that expends energy and plays a crucial role in overall health. It has been observed that physical activity levels have decreased in the population, contributing to rising obesity rates. Additionally, physical activity is a significant lifestyle factor that influences the prevalence and progression of conditions such as sarcopenia and frailty. Health guidelines recommend a minimum amount of daily exercise to promote well-being and mitigate these health issues. Overall, engaging in regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">20863ac06779722abc2cbc2dd023777e,a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642,e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2</data>
      <data key="d3">996</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7810</data>
      <data key="d7">faa49ae6bb4d46099b4c8d09e48dc955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIETY OF SPANISH COMMUNITY NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Nutrici&#243;n Comunitaria (SENC) is an organization focused on community nutrition in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d3">1552</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7811</data>
      <data key="d7">f06a99f49013482b92ed2c3accc7b786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS, or saturated fatty acids, are a type of fat that can significantly impact cholesterol levels and are often compared to unsaturated fats in dietary studies. These fats are typically recommended to be limited in a healthy diet due to their association with cardiovascular health. It is particularly important to restrict the intake of saturated fatty acids in children's diets to promote heart health. Additionally, &#193;CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS are included in nutritional information and are frequently evaluated in dietary research for their effects on health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0090177678aee58d08471d09d24d2842,06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,148443357888793655b663333268775a,76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1</data>
      <data key="d3">1576</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">7812</data>
      <data key="d7">5a93578110c94b70b8fea8790564838c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APORTES DIET&#201;TICOS RECOMENDADOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary Reference Intakes (DRIs) are a set of reference values used to plan and assess nutrient intakes.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d3">1545</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7813</data>
      <data key="d7">d86f089541de418aa5d3aeb8a95c020e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMENDACIONES DE 2015 SOBRE AZ&#218;CARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The 2015 recommendations on sugar intake provide guidelines for adults and children regarding sugar consumption.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d3">1552</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7814</data>
      <data key="d7">5dc8b3ab328f499caa7337653b96d294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA ADECUADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">INGESTA ADECUADA refers to the recommended intake levels of various nutrients, specifically tailored for children. This concept encompasses adequate intake, which is defined as a recommended intake level of a nutrient based on observed or experimentally determined estimates of nutrient intake by a group of healthy individuals. Thus, INGESTA ADECUADA serves as a guideline to ensure that children receive the necessary nutrients for their growth and development, based on established dietary recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">7815</data>
      <data key="d7">66a58dd5bf2948b08413173677947f72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBRA TOTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Total fiber is the sum of dietary fiber and functional fiber, which is important for digestive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d3">1546</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7816</data>
      <data key="d7">2d3aae292da741a7a6cf412c81e87d21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA DE EPA + DHA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The intake of EPA (Eicosapentaenoic acid) and DHA (Docosahexaenoic acid) is recommended for cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416</data>
      <data key="d3">1544</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7817</data>
