    <node id="VARONES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The entity "VARONES" refers to a demographic group of males, which, despite being less studied than their female counterparts, also faces a significant risk of developing eating disorders, with a prevalence ratio of 9:1 compared to women. This group is categorized by age for health and demographic statistics, specifically including males aged 19-30 years, 31-50 years, 51-70 years, and those over 70 years. Additionally, males aged 20 years and older are considered for dietary intake recommendations. The data also indicates that these males participated in a study focused on measuring grip strength, highlighting their involvement in health-related assessments. Overall, "VARONES" encompasses a diverse range of males with varying health metrics and dietary needs, underscoring the importance of addressing their specific health risks and requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457,4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,6c65beaf6ed5575b0945052270630136,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,a2675f78609440ca1162c24997360929,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,f9951c9666473dd8daea6c3f2bcf9a8e</data>
