    <node id="AGENCIA ESPA&#209;OLA DE CONSUMO, SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The AGENCIA ESPA&#209;OLA DE CONSUMO, SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA Y NUTRICI&#211;N, also known as the Spanish Agency for Consumer Affairs, Food Safety and Nutrition (AECOSAN), is tasked with the critical role of ensuring food safety and consumer protection throughout Spain. This agency is dedicated to safeguarding the health and rights of consumers by overseeing food safety standards and implementing regulations that protect public health.</data>
      <data key="d2">c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,e0102bb655b6476ce3296726e3aceb4a</data>
      <data key="d3">1585</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7848</data>
      <data key="d7">8cae848a025d406cb17c3e7c96081e48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOS GRASOS TRANS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACIDOS GRASOS TRANS, or trans fatty acids, are a type of unsaturated fat that have been linked to several health risks, notably cardiovascular disease and diabetes. These unhealthy fats are particularly detrimental for individuals with diabetes, as they can negatively impact cholesterol levels. It is recommended that trans fatty acids be avoided in the diet to promote better health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,f558c372d16630f14b614e232fc151de</data>
      <data key="d3">875</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">7849</data>
      <data key="d7">87526d03af9a42dabfbc2e0845692a51</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORTALIDAD TOTAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">MORTALIDAD TOTAL refers to the overall death rate within a population. This metric can be influenced by various factors, including dietary habits and health conditions, which play a significant role in determining the mortality outcomes in a given demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">c83e630c61a82784e0597259d89b96ea,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc</data>
      <data key="d3">875</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7850</data>
      <data key="d7">ad2d92f79e43421a9bb5eb020f6b0ed4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FESNAD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FESNAD, or the Spanish Federation of Nutrition and Dietetics, is an organization dedicated to promoting nutrition and dietary practices in Spain. It provides dietary reference intakes specifically tailored for the Spanish population, ensuring that nutritional guidelines are relevant and applicable to local dietary habits. Additionally, FESNAD plays a crucial role in establishing guidelines on the consumption of fats and oils in the diet, particularly for the adult Spanish population. This initiative is encapsulated in the Spanish Consensus on Fats and Oils in the Diet, which is actively promoted by FESNAD to enhance public understanding and adherence to healthy dietary practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127,f2b8b21255397ebbaf2b5d66ff6bde88</data>
      <data key="d3">1686</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">7851</data>
      <data key="d7">60a1f02abebf44c9a364e60e24add121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEPREM-HG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GEPREM-Hg refers to a study group dedicated to the prevention of methylmercury exposure in the Spanish population. This group has developed recommendations regarding fish consumption, which are based on the tolerable weekly intake of methylmercury established by the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA). GEPREM-Hg has created a consensus document that outlines specific consumption recommendations tailored to various factors such as age, weight, type of fish, and the possibility of pregnancy, aiming to minimize the risks associated with methylmercury exposure.</data>
      <data key="d2">018644ab78da6f804c57546f08ff6a65,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,8778654a17a48b8ea7b1cec378d52346</data>
      <data key="d3">1685</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">7852</data>
      <data key="d7">022bec95526f49038656e9a60838e8e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="USDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) is a government agency that plays a crucial role in promoting public health through its dietary guidelines for Americans. These guidelines include specific recommendations on cholesterol consumption, aiming to educate the public on healthy eating habits. Additionally, the USDA provides a comprehensive database of food composition and dietary surveys, which serves as a valuable resource for understanding nutritional data. To further assist families in making healthy food choices, the USDA created the "My Plate" nutritional guide, which is designed to help parents feed their children nutritious meals. Overall, the USDA is dedicated to enhancing the nutritional well-being of the American population through its various initiatives and resources.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,6da89a24c60015649c1d669e4e23fb2d,87cb06eed8a8c92c589d25ea2d5cfaec</data>
      <data key="d3">1547</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7853</data>
      <data key="d7">4febdbdf4d744bce8aaab5ddb83af8d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METILMERCURIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Methylmercury is a contaminant commonly found in fish, recognized for its potential adverse health effects. It is a toxic compound that poses significant risks, especially to vulnerable populations such as pregnant women and young children. Due to these health concerns, there are specific consumption recommendations in place to mitigate exposure to methylmercury.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1685</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">7854</data>
      <data key="d7">7d5c7e0196154ddfa7004efc306dfad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLESTEROL DIET&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Colesterol diet&#233;tico refers to dietary cholesterol obtained from animal foods, which plays a role in cardiovascular health. While it is a nutrient that can impact health, both the American Heart Association and the USDA suggest that dietary cholesterol does not require restriction in a healthy diet. This indicates that, for most individuals, moderate consumption of dietary cholesterol from animal sources can be part of a balanced diet without significant health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1544</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7855</data>
      <data key="d7">6067b2980f3c466b83025cb5a318bff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS TRANS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">&#193;CIDOS GRASOS TRANS, or trans fatty acids, are a type of fatty acid characterized by their strong positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis. These fats are isomers derived from unsaturated fatty acids, primarily produced during the hydrogenation process, which is commonly used in the production of margarine. Due to their adverse effects on cardiovascular health, nutritional guidelines recommend limiting the intake of trans fatty acids in the diet. Furthermore, it is particularly important to restrict these unhealthy fats in children's diets to prevent potential health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,1ad5b4d7f49ca2d3d44adc99227f07d8,3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2,59a6475dbe0ccafda60f2647dea78371,76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
      <data key="d3">1649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7856</data>
      <data key="d7">1aac9402136a4a68b2810d31b24bcc6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUGAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sugar refers to sweet, short-chain carbohydrates that are used in food and beverages, with guidelines suggesting limits on their intake for health reasons.</data>
      <data key="d2">018644ab78da6f804c57546f08ff6a65</data>
