    <node id="EUROPEAN FOOD SAFETY AUTHORITY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) is an agency that plays a crucial role in evaluating scientific evidence related to food safety and nutrition within the European Union. It provides independent scientific advice on food-related risks, including the assessment of food additives and the establishment of acceptable daily intake levels. EFSA is also involved in communicating both existing and emerging food safety issues to ensure public health. Notably, the agency has conducted studies on the effects of creatine supplementation on muscle strength, particularly in older adults, and has examined the relationship between creatine and resistance training. Through its comprehensive evaluations and guidance, EFSA aims to safeguard food safety and promote informed decision-making regarding nutrition in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d2">06a75d9ed2fc1cdca5b08759d3df04d4,34f5f2681b28d568aea92e2633ebae56,6907c82f1f024ed1b75f6aea88c47b3e,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611,e0102bb655b6476ce3296726e3aceb4a,edc9ccbe5d98671343d0119a309cddaf</data>
