    </node>
    <node id="PREDIMED STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The PREDIMED Study, which stands for PREvenci&#243;n con DIeta MEDiterr&#225;nea, is a comprehensive research initiative aimed at the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease through the adoption of a Mediterranean diet. This study investigates the various benefits of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular health, focusing on its effects on mortality, particularly in populations with high fish consumption. Additionally, the PREDIMED Study examines the impact of dietary alpha-linolenic acid and marine omega-3 fatty acids, further contributing to the understanding of how specific dietary components can influence cardiovascular outcomes. Overall, the PREDIMED Study plays a crucial role in exploring the relationship between diet and heart health, emphasizing the importance of the Mediterranean dietary pattern.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e153f7c5e2fcd13d3bf7a99298834e,8778654a17a48b8ea7b1cec378d52346,89ca65c4bdc30027c9c9ed1e1b442939,dbdb3cd3b9065e8846fd2eb15b9d5879,ea8be3e3b3d7195ddc85512be460b6f8</data>
