      <data key="d6">7933</data>
      <data key="d7">d03a7c5a0fda4e39b061d333b15b90ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALLETA MARIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Galleta Maria is a type of biscuit made primarily from wheat flour, sugar, and palm fat, with various nutritional components and ingredients listed for consumer information.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c</data>
      <data key="d3">375</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">7934</data>
      <data key="d7">055b19b90ede40eba40467b379017b24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIGO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TRIGO, or wheat, is a cereal grain that is widely consumed around the world and serves as a primary source of gluten. It is important to note that wheat must be excluded from the diets of patients with celiac disease due to its gluten content. Additionally, wheat can contain fructans, which may lead to symptoms in individuals who are sensitive to FODMAPs. In culinary applications, wheat is a key ingredient in products such as Galleta Maria, where it contributes to both the structure and nutritional value of the food. Furthermore, wheat is recognized as a major source of fructans in Western diets, playing a significant role in the intake of these carbohydrates.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">7935</data>
      <data key="d7">a2fd5e72a5104441b1069f65661f80e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PALMA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Palma refers to palm fat, an ingredient in Galleta Maria that contributes to its texture and flavor.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c</data>
