    </node>
    <node id="COMPOSICI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Composici&#243;n nutricional refers to the detailed breakdown of nutrients in Galleta Maria, including calories, fats, carbohydrates, and proteins.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c</data>
      <data key="d3">375</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7938</data>
      <data key="d7">520ce257f22c43bf859888831173d92f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FRUCTOSA, also known as fructose, is a simple sugar that is naturally found in many fruits and plants, contributing to their sweetness. It is sweeter than glucose and is often used in various food products, which can lead to increased consumption. While FRUCTOSA is absorbed more slowly than glucose, it can significantly affect uric acid metabolism, potentially leading to increased levels of hyperuricemia. 

In dietary contexts, FRUCTOSA is important to consider for individuals managing diabetes, as it can affect blood sugar levels. It is also noted that FRUCTOSA does not alleviate hypoglycemia in individuals with glycogen storage disease type I and may worsen acidosis. Additionally, some individuals may experience hereditary intolerance to FRUCTOSA due to a lack of the enzyme necessary for its metabolism, which can result in gastrointestinal symptoms similar to lactose malabsorption.

FRUCTOSA is included in products like Galleta Maria, enhancing their flavor profile. However, its consumption should be moderated, especially in children with glycogen storage disease type I, as excessive intake can lead to malabsorption issues and gastrointestinal discomfort. Overall, while FRUCTOSA is a common and naturally occurring sugar, its effects on health and metabolism warrant careful consideration in dietary practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,39a7166ca777be46a1613c54a746e2b8,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f,ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611,cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160,d028f23d86d7ed32eebe35c5d90765f2,e0a2b5f5d5b3682c870f787f54f6b5ef,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">863</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
