      <data key="d6">7939</data>
      <data key="d7">b66d37071c0745acbc6e9572e13a166c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TABLA 3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tabla 3" serves as a comprehensive resource that encompasses various aspects of nutrition and dietary assessment. It outlines the reference intake of vitamins and minerals for adults, providing essential guidelines for nutritional adequacy. Additionally, it presents commercial combinations of nitrogen and glucose solutions specifically designed for hypocaloric peripheral parenteral nutrition, which is crucial for patients requiring specialized dietary support.

Furthermore, "Tabla 3" includes a nutritional assessment based on weight loss percentages over time, allowing for the evaluation of dietary effectiveness and health outcomes. It also details the content of phenylalanine in various foods per 100 grams, which is particularly relevant for individuals managing specific dietary restrictions.

The table features data from a population study focusing on body mass index (IMC) among men and women aged 45 to 60 years, contributing to a better understanding of nutritional status within this demographic. In addition, "Tabla 3" outlines clinical parameters for monitoring patients receiving parenteral nutrition, ensuring that healthcare providers can effectively track patient progress and nutritional needs.

Moreover, it highlights the main problems encountered when analyzing dietary intake records, which is vital for improving dietary assessments and interventions. Lastly, "Tabla 3" addresses the negative aspects that powdered ingredients may exhibit when in contact with water, emphasizing the importance of formulation stability in nutritional products. Overall, "Tabla 3" is a multifaceted tool that integrates various nutritional data and considerations for both clinical and dietary applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2bd5549759c6a0d8393bb93fdccb747b,3d73ef14929e7391e915f739189e4dfa,45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,a4d8922d5e65304a84f8a61999f77933,b68bac9cb298a49d19de8db2a2b640a1,b90cbe653c368699b01ffc6af8d00221,cb8368db73f739b1f11f2a202c776e6d</data>
