      <data key="d7">6fb9384d1ad946429ce59631881b898b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEL&#205;ACOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Las personas cel&#237;acas son aquellas que tienen intolerancia al gluten y requieren productos espec&#237;ficos para su dieta.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d3">830</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">7953</data>
      <data key="d7">08f473b432ad46b8b5db5287cc5e5d03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GLUTEN is a protein found in wheat and related grains, including certain cereals. It plays a crucial role in the elasticity of dough, making it important in baking and food production. However, gluten can cause adverse reactions in individuals with celiac disease, a condition that necessitates the complete elimination of gluten from their diet to avoid serious health complications. Additionally, gluten can trigger reactions in those with gluten sensitivity. The certification process for gluten-free products is heavily influenced by the presence of gluten, ensuring that these products meet safety standards for those affected. Recent recommendations from the European Society for Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition (ESPGHAN) have also addressed the introduction of gluten into the diets of infants, indicating that guidelines on the timing of gluten introduction have been updated.</data>
      <data key="d2">1aab735899b0c557ec11da0558bcfc15,1d8aa686c6377246fee05010ef969018,281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,39a7166ca777be46a1613c54a746e2b8,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,7d6ee23789bfcf1d419eafb56a6d064f,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566,a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4,dfb6e1826ded0b8ca7cf3304d1b75d1a,e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c,e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d6">7954</data>
      <data key="d7">22fec0ac1a0f4a87bf430f5c02b57ce6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DECLARACIONES NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las declaraciones nutricionales son afirmaciones que sugieren que un alimento tiene propiedades beneficiosas espec&#237;ficas debido a su composici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7955</data>
      <data key="d7">4ebc969d8a2f4c499c9510cd9f2de9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DECLARACIONES DE PROPIEDADES SALUDABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las declaraciones de propiedades saludables afirman o sugieren una relaci&#243;n entre un alimento y la salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7956</data>
      <data key="d7">4a660ecedf314adc8adfce47cfdc2d14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DECLARACIONES DE REDUCCI&#211;N DE RIESGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las declaraciones de reducci&#243;n de riesgo afirman que el consumo de un alimento puede reducir significativamente un factor de riesgo de aparici&#243;n de una enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">7957</data>
