    </node>
    <node id="MEDIDAS ANTROPOM&#201;TRICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las medidas antropom&#233;tricas son datos que se recogen para evaluar el estado nutricional de un individuo.</data>
      <data key="d2">fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1434</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8032</data>
      <data key="d7">a9125bb34e444ea1a3517f6a65f2d404</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DATOS SOCIALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los datos sociales, como econ&#243;micos y laborales, son relevantes en la valoraci&#243;n nutricional de un paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d3">1434</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8033</data>
      <data key="d7">25ef346110f6416a8630ea0cd3441dec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL DATA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical data refers to the medical information collected about a patient, including recent weight loss, mental state, and systemic diseases that may interfere with nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">739</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">8034</data>
      <data key="d7">3158a5849dbe438b8edd6e26fceb5947</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIAL HISTORY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Social history encompasses the socioeconomic factors affecting a patient's health, such as income level, education, physical activity, and cultural practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8035</data>
      <data key="d7">a7267686513640e298e65e4ae0a29b48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTHROPOMETRIC MEASUREMENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anthropometric measurements are non-invasive assessments used to evaluate a patient's body composition and nutritional status, including weight, height, and body mass index.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8036</data>
      <data key="d7">d2e3769e24884c4a8cf4d10772856ea3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHYSICAL EXAMINATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Physical examination is a thorough assessment of a patient's physical condition, particularly in cases of malnutrition, to identify signs and symptoms related to nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8037</data>
      <data key="d7">cc932ceb9b504271a376ff72049823c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENTAL STATE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mental state refers to the psychological condition of a patient, which can impact their nutritional intake and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">739</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8038</data>
      <data key="d7">1d8c87d6e7a545419c0177c1050c280f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYSTEMIC DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Systemic diseases are health conditions that can interfere with a patient's ability to maintain proper nutrition, such as cancer or organ failures.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">739</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8039</data>
      <data key="d7">8e0bd3ef246c4274a20700896b3e19d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOXIC CONSUMPTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Toxic consumption includes the intake of harmful substances like alcohol or drugs, which can adversely affect nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b5b30d7b9371f8fe9e686c89dde3cb7</data>
      <data key="d3">739</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
