    <node id="COSTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COSTE refers to the financial expenditure associated with healthcare interventions, which is a critical factor in analyses of cost-effectiveness and cost-utility. Additionally, COSTE encompasses the costs associated with various dietary assessment methods. This dual focus highlights the importance of understanding both healthcare and dietary costs in evaluating overall health interventions and their economic implications.</data>
