    </node>
    <node id="ENCUESTA DE ADHERENCIA A LA DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Encuesta de Adherencia a la Dieta Mediterr&#225;nea is a survey designed to assess adherence to the Mediterranean diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">f14ec70726a24a574ae5d437903fddb8</data>
      <data key="d3">1445</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8161</data>
      <data key="d7">0c35b3f73da84c4389e4c7c57c126021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRIENTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRIENTE refers to the nutrients that are investigated in dietary studies to understand their impact on health.</data>
      <data key="d2">73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,f14ec70726a24a574ae5d437903fddb8</data>
      <data key="d3">1399</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8162</data>
      <data key="d7">69803f1cc59c49a6b51fc9418871b39f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETISTA-NUTRICIONISTA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A Dietitian-Nutritionist is a trained health professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics. They conduct dietary interviews to gather detailed information about individuals' eating habits and provide guidance on the appropriate intake of foods and liquids. In a clinical setting, a dietitian-nutritionist works under the supervision of a physician to manage dietary needs and meal planning, particularly in hospitals. Their role is essential in advising patients on how to maintain a balanced diet and make informed food choices to support their health.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,caeec333a833f2df895a80c4047485cb</data>
      <data key="d3">1376</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8163</data>
      <data key="d7">e1e30237f3e94e548e837514e4f76ebe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED MEATS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Red meats are consumed less frequently in the Mediterranean diet, emphasizing lower intake for health benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363</data>
      <data key="d3">1637</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8164</data>
      <data key="d7">04ea779299314e6192b743133968c06d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY HISTORY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary history refers to the process of assessing an individual's eating habits and fluid intake over time, with a particular focus on identifying foods that may contribute to health issues such as kidney stone formation. This method involves gathering detailed information about a patient's dietary practices, which can provide valuable insights for healthcare professionals in understanding and managing potential dietary-related health concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8165</data>
      <data key="d7">60d1b562436e48af8cadd1e686627d5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLIVE OIL">
      <data key="d0" />
