    <node id="PERSONAL DE ENFERMER&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Personal de Enfermer&#237;a" refers to the nursing staff responsible for various critical functions in patient care. This group includes both nurses and nursing assistants who are tasked with placing catheters and managing venous access in patients. Additionally, they play a vital role in translating dietary guidelines and monitoring patient intake within hospital settings. Their responsibilities encompass both technical procedures and patient education, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals under their supervision.</data>
      <data key="d2">67344d72dff60fcb903b258fbca95de5,b624abf4d303854800e88f2364d190f0</data>
