    <node id="HOSPITAL DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "HOSPITAL DIET" encompasses a systematic approach to diet planning for hospitalized patients, focusing on their unique physiological and pathological conditions. It involves the selection of appropriate dietary plans that cater to the specific health needs of patients, particularly after surgeries such as bariatric surgery. Hospital diets are structured meal plans designed to effectively manage nutritional intake, especially for individuals with specific health conditions like diabetes. These nutritional plans and protocols are established to ensure that patients receive the necessary dietary support during their hospital stay, taking into account their dietary restrictions and health requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">49279a0184d5222e806637f084f42c50,4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05,5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,7180911fea4c085adf139e1c4cd43151</data>
      <data key="d3">1246</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">8240</data>
      <data key="d7">ef4ec203184946299ca16845cc6692bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETAS PROGRESIVAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"DIETAS PROGRESIVAS" refers to a series of dietary plans specifically designed to support recovery and adapt to changes in a patient's condition following surgery or during medical treatment. These progressive diets are utilized to aid in the restoration of digestive function after a period of fasting, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food in a manner that is safe and conducive to their healing process.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b19145e0977ee48b7132c9915d8c284,4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05</data>
      <data key="d3">1246</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8241</data>
      <data key="d7">4f7ffc4f0ad74a6e8f82df5b608adcb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETAS ESPECIALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Special diets are non-coded diets tailored to individual patient needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05</data>
      <data key="d3">1246</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8242</data>
      <data key="d7">d054821da2dc4ef88c526f3163f90230</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRIENT DISTRIBUTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrient distribution in hospital diets typically consists of 50-55% carbohydrates, 30-35% lipids, and 10-20% proteins.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05</data>
      <data key="d3">1246</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8243</data>
      <data key="d7">6c56fc57e54f4d668bbe6e1664a0ea15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY RESTRICTIONS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary restrictions are essential for managing the health of patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, primarily aimed at limiting the intake of very long-chain fatty acids. In addition to this specific restriction, dietary guidelines for these patients may also encompass a variety of other limitations, including gluten-free, low-purine, and vegetarian options. These comprehensive dietary restrictions are designed to support the overall well-being and nutritional needs of individuals affected by this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618,4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8244</data>
      <data key="d7">e6b30b725cd749a4a8540a6b0c2cb8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ODONTOLOGICAL/FA&#769;CIL MASTICACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Odontological/easy chewing diets are tailored for patients with chewing or swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05</data>
      <data key="d3">1150</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8245</data>
      <data key="d7">aa1d9cb09f4441bb8140d944539afd72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERPROTEICA refers to a high-protein diet specifically designed for patients who require an increased protein intake. This includes individuals suffering from conditions such as burns or those experiencing metabolic stress, where the body&#8217;s protein needs are elevated. The Hiperproteica diet is particularly beneficial for patients with burns or increased catabolism, as it helps support recovery and maintain muscle mass during periods of heightened protein demand.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e7560a799f319bdc8ae25737acc4d05,c6406ac5c0c7b03d4ee61ca311fd783f</data>
      <data key="d3">1152</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">8246</data>
      <data key="d7">313abd52f5614816b5997d891878d4e9</data>
    </node>
