      <data key="d1">Boller&#237;a refers to a variety of baked goods, commonly known as pastries, which are often included in breakfast options within certain diet plans. These baked goods may contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol, which can affect individuals with specific intolerances. While some pastries can vary in gluten content, making them potentially suitable for gluten-free diets, it is important to note that pastries are not permitted in modified diets. Dietary guidelines suggest that pastries should be consumed occasionally and in moderation.</data>
