    </node>
    <node id="HUESOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HUESOS, or bones, are essential structures in the body that play a crucial role in providing support and protection to various organs. They are dependent on copper for their development and maintenance, highlighting the importance of this mineral in bone health. Additionally, certain types of bones can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This dual aspect of bones emphasizes their significance in both physiological functions and potential health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd22bf95ac5fc6dc95539efb99c5b11a,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8332</data>
      <data key="d7">1e33aada185f4c94bb8617e0f96c8fa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPINAS">
