      <data key="d1">Merienda is an afternoon snack that plays a significant role in children's diets, typically comprising approximately 10-15% of their total caloric intake. This snack not only serves as a source of energy but also contributes to the daily nutritional needs of children. Additionally, merienda can be tailored to include specific items for dietary management, making it suitable for individuals with dietary restrictions. Overall, merienda is an important component of a balanced diet, providing both nourishment and enjoyment during the afternoon hours.</data>
