    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA, or chronic liver disease, is a medical condition characterized by long-term damage to the liver, which can result in liver dysfunction and potentially lead to liver failure. This condition often necessitates nutritional support due to the risk of malnutrition, which may arise from the disease itself. Patients with HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA may experience complications such as malnutrition, encephalopathy, and sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of adequate nutritional intervention, including enteral feeding, to maintain health and manage the disease effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448,70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,94a9c497b06553e1f7643ff25e4b464f,d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
