    <node id="DIETARY RECOMMENDATIONS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary recommendations encompass a variety of guidelines aimed at promoting overall health and managing specific medical conditions through balanced nutrition. These recommendations are designed to prevent atherosclerosis and enhance cardiovascular health, ensuring individuals maintain a heart-healthy diet. For patients with chronic kidney disease, dietary recommendations focus on managing phosphorus levels to support kidney function. 

In the context of bariatric surgery, dietary recommendations provide essential guidelines for patients to follow post-operation, helping them achieve proper nutrition and maintain weight loss effectively. For individuals with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI), dietary recommendations emphasize a high carbohydrate intake along with a slightly elevated protein intake to manage symptoms and sustain energy levels.

For those managing diabetes, dietary recommendations include guidelines that prioritize low sugar and high fiber intake to help regulate blood sugar levels. Additionally, these recommendations suggest a gradual reintroduction of lactose to assess tolerance in individuals who may be lactose intolerant. Furthermore, it is advised to limit foods high in fructose and sorbitol, particularly in processed products, to alleviate symptoms of intolerance. Overall, dietary recommendations serve as a crucial framework for individuals to achieve optimal health and manage specific dietary needs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">24cc40d6e3b225945cd4d8c2484632e4,2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5,7180911fea4c085adf139e1c4cd43151,8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324,da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127,fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
