    <node id="KIWI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Kiwi is a small, brown, fuzzy fruit characterized by its bright green flesh and tiny black seeds. It is renowned for its unique sweet and tangy flavor, making it a popular choice among fruit lovers. The kiwi fruit is rich in dietary fiber and is included in dietary recommendations due to its numerous health benefits. It contains a significant amount of vitamin C, contributing to its nutritional value. Additionally, kiwi has a fructose content of 4-5 grams per 100 grams and a higher amount of galactose, ranging from 10-20 mg per 100 grams. Overall, kiwi is celebrated not only for its distinctive taste but also for its health-promoting properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe,8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84,9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a</data>
