    <node id="CELIAQU&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CELIAQU&#205;A, also known as Celiac Disease, is an autoimmune disorder characterized by an adverse reaction to gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. This condition necessitates a strict gluten-free diet to effectively manage symptoms and prevent potential complications. Ongoing research suggests that there may be potential links between probiotic treatment and the management of Celiac Disease, indicating a possible area for future therapeutic exploration. Overall, CELIAQU&#205;A requires careful dietary management to ensure the health and well-being of those affected.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a1ea1a4dfb1b591756a8dc60f504da2,8a7b2d5e0440750e36603c8d3f93a68a,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566</data>
      <data key="d3">829</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">8393</data>
      <data key="d7">08056d04dc944fbabdce6fb379c001b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA SIN GLUTEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"DIETA SIN GLUTEN" refers to a dietary model that excludes gluten, which is essential for the health of individuals with celiac disease and those with non-celiac gluten sensitivity. This gluten-free diet involves the complete elimination of foods containing gluten grains, making it a crucial treatment for celiac patients. The diet is designed to be nutritionally complete and includes a variety of meals for each day of the week, encompassing breakfast, lunch, and dinner options. Overall, "DIETA SIN GLUTEN" serves as a vital dietary regimen tailored to meet the specific needs of those affected by gluten-related disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1aab735899b0c557ec11da0558bcfc15,1cdda2c6d946ce6e48baae4230be531d,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,8a7b2d5e0440750e36603c8d3f93a68a,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566,a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4</data>
      <data key="d3">829</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">8394</data>
      <data key="d7">676c4f7f501f4b7ea0aea261cde94579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA POBRE EN PURINAS" is a dietary model specifically designed to limit purine intake, primarily aimed at patients suffering from gout. This diet includes specific meal recommendations that help manage and reduce uric acid levels in individuals with hyperuricemia. In addition to dietary management, the low-purine diet emphasizes the importance of weight reduction as a means to further alleviate symptoms and improve overall health for those affected by these conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdda2c6d946ce6e48baae4230be531d,8a7b2d5e0440750e36603c8d3f93a68a</data>
