    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional control for patients undergoing bariatric surgery aims to ensure adequate intake, limit complications, and address nutritional deficits.</data>
      <data key="d2">5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54</data>
      <data key="d3">1650</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">8429</data>
      <data key="d7">ebd88ab80c0342fda99196d9d197b748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUID DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "LIQUID DIET" refers to a specific dietary phase that is commonly implemented following bariatric surgery. This diet involves the consumption of only liquids, which is crucial for aiding recovery and adaptation after the surgical procedure. The primary purpose of the liquid diet is to protect the surgical sites and facilitate healing. It is characterized by small volumes of liquid intake, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food while minimizing the risk of complications. Additionally, a liquid diet can also be prescribed for patients with certain medical conditions, emphasizing its role in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, the liquid diet serves as an essential step in the post-operative care of bariatric surgery patients, focusing on liquid or liquid-form foods to support their recovery process.</data>
      <data key="d2">5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5,eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381</data>
      <data key="d3">1013</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8430</data>
      <data key="d7">fe8354b2d2df4f57963b892f8345e2ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLID DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A solid diet is the final phase of dietary reintroduction after bariatric surgery, transitioning from liquids to solid foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8431</data>
      <data key="d7">2e0bbff770c84ae8a91bd5e1868db100</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPPLEMENTAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Supplemental nutrition includes additional nutritional products provided to patients to meet dietary needs post-surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8432</data>
      <data key="d7">22a0520f92be4037897daf206212b98a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YOGURT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Yogurt is a dairy product that serves as a nutritious option for patients, particularly those who are lactose intolerant. It is a fermented dairy product that not only provides essential calcium but also allows individuals to enjoy a source of nutrition while minimizing lactose intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">605</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8433</data>
      <data key="d7">ef42eb44a56140cea262d3bfd50487bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEGUMES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Legumes are a category of plant foods recognized for their nutritional benefits, particularly their high protein and fiber content, which contribute positively to cardiovascular health. They are frequently highlighted in dietary guidelines, emphasizing their favorable phosphorus-to-protein ratio, making them suitable for renal patients. However, it is important to note that legumes are restricted in the diets of individuals who need to limit their potassium intake, as they contain high levels of potassium. Overall, legumes play a significant role in nutrition, but their consumption should be tailored to individual dietary needs, especially for those with specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b79601d85087d62f0d4890761776c04,5236affa95aaf73b0f2d08e839e4db54,da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127</data>
      <data key="d3">1631</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8434</data>
      <data key="d7">e324276792494269a3af861b34ff030a</data>
    </node>
