    <node id="H&#205;GADO GRASO NO ALCOH&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">H&#237;gado Graso No Alcoh&#243;lico, also known as non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fat in the liver. This condition typically occurs in individuals who consume little or no alcohol. It can be associated with various factors, including iron overload. The presence of excess fat in the liver can lead to further complications if not managed properly.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
