    <node id="ENFERMEDADES CARD&#205;ACAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades card&#237;acas son condiciones que afectan el coraz&#243;n y pueden ser contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8489</data>
      <data key="d7">eadd198ddd914dd7a2168df093b11b1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBREPESO GRADO II">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El sobrepeso grado II se refiere a un IMC superior a 27 kg/m&#178; y puede estar asociado a comorbilidades que justifican el uso de dietas VLCD.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8490</data>
      <data key="d7">f2ee809ed8494918a7cfdd8606beefaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS PSIQUI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">TRASTORNOS PSIQUI&#193;TRICOS se refiere a condiciones de salud mental que pueden influir en el tratamiento y la nutrici&#243;n de los pacientes. Estas condiciones son consideradas contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas de muy bajo contenido cal&#243;rico (VLCD). Adem&#225;s, trastornos psiqui&#225;tricos como la depresi&#243;n cl&#237;nica son comunes en pacientes que padecen enfermedades cr&#243;nicas severas, lo que puede afectar negativamente su ingesta nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8491</data>
      <data key="d7">b05aff011fc24018be0b367f6013eaba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOREXIA/BULIMIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La anorexia y la bulimia son trastornos alimentarios que son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8492</data>
      <data key="d7">6426c866783145e5b5e28c434b575de1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGESTA CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La ingesta cal&#243;rica se refiere a la cantidad de calor&#237;as consumidas a trav&#233;s de los alimentos, que puede aumentar con alimentos de alta densidad energ&#233;tica.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1525</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8493</data>
      <data key="d7">c5cd41c837ea41a39948f584504a7b2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PALATABILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La palatabilidad se refiere a la aceptaci&#243;n y el placer que se experimenta al consumir alimentos, a menudo influenciada por el contenido de grasa.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1523</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8494</data>
      <data key="d7">425444fc224642ddb9acfdcacf5b96ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIOS DE INTERVENCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los estudios de intervenci&#243;n son investigaciones que analizan el efecto de modificar la densidad energ&#233;tica en la dieta sobre la p&#233;rdida de peso.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1525</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8495</data>
      <data key="d7">1e63fc8f54f441b2875f3b6629c62a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRODUCTOS COMERCIALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los productos comerciales son alimentos dise&#241;ados para ser utilizados en dietas de muy bajo contenido cal&#243;rico, como barritas y galletas.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">720</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8496</data>
      <data key="d7">244736b89d3c4e07ac3b92589764cf42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#193;S DE 12 KCAL/KG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">M&#225;s de 12 kcal/kg se refiere a la cantidad de calor&#237;as que se considera alta en comparaci&#243;n con las dietas de muy bajo contenido cal&#243;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8497</data>
      <data key="d7">637aeacafb5d49ae8179c9fde40e7e82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#193;S BARATOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los alimentos energ&#233;ticamente m&#225;s densos suelen ser m&#225;s baratos, lo que puede influir en las decisiones de consumo.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1523</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8498</data>
      <data key="d7">a01063901958478c97f99684735f427f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOTIVOS DE SALUD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los motivos de salud son razones que pueden justificar la necesidad de una p&#233;rdida de peso r&#225;pida, como condiciones m&#233;dicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8499</data>
      <data key="d7">93632a62c3e840b8a65db97ca8fab2de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PER&#205;ODOS SUPERIORES A 16 SEMANAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los per&#237;odos superiores a 16 semanas se refieren a la duraci&#243;n recomendada para el uso de dietas VLCD, que no se aconseja exceder.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8500</data>
      <data key="d7">2e0aec8d1fdb44c08e1287d2f4b18d5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPOSICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La composici&#243;n se refiere a los nutrientes y calor&#237;as que contienen los productos de muy bajo contenido cal&#243;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">720</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8501</data>
      <data key="d7">a549c0ac11004bad81212f9acfea9afe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DURACI&#211;N DE USO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La duraci&#243;n de uso se refiere al tiempo recomendado para seguir una dieta VLCD, que no debe exceder 16 semanas.</data>
      <data key="d2">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8502</data>
      <data key="d7">cb38182d309f48c4918f3adf1e1978db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES TYPE 1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes Type 1 is an autoimmune medical condition characterized by the body's inability to produce insulin, leading to elevated blood glucose levels. This condition increases the risk of developing ketosis and hypoglycemia, especially in patients who are following a Very Low-Calorie Diet (VLCD). Additionally, Diabetes Type 1 has been associated with celiac disease, which is thought to be linked through shared genetic factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6,3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8503</data>
      <data key="d7">b0ff3236b2464111a0d1dca5be84424d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORNISH DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ornish Diet is a low-fat diet that emphasizes the reduction of fat intake and is designed for weight loss and cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8504</data>
      <data key="d7">7487fb4403ed4e05b6269a169aad18c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRITIKIN DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Pritikin Diet is another low-fat dietary approach aimed at modifying lifestyle for the prevention of cardiovascular disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8505</data>
      <data key="d7">703225e69008474d9a69a294a91d761f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTROINTESTINAL DISCOMFORT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrointestinal discomfort is a common side effect associated with VLCD, including symptoms like nausea and constipation.</data>
      <data key="d2">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6</data>
      <data key="d3">719</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8506</data>
      <data key="d7">131c479904b54b44a0c1d30a763c2ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN ACADEMY OF FAMILY PHYSICIANS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Academy of Family Physicians is a professional organization that provides guidelines on dietary practices, including definitions of low-carbohydrate diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1380</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8507</data>
      <data key="d7">f51eb92ecf364a258fd8642c38ba9104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETAS BAJAS EN HIDRATOS DE CARBONO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Low-carbohydrate diets (DBHC) are dietary plans that restrict carbohydrate intake and have gained popularity for weight loss and metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d2">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1380</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">8508</data>
      <data key="d7">3eb3f0de456547eea1ca57f232864aa3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA ATKINS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Atkins Diet, known in Spanish as "la dieta Atkins," is a low-carbohydrate diet that emphasizes high protein and fat intake while significantly limiting carbohydrate consumption. It is often classified as a hyperproteic diet and has gained popularity for its effectiveness in weight loss, frequently being referred to as a miracle diet. The diet's approach focuses on reducing carbohydrate intake to promote fat burning and weight loss, making it a well-known option for those seeking to manage their weight.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7,64347a9be918a67f786cbdf9f9db9c8a,880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1375</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8509</data>
      <data key="d7">71168e1d8fdf44fe97b7f97782d217eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOUTH BEACH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The South Beach Diet is another popular low-carbohydrate diet that focuses on healthy fats and proteins while reducing carbohydrate intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1380</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8510</data>
      <data key="d7">5a4b472cb00a40df9923a2703e17f07a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CETOG&#201;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ketogenic diets are a type of very low-carbohydrate diet that induces ketosis, mentioned in the context of low-carbohydrate diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1380</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8511</data>
      <data key="d7">7713a5cbd2474c23ad46620df91044b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERFIL LIP&#205;DICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lipid profile refers to the levels of various types of fats in the blood, which can be affected by dietary choices, including low-carbohydrate diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d3">1380</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8512</data>
      <data key="d7">849ca26dd3f740679ffc2114990db541</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS" refers to side effects that are a significant concern in the development of obesity treatments. These side effects can also be observed in other medical treatments, such as oncological therapies, where they manifest as symptoms like nausea and loss of appetite, which negatively impact the patient's nutrition. Additionally, side effects can arise from low-carbohydrate diets, leading to adverse reactions such as constipation and headaches. Overall, "EFECTOS SECUNDARIOS" encompasses a range of adverse reactions that can affect both obesity treatments and other medical interventions, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing these effects to ensure patient well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162,9c3716c3860855ce045a1e5d9d30b9d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1086</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8513</data>
      <data key="d7">f5767aa6261d444d978f83fad456365b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DBHC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DBHC refers to a type of diet that has been studied for its long-term safety and efficacy, particularly in relation to fat consumption and mortality rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">5116416429465894c102d9fb93d6a8fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1892</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8514</data>
      <data key="d7">86154402935b405fb1a2e55661db869c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DBIG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DBIG refers to diets with a low glycemic index, which classify carbohydrates based on their impact on blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">5116416429465894c102d9fb93d6a8fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">8515</data>
      <data key="d7">b60fbd6ba53549d1afa3b91fa07d234d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONTIGNAC">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Montignac is a popular figure associated with low glycemic index diets, known for promoting dietary methods that emphasize carbohydrate quality.</data>
      <data key="d2">5116416429465894c102d9fb93d6a8fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1894</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
