      <data key="d6">8521</data>
      <data key="d7">2c57cdaec9114416a258f504d4273ed1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta hiperproteica se refiere a un tipo de dieta que tiene un alto contenido de prote&#237;nas, generalmente superior al 20-30% del aporte cal&#243;rico total, y se ha popularizado por su potencial efecto en la p&#233;rdida de peso.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7</data>
      <data key="d3">1375</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">8522</data>
      <data key="d7">7ea55edc3050421383940ec8672d193e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA DE LA ZONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta de la Zona es un enfoque diet&#233;tico que propone una proporci&#243;n de nutrientes de 40% carbohidratos, 30% prote&#237;nas y 30% grasas, y se considera una dieta hiperproteica.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7</data>
      <data key="d3">1375</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8523</data>
      <data key="d7">d4f67848332041e9bed1241a6295649e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIOXIDANTES FEN&#211;LICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los antioxidantes fen&#243;licos son compuestos que se derivan del consumo de fibra y que pueden ser reducidos por dietas bajas en carbohidratos, afectando la salud intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7</data>
      <data key="d3">1375</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8524</data>
      <data key="d7">c4455e8738ce4b0abf6e9474d4bc2818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNES BLANCAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CARNES BLANCAS, which refers to white meats such as poultry and rabbit, are preferred in the Mediterranean diet over red and processed meats, contributing to a healthier eating pattern. These white meats are included in dietary guidelines that emphasize specific health considerations, highlighting their role in promoting overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df</data>
      <data key="d3">1379</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8525</data>
      <data key="d7">eb8f31c112c34c4bba4b128ecf5adf9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNES ROJAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CARNES ROJAS, or red meats, are consumed in lesser quantities within the Mediterranean diet, which is associated with various health benefits. Dietary guidelines discuss red meat consumption, highlighting its potential link to cancer and recommending moderation based on its health impacts. Additionally, red meats are identified as a significant source of saturated fats, which can impair renal excretion of urate, leading to elevated uric acid levels. Overall, the consumption of red meats is approached with caution in dietary recommendations due to these health considerations.</data>
      <data key="d2">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df</data>
      <data key="d3">1387</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">8526</data>
      <data key="d7">057fe470e60940ecb7fbffcd15f7e7d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">L&#225;cteos, or dairy products, encompass a variety of food items derived from milk, including milk, cheese, and yogurt. These products are recognized for their high-quality proteins and essential nutrients, particularly calcium, which are crucial for children's growth and development. Dietary guidelines recommend the inclusion of dairy products in children's diets due to their health benefits. However, it is noted that the consumption of dairy is relatively low in the Mediterranean diet, which may contribute to certain health risks.

In terms of dietary recommendations, it is advised that dairy products be consumed in controlled portions, with a limit of two servings per day suggested before medical tests. Additionally, it is important to avoid commercial dairy preparations that may contain gluten. Low-fat dairy products, in particular, have been associated with lower uric acid levels and a reduced risk of hyperuricemia. Overall, while dairy products are beneficial, moderation and careful selection are emphasized to maximize their health benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,08edfb59071449728499ca59eb51ac84,108b158c33fead285203903273758748,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,73896da11a9ec209fb3e5b61f19f81df,b5db5210dfb726bf3f6d3fae82598596,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e</data>
      <data key="d3">1400</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">8527</data>
      <data key="d7">c68d06f1933741d282212a010408dbef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZ&#218;CARES A&#209;ADIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dieta mediterr&#225;nea se caracteriza por un bajo consumo de az&#250;cares a&#241;adidos, lo que puede ayudar a prevenir enfermedades metab&#243;licas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f</data>
