    </node>
    <node id="SEMISOLID DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SEMISOLID DIET" is a dietary phase that follows the liquid diet, primarily designed for individuals transitioning back to solid foods. This phase consists of pureed or mashed foods, allowing for a gradual reintroduction of more solid textures. It is particularly relevant for patients who have undergone bariatric surgery, as it serves as a transitional stage where they can safely incorporate pur&#233;es and soft foods into their diet. The semisolid diet plays a crucial role in helping individuals adjust their eating habits while ensuring proper nutrition during recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5</data>
      <data key="d3">1013</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">8536</data>
      <data key="d7">3651709c7a51407480335aca1e7e8a01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET" is the final phase following bariatric surgery, designed for patients to gradually reintroduce a variety of foods into their diet. During this phase, individuals are encouraged to focus on nutritional balance while consuming easily digestible solid foods. This diet allows for a broader range of food options, supporting the transition to a more typical eating pattern while still prioritizing the health and nutritional needs of the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324,ae99604da4e0a7da3a6e99e197205ab5</data>
      <data key="d3">1013</data>
