    <node id="N ENGLAND JOURNAL OF MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The New England Journal of Medicine is a prestigious medical journal recognized for its contributions to the field of medicine. It publishes a wide range of research and reviews on various medical topics, including significant issues such as the complications associated with central venous catheterization. Additionally, the journal has featured studies that explore dietary impacts on health, including a notable study that compared the effects of low-carbohydrate and low-fat diets in individuals with severe obesity. Through its rigorous publication standards, the New England Journal of Medicine plays a vital role in disseminating important medical knowledge and research findings.</data>
      <data key="d2">0381a11415dca4cfeda74f1de745d6ae,719fff2d16bc334d3d4b53f070373a10</data>
      <data key="d3">1840</data>
