    </node>
    <node id="COCHRANE DATABASE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cochrane Database is a comprehensive collection of databases in the fields of medicine and other healthcare specialties, primarily focused on providing high-quality, independent evidence to inform healthcare decision-making. It contains systematic reviews and meta-analyses that offer evidence-based information on various healthcare interventions. Among its extensive resources, the Cochrane Database includes systematic reviews that specifically address interventions for conditions such as cystic fibrosis, as well as published reviews on topics like low glycemic index diets for managing overweight and obesity. Overall, the Cochrane Database serves as a vital tool for healthcare professionals seeking reliable evidence to guide their clinical practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">0381a11415dca4cfeda74f1de745d6ae,3534154ea7562c7d4abe51bf29546109,c3e74ddf9529482684f4b62e713df49b,d6a596828c4ca22ce0a49c5ba26b33e8,ea8be3e3b3d7195ddc85512be460b6f8</data>
      <data key="d3">1055</data>
