    <node id="FUTURO DE LOS TRATAMIENTOS PARA LA OBESIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The future of obesity treatments involves ongoing research and development of new therapies and interventions to manage obesity effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">89ca65c4bdc30027c9c9ed1e1b442939</data>
      <data key="d3">1463</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8568</data>
      <data key="d7">1fd66c66fe784e8eaef23bd7506926cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LORCASERINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lorcaserina is a serotonin receptor agonist that has been approved by the FDA for the treatment of obesity. However, it was rejected by the European Medicines Agency (EMA) due to safety concerns. This weight loss medication is often discussed alongside other central action drugs, such as fentermina and topiramato, highlighting its role in the pharmacological landscape of obesity treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1416</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8569</data>
      <data key="d7">5b1b2a52d5dc4d058ad0b21d67f35203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENTERMINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fentermina is a medication primarily used in combination with topiramate for the treatment of obesity. It is a noradrenergic agent that has been approved by the FDA for appetite reduction in individuals struggling with obesity. Fentermina was initially marketed in 1956, highlighting its long-standing presence in the pharmacological landscape. However, it is important to note that while it has received FDA approval, it has not been approved by the European Medicines Agency (EMA).</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8570</data>
      <data key="d7">765040c0871f4df6a2c073a0f4e08735</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLOSSOM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The BLOSSOM study is a clinical trial designed to evaluate the effectiveness, efficacy, and tolerability of lorcaserin for obesity management. This study involves a total of 4,008 subjects and spans a duration of 52 weeks.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8571</data>
      <data key="d7">48879a5d7dc948129e3bb23faefeb0ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINOREX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Aminorex was a weight loss drug introduced in 1965 but was withdrawn in 1968 due to hypertension pulmonary risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8572</data>
      <data key="d7">7f3aea59083642b0b91cdf1889877416</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAZINDOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mazindol was a weight loss medication introduced in 1970 and suspended in 1993 in Australia due to safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8573</data>
      <data key="d7">086823eb605b465e87bc9e17bc40a367</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENFLURAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fenfluramina was a weight loss drug approved in Europe in 1963 and in the US in 1973, withdrawn due to cardiac valve disease and pulmonary hypertension risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8574</data>
      <data key="d7">04ce5ef73483458fa4efbddbe4231495</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEXFENFLURAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dexfenfluramina was introduced in 1985 in Europe and 1996 in the US but was withdrawn due to risks of cardiac valve disease and pulmonary hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8575</data>
      <data key="d7">c9af6e7f1f704bee95a2269cebe11231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIBUTRAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sibutramina is a weight loss medication that was approved in the United States in 1997 and in Europe in 2001. It has been compared to other weight loss drugs, such as fentermina and topiramato, particularly regarding patient abandonment rates. However, due to concerns over cardiovascular risks, Sibutramina was withdrawn from the market in 2010.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8576</data>
      <data key="d7">29c41b3e787347a090fd5e1868b75157</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIMONABANT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Rimonabant was approved in Europe in 2006 for obesity treatment but was withdrawn in 2009 due to severe psychiatric side effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8577</data>
      <data key="d7">7c5ca49ae36941539603e4e9fbb15ad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DINITROFENOL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">35dc97b15f3fd556acbfdb405eadda06</data>
