      <data key="d7">32c92fcaea074303996f315efb5ceedc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLOOM-DM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The BLOOM-DM study is a clinical trial focused on the effects of lorcaserin for obesity management in patients with diabetes, involving 604 patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8580</data>
      <data key="d7">f8aef728f82f43ffbd79bdc66a115380</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LORCASERIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lorcaserin is a medication used for weight management, approved by the FDA in 2012, with a modest efficacy profile and various side effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1416</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8581</data>
      <data key="d7">952bbd3227904cbc947d608cbe243d2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOPIRAMATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Topiramate is a medication approved for partial seizures and migraine prophylaxis, which is used in combination with fentermina for obesity treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8582</data>
      <data key="d7">9e40f7dbfeca4a6d91d6da00737ad0d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QSYMIAR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Qsymia is a combination medication of fentermina and topiramate approved by the FDA in 2012 for obesity treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8583</data>
      <data key="d7">0c7bc98dadf24ed49e05c9d8f05c6572</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEROTONIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Serotonin is a neurotransmitter involved in mood regulation, which is mentioned in relation to the effects of lorcaserin and its potential side effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8584</data>
      <data key="d7">58c8208e524842b8a65e830acb17165e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARCINOGENICITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Carcinogenicity refers to the potential of a substance to cause cancer, which is a concern raised regarding lorcaserin based on animal studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8585</data>
      <data key="d7">8caabe509f024d02a8feb79ba441caf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NAUSEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nausea is a common side effect experienced by subjects taking liraglutida, as reported in clinical trials. Additionally, it is also one of the significant side effects reported in studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations. This indicates that nausea is a notable adverse effect associated with both liraglutida and lorcaserin, highlighting its prevalence in clinical settings related to these medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,90c684dca4542bbe1177afd26e78581e</data>
      <data key="d3">740</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8586</data>
      <data key="d7">7930a531b56348ea90345499e6cfc850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEADACHES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Headaches are a common side effect associated with the use of lorcaserin and its combinations in obesity treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8587</data>
      <data key="d7">3181f3ad66114ba482722eeec662524d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIZZINESS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dizziness is another side effect reported in the studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8588</data>
      <data key="d7">8fdee166b2e24bea9593349e61536f81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASTHENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Asthenia, or weakness, is a side effect noted in the context of lorcaserin treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8589</data>
      <data key="d7">08f1491c10f3498b9087bed9daa863f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSTIPATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Constipation is a side effect associated with the use of lorcaserin in obesity management.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8590</data>
      <data key="d7">956a9fc8bd2f4d2cb97c72edc31fd310</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DRY MOUTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dry mouth is a side effect reported in the studies involving lorcaserin and its combinations.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8591</data>
      <data key="d7">6ab3c457315c476abf4ff93d56c04836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYNDROME SEROTONINERGICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serotonin syndrome is a potentially life-threatening condition that can occur with certain medications, mentioned as a contraindication for lorcaserin.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8592</data>
      <data key="d7">4dec94d524d444d38a54bed995cf33b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYNDROME NEUROL&#201;PTICO MALIGNO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neuroleptic malignant syndrome is a severe reaction to antipsychotic medications, mentioned as a contraindication for lorcaserin.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8593</data>
      <data key="d7">0b0505634a7e44fa8824938f42de7ffe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA AVANZADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Advanced chronic kidney disease is identified as a contraindication for the use of lorcaserin. This condition, referred to as "ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA AVANZADA," indicates a severe decline in kidney function, which may pose risks when using certain medications like lorcaserin.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,a25b0f84bc321cad942a2e33f681a5e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1744</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8594</data>
      <data key="d7">e3904316db5842fda039cc55d902a387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALVULOPAT&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Valvulopathies refer to diseases of the heart valves, which are mentioned as a precaution for lorcaserin use.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8595</data>
      <data key="d7">2e32a9eac9ff41a6875715ef6a3e6300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRADICARDIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bradycardia, or slow heart rate, is mentioned as a precaution for the use of lorcaserin.</data>
      <data key="d2">623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8596</data>
      <data key="d7">867ed448b88a4a048625ad16cbac8ec4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EQUIP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EQUIP is a phase III randomized controlled trial that evaluates the combination of controlled-release phentermine and topiramate for the treatment of obesity in severely obese adults. The trial specifically studies the effects of this combination therapy, aiming to assess its efficacy and safety in managing obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,623ef060e116bc05259d5e6d3d8c0996,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1415</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8597</data>
      <data key="d7">b06f193d108449d88a870923cd4cc5e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENTERMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fentermina is a medication used for weight loss, often combined with topiramate to enhance its effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1415</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8598</data>
      <data key="d7">f5656c692c8d4015b98d56b86cf346fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONQUER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CONQUER is a randomized, placebo-controlled, phase 3 trial that investigates the effects of low-dose, controlled-release phentermine, also referred to as fentermina, in combination with topiramate. The study focuses on weight management and the associated comorbidities in overweight and obese adults. Through its design, CONQUER aims to provide insights into the efficacy of this medication regimen for improving health outcomes related to obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1415</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8599</data>
      <data key="d7">116bfa1dee184c988140182f8d67a64a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEQUEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SEQUEL is a randomized, placebo-controlled, phase 3 extension study that focuses on sustained weight loss and metabolic benefits associated with controlled-release phentermine/topiramate. This study serves as an extension of the CONQUER trial, continuing to follow participants for a duration of two years.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cc73922b5279318629905f2bdc66906,af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1415</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8600</data>
      <data key="d7">bb02266c70a74fc2b4cf364717f5dc8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NALTREXONA/BUPROPION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Naltrexona/bupropion is a combination medication for weight loss that is also compared to fentermina and topiramato.</data>
