    <node id="ALTERACIONES HEP&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alteraciones hep&#225;ticas refers to liver disorders that encompass a range of liver abnormalities. These disorders are significant as they serve as a precaution for the use of certain medications, specifically fentermina and topiramato. Additionally, in pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition, alteraciones hep&#225;ticas can manifest as elevated liver enzymes and cholestasis, highlighting the importance of monitoring liver function in these individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d3">590</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8605</data>
      <data key="d7">f886fbd069fd46fc9d5715dac663539c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES COGNITIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alteraciones cognitivas refers to cognitive impairments that may occur with the use of fentermina and topiramato, especially when combined with other substances.</data>
      <data key="d2">af631316aa8584710d755d8c59e851b6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8606</data>
