    </node>
    <node id="COR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COR refers to the Contrave Obesity Research studies that evaluated the effectiveness of the bupropion-naltrexone combination in obese patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">488970234520652b063db88e8346031c</data>
      <data key="d3">314</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8612</data>
      <data key="d7">6bf0c81ea38d4da9a2db6e4320ab278e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COR-BMOD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">COR-BMOD is a study designed to evaluate the effects of intensive lifestyle changes in conjunction with a combination therapy of bupropion and naltrexone on weight loss. This trial specifically investigates the impact of naltrexone SR and bupropion SR as adjuncts to behavior modification, aiming to enhance weight loss outcomes through a comprehensive approach that includes both pharmacological and behavioral interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3eddab8e3e55bbd7e6cbcd3776fecb29,488970234520652b063db88e8346031c</data>
      <data key="d3">314</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8613</data>
      <data key="d7">314b3e33a65a4c15a25c797e7f4f971c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES CON SOBREPESO Y OBESIDAD">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients with overweight and obesity were the subjects of the studies evaluating the effectiveness of bupropion and naltrexone.</data>
      <data key="d2">488970234520652b063db88e8346031c</data>
      <data key="d3">314</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8614</data>
      <data key="d7">301cf47636a74c938323457b5821cdd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLELITIASIS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cholelithiasis, also known as colelitiasis, is the presence of gallstones in the gallbladder. This condition is significant as it necessitates caution for patients who are taking weight loss medications and certain other drugs. The presence of gallstones can lead to complications, making it important for healthcare providers to monitor and manage patients with this condition carefully.</data>
      <data key="d2">22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,488970234520652b063db88e8346031c</data>
      <data key="d3">1432</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8615</data>
      <data key="d7">06db2470e67546b9ac4ea91a78f22b21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WARFARINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Warfarina is an anticoagulant medication that plays a crucial role in preventing blood clots. It is important to note that Warfarina may interact with weight loss medications, necessitating careful monitoring of patients who are using both. Additionally, the efficacy of Warfarina can be significantly influenced by dietary factors, particularly vitamin K intake, which may counteract its anticoagulant effects. Furthermore, the absorption of Warfarina can be altered by enteral nutrition, potentially impacting its therapeutic action. Certain foods, especially those high in fat, can also decrease the effectiveness of Warfarina. Therefore, patients on Warfarina should be aware of these interactions and dietary considerations to ensure optimal therapeutic outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">488970234520652b063db88e8346031c,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,5eb14e2cbec104d89ad73e2ac968b7fd,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d3">1187</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">8616</data>
      <data key="d7">d3b134db6c904e7088ecd18d73109426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BN is a pharmaceutical treatment that reduces blood pressure and is involved in cardiovascular safety studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
