    </node>
    <node id="AGRP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AGRP (Agouti-Related Peptide) is a neuropeptide that stimulates appetite and is involved in energy homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4</data>
      <data key="d3">997</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8631</data>
      <data key="d7">3ed67588bf52434d871ea7911544c3ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GABA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GABA, or Gamma-Aminobutyric Acid, is an organic molecule that functions as a neurotransmitter in the brain. It plays a crucial role in inhibiting nerve transmission, which is essential for regulating various physiological processes, including appetite. Additionally, GABA is involved in the brain's defense mechanisms against cerebral edema, particularly during conditions of hyponatremia. Through its inhibitory effects, GABA contributes to maintaining the balance of excitatory and inhibitory signals in the nervous system, thereby supporting overall brain health and function.</data>
      <data key="d2">419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8632</data>
      <data key="d7">e5ee8c37155f4e2390a79425f74ab98b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N&#218;CLEOS HIPOTAL&#193;MICOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">N&#250;cleos hipotal&#225;micos refers to the hypothalamic nuclei that are involved in the regulation of hunger and satiety.</data>
      <data key="d2">419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4</data>
      <data key="d3">997</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8633</data>
      <data key="d7">3fb3cd860d0a4eb187bdd6c8d9fb2bb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SCALE STUDIES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The SCALE studies are clinical trials that evaluate the effectiveness of liraglutida in weight loss and its impact on various health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">90c684dca4542bbe1177afd26e78581e</data>
