    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOVASCULAR RISK">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiovascular risk encompasses the likelihood of experiencing heart-related health issues, which is influenced by various factors, including diet and lifestyle choices. In particular, cardiovascular risk markers are evaluated in relation to the effects of liraglutide, especially among diabetic patients. This evaluation highlights the importance of understanding how dietary patterns and food choices can impact cardiovascular health. Overall, cardiovascular risk is a multifaceted concept that integrates the effects of individual health behaviors and medical treatments on the potential for developing cardiovascular disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b79601d85087d62f0d4890761776c04,5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,90c684dca4542bbe1177afd26e78581e,e1766b4a9f6cff776650a29195cee9fc</data>
