    </node>
    <node id="ENSAYOS CL&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENSAYOS CL&#205;NICOS" refers to clinical trials, which are research studies designed to evaluate the effects and safety of medications and medical approaches in human subjects. These trials are regulated by specific legislation and are essential for testing the efficacy of new treatments. They encompass a variety of focuses, including the effectiveness and safety of enteral nutrition products. Recent randomized clinical trials have demonstrated the efficacy of the ketogenic diet in treating epilepsy. Additionally, clinical trials are also conducted to assess treatments for gluten sensitivity and irritable bowel syndrome, highlighting their role in advancing medical knowledge and improving patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">06adf563f18feaa5629f0e368a72d227,0fd4d7a9544dd7c2999b9ce1708919bc,22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,2e07cfac64a6162c745f1c392de1bff4,53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f</data>
      <data key="d3">861</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">8651</data>
      <data key="d7">feda37b4bfd1490491e41e9c2b305f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NORADRENALINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Noradrenalina, also known as norepinephrine, is a hormone and neurotransmitter that plays a significant role in various physiological processes. It can increase in response to a low-sodium diet, which may impact sleep and other bodily functions. Additionally, noradrenalina is involved in the mechanism of action of tesofensina, indicating its importance in both hormonal regulation and neurotransmission.</data>
      <data key="d2">22a361e57659e072600d6575631f6160,9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b</data>
      <data key="d3">1575</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8652</data>
      <data key="d7">9a1bf92955b3409e82c42285c83a7a56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METAP2">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MetAP2 is an enzyme that beloranif inhibits to reduce fat biosynthesis.</data>
