    <node id="GLUCAGON-LIKE PEPTIDE-1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) is a hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of glucose metabolism and appetite. It has garnered significant attention in the context of diabetes treatment and weight management, particularly in relation to the medication liraglutide. Through its functions, GLP-1 contributes to the control of blood sugar levels and helps in managing body weight, making it an important focus in therapeutic strategies for conditions such as diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">3eddab8e3e55bbd7e6cbcd3776fecb29,b602544ec2048878e40226cd2c0b29d4</data>
