    <node id="HBA1C REDUCTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HbA1c reduction is a clinical marker that improves with weight loss in obese patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">738</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8729</data>
      <data key="d7">81c6ea8869bd485c86aebcc87abcea70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TESOFENSINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tesofensine is a drug studied for its effects on body weight loss and quality of life in obese patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">738</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8730</data>
      <data key="d7">27ab0a17f2944930aa42e09424bdf8bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BELORANIB">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Beloranib is a pharmaceutical agent evaluated for weight loss efficacy and safety in obese adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">738</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8731</data>
      <data key="d7">95145689b0de475783176196ac871871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PYY3-36">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PYY3-36 is an enteroendocrine hormone that has been studied for its effects on energy intake and appetite in overweight individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">999</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8732</data>
      <data key="d7">f6f30e335f83436194829d0eb17d4dcd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GIP-OXYNTOMODULIN HYBRID PEPTIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A novel peptide that acts through GIP, glucagon, and GLP-1 receptors, showing weight-reducing properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">64821313d6eb9af473ab515aff2ba3c7</data>
      <data key="d3">738</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8733</data>
      <data key="d7">d8c118bd5ceb44f59f159a7a4deadbc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">RICA is an organization involved in studies related to obesity prevalence and its implications in health.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1553</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8734</data>
      <data key="d7">4ed898ea9b61406887161601faa1b1af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DI@BET.ES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Di@bet.es is an organization that conducts research on obesity and its related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1553</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8735</data>
      <data key="d7">36d5a723299e4f249598e8a334337bc2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EEUU">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">EEUU, or the United States, is a country characterized by a diverse healthcare landscape where coverage and funding for programs such as Medicare and Medicaid vary significantly. This variability extends to laws regarding artificial nutrition, which differ by state, influencing whether such interventions are classified as medical treatments or comfort measures. Additionally, the United States has been the site of significant epidemiological research, particularly concerning intestinal rhythm, as well as studies on the prevalence of gastrointestinal issues like constipation and diarrhea. Furthermore, the country is notable for its healthcare practices, with over 150,000 bariatric surgeries performed annually, reflecting its approach to obesity and related health concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,a6ccbda174f6599eeeb2e4cdb00db5f2,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1929</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">8736</data>
      <data key="d7">b382190a256e43ca902fe20e9fac2b03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DR. MASSON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dr. Masson is recognized as one of the pioneers of bariatric surgery, proposing the gastric bypass technique in the late 1960s.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8737</data>
      <data key="d7">9cc5fad3f8af4bfbb3a65b538c2beebc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBREPESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SOBREPESO refers to a condition characterized by an individual having more body weight than is deemed normal or healthy. This condition often serves as a precursor to obesity, which can have various health implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1633</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8738</data>
      <data key="d7">a7130d2c07e64d859aa525ee44eae841</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BANDA G&#193;STRICA AJUSTABLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adjustable gastric banding is a surgical weight-loss procedure that involves placing a band around the upper part of the stomach to limit food intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8739</data>
      <data key="d7">4fc0da88a9a9497e8bb60c578fe09f07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORBIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Morbid obesity refers to a condition where an individual has a body mass index (BMI) significantly higher than normal, leading to severe health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb9b69fc936b99615d48b5a9468bc052</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8740</data>
      <data key="d7">2d78f531843e46ca8e9615a0f877a47f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BANDA G&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Banda g&#225;strica is a surgical technique used for weight loss that creates a small gastric reservoir to limit food intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
      <data key="d3">1393</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8741</data>
      <data key="d7">4625be9e3fcd47988411946866cd359e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTRECTOM&#205;A VERTICAL LAPAROSC&#211;PICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrectom&#237;a vertical laparosc&#243;pica, also known as sleeve gastrectomy, is a minimally invasive surgical technique that removes a large portion of the stomach to aid in weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8742</data>
      <data key="d7">a4f51a62acdc4060bf570ccc046620b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BANDA G&#193;STRICA AJUSTABLE LAPAROSC&#211;PICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Banda g&#225;strica ajustable laparosc&#243;pica is a surgical procedure that involves placing an adjustable band around the stomach to control food intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8743</data>
      <data key="d7">94bee97930fa4f45b4ca98b234d309e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SADI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SADI, or single-anastomosis duodeno-ileal, is a surgical method that combines vertical gastrectomy with a duodeno-ileal anastomosis to treat obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
      <data key="d3">1390</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8744</data>
      <data key="d7">164e03c8a6aa4f169cc9df4200e1f2af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICAS QUIR&#218;RGICAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">b980df2798effe4d56b74a254734403c</data>
      <data key="d3">1393</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8745</data>
      <data key="d7">fba4de10fe2445d0ae89f2f372b05eb4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CB">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CB refers to bariatric surgery, a treatment indicated for patients with severe obesity. This type of surgery can lead to deficiencies in essential nutrients such as folic acid and vitamin B12, making careful monitoring necessary for those who undergo the procedure.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d3">674</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8746</data>
      <data key="d7">50f7cd6740ca4bc781df03d0c5995e68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMORBILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las comorbilidades son condiciones m&#233;dicas que pueden acompa&#241;ar a la obesidad y que pueden mejorar tras la cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8747</data>
      <data key="d7">89bbad6c8d8a4c5f8498ff7ffa2ab7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El riesgo quir&#250;rgico es un factor importante a considerar al evaluar a los pacientes para cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8748</data>
      <data key="d7">6b5f6d7c7f88435996fb79fe87a338dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N PREOPERATORIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La evaluaci&#243;n preoperatoria es un proceso fundamental para seleccionar adecuadamente a los candidatos para la cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8749</data>
      <data key="d7">b1209d9b0ff14cf0a6d6f3f5ba7c9b79</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HTA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HTA, or Hipertensi&#243;n Arterial, is a medical condition characterized by consistently elevated blood pressure levels. This condition, commonly referred to as hypertension, is often monitored in patients with diabetes due to the associated health risks. HTA can lead to serious health issues and is also recognized as a comorbidity in obese patients, which further increases the risk of complications. Overall, HTA is a significant health concern that requires careful management and monitoring to prevent adverse outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f2b31f5a0bba00ecee5e3a8fb2c83ea,29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a,66b7c4d336056f832579dc20ffb92992,b5db5210dfb726bf3f6d3fae82598596,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d3">623</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">23</data>
      <data key="d6">8750</data>
      <data key="d7">96c21152ccde4335824d6ffd3f4c7e55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATOLOG&#205;A RESPIRATORIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">PATOLOG&#205;A RESPIRATORIA refers to a range of conditions that impact pulmonary function and can necessitate specific nutritional management. These respiratory pathologies not only affect breathing but can also be comorbidities in patients suffering from obesity.</data>
      <data key="d2">169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8751</data>
      <data key="d7">d39d1efdc9ca4c1482188a85ba503a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tomograf&#237;a Computarizada (TC) is a medical imaging technique utilized to visualize internal structures of the body. It plays a crucial role in diagnosing various medical conditions, including those related to anorexia and bulimia. However, the use of TC can be complicated in patients with morbid obesity due to their size, which may pose challenges in obtaining clear images.</data>
      <data key="d2">de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8752</data>
      <data key="d7">90872380994a4ab69a902e24c836957b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La resonancia magn&#233;tica (RM) es una t&#233;cnica de imagen m&#233;dica que proporciona im&#225;genes detalladas de &#243;rganos y tejidos, siendo especialmente &#250;til para evaluar cambios neurol&#243;gicos en pacientes con trastornos alimentarios. Esta prueba diagn&#243;stica puede ser dif&#237;cil de realizar en pacientes con obesidad m&#243;rbida, lo que puede complicar su uso en esta poblaci&#243;n. La RM se utiliza para evaluar la salud de los tejidos blandos y del cerebro en pacientes que padecen trastornos alimentarios, lo que resalta su importancia en el diagn&#243;stico y seguimiento de estas condiciones.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8753</data>
      <data key="d7">3683004b7188493faa4b62473b07c7b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N PSICOL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La evaluaci&#243;n psicol&#243;gica es un paso importante en la preparaci&#243;n de pacientes para cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica, asegurando que est&#233;n mentalmente preparados para el cambio.</data>
      <data key="d2">de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8754</data>
      <data key="d7">90737d8fe79548c887093d009bc5a6d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N ANEST&#201;SICA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d3">1371</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8755</data>
      <data key="d7">980193fbddd64eb195cbe43ac02bcad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLINICAL TEAM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The clinical team is composed of healthcare professionals dedicated to supporting and guiding patients throughout the bariatric surgery process, including pre-operative preparation and post-operative care. This team plays a crucial role in monitoring patients after surgery to prevent complications and ensure that they receive appropriate follow-up care. Their comprehensive approach aims to facilitate a successful recovery and promote the overall well-being of patients undergoing bariatric procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324,db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8756</data>
      <data key="d7">a30f4d1831d84a05a1de86555c684e81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIMARY CARE TEAMS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary care teams collaborate closely with the clinical team to ensure comprehensive care for the patient post-surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8757</data>
      <data key="d7">1cb7f584107a4306a01a14be95976e66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYDRATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hydration is a vital process that involves maintaining adequate fluid intake, which plays a significant role in various health contexts. It is particularly critical in preventing kidney stones, as proper hydration helps to dilute urine and reduce the crystallization of minerals that can lead to stone formation. Additionally, hydration is essential for patients who have undergone bariatric surgery, as it helps prevent complications associated with insufficient fluid intake. Overall, maintaining proper hydration is crucial for overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86,8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8758</data>
      <data key="d7">64dbb5a31812417b81b0843ba3ac647d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCOHOL INTAKE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcohol intake is discouraged post-bariatric surgery due to its potential effects on nutrient absorption and the risk of addiction.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8759</data>
      <data key="d7">08425344c5dd412cafb27a663f2279b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Complications refer to potential health issues that may arise following bariatric surgery, necessitating careful monitoring and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">8ad412c188e4086d686c217c6c5c5324</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8760</data>
      <data key="d7">f7ae16fd67d549ed8af23f75932e58d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OMEPRAZOLE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Omeprazole is a medication recommended for use after bariatric surgery to reduce gastroesophageal reflux.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8761</data>
      <data key="d7">ac8c6935e1bd44099a35261124800ae6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL COMPLICATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional complications are frequent after bariatric surgery, including protein malnutrition and micronutrient deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8762</data>
      <data key="d7">2ecb29678eaa43c895e0f898e8799905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIMARY CARE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Primary care is involved in the protocolized coordination for the follow-up of patients after bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">261</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8763</data>
      <data key="d7">d115d29c5ca245f99709d5470011b365</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTRIC BYPASS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastric bypass is a surgical procedure for weight loss that alters the digestive system and can result in complications such as nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1014</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8764</data>
      <data key="d7">d1af5c32e4c34cc08131bffceb2cfb4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TEP refers to thromboembolic events, which are potential complications that can occur during or after bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8765</data>
      <data key="d7">b935bf8b72ed4857b07e899ca7cf58ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEIN MALNUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Protein malnutrition is a serious complication that can occur following bariatric surgery, especially after procedures such as biliopancreatic diversion. This condition is characterized by a range of symptoms, including edema, asthenia (weakness), hair loss, and an increased susceptibility to infections. It highlights the importance of monitoring nutritional status in patients who have undergone such surgical interventions to prevent and address potential deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2,db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1014</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8766</data>
      <data key="d7">19a842ab97df4d18bbde6e96f4279b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCIES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Micronutrient deficiencies are common complications following bariatric surgery, necessitating careful monitoring and supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1014</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8767</data>
      <data key="d7">f08e30c1f08b4f1e986d5e88835374dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BILIARY-PANCREATIC DIVERSION">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">db39b776f49b9fad2deb1dec7a0d3288</data>
      <data key="d3">1014</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8768</data>
      <data key="d7">d09fc33ec23a4830bad4a80b12506069</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DERIVACI&#211;N BILI PANCRE&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A surgical procedure that can lead to serious complications such as protein malnutrition and micronutrient deficiencies, particularly in the first year post-surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2</data>
      <data key="d3">1014</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8769</data>
      <data key="d7">af9b99b0534146b3baaa32772d11898d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Common in patients undergoing bariatric surgery, it can be prevented or treated early with proper follow-up and supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2</data>
      <data key="d3">586</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">8770</data>
      <data key="d7">dbd752a5415d4ddaaedc45597425f3b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAGNESIUM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Magnesium is a vital micronutrient and mineral that plays a critical role in numerous biological functions and processes within the body. It is essential for bone health and is involved in over 300 biochemical reactions, including those that regulate heart health. While magnesium deficiency is rare, it can occur in specific populations, such as patients experiencing significant diarrhea or those with liver disease, particularly in cases related to alcohol consumption. Dietary reference intake guidelines for magnesium are specified for different age groups, highlighting its importance across the lifespan. Additionally, magnesium contributes to the prevention of kidney stones by inhibiting crystallization, further underscoring its significance in maintaining overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,2e4409d82bf1cb293a2df7fc1a8cc9e7,2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,4a59488a9440b38afba989ca88d49ca3,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6,bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">583</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">8771</data>
      <data key="d7">41dead7930b54a248e9dc10061b5579f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINAS A, E Y K">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamins A, E, and K are fat-soluble vitamins that can be deficient after malabsorptive techniques, necessitating specific supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8772</data>
      <data key="d7">fd374e4578d641e58a88b8336ea77b52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BILIOPANCRE&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biliopancreatic diversion is a type of surgery that can lead to deficiencies in zinc, copper, and other micronutrients.</data>
      <data key="d2">91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d3">586</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8773</data>
      <data key="d7">8ea9036f725e4d8b99256280e36c2a5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOSE MONITORING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucose monitoring is a process used to track blood sugar levels, particularly in patients who have undergone bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">79afec9f55a4cb9aa31a7e4566dae279</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8774</data>
      <data key="d7">a499763d00c3409b95fcddb2becc0641</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENSITY MINERAL BONE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone mineral density refers to the amount of mineral matter per square centimeter of bones, which can decrease after bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">79afec9f55a4cb9aa31a7e4566dae279</data>
      <data key="d3">1012</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8775</data>
      <data key="d7">b2b108cab8a242d2bdefda35588245d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTIVITAMIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Multivitamins are dietary supplements that may be recommended for patients post-bariatric surgery to prevent nutrient deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">79afec9f55a4cb9aa31a7e4566dae279</data>
      <data key="d3">1654</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
