    <node id="DE LUIS DA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">De Luis DA is a prominent researcher engaged in various clinical trials that explore the intersection of nutrition and cancer, with a particular emphasis on enteral nutrition and its impact on patients. His work extends to studying the serum levels of zinc and copper in morbidly obese patients following biliopancreatic diversion, highlighting his focus on nutritional deficiencies in this population. Additionally, De Luis DA has made significant contributions to the field of home enteral nutrition in Spain, advocating for its importance in patient care. He is also an author who has addressed evidence-based nutrition practices in the context of acute pancreatitis and chronic liver disease, further underscoring his commitment to advancing nutritional science in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c,60d24674009cc67523f1ecdc63975fdc,8c198f866d8fb49a782cb57139b30d76,fff76d1cd0e64233a5727a707d80e2b9</data>
