    <node id="ZIEGLER TR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ziegler TR is a prominent researcher and author known for his extensive studies in the field of nutrition and its impact on various medical conditions. He has specifically focused on the efficacy and safety of glutamine-supplemented parenteral nutrition in surgical ICU patients, highlighting the importance of this amino acid in critical care settings. Additionally, Ziegler has investigated the clinical efficacy of glutamine in nutrition following bone marrow transplantation, further emphasizing its role in recovery and immune function. His research also extends to the study of copper deficiency that can occur after gastric bypass surgery, showcasing his interest in the nutritional challenges faced by patients undergoing significant surgical procedures. Furthermore, Ziegler has explored how glutamine regulates immune cell function, contributing to a deeper understanding of its potential benefits in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, Ziegler TR's work significantly advances the knowledge of nutritional interventions in critical and post-surgical care.</data>
      <data key="d2">29cd22ec41c1cb5160d9987958d6ae16,60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c,6efaddddefe1cf5ab78825e1d8c53cab,ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4</data>
      <data key="d3">1504</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8850</data>
      <data key="d7">5abb0c470af84450af78d5b8353412af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BALSA JA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Balsa JA is a researcher studying nutritional deficiency of selenium after bariatric surgery.</data>
