    <node id="ROUX-EN-Y GASTRIC BYPASS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Roux-en-Y gastric bypass is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves creating a small pouch from the stomach and connecting it directly to the small intestine.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8868</data>
      <data key="d7">05f8a5c29d05437181b3e2ad40206824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLEEVE GASTRECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sleeve gastrectomy is a surgical procedure for weight loss that involves removing a large portion of the stomach, leaving a tube-like structure.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8869</data>
      <data key="d7">53c09797717a4f31b675b326a1cae946</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMIN B12 DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B12 deficiency is a common issue following bariatric surgery, leading to various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8870</data>
      <data key="d7">48bde506a5dd4d969207a106bced3d5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICRONUTRIENT SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Micronutrient supplementation refers to the intake of vitamins and minerals to prevent deficiencies, particularly after bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8871</data>
      <data key="d7">85de8da6ce52447f95cbea8bdb9766fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional deficiency occurs when the body does not receive an adequate supply of essential nutrients, leading to various health issues. This condition is particularly concerning in vulnerable populations, such as infants, who may suffer significant health consequences due to insufficient nutrient intake. Additionally, nutritional deficiency can arise after bariatric surgery, where changes in the digestive system may hinder the absorption of vital nutrients. Furthermore, it is important to note that a lack of essential nutrients can exacerbate the symptoms and progression of conditions such as ELA (Eosinophilic Esophagitis), highlighting the critical role that proper nutrition plays in overall health and disease management.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c,9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3,cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c</data>
      <data key="d3">1236</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8872</data>
      <data key="d7">d31081ea0f0d44c0b297a0d2296288fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIUM AND VITAMIN D DEPLETION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcium and vitamin D depletion can occur after certain types of bariatric surgery, affecting bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8873</data>
      <data key="d7">4210e189ead143f7a195a0534c50a169</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUIDELINES ON VITAMIN D REPLACEMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Guidelines on vitamin D replacement provide recommendations for managing vitamin D levels in patients undergoing bariatric surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">60087d9d9e3b014675f0165172f59d1c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8874</data>
      <data key="d7">98a03fb5b7b6488ea07ea41f2614e652</data>
    </node>
