    <node id="TRASTORNO POR ATRAC&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TRASTORNO POR ATRAC&#211;N is an eating disorder that is characterized by recurrent episodes of binge eating, where individuals consume large quantities of food in a short period of time. Unlike other eating disorders, such as bulimia nervosa, individuals with trastorno por atrac&#243;n do not engage in subsequent purging behaviors or inappropriate compensatory actions. This disorder often leads to significant distress for those affected. In summary, trastorno por atrac&#243;n is defined by its compulsive eating episodes without the presence of purging, distinguishing it from other eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,ecf27310ce7cbfc335117dafa5d4eefb</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8878</data>
      <data key="d7">e66d51a31bb44e9c835635945c85be10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUJERES ADOLESCENTES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grupo demogr&#225;fico que presenta una prevalencia significativa de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, especialmente en pa&#237;ses occidentales.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8879</data>
      <data key="d7">843a2d1c60e24a72845292747826d1b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODELOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grupo profesional que parece estar m&#225;s afectado por trastornos de la conducta alimentaria debido a presiones sociales sobre la imagen corporal.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8880</data>
      <data key="d7">f9aff916193b4399a3b571a1628008ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATLETAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grupo profesional que tambi&#233;n muestra una mayor incidencia de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, posiblemente debido a la presi&#243;n para mantener un peso espec&#237;fico.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1598</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8881</data>
      <data key="d7">eb4be4a8fcde4bc497ead17460667670</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GIMNASTAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Grupo profesional que se encuentra en riesgo elevado de desarrollar trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, similar a modelos y atletas.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8882</data>
      <data key="d7">867cf60edc684bc2b66e0fd76a0fbe58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAJA AUTOESTIMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La baja autoestima es un factor de riesgo significativo para el desarrollo de trastornos de la conducta alimentaria, afectando a muchos pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8883</data>
      <data key="d7">e804d8359c1a41a6a762c53c05d2882b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBESIDAD INFANTIL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La obesidad infantil es un antecedente que puede aumentar el riesgo de desarrollar trastornos de la conducta alimentaria en la adolescencia.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8884</data>
      <data key="d7">f4ccb36a0890434695beeb3338cbfcb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES NEUROQU&#205;MICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las alteraciones neuroqu&#237;micas, como la disregulaci&#243;n de la serotonina, son factores biol&#243;gicos que pueden contribuir a los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8885</data>
      <data key="d7">9d5c95b7efd249ac8984ea9e4243a40b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTORES DE MAL PRON&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los factores de mal pron&#243;stico en los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria incluyen v&#243;mitos, conductas purgativas y p&#233;rdida de peso importante.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8886</data>
      <data key="d7">709ac8f6d7bf493299dcea6a46362efb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTORES DE BUEN PRON&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los factores de buen pron&#243;stico incluyen el inicio en adolescentes j&#243;venes y una duraci&#243;n corta de la enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d2">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8887</data>
      <data key="d7">9a4f8e133c59489792977ec82e8fc3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASOCIACI&#211;N AMERICANA DE PSIQUIATR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Psychiatric Association is a professional organization that publishes diagnostic criteria for mental disorders, including eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48</data>
      <data key="d3">1599</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8888</data>
      <data key="d7">87dc5a6e71cb4589a20792e9663307e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANSIEDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anxiety is another psychiatric condition frequently observed in patients with eating disorders, contributing to their overall psychological profile.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48</data>
      <data key="d3">1122</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8889</data>
      <data key="d7">616926b348e74e988b54997074e21680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRAUMAS PSICOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Psychological traumas can influence the development of eating disorders, affecting patients' mental health and coping mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8890</data>
      <data key="d7">501f1a00a15b47a6874bb15fd04c3536</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIN&#193;MICA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Family dynamics can significantly impact the psychological well-being of patients with eating disorders, often contributing to their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8891</data>
      <data key="d7">a722b6bf265545cfb85675392dec43fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSICOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PSICOTERAPIA es un tratamiento que implica la interacci&#243;n entre un paciente y un terapeuta, utilizado para abordar trastornos psicol&#243;gicos, incluyendo los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria. Este enfoque terap&#233;utico es fundamental en el tratamiento de los trastornos alimentarios, ya que se centra en tratar los problemas psicol&#243;gicos subyacentes y fomentar la recuperaci&#243;n del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8892</data>
      <data key="d7">c2a6e14f5a70486f878361adc69ec26b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N INICIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Initial assessment for patients with eating disorders includes various tests such as hemogram, glucose levels, and renal function tests.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8893</data>
      <data key="d7">65421fbbc3e840a59e1cadbab4147aea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRUEBAS A CONSIDERAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Subsequent tests for evaluating patients with eating disorders may include serum iron, hormonal levels, and gastrointestinal studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8894</data>
      <data key="d7">e7067219335d4e229c183553e1750a30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANIFESTACIONES CL&#205;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical manifestations of eating disorders are multisystemic due to malnutrition, affecting almost all parts of the body and potentially causing irreversible damage.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d3">1137</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8895</data>
      <data key="d7">2c9253967bec4f7680e5e3e462e94a3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiovascular alterations in patients with anorexia nerviosa include bradycardia, hypotension, and various electrocardiographic abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d3">1137</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8896</data>
      <data key="d7">50a63ae934c6412da9a24dcc2d012e60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS refer to a range of digestive issues commonly associated with anorexia nerviosa. These alterations include decreased gastrointestinal motility and delayed gastric emptying, which can significantly impact the digestive process. Additionally, these digestive disorders can affect nutrient absorption, potentially necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d3">1137</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8897</data>
      <data key="d7">78469c46fa96403f8cba2869bf1670e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTROPARESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastroparesis is a medical condition that affects the stomach muscles, preventing proper stomach emptying. It is often observed in diabetic patients and can lead to significant weight loss, particularly in cases such as anorexia nervosa. The condition is characterized by delayed gastric emptying, which can result in increased gastric residue, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Improvement in gastroparesis symptoms is typically achieved through nutritional rehabilitation and dietary adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d2">6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8898</data>
      <data key="d7">d97ef4c59bf443c3b537e3c66219f98c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NAS VISCERALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Visceral proteins are evaluated in the initial assessment to assess nutritional status and liver function in patients with eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8899</data>
      <data key="d7">67e08b7203064f18a9247bbd50a174c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO LIP&#205;DICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lipid studies are conducted to evaluate the fat levels in the blood, which can be affected by eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8900</data>
      <data key="d7">8a5accb13fae4410bd14dc66f0c93718</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCIONES RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Renal function tests are conducted to evaluate kidney health, which can be impacted by malnutrition in eating disorder patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8901</data>
      <data key="d7">36f8a0e5f6344f0d983e84b2baf5c11a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCIONES HEP&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Liver function tests are performed to assess the health of the liver, which can be affected by eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8902</data>
      <data key="d7">7b822ce33a19417e859fe9d6975166aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS ELEMENTAL DE ORINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urine elemental analysis is performed to assess metabolic and nutritional status in patients with eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8903</data>
      <data key="d7">8f61ec0935354decb56af742a488e413</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELECTROCARDIOGRAMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Electrocardiogram is a test used to monitor heart activity, which can be affected by eating disorders, particularly anorexia nerviosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8904</data>
      <data key="d7">6c46d78e18e94113b4cd6a2a96878b19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIERRO S&#201;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serum iron levels are tested to assess iron deficiency, which can occur in patients with eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8905</data>
      <data key="d7">64c311f78cf846b695d84972a817923b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE VITAMINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin levels are assessed to monitor nutritional deficiencies that can arise in patients with eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8906</data>
      <data key="d7">a12908c6c04c4ba29eed76e166e2c471</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMILASA S&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serum amylase levels are tested to evaluate pancreatic function, which can be affected by eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8907</data>
      <data key="d7">602ee9a300a44e04b3de94aacb0e9164</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIOS DEL TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastrointestinal studies are conducted to assess digestive health and complications in patients with eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8908</data>
      <data key="d7">debe12f950aa4e348c200488f4389528</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TC CRANEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cranial CT scan is used to assess brain health and detect any complications related to eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8909</data>
      <data key="d7">3564f1017011423eaaa8ce161f6a3642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECOCARDIOGRAMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Echocardiogram is used to assess heart structure and function, which can be affected by eating disorders.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8910</data>
      <data key="d7">efe029deab2a426a8ddf4785c7bca0b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An institution that may provide psychological and nutritional education to patients recovering from eating disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8911</data>
      <data key="d7">fbe033cfd7c14bec9b9c9b9a04f647ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCALOSIS METAB&#211;LICA HIPOCLOREMICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcalosis metab&#243;lica hipoclor&#233;mica is a metabolic disorder that can occur in patients with Bulimia Nervosa as a result of vomiting.</data>
      <data key="d2">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8912</data>
      <data key="d7">fbfaa39c8adc4c4590f2166bdaecb1cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMENORREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Amenorrhea is defined as the absence of menstruation and can manifest in two forms: primary and secondary. This condition is often observed in individuals with Anorexia Nervosa, where it is primarily linked to hormonal imbalances. In patients suffering from Anorexia Nervosa, the disruption of normal hormonal function can lead to the cessation of menstrual cycles, highlighting the significant impact of this eating disorder on reproductive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8913</data>
      <data key="d7">f1617284e406440f8b9c67cbd93a7850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDUCACI&#211;N PSICOL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Psicological education is crucial for patients recovering from eating disorders, helping them understand their conditions and develop coping strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8914</data>
      <data key="d7">d9065d8cab41484db8ffcd4d4a3fd097</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REVISI&#211;N DENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dental check-ups are recommended for patients with Bulimia Nervosa to monitor and address dental health issues caused by vomiting.</data>
      <data key="d2">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8915</data>
      <data key="d7">ce9bc0c4b82742ce95244be07aed3213</data>
    </node>
    <node id="17-BETA ESTRADIOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">17-Beta Estradiol is a form of estrogen used in hormone replacement therapy, which has been studied for its effects on bone mass in adolescents with Anorexia Nervosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d3">1588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8916</data>
      <data key="d7">f69ca219cbff4f34aa22b609d0cf7c48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHEAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate (DHEAS) is a hormone that has shown controversial results when administered alongside oral contraceptives in patients with Anorexia Nervosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d3">1588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8917</data>
      <data key="d7">9f50bd6f1ae54680b61fbb583d6cb78f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TERIPARATIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Teriparatide is a medication that has demonstrated significant improvement in bone mass and increased bone density in adult women suffering from Anorexia Nervosa after a short treatment period. This treatment is particularly beneficial for addressing the bone health challenges faced by women with this eating disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543,bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d3">1588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8918</data>
      <data key="d7">b4d8d70378be498cbcf57a3ede1d97c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BONE DENSITOMETRY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone densitometry is a diagnostic procedure recommended for patients with Anorexia Nervosa who have experienced amenorrhea for more than six months to assess bone density.</data>
      <data key="d2">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d3">1588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8919</data>
      <data key="d7">d60c0a6e31ae4a1692556fee330f54eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL REHABILITATION">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Nutritional rehabilitation involves the process of restoring nutritional health in individuals suffering from eating disorders, particularly anorexia nervosa. This approach aims to address the deficiencies and imbalances in nutrition that can arise from such disorders, facilitating recovery and promoting overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">0692eb750371d46b9fff71ec305df6ce,bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d3">1592</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8920</data>
      <data key="d7">52fed213fd274dfd8f789a7e932f12a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GHRELIN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ghrelin is a hormone that plays a significant role in regulating appetite and influencing various hormonal releases, particularly in patients with anorexia nervosa. Research has shown that ghrelin levels are elevated in individuals suffering from anorexia nervosa, indicating a state of negative energy balance. This elevation suggests that ghrelin may be involved in the physiological responses associated with this eating disorder, highlighting its importance in understanding appetite regulation and energy homeostasis in affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8921</data>
      <data key="d7">3dcb62526c8840d282a3ac5d4ad1193a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTROGENS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Estrogens are hormones whose production decreases in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa due to loss of weight and fat mass.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8922</data>
      <data key="d7">19ac0c6aeba447afbd6707a65e984254</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MENSTRUATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Menstruation recovery is an important indicator of healing in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8923</data>
      <data key="d7">8f66980bcec3494682b6fd2921534dda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RT3">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Reverse T3 (rT3) is a thyroid hormone that may be elevated in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, indicating metabolic adaptation to malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d3">1596</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8924</data>
      <data key="d7">0ba0abe01dd94f01becf4138e4707213</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOTIVACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Motivation is a key factor in the treatment of patients with eating disorders, influencing their willingness to normalize eating habits and collaborate in treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8925</data>
      <data key="d7">57d60f9994d04d23aefdf67ef4d61193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CREATININE EXCRETION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatinine excretion refers to the measurement of creatinine levels in urine collected over a 24-hour period. This metric is utilized to assess muscle mass in individuals, providing valuable insights into their overall health. Specifically, in patients with chronic liver disease, 24-hour urine samples of creatinine excretion serve as an important method for evaluating muscle mass, which can be affected by the condition. Thus, creatinine excretion is a significant indicator in both general health assessments and in the context of chronic liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5660be03d70d5dd506c197283dd79ae,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1132</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">8926</data>
      <data key="d7">6459d00a072841ccb4dfa1de60ef653e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="24-HOUR URINE TEST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The 24-hour urine test measures various substances, including creatinine, to evaluate muscle mass and nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5660be03d70d5dd506c197283dd79ae</data>
      <data key="d3">693</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8927</data>
      <data key="d7">ec30c7aad5b14d42890898aedc185a12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AN, which stands for Anorexia Nervosa, is a type of eating disorder that significantly impacts dietary habits and caloric intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6469f98d2161058fb7b214a1a800441,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">8928</data>
      <data key="d7">19a5ac0941dd4422b408a448df1e6c7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN&#218;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MEN&#218; refers to a planned list of foods designed to assist patients with eating disorders in establishing healthy eating habits. Additionally, it serves as a structured meal plan that adheres to dietary restrictions for patients undergoing dialysis, specifically focusing on low potassium and phosphorus intake. This dual purpose highlights the importance of tailored nutritional guidance for individuals with specific health needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d3">624</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8929</data>
      <data key="d7">4bdf1dba82654495a400aec4323d22dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN GRASAS SALUDABLES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alimentos ricos en grasas saludables, such as fatty fish and olive oil, are recommended for patients with bulimia nervosa. These foods provide essential nutrients and can support overall health while addressing the specific dietary needs of individuals dealing with this eating disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8930</data>
      <data key="d7">64e08255a61243c48fd7676a9870fb0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATRACONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Binge eating episodes are a significant concern for patients with bulimia nervosa, requiring careful dietary planning.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">8931</data>
      <data key="d7">8fc8981b43b942c0a5019edecee7d9d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAXANTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Laxantes are substances that play a significant role in altering bowel movements and are commonly used to treat constipation. They function through various mechanisms to facilitate bowel movements, making them an essential option for individuals experiencing this condition. However, laxantes can also impact the results of breath tests for carbohydrate malabsorption, which is an important consideration in clinical settings. Additionally, laxatives are often misused by patients with bulimia nervosa, leading to complications that can adversely affect their dietary needs. Overall, while laxantes serve a critical purpose in managing constipation, their misuse and potential effects on diagnostic tests highlight the need for careful monitoring and responsible use.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88,beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d3">1406</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">8932</data>
      <data key="d7">27d0f443b10142c09dacee24d9e8b20a</data>
    </node>
