    <node id="REFEEDING SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Refeeding syndrome is a potentially fatal condition that can arise when feeding is resumed in individuals who are malnourished. This syndrome is particularly relevant in the treatment of eating disorders, such as anorexia nervosa, and is also a significant concern for malnourished patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The condition underscores the risks associated with reintroducing nutrition to individuals who have been in a state of starvation or severe malnutrition, highlighting the need for careful management and monitoring during the refeeding process.</data>
      <data key="d2">0692eb750371d46b9fff71ec305df6ce,770e8796aac9c96d967ef99d1f307e06,a265c943c66b9cb5d09f89d40ddb995f</data>
