    </node>
    <node id="TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El tracto gastrointestinal es el sistema de &#243;rganos que se encarga de la digesti&#243;n y absorci&#243;n de nutrientes en el cuerpo humano.</data>
      <data key="d2">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d3">1002</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8986</data>
      <data key="d7">5a17b0f817be4635826eb7707b08c0d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTESTINO GRUESO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El intestino grueso es la parte del tracto gastrointestinal donde reside la mayor cantidad de bacterias y se lleva a cabo la absorci&#243;n de agua y electrolitos.</data>
      <data key="d2">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d3">1002</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8987</data>
      <data key="d7">fe02c82556bc4491afbae4d3641d1303</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EST&#211;MAGO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El est&#243;mago es un &#243;rgano del tracto gastrointestinal donde se inicia la digesti&#243;n de los alimentos y alberga diversas bacterias, incluyendo Helicobacter pylori.</data>
      <data key="d2">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d3">1810</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8988</data>
      <data key="d7">bb001b2ce37a4aed865c741c1caf368b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUODENO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The duodeno, or duodenum, is the first part of the small intestine, playing a crucial role in the digestive process. It is primarily responsible for the chemical digestion of food, aided by enzymes and bile. In addition to its digestive functions, the duodeno is significant for nutrient absorption, specifically calcium and copper. Furthermore, it is the site where the final digestion of carbohydrates occurs, highlighting its importance in the overall digestive system.</data>
      <data key="d2">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d3">620</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">8989</data>
      <data key="d7">9c126ae9343047dd94cdb1192410dbc5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARTO NATURAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parto natural (natural birth) is associated with the newborn acquiring a microbiota similar to that of the mother's vaginal microbiota.</data>
      <data key="d2">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d3">661</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8990</data>
      <data key="d7">36f540fed2bc48dba94b8e028856acce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTANCIA NATURAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactancia natural (natural breastfeeding) is a key factor in the development of the newborn's intestinal microbiota, providing a continuous supply of beneficial bacteria.</data>
      <data key="d2">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d3">661</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">8991</data>
