    <node id="ACINETOBACTER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria known for its role in causing infections, particularly in healthcare settings, where it poses a significant risk to patients with invasive devices. In addition to its pathogenic potential, Acinetobacter has been positively associated with obesity and has been the subject of research concerning metabolic health and obesity. This dual role highlights the importance of understanding Acinetobacter not only as a potential infectious agent but also in the context of metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">05360f0d7332f748b436b98d64e4eeb7,959173b0e9d9c5ea2edabff579240462,be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a</data>
