    </node>
    <node id="PSEUDOALTEROMONAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudoalteromonas is a genus of bacteria that has garnered attention for its potential implications in health and disease. Notably, it has been positively associated with obesity, suggesting a significant role in metabolic processes. Research surrounding Pseudoalteromonas continues to explore its various effects on human health, highlighting its importance in understanding the complex interactions between gut microbiota and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">05360f0d7332f748b436b98d64e4eeb7,959173b0e9d9c5ea2edabff579240462</data>
