    <node id="SHIGELLA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Shigella is a genus of bacteria known for causing bacillary dysentery, which is characterized by diarrhea that contains blood and mucus. Additionally, Shigella has been positively associated with obesity, indicating a potential link between this bacterial genus and weight-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">959173b0e9d9c5ea2edabff579240462,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
