    <node id="E. COLI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">E. coli, or Escherichia coli, is a species of bacteria that has a complex relationship with human health. It has been positively associated with obesity, indicating that certain strains may play a role in weight regulation. Additionally, some strains of E. coli can be utilized as probiotics, contributing to gut health by promoting a balanced microbiome. This dual nature highlights the importance of distinguishing between different strains of E. coli, as their effects on health can vary significantly.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a1ea1a4dfb1b591756a8dc60f504da2,959173b0e9d9c5ea2edabff579240462</data>
      <data key="d3">1025</data>
