      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gordon JI is a researcher dedicated to exploring the role of gut microbes in human health and obesity. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of host-bacterial mutualism within the human intestine, highlighting the intricate relationships between humans and their gut microbiota. Through his work, Gordon JI aims to shed light on how these microbial communities influence various aspects of health, particularly in relation to obesity.</data>
