    <node id="INFLAMMATORY BOWEL DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) refers to a group of inflammatory conditions affecting the colon and small intestine, characterized by chronic inflammation of the gastrointestinal tract. This group primarily includes Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis. The development and progression of IBD may be influenced by gut microbiota, highlighting the complex interplay between the immune system and the microorganisms residing in the gut.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d7ac56ec0eb2f724386a39de8551134,23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40,b3ddc7e512f6a789fa4cef18e7b18fab,e7a633f303c813ee9f0b7f55e7a0968a</data>
