    <node id="UNIDADES DE INTERCAMBIO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Unidades de intercambio are units used in dietary planning to help manage carbohydrate intake, particularly for individuals with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e</data>
      <data key="d3">872</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9250</data>
      <data key="d7">31f5a95352c640ee9ecf9f9e60d89610</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cereales, or cereals, are grains that serve as a staple in many diets around the world, providing essential carbohydrates and nutrients. They are often combined with legumes to enhance the protein quality in diets. Cereales are particularly important in a child's diet, as they offer vital nutrients necessary for growth and development. 

However, the purine content in different types of cereales can vary, with some having low levels that may impact uric acid levels in the body. Additionally, while cereales are generally considered non-dairy foods, they may contain galactose, which necessitates caution for individuals with galactosemia. 

Cereales are also permitted in modified diets and are recommended during episodes of diarrhea, with options such as rice, wheat, and oats suggested for their nutritional benefits. It is important to note that some cereales can contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. Overall, cereales are a fundamental part of many diets, but specific dietary restrictions must be considered for certain health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb,743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c,7d2050a2481adc105bdebbcf2af1a173,b5db5210dfb726bf3f6d3fae82598596,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978,ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79,e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">9251</data>
      <data key="d7">e7aac04659734719b40b00b808788581</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUB&#201;RCULOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TUB&#201;RCULOS, which include root vegetables such as potatoes and sweet potatoes, are gluten-free foods that serve as significant sources of carbohydrates in diets. These tubers are particularly suitable for celiac patients, providing essential nutrients without the presence of gluten.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821,e9d9dbd1ccc60737441dcf7bfeef638e</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
