    <node id="EASD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD) is an organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and management of diabetes. It provides comprehensive guidelines and evidence-based recommendations for diabetes care and research, aiming to improve outcomes for individuals affected by the condition. Through its initiatives, EASD plays a crucial role in shaping best practices in diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d2">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">871</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9259</data>
      <data key="d7">86c202bd7908496eaa3c4998ebfa256c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycemia refers to the presence of glucose in the blood, a critical factor in managing diabetes. It is essential for individuals with diabetes to carefully monitor their glycemia levels, particularly during pregnancy and lactation, to ensure proper health outcomes for both the mother and the child.</data>
      <data key="d2">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">873</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9260</data>
      <data key="d7">559e044026a0453398c08c18b63631a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGH GLYCEMIC INDEX FOODS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">High glycemic index foods are those that cause a rapid increase in blood sugar levels and are generally advised to be limited in a diabetic diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">873</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9261</data>
      <data key="d7">99523e9d87824d028c37994cf3a68203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOW GLYCEMIC INDEX FOODS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Low glycemic index foods are those that result in a slower, more gradual increase in blood sugar levels, recommended for better glycemic control.</data>
      <data key="d2">c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">873</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9262</data>
      <data key="d7">2ab8274a53f54de68951326af762587c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLYUNSATURATED FATTY ACIDS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyunsaturated fatty acids, such as omega-3s, are beneficial fats that can help reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease, particularly in diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">c98ed25e58194d76463e3553fb3f3c15</data>
      <data key="d3">987</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9263</data>
      <data key="d7">2988dcbf066e4867941f1a9a8aef93c6</data>
