    </node>
    <node id="GESTATIONAL DIABETES MELLITUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gestational Diabetes Mellitus is a form of diabetes that occurs during pregnancy and requires specific dietary management to ensure the health of both the mother and the baby.</data>
      <data key="d2">cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
      <data key="d3">141</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">9361</data>
      <data key="d7">ae8fc9f9ef9d4df2827efe5b0e4817e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition therapy encompasses dietary interventions designed to address the specific nutritional needs of individuals facing various health challenges. It plays a crucial role in managing diabetes by focusing on dietary strategies that aim to improve health outcomes for those affected by the condition. Additionally, nutrition therapy is also vital for cancer patients, particularly those undergoing treatment for esophageal cancer, as it helps manage their unique nutritional requirements during a critical time in their health journey. Overall, nutrition therapy serves as an essential component in the holistic management of both diabetes and cancer, promoting better health and well-being for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7</data>
      <data key="d3">141</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">9362</data>
      <data key="d7">8e5553e02a3a471ea22517107a8d3c4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MATERNA AND NEWBORN OUTCOMES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Maternal and newborn outcomes refer to the health results for mothers and their babies, particularly in the context of managing gestational diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9363</data>
      <data key="d7">8f3151e4903a4123a518c25236047dff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY INTERVENTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary intervention refers to the changes made in a person's diet to manage health conditions, such as gestational diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
      <data key="d3">141</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
