    </node>
    <node id="RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED TRIALS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) are studies designed to randomly assign participants to various interventions in order to compare the outcomes of those interventions. These trials are commonly utilized in clinical research, particularly in the fields of nutrition and health, to assess the effects of different treatments or interventions on health outcomes. By employing randomization, RCTs aim to eliminate bias and ensure that the results are attributable to the interventions being tested, thereby providing robust evidence for their efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f06578cbfda22ce8c7d322ba35a93a1,cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
      <data key="d3">141</data>
