    <node id="GLYCOGEN PHOSPHORYLASE">
      <data key="d0">ENZYME</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycogen phosphorylase is the enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate, playing a key role in glucose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">24cc40d6e3b225945cd4d8c2484632e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1732</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9510</data>
      <data key="d7">535c3d88a37444e2a86d5e6b88b646c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMNIOCENTESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Amniocentesis is a medical procedure utilized for prenatal diagnosis, allowing for the analysis of amniotic fluid to detect various genetic conditions. This procedure can be employed to identify galactosemia, a metabolic disorder, as well as to detect the mutation associated with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI). Through the examination of the amniotic fluid, healthcare providers can gain valuable insights into the genetic health of the fetus.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,24cc40d6e3b225945cd4d8c2484632e4</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9511</data>
      <data key="d7">4a1a2f29d9564c6ab61cd1e2f23f6351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GSDIX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GSDIX is a condition that primarily affects the liver and is classified as the most common glycogen storage disease, with an estimated prevalence of 1 in 100,000 individuals. This condition arises from mutations in genes that code for phosphorylase b kinase, which plays a crucial role in glycogen metabolism. To manage the symptoms of GSDIX, particularly hypoglycemia, specific dietary treatments are required.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">1729</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">9512</data>
      <data key="d7">1223093ff3cc4c8cba1ea20558e33f8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHKA2">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">PHKA2 is a gene located on the X chromosome that codes for the hepatic isoform of the alpha subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXa.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">1729</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9513</data>
      <data key="d7">bb424ae0e12c4d66af6328fe8377199e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHKB">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">PHKB is a gene located on chromosome 16 that codes for the beta subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXb.</data>
