    <node id="GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycogen storage disease refers to a group of inherited metabolic disorders characterized by the abnormal storage of glycogen in the body. These disorders arise from enzyme deficiencies that disrupt the normal metabolism of glycogen, leading to its accumulation in various tissues.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bba475c47cc7e804e16c70787b247f9,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">1696</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">9517</data>
      <data key="d7">efd7fdc27e7e4fd5ab995df56c52ba44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA RICA EN HC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A diet rich in carbohydrates (HC) is recommended for patients with glycogen storage diseases to manage their condition and prevent hypoglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">1600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
