      <data key="d7">8de2c6a5c0f84a57a4a956a2a49abc26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROMOSOMA X">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Cromosoma X is one of the sex chromosomes in humans, playing a crucial role in genetic inheritance and the determination of biological sex. It is notable for housing several important genes, including those related to glycogen storage diseases. Additionally, the X chromosome contains the gene responsible for X-ALD (X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy), which is specifically located at the Xq28 position. This highlights the significance of Cromosoma X in both normal physiological functions and in the context of certain genetic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
      <data key="d3">1729</data>
