      <data key="d7">51f3595dfece4f6b9344a66840e17aa4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROMOSOMA 16">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Chromosome 16, also known as Cromosoma 16, is an autosome in humans that plays a significant role in genetic health. It contains genes associated with various diseases, including mutations linked to inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, this chromosome houses several genes related to glycogen storage diseases, highlighting its importance in metabolic functions and disease susceptibility.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40,eb1f89320202c337496dbad5ca168356</data>
