      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Pl&#225;tano is a type of banana, recognized as a fruit that is rich in dietary fiber. It is a food item that can contain varying levels of FODMAPs, which may impact individuals who are sensitive to these compounds. Additionally, Pl&#225;tano contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a</data>
      <data key="d3">833</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9546</data>
      <data key="d7">6c28364da8bb4e6eaa273dd8cf242ddd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COL DE BRUSELAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Col de Bruselas is a vegetable that contains a moderate amount of galactose, between 5-10 mg per 100 g.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9547</data>
      <data key="d7">395616b20e6648bc9052b80e676116f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#193;TIL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">D&#225;til, also known as date, is a sweet fruit commonly found in Middle Eastern cuisine. It is often consumed dried or used in various desserts. In terms of nutritional content, D&#225;til contains a higher amount of galactose, ranging from 10 to 20 mg per 100 grams. This fruit is not only a popular ingredient in culinary dishes but also offers specific nutritional benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9548</data>
      <data key="d7">463610c2897e452ea4825ecdcb670f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactosa-1-fosfato uridil transferasa (GALT) is an enzyme that converts galactose-1-phosphate and uridine diphosphate glucose into uridine diphosphate galactose and glucose-1-phosphate, and is expressed by the GALT gene on chromosome 9p13.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d3">845</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9549</data>
      <data key="d7">687186e9c03c464aa15e40829c25f3d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTITOL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactitol is a sugar alcohol that is produced from galactose through the action of aldose reductase. It is a metabolite that can accumulate in the lens of the eye, particularly in patients with galactosemia, a metabolic disorder characterized by the inability to properly metabolize galactose. This accumulation of galactitol is associated with the development of cataracts, a common complication in individuals with classic galactosemia and those with galactokinase deficiency. In patients with galactosemia, monitoring the levels of galactitol is important to assess dietary compliance and potential transgressions, as elevated levels can indicate toxicity and contribute to the risk of cataract formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">9550</data>
      <data key="d7">3f0b623f3c3a47b6a686f565d052608c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO GALACT&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cido galact&#243;nico is a metabolite that is formed from galactose and plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It is produced through the action of the enzyme galactose dehydrogenase and can be utilized in alternative metabolic pathways. This compound is integral to the overall process of galactose metabolization, highlighting its importance in biochemical processes related to this sugar.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">845</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9551</data>
      <data key="d7">af6682b2f76648f69eb728e407936f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#205;A LELOIR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Leloir pathway is a metabolic pathway that converts galactose into glucose, involving several enzymatic steps and is crucial for proper carbohydrate metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d3">845</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9552</data>
      <data key="d7">77e270b0d4ba4e85911b61d5bb185af9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN GALT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The GALT gene is responsible for encoding the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, and mutations in this gene can lead to galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d3">845</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9553</data>
      <data key="d7">89d07defaa684dd086d60974af150d6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOSA DESHIDROGENASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactosa deshidrogenasa, also known as galactose dehydrogenase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It catalyzes the oxidation of galactose, converting it into &#225;cido galact&#243;nico (galactonic acid). This enzymatic reaction is an important step in the metabolic pathway of galactose, facilitating its proper utilization in biological processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">845</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9554</data>
      <data key="d7">81e10934b43e41b6bd5fbc9986605d4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALDOSA REDUCTASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Aldose reductase is an enzyme that converts galactose into galactitol, playing a role in the polyol pathway of sugar metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9555</data>
      <data key="d7">a31cb7271d7a45d8ad0552b6ec52fae0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOKINASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactokinasa, also known as galactokinase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It catalyzes the conversion of galactose into galactose-1-phosphate (Gal-1-P), which is the first step in the metabolic pathway for galactose. This enzyme is particularly significant in the context of the genetic condition known as galactosemia, a disorder that affects the body's ability to process galactose properly. The activity of galactokinasa is essential for the proper metabolism of galactose, and deficiencies in this enzyme can lead to the accumulation of galactose in the body, resulting in various health complications associated with galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">9556</data>
      <data key="d7">1c44f1dd828e41e58738a932af37834f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISIOPATOL&#211;GIA Y DIAGN&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The section on physiopathology and diagnosis discusses the clinical implications and diagnostic criteria for galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase deficiency or galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9557</data>
      <data key="d7">33f8be2cf0f445b59c852cb5af275d78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase deficiency, also known as galactosemia, is a genetic disorder that affects the metabolism of galactose.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9558</data>
      <data key="d7">1a9f306452f947c9906aed856eb8050a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOPROTE&#205;NAS Y GLUCOL&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycoproteins and glycolipids are biomolecules formed from carbohydrates and play essential roles in cell structure and function.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9559</data>
      <data key="d7">65caa95807c24f32bf315cdcb64e0cf0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">LACTASA is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the digestion of lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. It hydrolyzes lactose into its constituent sugars, glucose and galactose, which are essential for energy derived from milk carbohydrates in mammals. A deficiency in lactase is commonly observed in patients with celiac disease, leading to lactose intolerance. Although lactase is not inducible, its production can adapt with continuous consumption of lactose, allowing some individuals to better digest lactose over time.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30</data>
      <data key="d3">843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">9560</data>
      <data key="d7">d8d58945d06f41cc9f7af858419ac0bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOSEMIA CL&#193;SICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactosemia cl&#225;sica es una enfermedad metab&#243;lica causada por un d&#233;ficit grave de la actividad enzim&#225;tica, con una incidencia de 1:50,000 reci&#233;n nacidos vivos y manifestaciones cl&#237;nicas que comienzan tras el nacimiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">9561</data>
      <data key="d7">391c6e319632470eb90c6153f76ae1a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GALT, or Galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase, is a crucial enzyme responsible for the metabolism of galactose. The gene GALT is essential for this process, and mutations in this gene lead to a condition known as classical galactosemia. The activity of the GALT enzyme is measured to diagnose galactosemia and its various forms. This enzyme plays a significant role in the proper processing of galactose, and its deficiency can result in serious metabolic complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9562</data>
      <data key="d7">6d31a76f6e8f4d759cc0cf33be096d76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERITROCITOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Erythrocytes, also known as red blood cells, play a significant role in the diagnosis of galactosemia by measuring GALT activity and galactose levels. These cells express the galactokinase gene (GALK1), which is crucial for galactose metabolism. Additionally, erythrocytes exhibit enzymatic activity related to galactose, further highlighting their importance in metabolic processes involving this sugar.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa,ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">840</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9563</data>
      <data key="d7">46a7e957e6654af9b99b27f63d0f1a97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NORTE DE EUROPA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Regi&#243;n donde se encuentra la mutaci&#243;n homocigota cl&#225;sica del gen GALT, t&#237;pica en la poblaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9564</data>
      <data key="d7">967fe55da1dc4e318f147d2865c4d4d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUR DE ALEMANIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Regi&#243;n donde se encuentra una mutaci&#243;n relativamente frecuente del gen GALT que causa galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9565</data>
      <data key="d7">72859f4ae4bc498a824d87896c80751c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CROACIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Pa&#237;s donde se encuentra una mutaci&#243;n del gen GALT que causa galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9566</data>
      <data key="d7">58c4e1c766c74dd28e19fb0a47f2be86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRISTALINO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El cristalino es una parte del ojo donde se depositan los efectos osm&#243;ticos del galactitol en pacientes con galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9567</data>
      <data key="d7">fcdba4ca75bc4ee188068c8192896189</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los niveles de galactosa libre plasm&#225;tica son un indicador clave en el diagn&#243;stico de galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9568</data>
      <data key="d7">1f1023bbaee34f878a68243242bfe3da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE GAL-1-P">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NIVEL DE GAL-1-P is a significant marker in the diagnosis and management of classic galactosemia. The levels of Gal-1-P in erythrocytes serve as an important indicator for diagnosing this condition. Additionally, monitoring the level of Gal-1-P is crucial for assessing the effectiveness of dietary restrictions in individuals affected by galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9569</data>
      <data key="d7">a11e6d31664e4503a94e407b8b01a883</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIAGN&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "DIAGN&#211;STICO" encompasses various processes related to the identification of medical conditions and diseases. Diagnosis of fructan intolerance typically involves dietary elimination and monitoring symptom improvement. In the context of inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosis is essential for effective management. Additionally, "diagn&#243;stico" refers to identifying elevated homocysteine levels, which is often done through plasma concentration tests. It also includes the identification of urea cycle disorders through biochemical tests and enzyme activity measurements. In the realm of food allergies and intolerances, diagnosis involves pinpointing the cause of symptoms through testing and ruling out other disorders. Furthermore, early diagnosis of classic galactosemia is critical to prevent complications. Overall, "DIAGN&#211;STICO" represents a comprehensive approach to identifying various health conditions through specific testing and assessment methods.</data>
      <data key="d2">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a,53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead,a519216aaee7bf8a1317f5d6b522c4b6,b1d588e0c9c4cef32da41373afbd1901,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">838</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9570</data>
      <data key="d7">a1cd7df58f3f47c28cf7d7aae915e6db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#914;-CETOGALACT&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#946;-Cetogalact&#243;nico es un metabolito en la v&#237;a de metabolizaci&#243;n de la galactosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9571</data>
      <data key="d7">f70006b7901149d5b03044e7f4b92768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XILULOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Xilulosa es un metabolito que se forma en la v&#237;a de las pentosas fosfato, relacionada con el metabolismo de la galactosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9572</data>
      <data key="d7">70f2acca75c0474a9ba0dc12d421dd92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#205;A DE LAS PENTOSAS FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La v&#237;a de las pentosas fosfato es una ruta metab&#243;lica que genera intermediarios importantes en el metabolismo de carbohidratos, incluyendo galactosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9573</data>
      <data key="d7">e5bcc7b60836486aaf2ae4c5abd2a69d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactosa-1-fosfato es un metabolito que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es crucial para su conversi&#243;n a glucosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9574</data>
      <data key="d7">fbd2b65bc34b4424a38bc335c1f44ea6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UDP-GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UDP-galactosa es un nucle&#243;tido que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es importante para la s&#237;ntesis de macromol&#233;culas glicosiladas.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9575</data>
      <data key="d7">e12139b412aa45488760185ca95939c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PIRUVATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Piruvato, also known as pyruvate, is a final metabolite in the glycolysis process, generated from glucose. It is also associated with the metabolism of galactose. Additionally, pyruvate is recognized for its potential benefits in enhancing energy production, particularly among athletes who may utilize it to improve their performance.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e8ab018917854d76a0137102e0392bd,449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
