      <data key="d7">0eacf2ca220140008e99c670fd1eb9dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACROMOL&#201;CULAS GLICOSILADAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las macromol&#233;culas glicosiladas son compuestos que se forman a partir de la uni&#243;n de az&#250;cares, incluyendo galactosa, y son importantes en la biolog&#237;a celular.</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9577</data>
      <data key="d7">478a46b6ab9c473e8e1fa72a5439735a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOL&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactol&#237;pidos are lipids that contain galactose, playing a significant role in the context of metabolic disorders associated with galactose. Additionally, they are essential components of cellular membranes, highlighting their importance in both metabolic processes and structural integrity within cells.</data>
      <data key="d2">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f,f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9578</data>
      <data key="d7">f4eeddda41f74de284df30992636be6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOPROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las galactoprote&#237;nas son prote&#237;nas que contienen galactosa y desempe&#241;an roles importantes en diversas funciones biol&#243;gicas.) &lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9579</data>
      <data key="d7">1c9902a4b4b44eb79f92c5619e157fc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFROAMERICANS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Afroamericans are a demographic group that is frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, which is associated with a specific genetic mutation.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9580</data>
      <data key="d7">340b27d7500c49c19082f3ca97d34857</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICANS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Africans, particularly those native to South Africa, are also frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, sharing the same genetic mutation as Afroamericans.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9581</data>
      <data key="d7">87274aab1bc240c3902ca71f9b730362</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUARTE VARIANT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Duarte variant is a biochemical variant of galactosemia characterized by partial residual GALT activity, leading to milder symptoms and complications compared to classical galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9582</data>
      <data key="d7">fb0b2e1d61db47dd860f73f505d97887</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEONATAL SCREENING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neonatal screening for galactosemia is a program that detects elevated levels of galactose and GALT enzyme activity in newborns to diagnose the disorder early.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9583</data>
      <data key="d7">21717b7b41ae4f9ab0e724da0d0f903e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AL&#201;LO DUARTE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Duarte allele is a genetic variant associated with a milder form of galactosemia, affecting GALT activity in individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9584</data>
      <data key="d7">ad785d81f06a4a89b1928f0023275aa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEONATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A neonate is a newborn baby, particularly one that is suspected to have galactosemia based on screening results or family history.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9585</data>
      <data key="d7">7f0b899e0a6548ccb9c3a3a58bc23f16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOPSIA CORIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chorionic villus sampling (biopsia corial) is a prenatal test that can be used to diagnose genetic disorders, including galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9586</data>
      <data key="d7">f6dbb50a26e14da99fb532c3eda3ed24</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAL-1-P">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gal-1-P, also known as Galactose-1-phosphate, is a significant metabolite measured in patients to monitor dietary compliance and metabolic control in individuals with galactosemia. This substance is particularly elevated in patients with certain forms of galactosemia, making it a crucial marker in the screening and management of the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">840</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9587</data>
      <data key="d7">9aa09e4f82d54fb38c5e61882d53c896</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL DE GALACTITOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The level of galactitol is monitored in patients with galactosemia to assess dietary compliance and potential complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9588</data>
      <data key="d7">7a4ea591a5074b4eab5abc6335772bd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMULAS DE SOJA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Soy formulas are recommended for infants with galactosemia as a substitute for milk-based formulas.</data>
      <data key="d2">743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9589</data>
      <data key="d7">0aa3ba9a496e41448f50c974fa8bc976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS" refers to a category of foods that are permissible for consumption by individuals with specific dietary restrictions. These allowed foods are tailored for patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption, adhering to established dietary guidelines. Additionally, for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, the permitted foods include natural dairy products, certain meats, and specific vegetables. Furthermore, for those with galactosemia, the allowed foods must contain less than 5 mg of galactose per 100 g. Lastly, "ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS" also encompasses foods suitable for a broad low-sodium diet, as detailed in Tabla 2. This comprehensive overview highlights the diverse dietary needs that "ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS" addresses, ensuring safe and appropriate food choices for individuals with these conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">01d788abeab4fc29c425bf27168356e2,743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950,e329b5d4c64709889680df357bd1cc09</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9590</data>
      <data key="d7">4c1bd14371004309b61185b293b8eef2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS PROHIBIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Foods that are prohibited for individuals with galactosemia, which contain more than 20 mg of galactose per 100 g.</data>
      <data key="d2">743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9591</data>
      <data key="d7">24e680f65a034252a6627703d0645263</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VISCERAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Viscera are non-dairy foods that may contain galactose and should be consumed with caution by individuals with galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9592</data>
      <data key="d7">72bf3fc8916546e4816ebadb95381c28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS MANUFACTURADOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Manufactured foods may contain galactose or lactose and should be carefully checked by individuals with galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9593</data>
      <data key="d7">c0881570568b4049bd387a9fc542eed8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALK1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GALK1 is the gene that encodes the enzyme galactokinase, located on chromosome 17q25.1.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d3">840</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9594</data>
      <data key="d7">bf3ac40cb6534a74a84fcd01e8b88bb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GALE is a gene located on chromosome 1p36 that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It encodes an enzyme known as uridin difosfato galactosa-4-epimerasa (GALE), which is essential for the proper processing of galactose in the body. Mutations or deficiencies in the GALE gene can lead to various clinical deficits, highlighting its importance in metabolic pathways related to galactose.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9595</data>
      <data key="d7">8e4c9d7af5514ba0ac17c27a6c15d012</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTONATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Galactonate is a compound derived from galactose that can be used for energy production.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9596</data>
      <data key="d7">fd8cc447528246a98e5449c11d718ec4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATARATAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cataracts are a condition that can develop due to the accumulation of galactitol in the lens of the eye, particularly in infants with galactokinase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9597</data>
      <data key="d7">1123eb4f736e48209075cbc4e9db3d45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA SIN L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A lifelong dairy-free diet is recommended for patients with galactokinase deficiency to prevent the formation of cataracts.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d3">839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9598</data>
      <data key="d7">f6913e380f2d40238a9f7eb5d8c1fb50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEUCOCITOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Leucocitos, also known as leukocytes, are white blood cells that play a crucial role in the immune response. They are involved in defending the body against infections and diseases. Additionally, leucocitos are affected by galactose metabolism, as they express the galactokinase gene (GALK1), which is essential for the metabolism of galactose. This connection highlights the dual role of leucocitos in both immune function and metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">840</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9599</data>
      <data key="d7">676d79b0de7041cf8968b5bdfeaeadaf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALDOB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">ALDOB is a gene located on chromosome 9q22.3 that encodes the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase. This enzyme plays a crucial role in fructose metabolism. Additionally, ALDOB is significant in the context of hereditary fructose intolerance, as it is the gene responsible for encoding the enzyme that is deficient in this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9600</data>
      <data key="d7">176512da35a74d778f541fc0080f3809</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT PERIF&#201;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">D&#233;ficit perif&#233;rico is a clinical form of galactosemia limited to erythrocytes and leukocytes, resulting in asymptomatic individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9601</data>
      <data key="d7">c3472d11a5b44d81b07918cfe0e5060a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT GENERALIZADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">D&#233;ficit generalizado is a clinical form of galactosemia where GALE activity is deficient in all tissues, resembling classic galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9602</data>
      <data key="d7">37aaf670248b4f48ad75747717015b8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT INTERMEDIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">D&#233;ficit intermedio is a clinical form of galactosemia with reduced GALE activity in erythrocytes and leukocytes, but not presenting acute symptoms at birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d3">837</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9603</data>
      <data key="d7">fbd0fe3c8b7f4e61b3f1ba2a5f565b62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA-1-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructose-1-phosphate is a compound that accumulates in the body due to the deficiency of the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">864</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9604</data>
      <data key="d7">d1e509f125ed426797e883d36947d97a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA-6-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructose-6-phosphate is an intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is affected by fructose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9605</data>
      <data key="d7">c03bb77f4fbd4854a0fd42dc3380bfc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA-1,6 BIFOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate is a key intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is produced from fructose-1-phosphate.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">864</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9606</data>
      <data key="d7">403f09ccd00149ec8e154d34f648984d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLICERALDEHIDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glyceraldehyde is a product of fructose metabolism that is involved in energy production.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">864</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9607</data>
      <data key="d7">28d8a430ac1242198a0bc0027d041d2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLICERALDEHIDO-3-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is an important intermediate in the glycolytic pathway derived from glyceraldehyde.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">864</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9608</data>
      <data key="d7">d6cf855836284f64919ffddc4cf8c9fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIHIDROXIACETONA FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is another product of fructose metabolism that plays a role in energy production.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">864</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9609</data>
      <data key="d7">911cbe0a9d8a431189ea904c43af0a11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCULO Y OTROS TEJIDOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Muscle and other tissues are involved in the metabolism of fructose and its intermediates.</data>
      <data key="d2">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9610</data>
      <data key="d7">77fc0fedb8a743a182af3a7288507e8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEREDITARY FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Hereditary fructose intolerance is a genetic condition that impairs the body's ability to metabolize fructose. This metabolic disorder can lead to a range of clinical manifestations, particularly complicating dietary management in infants. Individuals with this condition are unable to properly process fructose, which can result in various health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950,cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">9611</data>
      <data key="d7">531a883d3d53474184a389ab93893f89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA-1-FOSFATO ALDOLASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructosa-1-fosfato aldolasa is an enzyme involved in the metabolism of fructose, and its deficiency leads to hereditary fructose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d2">ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9612</data>
      <data key="d7">efc2b5508d774a0e8baca4a3d8e96369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS NO PERMITIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALIMENTOS NO PERMITIDOS" refers to foods that must be avoided by individuals with specific dietary restrictions. These prohibited foods include items that should be excluded from the diets of patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption, as outlined in dietary guidelines. Additionally, for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, prohibited foods encompass condensed milk, industrial ice creams, and certain processed meats. It is essential for those affected by these conditions to adhere to these restrictions to manage their health effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950,e329b5d4c64709889680df357bd1cc09</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9613</data>
      <data key="d7">bd46761b63c44eb98210608dbd3a9bf8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOLATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FOLATO is a B vitamin that plays a vital role in cell division, DNA synthesis, and repair. It is particularly crucial during periods of rapid growth, making it essential for various life stages. Dietary intake recommendations for folate emphasize its importance in maintaining overall health. Additionally, folate is recommended as a vitamin supplement for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, highlighting its significance in supporting health in specific populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728</data>
      <data key="d3">630</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9614</data>
      <data key="d7">874aed3692b44ccd9b6241c17572e2bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLEJO B">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">COMPLEJO B refers to a group of B-complex vitamins that play a crucial role in health and metabolic processes. These vitamins are often found to be deficient in cirrhotic patients, which can negatively impact their overall health and recovery. Additionally, Vitamin B complex is recommended for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, as it supports essential metabolic functions. Thus, COMPLEJO B is significant for both individuals with liver conditions and those with specific metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92,ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950</data>
      <data key="d3">848</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9615</data>
      <data key="d7">a14ce47e7f3a4feebfcb1824b793b175</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRUSELAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Bruselas is a city known for its diverse agricultural products including various vegetables and fruits.</data>
      <data key="d2">9d56eb0b82a3266e422a6a8ac5e63944</data>
      <data key="d3">1877</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">18</data>
      <data key="d6">9616</data>
      <data key="d7">d42b7855d6ea43ea9f265303524c3337</data>
