      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9660</data>
      <data key="d7">2bf6aa8be55e47bb8e58bdb8819e3ca8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHICLE &#171;SIN AZ&#218;CAR&#187;">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Chicle &#171;sin az&#250;car&#187; is sugar-free chewing gum, often used as a breath freshener.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9661</data>
      <data key="d7">9dfbdd8dbff14532808aa07bc170c364</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIVER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The liver is a vital organ that plays a significant role in various physiological processes. It is primarily affected by hemochromatosis, a condition that can lead to serious complications such as cirrhosis and hepatocarcinoma. Additionally, the liver is the primary site for gluconeogenesis, which is essential for glucose metabolism. This organ's functions are critical for maintaining overall metabolic homeostasis in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9662</data>
      <data key="d7">40ce45997fb8484e9303d75af6143cf3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRAIN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The brain is a vital organ that relies exclusively on glucose as its energy source.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1717</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9663</data>
      <data key="d7">b1fe17e56c4d48fb85f4c23ae41309df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTESTINE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The intestine is a crucial component of the digestive system, playing a significant role in the absorption of nutrients, which is essential for overall nutrition. Additionally, the intestine is involved in gluconeogenesis, contributing to the production of glucose in the body. However, it is important to note that the intestine can also be a site of inflammation and damage in individuals with celiac disease, where gluten triggers adverse reactions. Thus, the health of the intestine is vital not only for nutrient absorption and glucose production but also for preventing inflammatory conditions related to dietary components.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84,4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368,fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9664</data>
      <data key="d7">e781147fe68346d0ba2f7aa01b01b661</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSE-1,6-BISPHOSPHATASE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase is an enzyme that is a key regulatory step in gluconeogenesis, converting fructose-1,6-bisphosphate to fructose-6-phosphate.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9665</data>
      <data key="d7">fbc3fb370aae49bc8bfc2e4eb70f9b9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PYRUVATE CARBOXYLASE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pyruvate carboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of pyruvate to oxaloacetate, an important step in gluconeogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9666</data>
      <data key="d7">dea0b15c337242b7a7f0e3194857fb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLYCERALDEHYDE-3-PHOSPHATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is a three-carbon sugar that is an intermediate in both glycolysis and gluconeogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9667</data>
      <data key="d7">5216d7f7d68545eda554b14ba5825ccb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactate is a byproduct of anaerobic metabolism and can be converted back to glucose through gluconeogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9668</data>
      <data key="d7">1117683e917b46f786d0245ecb7ecc9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOSA-1,6-BIFOSFATASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructosa-1,6-bifosfatasa is a key enzyme in gluconeogenesis that catalyzes the conversion of fructose-1,6-bisphosphate to fructose-6-phosphate, and its deficiency leads to a specific metabolic disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">1734</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">9669</data>
      <data key="d7">289a4063c06845ebbf5f081b7a4bad80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETIL-COA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetyl-CoA is a central metabolite in energy production, formed from pyruvate, and plays a crucial role in the Krebs cycle. It serves as a key metabolic intermediate involved in various biochemical pathways, including those affected by Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD).</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9670</data>
      <data key="d7">3c395239ef3a4830a6b92c0244e46abe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALACETATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxaloacetate is a four-carbon molecule that is a key intermediate in the Krebs cycle and gluconeogenesis, formed from pyruvate.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9671</data>
      <data key="d7">0257547306664bdcb822bfbcde803c26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFOENOLPIRUVATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Phosphoenolpyruvate is an important intermediate in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, derived from oxaloacetate.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9672</data>
      <data key="d7">2c56fd50393142d7a51c50647a9fc28e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASPARTATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Aspartate, also known as aspartic acid, is an amino acid that can be synthesized from oxaloacetate. It plays a significant role in various metabolic processes, including the urea cycle and gluconeogenesis. Additionally, aspartate is recognized for its benefits in enhancing recovery after exercise, making it a valuable compound for athletes and individuals engaged in physical training.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9673</data>
      <data key="d7">551b81abe22d4b0f8f82185c24397fc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Malate is an intermediate in the citric acid cycle and gluconeogenesis, formed from oxaloacetate.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9674</data>
      <data key="d7">12ca6183c1bf4641b4220c45c59c41d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLICEROL-3-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycerol-3-phosphate is an intermediate in the conversion of glycerol to glucose and is involved in lipid metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9675</data>
      <data key="d7">b007cfb1bec746e4987d6be37fe36abc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIHIDROXIACETONA-FOSFATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is an intermediate in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, derived from glycerol-3-phosphate.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9676</data>
      <data key="d7">bab98fd733f6413bbeeda6b9ddc2525a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CICLO DE KREBS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Krebs cycle, also known as the citric acid cycle, is a key metabolic pathway that generates energy through the oxidation of acetyl-CoA.</data>
      <data key="d2">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d3">461</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9677</data>
      <data key="d7">f808b732cee74a65af1394f1c69a6f5b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMILASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Amilasa is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of starch into sugars, playing a crucial role in carbohydrate digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1736</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9678</data>
      <data key="d7">9a1ae0a2476046508b1581fc59da4a60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMIDON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Almidon is a polysaccharide that serves as a major carbohydrate storage form in plants, composed of amylose and amylopectin.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d3">1736</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9679</data>
      <data key="d7">60f5491d88434fc28d3c335ef28515a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISOMALTOSA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Isomaltosa is a disaccharide composed of two glucose units, which is produced during the digestion of starch. It plays a significant role in the digestion and absorption of carbohydrates, particularly through enzymatic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9680</data>
      <data key="d7">223e7a8754fd4b05b503a3c0fe0ec0ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALTOSA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Maltosa is a disaccharide composed of two glucose molecules, which is formed during the digestion of starch by the enzyme amylase. It plays a significant role in carbohydrate metabolism, highlighting its importance in the body's energy processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9681</data>
      <data key="d7">55c2a93481c64114ac35c103ad567304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTANOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructanos are carbohydrates composed of fructose units, functioning as storage carbohydrates in plants and synthesized by certain fungi and bacteria. These naturally occurring carbohydrates are commonly found in cereals and vegetables. However, it is important to note that fructans can lead to intolerance in some individuals when consumed in large quantities.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">9682</data>
      <data key="d7">d52dafb71abd4b09b0c56f04710d79a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SGLT1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SGLT1 is a sodium-glucose cotransporter that plays a crucial role in the absorption of glucose and galactose in the intestines. It is specifically the intestinal monosaccharide transporter that is influenced by mutations in the SLC5A1 gene. These mutations can result in a condition known as glucose-galactose malabsorption, which impairs the body's ability to absorb these essential sugars.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,e329b5d4c64709889680df357bd1cc09</data>
      <data key="d3">846</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9683</data>
      <data key="d7">aa0f1cb66b2c4236b9d9cf71bd500102</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUT5">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GLUT5 is a transporter protein that facilitates the absorption of fructose in the intestines.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d3">863</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9684</data>
      <data key="d7">65f4d0bdf7a941a49cb2656d36f58d77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENTEROCITOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterocytes are specialized cells lining the intestines that are involved in nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d3">620</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9685</data>
      <data key="d7">bf3c29e5f9bd4716b84f2fe64f0812ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VENA PORTA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The portal vein is a major vein that carries blood from the gastrointestinal tract to the liver for processing.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9686</data>
      <data key="d7">5f6ad297d19641a69e2ce0cc8f564160</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLIGOFRACTOSA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Oligofructosa are short-chain fructans recognized for their role as dietary fibers, offering a range of health benefits. This type of prebiotic fiber is particularly noted for its ability to support gut health and is commonly utilized in various dietary formulations.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a</data>
      <data key="d3">1678</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9687</data>
      <data key="d7">fc5aad0d09e042adbf8104bd1c208d8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALTODEXTRINAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Maltodextrins are carbohydrate polymers and polysaccharides that serve multiple purposes in the food and beverage industry. They are primarily used as food additives and are produced from starch through a process of partial hydrolysis. In sports drinks, maltodextrins play a crucial role by providing energy and enhancing the absorption of fluids. Additionally, they are significant in the digestion process, contributing to the overall nutritional value of various products.</data>
      <data key="d2">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1736</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">9688</data>
      <data key="d7">24300e88f09e4d7896896c8ad6d48a47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SACARASA-ISOMALTASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sacarasa-Isomaltasa is an enzyme that plays a vital role in carbohydrate metabolism by breaking down sugars, particularly sucrose and isomaltose. It catalyzes the hydrolysis of sucrose and products derived from starch digestion, such as isomaltose and various dextrins, specifically targeting their &#945;-1,6 bonds. This enzymatic activity is essential for aiding in digestion and facilitating the proper utilization of carbohydrates in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">6ff2742793c37a38db1c11c14d2a6629,a079902e52676a05df746098c930a0e7,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1754</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9689</data>
      <data key="d7">09aacfeb5b1f49d085009489ded02042</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BORDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Borde refers to the brush border of the intestinal epithelium, where nutrient absorption occurs.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9690</data>
      <data key="d7">f896a1f3af964dcba4f058e88b6b0913</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOPLASMA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citoplasma is the gel-like substance within cells where various cellular processes occur, including metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9691</data>
      <data key="d7">9a6864e54dec455882a262652e32849f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TREHALOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Trehalosa is a sugar composed of two glucose molecules, known for its role in energy storage and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9692</data>
      <data key="d7">0a1bec680b1e44ae9289cd1ad692244e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIOLES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Polioles are sugar alcohols used as sweeteners and are involved in carbohydrate metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">850</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9693</data>
      <data key="d7">b5528715569041c38112f726fa9b736b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANITOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mannitol is a type of polyol, specifically a sugar alcohol, that is commonly used as a sweetener. It possesses unique absorption characteristics in the intestine, which can be beneficial in certain applications. However, it is important to note that mannitol may cause digestive issues for some individuals, highlighting the need for caution in its consumption.</data>
      <data key="d2">f713611b23199b8a9eb9c28377b9f128,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9694</data>
      <data key="d7">a45af8ed80a84546a63097b197cd4156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALTITOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Maltitol is a sugar alcohol used as a sugar substitute, known for its lower caloric content.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9695</data>
      <data key="d7">6bbae5e8bb9b412696a8c38d7559c184</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XILITOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Xilitol is a sugar alcohol commonly used as a sweetener. It is known for its dental health benefits, making it a popular choice in products aimed at promoting oral hygiene. However, it is important to note that xylitol may cause digestive discomfort in some individuals, particularly when consumed in larger quantities.</data>
      <data key="d2">f713611b23199b8a9eb9c28377b9f128,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9696</data>
      <data key="d7">759a30617b134751a9a3123cda44a108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FOS, or Fructooligosaccharides, are short-chain fructans that serve as prebiotic fibers, promoting gut health. They are commonly utilized in various dietary products due to their beneficial effects on the digestive system. FOS are recognized for their ability to enhance the growth of beneficial gut bacteria, thereby contributing to overall digestive wellness.</data>
      <data key="d2">751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">780</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9697</data>
      <data key="d7">d545e8ca2ac045b6832d4b2f1f500ee8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GOS (Galactooligosaccharides) are short-chain galactose polymers that are not digested in the intestine and have prebiotic properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1523</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9698</data>
      <data key="d7">b40b745c9f0d48ce97da6bb2c2e198e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGCC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AGCC, or short-chain fatty acids, are produced during the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates and sugars in the colon. These fatty acids play a significant role in gut health by contributing to the maintenance of a healthy gut microbiome. Additionally, AGCC are involved in the reabsorption of water and sodium in the colon, highlighting their importance in overall digestive health and fluid balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9699</data>
      <data key="d7">931a9d39262a4e51881af8283db1a978</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Digesti&#243;n is the process of breaking down food into nutrients that can be absorbed by the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">893</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9700</data>
      <data key="d7">b5b108134b054cf49b63b52a1a879295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Absorci&#243;n is the process by which nutrients from digested food are taken up into the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">893</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9701</data>
      <data key="d7">73516f1c0d644907bbd549bd15f2f7b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENZIMAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Enzymas are biological catalysts that play a crucial role in facilitating biochemical reactions within the body. They are primarily proteins that catalyze chemical reactions, including the digestion of carbohydrates and fats. Enzymas are present in various bodily fluids, such as chyle, where they assist in the digestion of nutrients, ensuring efficient metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1736</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9702</data>
      <data key="d7">6c1a65cb2fc342f594ace73dcd901f9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#914;-HIDROLASAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#946;-hidrolasas are enzymes that hydrolyze &#946;-glycosidic bonds in carbohydrates, playing a key role in their digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9703</data>
      <data key="d7">f68b20c659ae485c9a4b79552e0056a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLORA BACTERIANA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FLORA BACTERIANA refers to the community of bacteria present in the gut, which plays a vital role in the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates. This intestinal flora is unique to each individual and is essential for maintaining digestive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">1004</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9704</data>
      <data key="d7">b8c9186f675a4a0cbd84ef98c5ec375b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISTENSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Distensi&#243;n is a condition characterized by swelling or bloating in the abdomen, which can result from the accumulation of gas or fluid. This condition may also arise specifically from the buildup of undigested carbohydrates in the digestive system.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9705</data>
      <data key="d7">2198a0f03e0b4fa5a43f34e1672ccf03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALDIGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Maldigesti&#243;n is the inadequate digestion of food, which can lead to symptoms such as bloating and discomfort.</data>
      <data key="d2">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d3">822</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9706</data>
      <data key="d7">0ddf5302b1214f78a4b1d5d6c07d643e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROFLORA COL&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Microflora col&#243;nica refers to the bacteria present in the colon that play a crucial role in the fermentation of undigested sugars.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1735</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9707</data>
      <data key="d7">0c8eba18d07945548e5657adbb0fd4fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEST DEL ALIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Test del Aliento" is a diagnostic procedure designed to identify carbohydrate malabsorption, specifically focusing on malabsorption of fructose. This test measures the levels of hydrogen and methane in the breath after the ingestion of fructose. By analyzing these gas levels, healthcare professionals can confirm the presence of fructose malabsorption in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">9708</data>
      <data key="d7">df49ca60d4c54cddbb2931d9f39e7240</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUMULACI&#211;N INTRALUMINAL DE AZ&#218;CAR NO DIGERIDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Accumulation of undigested sugar in the intestinal lumen can lead to symptoms of distension and diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9709</data>
      <data key="d7">4862e5d2a5f946f6a1d6946edb8d9db0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IRRITACI&#211;N REGI&#211;N ANAL Y PERIN&#201;">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Irritation in the anal and perineal region can occur due to the acidic nature of the stool resulting from malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9710</data>
      <data key="d7">0a82f95be51549eeb47e0d797f22bddb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDR&#211;GENO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hydrogen is a gas produced during the fermentation of carbohydrates in the colon, which is measured in breath tests for diagnosing malabsorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9711</data>
      <data key="d7">3330a698540a477fa710becd9afa7769</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METANO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Methane is another gas produced during fermentation in the colon, which can also be measured in breath tests.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9712</data>
      <data key="d7">7426e0831eec42198d1e01d64588d32b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREPARACIONES PARA COLONOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Preparaciones para colonoscopia are procedures that can affect the microbiota and should be avoided before breath tests.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9713</data>
      <data key="d7">d7dcabdcdce2419aafe8cdca245f6976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA BAJA EN HC FERMENTABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dieta baja en HC fermentables is a dietary approach recommended before breath tests to ensure accurate results.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d3">1737</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9714</data>
      <data key="d7">a3ef7b7c1bfa49d6af553132f34a5416</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LCT">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">Long-chain triglycerides (LCT) are fats that play a crucial role in providing essential fatty acids, particularly in infant nutrition. However, they may also have adverse effects on liver function in patients suffering from chronic pancreatitis. Additionally, the LCT gene is significant as it encodes the lactase enzyme, which is essential for the digestion of lactose. This gene is responsible for the production of lactase, enabling the breakdown of lactose in the body. Thus, LCT encompasses both dietary fats important for nutrition and a gene vital for lactose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">814</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">9715</data>
      <data key="d7">38cf580d72244ce785b8890848835165</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Africa has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, ranging from 65-75%.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9716</data>
      <data key="d7">769d7354482f4abfbceea956aa8a3738</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Asia has the highest prevalence of lactose intolerance, exceeding 90%.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9717</data>
      <data key="d7">6ec6a1bae42d44c698387c6a5c5f0ff8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIVE AMERICANS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Native Americans have a very high prevalence of lactose intolerance, estimated at 90-95%.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9718</data>
      <data key="d7">edb110b9661945a4a1d4e919df1f1e16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HAPLOTYPES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Haplotypes are genetic variations associated with lactase persistence in different populations.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9719</data>
      <data key="d7">21e31637e4524d418715529c90781f4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) are genetic variations that influence lactase expression and persistence.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9720</data>
      <data key="d7">8bc17d06e50942398d4d975139d23e4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOLACTASIA DEL ADULTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipolactasia del adulto es la causa m&#225;s frecuente de intolerancia a los hidratos de carbono, t&#237;pica en ni&#241;os mayores y adultos.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">850</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9721</data>
      <data key="d7">2410b46420834c8a8ddc8515dbfa1891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERIODO PERINATAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El per&#237;odo perinatal es el tiempo alrededor del nacimiento, donde la expresi&#243;n de lactasa aumenta.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">843</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9722</data>
      <data key="d7">cac4c4eae0ec4b87b80d97e5eef3e24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO IRRITABLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "S&#237;ndrome de Intestino Irritable" (Irritable Bowel Syndrome, IBS) is a common gastrointestinal disorder characterized by a range of symptoms including cramping, abdominal pain, bloating, gas, and alterations in bowel habits such as diarrhea or constipation. It is classified as a functional gastrointestinal disorder, meaning that it affects the normal functioning of the digestive system without any identifiable structural abnormalities. Symptoms often worsen after meals and can include abdominal pain and urgency to defecate.

Diagnosis of IBS requires differentiation from other conditions, such as lactose intolerance and celiac disease, as it can exhibit similar symptoms. Additionally, IBS can be influenced by food intolerances and may exacerbate symptoms related to fructose malabsorption. Current research is exploring potential treatments for IBS, including the use of probiotics, to help manage its symptoms effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c,19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,5a1ea1a4dfb1b591756a8dc60f504da2,7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f,9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1,e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d3">850</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">9723</data>
      <data key="d7">cbef16e332cd4ff08d62c83dbf61927d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIMORFISMOS DE NUCLE&#211;TIDO &#218;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los polimorfismos de nucle&#243;tido &#250;nico son variaciones gen&#233;ticas que afectan la expresi&#243;n del gen LCT y la persistencia de lactasa.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea</data>
      <data key="d3">814</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9724</data>
      <data key="d7">078c0a402654405190094b910b50899e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTOLERANCIA A LACTOSA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Lactose intolerance is a condition known as "INTOLERANCIA A LACTOSA," where individuals are unable to properly digest lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. This condition can also manifest as a secondary issue for patients who have celiac disease, indicating a potential link between the two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">19e349f627670b1a9ccfa5d10f86bbea,e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d3">850</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9725</data>
      <data key="d7">0f867b3cfa454dd19e7d5a37b1ed2c85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FINLAND">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Finland is a country where the majority of patients with congenital lactase deficiency have been described.</data>
      <data key="d2">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">814</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9726</data>
      <data key="d7">496c20360d154243a7c17a0e3c6e2a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactose Intolerance is a common condition affecting approximately 10% of the population, characterized by the inability to digest lactose, a sugar found in milk. This condition arises from a deficiency in the enzyme responsible for breaking down lactose, leading to various gastrointestinal symptoms after the consumption of dairy products. Individuals with lactose intolerance often experience discomfort and digestive issues, which can also impact their calcium intake from dairy sources. Overall, lactose intolerance presents significant challenges for those affected, particularly in managing their diet and ensuring adequate nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90,bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922,ccd3c800d2985d4ad5e2c8d6e88b1b68,e119877a92b580500f5e5b0307401732,e3203d9f5bd82749de9eee35c52c67ce,fa4851ce095f27e98350dcb826e5b09c</data>
      <data key="d3">811</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">9727</data>
      <data key="d7">bedef4fc20e64575aa8b5ebd8e44ffc1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTASE DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactase deficiency refers to the reduced activity of the lactase enzyme, which can lead to lactose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d2">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">814</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9728</data>
      <data key="d7">0b5b75c23cf34e21a8c0e9e87bb4cea4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CELIAC DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Celiac disease is an autoimmune disorder triggered by the ingestion of gluten, which leads to damage in the small intestine. This damage can result in malabsorption of essential nutrients, including calcium, thereby impacting bone health and potentially leading to various nutritional deficiencies. Additionally, the condition can cause secondary lactose intolerance due to the impairment of the intestinal lining. Celiac disease manifests through a range of gastrointestinal and extraintestinal symptoms, necessitating a strict gluten-free diet to manage the disorder and prevent further complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821,17593b5969d4126aef1c56a7d32dc922,3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922,e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">43</data>
      <data key="d6">9729</data>
      <data key="d7">d5bd6808230140e0bfd9df9e6e6a5cfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABDOMINAL PAIN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Abdominal pain is a symptom that can arise from lactose intolerance due to the inability to digest lactose properly.</data>
      <data key="d2">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">811</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9730</data>
      <data key="d7">b344b12baa3943f48b5556aa05077f9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METEORISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Meteorism, or bloating, is a symptom that can occur in individuals with lactose intolerance after consuming lactose.</data>
      <data key="d2">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">811</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9731</data>
      <data key="d7">51a826a365f044fa848d6235483683cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOSE ELIMINATION DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A lactose elimination diet is a method used to diagnose lactose intolerance by removing lactose from the diet and observing symptom resolution.</data>
      <data key="d2">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">811</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9732</data>
      <data key="d7">a3cbebf2bae648b0a0c5bd246be32d26</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYDROGEN BREATH TEST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The hydrogen breath test is a non-invasive diagnostic procedure utilized to assess lactose intolerance. This test measures hydrogen levels in the breath following the ingestion of lactose. By analyzing the hydrogen concentration, healthcare providers can determine whether an individual has difficulty digesting lactose, thereby diagnosing lactose intolerance effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d3">811</data>
