    </node>
    <node id="DIARRHEA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">Diarrhea is a common condition that can arise in various medical contexts. It frequently occurs as a complication in patients undergoing antineoplastic treatment, necessitating dietary adjustments and careful management to mitigate its effects. Additionally, diarrhea is a prevalent symptom associated with celiac disease, typically triggered by the consumption of gluten. This highlights the importance of understanding the underlying causes of diarrhea in different patient populations to provide appropriate care and dietary guidance.</data>
      <data key="d2">2194de4eaed685b07d8f4c7a397de0ce,3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
