    <node id="NUTRITIONAL OBJECTIVES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional objectives are designed to prevent severe complications associated with hereditary hemochromatosis through specific dietary recommendations and management strategies. Additionally, these objectives emphasize the importance of managing lactose intake to alleviate symptoms while ensuring that individuals receive adequate nutrition. Furthermore, they focus on reducing the intake of fructose and sorbitol to help alleviate symptoms in individuals with dietary intolerances. Overall, the nutritional objectives encompass a comprehensive approach to dietary management aimed at improving health outcomes for individuals with various dietary needs and conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5,83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271,fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
