    <node id="EMBUTIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">EMBUTIDOS are processed meats that are generally advised to be limited in children's diets due to various health concerns. These meats can sometimes contain lactose and may also include gluten, which necessitates caution for individuals with celiac disease, depending on the manufacturer's information. EMBUTIDOS typically have a high sodium content and are discouraged in diets that require gluten control, as they may contain gluten. Nutritionally, they provide 2.4 mg of iron per 100 grams, but their high fat content raises concerns, despite having an acceptable phosphorus ratio. Overall, dietary guidelines recommend that processed meats like EMBUTIDOS should be consumed occasionally and in moderation, and they are not permitted in modified diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,08edfb59071449728499ca59eb51ac84,26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81,347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb,61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,6ff2742793c37a38db1c11c14d2a6629,7d2050a2481adc105bdebbcf2af1a173,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728</data>
