    <node id="TEST DE HIDR&#211;GENO ESPIRADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TEST DE HIDR&#211;GENO ESPIRADO" is a diagnostic method utilized to assess various gastrointestinal conditions. Primarily, it is employed to diagnose lactose intolerance by measuring the amount of hydrogen present in the breath following the ingestion of lactose. Additionally, the test serves as a tool to confirm glucose-galactose malabsorption by evaluating hydrogen levels after the consumption of sugar. This dual application highlights the test's significance in identifying different types of carbohydrate malabsorption issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd,e329b5d4c64709889680df357bd1cc09</data>
      <data key="d3">844</data>
