    </node>
    <node id="POL&#205;MEROS DE GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pol&#237;meros de glucosa are complex carbohydrates that consist of glucose polymers. They are particularly relevant in dietary considerations for individuals with specific metabolic conditions. For those with fructosa malabsorption, it is advised to avoid these polymers due to potential adverse effects. Conversely, in certain dietary treatments, particularly in special situations, pol&#237;meros de glucosa are added to liquids to enhance energy intake. Additionally, they play a crucial role in the dietary management of patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease, where they are utilized to prevent catabolism. Thus, while they can be beneficial in specific contexts, caution is warranted for individuals with certain metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e,5e5296bf59e1f2b0fbeace9cc0e62ef5,91c1a9b0c0d7cb718d7711ef7384a142</data>
      <data key="d3">800</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9768</data>
      <data key="d7">395f6e8c7dd44f3886c066ed82eefc96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REHIDRATACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rehidrataci&#243;n refers to the process of restoring fluids, which is crucial for individuals experiencing diarrhea due to malabsorci&#243;n de fructosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e</data>
      <data key="d3">862</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9769</data>
      <data key="d7">6b3c5d9fc55f40f88b9929298989ddfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SII">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SII, or Irritable Bowel Syndrome, is a common functional gastrointestinal disorder that affects the large intestine. It is characterized by a range of symptoms including cramping, abdominal pain, bloating, gas, and alterations in bowel habits such as diarrhea or constipation. The condition can be influenced by the intake of certain carbohydrates, particularly fructans, fructose, and sorbitol, which may trigger or exacerbate symptoms. Effective management of SII often requires careful dietary adjustments to minimize discomfort and maintain digestive health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6886c5b652319bea0ba2427a3fdbf701,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead,fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">9770</data>
      <data key="d7">c7924661736548c9b3358b166fdda20b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTARY PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alimentary products refer to food items that may contain varying levels of fructose and sorbitol, impacting dietary intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">849</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9771</data>
      <data key="d7">88941bb24cf54aa5b8ff4907524dc01f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIGHT PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Light products are food items marketed as low-calorie, which may contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">849</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9772</data>
      <data key="d7">7a55a030ae154ed4af72f9d3505c4bdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETIC PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetic products are specially formulated foods that may still contain fructose and sorbitol, impacting those with intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">850</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9773</data>
      <data key="d7">9f9f229389084bdc866158dd46e6a9af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUIT JUICES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fruit juices often contain high levels of fructose and can exacerbate symptoms in individuals with dietary intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">849</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9774</data>
      <data key="d7">da1a823b50614b3ca754c4d0c5f545d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATIENTS WITH INTESTINAL DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients with intestinal diseases may require dietary adjustments to manage symptoms related to fructose and sorbitol intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d3">1643</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9775</data>
      <data key="d7">82c2c9b8a8e24ad4b1982338e01ec6f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FRUCTANOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Foods high in fructans include wheat and certain vegetables, which can lead to digestive issues for some individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9776</data>
      <data key="d7">97cc6e3f16d642a4933286eb3284ee9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FODMAP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FODMAP refers to a group of short-chain carbohydrates that are poorly absorbed in the small intestine and can lead to digestive issues in some individuals, particularly those with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) and Crohn's disease. These fermentable carbohydrates can trigger gastrointestinal symptoms, making them a significant focus of dietary recommendations for individuals sensitive to them. The study of FODMAPs is also relevant in the context of gluten sensitivity, as they can exacerbate symptoms in susceptible individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">1d7ac56ec0eb2f724386a39de8551134,21dc8cb1a5078e23dae18b9c62b05625,527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1,53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d3">833</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">9777</data>
      <data key="d7">91dee41614df4f0b95368ebc48802cc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSIBILIDAD VISCERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Visceral sensitivity refers to the heightened response of individuals to gastrointestinal stimuli, which may contribute to symptoms of intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d2">79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9778</data>
      <data key="d7">1ed3ad6568e44cdbb6d2e1cbbb14a521</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS PROCESADOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">ALIMENTOS PROCESADOS, or processed foods, are often characterized by their high phosphorus content, primarily due to the additives used in their production. As a result, these foods should be limited in renal diets to promote better health outcomes for individuals with kidney issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81,79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">9779</data>
      <data key="d7">a260fc640d4a4a948155e99a651dd6f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RA&#205;Z DE ACHICORIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ra&#237;z de achicoria is a food item that is high in fructans and can contribute to FODMAP-related digestive symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246</data>
      <data key="d3">833</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9780</data>
      <data key="d7">6c788349b8f84772866d89234d1d1a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CENTENO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Centeno, also known as rye, is a cereal grain that contains gluten, making it unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. It can also contain fructans, which may contribute to digestive issues related to FODMAPs. As such, those with gluten sensitivities or FODMAP-related digestive concerns should avoid consuming centeno.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9781</data>
      <data key="d7">7bcd0e17e14e4a93a5c562570d410e4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEBOLLINO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cebollino is a food item that contains fructans and can affect those with FODMAP intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246</data>
      <data key="d3">833</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">9782</data>
      <data key="d7">d6d0abce0f894e8293d49770fc60cc3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AVENA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Avena, commonly known as oats, is a cereal grain that is generally considered to have a low FODMAP content, making it suitable for many individuals with dietary sensitivities. It is low in purines, which can be beneficial for those managing uric acid levels. However, there are some concerns regarding its safety for patients with celiac disease. While oats can be consumed by individuals with celiac disease if they are processed to avoid gluten contamination, there remains some uncertainty about their potential toxicity for these patients. Additionally, while oats can be included in gluten-free diets, they may still pose issues for those with gluten sensitivity. Overall, Avena is a versatile grain that can be beneficial for many, but caution is advised for individuals with specific dietary restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566,f713611b23199b8a9eb9c28377b9f128</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9783</data>
      <data key="d7">fa7a49ec967540608b4c364dd07102c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AJO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">AJO, commonly known as garlic, is recognized for its numerous health benefits. It is particularly noted for its anti-aggregating properties, which can help prevent the clumping of platelets in the blood, thereby promoting cardiovascular health. Additionally, garlic has a positive influence on lipid metabolism, contributing to better management of cholesterol levels. Overall, AJO is valued not only as a flavorful ingredient in various cuisines but also for its potential health-promoting effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">6c98e1347f14c72617198a910cf8c246,eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
      <data key="d3">833</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">9784</data>
      <data key="d7">016e08be3fc4401f99e5bfdd876f5089</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICIONISTA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A nutritionist is a professional who specializes in the study of nutrition and dietary practices, providing guidance on dietary restrictions and nutritional support for patients with specific health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">21dc8cb1a5078e23dae18b9c62b05625</data>
      <data key="d3">895</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
