    </node>
    <node id="LACTASE PERSISTENCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactase persistence refers to the continued production of lactase enzyme into adulthood, allowing for the digestion of lactose.</data>
      <data key="d2">ccd3c800d2985d4ad5e2c8d6e88b1b68</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">9960</data>
      <data key="d7">a111f54ca8614a24bb67a150bad3c382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FODMAPS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FODMAPs are a group of fermentable oligosaccharides, disaccharides, monosaccharides, and polyols, which are short-chain carbohydrates that can lead to digestive issues in certain individuals. This is particularly true for those suffering from irritable bowel syndrome (IBS).</data>
      <data key="d2">bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c,ccd3c800d2985d4ad5e2c8d6e88b1b68</data>
      <data key="d3">836</data>
