      <data key="d6">10067</data>
      <data key="d7">993f41651de44318ad6372efbbe81541</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEODISTROFIA RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteodistrofia renal, also known as renal osteodystrophy, is a bone disorder that arises in patients suffering from chronic kidney disease. This condition is primarily caused by imbalances in calcium, phosphate, and vitamin D levels, which are critical for maintaining healthy bone structure. Renal osteodystrophy is recognized as a complication of chronic kidney disease and is often associated with issues related to phosphorus metabolism. As a result, patients with chronic kidney disease may experience significant alterations in their bone health due to these metabolic disturbances.</data>
      <data key="d2">7ba4a7e7b4c409f6d4c6979a7de6c832,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10068</data>
      <data key="d7">1c5024f151824e7cac00b2f1413324a6</data>
    </node>
