    <node id="CITOQUINAS PROINFLAMATORIAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citoquinas proinflamatorias son prote&#237;nas que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en la modulaci&#243;n de la respuesta inmune. Estas mol&#233;culas de se&#241;alizaci&#243;n se encuentran elevadas en pacientes con insuficiencia renal cr&#243;nica, lo que contribuye a la inflamaci&#243;n y malnutrici&#243;n en estos individuos. Adem&#225;s, las citoquinas proinflamatorias aumentan durante episodios de inflamaci&#243;n, lo que puede afectar negativamente la salud de pacientes en estado cr&#237;tico. En resumen, las citoquinas proinflamatorias son fundamentales en la regulaci&#243;n de la respuesta inmune y tienen un impacto significativo en la salud de aquellos que padecen condiciones cr&#237;ticas y enfermedades cr&#243;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10070</data>
      <data key="d7">f07e2c5d8ef34b3295ccce8a9e56f14e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOALDOSTERONISMO HIPERRENIN&#201;MICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El hiperaldosteronismo hiperrenin&#233;mico es una condici&#243;n que se presenta en el s&#237;ndrome nefr&#243;tico, causando retenci&#243;n de agua y sodio.</data>
      <data key="d2">61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181</data>
      <data key="d3">1085</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10071</data>
      <data key="d7">f759ca6c1def4379b4b12782576dc659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETISTAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los dietistas son expertos en nutrici&#243;n que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en la planificaci&#243;n y evaluaci&#243;n de la ingesta diet&#233;tica de los pacientes, especialmente en contextos de nutrici&#243;n enteral. Estos profesionales de la salud est&#225;n especializados en ayudar a los pacientes a mantener una dieta adecuada, lo cual es particularmente importante en condiciones m&#233;dicas como la insuficiencia renal. Adem&#225;s, los dietistas son responsables de la planificaci&#243;n y supervisi&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n de los pacientes, asegurando que sus necesidades diet&#233;ticas sean atendidas de manera efectiva y personalizada.</data>
      <data key="d2">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21,a87e8e113488b153c5b4b2d2fca712c0</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10072</data>
      <data key="d7">c9ff506dfc9c4dbf980e4444bc1f7dd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NFK-DOQI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NFK-DOQI es una organizaci&#243;n que establece gu&#237;as y recomendaciones para el tratamiento de pacientes con enfermedad renal, incluyendo la evaluaci&#243;n nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">a87e8e113488b153c5b4b2d2fca712c0</data>
      <data key="d3">1154</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10073</data>
      <data key="d7">2eb757143dd248c4a2ff731964a9e1a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOALBUMINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoalbuminemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of albumin in the blood. This condition can arise in various clinical contexts, including patients with inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatitis, celiac disease, and renal insufficiency. Hipoalbuminemia is often associated with poor nutritional status, which can lead to worse outcomes in surgical patients and indicate malnutrition and absorption issues in those with celiac disease. 

The low levels of albumin can significantly affect drug metabolism and efficacy, as well as the measurement of calcium in the blood. Additionally, hipoalbuminemia decreases the oncotic pressure of plasma, contributing to fluid accumulation, particularly in cases of liver cirrhosis. Overall, hipoalbuminemia is a critical condition that reflects underlying health issues and can have serious implications for patient management and treatment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,2754a719b063eed550046e5b405be3d5,30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4,a87e8e113488b153c5b4b2d2fca712c0,c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c</data>
      <data key="d3">820</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">10074</data>
      <data key="d7">46630ca5624a4f819629e9e76b26d18a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOPPS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Dialysis Outcomes and Practice Patterns Study (DOPPS) is a research study that evaluates the outcomes of dialysis patients and their nutritional status across various demographics in Europe and the USA.</data>
      <data key="d2">541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292</data>
      <data key="d3">1155</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10075</data>
      <data key="d7">7a7c6f5a4fe1421983d1bc0fcd95c200</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEAVEY ET AL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Leavey et al is a research group that conducted a study on the relationship between body mass index and mortality in patients with renal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292</data>
      <data key="d3">1155</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10076</data>
      <data key="d7">8cbea35875e3403ca34b31f305644275</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CREATININA S&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Creatinina s&#233;rica is a serum level measurement that indicates muscle mass and protein intake in patients with terminal renal insufficiency treated with dialysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292</data>
      <data key="d3">1155</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10077</data>
      <data key="d7">bda31f0c15ad4447a5a26040e006cf89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA HIPOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A hypoproteic diet is a dietary regimen that restricts protein intake, often recommended for patients with renal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0</data>
      <data key="d3">1104</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10078</data>
      <data key="d7">219b050d6e214c74b4fb2f570f685792</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIQUISTOSIS RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polycystic kidney disease is a genetic disorder that affects kidney function and may not respond to low-protein diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0</data>
      <data key="d3">1104</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10079</data>
      <data key="d7">4397d6ca1eae4d2aa4f742cc8f8ed03c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IRC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic kidney disease (IRC) is a long-term condition where the kidneys do not work effectively, requiring dietary management.</data>
      <data key="d2">532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0</data>
      <data key="d3">1104</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10080</data>
      <data key="d7">606eba2ecc294dadb0d6081bf6ed409c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO RENAL AGUDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FALLO RENAL AGUDO, or acute renal failure, is characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function. This condition necessitates nutritional support and careful monitoring of electrolytes to manage the patient's health effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,e321db63d9b561eb98a4f01853b141ad</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10081</data>
      <data key="d7">85ce5371b9ca44c3885463076246954a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL emphasizes the importance of nutritional support for patients with various health conditions, particularly those with renal issues. The focus is on maintaining a balanced intake of nutrients to promote overall health. Additionally, NUTRICI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL provides tailored nutritional support strategies for patients with specific health conditions, such as fibrosis qu&#237;stica, ensuring that their unique dietary needs are met effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">665d7ba0d30bda94b0d549dc1822d7f7,95ef1473677a26ea6ad77c7db0c55e5e</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10082</data>
      <data key="d7">abba6f55ac614d49a003b7fc756e4c05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZARAZAGA ET AL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Zarazaga et al is a reference to a group of researchers who conducted a review on dietary recommendations for patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10083</data>
      <data key="d7">f7b7d904a13a408d95ed85a318f8ca8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KIDNEY FOUNDATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Kidney Foundation provides guidelines and recommendations for the nutritional management of patients with kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10084</data>
      <data key="d7">0a8c48f788b0462cafc012c16683d5f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIALYSIS PERITONEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DIALYSIS PERITONEAL refers to peritoneal dialysis, a treatment for kidney failure that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood. This method effectively removes toxins and excess fluids, providing an alternative to traditional hemodialysis for patients with compromised kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d2">9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d3">1650</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">10085</data>
      <data key="d7">91f0655f645e4ad3afc4684e15796ac4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN LA INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional management in chronic kidney disease focuses on maintaining nutritional status and improving quality of life for patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d3">1623</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10086</data>
      <data key="d7">48c331fe66744bfca66857a692956556</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidosis is a metabolic condition that can significantly impact patients with chronic kidney disease, influencing their nutritional status and treatment options. Additionally, it is a chronic state that affects individuals following a ketogenic diet, increasing the risk of bone demineralization. This dual impact highlights the importance of monitoring and managing acidosis in both chronic kidney disease patients and those adhering to specific dietary regimens.</data>
      <data key="d2">06adf563f18feaa5629f0e368a72d227,bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d3">1940</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10087</data>
      <data key="d7">425f932b213f4e479bfd8e15087b7767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSULINORRESISTENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insulin resistance is a condition characterized by the body's cells failing to respond effectively to insulin. This condition can complicate the management of patients with chronic kidney disease, as it impacts their nutritional needs. Additionally, insulin resistance may be exacerbated by surgical stress, further complicating the overall health and treatment of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc,d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae</data>
      <data key="d3">590</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10088</data>
      <data key="d7">0f4cf7e5cce1489aabe0296a38a6af7f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS DIET&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary supplements are used to ensure adequate nutrient intake in patients with chronic kidney disease, particularly those with protein restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10089</data>
      <data key="d7">f875998239a545ddbe2d94a1f25f1a32</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN PREDIALISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition in pre-dialysis focuses on maintaining nutritional status before the initiation of dialysis treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10090</data>
      <data key="d7">b72228b42d3243e69634e8cab65a9198</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN HEMODI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition in hemodialysis involves specific dietary recommendations to support patients undergoing this treatment for kidney failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10091</data>
      <data key="d7">6393c2382a314ea9905c0e0d6c47b11f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition in peritoneal dialysis addresses the unique dietary needs of patients receiving this form of kidney treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf76380d2417653bab17a6a9b91d85bc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10092</data>
      <data key="d7">1ceaf9113880406c8b12b9ca36e9065a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEFROPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nefropat&#237;a refers to kidney disease, which can be managed with dietary adjustments and nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce</data>
      <data key="d3">303</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10093</data>
      <data key="d7">75601ad222d146b7a3d2a26d86730a8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA BAJA EN PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A low-protein diet is recommended for patients with renal insufficiency to manage their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10094</data>
      <data key="d7">c2c6cea342b749a69988d27bbf0694f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RADICALES LIBRES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Free radicals are harmful compounds that can be produced in excess due to renal dysfunction, and dietary management aims to reduce their production.</data>
      <data key="d2">c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce</data>
      <data key="d3">303</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10095</data>
      <data key="d7">49af5f8a4d72490ca3c9f2ed51c51646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ULTRAFILTRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ultrafiltration is a process used in dialysis to remove excess fluid from the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1</data>
      <data key="d3">1623</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10096</data>
      <data key="d7">5aff506aafad4978a909e5f71da4e9ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REAGUDIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Reagudization refers to the worsening of a medical condition, often requiring a change in treatment or management.</data>
      <data key="d2">9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10097</data>
      <data key="d7">6a48d19f3c6c4b87a86e2c7c518fb479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERYTHROPOIETIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Erythropoietin is a hormone used in the treatment of anemia, particularly in patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1627</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10098</data>
      <data key="d7">1e7e41965be445eeae29930097890767</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY ADVICE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary advice is guidance provided to patients to help them meet their nutritional needs while managing dietary restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1250</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10099</data>
      <data key="d7">a0d6c4f3e35044d786c48bec93213014</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALORIC NEEDS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Caloric needs refer to the amount of energy required by patients, which can vary based on their medical condition, especially in renal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10100</data>
      <data key="d7">025e849e5be14c09993c43c1d38a9870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTUDIO FINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Estudio FINE is a significant clinical study that evaluated the effects of parenteral nutrition during hemodialysis on patient outcomes over a year.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1e7cd9fdc3093bc5902030d654d0763</data>
      <data key="d3">1158</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
