      <data key="d7">b5d02cb2e9574cb9ae6543a330735057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICO-PROTEICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MALNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICO-PROTEICA refers to a severe form of malnutrition characterized by deficiencies in both protein and calories. This condition can arise from various factors, including the failure of renal function, which significantly impacts the overall health of the affected individual. The consequences of malnutrici&#243;n cal&#243;rico-proteica can be profound, leading to a deterioration in health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">2a387a0f62fd64b31ecf55b1538932c2,e321db63d9b561eb98a4f01853b141ad</data>
      <data key="d3">1154</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10104</data>
      <data key="d7">1e59202240e04e90931ae7764921c4bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KIDNEY DISEASES OUTCOMES QUALITY INITIATIVE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Kidney Diseases Outcomes Quality Initiative (K/DOQI) is an organization that provides guidelines for the management of kidney diseases, including nutrition guidelines for patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d3">747</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">10105</data>
      <data key="d7">69612b22c314402ab317e8915c1d769c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIALYSIS OUTCOMES AND PRACTICE PATTERNS STUDY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Dialysis Outcomes and Practice Patterns Study (DOPPS) is a comprehensive research initiative that investigates various aspects of hemodialysis practices and outcomes across multiple countries. This study specifically focuses on the predictors and consequences of altered mineral metabolism in patients undergoing dialysis, as well as examining nutritional indicators and patient adherence. By analyzing these factors, DOPPS aims to enhance the understanding of dialysis outcomes and improve practice patterns in the treatment of patients with kidney failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d3">745</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">10106</data>
      <data key="d7">995c5e22c56d40b38b837becb17840d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY OF RENAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Society of Renal Nutrition and Metabolism is an organization dedicated to improving the nutritional care of patients with kidney disease through research and consensus statements.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d3">746</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10107</data>
      <data key="d7">789d21f92b4a4ab69e7c644d8442086a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nutrition Guidelines are a set of recommendations developed by K/DOQI and other organizations to guide healthcare providers in the nutritional management of patients with kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d3">747</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10108</data>
      <data key="d7">6f2aa7dc13e540d5bec34495c10f55d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPEN GUIDELINES ON ENTERAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The ESPEN Guidelines on Enteral Nutrition offer evidence-based recommendations aimed at the nutritional management of patients across various medical conditions. These guidelines specifically address the needs of patients with renal failure as well as those suffering from pancreatitis, ensuring a comprehensive approach to enteral nutrition tailored to different health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2,60d24674009cc67523f1ecdc63975fdc</data>
      <data key="d3">714</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10109</data>
      <data key="d7">81a1434c50854612ab9ab8677e09eea5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUTE RENAL FAILURE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acute renal failure is a medical condition characterized by a sudden decrease in kidney function, requiring nutritional management to support recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10110</data>
      <data key="d7">4741f4c0d98f4a51bcd760bd58c833a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN JOURNAL OF KIDNEY DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Journal of Kidney Disease is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews related to kidney disease and its management.</data>
      <data key="d2">5705dc62240c8f823dd1bc15770d5ab2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10111</data>
      <data key="d7">18f8e3ba3ca14d61a5e6ae5de0791551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANO NJ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cano NJ is a researcher known for his work on nutritional management in patients with kidney disease, including guidelines for enteral nutrition.</data>
