    <node id="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO VIRGEN DEL ROC&#205;O">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital Universitario Virgen del Roc&#237;o is a hospital in Sevilla specializing in various medical fields including Endocrinology, Nutrition, and Digestive System.</data>
      <data key="d2">9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f</data>
      <data key="d3">852</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10119</data>
      <data key="d7">df8180e6453745b594e5578d1fa35837</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA CR&#211;NICA" refers to chronic liver disease (EHC), a medical condition that often presents silently and can lead to severe complications such as portal hypertension and cirrhosis. This condition encompasses a range of disorders that result in long-term liver damage, including cirrhosis and hepatitis. Chronic liver disease is associated with malabsorption, metabolic disturbances, and diabetes mellitus, which can further complicate the health of affected individuals. Additionally, it is linked to malnutrition and has an adverse impact on patient outcomes, particularly for those who are candidates for liver transplantation. Overall, chronic liver disease poses significant health risks and requires careful management to mitigate its complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c,9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f,b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854</data>
      <data key="d3">1788</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">10120</data>
      <data key="d7">0f4f4ffb691c4dc19c18d44cc911c670</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;AS CR&#211;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatopat&#237;as cr&#243;nicas are chronic liver diseases that can be exacerbated by conditions of iron overload, such as hemochromatosis. These chronic liver diseases may necessitate liver transplantation as a therapeutic alternative. Additionally, hepatopat&#237;as cr&#243;nicas can contribute to the development of iron overload conditions, highlighting the complex interplay between liver health and iron metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d3">1710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10121</data>
      <data key="d7">b371ca90447d4449bc6cb85b3c79009f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS B (VHB)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatitis B virus is a major cause of liver disease, affecting 1-2% of the general population and leading to cirrhosis in 30% of patients over time.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d3">1817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10122</data>
      <data key="d7">42599f6bc8fb48128642bfef6db8713f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS C (VHC)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatitis C virus is another significant cause of liver disease, with a similar prevalence and progression to cirrhosis as hepatitis B.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d3">1817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10123</data>
      <data key="d7">c44dde5995f64777839480cd6b5ed31d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMOCRMATOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemochromatosis is a medical condition characterized by excessive accumulation of iron in the body, which can result in significant health complications. This condition can lead to serious issues such as liver cirrhosis and diabetes mellitus, as well as liver damage. The iron overload associated with hemochromatosis poses risks to various organs, making it a critical health concern that requires careful management and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">24</data>
      <data key="d6">10124</data>
      <data key="d7">0319c6388d9047bda296a2521300741d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PERITONITIS BACTERIANA ESPONT&#193;NEA (PBE)">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Spontaneous bacterial peritonitis is an infection of ascitic fluid that occurs in patients with cirrhosis, often requiring medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10125</data>
      <data key="d7">019fd9e54a2149bcb5eb32dba3fa86ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CETOG&#201;NESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ketogenesis is the metabolic process by which ketone bodies are produced from fatty acids, particularly during periods of low carbohydrate intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10126</data>
      <data key="d7">3e2d9bbf33564357be716d45f3de9114</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DETOXIFICACI&#211;N DEL AMON&#205;ACO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Detoxification of ammonia is a critical liver function that converts toxic ammonia into urea for excretion, essential for maintaining metabolic balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10127</data>
      <data key="d7">0631839459ee4c2c99fc782b1d27fd90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTESIS DE UREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urea synthesis is a metabolic process that converts ammonia into urea, which is then excreted in urine, playing a vital role in nitrogen metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10128</data>
      <data key="d7">addaf76c13bb4f8d856214c70e0c45b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLISMO DEL HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iron metabolism refers to the processes involved in the absorption, transport, and storage of iron in the body, crucial for producing hemoglobin.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10129</data>
      <data key="d7">a40b2965d88648ae80b2bc150d8a5936</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLISMO DEL COBRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Copper metabolism involves the absorption, transport, and utilization of copper, an essential trace mineral important for various enzymatic functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10130</data>
      <data key="d7">d7ff9ad4edff4920941df62753610dc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N PROLONGADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prolonged hospitalization refers to extended stays in a hospital, often due to complications arising from chronic conditions like liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10131</data>
      <data key="d7">d79f0164a5b64010b785504a6bf75bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORTALIDAD POSTOPERATORIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Postoperative mortality refers to death occurring after surgical procedures, which can be influenced by factors such as malnutrition in liver transplant patients.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10132</data>
      <data key="d7">03d1a117731841cea3ee51ec416482ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHILD-PUGH CLASSIFICATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Child-Pugh classification is a scoring system used to assess the prognosis of chronic liver disease, particularly cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10133</data>
      <data key="d7">74a9fa4d3a9a4183a49d9b0a580b4510</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MELD SCORE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The MELD score is a system used to prioritize patients for liver transplantation based on the severity of liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1790</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10134</data>
      <data key="d7">5d6a05fcfa5f4671a191287c774495f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VARICES GASTROESOF&#193;GICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastroesophageal varices are dilated veins in the esophagus that can occur due to portal hypertension, often a complication of liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1820</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10135</data>
      <data key="d7">3db7c04e1de24fa797bfcbad7d6927c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPULMONAR SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatopulmonary syndrome is a condition that affects the lungs and is associated with liver disease, leading to difficulty in oxygenation.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10136</data>
      <data key="d7">50ef37c2a487468db5fc8e15570bfe6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOCARDIOPAT&#205;A CIRR&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cirrhotic cardiomyopathy is a cardiac condition that can occur in patients with cirrhosis, affecting heart function.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10137</data>
      <data key="d7">63ed8a50e49147a6a844ea1438231f7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME HEPATORRENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatorenal syndrome is a serious complication of advanced liver disease characterized by kidney failure.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10138</data>
      <data key="d7">20100cf25b9841d6838ec6d0639ab2a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME HEPATODRENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatoadrenal syndrome is a condition where adrenal function is impaired due to liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10139</data>
      <data key="d7">2fdc794b0e034d719ac679940aab516e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES DE COAGULACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Coagulation disorders are common in liver disease due to impaired synthesis of clotting factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10140</data>
      <data key="d7">e6e60822d70e4e3b97cc703ebf8049a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEUCO-PLAQUETOPENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Leukopenia and thrombocytopenia are conditions characterized by low white blood cell and platelet counts, often seen in liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10141</data>
      <data key="d7">aeb3634bf030420d8efc766ab2d0a1f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional support is critical in managing chronic liver disease, as malnutrition is a common complication.</data>
      <data key="d2">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10142</data>
      <data key="d7">3b065396bf6e43c99a0024e81bffd0c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE DE H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The "TRASPLANTE DE H&#205;GADO" is a surgical procedure that may be necessary for patients suffering from advanced liver disease. This procedure involves the replacement of a diseased liver with a healthy liver from a donor, and it is typically considered when other treatments have failed to improve the patient's condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10143</data>
      <data key="d7">8369474caa364cca86862c2f17905546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EHCA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EHCA refers to a condition associated with advanced stages of liver disease, particularly end-stage liver disease. This condition significantly impacts patients' nutritional status, leading to complications such as malnutrition and other health issues. Patients with EHCA experience metabolic alterations that pose nutritional challenges, necessitating specialized nutritional support to manage their health effectively. Overall, EHCA encompasses the various complications and health issues that arise in individuals suffering from chronic liver disease, particularly in its later stages.</data>
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab,fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10144</data>
      <data key="d7">75f2c87d1fcc417198f72fe9c650d3eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXIDATION OF LIPIDS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The oxidation of lipids is a metabolic process that provides energy, particularly during fasting, and is heightened in patients with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10145</data>
      <data key="d7">0edfecafe3df465fb59b6dca332e665a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMMONIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ammonia is a compound that can accumulate in the body, particularly in liver disease, and is associated with metabolic disturbances affecting muscle function.</data>
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10146</data>
      <data key="d7">170ff65ce0f148a7ae1658136a03e8ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEOGLUCONEOGENESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neoglucogenesis is the metabolic process of producing glucose from non-carbohydrate sources, which is altered in patients with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10147</data>
      <data key="d7">a71be4a1d5bd431993f5a538301ca7d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERMETABOLISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypermetabolism is a condition characterized by an increased metabolic rate, which is often observed in critically ill patients. This heightened metabolic state can also occur in individuals with liver disease, resulting in muscle loss and various other complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">37182848d30a82f99b7a617859ac6e0d,5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,723cbca2d5cfbf8cf05a923c52569641</data>
      <data key="d3">245</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10148</data>
      <data key="d7">586ea2746b36440992e7cb1457d6cbfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALORIMETRY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calorimetry is a method used to measure energy expenditure, which is crucial for determining the nutritional needs of patients. This technique is particularly recommended for assessing metabolic rates in individuals with liver disease. In clinical settings, calorimetry is frequently employed to evaluate the metabolic needs of patients, providing valuable insights into their energy requirements. Overall, calorimetry serves as an important tool in understanding and managing the metabolic health of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,ec94449c6ffff75664588262301de0a6,fb0c6cd346ca91e15f8ff1cc07570d9d</data>
      <data key="d3">245</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10149</data>
      <data key="d7">e947b310a521452f891e18ba1a5a6c6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPOLYSIS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10150</data>
      <data key="d7">23736e54924945d995e7b57a8128b4dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTE CIRR&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El paciente cirr&#243;tico es una persona que padece cirrosis, una enfermedad hep&#225;tica cr&#243;nica que afecta su estado nutricional y requiere valoraci&#243;n nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d2">c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b</data>
      <data key="d3">1165</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">10151</data>
      <data key="d7">9f483feae66145fd98ed45411201796a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDEMAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EDEMAS refers to swellings that occur due to excess fluid being trapped in the body's tissues. This condition can be particularly concerning for patients with kidney issues, as it may indicate underlying health problems. Additionally, edemas can complicate nutritional assessments in patients with cirrhosis, as the accumulation of fluid in the tissues can affect overall health and nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b,d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1165</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10152</data>
      <data key="d7">22f5dbbc5a0c41e88f6118010f474ddc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESTRICCIONES DIET&#201;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las restricciones diet&#233;ticas son limitaciones en la ingesta de ciertos alimentos que pueden ser necesarias para el manejo del paciente cirr&#243;tico.</data>
      <data key="d2">c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b</data>
      <data key="d3">1165</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10153</data>
      <data key="d7">e4e2368e03094401a657439038413112</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCLE STRENGTH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Muscle strength is a vital component in evaluating the nutritional status of patients with cirrhosis and plays a significant role in the assessment of sarcopenia. It is commonly measured using handgrip dynamometry, which is a standard method for quantifying muscle strength. Additionally, muscle strength can be assessed through various tests, including handgrip strength and knee extension. Overall, muscle strength serves as an important physical attribute that reflects an individual's health and functional capacity.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595,a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10154</data>
      <data key="d7">a2e9e84d39214561957d5d21dfb9b814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOELECTRICAL IMPEDANCE ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a method used to estimate body composition, including fat and lean mass, which is relevant in nutritional assessments.</data>
      <data key="d2">f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10155</data>
      <data key="d7">e932b2cd507643b98dcbb87274efd734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL NUTRITIONAL PRIORITIZING TOOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Royal Free Hospital Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) is a global scheme for assessing nutritional risk in patients with cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92</data>
      <data key="d3">911</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10156</data>
      <data key="d7">6499d4da2c084d77b6baf7bfaf2440ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES CIRR&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">PACIENTES CIRR&#211;TICOS refers to individuals suffering from cirrhosis, a serious liver condition that often leads to nutritional deficiencies. These patients require specific dietary assessments and nutritional guidelines to effectively manage their condition. Proper nutrition is crucial for cirrhotic patients to support their health and mitigate the complications associated with their illness.</data>
      <data key="d2">3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab,4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">10157</data>
      <data key="d7">3354135ba3964722b76d6a8817430d8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROYAL FREE HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Royal Free Hospital is a healthcare institution that utilizes the Nutritional Prioritizing Tool (RFH-NPT) for assessing malnutrition risks in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10158</data>
      <data key="d7">97d7aa6e37a44a48ad12fb4c5d69f734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EHC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">EHC refers to patients with chronic liver disease, particularly those experiencing sarcopenia, which is a significant concern in nutritional management.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10159</data>
      <data key="d7">04f924ffd102434bb73b6d41aeff07a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESTRICCI&#211;N DE SODIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sodium restriction is a dietary intervention often recommended for patients with liver conditions to manage fluid retention and ascites.</data>
      <data key="d2">3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10160</data>
      <data key="d7">ec8818cae1e043e095472c39b82bfcf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESTRICCI&#211;N DE PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Protein restriction is a dietary practice that is generally discouraged in patients with liver disease, as it can worsen nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10161</data>
      <data key="d7">bad8fcc528f248ab85b3c2964db3aa86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUMENTO DE MASA GRASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Increase in fat mass can occur in patients with liver disease if caloric intake is not properly managed.</data>
      <data key="d2">3437d6cdf014282ec447fc7f4de92cab</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10162</data>
      <data key="d7">d4afc2fb956a4fef810b62146c4670f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ECHA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ECHA refers to a condition related to hepatic encephalopathy and nutritional deficiencies in patients with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">1786</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10163</data>
      <data key="d7">389403cce7d242b49c2eca31be1d46a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOLIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Folic acid is a water-soluble B vitamin that plays a vital role in DNA synthesis and repair, making it particularly important during pregnancy. It is essential for the proper development of the fetus and helps prevent neural tube defects. Additionally, folic acid is often found to be deficient in individuals with alcohol-related liver disease, highlighting its significance in overall health and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">acfde2ff93b969353912836034d74242,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">1789</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10164</data>
      <data key="d7">291f05c97c0846a6b8340f164c8a79b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SANGRADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SANGRADO refers to bleeding, which can manifest as a complication in various medical contexts. In patients with liver disease, bleeding may lead to episodes of hepatic encephalopathy, a serious condition affecting brain function. Additionally, bleeding is a potential complication associated with the use of central venous access for nutritional support, indicating the risks involved in such medical procedures. Furthermore, in patients with gastrointestinal bleeding (GEP), bleeding is considered a minor complication that may arise due to damage to the vasculature at the site of implantation. Overall, SANGRADO encompasses various scenarios where bleeding can pose significant health risks, particularly in patients with underlying conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">60a2803170af3c20448ef70091bdfadd,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10165</data>
      <data key="d7">0694825255fd4141ba824ecf19fe42b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABUSO DE SUSTANCIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Substance abuse can lead to liver damage and is a significant factor in the development of hepatic encephalopathy.</data>
      <data key="d2">ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d3">1787</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10166</data>
      <data key="d7">1338f2bafea848afbde772b3e29fcb1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE ORIGEN ALCOH&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcoholic liver disease is a condition caused by excessive alcohol consumption, leading to liver damage and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
      <data key="d3">852</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10167</data>
      <data key="d7">a87f7729bd3c423697c6990495b87761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULAS ENRIQUECIDAS EN AACR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enriched formulas in AACR are specialized nutritional formulas designed to provide additional nutrients for patients, particularly those with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
      <data key="d3">852</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10168</data>
      <data key="d7">1a5d278d48924b29ab5653b231f2ae76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLANGITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cholangitis is an infection of the bile duct that can complicate liver disease and affect nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">d59761afc53676cf5d1fe62616f0d7d7</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10169</data>
      <data key="d7">7891b363d4e245aa895fad25586700df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIEDAD EUROPEA DE NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ESPEN is an organization that provides guidelines for enteral nutrition, recommending early nutritional support for patients post-liver transplant.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d3">611</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10170</data>
      <data key="d7">78a0f64d6ee04f9fa8496de5d2781be1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE RENUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Refeeding syndrome is a dangerous condition that can occur when feeding is restarted in malnourished patients, leading to severe electrolyte imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10171</data>
      <data key="d7">0c207642690c48a2a522c14db89438ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJERCICIO AER&#211;BICO Y DE RESISTENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aerobic and resistance exercise are recommended for improving physical activity levels in patients recovering from liver transplant.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10172</data>
      <data key="d7">b33acb9f26574337b6343ca979359329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIPS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">TIPS, or Transjugular Intrahepatic Portosystemic Shunt, is a medical procedure designed to address portal hypertension, which is frequently associated with liver disease. This procedure is particularly beneficial for treating conditions such as quilot&#243;rax that arise as a secondary complication of portal hypertension. By creating a shunt, TIPS offers a potential resolution for these conditions, improving patient outcomes related to elevated portal pressure.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,fe69a5b07baa1ca7328e65ff39f7719a</data>
      <data key="d3">1798</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10173</data>
      <data key="d7">cc45a00c3d9d4f93b7d2916ace93d8a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRRHOSIS HEPATICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cirrhosis is a severe liver condition that can lead to malnutrition and other complications in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d3">794</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10174</data>
      <data key="d7">2d988ec812354fc39a5924471adb3dda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KALAFATELI M">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kalafateli M is an author of a study that discusses the impact of malnutrition and sarcopenia on post-liver transplantation outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10175</data>
      <data key="d7">4b268ce404de42d381f5cb573885774e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MANTZOUKIS K">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mantzoukis K is a co-author of research related to malnutrition and sarcopenia in liver disease patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10176</data>
      <data key="d7">6ee25f777b824b1aa86d774d62f39a2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHOI YAU Y">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Choi Yau Y is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition and sarcopenia in liver transplantation outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10177</data>
      <data key="d7">b1eec2e5f701464ea74fc6393e8667f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPANISH LIVER TRANSPLANT REGISTRY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Spanish Liver Transplant Registry collects data on liver transplant outcomes and is referenced in the context of liver disease management.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10178</data>
      <data key="d7">e285d2179e6c47048be26373e01403c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPPLEMENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Supplements are additional nutritional products that are recommended for patients who cannot meet their dietary needs through food alone.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f</data>
      <data key="d3">704</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10179</data>
      <data key="d7">6cc91bda0c2f4a3a8d5828a3911b816d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POST-LIVER TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Post-liver transplantation refers to the period after a liver transplant, where patients require careful nutritional management.</data>
      <data key="d2">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10180</data>
      <data key="d7">7ed76cc66e29421aa0e0a82ecf1db079</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCLE DEPLETION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Muscle depletion is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, which poses significant health risks. It is particularly concerning in patients with liver cirrhosis, as it increases the risk of hepatic encephalopathy, a serious complication of liver dysfunction. Additionally, muscle depletion is a critical issue in cancer patients, where it is often linked to cancer cachexia&#8212;a syndrome that leads to severe weight loss and muscle wasting. This condition adversely affects the prognosis of cancer patients, highlighting the importance of addressing muscle depletion in both liver disease and cancer care.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,fb7b0d121f195e2a472f3d47e28ccff9</data>
      <data key="d3">1515</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10181</data>
      <data key="d7">417d3af58ace4252af16b4ef584d3405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATIC ENCEPHALOPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatic encephalopathy is a decline in brain function that occurs as a result of severe liver disease. This condition leads to a buildup of toxins in the bloodstream, which can significantly impair cognitive function and overall neurological health.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973,bf2e1510b4d6b43da85e8086d93e5602</data>
      <data key="d3">1515</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">10182</data>
      <data key="d7">726d1e11977646dc85df1968a63ed41f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRRHOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by the replacement of healthy liver tissue with scar tissue, which leads to liver dysfunction and can progress to liver failure. It represents a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver, resulting from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis and chronic alcoholism. Additionally, cirrhosis increases the risk of developing hepatocellular carcinoma, a type of liver cancer.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973,49e6a5571bf2f206ac38ac536d70f710,5aaadc19de8fb96a4951c0ba38192991,83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
      <data key="d3">1510</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">34</data>
      <data key="d6">10183</data>
      <data key="d7">c7d9bc0da732443e96238189b9c05384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MELD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MELD (Model for End-Stage Liver Disease) is a scoring system used to assess the severity of chronic liver disease and prioritize patients for liver transplantation.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b</data>
      <data key="d3">1514</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10184</data>
      <data key="d7">9f15007cb32d4552a67c1798640e6995</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEIN-CALORIE MALNUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Protein-calorie malnutrition is a condition that occurs when the body does not get enough protein and calories, which can be particularly detrimental in patients with liver cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10185</data>
      <data key="d7">6dfcef8117684606aeb0014d71441328</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONTANO-LOZA AJ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Montano-Loza AJ is a researcher and author known for his significant contributions to the field of liver transplantation and cirrhosis. He has published studies focusing on muscle wasting and its implications for liver transplantation outcomes. Additionally, Montano-Loza AJ has investigated the association between sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass, and mortality in patients suffering from cirrhosis. His work highlights the critical relationship between muscle health and patient prognosis in liver-related diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973</data>
      <data key="d3">1514</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10186</data>
      <data key="d7">c78df3487d24423d81003077930ee3db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TANDON P">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tandon P is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of liver health. They have studied the prevalence of severe muscle depletion in patients on the liver transplant waitlist, highlighting the critical health challenges faced by these individuals. Additionally, Tandon P has contributed to a meta-analysis on nutritional supplementation in cirrhosis, further emphasizing their commitment to advancing knowledge and improving patient outcomes in liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973</data>
      <data key="d3">1515</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10187</data>
      <data key="d7">8dedf40d77984155b9cd481a0127949f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARA N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Hara N is a researcher who has investigated the prognostic factors for overall survival in patients with cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b</data>
      <data key="d3">1510</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10188</data>
      <data key="d7">8ade9bfef4ee4e25ad32c58fcdf4675e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARIAS S">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Carias S is a researcher who has studied the association between nonalcoholic steatohepatitis and sarcopenic obesity in cirrhosis patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b</data>
