    <node id="OCKENGA J">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ockenga J is a researcher and author known for his contributions to the field of medical research, particularly in relation to nutrition and metabolic disorders. He studied the correlation of bound leptin with energy expenditure in patients suffering from cirrhosis, providing insights into the metabolic changes associated with this condition. Additionally, Ockenga J researched the effects of glutamine-enriched total parenteral nutrition in patients with acute pancreatitis, highlighting the importance of nutritional support in managing this serious condition. Furthermore, he reviewed the topics of anorexia and cachexia in gastrointestinal cancer, contributing to the understanding of these complex issues that affect patients with cancer. Through his work, Ockenga J has made significant contributions to the understanding of nutrition and metabolism in various clinical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">49e6a5571bf2f206ac38ac536d70f710,60d24674009cc67523f1ecdc63975fdc,a496bf37d4cc9b6246f5eb6b66b03d8a</data>
