    </node>
    <node id="ASCITES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ascites is the accumulation of fluid in the abdominal cavity, commonly associated with cirrhosis and liver disease. It is often observed in patients suffering from liver cirrhosis, which can impact their energy expenditure. Additionally, ascites can be related to various medical conditions, including chylous ascites, highlighting its multifaceted nature in clinical presentations.</data>
      <data key="d2">9ea9816b490492ba0030e6ba4bc3bb9f,a35fdf8cbbb5fe4783572ea6e86f7776,c45c1688135653a80812cdaf426ec9a3</data>
