    <node id="CABRE E">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cabre E is an author who has made significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to liver disease. He is involved in the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition specifically tailored for patients with liver conditions. Additionally, Cabre E has conducted research focusing on the nutritional aspects of chronic liver disease, enhancing the understanding of dietary needs in this patient population. Furthermore, he has studied the reliability of bioelectrical impedance analysis as a method for assessing body composition in individuals with cirrhosis, contributing valuable insights into the management of this condition.</data>
