      <data key="d6">10404</data>
      <data key="d7">f05a119d07ca4c6b9c318590836f4e0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARETAEUS DE CAPADOCIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Aretaeus de Capadocia was a physician in the second half of the 2nd century BC who first described the condition known as celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10405</data>
      <data key="d7">327b26eb5e764d1fbd0f9ecc4a4f376d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SAMUEL GEE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Samuel Gee was a physician who provided a more contemporary clinical report on celiac disease in 1888, emphasizing the importance of dietary regulation in treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10406</data>
      <data key="d7">828c9c939d524b19849e397b560b946d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTEN DICKE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gluten Dicke was a researcher who made a significant discovery regarding the relationship between gluten consumption and celiac disease after World War II.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10407</data>
      <data key="d7">0ec84df1ccd84f178c26c38ac0ce75e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HLA DQ2">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HLA DQ2 is a genetic marker associated with a higher predisposition to celiac disease and related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10408</data>
      <data key="d7">15e0cf4e722d4b9fb285c5af828362e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HLA DQ8">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HLA DQ8 is another genetic marker linked to an increased risk of developing celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10409</data>
      <data key="d7">fc8a600b7cc34efe89b711b1685373e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MINERALS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Minerals are inorganic elements that are essential for human health and play a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are commonly found in dietary supplements and are vital for maintaining overall well-being. Additionally, the absorption of these inorganic nutrients can be impaired in individuals with celiac disease, highlighting the importance of understanding mineral intake and its impact on health.</data>
      <data key="d2">33d5ce24ed9abf269f25077518d11a85,3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d3">1607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10410</data>
      <data key="d7">8295742e8564489b8b12edd724317c3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperplasia is an increase in the number of cells, which can occur in the intestinal mucosa of individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10411</data>
      <data key="d7">d5329fe3f90e4728857e5ccc83d17611</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROPHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atrophy refers to the wasting away or decrease in size of the intestinal villi, a characteristic of celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10412</data>
      <data key="d7">2da2c102115846d59cfa527b796a4fa4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMMUNE RESPONSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The immune response is the body's reaction to gluten in individuals with celiac disease, leading to inflammation and damage.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10413</data>
      <data key="d7">07669e5cbba04e6794f984f64086c9d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LYMPHOCYTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell involved in the immune response, which plays a role in the pathology of celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10414</data>
      <data key="d7">d17a22e916704cb78deb138912e4af55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIGLIADIN ANTIBODIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Antigliadin antibodies are markers that can indicate an autoimmune response to gluten in individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10415</data>
      <data key="d7">eb630452700c46d5a8798486c5dced38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIENDOMYSIAL ANTIBODIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Antiendomysial antibodies are another type of antibody that can be present in individuals with celiac disease, indicating intestinal damage.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10416</data>
      <data key="d7">aca33d2b92ba4408ba259731d4ef5039</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIRETICULIN ANTIBODIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Antireticulin antibodies are associated with celiac disease and can be used as a diagnostic marker for the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10417</data>
      <data key="d7">ddc252103d0a425fa6da6a20b5fee5dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTEN SENSITIVITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gluten sensitivity is a condition characterized by individuals experiencing symptoms related to gluten consumption. It is distinct from celiac disease, meaning that those with gluten sensitivity do not have the autoimmune response associated with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84,bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c,e119877a92b580500f5e5b0307401732</data>
      <data key="d3">836</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10418</data>
      <data key="d7">3fb531eb39a14a7dbb3fbe3bde6103cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ICEBERG CELIAC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The iceberg celiac theory suggests that many individuals with celiac disease may remain undiagnosed, with only a small percentage showing classic symptoms.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">3ec4c9fa90e7083cd895d95efed02f84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10419</data>
      <data key="d7">3c87f89763db4bd6b49776f6b2f869e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEREAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Cereal is a type of grain that is rich in carbohydrates and includes various species consumed by humans such as wheat, barley, and corn.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d3">647</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10420</data>
      <data key="d7">356993616b2d4b2d98d528561ec66b48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARINA DE CEREAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Flour made from cereal grains, primarily used in baking and cooking.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10421</data>
      <data key="d7">d3df5d095bdf40c6a25604da51552eee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA, or non-celiac gluten sensitivity, is a condition characterized by gastrointestinal symptoms that occur in response to gluten consumption. Unlike celiac disease, individuals with this sensitivity do not exhibit the same diagnostic markers associated with celiac disease. This distinction highlights that while both conditions involve adverse reactions to gluten, they are fundamentally different in their underlying mechanisms and diagnostic criteria.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10422</data>
      <data key="d7">278ff19ec0a14f76a5ab7ea367c2f629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Corn is a cereal grain that is widely used in various food products and is gluten-free.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10423</data>
      <data key="d7">8469e4f275a24cdba15ec16ec5b0ee92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARLEY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Barley is a cereal grain that contains gluten and can trigger symptoms in individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d3">828</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10424</data>
      <data key="d7">5e65197a448a47988a6df5a74dada148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMINAS DEL GRUPO B">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">B vitamins are a group of water-soluble vitamins that play important roles in cell metabolism and are found in various cereals.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d3">647</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10425</data>
      <data key="d7">4398e7a4dc454ee5b2c9e0194196cdbf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS EXTRAINTENSTINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Extraintestinal symptoms are non-digestive reactions that can occur in individuals with celiac disease, such as fatigue and headaches.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10426</data>
      <data key="d7">33ac585bcde44095a92da9c220dffb7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA LIBRE DE GLUTEN" refers to a gluten-free diet, which is a dietary regimen that excludes foods containing gluten. This diet is primarily adopted by individuals diagnosed with celiac disease or those who experience gluten sensitivity. Research has shown that a gluten-free diet can also be beneficial for some patients suffering from irritable bowel syndrome and gluten sensitivity, as indicated by clinical trials. It is particularly recommended for patients with celiac disease to help manage and control the symptoms associated with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f,9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10427</data>
      <data key="d7">64882b764838467a9558af97c2124640</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUMANO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">HUMANO refers to humans, who are classified as primates. One notable characteristic of humans is the absence of the enzyme uricase, which results in elevated levels of uric acid in their bodies compared to other mammals. Additionally, humans are susceptible to celiac disease and gluten sensitivity, conditions that can trigger a range of symptoms when gluten is consumed.</data>
      <data key="d2">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10428</data>
      <data key="d7">077afefdacf546d28b4336e625330a5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES MELLITUS 1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La diabetes mellitus tipo 1 es una enfermedad autoinmune que se ha asociado con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, presentando un riesgo mayor en pacientes cel&#237;acos.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10429</data>
      <data key="d7">58426e4c03b045ecaae7b2bb17c2ba44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE SJ&#214;GREN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad de Sj&#246;gren es otra patolog&#237;a autoinmune que puede estar asociada con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10430</data>
      <data key="d7">d097d520f5024ad4845ad9e9478adafc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFERTILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La infertilidad puede ser una complicaci&#243;n en pacientes con enfermedad cel&#237;aca, a menudo relacionada con deficiencias nutricionales.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10431</data>
      <data key="d7">dbe1e38af63c4feeb9a2e56409c11d9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABORTOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los abortos de repetici&#243;n pueden estar asociados con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, debido a problemas de malnutrici&#243;n y autoinmunidad.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10432</data>
      <data key="d7">9a5b774299234abf9ea1b26579bb9ac0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS NEUROPSIQUI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los trastornos neuropsiqui&#225;tricos son manifestaciones que pueden asociarse con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, incluyendo ataxia, cefaleas y trastornos ansioso-depresivos.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10433</data>
      <data key="d7">4f7de067da1d4eb385c2fba6c25a324e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARTRITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Artritis es una condici&#243;n que puede aparecer en un porcentaje significativo de adultos que padecen enfermedad cel&#237;aca, lo que sugiere una relaci&#243;n entre ambas condiciones.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2,84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10434</data>
      <data key="d7">beed6788257642c59a1788b30f3d94de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DERMATITIS HERPETIFORME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dermatitis herpetiforme es una erupci&#243;n cut&#225;nea que se asocia con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca. Esta condici&#243;n se manifiesta a trav&#233;s de lesiones ves&#237;culo-papulosas y pruriginosas, afectando de manera sim&#233;trica las extremidades y la regi&#243;n gl&#250;tea.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9,e0a2b5f5d5b3682c870f787f54f6b5ef</data>
      <data key="d3">821</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10435</data>
      <data key="d7">b672ac2c0c1445dfbf8e1fa6bb649481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SINDROME DE DOWN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de Down es una condici&#243;n gen&#233;tica que se ha asociado con un riesgo significativamente mayor de desarrollar enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10436</data>
      <data key="d7">d30142ddfd8d41e4be84ca4329bbf642</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD TIROIDEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los trastornos tiroideos autoinmunes, como el hipotiroidismo, son m&#225;s frecuentes en pacientes con enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10437</data>
      <data key="d7">7f85380bb28d486e903c028709343658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD HEPATICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad hep&#225;tica puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad cel&#237;aca, incluyendo hepatitis autoinmune y cirrosis biliar primaria.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10438</data>
      <data key="d7">b8ee08ecc98f4ace941ac3d7c944a5c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOCARDITIS Y MIOCARDIOPATIA DILATADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La miocarditis y la miocardiopat&#237;a dilatada son condiciones card&#237;acas que pueden asociarse raramente con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10439</data>
      <data key="d7">216dd2aeb01e4ac5b36e6a69ecfce9a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOESPLENISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El hipoesplenismo es una condici&#243;n que se ha descrito en casos asociados a la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, aumentando el riesgo de infecciones severas.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10440</data>
      <data key="d7">2862de9bb0e04d72ba02fc99a341b529</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT SELECTIVO DE IGA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El d&#233;ficit selectivo de IgA aparece en un 1-2% de los pacientes cel&#237;acos, lo que indica una posible relaci&#243;n con la enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10441</data>
      <data key="d7">722e04b1ec7946bdbd58500f6286462e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIESGO DE NEOPLASIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El riesgo de aparici&#243;n de ciertos tumores, como linfoma intestinal no-Hodgkin, parece estar aumentado en pacientes con enfermedad cel&#237;aca.</data>
      <data key="d2">84ce554b4fe9832d90b74a225fe956b9</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10442</data>
      <data key="d7">efdec4be2faa4e20b5d3ee31146fcac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES EN LAS FANERAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las alteraciones en las faneras, como piel, pelo y u&#241;as, pueden ser s&#237;ntomas de deficiencias nutricionales en pacientes cel&#237;acos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
