    <node id="ANTICUERPOS EMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los anticuerpos EMA son marcadores serol&#243;gicos utilizados en el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, indicando la presencia de una respuesta inmune al gluten.</data>
      <data key="d2">41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10451</data>
      <data key="d7">17bc442a695645d091a833ea8cd0ab85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICUERPOS TTG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los anticuerpos antitransglutaminasa (tTG) son pruebas serol&#243;gicas que ayudan a diagnosticar la enfermedad cel&#237;aca al detectar la respuesta inmune al gluten.</data>
      <data key="d2">41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10452</data>
      <data key="d7">b0f6898481d14034874ff7bd676d010a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D-XILOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La D-xilosa es un monosac&#225;rido utilizado en pruebas para evaluar la absorci&#243;n intestinal y la integridad de la mucosa intestinal en el diagn&#243;stico de malabsorci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392</data>
      <data key="d3">816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10453</data>
      <data key="d7">188c1d4eab7747bcba1b5ccfc007a27e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETISTA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A dietitian is a healthcare professional who specializes in nutrition and diet planning, particularly for patients with specific dietary needs. This expertise is especially crucial for individuals with conditions such as celiac disease, as a specialized dietitian can tailor dietary recommendations to meet their unique requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10454</data>
      <data key="d7">764842eab63e443a9ecff09307dc571c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEBADA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">La cebada es otro cereal que contiene gluten y es perjudicial para los pacientes con celiaqu&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566</data>
      <data key="d3">829</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10455</data>
      <data key="d7">6df312c4d6a448c0b195f8b4566f01fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMARANTO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El amaranto es un cereal sin gluten que se puede consumir de forma segura por los pacientes con celiaqu&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">8eef8cced3d7433de267e8e624813566</data>
      <data key="d3">829</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10456</data>
      <data key="d7">23d07ddd2d5043e2bb4450b06c28a347</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Un equipo multidisciplinario que proporciona seguimiento continuo a pacientes con enfermedad celiaca para supervisar la efectividad del tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10457</data>
      <data key="d7">62dfb8a6629d4c2dbb98c0108cba2fd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALORIC REQUIREMENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Requerimientos cal&#243;ricos que deben ser calculados y adaptados a las necesidades individuales de los pacientes con enfermedad celiaca.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4</data>
      <data key="d3">829</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10458</data>
      <data key="d7">9abb71bcce094e118ee34305eee542a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY HABITS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary habits refer to the patterns of food consumption that can significantly impact health outcomes, including cardiovascular health. These habits encompass various aspects of an individual's diet, including the types of foods consumed and the frequency of consumption. Additionally, it is important to consider the previous dietary habits of patients, particularly when adapting to specific dietary requirements, such as following a gluten-free diet. Respecting and adapting these prior habits is crucial for ensuring compliance and promoting overall health in individuals making dietary changes.</data>
      <data key="d2">2f1fed346bb25032751634adf513337a,a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4</data>
      <data key="d3">1618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10459</data>
      <data key="d7">392281868e7f4ea6bd84a42ef5f9463d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD DE ESPA&#209;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ministry of Health of Spain oversees public health policies and provides guidelines regarding celiac disease and gluten-free diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10460</data>
      <data key="d7">e348428625d944ed964bdfde2dad93c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CELIAC SPRUE ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Celiac Sprue Association is a U.S.-based organization that provides support and resources for individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">810</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10461</data>
      <data key="d7">170a4bc8255a43069aef3437634661fd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF DIABETES AND DIGESTIVE AND KIDNEY DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) is a component of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) that focuses on conducting research and disseminating information related to various health issues. This institute is dedicated to studying digestive diseases, including celiac disease, and also provides valuable information on lactose intolerance. Through its research initiatives and educational resources, the NIDDK aims to enhance understanding and treatment of conditions affecting diabetes, digestive health, and kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821,bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c</data>
      <data key="d3">809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10462</data>
      <data key="d7">6a204af62b224e188846f1b5c1e6ce0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTEN INTOLERANCE GROUP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gluten Intolerance Group is an organization that offers support and resources for individuals with gluten-related disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">810</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10463</data>
      <data key="d7">ddc53ba40081407e972f40db1d62327d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SCOTT ADAMS ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An association that supports individuals with celiac disease and promotes awareness about gluten-free diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10464</data>
      <data key="d7">35a8da6cfea447d7af0c981721f2c74a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN COELIAC SOCIETIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An association that represents various organizations across Europe focused on celiac disease and gluten-free living.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10465</data>
      <data key="d7">ba1af98e7a684080a693e14907843d47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTEN-FREE DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The gluten-free diet is a dietary regimen that excludes gluten, a protein found in wheat, barley, and rye. This diet is essential for managing celiac disease and gluten intolerance, as it helps individuals avoid the adverse health effects associated with the consumption of gluten.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821,17593b5969d4126aef1c56a7d32dc922</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10466</data>
      <data key="d7">2f924c8d65724dbca1ffeb8869ed34d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARINA DE MA&#205;Z">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Corn flour is a gluten-free alternative to wheat flour that can be used in various recipes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10467</data>
      <data key="d7">1960e1e6ca4c47e6bce1a1d80d6ac4e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARINA DE PATATAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Potato flour is another gluten-free substitute that can be used in cooking and baking.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10468</data>
      <data key="d7">b30ddeb5693a463487912d4ada599e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HARINA DE ARROZ">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Rice flour is a gluten-free flour option that is often used in gluten-free recipes.</data>
      <data key="d2">1387d49a5eae8a32dd81f2f9991a4821</data>
      <data key="d3">807</data>
