    <node id="HOMOCISTINURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Homocystinuria is a metabolic disorder resulting from a deficiency in cystathionine beta-synthase, leading to the accumulation of homocysteine.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38</data>
      <data key="d3">853</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10529</data>
      <data key="d7">43fa84e0fec3429eada6d5d8cec41759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE ORINA DE JARABE DE ARCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ENFERMEDAD DE ORINA DE JARABE DE ARCE," known as Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD), is an amino acid metabolism disorder. It is characterized by a deficiency in the branched-chain alpha-keto acid dehydrogenase complex. This deficiency results in the accumulation of specific amino acids in the body, which can lead to various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38,06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027</data>
      <data key="d3">1743</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">10530</data>
      <data key="d7">cede1024a0e745edb51277b4f1f4b976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERRORRES INNATOS DEL CICLO DE LA UREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urea cycle disorders are genetic conditions that result in a deficiency of one of the enzymes in the urea cycle, leading to the accumulation of ammonia in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38</data>
      <data key="d3">851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10531</data>
      <data key="d7">9864f96c93694dfface45577e2374641</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GLUCOGENOSIS refers to a group of diseases known as glycogen storage diseases, which are characterized by alterations in glycogen synthesis or degradation. These metabolic disorders arise from defects in the enzymes responsible for glycogen synthesis and breakdown, resulting in the excessive accumulation of glycogen in various tissues. The underlying cause of glucogenosis is typically enzyme deficiencies that disrupt normal glycogen metabolism, leading to abnormal storage of glycogen in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">10532</data>
      <data key="d7">c8dabb3225fc4e36b2a4d8a92ff7e60d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLOPAT&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic disorders are conditions that disrupt normal metabolism, leading to the accumulation of toxic substances in the body due to enzyme deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38</data>
      <data key="d3">1445</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10533</data>
      <data key="d7">9ab9122f68714da6a03942418538d053</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BADAJOZ">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38</data>
      <data key="d3">853</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10534</data>
      <data key="d7">c8d128ab80c54d9eb977022ac1689cd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH) is an essential enzyme that plays a critical role in the metabolism of phenylalanine, converting it into tyrosine. A deficiency in PAH is the underlying cause of phenylketonuria (PKU), a genetic disorder that can lead to serious health issues if not managed properly. In the context of treatment, the functional gene for PAH is introduced in gene therapy to address this deficiency in patients with PKU.</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">1502</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">10535</data>
      <data key="d7">3ba925651dd846eeb4d77563f23bf66a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BH4">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tetrahydrobiopterin is a cofactor necessary for the activity of phenylalanine hydroxylase and is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10536</data>
      <data key="d7">24a3316cb0644603ab918fa8fe09bb2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DHPR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dihydropteridine reductase is an enzyme that plays a role in the regeneration of tetrahydrobiopterin, which is crucial for neurotransmitter synthesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10537</data>
      <data key="d7">90af07595ad842c2bcaebf2faeae3dce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PKU">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a genetic and metabolic disorder characterized by the accumulation of phenylalanine in the body. If left untreated, this accumulation can lead to severe neurological issues. To prevent such damage, individuals with PKU require careful dietary management to control their phenylalanine levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">1503</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">10538</data>
      <data key="d7">781828dbfc7e4144825ac1b3fa644bcc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HPA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperphenylalaninemia benign (HPA) is a mild form of phenylketonuria characterized by lower levels of phenylalanine that do not require dietary treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">856</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10539</data>
      <data key="d7">4345df0536a64503afe6f86545eec108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IVS10">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">IVS10 is the most common mutation associated with phenylketonuria in Southern Europe, affecting the PAH gene.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d3">1502</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
