    <node id="L-TIROSINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">L-Tirosina is a non-essential amino acid that is produced from phenylalanine and plays a crucial role in the production of neurotransmitters. It is often included in nutritional discussions due to its importance in various physiological processes. Additionally, L-Tirosina may require supplementation in certain cases, particularly for individuals with phenylketonuria, a genetic disorder that affects the metabolism of phenylalanine.</data>
      <data key="d2">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a,b789dfd7a5aa36fac33c5c881a1a4981,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc</data>
