    <node id="PATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PATO, which refers to duck, is a type of poultry commonly used in various cuisines. However, it is important to note that duck is not allowed in modified diets due to its potential health implications. Specifically, PATO, or duck, is a bird that can have a significant purine content, which may influence uric acid levels in individuals. Therefore, while PATO is a popular culinary choice, its consumption may be restricted for those managing dietary concerns related to purine intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,5e5296bf59e1f2b0fbeace9cc0e62ef5</data>
