    <node id="NAVB">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NAVB is an organization involved in dietary management and treatment protocols for conditions like phenylketonuria (PKU).</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10626</data>
      <data key="d7">20d27a5c055c4cc89b333a2d4f5100ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHENYLKETONURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a metabolic disorder that necessitates strict dietary management to prevent complications both during pregnancy and throughout an individual's life.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427,9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">10627</data>
      <data key="d7">d65a6d5199404a8891a43aa731361b0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOMACROPEPTIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucomacrop&#233;ptido (GMP) is a dairy-derived peptide that contains very low amounts of phenylalanine and is used to improve dietary options for PKU patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10628</data>
      <data key="d7">19de9948593343b48a7480d8d9f347c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LNAA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">LNAA is a therapeutic option designed to decrease the passage of phenylalanine (Phe) to the brain, making it particularly effective for patients with poor adherence to dietary restrictions. It refers to neutral amino acids that compete with phenylalanine for transport across the blood-brain barrier, thereby aiding in the management of phenylketonuria (PKU).</data>
      <data key="d2">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027,8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1503</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10629</data>
      <data key="d7">c567d66418ab4bfe80c62f583dfc4fe0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TYROSINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tyrosine is an amino acid that may be supplemented during pregnancy for women with PKU to support metabolic needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10630</data>
      <data key="d7">8971b331852445948400d62e37d0e77c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNITINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Carnitine is a nutrient that plays a significant role in metabolic processes and may be evaluated for potential deficiency in patients with Phenylketonuria. Additionally, it is administered during hyperammonemic crises to improve metabolic status in patients with glycogen storage diseases, also known as glucogenosis. This highlights the importance of carnitine in managing specific metabolic disorders and its potential therapeutic applications in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">1691</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10631</data>
      <data key="d7">e8e6257d14ae4f848e964ef5437a941f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="L-PUFA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">L-PUFA refers to long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids that may be considered for supplementation in the management of PKU.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10632</data>
      <data key="d7">815de28a872c487cbe38e99edbec30d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FETAL LIVER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The fetal liver is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine during pregnancy, particularly in the context of maternal PKU management.</data>
      <data key="d2">8c74843de8cb570c0601b11d59744427</data>
      <data key="d3">1690</data>
