    <node id="HOMOCYSTINURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Homocystinuria is a genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in cystathionine beta-synthase, which results in elevated levels of homocysteine in the blood. This condition is classified as an autosomal recessive disorder that affects methionine metabolism, leading to the accumulation of homocysteine and related compounds.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bba475c47cc7e804e16c70787b247f9,4351677d6166c9c88ab941dc8dcecb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1697</data>
