    <node id="HYPERTRANSAMINASEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypertransaminasemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of transaminases in the blood. This condition can occur in patients with urea cycle disorders as well as in those with hepatic glycogenosis. The presence of elevated transaminases indicates potential liver dysfunction or other metabolic disturbances, highlighting the importance of monitoring these enzyme levels in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
