    </node>
    <node id="OTC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">OTC, or Ornithine Transcarbamylase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, which is essential for the detoxification of ammonia in the body. A deficiency in OTC can result in hyperammonemia, a condition characterized by elevated levels of ammonia in the blood, which can be harmful. Additionally, OTC deficiency is associated with specific types of glycogen storage diseases, known as glucogenosis. This highlights the enzyme's importance not only in ammonia metabolism but also in broader metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10702</data>
      <data key="d7">3f9ffeef41284de8828eaae3fcd3aa2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ASS (Argininosuccinate Synthetase) is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, which is essential for the metabolism of nitrogen in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10703</data>
      <data key="d7">d891ea0e167748168a171d5eace97fd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ASL, or Argininosuccinate Lyase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle by facilitating the conversion of argininosuccinate into arginine and fumarate. A deficiency in ASL is linked to a specific type of glycogen storage disease, known as glucogenosis, highlighting its importance in metabolic processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10704</data>
      <data key="d7">835403181d2140049d2540987a8348ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMONIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ammonia is a toxic substance that can accumulate in the body due to metabolic disorders, leading to serious health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880</data>
      <data key="d3">58</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10705</data>
      <data key="d7">df594b90cd6141a5af9f8826c5b5b3ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CPS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">CPS, or Carbamoyl phosphate synthetase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle. Deficiencies in this enzyme are associated with glucogenosis, a condition that affects the metabolism of glycogen.</data>
      <data key="d2">0906c46e832ce2db9f1c58e6e8b54880,d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10706</data>
      <data key="d7">954067c699c24ca09e172f331f8fec27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENESIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucogenesis is the process of glycogen synthesis, which can be affected in glucogenosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10707</data>
      <data key="d7">3bd9330f2f3a426c955402e84221f108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TYPE I GLUCOGENOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Type I glucogenosis, first described in 1929 by von Gierke, is characterized by hypoglycemia and hepatomegaly.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">10708</data>
      <data key="d7">d6c1fe17fc2a4d6fa08ed57a97c915f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VON GIERKE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Von Gierke was the discoverer of type I glucogenosis in 1929.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10709</data>
      <data key="d7">56805632fa3d4dc8a2cb87f782af5875</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUTOSOMAL RECESSIVE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Most glucogenosis diseases are inherited in an autosomal recessive manner, except for certain types linked to the X chromosome.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10710</data>
      <data key="d7">2bace72ba7d44531946128cc70bc7b14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATIC GLYCOGENOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatic glucogenosis refers to glycogen storage diseases that primarily affect the liver and are of nutritional interest.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10711</data>
      <data key="d7">43f1f8e407ce43888cf3ff926c3493f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALPROIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Valproic acid is a medication that should not be used for seizures in patients with glucogenosis as it decreases urea cycle activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10712</data>
      <data key="d7">0492b2939cae482682cb8b65d26c842c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHENOBARBITAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phenobarbital is another medication that is contraindicated in glucogenosis due to its effect on the urea cycle.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10713</data>
      <data key="d7">0694a20bfa37495ebb2f7963e717e503</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERAMMONEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperammonemia is a condition that can occur in patients with glucogenosis, requiring specific treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">1691</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10714</data>
      <data key="d7">9e356988b2704d75bcfb6818535a9c92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEPHROMEGALY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nephromegaly can be associated with glucogenosis and may present with proteinuria and renal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10715</data>
      <data key="d7">3c1f61dc9bcf43d494a94a887dd26c19</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METABOLIC ACIDOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Metabolic acidosis can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in the context of hypoglycemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">d1b2835d6e86f09adefd22378bb6da15</data>
      <data key="d3">449</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10716</data>
      <data key="d7">e2b0d3d887bb47bf8753b03acf865bf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucogenosis de tipo I is a metabolic disorder characterized by the deficiency of the enzyme glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to hypoglycemia and lactic acidosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">10717</data>
      <data key="d7">251fb0fb810e40069eaa0d7ab4b16dc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE VON GIERKE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad de Von Gierke is a condition marked by the deficiency of glucose-6-phosphatase, resulting in the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and associated metabolic issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">10718</data>
      <data key="d7">6e4452dde3f342828f0c523f234bae70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOQU&#205;MICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bioqu&#237;mico refers to the biochemical analysis performed to diagnose conditions like glucogenosis de tipo I and enfermedad de Von Gierke.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10719</data>
      <data key="d7">113a6a3245f448c794a19e0444ec0b9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENOSIS MUSCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucogenosis muscular is a category of glycogen storage diseases that primarily affect muscle tissue, resulting in muscle-related symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10720</data>
      <data key="d7">4ae19c006edb479cb8b0d1d72b7fffa6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENOSIS GENERALIZADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucogenosis generalizada encompasses glycogen storage diseases that affect multiple organs and systems in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10721</data>
      <data key="d7">209239bdad104a7c9b8665c1eb0cb100</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAJA ESTATURA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Baja estatura is a clinical symptom that can occur in patients with glucogenosis, particularly in hepatic forms.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10722</data>
      <data key="d7">e85e102ba3f342df8a9843d01e4a88b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERLACTACIDEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperlactacidemia is a condition of elevated lactate levels in the blood, often seen in metabolic disorders like glucogenosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10723</data>
      <data key="d7">fb27718d8684418f8cdd089c879ee143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiopat&#237;a refers to heart disease, which encompasses various conditions affecting the heart. In the context of glucogenosis, particularly the muscular forms, cardiopat&#237;a can manifest as a symptom. Additionally, it is noted that cardiopat&#237;a can also be caused by the accumulation of iron in the myocardium. Thus, cardiopat&#237;a is a broad term that includes heart diseases resulting from different underlying conditions, including metabolic disorders and iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10724</data>
      <data key="d7">76dec5fc7a804d66afad49c7cccb8411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIOTON&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mioton&#237;a is a condition characterized by delayed relaxation of muscles after contraction, which can occur in some muscular glucogenosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10725</data>
      <data key="d7">85a9fcf032c848f1a203b3702d9d1734</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA HEMOL&#205;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia hemol&#237;tica is a medical condition characterized by the accelerated destruction of red blood cells, resulting in a higher rate of red blood cell breakdown than their production. This condition can lead to elevated levels of &#225;cido &#250;rico in the body. Anemia hemol&#237;tica may also be associated with certain types of glucogenosis, which are metabolic disorders affecting glycogen storage and utilization.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10726</data>
      <data key="d7">b14eb674b27a40259de186e06a34ee7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONVULSIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Convulsiones are seizures that can occur in patients with certain types of glucogenosis, particularly those affecting the nervous system. Additionally, convulsiones can also manifest in severe cases of hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10727</data>
      <data key="d7">70eedf4e9b714eacaf52496dc900b3d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOPSIA DE TEJIDO HEP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biopsia de tejido hep&#225;tico is a diagnostic procedure used to assess liver conditions, including glucogenosis.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10728</data>
      <data key="d7">749e79693bc94124bba97a74c9e9680f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARDIOMIOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardiomiopat&#237;a is a condition characterized by heart muscle disease, which can lead to heart failure and other complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">28633689bf0b9bc990e61fb26722ce16</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10729</data>
      <data key="d7">8764c35525ad4781a4216a2fe1a73bc3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAFLORA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Lafora is associated with a genetic condition known as Lafora disease, which involves a deficiency of laforin and leads to various neurological symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">28633689bf0b9bc990e61fb26722ce16</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10730</data>
      <data key="d7">b3047d6fbf4442d78ede075dd2f7d71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glucogenosis tipo I is a metabolic disorder affecting the body's ability to break down glycogen, leading to various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">28633689bf0b9bc990e61fb26722ce16</data>
      <data key="d3">1179</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">10731</data>
      <data key="d7">6c512aa98d2349598e72fc80539c9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLYCOSADE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycosade is a modified starch that helps maintain blood glucose levels during fasting periods, particularly useful for patients with metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">28633689bf0b9bc990e61fb26722ce16</data>
      <data key="d3">1179</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10732</data>
      <data key="d7">8b828a688d9a40ba9d8dedfe249682b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VON GIERKE TYPE IA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Von Gierke Type Ia is a specific type of hepatic glycogen storage disease characterized by a deficiency in glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to severe hypoglycemia and other metabolic complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d3">1822</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10733</data>
      <data key="d7">70210c3c196f484c85e39c26d9d9b7a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GM-CSF">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF) is a cytokine used in the treatment of certain metabolic disorders to stimulate the production of white blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d2">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10734</data>
      <data key="d7">34c9ef6d1138476aba8f5a5e8e17d7a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="G-CSF">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Granulocyte colony-stimulating factor (G-CSF) is a cytokine that promotes the production of neutrophils and is used in the treatment of neutropenia in metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10735</data>
      <data key="d7">0caba78353904236b5bdb242d0eb6ce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIO Y VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcium and vitamin D are essential nutrients that may be beneficial as supplements in the treatment of hepatic glycogen storage diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10736</data>
      <data key="d7">fa9500486aa34dd9bda7ff4c0fcf7766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IECA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">IECA, or angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, are medications recommended for patients experiencing microalbuminuria, particularly in the context of metabolic disorders. These medications play a crucial role in managing conditions associated with kidney function and protein excretion. Additionally, it has been noted that IECA may be associated with the occurrence of diarrhea as a side effect.</data>
      <data key="d2">44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d3">898</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10737</data>
      <data key="d7">504d73cdd15646288d5695e57300d439</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHENYLALANINE HYDROXYLASE DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phenylalanine hydroxylase deficiency is a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process phenylalanine, leading to various health issues if untreated.</data>
      <data key="d2">9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b</data>
      <data key="d3">1689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">10738</data>
      <data key="d7">04bf09fea46c47749261ab942dbba59d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF HUMAN GENETICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Journal of Human Genetics publishes research related to human genetics, including studies on phenylketonuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b</data>
      <data key="d3">1689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10739</data>
      <data key="d7">71269d41f51b4cbb850cdc5bab344df3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARCHIVES OF DISEASE IN CHILDHOOD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Archives of Disease in Childhood is a journal that publishes research on childhood diseases, including dietary treatments for phenylketonuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b</data>
      <data key="d3">1689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10740</data>
      <data key="d7">e770f512fa8d4ba19019d62b38bfd1eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XI REUNI&#211;N ASOCIACI&#211;N DE NEUROCIENCIAS DEL DESARROLLO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The XI Reuni&#243;n Asociaci&#243;n de Neurociencias del Desarrollo is a meeting focused on developmental neuroscience, which may include discussions on metabolic disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">9783830959445135c718dc21daa0a46b</data>
      <data key="d3">1689</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
