    <node id="GRASA SATURADA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GRASA SATURADA refers to saturated fat, a type of fat that can significantly impact cardiovascular health and is frequently discussed in dietary studies. This type of fat is primarily found in animal-based foods and tropical oils. It is associated with an increase in cholesterol levels and a heightened risk of cardiovascular diseases (ECV). Research indicates that replacing saturated fat with monounsaturated fatty acids can lead to a reduction in LDL cholesterol, suggesting that dietary choices regarding fat types can influence heart health.</data>
      <data key="d2">76da5650c43a6cbc7270a05d3aa3fa1d,e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061</data>
      <data key="d3">1399</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">10764</data>
      <data key="d7">a9f63d59d16b41b4966824e9b18b5e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS DE CADENA LARGA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Los &#225;cidos grasos saturados de cadena larga son un tipo de grasa que se asocia con un mayor riesgo de arteriosclerosis y ECV.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0227f83ebee602b6c9d7163630e495e</data>
      <data key="d3">1399</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
