    </node>
    <node id="AGPI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AGPI, or Acidos Grasos Poliinsaturados, refers to polyunsaturated fatty acids that play a significant role in health by reducing inflammation and enhancing muscle response. These fatty acids are recommended as substitutes for saturated fats, contributing to lower cholesterol levels and promoting overall cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2,a25b0f84bc321cad942a2e33f681a5e4</data>
      <data key="d3">1649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10772</data>
      <data key="d7">d56d5f9dfcbb48f28f47f6e179184d8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AGM refers to monounsaturated fatty acids, which are recognized as healthier dietary options compared to saturated fats. These fatty acids are considered beneficial for heart health and play a significant role in the Mediterranean diet. Monounsaturated fatty acids (AGM) are healthy fats found in foods such as olive oil and nuts, contributing to overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">0090177678aee58d08471d09d24d2842,3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2,e04e16f606e0bc5eeb59e2d5388ab061</data>
      <data key="d3">1649</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">10773</data>
      <data key="d7">2dcf635cb1f24f428aab88de5f18f283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GSAT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GSAT refers to saturated fatty acids, which are being studied for their association with coronary heart disease.</data>
