    <node id="MARGARINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Margarina is a type of fat spread that consists of 18% saturated fats, 48% monounsaturated fats, and 29% polyunsaturated fats. It is commonly used in cooking and baking. However, it is recommended that its consumption be limited in children's diets due to health considerations. Additionally, Margarina can be included in modified diets under specific conditions, indicating its versatility in various dietary plans.</data>
      <data key="d2">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10781</data>
      <data key="d7">43a61c6faa474715a4512b4a6ec299b5</data>
    </node>
