    <node id="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cidos Grasos de Cadena Corta, or short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), are a type of fatty acid characterized by having one to six carbon atoms. They are primarily produced through the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates and dietary fibers in the colon. These fatty acids play a crucial role in various physiological processes and are absorbed by the colon. Notably, SCFAs have no effect on atherogenesis and thrombogenesis, indicating their neutral impact on certain cardiovascular conditions. Overall, &#193;cidos Grasos de Cadena Corta are important metabolites that contribute to gut health and metabolic functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3,3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a</data>
      <data key="d3">1004</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10793</data>
      <data key="d7">b558076a55554c19b40f0db7ab997a46</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO L&#193;URICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A type of fatty acid with a positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10794</data>
      <data key="d7">9f28f91fc7834415800659a2d3a0df1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO MIR&#205;STICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A type of fatty acid with a strong positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10795</data>
      <data key="d7">88e816d5fcf34349b25eeec168a76c9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO PALM&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A type of fatty acid with a moderate positive effect on both atherogenesis and thrombogenesis.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d053ac744015b40d8790ff91b5d02f2</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">10796</data>
