    <node id="ANNALS OF INTERNAL MEDICINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Annals of Internal Medicine" is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research and reviews related to various topics in internal medicine. It has published studies on conditions such as pagophagia and iron deficiency anemia, as well as hyponatremia. Additionally, the journal has featured a subgroup analysis of a randomized trial investigating the prevention of diabetes through Mediterranean diets. Through its diverse range of articles, the "Annals of Internal Medicine" contributes significantly to the field of internal medicine by disseminating important findings and insights.</data>
