    </node>
    <node id="X-ALD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">X-ALD is a hereditary disorder linked to the X chromosome, characterized by an inability to degrade very long-chain fatty acids, leading to various clinical manifestations.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">10988</data>
      <data key="d7">1df117c4316f4ee8bf80c22570c9abdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALDP">
      <data key="d0">PROTEIN</data>
      <data key="d1">ALDP, or Adrenoleukodystrophy Protein, is a peroxisomal membrane protein that plays a crucial role in the transport of very long-chain fatty acids. Alterations in ALDP are associated with X-linked Adrenoleukodystrophy (X-ALD), a genetic disorder that affects the nervous system and adrenal glands. The study of ALDP is significant for both the diagnosis and understanding of X-ALD, highlighting its importance in the context of this disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618,b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">10989</data>
      <data key="d7">6b8033e5776e4ebd8d848601223219da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADRENOMIELONEUROPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenomieloneuropathy is a form of X-ALD that typically presents in young adults, characterized by progressive spastic paraparesis and sphincter disturbances.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10990</data>
      <data key="d7">d204fe01de6c45c590b6edb0fbaf8680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE ADDISON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Addison's syndrome is a condition that can occur in about 10% of X-ALD patients, characterized by primary adrenal insufficiency without apparent neurological involvement.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10991</data>
      <data key="d7">e5929b36da064c5c9625308b799e51c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMA CEREBRAL INFANTIL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The childhood cerebral form of X-ALD is characterized by rapid progression of symptoms starting between ages 3 and 10, including hyperactivity and poor school performance.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10992</data>
      <data key="d7">a60beb9973d7496bb91ef6f507c9bef1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADULT CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The adult cerebral form of X-ALD typically begins in the third decade of life and progresses similarly to the childhood form.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10993</data>
      <data key="d7">67e759fc0fed4a479401cb4753ffe576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADRENOMIELONEUROPAT&#205;A DEL ADULTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adult adrenomieloneuropathy usually presents in young adults with progressive spastic paraparesis and sphincter disturbances.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10994</data>
      <data key="d7">19045de85a3e4817ae239b97120cd188</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA ADRENOCORTICAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenal insufficiency is a common condition in X-ALD patients, often requiring study and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">b8eac0e9c85a85238f3a45f939dadb82</data>
      <data key="d3">1728</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10995</data>
      <data key="d7">4f660b7a53a644f8811f9e7ccedad656</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTEX ADRENAL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The adrenal cortex is the outer part of the adrenal glands, which are responsible for producing hormones, and is affected in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10996</data>
      <data key="d7">854f627051ab4e1093fee7adcad46dff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEXA-COSANOIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hexacosanoic acid (C26:0) is a very long-chain fatty acid that accumulates in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, contributing to the disease's pathology.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10997</data>
      <data key="d7">5fe259fd2e1a4686b801d462ece83f0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TETRA-COSANOIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tetracosanoic acid (C24:0) is another fatty acid that accumulates in lower amounts in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">10998</data>
      <data key="d7">920d0375dfd24d4cb837dad8f36568dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGCML">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">AGCML is a biochemical marker associated with adrenoleukodystrophy, a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. It is monitored during treatment to assess the condition of patients. AGCML refers specifically to very long-chain saturated fatty acids that accumulate in the bodies of individuals with adrenoleukodystrophy, leading to various health issues. These fatty acids can cause metabolic problems and are also linked to Reye-like syndrome, which further complicates the health of affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079,34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1499</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">10999</data>
      <data key="d7">7de01d3ba29940ad865ded127285c3c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROBLASTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibroblasts are cells that can be cultured to study the oxidation rates of AGCML in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11000</data>
      <data key="d7">0e5a8c890d4b4dc8b07cb777d121978e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLASMA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Plasma is the liquid component of blood that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes. It serves as a medium for transporting nutrients, hormones, and waste products throughout the body. Additionally, plasma is significant in medical diagnostics, as it allows for the measurement of fatty acid levels, which can be instrumental in diagnosing conditions such as adrenoleukodystrophy.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618,79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11001</data>
      <data key="d7">f75084e730004c42bb08f2fc0df9c634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AXONOPATHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Axonopathy is a condition characterized by the degeneration of axons, which is a significant finding in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11002</data>
      <data key="d7">3fc499be86e8401e8394b10605294862</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADRENAL INSUFFICIENCY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenal insufficiency is a common complication in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, often requiring steroid treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11003</data>
      <data key="d7">a69a9694601443f4a84a5aaa5a7e0505</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GENE MUTATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gene mutations related to adrenoleucodistrofia can be studied to aid in diagnosis, although no prevalent mutation has been identified.</data>
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11004</data>
      <data key="d7">29a008a2b0a04b569fce948a4984b4a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORFOLOGICALLY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">34299d74df25d13e56cd62aab766e618</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11005</data>
      <data key="d7">f1054d97c951433792b7aee18731798d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD) is a genetic disorder that impacts the metabolism of specific fatty acids, resulting in the buildup of very long-chain fatty acids in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">11006</data>
      <data key="d7">ddf10c9417204431974165aa97798120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RIZZO ET AL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Rizzo et al are researchers who demonstrated the effects of oleic acid on fibroblasts from ALD patients in 1986.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11007</data>
      <data key="d7">ef177e4347644c338b6e889a5333d991</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITE DE LORENZO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Aceite de Lorenzo is a dietary supplement specifically utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD), a genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. This treatment aims to normalize plasma concentrations of very long-chain fatty acids, particularly focusing on reducing levels of C26:0 in patients with ALD. The formulation of Aceite de Lorenzo combines glycerol trioleate and glycerol trierucate, which work together to achieve this normalization.

While Aceite de Lorenzo has therapeutic benefits, it is important to note that it may also cause side effects, including plaquetopenia (a reduction in platelet count) and a decrease in essential fatty acids. Despite these potential adverse effects, Aceite de Lorenzo remains a significant dietary intervention for managing the symptoms and progression of Adrenoleukodystrophy.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8,c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">11008</data>
      <data key="d7">2e090f7d84924a4dbe19143ede43a460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GTO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GTO, or glycerol trioleate, is a dietary component utilized in the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). It is recognized as an alternative treatment option that can be continued even if Lorenzo's oil is discontinued due to potential side effects. GTO is notable for its high percentage of oleic acid, which contributes to its therapeutic properties in managing ALD.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11009</data>
      <data key="d7">5c069094a9e44d8ca21637f1325c986f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GTE, or Glycerol trierucate, is a dietary component characterized by a high percentage of erucic acid. It is utilized in conjunction with GTO for the treatment of Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). However, it is important to note that GTE treatment may be suspended if patients using Lorenzo's oil experience thrombocytopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11010</data>
      <data key="d7">7a34ed1a72f2488f85d0db531a025e1e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C26:0">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">C26:0, also known as hexacosanoic acid, is a very long-chain saturated fatty acid that plays a significant role in the diagnosis of adrenoleucodystrophy (ALD). This fatty acid accumulates in patients suffering from ALD, and efforts are made to reduce its levels through dietary interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,9ceafecc91648750126099fd54024495</data>
      <data key="d3">1498</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11011</data>
      <data key="d7">8a5b25d1b7164bbbab938d3b83fe4453</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO OLEICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cido Oleico is a monounsaturated fatty acid recognized for its safety in emulsions intended for patients requiring nutritional support. Additionally, it has been utilized in fibroblast cultures to lower levels of C26:0 in patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This dual application highlights its significance in both nutritional and therapeutic contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11012</data>
      <data key="d7">37b518f4106a4073a77b770000f3207c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO ER&#218;CICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">&#193;cido er&#250;cico es un &#225;cido graso que se encuentra en los l&#237;pidos plaquetarios y est&#225; relacionado con la plaquetopenia en pacientes que utilizan aceite de Lorenzo. Este &#225;cido graso tambi&#233;n se encuentra en aceites de colza y mostaza, y es importante destacar que los pacientes con adrenoleucodistrofia (ALD) no pueden metabolizarlo adecuadamente.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11013</data>
      <data key="d7">38632c291fa1441ab664fff9679444ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA RESTRINGIDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The restricted diet is a treatment approach for ALD that limits saturated very long-chain fatty acids.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11014</data>
      <data key="d7">12088c762c414bbdb44c44e2e537d346</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVEL PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plasma levels refer to the concentration of fatty acids in the blood, which are monitored in ALD patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9</data>
      <data key="d3">1498</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11015</data>
      <data key="d7">a08f121a89544e7884f22d378c95b9d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROBLASTOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11016</data>
      <data key="d7">ba3f5568a09d4c98b98cf4001f048737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADRENOLEUCOMIELOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La adrenoleucomielopat&#237;a es una enfermedad neurol&#243;gica que puede no responder al tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo en estados avanzados.</data>
      <data key="d2">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11017</data>
      <data key="d7">9d2c1205778847e188ee8f6498cfec58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE DE M&#201;DULA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TRASPLANTE DE M&#201;DULA &#211;SEA" refers to a bone marrow transplant procedure that is sometimes utilized in the treatment of various medical conditions, including Adrenoleukodystrophy (ALD). This procedure may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition to help reduce infection rates during recovery. While bone marrow transplants have been performed in certain cases of ALD, the effectiveness of this treatment remains uncertain, particularly in advanced stages of the disease. However, it is considered a treatment option for patients who exhibit moderate neurological involvement in ALD.</data>
      <data key="d2">202e4fa915a698c9d9164c3fcc61534e,9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8,c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11018</data>
      <data key="d7">15af9a0f9b454dfd84e009dcf4d46666</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES ASINTOM&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los pacientes asintom&#225;ticos pueden beneficiarse del tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo, que reduce la frecuencia y severidad del deterioro neurol&#243;gico.</data>
      <data key="d2">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11019</data>
      <data key="d7">216982af0ec349bf87b9b197a10289e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES CON DISFUNCI&#211;N ADRENAL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los pacientes con disfunci&#243;n adrenal o neurol&#243;gica preexistente pueden no ver mejoras con el tratamiento de aceite de Lorenzo.</data>
      <data key="d2">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d3">353</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11020</data>
      <data key="d7">b03d2918be104a6683e2a9d05117db4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALPROATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Valproato is a medication that has shown neuroprotective capabilities in animal models for adrenoleucodistrofia and has potential antioxidant effects in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11021</data>
      <data key="d7">40d3d706408b4ada8f60310a6a49feb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOVASTATINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lovastatina, also known as lovastatin, is a medication primarily used to reduce cholesterol levels in the body. Its effectiveness can be influenced by food intake. Additionally, lovastatina has therapeutic applications beyond cholesterol management; it can also reduce AGCML levels in patients suffering from adrenoleucodistrofia. The drug functions by inhibiting nitric oxide synthase, contributing to its diverse pharmacological effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94</data>
      <data key="d3">354</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11022</data>
      <data key="d7">165940fb475b43ce844b446f3d6fb638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETA-INTERFER&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Beta-interfer&#243;n is an immunosuppressive agent that has been tested for reducing inflammatory responses in brain lesions associated with ALD but has not shown significant clinical improvement.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11023</data>
      <data key="d7">c7b045763e954662bee64e78190887c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MITOXANTRONE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Mitoxantrone is an immunosuppressive agent that has been trialed for treating ALD-related brain lesions without significant success.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11024</data>
      <data key="d7">9d519b1d549e40fe8cc867a860f13e38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INMUNOGLOBULINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Immunoglobulins, also known as "inmunoglobulinas," are antibodies produced by the immune system that play a crucial role in identifying and neutralizing pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They are essential components of the immune response and are found in bodily fluids like chyle. In addition to their protective functions, inmunoglobulinas have been investigated as immunosuppressive agents in the treatment of autoimmune liver disease (ALD) to help reduce inflammation. However, studies have indicated that they have not demonstrated significant clinical improvement in this context. Overall, inmunoglobulinas are vital for immune defense while also being explored for their potential therapeutic applications in certain medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d3">1797</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11025</data>
      <data key="d7">ad9b3a2e65fd47ee93d7c7a6e0946a10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BACLOFENO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Baclofeno is a medication used to treat spasticity as a complication of adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11026</data>
      <data key="d7">7a17ea5f4fb04b0085b22a58b099c65c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIGABATRINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Vigabatrina is a drug used to treat seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11027</data>
      <data key="d7">6de5652dcb804e2fa3ac1acf159c348e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FENOBARBITAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fenobarbital is a medication that enhances penetration into the nervous system and has a delayed elimination effect, which can lead to drowsiness. It is primarily used to control seizures in patients suffering from adrenoleucodystrophy.</data>
      <data key="d2">0745ce31d3922cbba1497dbe1d2845de,0a9b42ff082f2d0bb036ec3365d9a6e9</data>
      <data key="d3">1500</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11028</data>
      <data key="d7">a52c391b456140b8aba19a96872379d2</data>
