    </node>
    <node id="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adrenoleukodystrophy is a genetic disorder that primarily affects lipid metabolism, leading to the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids in the body. This condition has significant impacts on both the nervous system and the adrenal glands, resulting in a range of neurological symptoms. The disorder is characterized by its progressive nature, which can lead to severe complications if not managed appropriately.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f,c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d3">1489</data>
