    <node id="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone Marrow Transplantation is a journal dedicated to publishing research on hematopoietic stem cell transplantation and related fields. The term "bone marrow transplantation" refers to a medical procedure that involves administering high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells. This procedure is primarily used to treat various conditions, particularly hematological malignancies, where the bone marrow is either replaced or supplemented. Additionally, bone marrow transplantation serves as a treatment option for several genetic disorders, such as adrenoleukodystrophy, with the goal of restoring normal function in the central nervous system.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f,6efaddddefe1cf5ab78825e1d8c53cab,73d47e377c2910da3393d7bb65f80e8e,c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1,ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4</data>
