    <node id="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">QUILOT&#211;RAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can manifest as a pleural effusion and may lead to symptoms such as dyspnea (difficulty breathing) and cough. Chylothorax can occur spontaneously or as a result of trauma, often linked to surgical procedures or disorders of the lymphatic system. Treatment for QUILOT&#211;RAX typically involves dietary modifications, including specific diets aimed at managing fat metabolism, as well as various medical interventions. These interventions may include surgical techniques and interventional radiology, depending on the underlying cause of the condition. Overall, careful management is essential to address the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural cavity and to alleviate associated symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86,9927d054458e409309b9e917cbb6a10c,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9,ba4a819ecea2015fc907ed907767f6c5,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d3">1798</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">33</data>
      <data key="d6">11069</data>
      <data key="d7">b30c3214b92746fb938e342ea2126943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ascitis quilosa is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of chyle, a lymphatic fluid, in the abdominal cavity. This condition often arises due to the rupture or obstruction of abdominal lymphatic ducts and is typically observed around the fifth postoperative day when patients have begun an oral diet. Ascitis quilosa can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may necessitate dietary modifications or surgical intervention. It is associated with various medical conditions and can cause symptoms such as abdominal distension. Treatment approaches for ascitis quilosa may include conservative management or surgical options, depending on the severity and underlying causes. In summary, ascitis quilosa involves the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the peritoneal cavity, requiring specific medical and dietary management to address the associated complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86,9927d054458e409309b9e917cbb6a10c,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9,ba4a819ecea2015fc907ed907767f6c5,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d3">1796</data>
