    <node id="AMILOIDOSIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Amyloidosis is a disease characterized by the accumulation of amyloid proteins in various organs, which can lead to serious health conditions. This condition can result in complications such as ascitis quilosa and is associated with chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction, affecting multiple organs, including the gastrointestinal system. The buildup of these abnormal proteins can impair the function of the intestines, potentially affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating the use of parenteral nutrition for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d3">1796</data>
