    <node id="TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL&#211;GICO" refers to pharmacological treatment, which involves the use of medications to manage various medical conditions. Specifically, it includes the administration of drugs such as somatostatin or octreotide, which are utilized to address conditions like quilot&#243;rax (chylothorax) and ascitis quilosa (chylous ascites). Additionally, pharmacological treatment may also affect a patient's ability to receive enteral nutrition, indicating that the use of these medications can have implications for nutritional management in patients undergoing such treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d3">1798</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11102</data>
      <data key="d7">87ae47baa653466cbbba4c60e0116933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">"TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR" refers to a management approach that employs non-surgical methods to address medical conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites. This treatment strategy emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies as initial interventions, prioritizing resolution of the condition without resorting to invasive surgical options.</data>
      <data key="d2">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d3">1798</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11103</data>
      <data key="d7">b482aeb110924cc78c312da19bbf1ee9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA MODIFICADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA MODIFICADA" refers to a therapeutic dietary approach specifically designed to manage conditions such as quilot&#243;rax and ascitis quilosa. This modified diet focuses on reducing the intake of long-chain triglycerides while supplementing with medium-chain triglycerides. The primary goal of the dieta modificada is to address the unique nutritional needs associated with these health conditions, promoting better health outcomes through careful dietary management.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d3">486</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11104</data>
      <data key="d7">73f9893528af4b47aed08dc61d31e764</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEJIDOS PERIF&#201;RICOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Tejidos perif&#233;ricos refers to peripheral tissues in the body where fatty acids are transported and utilized.</data>
      <data key="d2">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d3">486</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11105</data>
      <data key="d7">7487cd3ff124443ab997e0f1bf080305</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTARY SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional supplementation with TCM is a dietary approach aimed at enhancing energy intake and improving the organoleptic properties of low-fat diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375</data>
      <data key="d3">486</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11106</data>
      <data key="d7">e8ea8d45710f48839977cb379b2dec08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIPIDS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LIPIDS are a group of fats that play a crucial role in nutrition and energy supply. They are particularly important in medical settings, such as in patients with prolonged stays in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), where lipid emulsions serve as a source of energy and essential fatty acids. The evaluation of lipids focuses on their fatty acid composition and stability, especially in nutritional products designed for various dietary needs. In the context of pancreatitis, lipids can be administered intravenously; however, their use is controversial due to potential complications that may arise. Additionally, dietary advice regarding the selection of foods in modified diets often emphasizes the importance of long-chain and medium-chain triglycerides, highlighting the diverse applications and considerations surrounding lipids in both clinical and dietary contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,440978f75b135fa97eb7b99ca379e9a4,46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf,a66b01654a2f495559fd1a24efc0e64e,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155</data>
