    <node id="WILDER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Wilder was a researcher who in 1921 described the ketogenic diet, attributing its anticonvulsant properties to the production of ketone bodies.</data>
      <data key="d2">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d3">1940</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11221</data>
      <data key="d7">1f4f72a2690a4cb8b99309480cb8df93</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MAE, which stands for "medicamentos antiepil&#233;pticos," is a treatment approach primarily used for managing epilepsy, particularly in patients with refractory epilepsy. While MAE has become the primary treatment option for epilepsy, effectively controlling seizures, it has also led to dietary treatments, such as the ketogenic diet, being considered secondary options. The efficacy of the ketogenic diet can vary among patients, and in some cases, it may still play a role in the overall treatment plan alongside antiepileptic medications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e,2d07762e6db07c2587caceac3427a1c7,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02</data>
      <data key="d3">1942</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11222</data>
      <data key="d7">cdc99b5e9a1b4652b789d1e111b8ec1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRISIS EPILEPTICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Epileptic seizures are episodes of uncontrolled electrical activity in the brain, which can be managed through various treatments, including dietary approaches.</data>
      <data key="d2">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d3">1942</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11223</data>
      <data key="d7">695034c12eb549e2a68d407883eed55d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCLEROSIS TUBEROSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esclerosis tuberosa es un trastorno gen&#233;tico que provoca el crecimiento de tumores benignos en diversos &#243;rganos, incluyendo el cerebro. Esta condici&#243;n puede estar asociada con la epilepsia, lo que la convierte en un foco de atenci&#243;n en el tratamiento de esta enfermedad. Adem&#225;s, la esclerosis tuberosa es una de las condiciones para las cuales se aplica la dieta cetog&#233;nica, un enfoque diet&#233;tico que ha mostrado beneficios en el manejo de la epilepsia.</data>
      <data key="d2">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e,a8929d6c031b44205ed738ec0a0cd435</data>
      <data key="d3">1940</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11224</data>
      <data key="d7">010a586c8a1e49d18011d985c83ab4a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE LENNOX-GASTAUT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lennox-Gastaut syndrome is a severe form of epilepsy characterized by multiple types of seizures and is treated with the ketogenic diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d3">1940</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
