    </node>
    <node id="PEDIATRICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pediatrics is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to the health and medical care of infants, children, and adolescents. It publishes a wide range of research and reviews focused on child health, including studies on various topics such as vitamin K status in children with cystic fibrosis and the impact of iron deficiency on cognitive achievement among school-aged children. The journal also provides guidelines for the diagnosis and prevention of iron deficiency in infants and young children, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in pediatric health. Overall, Pediatrics serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge and practices related to the health and well-being of children.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f06578cbfda22ce8c7d322ba35a93a1,3704ab8452a14a91fe92eee82e9739fb,4eb41f33f9aba3b8ecd3906de91a1345,9303a85464d02f1cc012aaca21edf9bb,c3e74ddf9529482684f4b62e713df49b,e533f9391cb85c02809d6f09d3a4d08e</data>
