    <node id="DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO" refers to a potassium-controlled diet specifically designed to limit potassium intake. This dietary regimen is particularly important for managing conditions such as hyperkalemia, especially in patients with renal issues. Additionally, the diet plays a crucial role in regulating potassium levels, which is vital for maintaining cardiovascular and muscular health. By controlling potassium intake, individuals can better manage their health conditions and promote overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">31b61ae47905168ef430433c9eb5237a,9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b</data>
      <data key="d3">832</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11380</data>
      <data key="d7">3f708ec059074a9aa36e88ae5006e1da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL CONTINUA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Continuous peritoneal dialysis is a treatment that allows for a lower risk of hyperkalemia due to constant therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">31b61ae47905168ef430433c9eb5237a</data>
      <data key="d3">1153</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11381</data>
      <data key="d7">ffa8232c1a304cd98ad5069cfd8f2aa0</data>
    </node>
