    <node id="HORMONAS CALCITROPAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las hormonas calciotropas son un grupo de tres hormonas que regulan el metabolismo del calcio en el cuerpo, actuando en el intestino, ri&#241;&#243;n y hueso.</data>
      <data key="d2">dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11467</data>
      <data key="d7">aaffd8dff1024676932ec80ad0b802e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GL&#193;NDULAS PARATIROIDES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Las gl&#225;ndulas paratiroides son gl&#225;ndulas endocrinas que regulan los niveles de calcio en la sangre mediante la secreci&#243;n de hormona paratiroidea.</data>
      <data key="d2">dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11468</data>
      <data key="d7">067c7b8b7b6b433daac5ab164f2a6980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCALOSIS METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La alcalosis metab&#243;lica es un trastorno que tambi&#233;n puede aumentar la fijaci&#243;n del calcio a la alb&#250;mina, afectando los niveles de calcio ionizado.</data>
      <data key="d2">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11469</data>
      <data key="d7">9f8a6ea7daf44b359b826c370c1a1a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIO PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11470</data>
      <data key="d7">929071c7c3524aa796fafe0d7b61fe02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FGF-23">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El FGF-23 es una hormona producida por los osteocitos que tiene un efecto fosfat&#250;rico potente, disminuyendo la absorci&#243;n intestinal de f&#243;sforo.</data>
      <data key="d2">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d3">1157</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11471</data>
      <data key="d7">896cd51ab4084c7792274c5e5a7f1598</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A controlled calcium diet, known as "DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO," is an approach that emphasizes the regulation of calcium intake to prevent and treat conditions such as osteoporosis and hypercalcemia. This dietary strategy focuses on achieving a balanced nutrient intake, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary amounts of calcium while managing their overall health. By carefully monitoring calcium consumption, this diet aims to support bone health and prevent complications associated with excessive calcium levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11472</data>
      <data key="d7">db8697a770534fd2b2591d4719c5a4f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALUMINIO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Aluminio is a chemical element that serves as a component in certain antacids. It has been noted for its ability to inhibit gastric motility, which can lead to gastrointestinal complications, particularly when combined with enteral nutrition. Additionally, aluminum is associated with toxicity in parenteral nutrition, which can adversely affect bone mass. The element is linked to various medical conditions and poses a risk of intoxication, highlighting the need for caution in its use within medical treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">5eb14e2cbec104d89ad73e2ac968b7fd,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2,fc664efd4e1c463dc21857e596b68b46</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11473</data>
      <data key="d7">23262ee32e7d42269e65d06e34e5a802</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIAZIDAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">TIAZIDAS, or thiazides, are a class of diuretics that play a significant role in influencing the levels of calcium and phosphorus in the body. These medications are known for their ability to retain calcium, which can have various effects on the body's mineral balance.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11474</data>
      <data key="d7">ebacc9042f6141269c35b36e602f0cc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITALIZADOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The term "HOSPITALIZADOS" refers to hospitalized patients, who are individuals receiving medical care in a hospital setting. These patients often require nutritional support during their stay to aid in their recovery and overall health management.</data>
      <data key="d2">428ea9c156fe3f0571b20d5d81648868,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d3">1157</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11475</data>
      <data key="d7">e8d35ecc0ac74f02856ea79821e4f01d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES S&#201;PTICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients who are septic are also at increased risk for developing hypophosphatemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11476</data>
      <data key="d7">279dfed4767e497089e723a670253105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIFICACIONES DE TEJIDOS BLANDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Soft tissue calcifications are complications that can arise from prolonged elevated phosphorus levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11477</data>
      <data key="d7">7bf406ca26944a9997b0e20b3f2d8606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUESO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">HUESO, which translates to "bone" in English, serves as a major storage site for magnesium in the body, containing approximately 60% of the total body magnesium.</data>
      <data key="d2">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11478</data>
      <data key="d7">eb3af7c93d614d8e8c59c71d51d5d71a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARBONATO DE LANTANO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lanthanum carbonate is a medication used to reduce phosphate levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11479</data>
      <data key="d7">e4e6d1f8aba1489f9ae11bde0dc24e78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTH INTACTA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Intact parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone that regulates calcium and magnesium levels in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11480</data>
      <data key="d7">b260575305e94a31bb22e00d2f046944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEVELAMER">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11481</data>
      <data key="d7">0edea0d7c4a74fceb3f59578cec1a899</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE WHIPPLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad de Whipple es una enfermedad infecciosa que afecta la absorci&#243;n intestinal, lo que puede llevar a deficiencias de magnesio.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11482</data>
      <data key="d7">3f40c94863f743519af2f2b634c96250</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#193;RMACOS INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los f&#225;rmacos inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producci&#243;n de &#225;cido en el est&#243;mago y pueden contribuir a la malabsorci&#243;n de magnesio.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">612</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11483</data>
      <data key="d7">6665557a3c7a45c6aa5ef255c807c980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESORCI&#211;N &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La resorci&#243;n &#243;sea es el proceso por el cual el tejido &#243;seo es descompuesto, lo que puede aumentar el riesgo de osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11484</data>
      <data key="d7">7dfc272051cf437f827ef2d446eb07eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMACI&#211;N &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La formaci&#243;n &#243;sea es el proceso de creaci&#243;n de nuevo tejido &#243;seo, que se ve afectado por factores hormonales y nutricionales.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11485</data>
      <data key="d7">4aa396482adc439ca2e38cb00fc0f735</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PROTE&#205;NA is a macronutrient that plays a crucial role in healing and immune response, making it particularly important in the nutritional management of critically ill patients. However, an excessive intake of protein in the diet can disrupt the balance of electrolytes, including magnesium, potentially leading to a condition known as hypomagnesemia. This highlights the importance of maintaining a balanced protein intake to support health while avoiding negative effects on electrolyte levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d3">643</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11486</data>
      <data key="d7">4eefde612def456bb62407099700e698</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAX">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fracture Risk Assessment Tool (FRAX) is a computer tool used to evaluate the risk of fractures in patients, calculating the probability of suffering a fracture within ten years.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11487</data>
      <data key="d7">8423b3f5b3224a5a81cae104b16d9be5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VITAMIN K">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin K is a fat-soluble vitamin that plays a crucial role in blood clotting and bone health. It is essential for the proper functioning of various proteins involved in these processes, particularly in the mineralization of the organic matrix of collagen in bones. Vitamin K is often monitored in patients with specific conditions, such as those with FQ (fluoroquinolone) and EPOC (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease), as it has particular recommendations for these individuals. Overall, Vitamin K is vital for maintaining both blood coagulation and bone metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1,acfde2ff93b969353912836034d74242,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">11488</data>
      <data key="d7">58c586e1978b4e7a8fd3550066138fd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOBACCO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tobacco is an independent risk factor for fractures, accelerating bone mass loss, especially in women.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11489</data>
      <data key="d7">2ff2dbb67fda4fecbd3031cb48d73815</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAFFEINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Caffeine can increase urinary calcium excretion, which may affect calcium balance in elderly individuals or postmenopausal women.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11490</data>
      <data key="d7">1061b5c325ef41a49cc3b3da6637e7d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEDENTARISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sedentarism is a lifestyle factor that can increase the risk of developing osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11491</data>
      <data key="d7">fdc0d482510b4427adce0ce385ac50de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMOKING">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Smoking is a lifestyle factor that contributes to the risk of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11492</data>
      <data key="d7">3416ac511ba449e186506b377251edb5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETARY IMBALANCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary imbalance, including low calcium intake, is a significant risk factor for osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11493</data>
      <data key="d7">b0e82fd496334a7a921fe5214cbe4d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTIANDROGENS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Antiandrogens are medications that may increase the risk of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11494</data>
      <data key="d7">dcdb03ebe13c49ac907ced8d925054fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THYROXINE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Excessive doses of thyroxine can lead to osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11495</data>
      <data key="d7">0589f4675e3448889e9f72f32784f3e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICONVULSANTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Certain anticonvulsants are associated with an increased risk of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11496</data>
      <data key="d7">dfa0e480e13f4a0081b104fc0df5098f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENDOCRINOPATHIES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Endocrinopathies such as hyperthyroidism and Cushing's disease can contribute to the risk of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11497</data>
      <data key="d7">60f72c4acb1443059340b12bf73eefa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALABSORPTIVE DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malabsorptive diseases can lead to osteoporosis due to inadequate nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11498</data>
      <data key="d7">6401fcd148114c65a03da356a6dd698e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RENAL DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Renal diseases can affect bone health and contribute to osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11499</data>
      <data key="d7">c1f55b7841cd46b2a0d9932b76f0c9ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMATOLOGICAL DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hematological diseases can impact bone density and contribute to osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11500</data>
      <data key="d7">a800cd239b6e4df99e59078e03c3f611</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHRONIC INFLAMMATORY DISEASES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic inflammatory diseases can lead to an increased risk of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11501</data>
      <data key="d7">819595073d9d472cb3d354bf2fc01d6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAL CHANGES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">65ba063e1a9e43a87dbfe9cf627674b1</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11502</data>
      <data key="d7">a54ffce04471457e8bc5a7d492dce083</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIUM-RICH DIET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A calcium-rich diet is recommended for various life stages and conditions to support bone health and prevent osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">605</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">11503</data>
      <data key="d7">958c377dcf4044a696ae0c5bf42b470d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MILK">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Milk is a primary dietary source of calcium, essential for maintaining bone health and preventing osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">605</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11504</data>
      <data key="d7">10c5dbd0f2f74b96986e7e622c538c88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SARDINES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sardines are a type of fish that are high in calcium and are recommended as part of a calcium-rich diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">605</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11505</data>
      <data key="d7">0ccef78b6435471b80c3b28e514b023b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMONDS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Almonds are a source of calcium and are included in dietary recommendations for bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">605</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11506</data>
      <data key="d7">627c03b568534665a857e0fd36185f64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHRONIC DIARRHEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic diarrhea can result in malabsorption of nutrients, including calcium, which is essential for bone health.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11507</data>
      <data key="d7">900dbe7dc0f141838b52f77ac6b4f8f6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEONATAL HYPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Neonatal hypocalcemia is a condition of low calcium levels in newborns, which can affect bone development.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11508</data>
      <data key="d7">fd422385f8d14264b806aa25dbbcd90c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RICKETS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rickets is a childhood disease primarily caused by a deficiency of vitamin D, calcium, or phosphate. This deficiency results in weak or soft bones in children, making them more susceptible to deformities and fractures. The condition highlights the importance of adequate nutrition and vitamin intake during the developmental years.</data>
      <data key="d2">9303a85464d02f1cc012aaca21edf9bb,b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d3">478</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11509</data>
      <data key="d7">ec21de95080e4cf3aa91f6f9f0cabd4d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FITATES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fitates are compounds found in some plant foods that can inhibit calcium absorption, impacting dietary calcium effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11510</data>
      <data key="d7">d9ea6e8eba7749178230309d6bc4fbc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALATES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalates are naturally occurring substances in some foods that can reduce calcium absorption, affecting dietary calcium intake.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">b978fd4738db41f132b50cb77c321c90</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11511</data>
      <data key="d7">cc4b6e99c0814ab88cd7786ebcb13f2d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FITATOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FITATOS are compounds found in certain plant foods that play a significant role in influencing mineral absorption, particularly in the context of infant nutrition. These compounds, also known as phytates, are known to inhibit the absorption of calcium, and they are commonly found in cereal bran. Understanding the impact of FITATOS is essential for ensuring adequate mineral intake, especially for infants who are in critical stages of growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">8f2e38ed25a683975b314e8e56721ad6,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d3">632</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11512</data>
      <data key="d7">7deb76a61b9d406fba24b8c6e94a1727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS refers to fortified foods that have been enhanced with additional nutrients to improve their dietary value. These products typically include added nutrients such as calcium and iron, which are essential for preventing deficiencies, particularly in at-risk populations. The primary goal of fortifying these foods is to enhance their nutritional content and support better health outcomes by addressing common nutrient deficiencies. In summary, ALIMENTOS FORTIFICADOS are enriched foods designed to provide essential nutrients and improve overall dietary intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11513</data>
      <data key="d7">8eef501cef704610a5ce1e503d34b405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALCIO EN LA DIETA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Calcium in the diet is crucial for maintaining bone health and preventing osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d3">604</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11514</data>
      <data key="d7">41a7c653502d4dd3b32952dc2ecf6af6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITRICOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrus fruits are high in vitamin C, which aids in calcium absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11515</data>
      <data key="d7">7e10ff1c777d4661b89db8536886120f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="K-DOQI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">K-Doqi son las gu&#237;as que recomiendan un aporte diet&#233;tico de f&#243;sforo para pacientes con enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d3">1157</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11516</data>
      <data key="d7">d5c57d1214e441aba1eb42fa5bf459b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS PROTEICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los alimentos proteicos son fuentes de f&#243;sforo que deben ser seleccionadas cuidadosamente en la dieta de pacientes con enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11517</data>
      <data key="d7">c782cb76ae13470ca0919d86b5f92e0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO F&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#225;cido f&#237;tico es una forma de f&#243;sforo que se encuentra en alimentos vegetales y tiene una biodisponibilidad inferior al f&#243;sforo org&#225;nico.</data>
      <data key="d2">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11518</data>
      <data key="d7">060700fd379d4e8dbf1c47a0d330899d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADITIVOS ALIMENTARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los aditivos alimentarios son compuestos que pueden contener f&#243;sforo inorg&#225;nico y se utilizan en la industria alimentaria, afectando la absorci&#243;n de f&#243;sforo en la dieta.</data>
      <data key="d2">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d3">622</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11519</data>
      <data key="d7">a91eb6505e1c4617b98ba7f93c417337</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARRIL G.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Barril G. is the author of the phosphorus/protein ratio tables published in 2013 for the Spanish population.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae1766e8ae855b3c79ad6d5fdefab1b0</data>
      <data key="d3">1625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11520</data>
      <data key="d7">9e2fbc27de7341b08e399e2aec8d7d17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHOSPHORUS/PROTEIN RATIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The phosphorus/protein ratio is a measurement used to assess dietary phosphorus in relation to protein intake, particularly important for patients with chronic kidney disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae1766e8ae855b3c79ad6d5fdefab1b0</data>
      <data key="d3">1625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11521</data>
      <data key="d7">51adc8b3f6e14dbbb71080f264e333ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADDITIVOS ALIMENTARIOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Additives are substances added to food products to enhance flavor, appearance, or preservation, which can include phosphorus.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae1766e8ae855b3c79ad6d5fdefab1b0</data>
      <data key="d3">584</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11522</data>
      <data key="d7">6caca3cd7bf04b4aa5dc86973622e88b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERFOSFATEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HYPERFOSFATEMIA is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of phosphorus in the blood. This condition can arise from excessive nutritional intake of phosphate or may be associated with underlying health issues, particularly in patients with renal problems. Management of hyperfosfatemia often requires dietary adjustments to control phosphate levels effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">ae1766e8ae855b3c79ad6d5fdefab1b0,cff2f16dff598dbf0bff544091c77837</data>
      <data key="d3">1523</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11523</data>
      <data key="d7">61a79b689c794a2ca66ee4843d6198b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUESO DE BURGOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Queso de Burgos is a type of cheese known for its low phosphorus content, with a ratio of 13.70 mg/g.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11524</data>
      <data key="d7">9e0eeed842be481c86dcfa0394d3d372</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUESOS UNTABLES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Untable cheeses are discouraged due to their high phosphorus content, with a ratio of 48.24 mg/g.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11525</data>
      <data key="d7">a4c7cb5d7c5a4ab9bdd8b41a6bad8a3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LECHE DE SOJA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Soy milk is an alternative to cow's milk with a lower phosphorus ratio, but caution is advised regarding additives.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11526</data>
      <data key="d7">32fcd97dacab44e4a376d89dfec6e074</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LECHE DE ALMENDRA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Almond milk is another alternative to cow's milk, recommended to be limited for renal patients due to high potassium content.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11527</data>
      <data key="d7">6d0b6683b8e8425abf0025b20094de44</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLARA DE HUEVO AISLADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Isolated egg whites have a low phosphorus ratio of 1.42 mg/g and are ideal for dialysis patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11528</data>
      <data key="d7">dd395a6fc8f84e198fc8a5a248635703</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNE FRESCA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fresh meat has a phosphorus ratio below 16 mg/g, with recommendations for white meat like chicken and turkey.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d3">817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11529</data>
      <data key="d7">abc8bab4f8884d7489680f5b86801d9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JAMONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ham is recommended due to lower fat content and an acceptable phosphorus ratio between 3.64 and 12.57 mg/g.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d3">817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11530</data>
      <data key="d7">0a9b0386522c4a5d913242a948fba595</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#201;MOLA DE TRIGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wheat semolina is recommended as a cereal option with a lower phosphorus ratio.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d3">1378</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11531</data>
      <data key="d7">0fd61e1beecd41a8835c852b5d5009f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUESO BLANCO DESNATADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Skimmed white cheese is advised due to its lower phosphorus levels compared to other cheeses.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11532</data>
      <data key="d7">26fa1888a63f4cd3b86f081eb54bbb0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNE BLANCA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">White meat, such as chicken and turkey, is recommended for its lower phosphorus content.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11533</data>
      <data key="d7">c44f59517b014ab0b0385f24955f90c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTES MAGROS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lean cuts of beef and pork are suggested for their acceptable phosphorus ratios.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11534</data>
      <data key="d7">af8d96d0905443bd945642daabb0d6fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS SIN FOSFATOS A&#209;ADIDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Foods labeled "without added phosphates" are becoming available, which is beneficial for phosphorus management.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d3">835</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11535</data>
      <data key="d7">011563605b12498e9a6d8aa198cf3096</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PESCADOS CON RATIO BAJO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fish with a low phosphorus/protein ratio are recommended for renal patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d3">981</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11536</data>
      <data key="d7">6823a2ac72e444bfb063b18b14e35524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RATIO F&#211;SFORO/PROTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The phosphorus/protein ratio is an important measure for dietary recommendations for renal patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11537</data>
      <data key="d7">e2d4589310cf401b8dc670506c505f85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS INTEGRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Whole foods are generally discouraged due to their high phosphorus content.</data>
      <data key="d2">26e7a15d14f527bbd2b99f7a7bc55d81</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11538</data>
      <data key="d7">40707394f6d6417c94b678d4c455e73c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BAKERY PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bakery products are discussed in relation to their nutritional content and recommendations for renal patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11539</data>
      <data key="d7">22ebdc53d4d741d1a2aa76794876fcad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLA BEVERAGES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cola beverages are mentioned for their high phosphorus content due to additives, making them unsuitable for renal patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">da58daf0bc31441182ccfd5807a91127</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11540</data>
      <data key="d7">63f510a1a0524b649c4d05adc17ba17e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VERDURAS Y HORTALIZAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"VERDURAS Y HORTALIZAS" refers to a category that encompasses vegetables and greens, which are generally recommended for consumption at least twice a day for a healthy diet. However, for patients with specific dietary needs, the intake of "verdurasy hortalizas" is advised to be limited to 1-2 rations per day. Additionally, it is suggested that certain cooking techniques be employed to reduce the potassium content in these vegetables, ensuring they are suitable for those with dietary restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d2">72ed1fffc10ea163a92b5f1a7b972732,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11541</data>
      <data key="d7">30be61f4e1804857aa7556cdd1a580be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNES O PESCADO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Carnes o pescado are recommended at 1-2 rations per day, depending on the dialysis technique, with specific guidelines for phosphorus/protein ratio.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11542</data>
      <data key="d7">61ed71a2164b480ebc4aeda483c0ac35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZ&#218;CARES SIMPLES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Az&#250;cares simples are to be consumed occasionally, individualized according to the dialysis technique.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11543</data>
      <data key="d7">7bf8521af0044681bb6195b0f9d8e85c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOLLER&#205;A Y REPOSTER&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Boller&#237;a y reposter&#237;a are discouraged, especially industrially made products.</data>
      <data key="d2">cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978</data>
      <data key="d3">1163</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11544</data>
      <data key="d7">ebf4437474e6441683e182f1160e2d7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FESNAD 2010">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FESNAD 2010 refers to the dietary reference intake guidelines established for minerals, specifically focusing on magnesium, for the Spanish population. These guidelines provide essential recommendations aimed at ensuring adequate mineral intake among individuals in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d3">1539</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">18</data>
      <data key="d6">11545</data>
      <data key="d7">65bc1514e5e7446fa87e61f94e67f3b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS DE ORIGEN ANIMAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Animal-derived foods such as dairy, fish, and eggs have higher magnesium bioavailability compared to plant-based foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11546</data>
      <data key="d7">69a0e0f95efc4d73b3d8b36882aec224</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS DE ORIGEN VEGETAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Plant-based foods generally contain more magnesium but have lower bioavailability due to the presence of phytates and oxalates.</data>
      <data key="d2">846a0cb8b0428de4dd313cf55913d6bd</data>
      <data key="d3">587</data>
