      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Bryant RJ is a researcher who has focused on the effects of vitamin E and C supplementation on exercise-induced peroxidation in trained cyclists. In addition to his research on antioxidants and athletic performance, he is also an author who discusses the implications of the new Dietary Reference Intakes (DRI) for calcium, particularly in relation to osteoporosis. Through his work, Bryant RJ contributes valuable insights into both sports nutrition and bone health.</data>
