    <node id="ANEMIA FERROP&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia ferrop&#233;nica, also known as iron deficiency anemia, is a medical condition characterized by a deficiency of iron in the body, which leads to a reduction in hemoglobin levels. This deficiency affects the body's ability to transport oxygen effectively, resulting in various clinical manifestations such as fatigue and paleness. It is recognized as the most common nutritional disorder worldwide, primarily caused by a lack of iron that leads to decreased erythrocyte production.

In infants, anemia ferrop&#233;nica can be associated with the early substitution of breast milk or infant formulas with whole cow's milk before the age of one year. Additionally, this condition can impact the physical performance of athletes due to insufficient iron levels. It may also result from blood loss in the feces, which is often linked to food allergies and gastrointestinal conditions. Overall, anemia ferrop&#233;nica is a significant health concern that can affect individuals across different age groups and lifestyles.</data>
      <data key="d2">056e169253fe046c2922537bb79ba187,4e8b65ec9939ccf2152e68fa7f8b12c4,6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc,693b5721c7fc52c8165c48b580777840,700a4472a23342b891a5685b622437d2,79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458,b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">35</data>
      <data key="d6">11610</data>
      <data key="d7">6642d98a5ec547178b1b63bc9dee920e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL ANEMIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional anemias are anemias caused by inadequate intake of iron, proteins, trace elements, or vitamins.</data>
      <data key="d2">4e8b65ec9939ccf2152e68fa7f8b12c4</data>
      <data key="d3">1809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11611</data>
      <data key="d7">09beff38aebb488ba334b3d61308686e</data>
    </node>
