    <node id="GASTRECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GASTRECTOM&#205;A is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of part or all of the stomach. This procedure is often performed for patients suffering from gastric cancer or severe ulcers. Gastrectom&#237;a can lead to malabsorption of nutrients due to the significant alteration of the digestive system. It is primarily utilized in the treatment of gastric cancer, highlighting its importance in managing severe gastrointestinal conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc,70a9e916b8c55784c53828958c76eb09,b0ffa7260c4fc20462ad4c9bedcbfae7,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c</data>
      <data key="d3">1087</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11616</data>
      <data key="d7">8a69c4e18787405aaade14a68b407491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SANGRADO UTERINO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Uterine bleeding is a common cause of iron deficiency anemia, particularly in women.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11617</data>
      <data key="d7">a392f747923c4f2bb48d2f677651ae2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ULCUS GASTRODUODENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gastro-duodenal ulcers are sores that develop on the lining of the stomach or the upper part of the small intestine, often causing bleeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11618</data>
      <data key="d7">b456d3ba789e4e7c8fa2d059262c895e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMORROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemorrhoids are swollen veins in the lower rectum and anus that can cause bleeding, contributing to iron deficiency anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11619</data>
      <data key="d7">0829419490d3496d85a2d61a14095b38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVERTICULOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diverticulosis is a condition characterized by the formation of small pouches in the colon, which can lead to complications such as bleeding and anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11620</data>
      <data key="d7">2ab1764daece4e80913e5456931520ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANGIODISPLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Angiodysplasia is a vascular malformation that can cause gastrointestinal bleeding, contributing to iron deficiency anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11621</data>
      <data key="d7">00bef809b33d46b785b76ba636f62c9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLIPOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyposis refers to the presence of multiple polyps in the gastrointestinal tract, which can lead to bleeding and anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11622</data>
      <data key="d7">25d3f2b22979426ba6850030c7b52051</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACLORHIDRIA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">ACLORHIDRIA is a condition characterized by the absence of hydrochloric acid in gastric secretions. This lack of hydrochloric acid can significantly impact the body's ability to absorb iron, potentially leading to deficiencies and related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc,7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11623</data>
      <data key="d7">0d49df798d594295b9ec43b6d4e0fcdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLUMMER-VINSON SYNDROME">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plummer-Vinson syndrome is a rare condition associated with severe iron deficiency anemia, characterized by esophageal webs and difficulty swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11624</data>
      <data key="d7">98f09ee9c55b4df495b80f82696607c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMOGLOBINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemoglobina is a protein found in red blood cells that plays a crucial role in transporting oxygen throughout the body. It is a key factor in diagnosing anemia, as the levels of hemoglobin are critical indicators of this condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b</data>
      <data key="d3">1809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11625</data>
      <data key="d7">8c957aa470954c46bbe73fdf3c640a1f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUCOSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mucosas refer to the mucous membranes in the body, which can be affected by iron deficiency, leading to symptoms like glossitis and angular cheilitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11626</data>
      <data key="d7">ff2a40a7758b4477a8c85a0d5dc1c9ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLANDULAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glandulas refer to glands in the body that can be impacted by nutritional deficiencies, including those related to iron.</data>
      <data key="d2">b65e3955444a7fb402ab92a8ae46311b</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11627</data>
      <data key="d7">954d6464b44146b49bd5eeda1a912445</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFATO FERROSO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfato ferroso is a common oral iron supplement used to treat iron deficiency anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11628</data>
      <data key="d7">d1b5a96dd36a43abb8fd14a421e22e5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLONOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Colonoscopy is a medical procedure used to examine the colon and rectum, often performed to investigate gastrointestinal issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11629</data>
      <data key="d7">db04003cbb0b49bfa5d6a7468742fc0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOMOGRAF&#205;A COMPUTARIZADA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tomograf&#237;a Computarizada, commonly known as computed tomography (CT), is a sophisticated medical imaging technique that provides detailed information about the body's internal structures. It is particularly valuable in critical care settings, offering insights into body composition for critically ill patients. This imaging method is instrumental in diagnosing a variety of medical conditions. For instance, it is used to confirm the diagnosis of pancreatitis, assess its severity and complications, and study mesenteric pathology, including the diagnosis of intra-abdominal collections. Additionally, high-resolution computed tomography (HRCT) serves as a specialized diagnostic tool for confirming bronchiectasis and evaluating structural changes in the lungs. Overall, Tomograf&#237;a Computarizada is essential for creating comprehensive images of internal organs, aiding in the diagnosis and management of numerous health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458,86aa5f95aae53ab120c5c63eda5486bc,b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">11630</data>
      <data key="d7">68a8ccb68c9249ce8b766b1ca0859472</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOCITOSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trombocitosis is a condition characterized by an elevated platelet count in the blood, which can occur in response to various stimuli, including active bleeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11631</data>
      <data key="d7">73d3dc4f0d93451bac9f432ba01da1e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBROCOLONOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fibrocolonoscopia is a procedure that allows for the examination of the colon using a flexible tube with a camera, often used to diagnose gastrointestinal issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">79435b6ab45648695f4a36f31b7fb458</data>
      <data key="d3">1808</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11632</data>
      <data key="d7">c1f2c59468c24b619cbaf9e3da05bc60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The EMEA, or European Medicines Agency, is an agency responsible for the evaluation and supervision of medicinal products within the European Union. In a significant development, the EMEA approved teduglutida in Europe in the same year that the FDA granted its approval, highlighting the agency's role in ensuring the availability of important medicinal products to the European market.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059,e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d3">1049</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11633</data>
      <data key="d7">7425a7da3ab14bce91a246ca605d3f94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALABSORCION DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iron malabsorption is a condition where the body cannot absorb iron effectively, leading to potential anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">11634</data>
      <data key="d7">00019f7b8ce44ad78503d451f3e63c69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NI&#209;OS LACTANTES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Infants under one year old who may require iron supplementation due to dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11635</data>
      <data key="d7">124c8d9d6e8e41aca1380553bb2ed7ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIERRO SACA-ROSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iron saccharate is an intravenous iron preparation known for its safety and effectiveness in treating iron deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1049</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11636</data>
      <data key="d7">82b6e2a522d54f2c8b53db510cb863ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE RENDU-OSLER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rendu-Osler disease is a genetic disorder that can lead to continuous and uncontrollable bleeding, increasing the need for iron treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11637</data>
      <data key="d7">541c593bc79245efada75ae3a0ee45af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Severe heart failure is a condition that may require iron supplementation due to increased iron needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11638</data>
      <data key="d7">50ef16bc1e944074b0b75d9c24456279</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESECCIONES INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intestinal resections are surgical procedures that may lead to malabsorption of iron, necessitating iron supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11639</data>
      <data key="d7">7ec0fb9286c2421cbd9a07a1d025f213</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARNES Y PESCADOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Meat and fish are dietary sources of iron that should be introduced to infants after six months to prevent iron deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11640</data>
      <data key="d7">92f6f12b8bf44fed901b53fbc0d53434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FORMULAS INFANTILES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Infant formulas fortified with iron are recommended for infants who do not receive breast milk.</data>
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1812</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11641</data>
      <data key="d7">369202aa0a4c4d65b7c050c616976727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIERRO CARBOXIMALTOSA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">7db70a783ce99dcbd067aa16de5d8059</data>
      <data key="d3">1049</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11642</data>
      <data key="d7">4e554d807b8d43d2a2c465032514b35d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA MATERNA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Maternal anemia is a condition characterized by a deficiency of red blood cells or hemoglobin in pregnant women, which can lead to severe health risks for both the mother and the newborn.</data>
      <data key="d2">868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1615</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11643</data>
      <data key="d7">21f3452094254a8990ef302db52c8a27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIT DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iron deficiency is a common nutritional issue that can lead to anemia and is particularly prevalent among women in developing countries.</data>
      <data key="d2">868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1615</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11644</data>
      <data key="d7">8d5987d486c34b93863b84841d68a9c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO CON HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Iron treatment refers to the administration of iron supplements to individuals with iron deficiency or anemia to restore normal levels of iron in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1615</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11645</data>
      <data key="d7">d374942de2e34535ac50179fe7beb115</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPLEMENTOS DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"SUPLEMENTOS DE HIERRO" refers to iron supplements, which are pharmaceutical products designed to increase iron intake, particularly for individuals at risk of deficiency, such as pregnant women. These supplements are commonly used to treat iron deficiency and anemia, helping to restore adequate iron levels in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,868defec6ca59b677cc97ac9a6b777bd</data>
      <data key="d3">1809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11646</data>
      <data key="d7">c3faa77c1dd14f26bd0010863a2ea52b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIENCIA DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La deficiencia de hierro es la alteraci&#243;n nutricional m&#225;s frecuente a nivel mundial, constituyendo m&#225;s de la mitad de los casos de anemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d3">1809</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11647</data>
      <data key="d7">39ca222e1c8b4e3f921efdb3f9bff976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN HFE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The HFE gene, located on the short arm of chromosome 6, is associated with iron metabolism and plays a crucial role in the regulation of iron levels in the body. Mutations in the HFE gene are linked to hereditary hemochromatosis, a genetic disorder characterized by excessive iron accumulation in the body, which can lead to various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11648</data>
      <data key="d7">721ed1b376ef425a905172616bb5221e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACI&#211;N C282Y">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MUTACI&#211;N C282Y refers to a specific mutation in the HFE gene that is commonly associated with hereditary hemochromatosis. This mutation is the most prevalent cause of type 1 hemochromatosis, which significantly impacts the body's ability to absorb iron. As a genetic alteration, C282Y leads to hereditary hemochromatosis, resulting in an excessive accumulation of iron in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11649</data>
      <data key="d7">31ed96083794476f9fec14a2164914e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTACI&#211;N H63D">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La mutaci&#243;n H63D en el gen HFE es una alteraci&#243;n gen&#233;tica que puede asociarse con la sobrecarga f&#233;rrica, especialmente cuando se presenta en combinaci&#243;n con la mutaci&#243;n C282Y. Aunque la mutaci&#243;n H63D est&#225; relacionada con la hemocromatosis, su efecto es considerado menos severo en comparaci&#243;n con el de la mutaci&#243;n C282Y.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11650</data>
      <data key="d7">1c0cd7e703084428ad059657e971b11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIERRO HEMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El hierro hemo es una forma de hierro que se encuentra en productos de origen animal y es m&#225;s f&#225;cilmente absorbido por el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11651</data>
      <data key="d7">fd8d5d2cf4fe497ab7f5431d347657e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIERRO NO HEMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El hierro no hemo es una forma de hierro que se encuentra en alimentos de origen vegetal y es menos absorbible que el hierro hemo.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d3">610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11652</data>
      <data key="d7">e98a4e4bb862480baebd425d0a451555</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO ASC&#211;RBICO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">&#193;cido Asc&#243;rbico, commonly known as ascorbic acid or Vitamin C, is a vital nutrient that plays a significant role in maintaining skin health. This essential vitamin is predominantly found in various fruits, particularly citrus fruits, strawberries, and peppers.</data>
      <data key="d2">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d3">610</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11653</data>
      <data key="d7">fe6446c5b3734ca5b1625e41f0242e4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPCIDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepcidin is a small peptide that regulates iron absorption and release in the body, playing a crucial role in iron homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11654</data>
      <data key="d7">6465c2df994942b69c2d8a371fb593ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DMT1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">DMT1 is a transporter that facilitates the absorption of ferrous iron across the intestinal membrane.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11655</data>
      <data key="d7">2a6377945b134666b73c69ed1cea9a2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FERROPORTINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ferroportin is a transporter that exports iron from cells into the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11656</data>
      <data key="d7">b3cdd7a59890468f85aa85b418948bd2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HFE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">HFE is a gene that plays a crucial role in hereditary hemochromatosis, a genetic condition characterized by excessive iron accumulation in the body. This gene influences iron metabolism and is responsible for encoding a protein that is integral to the regulation of iron levels. Mutations in the HFE gene are linked to certain forms of hereditary hemochromatosis, leading to disruptions in normal iron homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec,45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,e376d9f50b7608f5b6d1f88877fde59e</data>
      <data key="d3">365</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11657</data>
      <data key="d7">77ad99225959411a964049b523c5e375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACR&#211;FAGOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MACR&#211;FAGOS, or macrophages, are immune cells that play a crucial role in the body's defense mechanisms. They are particularly stimulated in the context of inflammatory bowel diseases, where they contribute to the immune response. Additionally, macrophages are involved in iron metabolism, functioning by storing and releasing iron as needed. This dual role highlights their importance not only in immune responses but also in maintaining iron homeostasis within the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,df0e6695be23c07606ca5b9accc62df2</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11658</data>
      <data key="d7">a5b68e26a4b240738214f4ecbf789459</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARTICULACIONES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Joints can also accumulate excess iron, leading to complications in hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11659</data>
      <data key="d7">29ec4d6b30cc41928c8d74aee8b36268</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S65C">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">S65C is another mutation related to iron overload when associated with the C282Y mutation in hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d3">1816</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11660</data>
      <data key="d7">5ab95676d7e64c6aaeaf88d86c2ff23a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C282Y">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">C282Y is a specific mutation in the HFE gene that is associated with hereditary hemochromatosis, a condition that can lead to iron overload in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079,a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11661</data>
      <data key="d7">095d7d44175a424b947b8e4131eca9f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEDCA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BEDCA is a database that provides nutritional information, including data on iron absorption in various foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11662</data>
      <data key="d7">467f82b09abd464fa3909c6147ea7af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICA SUBSAHARIANA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Africa subsahariana is a region where iron overload conditions can occur due to dietary factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d3">1519</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11663</data>
      <data key="d7">79bad123e13845c5a917f2ab71fcd891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HJV">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">HJV is a gene associated with juvenile hemochromatosis, affecting iron regulation in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d3">1521</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11664</data>
      <data key="d7">df028bdfd0d0415da60c8135ab3f6b7b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLC40A1">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SLC40A1 is a gene that encodes ferroportin, a protein involved in iron transport and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
