    </node>
    <node id="HH TIPO 5">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HH tipo 5 refers to hereditary hemochromatosis associated with mutations in the ferritin gene.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11672</data>
      <data key="d7">aba081517aae419195fa2fcf1e381c1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATITIS C">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatitis C is a viral infection that primarily affects the liver and is known to lead to chronic liver disease. It is particularly significant in patients with hemochromatosis, a condition characterized by iron overload, as Hepatitis C can complicate their health status. The infection poses a risk for individuals with hemochromatosis, highlighting the importance of monitoring liver health in these patients. Overall, Hepatitis C is associated with both liver complications and iron overload, making it a critical concern in the context of liver-related diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec,4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11673</data>
      <data key="d7">3aff97ed606746a9843426f2b859771f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEATOHEPATITIS NO ALCOH&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esteatohepatitis no alcoh&#243;lica is a condition characterized by liver inflammation and fat accumulation, which can be associated with iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d3">1710</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11674</data>
      <data key="d7">cfd8f1b90c144118bf8a6573d94021e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMOCIGOTOS C282Y">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">1cdec368125a3e3fd5c3c7accc5b89ec</data>
      <data key="d3">1519</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11675</data>
      <data key="d7">755aed76222e4def96136c5e913692b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERPIGMENTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hyperpigmentation is a skin condition characterized by dark patches on the skin, often associated with hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11676</data>
      <data key="d7">d6095122b0ad4b6390d4de33b5ad4dcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FERRIC METABOLISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ferric metabolism refers to the body's process of handling iron, which is often disrupted in conditions like hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11677</data>
      <data key="d7">6f90fdcac96144d59bfecb0d994e9818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECARGA DIET&#201;TICA DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sobrecarga diet&#233;tica de hierro is the condition of iron overload resulting from excessive dietary intake of iron.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11678</data>
      <data key="d7">8a9275e5a4bb44fbba806b8381d48007</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECARGA PARENTERAL DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sobrecarga parenteral de hierro refers to iron overload that occurs due to intravenous iron administration.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11679</data>
      <data key="d7">e6efcfb40a274dc68e13c9a808c2f5a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRANSFUSIONES DE GL&#211;BULOS ROJOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Transfusiones de gl&#243;bulos rojos are blood transfusions that can lead to iron overload in patients receiving multiple transfusions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11680</data>
      <data key="d7">fd7a0a627fa043ae807fcc0cbc12a75a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INYECTABLES DE HIERRO INTRAVENOSO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inyecciones de hierro intravenoso are intravenous iron injections that can contribute to iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11681</data>
      <data key="d7">7d9c24c336b54807b63887727d7f3105</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMODI&#193;LISIS A LARGO PLAZO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemodi&#225;lisis a largo plazo refers to long-term dialysis treatment that can lead to iron overload due to repeated blood transfusions or iron supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11682</data>
      <data key="d7">c5a1b8c3e8a349c8981ba0023d7bab11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEATOPAT&#205;A NO ALCOH&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esteatopat&#237;a no alcoh&#243;lica refers to non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, which can be related to iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11683</data>
      <data key="d7">196ce2f716824124b8ddb912ea998e69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A ALCOH&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hepatopat&#237;a alcoh&#243;lica is liver disease caused by excessive alcohol consumption, which can interact with iron overload conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11684</data>
      <data key="d7">1672e56842d34f53b1d1254a328a46ec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA CON SOBRECARGA F&#201;RRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia con sobrecarga f&#233;rrica is a type of anemia that occurs in conjunction with iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11685</data>
      <data key="d7">7260871f62a749438d43d80a17c4b4e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TALASEMIA MAYOR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Talasemia mayor es una enfermedad hereditaria grave que afecta la producci&#243;n de hemoglobina en el organismo. Esta condici&#243;n puede requerir tratamientos intensivos, incluyendo trasplantes de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas. Adem&#225;s, los pacientes con talasemia mayor a menudo necesitan recibir transfusiones de sangre frecuentes, lo que puede resultar en una sobrecarga de hierro en el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd,db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11686</data>
      <data key="d7">71c153b9bac940df9072798a45f6ad7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA SIDEROBL&#193;STICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia siderobl&#225;stica is a type of anemia characterized by the presence of ringed sideroblasts in the bone marrow, often associated with iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11687</data>
      <data key="d7">25457e59fc274bab921de2e920c56e0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA HEMOL&#205;TICA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia hemol&#237;tica cr&#243;nica is a chronic form of anemia that can lead to iron overload due to increased red blood cell destruction.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11688</data>
      <data key="d7">45f1d0dd2afc4a56ac1152d5a339d280</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANEMIA APL&#193;SICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anemia apl&#225;sica is a condition where the bone marrow fails to produce sufficient blood cells, which can be complicated by iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11689</data>
      <data key="d7">d624bd4b25074808914eeb3abbfe8127</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D&#201;FICIT DE PIRUVATO KINASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">D&#233;ficit de piruvato kinasa is a rare genetic disorder that can lead to hemolytic anemia and may be associated with iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11690</data>
      <data key="d7">86b776660b954a6f84bbcf9877e7e035</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACERULOPLASMINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aceruloplasminemia is a rare genetic disorder that affects iron metabolism and can lead to iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11691</data>
      <data key="d7">0a5583b4451d43a7b738b64c9f531858</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATRASFERRINEMIA CONG&#201;NITA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atrasferrinemia cong&#233;nita is a rare genetic disorder that affects iron transport in the body, leading to iron overload.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11692</data>
      <data key="d7">123b975b3bc642ad89bff5e336cf92a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECARGA NEONATAL DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sobrecarga neonatal de hierro refers to iron overload that can occur in newborns, often due to transfusions or maternal iron supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11693</data>
      <data key="d7">42ecbe7b42124e5694bd1deb0630a1d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECARGA ADQUIRIDA DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d3">1709</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11694</data>
      <data key="d7">a66fcce249044fb9b353a6fb3ed5c9ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA FOLICULOESTIMULANTE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La hormona foliculoestimulante es otra hormona producida por la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria que es esencial para el desarrollo de los fol&#237;culos ov&#225;ricos en las mujeres y la producci&#243;n de esperma en los hombres.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d3">1345</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11695</data>
      <data key="d7">f8afade8609d4dddb366707adc8bb873</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARTROPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La artropat&#237;a es una enfermedad de las articulaciones que puede ser causada por la acumulaci&#243;n de cristales de pirofosfato c&#225;lcico, resultando en dolor y discapacidad.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11696</data>
      <data key="d7">fd42f4fa543d400390f04f61fdc18b68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECARGA F&#201;RRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La sobrecarga f&#233;rrica es una condici&#243;n en la que hay un exceso de hierro en el cuerpo, lo que puede causar da&#241;o a &#243;rganos y tejidos.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">11697</data>
      <data key="d7">de74023d15c0478283d6cd77893fff9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOLOR MUSCULOESQUEL&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El dolor musculoesquel&#233;tico puede ser un s&#237;ntoma de artropat&#237;a y puede mejorar con tratamientos como las flebotom&#237;as.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11698</data>
      <data key="d7">641715c1335243769f690eab95281ca7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLEBOTOM&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FLEBOTOM&#205;AS refers to medical procedures that involve the extraction of blood from a patient. These procedures are particularly significant in the treatment of conditions such as hemochromatosis, where they are employed to reduce excess iron levels in the body. By performing phlebotomy, healthcare providers can help alleviate iron overload, which is crucial for preventing serious complications, including cirrhosis and diabetes. Overall, phlebotomy serves as a therapeutic intervention aimed at managing iron levels and improving patient health.</data>
      <data key="d2">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3,9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d3">1817</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11699</data>
      <data key="d7">d7534e4e101d40298985b2100f56cbd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA ALCOH&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad hep&#225;tica alcoh&#243;lica es un da&#241;o al h&#237;gado causado por el consumo excesivo de alcohol, que puede complicar la evaluaci&#243;n de la ferritina.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11700</data>
      <data key="d7">8a34a1caaf334a14a13a07d02627e4db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA POR VIRUS C">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hepatopat&#237;a cr&#243;nica por virus C es una infecci&#243;n del h&#237;gado que puede causar inflamaci&#243;n y da&#241;o hep&#225;tico, afectando los niveles de ferritina.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11701</data>
      <data key="d7">2838f27370d1424b98c7f719727038ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA POR VIRUS B">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hepatopat&#237;a cr&#243;nica por virus B es otra infecci&#243;n que puede afectar la funci&#243;n hep&#225;tica y los niveles de hierro en el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11702</data>
      <data key="d7">a258db96102d48babc1103a6077cea52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PORFIRIA CUT&#193;NEA TARDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La porfiria cut&#225;nea tarda es un trastorno que afecta la piel y puede estar relacionado con la sobrecarga de hierro.</data>
      <data key="d2">68c1e1d1d60cf84e8ba37450cd6dc7d3</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11703</data>
      <data key="d7">a35a114f45ea4d678e24c3271b522ecd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IST">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">IST, or the Iron Saturation Test, is a diagnostic test utilized to evaluate iron levels in the body. It is particularly relevant in the context of conditions such as hereditary hemochromatosis (HH). The test helps in assessing the amount of iron bound to transferrin, which is crucial for diagnosing and managing iron overload disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c,a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1821</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11704</data>
      <data key="d7">8c142066b27241ac80a9a7c0e91e093a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H63D">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">H63D is another mutation in the HFE gene that, when combined with C282Y, can indicate a predisposition to hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11705</data>
      <data key="d7">790baa4157024a51beeaeb8a583ab887</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HH, or hereditary hemochromatosis, is a genetic condition that causes excessive iron absorption and accumulation in the body, leading to various health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">11706</data>
      <data key="d7">19e68832b16e4f889f5496d7092242ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMILIARES DE 1ER GRADO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">First-degree relatives of patients with hereditary hemochromatosis are recommended to undergo genetic testing to assess their risk of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11707</data>
      <data key="d7">e0b056c448ee422983157eed628a2a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FERRITINA E IST">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ferritina and IST are tests used to evaluate iron levels and diagnose conditions related to iron overload, particularly in hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11708</data>
      <data key="d7">1e3e2627ab7c45a8a78b94fbd7718279</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRANSAMINASAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Transaminasas are enzymes that, when elevated, indicate liver damage and are relevant in the diagnosis of hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11709</data>
      <data key="d7">44e96a3beef844e89fa5ad26129911cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRIBADO POBLACIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cribado poblacional refers to population screening for hereditary conditions, including hereditary hemochromatosis, to identify at-risk individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d3">1818</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11710</data>
      <data key="d7">c9f348f0948b4374ad4f9dbe4313a0ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOMOCIGOTOS C282TY/C282Y">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Individuals with the genetic mutation C282TY/C282Y, at high risk of developing hereditary hemochromatosis (HH) due to a 70% penetrance rate.</data>
      <data key="d2">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d3">1821</data>
