      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11802</data>
      <data key="d7">db4f1a5e33ef4d6ea59b1d7516355c73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHINODA, S">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Shinoda, S is an author of a study on pathogenic factors of vibrios, particularly Vibrio vulnificus.</data>
      <data key="d2">4216916ebab948061d2dca4afe7e1e84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11803</data>
      <data key="d7">833c94f1dfec4316871d9e54c480d2b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIBRIO VULNIFICUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vibrio vulnificus is a pathogenic bacterium associated with various infections, particularly in individuals with liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">4216916ebab948061d2dca4afe7e1e84</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11804</data>
      <data key="d7">9c46161ea9984ccc960bed5532ac194e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUPROENZIMAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CUPROENZIMAS refers to enzymes that contain copper and are essential for various biochemical processes in the body. These processes include electron transport and neurotransmitter metabolism, highlighting the critical role that copper-containing enzymes play in maintaining physiological functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">11</data>
      <data key="d6">11805</data>
      <data key="d7">11ef943e5d394fa4a698397cbb8ee1fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#218;SCULOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">M&#218;SCULOS are tissues in the body that play a crucial role in physical activity, requiring energy primarily in the form of glycogen and glucose to function effectively. Additionally, these muscles depend on copper for various metabolic functions, highlighting the importance of both energy sources and essential minerals in maintaining muscle health and performance.</data>
      <data key="d2">490f5e3c6dbf3754eee50c52154da09a,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">663</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11806</data>
      <data key="d7">4e81f1784e7947aeadccd91c6db55369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEJIDO EL&#193;STICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Elastic tissue is a type of connective tissue that requires copper for its synthesis and maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11807</data>
      <data key="d7">c7779b7b0b764efa962f9ccea3fc99cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NOREPINEFRINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Norepinephrine is a neurotransmitter that is derived from dopamine and plays a role in the body's response to stress.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1294</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11808</data>
      <data key="d7">47ecede232224c86852ea1e84605e72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MELANINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Melanin is a pigment responsible for the color of skin, hair, and eyes, and its synthesis is influenced by copper-containing enzymes.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11809</data>
      <data key="d7">a5eea6996fd74cc3bbbc9211231246e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIROSINASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tyrosinase is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of tyrosine to melanin and is dependent on copper for its activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11810</data>
      <data key="d7">9b5a651e7e644facb7c748461a8da55e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPER&#211;XIDO DISMUTASA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Super&#243;xido dismutasa is a copper-containing enzyme that plays a crucial role in protecting cells from oxidative damage. It catalyzes the conversion of superoxide radicals, which are harmful byproducts of cellular metabolism, into oxygen and hydrogen peroxide. By facilitating this conversion, super&#243;xido dismutasa helps to mitigate the effects of oxidative stress, thereby safeguarding cellular integrity and function.</data>
      <data key="d2">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11811</data>
      <data key="d7">62b1f43f74474380bb30be20cefd1b70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROTRANSMISORES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Neurotransmitters are chemical messengers in the nervous system that are influenced by copper-containing enzymes in their metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d3">1823</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11812</data>
      <data key="d7">d4e909d430dc48538bd6ed3d0de02212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CERULOPLASMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Ceruloplasmina, also known as ceruloplasmin, is a glycoprotein that plays a vital role in copper metabolism and transport in the body. It is a protein that carries copper in the blood, containing seven copper atoms per molecule. Ceruloplasmina is significant in diagnosing copper metabolism disorders, particularly Wilson's disease, as its levels are often measured to assess copper deposits in the body. Additionally, it is involved in iron metabolism, functioning as ferroxidase I. Overall, ceruloplasmina serves as an important indicator of copper levels and is crucial for maintaining proper copper and iron homeostasis in the organism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d3">1794</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11813</data>
      <data key="d7">af878116d6a4445b9fa5e4625dd2f868</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATP7A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ATP7A is a gene that encodes a copper-transporting ATPase, which is essential for copper metabolism and its incorporation into proteins. This gene is associated with several disorders, including a condition resembling Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, which leads to neuropathy in adults. Additionally, ATP7A is linked to Menkes disease and Wilson's disease, both of which also affect copper metabolism. Overall, ATP7A plays a critical role in maintaining proper copper levels in the body, and its dysfunction can result in significant neurological and metabolic issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d3">1794</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11814</data>
      <data key="d7">a41b4c528f514945b94935f4ab7905b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATP7B">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ATP7B is a gene located on chromosome 13 that plays a critical role in copper transport and the elimination of excess copper from the body. It is associated with Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder characterized by the accumulation of copper in various tissues due to mutations in the ATP7B gene. The analysis of ATP7B is essential for the genetic diagnosis of Wilson's disease and for conducting family screening to identify at-risk individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,b5c30f293b197b201d278f0660640b86</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11815</data>
      <data key="d7">e22d2ff3d16c48788605bb32cf869ca7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE MENKES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Menkes disease is a genetic disorder caused by mutations in the ATP7A gene, which results in a deficiency of copper in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d3">1794</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11816</data>
      <data key="d7">c5324f0447e54d5ab67cc947865ba5cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIAMINOOXIDASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Diamine oxidase is a copper-containing enzyme that inactivates histamine in the body, affecting digestive processes and allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d3">379</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11817</data>
      <data key="d7">173052312f6f46fabf254d37fe63a8e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Histamina is a chemical compound that plays a crucial role in local immune responses and the regulation of various physiological functions, particularly in the gut. It is classified as a vasoactive amine, which means it can affect blood vessel dilation and permeability. Histamine is also associated with food intolerance, as it can be found in a wide range of foods and may trigger adverse reactions in sensitive individuals. In the context of allergic reactions, histamine is released and can lead to symptoms such as urticaria (hives) and headaches. Overall, histamine is significant not only for its physiological functions but also for its involvement in allergic responses and food intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d2">527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1,53b06c2465283c8a863ad8a69118725f,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f</data>
      <data key="d3">379</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">11818</data>
      <data key="d7">3a8fb6f804a24b9eaa235e21f2e8f252</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METALOTIONEINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Metallothioneins are proteins that bind heavy metals, including copper, and play a role in metal metabolism and detoxification.</data>
      <data key="d2">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d3">1822</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11819</data>
      <data key="d7">5159c85dda864271a901c1380b9fa194</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REACCIONES AL&#201;RGICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"REACCIONES AL&#201;RGICAS" refer to immune responses that occur when the body reacts to substances it perceives as harmful, known as allergens. These reactions often involve the release of histamine and can vary in severity and type of symptoms. The immune system's response to these allergens can manifest in various ways, highlighting the diverse nature of allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d2">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,bc394d70461777b6300d5449185a7859</data>
      <data key="d3">1528</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11820</data>
      <data key="d7">6e51d98bc719402c9930285b6eea7434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BALANCE DE COBRE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El balance de cobre en el organismo se refiere a la cantidad de cobre que se ingiere, se absorbe y se elimina, siendo fundamental para la salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849</data>
      <data key="d3">27</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11821</data>
      <data key="d7">65e018a16e73431d88fc13d9592b9aad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES PLASM&#193;TICOS DE COBRE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los niveles plasm&#225;ticos de cobre son medidos para evaluar la cantidad de cobre en el organismo y su relaci&#243;n con diversas condiciones de salud.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849</data>
      <data key="d3">27</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11822</data>
      <data key="d7">02b9b17354eb4bddb8b0f15d933ccb5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN COBRE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Los alimentos ricos en cobre, como las ostras y v&#237;sceras animales, son importantes para cubrir las necesidades diarias de este mineral.</data>
      <data key="d2">d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849</data>
