    </node>
    <node id="C&#211;RNEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The cornea is affected in Wilson's disease due to copper deposits, which can lead to vision problems.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11839</data>
      <data key="d7">a0b81031a0524b7998b05bb0ed6414a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RI&#209;ONES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Ri&#241;ones, or kidneys, are organ meats known for their high levels of purines, which can contribute to the risk of hyperuricemia. Additionally, the kidneys are affected by Wilson's disease, a condition characterized by the accumulation of copper in the body, leading to potential renal dysfunction.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11840</data>
      <data key="d7">425440572cec4fac96b22d7007dd05ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTERNOCLEIDOMASTOIDEO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The sternocleidomastoid muscle is part of the muscular system and may be referenced in relation to conditions affecting copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11841</data>
      <data key="d7">d03f63dd01c34c7cb927e4a4434c7a20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HERNIAS INGUINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Inguinal hernias are a condition that may occur in individuals with certain genetic disorders, including those affecting copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11842</data>
      <data key="d7">a94014ee2f7b405e8b580e6f3da2f234</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVERT&#205;CULOS DE LA VEJIGA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bladder diverticula are a condition that may be associated with genetic disorders affecting copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11843</data>
      <data key="d7">a8fb5c2c32f14efaab923f2546522808</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TORTUOSIDAD VASCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Vascular tortuosity is a condition that may be observed in patients with disorders related to copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11844</data>
      <data key="d7">c4073b467d6540eb81bbf203b4974ba8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;A DISTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Distal neuropathy is a condition that can occur in adults with disorders like Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, which may be related to copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11845</data>
      <data key="d7">3e8b4fa6f45048bfa5528bbb0340bd2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFORMIDADES DE PIE CAVUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cavus foot deformities can occur in individuals with neuropathy related to copper metabolism disorders.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11846</data>
      <data key="d7">0b91f9dfd0ce41328fa71677660eb8f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NIVELES DE COBRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Copper levels are critical in diagnosing and managing disorders related to copper metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11847</data>
      <data key="d7">eec66fef731b42bd91d70c45c0200a88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AASLD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases (AASLD), known in Spanish as la Asociaci&#243;n Americana para el Estudio del H&#237;gado, is an organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and treatment of liver diseases. AASLD provides evidence-based recommendations for the diagnosis and treatment of various liver conditions, including Wilson's disease. Through its guidelines and research initiatives, AASLD plays a crucial role in improving patient care and outcomes in the field of hepatology.</data>
      <data key="d2">41a33a13610bbae73208f0d201781724,5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d3">1791</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11848</data>
      <data key="d7">5314a02580bd4d9a9a3935539caee9d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EASL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La Asociaci&#243;n Europea para el Estudio del H&#237;gado (EASL) es una organizaci&#243;n que tambi&#233;n ofrece directrices y recomendaciones para el manejo de enfermedades hep&#225;ticas, incluyendo la EW.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d3">1791</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11849</data>
      <data key="d7">c5d181b993d14ff98a798ea790425ca8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SICILIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Sicilia es una isla italiana donde la Enfermedad de Wilson se presenta con mayor frecuencia en comparaci&#243;n con otras regiones.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11850</data>
      <data key="d7">3d4a68ba78784217a29fc9dd4710bc69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ITALIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Italia, known as Italy, is a country where the Enfermedad de Wilson is notably more prevalent, particularly in its southern regions. Recent studies conducted in Italia have focused on the survival rates of patients suffering from s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto. Additionally, Italia has established regulations for NED funding since 1988, reflecting its commitment to healthcare and research. However, it is also one of the eight countries that face challenges in data collection for epidemiological studies, which may impact the comprehensiveness of health-related research within the nation.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d,998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17,eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1928</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11851</data>
      <data key="d7">98562ee1be8a4caba4f8fd3d0c7c6a14</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NTOMAS NEUROL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los s&#237;ntomas neurol&#243;gicos son manifestaciones cl&#237;nicas que pueden aparecer en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson, relacionados con la acumulaci&#243;n de cobre en el sistema nervioso.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11852</data>
      <data key="d7">6fb60980b0b34f8683aee896b6ded8ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANILLO DE KAYSER-FLEISCHER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El anillo de Kayser-Fleischer es un hallazgo cl&#237;nico que se debe descartar en pacientes con sospecha de Enfermedad de Wilson, aunque su ausencia no excluye el diagn&#243;stico.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11853</data>
      <data key="d7">215661a09f6540caacc720bb87433ca0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOLOR DE CABEZA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El dolor de cabeza es uno de los s&#237;ntomas que pueden presentarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson, especialmente en etapas avanzadas.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11854</data>
      <data key="d7">8d0495e8def14b40b4860be8fcf340b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEMBLORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los temblores son un s&#237;ntoma neurol&#243;gico que puede manifestarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson debido a la acumulaci&#243;n de cobre.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11855</data>
      <data key="d7">9735eb4ee82849edb42fa1616e99a8f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIFICULTAD DE COORDINACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La dificultad de coordinaci&#243;n es un s&#237;ntoma neurol&#243;gico que puede presentarse en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11856</data>
      <data key="d7">c952968ea24a439396865c56aeb9b5f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ABORTOS ESPONT&#193;NEOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los abortos espont&#225;neos repetidos e inexplicables son s&#237;ntomas que pueden presentarse en mujeres premenop&#225;usicas con Enfermedad de Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11857</data>
      <data key="d7">755a60900c41442c9013ff055a8c5283</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FATIGA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La fatiga es uno de los primeros s&#237;ntomas que pueden aparecer en pacientes con Enfermedad de Wilson.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11858</data>
      <data key="d7">ff95831e66ce49d8a9bff3c7caebcc95</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EW">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EW refers to Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder characterized by excessive copper accumulation in the body, which primarily affects the liver and brain. This condition necessitates treatment to manage the copper levels and may ultimately require liver transplantation in severe cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">11859</data>
      <data key="d7">6a0548a2a04c4c12af2aec585e57bf18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="D-PENICILAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">D-Penicillamine is a chelating agent and a pharmaceutical treatment primarily used in the management of Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder that leads to excessive copper accumulation in the body. It functions by helping to eliminate excess copper, thereby reducing its levels in the body. D-Penicillamine is considered a first-line medication for this condition, effectively aiding in the treatment and management of copper toxicity associated with Wilson's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1,d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">11860</data>
      <data key="d7">faaca90354f14d3ab97b582bc88ef38c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIENTINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Trientina, also known as Trientine, is a medication utilized as an alternative treatment for Wilson's disease, a genetic disorder that leads to excessive accumulation of copper in the body. It functions as a chelator, effectively binding to excess copper and facilitating its removal from the body. Trientine is often noted for being better tolerated than D-Penicillamine, another chelating agent used in the treatment of Wilson's disease. Overall, Trientina serves as a valuable option for managing this condition by helping to reduce copper levels and mitigate its associated health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c,d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11861</data>
      <data key="d7">f9aed86456ac4b2c9b30e6a7715d4fd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEPATITIS AUTOINMUNE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Autoimmune hepatitis is a condition that can be confused with Wilson's disease, requiring careful diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11862</data>
      <data key="d7">865d7599fe714d758ac5ea3be8c5f7a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMILIARES DE PRIMER GRADO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">First-degree relatives are family members of a patient diagnosed with Wilson's disease (EW) who should be evaluated for the condition due to genetic factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11863</data>
      <data key="d7">9ed2d15cbcfb4292877d0c2fcfcb83c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA HEP&#193;TICA AGUDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"INSUFICIENCIA HEP&#193;TICA AGUDA," or acute liver failure, is a critical and severe condition that can arise in patients suffering from Wilson's disease. This medical emergency necessitates immediate intervention to address the potentially life-threatening complications associated with the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c,3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11864</data>
      <data key="d7">60093c980e4f44a88018cb13e75c1a5e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUPRURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cupruria refers to the presence of excess copper in urine, which is a diagnostic indicator for Wilson's disease (EW).</data>
      <data key="d2">1dbfa8fa6421e3dd5e585baa8a10c25c</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11865</data>
      <data key="d7">4b7b8c6cb60d4913aa2130ad03288987</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KAYSER-FLEISCHER RINGS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Kayser-Fleischer rings are deposits of copper in the cornea, often seen in patients with Wilson's disease, detectable by slit lamp examination.</data>
      <data key="d2">3898563966943dbfc8a0f6e84bc627b1</data>
      <data key="d3">1793</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
