    </node>
    <node id="ACETATO DE ZINC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetato de zinc is a treatment for Wilson's disease that blocks intestinal copper absorption and is used as a chronic maintenance therapy.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11891</data>
      <data key="d7">00097ed18a8740f2bf839de462dff558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE HEMOL&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemolytic syndrome is a condition that can occur as a complication of Wilson's disease due to liver dysfunction and copper toxicity.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11892</data>
      <data key="d7">0529b9d392474bf3b8b124f3b98e50c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METALOTIONE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Metallothioneins are proteins that bind metals, including copper, and play a role in the body's response to copper overload in Wilson's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11893</data>
      <data key="d7">7f790982b1864b248b2862d5585def20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUINOLONAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Quinolonas son una clase de antibi&#243;ticos que pueden estar relacionados con la aparici&#243;n de diarrea. Adem&#225;s, estos antibi&#243;ticos pueden interactuar con minerales presentes en la dieta, lo que puede afectar su eficacia. Tambi&#233;n se ha observado que las quinolonas pueden interferir con tratamientos para la enfermedad de Wilson, especialmente en lo que respecta a la absorci&#243;n de cobre.</data>
      <data key="d2">44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1792</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11894</data>
      <data key="d7">941ff61025d84ed9b050b2a102560744</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TETRACICLINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">TETRACICLINAS, or tetracyclines, are a group of antibiotics known for their ability to form insoluble complexes with dietary minerals. This characteristic can affect the absorption and efficacy of the antibiotics when taken alongside certain foods or supplements. Additionally, tetracyclines can interact with treatments for Wilson's disease, which is a condition that affects copper metabolism in the body. This interaction may have implications for the management of patients undergoing treatment for this disease, highlighting the importance of considering potential drug interactions when prescribing tetracyclines.</data>
      <data key="d2">ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d3">1870</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11895</data>
      <data key="d7">2a398d14437a4c4d9d1370cd27366aa6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WILSON'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wilson's disease is a genetic disorder characterized by the excessive accumulation of copper in the body. This condition can lead to a range of health issues, primarily affecting the liver and causing neurological problems. The disorder results from a defect in the body's ability to eliminate copper, leading to its toxic buildup and subsequent health complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">41a33a13610bbae73208f0d201781724,994c13f250eafe4b1a52d40b56230a0c</data>
      <data key="d3">1508</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">11896</data>
      <data key="d7">a627d7e56bfc48efa32dccaab46cb5cf</data>
    </node>
