      <data key="d7">4ba2ab72713a4af49caab2be20cd8a0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XANTINA OXIDASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La xantina oxidasa es una enzima que cataliza la conversi&#243;n de hipoxantina y guanina a xantina y &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11917</data>
      <data key="d7">ebd3a4ed86004b1895b998e94eb5e3ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALANTO&#205;NA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La alanto&#237;na es el producto final de la transformaci&#243;n del &#225;cido &#250;rico en mam&#237;feros.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11918</data>
      <data key="d7">50379fd3a718461b939ef233c363a3b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PURINAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">PURINAS are molecules that are integral components of nucleic acids and are metabolized in the body to produce uric acid. These compounds, found in various foods, can lead to increased uric acid production, which may contribute to conditions such as hyperuricemia. The metabolism of purines is significant as it can elevate uric acid levels, potentially impacting health and leading to related medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1384</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11919</data>
      <data key="d7">56c50dbf326e418e83b6e5fc878f7b03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEBUXOSTAT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El febuxostat es un inhibidor utilizado en el tratamiento de la hiperuricemia, que afecta la producci&#243;n de &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11920</data>
      <data key="d7">8126bcce7fae4bb996db8ba30da270a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXANTINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxantina is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the degradation of purines within the human body. It facilitates the conversion of guanosine into guanine, thereby participating in the metabolic processes associated with purines. Additionally, hipoxantina serves as an intermediary in purine metabolism, where it is further converted into xantina. This highlights its importance in the biochemical pathways that manage purine levels in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11921</data>
      <data key="d7">cebaad1afc5c46c5af01e2c033aa7203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUANINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Guanina, also known as guanine, is a purine base that plays a crucial role in the structure of nucleic acids in living organisms. It is produced from guanosine and is involved in various metabolic processes. In addition, guanina is metabolized through intermediates such as hypoxanthine and xanthine, ultimately leading to the formation of uric acid. This highlights its significance not only in genetic material but also in metabolic pathways within the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11922</data>
      <data key="d7">04d7f42d519945238658e46d2f7266b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XANTINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Xantina is a compound that is formed during the metabolism of purines. It specifically arises from the degradation of purines, particularly through the breakdown of hypoxanthine and guanine. Ultimately, xantina is converted into uric acid, which is a key component in the purine metabolism pathway.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11923</data>
      <data key="d7">7586155248d14cbab4acefbc179818dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;LCULOS DE &#193;CIDO &#218;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los c&#225;lculos de &#225;cido &#250;rico son dep&#243;sitos s&#243;lidos que se forman en la orina debido a la baja solubilidad del &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11924</data>
      <data key="d7">d89c6e258a314f8fb79ed7513ea82942</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUANOSINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La guanosina es un nucle&#243;sido que se forma a partir de la degradaci&#243;n de las purinas y se convierte en guanina.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11925</data>
      <data key="d7">292f3aef2dd34e7c979baabc6fb78c42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOSINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La adenosina es un nucle&#243;sido que se forma a partir de la degradaci&#243;n de las purinas y se convierte en inosina.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11926</data>
      <data key="d7">5244d819679c4d03acb4294a2c78d53b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUCLE&#211;SIDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los nucle&#243;sidos son compuestos formados por una base nitrogenada unida a un az&#250;car, que son productos intermedios en el metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1385</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11927</data>
      <data key="d7">d3cf8d5c9b3449599d7e1aec90ea207b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="URATO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11928</data>
      <data key="d7">2b4464f3f5854dc9bb245123edfc73e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="URICASA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Uricasa is an enzyme that converts uric acid into allantoin, which is more easily excreted from the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11929</data>
      <data key="d7">e8e2002c328e4aedb15b66021f90e92e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">GOTA, also known as gout, is a form of inflammatory arthritis that arises from the body's inflammatory response to the deposition of monosodium urate crystals in joints and tissues, primarily due to elevated levels of uric acid. This condition is characterized by sudden and severe attacks of pain, swelling, and redness in the affected joints. GOTA is often associated with the formation of uric acid stones, which can occur as a result of the high uric acid levels in the body. Overall, GOTA represents a clinical syndrome that significantly impacts the quality of life of those affected, manifesting through intense joint pain and inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d2">393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1387</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">11930</data>
      <data key="d7">5b25b7ebbb2447df842ca481dbe4a788</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS MIELOPROLIFERATIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trastornos mieloproliferativos are disorders of the bone marrow that can result in increased production of &#225;cido &#250;rico due to high cell turnover.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11931</data>
      <data key="d7">c84a7379ce15482eb795c652cfed7101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS LINFOPROLIFERATIVOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Trastornos linfoproliferativos are conditions that involve the proliferation of lymphocytes, which can also lead to elevated levels of &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11932</data>
      <data key="d7">89e4353ef37848498ff54e5a5cec1fa8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SORIASIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sor&#237;asis is a skin condition that can contribute to increased production of &#225;cido &#250;rico in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11933</data>
      <data key="d7">86fa3840cfac44a78c0beead7406eaab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIT DE VITAMINA B12">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deficit de vitamina B12 can lead to metabolic changes that may increase the production of &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11934</data>
      <data key="d7">a677fa28a6ff42488a4ef1d07d58853c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIUR&#201;TICOS TIAZ&#205;DICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diur&#233;ticos tiaz&#237;dicos are common medications that can decrease the renal elimination of &#225;cido &#250;rico, contributing to hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11935</data>
      <data key="d7">4700750abd3a4e58bbf9f3e960458f6d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SALICILATOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Salicilatos at low doses can also reduce the elimination of &#225;cido &#250;rico, leading to increased levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11936</data>
      <data key="d7">b43d1ae1fb6d4ac7a7d8743e98bea44d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALANTOINA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d3">1388</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11937</data>
      <data key="d7">31072e71fff8437884a4907e8a6997f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#193;LCULO RENAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#225;lculo renal refers to kidney stones, which are hard deposits made of minerals and salts that form inside the kidneys. These deposits can lead to significant pain and complications within the urinary tract. In summary, c&#225;lculos renales are characterized as hard mineral and salt formations in the kidneys, often resulting in discomfort and potential health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290</data>
      <data key="d3">1383</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11938</data>
      <data key="d7">d51efc76d75b41efba0894cb5cb1ca3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERCALCIURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPERCALCIURIA is a condition characterized by an excessive amount of calcium in the urine. This elevated calcium level can predispose individuals to the formation of kidney stones and is often associated with various metabolic disorders. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish, with the Spanish description emphasizing the same key points regarding the elevated calcium levels and the potential risk of developing renal calculi.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1383</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11939</data>
      <data key="d7">dcda0ec65c9d4adb8ec5e5f079565062</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD VASCULAR MANIFIESTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad vascular manifiesta se refiere a condiciones en las que hay evidencia de enfermedad en los vasos sangu&#237;neos, lo que puede estar relacionado con la hiperuricemia y el riesgo cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d2">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9</data>
      <data key="d3">1386</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11940</data>
      <data key="d7">8bdaeeac3a9e44d88409731dabb5be65</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERPARATIROIDISMO PRIMARIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hiperparatiroidismo primario is a medical condition where the parathyroid glands produce too much parathyroid hormone, leading to elevated calcium levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11941</data>
      <data key="d7">7d207ed6b0aa40ec97f111ea08c4d2a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCAUCALCEMIA IDIOP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipocalcemia idiop&#225;tica is a condition where there is a decrease in calcium levels in the urine without a known cause, often associated with significant bone mass loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11942</data>
      <data key="d7">5e872434cdca455f83e7601202f98b65</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALATO C&#193;LCICO MONOHIDRATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalato c&#225;lcico monohidratado, also known as whewellita, is a type of kidney stone that forms in alkaline urine and is associated with specific urinary pH levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11943</data>
      <data key="d7">a289f432543e45259f99beae9a77e04d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALATO C&#193;LCICO DIHIDRATO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalato c&#225;lcico dihidratado, or weddellite, is another type of calcium oxalate stone that can form in the kidneys, particularly in acidic urine.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11944</data>
      <data key="d7">2c0bf36c19f64d048aa322ea1a44430e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFATO C&#193;LCICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fosfato c&#225;lcico, or brushite, is a type of kidney stone that forms in specific urinary pH conditions and is associated with hypercalciuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11945</data>
      <data key="d7">0af32f1d4fc84be8a3f7119925aadaa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFATO AM&#211;NICO MAGN&#201;SICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fosfato am&#243;nico magn&#233;sico, or struvite, is a type of kidney stone that often forms in the presence of urinary infections and alkaline urine.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11946</data>
      <data key="d7">a9df8c7bc9ce486e875aa46f6586d944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CISTINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cistina is an amino acid that can lead to the formation of kidney stones in individuals with a genetic disorder known as cystinuria.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11947</data>
      <data key="d7">2960f516b3be4284b50e7f7c544f5915</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALOBACTER FORMIGENES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalobacter formigenes is a gram-negative anaerobic bacterium that plays a role in degrading oxalate in the intestine, potentially affecting oxalate absorption and kidney stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">618</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11948</data>
      <data key="d7">1c3f423d7e2c4183ac5222afc25618fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOXALURIA refers to a condition characterized by low levels of oxalate in the urine. This condition can influence kidney stone formation, as oxalate is a key component in the development of certain types of stones. Additionally, dietary factors can play a significant role in the levels of oxalate present in the urine, further impacting the condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">11949</data>
      <data key="d7">113d1778cfda4a1ca094aa4df6a7d9af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA IDIOP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria idiop&#225;tica is a rare condition characterized by low oxalate levels in the urine without a known cause.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11950</data>
      <data key="d7">31f8c6371b4640d0a150c80300494209</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA SECUNDARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria secundaria is a condition where low oxalate levels in the urine are caused by an underlying medical condition or dietary factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11951</data>
      <data key="d7">90cdd89fb34c4ad6be6ce509fbe8a911</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOXALURIA PRIMARIA is a genetic disorder characterized by abnormal oxalate levels in the body. There are two distinct forms of this condition: one leads to hyperoxaluria, where the body produces excessive amounts of oxalate, resulting in the formation of kidney stones. Conversely, the other form is associated with hypoxaluria, which is marked by low levels of oxalate in the urine and may potentially impact kidney function. This duality in the condition highlights the complexity of HIPOXALURIA PRIMARIA and its varying effects on renal health.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11952</data>
      <data key="d7">8c2987dba9c14282a0870b4bd25fa022</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA RELATIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria relativa refers to a condition where oxalate levels are low relative to other substances in the urine, which may influence kidney stone risk.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11953</data>
      <data key="d7">e44e6f0e9cf34456aa53aaac92530ce0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria cr&#243;nica is a long-term condition characterized by persistently low oxalate levels in the urine, which can have various health implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11954</data>
      <data key="d7">8b4aa497eee84992bb4701526300a13b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA AGUDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria aguda is a sudden onset of low oxalate levels in the urine, which may be triggered by dietary changes or medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11955</data>
      <data key="d7">ec17dffe71f94cedb3c55b74ccd160d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOXALURIA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hipoxaluria familiar is a hereditary condition that leads to low oxalate levels in the urine, affecting family members across generations.</data>
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">315</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11956</data>
      <data key="d7">ec85d9ab4afe4f54a6b98b79e9de08f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCAUCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d3">1383</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11957</data>
      <data key="d7">ec1b83d3566f49fe95a19c0fc048a95e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LITIASIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">LITIASIS refers to the formation of stones in the urinary tract, often associated with various metabolic disorders and dietary factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">11958</data>
      <data key="d7">cd8c866cf19c4cd6a68bc605c1322fea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CISTINURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CISTINURIA is a hereditary tubulopathy affecting the transport of cystine and basic amino acids, leading to the formation of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11959</data>
      <data key="d7">ca4801f8dca045e293e8e9a04c6dae9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDO URICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACIDO URICO refers to a metabolic condition characterized by the formation of uric acid stones in the urinary tract. Uric acid is a waste product that results from the breakdown of purines, which are substances found in certain foods and drinks. Elevated levels of uric acid in the body can lead to various health issues, including hyperuricemia, a condition marked by excessive uric acid in the blood, and gout, a type of inflammatory arthritis caused by the accumulation of uric acid crystals in the joints.</data>
      <data key="d2">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c,64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11960</data>
      <data key="d7">411a8ac9d8fc4ac2ab43ef0b0920c891</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITRATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">CITRATO is a significant inhibitor of urinary crystallization, especially in the formation of calcium oxalate crystals. This compound plays a crucial role in preventing the formation of calcium stones in the urine, and its effectiveness is influenced by dietary intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c,e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">11961</data>
      <data key="d7">f1d21808b7cf4e5794ea0a75aeff6f2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCASTRITURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOCASTRITURIA refers to a condition characterized by low levels of citrate in urine, which can lead to increased risk of stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11962</data>
      <data key="d7">04563070e412416bb73f32bb6794e3c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOCRITURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HIPOCRITURIA is a condition where there is a deficiency of citrate in urine, leading to a higher risk of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11963</data>
      <data key="d7">ccb0536351db4c2ab1230a9bba75a9e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS TUBULAR RENAL DISTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACIDOSIS TUBULAR RENAL DISTAL is a renal condition characterized by its impact on urinary pH and the potential for stone formation. This condition affects the kidneys' ability to properly acidify urine, leading to various metabolic disturbances.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c,a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11964</data>
      <data key="d7">bbfac8126b0f48d5920a45a4af20b065</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERCITRATURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HYPERCITRATURIA is a condition characterized by high levels of citrate in urine, which can help prevent stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">11965</data>
      <data key="d7">3a15391a131144dfba2beb29172030b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HYPERURICOSURIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">HYPERURICOSURIA is a condition involving excessive uric acid in the urine, which can lead to the formation of uric acid stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11966</data>
      <data key="d7">a997e1aefcf34dcc971b6bbe580cd9d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROBENECID">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Probenecid is a medication that plays a significant role in increasing uric acid excretion in urine, which can potentially influence the formation of kidney stones. It is primarily utilized in the treatment of gout and is effective in managing conditions associated with elevated uric acid levels. By enhancing the excretion of uric acid, Probenecid helps to alleviate symptoms related to gout and reduces the risk of kidney stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86,64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11967</data>
      <data key="d7">2996d07f9ed746cd934063662232c153</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFINPIRAZONA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">SULFINPIRAZONA is a drug that can help lower uric acid levels in the body, influencing the risk of uric acid stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11968</data>
      <data key="d7">1c17d2a28d4d45489cb25d503648f464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BENZBROMARONA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">BENZBROMARONA is a medication used to treat high uric acid levels, which can impact the formation of uric acid stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11969</data>
      <data key="d7">d163ef71998743be98f07de425546885</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOSARTAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">LOSARTAN is an antihypertensive medication that may influence uric acid levels and thus affect stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">64d85b2cd48849f9143370c8c04ab04c</data>
      <data key="d3">1411</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11970</data>
      <data key="d7">857ce3d4a9ff47e3973de303365b5aa9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Evaluaci&#243;n metab&#243;lica is a diagnostic process to assess the metabolic factors contributing to kidney stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11971</data>
      <data key="d7">a2b5cd1df0a94a69a9777bf220435864</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HISTORIA LITI&#193;SICA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Historia liti&#225;sica refers to the patient's history of kidney stones, including the number and type of stones previously formed.</data>
      <data key="d2">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11972</data>
      <data key="d7">9ac6e7795c0642a7b36b79f3acdfe651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETAS MALABSORTIVAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietas malabsortivas are diets that lead to poor absorption of nutrients, which can contribute to the formation of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11973</data>
      <data key="d7">d15c4e6aaf0f44e7b2b8c98d97c2c1d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACETAZOLAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetazolamina is a medication used to treat certain types of kidney stones and other conditions related to fluid retention.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11974</data>
      <data key="d7">5fc7fca1f1624aac85bed32ce7180e55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIAMTERENE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Triamterene is a diuretic medication that can be used in the management of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11975</data>
      <data key="d7">708ec5cd466e41c9b168f8a601b7ba4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INDINAVIR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Indinavir is an antiviral medication that can have side effects related to kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11976</data>
      <data key="d7">466b68a062884463841d392e2a71d546</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANATOMICAL ALTERATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anatomical alterations in the kidneys can lead to conditions such as kidney stones and other urinary tract issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11977</data>
      <data key="d7">28b49307626d45f98f1d5b955bdcd191</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLOOD AND URINE ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Blood and urine analysis are essential diagnostic tools for evaluating kidney function and identifying potential causes of nephrolithiasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11978</data>
      <data key="d7">5a51efcbbceb4c209dc21811627fca67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMAGING STUDIES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Imaging studies help identify anatomical abnormalities and assess metabolic activity related to kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11979</data>
      <data key="d7">cec7e466f4974a0481d2c385ddca0b45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="24-HOUR URINE COLLECTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">24-hour urine collection is a method used to evaluate the composition of urine and assess risk factors for kidney stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11980</data>
      <data key="d7">4646e16935954c22bb01aefda65858aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITRUS JUICES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrus juices, particularly orange juice, are recognized for their potential protective effects against kidney stones, primarily attributed to their high citrate content. These juices are known to increase urinary citrate levels, which is beneficial in reducing the risk of stone formation. The high potassium citrate content in citrus juices further contributes to this protective effect, making them a valuable addition to the diet for those concerned about kidney stone development.</data>
      <data key="d2">550574bce077f34348bd11c78dc814a1,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11981</data>
      <data key="d7">7a860f0f1d8b4692a11625923ed9d552</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUGARY SODAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sugary sodas may increase the risk of kidney stones and are generally advised against in patients with a history of nephrolithiasis.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11982</data>
      <data key="d7">d1cd92aff4364bfd8bb6e4f298f938df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPORTS DRINKS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sports drinks containing electrolytes and carbohydrates do not significantly affect urinary excretion of calcium or other salts.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1409</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11983</data>
      <data key="d7">a22ac25692bb452287d4cad987d68c9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KIDNEY STONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Kidney stones are solid masses made of crystals that originate in the kidneys. They can cause significant pain and complications for those affected.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86,a0162312192878417ef2c4ef8f9cffba</data>
      <data key="d3">1651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">11984</data>
      <data key="d7">1667330e567b4881952dfde65ce5d5a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="URIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Uric acid is a waste product formed from the breakdown of purines, and its levels are significant in the formation of certain types of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11985</data>
      <data key="d7">efde2496dd3d49bc8bdecc932c42d8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalate is a compound commonly found in a variety of foods. It has the potential to combine with calcium, which can lead to the formation of kidney stones. Additionally, the levels of oxalate in urine can be influenced by dietary choices, further contributing to the risk of kidney stone development.</data>
      <data key="d2">550574bce077f34348bd11c78dc814a1,60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">11986</data>
      <data key="d7">1d26b8fb4fcc46b2a744ade36724d8ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHOSPHATE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Phosphate is a chemical compound that can also contribute to the formation of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11987</data>
      <data key="d7">1879b3d65bf74fb19dfc57a08ab633ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RENAL ANATOMY">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">60d4458582de1ce500542bb9bfb34a86</data>
      <data key="d3">1651</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11988</data>
      <data key="d7">5cc602169459451eb9935792986bae50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIETY OF UROLOGY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Society of Urology provides guidelines for the prevention of kidney stones, including recommendations on calcium intake.</data>
      <data key="d2">451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11989</data>
      <data key="d7">607e6060bbe8494aa89574c43e74b662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OXALATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxalato is a compound commonly found in various foods. It is known to contribute to the formation of kidney stones, particularly when consumed in high amounts or when it is not adequately bound by calcium. This dual role highlights the importance of managing oxalate intake to mitigate the risk of kidney stone formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61,e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">11990</data>
      <data key="d7">e3f71bbea2394e81a101b8a0a1a091c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NAS ANIMALES">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Animal proteins should be limited to 0.8 g/day to help prevent kidney stones, except for dairy products.</data>
      <data key="d2">451bbcaee8b1a025277b84488ea7db61</data>
      <data key="d3">1381</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">11991</data>
      <data key="d7">16d48298cd6c4926a84278879db8b7da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACELGA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Swiss chard is a leafy green vegetable that is rich in oxalate, which can contribute to kidney stone development.</data>
