      <data key="d1">CACAO is a sweetened cocoa product that is derived from cacao beans. It is important to note that CACAO should not be given to infants before the age of one due to its sugar content. Additionally, cocoa, which is produced from cacao beans, contains oxalate, a compound that may increase the risk of kidney stones. Therefore, while CACAO can be enjoyed by older children and adults, caution is advised regarding its consumption by infants and individuals susceptible to kidney stones.</data>
