      <data key="d6">12097</data>
      <data key="d7">c18063c397434a3ca944fd609560a335</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PA&#205;SES AFRICANOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">African countries are significantly affected by diarrhea, with a high incidence of cases leading to child mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12098</data>
      <data key="d7">acb2f493eea74de1b9c42ae4e50f5bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PA&#205;SES DEL SUDESTE ASI&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Southeast Asian countries experience a high prevalence of diarrhea, particularly among children under five years old.</data>
      <data key="d2">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12099</data>
      <data key="d7">86cb6938bbd54f63a7a7a09ff9a6c9ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PA&#205;SES INDUSTRIALIZADOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "PA&#205;SES INDUSTRIALIZADOS" refers to industrialized countries, which typically do not encounter life-threatening risks from acute diarrhea. However, these countries do experience socio-sanitary impacts associated with chronic diarrhea, which has a higher prevalence in these regions due to various lifestyle factors.</data>
      <data key="d2">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12100</data>
      <data key="d7">f82c003c67aa4a7b90d67b9c55cf96ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTULOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactulosa is a synthetic sugar that serves multiple purposes in health care. Primarily, it is recognized as a laxative used to treat constipation. Additionally, Lactulosa functions as a prebiotic, resisting digestion and promoting gut health. This dual role highlights its importance in both alleviating digestive issues and supporting overall gastrointestinal well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12101</data>
      <data key="d7">c7b3172e584c47d9b0d8b73ede10735a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INULINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Inulina is a type of soluble fiber that serves as a prebiotic, promoting the growth of beneficial gut bacteria. It is commonly used in dietary and nutritional products due to its health benefits and positive effects on digestive health. Inulina is recognized for its prebiotic properties, making it a valuable ingredient in various food products aimed at enhancing gut health.</data>
      <data key="d2">16e694ae79763a00ceb974feca8e733d,242f6cf03a4c50245e71fee58de41d18,751947d2192006b89bb703587d56df99,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,d7995c4e4e8e09e71d30c87b5f02b18a</data>
      <data key="d3">780</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">12102</data>
      <data key="d7">0a6ef6e349354b4e803905a3dbc1563e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC&#193;RIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructooligosaccharides (FOS) are prebiotic carbohydrates that promote the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut.</data>
      <data key="d2">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12103</data>
      <data key="d7">bc4f9ecc97d74d44bd937a9835d5d390</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DEL INTESTINO IRRITABLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome del intestino irritable (SIC), conocido en ingl&#233;s como Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS), es una condici&#243;n gastrointestinal com&#250;n que puede ser influenciada por la dieta y la fermentaci&#243;n de alimentos. Esta afecci&#243;n se caracteriza por s&#237;ntomas como dolor abdominal y cambios en los h&#225;bitos intestinales, que pueden incluir episodios de diarrea. El s&#237;ndrome del intestino irritable es frecuentemente discutido en el contexto de la salud intestinal, lo que resalta su relevancia en el bienestar general del sistema digestivo.</data>
      <data key="d2">527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1,b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">825</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12104</data>
      <data key="d7">7240d8624dd14f0590b9dbc0aafe1c0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GALACTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC&#193;RIDOS">
      <data key="d0" />
