    <node id="GIARDIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Giardia is a protozoan parasite that can cause gastrointestinal illness, leading to persistent diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1753</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12112</data>
      <data key="d7">8de6e581a9b04277ab4f76fb649e3cc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRYPTOSPORIDIUM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cryptosporidium is a parasite that can cause gastrointestinal infections, often resulting in diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1753</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12113</data>
      <data key="d7">1d9c349d4e294282900a9518cdfdddfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ETIOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Etiolog&#237;a refers to the study of the causes of diseases, in this context, it relates to the causes of diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12114</data>
      <data key="d7">cd041044be7647699546adf9845dcdc5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROTE DE EII">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Brote de EII refers to an outbreak of inflammatory bowel disease, which can present with symptoms including diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12115</data>
      <data key="d7">fb713ef726914f9fa355296d431e0754</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SRO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SRO refers to Oral Rehydration Solutions, which are used to prevent dehydration caused by diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1739</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12116</data>
      <data key="d7">ffe40282607e4559bb8d4bace44347a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIARREA AGUDA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">DIARREA AGUDA, or acute diarrhea, is a medical condition characterized by the rapid onset of frequent loose or watery stools. This condition can be potentially life-threatening if not managed properly, particularly in vulnerable populations such as children and the elderly. Treatment often involves the use of rehydration solutions to prevent dehydration, and in some cases, antibiotics may be required to address underlying infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b,db3e6b8c8514f310618353612e378ce6</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">27</data>
      <data key="d6">12117</data>
      <data key="d7">18c6e3320fd4458199c7153a4b97cc7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RACECADOTRILO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El racecadotril es un f&#225;rmaco que se utiliza para tratar la diarrea aguda, actuando como un inhibidor de las encefalocinasas y disminuyendo la secreci&#243;n intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12118</data>
      <data key="d7">9e595f298685442a95be5941e23c8910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INMUNODEPRIMIDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La inmunodepresi&#243;n es una condici&#243;n que puede aumentar el riesgo de complicaciones en pacientes con diarrea aguda, como aquellos con VIH o que han recibido trasplantes.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12119</data>
      <data key="d7">d6fb061854c442a6a92511940e7a970e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIARREA SANGUINOLENTA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diarrea sanguinolenta, or bloody diarrhea, is a severe symptom that necessitates immediate medical attention. It may indicate a serious underlying infection. This condition is characterized by the presence of blood in the stool and is considered a significant health concern that requires prompt evaluation and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12120</data>
      <data key="d7">383558be778b4cddb4adbdb748a6d6a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIDRATACI&#211;N ORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hidrataci&#243;n oral es un m&#233;todo de tratamiento clave en la gesti&#243;n de la diarrea aguda, utilizando soluciones de rehidrataci&#243;n oral para prevenir la deshidrataci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12121</data>
      <data key="d7">3dcfe18a43f54587ac172ef614761707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLUCI&#211;N DE REHIDRATACI&#211;N ORAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La soluci&#243;n de rehidrataci&#243;n oral es un tratamiento utilizado para reponer l&#237;quidos y electrolitos en pacientes con diarrea aguda.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12122</data>
      <data key="d7">54ff395bacce434684cc6385c3c3f74e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CULTIVO DE HECES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El cultivo de heces es una prueba diagn&#243;stica que puede ser necesaria en casos de diarrea aguda para identificar la causa de la infecci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12123</data>
      <data key="d7">fe66779bf01749ee84f0056ccaceaf15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO SINTOM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El "TRATAMIENTO SINTOM&#193;TICO" se refiere a las intervenciones m&#233;dicas dise&#241;adas para aliviar los s&#237;ntomas de la diarrea, tanto en casos cr&#243;nicos como agudos, sin abordar la causa subyacente de la afecci&#243;n. Este enfoque se centra en proporcionar alivio a los pacientes, mejorando su bienestar temporalmente, mientras que la causa ra&#237;z de la diarrea permanece sin tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">28f6d6818b8f0ce3d2b8f483fe0dac6c,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12124</data>
      <data key="d7">4d7a75cedcfb4386921005cbed5c61a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOBACILLUS RHAMNOSUS GG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG is a probiotic strain that has shown effectiveness in managing acute diarrhea, particularly of viral origin.</data>
      <data key="d2">c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12125</data>
      <data key="d7">5c92067aab824c4193c55f8fa76511cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SACCHAROMYCES BOULARDII">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Saccharomyces boulardii is a probiotic yeast recognized for its effectiveness in treating gastrointestinal disorders. It is particularly noted for its role in treating and preventing acute diarrhea, especially in cases associated with antibiotic use. Additionally, Saccharomyces boulardii is utilized to support overall gut health, making it a valuable option for individuals seeking to improve their digestive well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1024</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12126</data>
      <data key="d7">049c103a3931486eb517cbcc351c469c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROBIOTICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Probiotics are live microorganisms that offer various health benefits, particularly in the context of gastrointestinal health. They are often included in enteral nutrition to enhance outcomes in trauma patients and have been studied for their potential role in preventing complications associated with severe pancreatic diseases. Probiotics may also help improve gut health and reduce side effects from treatments such as radiotherapy, as well as assist in managing gastrointestinal disorders like acute diarrhea.

However, the use of probiotics in certain populations, particularly immunocompromised patients, is controversial due to potential risks. Additionally, while probiotics may provide benefits in critical care settings, their use is generally not recommended for most ICU patients due to inconsistent data regarding their efficacy. Overall, probiotics are recognized for their potential health benefits, but caution is advised in specific patient groups.</data>
      <data key="d2">2194de4eaed685b07d8f4c7a397de0ce,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b,cae7bf8d7b8c9d1f34a87ef41ff39a17,fb24bf4c9fcf60bbc1dd56cd60ba0a47</data>
      <data key="d3">1210</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">12127</data>
      <data key="d7">41f8ded8c6164b49a6d640f040e1e554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PREBIOTICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Prebiotics are non-digestible food components that play a crucial role in promoting the growth of beneficial microorganisms in the intestines. They are known to stimulate the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut, which can potentially aid in the management of various gastrointestinal issues, including diarrhea and inflammatory bowel disease. By fostering a healthy gut microbiome, prebiotics contribute to overall digestive health and may offer therapeutic benefits for individuals suffering from these conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12128</data>
      <data key="d7">7b63097214b544b191fb9aa871550d35</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEVOFLOXACINO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Levofloxacino is another quinolone antibiotic that can be used to treat severe cases of diarrhea caused by bacterial infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12129</data>
      <data key="d7">a9730056c28c4e948c57f411f524b952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZITROMICINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Azitromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that may be used in cases of acute diarrhea when bacterial infection is suspected.</data>
      <data key="d2">c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12130</data>
      <data key="d7">ede2223c0fff46c9b53b27abd937365e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ERITROMICINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Eritromicina is a macrolide antibiotic that is utilized to treat various bacterial infections, including those that may lead to acute diarrhea. It is particularly effective in critical care patients and can assist in facilitating the passage of a feeding tube through the digestive system. However, it is important to note that eritromicina should be taken on an empty stomach to enhance its absorption. Additionally, the antibiotic can be associated with the production of diarrhea as a side effect. It is also noteworthy that eritromicina can be degraded in an acidic environment, which may impact its absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94,c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1752</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">12131</data>
      <data key="d7">4249a2eee8bc44eb87cc2bec0d36ced5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FECAL MICROBIOTA TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) is a procedure being researched for the treatment of severe and recurrent diarrhea caused by Clostridium difficile.</data>
      <data key="d2">c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12132</data>
      <data key="d7">4c36e184572d41ba9ceaca2618194663</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUINOLONES">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">c71444e871ecb476be3ad3eef136161b</data>
      <data key="d3">1750</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12133</data>
      <data key="d7">b7b60659aa574fadbadf61f42dc34a28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PA&#205;SES EN V&#205;AS DE DESARROLLO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Developing countries where infectious causes are more prevalent in cases of chronic diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12134</data>
      <data key="d7">28d066c544b34749a163ec0d9e5463c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F75">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F75 is a special nutritional treatment formula used for severe acute malnutrition associated with diarrhea in children, administered orally or via a nasogastric tube.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12135</data>
      <data key="d7">ddbc811eff8042f2823f0064a1be0c49</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F100">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F100 is another special nutritional treatment formula for severe acute malnutrition, similar to F75, used in pediatric cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12136</data>
      <data key="d7">28361cfb1424462e94ed31f263b93214</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PL&#193;TANOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bananas are recommended for patients with diarrhea due to their potassium content and ability to help firm stools.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12137</data>
      <data key="d7">4f585329e6d143faa49863a85c95483c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VEGETALES COCIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Cooked vegetables are advised for patients with diarrhea as they provide essential nutrients while being easier to digest.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12138</data>
      <data key="d7">3a8de9a9f9ae4db5802c484898949618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactose intolerance can develop secondary to infectious enteritis, affecting dietary choices during recovery from diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12139</data>
      <data key="d7">6e5987c5a27a49cdb40f8723a560d8c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALMID&#211;N COCIDO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d3">824</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12140</data>
      <data key="d7">043dcfef858741808ee2ec3703455827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLITIS ULCEROSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Colitis ulcerosa, also known as ulcerative colitis (UC), is an autoimmune disease and a form of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) that primarily affects the colon and rectum. It is characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucosa and submucosa, leading to a range of symptoms including rectal bleeding, abdominal pain, and chronic diarrhea. The condition can result in significant gastrointestinal distress and may lead to nutritional deficits and problems with nutrient absorption, particularly during acute flare-ups. Colitis ulcerosa is a chronic condition that requires ongoing management and may necessitate nutritional intervention to address complications arising from the disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40,449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46,4ec3e8cb1f21808e70bbc71cb26d7396,609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186,88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,a519216aaee7bf8a1317f5d6b522c4b6,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">12141</data>
      <data key="d7">eb21276deb5740e6882021dd23ea450f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VASCULITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La vasculitis es una inflamaci&#243;n de los vasos sangu&#237;neos que puede afectar el sistema digestivo y contribuir a la diarrea cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12142</data>
      <data key="d7">d5efc3d915844826a02b2fe85e704492</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AN&#193;LISIS DE HECES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El an&#225;lisis de heces es una prueba diagn&#243;stica que puede ayudar a identificar la causa de la diarrea cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12143</data>
      <data key="d7">f5a6a7f693744de786019731a5bb913f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO ETIOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El tratamiento etiol&#243;gico se refiere a las intervenciones m&#233;dicas que buscan resolver la causa subyacente de la diarrea cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12144</data>
      <data key="d7">e4f7f7846c4b42f09774ef74bd11f5c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES SIST&#201;MICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades sist&#233;micas son condiciones m&#233;dicas que pueden afectar m&#250;ltiples sistemas del cuerpo y contribuir a s&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12145</data>
      <data key="d7">37c3e46402e54d32a0564962541f3af4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades intestinales son trastornos que afectan el intestino y pueden causar s&#237;ntomas como diarrea cr&#243;nica.</data>
      <data key="d2">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d3">847</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12146</data>
      <data key="d7">a0395017c8dc46dca4dfa7a60c6def90</data>
    </node>
