    <node id="SAQUINAVIR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Saquinavir is an antiretroviral medication classified as an HIV protease inhibitor. It is known to potentially cause diarrhea as a side effect. Additionally, the metabolism of Saquinavir can be inhibited by grapefruit juice, which may lead to increased levels of the drug in the body. Conversely, high amounts of garlic can reduce the absorption of Saquinavir, potentially diminishing its effectiveness.</data>
