      <data key="d6">12191</data>
      <data key="d7">0629c3fd2fc642cea5c4854207e4d273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "MICROBIOMA INTESTINAL," or human intestinal microbiome, is a significant area of scientific research, particularly concerning its crucial role in health and disease. This microbiome encompasses the genetic makeup of the bacteria residing in the gut, which is essential for various aspects of health and metabolism. Understanding the complexities of the intestinal microbiome is vital for uncovering its impact on overall well-being and the potential implications for various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">90f122c65fbb08f52e052d0e22714849,beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d3">1004</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12192</data>
      <data key="d7">18dae051486d47c49c08f40217e161ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTRE&#209;IMIENTO CR&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic constipation is a long-term condition that affects bowel movements and can lead to various health issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12193</data>
