    </node>
    <node id="LAXANTES OSM&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Osmotic laxatives, such as magnesium sulfate and sodium sulfate, work by increasing water retention in the intestines.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d3">1406</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12194</data>
      <data key="d7">f7e83f87e31346d197e657f2c8c06609</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAXANTES ESTIMULANTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Stimulant laxatives, like bisacodyl and senna, stimulate bowel movements by acting on the intestinal nerves.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d3">1406</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12195</data>
      <data key="d7">71e0bfa10d844a259418ae871f38e967</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAXANTES EMOLIENTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Emollient laxatives, such as docusate sodium, help soften stool by mixing water with fats.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d3">1406</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12196</data>
      <data key="d7">aa4ee7eb922b4facb3567026fef5c20a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAXANTES QUE AUMENTAN EL BOLO INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Laxatives that increase intestinal bulk, like methylcellulose and psyllium, absorb water to enhance stool volume.</data>
      <data key="d2">beef8f83c872431c6e371987b717e43b</data>
      <data key="d3">1406</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12197</data>
