    <node id="SEPSIS POR CAT&#201;TER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sepsis por cat&#233;ter is a serious complication that can arise in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. This condition is characterized by a severe infection that may occur as a result of the use of central venous catheters. It highlights the risks associated with catheter use in the context of nutritional support, emphasizing the need for careful monitoring and management to prevent such infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ce6342fdfe4419826c1ab2f84c56247,be7eb01a6daf673db6a127f66c79c96c</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12257</data>
      <data key="d7">ca2b0dc03b064bc28fdab7682d00bb7c</data>
    </node>
