    </node>
    <node id="COBALAMINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Cobalamin, also known as vitamin B12, is a crucial nutrient that can be malabsorbed in patients with pancreatic conditions, leading to deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825</data>
      <data key="d3">822</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12267</data>
      <data key="d7">f49cb613cf83481a8f67d02fd2e448b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALCOHOLISM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alcoholism is a chronic condition that significantly impacts health, particularly by exacerbating pancreatic diseases and leading to nutritional deficiencies. It is recognized as the primary etiology of chronic pancreatitis, a serious inflammation of the pancreas. To improve patient outcomes, individuals suffering from chronic alcoholism must achieve absolute abstinence from alcohol.</data>
      <data key="d2">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3</data>
      <data key="d3">1198</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12268</data>
      <data key="d7">c9df1fac57e44b55b2760dde85af7375</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIE&#769;TICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Dietary management involves strategies to adjust food intake for patients with pancreatic diseases to alleviate symptoms and improve nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825</data>
      <data key="d3">1197</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12269</data>
      <data key="d7">ace5b37b4c2f4740a0b236f59f591b16</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTADO NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ESTADO NUTRICIONAL" refers to the overall health condition of an individual in relation to their dietary intake and the utilization of nutrients by the body. It encompasses the assessment of how well a person's nutritional needs are being met and how effectively their body absorbs and uses these nutrients. This concept is particularly significant in the context of patients with pancreatic diseases, where nutritional status plays a critical role in their overall health and management.</data>
      <data key="d2">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825,ac274a54f27601e9d60118e72fc2ba94</data>
      <data key="d3">619</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12270</data>
      <data key="d7">91846610682c4cf8a211ce05ba6aa589</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional Support Therapy is a treatment approach designed to provide adequate nutrition to patients, particularly those who are unable to eat normally. It is a standard practice in the medical field, especially for critically ill patients, where guidelines exist for the provision and assessment of nutrition support therapy. Additionally, Nutritional Support Therapy is recognized as an essential intervention for patients with pancreatitis, ensuring they receive the necessary exogenous nutrients to aid in their recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">242fceb82929615af653d9f8574b0ef5,69bfdb98603d3d8c4733cb795f4c82f3,ceb66a898fed371e013171c43a87e1d1</data>
      <data key="d3">684</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">12271</data>
      <data key="d7">0d1db941992e43dcbb2fdc1ac4e6d4a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEATORREA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esteatorrea is a medical condition characterized by the presence of excess fat in the feces, which often indicates underlying malabsorption issues. This condition can be particularly relevant in the context of diabetes management, as it may affect the absorption of nutrients. Esteatorrea is commonly observed in patients with pancreatitis, where malabsorption is a significant concern. Overall, the presence of excess fat in feces serves as an important clinical indicator of digestive health and potential complications related to various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4c37affdd97e7772d1ea27aee34533b8,67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d3">198</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12272</data>
      <data key="d7">d8d7e5d46c8a4d5b87cb02cb31b0140a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPORTE M&#201;DICO-SOCIAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Soporte m&#233;dico-social is the medical and social support system that helps patients achieve abstention from alcohol and manage their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d3">198</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12273</data>
      <data key="d7">210b7231f3934c6184dadc20ff1b1123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLOQUE: NUTRICI&#211;N EN PATOLOG&#205;A DEL TUBO DIGESTIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">This section discusses nutritional management in digestive tract pathologies, particularly focusing on pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d3">198</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12274</data>
      <data key="d7">4344deda2a8b40b2afd7efe92fc41be2</data>
