    <node id="ABSTENCI&#211;N EN&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Abstenci&#243;n en&#243;lica refers to the cessation of alcohol consumption, which is crucial for managing pancreatitis and preventing further complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d3">198</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12275</data>
      <data key="d7">dee304730771425d8b4aba5e41e34eb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUBO DIGESTIVO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TUBO DIGESTIVO," or digestive tract, is a vital anatomical structure responsible for processing food and facilitating digestion and nutrient absorption. It serves as the pathway through which enteral nutrition is administered directly to patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings. The functionality of the tubo digestivo is crucial for determining the type of nutritional support required, especially in medical conditions such as pancreatitis, where specific nutritional management is necessary. Additionally, the tubo digestivo can be the subject of various diagnostic explorations to assess its health and functionality. Overall, the tubo digestivo plays a central role in both the digestive process and the management of nutritional needs in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">072912695b1cff9f390d4ead3b9ad742,67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d,6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,ec4fd77add427ab49ea4b8687b94b263</data>
      <data key="d3">1189</data>
