    <node id="ANTICUERPOS ANTICITOPLASMA DE NEUTR&#211;FILOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Anticuerpos anticitoplasma de neutr&#243;filos (p-ANCA) are antibodies that are often present in patients with ulcerative colitis, indicating an autoimmune response.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12341</data>
      <data key="d7">25a09035afc34f4ba8172bed6738ee03</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICUERPOS ANTI-SACCHAROMYCES CEREVISIAE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Anticuerpos anti-Saccharomyces cerevisiae (ASCA) are antibodies associated with Crohn's disease, indicating a potential relationship with inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12342</data>
      <data key="d7">59016b81a1594e45914cae275afdad20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GEN NOD-2/CARD15">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The NOD-2/CARD15 gene is associated with the immune response and has been linked to the development of Crohn's disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">23b65526747fa6950a347d0f0a597a40</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12343</data>
      <data key="d7">242ec7235558432fa488ebebb93e9e13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFASALACINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfasalacina is a medication primarily utilized as a first-line treatment for ulcerative colitis, where it plays a crucial role in reducing inflammation. Additionally, it is important to note that sulfasalacina can interfere with the absorption of nutrients in patients suffering from inflammatory bowel disease. This dual function highlights both its therapeutic benefits and potential side effects in managing gastrointestinal conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">88647cc4d1748c5bb058d4aab1817d63,ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12344</data>
      <data key="d7">2cfbc2a0dd1a4e3191d4f19dbe400d90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMINOSALICILATOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Aminosalicylic drugs are used in the treatment of ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease to maintain remission and reduce inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12345</data>
      <data key="d7">bff17e7d88644f149fac415e2fd5e899</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TENESMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tenesmus is a symptom characterized by a constant feeling of needing to pass stools, often associated with colitis ulcerosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12346</data>
      <data key="d7">5d7f023249534f98b907851463178700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="URGENCIA DEPOSICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urgency of defecation is a symptom that can occur in patients with colitis ulcerosa, indicating inflammation of the rectum.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d3">667</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12347</data>
      <data key="d7">1168213584214dcaa82d154a3f2ffcfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CU">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CU refers to Colitis Ulcerosa, also known as ulcerative colitis, which is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease that primarily affects the colon. This condition is characterized by acute flare-ups and can lead to severe malnutrition if not properly managed. Treatment is essential to alleviate symptoms and maintain remission. Additionally, it is important to note that "CU" can also refer to copper, an essential trace element required in small amounts for various biological functions, particularly in the context of parenteral nutrition. However, in the context of the provided descriptions, CU predominantly pertains to Colitis Ulcerosa.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa</data>
      <data key="d3">327</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">12</data>
      <data key="d6">12348</data>
      <data key="d7">26c21c2eb76f46a19b7a90b6fc8052dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EC, or Enfermedad de Crohn, is a type of inflammatory bowel disease characterized by its chronic nature. This condition can lead to malnutrition and necessitates a variety of treatment approaches to manage its symptoms and complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807,c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">12349</data>
      <data key="d7">667fbb842332414ea892476c5457df38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BUDESONIDA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Budesonida is a corticosteroid that helps suppress inflammation in patients with inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">327</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12350</data>
      <data key="d7">4820b732ec4a4c36abf2976bb111d502</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLARITROMICINA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Claritromicina is an antibiotic that may be used in the treatment of severe inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12351</data>
      <data key="d7">b518951b706f4e158d599ae3a04fc30c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="METRONIDAZOL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Metronidazol is an antibiotic that is utilized to treat a variety of infections, particularly those caused by anaerobic bacteria. It is indicated for severe forms of inflammatory bowel disease, especially in cases involving perianal complications. Additionally, metronidazol is effective in addressing bacterial overgrowth in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The medication also has the capability to inhibit aldehyde dehydrogenase, which can impact alcohol metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04,1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa,4f1c852e5d25eed4db322b75624d3e2b,5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12352</data>
      <data key="d7">744bb7bb836444da9179c4967b0c547f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFLIXIMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Infliximab is a biological therapy that targets tumor necrosis factor (TNF) and is used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12353</data>
      <data key="d7">494ce500e18c4a37adac334c38180721</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADALIMUMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Adalimumab is a monoclonal antibody used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease, particularly effective against TNF.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12354</data>
      <data key="d7">c253adadacd14391afc1969e26ef7974</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOLIMUMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Golimumab is another anti-TNF monoclonal antibody used in the management of inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12355</data>
      <data key="d7">de7033c1f5bb4711a9ce8291d15bf920</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CERTOLIZUMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Certolizumab is a biological agent that targets TNF and is used in the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12356</data>
      <data key="d7">9af4aecff9bd40e08e1359d2ce124fa9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VEDOLIZUMAB">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Vedolizumab is a monoclonal antibody used to treat inflammatory bowel disease by targeting specific integrins involved in inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">326</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12357</data>
      <data key="d7">2d07034189544415adb1fd1a2d593a8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INMUNOMODULADORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Immunomodulators such as 6-mercaptopurina, azatioprina, and metotrexato are used for maintenance treatment in inflammatory bowel disease, particularly when other treatments fail.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">327</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12358</data>
      <data key="d7">6cb132a41ce94cb8b0d25e8c9a118ff9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TERAPIAS BIOLOGICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Biological therapies, including monoclonal antibodies against TNF, have revolutionized the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease, providing new options for management.</data>
      <data key="d2">5785beff5a0642d55deb146b2a454807</data>
      <data key="d3">327</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12359</data>
      <data key="d7">5f30b93f80df4367b24515ae31db2625</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deficiencia Energ&#233;tico-Prot&#233;ica, un estado de desnutrici&#243;n que puede ocurrir en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal</data>
      <data key="d2">c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa</data>
      <data key="d3">668</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">12360</data>
      <data key="d7">19513d7866dc4bc795e7a75e7f6a0123</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA RESTRICTIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Una dieta que limita ciertos alimentos, que puede contribuir a la desnutrici&#243;n en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal</data>
      <data key="d2">c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa</data>
      <data key="d3">668</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12361</data>
      <data key="d7">48238dd778fb49d495cccc2b30fdefa4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SANGRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">P&#233;rdida de sangre gastrointestinal que puede ocurrir en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal, contribuyendo a la desnutrici&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d2">c9790e5e47712b100fb4870d35a3edfa</data>
      <data key="d3">668</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12362</data>
      <data key="d7">94b56c999cd6402392d78dc6da306671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTR&#201;S PSICOSOCIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El estr&#233;s psicosocial se asocia con la EII, manifest&#225;ndose en ansiedad y depresi&#243;n, especialmente en adultos y ni&#241;os."</data>
      <data key="d2">eaa2ba81b06f325e284b5dbdc45b5c9f</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12363</data>
      <data key="d7">d4ef0f032f6a4983adf8bcc13ea47d34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N-TELOP&#201;PTIDO DE COL&#193;GENO TIPO I">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El N-telop&#233;ptido de col&#225;geno tipo I es un marcador de resorci&#243;n &#243;sea que se mide en orina en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12364</data>
      <data key="d7">8e1d0b48cd4f47e0be427bc2ce7eb827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIALOPROTE&#205;NA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La sialoprote&#237;na &#243;sea es un marcador utilizado para evaluar la resorci&#243;n &#243;sea en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12365</data>
      <data key="d7">42099e6cc11248cab6c2bdcb52cbff96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOSFATASA ALCALINA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La fosfatasa alcalina &#243;sea es un marcador que se utiliza para evaluar la salud &#243;sea en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">45ae0837b0632b026fac1053b7d9d4e8</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12366</data>
      <data key="d7">38bcfbe4ef434612aa9ffb4d45a34b69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EII">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">EII refers to inflammatory bowel disease, encompassing conditions such as Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis that affect the digestive tract.</data>
      <data key="d2">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">12367</data>
      <data key="d7">d19b2d3247cc4c6ea3416609f11246c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIFOSFONATOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Bisphosphonates are a class of medications approved by the FDA for the prevention of osteoporosis. They are specifically indicated for use in patients with osteopenia, as they help to reduce bone resorption markers. These medications are prescribed at specific dosages to effectively manage and treat conditions related to bone density loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">1414</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12368</data>
      <data key="d7">e389e5c87cbc46b8b4df2467d8dd3bd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="B12">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Vitamin B12 is a vitamin that may be supplemented in high doses for patients with moderate deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d2">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12369</data>
      <data key="d7">d47dae2d13a04b50bd36eb48f73e4ee3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLORA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Intestinal flora refers to the community of microorganisms in the gut, which can be altered in patients with EII and affect lactose digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c</data>
      <data key="d3">844</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12370</data>
      <data key="d7">dfaf360032fa4e7584f46c2d25ba2f88</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLESTRA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Olestra es un sustituto de grasa que ha sido aprobado por la FDA y se utiliza en productos alimenticios para reducir el contenido cal&#243;rico.</data>
      <data key="d2">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12371</data>
      <data key="d7">d217531624c64e35a8947fa9a0bd8690</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLLESTERAMINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La colesteramina es un medicamento que se utiliza para reducir los niveles de colesterol en la sangre y puede afectar la absorci&#243;n de grasas.</data>
      <data key="d2">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d3">672</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12372</data>
      <data key="d7">becd59c2945f47dd9e170c99eeb6a47d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULAS ENTEROCUT&#193;NEAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#237;stulas enterocut&#225;neas are abnormal connections between the intestine and the skin that can complicate nutritional management in patients. These fistulas can lead to severe malnutrition due to the loss of intestinal contents and impaired nutrient absorption. Treatment options for f&#237;stulas enterocut&#225;neas may include nutritional support through Total Parenteral Nutrition (NPT), provided that certain conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf,379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,4ec3e8cb1f21808e70bbc71cb26d7396</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12373</data>
      <data key="d7">6ece78a59d3a473bb37c57da272d3081</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITES DE OLIVA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Tipo de aceite utilizado en dietas enterales polim&#233;ricas que puede ser beneficioso para pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal</data>
      <data key="d2">417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12374</data>
      <data key="d7">4fb5d158f5f549fcb7835951d861faf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Proceso biol&#243;gico que puede requerir un aumento en la ingesta nutricional, especialmente en ni&#241;os y adolescentes</data>
      <data key="d2">417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34</data>
      <data key="d3">1084</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12375</data>
      <data key="d7">6d8d5b6777d741b0bbb95eff4082735e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTOM&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">OSTOM&#205;AS are surgical procedures that involve creating an opening, known as a stoma, to allow for the discharge of body wastes. These procedures are often necessary for patients with conditions such as POIC (P&#233;rdida de Oclusi&#243;n Intestinal Cr&#243;nica) to facilitate the drainage of intestinal contents and support long-term enteral nutrition. Ostom&#237;as can significantly impact a patient's nutritional status and may require careful evaluation, sometimes involving contrast administration. While these surgical openings serve essential functions for waste elimination and feeding, they can also lead to complications that need to be managed. Overall, ostom&#237;as are critical interventions that provide necessary support for individuals with specific medical needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada,3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">12376</data>
      <data key="d7">6ffcf2c2f29d4465b812f18dbc6a9798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME SUBOCLUSIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sindrome suboclusivo is a condition that may be managed with NPT and digestive aspiration to avoid surgery.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d3">1077</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12377</data>
      <data key="d7">5f8fa204b15c4fc79dbd8d7e844704e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACTOBACILLI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactobacilli are a type of probiotic bacteria that can have beneficial effects on gut health.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d3">1024</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12378</data>
      <data key="d7">e71698336da549308ba8d081b5b530ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VSL-3">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VSL-3 is a specific probiotic formulation that contains a mixture of eight different bacterial strains. It is recognized for its effectiveness in managing gastrointestinal health, particularly in conditions such as ulcerative colitis.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472,b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a</data>
      <data key="d3">327</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12379</data>
      <data key="d7">0f132bcd70984aaf9684d14f308e6ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTICOESTEROIDES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Corticosteroids are anti-inflammatory medications often used in the treatment of IBD to reduce inflammation and manage symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12380</data>
      <data key="d7">2ed3b19b811e49a7b46a373c64e1f9bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECCIONES POSTOPERATORIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Postoperative infections are complications that can arise after surgery, which may be influenced by nutritional status and treatment methods.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12381</data>
      <data key="d7">822e7a2964964329919d2ee8487d72e6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DA&#209;O DEL CONDUCTO LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Lymphatic duct damage can occur during medical procedures and may complicate nutritional treatments like NPT.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12382</data>
      <data key="d7">c512ad70fb8043c898fae1dbccad975c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFICIT DE COBRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Copper deficiency is a potential complication of long-term nutritional treatments that require monitoring of micronutrient levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12383</data>
      <data key="d7">2d06068dd27c4390902170b9ec9c885f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENCEFALOPAT&#205;A DE WERNICKE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wernicke's encephalopathy is a neurological condition caused by thiamine deficiency, which can be a risk in patients receiving certain nutritional therapies.</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12384</data>
      <data key="d7">d7825c9250fe436c9efff4ab6f8b0506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BERI-BERI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Beri-beri is a disease caused by thiamine deficiency, which can occur in patients with inadequate nutritional support.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">379909adba66c6e316f560669cd30472</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12385</data>
      <data key="d7">e8d55fb5b91c45c0ae5c8c1b582dd036</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYMBIOTICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Symbiotics are combinations of probiotics and prebiotics that may enhance the health benefits of both.</data>
      <data key="d2">b6057c29c69893d65ebeb35c05eb845a</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12386</data>
      <data key="d7">9ec5da26b58f403db8cd0ffab11991e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES INFLAMATORIAS INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedades Inflamatorias Intestinales son condiciones que afectan el tubo digestivo, requiriendo atenci&#243;n m&#233;dica y nutricional especial. Estas enfermedades pueden provocar desnutrici&#243;n y d&#233;ficits de micronutrientes, lo que subraya la importancia de un manejo adecuado y un enfoque integral en su tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">b4580c82418cd4df97f400e183702858,df0e6695be23c07606ca5b9accc62df2</data>
      <data key="d3">1006</data>
