      <data key="d6">12470</data>
      <data key="d7">5b17427506d249c5b015833f8f862dc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULA ENTERO-CUT&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Una f&#237;stula entero-cut&#225;nea (FEC) es un tipo espec&#237;fico de f&#237;stula que conecta el tracto gastrointestinal intraabdominal con el exterior del cuerpo, a menudo resultando de condiciones m&#233;dicas severas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d3">602</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12471</data>
      <data key="d7">de34b2f130f9428688c592fc209ee3df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POIC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pseudoobstrucci&#243;n intestinal cr&#243;nica (POIC) is a rare and severe disorder that simulates intestinal obstruction without a fixed anatomical cause. It is characterized by chronic symptoms such as abdominal pain and vomiting, which can lead to significant issues with intestinal motility. Due to its nonspecific symptoms, POIC often results in a long diagnostic delay, necessitating a high level of suspicion and the exclusion of mechanical obstruction for accurate diagnosis. The condition can severely impact patients' nutritional status, often requiring nutritional support and specific management strategies. Additionally, POIC is sometimes associated with Short Bowel Syndrome, highlighting the need for education and tailored nutritional care for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066,4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379,e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d3">652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">12472</data>
      <data key="d7">f29866e5fe2847cb9f764d5779d529ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE HIRSCHSPRUNG">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad de Hirschsprung es una condici&#243;n cong&#233;nita que afecta la motilidad intestinal, ocurriendo en aproximadamente uno de cada 6000 nacidos y puede llevar a complicaciones severas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d3">652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12473</data>
      <data key="d7">f8d027c809064b5a9ab3c09212309410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VIRUS NEUROTROPOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los virus neurotropos, como el herpesvirus y el virus JC, han sido implicados en la etiolog&#237;a de la pseudoobstrucci&#243;n intestinal cr&#243;nica, afectando el sistema nervioso y la funci&#243;n intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d3">652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12474</data>
      <data key="d7">ea0ed7d6fc95495c8c469edfd9402693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES GRANULOMATOSAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las enfermedades granulomatosas, como la tuberculosis, pueden causar f&#237;stulas intestinales, complicando el manejo cl&#237;nico del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12475</data>
      <data key="d7">ffaeca2fcfd34db59d6b0804ff67378f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROPAT&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las neuropat&#237;as son condiciones que pueden causar problemas en la motilidad intestinal, contribuyendo a la pseudoobstrucci&#243;n intestinal cr&#243;nica en algunos pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12476</data>
      <data key="d7">791c06ef884a4af8994a334337e701ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASTORNOS ESPEC&#205;FICOS DE LA POIC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los trastornos espec&#237;ficos de la POIC incluyen complicaciones como deshidrataci&#243;n y alteraciones electrol&#237;ticas, que son relevantes para el manejo de esta condici&#243;n.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12477</data>
      <data key="d7">0e80f05835d844c2a3888f672ae9c3fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="V&#193;LVULA ILEOCECAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La v&#225;lvula ileocecal regula el paso de contenido al colon y act&#250;a como barrera entre el colon y el intestino delgado.</data>
      <data key="d2">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9</data>
      <data key="d3">1004</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12478</data>
      <data key="d7">77d3510098fc4d9b8129aa12a12a852d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTENSIVE NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intensive nutritional support is a treatment approach for patients with intestinal failure to maintain nutritional status and prevent malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12479</data>
      <data key="d7">ef5d20e90abb41b9bbb6f19bd9597e41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADAPTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adaptation is a biological process where the remaining intestine adjusts to take over the functions of the lost intestine, enhancing nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d3">654</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12480</data>
      <data key="d7">a193cf502e714a49beb6651a7f60c4f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHILDREN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Children are individuals in the developmental stage from birth to adolescence, characterized by their unique nutritional needs and vulnerability to malnutrition and growth issues. During this early stage of life, children may require specialized nutritional support and solutions to ensure their health and proper development. Additionally, children possess a greater capacity for intestinal adaptation, particularly following extensive resections of the intestine, which highlights their resilience and adaptability during this critical period of growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368,4c07b8e0a5058216ff9f2f748bde2ada,abd9a4b801dbdaca1708f0e22331a829,bb7584256e051f1c3d8cb13502ade155</data>
      <data key="d3">795</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">12481</data>
      <data key="d7">d4a08cce6c5b45fda96c36a4aae2a457</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIGESTIVE SECRETIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Digestive secretions are fluids produced by the digestive system that aid in the breakdown and absorption of nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d3">1260</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12482</data>
      <data key="d7">7e2a2ba27106419fb8475aa22f498342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANATOMY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anatomy refers to the structure of the body and its parts, playing a vital role in various medical contexts. It is essential for understanding the implications of intestinal loss in patients with Short Bowel Syndrome (SIC), as well as for determining the most suitable sites for venous access. This knowledge of anatomical structures is crucial for effective medical interventions and patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826,4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d3">763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12483</data>
      <data key="d7">a5f6d4c9426d4da39025a4e9411afd8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUIDS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d3">1260</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12484</data>
      <data key="d7">54ed36b2c5904657999d4f47d73a9e7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CINE-RM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cine-RM is an emerging technique for diagnosing intestinal pathologies, particularly useful in the context of POIC.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066</data>
      <data key="d3">652</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12485</data>
      <data key="d7">618753b6ec4e40058f1aecb68012aea1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FALLO INTESTINAL AGUDO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fallo intestinal agudo is a critical condition requiring investigation of underlying causes such as electrolyte imbalances, pancreatitis, or sepsis.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12486</data>
      <data key="d7">53224602619a46d4abfa3c169afc7e6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TR&#193;NSITO INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tr&#225;nsito intestinal is a diagnostic procedure involving the use of contrast to assess the length of the remaining intestine and its functionality.</data>
      <data key="d2">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12487</data>
      <data key="d7">7e7d04f072cd47eb80b6d313e1d4d831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FEC, which stands for Enterocutaneous Fistula, is a medical condition characterized by an abnormal connection between the gastrointestinal tract and the skin. This condition, also referred to as "fistula entero-cut&#225;nea" or "f&#237;stula enteral cr&#243;nica," necessitates careful nutritional management due to its catabolic nature. Patients with FEC often require nutritional support, which may involve the use of enteral or parenteral nutrition, as the condition can lead to significant challenges in nutrient absorption. Additionally, FEC is associated with chronic intestinal failure, where the intestines are unable to adequately absorb nutrients, further emphasizing the need for medical intervention and comprehensive management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc,c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675,e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d3">656</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">22</data>
      <data key="d6">12488</data>
      <data key="d7">3c044d9d996f4a399286bfb111e465c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GATORADE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Gatorade is a commercial sports drink that is often misunderstood as isotonic but is actually hypotonic.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12489</data>
      <data key="d7">fd56f7be7ff343d397d05035d46f620f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUERORAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sueroral is a type of oral rehydration solution that contains sodium and is used for hydration.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12490</data>
      <data key="d7">4657b42c422743e4ae40c7ca67948313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUERORAL HIPOS&#211;DICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sueroral hipos&#243;dico is a low-sodium oral rehydration solution.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12491</data>
      <data key="d7">7b9c612347e4469fa1dddbb7d5cef4cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUIDOS HIPOTONICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hypotonic liquids are solutions that have a lower sodium content and can also increase net digestive losses.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d3">657</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12492</data>
      <data key="d7">dd9b7b89358c42df83f6beacb2362332</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAPSULA DE CLORURO SODICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A capsule containing sodium chloride that may be recommended for patients to take with isotonic liquids to avoid complete restriction of hypotonic liquids.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12493</data>
      <data key="d7">c6ff32765b234dfc9bc5b9dde4a43a8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA BAJA EN LACTOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A low-lactose diet is recommended for patients to optimize intestinal motility and reduce the risk of bacterial overgrowth.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d3">657</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12494</data>
      <data key="d7">bed9deb5a90d4c288ba220f592f1fd07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUIDOS HIPERTONICOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d3">657</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12495</data>
      <data key="d7">56eb99fa0d3c479f8c8f6c67da527e36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUIDOS ISOTONICOS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12496</data>
      <data key="d7">ee9ded609c1b45cfb5971b5ceeab9c27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES CON FALLA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients suffering from intestinal failure, either acute or chronic, who require nutritional support to manage their condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">72</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">12497</data>
      <data key="d7">1787c7177e734d0b81777411a375fdfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N HYPERF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A dietary approach that involves providing a high-calorie intake to patients with reduced absorptive capacity.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">72</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12498</data>
      <data key="d7">c5857badef284ff3873af5df23768d9c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N POLIM&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A type of enteral nutrition formula that contains intact macronutrients, used for patients with some digestive capacity.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">72</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12499</data>
      <data key="d7">9176ad9105634aa6af052fa132d02e64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETA ELEMENTAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A specialized diet consisting of easily digestible nutrients, often used for patients with severe malabsorption issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">72</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12500</data>
      <data key="d7">b2b97a495acb4d82b2b1688a75d46948</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d3">1103</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12501</data>
      <data key="d7">d2a957eaf97e42e3b60fbce72e9b6106</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAT&#201;TER TUNELIZADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un cat&#233;ter tunelizado es un dispositivo m&#233;dico utilizado para el acceso venoso a largo plazo, recomendado para pacientes que requieren nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12502</data>
      <data key="d7">df22879fbdff4795924d427d3479c87a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISPOSITIVO IMPLANTABLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Un dispositivo implantable es un tipo de cat&#233;ter que se coloca quir&#250;rgicamente bajo la piel para el acceso venoso, utilizado en pacientes con necesidades de nutrici&#243;n a largo plazo.</data>
      <data key="d2">c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12503</data>
      <data key="d7">c8e0ce2f54284a6c97a801c5a966163a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DANIEL DRUCKER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Daniel Drucker is a scientist who isolated, cloned, and characterized the glucagon-like peptide type 2 (GLP-2) in 1997.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d3">655</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12504</data>
      <data key="d7">49647fb3553a496692d62a04aac3eca5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEDUGLUTIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Teduglutida is a pharmacological analog of GLP-2 used for treating short bowel syndrome (SIC) in patients aged 1 year or older.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d3">655</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">12505</data>
      <data key="d7">a94d0c7128c14b20921cc03edf2e7b72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OCTREOTIDO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Octreotide is a medication recommended for short-term use in patients with terminal jejunostomy and high output.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d3">655</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12506</data>
      <data key="d7">2fcf904cd4d648c9a57bfa8426900fd1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADENOMAS DE COLON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Colon adenomas are benign tumors that can develop in the colon, which may increase in number and size with certain treatments.</data>
      <data key="d2">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d3">655</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12507</data>
      <data key="d7">2129c71597524f428b99fb63238f0e54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El trasplante intestinal es un procedimiento quir&#250;rgico que se ha establecido como una opci&#243;n de tratamiento para pacientes que sufren de fallo intestinal cr&#243;nico. Este procedimiento permite la restauraci&#243;n de la funci&#243;n intestinal, lo que es crucial para la salud y el bienestar de los pacientes. Est&#225; indicado especialmente en aquellos que presentan complicaciones graves relacionadas con la nutrici&#243;n parenteral, as&#237; como en casos de fallo intestinal severo que amenazan la vida.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747,eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12508</data>
      <data key="d7">beb26f5fa6534451b1749e52a9281bad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA ASOCIADA A FALLA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad hep&#225;tica asociada a fallo intestinal (EHAFI) es una complicaci&#243;n que puede surgir en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto, manifest&#225;ndose como colestasis o esteatosis hep&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12509</data>
      <data key="d7">5e57e79a20ef4b86998db7526ddff6fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLUIDOS INTRAVENOSOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los fluidos intravenosos son soluciones administradas a trav&#233;s de una vena para tratar la deshidrataci&#243;n y mantener la hidrataci&#243;n en pacientes, especialmente aquellos con condiciones cr&#237;ticas como el s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12510</data>
      <data key="d7">229be51eeccd4d208a792060149d61b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROMBOSIS VENOSA CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La trombosis venosa central es una complicaci&#243;n que puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici&#243;n parenteral, afectando su tratamiento y salud general.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747</data>
      <data key="d3">588</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12511</data>
      <data key="d7">c1a36782408c49298505e247ecb8f9b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESHIDRATACI&#211;N SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La deshidrataci&#243;n severa es una condici&#243;n que puede presentarse en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto, a pesar de la administraci&#243;n de fluidos intravenosos y nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12512</data>
      <data key="d7">0a7124bfc3114583a3946198b6ff6e63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO ULTRACORTO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El s&#237;ndrome de intestino ultracorto es una condici&#243;n cr&#237;tica que puede llevar a la necesidad de trasplante intestinal en pacientes con fallo intestinal cr&#243;nico.</data>
      <data key="d2">ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747</data>
      <data key="d3">600</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12513</data>
      <data key="d7">e8408bd50f214e35878a1cef25652aad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EHAFI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EHAFI refers to a condition that requires specific prophylactic measures to be applied in patients, particularly in the context of nutritional support and lipid administration.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12514</data>
      <data key="d7">7bf541d4cf69463ba0e5957a4a7ca623</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAPTOMICINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Daptomicina is an antibiotic that is effective against biofilms formed on central venous catheters and is used in the treatment of infections related to these catheters.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12515</data>
      <data key="d7">f1e519565b0a45c9854ff783a728442d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NPD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NPD, which stands for Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral Domiciliaria, refers to a type of nutritional support provided at home, specifically regulated under the Spanish healthcare system. This method of nutritional support is particularly utilized for patients with intestinal failure, employing Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) to meet their dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1929</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">12516</data>
      <data key="d7">67e7298f2f6a499c8b0d51778b814386</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACIDOSIS D-L&#193;CTICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidosis D-l&#225;ctica is a significant complication in patients with SIC, resulting from the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates by Lactobacillus.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12517</data>
      <data key="d7">ced6d701c9a04f4ba0482983e582abe0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAT&#201;TER VENOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "CAT&#201;TER VENOSO CENTRAL" is a medical device designed for intravenous access in patients, facilitating the administration of treatments and medications. It is particularly essential for delivering high-osmolarity parenteral nutrition. However, the use of central venous catheters is not without risks, as they can lead to complications such as infections and thrombosis. Overall, while the central venous catheter serves a critical role in patient care, healthcare providers must be vigilant about the potential complications associated with its use.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,538970e30e9d0e758546ca1a3cf5a205,6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee</data>
      <data key="d3">760</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">12518</data>
      <data key="d7">d38190b67fac4532b1f6b5ef6a4ce114</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISTULA ARTERIOVENOSA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An arteriovenous fistula may be beneficial for some patients for the administration of NPD, providing an alternative access route.</data>
      <data key="d2">6b49a9a43dc167f62a772b262afe2bee</data>
      <data key="d3">653</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12519</data>
      <data key="d7">d8381e7ea5e14c2dac922012c79c872f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#205;STULA ARTERIOVENOSA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A surgical procedure used for the administration of NPD3, potentially beneficial for some patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d3">768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12520</data>
      <data key="d7">b7092097010f4dc3a702181ede9cd2d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUSRUTA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">An ancient Indian physician known as the father of medicine, who described treatments for entero-cutaneous fistulas in his work Susrutasamhit.</data>
      <data key="d2">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d3">656</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12521</data>
      <data key="d7">67dd851742a242eda44714f4e7486a9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANTICOAGULANTES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Medications used to treat venous thrombosis, varying in duration based on individual patient needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d3">768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12522</data>
      <data key="d7">9e1750b9a5da49d3976bc5326fa6f0bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLUCI&#211;N SALINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A saline solution recommended for flushing catheters to prevent obstruction and maintain patency.</data>
      <data key="d2">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d3">769</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
