    </node>
    <node id="SUCRALFATO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Sucralfate is a medication primarily used to treat ulcers and is included in the treatment options for patients undergoing FEC (chemotherapy regimen). It is important to administer sucralfate with caution, particularly when used in conjunction with enteral nutrition, as it can lead to complications such as obstruction of feeding tubes. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, sucralfate should be taken with meals. Overall, while sucralfate is effective for ulcer treatment, careful consideration is necessary when integrating it into the care of patients receiving enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,0e014859b304da60c29590e36c9cbc85,e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201,fc664efd4e1c463dc21857e596b68b46</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12527</data>
      <data key="d7">ab5bfac6dde844c38dbf14d59ae92f0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OCTRE&#211;TIDO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A medication used in the management of high-output fistulas, included in the treatment options for patients with FEC.</data>
