    <node id="NRI">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nutrition Risk Index (NRI) is a method utilized to evaluate the nutritional status of patients. It serves as a scoring system that assesses the nutritional risk of individuals primarily based on their albumin levels and weight. This index is instrumental in identifying patients who may be at risk of malnutrition, thereby facilitating timely interventions to improve their nutritional health.</data>
      <data key="d2">58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">794</data>
