      <data key="d6">12597</data>
      <data key="d7">6a16775b0e8240edb9a6f208c8cd261f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MULTIDISCIPLINARY INTEGRATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Multidisciplinary integration involves collaboration among various healthcare professionals, which is essential for the successful implementation of ERAS protocols.</data>
      <data key="d2">fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1242</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12598</data>
      <data key="d7">8c9c2e38491246ea896de6d55fba6824</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POSTOPERATIVE COMPLICATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Postoperative complications refer to adverse effects that can arise following surgical procedures. These complications can be influenced by various factors, including a patient's nutritional status and changes in body composition resulting from cancer treatment. Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols are designed to mitigate these complications by providing improved nutritional support and comprehensive care, thereby promoting better recovery outcomes for patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">0a742cf103e30cf0fadaf6ffabbbde2d,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7,fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">743</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12599</data>
      <data key="d7">00a8554178c644bdb94fe82891ee122f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL STAY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital stay refers to the duration a patient remains in the hospital following surgery. This duration can be influenced by various factors, including the patient's nutritional status and the implementation of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols. Additionally, nutritional support and interventions play a significant role in determining the length of time a patient spends in the hospital.</data>
      <data key="d2">ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29,fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12600</data>
      <data key="d7">eb517804e7fd4b5cb1d83286a8253b97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="READMISSION RATES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Readmission rates refer to the frequency of patients returning to the hospital after discharge, which can be affected by nutritional support and surgical protocols.</data>
      <data key="d2">fab4b91ddb77bd16a93a3808a9c12b4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
