    <node id="SURGERY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Surgery is a medical procedure commonly utilized in the treatment of esophageal cancer. It plays a crucial role in managing the disease, but it also significantly impacts the nutritional status of patients. This impact can lead to complications, particularly in those who are malnourished. Therefore, careful management of nutrition and body composition is essential both before and after the operation to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Studies have highlighted the importance of nutritional support in the postoperative recovery of cancer patients undergoing surgery, emphasizing that such support may be necessary to mitigate potential complications and enhance recovery. Overall, surgery is a vital medical service that requires comprehensive care, including attention to the nutritional needs of patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,758bc764453f49b9097073c5175470cc,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7,f73cc4b49b42b9c9d60bc906430ffe90,fb7b0d121f195e2a472f3d47e28ccff9</data>
      <data key="d3">1229</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">12609</data>
      <data key="d7">1d22e107f06d43b0ad5ec8171f34e78d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AYUNO PREOPERATORIO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AYUNO PREOPERATORIO refers to the practice of fasting prior to surgical procedures, which has been developed and refined over time to minimize the risk of complications during surgery. This preoperative fasting is recommended to ensure patient safety and improve surgical outcomes by preventing issues such as aspiration and other related complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d3">1139</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">12610</data>
      <data key="d7">71e3d24c25d34eb4804c628cdc6ffd12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANESTESIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anesthesia is a medical intervention used during surgery to prevent pain and awareness, influencing preoperative fasting guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d2">2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee</data>
      <data key="d3">1139</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12611</data>
      <data key="d7">6837023e9ece4450aef5fdad2e391bdc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRUG&#205;A GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CIRUG&#205;A GASTROINTESTINAL refers to surgical procedures performed on the gastrointestinal tract. These procedures may necessitate nutritional support both before and after the surgery, ensuring that patients receive the necessary care to aid in their recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,f087e20586f6b263059597e194a04993</data>
      <data key="d3">1134</data>
