    <node id="FRADEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The FRADEA study is a Spanish study that reported on the prevalence of frailty among elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642</data>
      <data key="d3">1766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12679</data>
      <data key="d7">4461078de6904fda93caa30e1eb8555b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GENDER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gender is a demographic factor that influences the prevalence of sarcopenia and frailty, with variations observed between men and women.</data>
      <data key="d2">a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642</data>
      <data key="d3">1020</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12680</data>
      <data key="d7">9d4edd7a5a8348939588128e47373111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATEL ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patel et al. are researchers who evaluated the prevalence of sarcopenia in a cohort study in Hertfordshire.</data>
      <data key="d2">a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12681</data>
      <data key="d7">ca40112773114f07aba5e813bd4540f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LONGITUDINAL ENGLISH STUDY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Longitudinal English Study on aging assessed the prevalence of frailty among older adults in England.</data>
      <data key="d2">a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12682</data>
      <data key="d7">5a027086275b4fc3bbefbbb8b5bd3ce3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASAN&#201;S ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Masan&#233;s et al. conducted research in Spain to establish reference points for diagnosing sarcopenia using bioelectrical impedance analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12683</data>
      <data key="d7">2ee5f82194a14012a116981d8c6ba3ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIAGN&#211;STICO DE SARCOPENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The diagnosis of sarcopenia involves criteria that assess muscle mass and physical function, which have evolved over time.</data>
      <data key="d2">a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12684</data>
      <data key="d7">eea12a2d1987490dbbb123d780e8082d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISIOPATOLOG&#205;A DE LA SARCOPENIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The pathophysiology of sarcopenia includes various factors such as hormonal changes, inflammation, and aging that contribute to muscle loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12685</data>
      <data key="d7">05a1f621ef1744d3a0e2156fd321510d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FACTORES DE ESTILO DE VIDA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12686</data>
      <data key="d7">678f8ca942ce44329cee032ed20a2f7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EWGSOP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The European Working Group on Sarcopenia in Older People (EWGSOP) provides guidelines and criteria for diagnosing sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12687</data>
      <data key="d7">576254cb4f44424e811aa79bc5a9feb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IWG">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Working Group on Sarcopenia (IWG) develops consensus definitions and diagnostic criteria for sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12688</data>
      <data key="d7">3b43a151b2fc4fba82936b1a0801272c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SCWD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Sarcopenia, Cachexia and Wasting Disorders (SCWD) focuses on the study and management of muscle wasting conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12689</data>
      <data key="d7">592bb7c275df401693aedb44f3540f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WALKING SPEED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Walking speed is a functional measure used to assess mobility and physical performance in individuals, often evaluated in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12690</data>
      <data key="d7">96493a11b8c649fa96d60c28862ceedd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCLE MASS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Muscle mass refers to the amount of muscle tissue in the body, which plays a crucial role in overall health and physical function. It can be significantly affected by various factors, including cancer and its treatments, which may lead to a decreased muscle mass and an increased need for nutritional support to help maintain or restore muscle tissue. Additionally, muscle mass can be evaluated using techniques such as Bioelectrical Impedance Analysis (BIA) and Dual-Energy X-ray Absorptiometry (DEXA), which provide insights into an individual's muscle composition and health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">11cbdce47eee11a80ab609f3b786bcc1,76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d3">469</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12691</data>
      <data key="d7">36536c333ce14a78b82840bafef6d81f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KNEE EXTENSION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Knee extension is a physical test used to measure muscle strength in the lower body, relevant in assessing sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">76d78b3e33659e952b0d2835f5bdf595</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12692</data>
      <data key="d7">139668623d4b45df921dc4127404b1d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGE AGEING">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Age Ageing is a journal that publishes research related to aging, including studies on sarcopenia and its implications for older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a</data>
      <data key="d3">1767</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12693</data>
      <data key="d7">1d03ad00e93a4c0da26ef8393d707b4a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FUNCTIONAL STATUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Functional status refers to an individual's ability to perform activities of daily living, which can be affected by sarcopenia and related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12694</data>
      <data key="d7">7b540a0334154d63bef5373696aa3a07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHRONIC OBSTRUCTIVE PULMONARY DISEASE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) is a progressive lung disease characterized by increasing breathlessness and breathing difficulties. It is primarily caused by long-term exposure to irritating gases or particulate matter, most commonly from cigarette smoke, as well as other harmful substances. COPD is often associated with bronchiectasis and can also be related to cystic fibrosis. The condition not only affects respiratory function but can also negatively impact muscle mass and strength, particularly in older adults. Additionally, individuals with COPD may require nutritional support to manage their health effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,4eb41f33f9aba3b8ecd3906de91a1345,6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68,6f500b6f65f41f4fc89abcf53a4e409e,cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
      <data key="d3">1034</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">12695</data>
      <data key="d7">4929af78ed0945d0956663e0c138df6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition that can contribute to muscle weakness and sarcopenia in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d2">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12696</data>
      <data key="d7">34b607c649fc4ab7adf6ba6cf231c3a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISIOPATOL&#211;GIA DE LA FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La fisiopatolog&#237;a de la fragilidad se refiere a los cambios biol&#243;gicos y metab&#243;licos que ocurren en el cuerpo, especialmente en los sistemas inmunol&#243;gico, neuroendocrino y musculoesquel&#233;tico, que contribuyen a la fragilidad en los ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12697</data>
      <data key="d7">71d8b54cefc340b2ba948e58ab049977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FNT-&#913;">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El factor de necrosis tumoral alfa (FNT-&#945;) es una citoquina involucrada en la inflamaci&#243;n y se ha asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12698</data>
      <data key="d7">4fbf72e8e6b94ebfaea3822ce31b59b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMA NEUROENDOCRINO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El sistema neuroendocrino es un sistema que regula las hormonas en el cuerpo y se ha relacionado con la aparici&#243;n de fragilidad en el envejecimiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000</data>
      <data key="d3">1762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12699</data>
      <data key="d7">f663ea4d74644312ad9fea49609890c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMA MUSCULOESQUEL&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El sistema musculoesquel&#233;tico incluye m&#250;sculos y huesos, y su deterioro est&#225; asociado con la fragilidad y la sarcopenia en los ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12700</data>
      <data key="d7">2727c4c4ae674c00b99853471c9ba1c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FISICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#237;sica is a field of study that encompasses the principles of matter and energy, often related to health and physical conditions such as sarcopenia and frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12701</data>
      <data key="d7">61d4278e2cdc43cfaa5e25da80bd3cc0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CES-D">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Center for Epidemiologic Studies Depression Scale (CES-D) is a screening tool used to identify depressive symptoms in the general population.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12702</data>
      <data key="d7">f348ef29549b4b91b994600d2c1fb0eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PATOLOGIAS ESPECIFICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Patolog&#237;as espec&#237;ficas refers to specific health conditions that may be diagnosed based on certain criteria, including frailty.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12703</data>
      <data key="d7">8e21bd0c769a47dc84089af7858a0774</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERVENCION NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intervenci&#243;n nutricional refers to dietary interventions aimed at improving nutritional status, particularly in the elderly to combat frailty and sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d3">762</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12704</data>
      <data key="d7">8c23a91089134325b119c4d66d4666db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EJERCICIO FISICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ejercicio f&#237;sico refers to physical exercise, which is an important component in the management and prevention of frailty and sarcopenia.</data>
      <data key="d2">56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d3">1768</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12705</data>
      <data key="d7">e1357930f7b44dcbbb5771ba6f4b5673</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCULO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">M&#250;sculo refers to muscle tissue, which has a maximum storage limit for creatine. This tissue is influenced by supplementation, indicating that the amount of creatine that can be stored in muscle is finite and can be enhanced through dietary or supplemental means.</data>
      <data key="d2">06a75d9ed2fc1cdca5b08759d3df04d4,56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12706</data>
      <data key="d7">d046392cac13473188436ba4fa4f54da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAIL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Frail is a set of criteria used to evaluate the fragility of elderly individuals, focusing on their physical capabilities and health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49</data>
      <data key="d3">1764</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12707</data>
      <data key="d7">d95ddd4f1eb44fada50db8042cf543ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRE-FRAGILITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pre-fragility refers to a state where individuals meet 1-2 criteria indicating they are at risk of becoming frail, highlighting the need for intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49</data>
      <data key="d3">1132</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12708</data>
      <data key="d7">86d06853f96c435b92d5a8b11a0f41fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRAGILITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fragility is a condition characterized by the presence of 3 or more criteria indicating a significant decline in physical health and increased dependency.</data>
      <data key="d2">5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49</data>
      <data key="d3">1132</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12709</data>
      <data key="d7">aebb2a12518142fab5eea5ff282dac09</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRUPO DE EXPERTOS DE ESPEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El Grupo de Expertos de ESPEN es un grupo que proporciona directrices sobre la nutrici&#243;n en pacientes, incluyendo ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d2">78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12710</data>
      <data key="d7">204e5abf0d3a4ccc9f203ea82716212d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSCULATURA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">MUSCULATURA refers to the muscle mass of the body, which is influenced by protein intake and physical activity. Muscle mass and strength are essential for maintaining physical independence, particularly in the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e,78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59</data>
      <data key="d3">1745</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">12711</data>
      <data key="d7">df09660b870943f1a0977b8b78fc828a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FRUCTOOLIGOSAC&#193;RIDOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fructooligosaccharides are prebiotic fibers that promote the growth of beneficial gut bacteria and have been shown to improve muscle strength in frail elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090</data>
      <data key="d3">1763</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12712</data>
      <data key="d7">b49ca29a199f467a8c4007c246ba6171</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENSAYO CL&#205;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ENSAYO CL&#205;NICO," or clinical trial, is a type of experimental study designed to evaluate the effects of specific interventions on health outcomes. These interventions can include medical treatments, dietary patterns, and supplements, particularly in populations such as the elderly. Clinical trials involve the assignment and control of a study factor to assess its impact on health, thereby contributing valuable data to the field of medical research.</data>
      <data key="d2">15bf355c0b0b669417d28ad0aad190c2,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,dabdb883b39fe459da7aab4a4e7242cb</data>
      <data key="d3">347</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12713</data>
      <data key="d7">2503a0f918544544ae57455d21754d72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEHIDROEPIANDROSTERONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dehidroepiandrosterona is a hormone studied for its effects on muscle mass and strength in postmenopausal women and men with low testosterone levels.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12714</data>
      <data key="d7">c7e1b3f0ae074d65aa30129da330701a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIBOLONA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tibolone is a hormonal compound that has shown potential benefits in increasing grip strength and lean mass in postmenopausal women.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12715</data>
      <data key="d7">096d462f214045da8030b4e842b12680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTARINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ostarine is a selective androgen receptor modulator that has shown proven effects on muscle in animal models.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12716</data>
      <data key="d7">8341753708de45f78671a4050520562e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODULADORES SINT&#201;TICOS DE ANDR&#211;GENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Synthetic androgen modulators are drugs being researched for their potential benefits in treating muscle-related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12717</data>
      <data key="d7">5ebbb6b69c204adc9845b11d4bd18c2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INHIBIDORES DE LA ENZIMA CONVERTIDORA DE ANGIOTENSINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ACE inhibitors are being studied for their effects on functional capacity and muscle strength.</data>
      <data key="d2">3f21321c62f3e5ee31c822e90ca6b89e</data>
      <data key="d3">1745</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12718</data>
