    <node id="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN CRITICAL PATIENTS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutritional support in critical patients is a medical approach discussed in recent years, focusing on the nutritional needs of critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1231</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12866</data>
      <data key="d7">e0b0ca7df81942819b508a803c16db97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIDADES DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Unidades de Cuidados Intensivos (ICUs) are specialized hospital departments designed to provide intensive care and monitoring for critically ill patients. Within these healthcare settings, catheter-related infections pose a significant concern, highlighting the critical nature of infection control in the management of patients in ICUs.</data>
      <data key="d2">afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc,fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d3">766</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12867</data>
      <data key="d7">14d5498ac958465eab666602ad81326f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DESNUTRICI&#211;N CAL&#211;RICO-PROTEICA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">afdd80af18df0213292a5858afeae9cc</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12868</data>
      <data key="d7">7126658a73b947b495cf7f6d508e6a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NUTRIC SCORE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The NUTRIC SCORE is a comprehensive scoring system designed to assess the nutritional risk of critically ill patients, particularly in critical care settings. It serves as a valuable tool for quantifying the risk of these patients developing adverse events and helps identify individuals who would benefit from optimized nutritional support. The NUTRIC Score utilizes an online calculator to evaluate various health parameters, providing a scoring system that indicates the risk of poor clinical outcomes. Additionally, it assesses the need for aggressive nutritional intervention, ensuring that healthcare providers can make informed decisions regarding nutritional care for critically ill patients. Overall, the NUTRIC SCORE is essential for improving patient outcomes through targeted nutritional assessment and intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c,723cbca2d5cfbf8cf05a923c52569641,7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3,b1b42f264a7bfe8d5c9b931ef8b29b02,c07baf818737d704c290ca0f5eefd30f,d92f4ecdee41ca35485c997a95642c5b,fb0c6cd346ca91e15f8ff1cc07570d9d</data>
      <data key="d3">687</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">12869</data>
      <data key="d7">ba224aea2e13466f9a4f213ce97fccec</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONAS CONTRARREGULADORAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Counter-regulatory hormones are involved in the metabolic response to stress in critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12870</data>
      <data key="d7">00c5852915bf44b8be963885f2c7dbfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUC&#211;GENOLISIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Glycogenolysis is the process of breaking down glycogen to glucose, which is increased in critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12871</data>
      <data key="d7">6c0e09bca13d46f78527db76d4016fae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISFUNCI&#211;N MULTIORG&#193;NICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Multi-organ dysfunction is a serious condition that can occur in critically ill patients, leading to increased mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12872</data>
      <data key="d7">1f5b6b2043a7483e8cd175d4efe12807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TIEMPO DE HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Length of hospitalization is often prolonged in critically ill patients due to complications and recovery needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12873</data>
      <data key="d7">05625dd3477049e28979254852d8101c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DA&#209;O OXIDATIVO CELULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cellular oxidative damage can occur in critically ill patients and is a factor in their overall health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1101</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12874</data>
      <data key="d7">ecfd0aa1e2434bdb9ccf7b03eb8ae299</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N NUTRICIONAL COMPLETA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A complete nutritional assessment is essential for critically ill patients to determine their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1095</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12875</data>
      <data key="d7">60c1c32e52074b3c9a152899725b9712</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EVALUACI&#211;N DE LA FUNCI&#211;N MUSCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Assessment of muscle function is important for understanding the health status of critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">25192e60a2c23bd74095f4602efeac4c</data>
      <data key="d3">1095</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12876</data>
      <data key="d7">46be572c464c4a9693573553877c8e8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANADIAN SOCIETY FOR CLINICAL NUTRITION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Canadian Society for Clinical Nutrition (CSCN) offers guidelines regarding nutritional practices and recommendations for critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">d92f4ecdee41ca35485c997a95642c5b</data>
      <data key="d3">687</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12877</data>
      <data key="d7">7c657959c0064ecc916e254c9c33fcd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRITICAL CARE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Critical Care is both a medical specialty and a journal dedicated to the management and treatment of critically ill patients. As a medical specialty, Critical Care focuses on the diagnosis and management of life-threatening conditions, which may include situations that require parenteral nutrition. The term also encompasses the specialized care provided to patients facing such severe health challenges, often necessitating intensive monitoring and treatment. The journal serves as a platform for publishing research that advances the understanding and practices related to the care of these critically ill individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">384e13475cc83e77e160fd6be9a88e73,64378df2be6b08b39bd652c0a2d3789c,d92f4ecdee41ca35485c997a95642c5b</data>
      <data key="d3">1722</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12878</data>
      <data key="d7">fc91ece751ab44a6a3409bbb6dbd6aa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTE CR&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The entity "PACIENTE CR&#205;TICO" refers to a critically ill patient who is in a life-threatening condition and requires intensive medical care and close monitoring. Such patients often need specialized nutritional support, which may include parenteral nutrition. Additionally, they can benefit from immunomodulatory formulas to aid in their recovery. Overall, a paciente cr&#237;tico is characterized by their severe health status, necessitating comprehensive medical attention and tailored nutritional interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088,195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,2bd5549759c6a0d8393bb93fdccb747b,428ea9c156fe3f0571b20d5d81648868,d92f4ecdee41ca35485c997a95642c5b</data>
      <data key="d3">643</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">15</data>
      <data key="d6">12879</data>
      <data key="d7">6ad9898fc8a347e0abbe82248dde290b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CSCN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CSCN, or the Canadian Society for Clinical Nutrition, is a Canadian organization dedicated to providing clinical guidelines for nutrition in critically ill patients. The society emphasizes the importance of enteral nutrition over parenteral nutrition for this patient population, advocating for practices that enhance patient care and recovery through appropriate nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4,c07baf818737d704c290ca0f5eefd30f</data>
      <data key="d3">684</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12880</data>
      <data key="d7">c10d118289e44da38b00a1eec8d57ff2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GASTO CAL&#211;RICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Caloric expenditure refers to the total number of calories burned by a patient, which is crucial for determining nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">195affa22ecd2f7b1cdce3d72fc1cba4</data>
      <data key="d3">643</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12881</data>
      <data key="d7">3edfee7f5e304948bdcbb8be6089243e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHOBAN P">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Choban P is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.</data>
      <data key="d2">7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3</data>
      <data key="d3">1839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12882</data>
      <data key="d7">452f693ab8444281891f36f9eec51c1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DICKERSON R">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dickerson R is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.</data>
