      <data key="d7">9f6f718274d34d0bba7e5b6d7b775be2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WORTHINGTON P">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Worthington P is one of the authors of the ASPEN Clinical Guidelines for nutrition support.</data>
      <data key="d2">7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3</data>
      <data key="d3">1839</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12885</data>
      <data key="d7">6b8129cce8574232955d565ed4619b21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMODYNAMIC STABILITY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hemodynamic stability refers to the stable condition of a patient's blood circulation, which is crucial before initiating nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12886</data>
      <data key="d7">53fe864fa47e4c80b7b043261df810cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROCIRCULATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microcirculation involves the flow of blood through the smallest blood vessels, which can be compromised in critically ill patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12887</data>
      <data key="d7">8293b518921f418391107ff6b7486553</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDA PRE- O POSTPIL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sonda pre- o postpil&#243;rica refers to feeding tubes placed before or after the pylorus in the stomach, used in critical care settings.</data>
      <data key="d2">7295ffd1826d8ea12cf9f832ba6f80b3</data>
      <data key="d3">1257</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12888</data>
      <data key="d7">6e3b28adf4664074b424f9cac5733f4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">"PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS" refers to individuals in severe medical conditions who require intensive medical care and specialized nutritional interventions. These patients often face complications such as intestinal microcirculation damage and may experience conditions like hypoalbuminemia due to dilution. As a result, they necessitate careful evaluation of their nutritional status and may require parenteral nutrition to support their health. Overall, "PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS" are characterized by their need for close monitoring and tailored medical attention to address their compromised health.</data>
      <data key="d2">01704aec4089b2f0f24dd0f0841b5ecf,4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54,4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,9562f39f9e78644164daeff3177a2f84,9e4c5851293c18ef6b304ff6293b0be5,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855,c70d301baddcdcdefbba9b024ad4f3c5,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5</data>
      <data key="d3">640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">41</data>
      <data key="d6">12889</data>
      <data key="d7">257d38ba44064332a400d59dae0a785f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#193;RMACOS VASOPRESORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los f&#225;rmacos vasopresores son medicamentos utilizados para aumentar la presi&#243;n arterial en pacientes hipotensos, y su uso debe ser monitoreado durante la nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12890</data>
      <data key="d7">8098d442c3f94775afcbd178b2a10432</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA DE LA MUCOSA G&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La atrofia de la mucosa g&#225;strica es una condici&#243;n que puede prevenirse mediante la administraci&#243;n adecuada de nutrici&#243;n enteral en pacientes cr&#237;ticos.</data>
      <data key="d2">4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12891</data>
      <data key="d7">eddd13b9b6274a1d8c06ca3b70d25606</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIGNOS DE ISQUEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los signos de isquemia incluyen distensi&#243;n abdominal, cantidad de residuo g&#225;strico y presencia de acidosis metab&#243;lica, que deben ser vigilados en pacientes que reciben nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12892</data>
      <data key="d7">ee41d8ca35624b2ba08a39644cda95d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROCIRCULACI&#211;N INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12893</data>
      <data key="d7">b2a3c7cbdc7f49fd83e1b988a7b144a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEPSIS SEVERA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SEPSIS SEVERA is a severe condition characterized by a life-threatening response to infection, which leads to injury of the body's own tissues and organs. This condition was included as part of the study criteria for patients who were receiving various nutritional support methods. The severity of sepsis underscores its critical nature in clinical settings, highlighting the importance of effective management and intervention strategies.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996,9e4c5851293c18ef6b304ff6293b0be5</data>
      <data key="d3">640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12894</data>
      <data key="d7">4ee571e3094847e2b9a349ec191a9cf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#211;RMULA DE NE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Formula de NE refers to the specific nutritional formulas used in enteral nutrition for patients, tailored to their medical needs.</data>
      <data key="d2">4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996</data>
      <data key="d3">640</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12895</data>
      <data key="d7">f55149fde7264190875669953944767f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANADIAN GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Canadian guidelines provide recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, particularly regarding the use of specific formulas and supplements in patients with sepsis and other critical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12896</data>
      <data key="d7">f19ba47e12844591acf9386971e33b29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRITICAL PATIENT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">A critical patient is an individual who is in a life-threatening condition that necessitates intensive medical care and monitoring. These patients often require specialized nutritional support as part of their treatment. The care provided to critical patients is crucial due to the severity of their health status, highlighting the need for comprehensive medical attention.</data>
      <data key="d2">723cbca2d5cfbf8cf05a923c52569641,8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d3">245</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">12897</data>
      <data key="d7">dda726282db541c39815cfa6c72f99b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glutamine (Gln) is another amino acid discussed in the context of nutritional support for critically ill patients, but its supplementation is not recommended due to lack of demonstrated benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12898</data>
      <data key="d7">bca3349fe221417ea21018cd36b0a4a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIBER ENRICHED FORMULAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fiber enriched formulas are nutritional preparations that include fiber to aid in digestion and nutrient absorption, but their routine use is not recommended in critical patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d3">1214</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
