    </node>
    <node id="NUTRITION SUPPORT THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nutrition Support Therapy refers to the clinical practice of providing nutritional support to critically ill patients. It encompasses the methods and practices used to deliver nutritional support to patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through oral intake. This therapy is essential for ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition during their recovery process, particularly when they are unable to consume food normally.</data>
      <data key="d2">21e6d7085f520d8a2f415746dc7eab71,d26aec24f3f8c930c1c4b1d464bacd6b</data>
      <data key="d3">1839</data>
