      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">12947</data>
      <data key="d7">174c6c67011643c58f092369da428d5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSIDAD DE M&#193;LAGA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Universidad de M&#225;laga is an educational institution where Casilda Olveira Fuster is affiliated.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d3">341</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12948</data>
      <data key="d7">c841bf86537a4e8c97c16c7e3913219e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRONQUIECTASIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bronchiectasis, or bronquiectasias, is a medical condition characterized by the abnormal and permanent dilation of the bronchi. This dilation leads to a buildup of mucus, which significantly increases the risk of chronic respiratory infections and other complications. The condition often arises from infections or other lung diseases, and it is associated with chronic inflammation of the airways. As a result, individuals with bronchiectasis may experience not only respiratory issues but also nutritional deficiencies due to the impact on overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6,bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977</data>
      <data key="d3">1037</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">12949</data>
      <data key="d7">ff5ea85c4ab24510bbacaa725e6b0c07</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UGC DE ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UGC de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n is a clinical unit specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at the Hospital Regional Universitario de M&#225;laga.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d3">341</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12950</data>
      <data key="d7">e6a0d39d68b8483aaec31db9133cdb27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UGC DE NEUMOLOG&#205;A Y CIRUG&#205;A TOR&#193;CICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">UGC de Neumolog&#237;a y Cirug&#237;a Tor&#225;cica is a clinical unit specializing in pulmonology and thoracic surgery at the Hospital Regional Universitario de M&#225;laga.</data>
      <data key="d2">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d3">341</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12951</data>
      <data key="d7">43ba240e72c84d3bba94454175c10f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RTFQ">
      <data key="d0">GENE</data>
      <data key="d1">RTFQ refers to a gene that codes for a protein functioning as a chloride channel. This protein plays a crucial role in maintaining the balance of salt and water in various tissues, particularly in the respiratory and digestive systems. Mutations in the RTFQ gene can lead to significant health issues, notably in individuals with cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder that severely impacts lung function and digestive health. To address these challenges, specific medications are being developed to restore the function of the RTFQ protein, offering hope for improved health outcomes for patients affected by cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">12952</data>
      <data key="d7">6db24fe6a6d043e4a0d67d891d2c577f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPOC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">EPOC, or Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), is a progressive lung disease characterized by obstructive ventilatory disorders that lead to increasing breathlessness and significant difficulties in breathing. This condition is often linked to long-term exposure to irritating gases or particulate matter, particularly from cigarette smoke, as well as various environmental factors. EPOC affects a large portion of the population, especially older adults, and is associated with systemic manifestations that can impact overall health.

Patients with EPOC may experience significant nutritional issues, necessitating dietary evaluations and monitoring of muscle function. The disease can also lead to complications such as the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), which can affect treatment duration. Due to its progressive nature, EPOC requires regular monitoring and treatment to manage symptoms and improve quality of life. Overall, EPOC is a serious condition that poses considerable morbidity and mortality risks, highlighting the importance of awareness and management strategies for those affected.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722,bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf,cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281,ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1037</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">72</data>
      <data key="d6">12953</data>
      <data key="d7">c113b0fb8db64c5897ed59856be35d3b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IBERPOC">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">IBERPOC is a comprehensive study focused on Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) in Spain. It has identified the prevalence of COPD, which affects a significant portion of the adult population. Additionally, the study explores various aspects of the disease, providing valuable insights into its impact on the population.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2,6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1048</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12954</data>
      <data key="d7">39be294c405f4bb7a5dbf90941b32dcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA PANCREATICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pancreatic insufficiency is a condition often associated with certain classes of RTFQ gene mutations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12955</data>
      <data key="d7">b27d6600bfac44e28cc5b724b71a47c0</data>
    </node>
