      <data key="d3">1048</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12956</data>
      <data key="d7">bb62463bff3d4b26a60b4ad168da644b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EPI-SCAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">EPI-SCAN is a study that reported a global prevalence of COPD in Spain, highlighting the impact of the disease on public health.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1048</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12957</data>
      <data key="d7">6965c59faa134e03b80980a729ad3e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEUTA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Ceuta is a city in Spain noted for having one of the highest mortality rates for COPD among women.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12958</data>
      <data key="d7">d95f42c4ddcb4917ab32e44dd5f2a5a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMOLOGIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Neumolog&#237;a refers to the field of medicine that deals with respiratory diseases, including COPD.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12959</data>
      <data key="d7">318225fb8a954737a6071a888b38fd4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUTATION CLASSIFICATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mutation classification refers to the categorization of genetic mutations that can impact diseases like cystic fibrosis, which may relate to respiratory conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12960</data>
      <data key="d7">24d95c6118cf49c5852493b8e5852462</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORBIDIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Morbidity refers to the incidence of disease, which is notably high for COPD in Spain, causing significant health concerns.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12961</data>
      <data key="d7">9a87ed00e86c4e11a551fde61878963c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDUCACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Education level is identified as a significant risk factor for the prevalence of COPD, impacting diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12962</data>
      <data key="d7">597c83590619438d9acac0b884ef414b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TABACCO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d3">1053</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">12963</data>
      <data key="d7">a99daaf1a2874b47b8dafde22e4b3442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEV1">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">FEV1, or Volumen Espiratorio Forzado en el primer segundo, is a critical measure utilized to evaluate lung function in patients diagnosed with EPOC (Enfermedad Pulmonar Obstructiva Cr&#243;nica). This metric assesses the volume of air that can be forcibly exhaled in the first second of a breath, providing essential insights into the respiratory health of individuals suffering from this chronic condition.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d3">1040</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12964</data>
      <data key="d7">eb9a09b90bfc4a7b82f409ecbcbbd3f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACTIVIDAD F&#205;SICA HABITUAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La actividad f&#237;sica habitual es un factor que puede influir en la calidad de vida y el pron&#243;stico de los pacientes con EPOC.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12965</data>
      <data key="d7">8e6d38c0c89b4641b687e00972f9b5b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISNEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La disnea es un s&#237;ntoma com&#250;n en pacientes con EPOC, caracterizado por la dificultad para respirar.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12966</data>
      <data key="d7">6110d6934e2645dcaaa831a08206ce18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DETERIORO DE LA FUNCI&#211;N PULMONAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El deterioro de la funci&#243;n pulmonar es un indicador clave en la progresi&#243;n de la EPOC y su manejo cl&#237;nico.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12967</data>
      <data key="d7">8dcfedf121524c45ad1cd6853e410981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATRAPAMIENTO A&#201;REO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El atrapamiento a&#233;reo es un fen&#243;meno que ocurre en la EPOC, donde el aire queda atrapado en los pulmones, dificultando la respiraci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12968</data>
      <data key="d7">268562792dc44a2cb4e9d3d3dd8842fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES GASOM&#201;TRICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las alteraciones gasom&#233;tricas son cambios en los niveles de gases en la sangre que pueden ocurrir en pacientes con EPOC.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12969</data>
      <data key="d7">d88599cedd684ae3b7ea9192fac5885f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPERTENSI&#211;N PULMONAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipertensi&#243;n pulmonar es una complicaci&#243;n que puede desarrollarse en pacientes con EPOC, afectando su pron&#243;stico.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12970</data>
      <data key="d7">755982192d1c4a6b8348762ee0860110</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXACERBACIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las exacerbaciones son episodios agudos de empeoramiento de los s&#237;ntomas en pacientes con EPOC, que pueden requerir atenci&#243;n m&#233;dica.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12971</data>
      <data key="d7">0748831c4c3e44aab0705a1a8cccd45e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INGRESOS HOSPITALARIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los ingresos hospitalarios son una medida de la gravedad de la EPOC y su impacto en la salud del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d2">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">12972</data>
      <data key="d7">9ffb499c319e408bb0509f8dc90b3a64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRROSIS BILIAR FOCAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Focal biliary cirrhosis is a liver condition that can develop in patients with cystic fibrosis, characterized by damage to the bile ducts.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1820</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12973</data>
      <data key="d7">6bcd9d90baf849c9ae8d200e734a90f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACIONES DEL METABOLISMO HIDROCARBONADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alterations in carbohydrate metabolism are common in cystic fibrosis patients, leading to complications such as diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12974</data>
      <data key="d7">a2ee51b59ea0422883ff5241379d0a2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FQ">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis is a common complication that increases with age among affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">12975</data>
      <data key="d7">e5fe731e5edc4f07be90eb61b2522b70</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;LEO MECONIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">&#205;LEO MECONIAL refers to a medical condition known as meconium ileus, which occurs in approximately 5% of patients with cystic fibrosis. This condition is characterized by intestinal obstruction at birth due to the blockage of the intestines by thick meconium. As a result, affected newborns require prompt medical treatment to address the obstruction and manage the associated complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
