    </node>
    <node id="ATROFIA MUSCULAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atrofia muscular, or muscle atrophy, is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass. This phenomenon is particularly prevalent in patients with ELA (Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis) as well as those suffering from chronic respiratory diseases. In these patients, muscle wasting can be attributed to a combination of factors, including nutritional deficiencies and increased energy requirements, which lead to inactivity. The condition highlights the importance of addressing both nutritional needs and physical activity to mitigate the effects of muscle atrophy in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13016</data>
      <data key="d7">34a3ca8a915247b883667a0f9a81dd82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BQ">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">BQ refers to Bronchiectasis, a condition characterized by the abnormal and permanent dilation of the bronchi, leading to chronic respiratory issues. This condition results in the airways of the lungs becoming abnormally widened, which causes a build-up of excess mucus, making the lungs more susceptible to infections. Additionally, Bronchiectasis, also known as Bronquiectasias, requires assessments of dietary and muscle function, highlighting its impact on overall health. The condition has been associated with respiratory rehabilitation, which can lead to improvements in exercise capacity and quality of life. Furthermore, the abnormal widening of the bronchi can also affect nutrition, indicating the multifaceted nature of this respiratory disorder.</data>
      <data key="d2">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c,f1f6ad756644e84b6caa8e4e3adb94da,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">14</data>
      <data key="d6">13017</data>
      <data key="d7">72aaa5edc5f64525a929a577990d7841</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">VALORACI&#211;N refers to the comprehensive assessment of nutritional intake and status, which is essential for patient care in hospitals. This process includes evaluating a patient's attitude towards enteral nutrition, a critical aspect for their psychological and nutritional management. Additionally, VALORACI&#211;N encompasses the assessment of dietary adherence and nutritional status specifically in patients with chronic diseases, highlighting its importance in managing their overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">4fbc9ba7c1f3ff190b594c75e7eac015,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,d66eff5b0a0e16993c167d3a6ffef395</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13018</data>
      <data key="d7">e0fb776818ab4a76a41b02ecb55aaa2f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DINAMOMETR&#205;A DE MANO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dinamometr&#237;a de mano is a simple and cost-effective method to measure handgrip strength, correlating with muscle mass and nutritional status.</data>
      <data key="d2">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">13019</data>
      <data key="d7">2799a63287a748b48affca79e5b506c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEIN-INDUCED DEFICIT OF VITAMIN K">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">PIDVK is a marker used to assess vitamin K deficiency, particularly in patients with chronic diseases like FQ.</data>
      <data key="d2">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13020</data>
      <data key="d7">24f01ea2bb35438cbdccc808133f3a6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTEOCALCIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Osteocalcin is a protein involved in bone metabolism and can indicate vitamin K status, relevant in chronic disease management.</data>
      <data key="d2">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13021</data>
      <data key="d7">97a9176cb84a48878213918155e9efe9</data>
    </node>
