      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13022</data>
      <data key="d7">76951e7b1486465b934b6a7f28009482</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IPE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">IPE, or Insuficiencia Pancre&#225;tica Exocrina, refers to a medical condition characterized by exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, where the pancreas fails to produce sufficient digestive enzymes. This condition significantly impacts nutrient absorption, particularly in patients with cystic fibrosis, necessitating tailored dietary management and specific nutritional interventions. Additionally, monitoring of vitamin and mineral levels is crucial for individuals with IPE to ensure adequate nutrition and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233,c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1039</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13023</data>
      <data key="d7">7c02e27a3e0d4acb9d25ce51ece5329e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTEINA C REACTIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">C-reactive protein is a marker of inflammation in the body, often measured to assess inflammatory conditions, including in patients with FQ.</data>
      <data key="d2">d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13024</data>
      <data key="d7">4e7444d4ad394ca494677d6cce246ec4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TNF-ALFA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumor necrosis factor-alpha is a cytokine involved in systemic inflammation, which may be relevant in the context of chronic diseases like FQ.</data>
      <data key="d2">d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13025</data>
      <data key="d7">a7071dc9ad4c4a3aaca0e909c1b8f9d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DENSIDAD MINERAL OSEA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone mineral density is a measure of bone strength and is important for assessing osteoporosis risk, particularly in patients with FQ.</data>
      <data key="d2">d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13026</data>
      <data key="d7">4aedaf5dd05c483dae72e30ee321ff30</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Z-SCORE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Z-score is a statistical measurement that serves multiple purposes in different contexts. It is primarily used to evaluate growth in children by comparing an individual's growth metrics to a reference population. Additionally, the Z-score is utilized in the medical field to assess bone density in patients with conditions such as cystic fibrosis (FQ), indicating how a specific value relates to the mean of a group. Overall, the Z-score provides a standardized way to understand how an individual compares to a broader population, whether in terms of growth or health metrics.</data>
      <data key="d2">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d3">1038</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13027</data>
      <data key="d7">6aceeca853b34f3cb08c7e537c34b12e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CYSTIC FIBROSIS FOUNDATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation is a non-profit organization dedicated to advancing research and care for individuals with cystic fibrosis. It focuses on funding research initiatives and providing essential support for those affected by the condition. Additionally, the foundation offers guidelines and recommendations for managing cystic fibrosis, which include dietary needs and supplementation, as well as comprehensive support for treatment and care management. Through its efforts, the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation plays a crucial role in improving the quality of life for individuals living with cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">c2211f0deb7328a77cb632140690da03,c3e74ddf9529482684f4b62e713df49b,cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4,fea8c7e37cd76ac988e0b242cb84fe6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1035</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">13028</data>
      <data key="d7">e5171bb6a19d441b9d85d4268838ef78</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BETACAROTENOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Beta-carotene is a source of Vitamin A that may be safer for supplementation compared to retinol, especially in certain health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233</data>
      <data key="d3">611</data>
