    </node>
    <node id="ADMINISTRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "ADMINISTRACI&#211;N" encompasses the processes involved in providing essential medical care to patients, particularly those with specific health conditions. It includes the administration of pancreatic enzymes, which is vital for managing cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder that affects the lungs and digestive system. Additionally, "ADMINISTRACI&#211;N" refers to the methods of delivering enteral nutrition to patients, which can be done either continuously or intermittently, depending on the individual needs of the patient. This comprehensive approach to administration highlights the importance of tailored medical interventions in improving patient health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">8178ba40e7ef08e569845c1f3f1621cc,c926a8237fba5d5bc497ac2165bbb039</data>
      <data key="d3">1050</data>
