    <node id="SCOTTISH INTERCOLLEGIATE GUIDELINES NETWORK">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network (SIGN) is an organization dedicated to developing evidence-based clinical practice guidelines for the National Health Service (NHS) in Scotland. SIGN plays a crucial role in enhancing healthcare practices by providing a systematic approach to clinical guidelines. Additionally, the organization has established a classification system for these guidelines, ensuring that they are organized and accessible for healthcare professionals. Through its efforts, SIGN aims to improve the quality of care and health outcomes for patients in Scotland.</data>
      <data key="d2">723cbca2d5cfbf8cf05a923c52569641,f5d0adafea7d8fe8216c624188ddad04,faa6d27a781e64a98fe101236a44dc16</data>
