    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" refers to a form of home nutritional therapy designed for patients who can digest food but are unable to obtain sufficient nutrients through oral intake. This specific type of home artificial nutrition involves delivering nutrients directly to the stomach or intestine, making it a crucial method for providing nutritional support to patients in their homes. It is particularly beneficial for individuals with neurological diseases and is a significant aspect of pediatric care, facilitating the early reintegration of children into their families while ensuring they receive necessary nutritional support.

Home enteral nutrition (NED) encompasses the provision of nutrition through enteral means, which has been documented in various registries over the years. It serves patients with special nutritional needs, including those with specific medical conditions that hinder their ability to consume adequate nutrition through regular food. The approach has been evaluated for its cost-effectiveness and its impact on health outcomes, highlighting its importance in managing the nutritional needs of patients at home.</data>
      <data key="d2">0482404f71667592ce2b0f771153ece8,0d083c309fb6f4d0d16c0e2b23ea5c8b,4e86ca77481672995a03989d321652bc,651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987,7c815eb3ecbf3e8cb61d3f9e27d9e061,7e3e2024996e402fc0ab62933ab9417b,7ea112a550fd775a80c3eda15663fba5,ed9b8701ef76cf4813eccfc58d6be998,fff76d1cd0e64233a5727a707d80e2b9</data>
      <data key="d3">1923</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">13</data>
      <data key="d6">13236</data>
      <data key="d7">38ead27ad8b8402eb34aa9645358efe8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR PARENT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The American Society for Parent is an organization that provides guidelines for nutritional support in patients requiring artificial nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">651bf69cdd5aec52b456cbea567f1987</data>
