      <data key="d7">c66fdd6e64e64ee7b4fe27ab1bd53593</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD VASCULAR CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Enfermedad Vascular Cerebral, tambi&#233;n conocida como enfermedad cerebrovascular, es una condici&#243;n que afecta el suministro de sangre al cerebro. Esta enfermedad puede resultar en complicaciones significativas, como la disfasia y la desnutrici&#243;n, especialmente despu&#233;s de un accidente cerebrovascular. Los problemas de salud y nutrici&#243;n en los pacientes son comunes debido a la interrupci&#243;n del flujo sangu&#237;neo, lo que resalta la importancia de una atenci&#243;n adecuada y oportuna para mitigar sus efectos.</data>
      <data key="d2">9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca</data>
      <data key="d3">1188</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">13238</data>
      <data key="d7">5c250de2cb084c50a29958d98e226506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BRONCOASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">BRONCOASPIRACI&#211;N refers to a medical condition characterized by the inhalation of food, liquid, or vomit into the lungs. This condition often occurs in patients with dysphagia, a swallowing disorder, and poses significant health risks, particularly during enteral feeding. The entry of these substances into the lungs can lead to serious complications, including pneumonia and other infections. Therefore, bronchoaspiration is a critical concern in medical settings, especially for vulnerable patients who may have difficulty swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13239</data>
      <data key="d7">246fe5db28af482294e44879122f3612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMON&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pneumonia is a serious infection that can occur as a result of bronchoaspiration, with a high mortality rate among affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540</data>
      <data key="d3">953</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13240</data>
      <data key="d7">5005b25718224d7eb0f66ec9c9c80956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Infecci&#243;n refers to the invasion and multiplication of microorganisms in body tissues, representing a significant health concern, particularly in patients with catheters. It is the most common complication associated with the use of central venous catheters, which can lead to either local or systemic infections. Patients receiving parenteral nutrition are especially at risk for developing infections related to these catheters. Additionally, individuals who are immunosuppressed, such as those who have undergone hematopoietic transplants, are also vulnerable to infections due to their weakened immune systems. Furthermore, infections can arise as complications from dysphagia and malnutrition, contributing to increased morbidity in affected patients. Overall, the risk of infection is a critical consideration in the management of patients with various medical conditions and interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728,81bb0be389c10331fb2a5568b6c379dc,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378,e5313f692c0a8259c93be803a704413c,ff844169c2b512733f5bde26e6f1ed32</data>
      <data key="d3">758</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">13241</data>
      <data key="d7">51b04869fe6a441f87173ff57f45fc22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INMUNODEPRESI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">INMUNODEPRESI&#211;N refers to a medical condition characterized by a weakened immune system, which can result from various factors, including malnutrition and cancer treatments. This state of immunodepression leads to a less effective immune response, making individuals more susceptible to infections and other health complications. Specifically, in the context of cancer patients, malnutrition and dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) are significant contributors to this condition, further exacerbating the challenges faced by those affected.</data>
      <data key="d2">0356b6c10b29c66d9b064df6bfef178d,38c7f97d650c77986c2dc9132aa20fdb,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378</data>
      <data key="d3">1099</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13242</data>
      <data key="d7">9a52899de024413d9e604f9b2acc05a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALA CICATRIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Poor healing is a condition that can occur due to malnutrition, which may be linked to dysphagia in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378</data>
      <data key="d3">1099</data>
