    <node id="HIDROELECTROL&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Balance hidroelectrol&#237;tico refers to the maintenance of electrolyte levels in patients, which is crucial for their overall health, especially in those receiving enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">13254</data>
      <data key="d7">da70ed8bdd0845998bf55da965994fc7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#218;SCULOS RESPIRATORIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">M&#250;sculos respiratorios are the muscles involved in breathing, which can be affected by ELA and its nutritional implications.</data>
      <data key="d2">02d838eb7d60f4fe558e304b6b6933e8</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">13255</data>
      <data key="d7">769b780f55da4efe85e65efcbc6bd4cf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOSPITAL BELLVITGE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Hospital Bellvitge is a medical institution that conducts studies on the management of patients with ELA, demonstrating the benefits of a multidisciplinary approach in patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c</data>
      <data key="d3">1236</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13256</data>
      <data key="d7">2075a2cbb96c47bbb7d78b632fa36766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Esclerosis Lateral Amiotr&#243;fica (ELA) is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that affects motor neurons, leading to muscle atrophy and various complications, including dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d2">cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c</data>
      <data key="d3">1236</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">13257</data>
      <data key="d7">b27616ee2c484568b96d514fc91d8586</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMMUNE SYSTEM DYSFUNCTION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Immune system dysfunction occurs in ELA patients, increasing the risk of infections and complicating their overall health status.</data>
      <data key="d2">cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c</data>
      <data key="d3">1236</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13258</data>
      <data key="d7">65a31d8d1e1d406cac54f917d4893db6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BODY COMPOSITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Body composition refers to the proportion of fat and non-fat mass in the body, and it plays a crucial role in the nutritional management of patients, particularly those with esophageal cancer (ELA patients). Body composition analysis in these patients helps determine the levels of fat, lean mass, and hydration, which are essential for tailoring effective nutritional strategies. Additionally, it is important to note that body composition can change significantly in patients undergoing treatment for esophageal cancer, highlighting the need for ongoing assessment and adjustment of nutritional plans.</data>
      <data key="d2">ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7,cea5f90ebf49c4157cab16ee26b9d97c</data>
      <data key="d3">743</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13259</data>
      <data key="d7">6704d48e728b48b387604ecb560390d2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGI&#201;NICO-DIET&#201;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Las medidas higi&#233;nico-diet&#233;ticas son pr&#225;cticas recomendadas para optimizar la ingesta nutricional en pacientes con esclerosis lateral amiotr&#243;fica.</data>
      <data key="d2">1adf391b13598f3ffe28ae596ff49438</data>
      <data key="d3">1445</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13260</data>
      <data key="d7">83dea46091ce43738e72a41aa21992e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUPORTE NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">SUPORTE NUTRICIONAL se refiere a un conjunto de intervenciones dise&#241;adas para mejorar el estado nutricional de los pacientes, especialmente aquellos que est&#225;n en riesgo de desnutrici&#243;n. Estas intervenciones son fundamentales para asegurar que los pacientes reciban la nutrici&#243;n adecuada necesaria para su recuperaci&#243;n y bienestar.</data>
      <data key="d2">1adf391b13598f3ffe28ae596ff49438,e510500bd5a5f16a0bf0353cfdb79c13</data>
      <data key="d3">1145</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13261</data>
      <data key="d7">e28122410c8b4e80a0a1f8177e31f28f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COBALAMINA (B12)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La cobalamina, o vitamina B12, es esencial para la mielinizaci&#243;n, un proceso cr&#237;tico para la funci&#243;n neuronal.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13262</data>
      <data key="d7">15c2c143155945fd93ac93cda0405e3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PIRIDOXINA (B6)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La piridoxina, o vitamina B6, es importante para la s&#237;ntesis de reguladores bioqu&#237;micos que afectan la funci&#243;n cerebral.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13263</data>
      <data key="d7">7005170791734d949ac6abb81f4df8d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#193;CIDO F&#211;LICO (B9)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#225;cido f&#243;lico, o vitamina B9, es crucial para el desarrollo fetal del sistema nervioso central.</data>
      <data key="d2">c6562eb1ee41febabe53bb8f2152f119</data>
      <data key="d3">607</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13264</data>
