    <node id="AMYOTROPHIC LATERAL SCLEROSIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that primarily affects nerve cells in the brain and spinal cord. This neurological condition specifically targets motor neurons, leading to a decline in muscle control and function. ALS is a significant focus of clinical management and ongoing research, as advancements in understanding and treating the disease continue to evolve.</data>
      <data key="d2">37182848d30a82f99b7a617859ac6e0d,499132ff7f7da81d7effbadf776c5b54</data>
