    <node id="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A is a specialized field of study that addresses the nutritional needs and interventions for cancer patients. This discipline emphasizes the critical importance of screening and diagnosing malnutrition, which can significantly impact patient outcomes. It focuses on the dietary practices and recommendations necessary for cancer patients, particularly during and after treatments such as chemotherapy, hematopoietic cell transplants, and surgical procedures.

The field recognizes the unique nutritional challenges faced by patients, especially those undergoing treatment for head and neck tumors, and aims to enhance recovery and improve the quality of life through tailored dietary strategies. Nutritional support in oncology encompasses managing the dietary needs of patients before, during, and after treatment, including the implementation of nutritional guidelines and protocols for post-surgical care. This comprehensive approach ensures that cancer patients receive the necessary nutritional interventions to optimize their health and recovery throughout their treatment journey.</data>
      <data key="d2">08d8220e35364eb95bacafae7dd2953b,2194de4eaed685b07d8f4c7a397de0ce,38c7f97d650c77986c2dc9132aa20fdb,42e8a4a4bff905ef121f1101d65c959f,5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,58af2bdd20eeb5647ecc8088732833d8,5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2,7c43869fff0960219e47d176597b35b8,b0ffa7260c4fc20462ad4c9bedcbfae7,eae8ddef005974a2ffe71cf7c61b0634</data>
