    </node>
    <node id="CANCER CACHEXIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cancer cachexia is a complex syndrome that significantly impacts cancer patients, characterized by severe body weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and alterations in metabolism. This condition often involves not only the loss of muscle but also fat, leading to a notable decline in overall body composition. It is frequently observed in patients with advanced stages of cancer, particularly those suffering from pancreatic and esophageal cancers. The syndrome is associated with decreased appetite, which further exacerbates the nutritional challenges faced by these patients. Due to its profound effects on health and quality of life, cancer cachexia has become a significant focus of research within the field of oncology, highlighting the need for specialized nutritional interventions and support to manage this debilitating condition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">a496bf37d4cc9b6246f5eb6b66b03d8a,bb209dcfffac9c89dae0ad4ed2908d85,bef1f848ac9b922f7361b740210a8314,cae7bf8d7b8c9d1f34a87ef41ff39a17,ce2e5f8df5ad472bb255174d496cc1d7,fb7b0d121f195e2a472f3d47e28ccff9</data>
      <data key="d3">1206</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">17</data>
      <data key="d6">13508</data>
      <data key="d7">be72f79a204844b4b3e3d09f87e95fd4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SERUM C-REACTIVE PROTEIN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Serum C-reactive protein is a marker that is studied in relation to prognosis in esophageal carcinoma.</data>
