    </node>
    <node id="M.&#170; &#193;NGELES VALERO ZANUY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">M.&#170; &#193;ngeles Valero Zanuy is a medical professional specializing in nutrition at Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre.</data>
      <data key="d2">5c69bb68f0d23a5aa15fa31301aa13c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1441</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13734</data>
      <data key="d7">25fbabb0d6ae4dd79ff66818e98edcbd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS" is a medical procedure that involves the transfer of hematopoietic stem cells to treat a variety of diseases, including certain types of cancer, blood disorders, and hematological tumors. This treatment is considered potentially curative for various hematological diseases and some solid tumors. The procedure typically requires the administration of high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells. Additionally, the context of this transplantation includes discussions on the importance of nutritional support for patients undergoing the procedure, highlighting the comprehensive care needed during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">3e6ae05671fed21e332ee155332df21e,4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4,5c69bb68f0d23a5aa15fa31301aa13c2,f333e5a9af59dd8504607b2559ac35dd</data>
      <data key="d3">1100</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">30</data>
      <data key="d6">13735</data>
      <data key="d7">ad4bbda8bbee402eb91559e38ed4765c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD DE INJERTO CONTRA HU&#201;SPED">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Graft-versus-host disease (GVHD), known in Spanish as "Enfermedad de Injerto Contra Hu&#233;sped" (EICH), is a serious complication that can arise following hematopoietic cell transplantation. This condition occurs when the transplanted cells, or graft, initiate an immune response against the recipient's body, leading to significant morbidity and mortality. GVHD is characterized by the transplanted cells attacking the recipient's tissues, which can result in various clinical manifestations. The disease highlights the complexities and risks associated with hematopoietic cell transplants, underscoring the importance of monitoring and managing potential complications in transplant recipients.</data>
      <data key="d2">27c75984e62c5adcac1ac33cbdc520dc,4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4,5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972,5c69bb68f0d23a5aa15fa31301aa13c2</data>
      <data key="d3">1097</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">13736</data>
      <data key="d7">02875907be994f2a98adbae1cedc0055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDAD VENOCLOSIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La enfermedad venoclusiva es una complicaci&#243;n que puede surgir tras un trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematol&#243;gicas, caracterizada por la obstrucci&#243;n de las venas del h&#237;gado.</data>
      <data key="d2">4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4</data>
      <data key="d3">1100</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13737</data>
      <data key="d7">f3cf1b9131624c739be624ad0cf41d9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APLASIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Aplasia is a medical condition characterized by the absence or significant reduction of normal cell production in the bone marrow. This condition often arises as a complication following a hematopoietic stem cell transplant. In Spanish, it is described as "una condici&#243;n en la que hay una disminuci&#243;n o ausencia de c&#233;lulas en la m&#233;dula &#243;sea," highlighting its impact on the bone marrow's ability to produce essential blood cells. Aplasia can lead to various health issues due to the insufficient production of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, which are crucial for overall bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4,408288a47065e62d79bbc9b19df87c61</data>
      <data key="d3">503</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13738</data>
      <data key="d7">f4a56d4f1c664739aa6af11a390c8f4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CITOST&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Los citost&#225;ticos son medicamentos utilizados en quimioterapia para detener el crecimiento de c&#233;lulas cancerosas y son administrados durante el trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematol&#243;gicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4</data>
      <data key="d3">1100</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13739</data>
      <data key="d7">a4a2dbdfc6d44d0e857e8bf2339b9880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS son las c&#233;lulas de la sangre que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en los trasplantes, utilizados para tratar diversas enfermedades hematol&#243;gicas.</data>
      <data key="d2">4015c8a1a16c5c93f3b853d9cac57bf4,db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1102</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">13740</data>
      <data key="d7">8d9260b43f6948d580d39e6bb94d76d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALOG&#201;NICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Alog&#233;nico refers to a type of bone marrow transplantation in which the donor is a different individual, as opposed to an autologous transplant where the donor and recipient are the same person. This procedure often necessitates additional nutritional support for the recipient. The alog&#233;nico transplant involves the use of compatible donor cells to treat both malignant and non-malignant diseases.</data>
      <data key="d2">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1,db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1129</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">13741</data>
      <data key="d7">70f6ef316e9c4017af2068b56ea64d28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUT&#211;LOGO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AUT&#211;LOGO refers to a type of bone marrow transplantation in which the donor is the patient themselves. This procedure utilizes the patient's own hematological cells, thereby avoiding issues related to compatibility.</data>
      <data key="d2">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1,db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1102</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13742</data>
      <data key="d7">a0f34fe813d942709c4dbf3c4539696d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEDULA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La m&#233;dula &#243;sea es el tejido donde se producen las c&#233;lulas sangu&#237;neas y de donde se obtienen c&#233;lulas para trasplantes.</data>
      <data key="d2">db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1102</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13743</data>
      <data key="d7">05ac94bcdd104b6ba5e56529f13c2ccf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SANGRE PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">La sangre perif&#233;rica es la sangre que circula en el cuerpo y de la cual se pueden obtener c&#233;lulas hematol&#243;gicas mediante af&#233;resis.</data>
      <data key="d2">db0a4fc296a2fd5ecfbc4afcda444738</data>
      <data key="d3">1102</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">13744</data>
      <data key="d7">5ffbb896927a4ec7baa9d85db4911c44</data>
