    </node>
    <node id="CENTERS FOR DISEASE CONTROL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Centers for Disease Control (CDC) is a national public health institute in the United States that plays a crucial role in providing guidelines on health practices and disease prevention. The CDC offers comprehensive recommendations aimed at promoting health and preventing diseases, which include specific dietary guidelines for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplants. As a key agency in public health, the CDC is dedicated to improving health outcomes and ensuring the well-being of the population through its evidence-based directives.</data>
      <data key="d2">17fc469cf1ddbb8fa68bad4446bd65e6,81bb0be389c10331fb2a5568b6c379dc</data>
      <data key="d3">1266</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13788</data>
      <data key="d7">9a75dc2c93ab4530976b36e298bb8a55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS COMERCIALMENTE EST&#201;RILES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Commercially sterile foods are those with extremely low levels of microorganisms, prepared in controlled environments to ensure safety for patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">17fc469cf1ddbb8fa68bad4446bd65e6</data>
      <data key="d3">1266</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13789</data>
      <data key="d7">e09359986e624aeb852682153885b11c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS MUY LIMPIOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Very clean foods are fresh foods with lower microorganism content than regular hospital diets, prepared under strict hygiene conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">17fc469cf1ddbb8fa68bad4446bd65e6</data>
      <data key="d3">1266</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">13790</data>
      <data key="d7">242c515724af400eaf8d8b9e17571bb5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ACOR is an organization that provides information related to leukemia and patient care, including dietary recommendations for patients undergoing treatment.</data>
      <data key="d2">2194de4eaed685b07d8f4c7a397de0ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1554</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">13791</data>
      <data key="d7">b1ec9d53e3ab4bce8e7b780366854d11</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CDC">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) is a national public health institute in the United States that plays a crucial role in providing health guidelines and standards. It is responsible for disseminating information related to health and safety, including specific growth patterns for children. The CDC's mission encompasses a wide range of public health initiatives aimed at improving the overall health of the population.</data>
      <data key="d2">2194de4eaed685b07d8f4c7a397de0ce,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7,e9bb1d3d1af940dd655e0cca9bbb5c02</data>
