    </node>
    <node id="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bone Marrow Transplant refers to both a medical procedure and a scholarly journal. As a medical procedure, it involves the replacement or supplementation of bone marrow, often necessitating nutritional support due to potential complications. This procedure typically entails the transplantation of blood stem cells to treat a variety of conditions, including cancers and blood disorders. Additionally, Bone Marrow Transplant is a journal dedicated to publishing research related to bone marrow transplantation and associated studies, contributing to the academic and clinical understanding of this important medical field.</data>
      <data key="d2">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,33900ea313cbdf466c2bebc1f587e2bf,42b1be887a83da3e796a9cec7a082b11,73d47e377c2910da3393d7bb65f80e8e</data>
      <data key="d3">1255</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">13804</data>
      <data key="d7">b5fc96c49cd7461ea39743b4e658262d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEMATOLOGICAL PATIENT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Patients suffering from blood-related diseases who may require nutritional support during treatment, especially after bone marrow transplants.</data>
      <data key="d2">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e</data>
