    <node id="HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Hematopoietic cell transplantation is a medical procedure utilized to treat a range of diseases, particularly various cancers and blood disorders. This procedure involves the infusion of blood-forming stem cells, which serve to replace damaged or diseased bone marrow with healthy cells. By restoring the bone marrow's function, hematopoietic cell transplantation aims to improve the patient's overall health and combat the effects of the underlying conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">73d47e377c2910da3393d7bb65f80e8e,c21f51b529806fd52e9f478e2ab6ef7b</data>
      <data key="d3">1199</data>
