    <node id="ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS" refers to adverse reactions caused by the consumption of certain foods, mediated by the immune system. These food allergies represent a heterogeneous group of diseases characterized by immunological mechanisms, often manifesting in childhood and frequently resolving before adulthood. In predisposed individuals, food allergies can trigger severe immune responses to specific foods, leading to various clinical manifestations. These reactions may include immediate responses as well as delayed symptoms, depending on the type of immune response involved. A comprehensive medical history is essential to determine whether symptoms are indeed adverse reactions to particular foods. Food allergies are abnormal immune responses to antigens released in the digestive tract, primarily mediated by Immunoglobulin E (IgE), which can result in adverse reactions to specific food items.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d6ee23789bfcf1d419eafb56a6d064f,7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f,9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1,a562e90891c11da0293bc7de511acc8f,d10e6c00bbb982bda449b9cb815691a3,ee7fb587e5ab0f265d2036071b632b36</data>
      <data key="d3">371</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">42</data>
      <data key="d6">14000</data>
      <data key="d7">903f9075de014f6dad8fc328ba7740a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS refer to adverse reactions to certain foods that do not involve the immune system, distinguishing them from food allergies. These intolerances are often linked to enzyme deficiencies, such as lactose intolerance, where the body lacks the necessary enzymes to properly digest specific foods. The reactions associated with food intolerances are non-immune and can lead to various symptoms, particularly gastrointestinal issues, as well as other health problems. In summary, INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS are characterized by their non-IgE mediated nature, resulting in a range of adverse effects without the involvement of the immune response.</data>
      <data key="d2">39a7166ca777be46a1613c54a746e2b8,7d6ee23789bfcf1d419eafb56a6d064f,9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd,9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1</data>
      <data key="d3">841</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">10</data>
      <data key="d6">14001</data>
      <data key="d7">882e1a8f832c4ee1a0a56dddda3559bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="URTICARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Urticaria is a skin reaction characterized by hives, often associated with allergic responses to food.</data>
      <data key="d2">9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1</data>
      <data key="d3">371</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14002</data>
      <data key="d7">f6b3bad1f6874675b3d264d72a5b1c73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANAFLAXIA AL&#201;RGICA ORAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anafilaxia al&#233;rgica oral is a severe allergic reaction that occurs after the ingestion of certain foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1</data>
      <data key="d3">371</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
