    <node id="ACAD&#201;MIA AMERICANA DE PEDIATR&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Academia Americana de Pediatr&#237;a (AAP) is an organization dedicated to pediatric health, providing essential guidelines and recommendations for various aspects of child care. Among its key contributions, the AAP offers advice on the introduction of solid foods for children at high risk of food allergies, ensuring that parents and caregivers are informed about best practices to promote health and safety. Additionally, since 2008, the AAP has also recommended vitamin D supplementation for children, highlighting its importance in maintaining optimal health during early development. Through these initiatives, the AAP plays a crucial role in guiding pediatric care and supporting the well-being of children.</data>
      <data key="d2">527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1,b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a</data>
      <data key="d3">614</data>
