    <node id="ETILSUCINATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Etilsuccinato is a compound that is less susceptible to acidic pH, leading to more complete absorption compared to other compounds.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14207</data>
      <data key="d7">08560601826f4f5f95cfe8039834b74c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTOLATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Estolato is a compound that is less susceptible to acidic pH, leading to more complete absorption compared to other compounds.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14208</data>
      <data key="d7">061932b938c340b784432196762d99bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTEARATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Estearato is a compound that is more susceptible to acidic pH, affecting its absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14209</data>
      <data key="d7">7f9051cc7f3c4d429cc50aba1ecfb7f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRISEOFULVINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Griseofulvina is a medication known for its ability to cause abnormal taste sensations. It is characterized as liposoluble, meaning it dissolves in fats, and its absorption in the body is enhanced by the presence of bile salts.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d3">359</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">14210</data>
      <data key="d7">51d7c587c4354322aa94f1d74067d69f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HALOFANTRINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Halofantrina is a medication that is liposoluble and its absorption is facilitated by bile salts.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d3">359</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14211</data>
      <data key="d7">d395c5ce139f46aa96f7916819be14b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FURANOCUMARINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Furanocoumarins are compounds found in grapefruit juice that can inhibit the CYP3A4 enzyme, affecting drug metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d3">359</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14212</data>
      <data key="d7">473e764e966542d3896671a5f1d2212c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERACCIONES FARMACOCIN&#201;TICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Interacciones farmacocin&#233;ticas are interactions that alter the pharmacokinetics of a drug, affecting its absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d3">322</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14213</data>
      <data key="d7">9d69788b65be4b41b464ce345a6782e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOTILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Motilidad refers to the physiological movement within the gastrointestinal tract that can affect drug absorption.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a</data>
      <data key="d3">322</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14214</data>
      <data key="d7">2837cf751f85465784f0e9d36f6acf36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECRECIONES GASTROINTESTINALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Secreciones gastrointestinales are bodily fluids produced in the gastrointestinal tract that play a crucial role in the dissolution and absorption of medications. These secretions contain various electrolytes and minerals, which are essential for the proper functioning of the digestive system.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260</data>
      <data key="d3">322</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">14215</data>
      <data key="d7">ee8e6a44520d491da09576696dc7f918</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">pH is a critical measure that influences various biological and chemical processes, particularly in the context of clinical nutrition and pharmacology. It affects the solubility of proteins in clinical nutrition products, thereby impacting their stability and effectiveness. Additionally, pH refers to the acidity or alkalinity of the gastrointestinal environment, which plays a significant role in drug absorption. Understanding pH is essential for optimizing both nutritional products and medication efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a,dc38a37c30b175667931b84a9c9103bb</data>
      <data key="d3">322</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">14216</data>
      <data key="d7">13f9c170defe4ed985f3630bb4119ded</data>
    </node>
    <node id="F&#193;RMACO">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">F&#225;rmaco refers to the medication used in the treatment of conditions such as Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). In this context, tolvapt&#225;n is specifically mentioned as the medication utilized for this purpose.</data>
      <data key="d2">18d237ccee6cf99bff4690087156025a,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e</data>
      <data key="d3">322</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">14217</data>
      <data key="d7">8cb012beeeb2448480817a017676fc4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISONIAZIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Isoniazida is a medication that is primarily used in the treatment of tuberculosis. It is important for patients to be aware that Isoniazida can cause adverse reactions when ingested with foods containing histamine, which may lead to symptoms such as facial flushing and severe headache. To enhance the absorption of the medication, it is recommended that Isoniazida be taken on an empty stomach.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14218</data>
      <data key="d7">3c317c5c33264dada428cbb6242c97b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZIDOVUDINA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Zidovudina is an antiretroviral medication whose absorption can be significantly reduced by high-fat foods.</data>
      <data key="d2">75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d3">891</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14219</data>
      <data key="d7">722191637a2c49d794e3e37ae7ff87f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIETAS RICAS EN VITAMINA K">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Diets high in vitamin K can antagonize the effects of anticoagulants like warfarina.</data>
      <data key="d2">75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d3">1187</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14220</data>
      <data key="d7">572f75b8ae45493a8d70fa7994573271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN HISTAMINA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Foods high in histamine can provoke hypertensive crises in patients taking monoamine oxidase inhibitors.</data>
      <data key="d2">75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14221</data>
      <data key="d7">eed16e0e0cdc4a5395396d224829b9bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN GRASA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">High-fat foods can reduce the absorption of certain antiretroviral medications by up to 50%.</data>
      <data key="d2">75b625e1dd088fa7beed19a4142f726f</data>
      <data key="d3">891</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">14222</data>
      <data key="d7">262e2a8004e74892b45146f9e3eea606</data>
