    <node id="F&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">F&#211;LICO refers to Folic Acid, also known as Vitamin B9, which is a water-soluble vitamin essential for DNA synthesis and repair. It plays a critical role during periods of rapid growth, making it particularly important for pregnant women and individuals in developmental stages. Additionally, F&#243;lico is a medication that is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. This dual significance highlights F&#211;LICO's importance both as a vital nutrient and as a therapeutic agent.</data>
      <data key="d2">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e,808759fcf017fe581d5c893c7a29c5be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14271</data>
      <data key="d7">4ad749ae4e3243bb897ac23d4c9b33d6</data>
    </node>
