    <node id="VALLADOLID">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Valladolid is a city in Spain known for its significant contributions to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. It is home to the Centro de Investigaci&#243;n de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n, a research center dedicated to advancing knowledge in these areas. Additionally, the city houses the Hospital Cl&#237;nico Universitario, which plays a crucial role in clinical care and research. Valladolid has also been referenced in publications related to clinical nutrition and metabolism, highlighting its importance in the academic and medical communities.</data>
      <data key="d2">6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa,ec69668515f0a014f1a602bcdc46c47f</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14557</data>
      <data key="d7">1b0773f1e6794c129567cb7cd5332aee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N POR V&#205;A ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract through a tube, which has been referenced since 1589.</data>
      <data key="d2">6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1189</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14558</data>
      <data key="d7">4b7ab2a8f22c4317b1a5cb3629026fad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sondas are medical devices specifically designed for enteral feeding, which includes various types of tubes such as nasogastric, nasoduodenal, and nasojejunal tubes. They are utilized to provide nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally. Additionally, Sondas can be used for feeding patients through gastrostomy or jejunostomy, offering a range of types and sizes to accommodate different patient needs. Overall, Sondas play a crucial role in the administration of enteral nutrition when oral intake is not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa</data>
      <data key="d3">1149</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">14559</data>
      <data key="d7">8d0b6d9d19414805adc12f51ff6787f3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SONDA NASOENT&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A nasoenteric tube is a type of feeding tube that is inserted through the nose and extends into the small intestine, used for patients requiring long-term nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14560</data>
      <data key="d7">fc6682a3d07a47e99eb79fe67a3ce5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALGORITMO PARA LA ELECCI&#211;N DE ACCESO EN NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">An algorithm designed to guide the choice of access for enteral nutrition, considering patient conditions and risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14561</data>
      <data key="d7">f3038131e4bf46b0b13f97758266baf0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PEREIRA JL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Pereira JL is a researcher who plays a significant role in the recommendations for managing hyperglycemia in patients receiving artificial nutrition. Additionally, Pereira JL is recognized as an author referenced in the context of enteral nutrition guidelines and practices, contributing valuable insights to the field.</data>
      <data key="d2">64378df2be6b08b39bd652c0a2d3789c,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d3">1722</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14562</data>
      <data key="d7">f9a8155a494746148c7adbce0376cfc6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAPAROTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Laparotom&#237;a is a surgical procedure that involves making an incision into the abdominal cavity. This procedure is often utilized to access internal organs for various medical interventions. It may impact a patient's ability to tolerate enteral nutrition. The term "laparotom&#237;a" is the Spanish equivalent of "laparotomy," and both descriptions highlight its role in surgical practices, particularly in relation to the abdominal wall.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6,a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">14563</data>
      <data key="d7">1c955e565f4448f1ae07f7b1e2ba93b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEF&#193;LICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Traumatismo craneoencef&#225;lico, or cranioencephalic trauma, refers to injuries affecting both the brain and skull. This type of traumatic brain injury can complicate enteral feeding processes and may lead to serious complications, necessitating immediate medical attention. Additionally, it can result in conditions such as SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion), and the duration of treatment for such injuries can vary significantly. Overall, Traumatismo craneoencef&#225;lico represents a critical medical condition that requires prompt and effective management.</data>
      <data key="d2">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14564</data>
      <data key="d7">6165847305744f21b1db3f64ffae6f48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MIXEDEMA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Myxedema is a severe form of hypothyroidism that can affect a patient's metabolism and nutritional requirements.</data>
      <data key="d2">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14565</data>
      <data key="d7">380a33c8920e4aaea9433386997d3759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIADOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">El fiador es un dispositivo que facilita la colocaci&#243;n de la sonda, proporcionando rigidez y evitando la perforaci&#243;n durante el procedimiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1192</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14566</data>
      <data key="d7">7042c25ebed64d6f9c6261e555571d9b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGIENE BUCAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La higiene bucal es un procedimiento que se debe mantener adecuadamente en los d&#237;as sucesivos tras la colocaci&#243;n de la sonda para evitar complicaciones.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1192</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14567</data>
      <data key="d7">d4450e16de204185b775170f172deaa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RADIOL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La comprobaci&#243;n radiol&#243;gica es el m&#233;todo m&#225;s seguro para verificar la posici&#243;n correcta de la sonda tras su colocaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1192</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14568</data>
      <data key="d7">73e4c5213ffb41eaa302bd1968f5aa39</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La obstrucci&#243;n es una complicaci&#243;n que puede ocurrir en el uso de sondas, afectando hasta el 9% de los casos.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1182</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14569</data>
      <data key="d7">c1daa55b3405480f8d956517ea74d831</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPROBACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La comprobaci&#243;n de la posici&#243;n de la sonda es un paso crucial para asegurar su correcta colocaci&#243;n y funcionamiento.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1182</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14570</data>
      <data key="d7">01cb57a0db8043ec9d219fdc40521e9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTE CON RIESGO DE BRONCOASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">El paciente con riesgo de broncoaspiraci&#243;n es aquel que no debe recibir una Sonda Nasog&#225;strica debido a complicaciones potenciales.</data>
      <data key="d2">c78e1786c296e2b8a7ad428c0fb10c36</data>
      <data key="d3">1192</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14571</data>
      <data key="d7">61e572b5e9f944e68833b600869d0352</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#205;LEO EN EL COLON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El &#237;leo en el colon es una condici&#243;n que puede durar de 3 a 5 d&#237;as, afectando el tr&#225;nsito intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d2">838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14572</data>
      <data key="d7">d3d1390e0fe24834819d1605d639b49c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUMON&#205;A ASPIRATIVA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NEUMON&#205;A ASPIRATIVA is a serious complication that can arise from the use of enteral feeding tubes. This condition occurs when food or liquid inadvertently enters the lungs, leading to potential respiratory issues. In Spanish, it is described as a grave complication that can occur due to the entry of digestive contents into the respiratory tract.</data>
      <data key="d2">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9,838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14573</data>
      <data key="d7">b060776481d047c99d3eb191884c8e66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPROBACI&#211;N RADIOLOGICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La comprobaci&#243;n radiol&#243;gica es un procedimiento utilizado para confirmar la correcta colocaci&#243;n de la sonda nasog&#225;strica o nasoenteral.</data>
      <data key="d2">838b9736f0199a50d032077e4b74cbc6</data>
      <data key="d3">1186</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14574</data>
      <data key="d7">42bc57e570d24835b741cbc8c2a7d193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PONSKEY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">PONSKEY is recognized as one of the pioneers of the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, significantly contributing to advancements in minimally invasive feeding procedures.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d3">1147</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14575</data>
      <data key="d7">312919f52c834083901526f10baa0e0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAUDEREZ">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">GAUDEREZ is a medical professional recognized for co-developing the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, which significantly improved patient care in nutritional support. In 1979, Gauderez was among the first physicians to practice endoscopic gastrostomy, contributing to the establishment of this technique as the preferred method for enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f,4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14576</data>
      <data key="d7">8c2ce33da608444798f2d904a38bb124</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTERACI&#211;N DEL NIVEL DE CONSCIENCIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A medical condition where a patient experiences changes in awareness or responsiveness, which can be critical in assessing overall health.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14577</data>
      <data key="d7">f3534a2d63db4912b4002b0eb8e54926</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HERNIAS HIATAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A condition where part of the stomach pushes through the diaphragm into the chest cavity, often leading to complications in digestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14578</data>
      <data key="d7">6f80a5e1e88549439a3b2be6c3809154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N G&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A blockage in the stomach that prevents food from passing into the small intestine, requiring medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14579</data>
      <data key="d7">6ec20f4d5261432a864533d1ad9fefee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS LOCALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Local infectious complications that can arise from medical procedures, such as otitis and sinusitis, affecting patient recovery.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14580</data>
      <data key="d7">7adb9c1aba0747f588340be1e97a8f9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPLICACIONES MEC&#193;NICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mechanical complications that can occur from the use of medical devices, such as injuries from pressure sores or local infections.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14581</data>
      <data key="d7">bb0519098ccd47ba90bb052086711b01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADOS DE LA SONDA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The practices involved in maintaining and caring for feeding tubes to prevent complications and ensure patient safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14582</data>
      <data key="d7">afcda91119094356a462e09c20b99728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACCESO INVASIVO AL TUBO DIGESTIVO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A medical procedure that involves creating an opening in the digestive tract for feeding or other interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14583</data>
      <data key="d7">48ab326af1214c249dd89884d04e073d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROCESOS FUNCIONALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Functional disorders of the digestive system that may necessitate surgical interventions like enterostomies.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14584</data>
      <data key="d7">f148c365c1e24738ad1bc7820417f7f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFECCIONES ABDOMINALES ACTIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Active abdominal infections that can pose risks during surgical procedures, necessitating careful evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14585</data>
      <data key="d7">ab36b86c6c1d43399c79b407a9759ac6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENFERMEDADES NEUROL&#211;GICAS DEGENERATIVAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Degenerative neurological diseases that can affect swallowing and digestion, leading to the need for nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14586</data>
      <data key="d7">7817eb96fdef4724a827a48b20baf9dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICAS ENDOSC&#211;PICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Minimally invasive procedures performed using an endoscope, often preferred for their lower risk and quicker recovery times.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">4dffad2ae717727b21f2294ac520f2be</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">14587</data>
      <data key="d7">507df852b418444e9b10edd476667caf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE PONSKY-GAUDERER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La t&#233;cnica de Ponsky-Gauderer es un m&#233;todo espec&#237;fico para realizar una gastrostom&#237;a endosc&#243;pica, que implica el uso de un endoscopio y anestesia t&#243;pica para facilitar la inserci&#243;n de la sonda.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14588</data>
      <data key="d7">62f788de04c84398b61a1179ec83d301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE SACKS-VINE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La t&#233;cnica de Sacks-Vine es un m&#233;todo de colocaci&#243;n de sonda de gastrostom&#237;a que se realiza bajo visi&#243;n endosc&#243;pica, utilizando una aguja introductora para guiar el cat&#233;ter al est&#243;mago.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14589</data>
      <data key="d7">91ed1893ec6f45a29ea987024d43f47b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE RUSSELL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La t&#233;cnica de Russell es un procedimiento percut&#225;neo para la colocaci&#243;n de una sonda de gastrostom&#237;a, que utiliza un bal&#243;n tipo Foley y control endosc&#243;pico para asegurar la correcta colocaci&#243;n de la sonda.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14590</data>
      <data key="d7">7d4ad1b6d75d493dbf10d1e4d16def6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A ENDOSC&#211;PICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La yeyunostom&#237;a endosc&#243;pica es un procedimiento que permite la inserci&#243;n de una sonda en el yeyuno, indicado para pacientes con riesgo de aspiraci&#243;n, manteniendo la motilidad y funci&#243;n absortiva del intestino.</data>
      <data key="d2">4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14591</data>
      <data key="d7">4d7c9cad397f451bab1e4128d681b639</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANESTESIA LOCAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anestesia local is a type of anesthesia utilized in various medical procedures, including faringostom&#237;a and gastrostom&#237;a endosc&#243;pica. Its primary purpose is to minimize pain in the specific area being treated, allowing for the procedure to be performed with reduced risk of complications compared to general anesthesia. This localized approach enhances patient safety and comfort during interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,4041e05fe2f79ca70bbf0522cc31be8f</data>
      <data key="d3">1148</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14592</data>
      <data key="d7">ba41f0310ee44f858958ac3eb0719ccf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARINGOSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Faringostom&#237;a is a surgical procedure for placing a feeding tube through the piriform sinus into the neck, indicated for trauma or malformations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7</data>
      <data key="d3">1149</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14593</data>
      <data key="d7">1443174953a04fe797743686a9c61ec4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MALFORMACIONES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Malformaciones are congenital anomalies that may require surgical procedures such as faringostom&#237;a for feeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14594</data>
      <data key="d7">9b38c6bb6e804fdea80ee5ccb142ec97</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTOM&#205;AS QUIR&#218;RGICAS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14595</data>
      <data key="d7">46a7e05aee3a4c1dbacce184bc25c726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A QUIR&#218;RGICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Yeyunostom&#237;a quir&#250;rgica is a surgical procedure performed as a complement to gastrointestinal surgery to avoid risks associated with parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">14596</data>
      <data key="d7">ca6f7eac5ad64b488ef1fd6872d7f4aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE STAMM">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">T&#233;cnica de Stamm is a simple method for gastrostomy, suitable for high surgical risk cases or temporary gastrostomy.</data>
      <data key="d2">a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14597</data>
      <data key="d7">c57a5170ee3346928cb27ec2ddb4f3a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE WITZEL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">T&#233;cnica de Witzel involves creating a seromuscular tunnel around the catheter to reduce leakage risk during yeyunostom&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14598</data>
      <data key="d7">0b34baccd82543e7a994a3a629fc119e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="T&#201;CNICA DE JANEWAY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">T&#233;cnica de Janeway is a method for permanent gastrostomy using a Foley catheter within a gastric tunnel.</data>
      <data key="d2">a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14599</data>
      <data key="d7">d6352afe33c44e469727956ded3c13f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OSTOM&#205;AS RADIOLOGICAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ostom&#237;as radiol&#243;gicas refer to procedures like gastrostom&#237;a radiol&#243;gica percut&#225;nea, which do not require anesthesia or endoscopy.</data>
      <data key="d2">a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">14600</data>
      <data key="d7">be8065bbe66d4eab852df0cd86421e4e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANESTESIA GENERAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ANESTESIA GENERAL is a medical procedure utilized to induce unconsciousness in patients during surgical operations, including procedures such as the placement of feeding tubes. While it is essential for facilitating various surgeries, ANESTESIA GENERAL also carries inherent risks associated with surgical interventions.</data>
      <data key="d2">70e48774a3f732e015a59d38ba2fa5d5,a956cded459a9729e0f2f62707249acc</data>
      <data key="d3">1146</data>
