    <node id="ACETATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Acetato is a compound utilized in medical treatments, particularly recognized for its role as an additive in parenteral nutrition solutions. It serves multiple functions, including helping to maintain the body's acid-base balance and acting as a precursor to bicarbonate in cases of metabolic acidosis. Additionally, Acetato is a source of energy and is considered an essential electrolyte in the nutritional requirements for pediatric patients, particularly in parenteral nutrition. Overall, Acetato plays a crucial role in supporting the metabolic needs and pH balance of individuals receiving specialized nutritional care.</data>
      <data key="d2">9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2,d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260,d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723,e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d3">625</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
