    </node>
    <node id="INTESTINAL FAILURE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Intestinal failure is a medical condition characterized by the inability of the intestines to absorb sufficient nutrients and fluids, which often necessitates the use of parenteral nutrition. This condition predominantly affects pediatric patients, who may require home parenteral nutrition to manage their nutritional needs. Intestinal failure is considered a serious health issue and is frequently discussed in relation to liver disease and transplantation, highlighting its complexity and the critical care required for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d2">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,384e13475cc83e77e160fd6be9a88e73,52d93d6adba464a2397ddec01d152840</data>
      <data key="d3">594</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14729</data>
      <data key="d7">a890abfb5e6d40b9ad1637ffb4b8a32e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO is a condition characterized by an abnormal increase in bacteria in the intestines. This condition is particularly relevant for patients with intestinal failure, as it can significantly impact their liver health. In cases where patients are receiving parenteral nutrition, SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO may necessitate empirical treatment with metronidazole to manage the bacterial overgrowth effectively.</data>
      <data key="d2">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d3">594</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">14730</data>
      <data key="d7">76dd5b9ff34544a7869e02aa6c72646a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRASPLANTE AISLADO DE INTESTINO DELGADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A surgical procedure to replace the small intestine, which can improve liver function in patients with hepatobiliary complications related to parenteral nutrition.</data>
