    </node>
    <node id="TRATAMIENTO DE LA HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Treatment of hyponatremia in the context of artificial nutrition</data>
      <data key="d2">8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15026</data>
      <data key="d7">a5fe7a61bad1405c8861724e0b9b1f86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SRAA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The SRAA, or Sistema Renina-Angiotensina-Aldosterona, is a crucial hormonal system that plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and maintaining fluid balance within the body. This system operates by coordinating the actions of various hormones, including renin, angiotensin, and aldosterone. It is important to note that the SRAA is inhibited during antidiuresis, a process mediated by antidiuretic hormone (ADH), which further influences fluid retention and blood pressure regulation. Overall, the SRAA is essential for homeostasis, ensuring that blood pressure remains stable and that the body's fluid levels are appropriately managed.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">15027</data>
      <data key="d7">ccff15efac66415e9b872fa9af366dd5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N. PARAVENTRICULAR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The paraventricular nucleus is a part of the hypothalamus that plays a role in the secretion of hormones including ADH.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15028</data>
      <data key="d7">fe923f9bf8164d54ad1d7e44c15131db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N. SUPRA&#211;PTICO">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The supraoptic nucleus is another part of the hypothalamus involved in the production of ADH.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d3">1324</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15029</data>
      <data key="d7">a3211d75d7694cdea841e9c410044681</data>
    </node>
    <node id="H2O">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Water (H2O) is the primary substance regulated by ADH in the body.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15030</data>
      <data key="d7">0da168222b58437483eca1043c7a8a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUAPORINAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Aquaporins are water channel proteins that facilitate the transport of water across cell membranes, regulated by ADH.</data>
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15031</data>
      <data key="d7">69d1e64888ec403bbcf991bd4a2a73ac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORMONA ADRENOCORTICOTROPA">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d3">1327</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15032</data>
      <data key="d7">536b6d331ca14b069082a318fb7050c9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLOQUE: SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A section or block focused on advanced nutritional support, particularly in relation to maintaining body water in threatening situations</data>
      <data key="d2">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15033</data>
      <data key="d7">73c0024e9a94456eb1f5dd426084f98b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROLOGICAL MANIFESTATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Clinical symptoms related to the nervous system that arise from hyponatremia, including headache, lethargy, confusion, and severe outcomes like coma and seizures</data>
      <data key="d2">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d3">1851</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15034</data>
      <data key="d7">3a095f7da8504644adec1c4413c28442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NEUROHYPOPHYSIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The part of the pituitary gland that releases ADH, playing a crucial role in water retention and the development of conditions like SIADH</data>
      <data key="d2">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15035</data>
      <data key="d7">a0f9e5f219c04f70884eeba9c58aa91c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="P&#201;PTIDO NATRIUR&#201;TICO ATRIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">A hormone that promotes sodium excretion and is involved in the body's response to increased plasma volume</data>
      <data key="d2">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d3">317</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15036</data>
      <data key="d7">d5544c7d4f884856a3d1dee10ecd8384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLUTAMATO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Glutamato is an organic molecule that serves as a neurotransmitter in the brain, playing a role in the body's response to cerebral edema during hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15037</data>
      <data key="d7">be3ac8877e81488fb3562adde38f50df</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INOSITOL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Inositol is an organic compound that is involved in the cellular processes and may help in reducing cerebral edema during hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15038</data>
      <data key="d7">675922aea0c14f1d8ace764297376e0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTE&#205;NAS TOTALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prote&#237;nas totales refer to the total amount of proteins in the blood, which can influence sodium measurements and the diagnosis of hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15039</data>
      <data key="d7">b2f2bbd58e884758bf42984ca363b9e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESPANOL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">El territorio espa&#241;ol es el &#225;rea geogr&#225;fica donde se realizan estudios sobre la natremia y la hiponatremia en pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d2">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15040</data>
      <data key="d7">a5ce7e4fd5b24b9f90f65c6555eb47d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIPOPROTEINEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La hipoproteinemia es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica caracterizada por niveles bajos de prote&#237;nas en la sangre, que puede influir en la natremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15041</data>
      <data key="d7">0215fb9f622c4ee49b3ea30cda2538ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EDEMA PULMONAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El edema pulmonar es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que puede ser un signo de hiponatremia hipervol&#233;mica y se caracteriza por la acumulaci&#243;n de l&#237;quido en los pulmones.</data>
      <data key="d2">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15042</data>
      <data key="d7">40c75120fcaa491faee21c5edda4ac54</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ORTOSTATISMO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El ortostatismo es una condici&#243;n que se refiere a la ca&#237;da de la presi&#243;n arterial al ponerse de pie, que puede indicar hipovolemia en pacientes con hiponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15043</data>
      <data key="d7">301c388135964c0caff50c585bda4145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIRROSIS HEPATICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cirrhosis hep&#225;tica is a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver caused by many forms of liver diseases and conditions, such as hepatitis and chronic alcoholism.</data>
      <data key="d2">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15044</data>
      <data key="d7">16d13e3776dc4f49a13c41214d6e6596</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIUR&#201;TICOS TIAZIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Diur&#233;ticos tiazida are a class of diuretics that are commonly used to treat high blood pressure and can cause hiponatremia in some patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d3">1429</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15045</data>
      <data key="d7">84de94f5744a4c0bafd5ebd80654b34c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIUR&#201;TICOS DEL GRUPO TIAZIDA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Diur&#233;ticos del grupo tiazida are a class of medications commonly used to treat high blood pressure and fluid retention, which can lead to conditions like hiponatremia in some patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1427</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15046</data>
      <data key="d7">047242fddb0b45c58e3e0daafae930e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria is a condition where the adrenal glands do not produce sufficient steroid hormones, which can contribute to electrolyte imbalances such as hyperkalemia and metabolic acidosis.</data>
      <data key="d2">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1430</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15047</data>
      <data key="d7">2f3dcbedb58c4d90a84eb791e464785d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GTTK">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">GTTK is a diagnostic test used to evaluate the function of mineralocorticoid receptors and assess aldosterone levels in patients with suspected adrenal insufficiency.</data>
      <data key="d2">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d3">1430</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15048</data>
      <data key="d7">cb2b135b952e4860ad3f0094158dcca4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELLISON DH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ellison DH is a researcher who contributed to the understanding of SIADH and its diagnostic criteria, as referenced in the New England Journal of Medicine.</data>
      <data key="d2">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15049</data>
      <data key="d7">a90105e44b0f4686b9475c1f78659c99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VERBALIS ET AL.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Verbalis et al. are researchers who provided insights into the main causes of SIADH, as referenced in The American Journal of Medicine.</data>
      <data key="d2">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15050</data>
      <data key="d7">4df8960cd7694d31a905589fa9ab4916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL" (central nervous system, CNS) plays a vital role in the proper development of swallowing and feeding behaviors in children. Additionally, the CNS can be impacted by a range of disorders, such as tumors and inflammatory diseases, which may result in conditions like Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH). This highlights the importance of the CNS not only in developmental processes but also in its susceptibility to various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7,addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d3">1178</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15051</data>
      <data key="d7">88f66f5e4e174aa5acd1222a3034bd66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARMACOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pharmacological factors can stimulate the secretion of ADH, leading to SIADH, as discussed in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
