    </node>
    <node id="CONIVAPT&#193;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Conivapt&#225;n is a medication that functions as a vasopressin receptor antagonist, specifically designed to treat hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. It is administered intravenously and works by antagonizing the effects of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), thereby helping to restore normal sodium levels in patients.</data>
      <data key="d2">500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d3">1420</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15072</data>
      <data key="d7">6007f20f1f174a0585ce3825779b31ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FURST">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">La f&#243;rmula de Furst es un c&#225;lculo utilizado para estimar la capacidad renal de eliminar agua libre, relevante en el manejo de la hiponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1424</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15073</data>
      <data key="d7">f77b6394f3e44bb6ab47f1263c7ec431</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTOXICACI&#211;N AGUDA DE AGUA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">La intoxicaci&#243;n aguda de agua es una condici&#243;n que puede llevar a hiponatremia, resultando de la ingesta excesiva de agua en un corto per&#237;odo de tiempo.</data>
      <data key="d2">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d3">1424</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15074</data>
      <data key="d7">1aba2fe7480842bd813528a8b9c44120</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FURSEMIDE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Furosemide is a medication used to promote the elimination of free water in patients with SIADH, administered either intravenously or orally.</data>
      <data key="d2">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7</data>
      <data key="d3">1422</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15075</data>
      <data key="d7">5729a809b30f46148d25a4fd5a0807a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AZOTEMIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Azotemia is a medical condition characterized by an excess of nitrogenous waste products in the blood, often due to kidney dysfunction.</data>
      <data key="d2">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7</data>
      <data key="d3">1422</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15076</data>
      <data key="d7">fdf2684935094d2482b5c8a310ffea4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FURST FORMULA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Furst formula is a calculation utilized in the medical field to estimate renal capacity for eliminating free water, particularly in patients diagnosed with Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it serves as a method for calculating sodium and potassium levels in patients experiencing hyponatremia. This dual application highlights the formula's importance in managing electrolyte imbalances and assessing renal function in specific clinical scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d2">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215</data>
      <data key="d3">1426</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15077</data>
      <data key="d7">d22b0d8609c54752be129d1702833ee3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR" is a comprehensive multidisciplinary algorithm designed for the management of hyponatremia, particularly in cases secondary to the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). This algorithm offers detailed guidelines for treatment options, ensuring effective management of hyponatremia in patients. It is especially relevant for individuals receiving artificial nutrition, providing tailored recommendations to address their specific needs. Overall, the algorithm serves as a crucial tool for healthcare professionals in optimizing the care of patients with hyponatremia.</data>
      <data key="d2">306519cca8810e0ff1c973128a75200a,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d3">1421</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15078</data>
      <data key="d7">91b4d31701974ea7994e3a2e84f90f0e</data>
    </node>
