    <node id="ENDOCRINOL NUTR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">ENDOCRINOL NUTR is a journal that has contributed to the field of endocrinology and nutrition by publishing significant studies and reviews. In 2013, it published a study focused on the management of hyponatremia caused by the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), conducted by the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service of Hospital Cl&#237;nico San Carlos. Additionally, in 2014, the journal published a systematic review examining the use of urea as a treatment option for managing SIADH. These publications highlight the journal's commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in endocrinology and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">b96414a52f13cac336436d9e8173baef</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15181</data>
      <data key="d7">2c67ab3d12314ebe92f9375df047cfbc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRIT CARE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">CRIT CARE is a journal dedicated to publishing research in the field of critical care medicine, encompassing a wide range of topics, including pediatric care. In 2010, the journal featured a study focused on the treatment of euvolemic hyponatremia within the intensive care unit, highlighting its commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in critical care settings.</data>
