    <node id="NCHS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The National Center for Health Statistics (NCHS) is an organization that provides data on the growth and nutrition of school-aged children and adolescents in the United States. However, it is important to note that the NCHS was replaced by the CDC's 2000 growth standards in the United States, indicating a shift in the authority and standards used for assessing growth and nutrition in this demographic.</data>
      <data key="d2">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
