      <data key="d1">The term "Schofield" refers to a set of equations utilized for estimating basal metabolic expenditure, particularly in children, by taking into account their weight and height. These equations are significant in the context of predicting energy requirements for patients, especially pediatric populations. The Schofield equations provide a valuable tool for healthcare professionals in assessing the metabolic needs of children, ensuring appropriate nutritional support and energy balance.</data>
