    <node id="ALIMENTACI&#211;N COMPLEMENTARIA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">ALIMENTACI&#211;N COMPLEMENTARIA refers to the crucial period in an infant's dietary development when complementary foods are introduced alongside breastfeeding. This process typically begins after 17 weeks of age and is recommended to occur before the infant reaches 26 weeks. During this phase, solid foods are gradually incorporated into the infant's diet to ensure they receive adequate nutrition as they grow.</data>
      <data key="d2">11662a6f83b8217976d8c9c5d33fe7fd,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
