    </node>
    <node id="EMBOLISMO A&#201;REO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Air embolism is a condition where air enters the vascular system, which can occur as a complication during catheter insertion.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15597</data>
      <data key="d7">c4d9ca3c206241f78d5c9320fc2dba60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LESI&#211;N DE UN PLEXO NERVIOSO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nerve plexus injury refers to damage to a network of nerves, which can occur as a complication during catheter insertion.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15598</data>
      <data key="d7">fb880a81f81c431588c6aedf660d615a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOCALIZACI&#211;N AN&#211;MALA DEL CAT&#201;TER">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Abnormal catheter placement refers to incorrect positioning of the catheter, which can lead to complications.</data>
      <data key="d2">fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15599</data>
