    <node id="DERECHO SANITARIO">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Health law encompasses regulations and ethical standards that govern medical practices and patient rights.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa</data>
      <data key="d3">1557</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">15799</data>
      <data key="d7">4d46d5207f7e4f6d871aabd9500ef8b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSTITUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Constitution of Spain provides the legal framework for patient rights and healthcare regulations.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa</data>
      <data key="d3">1557</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15800</data>
      <data key="d7">bd61e8449ed6442caa4dd2cc6aa4be9e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARLAMENTO ESPA&#209;OL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Spanish Parliament enacts laws that govern healthcare practices and patient rights in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa</data>
      <data key="d3">1557</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15801</data>
      <data key="d7">0845420b32664205a9bc3ed31a98a68f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMUNIDADES AUT&#211;NOMAS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The "COMUNIDADES AUT&#211;NOMAS" refer to the autonomous communities in Spain, which possess their own regulations and laws concerning healthcare and patient rights. Each autonomous community is responsible for managing health services within its respective jurisdiction, leading to variations in the organization and regulation of healthcare practices. Notably, there are differences in the regulation of home artificial nutrition across these communities, reflecting the diverse approaches to healthcare management within Spain's autonomous regions.</data>
      <data key="d2">123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,7c815eb3ecbf3e8cb61d3f9e27d9e061</data>
      <data key="d3">1918</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15802</data>
      <data key="d7">1acaecfde335491d9b7535c2750b9c96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HUELGA DE HAMBRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"HUELGA DE HAMBRE" refers to a hunger strike, which is a form of protest where individuals refuse to eat in order to draw attention to their demands or grievances, particularly in detention settings. This method of protest is often undertaken by inmates who seek to highlight their conditions or treatment. While hunger strikes can be a powerful means of advocacy, they also pose significant ethical dilemmas in healthcare, especially concerning patient rights and the implications for medical intervention. Additionally, engaging in a huelga de hambre carries serious risks, including the potential for death or permanent harm to the individuals involved.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8ce52208981fd781dcf23f690f6c3c,3a39d5a157094736650455097e986fdd,5099515cbc35bc6330fb794c4f1d715d,574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,87ab96c9e47970751fc97c244c4b4534,f8440456e04065bd27e87482b8d2db89</data>
      <data key="d3">1938</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">15803</data>
      <data key="d7">bdb47912cf224894b0886d00b1260961</data>
    </node>
    <node id="M&#201;DICO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">M&#201;DICO refers to a healthcare professional who plays a crucial role in diagnosing and treating patients. This individual is responsible for evaluating the necessity of treatment and may intervene in cases of involuntary hospitalization. Additionally, M&#201;DICO must navigate various ethical dilemmas in their practice, ensuring that patient care is both effective and ethically sound.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa,eaa675a346becd53a4fcfacbb99def88</data>
      <data key="d3">1080</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15804</data>
      <data key="d7">675224363c7f4ba9848d28c737d32d36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALORES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Values are fundamental beliefs that influence ethical decision-making in healthcare.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15805</data>
      <data key="d7">1062c00499164e0aa9613617e1e6a07c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIGNIDAD HUMANA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Human dignity is a core principle that underpins ethical considerations in medical practice and patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">574c4f0c1e9d196b5007cf183174ecaa</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15806</data>
      <data key="d7">bd55756cc1df4a3c87665049f9f46b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOCIEDAD ESPA&#209;OLA DE CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sociedad Espa&#241;ola de Cuidados Paliativos (SECPAL) is an organization that addresses issues related to palliative care and ethical decisions at the end of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d</data>
      <data key="d3">42</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15807</data>
      <data key="d7">158304b4827e4b4783bde16669f5e7b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CULTURA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mediterranean culture is characterized by its approach to care and treatment, emphasizing family protection and the importance of hydration and nutrition as symbols of care.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d</data>
      <data key="d3">42</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15808</data>
      <data key="d7">a71bc087800445eeb0e04d0070c2ee2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CULTURA ANGLOSAXONA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Anglo-Saxon culture emphasizes individual autonomy and the right to make informed decisions regarding health care, particularly at the end of life.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d</data>
      <data key="d3">42</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15809</data>
      <data key="d7">5a11836a04904203bc6ed7704364c81f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PACIENTES TERMINALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Terminal patients are those who have exhausted therapeutic options and have a limited life expectancy, often facing ethical and legal dilemmas in their care.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d</data>
      <data key="d3">42</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">15810</data>
      <data key="d7">2ae9a9ee2e034463b356e46b243b96a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DECISION &#201;TICA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">An ethical decision is a choice made regarding the care of individuals, particularly in critical situations such as end-of-life care, which can have irreversible consequences.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d</data>
      <data key="d3">42</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15811</data>
      <data key="d7">07129a0fc1f84aa39a105f99a220516c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">CUIDADO refers to the concept of care, which encompasses the actions taken to support and maintain the health and well-being of individuals, particularly in medical contexts. This notion of care extends to providing support for individuals, especially at the end of life, and is viewed variably across different cultures.</data>
      <data key="d2">46c8c4b701aeb8284e92c06443f5128d,bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1181</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15812</data>
      <data key="d7">2fb585c3cfa94d399f0b6511fad01587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TERRY SCHIAVO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Terry Schiavo was a woman involved in a highly publicized legal case regarding the withdrawal of life support and enteral nutrition due to her persistent vegetative state.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1190</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15813</data>
      <data key="d7">88d8fcbf1b124f1ea6c4b274f33acbfe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUGLANA ENGLANO">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Euglana Englano is another individual referenced in discussions about the ethical and legal implications of withdrawing enteral nutrition in patients with permanent vegetative states.</data>
      <data key="d2">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1190</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15814</data>
      <data key="d7">965d68d78e70486baf01782a1764ae58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUTONOM&#205;A DEL PACIENTE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">AUTONOM&#205;A DEL PACIENTE refers to the right of patients to make informed decisions regarding their medical care and treatment. This concept emphasizes that patients have the authority to choose their course of action in healthcare matters, including critical aspects such as nutrition and hydration. The principle of patient autonomy underscores the importance of informed consent and the respect for individual preferences in the context of medical decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d2">4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a,bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1190</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">15815</data>
      <data key="d7">32d2fc76aaae43e8a5313dd529d865ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO" refers to the process of obtaining voluntary agreement from participants before they engage in clinical trials or medical treatments. It is a fundamental aspect of healthcare that requires patients to provide their free and informed consent after receiving adequate information about the proposed interventions. This process is both a legal and ethical obligation, ensuring that patients are fully aware of and agree to the medical procedures and treatments they will undergo. In summary, "CONSENTIMIENTO INFORMADO" is essential for protecting patient autonomy and ensuring informed decision-making in medical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fd4d7a9544dd7c2999b9ce1708919bc,4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a,9934fdd98a0d66fb3ff7ac1b56b18460,bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27,e475fe60f9aab6773eddfe8bad25eef6</data>
      <data key="d3">1065</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">15816</data>
      <data key="d7">a5e951539b7041b29bfaceedb42f4a0e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS are legal documents that enable individuals to outline their preferences for medical treatment in situations where they may become unable to communicate their wishes. These documents serve as a means for individuals to express their desires regarding medical care, ensuring that their treatment aligns with their values and choices, even when they cannot voice them.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a,bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1190</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15817</data>
      <data key="d7">5e67cf3b77ba48f4bbbf30baf65357b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TESTAMENTO VITAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The "TESTAMENTO VITAL," also known as a living will, is a legal document that serves as an advance directive. It specifies an individual's preferences regarding medical treatment and life-sustaining measures in situations where they are unable to make decisions for themselves. This document outlines the person's wishes concerning their medical care, ensuring that their preferences are respected even when they cannot communicate them directly.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a,bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d3">1190</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15818</data>
      <data key="d7">deeaf2a1539f409a812274f1f43b4f87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEGO&#209;A ROM&#193;N">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Bego&#241;a Rom&#225;n is a professor at the University of Barcelona, where she contributes to the academic community through her teaching and research. In addition to her academic role, she serves as the President of the Ethics Committee of Social Services in Catalonia, overseeing ethical standards and practices within the social services sector. Furthermore, she is a member of the Bioethics Committee of Catalonia, where she engages in discussions and decisions regarding ethical issues in the field of bioethics.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a,3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">15819</data>
      <data key="d7">859d5cd4cfd24e589929aa905e814cd9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSITY OF BARCELONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The University of Barcelona is a public university in Spain where Bego&#241;a Rom&#225;n teaches.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15820</data>
      <data key="d7">60bd86b6aedf49e5b01e42d07800397f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CATALONIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Catalonia is an autonomous community in northeastern Spain, where the Ethics Committee of Social Services operates.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15821</data>
      <data key="d7">cb02dd2d791c48ff87f539cb2a8866c5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ETHICS COMMITTEE OF SOCIAL SERVICES OF CATALONIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ethics Committee of Social Services of Catalonia is responsible for addressing ethical issues in social services in the region.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15822</data>
      <data key="d7">28bca7a0497f4d658b4fcbf2ec869c02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIOETHICS COMMITTEE OF CATALONIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Bioethics Committee of Catalonia provides guidance on ethical issues related to health and medical practices in the region.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15823</data>
      <data key="d7">e808c99a28904767a506c2e68b3deb0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONFLICTOS &#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Conflictos &#233;ticos refer to ethical dilemmas that arise in medical and healthcare settings, particularly concerning end-of-life decisions and patient autonomy.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15824</data>
      <data key="d7">85defe19a85b4ad9baafa26f1a62f36a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRINCIPIO DE PROPORCIONALIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">El principio de proporcionalidad is an ethical principle that states that medical treatment should only be provided if the benefits outweigh the burdens for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15825</data>
      <data key="d7">fe7559c048f2492db43b09873dee82ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUIDADOS B&#193;SICOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cuidados b&#225;sicos refer to fundamental care practices provided to all individuals, including those who are unable to eat or drink normally.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15826</data>
      <data key="d7">fff3979b24d64a3c9922c6627e027527</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACUERDOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Acuerdos refer to agreements made among healthcare professionals, patients, and families regarding treatment decisions, especially in complex cases.</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15827</data>
      <data key="d7">007a5d01737a4f6f9f079962ee1e5f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MODELOS CULTURALES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Modelos culturales refer to the cultural frameworks that influence healthcare practices and decision-making processes in different societies.)&lt;|COMPLETE|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">05d8d8e5292374b82ba2b4afdd3d700a</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">15828</data>
      <data key="d7">1420adcafba943739dcd87536bc50277</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSIDAD DE BARCELONA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The University of Barcelona is an educational institution where Bego&#241;a Rom&#225;n teaches.</data>
      <data key="d2">3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1577</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">15829</data>
      <data key="d7">309c56ec925c4bdd92eaa4b5b21b756f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIEGO GRACIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Diego Gracia is a professor who advocates for a deliberative process in clinical nutrition decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d2">3775bd9e3567a81cf7b7acf1e2741f6f</data>
      <data key="d3">1578</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15830</data>
