    </node>
    <node id="TRIBUNAL CONSTITUCIONAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tribunal Constitucional, also known as the Constitutional Court of Spain, serves as the highest authority in matters concerning the constitutionality of laws and the protection of fundamental rights within the country. It plays a crucial role in ensuring that both legislative actions and governmental measures adhere to the Spanish Constitution. Notably, the Tribunal has made significant rulings regarding the rights of inmates, including those who engage in hunger strikes, thereby influencing the legal landscape surrounding human rights in Spain. Through its decisions, the Tribunal Constitucional upholds the principles of justice and constitutional governance, reinforcing the rule of law in the nation.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f8ce52208981fd781dcf23f690f6c3c,87ab96c9e47970751fc97c244c4b4534,f8440456e04065bd27e87482b8d2db89</data>
