    </node>
    <node id="RECURSOS SANITARIOS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">"RECURSOS SANITARIOS" refers to the various resources utilized in healthcare, encompassing all the tools, personnel, materials, and facilities necessary for providing medical care. These resources are essential for effective healthcare delivery and are subject to analysis for cost-effectiveness. The allocation of "recursos sanitarios" is crucial in the micro-management of healthcare services, ensuring that the right inputs are available for optimal patient care.</data>
      <data key="d2">66c092d222e72c03a1f36507ce355cd4,c1fce1d059978d0a9ee9e63f75c8ca98,f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1274</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">15928</data>
      <data key="d7">04fcedd93faf4b5d9a0d78e52222d41b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MACROGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Macrogesti&#243;n represents the health policy perspective where the state intervenes to enhance equity and correct market dysfunctions.</data>
      <data key="d2">f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1272</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
