      <data key="d6">15929</data>
      <data key="d7">f12c59f383c34f04b84571212784c97e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MESOGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">MESOGESTI&#211;N refers to a management approach that emphasizes the decentralization of management responsibilities to healthcare centers. This strategy aims to enhance service delivery and operational efficiency within the healthcare system. It involves the coordination and motivation of staff within these centers, ensuring that they operate effectively within a regulated environment. By focusing on local management, MESOGESTI&#211;N seeks to improve the overall quality of healthcare services provided to the community.</data>
      <data key="d2">26765fd0d663c8708d7bd6a545de3e2c,f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1273</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">4</data>
      <data key="d6">15930</data>
      <data key="d7">3f22e2e7081c4db9b3060a6dc433fb6a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Microgesti&#243;n refers to the decentralization of management within healthcare settings, empowering individual healthcare professionals to enhance efficiency and accountability. This approach necessitates the active involvement of health center staff, particularly clinicians, who are responsible for making decisions that impact approximately 70% of health resources. By distributing management responsibilities, Microgesti&#243;n aims to improve the overall effectiveness of healthcare delivery.</data>
      <data key="d2">26765fd0d663c8708d7bd6a545de3e2c,f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1274</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">15931</data>
      <data key="d7">692d6c35ec854720afc152842279954e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EEIS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Evaluaci&#243;n econ&#243;mica de las intervenciones sanitarias (EEIS) is a process that allows for informed decision-making regarding health interventions based on cost-effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d2">f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d3">1272</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
