      <data key="d6">16006</data>
      <data key="d7">2db268c8eda5450b95d3159f8d0eae0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008 is a quality management standard that was commonly used before being replaced by UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">336</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16007</data>
      <data key="d7">da5b6cc123b545148ff94b60c453a322</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015 is the updated quality management standard that became mandatory in 2017.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">336</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16008</data>
      <data key="d7">758734daa8184a01916e9b48117e743b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIMENSIONES DE CALIDAD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dimensiones de calidad" refers to the criteria and various aspects used to evaluate the quality of healthcare services. This concept encompasses multiple dimensions, including structure, process, and outcome dimensions, as well as accessibility, adequacy, and effectiveness. Together, these dimensions provide a comprehensive framework for assessing the overall quality of healthcare delivery.</data>
      <data key="d2">03b047c49cda5e7bb642efcc9109ccc6,0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">922</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">16009</data>
      <data key="d7">adf4479fa43b4fe3877b95c83302bd3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESTRUCTURA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Estructura refers to the characteristics of the environment in which healthcare is provided, including the necessary resources.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">922</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16010</data>
      <data key="d7">4764ac2458194f31985e5ccc51992f99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROCESO">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Proceso refers to the utilization of resources in the delivery of healthcare services, which can be related to both patients and organizations.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">922</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16011</data>
      <data key="d7">50124b723117411d9791f360c999325f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESULTADOS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Resultados refer to the effects of healthcare interventions on individuals or society, including both intermediate and final outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e4628d74bee9cdd38f544f119527748</data>
      <data key="d3">922</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16012</data>
      <data key="d7">402259a2e3954194a9f8cbecce49ea0b</data>
    </node>
