    </node>
    <node id="MEZCLA">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mezcla refers to the mixing process of ingredients in clinical nutrition, which is crucial for achieving the desired consistency and stability.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9e4179f945ec9152199511522d70159</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16106</data>
      <data key="d7">ee6d12e6f6f84e55aee9ac6d7926ea91</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRODUCTO FINAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Producto final refers to the end product of clinical nutrition formulations, which must meet specific quality and stability standards.</data>
      <data key="d2">d9e4179f945ec9152199511522d70159</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16107</data>
      <data key="d7">a75fe75737fb48e9a3e0ad9d95ddb9bc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PART&#205;CULAS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Part&#237;culas refer to the small components in mixtures that can affect the overall stability and quality of clinical nutrition products.</data>
