    </node>
    <node id="PHOSPHATE STABILITY TEST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The phosphate stability test involves subjecting a product to an acidic environment and heat to determine its stability and coagulation properties.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">16123</data>
      <data key="d7">c6e0e5f7bb7442638725301d19001473</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROBIOLOGICAL CONTROLS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microbiological controls are evaluations conducted to confirm the effectiveness of thermal treatment in ensuring product sterility and safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16124</data>
      <data key="d7">9a554ac088aa4896ab84ef7307251f8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHYSICAL-CHEMICAL CONTROLS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Physical-chemical controls are measures taken during product development to assess various attributes such as pH, viscosity, and particle size distribution.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16125</data>
      <data key="d7">6f4c595f1132425cb0b615d9f8250a27</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENSORY EVALUATION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sensory evaluation involves internal tastings to assess and select samples based on their organoleptic properties like color, odor, flavor, and texture.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16126</data>
      <data key="d7">0d2d342ee9174bc0a127c7fa5776f871</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LABORATORY SCALE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Laboratory scale refers to the initial phase of product development where experiments are conducted to achieve desired results before scaling up.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16127</data>
      <data key="d7">0558da74e5c24e63896ce3467c545643</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEMI-INDUSTRIAL SCALE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Semi-industrial scale is the phase where the laboratory protocol is reproduced in a production plant at a larger volume than laboratory scale.</data>
      <data key="d2">067a2eec3da66594167147aca615fa03</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">16128</data>
