    <node id="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL INFANTIL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Insuficiencia renal infantil is a condition that compromises the growth of the patient and can lead to malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf</data>
      <data key="d3">1131</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16284</data>
      <data key="d7">1b8b990992be4169bde1276d59ed7289</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NED">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">NED is a multifaceted entity that encompasses both a nutritional support program and a medical condition. As a nutritional support program, NED focuses on providing home care for elderly patients, specifically managing their nutritional needs to enhance their quality of life. Additionally, NED refers to a nutritional therapy designed for patients, particularly those suffering from gastrointestinal cancer, aimed at maintaining weight and improving overall quality of life. The term NED also stands for Nutrici&#243;n Enteral Domiciliaria, which signifies enteral nutrition administered at home, with varying regulations and practices across different countries. Furthermore, NED has been studied epidemiologically as a medical condition in various countries, highlighting its significance in both clinical and nutritional contexts.</data>
      <data key="d2">0d083c309fb6f4d0d16c0e2b23ea5c8b,29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721,eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1928</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">27</data>
      <data key="d6">16285</data>
      <data key="d7">c7f0645d632d4facafbe6089d56bdbb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SNS stands for Sistema Nacional de Salud, the national health system in Spain that includes provisions for NPD and NED.</data>
      <data key="d2">f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1929</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">16286</data>
      <data key="d7">5ee8bd45fb3c4ac28bac6c5bee32da9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="B&#201;LGICA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">B&#233;lgica is Belgium, where patients may have to cover part of the costs for NED.</data>
      <data key="d2">f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1928</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">16287</data>
      <data key="d7">40e04e22e7994ce5a2706268637b90ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POLONIA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Polonia refers to Poland, a country that is included in the epidemiological study of NED. In this context, patients in Poland may be required to cover a portion of the costs associated with NED.</data>
      <data key="d2">eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d3">1928</data>
