    </node>
    <node id="SUSTAIN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">SUSTAIN is A.S.P.E.N.'s National Patient Registry for Nutrition Care, specifically designed to focus on home parenteral nutrition outcomes. Established in 2011, SUSTAIN aims to include 100% of incident and prevalent patients with nutrition-related disorders (NPD). This comprehensive registry serves as a vital resource for tracking and improving the quality of nutrition care provided to patients receiving home parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d2">efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608,fff76d1cd0e64233a5727a707d80e2b9</data>
      <data key="d3">563</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">16301</data>
      <data key="d7">e7dfb5e8eafd4b35a0b7e6e6d209dd04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="USA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The USA is a country where the OASIS registry was established to track patients with NPD.</data>
