    <node id="NI&#209;OS/AS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "Ni&#241;os/as" refers to children categorized by specific age groups for health and demographic statistics, encompassing those aged 1 to 19 years. More specifically, it includes children aged 1-3 years, 4-8 years, 9-13 years, and 14-18 years. This categorization is important for establishing dietary intake recommendations and guidelines, particularly concerning essential nutrients such as sodium and other minerals. Ni&#241;os/as are also included in dietary reference intake guidelines, which provide tailored dietary recommendations to support their health and development during these critical growth stages.</data>
      <data key="d2">4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,6c65beaf6ed5575b0945052270630136,8ebb2b77b6f63f52544326a7ea94df61,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
