    <node id="FLUOR">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">FLUOR, commonly known as fluoride, is a mineral recognized for its role in preventing dental cavities. It is essential for maintaining oral health, and its dietary reference intake is specified for various age groups in health guidelines. The recommended daily intake levels of fluoride are outlined in dietary guidelines to ensure adequate consumption for optimal health benefits.</data>
      <data key="d2">565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d3">583</data>
      <data key="d4">2</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">16550</data>
      <data key="d7">28f451cb940f45f7b4c4c76d3505e925</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7-12 MESES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The term "7-12 meses" refers to the age group of infants aged 7 to 12 months. This period is characterized by specific dietary recommendations tailored to meet the nutritional needs of infants as they transition from exclusive breastfeeding or formula feeding to the introduction of solid foods. During this stage, it is essential to provide a balanced diet that supports growth and development, ensuring that infants receive the necessary nutrients for their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d2">565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be,74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445</data>
