    </edge>
    <edge source="SENPE" target="ANECIPN">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SENPE and ANECIPN collaborate in the field of pediatric enteral nutrition, focusing on establishing standards for this area in Spain. Their partnership aims to enhance the quality and consistency of enteral nutrition practices for pediatric patients, ensuring that they receive optimal care and support.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036</data>
      <data key="d11">c394d0b88c0f42da9315c750a501a02a</data>
      <data key="d12">59</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SENPE" target="SECP">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SENPE and SECP are organizations that collaborate in the development of consensus documents focused on pediatric nutrition. They work together to establish clinical nutrition and metabolism standards specifically tailored for pediatric patients, ensuring that best practices are followed in the care and treatment of children.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a69e2f952998ea5b7109ad2d51a7849,b410dfc796e4ac9178ac19ac368e2036</data>
      <data key="d11">06d79b08bfe646d5aa503b2be00c1573</data>
      <data key="d12">60</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SENPE" target="MADRID">
