      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="DISFAGIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a broader term that encompasses oropharyngeal dysphagia, which is specifically addressed in the book.</data>
      <data key="d10">734812860aa1e2e5c5ae35a39eb5a865</data>
      <data key="d11">cfbe30bd4d604a438de75a4987ec3b84</data>
      <data key="d12">101</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="ENFERMEDADES NEUROL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oropharyngeal dysphagia is commonly associated with neurological diseases, affecting a significant percentage of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">2d07618f91664c4c87241908df204994</data>
      <data key="d12">102</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="QUIMIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chemotherapy can lead to oropharyngeal dysphagia in patients undergoing treatment for head and neck tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">e74441a4b60b4f87bd65fb2168718fca</data>
      <data key="d12">103</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="RADIOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Radiotherapy is a treatment that can result in oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in patients with head and neck cancers</data>
      <data key="d10">ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">0220aec5e2b14027b7667acd61a5c177</data>
      <data key="d12">104</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="NEUMON&#205;AS POR ASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oropharyngeal dysphagia can lead to aspiration pneumonia, which is a serious complication</data>
      <data key="d10">ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">012287f9dcb54557b58a1a6946b83cce</data>
      <data key="d12">105</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="DESHIDRATACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dehydration is a common consequence of oropharyngeal dysphagia, affecting patient health</data>
      <data key="d10">ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">0e5ced24e60a47ce94a71732ad1df945</data>
      <data key="d12">106</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oropharyngeal dysphagia and malnutrition are closely interconnected, with malnutrition being a common consequence of oropharyngeal dysphagia that significantly affects patient health. The presence of oropharyngeal dysphagia poses a substantial risk for malnutrition, which in turn impacts recovery and overall health outcomes for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">a76f25b0b56092f8125f49ec456f78df,ea0b88195d04b227bedf7fa3cb3b6513</data>
      <data key="d11">8da209901db243ddb79a23ccae867a09</data>
      <data key="d12">107</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="BOLLO ALIMENTICIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La disfagia orofar&#237;ngea se refiere a la dificultad en el paso del bolo alimenticio desde la boca al es&#243;fago.</data>
      <data key="d10">d2aaa88e54c474e2077b1e3791828964</data>
      <data key="d11">0015e42d32d947baab4269e7d8339384</data>
      <data key="d12">108</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="EES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Disfagia orofar&#237;ngea is often related to dysfunction of the EES, which can lead to swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d11">00e764ff7d8147208c84f5771b43faeb</data>
      <data key="d12">109</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Crohn's disease can cause symptoms of oropharyngeal dysphagia due to inflammation and structural changes in the gastrointestinal tract.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d11">9d0a27a9fd5442d4a0448f7257ca011b</data>
      <data key="d12">110</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="MIOSITIS POR CUERPOS DE INCLUSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Inclusion body myositis can lead to muscle weakness affecting swallowing, resulting in oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d11">d63cb597598444e79cd5eb4f91225aea</data>
      <data key="d12">111</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="EJERCICIO SHAKER">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Shaker exercise is a therapeutic approach to improve swallowing function in patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d11">f540b2c20c224ebb9d181fe627164628</data>
      <data key="d12">112</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="MANIOBRA DE MENDELSOHN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mendelsohn maneuver is a technique used to enhance swallowing coordination in individuals with oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4707350a1cb759e58f3d611445992ba</data>
      <data key="d11">b546cbbc001241ce99447a240c3a1f39</data>
      <data key="d12">113</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="NEUMON&#205;A POR ASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia orofar&#237;ngea is a primary factor leading to aspiration pneumonia due to swallowing difficulties</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d11">97a4a6fc93f54631ae10d750b103c8dc</data>
      <data key="d12">114</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="PACIENTES">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia orofar&#237;ngea is a condition that affects patients, requiring careful attention and treatment. Individuals suffering from this type of dysphagia are at an increased risk for aspiration pneumonia and other related complications, highlighting the importance of proper management and intervention for these patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7,754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462</data>
      <data key="d11">edfe652f71124ca0958604da8344cab4</data>
      <data key="d12">115</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="ENFERMEDADES NEURODEGENERATIVAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neurodegenerative diseases often lead to dysphagia, increasing the risk of aspiration pneumonia</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d11">472447c31003408dbb38cc011a16f8fa</data>
      <data key="d12">116</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="ACCIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A cerebrovascular accident can cause dysphagia, which is a risk factor for aspiration pneumonia</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d11">7b660c15d793407186631f7aebaa4bde</data>
      <data key="d12">117</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="SENSORIALIDAD LAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Impaired laryngeal sensitivity can lead to dysphagia and increase the risk of aspiration</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d11">07100aa2ded545a59652a2f21794296c</data>
      <data key="d12">118</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" target="REFLEJO TUSIGENO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysfunction of the cough reflex can contribute to the risk of aspiration pneumonia in dysphagic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">60e73f6536e23a61362ac00a9a9149d7</data>
      <data key="d11">453ebf89763f44249ba7a765171ae213</data>
      <data key="d12">119</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
