      <data key="d9">Spain performs a significant number of liver transplants annually, indicating a relationship between the country and the procedure</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">546dcc955edc4cadbb8fc6df2b683f52</data>
      <data key="d12">235</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Heart Association's guidelines are applicable to Spain, which also fails to meet the recommended saturated fat intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">59a6475dbe0ccafda60f2647dea78371</data>
      <data key="d11">3a7482d07afa4900b02bedd6186a075f</data>
      <data key="d12">236</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="SOCIETY EUROPEA DE CARDIOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Society of Cardiology's recommendations are relevant to Spain, which does not meet the suggested fat intake levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">59a6475dbe0ccafda60f2647dea78371</data>
      <data key="d11">58e4f3084ada453980dbec57f191c756</data>
      <data key="d12">237</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="PREDIMED">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PREDIMED study was conducted in Spain, highlighting the impact of the Mediterranean diet on the local population's health.</data>
      <data key="d10">633a3a90a82e02d05096b361ddba3ad7</data>
      <data key="d11">66a081d42755408b86f9a390505afc3e</data>
      <data key="d12">238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Spain has an average potassium intake of 4.87 g/day, which is relevant to dietary discussions about potassium levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">31b61ae47905168ef430433c9eb5237a</data>
      <data key="d11">4b108e735c124b2e9ee611a229032429</data>
      <data key="d12">239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic kidney disease affects approximately 10% of the adult population in Spain</data>
      <data key="d10">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d11">ad47e08b259041dd9f0cc925de22b76b</data>
      <data key="d12">240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="LITIASIS BILIAR">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In Spain, biliary lithiasis is the most common cause of acute pancreatitis, particularly among women</data>
      <data key="d10">71df6da8c96a533357f4380fd6066417</data>
      <data key="d11">eba2933841a84f459a8363f159374462</data>
      <data key="d12">241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">En Espa&#241;a, se ha encontrado una prevalencia de nutrici&#243;n parenteral en adultos, lo que refleja la necesidad de este tratamiento en la poblaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">947003ce93f64108bac3687ba2ad34dc</data>
      <data key="d12">242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">En Espa&#241;a se ha documentado una prevalencia significativa de EPOC, lo que indica un impacto importante en la salud p&#250;blica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22</data>
      <data key="d11">3c7ff08bb2694d26937e6c35af291aa3</data>
      <data key="d12">243</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="GALICIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galicia is an autonomous community within Spain, which has its own regulations regarding NED.</data>
      <data key="d10">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2</data>
      <data key="d11">f80a7f1e71894c9aa9774ee5c77fb7cd</data>
      <data key="d12">244</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="CATALU&#209;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Catalu&#241;a is an autonomous community in Spain with specific practices for the dispensing of NED products.</data>
      <data key="d10">0df5ab4ef9db16004ddebefc8290f5f2</data>
      <data key="d11">c2714ebef0064419962ef161ca6f09a3</data>
      <data key="d12">245</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="NADYA-SENPE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NADYA-SENPE conducts annual registries of NED in Spain</data>
      <data key="d10">eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10</data>
      <data key="d11">684da93a4c36466c877699cddad6a807</data>
      <data key="d12">246</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="NED">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NED has been studied in Espa&#241;a among other countries</data>
      <data key="d10">eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10</data>
      <data key="d11">30bb41c9cf2b48678ca08e80c33f506e</data>
      <data key="d12">247</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA Y AMBULATORIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The group of Artificial Nutrition Domiciliary and Ambulatory is focused on the situation of NED in Espa&#241;a</data>
      <data key="d10">eab1daf48c7ca09f43fc115a3379cc10</data>
      <data key="d11">6c4ace6ad4ab4f99acc5c4b33e0234b3</data>
      <data key="d12">248</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La legislaci&#243;n en Espa&#241;a regula las decisiones sobre nutrici&#243;n artificial, permitiendo a los pacientes decidir sobre su uso</data>
      <data key="d10">a6ccbda174f6599eeeb2e4cdb00db5f2</data>
      <data key="d11">685ce560ee6b4636bd1aeb56a2ee2de5</data>
      <data key="d12">249</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="THAO-SALUD INFANTIL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">THAO-SALUD INFANTIL is a program implemented in Spain to address public health issues related to obesity.</data>
      <data key="d10">a13a13b249ba729ec581f7a16ec5eae5</data>
      <data key="d11">ccd9001a5c33492b9f0ee05c510d85c0</data>
      <data key="d12">250</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="PROYECTO PREDIMED">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Proyecto PREDIMED se realiz&#243; en Espa&#241;a, lo que indica una relaci&#243;n directa entre el ensayo cl&#237;nico y el pa&#237;s donde se llev&#243; a cabo.</data>
      <data key="d10">dabdb883b39fe459da7aab4a4e7242cb</data>
      <data key="d11">ee4cd7185ad042d3af208dbe617d76af</data>
      <data key="d12">251</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="FESNAD 2010">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FESNAD 2010 guidelines are specifically for the Spanish population</data>
      <data key="d10">acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d11">fe0cf30336174856a7d5cf41d747c9ca</data>
      <data key="d12">252</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPA&#209;A" target="M&#193;LAGA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M&#225;laga is a city located in Spain, known for its studies on health and nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">dbfd111867924ed831f05d8fff01888b</data>
      <data key="d11">ed189dd9362f4e55930bf90762f2cf70</data>
      <data key="d12">253</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="FISIOLOG&#205;A DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Disfagia is a symptom that is studied within the context of the physiology of swallowing</data>
      <data key="d10">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d11">04941b81958f4c8997c306c7dbdad141</data>
      <data key="d12">254</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea" serves as a comprehensive resource for the assessment and management of dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing. This manual offers valuable solutions and insights aimed at effectively managing dysphagia, including practical recipes specifically tailored for individuals experiencing this condition. Through its detailed guidance, the manual addresses the various challenges associated with dysphagia, providing both theoretical knowledge and practical applications to enhance the quality of life for those affected.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,dad5cb424b9586e4e672ed57db1f4fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">d2950f99769749d48cf8349e65ff6e1b</data>
      <data key="d12">255</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="LANCASTER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lancaster has contributed to the definition and understanding of dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d11">0ead1f4130f94fedb8e9e25a7d47a601</data>
      <data key="d12">256</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">34.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia, also known as degluci&#243;n, is defined as a difficulty in the process of swallowing. It directly affects the ability to swallow, making it a central concern in medical assessments. Dysphagia is particularly significant in patients with conditions such as multiple sclerosis or stroke, as it necessitates regular evaluations to monitor and manage the swallowing difficulties. This disorder impairs the capacity to swallow adequately, highlighting the importance of understanding and addressing dysphagia in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ae09eb472a346b355bc66df2fea519f,665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191,b2fcedcb1399bd22a82d188227aa9fad</data>
      <data key="d11">a345bf9320294fa88b99077930994c3d</data>
      <data key="d12">257</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="MORBIMORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Morbimortalidad is a consequence of the complications arising from dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d11">8bd44a37f4894796b6ba1799a60be82b</data>
      <data key="d12">258</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="TRASTORNOS DEL &#193;NIMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mood disorders can be a psychological impact of living with dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d11">36f66cafebec4f6fb3b7833082847926</data>
      <data key="d12">259</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="AISLAMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Isolation can occur as a social consequence for individuals suffering from dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">afc1e23538d13759662d0a4ea2d45191</data>
      <data key="d11">8ba4970ba1f74cb8ae32b6142ba152e3</data>
      <data key="d12">260</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="CEREBRO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El cerebro regula la degluci&#243;n, y su da&#241;o puede resultar en disfagia</data>
      <data key="d10">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d11">c29489dc930f4ed0b26a0a65b99205e3</data>
      <data key="d12">261</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ACCIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La disfagia puede ser una consecuencia del accidente cerebrovascular, afectando la capacidad de tragar</data>
      <data key="d10">f8f8f31481daf6b8d0cc5e103a31b2a9</data>
      <data key="d11">3d0108eb47714fd3a0eb304103fa6de2</data>
      <data key="d12">262</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ACIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La disfagia puede ser una consecuencia del accidente cerebrovascular debido a la p&#233;rdida de conectividad funcional en la red de degluci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d11">180a07c4c8b143f98ccfb991f7c7dc26</data>
      <data key="d12">263</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ENFERMEDAD DE PARKINSON">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia, or difficulty swallowing, is highly prevalent among patients with Parkinson's disease. The condition arises due to changes in swallowing mechanisms caused by the disease's impact on motor pathways. As a result, individuals with Parkinson's may experience significant challenges related to their ability to swallow effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735</data>
      <data key="d11">a556f7d682124301b95c05452655dbdf</data>
      <data key="d12">264</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="P. CLAV&#201;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">P. Clav&#233; ha investigado la disfagia y ha desarrollado m&#233;todos para evaluar su impacto en pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d11">34868a921f7e48da80f292568edd7f7f</data>
      <data key="d12">265</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ESCLEROSIS LATERAL AMIOTR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia, or difficulty swallowing, is a significant concern for patients with Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), known in Spanish as esclerosis lateral amiotr&#243;fica. This condition is associated with dysphagia in a notable percentage of patients, as the disease affects the upper motor neurons, which can lead to complications in the swallowing process. Consequently, individuals with ALS may experience challenges in deglutition due to the impact of the disease on their motor neuron function.</data>
      <data key="d10">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">88c8c388282e44ffb9c22b5e45805278</data>
      <data key="d12">266</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ATROFIA MUSCULAR BULBOESPINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La atrofia muscular bulboespinal puede causar problemas de degluci&#243;n debido a la reorganizaci&#243;n funcional en la corteza sensitivo-motora.</data>
      <data key="d10">665ed3c8d60f8ac770c48c9f59596eea</data>
      <data key="d11">a7ea7e88e5fe45b099d7e80e36f85bc1</data>
      <data key="d12">267</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a common condition affecting elderly patients, leading to difficulties in swallowing</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">0f754b05fa9c475a96aef2d1407649fd</data>
      <data key="d12">268</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Sistema Nacional de Salud addresses the issue of dysphagia as a significant health concern affecting the population</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">762bede9405d4de89e9f24ccf0652dcf</data>
      <data key="d12">269</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ENFERMEDAD DE ALZHEIMER">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alzheimer's disease is associated with a high prevalence of dysphagia among patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">d0ee65a082ec4eeeab7266db469d3e2f</data>
      <data key="d12">270</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ESCLEROSIS M&#218;LTIPLE">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a common complication in patients with multiple sclerosis (esclerosis m&#250;ltiple), necessitating specific nutritional management. This condition is significantly linked to multiple sclerosis, affecting a notable percentage of those diagnosed with the disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ae09eb472a346b355bc66df2fea519f,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">609befa2fe7f4e0cb0fdf3d8d0c691df</data>
      <data key="d12">271</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ACCIDENTES CEREBROVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cerebrovascular accidents are a common cause of dysphagia in affected individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">bc1a520e6c674652b32870180f6d1655</data>
      <data key="d12">272</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="NEUMON&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, can significantly increase the risk of aspiration pneumonia. This makes dysphagia a critical health issue, as the aspiration of food or liquids into the lungs can lead to pneumonia. Therefore, individuals with dysphagia are at a heightened risk for developing pneumonia as a result of this aspiration.</data>
      <data key="d10">98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">a77ca7ed4ecb4637aa7b0ef623f476a6</data>
      <data key="d12">273</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="PA&#205;SES DESARROLLADOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The increase in the elderly population in developed countries is expected to raise the prevalence of dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">56d45e322b2b43168562691a6f041c3d</data>
      <data key="d12">274</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="DIFICULTADES PARA TRAGAR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Difficulties swallowing is synonymous with dysphagia, representing the same health issue</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">4eb0c9b6534a45ed9a2345d3d107943c</data>
      <data key="d12">275</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="PATOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Various pathologies increase the prevalence of dysphagia among affected individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">798b38ee52dc4e03aefe02360b9dd35a</data>
      <data key="d12">276</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="REINO UNIDO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Studies in the United Kingdom indicate a high prevalence of dysphagia among the elderly</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">29290c0db66042ed83c41fa02ee3baec</data>
      <data key="d12">277</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="FRANCIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Research in France shows a significant prevalence of dysphagia in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">3b26213279b04d76bbd2379a3625326b</data>
      <data key="d12">278</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ALEMANIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Germany has reported a lower prevalence of dysphagia compared to other countries</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">218fc82c7a714295a7980699d4aa058e</data>
      <data key="d12">279</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="JAP&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Japan has documented figures related to the prevalence of dysphagia among the elderly</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">4e7cc4c693254c6a9177c4faa0e6496c</data>
      <data key="d12">280</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="PA&#205;SES BAJOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Netherlands has reported prevalence rates of dysphagia among older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">e28f0577e97765bca9099d5dc4a4fcc5</data>
      <data key="d11">d682a04d2c804a288b80328123dfa6a8</data>
      <data key="d12">281</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="EAT-10">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The EAT-10, also known as the Eating Assessment Tool, is a questionnaire designed to assess symptoms of dysphagia in patients. It serves as a screening tool to evaluate the difficulties individuals may experience while eating and swallowing. The EAT-10 is specifically utilized to identify and quantify the severity of dysphagia symptoms, aiding healthcare professionals in diagnosing and managing this condition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d3134a53f89ef62070b5c3b2a7bc136,b44e720874efa74c538dd573ee936378,d96ab48565912e67fdb51ccdf5a100ac</data>
      <data key="d11">c0e5795954c94c6ab07dbc108860f4f5</data>
      <data key="d12">282</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ICTUS">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a common complication that can occur following an ictus (stroke), significantly impacting the nutritional status of affected patients. It is important to recognize that dysphagia may present in individuals who have experienced an ictus, necessitating appropriate treatment to address this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ae09eb472a346b355bc66df2fea519f,9449ed00392e250aa871c689af51a540</data>
      <data key="d11">2eac2bb87d6347d8934ae556248867ad</data>
      <data key="d12">283</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ERGE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia, or difficulty in swallowing, can be a symptom of ERGE (Enfermedad por Reflujo Gastroesof&#225;gico), indicating a significant relationship between swallowing difficulties and esophageal reflux. In particular, ERGE can lead to dysphagia in patients, especially those who have experienced a prolonged course of the condition. This connection highlights the impact of esophageal reflux on swallowing function and the importance of addressing both issues in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6,f7c941bced546a7d607c30a9a5e9d887</data>
      <data key="d11">331ae85373ee430a8b8671b8b3d5e2b4</data>
      <data key="d12">284</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ANILLO DE SCHATZKI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El anillo de Schatzki es una de las causas que puede provocar disfagia en los pacientes</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">e2a12cfba49448f6b5ec604f9c95922f</data>
      <data key="d12">285</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ENDOSCOPIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La endoscopia es el estudio de primera elecci&#243;n para investigar la causa de la disfagia</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">8ab164e9988648c5af89e0d8e44443c0</data>
      <data key="d12">286</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="MANOMETR&#205;A ESOF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La manometr&#237;a esof&#225;gica se utiliza para diagnosticar trastornos motores del es&#243;fago en pacientes con disfagia</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">b59f08d7c90b42a2b2bb50da3458e142</data>
      <data key="d12">287</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ESOFAGITIS EOSINOF&#205;LICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La esofagitis eosinof&#237;lica es una causa frecuente de disfagia diagnosticada mediante endoscopia</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">1e7f06e5ece743eb9bf6701c610a9181</data>
      <data key="d12">288</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="FLUOROSCOPIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fluoroscopia puede ser utilizada para evaluar la disfagia y ayudar a identificar su origen</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">7e367e70b89f4cc38785f10e7309bca4</data>
      <data key="d12">289</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="TUMORES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores son una causa que debe ser excluida en pacientes con disfagia, lo que implica su evaluaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">793cf800a03a418e85c9b2e1dd373a66</data>
      <data key="d12">290</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="DIVERT&#205;CULOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los divert&#237;culos son una de las causas menos frecuentes de disfagia que deben ser consideradas en el diagn&#243;stico</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">ee474361827f4525b8da1238f3bd1975</data>
      <data key="d12">291</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="TRASTORNOS MOTORAS DEL ES&#211;FAGO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los trastornos motores del es&#243;fago son una posible causa de disfagia que se debe investigar</data>
      <data key="d10">cfd217c3642e90cb9f3e1ff854830bd6</data>
      <data key="d11">344127dfcd8446e886a3f379aeb29290</data>
      <data key="d12">292</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#205;NGEA is involved in addressing the nutritional needs of patients with dysphagia through assessment and intervention</data>
      <data key="d10">39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8</data>
      <data key="d11">53e07ca7ab7e4f2b921ee8c73409be1d</data>
      <data key="d12">293</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="PACIENTES">
      <data key="d8">51.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a condition that significantly impacts patients, particularly those with specific health issues such as esophageal cancer and cerebrovascular disease. Patients with esophageal cancer experience dysphagia, which severely affects their ability to eat and can lead to nutritional deficiencies. Similarly, patients with cerebrovascular disease frequently suffer from dysphagia, hindering their capacity to feed themselves properly. This condition poses considerable challenges for patients, as they often struggle with swallowing, which can compromise their nutritional status and overall health. To address these challenges, many patients with dysphagia may require enteral nutrition to ensure they receive adequate nutrient intake. Overall, dysphagia is a critical concern for patients, necessitating medical attention and intervention to manage their dietary needs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,5664277128c865feb0e93f9fd56a3d05,98f9ca00cf50b7e359aa41f1d58d0735,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca</data>
      <data key="d11">ea826c8814934216a737556c13b32092</data>
      <data key="d12">294</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISFAGIA" target="ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a condition that requires careful consideration when it comes to food consumption. Certain foods must be modified to ensure safe consumption for patients with dysphagia. This involves adapting the type and consistency of foods to meet the specific needs of individuals affected by this condition. Proper modifications are essential to facilitate safe eating and prevent complications associated with swallowing difficulties.</data>
      <data key="d10">2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8</data>
      <data key="d11">01cab0b2010c458fa0ce062924686a1b</data>
      <data key="d12">295</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
