    </edge>
    <edge source="VEGENAT&#174; HEALTHCARE" target="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA: SOLUCIONES MULTIDISCIPLINARES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vegenat&#174; Healthcare provided support for the creation of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593</data>
      <data key="d11">0cafc4c3671f4c9ba0be60b319f0c73d</data>
      <data key="d12">437</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="JAVIER COELLO" target="DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA: SOLUCIONES MULTIDISCIPLINARES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Javier Coello was the editor responsible for the production of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593</data>
      <data key="d11">20fb5f1ebe004720b306ec04c6682fa8</data>
      <data key="d12">438</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CUIDADORES">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients, particularly those suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, depend on caregivers for essential support and assistance in managing their health conditions. Caregivers play a crucial role in helping these patients navigate the challenges associated with their dysphagia, ensuring they receive the necessary care and guidance to maintain their well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593,b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d</data>
      <data key="d11">f08ac2785c074aa6a806762177dd02ab</data>
      <data key="d12">439</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">48.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entities "PACIENTES" and "NUTRICI&#211;N" are closely interconnected, particularly in the context of health management following surgical procedures. Patients must adhere to a suitable nutritional plan to maintain their health after bariatric surgery, which is crucial for their recovery. A specific nutritional approach is necessary to enhance their overall health and facilitate recovery post-surgery. Additionally, nutritional rehabilitation plays a vital role for patients with eating disorders, helping to restore health and rectify nutritional deficiencies. 

Furthermore, patients require nutritional support to optimize their health both before and after surgical interventions. This is particularly important for those dealing with dysphagia, as they need proper nutrition to sustain their health. Patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, in particular, necessitate specialized nutrition to effectively manage their swallowing difficulties. Overall, a comprehensive nutritional strategy is essential for the well-being of patients across various health challenges.</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593,acba2f4838c3e73b321d9dcc6ba6fe55</data>
      <data key="d11">73494c2a78844e1d800f942a19659559</data>
      <data key="d12">440</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="REHABILITACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia undergo rehabilitation to improve their swallowing capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d10">669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593</data>
      <data key="d11">99c28a2eca5a48a9b5f5d5ab709562e6</data>
      <data key="d12">441</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="OTORRINOLARINGOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia are treated by specialists in otorhinolaryngology for their swallowing disorders.</data>
      <data key="d10">669a55d41ff26c3ea749aaa095688593</data>
      <data key="d11">067be72f91394a218ee6006106376995</data>
      <data key="d12">442</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ENFERMERAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nurses are responsible for identifying patients at risk of dysphagia and providing necessary care</data>
      <data key="d10">754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462</data>
      <data key="d11">e9cf8e435bd64bd0b70a82e7fbc05e95</data>
      <data key="d12">443</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="TRASTORNOS DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients may experience swallowing disorders that require professional assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">754053396bd343e6bea58cadc2842462</data>
      <data key="d11">0f78c06e9b424b77888ed0fa726e91ae</data>
      <data key="d12">444</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">52.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral nutrition is a critical medical intervention utilized for patients who are unable to consume food orally due to various health conditions. This form of nutrition is particularly essential for patients undergoing procedures such as esophagectomy, as it supports their recovery process. Additionally, patients suffering from severe dysphagia are often recommended to receive enteral nutrition through a feeding tube to ensure they receive adequate nutrition and maintain their digestive health. Overall, patients are the primary recipients of enteral nutrition, which is designed to meet their specific dietary needs when oral intake is not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544,acba2f4838c3e73b321d9dcc6ba6fe55,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">eb540438c8b64fa3a9e1764f65dc24ae</data>
      <data key="d12">445</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="VIDEOFLOROSCOPIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with dysphagia may undergo videofluoroscopy to evaluate their swallowing function and guide treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac</data>
      <data key="d11">010779ac47354a5d858b73fe22cfc02f</data>
      <data key="d12">446</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with prolonged dysphagia are advised to receive nutrition through a nasogastric tube to prevent malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">76be4651996e2afabd433daa9f5fd3ac</data>
      <data key="d11">680ae2923b7542bb821dadfdc69943cd</data>
      <data key="d12">447</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="IBP">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients are often prescribed IBP as part of their treatment for conditions like RGE and dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">b58b0258891d9207b27237bab6a03946</data>
      <data key="d11">848d2277d9d349539d2ec1482a1c9c64</data>
      <data key="d12">448</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients are individuals who receive medical care in hospitals, where their nutritional needs are assessed to ensure proper recovery and health management. Specifically, patients with acute pancreatitis require hospitalization for treatment, as this condition necessitates specialized medical attention. Additionally, patients suffering from dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing, often experience prolonged hospital stays due to the complexities associated with their care. Overall, hospitals play a crucial role in addressing the diverse health needs of patients, particularly those with specific medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">23c483bf9bf70d04577ef3735a1ca2e8,39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
      <data key="d11">8bb27a8db8f240ada8b62b4c3cd656a0</data>
      <data key="d12">449</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional screening is performed on patients to identify those at risk of malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8</data>
      <data key="d11">7f05edd3381d4ec3b6a3c676afa55422</data>
      <data key="d12">450</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DIETA BASAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The basal diet serves as a standard meal plan for patients who do not require special dietary modifications</data>
      <data key="d10">80220ae2bbcfeda884776e0ed9103390</data>
      <data key="d11">128a6457510c488281537b6d5bacc730</data>
      <data key="d12">451</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DIETAS TERAP&#201;UTICAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Therapeutic diets are tailored for patients with specific dietary needs, indicating a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">80220ae2bbcfeda884776e0ed9103390</data>
      <data key="d11">effdc47ffac7492f883456f96efde929</data>
      <data key="d12">452</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="COCINA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hospital kitchen prepares meals specifically for patients, including those with dietary restrictions due to health conditions</data>
      <data key="d10">80220ae2bbcfeda884776e0ed9103390</data>
      <data key="d11">a286fc789afe4905b5c3328ee2a72840</data>
      <data key="d12">453</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CALIDAD ORGANOL&#201;PTICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The sensory quality of meals is important for patient satisfaction and acceptance</data>
      <data key="d10">80220ae2bbcfeda884776e0ed9103390</data>
      <data key="d11">abcf70a474054511b07e359335b7c8b8</data>
      <data key="d12">454</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA" is designed to enhance the health and well-being of "PACIENTES" suffering from dysphagia. It offers a collection of recipes and guidelines tailored to meet the needs of individuals with swallowing difficulties. Additionally, the manual includes specific exercises aimed at helping these patients manage their condition more effectively. Through its comprehensive approach, the manual serves as a valuable resource for improving the quality of life for those affected by dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">0d5d152382113aa1b8faab4e554c88cd,dad5cb424b9586e4e672ed57db1f4fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">d2188a87ebe1455a965d46c2a5b70dbb</data>
      <data key="d12">455</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients often experience difficulties in the swallowing process, which requires targeted rehabilitation</data>
      <data key="d10">0d5d152382113aa1b8faab4e554c88cd</data>
      <data key="d11">356823120dfb450b8d6d3bc3f11339df</data>
      <data key="d12">456</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="UFDOF">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">UFDOF provides specialized care and treatment for patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">d8fa59c6af96b4ebb96f2c6b4ddb5473</data>
      <data key="d11">50808cde0ee94efda5f3cc44d25f3ba9</data>
      <data key="d12">457</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CONSULTA PRIMERA DISFAGIA OROFAR&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Consulta Primera Disfagia Orofar&#237;ngea is specifically designed for patients suspected of having dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">d39d7f5c024a44d7a2df5a25967a7e2b</data>
      <data key="d12">458</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients undergo videofluoroscopias to assess their swallowing function</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">53518bb60be743afb888e88b8f6272fb</data>
      <data key="d12">459</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="MUST">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MUST is used to evaluate the nutritional risk of patients with dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">2721321c58f04668b5549350452e70c3</data>
      <data key="d12">460</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="MNA S-F">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MNA S-F is utilized to assess the nutritional status of elderly patients with dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">00c20caed5744ee88987905ecce3e9cf</data>
      <data key="d12">461</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ICTUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with dysphagia may have a history of ictus, which can affect their swallowing ability</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">2132429e0f7e43bd8ace6a174ff05e72</data>
      <data key="d12">462</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALIMENTOS SEGUROS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients are provided with safe foods during the evaluation of their swallowing function</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">28b2d8ac08ab4ee79f8c863950ec2008</data>
      <data key="d12">463</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients are assessed for their ability to handle dangerous foods during dysphagia evaluations</data>
      <data key="d10">1fad843d053b1ec4805a4e7c6be9ceb3</data>
      <data key="d11">c3b67e49650241358b8f8ba0504647c9</data>
      <data key="d12">464</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CUESTIONARIOS DE SATISFACCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients provide feedback through satisfaction questionnaires, which are essential for evaluating and improving the quality of care</data>
      <data key="d10">5dd39815651d2d44f18c16e69696c0cf</data>
      <data key="d11">5c564692a3fb459998d41dc02c724cf0</data>
      <data key="d12">465</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients interact with healthcare professionals for diagnosis, treatment, and management of their health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d</data>
      <data key="d11">70b46634bed24d88a919de9cf537c962</data>
      <data key="d12">466</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="HISTORIA CL&#205;NICA ELECTR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The historia cl&#237;nica electr&#243;nica contains essential health data about patients, facilitating better healthcare delivery.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d</data>
      <data key="d11">dec6fbdab3ce4d21a74a510945a7c07a</data>
      <data key="d12">467</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DISPOSITIVOS TECNOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Technological devices help patients monitor their health conditions and collect data for better management of disfagia orofar&#237;ngea.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7034350b98abd27ed6af7560149691d</data>
      <data key="d11">ccd88a9b6e6b40149acdc882d66663a6</data>
      <data key="d12">468</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALIMENTACION ADAPTADA TRADICIONAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with dysphagia require traditional adapted food to meet their dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">3a7dac32347984360ee9e87767129272</data>
      <data key="d11">7730369765ac47f297d4be8bd5102417</data>
      <data key="d12">469</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALIMENTACION ADAPTADA COMERCIAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with dysphagia may utilize commercially adapted food options for easier consumption.</data>
      <data key="d10">3a7dac32347984360ee9e87767129272</data>
      <data key="d11">de5348f8eef84520810f817d3a47971c</data>
      <data key="d12">470</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="TEXURAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with dysphagia benefit from food textures that are modified to aid in swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d10">3a7dac32347984360ee9e87767129272</data>
      <data key="d11">a9db2352f3a8441d8e002e6379c6c07e</data>
      <data key="d12">471</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="TRATAMIENTO REHABILITADOR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients diagnosed with dysphagia undergo rehabilitative treatment to improve their swallowing abilities.</data>
      <data key="d10">3a7dac32347984360ee9e87767129272</data>
      <data key="d11">aa71cc0c1f0346558d4c2131bd786c44</data>
      <data key="d12">472</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">57.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PACIENTES are individuals who may require NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not possible due to various medical complications. This form of nutrition is specifically indicated for patients suffering from severe malnutrition, particularly when enteral nutrition cannot be administered. Patients receiving parenteral nutrition are those who cannot meet their nutritional needs through oral intake or other means, and they may also be recipients of home parenteral nutrition based on their specific medical conditions. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical alternative for patients who are unable to receive adequate nutrition through enteral routes.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,4ec3e8cb1f21808e70bbc71cb26d7396,538970e30e9d0e758546ca1a3cf5a205,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588,acba2f4838c3e73b321d9dcc6ba6fe55,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">db68725bbfd145bfafd8ebc98bae02ec</data>
      <data key="d12">473</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="S&#205;NDROME DE REALIMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patients at risk are those who may develop refeeding syndrome due to their nutritional status and medical conditions. These patients require careful monitoring and preventive measures during nutritional therapy to mitigate the risk of this syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">2f2f1caea1f546949d97b872e7eda822</data>
      <data key="d12">474</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="TIAMINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Thiamine is administered to patients at risk during the first week of nutritional therapy to prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">4d7428b60b4e4792af0bb72eeab73060</data>
      <data key="d12">475</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="&#193;CIDO F&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Folic acid is an essential nutrient provided to patients at risk during nutritional therapy to support their health. It plays a crucial role in the recovery process, particularly for patients with eating disorders, who may experience deficiencies in folic acid that can hinder their progress. Therefore, ensuring adequate folic acid intake is vital for these patients to enhance their overall well-being and facilitate recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">038fb6ed32f14d4681c601ef14ba8c7b</data>
      <data key="d12">476</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con anorexia nerviosa son un grupo en riesgo de desarrollar complicaciones durante la nutrici&#243;n enteral. Para recuperarse de su condici&#243;n, estos pacientes requieren una rehabilitaci&#243;n nutricional espec&#237;fica, as&#237; como un apoyo nutricional especializado para abordar su grave desnutrici&#243;n. En muchos casos, puede ser necesario recurrir a la nutrici&#243;n enteral para tratar la desnutrici&#243;n severa que presentan.</data>
      <data key="d10">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,46912552a886d029c4aa16e3ea9a0e27,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">f29bbd05ec0f42cb9b268645975ec014</data>
      <data key="d12">477</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entity "PACIENTES" refers to individuals who may experience "DESNUTRICI&#211;N," a condition characterized by inadequate nutrition. Patients suffering from desnutrici&#243;n require careful monitoring and nutritional intervention to restore their health. In some cases, this may necessitate the administration of parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. Overall, addressing desnutrici&#243;n in patients is crucial for their recovery and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">40fbc53467b8460d1d2d6bcd0d6dbf2a,b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">1767d8e23cad4dee863216e6d32783e6</data>
      <data key="d12">478</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with enfermedades cr&#243;nicas often face challenges in maintaining proper nutrition due to their health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">8e4782d14c9744c6a5914712471b2bfe</data>
      <data key="d12">479</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALCOHOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with alcoholismo may experience nutritional deficiencies and require targeted nutritional therapy.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">9c04bd63cf3945d6b0e6adb1ec1131ba</data>
      <data key="d12">480</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DROGADICCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with drogadicci&#243;n may have compromised nutritional status and need specialized dietary support.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">2afd3c770af14f9ab7223b3fdb39e227</data>
      <data key="d12">481</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALTO GRADO DE ESTR&#201;S METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients experiencing alto grado de estr&#233;s metab&#243;lico require careful nutritional management to meet their increased metabolic needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">217465aab7254774b4919bc8921b3317</data>
      <data key="d12">482</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="S&#205;NDROMES DE MALA ABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with s&#237;ndromes de mala absorci&#243;n need specific dietary adjustments to ensure adequate nutrient intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">e6f857fc403941feab2c88f6ca90c132</data>
      <data key="d12">483</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ARGININA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The use of arginine in patient nutrition is questioned due to insufficient evidence for routine use</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">a5a8386a8fa9412bbba3dadfc5575b03</data>
      <data key="d12">484</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CALORIMETR&#205;A INDIRECTA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Indirect calorimetry is a method utilized to assess the energy requirements of patients, particularly those with eating disorders. This technique provides an estimation of the energy needs of patients, allowing for tailored nutritional interventions and management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd,fb23af50b771da28e73b9545fa4f09b0</data>
      <data key="d11">a7e33e8e7b60426fb221d98b2efbe3ae</data>
      <data key="d12">485</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="HARRIS BENEDICT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Harris-Benedict equation is applied to calculate the energy requirements of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">3171bfcb52cc452ab403f03bb801084d</data>
      <data key="d12">486</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="SEPSIS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients requiring parenteral nutrition are at an increased risk of developing sepsis, which can complicate their treatment. Additionally, patients who are diagnosed with sepsis have specific nutritional requirements that differ from those of patients without the condition. This highlights the importance of tailored nutritional support for patients with sepsis, particularly those who are also dependent on parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">6a461872cd7a45d89b0c1511e6b9cb96</data>
      <data key="d12">487</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="MACRONUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The distribution of macronutrients is crucial for meeting the nutritional needs of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">16d2b7f2b7cb4af4ae7b0ae5887ec09b</data>
      <data key="d12">488</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="REQUERIMIENTOS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional requirements are tailored to meet the specific needs of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">e8701948ca26409bb13de03e93fd6177</data>
      <data key="d12">489</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Blood glucose levels are monitored to assess the metabolic state of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">e0f66c278da745a8b2ebad66b917551a</data>
      <data key="d12">490</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Proteins are a critical component of the dietary needs for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">bf1c5059f6bc403b84a97289f97553d9</data>
      <data key="d12">491</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="L&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lipids are included in the dietary recommendations for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">771e6f3e4b7540dd9ca8d204e624fc14</data>
      <data key="d12">492</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="GL&#218;CIDOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbohydrates are part of the nutritional guidelines for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">43883071d6db17a632d928bc976776fd</data>
      <data key="d11">d1e6a59295e04a4b8836897db5edf828</data>
      <data key="d12">493</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gastrostom&#237;a is a medical procedure performed on pacientes who require nutritional support due to various medical conditions. This method is commonly utilized to provide nutrition to pacientes who have difficulties swallowing, ensuring they receive the necessary sustenance for their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f7dbd2afca6dc5582d55fb39b0f55b7,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">b5c12a123a4f4030ac329378417b16f9</data>
      <data key="d12">494</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with cystic fibrosis (FQ) are individuals affected by this genetic disorder, which leads to a range of health complications. They often experience severe respiratory issues and face significant nutritional challenges due to the disease. One of the common problems associated with cystic fibrosis is malabsorption, which can necessitate the use of enteral nutrition to ensure that patients receive adequate nourishment. As a result, many patients with cystic fibrosis require enteral nutrition to address their digestive difficulties and maintain their overall health.</data>
      <data key="d10">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">edb20991633046128701f07eba2719f4</data>
      <data key="d12">495</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="&#205;LEO G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con &#237;leo g&#225;strico pueden necesitar nutrici&#243;n enteral debido a la obstrucci&#243;n del vaciamiento g&#225;strico.</data>
      <data key="d10">e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">6489e3b9e1d3477ca508b639c582c8f5</data>
      <data key="d12">496</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="PANCREATITIS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with pancreatitis may require enteral nutrition to prevent stimulation of the pancreas and to address digestive complications associated with the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">17f6f0c16f6a417889bc642aa046a07c</data>
      <data key="d12">497</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="F&#205;STULAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con f&#237;stulas pancre&#225;ticas pueden necesitar nutrici&#243;n enteral para manejar su condici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">e4019011dbf10f2c4b73d33215d7631d</data>
      <data key="d11">9a878e17a7ec48ff9277b14d10b6e89d</data>
      <data key="d12">498</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients on home parenteral nutrition often require monitoring and supplementation of vitamin D, as this vitamin plays a crucial role in their overall health. Additionally, vitamin D levels are associated with the health outcomes of patients suffering from chronic respiratory diseases, indicating its importance in managing these conditions. Therefore, maintaining adequate vitamin D levels is essential for both patients on home parenteral nutrition and those with chronic respiratory issues to support their health and improve their outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">220f261b085142ebbf0bf0c3af37dd7f</data>
      <data key="d12">499</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="DENSITOMETR&#205;AS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients receiving parenteral nutrition undergo periodic densitometries to monitor bone health</data>
      <data key="d10">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">fbcdaf2ed84146df9d9228796ba1af5f</data>
      <data key="d12">500</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="T-SCORE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The T-score is used to evaluate bone density in patients receiving parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">66f0e53c88dd48a3a289f82a24ff14e5</data>
      <data key="d12">501</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="PTHI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PTHi levels are monitored in patients to assess their calcium metabolism and bone health</data>
      <data key="d10">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">f6a6b66cb6ac49089339f80b25eccf63</data>
      <data key="d12">502</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcemia levels are critical for evaluating the health of patients on parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">2aaff47c9f5643b3aea00b123eed4866</data>
      <data key="d12">503</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="MELAS">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pacientes are individuals diagnosed with MELAS, experiencing its various symptoms and manifestations.</data>
      <data key="d10">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">13735bae20c940a79904584c604ec4cd</data>
      <data key="d12">504</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="IMC">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Body Mass Index (IMC) is a critical tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of patients, particularly those with specific health conditions such as cancer and MELAS. In the context of cancer patients, the IMC is employed to assess their nutritional status prior to surgery, ensuring that they are in optimal health for the procedure. Similarly, for patients with MELAS, low IMC values are indicative of a risk of malnutrition, highlighting the importance of monitoring their nutritional health. Overall, the assessment of patients' nutritional status through IMC is essential for effective health management across various medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c0d1f274b31d130e4feb8e46fbeb764,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0,e4002acd67016cc1f7428e0a3ab42977</data>
      <data key="d11">426f46da258d46669287905fe67b1fc4</data>
      <data key="d12">505</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="S&#205;NTOMAS GASTROINTESTINALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">S&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales are common among pacientes with MELAS, increasing their risk of malnutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">fa45676ea0f847fc9331d347d17b5866</data>
      <data key="d12">506</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con obesidad pueden requerir cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica para tratar su condici&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f</data>
      <data key="d11">ddd99a36fde040229262c3dfedb33806</data>
      <data key="d12">507</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="EJERCICIO F&#205;SICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes son recomendados a realizar ejercicio f&#237;sico para mejorar su salud despu&#233;s de la cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f</data>
      <data key="d11">69f3479a5cdc484a9de94ddec8a8ad22</data>
      <data key="d12">508</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="TABACO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes deben evitar el tabaco para mejorar su salud, especialmente despu&#233;s de la cirug&#237;a</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f</data>
      <data key="d11">cdc02e1d266543768663667ea22bfc62</data>
      <data key="d12">509</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes deben evitar el alcohol para prevenir complicaciones tras la cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f</data>
      <data key="d11">443677e2e4b24fc79bb4851c972f531a</data>
      <data key="d12">510</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="RIESGO NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes que se someten a cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica enfrentan un riesgo nutricional que requiere supervisi&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f</data>
      <data key="d11">cc48cb3f60fe4a7aa19d6f8aea336309</data>
      <data key="d12">511</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
