    <edge source="PACIENTES" target="HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a condition commonly observed in hospitalized patients, especially among those receiving artificial nutrition. These patients are diagnosed with hyponatremia, which indicates that they have low sodium levels in their blood. As a result, they require treatment to manage this condition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61</data>
