      <data key="d12">675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and MALNUTRICI&#211;N are closely related concepts that highlight the importance of adequate nutrition in various health contexts. Malnutrition is a consequence of inadequate nutrition, which significantly impacts the growth and development of children. It is a critical concern that requires effective nutritional management, particularly in surgical patients, where proper nutrition can influence recovery outcomes. Additionally, nutrition plays a vital role in preventing and managing malnutrition in cancer patients, affecting their overall health and the success of their treatment. The field of nutrition addresses issues related to malnutrition and its assessment, emphasizing that proper nutrition is essential not only for children but also for patients with renal conditions and other health issues. Therefore, ensuring adequate nutrition is a fundamental focus in health assessments to prevent malnutrition across different populations.</data>
      <data key="d10">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f,0bc48d0666e895b990c211acf7cbcf23,21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292,ce62d279f86b3364fed4e121ad2d5e1f</data>
      <data key="d11">f58471bec6a04bd2b088a7e71e9d5f6e</data>
      <data key="d12">676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="PACIENTE S&#201;PTICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n es crucial para el tratamiento de pacientes s&#233;pticos, ayudando a prevenir la desnutrici&#243;n y complicaciones</data>
