      <data key="d11">0a73d029380c4b2a81d3810712af24f6</data>
      <data key="d12">677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="ALIMENTACI&#211;N POR SONDA GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La alimentaci&#243;n por sonda gastrointestinal es un m&#233;todo preferido dentro del soporte nutricional en pacientes cr&#237;ticos</data>
      <data key="d10">422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">8a1289bc64ee43b7b5b3be42eab0a0de</data>
      <data key="d12">678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">61.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N encompasses the broader process of providing essential nutrients to individuals, which includes various methods of nutritional support. One specific method within this framework is NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which serves as an alternative approach when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not feasible. NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is particularly important for patients who are unable to consume food orally, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for their health and recovery. This method highlights the critical role of NUTRICI&#211;N in patient care, as it provides a vital nutritional intervention when traditional enteral feeding methods cannot be utilized. Overall, NUTRICI&#211;N and NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL work together to ensure that patients receive adequate nutritional support tailored to their specific needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a,2ebe12524f7750215eee73b328b601ee,422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced,61a35dc8c2c6728e1df80cb1037e6296,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,9927d054458e409309b9e917cbb6a10c,c07baf818737d704c290ca0f5eefd30f,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d11">2f55f8a2b3f64021b6b82f9ea4c986c8</data>
      <data key="d12">679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL COMPLEMENTARIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral complementaria se indica para asegurar que los pacientes cr&#237;ticos reciban suficientes nutrientes</data>
      <data key="d10">422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">a4a6f50614d54c11a38215654cd121cd</data>
      <data key="d12">680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and DESNUTRICI&#211;N are closely related concepts in the context of health and patient care. Adequate nutrition is essential for preventing desnutrici&#243;n, particularly in critical patients. Nutritional support plays a vital role in both preventing and treating desnutrici&#243;n, highlighting its importance in healthcare settings. Furthermore, proper nutrition is crucial for preventing malnutrition, especially among vulnerable populations such as the elderly. Overall, the relationship between NUTRICI&#211;N and DESNUTRICI&#211;N underscores the necessity of effective nutritional strategies to safeguard health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">0ed0218136adceb16e9f246f3072e6dd,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">b5c6213004b241bdaafd5c67a3c874a9</data>
      <data key="d12">681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="COMPLICACIONES SECUNDARIAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Iniciar la nutrici&#243;n a tiempo es crucial para prevenir complicaciones secundarias en pacientes cr&#237;ticos</data>
      <data key="d10">422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">f7554364cb994475960c74d1eb6ea362</data>
      <data key="d12">682</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">69.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL are interconnected concepts within the field of nutritional support. NUTRICI&#211;N refers to the broader concept of providing essential nutrients to individuals, which includes various methods such as NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL. NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL, specifically, is a targeted approach to delivering nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally, making it a crucial aspect of overall nutritional management, particularly for those with gastrointestinal issues.

Enteral nutrition is essential for ensuring adequate nutrient intake in patients, especially in cases where oral consumption is not possible. This method is particularly significant for premature newborns, as it supports their growth and development. Additionally, enteral nutrition plays a vital role in the nutritional management of patients suffering from conditions such as acute pancreatitis, where it serves as a primary intervention.

In summary, NUTRICI&#211;N encompasses a variety of nutritional support methods, with NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL being a specific and critical approach for patients requiring assistance in nutrient intake due to their inability to eat orally.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a,2ebe12524f7750215eee73b328b601ee,6886c5b652319bea0ba2427a3fdbf701,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3,79a751fb45e4b69c946d088100f43654,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,9927d054458e409309b9e917cbb6a10c,9e4c5851293c18ef6b304ff6293b0be5,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b,f84386a9907d954b9cf46475d0d45243</data>
      <data key="d11">49f44ae075d74e5fb35509e3023f4c6c</data>
      <data key="d12">683</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
