    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="ENVEJECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and ENVEJECIMIENTO are closely interconnected, as aging significantly impacts nutritional needs and dietary recommendations for the elderly. As individuals age, their nutritional requirements evolve, making proper nutrition a critical factor in the aging process. This relationship highlights the importance of tailored dietary approaches to meet the changing needs of older adults, ensuring their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">d87d69948a104165b4d8cc5a1068ed52</data>
      <data key="d12">703</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and FRAGILIDAD are closely interconnected concepts, particularly in the context of elderly care. The fragility observed in older adults can be effectively addressed through appropriate nutritional strategies and supplementation. Nutritional interventions play a vital role in managing frailty among elderly individuals, highlighting the importance of a well-balanced diet and targeted nutritional support to enhance their overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">5f15452403a4c9b4b3c7a48bac634a04,b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">d049df426ef24fe890b88614173b7446</data>
      <data key="d12">704</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N y HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N est&#225;n interrelacionadas, ya que la hospitalizaci&#243;n frecuentemente incorpora un enfoque en la nutrici&#243;n para garantizar que los pacientes reciban la alimentaci&#243;n adecuada durante su tratamiento. Esto es especialmente relevante en el caso de la hospitalizaci&#243;n de ancianos, quienes a menudo requieren atenci&#243;n nutricional espec&#237;fica para mejorar su estado de salud. En resumen, la nutrici&#243;n juega un papel crucial en el proceso de hospitalizaci&#243;n, contribuyendo al bienestar y recuperaci&#243;n de los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,5f15452403a4c9b4b3c7a48bac634a04</data>
      <data key="d11">a42da51a20124b7492b9f7ddac298341</data>
      <data key="d12">705</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="ALIMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and ALIMENTACI&#211;N are closely interconnected concepts, with proper feeding being essential for the effective utilization of nutrients. ALIMENTACI&#211;N focuses on dietary needs and serves as a fundamental component of NUTRICI&#211;N. This relationship is particularly significant in the context of premature newborns, where appropriate feeding practices are crucial for their nutritional health and development.</data>
      <data key="d10">12281055b260e7dc55fcaeeab7eefde6,54a47e2936e787ab5943e2d75afc03f1,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3</data>
