    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and DIETOTERAPIA are closely related concepts within the field of health and wellness. Dietoterapia, or dietotherapy, is a key component of nutritional practices that focuses on improving health outcomes, particularly during pregnancy. It involves making dietary adjustments based on nutritional principles to address various health conditions. The practice of dietotherapy is fundamentally rooted in nutrition, emphasizing the importance of tailored nutritional support to manage and enhance health. Overall, dietotherapy serves as a vital approach within nutrition, aimed at fostering better health through informed dietary choices and interventions.</data>
      <data key="d10">03b7a89c9bb1dfd115acef377b491808,1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b,87cb06eed8a8c92c589d25ea2d5cfaec,cca60bfbb1e73ceda513fbcaf0866a8f,e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d11">7345a7e0c592490b838d31f25677cfc1</data>
      <data key="d12">718</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA are closely related concepts that emphasize the importance of nutrition in clinical settings. NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA specifically focuses on the application of nutritional science to various clinical scenarios, particularly for pregnant women. It addresses the dietary needs and interventions necessary for maintaining health and managing diseases. A key component of NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA is nutritional support, which is essential for meeting the dietary requirements of individuals in both health and disease contexts. Overall, both NUTRICI&#211;N and NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA highlight the critical role that nutrition plays in promoting health and well-being in clinical environments.</data>
      <data key="d10">03b7a89c9bb1dfd115acef377b491808,1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b,c879347903aabeef630597c99cff2275</data>
      <data key="d11">70381d32283247a1a777e34990aef7dd</data>
      <data key="d12">719</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="METABOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N and METABOLISMO are closely interconnected concepts in the study of human health. Metabolism is significantly influenced by nutrition, as the body processes various nutrients to generate energy. Understanding metabolism is essential for comprehending how these nutrients are utilized within the body, particularly during critical periods such as pregnancy, where the processing of nutrients plays a vital role in both maternal and fetal health.</data>
      <data key="d10">03b7a89c9bb1dfd115acef377b491808,cca60bfbb1e73ceda513fbcaf0866a8f</data>
      <data key="d11">3de00b35e1ec4754b8182e694477ded3</data>
      <data key="d12">720</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N refers to the practices and guidelines associated with home parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering nutritional support directly into the bloodstream of patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through traditional means. NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA specifically focuses on the provision of this nutritional support in a home setting. It is essential for patients undergoing home parenteral nutrition to receive adequate nutrients to maintain their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445,8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">f03fa8c6d1fc4b91ae72022473ee0f11</data>
      <data key="d12">721</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
