    <edge source="HOSPITAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hospital plays a crucial role in providing enteral nutrition, which is essential for patients who are unable to consume food orally. This service is particularly important for pediatric patients, as the hospital offers the necessary environment and trained personnel to implement enteral nutrition effectively. Additionally, hospitals cater to a diverse range of patients requiring enteral nutrition, including those with diabetes, eating disorders, and acute pancreatitis. Thus, enteral nutrition is an integral part of the treatment protocols within hospitals, ensuring that patients with various medical conditions receive the nutritional support they need.</data>
