    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a condition that requires careful management, particularly in hospitalized patients, where nutritional support plays a critical role. In cases where enteral nutrition is not feasible or fails, parenteral nutrition may be indicated for diabetic patients. This approach ensures that their nutritional needs are met while effectively managing their diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009</data>
      <data key="d11">8467e84496b040bbbe2fbface9efbcd5</data>
      <data key="d12">1499</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ALZHEIMER">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is associated with an increased risk of Alzheimer's disease, linking metabolic health to cognitive decline</data>
      <data key="d10">53e49c7e4c8bca9063d743acb9997132</data>
      <data key="d11">6057e6c8f5fd47a4bfc7e9835d4cc1b9</data>
      <data key="d12">1500</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HYPOGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic condition characterized by high blood sugar levels, which can lead to various complications, one of the most common being hypoglycemia. Hypoglycemia, or low blood sugar, can occur in individuals with Diabetes Mellitus, particularly in patients undergoing treatment. It is essential for these individuals to manage hypoglycemia through careful dietary planning to prevent its occurrence and maintain stable blood glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,5b487245068b8e8b87ffcc04970aaff4</data>
      <data key="d11">33d21cabb9284f60951e371157a40d48</data>
      <data key="d12">1501</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic condition that affects the body's ability to regulate blood sugar levels. One of the potential complications associated with Diabetes Mellitus is hypoglycemia, which occurs when blood sugar levels drop too low. This condition can arise due to improper management of blood sugar levels, particularly when insulin or certain medications are used to treat diabetes. Therefore, individuals with Diabetes Mellitus must carefully monitor their blood sugar levels to prevent hypoglycemia, which is a common complication of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9</data>
      <data key="d11">12406b517c8d40a68ca168805e50c025</data>
      <data key="d12">1502</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CETOACIDOSIS DIAB&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic condition characterized by high blood sugar levels due to the body's inability to produce or effectively use insulin. If blood sugar levels are not properly controlled, Diabetes Mellitus can lead to serious complications, one of which is diabetic ketoacidosis. Diabetic ketoacidosis is a severe and potentially life-threatening complication that arises from poorly managed Diabetes Mellitus. It occurs when the body starts breaking down fat at an excessive rate, leading to the production of ketones, which can cause the blood to become acidic. Proper management of Diabetes Mellitus is crucial to prevent the onset of diabetic ketoacidosis and other related complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3,ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9</data>
      <data key="d11">a7d818cde7904c03a5ad3cbb311aaab9</data>
      <data key="d12">1503</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
