    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a condition that can significantly influence the effectiveness of enteral nutrition, particularly in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis. In many cases, individuals with diabetes mellitus require enteral nutrition to adequately address their dietary needs, especially in settings such as hospitals or for elderly patients. This nutritional approach is particularly crucial for managing the nutritional requirements of patients with diabetes mellitus who may experience severe malnutrition due to various conditions, including MELAS. Overall, enteral nutrition plays a vital role in the dietary management of patients with diabetes mellitus, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for recovery and health maintenance.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ba0aa1d1330351a62eb6319ffdd30db,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,8b074745f27ee51afc8337a49fafacfa</data>
