    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="MELAS">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a prevalent endocrine manifestation that is associated with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). It affects a significant portion of patients diagnosed with MELAS and can be considered a metabolic complication in these individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">7dac740d9abc4e20b5e9550737364fe9</data>
      <data key="d12">1541</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="AMERICAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic condition that affects how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). The American Diabetes Association (ADA) plays a crucial role in providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of Diabetes Mellitus. These guidelines encompass various aspects of diabetes care, including nutrition therapy recommendations, which are essential for effective management of the condition. The ADA's resources aim to support individuals with diabetes in achieving optimal health outcomes through informed management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2b31f5a0bba00ecee5e3a8fb2c83ea,58db9fa69ca87ec24d7117fea6f2fe88,cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
