      <data key="d9">The patient is receiving treatment for diabetes mellitus at Hospital Universitario Doctor Peset</data>
      <data key="d10">3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d</data>
      <data key="d11">d359a7058d4e4e26a9cf873c7c87853d</data>
      <data key="d12">1560</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic condition that affects the body's ability to regulate blood glucose levels. Insulina, or insulin, plays a crucial role in the management of this disease. It is essential for controlling glucose levels in the body, and resistance to insulin can contribute to the development of Diabetes Mellitus, particularly in patients with liver disease. In the context of treatment, patients diagnosed with Diabetes Mellitus, such as those with type 2 diabetes, often require insulin therapy to effectively manage their condition and maintain stable blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436,3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d</data>
      <data key="d11">38709f3fec0b4068bb4539d899d59490</data>
      <data key="d12">1561</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
