    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="OBESIDAD">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus and obesity are closely interconnected conditions, with dietary factors playing a crucial role in their development. Both diabetes mellitus and obesity are linked to the consumption of red and processed meats, highlighting the impact of dietary habits on these health issues. Obesity is recognized as a significant risk factor for the development of diabetes mellitus, further emphasizing the relationship between the two conditions. Overall, the interplay between obesity and diabetes mellitus underscores the importance of addressing dietary habits to mitigate the risks associated with both conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4,4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
