    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ADA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association (ADA) plays a crucial role in the management and diagnosis of Diabetes Mellitus. It provides comprehensive guidelines and criteria for diagnosing the condition, which include specific blood glucose ranges. Additionally, the ADA offers recommendations for managing Diabetes Mellitus, emphasizing the importance of dietary advice and monitoring practices. Through these guidelines, the ADA aims to support individuals in effectively managing their diabetes and improving their overall health.</data>
      <data key="d10">48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4,b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,f558c372d16630f14b614e232fc151de</data>
