      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a condition that directly impacts glycemia, making the management of blood sugar levels crucial for individuals affected by this disease. Effective management of diabetes requires careful monitoring of glycemia, which is particularly important during pregnancy and lactation. This highlights the interconnectedness of diabetes mellitus and glycemia, emphasizing the need for vigilant blood sugar control to ensure the health and well-being of those living with diabetes.</data>
