      <data key="d9">Calor&#237;as are a critical factor in managing diabetes through diet, influencing dietary recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d10">c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">89de1dea6d094613bcc3c808f08da85a</data>
      <data key="d12">1603</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ALMIDONES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Almidones are carbohydrates that can impact blood sugar levels and are discussed in dietary guidelines for diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">8ce8e6f928e94f0db1dbbf59a9caa4c4</data>
      <data key="d12">1604</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="EDULCORANTES CAL&#211;RICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Edulcorantes cal&#243;ricos are compared to other sweeteners in terms of their effects on diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d10">c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">748e3fcdba274aee866380c8ce31510e</data>
      <data key="d12">1605</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="EDULCORANTES NO CAL&#211;RICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Edulcorantes no cal&#243;ricos are discussed in the context of dietary management for diabetes, providing alternatives to sugar.</data>
      <data key="d10">c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">2ba19914f7614d86a6c83109be36f6b3</data>
      <data key="d12">1606</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ASPARTAMO">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a condition that affects how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). Aspartame, a low-calorie sweetener, is commonly used in various products specifically designed for individuals with diabetes mellitus. It serves as a dietary recommendation for those managing the condition, offering a suitable low-calorie sweetener option that helps individuals maintain their dietary goals without compromising on taste.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">942847e5d0844514841b1d9474f8880a</data>
      <data key="d12">1607</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="SUCRALOSA">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that requires careful dietary management to maintain blood sugar levels. Sucralosa, also known as sucralose, is a non-caloric sweetener that is particularly suitable for individuals with diabetes mellitus. It is often discussed in the context of dietary management for diabetes, as it provides a sweet taste without contributing calories or affecting blood glucose levels. This makes sucralose an effective option for those looking to manage their diet while still enjoying sweet flavors.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">2039236729da4a4bb558029b979ed270</data>
      <data key="d12">1608</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="TAUMATINA">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that requires careful management of dietary choices, particularly regarding sugar intake. Taumatina, also known as thaumatin, is recognized in dietary recommendations for diabetes management as a natural sweetener. It is beneficial for individuals with diabetes mellitus who are looking to reduce their sugar consumption. By incorporating taumatina into their diets, those managing diabetes can enjoy a sweet taste without the associated risks of high sugar intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">6ae265c273154b97b11085be0a39dfae</data>
      <data key="d12">1609</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ESTEVIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that affects how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). In the context of dietary management for diabetes, Estevia, also known as Stevia, is highlighted as a natural sweetener option. Estevia is utilized in various products specifically designed for individuals with diabetes mellitus, aiding them in managing their sugar consumption effectively. This natural sweetener provides a way for those with diabetes to enjoy sweetness in their diets without the associated risks of elevated blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4,c958206b5546e8b46ab48b3f50e60611</data>
      <data key="d11">6c8459d45875435b900af4a6c50dfaab</data>
      <data key="d12">1610</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="EASD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The EASD offers evidence-based recommendations for the management of diabetes mellitus, complementing the guidelines from the ADA.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4</data>
      <data key="d11">f604172f043e4f7eab10a9e98f09b691</data>
      <data key="d12">1611</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="SODIO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sodium intake is recommended to be reduced in patients with diabetes mellitus to help manage blood pressure and health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1698ec972215d493ab6114914dde2a4</data>
      <data key="d11">b96ad0e2d4b347bab686645a0f834cb2</data>
      <data key="d12">1612</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
