      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="VEGETARIAN DIETS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vegetarian diets can be beneficial for individuals with diabetes, providing a lower intake of saturated fats and promoting better health outcomes</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777</data>
      <data key="d11">6a52d55dacb34caba1ad47e77969a55c</data>
      <data key="d12">1624</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="NUTRIENTS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutrient management is critical for individuals with diabetes to maintain proper health and metabolic control</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777</data>
      <data key="d11">ca799f0821ee4dc3be705e1abee8dc5e</data>
      <data key="d12">1625</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HYPERGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that frequently results in hyperglycemia, which is characterized by elevated blood sugar levels. Effective management of diabetes is crucial to prevent complications associated with hyperglycemia. This includes careful dietary management, as hyperglycemia is a common complication of diabetes that necessitates attention to diet and lifestyle choices.</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777,eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381</data>
      <data key="d11">3778718728dc4ebe9c9b4712644b471a</data>
      <data key="d12">1626</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CALORIES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Caloric intake must be monitored and adjusted for individuals with diabetes to maintain healthy blood sugar levels</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777</data>
      <data key="d11">a8a98494d63641659f45415ecba4b8f5</data>
      <data key="d12">1627</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="VITAMINS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Certain vitamins may need to be supplemented in individuals with diabetes, particularly in the elderly</data>
      <data key="d10">27f06efb5e9ac8bbc3f8bd31ee5a2777</data>
      <data key="d11">2b58ca8e3a9d4bcd8c367a8bfb2aaaed</data>
      <data key="d12">1628</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="RAMAD&#193;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus management is significantly affected by the fasting practices during Ramadan, requiring careful dietary adjustments</data>
      <data key="d10">62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8</data>
      <data key="d11">0f2a11fd8c7044eaaebe971869597ded</data>
      <data key="d12">1629</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="PRODUCTOS ENRIQUECIDOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enriched products are recommended for individuals with diabetes to ensure adequate intake of essential vitamins and minerals</data>
      <data key="d10">62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8</data>
      <data key="d11">aba661d6ee5c4fd89a7bf4ff9b973f75</data>
      <data key="d12">1630</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition characterized by elevated levels of glucose in the blood, known as glucemia. Glucemia serves as a crucial indicator in the diagnosis of diabetes mellitus, as high levels can signify the presence of the disease. Furthermore, monitoring glucemia is essential for effectively managing diabetes mellitus, particularly in relation to physical activity, as it is important to check glucose levels before and after exercise to ensure proper health management.</data>
      <data key="d10">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436,48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4</data>
      <data key="d11">d257df2bee5744f08b2af6537cb043ba</data>
      <data key="d12">1631</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CARBOHIDRATOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbohidratos intake is important for individuals with diabetes to maintain stable blood sugar levels during exercise</data>
      <data key="d10">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436</data>
      <data key="d11">48e60f8c93074f178a60730c42e9363b</data>
      <data key="d12">1632</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CETOACIDOSIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cetoacidosis is a complication that can arise from poorly managed diabetes mellitus</data>
      <data key="d10">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436</data>
      <data key="d11">3a35c1f3e2bb4da5b15deb5708df7753</data>
      <data key="d12">1633</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CETONURIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cetonuria can indicate a lack of insulin in individuals with diabetes, signaling potential complications</data>
      <data key="d10">21339c051dc2f47471026673b3ac6436</data>
      <data key="d11">9627f2fa1ce141289b8fa7d4ce4e8219</data>
      <data key="d12">1634</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="EHH">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition characterized by high blood sugar levels, which can lead to various complications. One such complication is EHH (Euglycemic Hyperglycemic Hyperosmolar State), a serious condition that can complicate the management of diabetes. EHH often arises in patients with diabetes mellitus, particularly those experiencing extreme hyperglycemia. The presence of EHH necessitates specific dietary and medical interventions to effectively manage both the diabetes and its associated complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9,eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381</data>
      <data key="d11">e9dac3333c3a45b7830418b27abada38</data>
      <data key="d12">1635</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ACTIVIDAD F&#205;SICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Physical activity is a critical component of diabetes management, affecting blood sugar control and insulin sensitivity</data>
      <data key="d10">ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9</data>
      <data key="d11">2edcae43433f4d7b91c482c852b50885</data>
      <data key="d12">1636</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CAD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CAD is a common complication in patients with diabetes, necessitating careful dietary management to reduce risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">eeb6e04f12698ee82912bdf775d79381</data>
      <data key="d11">d90f035da4494e658f92eff833e382b2</data>
      <data key="d12">1637</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
