    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional guidelines are essential for managing diabetes effectively through dietary choices</data>
      <data key="d10">502bae6c907e900b95f5fe6aa963b0fc</data>
      <data key="d11">6d7fa96f38de491096b856f59dd9b061</data>
      <data key="d12">1640</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="NUTRITION THERAPY">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutrition therapy is essential for managing Diabetes Mellitus and maintaining blood glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">cd2217af0cd2e70226661f038043911b</data>
      <data key="d11">5c8d40e1ec544732aed4e442752446ab</data>
      <data key="d12">1641</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes mellitus puede ser una complicaci&#243;n de la enfermedad hep&#225;tica cr&#243;nica, afectando la supervivencia a largo plazo de los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503</data>
      <data key="d11">dc5fdf709c6c4f09abb93dc3a0345bd3</data>
      <data key="d12">1642</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cirrosis puede llevar al desarrollo de diabetes mellitus en pacientes debido a alteraciones en el metabolismo de la glucosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503</data>
      <data key="d11">f9d1695993e04e4b96fb7f52320eb831</data>
      <data key="d12">1643</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HEMOCRMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis can cause diabetes mellitus due to iron accumulation in the pancreas</data>
      <data key="d10">4d0492ec64ce1b97c53328d60bd5bbdd</data>
      <data key="d11">12fabed165434cf3aea60f93511a84c6</data>
      <data key="d12">1644</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HEREDITARY HEMOCHROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hereditary hemochromatosis can result in diabetes mellitus as a complication due to iron overload affecting insulin production.</data>
      <data key="d10">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d11">a0cbeaf4e60f4294825d6fa3d720ee8b</data>
      <data key="d12">1645</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HIPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperuricemia can be linked to diabetes mellitus, as both conditions can coexist and influence each other.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">e87f1cfa54804919a90a6c302dd5c6f4</data>
      <data key="d12">1646</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="DIARREA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes mellitus mal controlada puede contribuir a la aparici&#243;n de diarrea cr&#243;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d11">3f88fe94b12441a6b43c67f9ec91d485</data>
      <data key="d12">1647</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ENFERMEDAD DE CHAGAS">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions can be associated with systemic health issues and may require careful management</data>
      <data key="d10">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c</data>
      <data key="d11">9cc49fde6b75473d96a0835534708637</data>
      <data key="d12">1648</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="ENFERMEDAD ENDOCRINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is classified as an endocrine disorder due to its hormonal implications</data>
      <data key="d10">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c</data>
      <data key="d11">3b8d9b55dd2b4ce980fc22e79f5021e7</data>
      <data key="d12">1649</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HIPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions can be related to metabolic dysfunctions and may require careful monitoring</data>
      <data key="d10">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c</data>
      <data key="d11">94372825a1d44c2eb1087070960e0608</data>
      <data key="d12">1650</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="HIPOTIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypothyroidism can influence blood sugar levels and metabolic processes</data>
      <data key="d10">0f51b0c02b1e8200f9a98b830621c55c</data>
      <data key="d11">c554b4d8404a4f9f8469f030b8908bc9</data>
      <data key="d12">1651</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="PANCREATITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus often occurs as a complication of chronic pancreatitis, indicating a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2</data>
      <data key="d11">f6c6001a14f140dcb2b372f52200c9f8</data>
      <data key="d12">1652</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="SARCOPENIA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus and sarcopenia are interrelated conditions that can significantly impact health, particularly in older adults. Diabetes mellitus can exacerbate the effects of sarcopenia, leading to further muscle loss and associated health complications. Conversely, sarcopenia can also be worsened by diabetes mellitus, contributing to the overall decline in muscle mass and function. This interplay between the two conditions highlights the importance of addressing both diabetes and sarcopenia to improve health outcomes in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27</data>
      <data key="d11">ae49fda3b6f44be893d809c314d9f83e</data>
      <data key="d12">1653</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes mellitus and fibrosis qu&#237;stica (cystic fibrosis) can co-exist, leading to complications in the nutritional management of affected patients. The presence of diabetes mellitus can complicate the nutritional strategies required for individuals with fibrosis qu&#237;stica, necessitating careful consideration in their dietary planning and management.</data>
      <data key="d10">95ef1473677a26ea6ad77c7db0c55e5e,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4</data>
      <data key="d11">6e269205b38f46c4960044565be07319</data>
      <data key="d12">1654</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="FORMULAS ESPEC&#205;FICAS PARA DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Specific formulas for diabetes are necessary for managing patients with both diabetes and fibrosis qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">95ef1473677a26ea6ad77c7db0c55e5e</data>
      <data key="d11">f0c9acbd778a4c83905ac6468a81d7a9</data>
      <data key="d12">1655</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="TEST DE TOLERANCIA ORAL A LA GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Test de Tolerancia Oral a la Glucosa es utilizado para diagnosticar la diabetes mellitus al medir la respuesta del cuerpo a la glucosa</data>
      <data key="d10">48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4</data>
      <data key="d11">9e2c22ba6f7f4d51bf669e7460344ef0</data>
      <data key="d12">1656</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="OMS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La OMS establece criterios diagn&#243;sticos para la diabetes mellitus, incluyendo el uso del TTOG</data>
      <data key="d10">48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4</data>
      <data key="d11">dc31edaca0c34aa4a9964938947bcb30</data>
      <data key="d12">1657</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="GEP">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes mellitus are at increased risk for complications during GEP procedures</data>
      <data key="d10">b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707</data>
      <data key="d11">06b946c0067640ab9165792c9b5ad835</data>
      <data key="d12">1658</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS" target="BRONCOASPIRATION">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes mellitus may experience higher rates of broncoaspiration due to their condition</data>
      <data key="d10">b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707</data>
      <data key="d11">02fc20a0975940f79ebd3400ef54394b</data>
      <data key="d12">1659</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO CR&#211;NICO" target="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic alcoholism is one of the leading causes of cirrhosis, linking the two conditions</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">1ac1c06ed659449e8be9dbc6010c1ef8</data>
      <data key="d12">1660</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO CR&#211;NICO" target="PANCREATITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic alcoholism is a leading cause of chronic pancreatitis, linking the two events closely</data>
      <data key="d10">803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2</data>
      <data key="d11">cccc66a8c43c4c789269b318b6fbb2b1</data>
      <data key="d12">1661</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEOPLASIAS" target="C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neoplasms can be cancerous and are influenced by dietary factors, making them a significant health concern.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">988a4a49db1c4d88bf330eea4003b2bf</data>
      <data key="d12">1662</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEOPLASIAS" target="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neoplasias can cause ascitis quilosa due to obstruction of lymphatic flow</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">db5f10456d714b8084459bd0c676e628</data>
      <data key="d12">1663</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEOPLASIAS" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neoplasias can lead to complications such as quilot&#243;rax, affecting the management and prognosis of the patient.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">0f32909c642d477c8bb0a25b0f21ca76</data>
      <data key="d12">1664</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BOCIO" target="HIPOTIROIDISMO CONG&#201;NITO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bocio can be a clinical manifestation in cases of congenital hypothyroidism due to insufficient hormone production</data>
      <data key="d10">0171dc124a749b9b7abb823f09b1aba7</data>
      <data key="d11">254f49796c5b439583d6c6179c129bb8</data>
      <data key="d12">1665</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CAVIDAD ORAL" target="DOF">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The oral cavity is where sensory stimulation occurs to aid in the swallowing process for patients with dysphagia oropharyngeal</data>
      <data key="d10">c257fcbbfdc5ac2678d371cee5c12edf</data>
      <data key="d11">ac7892891e304cd78c60c3a6cf85d31a</data>
      <data key="d12">1666</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CAVIDAD ORAL" target="HIGIENE BUCODENTAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hygiene of the cavidad oral is a critical aspect of maintaining overall health and preventing infections</data>
      <data key="d10">04fc50226ccbf87e5833a09d52275757</data>
      <data key="d11">2862d49056ad4b3ba6383794d14380a3</data>
      <data key="d12">1667</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CAVIDAD ORAL" target="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oral cavity hygiene is essential for critical patients receiving enteral nutrition to prevent infections</data>
      <data key="d10">4ce0bfcd129ba597d70d90d2120c1996</data>
      <data key="d11">7211513594dd4f618c9ba5901aca8e85</data>
      <data key="d12">1668</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PRESBIFAGIA" target="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Presbifagia describes the age-related changes affecting elderly patients' swallowing abilities</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">ad7f16c32dc54609a1e79f0bb4f47500</data>
      <data key="d12">1669</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="SARCOPENIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is a significant factor affecting the swallowing ability of elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">692a4d8e88b94b81bda758544c89751d</data>
      <data key="d12">1670</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="DINAPENIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dinapenia contributes to the swallowing difficulties experienced by elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">000ad9643564469f92db72bacd3694fb</data>
      <data key="d12">1671</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="KRATOPENIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kratopenia affects the endurance of elderly patients, impacting their ability to swallow</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">6569d5b853b345748c2b80b2242b1ba5</data>
      <data key="d12">1672</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="F&#193;RMACOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Certain medications can exacerbate swallowing difficulties in elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">185a8dfecb0b41249c0e487e1bcf0578</data>
      <data key="d12">1673</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="DOF">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia oropharyngeal dysfunction is particularly prevalent among elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">43f45d59526d45b3a260d383bc518a05</data>
      <data key="d12">1674</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="ENVEJECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aging is a significant factor that increases the risk of dysphagia in elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">7aa9366155684b4380bba5a9c5e2b5f3</data>
      <data key="d12">1675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="MASA MUSCULAR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Loss of muscle mass is a contributing factor to swallowing difficulties in elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">88b3ab3d5770442c86f39c930ef37acc</data>
      <data key="d12">1676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE MAYOR Y MAYOR-MAYOR" target="FUNCIONALIDAD DE LA DEGLUCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The functionality of swallowing is often compromised in elderly patients due to various health issues</data>
      <data key="d10">e34366e525fb1dbc8468a7f4e6d91cb7</data>
      <data key="d11">e2a4367ead6243cf8c626e0bd0e1d003</data>
      <data key="d12">1677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="DOF">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia can contribute to dysphagia by weakening the muscles involved in swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d10">0bff3417518c19ae80d20de8150be58b</data>
      <data key="d11">0192ed83cae74049ad18a39e40e5bc89</data>
      <data key="d12">1678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">38.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia and fragilidad (fragility) are closely related conditions that significantly impact the health of elderly patients. Fragility is often associated with sarcopenia, which involves the loss of muscle mass and strength. This relationship is intrinsic, as sarcopenia is recognized as one of the primary causes of the frailty syndrome in older adults. Both sarcopenia and fragilidad are characterized by a decline in strength and an increase in vulnerability, making them critical factors in the overall health and well-being of the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d10">00a918807f0c6568ea1d9f0c41f1ad49,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6,56da8c0bffe9c7811cc9790d767f4972,a6a4604a5fc2c91b714b6ba568bb0090,bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c</data>
      <data key="d11">d8b93cae7fd349649eafe89f2f89dc52</data>
      <data key="d12">1679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="ELDERLY POPULATION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The elderly population is at risk of sarcopenia, which contributes to frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d11">ea90d02a2d754d46923dd1d6e10cca9f</data>
      <data key="d12">1680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="MULTIMORBIDITY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Multimorbidity can lead to sarcopenia, as multiple chronic conditions can affect muscle mass and strength</data>
      <data key="d10">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d11">bd8f3f57386c4ebcaa5b2d25793b84e0</data>
      <data key="d12">1681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="MORLEY JE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Morley JE has contributed to the understanding of sarcopenia in the context of frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">ea432f742f5cd2b4840a984ae35a9d09</data>
      <data key="d11">dfcd27d1e45349b4900da3903c3993eb</data>
      <data key="d12">1682</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="FRAGILIDAD COGNITIVA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is linked to cognitive frailty, as both conditions can influence each other in the elderly</data>
      <data key="d10">b5f705e0ba650f5ad1f558446be0191e</data>
      <data key="d11">d6136322847347198efcfdc1f1aaee2c</data>
      <data key="d12">1683</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="EUROPEAN CONSENSUS">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, particularly in the elderly. The European Consensus outlines the diagnostic criteria and management strategies for sarcopenia, providing comprehensive guidelines for its diagnosis. This consensus emphasizes the connection between sarcopenia and frailty in elderly patients, highlighting the importance of recognizing and addressing this condition to improve health outcomes in this vulnerable population.</data>
      <data key="d10">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,a527688a9f74d33efc23a2a94d33163b</data>
      <data key="d11">951526f0209545e48bdeb5185de19c4e</data>
      <data key="d12">1684</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="FRAILTY">
      <data key="d8">57.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia and frailty are interrelated conditions that frequently coexist in older adults. Both conditions are characterized by a decline in muscle mass and physical capacity, which are key features that link them. Sarcopenia, defined as the loss of muscle mass, is often considered a contributing factor to frailty, increasing the vulnerability of elderly patients to various health issues. As such, sarcopenia is recognized as a characteristic of frailty, highlighting the close relationship between these two conditions in the aging population.</data>
      <data key="d10">066ca85c476fdb709bb2b588cb86a55a,4b3664b368fad59fd55189a65e19b000,5898660be8944e9248ba187ffd7553b1,8205166235be6abd77947eb2f7c5ab27,87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c,a830f202c73ba48c11fb8863e0e4a642,e155d9b2d1858daab734fd68a45d0c0a</data>
      <data key="d11">763ca5ad98dc449dbc47fdec6c529293</data>
      <data key="d12">1685</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="HANDGRIP STRENGTH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Handgrip strength is a key measure used in the diagnosis of sarcopenia</data>
      <data key="d10">87e62f930efe0b81911357297ccd271c</data>
      <data key="d11">a75f427dbca249109e2b124a85e180f5</data>
      <data key="d12">1686</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="JAPANESE WOMEN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The study conducted by Kim HK involved Japanese women suffering from sarcopenia</data>
      <data key="d10">2f194bef97e28167f81acc7a66ac56ab</data>
      <data key="d11">d26a589e4ff4463c8f4d49136d6baff5</data>
      <data key="d12">1687</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="DIETA IDEAL PARA LOS MAYORES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ideal diet for older adults aims to prevent sarcopenia through adequate protein and amino acid intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d11">22de6de39c7647119215f625acf6dd18</data>
      <data key="d12">1688</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="AMINO ACID SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amino acid supplementation is investigated as a treatment for sarcopenia in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">d93c7f9ea61d85e6be22df63c4b67d4d</data>
      <data key="d11">ec9004fb494f409c8a85cc30ad645b2a</data>
      <data key="d12">1689</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="BIA MULTIFRECUENCIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BIA multifrequency can help monitor changes in body composition related to sarcopenia</data>
      <data key="d10">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f</data>
      <data key="d11">7ded80e1cd794edea56ee73a36bdeb24</data>
      <data key="d12">1690</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis is a liver condition that frequently results in sarcopenia, which is characterized by a reduction in muscle mass and strength. The metabolic alterations and nutritional deficiencies associated with cirrhosis contribute significantly to the development of sarcopenia. As such, sarcopenia is recognized as a common complication of cirrhosis, impacting the overall health and physical capabilities of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c,5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854</data>
      <data key="d11">90c3474481c94f96bef982af57b064c1</data>
      <data key="d12">1691</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="CHILD-PUGH CLASSIFICATION">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is an important factor that can influence the Child-Pugh classification in assessing liver disease</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">fdcbf2cff8fd47e8801f802e87647a68</data>
      <data key="d12">1692</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia and malnutrition are closely interconnected, particularly in patients with cirrhosis. Malnutrition in these patients encompasses sarcopenia, which is characterized by a reduction in muscle mass and strength. Inadequate nutrition significantly contributes to the development of sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of addressing nutritional deficiencies to mitigate muscle loss in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b9c137acf3599eaa41c3514aba67a8a,b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854</data>
      <data key="d11">823d6ca859964a6dacc339d2ca81072d</data>
      <data key="d12">1693</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="EHCA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with EHCA frequently experience sarcopenia as a result of accelerated protein catabolism and malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d11">04c461f6d2294bcc9a551cb0255d4e72</data>
      <data key="d12">1694</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTION">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, which can significantly impact the health and quality of life of individuals, particularly those with liver disease. Nutritional intervention plays a crucial role in addressing this issue, as it can help mitigate the effects of sarcopenia in patients suffering from liver-related ailments. Furthermore, nutritional intervention is recognized as a key strategy in managing sarcopenia and preventing its progression to fragility. By implementing appropriate dietary changes and nutritional support, individuals at risk of sarcopenia can improve their muscle health and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,5d87d36fec170e242e5e50305a1bec49</data>
      <data key="d11">d803cb53bc0a44808a386a40b75d3009</data>
      <data key="d12">1695</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="AMMONIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased ammonia levels can contribute to sarcopenia by disrupting muscle metabolism and function</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d11">55dbaa73b49646dc82737e8b1ab009ec</data>
      <data key="d12">1696</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
