    <edge source="SARCOPENIA" target="MALNUTRITION">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sarcopenia is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength, which can be significantly influenced by malnutrition. In particular, malnutrition is a contributing factor to the development of sarcopenia, especially in patients suffering from liver disease and liver cirrhosis. This relationship highlights the importance of adequate nutritional support in managing and preventing sarcopenia in these vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d10">025274b58725397020078dea52ea012b,125bf798b37a7f42c661002099924973</data>
      <data key="d11">a8394128b70c4f4385fdc532bde2e16e</data>
