    </edge>
    <edge source="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" target="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support may involve the use of a nasogastric tube for patients who cannot eat by mouth</data>
      <data key="d10">f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
      <data key="d11">be4e473fcde94061801d15ebda17a772</data>
      <data key="d12">1975</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA, or nasogastric tube, is a medical device employed to administer NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL, or enteral nutrition, to patients who are unable to receive oral feeding. This method is particularly useful for short-term feeding solutions, allowing healthcare providers to deliver essential nutrients directly to the stomach. The use of nasogastric tubes is a common practice in clinical settings for patients requiring nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d10">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d,a089d87928ddde83e1945eece488d3f5,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca</data>
      <data key="d11">93f96338eb5c40c997e04c032f93192b</data>
      <data key="d12">1976</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sonda nasog&#225;strica is a method of enteral nutrition discussed in the context of post-surgical care for oncology patients</data>
      <data key="d10">7c43869fff0960219e47d176597b35b8</data>
      <data key="d11">ef4e6a8918994dbca42d9c4b84a0cc7e</data>
      <data key="d12">1977</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SONDA NASOG&#193;STRICA" target="FIADOR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El fiador es un dispositivo utilizado en la colocaci&#243;n de la Sonda Nasog&#225;strica para facilitar su inserci&#243;n</data>
