    <edge source="HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N" target="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entity "HOSPITALIZACI&#211;N" refers to the process of admitting a "PACIENTE" for medical care. In this context, the patient may be hospitalized to receive treatment for eating disorders when their condition is severe or does not improve with outpatient care. Specifically, the patient was hospitalized due to severe malnutrition and associated health complications, as well as for the treatment of other serious medical conditions. This indicates that the hospitalization was necessary to address critical health issues that could not be managed effectively in an outpatient setting.</data>
      <data key="d10">3bd6f34f55dc7500746b997ebeecf327,449d46789f604265753884e2d371ec8c,b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf</data>
