    <edge source="DYSPHAGIA" target="HEAD NECK">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DYSPHAGIA and HEAD NECK are interconnected through research focused on the impact of head and neck cancers on swallowing functions. The journal "Head &amp; Neck" publishes studies that explore the relationship between these cancers and dysphagia, highlighting the swallowing difficulties experienced by patients diagnosed with head and neck cancer. This body of work aims to enhance understanding of the swallowing issues that arise in this patient population, thereby contributing to improved management and treatment strategies for dysphagia associated with head and neck malignancies.</data>
