    <edge source="DYSPHAGIA" target="IOWA ORAL PERFORMANCE INSTRUMENT">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dysphagia is a condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, and the Iowa Oral Performance Instrument (IOPI) is a valuable tool utilized in research to assess various parameters pertinent to this condition. The IOPI specifically measures strength and endurance in patients suffering from dysphagia, thereby establishing a direct relationship between the instrument and the management of the condition. Through its application, the IOPI aids in understanding the functional capabilities of individuals with dysphagia, contributing to better diagnosis and treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">1d3c30089c42a02917c7625774aa29f2,f943b9dd611368ee970abcd341b660a9</data>
