      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PATIENT" target="MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mini Nutritional Assessment is utilized to evaluate the nutritional status of patients. This assessment helps in determining the nutritional needs and potential risks of malnutrition among individuals, ensuring that appropriate interventions can be implemented to support their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">67ac4ae2f7a1b9b3455a1d1da9c20161,687a74f539aea483b8c6611f3b062931</data>
      <data key="d11">92923e24481044d09cf4eec385138a70</data>
      <data key="d12">2321</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PATIENT" target="NUTRITIONAL TREATMENT PLAN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients identified as malnourished or at risk are the ones who will receive a nutritional treatment plan.</data>
      <data key="d10">c639615d7681ffeb945a996d231bb7aa</data>
      <data key="d11">222baa1f22544457b160d8383a4e7075</data>
      <data key="d12">2322</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PATIENT" target="DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a condition that directly affects patients, necessitating tailored nutritional strategies to manage their health. Patients diagnosed with diabetes must carefully manage their condition through diet, as it significantly influences their dietary and nutritional needs. Therefore, individuals with diabetes are required to adopt specific dietary practices to effectively control their condition and maintain overall well-being.</data>
