    <edge source="PATIENT" target="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT">
      <data key="d8">41.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support is crucial for patients, particularly those with diabetes, as it plays a significant role in effectively managing their condition. This support is especially important for patients in critical care, where careful monitoring and management of nutritional intake and health conditions are necessary. Patients receiving nutritional support must meet their energy and protein needs, particularly during periods of illness or recovery. In specific cases, such as patients with oncological conditions, like those affected by neuroendocrine tumors, nutritional support becomes even more vital to address the unique challenges posed by their health status. Overall, nutritional support is an essential component of patient care, ensuring that their dietary needs are met to promote recovery and overall well-being.</data>
