    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" target="MUST">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA utilizes the MUST tool as an essential component for screening malnutrition in community settings. MUST, which stands for Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool, is specifically designed to assess nutritional status and identify individuals at risk of malnutrition within the community. This tool plays a crucial role in the field of clinical nutrition, ensuring that appropriate interventions can be implemented to address malnutrition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d11">dadd57ddcf3d4773ac34a8cda1b3cfe8</data>
      <data key="d12">2504</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" target="NRS-2002">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA employs the NRS-2002 tool, which is specifically designed for assessing nutritional risk in hospitalized patients. The NRS-2002 is a valuable instrument in clinical nutrition, facilitating the evaluation of the nutritional status of individuals in a hospital setting.</data>
      <data key="d10">4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d11">e1534200b48047be9a60b12200f93dd6</data>
      <data key="d12">2505</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" target="VSG">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clinical Nutrition employs the VSG method for evaluating nutritional status in hospital settings</data>
      <data key="d10">4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185</data>
      <data key="d11">1728c5fc1d7b412a95943520b10f1531</data>
      <data key="d12">2506</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA" target="MNA">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA encompasses the use of the MNA (Mini Nutritional Assessment) as a tool for evaluating the nutritional status of elderly patients. The MNA is specifically designed to assess the nutritional needs and conditions of older adults, making it an essential component in the field of clinical nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4734ce2075bc72c352950c018bab7185,fbbb8c2530f7ac5635ecf5110ea186b2</data>
      <data key="d11">b186f48132f847e1b7f5513d51858ecf</data>
