    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">61.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL refer to forms of nutritional support provided to patients who are unable to consume food orally. Enteral nutrition is a specific type of artificial nutrition that is particularly recommended for patients experiencing moderate to severe health issues, including those with diabetes. It is utilized when patients cannot feed themselves through traditional oral means, ensuring they receive essential nutrients. 

In clinical settings, enteral nutrition is a common practice and is often employed as part of a broader nutritional intervention strategy. While enteral feeding is a primary method of providing nutritional support, it may not always be sufficient on its own, indicating that additional nutritional support methods may be necessary. Overall, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the management of patients requiring artificial nutrition, ensuring they receive adequate dietary intake when oral consumption is not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d10">397cb82cce268866351c44a5b38ccb8b,4b19145e0977ee48b7132c9915d8c284,61ece3be5a1146d0a386ccd0a379c88b,8d1eb00b23450a2f2cb1243ea32aa36f,a6ccbda174f6599eeeb2e4cdb00db5f2,b4580c82418cd4df97f400e183702858,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613</data>
      <data key="d11">7b2bd24f6e7d44bdb93ecc373a428bd0</data>
      <data key="d12">2602</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
