    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PANCREATITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">74.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and PANCREATITIS AGUDA are closely related in the context of managing patients with acute pancreatitis. Acute pancreatitis can complicate the administration of enteral nutrition due to the reduced stimulation of pancreatic secretions. However, enteral nutrition is considered essential when patients with acute pancreatitis are stable enough to tolerate oral intake. It plays a crucial role in the management of these patients, particularly in severe cases, as it ensures adequate nutritional support and helps reduce the incidence of infections, thereby improving recovery outcomes.

Enteral nutrition is recommended for patients with acute pancreatitis to enhance their nutritional status and support clinical evolution. It serves as a vital nutritional intervention through the gastrointestinal tract, which is beneficial for patients suffering from this condition. Overall, enteral nutrition is recognized as a key treatment option for managing acute pancreatitis, especially in more severe forms of the disease, to ensure proper nourishment and facilitate recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,5d4476c2c40af44f9d54628af0ac463d,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,b1464c57df2eaa651a10c1522ab7db68,be7eb01a6daf673db6a127f66c79c96c,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
      <data key="d11">68f6a8d267db4660b846ff3f60a303f5</data>
      <data key="d12">2641</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
