    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is a form of nutritional support that may be necessary for patients with CIRROSIS who are unable to maintain adequate oral intake or meet their nutritional needs through oral means. This intervention is crucial for ensuring that individuals with CIRROSIS receive the essential nutrients required for their health and recovery, particularly when their ability to consume food normally is compromised.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d11">3e8f815f661a4a7abbfd36f10e3c7cb5</data>
      <data key="d12">2643</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ESPEN">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is a key focus of the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN), which provides guidelines and recommendations for its use in various clinical scenarios. According to ESPEN, enteral nutrition is particularly beneficial for patients with liver diseases, as it can help manage their nutritional needs effectively. Additionally, ESPEN advocates for enteral nutrition as a method to enhance intestinal adaptation, which is crucial for patients recovering from gastrointestinal surgeries or conditions. Furthermore, ESPEN emphasizes the importance of enteral nutrition for critically ill patients, highlighting its role in supporting their overall health and recovery during critical care.</data>
      <data key="d10">61890d3cb54fb752b95a4dfad8db8bb6,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d11">178c48cd8e71491198f34740b2b8d514</data>
      <data key="d12">2644</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HEPATOPAT&#205;A">
