    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DE LUIS ROM&#193;N DA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is a field of study that focuses on providing nutrition to individuals who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. De Luis Rom&#225;n DA is an author who has made significant contributions to this area, enhancing the understanding and knowledge surrounding enteral nutrition. He has written extensively on the subject, sharing insights and research that inform best practices in the administration and management of enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347</data>
      <data key="d11">007f459165504774b8ed9d0a69bdb258</data>
      <data key="d12">2675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="TERRROBA LARUMBE C">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Terrroba Larumbe C is an author contributing to the knowledge on enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347</data>
      <data key="d11">8a57e611bd914ebd9351377ad047ee15</data>
      <data key="d12">2676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and GASTROSTOM&#205;A are closely related concepts in the context of providing nutritional support to patients. Gastrostomy is a medical procedure that facilitates enteral nutrition for individuals who require long-term nutritional assistance. This procedure is particularly important for patients who cannot tolerate oral diets or when oral feeding is not feasible. In such cases, gastrostomy serves as a viable option to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients directly into the stomach, thereby supporting their overall health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3,7469cc60475806b519e91abe2796aead,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,bd3be91ff178508497a810f873861eca</data>
      <data key="d11">a872d0746cb8444194e9beab2542d5d8</data>
      <data key="d12">2677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and DIETOTERAPIA are closely related concepts within the field of clinical nutrition management. Dietoterapia plays a crucial role in enteral nutrition by allowing healthcare professionals to create personalized dietary plans that cater to the specific needs of patients. This practice encompasses enteral nutrition as a fundamental component, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients through this method. Nutrici&#243;n enteral is frequently utilized within the framework of dietoterapia to effectively deliver essential nutrients to individuals who may have difficulty consuming food orally. Together, these entities highlight the importance of tailored nutritional strategies in supporting patient health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">2206bb4d5efe2dcf644ee48468ea112c,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,e5ec5005272f7691eba86e2cc7240f5a</data>
      <data key="d11">e51259dc87de456a8aa944167a8070ac</data>
      <data key="d12">2678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="F&#205;STULAS DIGESTIVAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Digestive fistulas may require specific management in enteral nutrition practices</data>
      <data key="d10">76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347</data>
      <data key="d11">df24f4e5f05748389276a88ecfcb64c7</data>
      <data key="d12">2679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL is a critical intervention for patients diagnosed with S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO, commonly known as short bowel syndrome. This condition arises when a significant portion of the small intestine is absent or has been surgically removed, leading to challenges in nutrient absorption. To address these challenges, enteral nutrition is employed to ensure that patients receive an adequate intake of essential nutrients despite the reduced length of their intestines. Consequently, patients with short bowel syndrome often rely on enteral nutrition support to meet their dietary needs and maintain their overall health.</data>
      <data key="d10">6321383c8b1370699d20007624cd87c8,76bdd5f53571ff68dd1e439219572347,f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d11">4f5315e6ef41400c809a510752c290d0</data>
      <data key="d12">2680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="FORMULAS ENTERALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral nutrition often involves the use of enteral formulas to provide necessary nutrients</data>
      <data key="d10">f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
      <data key="d11">2881b40d17cb4382aabd2fcd8da67856</data>
      <data key="d12">2681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
