      <data key="d11">19ab26c36853490691a300d7fde6a837</data>
      <data key="d12">2848</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="VAR&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El var&#243;n de 75 a&#241;os est&#225; recibiendo nutrici&#243;n enteral debido a su incapacidad para alimentarse por v&#237;a oral.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21</data>
      <data key="d11">db277a32167949edaa096f0a7a9b2e49</data>
      <data key="d12">2849</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="IMC">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral se eval&#250;a en funci&#243;n del IMC del paciente para determinar su estado nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21</data>
      <data key="d11">d809e510b0e2498983e36845ed099496</data>
      <data key="d12">2850</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EST&#193;NDAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n est&#225;ndar es el tipo de nutrici&#243;n enteral que se est&#225; administrando al var&#243;n de 75 a&#241;os.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21</data>
      <data key="d11">0dbde1255598423a80ed304dda85917a</data>
      <data key="d12">2851</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="BOLOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral puede ser administrada en forma de bolos, que es una t&#233;cnica utilizada en el tratamiento del var&#243;n de 75 a&#241;os.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b0e0d4e1d3067bf7e0e850063a43d21</data>
      <data key="d11">4a2b889348144fddbbe3f7fc7fde4163</data>
      <data key="d12">2852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="RESIDUO G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL y RESIDUO G&#193;STRICO est&#225;n interrelacionados en el contexto del cuidado de pacientes que reciben nutrici&#243;n enteral. El monitoreo del residuo g&#225;strico es una pr&#225;ctica recomendada para asegurar la tolerancia a la alimentaci&#243;n en estos pacientes. La medici&#243;n del residuo g&#225;strico se realiza con el prop&#243;sito de evaluar la tolerancia del paciente a la nutrici&#243;n enteral, lo que es crucial para ajustar el tratamiento y garantizar la efectividad de la nutrici&#243;n administrada.</data>
      <data key="d10">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289,69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">ea136576e3b44ca296469f29715c25dc</data>
      <data key="d12">2853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ESTRATEGIAS PARA REDUCIR EL RIESGO DE ASPIRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las estrategias se implementan para mejorar la seguridad del paciente durante la nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289</data>
      <data key="d11">69aa02ba12164f57b69db0eb765c4f47</data>
      <data key="d12">2854</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="BLOQUE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El bloque de soporte nutricional avanzado proporciona directrices para la administraci&#243;n de nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289</data>
      <data key="d11">82cd817a2c0e4ea2aa786a0e2f315122</data>
      <data key="d12">2855</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="FIGURA 2">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La figura 2 muestra el manejo del residuo g&#225;strico en el contexto de la nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289</data>
      <data key="d11">929a741e709c4648893d6792257d5950</data>
      <data key="d12">2856</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="TABLA 4">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La tabla 4 detalla estrategias espec&#237;ficas para mejorar la seguridad de la nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">13c6297da17b9be4a67cf439f62cd289</data>
      <data key="d11">34993a884a114a04b291d78693a78bab</data>
      <data key="d12">2857</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="GASTROPARESIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La gastroparesia es una condici&#243;n que puede complicar la nutrici&#243;n enteral al afectar el vaciado g&#225;strico.</data>
      <data key="d10">6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a</data>
      <data key="d11">a1ab2a7ac67a478387e8de44f697b966</data>
      <data key="d12">2858</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="VACIADO G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El vaciado g&#225;strico es un proceso esencial que afecta la eficacia de la nutrici&#243;n enteral en los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a</data>
      <data key="d11">a50021d59eaf4878aa6b9c0b68e33fbf</data>
      <data key="d12">2859</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="T&#201;CNICA DE ADMINISTRACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La t&#233;cnica de administraci&#243;n es crucial para la correcta implementaci&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral en los pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">6a5102072d17111dafe768ab7d38f41a</data>
      <data key="d11">2dca27ef7a46409090c0a6f5a0f37aa3</data>
      <data key="d12">2860</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Advanced nutritional support often involves enteral nutrition, which can be associated with diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d10">d3e1df90991ea82fcccbd02589473ead</data>
      <data key="d11">3f7f2a54de5842af8d391109f24c5184</data>
      <data key="d12">2861</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="OSTOM&#205;AS">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and OSTOM&#205;AS are interconnected in the context of medical procedures for patients requiring long-term nutritional support. Ostomies are surgical interventions that may be performed on patients who need enteral nutrition, providing a means for these individuals to receive essential nutrients when traditional methods are not viable. This surgical option is particularly relevant for those who require ongoing enteral nutrition, highlighting the role of ostomies in facilitating adequate dietary intake for patients with specific health needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada,7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d11">fd48d6bc4eb64172ba39ed55447db260</data>
      <data key="d12">2862</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="AGENTES ANTIDIARREICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Antidiarrheal agents may be used in patients receiving enteral nutrition to manage diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">09e9623b3facc5045e80541b1cd2cada</data>
      <data key="d11">ff37923135a84f74940bfbf4406410b9</data>
      <data key="d12">2863</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DIARREA INFECCIOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral puede llevar a la diarrea infecciosa como una de sus complicaciones</data>
      <data key="d10">e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">dba0cf9225204fcfa6ddd853663f2641</data>
      <data key="d12">2864</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ESTOMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral puede requerir la creaci&#243;n de un estoma, que puede estar sujeto a infecciones</data>
      <data key="d10">e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">65afb668a6e44e5c8cc7f156802bbb5d</data>
      <data key="d12">2865</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HIDRATACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and HIDRATACI&#211;N are closely related components in patient care, particularly for those who require nutritional support. Hydration is often administered alongside enteral nutrition to ensure that patients receive adequate fluids, which is crucial for their overall health. Additionally, hydration is considered an essential element of enteral nutrition, as it helps to prevent complications that may arise from inadequate fluid intake. Together, these two aspects work synergistically to support the well-being of patients receiving enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27,e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">34dec17d3e8b44c78abe149022671f89</data>
      <data key="d12">2866</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NAUSEAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral puede causar n&#225;useas en algunos pacientes, lo que puede complicar su tratamiento</data>
      <data key="d10">e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">08f3690034514d0299fe14dba119e4a2</data>
      <data key="d12">2867</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="V&#211;MITOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los v&#243;mitos pueden ser una complicaci&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral, afectando la eficacia del tratamiento</data>
      <data key="d10">e7a9d9aa3031b4c032d724047f80ebe9</data>
      <data key="d11">5cce1740ae744a3496e8f2622c9692c1</data>
      <data key="d12">2868</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ALIMENTACI&#211;N POR V&#205;A ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral feeding is a method of providing nutrition that falls under the broader category of enteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa</data>
      <data key="d11">8f27bf548bc8427ca9db3175c4eb98ef</data>
      <data key="d12">2869</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SONDAS">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL refers to the process of delivering nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, typically when oral intake is not possible. SONDAS, or feeding tubes, are essential tools in this process, as they are specifically designed to administer enteral nutrition to patients who cannot consume food orally. These devices facilitate the delivery of necessary nutrients, ensuring that individuals receive adequate nutrition despite their inability to eat by mouth.</data>
      <data key="d10">44b25f00a145b92a9875173aafbc27c8,6906ee13020e48a5d50fc97dc22928fa</data>
      <data key="d11">40da6a07d8d74c66b693d021f8f5282c</data>
      <data key="d12">2870</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SONDA NASOENT&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nasoenteric tubes are utilized in enteral nutrition for patients requiring longer-term support</data>
      <data key="d10">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d11">dce00489654943d5b0406b3f210b1b57</data>
      <data key="d12">2871</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ALGORITMO PARA LA ELECCI&#211;N DE ACCESO EN NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The algorithm provides guidance on the access methods for enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">7d29ccd4b2eeb48ab5572fd3c6c2802d</data>
      <data key="d11">c350e6b017e143188ca72a4aa035d6c7</data>
      <data key="d12">2872</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="DALY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Daly's research involved the evaluation of immunomodulatory formulas in the context of enteral nutrition for surgical patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f965e7f43fe2ea0144b4b16715a04ba</data>
      <data key="d11">f70a0fc5af1440f992122b7ed45518bd</data>
      <data key="d12">2873</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SENKAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Senkal's study focused on the effects of enteral nutrition before and after surgery, contributing to the understanding of nutritional support in surgical patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f965e7f43fe2ea0144b4b16715a04ba</data>
      <data key="d11">f8d09a67c547476d8f4aab918a81c567</data>
      <data key="d12">2874</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ANA BEL&#201;N MART&#205;NEZ ZAZO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ana Bel&#233;n Mart&#237;nez Zazo is involved in pediatric nutrition, which includes enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">2a2468b526a34096954a2910f03281c3</data>
      <data key="d12">2875</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="&#211;SCAR RUBIO CABEZAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#211;scar Rubio Cabezas's research in pediatric endocrinology may involve aspects of enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">3c7b88039ca142dabeac0504640e44b6</data>
      <data key="d12">2876</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CONSUELO PEDR&#211;N GINER">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Consuelo Pedr&#243;n Giner specializes in nutrition, which includes enteral nutrition for pediatric patients</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">7c28c8a47e0440769ba6540c9752461d</data>
      <data key="d12">2877</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HOSPITAL LA MORALEJA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospital La Moraleja provides pediatric care, including enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">c997b3ebdbeb44959b45abde9b4df4d3</data>
      <data key="d12">2878</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="HOSPITAL INFANTIL UNIVERSITARIO NI&#209;O JES&#218;S">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospital Infantil Universitario Ni&#241;o Jes&#250;s provides pediatric care, including enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">6f3657ed2ddd481f8268147c2fb68279</data>
      <data key="d12">2879</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="JOURNAL OF PEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY AND NUTRITION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition publishes research related to enteral nutrition in children</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">0974e070b5cf40a8a07799b23be03304</data>
      <data key="d12">2880</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF PEDIATRICS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Journal of Pediatrics includes studies and articles on enteral nutrition for pediatric patients</data>
      <data key="d10">561247e03fd2c7b8ca61c7f8ee874d38</data>
      <data key="d11">cbb95721658645e598eae7617a42de50</data>
      <data key="d12">2881</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA are closely related concepts in the context of providing nutritional support to children. Nutritional support for children frequently utilizes enteral nutrition as the primary method of delivery. This approach is particularly important in pediatric care, where enteral nutrition methods are employed to address various feeding disorders. Together, these entities highlight the significance of enteral nutrition in ensuring adequate dietary intake and support for pediatric patients facing nutritional challenges.</data>
      <data key="d10">e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87,ec4fd77add427ab49ea4b8687b94b263</data>
      <data key="d11">2790186db28c45e69a37e180cfacb58e</data>
      <data key="d12">2882</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="F&#211;RMULAS A PARTIR DE ALIMENTOS NATURALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Natural food-based formulas are utilized in enteral nutrition for patients with chronic diseases</data>
      <data key="d10">e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87</data>
      <data key="d11">391f563121264f2794e6938555af75df</data>
      <data key="d12">2883</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="RECI&#201;N NACIDOS PREMATUROS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral es esencial para el cuidado y la alimentaci&#243;n de los reci&#233;n nacidos prematuros, ayudando a evitar complicaciones como la desnutrici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3</data>
      <data key="d11">3b85ef1d0e1848668ccbb9467b8ded36</data>
      <data key="d12">2884</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="LECHE MATERNA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La leche materna es un componente clave en la nutrici&#243;n enteral de los reci&#233;n nacidos prematuros, proporcionando nutrientes esenciales y mejorando la adaptaci&#243;n intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3</data>
      <data key="d11">fe5a00effe3f4b3d8d7d3425d6fc10d2</data>
      <data key="d12">2885</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CPAP">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El uso de CPAP puede afectar la tolerancia a la nutrici&#243;n enteral en reci&#233;n nacidos prematuros, lo que requiere un manejo cuidadoso.</data>
      <data key="d10">724f16660e0077267b0836a0e1fb02c3</data>
      <data key="d11">17aa5b97cc724a04bb7c88a4187b956e</data>
      <data key="d12">2886</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ALIMENTACI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral y la alimentaci&#243;n parenteral son dos m&#233;todos de nutrici&#243;n artificial utilizados en pacientes que no pueden alimentarse de manera convencional.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">2e6b1bd0acf24a95a25a37ca7156485e</data>
      <data key="d12">2887</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PACIENTE PEDI&#193;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes pedi&#225;tricos a menudo requieren nutrici&#243;n enteral debido a sus necesidades espec&#237;ficas de desarrollo y salud.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">8dc14574ebbb481eaf0c3a013fabd59f</data>
      <data key="d12">2888</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="EDAD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La edad del paciente influye en la cantidad y tipo de nutrici&#243;n enteral que se debe administrar.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">4767eb81d5c44cb384655510e2ee5794</data>
      <data key="d12">2889</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="RITMO INICIAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El ritmo inicial es un componente clave en la administraci&#243;n de nutrici&#243;n enteral, determinando c&#243;mo se inicia el tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">8ff71044409f4f5e8a209a1bcf1da81d</data>
      <data key="d12">2890</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="AUMENTO DIARIO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El aumento diario es un aspecto cr&#237;tico en la progresi&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral, ajust&#225;ndose seg&#250;n la respuesta del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">dd745879d1da4f84a1006bf6246c6d15</data>
      <data key="d12">2891</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="M&#193;XIMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El m&#225;ximo se establece para asegurar que la nutrici&#243;n enteral no exceda la capacidad del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">61a67472bc154a419dda5ddf284a80a7</data>
      <data key="d12">2892</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N POSTPIL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n postpil&#243;rica es una modalidad de nutrici&#243;n enteral utilizada en pacientes con necesidades espec&#237;ficas.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">53bbcae3e6934f04840508c57c8958b5</data>
      <data key="d12">2893</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="LOGOPEDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El logopeda trabaja en la rehabilitaci&#243;n de la degluci&#243;n, lo cual es crucial para los ni&#241;os que reciben nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">1954fd8f08f7411d95d88363fc3603ab</data>
      <data key="d12">2894</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PSIC&#211;LOGO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El psic&#243;logo ayuda a abordar los aspectos emocionales y conductuales relacionados con la alimentaci&#243;n en ni&#241;os que reciben nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">cf2dc4e06ae6495eb17bec4c7734047f</data>
      <data key="d12">2895</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PEDIATRA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El pediatra es responsable de la prescripci&#243;n y supervisi&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral en pacientes pedi&#225;tricos.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">fa504c4274d64170b514b09f48767305</data>
      <data key="d12">2896</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="FAMILIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La familia juega un papel crucial en el apoyo y la implementaci&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral en el hogar.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">0033533a089c4ab88e2de2331469dd5b</data>
      <data key="d12">2897</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="ENFERMOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los enfermos son los beneficiarios de la nutrici&#243;n enteral, que les ayuda a mejorar su calidad de vida.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">21ad2707763149a696c61333e3c71b87</data>
      <data key="d12">2898</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El desarrollo adecuado del sistema nervioso central es esencial para la alimentaci&#243;n y la degluci&#243;n en ni&#241;os que reciben nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b85b34282f79a12349b7e1d967b1a7</data>
      <data key="d11">2bd63e16990841d0b65e794a62d48c4d</data>
      <data key="d12">2899</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Home enteral nutrition is a specific application of enteral nutrition in pediatric care</data>
      <data key="d10">7ea112a550fd775a80c3eda15663fba5</data>
      <data key="d11">1a7a7109ced84b9e90ee247ab37d5292</data>
      <data key="d12">2900</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="TERRY SCHIAVO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Terry Schiavo's case raised significant ethical questions about the withdrawal of enteral nutrition in patients with persistent vegetative states</data>
      <data key="d10">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d11">1e34777a580042ffb78ab57cad9b6a5a</data>
      <data key="d12">2901</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="EUGLANA ENGLANO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Euglana Englano's situation is similar to that of Terry Schiavo, highlighting the ethical dilemmas surrounding enteral nutrition withdrawal</data>
      <data key="d10">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d11">35472c6c10dd436892533750bdb15235</data>
      <data key="d12">2902</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="CUIDADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral nutrition is considered a form of medical care aimed at providing essential nutrients to patients</data>
      <data key="d10">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d11">8ebcc1693cca45d59ace0e191cb64004</data>
      <data key="d12">2903</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="GRUPOS RELACIONADOS CON EL DIAGN&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral es un procedimiento que puede influir en la clasificaci&#243;n de pacientes en los GRD, afectando su complejidad y consumo de recursos</data>
      <data key="d10">b6336e61e2a290a5c471fd72297d6093</data>
      <data key="d11">c008bd6e0a85475590894e14d286231a</data>
      <data key="d12">2904</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="RIESGO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Managing risks is crucial in enteral nutrition to prevent complications related to feeding methods.</data>
      <data key="d10">07e45dae0f017eba9ef9f48439de5c59</data>
      <data key="d11">c9cf165fec8c4640a75c3b2f303e695e</data>
      <data key="d12">2905</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ORAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral se utiliza cuando la nutrici&#243;n oral no es suficiente para satisfacer las necesidades del paciente.</data>
      <data key="d10">3159307e5633698722f72fde1e82702f</data>
      <data key="d11">08d0c70292ad4655a9a2d9c996f84c0b</data>
      <data key="d12">2906</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="PACIENTES CR&#211;NICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic patients may receive enteral nutrition to manage their health conditions and improve their quality of life</data>
      <data key="d10">29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721</data>
      <data key="d11">8731c386785f417b9d729db47c8e4a63</data>
      <data key="d12">2907</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n enteral es un componente de la nutrici&#243;n artificial domiciliaria, utilizada para pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por v&#237;a oral.</data>
      <data key="d10">123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490</data>
      <data key="d11">aa703834e3074f2fa937a25f38169083</data>
      <data key="d12">2908</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIBADO" target="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients undergo screening (cribado) to assess their nutritional risk before surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfa3e3e6e6101b4d607871e17276705</data>
      <data key="d11">f2e5062d75a34785b00329e4b96d9adf</data>
      <data key="d12">2909</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIBADO" target="ALTERACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Screening is often used to detect alterations in health before symptoms appear</data>
      <data key="d10">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d11">3fce01282302499eba096a3a9dc0edaa</data>
      <data key="d12">2910</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MCHORNEY CA" target="SWALLOWING QUALITY OF LIFE QUESTIONNAIRE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">McHorney CA is a key author in the development of the SWAL-QOL questionnaire</data>
      <data key="d10">188b9989e78550b42ac06b2d89822bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">3d630d8d989f48a2ad1171bf6ed76dd6</data>
      <data key="d12">2911</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BURGOS R" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO PUERTA DEL MAR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Burgos R has contributed to malnutrition studies at Hospital Universitario Puerta del Mar</data>
      <data key="d10">d52ef4e5955918a8a47b697fcdb4096f</data>
      <data key="d11">dd6609b1ac0a4f9282a70e052970dadd</data>
      <data key="d12">2912</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="&#205;NGEA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#205;NGEA follows the guidelines set by ESPEN for nutritional assessment and treatment in patients with dysphagia</data>
      <data key="d10">39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8</data>
      <data key="d11">83b8ff42b72f40808c1e5bcbfed5627e</data>
      <data key="d12">2913</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING 2002">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends the Nutritional Risk Screening 2002 as a gold standard for assessing nutritional risk in hospitalized patients</data>
      <data key="d10">39f9c76ac9952fa528996c6dc7b33ed8</data>
      <data key="d11">cac2950f89f04448b5fe92a55cc2276a</data>
      <data key="d12">2914</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N UNIVERSAL SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MUST tool is recommended by ESPEN for identifying malnutrition risk in adults</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfa3e3e6e6101b4d607871e17276705</data>
      <data key="d11">641cc33d6f7b4a9291b5864be04bfb7d</data>
      <data key="d12">2915</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="BAPEN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN and BAPEN are both organizations dedicated to the promotion of clinical nutrition and metabolism, with ESPEN representing a European focus and BAPEN a British one. They collaborate to provide guidelines for clinical nutrition, working together to enhance the standards and practices in this vital field.</data>
      <data key="d10">0379ef9e3f56ccd30c572884eb5bd723,ebfa3e3e6e6101b4d607871e17276705</data>
      <data key="d11">7a8a7b97448e496cabb64e02072d2417</data>
      <data key="d12">2916</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN, the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, plays a crucial role in the management of nutritional needs for patients with cirrhosis. The organization provides comprehensive clinical guidelines that outline best practices for addressing the nutritional requirements of these patients. Additionally, ESPEN emphasizes the importance of utilizing various nutritional assessment methods to ensure that the specific needs of individuals with cirrhosis are effectively met. Through these efforts, ESPEN aims to improve the overall health and quality of life for patients suffering from this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d11">6c9c4e987e014e3cb881f6fb9cb79c9d</data>
      <data key="d12">2917</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">32.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN (European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism) provides comprehensive guidelines for the use of parenteral nutrition, particularly in situations where enteral feeding is not feasible. These guidelines cover a range of clinical scenarios, including the administration of parenteral nutrition in patients with pancreatitis, liver diseases, and those experiencing intestinal failure. Additionally, ESPEN emphasizes the importance of managing patients who require nutritional support, ensuring that their specific needs are met. The organization also addresses the use of parenteral nutrition in post-surgical patients, highlighting best practices for effective nutritional management in these contexts. Overall, ESPEN's guidelines serve as a critical resource for healthcare professionals involved in the care of patients requiring parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,61890d3cb54fb752b95a4dfad8db8bb6,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682,f087e20586f6b263059597e194a04993</data>
      <data key="d11">c7c63348d4be48d8b0d60f55f51b828d</data>
      <data key="d12">2918</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="TRASPLANTE HEP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides clinical guidelines for nutritional treatment in liver transplantation, influencing patient care</data>
      <data key="d10">b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa</data>
      <data key="d11">c550742dc7d3425792a4b9c7ba8292ca</data>
      <data key="d12">2919</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="GU&#205;AS CL&#205;NICAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN's clinical guidelines provide recommendations for managing nutritional needs in liver transplant patients</data>
      <data key="d10">b86f20e3d8bb0128635881d88ba6bdfa</data>
      <data key="d11">dac2de1e3a80480ca5d563fbb5f3a63d</data>
      <data key="d12">2920</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN, the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, plays a crucial role in establishing guidelines for nutritional support across various medical contexts. It emphasizes the importance of nutritional support for malnourished patients, particularly those undergoing hemodialysis. Additionally, ESPEN provides comprehensive guidelines that inform best practices for nutritional support in diverse medical situations, including oncology. The organization also recommends preoperative nutritional support for patients identified as being at high nutritional risk, highlighting the significance of tailored nutritional interventions in improving patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">36cffc3e7c3a6fe82e50787e939f7537,58ae94a34f90df368b032f1618c7bcec,97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4,c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d11">33b6120139804ae7b84bfd7c6959131b</data>
      <data key="d12">2921</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="TPH">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends enteral nutrition for patients undergoing TPH</data>
      <data key="d10">61890d3cb54fb752b95a4dfad8db8bb6</data>
      <data key="d11">a153519b16a44b869acbb3fdb0e3b9c2</data>
      <data key="d12">2922</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="GLUTAMINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines that include studies on glutamine and its nutritional implications</data>
      <data key="d10">ce8f5f24dbbf8624e49a6f85c2ad0d04</data>
      <data key="d11">a61d80a185a54f18a35c5a37906600f3</data>
      <data key="d12">2923</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN (the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism) recommends the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) as an effective screening tool for identifying nutritional risk and detecting malnutrition specifically in elderly populations, particularly among frail elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">54633fef79a422c0fada846ff2b861ba,687a74f539aea483b8c6611f3b062931</data>
      <data key="d11">07068e4ca4484ce58569c77b05d59f66</data>
      <data key="d12">2924</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MNA">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN (the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism) recommends the use of the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) tool for elderly patients. This recommendation emphasizes the importance of MNA in detecting malnutrition risk specifically in frail elderly individuals. ESPEN advocates for MNA as an effective nutritional screening method to identify those at risk of malnutrition within the elderly population.</data>
      <data key="d10">14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
      <data key="d11">2961b9e7ec1541c58fdde6b07d019e9f</data>
      <data key="d12">2925</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends the use of the NRS 2002 tool for nutritional risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822</data>
      <data key="d11">dad43ef373db462bbdba2f76287360af</data>
      <data key="d12">2926</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MALNUTRITION UNIVERSAL SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends the MUST tool for screening malnutrition in various settings</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822</data>
      <data key="d11">19c900c0b139493ab1b3dff435843e6f</data>
      <data key="d12">2927</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="FORBES A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Forbes A contribuy&#243; a las gu&#237;as de ESPEN sobre nutrici&#243;n cl&#237;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb</data>
      <data key="d11">a56f02967cef49f7b110bc8790d98156</data>
      <data key="d12">2928</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="KLEK S">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Klek S contribuy&#243; a las gu&#237;as de ESPEN sobre la gesti&#243;n de la falla intestinal aguda</data>
      <data key="d10">0a844e2dc679c0578ba4bdeda742c2eb</data>
      <data key="d11">cead427a7188424b8ec3cceabddf0920</data>
      <data key="d12">2929</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="WEIMANN A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Weimann A contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition in surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">8281bce9bf3e465d8eac52817eaf2903</data>
      <data key="d12">2930</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="ARENDS J">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arends J contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on nutrition in cancer patients</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">67cdad2d6ae44b4182bf925dd44fba7f</data>
      <data key="d12">2931</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="CANCER">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines specifically addressing the nutritional needs of cancer patients</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">4a36d3f046ed42bfb7f9fe1892d3a4ac</data>
      <data key="d12">2932</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="DEMENTIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN, the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, provides comprehensive guidelines for managing nutritional support in patients with dementia. These guidelines include specific recommendations aimed at ensuring that individuals with dementia receive appropriate nutritional care to support their health and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">242881af1a0439ab16c10b788cff01fd,dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">fe3479ce31664c0b96605e2b8f3ea291</data>
      <data key="d12">2933</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN, the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, provides comprehensive guidelines for the management of short bowel syndrome (S&#237;ndrome de Intestino Corto). These guidelines encompass various aspects of care, with a particular emphasis on nutritional strategies to support individuals affected by this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a65e02e4e364419b836920c093055fe,9f3f6014b1a9e68b22c02862a9143a33</data>
      <data key="d11">76b9a9f2b92d440aa266752d57ccc418</data>
      <data key="d12">2934</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines that the Ministry of Health follows for home parenteral nutrition practices</data>
      <data key="d10">e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb</data>
      <data key="d11">e57db28425234ed78ce8f4ad60122ca8</data>
      <data key="d12">2935</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN PACIENTE QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines that are referenced in the chapter 'Nutrici&#243;n en paciente quir&#250;rgico'.</data>
      <data key="d10">0b02ff4978fb09a0b2a360ae8c661337</data>
      <data key="d11">8bd869ba6396458e8422b0792ad1e5ea</data>
      <data key="d12">2936</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NOURISH">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The NOURISH study aligns with ESPEN's guidelines on the use of oral nutritional supplements for malnourished elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d11">33d3594b535b4a17ad999fd96f456619</data>
      <data key="d12">2937</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MALNOURISHED PATIENTS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends the use of oral nutritional supplements for malnourished patients to improve their health outcomes</data>
      <data key="d10">c940d6c62fa57d30867f7a8533492471</data>
      <data key="d11">26e0cc3702ff4b928263ab691cc4a549</data>
      <data key="d12">2938</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="DRE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN proporciona gu&#237;as sobre el soporte nutricional para pacientes con DRE, especialmente en demencia</data>
      <data key="d10">76c4ef07f382585bf943bfaf57372c86</data>
