      <data key="d12">2939</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las gu&#237;as de la ESPEN son relevantes para el manejo de la paciente con s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto.</data>
      <data key="d10">5cf8b1c5491f78fda9bca97f3d14c5a2</data>
      <data key="d11">6dfb2c5b557b4d4a81f9ea87d51eb8bd</data>
      <data key="d12">2940</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="ASPEN">
      <data key="d8">49.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN and ASPEN are professional organizations dedicated to the field of clinical nutrition, focusing on the development and dissemination of guidelines and recommendations for nutritional practices in healthcare settings. Both organizations emphasize the importance of nutritional support for various patient populations, including those undergoing surgery and oncology patients. They publish evidence-based guidelines that address the nutritional needs of patients with intestinal issues, highlighting their collaborative or complementary relationship in this area. Furthermore, ESPEN and ASPEN work together to establish international standards and practices for parenteral and enteral nutrition, demonstrating their coordinated efforts to enhance nutritional management across different healthcare contexts.</data>
      <data key="d10">07a16ed299a7f8bafcaa44a54495a9c3,2b8c323c265f8f7f3d15bf988bf1f9ee,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,90fe1d34782402a1896d33ad5bb47614,c3182f51249513a920db6b935632fead,eae8ddef005974a2ffe71cf7c61b0634,f75d1340b39e345875bf878dba07ab8c</data>
      <data key="d11">9a00ba1480ee41a48cedf53cce481eae</data>
      <data key="d12">2941</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="DM TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines that are relevant for managing patients with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus</data>
      <data key="d10">5aa4da1a8d1e0b60ec7e801c7db1701c</data>
      <data key="d11">7ad4876d78da4d249ecda6c9d3a048fc</data>
      <data key="d12">2942</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="MUST">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN recommends the use of the MUST (Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool) for nutritional screening in the general population, particularly emphasizing its application for community patients. This endorsement highlights the importance of the MUST tool in identifying individuals at risk of malnutrition, thereby facilitating timely interventions to improve nutritional health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866</data>
      <data key="d11">5de173b85913499ba95452e857bdc96a</data>
      <data key="d12">2943</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESPEN" target="NRS-2002">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN endorses the NRS-2002 method for assessing malnutrition risk in hospitalized patients and recommends its use for nutritional screening specifically in surgical patients. This highlights the importance of NRS-2002 as a reliable tool for identifying individuals at risk of malnutrition within these healthcare settings.</data>
      <data key="d10">14039baea6555ffc156768e503ff0b90,7906ee47aaf0c271f072790eaea05866</data>
      <data key="d11">12830e0bf30c4ff099d03ba546faf19c</data>
      <data key="d12">2944</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
