      <data key="d9">Scoring is used to assess the nutritional status of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfa3e3e6e6101b4d607871e17276705</data>
      <data key="d11">eceb65b3ec2547009aa894e8f2219a9d</data>
      <data key="d12">3036</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="CUIDADOR">
      <data key="d8">39.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entities "PACIENTE" (Patient) and "CUIDADOR" (Caregiver) are closely linked in the context of managing dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Caregivers play a crucial role in assisting patients with dietary modifications necessary for their condition. They ensure that patients are positioned correctly during meals and adhere to safety protocols to prevent choking. The caregiver's responsibilities include managing oropharyngeal dysphagia and ensuring that patients follow treatment recommendations. Overall, caregivers are essential in facilitating safe eating practices for patients with dysphagia, employing proper feeding techniques to enhance the patient's safety and well-being during meals.</data>
      <data key="d10">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,28e2e3a92ef4dd76af0898ae3e3df522,2d50b3b46d83d6e824edc64e142cbf8a,362634b4b8ce951770d2a81e572f15b2,7c842769e1890739769789ed10a08005</data>
      <data key="d11">f574525322d44a228f64d2b149fb7500</data>
      <data key="d12">3037</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="MEDICAMENTOS">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient, referred to as "PACIENTE," is influenced by the number of medications they take, which can have an impact on their nutritional status. Additionally, it is important to note that medications must be specially administered to the patient, particularly if they have dysphagia, to ensure their safety during the intake process. This highlights the need for careful management of the patient's medication regimen in relation to their overall health and specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515,8e8aac45bfe71fa006f622690dfdbbb8</data>
      <data key="d11">59c8ed2c60c2493b9e86a2949e34511e</data>
      <data key="d12">3038</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="JERINGAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Syringes should not be used for the patient with dysphagia to prevent aspiration</data>
      <data key="d10">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d11">6bd439aa62464635b43f6398862d16d8</data>
      <data key="d12">3039</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="PAJITAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Straws should be avoided for the patient with dysphagia to prevent aspiration</data>
      <data key="d10">0e756c1673317aaf495b90b8bcb02515</data>
      <data key="d11">f40d67f2e1684cf78aa152d3a8365f95</data>
      <data key="d12">3040</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="VASOS DE BOCA ANCHA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Wide-mouth cups are recommended for the patient with dysphagia to facilitate safe drinking</data>
