      <data key="d12">3043</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="DIETA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PACIENTE must adhere to a specific DIETA to effectively manage their diabetes and insulin requirements. This DIETA is tailored to meet the individual nutritional needs of the patients, ensuring that they receive the appropriate dietary support necessary for their health management.</data>
      <data key="d10">058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375,abf638322cfb1c522bfbee1852e28a19</data>
      <data key="d11">47977f9103b04346bfca2bcc7de98036</data>
      <data key="d12">3044</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional supplements are provided to patients to enhance their dietary intake</data>
      <data key="d10">058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375</data>
      <data key="d11">97b3cf4437624872925c2cb68c4b3c24</data>
      <data key="d12">3045</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="PLAN DE TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The treatment plan is specifically designed for the patient diagnosed with oropharyngeal dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b</data>
      <data key="d11">b9d67daa694b4d2a984c803d9a3d3ee9</data>
      <data key="d12">3046</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="FAMILIARES">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entities involved are "PACIENTE" (Patient) and "FAMILIARES" (Family Members). Family members play a crucial role in supporting the patient during their treatment for oropharyngeal dysphagia. They are not only a source of emotional and practical support but also have a significant role in medical decision-making. In situations where the patient is unable to consent to treatment, family members can be consulted to make decisions regarding the patient's medical care. Additionally, they may be asked to provide consent on behalf of the patient if the patient is incapacitated. This involvement underscores the importance of family in the patient's healthcare journey, particularly in critical moments when the patient's ability to make decisions is compromised.</data>
      <data key="d10">9934fdd98a0d66fb3ff7ac1b56b18460,e14475004a93d47a14d98dd4c5b5d02b,e475fe60f9aab6773eddfe8bad25eef6,eaa675a346becd53a4fcfacbb99def88</data>
      <data key="d11">1b127502413a4ff9ba2eae9f1feacd7e</data>
      <data key="d12">3047</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="CERVICOARTROSIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
