    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="HIGIENE BUCODENTAL">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entity "PACIENTE" is the recipient of "HIGIENE BUCODENTAL" practices, which are essential for maintaining oral health. Maintaining oral hygiene is crucial for the patient to prevent complications during feeding and ensure safety. This is particularly important for patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, as proper oral hygiene practices help prevent complications associated with their condition. Overall, the integration of oral hygiene practices is vital for the well-being of the patient.</data>
      <data key="d10">1719a8d20788e3b25240980cad2b6c5d,7c842769e1890739769789ed10a08005,bfc7f52d9f15519c092dee53ea9dcc33</data>
      <data key="d11">9d5954cfd55c4baaae72b1b0908f0969</data>
      <data key="d12">3060</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="ENFERMERA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The enfermera is responsible for providing oral care to the paciente, ensuring their hygiene and comfort</data>
      <data key="d10">bfc7f52d9f15519c092dee53ea9dcc33</data>
      <data key="d11">d18a8e8c1c9a4945af96ee773534cc31</data>
      <data key="d12">3061</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
