    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entity "PACIENTE" refers to individuals who may face challenges in meeting their nutritional needs. When patients are unable to consume food orally or when oral feeding is insufficient, they may require "NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" to prevent malnutrition. This artificial nutrition is crucial for maintaining the health of patients who cannot adequately nourish themselves through traditional means. However, it is important to note that patients receiving artificial nutrition are at risk for developing hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood. Additionally, the administration of artificial nutrition can influence sodium management, particularly in patients undergoing treatment for conditions such as SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion). Therefore, careful monitoring and management of sodium levels are essential for patients receiving artificial nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">306519cca8810e0ff1c973128a75200a,6c8b41c09b1ada129f0908d6e5d18185,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb</data>
