    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="PEG">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PEG, or Percutaneous Endoscopic Gastrostomy, is a method utilized for providing nutrition to patients who are unable to eat by mouth, particularly due to conditions such as dysphagia. This feeding technique allows for direct delivery of nutrients into the stomach, ensuring that patients receive the necessary sustenance when oral intake is not possible.</data>
