    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="IMC">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The IMC (&#205;ndice de Masa Corporal) of the paciente (patient) has been a crucial metric in evaluating her condition of obesidad m&#243;rbida (morbid obesity) and guiding her treatment. Recent assessments indicate that the IMC of the paciente has decreased, which suggests a deterioration in her estado nutricional (nutritional status). The IMC is widely used to assess the nutritional status of patients and to determine their risk of desnutrici&#243;n (malnutrition). Additionally, the patient's IMC is a critical factor in deciding the necessity for bariatric surgery, highlighting its importance in her overall health management.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a0d6adfbef59dd174ade59071dd9aa5,82d36ebbaaa026c713df2b7a47253efa,d6469f98d2161058fb7b214a1a800441,ea7d8ba0550547d4cff0b5d18c3f6ae5,efe29025266e1689abb9b0a2783e5ea3</data>
