    <edge source="PACIENTE" target="CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICILE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clostridium difficile, often referred to as C. difficile, is a common cause of diarrhea, particularly in patients who are undergoing multiple antibiotic therapies. In this context, a patient exhibiting gastrointestinal symptoms was tested for the presence of Clostridium difficile to determine if it was the underlying cause of her condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7a2c1e4dd77f47605fdb33f4a2c2bdf,d3e1df90991ea82fcccbd02589473ead</data>
