    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="NP">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support may also involve NP for patients who cannot receive nutrition enterally</data>
      <data key="d10">8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a</data>
      <data key="d11">a5bd1818826840ec923f3b014ee46930</data>
      <data key="d12">3712</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="PROTEINS">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support plays a crucial role in the health and recovery of various patient populations, particularly concerning the intake of proteins. For patients recovering from bariatric surgery, adequate protein intake is essential to facilitate healing and recovery. Similarly, diabetic patients require careful management of their protein intake to align with their specific dietary needs, ensuring that their nutritional support is tailored to their condition. Additionally, for patients with renal insufficiency, the intake of proteins is a critical component of their nutritional support, as it must be monitored and adjusted to prevent further complications. Overall, proteins are a fundamental aspect of nutritional support across these diverse patient groups, highlighting their importance in promoting health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">6517add809ee588bede013f59f20b0ef,8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a,97a728c18b63007d07b6a4a5fc22d5e4</data>
      <data key="d11">ad1783c635764c26a6e15b1226706fb3</data>
      <data key="d12">3713</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="FATS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support emphasizes limiting fat intake to manage diabetes effectively</data>
      <data key="d10">8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a</data>
      <data key="d11">0bc6c2fe14184c99be773df7af3a6f54</data>
      <data key="d12">3714</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="FIBER">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support encompasses various dietary components, with fiber playing a significant role in this context. Fiber is particularly highlighted for its benefits in managing patients with diarrhea, where it can help regulate bowel movements. Additionally, for diabetic patients, nutritional support includes specific recommendations for fiber intake, emphasizing its importance in maintaining overall health and managing blood sugar levels. Thus, fiber is a crucial element of nutritional support, beneficial for both gastrointestinal health and diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d10">8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a,8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d11">211ead19068540a0afcd53fb13a7eb22</data>
      <data key="d12">3715</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="ELECTROLYTES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support addresses the management of electrolytes in diabetic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a</data>
      <data key="d11">c097632bbea6456dbfeebd8b1da23701</data>
      <data key="d12">3716</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="HEAD AND NECK SURGERY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support is often required for patients undergoing head and neck surgery due to the impact on their ability to eat</data>
      <data key="d10">8c1c8ef18f5c90fe936a3ca920768ee2</data>
      <data key="d11">764127e40f2749a2991002a1486b91dc</data>
