    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="CANADIAN GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Canadian guidelines provide recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, including specific formulas and practices</data>
      <data key="d10">8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d11">6c5ab6a1dcd448248440da8fd1e7efbb</data>
      <data key="d12">3763</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="SEPSIS">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support plays a complex role in the context of sepsis. On one hand, it can increase the risk of sepsis in patients, especially those with compromised immune systems. On the other hand, it is critical for managing patients who are already suffering from sepsis, as their nutritional needs are often significantly altered due to the condition. Providing appropriate nutritional support is essential for these patients, as it can improve their recovery outcomes. Thus, while nutritional support may pose risks in certain vulnerable populations, it is also a vital component in the care of patients with sepsis to enhance their healing process.</data>
      <data key="d10">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1,ee3700469e1c419d283b34f38100fa29</data>
      <data key="d11">16e2a233ef844ee7b52a09e215252439</data>
      <data key="d12">3764</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="PROBIOTICS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Probiotics are considered as part of nutritional support strategies in critical care, although their use is limited due to inconsistent evidence</data>
      <data key="d10">8d9c5b85d058d0d3cde4479b5589a7d1</data>
      <data key="d11">ceb6af3c02c34acca3f451a6e886c133</data>
      <data key="d12">3765</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
