    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT" target="INFECTION">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support is a critical aspect of patient care, particularly for those undergoing procedures such as Gastroenteric Permeation (GEP). However, it is important to note that infection is a potential complication associated with these nutritional support procedures. Specifically, in hematological patients, the provision of nutritional support can lead to an increased risk of infection. This highlights the need for careful monitoring and management of infection risks when implementing nutritional support strategies in vulnerable patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d10">10bde114bd1285b3aeeec94dd4292d9e,b0b96ec7b9f57581fe18f0ac902af707</data>
