    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL" target="MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional screening processes like the Mini Nutritional Assessment are essential for identifying malnutrition risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">f764c1a74fbbce262e79b50639acb7bd</data>
      <data key="d11">530cb32958a545458beb8b56a31879f0</data>
      <data key="d12">3832</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL" target="NUTRICION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional screening is essential for identifying patients who may need further nutritional assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a</data>
      <data key="d11">c25700e9bb18413d87637774708d1085</data>
      <data key="d12">3833</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL" target="HOSPITALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El cribado nutricional se realiza en hospitales como parte de la atenci&#243;n a los pacientes ingresados.</data>
      <data key="d10">969bdfc6cc15b9089e96000addd87561</data>
      <data key="d11">9d680810c94d4a9fafde2e279e789245</data>
      <data key="d12">3834</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="TABLA VII">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Foods are listed in Table VII as part of the fluid intake for maintaining hydration balance.</data>
      <data key="d10">186a95fdfe908123ad6f42d43b52ee1d</data>
      <data key="d11">4b14307ed03b425290038e0d58488847</data>
      <data key="d12">3835</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="ESPESANTES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Foods can be thickened using thickeners to improve texture and safety for individuals with dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c1fcea6b2c2290b4c90ae1a511ca05d4</data>
      <data key="d11">c6a7ae277a2247c0a593e935a4024e61</data>
      <data key="d12">3836</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="SERVICIO DE COCINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Kitchen Service is responsible for preparing and serving foods that meet the nutritional needs of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">544f7d3afd9f7def46c357525e55cabf</data>
      <data key="d11">213ced75e855486aba05ef57e6766dd0</data>
      <data key="d12">3837</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="APPCC">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The APPCC system is designed to ensure the safety of alimentos by identifying and controlling potential hazards</data>
      <data key="d10">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d11">7b57ddab3a90426f895cc0d6686277b2</data>
      <data key="d12">3838</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="CIRCUITO ADECUADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Maintaining a adecuado circuito is essential for ensuring the safety of alimentos and preventing contamination</data>
      <data key="d10">3128497d6ade013c21bc21fd378528fb</data>
      <data key="d11">79f0e9e1969e487eb9dca32778100550</data>
      <data key="d12">3839</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="DIETA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entities "ALIMENTOS" and "DIETA" are closely related to dietary guidelines that emphasize the importance of specific food items in both children's diets and the nutritional needs of patients. The dietary guidelines recommend various foods that should be included in a child's diet to ensure they receive adequate nutrition. Additionally, the foods outlined in these dietary plans are essential for meeting the nutritional requirements of patients, highlighting the critical role that proper nutrition plays in health and development across different age groups.</data>
      <data key="d10">058edb7500a486cc3196de4ca335b375,56e7bab8da5c5e8d37b7545618a648bb</data>
      <data key="d11">710e95b832aa4e79af2553a7ec576606</data>
      <data key="d12">3840</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="HORMONAS TIROIDEAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ciertos alimentos pueden inhibir la producci&#243;n de hormonas tiroideas, afectando la salud tiroidea.</data>
      <data key="d10">89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">e3838a6a775145d8be6924dcacf4abd6</data>
      <data key="d12">3841</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition provides nutrients intravenously when oral or enteral intake is not possible, thus bypassing the digestive system</data>
      <data key="d10">1870ba6878c109f3023c9d15d0fa784b</data>
      <data key="d11">e99c964230cf4132ac1a13957991ee38</data>
      <data key="d12">3842</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="RECORDATORIO DE 24 HORAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Recordatorio de 24 horas involves recalling all food items consumed, thus directly relating to alimentos</data>
      <data key="d10">701eb4c24e94839def8d18882a2dda63</data>
      <data key="d11">60009081d364471ca10705caaa10e273</data>
      <data key="d12">3843</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="COCINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alimentos are prepared in the Cocina for patient meals</data>
      <data key="d10">caeec333a833f2df895a80c4047485cb</data>
      <data key="d11">42cb457b629948c98cc128559f504947</data>
      <data key="d12">3844</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="DIETA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hospital diet planning dictates specific foods to be included or excluded based on dietary needs</data>
      <data key="d10">8d7a18d8258ab74a0e56129f937a8a84</data>
      <data key="d11">cf5bb897d9bf47eea7bb54a9fb2153be</data>
      <data key="d12">3845</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="INGESTA CAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los alimentos con alta densidad energ&#233;tica pueden aumentar la ingesta cal&#243;rica</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">3e97018dd54a4ca2936838ac8b03ea72</data>
      <data key="d12">3846</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="PALATABILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los alimentos con mayor contenido de grasa suelen tener una mayor palatabilidad</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">cfb48c1d34784785a5eaee994e417745</data>
      <data key="d12">3847</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="M&#193;S BARATOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los alimentos energ&#233;ticamente m&#225;s densos suelen ser m&#225;s baratos, lo que puede influir en la elecci&#243;n de los consumidores</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">3fe169a81c8d46e8a5bcfb7a5b292449</data>
      <data key="d12">3848</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTOS" target="DIETAS POR RACIONES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alimentos are categorized in dietas por raciones to provide a structured approach to meal planning</data>
