      <data key="d11">ef43021059054cbc99d6fe355bb8cfe7</data>
      <data key="d12">4195</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="V&#211;MITOS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN CIRUG&#205;A DE TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vomiting is a significant concern in the nutritional management of patients undergoing surgery for head and neck tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">2bbe847617971cacfe15b2c970de2d21</data>
      <data key="d11">00fd4eb9af0b4fdabebab20b6db7e825</data>
      <data key="d12">4196</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="V&#211;MITOS" target="NA&#218;SEAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las n&#225;useas pueden llevar a v&#243;mitos, impactando negativamente la ingesta.</data>
      <data key="d10">9562f39f9e78644164daeff3177a2f84</data>
      <data key="d11">3db5c18fd2964618afa949703ca64eb9</data>
      <data key="d12">4197</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="V&#211;MITOS" target="ALERGIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los v&#243;mitos son un s&#237;ntoma com&#250;n en reacciones al&#233;rgicas alimentarias.</data>
      <data key="d10">693b5721c7fc52c8165c48b580777840</data>
      <data key="d11">5b1028414270471c98dfa7d343df23c2</data>
      <data key="d12">4198</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="VALORACI&#211;N GLOBAL SUBJETIVA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diarrea es un s&#237;ntoma que se considera en la Valoraci&#243;n Global Subjetiva para evaluar el estado nutricional</data>
      <data key="d10">e12655d89e99e57ce1f6d87563adf674</data>
      <data key="d11">953d703e57a543eeadef2dbb93c40b9a</data>
      <data key="d12">4199</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="HUP LA FE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HUP La Fe provides guidelines for managing diarrhea in patients receiving enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">52a0434694f8face489cdb4c8d206a9e</data>
      <data key="d11">b8886e7bf7fe43e18b9cc12d7ea7fccf</data>
      <data key="d12">4200</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="MALABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea is a common symptom associated with malabsorption syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246</data>
      <data key="d11">e31b74a7dff545f78bc90ef4cb0eb317</data>
      <data key="d12">4201</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diarrea puede incrementar las necesidades de l&#237;quidos y electrolitos en ni&#241;os, lo que debe ser considerado en su tratamiento nutricional</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801</data>
      <data key="d11">02e8a96ec16c49098acad7a51ab35a99</data>
      <data key="d12">4202</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea can lead to magnesium deficiency, indicating a direct relationship between the two.</data>
      <data key="d10">91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d11">cbbd82d3f09c49f0a5152e6e922bb80a</data>
      <data key="d12">4203</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="DISTENSI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DIARREA and DISTENSI&#211;N are interconnected conditions that can influence each other. Distensi&#243;n often accompanies diarrhea due to gas buildup in the intestines, which can occur as a result of various digestive issues. Conversely, distensi&#243;n can also lead to diarrhea, particularly when there is an excess of fluid in the intestines caused by undigested carbohydrates. This relationship highlights the complex interplay between these two gastrointestinal phenomena, where each can exacerbate the other.</data>
      <data key="d10">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">ef99284fe7c641638a9b9566a57755db</data>
      <data key="d12">4204</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="ACUMULACI&#211;N INTRALUMINAL DE AZ&#218;CAR NO DIGERIDO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The accumulation of undigested sugars can lead to diarrhea due to osmotic overload</data>
      <data key="d10">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d11">c04b716662d2408a8cc321098d513f40</data>
      <data key="d12">4205</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="IRRITACI&#211;N REGI&#211;N ANAL Y PERIN&#201;">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea can cause irritation in the anal and perineal region due to the acidic nature of the stool</data>
      <data key="d10">8c87213151750706e4e87956bfc9cb88</data>
      <data key="d11">bd5a6e793e844d66ab8c91f84c88e68c</data>
      <data key="d12">4206</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="MALABSORCI&#211;N DE FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrea is a common symptom experienced by individuals with malabsorci&#243;n de fructosa</data>
      <data key="d10">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e</data>
      <data key="d11">c9e7e88f79f543c8a5e20625a5606803</data>
      <data key="d12">4207</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="ENFERMEDAD CELIACA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diarrea es uno de los s&#237;ntomas m&#225;s comunes de la enfermedad cel&#237;aca, indicando un problema digestivo asociado.</data>
      <data key="d10">68c55f61003b7c0a490a0ee3bc97fcf2</data>
      <data key="d11">b06ce655d4e4463d8ea1eedab5918c22</data>
      <data key="d12">4208</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta cetog&#233;nica puede causar diarrea como una de sus complicaciones gastrointestinales m&#225;s comunes.</data>
      <data key="d10">bf7fc15e1aac41553dc6586efe68b8cb</data>
      <data key="d11">cbe47cf2f3af4f8db7af7a28d770f52b</data>
      <data key="d12">4209</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="SALUD P&#218;BLICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrea can have a significant impact on public health, especially in low-income countries</data>
      <data key="d10">235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3</data>
      <data key="d11">c38a6fa80f4d4354ba794e36ddbf08fd</data>
      <data key="d12">4210</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="OMS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The World Health Organization provides data and guidelines related to the global health issue of diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">0aa57fc31d0e408db1efcd51c91047ef</data>
      <data key="d12">4211</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="UNICEF">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">UNICEF reports on child mortality rates due to diarrhea, highlighting its impact on children under five</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">84da6942ea294816b9c8d9ac69144058</data>
      <data key="d12">4212</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PA&#205;SES AFRICANOS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea is a leading cause of death in children under five in African countries</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">643f103a0347483689571a9ecef9a597</data>
      <data key="d12">4213</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PA&#205;SES DEL SUDESTE ASI&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Southeast Asian countries have a high incidence of diarrhea cases, particularly affecting young children</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">6ad4e0288a954713a9e220de31057624</data>
      <data key="d12">4214</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PA&#205;SES INDUSTRIALIZADOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic diarrhea is more prevalent in industrialized countries, such as the "PA&#205;SES INDUSTRIALIZADOS," primarily due to various lifestyle factors. Despite the acute cases of diarrhea being less life-threatening, chronic diarrhea presents significant health challenges in these regions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">8528723c573948408bc0c424e82415dc</data>
      <data key="d12">4215</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="GALACTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC&#193;RIDOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactooligosaccharides may help alleviate diarrhea by promoting beneficial gut bacteria</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">6566b60f8fcd471da4a8ccb577f2eace</data>
      <data key="d12">4216</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="LACTULOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactulose is used to treat constipation and may help manage diarrhea by affecting gut flora</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">428efad8f41f4a61891e604e2faaadde</data>
      <data key="d12">4217</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="INULINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Inulin can support gut health and may help in managing diarrhea symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">5e551d7ef1e544148b33e3387fce97d3</data>
      <data key="d12">4218</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="FRUCTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSAC&#193;RIDOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fructooligosaccharides can promote gut health and may help in the management of diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">27a102eb131a43c594e536ab3da26731</data>
      <data key="d12">4219</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota plays a significant role in digestive health and can influence the occurrence of diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd</data>
      <data key="d11">08e7da7333434b889ea68873c951d5e8</data>
      <data key="d12">4220</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="S&#205;NDROME DEL INTESTINO IRRITABLE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrea and S&#237;ndrome del Intestino Irritable (Irritable Bowel Syndrome) are interconnected conditions, with diarrhea serving as a common symptom of Irritable Bowel Syndrome. This syndrome can lead to episodes of diarrhea, which can significantly affect an individual's quality of life. The relationship between the two highlights the importance of understanding how Irritable Bowel Syndrome can manifest through gastrointestinal symptoms such as diarrhea.</data>
      <data key="d10">b3c1bed11cc2df0412259e9296e606fd,e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">29fea1dcf6e5403890dd9762bc871e22</data>
      <data key="d12">4221</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PA&#205;SES EN V&#205;AS DE DESARROLLO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In developing countries, diarrhea is often caused by infectious agents, highlighting a different etiology</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">4e233ecf785643da86da04477cfb2851</data>
      <data key="d12">4222</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="F75">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F75 is used as a nutritional treatment for children suffering from severe malnutrition associated with diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">b8e29a8d6213433fbf2721a897e0cdbc</data>
      <data key="d12">4223</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="F100">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F100 is also used for treating severe malnutrition in children with diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">43ba91517ac04f13aacfa17a516b7909</data>
      <data key="d12">4224</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="ALMID&#211;N COCIDO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cooked starch is part of the dietary recommendations for managing diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">0f13de6ddd114a79a995c039a344eb63</data>
      <data key="d12">4225</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="CEREALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cereals are included in dietary recommendations for patients experiencing diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">9cb4ba787d6542bf8f8f43a34b3f94d4</data>
      <data key="d12">4226</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PL&#193;TANOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bananas are recommended for patients with diarrhea to help manage symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">bc0108539e50450fa98e2a66b6ef2475</data>
      <data key="d12">4227</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="YOGUR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Yogurt is suggested for patients with diarrhea due to its probiotic content</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">d09d1f2d2a8345138dffb4385dce88f1</data>
      <data key="d12">4228</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="SOPA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Soup is recommended for hydration and nutrition during diarrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">e318ae466c5fed49e6aeb9c9a23d2d38</data>
      <data key="d11">4f6e66bd33a14b6f8ea3683c2d29903a</data>
      <data key="d12">4229</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="VEGETALES COCIDOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cooked vegetables are advised for patients with diarrhea to provide nutrients</data>
