    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="FIBRA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fiber may play a role in preventing diarrhea, particularly in patients receiving enteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">0bdc356a46149def2545e7939372c20d</data>
      <data key="d11">e4fc91ffa45045f09e3a4bf7d7141240</data>
      <data key="d12">4238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="ESTRE&#209;IMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrea and estre&#241;imiento are both prevalent gastrointestinal symptoms that significantly affect health. These conditions can be interrelated, particularly in the context of irritable bowel syndrome (SII). Understanding the relationship between diarrhea and constipation is essential for effective management and treatment of these common gastrointestinal issues.</data>
      <data key="d10">44f263c31f91c1bc594cbb28bd397c89,90f122c65fbb08f52e052d0e22714849</data>
      <data key="d11">bf6aa171911d42498a47c44b121b7ff4</data>
      <data key="d12">4239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="DISBIOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Disbiosis is related to the occurrence of diarrhea, impacting health</data>
      <data key="d10">90f122c65fbb08f52e052d0e22714849</data>
      <data key="d11">c83f263b1c0b42979c982bdd3616070e</data>
      <data key="d12">4240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="PANCREATITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pancreatitis cr&#243;nica can cause diarrea due to malabsorption of nutrients</data>
      <data key="d10">67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">2211a7197710437fa1a972621946ba1b</data>
      <data key="d12">4241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="COLITIS ULCEROSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea is a primary symptom of colitis ulcerosa, often leading to significant discomfort and complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">ad855af99ce4e32899436ea8e739ccb4</data>
      <data key="d11">201078a4910e46228be207f1df13aea1</data>
      <data key="d12">4242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIARREA" target="EII">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea is a frequent symptom in patients with EII, which can be aggravated by lactose consumption</data>
      <data key="d10">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c</data>
