    <edge source="ASPEN" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ASPEN (American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition) establishes comprehensive guidelines regarding the use of parenteral nutrition for various patient conditions. Specifically, ASPEN provides recommendations for the administration of parenteral nutrition in patients suffering from pancreatitis, as well as those experiencing severe diarrhea and other related conditions. Additionally, ASPEN emphasizes the importance of parenteral nutrition for patients who are unable to receive nourishment through the digestive tract. These guidelines aim to ensure that patients receive appropriate nutritional support tailored to their specific medical needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,be7eb01a6daf673db6a127f66c79c96c</data>
      <data key="d11">8cedda61631d421fa609015e653b4ee2</data>
      <data key="d12">4335</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
