    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">38.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL are closely related concepts in the field of nutritional support. NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a specific method of providing nutrition artificially, particularly in patients who are unable to consume food normally due to various medical conditions. This form of nutrition is utilized when enteral feeding, which involves delivering nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, is not feasible or when the gastrointestinal tract is not functioning properly. 

NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL encompasses various methods of nutritional support, including NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, and is employed in situations where patients require nutritional assistance. Parenteral nutrition is an essential component of the overall management strategy for patients needing artificial nutrition, ensuring that they receive the necessary nutrients when traditional feeding methods are not possible. Thus, both NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL play critical roles in the care of patients with specific dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">397cb82cce268866351c44a5b38ccb8b,4b19145e0977ee48b7132c9915d8c284,61ece3be5a1146d0a386ccd0a379c88b,b4580c82418cd4df97f400e183702858,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb,dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613</data>
      <data key="d11">723342f2684444e3ae0712bc1b7dd946</data>
      <data key="d12">4586</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="BALANCE NITROGENADO (BN)">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition is assessed using nitrogen balance to evaluate protein intake and metabolic status in patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">30d5c2ac31f39f8177bec50f6b5e631b</data>
      <data key="d11">f04f206e715e42d69feb0b4806bfe8b5</data>
      <data key="d12">4587</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GENERALITAT HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Generalitat Hospital Universitari provides services related to Parenteral Nutrition for patients in need</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">339ced7217d242d7a312da61db83c827</data>
      <data key="d12">4588</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="LA FE UNIVERSITY AND POLYTECHNIC HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La Fe University and Polytechnic Hospital is associated with the educational aspects of Parenteral Nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">bee6c4446a084ae5acc7584e7241c94b</data>
      <data key="d12">4589</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="A. V&#193;ZQUEZ POLO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A. V&#225;zquez Polo is an author contributing to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">70cf59bffab041daa462b997e1593526</data>
      <data key="d12">4590</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="E. L&#211;PEZ BRIZ">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">E. L&#243;pez Briz is an author contributing to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">da3bc1c119ae4d6aafe04298c9db5dda</data>
      <data key="d12">4591</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="B. BALERDI P&#201;REZ">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">B. Balerdi P&#233;rez is an author who has contributed to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition, focusing on the methods and indications associated with this nutritional approach.</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d11">79ef94c2ed414584afce8edb171439a5</data>
      <data key="d12">4592</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="K. GARC&#205;A MALPARTIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">K. Garc&#237;a Malpartida is an author contributing to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">fa261fd53ba84543914489271a4f4626</data>
      <data key="d12">4593</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="M. ARGENTE PLA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M. Argente Pla is an author contributing to the chapter on Parenteral Nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">bfd843969b854df194b74fff074af5d2</data>
      <data key="d12">4594</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support in hospitals includes both parenteral and enteral nutrition methods</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">9cd803a952254f4caa899c1ec594d3e9</data>
      <data key="d12">4595</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPERCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition can be tailored to provide hypercaloric support for patients with high energy needs</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">cec2042bad8b4a08bc7ef919132b2d6e</data>
      <data key="d12">4596</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N HIPOPROTEICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition may be adjusted to provide hypoproteic support for patients with specific dietary restrictions</data>
      <data key="d10">820640c45c3a696fca3c8c45b680b19b</data>
      <data key="d11">b3941cfc49bf485bbef780d9d70314e1</data>
      <data key="d12">4597</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NP V&#205;A CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP v&#237;a central is a specific method of administering Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral for patients needing high osmolarity solutions</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">df9570fdca5848e39856049c0f874319</data>
      <data key="d12">4598</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NP V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP v&#237;a perif&#233;rica is another method of administering Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral, suitable for patients with lower osmolarity needs</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">e0356baa448548789e092714f6e14db0</data>
      <data key="d12">4599</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL HIPOCAL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral Hipocal&#243;rica is a specific type of Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral that provides fewer calories</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">437c9603c42545e486a868add3f6b4ec</data>
      <data key="d12">4600</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NP DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP Domiciliaria is a method of administering Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral in a home setting</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">f1e528091af642c59ef4f50a02109977</data>
      <data key="d12">4601</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NP CONTINUA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP Continua is a method of administering Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral continuously over 24 hours</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">8ed239c131034d6c836bae9bdd319612</data>
      <data key="d12">4602</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NP C&#205;CLICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP C&#237;clica is a method of administering Nutrici&#243;n Parenteral for shorter durations, typically less than 24 hours</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">7515b30cde0945af9cac3784335282ae</data>
      <data key="d12">4603</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="TROMBOFLEBITIS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a method of providing nutrition intravenously, which can lead to various complications. One notable potential complication associated with the administration of NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is TROMBOFLEBITIS. This condition is characterized by inflammation of a vein due to a blood clot and is commonly observed as a complication arising from the use of peripheral nutrition. Therefore, TROMBOFLEBITIS is recognized as a frequent issue that may occur in patients receiving NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing this risk during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ce6342fdfe4419826c1ab2f84c56247,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">98ae53d47feb4a5f8cf5ba2c5dc07d64</data>
      <data key="d12">4604</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VITAMINAS Y MINERALES">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. Patients on parenteral nutrition often require supplementation of VITAMINAS Y MINERALES, as these essential components are crucial for meeting the patient's nutritional needs. Including vitamins and minerals in parenteral nutrition is vital to ensure that patients receive a comprehensive and balanced intake of nutrients necessary for their health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,81d0f9e0238db446bd67439b8222ab32</data>
      <data key="d11">393d0e6149364043be998f80ca68269b</data>
      <data key="d12">4605</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ALTO ESTR&#201;S METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alto estr&#233;s metab&#243;lico is a condition that often leads to the need for parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">e60776298c8940eaa9a296d3712179b4</data>
      <data key="d12">4606</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">27.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a medical intervention utilized primarily in patients suffering from MALNUTRICI&#211;N, particularly when these individuals are unable to receive adequate nutrition through enteral methods. This form of nutrition is essential for restoring adequate nutrient levels in patients who cannot absorb nutrients through the gastrointestinal tract or who are unable to receive nutrition enterally for various reasons. The administration of parenteral nutrition is a critical approach to treating malnutrition, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery when other nutritional methods are insufficient.</data>
      <data key="d10">395385fad73fd5b7ed9eda114b482624,3ee948dc4ddfdc75daa8fe7db9bb471e,4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1,f087e20586f6b263059597e194a04993</data>
      <data key="d11">90039f7ae9c2446a97b288e5d0e12cfc</data>
      <data key="d12">4607</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#205;STULAS YEYUNALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#237;stulas yeyunales may indicate a relative indication for the use of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">e369f2b8f6b54a99afbfaf7dd5014ef8</data>
      <data key="d12">4608</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad inflamatoria may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition during acute phases</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">a222045cd4f243c4bb520f9276dce860</data>
      <data key="d12">4609</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO">
      <data key="d8">78.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO are closely related in the context of medical treatment for patients suffering from the latter condition. S&#237;ndrome de intestino corto, characterized by a significant reduction in the functional length of the intestine, often leads to severe malabsorption of nutrients. As a result, patients with this syndrome frequently require nutrici&#243;n parenteral to ensure they receive adequate nutrition. This form of nutrition is essential for those who cannot absorb sufficient nutrients through their intestines, making it a common and sometimes necessary treatment option.

In cases of severe s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto, nutrici&#243;n parenteral is considered an absolute indication, highlighting its critical role in managing the nutritional needs of affected individuals. The reliance on parenteral nutrition may be long-term, as the malabsorption issues associated with this syndrome complicate the ability to meet nutritional requirements through conventional dietary means. Overall, nutrici&#243;n parenteral serves as a vital intervention for patients with s&#237;ndrome de intestino corto, addressing their unique challenges related to nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,538970e30e9d0e758546ca1a3cf5a205,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,ace4abd79441a61d6688d67db2dc0747,b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0,bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,c00d7a0a842e45f78f71c27adecde3f9,cd63370bdd798f0b060b047dc29056ae,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d11">b3b1b871718242fda17514837fc1a4c4</data>
      <data key="d12">4610</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="PANCREATITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">77.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a critical component in the management of PANCREATITIS AGUDA, particularly for patients who are unable to tolerate oral feeding. In cases where enteral nutrition is not viable or fails to meet the energy requirements of the patient, parenteral nutrition becomes necessary. This form of nutritional support is typically utilized during the initial days of treatment for acute pancreatitis, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition intravenously when enteral routes are not possible or sufficient. Overall, parenteral nutrition is indicated for the effective management of patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, highlighting its importance in their care.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,57d361381e6ea4ddbc948891f9645009,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241,88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,9890cc3f628030fc8c4666d15e6b0259,b1464c57df2eaa651a10c1522ab7db68,be7eb01a6daf673db6a127f66c79c96c,caf14765027dbf6266841af0571a522e,f5ac70db902f1361fd681d1d109828c0</data>
      <data key="d11">8cb49dcce1b6495c8843cc4a221a2be9</data>
      <data key="d12">4611</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENTERITIS AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteritis aguda may lead to the need for parenteral nutrition due to digestive tract complications</data>
      <data key="d10">8169062e4a75aaf466ffa4affa509241</data>
      <data key="d11">426b38777504497c8df125a13c295d2b</data>
      <data key="d12">4612</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="&#205;LEO NO QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral es necesaria en casos de &#237;leo no quir&#250;rgico cuando el paciente no puede alimentarse adecuadamente</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">660c07cc358546d7b2c09f58491c750f</data>
      <data key="d12">4613</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMOS TERMINALES">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede no ser beneficiosa para enfermos terminales con pron&#243;stico de vida limitado</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">a6bdc063c81645b1b5220e2f6c84d597</data>
      <data key="d12">4614</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="V&#205;A DIGESTIVA NORMOFUNCIONANTE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral no es necesaria en pacientes con v&#237;a digestiva normofuncionante que pueden cubrir sus necesidades nutricionales</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">69b06ea0dbe34b7eae3e624d1b88f12c</data>
      <data key="d12">4615</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIDRATOS DE CARBONO">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL incorporates HIDRATOS DE CARBONO as a crucial component, providing essential energy for patients receiving this form of nutrition. The inclusion of hidratos de carbono in parenteral nutrition is vital, but it requires careful monitoring to ensure appropriate energy levels are maintained.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704</data>
      <data key="d11">1be88bc4f65b45259561b2fb6fbf5c54</data>
      <data key="d12">4616</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="L&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which includes L&#205;PIDOS, is a critical aspect of medical nutrition therapy. L&#205;PIDOS are an essential component of parenteral nutrition, providing necessary energy and essential fatty acids to patients who may not be able to receive adequate nutrition through oral or enteral routes. The administration of L&#205;PIDOS must be carefully managed and adjusted based on the individual patient's condition to ensure optimal nutritional support. Overall, L&#205;PIDOS play a vital role in the formulation of parenteral nutrition, contributing significantly to the caloric intake and overall health of patients receiving this type of therapy.</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704</data>
      <data key="d11">d9704ab8237d46ffa2550f5794b8f22b</data>
      <data key="d12">4617</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="AYUNO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral se utiliza en pacientes que deben ayunar durante per&#237;odos prolongados, como en situaciones pre o post-quir&#250;rgicas</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">c184ebf859ff45c0aeb523b2cb0bc57e</data>
      <data key="d12">4618</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ESTR&#201;S METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El estr&#233;s metab&#243;lico puede requerir la administraci&#243;n de nutrici&#243;n parenteral para satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales del paciente</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">6b416f981edf46e08fc985971737a358</data>
      <data key="d12">4619</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="RECHAZO DE INTERVENCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El rechazo de la intervenci&#243;n puede afectar la decisi&#243;n de proporcionar nutrici&#243;n parenteral a un paciente</data>
      <data key="d10">4b5441741b392c27b7f7c29cc79e13a5</data>
      <data key="d11">90978508facb4905a92f0ca75f4f7a94</data>
      <data key="d12">4620</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="EMULSIONES LIP&#205;DICAS">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the use of EMULSIONES LIP&#205;DICAS, which are administered to ensure adequate lipid intake and prevent complications associated with nutritional deficiencies. These lipid emulsions are essential components of parenteral nutrition, as they provide not only energy but also essential fatty acids necessary for the body's metabolic functions. Overall, lipid emulsions play a critical role in supporting patients who require parenteral nutrition by delivering vital nutrients that are otherwise difficult to obtain through traditional feeding methods.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,86450d0e00138163bc3427ff406aa842,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,c70d301baddcdcdefbba9b024ad4f3c5</data>
      <data key="d11">4acf2eb7d8f0481fa02710c1260477a4</data>
      <data key="d12">4621</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SERVICIO DE FARMACIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Pharmacy Service manages the nutritional products used in parenteral nutrition and ensures proper administration.</data>
      <data key="d10">b7fb13d01f792b754e667a3a5bcdba93</data>
      <data key="d11">1bc33bd7d45a4d3c872e487791181706</data>
      <data key="d12">4622</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLUTAMINE AND ANTIOXIDANTS TRIAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The trial investigates the effects of nutritional interventions, including parenteral nutrition, in critically ill patients</data>
      <data key="d10">3f3896c039ea7ef78de8bf5fb6e09a48</data>
      <data key="d11">ca78a425d17141c99e954f463e25df29</data>
      <data key="d12">4623</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CER-NEVIT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CER-NEVIT is a multivitamin composition used in parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d11">47ad228c51d34266a7df86a8843f9a31</data>
      <data key="d12">4624</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="A. NAVARRO EDUARDO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A. Navarro Eduardo is an author discussing the methods and indications of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d11">797b95fefdd84275870e9f2802a740e8</data>
      <data key="d12">4625</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through oral or enteral means. V&#205;A PERIF&#201;RICA is a specific method of access used in this process, serving as an alternative route for delivering parenteral nutrition. This approach allows for the administration of essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream through peripheral veins, making it a viable option for patients requiring nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d10">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,97270fe12224dcc1dc019b0d1026a7fd</data>
      <data key="d11">0ea09ee60bf54d618c137b7d0d52c5d5</data>
      <data key="d12">4626</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SOLDINGHER">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Seldingher technique is used to access veins for the administration of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">1334cc8229c84b899a3f5fff9293ac5c</data>
      <data key="d12">4627</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="UCIS ESPA&#209;OLAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Intensive Care Units in Spain implement protocols for the administration of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">40e2137d9fa246cfab82de2df47112a3</data>
      <data key="d12">4628</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA refer to the practice of providing nutritional support through parenteral means, specifically in a home setting. Home parenteral nutrition is a continuation of parenteral nutrition that aims to enhance patient care by allowing individuals to receive necessary nutritional support in the comfort of their own homes. This specific application of parenteral nutrition is designed for patients who require long-term nutritional assistance, facilitating their treatment and improving their quality of life. By transitioning from hospital to home care, parenteral nutrition can be effectively administered at home, ensuring that patients maintain their nutritional needs outside of a clinical environment.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,488affd4bfc1b1b4b9f5b6a054c97d80,896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe,9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d11">8db633bbe2fe48f59a134f954a5f8a20</data>
      <data key="d12">4629</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI I POLIT&#200;CNIC LA FE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospital Universitari i Polit&#232;cnic La Fe provides nutritional support through parenteral nutrition for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5</data>
      <data key="d11">47c6a7c0a1f144fe8ee86ec95a4722bc</data>
      <data key="d12">4630</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and HIPOGLUCEMIA are interconnected in the context of patient care. Hypoglycemia can occur in patients receiving nutrici&#243;n parenteral, particularly when insulin is administered. This condition is recognized as a potential complication of parenteral nutrition. It is crucial to manage blood sugar levels effectively to prevent hypoglycemia, underscoring the importance of diligent monitoring in patients undergoing this form of nutrition. Proper management and oversight are essential to mitigate the risks associated with hypoglycemia in individuals receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f</data>
      <data key="d11">e2ae08a789474f578e222701cf85c322</data>
      <data key="d12">4631</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to individuals who cannot consume food orally, typically through intravenous means. One of the potential complications associated with NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA, which can arise if the lipid intake during parenteral nutrition is not adequately managed. Specifically, HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA can occur as a direct result of lipid administration in parenteral nutrition, highlighting the importance of careful monitoring and control of lipid levels to prevent this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">ba00eef6ab78485b8d43360bda056bec</data>
      <data key="d12">4632</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HEPATOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">20.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and HEPATOPAT&#205;A are closely related in the context of patients requiring nutritional support. Hepatopathy can develop in patients on long-term parenteral nutrition, particularly due to the excess administration of glucose or lipids. In situations where enteral nutrition is contraindicated because of hepatopathy, parenteral nutrition becomes a necessary alternative. Additionally, patients with intestinal failure who are receiving parenteral nutrition are at an increased risk for developing liver disease. This highlights the complex interplay between nutritional support and liver health in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,20491afa9a4770e93e6cff9034f8b0f0,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d11">f70605dc7c37420cbfa97ac2b431ba6a</data>
      <data key="d12">4633</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMEDAD METAB&#211;LICA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and ENFERMEDAD METAB&#211;LICA &#211;SEA are interconnected, as prolonged parenteral nutrition can lead to metabolic bone disease. This condition may arise due to nutrient imbalances that occur during long-term parenteral nutrition, which can result in insufficient intake of essential nutrients necessary for maintaining bone health. Consequently, patients receiving parenteral nutrition are at risk of developing metabolic bone disease as a direct consequence of these nutritional deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f2182c320403c424563ba1a084c00d5,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d11">41e3deffd7b845ed9e8a235ace38364b</data>
      <data key="d12">4634</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL">
      <data key="d8">27.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a specialized form of nutrition that is utilized in cases of INSUFICIENCIA RENAL, particularly when the gastrointestinal tract is not functional. In such scenarios, parenteral nutrition becomes essential to provide the necessary nutrients and fluids that the body requires. Insuficiencia renal necessitates specific adjustments in the administration of parenteral nutrition to prevent potential complications. These adjustments may include careful management of fluid and nutrient intake to accommodate the altered physiological needs of patients with renal insufficiency. Overall, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical intervention for individuals with severe renal insufficiency when traditional nutritional methods are not viable.</data>
      <data key="d10">140611dbb8a68fc40712c946de92b73f,37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,e321db63d9b561eb98a4f01853b141ad</data>
      <data key="d11">b2f11b1bf2564ad1bce3f067b52db943</data>
      <data key="d12">4635</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CIRUG&#205;A ABDOMINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede ser necesaria para pacientes que se someten a cirug&#237;a abdominal y no pueden alimentarse por v&#237;a enteral</data>
      <data key="d10">44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd</data>
      <data key="d11">f4c204c8574c4311be54342b911e08cd</data>
      <data key="d12">4636</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#211;RMULAS INMUNOMODULADORAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las f&#243;rmulas inmunomoduladoras se administran como parte de la nutrici&#243;n parenteral para mejorar la recuperaci&#243;n del paciente</data>
      <data key="d10">44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd</data>
      <data key="d11">2fc46cc91c1a4b10bec06ff34c620f80</data>
      <data key="d12">4637</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#205;STULAS ENTERO-CUT&#193;NEAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las f&#237;stulas entero-cut&#225;neas pueden complicar la nutrici&#243;n enteral, haciendo necesaria la nutrici&#243;n parenteral</data>
      <data key="d10">44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd</data>
      <data key="d11">0fd7bd2404ed4935a60f6f2d73b3aa40</data>
      <data key="d12">4638</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La obstrucci&#243;n intestinal puede contraindicar la nutrici&#243;n enteral, requiriendo nutrici&#243;n parenteral</data>
      <data key="d10">44346a4b1b9a6d3ae2bc161314ff9efd</data>
      <data key="d11">0434c49905314ce186ab0aa8d56ae069</data>
      <data key="d12">4639</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#205;STULAS INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with intestinal fistulas may need parenteral nutrition when enteral methods are not feasible</data>
      <data key="d10">f7ca532ae3a834fd6643ad694d3e850c</data>
      <data key="d11">09d384f1b1844a2493a103731149a4b3</data>
      <data key="d12">4640</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE DISTR&#201;S RESPIRATORIO AGUDO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutrici&#243;n parenteral is often recommended for patients suffering from s&#237;ndrome de distr&#233;s respiratorio agudo to meet their increased nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">990beacde191409a9aa00ed4b0adbfa4</data>
      <data key="d12">4641</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HARRIS-BENEDICT">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. The HARRIS-BENEDICT formula plays a crucial role in this context, as it is utilized to calculate the caloric needs of patients receiving nutrici&#243;n parenteral. By determining the nutritional requirements through this formula, healthcare providers can develop effective parenteral nutrition strategies, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">c5c1cc7940f6422d981367a27b83ec04</data>
      <data key="d12">4642</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d8">62.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, prominently includes GLUCOSA (D-glucose) as a critical component. Glucose serves as a primary source of energy in parenteral nutrition formulations, essential for meeting the energy needs of patients, particularly those who are unable to consume food orally. It is especially important in the nutritional therapy of diabetic patients, where careful control of glucose administration is necessary to avoid potential complications. Overall, GLUCOSA plays a vital role in NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, providing necessary carbohydrates and energy to support patient health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,95b0d21cd06eb29e984e0882f8fac544,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">97faae0a37644b5bb41c091d32baf54c</data>
      <data key="d12">4643</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ACEITE DE OLIVA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aceite de oliva is suggested for use in parenteral nutrition formulations to ensure a balanced intake of fatty acids.</data>
      <data key="d10">df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">16163a678e1342f8a05e44ca83281a49</data>
      <data key="d12">4644</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VENTILACI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients requiring ventilaci&#243;n mec&#225;nica often need nutrici&#243;n parenteral to meet their nutritional needs during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">ec6faef2e2dd4fd28c35b776393c9d63</data>
      <data key="d12">4645</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIPERNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipernutrici&#243;n can occur in patients receiving nutrici&#243;n parenteral if not carefully monitored.</data>
      <data key="d10">df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">67326db891d74b0faebd86cff120a17a</data>
      <data key="d12">4646</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and PROTE&#205;NAS are closely related in the context of medical nutrition therapy. Proteins are recognized as a critical component of parenteral nutrition, with specific recommendations for their intake. They play an essential role in the recovery of critically ill patients, as they are necessary for tissue repair and overall recovery. Thus, the inclusion of adequate protein in parenteral nutrition is vital for supporting the health and recovery of patients who are unable to receive nutrition through traditional means.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,9fda43c414d32c5a8a3bb7354bfb1704,df410977169e29218f41ff919bd4e44b</data>
      <data key="d11">b4333d2b738241b5bfe37bfc76791b22</data>
      <data key="d12">4647</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="FRA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition is necessary for patients with acute renal failure when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not possible.</data>
      <data key="d10">cd16cc82ca1357af8c9c1ab73ea55c5a</data>
      <data key="d11">606965ae966a4de780dcf2d5eb8f4b31</data>
      <data key="d12">4648</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLUTAMINA">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. Within this context, GLUTAMINA, or glutamine, is recognized as an important nutrient. It is recommended as part of the nutritional support in parenteral nutrition for patients, particularly those experiencing metabolic stress. Research indicates that glutamine can improve clinical outcomes for these patients, making it a valuable supplement in their nutritional therapy.

Specifically, glutamine is advised for use in parenteral nutrition to enhance recovery in patients with acute pancreatitis. Additionally, it has been shown to support glycemic control in diabetic patients when included in their nutritional regimen. Overall, glutamine plays a significant role in optimizing the effectiveness of parenteral nutrition, contributing to better health outcomes for a variety of patient populations.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,6a12bee5b54e4c1706548bca972516e3,beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb,c70d301baddcdcdefbba9b024ad4f3c5</data>
      <data key="d11">b0fc8e5cf4304a41a765de74bc01985e</data>
      <data key="d12">4649</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and CIRROSIS are interconnected in the context of medical treatment. Cirrhosis can develop as a severe complication associated with parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream when a patient is unable to eat by mouth. Parenteral nutrition is specifically reserved for patients with cirrhosis when enteral feeding, or feeding through the gastrointestinal tract, is not feasible. This highlights the critical role of parenteral nutrition in managing the nutritional needs of cirrhosis patients under certain circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d10">9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f,ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d11">3f1fc712ecc34020b26b9331986d603d</data>
      <data key="d12">4650</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SUPLEMENTOS ORALES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition may be supplemented with oral nutrients when possible</data>
      <data key="d10">20491afa9a4770e93e6cff9034f8b0f0</data>
      <data key="d11">71f67d49208a42f898d9cc21b79d2d26</data>
      <data key="d12">4651</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="LOCHS H">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lochs H's guidelines on enteral nutrition may influence practices related to parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">b64b9397a6bf48bea788ea3450d062e2</data>
      <data key="d12">4652</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="OBSTRUCCIONES DE ALTO GRADO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High-grade obstructions can necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition for patients unable to tolerate enteral feeding</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">0c819b4bc7a94407ae40994041eb106f</data>
      <data key="d12">4653</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="FISTULAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with high-output fistulas may require parenteral nutrition to manage their nutritional needs</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">03b4408cfda14d6d94aba31cd42a1db1</data>
      <data key="d12">4654</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a medical intervention utilized when enteral nutrition is not feasible, particularly in patients suffering from ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL. This form of nutrition is especially important during severe flare-ups of the disease, as it provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. Thus, for individuals with inflammatory bowel disease, parenteral nutrition serves as a critical alternative to ensure adequate nutritional support when traditional methods are inadequate.</data>
      <data key="d10">417548e99612a123d61f9fd10807ce34,bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">5e1f060b91fd40b69b9b07aa0cf846bb</data>
      <data key="d12">4655</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MEGACOLON T&#211;XICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with toxic megacolon may need parenteral nutrition due to the inability to tolerate oral or enteral feeding</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">34c702824bd94acab3eea840b6a91753</data>
      <data key="d12">4656</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support via parenteral nutrition is indicated for patients with Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica when their gastrointestinal tract is not functioning</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">a5297caf719e43d5b351f3f5a7965433</data>
      <data key="d12">4657</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition is used for diabetic patients who cannot tolerate enteral feeding</data>
      <data key="d10">d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567</data>
      <data key="d11">09d3755c67994fd9acb255cb661b75af</data>
      <data key="d12">4658</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="AMERICAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association provides guidelines that inform practices related to nutritional therapy for diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd</data>
      <data key="d11">cc7e2b7a498c4d3baa2286af11af7a58</data>
      <data key="d12">4659</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="DIABETES UK">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes UK offers evidence-based nutrition guidelines that are relevant to the practices of nutritional therapy for diabetic patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd</data>
      <data key="d11">a36539c14e74413ca5de9b04dc8546f6</data>
      <data key="d12">4660</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The control of blood glucose levels is a critical aspect of managing diabetic patients receiving nutritional therapy.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd</data>
      <data key="d11">ddf823604175422c8878f71d3e4b48ae</data>
      <data key="d12">4661</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CROMO">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of nutrients directly into the bloodstream, often used for patients who cannot consume food orally. CROMO, or chromium, is an oligoelement that plays a role in various metabolic processes. While chromium supplementation may aid in improving glycemic control and insulin sensitivity in diabetic patients undergoing nutritional therapy, it is important to note that chromium can be nefrot&#243;xico (toxic to the kidneys) in neonates, necessitating careful monitoring of its administration in this vulnerable population. Therefore, while chromium has potential benefits in specific contexts, its use must be approached with caution, particularly in neonates receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc</data>
      <data key="d11">0188db88613140828549638d8a2e7c99</data>
      <data key="d12">4662</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIPERGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and HIPERGLUCEMIA are closely related, as hyperglycemia is a potential complication that can arise from improper management of parenteral nutrition. It is frequently observed in patients undergoing NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, making it a common concern in this context. Effective management of hyperglycemia is essential during nutritional therapy, particularly for diabetic patients, to prevent further complications. Therefore, careful monitoring and adjustment of nutritional strategies are crucial to mitigate the risk of HIPERGLUCEMIA in individuals receiving NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL.</data>
      <data key="d10">241d358b60724c07a75223b79c9e5f41,4f6c697d19c8a4459b3accd91f111bfd,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f</data>
      <data key="d11">6b2e8dc4001e4e7994661657628ab464</data>
      <data key="d12">4663</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMOS GERI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral es una intervenci&#243;n importante para los enfermos geri&#225;tricos que no pueden alimentarse adecuadamente por v&#237;a oral.</data>
      <data key="d10">54f3b76c0240696aa63ae60ad52b82b6</data>
      <data key="d11">83b7e7c1602a408abb9a915cb7a39740</data>
      <data key="d12">4664</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIPODERMOCLISIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both are methods of providing nutritional support and hydration to patients with specific medical needs</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">74ee52275cb3440aa65dff532fd5e72d</data>
      <data key="d12">4665</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ALPERS DH">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alpers DH authored a study that discusses nutritional considerations relevant to parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">7d7a79d4e5c64ec0a1c16be64fa0352a</data>
      <data key="d12">4666</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ASPEN BOARD OF DIRECTORS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ASPEN Board provides guidelines that include the use of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">f946d0ef0b3248749e66202639d78591</data>
      <data key="d12">4667</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="BARRERA R">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Barrera R's research on nutritional support is relevant to the practices of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">a191919944fe44b0b4feda9a543f284e</data>
      <data key="d12">4668</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="DE BLAUW I">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">De Blaauw I's study on metabolic changes in cancer anorexia relates to the need for parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">6da8c1a2e176488192b7c688c2d11e69</data>
      <data key="d12">4669</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GISBERT AGUILAR A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gisbert Aguilar A's work on dehydration and nutritional support is relevant to parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">d618646512e94915b2f15bf5a2c0d092</data>
      <data key="d12">4670</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="PLANAS DOMINGO J">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Planas Domingo J's research on cachexia-anorexia is relevant to the use of parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">6895740c1ca84c5fbcd95628b1d5f1d2</data>
      <data key="d12">4671</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="QUIMIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chemotherapy often leads to nutritional deficiencies, making parenteral nutrition necessary</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">16019798ce7448a0824d1f7588ff7b5d</data>
      <data key="d12">4672</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CUIDADOS PALIATIVOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In palliative care, parenteral nutrition may be used to improve the quality of life for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">df3e8fd56a2df522425984adc77392ab</data>
      <data key="d11">67f921a033584ffe94ddcba36e182b6b</data>
      <data key="d12">4673</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NI&#209;OS">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is primarily utilized for NI&#209;OS, who are the main recipients of this form of nutritional support. Parenteral nutrition is specifically tailored to meet the unique energy requirements of children, ensuring that their nutritional needs are adequately addressed. This method of nutritional support is especially indicated for those children who are unable to fulfill their dietary needs through oral or enteral means.</data>
      <data key="d10">2d14f6773b107ec9a872245c32ae0a94,37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801,cd63370bdd798f0b060b047dc29056ae</data>
      <data key="d11">1791cfb5c6d54c49a61213f91a14a42a</data>
      <data key="d12">4674</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="FIEBRE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fiebre puede aumentar las necesidades energ&#233;ticas y de l&#237;quidos en ni&#241;os, lo que debe ser considerado en su nutrici&#243;n parenteral</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801</data>
      <data key="d11">bc13c7a454ed4c1daf5571d4fbc1965f</data>
      <data key="d12">4675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La insuficiencia card&#237;aca puede influir en la cantidad de l&#237;quidos y nutrientes administrados en la nutrici&#243;n parenteral</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801</data>
      <data key="d11">6fe0cb3b9b304a50a461bdf87920831c</data>
      <data key="d12">4676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="EDMAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los edemas pueden requerir ajustes en la administraci&#243;n de l&#237;quidos en la nutrici&#243;n parenteral de los ni&#241;os</data>
      <data key="d10">37ca60bdc28109c9bec995e3c433c801</data>
      <data key="d11">126ee62e6ed948a1a4c68abd11b4d394</data>
      <data key="d12">4677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="AMINOSTERIL-N HEPA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aminosteril-N Hepa is a solution used in parenteral nutrition for patients with liver failure</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5</data>
      <data key="d11">321515a505f140d0bf1752b90662bee1</data>
      <data key="d12">4678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="NEPHROTECT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nephrotect is a solution used in parenteral nutrition for patients with renal failure</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5</data>
      <data key="d11">d9a20059280d41f281a7970e9affdd5d</data>
      <data key="d12">4679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, often includes the essential oligoelemento, HIERRO (iron). While the use of iron in parenteral nutrition is considered essential, it remains a subject of controversy. It is crucial to monitor iron levels and add it independently in parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies, particularly for patients who require this form of nutrition for extended periods. Therefore, iron supplementation is necessary to ensure the health and well-being of individuals receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">2bd5549759c6a0d8393bb93fdccb747b,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc</data>
      <data key="d11">1ec41a39207f43d8a4ecfbf41212a277</data>
      <data key="d12">4680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">59.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, plays a critical role in the care of patients who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral means. A key component of this nutritional support is CALCIO (calcium), which is essential for maintaining bone health and supporting various physiological functions. Adequate calcium intake is particularly crucial for patients receiving parenteral nutrition to prevent bone-related issues, especially in pediatric patients who require calcium for proper development.

Calcium is included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the body's mineral requirements, and it is recognized as a necessary supplement for these patients. However, the addition of calcium must be done with caution to avoid potential complications. Therefore, healthcare providers closely monitor and adjust calcium levels in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to ensure optimal metabolic health and prevent deficiencies. Overall, calcium is an indispensable mineral in parenteral nutrition, vital for the health and development of patients, particularly children.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">8a7cf6244da34205a1f9e6a440d57d7d</data>
      <data key="d12">4681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#211;SFORO">
      <data key="d8">39.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, is critically dependent on the inclusion of F&#211;SFORO (phosphorus) as an essential component. Phosphorus is necessary for the proper development of pediatric patients, making it a vital supplement in their parenteral nutrition regimen. It plays a crucial role in meeting the body's mineral requirements, and its levels are carefully adjusted based on the individual needs of each patient. Overall, phosphorus is recognized as an indispensable nutrient that must be incorporated into parenteral nutrition to ensure optimal health outcomes for patients, particularly in pediatric care.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">51ba48d386a84cc2a770fde62a689c06</data>
      <data key="d12">4682</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">40.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the inclusion of MAGNESIO (magnesium), which is an essential component for the proper development and metabolic function of patients, particularly pediatric patients. Magnesium plays a crucial role in various bodily functions and must be monitored and supplemented in parenteral nutrition solutions to prevent deficiencies. Its importance is underscored by the need for careful management in parenteral nutrition to ensure that patients receive adequate levels of this vital mineral.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48</data>
      <data key="d11">5a030921ba88462abdbb96bfef4d306b</data>
      <data key="d12">4683</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. One of the key components included in parenteral nutrition is TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS, which serve as a vital source of energy for patients. It is essential to monitor triglyceride levels during parenteral nutrition, particularly in patients with acute pancreatitis, to prevent potential complications. Continuous monitoring of triglycerides is crucial for all patients receiving parenteral nutrition to ensure their safety and the effectiveness of the treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,57ec3d3d82d22e19c09ea2b735ef7779,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">8e6a89f37bc9444f858e45e0eecdbaf8</data>
      <data key="d12">4684</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SODIO">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the use of SODIO as a critical component in its formulations. SODIO is included in parenteral nutrition solutions to help maintain fluid balance and is essential for the overall health of patients receiving this type of nutrition. It is particularly important to monitor and adjust sodium levels based on individual patient needs, ensuring that the electrolyte balance is maintained effectively. This is especially crucial for pediatric patients, who require careful management of their sodium intake as part of their parenteral nutrition regimen.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48</data>
      <data key="d11">7dc6bf1b8cc24ae2b6b1edb3d4c75674</data>
      <data key="d12">4685</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. POTASIO, or potassium, is an essential electrolyte included in parenteral nutrition solutions. It plays a crucial role in cellular function and is particularly important for pediatric patients. The levels of potassium in parenteral nutrition must be carefully monitored and adjusted according to the specific needs of each patient to ensure optimal health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416,d936cb199b788cfcddbfb6e51b1e6e48</data>
      <data key="d11">57996b512799426dbedb3fe972aacf5c</data>
      <data key="d12">4686</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="CLORO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to parenteral nutrition, includes CLORO, or chloride, as an essential electrolyte. Chloride plays a crucial role in the formulation of parenteral nutrition solutions, particularly for pediatric patients. It is necessary for fluid regulation within the body, highlighting its importance in maintaining electrolyte balance and overall health in individuals receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">4a88c4a9d485f88fca1d0f03e2e277a5,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416</data>
      <data key="d11">0306c3a37c8a44fe90d90c429fb825ad</data>
      <data key="d12">4687</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="OLIGOELEMENTOS">
      <data key="d8">35.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of OLIGOELEMENTOS, which are essential trace elements necessary for ensuring adequate nutritional support, particularly in pediatric patients. These trace elements play a critical role in promoting growth and development, making their management crucial in parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies. Oligoelementos are included in parenteral nutrition formulations to meet daily nutritional requirements, and their levels must be carefully monitored in patients receiving this type of nutrition. Overall, the incorporation of oligoelementos is vital for maintaining health in individuals dependent on parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">767b85090f694eeea2a5ebec0d1886ac</data>
      <data key="d12">4688</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VITAMINAS">
      <data key="d8">40.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. A critical component of this nutritional approach is VITAMINAS, which must be carefully monitored and included to meet the daily requirements of patients. Vitamins play a vital role in ensuring the proper development and health of patients, particularly in pediatric cases. Their inclusion in parenteral nutrition is essential to provide the necessary nutrients that support overall well-being and prevent deficiencies in individuals receiving this form of nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,c6db4a9613e32e9237476d5dcda073b3,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">d66eeb5d9fea47a5a8d49751f099e255</data>
      <data key="d12">4689</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="LIPOFUNDINA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to individuals who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. Within this context, LIPOFUNDINA is a lipid emulsion specifically utilized in parenteral nutrition. It serves as a vital component by supplying a source of energy and essential fatty acids, which are crucial for maintaining the nutritional needs of patients receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">0d637ee7524a4ec282b916594915e50c</data>
      <data key="d12">4690</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SMOFLIPID">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition intravenously to patients who are unable to consume food orally or through the gastrointestinal tract. SMOFLIPID is a specific lipid emulsion utilized within this context. It is designed to offer a balanced source of lipids, which includes essential omega-3 fatty acids, thereby enhancing the nutritional support provided through parenteral nutrition. SMOFLIPID plays a crucial role in ensuring that patients receive the necessary fats for their health and recovery when traditional feeding methods are not viable.</data>
      <data key="d10">a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">07948821b5db42c9946cfb3bbf799398</data>
      <data key="d12">4691</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLICEROFOSFATO S&#211;DICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sodium glycerophosphate is used in parenteral nutrition to prevent calcium-phosphate precipitation</data>
      <data key="d10">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">d6bdc15af7d64c93a171ec723eba646c</data>
      <data key="d12">4692</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ZINC">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is a medical practice that involves providing essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. One of the key components included in NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is ZINC, which is recognized as an essential trace element. ZINC is particularly recommended in pediatric parenteral nutrition to ensure that the nutritional needs of children are adequately met. It plays a crucial role in fulfilling the body's trace element requirements, thereby supporting overall health and development in patients receiving parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">df9c294295c84e538c029d02ee8670d7</data>
      <data key="d12">4693</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="COBRE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Copper is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements</data>
      <data key="d10">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">c616e9fd23f544d3884f823944493c7a</data>
      <data key="d12">4694</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MANGANESO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the administration of essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system. MANGANESO, or manganese, is a trace element that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements. However, it must be administered with caution, particularly in pediatric patients, due to the specific needs and sensitivities of this population.</data>
      <data key="d10">ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">b281c31d398f41eba2362643004e19ed</data>
      <data key="d12">4695</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SELENIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Selenium is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements</data>
      <data key="d10">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">dcb207d57f4146da9a0f00a7e86e2ff9</data>
      <data key="d12">4696</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MOLIBDENO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. MOLIBDENO, or molybdenum, is a trace element that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. In the context of NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, molybdenum is included to meet the body's trace element requirements. However, it is important to limit molybdenum intake in pediatric parenteral nutrition, particularly in cases of renal insufficiency, to prevent potential complications. Thus, while molybdenum is essential for nutritional balance, careful consideration must be given to its levels in specific patient populations, especially children with kidney issues.</data>
      <data key="d10">ee3d3ae4eef4cfe540602ad04ef172dc,ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">d069a350ca48417a9179d6e9c0ad1bcf</data>
      <data key="d12">4697</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="IODO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Iodine is included in parenteral nutrition to meet the body's trace element requirements</data>
      <data key="d10">ee5838dfb7aae573c969c1510fbf2d09</data>
      <data key="d11">e9a769d24dd440c88f0947d259ab002b</data>
      <data key="d12">4698</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ABNORMAL DOPPLER ENTERAL PRESCRIPTION TRIAL COLLABORATIVE GROUP">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
