    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HEPARINA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and HEPARINA are interconnected in the context of medical treatments. Heparin is commonly added to parenteral nutrition to prevent complications associated with catheter use, particularly to mitigate the risk of clotting in intravenous lines. In certain circumstances, heparin can be administered alongside parenteral nutrition, highlighting its role in enhancing the safety and efficacy of this nutritional support method.</data>
      <data key="d10">103ae80b955f35401aca706444999b29,20b676e149e50ddc54c40e2e1577e9ac,f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">802f8e96151d4ccd941bf7ed20bba188</data>
      <data key="d12">4702</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
