    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VITAMINA K1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin K1 is included in parenteral nutrition to support blood clotting</data>
      <data key="d10">f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">705d6590e98f474eb428622c55cac0a1</data>
      <data key="d12">4716</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ACIDO F&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Folic acid is included in parenteral nutrition to support DNA synthesis</data>
      <data key="d10">f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">19045bfe6c0a46ebb7a154905b7f249a</data>
      <data key="d12">4717</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="BIOTINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Biotin is included in parenteral nutrition to support metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">677bc75dc8da43eda0cef6a26c84963e</data>
      <data key="d12">4718</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VITAMINA B12">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin B12 is included in parenteral nutrition to support nerve function</data>
      <data key="d10">f757d4ff813fdf7b43b3382e7e1bd69c</data>
      <data key="d11">5321fced81db456782511b13fe750747</data>
      <data key="d12">4719</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="INSTITUTE FOR SAFE MEDICATION PRACTICES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ISMP includes parenteral nutrition among high-risk medications due to its complexity and potential for errors</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">3754243cb9d14984b8f6a1965d0c00be</data>
      <data key="d12">4720</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICI&#211;N CL&#205;NICA Y METABOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The book discusses parenteral nutrition as part of clinical nutrition and metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">110ebc0ae16a46dbacee26c141c7b18c</data>
      <data key="d12">4721</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="F&#205;STULA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL and F&#205;STULA INTESTINAL are closely related in the context of patient care. Intestinal fistulas can complicate enteral nutrition, which may lead to the necessity of parenteral nutrition for certain patients. Specifically, parenteral nutrition is indicated for those with intestinal fistulas who are unable to absorb nutrients through the gastrointestinal tract. This highlights the critical role of parenteral nutrition in managing patients with intestinal fistulas, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients when traditional methods are not viable.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,dbd97c366d747303c58ef40ebfd44ea5</data>
      <data key="d11">ceb94a92a706422a90ce65d33efe31ba</data>
      <data key="d12">4722</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition is often required for patients with mechanical intestinal obstruction who cannot receive oral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">8a063ad2c9ad46189a3e68060e62138b</data>
      <data key="d12">4723</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ALTERACIONES DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with altered intestinal motility may require parenteral nutrition to meet their nutritional needs</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">6ea2a95be294425795d11f53d4679ddf</data>
      <data key="d12">4724</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="AFECTACI&#211;N EXTENSA DE LA MUCOSA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Extensive damage to the intestinal mucosa can lead to malabsorption, necessitating parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">800aea36b6b6420dab786308776c9e4c</data>
      <data key="d12">4725</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA LARGA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Long-chain triglycerides were used in early formulations of lipid emulsions for parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f</data>
      <data key="d11">cbef3296283245728ad02ad10e2a6aaa</data>
      <data key="d12">4726</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA MEDIA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to individuals who are unable to consume food orally. One of the components that can be included in this form of nutrition is TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA MEDIA, or medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs). These triglycerides are utilized in parenteral nutrition to supply energy and essential nutrients. Specifically, MCTs are incorporated into second-generation lipid emulsions designed for parenteral nutrition, enhancing the nutritional support provided to patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9927d054458e409309b9e917cbb6a10c</data>
      <data key="d11">18d638ad9a5a40779a80b77f5b4cd858</data>
      <data key="d12">4727</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS &#937;-3">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the use of lipid emulsions, which can include &#193;CIDOS GRASOS &#937;-3, specifically Omega-3 fatty acids. These fatty acids are incorporated into fourth-generation lipid emulsions in parenteral nutrition due to their significant health benefits. The inclusion of Omega-3 fatty acids in these emulsions enhances the nutritional support provided to patients receiving parenteral nutrition, highlighting their importance in modern nutritional therapies.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9480cb55d00db88cfe1decdf011cb41f</data>
      <data key="d11">8e3cf1fe1ce648cb8bd40e8826dcecec</data>
      <data key="d12">4728</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="AMINO&#193;CIDOS">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the use of AMINO&#193;CIDOS, which are essential components in parenteral solutions. These amino acids play a critical role in providing nutrition to patients who cannot receive food through traditional means. They are vital for meeting patients' protein requirements, maintaining body mass, and supporting protein synthesis. In summary, amino acids are key ingredients in the formulation of parenteral nutrition, delivering essential nutrients to patients in need.</data>
      <data key="d10">45628dcc866de3617e83105d66f901ad,5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,a9268f98da988e7f94a3faf7bc7627c7</data>
      <data key="d11">6ba7fbfa3d28427583c5618b99f7ae61</data>
      <data key="d12">4729</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MICRONUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL involves the careful management of MICRONUTRIENTES to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients without experiencing deficiencies or excesses. It is crucial to monitor micronutrient levels closely in parenteral nutrition, as these nutrients are essential for maintaining health. The inclusion of micronutrients in parenteral nutrition is aimed at preventing deficiencies in patients who rely on this method of nutrition. Overall, the careful management of micronutrients is vital for the effectiveness of parenteral nutrition therapy.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8,c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d11">3170a17bd53f4c788d13e5bd88d8b1c6</data>
      <data key="d12">4730</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="FOSFATO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, which refers to the intravenous administration of nutrients, relies on various components to ensure effective metabolic support. One such component is FOSFATO, or phosphate, which is essential for numerous metabolic functions. While phosphate is included in parenteral nutrition solutions, it necessitates careful management to prevent potential complications associated with its use. Thus, the incorporation of FOSFATO in NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL is vital, but it must be monitored closely to maintain patient safety and health.</data>
      <data key="d10">5fb0e4d2f6efd6c6abcd9f7b7583ed7f,9f0536c07d1aae0e5d1a66d06697f416</data>
      <data key="d11">9e0ca7efcea84a8386b1136e96501450</data>
      <data key="d12">4731</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
