    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally. SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO encompasses practices related to NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL, focusing on the management and implementation of this nutritional support for patients. Together, these entities highlight the importance of advanced nutritional support techniques in ensuring that individuals who cannot eat by mouth receive the necessary nutrients for their health and recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">241d358b60724c07a75223b79c9e5f41,4ce6342fdfe4419826c1ab2f84c56247</data>
      <data key="d11">5de813f7edc54858b0e43fddb86a1aff</data>
      <data key="d12">4850</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="INSULINA REGULAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulina regular is commonly administered within the context of nutrici&#243;n parenteral to manage blood glucose levels</data>
      <data key="d10">6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">3d6b97d9384142f3a29eeea4ea902504</data>
      <data key="d12">4851</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="TRIGLICERIDOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Monitoring triglic&#233;ridos is essential in managing patients receiving nutrici&#243;n parenteral to prevent complications</data>
      <data key="d10">6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">61844f98c0db4aba9cc8871f69672c72</data>
      <data key="d12">4852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="COMPLICACIONES DE LA NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Complicaciones de la nutrici&#243;n parenteral are potential risks associated with the treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">69798e8291734ec39689694fb47d4a49</data>
      <data key="d12">4853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ALTERACIONES HEPATOBILIARES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alteraciones hepatobiliares can develop in patients on long-term parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">683670ce4acf464981de8fbe3e3e31c0</data>
      <data key="d12">4854</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="C&#193;TEDRA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;tedra complications are associated with the use of catheters in patients receiving parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">6289e9e0b5871fb9a2f2f691429bb4f8</data>
      <data key="d11">fa5c7b24adc7471fa8b3f0361349ab03</data>
      <data key="d12">4855</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="HEPATOBILIARY COMPLICATIONS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support through parenteral nutrition is associated with various hepatobiliary complications such as steatosis and cholestasis</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b</data>
      <data key="d11">fb052d61fe18460d8a1c205abc1029c8</data>
      <data key="d12">4856</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="INTESTINAL FAILURE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parenteral nutrition is often required for patients suffering from intestinal failure</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b</data>
      <data key="d11">8cd4255f175246a89477d636f5ccf961</data>
      <data key="d12">4857</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. In this context, VITAMINA D plays a crucial role, as Vitamin D levels are monitored in patients receiving parenteral nutrition to prevent deficiencies. It has been observed that Vitamin D levels may be insufficient in patients on prolonged parenteral nutrition, highlighting the importance of regular monitoring. Consequently, Vitamin D supplementation is recommended for patients undergoing parenteral nutrition who exhibit specific deficiencies, ensuring that their nutritional needs are adequately met.</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d11">fe95fc7bb66542b4b63f68b96467dcb6</data>
      <data key="d12">4858</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="COLESTASIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cholestasis is often associated with parenteral nutrition, typically occurring after steatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b</data>
      <data key="d11">ba22f11d53ed4783a9b91d49e8d0424f</data>
      <data key="d12">4859</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition to patients intravenously, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. This approach can be beneficial in managing patients with ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA, as parenteral nutrition has the potential to prevent or reverse liver disease in certain cases. However, it is important to note that underlying liver disease can complicate the management of patients receiving parenteral nutrition, indicating that careful consideration and monitoring are necessary when administering this form of nutrition to individuals with liver conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">036e8182deab774d39f06cd811738c9b,e55543c6579d036d25f25eb2ff63fcf2</data>
      <data key="d11">4c2e3f6bb9dd4bbea55e40c54421975d</data>
      <data key="d12">4860</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede causar complicaciones hep&#225;ticas, incluyendo esteatosis y colestasis, afectando la funci&#243;n del h&#237;gado.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">0226603b9de7442dbb78a95b553453e3</data>
      <data key="d12">4861</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ACIDOS GRASOS ESENCIALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El uso de nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede llevar a d&#233;ficits de &#225;cidos grasos esenciales, contribuyendo a problemas hep&#225;ticos.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">f841eaf123c744c792316ea11b75eb84</data>
      <data key="d12">4862</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="METRONIDAZOL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El metronidazol se utiliza para tratar el sobrecrecimiento bacteriano que puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">e9af5994cc51481cae5e8f733f7defe8</data>
      <data key="d12">4863</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="ESTEATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede contribuir al desarrollo de esteatosis hep&#225;tica debido a la sobrealimentaci&#243;n y la falta de nutrientes esenciales.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">3e3b3bb32dec49ccbf92d521e6dcc306</data>
      <data key="d12">4864</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="COLECISTOQUININA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede disminuir la producci&#243;n de colecistoquinina, afectando el flujo biliar.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">df8b525fa2a94f088263e9b81ae9d43e</data>
      <data key="d12">4865</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="SECRETINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La falta de est&#237;mulo enteral en la nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede reducir la producci&#243;n de secretina, afectando la funci&#243;n digestiva.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">4efa1de0da8f436cb66b09118fbf93ae</data>
      <data key="d12">4866</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GASTRINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede influir en los niveles de gastrina, afectando la motilidad intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">2f3313a8d7304eb4acff4c8561b4c5d7</data>
      <data key="d12">4867</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="MOTILINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ausencia de ingesta oral en la nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede reducir la producci&#243;n de motilina, afectando la motilidad intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">aeaebdb4308948f5b8fa13fb70c4a989</data>
      <data key="d12">4868</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="POLIPEPTIDO PANCREATICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede alterar la producci&#243;n de polip&#233;ptido pancre&#225;tico, afectando la funci&#243;n pancre&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">1affdea59c714427b87a30046a643b5b</data>
      <data key="d12">4869</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="GLUCAGON">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n parenteral puede influir en los niveles de glucag&#243;n, afectando el metabolismo de los nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">a5048d5edc0742c096a6a4f36518dfb3</data>
