      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRIENTES, specifically VITAMINA D, is an essential nutrient that plays a crucial role in calcium absorption, which is vital for maintaining healthy bones. Additionally, VITAMINA D is particularly important for infants, as it is one of the essential nutrients required for their healthy development, as emphasized in various nutritional guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d11">9258d88acbf54e6e954e3cd42588bdb7</data>
      <data key="d12">5366</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA A">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRIENTES, specifically VITAMINA A, is an essential nutrient that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is particularly important for vision, helping to maintain healthy eyesight. Additionally, VITAMINA A is included in dietary recommendations for infants, as it supports their growth and development. This highlights the significance of VITAMINA A not only for overall health but also for the proper development of young children.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d11">b224dfb4d6fa40bf950bb0768fcb649f</data>
      <data key="d12">5367</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA E">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRIENTES, specifically VITAMINA E, is an essential nutrient that plays a crucial role in protecting cells from damage. It is recognized for its antioxidant properties, which help to neutralize free radicals in the body. Additionally, VITAMINA E is included in the nutritional guidelines for infants, highlighting its importance as a vital nutrient for their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d11">63b748e076714013b498708ac9988bf6</data>
      <data key="d12">5368</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA B1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin B1 is part of the essential nutrients recommended for infants to support their growth and metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d11">b0dfe3af3a8e484f9ffd30bfd6866f4c</data>
      <data key="d12">5369</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA B2">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin B2 is included in the dietary recommendations for infants as a necessary nutrient for energy production.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d11">60fa93dabe71479dbab177eeb375ebfd</data>
      <data key="d12">5370</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA B6">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRIENTES, specifically VITAMINA B6, is an essential nutrient that plays a crucial role in protein metabolism. It is particularly important for infants, as it is included in dietary recommendations to meet their nutritional needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d11">cfa2aeb61ff94af39629017de831488f</data>
      <data key="d12">5371</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRIENTES" target="VITAMINA B12">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRIENTES, specifically VITAMINA B12, is an essential nutrient that plays a vital role in nerve function. It is particularly crucial for infants' health, as it is included in the nutritional guidelines for their development.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96,f718747b68f5c2d9d67148f05fd2d4ef</data>
      <data key="d11">c8b26b08d64e4213a4cb1da98127a6dc</data>
      <data key="d12">5372</data>
