    </edge>
    <edge source="FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION" target="VITALSTIM&#174;">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The FDA approved the VitalStim&#174; device for use in treating dysphagia, ensuring its safety and efficacy for patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">3663476d8b1342e396598b6ab5460adb</data>
      <data key="d12">5451</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION" target="HICKMAN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The FDA regulates the use of Hickman catheters and provides guidelines for their use in medical treatments</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">a453d2c66b7a4335831f3b91b2a1cdd0</data>
      <data key="d12">5452</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION" target="PORT-A-CATH">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The FDA oversees the safety and efficacy of Port-a-Cath devices used for long-term intravenous access</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">6aae4c0a15ff4abba18a17cabcf1cfd8</data>
      <data key="d12">5453</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITALSTIM&#174;" target="CHATTANOOGA GROUP">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chattanooga Group is the manufacturer of the VitalStim&#174; device used for neuromuscular electrical stimulation in dysphagia treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">f7c460b72747403f97fbcf60e140a459</data>
      <data key="d12">5454</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PARKINSON'S DISEASE" target="DEGLUTORY DISORDERS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Parkinson's disease can lead to deglutory disorders, increasing the risk of aspiration and necessitating rehabilitation.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">370bc4e286f44e7982e6a685b7e8aeff</data>
      <data key="d12">5455</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER OF HEAD AND NECK" target="DEGLUTORY DISORDERS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer of the head and neck can cause deglutory disorders, requiring specific rehabilitation techniques.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">162d69fda1a54fa6b5c08a19cfa5e044</data>
      <data key="d12">5456</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER OF HEAD AND NECK" target="CLINICAL TRIALS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clinical trials are conducted to evaluate the effectiveness of treatments for patients with cancer of the head and neck, particularly regarding dysphagia.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">d40ea43eadc4498385dffa0d982029fe</data>
      <data key="d12">5457</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ELECTROSTIMULATION" target="DEGLUTORY DISORDERS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Electrostimulation is used as a treatment method for patients with deglutory disorders to enhance muscle function.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">1d2150df888541eb8da9b5b3e8feda96</data>
      <data key="d12">5458</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ELECTROSTIMULATION" target="NEUROMUSCULAR ELECTRICAL STIMULATION">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neuromuscular electrical stimulation is a form of electrostimulation used to treat dysphagia by enhancing muscle function.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">fe8f1685d4af40c88fef088522cca7f0</data>
      <data key="d12">5459</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DEGLUTORY DISORDERS" target="EXERCISES FOR VOCAL CORDS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Exercises for vocal cords are implemented in rehabilitation protocols to improve swallowing in patients with deglutory disorders.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">04f609a0f10441368fea61fe94b08656</data>
      <data key="d12">5460</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DEGLUTORY DISORDERS" target="SHERKER EXERCISES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Shaker exercises are specifically designed to improve swallowing function in patients with deglutory disorders.</data>
      <data key="d10">3109714174ef86262626929d5a436f11</data>
      <data key="d11">f2cec1142d894f31bdbb0cfba07f6ff2</data>
      <data key="d12">5461</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPILEPSIA" target="MELAS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EPILEPSIA is a significant neurological manifestation in pacientes with MELAS, affecting their health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">776055eeeb0e47e782f57ad09c0cbe5e</data>
      <data key="d12">5462</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPILEPSIA" target="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EPILEPSIA and DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA are closely related, as the ketogenic diet is utilized as a treatment method for managing epilepsy. Specifically, the ketogenic diet is effective in controlling seizures in patients with epilepsy, particularly in cases that are resistant to conventional medication. This dietary approach has shown significant efficacy in reducing the frequency of convulsions, making it a valuable option for individuals suffering from intractable epilepsy.</data>
      <data key="d10">06adf563f18feaa5629f0e368a72d227,1592143354d1ef792f8618ec03a32a16,2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d11">277777f1651042a68b4998705f4ab16c</data>
      <data key="d12">5463</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPILEPSIA" target="MAE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MAE represents the primary treatment for epilepsy, which has influenced the use of dietary treatments like the ketogenic diet</data>
      <data key="d10">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d11">45c1771f37714585b9173993043a4b03</data>
      <data key="d12">5464</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPILEPSIA" target="CRISIS EPILEPTICAS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Epileptic seizures are a defining characteristic of epilepsy, which can be managed through various treatments, including dietary approaches</data>
      <data key="d10">2653a906ad6e1a1c0811e8f26d6deb9e</data>
      <data key="d11">188b84857b9c4268b75e77ae5bd35ea2</data>
      <data key="d12">5465</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPILEPSIA" target="KETOGENIC DIET">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Epilepsia is a journal that has published extensive research on the efficacy and safety of the ketogenic diet as a treatment for intractable childhood epilepsy. The journal focuses on various treatments for epilepsy, and the ketogenic diet is a significant subject of investigation within its publications. Through its research, Epilepsia contributes to the understanding of the ketogenic diet's role in managing epilepsy, particularly in cases that are resistant to conventional therapies.</data>
      <data key="d10">19d0093eea71a0652dc1aa027fb454bb,3704ab8452a14a91fe92eee82e9739fb,e533f9391cb85c02809d6f09d3a4d08e</data>
      <data key="d11">1b57f8884250400d8a8728f31d282e76</data>
      <data key="d12">5466</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRARY MA" target="FUNCTIONAL ORAL INTAKE SCALE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Crary MA is an author of the Functional Oral Intake Scale, contributing to its development</data>
      <data key="d10">cb0b01ccd7736b620c0755a756a42e5b</data>
      <data key="d11">26d72596f272474c982bf14f279ca60e</data>
      <data key="d12">5467</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="J AM GERIATR SOC" target="AGING CLIN EXP RES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both journals publish studies related to aging and frailty, indicating a shared interest in geriatric health</data>
