    <edge source="ALZHEIMER" target="HOMOCISTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alzheimer's disease is a neurodegenerative condition characterized by cognitive decline, and it has been linked to various risk factors. One significant factor is homocysteine, an amino acid in the blood. Research indicates that high levels of homocysteine are associated with an increased risk of developing Alzheimer's disease. Specifically, elevated homocysteine levels are considered a risk factor for the onset of this condition, suggesting a potential relationship between homocysteine metabolism and cognitive health.</data>
      <data key="d10">7427cd5c0088cf9c6ea0134ccf5f7e4f,fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d11">eb625435f07e46c385e0a03f472bc19d</data>
      <data key="d12">5615</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALZHEIMER" target="FLAVONOIDES">
