    <edge source="NACIONES UNIDAS" target="ENDOCRINE SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The United Nations provides information and resources related to gender identity, which aligns with the guidelines of the Endocrine Society.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480</data>
      <data key="d11">c01c3ddea1d74b568fc43fdc448c3925</data>
      <data key="d12">5646</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NACIONES UNIDAS" target="FACE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FACE follows the recommendations set by the United Nations regarding gluten labeling standards</data>
      <data key="d10">1d8aa686c6377246fee05010ef969018</data>
      <data key="d11">b5b8817c6d6242e182022b89b4db3c1c</data>
      <data key="d12">5647</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NACIONES UNIDAS" target="DECLARACI&#211;N UNIVERSAL DE DERECHOS HUMANOS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Naciones Unidas adopt&#243; la Declaraci&#243;n Universal de Derechos Humanos en 1948, estableciendo derechos fundamentales para todas las personas.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a</data>
      <data key="d11">1837b054aa424c8cb51bed2daf3a4008</data>
      <data key="d12">5648</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NACIONES UNIDAS" target="UNESCO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">UNESCO es una agencia de la ONU que trabaja bajo su mandato para promover la educaci&#243;n y la cultura.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b9cc8ae09d12c1bf2e3c9b103a1050a</data>
      <data key="d11">fb2fc3fc07a94c9db7b4fa86fea4c54a</data>
      <data key="d12">5649</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIM KELSEY" target="AGENCIA DE SALUD DIGITAL AUSTRALIANA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tim Kelsey is the Executive Director of the Australian Digital Health Agency, directly linking him to the agency's initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a0cbd0175ff61eee9b252f8ba7040ed</data>
      <data key="d11">16a99d0e282246a5855fbd2b14f9062e</data>
      <data key="d12">5650</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIM KELSEY" target="NHS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tim Kelsey previously held a significant role in the NHS, connecting his experience in healthcare management to the organization.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a0cbd0175ff61eee9b252f8ba7040ed</data>
      <data key="d11">f1a4235a0b7d40f0b53e4c8cd1f6ca13</data>
      <data key="d12">5651</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AGENCIA DE SALUD DIGITAL AUSTRALIANA" target="AETSA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AETSA collaborates with the Australian Digital Health Agency on health technology assessments, linking their missions.</data>
      <data key="d10">5a0cbd0175ff61eee9b252f8ba7040ed</data>
      <data key="d11">b440b4b29be744a1aec4ddea2a68ed57</data>
      <data key="d12">5652</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AETSA" target="RED ETS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AETSA is part of the national network RED ETS, focusing on health technology evaluation in Spain.</data>
      <data key="d10">3a7dac32347984360ee9e87767129272</data>
      <data key="d11">cbfe1bef496646118385efae89b5e52c</data>
      <data key="d12">5653</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a condition that requires careful nutritional management, particularly for patients who may have additional health concerns. In the context of MELAS syndrome, it has been noted that artificial nutrition can contribute to the development of diabetes. Therefore, it is crucial for diabetic patients, especially those with complex conditions like MELAS, to receive tailored nutritional support to manage their health effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">e3370b71146ad5063d6b1e9c3d8a3bd2,f0a97cbd966f5a930d9355f589d05613</data>
      <data key="d11">2f04100d59d04c6ab8f03b32b5850a6d</data>
      <data key="d12">5654</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="MACRONUTRIENTS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is mentioned in relation to the distribution of macronutrients in the diet</data>
      <data key="d10">bfe875ea294b9a390193b5de532ff71b</data>
      <data key="d11">6dff19f800424784a74382210ac890bd</data>
      <data key="d12">5655</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="HYPERGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a chronic condition that frequently results in hyperglycemia, a state of elevated blood glucose levels. This relationship necessitates specific nutritional interventions and careful management to mitigate the risks associated with high blood sugar. Hyperglycemia is a common complication observed in patients with diabetes, and its severity can be further exacerbated by conditions such as pancreatitis. Therefore, effective management of diabetes is crucial to prevent hyperglycemia and its associated complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">178140d0d29364593546d7d21393f2c6,8413d4414414c5cb139198857cce327a,e36c9b09870e14d19aa6eb7c82514499</data>
      <data key="d11">65d6a361a86d405f86bd5cadb7c00adb</data>
      <data key="d12">5656</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="F&#211;RMULAS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional formulas are specifically designed to meet the dietary needs of diabetic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567</data>
      <data key="d11">f3d6fa215ce446d7a66f0fbb82ef3225</data>
      <data key="d12">5657</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL V&#205;A ORAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oral enteral nutrition is a method used to support diabetic patients who can still eat</data>
      <data key="d10">d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567</data>
      <data key="d11">ccf516e2838a4b298f6e8cdf149093c7</data>
      <data key="d12">5658</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="F&#211;RMULAS CON ALTO CONTENIDO EN GRASA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High-fat formulas are tailored for diabetic patients to manage carbohydrate intake</data>
      <data key="d10">d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567</data>
      <data key="d11">e4f88831cc94493aa930cf02005f0300</data>
      <data key="d12">5659</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="F&#211;RMULAS CON REPARTO EQUILIBRADO DE NUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Balanced nutrient formulas are designed to meet the specific needs of diabetic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">d3dab2869ed103bbf74ecb1a4a822567</data>
      <data key="d11">eb510b3ec5974326befefb46a10f8a76</data>
      <data key="d12">5660</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="ELDERLY POPULATION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The elderly population is at a higher risk of diabetes, which can lead to frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d11">88062e9a783d4c9ca213bdc717c527b8</data>
      <data key="d12">5661</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta mediterr&#225;nea se investiga por su impacto en la diabetes y la salud metab&#243;lica</data>
      <data key="d10">7e1b90e2c8714b39e283be229f6d5de3</data>
      <data key="d11">f8b0e9add0044229a14ed725d08ce84d</data>
      <data key="d12">5662</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="PAPENDOCRINIC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PapEndoCrinic program covers various aspects of diabetes management and treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">fc81f645a5600b374c960fd8739a0503</data>
      <data key="d11">82099ca198724cd6b86862d0dc6deab5</data>
      <data key="d12">5663</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="ACROMEGALY">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes can develop as a metabolic complication of acromegaly due to insulin resistance</data>
      <data key="d10">2261671ccad439da1ed9ea5a27857dc8</data>
      <data key="d11">1e33552cc4964df6abbc72bdffa0c3d7</data>
      <data key="d12">5664</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 1">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 1 diabetes is a specific form of diabetes characterized by autoimmune destruction of pancreatic beta cells</data>
      <data key="d10">d0231ac4e41b0e826d80763b5b8c61e0</data>
      <data key="d11">17730ee7ea1a47848e1348cbf00395a6</data>
      <data key="d12">5665</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="AMERICAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association (ADA) plays a crucial role in the management and understanding of diabetes. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for managing diabetes, which encompass various aspects such as classification, diagnosis, and treatment options. The ADA outlines standards for different types of diabetes and includes specific recommendations for surgical interventions when necessary. Through its guidelines, the ADA aims to improve the care and outcomes for individuals living with diabetes, ensuring that healthcare professionals have the necessary resources to provide effective management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">54bdd3faa067cdbb44671453ffaf4be5,5c11ed246e1a48261910b9b71b65014c,7855ffa74481ba85f44e9700279250e7,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">a68ed5d6a889413d86efe13b0312184e</data>
      <data key="d12">5666</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="MODY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MODY is a specific type of diabetes that is genetically inherited and characterized by different clinical features compared to other types of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">d8b4da3e50154e318acf17c1851a4f7d</data>
      <data key="d12">5667</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic renal insufficiency is a common complication of diabetes, particularly in poorly managed cases.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">4a2d90570a9c484d84199cbd069e5707</data>
      <data key="d12">5668</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="SULFONILUREAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sulfonylureas are a common treatment option for managing Type 2 diabetes, which is one of the main types of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">f53d797ed6ab4895a2b95a032054803c</data>
      <data key="d12">5669</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="LINAGLIPTINA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Linagliptina is a medication specifically designed for the treatment of Type 2 diabetes, a common form of diabetes. It is noteworthy that Linagliptina does not require dose adjustment in patients with severe renal impairment, making it a suitable option for individuals with compromised kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d10">630ac8fefe27e4b893831674a67dcc82,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">62970f2acbdb42bd92700d8d8547acaa</data>
      <data key="d12">5670</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="PREDIABETES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Prediabetes is a precursor to Type 2 diabetes, indicating a higher risk of developing the condition if not managed properly.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">14275bfe54d845fe9ef6abe68f333e80</data>
      <data key="d12">5671</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="DIABETES TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 2 diabetes is a specific form of diabetes characterized by insulin resistance and is one of the most common types of diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">1e04729f486e4d1f8e8e56d72594ba98</data>
      <data key="d12">5672</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin is a critical hormone used in the management of diabetes, particularly for individuals with Type 1 diabetes and those with advanced Type 2 diabetes. It serves as a primary treatment option for diabetes, playing a vital role in regulating blood sugar levels. Additionally, the management of diabetes can become more complex for patients who also have pancreatic cancer, as insulin treatment is essential for controlling their diabetes symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d10">bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3,f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">c2085176ecf24856b57954da9dd93cfd</data>
      <data key="d12">5673</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="COMPLICACIONES MICROVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Microvascular complications are common in individuals with poorly managed diabetes, highlighting the importance of effective treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">75634c3ee7dc4f35893cb23b47dcf7f2</data>
      <data key="d12">5674</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Treatment strategies are essential for managing diabetes and preventing complications associated with the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">2fbe88715ddc421f8de068266bc78b61</data>
      <data key="d12">5675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="GLUCOKINASE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucokinase is involved in the metabolic processes that are disrupted in diabetes, affecting insulin secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">9f71bc81fcdc421c90ad3340bcf6b5bd</data>
      <data key="d12">5676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="GLUT2">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GLUT2 is essential for glucose entry into &#946;-cells, which is critical in the context of diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">8828f78146b1418192a6393b2e2d8c23</data>
      <data key="d12">5677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="CALCIUM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium signaling is crucial for insulin secretion, which is impaired in diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">4ba98121948c4aafbef33c88ae58ccb8</data>
      <data key="d12">5678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSULIN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is characterized by issues related to insulin production and action</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">c7cac549503e402e8e340308fbff61ed</data>
      <data key="d12">5679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin resistance leads to increased fat accumulation in the liver, contributing to diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">abfcfc24b8294fa3b8e967ab400b7f4a</data>
      <data key="d12">5680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="M&#218;SCULO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin resistance affects muscle tissue's ability to uptake glucose, which is a key factor in diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">d6d42d6ed59f41378fb8588ed2a3c008</data>
      <data key="d12">5681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="CORAZ&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes can lead to cardiovascular complications due to insulin resistance affecting heart function</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">2bc989764cfa4e8692827528cc580404</data>
      <data key="d12">5682</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="RI&#209;&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin resistance can impact kidney function and glucose metabolism, contributing to diabetes complications</data>
      <data key="d10">c7c764ddf88b5379a4bb35819cd25b82</data>
      <data key="d11">d5a1dc476da54119bc2eb9fa23e150d2</data>
      <data key="d12">5683</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="C&#201;LULAS &#914;">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is characterized by dysfunction of beta cells, leading to impaired insulin secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">9baa05f21f51764ac1d0537294bdc7db</data>
      <data key="d11">4383076c9ed6449390f3547fe7caf09f</data>
      <data key="d12">5684</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="ACUTE MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes significantly increases the risk of acute myocardial infarction due to associated cardiovascular complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d11">c301e3b76b7c41a49400aaf5b9d3cbe8</data>
      <data key="d12">5685</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSUFICIENCIA CARD&#205;ACA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes significantly increases the prevalence and worsens the prognosis of heart failure among patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d11">36797daadb0840a19dde39e261018c8c</data>
      <data key="d12">5686</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="DISLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes often experience dyslipidemia, which heightens their risk for cardiovascular diseases.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d11">1c58d75df5d0496d81cd8ce53e7ff295</data>
      <data key="d12">5687</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="S&#205;NDROME CORONARIO AGUDO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a major risk factor for developing acute coronary syndrome due to its impact on cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d11">dcc2d07c2db5461a8449aa747e674b32</data>
      <data key="d12">5688</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="MORTALITY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is associated with increased mortality rates due to various complications, including cardiovascular diseases</data>
      <data key="d10">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
      <data key="d11">af9130740a004f0b9a9ff760fff919e3</data>
      <data key="d12">5689</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="RETINOPATHY DIAB&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes can lead to diabetic retinopathy, a serious eye condition</data>
      <data key="d10">dfe972dc8a4eabfc8948770fe113c833</data>
      <data key="d11">58e9677c61044bb6a0a9327f484f6a05</data>
