    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSULINA GLARGINA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulina glargina is a crucial component of the treatment regimen for managing diabetes. It is specifically utilized to help regulate and control blood glucose levels in patients diagnosed with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd</data>
      <data key="d11">26f0e36312d84b7b9ba35e0bd03301d7</data>
      <data key="d12">5741</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="INSULINA LISPRO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulina lispro is a medication specifically designed to control blood sugar spikes during meals for diabetic patients. It is commonly administered as part of a comprehensive treatment plan and is often used in conjunction with other therapies to effectively manage diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">bfdbf41efa08067d5ae1b1a67830affd</data>
      <data key="d11">2b7f7e36d9cc4bcab2944253a69a195b</data>
      <data key="d12">5742</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="CYSTIC FIBROSIS">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a common complication in patients with cystic fibrosis, significantly impacting their overall health management. This increased risk of developing diabetes in individuals with cystic fibrosis is primarily attributed to pancreatic dysfunction, which is a characteristic feature of the disease. As a result, the interplay between diabetes and cystic fibrosis necessitates careful monitoring and management to ensure optimal health outcomes for affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">1e997b2a6bf1c926a7a17d8b5ac1e699,cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
