    <edge source="DIABETES" target="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes significantly increases the risk of developing cardiovascular disease due to its effects on blood vessels and cholesterol levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50</data>
      <data key="d11">9f46fa78970147d28c9d9e11a119ee28</data>
      <data key="d12">5793</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="HIPOMAGNESEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes puede causar diuresis osm&#243;tica, lo que puede resultar en hipermagnesiuria y, por ende, hipomagnesemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d11">23f6b4d4221c48ffb8ff1c934c33df66</data>
      <data key="d12">5794</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="HEMATOCHROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes can be a complication of hereditary hemochromatosis due to the effects of iron on insulin production and glucose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271</data>
      <data key="d11">05b5aa258a8340b1998bf94017000973</data>
      <data key="d12">5795</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes is a condition that is frequently associated with an increased risk of developing kidney stones, also known as lithiasis renal. This significant connection between diabetes and lithiasis renal highlights the potential complications that individuals with diabetes may face regarding their kidney health.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb</data>
      <data key="d11">655ea6dbf7674e91a6ea5d083cf56309</data>
      <data key="d12">5796</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="BACTERIAS INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes may be affected by the gut microbiome and its interactions with the immune system.</data>
      <data key="d10">0d9c11c44c3cf4e1e3148949cc0a4096</data>
      <data key="d11">801f44b9f2644d7ea50e7c79969f080b</data>
      <data key="d12">5797</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="DISBIOSIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Disbiosis has been linked to diabetes, suggesting that gut health may influence metabolic disorders</data>
      <data key="d10">90f122c65fbb08f52e052d0e22714849</data>
      <data key="d11">85a744344cdf489eb1b76051f473177c</data>
      <data key="d12">5798</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="AYUNO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con diabetes deben seguir protocolos espec&#237;ficos de ayuno para manejar la glucemia antes de las pruebas</data>
      <data key="d10">e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d11">9c1f17cfe9314a8a92be7ed33b34066e</data>
      <data key="d12">5799</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES" target="METFORMINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El tratamiento con metformina est&#225; relacionado con el manejo de la diabetes y debe ser retirado antes de ciertos estudios</data>
      <data key="d10">e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d11">1fc5a3f52cb549579e64d9a8a5f80687</data>
      <data key="d12">5800</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La obesidad es un factor de riesgo que contribuye a la fragilidad en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d10">bdb8258b310cb9ed8a0e4354fac5a33c</data>
      <data key="d11">ec94fc947bf549a38d25d7ef10812d3d</data>
      <data key="d12">5801</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FRAILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad is related to frailidad as studies have shown a connection between weight loss and increased mortality in older adults.</data>
      <data key="d10">c10cd7b5fa3f7e4428da8371caba4087</data>
      <data key="d11">b6cb902cb2194f0688603eecf67f93a7</data>
      <data key="d12">5802</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="LIPIDOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad is often associated with lipid levels in the body, as excess body fat can result from high lipid levels and contribute to obesity-related health issues.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">b6f33beba957463a8edf68e2e2ec5db4</data>
      <data key="d12">5803</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CASOS CLINICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad may be discussed in various clinical cases to illustrate its impact on health and treatment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">497647ef252d428aa7cb80b67a0e634a</data>
      <data key="d12">5804</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="M&#211;DULO 8">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M&#243;dulo 8 discusses obesity as a significant health issue, linking it to various medical conditions and treatments.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">be47ed12806c440c9d8cb35a2d0cdc77</data>
      <data key="d12">5805</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La obesidad puede estar asociada con un aumento en los niveles de cortisol, afectando la salud hormonal</data>
      <data key="d10">e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d11">d2998f0b606345f99f10d641e64cf740</data>
      <data key="d12">5806</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="HIPERANDROGENISMO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity can affect hormone levels and is associated with hyperandrogenism, linking the two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">891845d69f624808b4fd952cfa81cf7b</data>
      <data key="d12">5807</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="SHBG">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad is associated with decreased SHBG levels, impacting testosterone availability</data>
      <data key="d10">4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55</data>
      <data key="d11">b54434cfcdb2434abdd10deeb8c2f05d</data>
      <data key="d12">5808</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="L&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad, or obesity, is a condition that is closely related to the consumption of l&#237;pidos, or lipids, and their impact on health and diet. It is often linked to the metabolism of l&#237;pidos, as dietary fats play a significant role in weight management. The relationship between obesity and lipids highlights the importance of understanding dietary fat intake and its effects on overall health.</data>
      <data key="d10">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,89b0bde0358432506a0e03d4691dd2ab</data>
      <data key="d11">ba2ed0d2f1ed44dcb56ecdf91d956296</data>
      <data key="d12">5809</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="TRASTORNOS ELECTROL&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad, or obesity, is a condition that can significantly impact an individual's health and is often associated with trastornos electrol&#237;ticos, or electrolyte disorders. The relationship between these two entities is notable, as obesity can lead to imbalances in the body's electrolyte levels. This disruption can further affect overall health, highlighting the importance of managing weight to maintain proper electrolyte balance and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">7ba6c80b1b1919de63502e93c6b9f6fa,89b0bde0358432506a0e03d4691dd2ab</data>
      <data key="d11">3d0deba34abb46ccbc4b50b83e87b145</data>
      <data key="d12">5810</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="OBESIDAD METAB&#211;LICAMENTE SANA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Metabolically healthy obesity is a type of obesity that does not present metabolic complications</data>
      <data key="d10">a63d12481faecf7a11206d83de199360</data>
      <data key="d11">9a05d5a6a5054b1c8573fbf7489fdf9c</data>
      <data key="d12">5811</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="EHGNA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity and EHGNA (Enfermedad Hep&#225;tica Grasa No Alcoh&#243;lica) are closely related health conditions. EHGNA is a condition that is significantly associated with obesity, affecting a large percentage of obese individuals. Conversely, obesity is recognized as a major contributing factor to the development of EHGNA, with a significant percentage of those who are obese being affected by this liver condition. This interrelationship highlights the importance of addressing obesity as a key factor in preventing and managing EHGNA.</data>
      <data key="d10">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129,7e4178b0d21cc5424b4c54bc5de42471</data>
      <data key="d11">eb0ddfadb18049d6a04886009f5456fd</data>
      <data key="d12">5812</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is a major risk factor for developing cardiovascular disease</data>
      <data key="d10">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129</data>
      <data key="d11">a9935f10e2894c89a73a6e13f542eab1</data>
      <data key="d12">5813</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is a significant risk factor for the development of coronary heart disease</data>
      <data key="d10">25aa0d91d4df6b3fc332cded1607a129</data>
      <data key="d11">8c3e7b2803834432885f275ccf1b15af</data>
      <data key="d12">5814</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="PEPTIDOS NATRIURETICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Natriuretic peptides are decreased in obesity, which exacerbates the effects of aldosterone and leptin</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">2dbdd414f180430e9b45de110bcc4964</data>
      <data key="d12">5815</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="LEPTINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Leptin levels are elevated in obesity and contribute to increased sympathetic tone and inflammation</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">4bc8f75aa4b441b980fc98b4e7adf301</data>
      <data key="d12">5816</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ALDOSTERONA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aldosterone levels are increased in obesity, leading to sodium retention and hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">07eb46c50b6c4880a624397cf673aa53</data>
      <data key="d12">5817</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="NEPRILISINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neprilysin is overexpressed in obesity, affecting the degradation of natriuretic peptides</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">dfbb851bc9504eac87864f75f19d4b0a</data>
      <data key="d12">5818</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="SISTEMA NERVIOSO SIMPATICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The sympathetic nervous system is activated in obesity, promoting sodium retention and fluid expansion</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">7d84c64d4a474970b15cdefa1023cee4</data>
      <data key="d12">5819</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FIBROSIS MIOCARDICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity leads to cardiac fibrosis through inflammatory processes and hormonal interactions</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">4d43ccbda8c94d2f876d433c780e8b00</data>
      <data key="d12">5820</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="VOLUMEN SANGUINEO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased blood volume is a hemodynamic change associated with obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">ee8d685c30504f29b6ccb0ac66c17363</data>
      <data key="d12">5821</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="VOLUMEN SISTOLICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased stroke volume is a hemodynamic effect observed in obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">2591103774104e2f8972c1185d3fc8fd</data>
      <data key="d12">5822</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="PRESION ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated blood pressure is a common consequence of obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">1537f209696c43b6b8a92cd921ea4df9</data>
      <data key="d12">5823</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="GROSOR DE LA PARED DEL VI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased left ventricular wall thickness is associated with obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">7a7c380610204592a2ad979953d2df55</data>
      <data key="d12">5824</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="HIPERTENSION PULMONAR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pulmonary hypertension can occur as a complication of obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">1548f6475ef54e83aa8477450cfb7654</data>
      <data key="d12">5825</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DISFUNCION DIASTOLICA DEL VI">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diastolic dysfunction of the left ventricle can be exacerbated by obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">f4bfa692e551498e8c491a7bde01750d</data>
      <data key="d12">5826</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DISFUNCION SISTOLICA DEL VI">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Systolic dysfunction of the left ventricle can be a potential outcome of obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">cfc3f6b1926b449786f2a2528d47346d</data>
      <data key="d12">5827</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FALLO VENTRICULAR DERECHO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Right ventricular failure can be a consequence of obesity-related cardiovascular complications</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">5ab3fc56622c42e5b0a9a79589dcd6fd</data>
      <data key="d12">5828</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ADIPONECTINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adiponectin levels are often decreased in obesity, affecting metabolic health</data>
      <data key="d10">c575e742f54d5f3f674a8e52ad041221</data>
      <data key="d11">556b219e54f24a04a491a1399fc996e8</data>
      <data key="d12">5829</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FIBRILACI&#211;N AURICULAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La obesidad aumenta el riesgo de padecer fibrilaci&#243;n auricular, aproximadamente un 50% m&#225;s alto que una persona con normopeso.</data>
      <data key="d10">884a8370915a18a005fb2fa913e4b95c</data>
      <data key="d11">44707373072e4d5e876e45789d5a6163</data>
      <data key="d12">5830</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="BUPROPION-NALTREXONE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bupropion-naltrexone is indicated for patients suffering from obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0</data>
      <data key="d11">c9367e2fec864328a3c7f7ea3f6b8e12</data>
      <data key="d12">5831</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DIABETES TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesidad y diabetes tipo 2 est&#225;n estrechamente relacionadas, ya que la obesidad es un factor de riesgo significativo para el desarrollo de diabetes tipo 2. Esta relaci&#243;n se evidencia en m&#250;ltiples estudios que destacan c&#243;mo el exceso de peso puede contribuir a la resistencia a la insulina, lo que a su vez aumenta la probabilidad de que una persona desarrolle esta enfermedad metab&#243;lica.</data>
      <data key="d10">419657aaa9492bbff3d218e00d2b0fd4,65e3dfcb7a0c5a2a09a98342c597c020</data>
      <data key="d11">409b4e087ce440f980813cf17bee7ad7</data>
      <data key="d12">5832</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">33.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity, referred to as "OBESIDAD," is a significant health concern that can lead to various complications, including diabetes. Bariatric surgery, known as "CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA," is a treatment option specifically designed for individuals suffering from obesity, particularly those with severe obesity or morbid obesity. This surgical intervention aims to facilitate weight loss and enhance the overall health of patients. It is especially beneficial for diabetic patients, as it not only helps in weight reduction but also contributes to the improvement of their health conditions. Overall, bariatric surgery serves as a crucial treatment for obesity, focusing on reducing weight and promoting better health outcomes for those affected.</data>
      <data key="d10">01d01bb87220a5cf6d7b37d95834e15f,2c7998e65812140cbdda2e4d9c972315,6b2c4f18c643a0fdca707628511bf0aa,de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d11">23ff50c56ad44f208f4cf2773819a63c</data>
      <data key="d12">5833</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Higher consumption of fruits and vegetables may reduce the risk of breast cancer and obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d11">ed55116df5034a47951b015d6fe91bca</data>
      <data key="d12">5834</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="C&#193;NCER VESICAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The risk of bladder cancer may be influenced by obesity and dietary factors</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d11">a2833c163d584cd8b181fae15696a854</data>
      <data key="d12">5835</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is a risk factor that may influence the development of prostate cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d11">6c8391c9dc2c4636be6b3b364200b2ff</data>
      <data key="d12">5836</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CEREALES INTEGRALES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo regular de cereales integrales se asocia con un menor &#237;ndice de masa corporal y menos posibilidades de desarrollar sobrepeso u obesidad.</data>
      <data key="d10">8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692</data>
      <data key="d11">eb5ca83fc2f74c8e8e604b15f3d2cc23</data>
      <data key="d12">5837</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Un mayor consumo de fibra diet&#233;tica se asocia con un menor peso corporal y per&#237;metro abdominal, lo que puede ayudar a prevenir la obesidad.</data>
      <data key="d10">8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692</data>
      <data key="d11">07cc54601e494e5f8ab403cae72d2fc4</data>
      <data key="d12">5838</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="PESCADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fish oil is associated with reduced body fat and weight in animal models, suggesting potential anti-obesity effects</data>
      <data key="d10">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a</data>
      <data key="d11">27a539842a35409483373790be7d3d19</data>
      <data key="d12">5839</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="GRASAS TRANS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de grasas trans se ha relacionado con un aumento en el peso corporal y la grasa visceral.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d11">6ee1033379fe4629b4e7655c040cdf1f</data>
      <data key="d12">5840</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de bebidas azucaradas se ha relacionado con un aumento en la incidencia de obesidad en ni&#241;os y j&#243;venes.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d11">ecd5c7541ef049a1adfb583d561c44d0</data>
      <data key="d12">5841</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La adherencia a la dieta mediterr&#225;nea puede reducir el peso corporal y mejorar la adiposidad</data>
      <data key="d10">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63</data>
      <data key="d11">f102b75495ca481cb555d402a8019a03</data>
      <data key="d12">5842</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ESTUDIO PREDIMED">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El estudio PREDIMED mostr&#243; que la dieta mediterr&#225;nea tiene efectos beneficiosos sobre la obesidad</data>
      <data key="d10">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63</data>
      <data key="d11">319a492ac96b49f0b1e7e55cfc074895</data>
      <data key="d12">5843</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOMETAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad cardiometab&#243;lica est&#225; relacionada con la obesidad y puede ser influenciada por la dieta</data>
      <data key="d10">01302d2656a8cbb49cb7505b3182cc63</data>
      <data key="d11">e0e795e1eda24403bc76f67c7e62ec7e</data>
      <data key="d12">5844</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity and type 2 diabetes mellitus are closely interconnected health conditions. Diabetes mellitus tipo 2 is frequently associated with obesity, as excess body fat can lead to insulin resistance, a key factor in the development of this form of diabetes. Consequently, obesity is recognized as a significant risk factor for the onset of type 2 diabetes, highlighting the importance of managing body weight to reduce the likelihood of developing this chronic condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666,dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d11">2b1faaf97d514d689dbd78590657e4af</data>
      <data key="d12">5845</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="C&#193;NCER DE COLON">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is associated with an increased risk of colon cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d11">17142879fea3416db1162c64014f8bf5</data>
      <data key="d12">5846</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="RANGOS ACEPTABLES DE DISTRIBUCI&#211;N DE NUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AMDR guidelines aim to reduce the risk of obesity and other chronic diseases</data>
      <data key="d10">dea64d5eb807430bc52e8bed6e30c393</data>
      <data key="d11">4c04b3f150d345f6bed8a91e4e236e83</data>
      <data key="d12">5847</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS SATURADOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High intake of saturated fatty acids is associated with obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">148443357888793655b663333268775a</data>
      <data key="d11">e00a66bf34714654bdc8c035416597dd</data>
      <data key="d12">5848</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="FIBRA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased fiber intake is associated with a lower risk of obesity</data>
      <data key="d10">7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3</data>
      <data key="d11">41ece14375ed4e7e83730b0919185a25</data>
      <data key="d12">5849</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is classified as a chronic disease that is influenced by lifestyle and dietary choices</data>
      <data key="d10">b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074</data>
      <data key="d11">8d7b69b5c1d14b95946ed2b192d33ab3</data>
      <data key="d12">5850</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is a significant health concern that is often managed through various strategies, one of which is dietotherapy. Dietotherapy involves implementing dietary changes to help control and reduce obesity. It is frequently employed as a treatment strategy aimed at managing obesity effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">701eb4c24e94839def8d18882a2dda63,87cb06eed8a8c92c589d25ea2d5cfaec</data>
      <data key="d11">f2b17484a0a34d17abf140a0cce0d2b0</data>
      <data key="d12">5851</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE LE&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The healthcare institution addresses obesity treatment, indicating a direct relationship with the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">89e0e7fac6984f367ae1649e9eaab7d7</data>
      <data key="d11">bca6fc2cfccd4ee4890718114303b7e5</data>
      <data key="d12">5852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="H&#205;GADO GRASO NO ALCOH&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease is commonly linked to obesity, as excess fat can accumulate in the liver.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">e7429a8832d048ddbb5a79e59ce81441</data>
      <data key="d12">5853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="S&#205;NDROME DE OVARIO POLIQU&#205;STICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polycystic ovary syndrome is frequently associated with obesity, as weight gain can exacerbate symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">dc0b8eba08dd448c9af3b7cc9b7eb345</data>
      <data key="d12">5854</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="APNEA OBSTRUCTIVA DEL SUE&#209;O">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obstructive sleep apnea is more prevalent in individuals with obesity due to excess weight around the neck area.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">27e9d732c0404a96a2a78db4e2ca4bde</data>
      <data key="d12">5855</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="ASTMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Asthma symptoms can be worsened by obesity, as excess weight can affect lung function.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">e6019658ad3140e1ae6ab3ad2d60ec62</data>
      <data key="d12">5856</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="OSTEOARTRITIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity increases the risk of osteoarthritis due to added stress on weight-bearing joints.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">dd8661a01f71422e80db3a9b20f300b9</data>
      <data key="d12">5857</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="INCONTINENCIA URINARIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity can contribute to urinary incontinence by increasing pressure on the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">dc92cf0f279146ca88cd515cadde4a56</data>
      <data key="d12">5858</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="CALORIMETR&#205;A INDIRECTA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Indirect calorimetry is often used to assess energy expenditure in individuals with obesity to tailor weight loss programs.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">640a72394f424c1a922a12b384526225</data>
      <data key="d12">5859</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="HARRIS-BENEDICT">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Harris-Benedict equation is utilized to estimate caloric needs in obese individuals for weight management.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">fb6e2e4166c54227966c1c7eb1a10f04</data>
      <data key="d12">5860</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="IRETON-JONES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Ireton-Jones equation helps determine energy requirements in obese patients, especially in clinical settings.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">fbfa346d3e274713be7b8b5bd95e7cbd</data>
      <data key="d12">5861</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="DENSIDAD ENERG&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Energy density is a key factor in obesity management, as lower energy-dense foods can aid in weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e40e9a9e041bbf1e7ca6eaa14080666</data>
      <data key="d11">7cc6e785f401467c9e6e97813dfb0601</data>
      <data key="d12">5862</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OBESIDAD" target="P&#201;NDULO DE PESO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
