      <data key="d12">5959</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OMS" target="CDC">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both the CDC and WHO are organizations involved in establishing health standards and guidelines for child growth</data>
      <data key="d10">7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
      <data key="d11">6aea834526e345868313092a36c8ae5d</data>
      <data key="d12">5960</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OMS" target="EURO-GROWTH 2000">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Euro-Growth 2000 study was developed under the auspices of the WHO to provide growth standards for European children</data>
      <data key="d10">7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
      <data key="d11">6735fa9550294ee7b7cc806e9ae1f74e</data>
      <data key="d12">5961</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OMS" target="BRAZIL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Brazil contributed data to the WHO's international growth reference patterns for children</data>
      <data key="d10">7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
      <data key="d11">dedd657b03e14200974a280fd70c4664</data>
      <data key="d12">5962</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OMS" target="INDIA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">India provides data on child growth and nutrition to the World Health Organization (WHO) in order to establish international standards. This data is utilized by the WHO to develop international growth reference patterns for children.</data>
      <data key="d10">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
      <data key="d11">88c55e643d5b4366823161112dd139da</data>
      <data key="d12">5963</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OMS" target="GHANA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ghana has played a significant role in contributing to the World Health Organization's (WHO) international growth reference patterns for children. The country provides valuable data on child growth and nutrition to the WHO, which is essential for establishing international standards. This collaboration highlights Ghana's commitment to improving child health and nutrition on a global scale.</data>
      <data key="d10">21634801ee74e0828836551dbeb8b1ed,7894b38e96733cb8fb258b4666f7d7b7</data>
