    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="ELDERLY POPULATION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The elderly population is more susceptible to cancer, which can lead to frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">97a29de0d5161aebffb702f69c6dd870</data>
      <data key="d11">a6304358419744739f9a08b13150b401</data>
      <data key="d12">6319</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="TIROIDES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The thyroid gland can develop cancer, specifically differentiated thyroid cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f</data>
      <data key="d11">c92e6830516b4f42957ab0a0e8088ca5</data>
      <data key="d12">6320</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="THYROID NODULES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Thyroid nodules can be benign or malignant, and their management is crucial in the context of differentiated thyroid cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">02db15b9ad7bc5655e1907ad3fa4e8ad</data>
      <data key="d11">9829889d890e4a34a375995d5abbf682</data>
      <data key="d12">6321</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="CALCITONIN">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcitonin levels are used as a biomarker to predict the presence of medullary thyroid cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">02db15b9ad7bc5655e1907ad3fa4e8ad</data>
      <data key="d11">775b3686dee941f3ac0a5bef0fe62750</data>
      <data key="d12">6322</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Enhanced Recovery After Surgery Society provides guidelines that are relevant for cancer patients undergoing surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">965d123606424d6bb42e288d24d1ee42</data>
      <data key="d12">6323</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="HIDRATOS DE CARBONO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intake of carbohydrates is recommended for cancer patients to help manage their preoperative state</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">63f30b781b9545df8babebdc28b0cae6</data>
      <data key="d12">6324</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS &#937;-3">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Omega-3 fatty acids may provide benefits for cancer patients by reducing inflammation and supporting immune function</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">9d07d8b08d794b818454f81ebc82b1c1</data>
      <data key="d12">6325</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="INSULINRESISTENCIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin resistance is a condition that can complicate the nutritional management of cancer patients</data>
      <data key="d10">dfc1e2e58310777aea7dc00c58cd384d</data>
      <data key="d11">7fe60e9cb0dc4b55940aff1ce8d9b853</data>
      <data key="d12">6326</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ESPEN provides guidelines on nutrition for cancer patients, emphasizing the importance of not exceeding recommended dietary allowances</data>
      <data key="d10">b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0</data>
      <data key="d11">0e5e04cb394f403087d149879dc010c5</data>
      <data key="d12">6327</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional supplementation is a critical topic in cancer care, with guidelines suggesting caution against high doses of certain vitamins</data>
      <data key="d10">b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0</data>
      <data key="d11">df20f29b553342a089d61b33be0997e6</data>
      <data key="d12">6328</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="TESTICULOS CRIPTORQU&#205;DICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cryptorchid testicles are associated with an increased risk of cancer if not treated</data>
      <data key="d10">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d11">e147ce249fe6457ea05d18e66df4fdce</data>
      <data key="d12">6329</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="ATROFIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Atrophy of the testicles can be a consequence of untreated cryptorchidism, which is also linked to cancer risk</data>
      <data key="d10">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d11">4ca6e7d7b5b84f32a703b812aa3ceeb0</data>
      <data key="d12">6330</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="HYPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer is a significant cause of hypercalcemia, particularly in hospitalized patients. This condition can arise through various mechanisms associated with cancer, such as the secretion of parathyroid hormone-related peptide (PTHrP) by tumors and the presence of osteolytic metastasis. Hypercalcemia is frequently observed as a complication in patients with solid tumors, highlighting the intricate relationship between cancer and elevated calcium levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d10">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783,ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d11">ef1c424a5a5d40b49dbbb7965564a24c</data>
      <data key="d12">6331</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de mama es uno de los tipos de c&#225;ncer m&#225;s com&#250;nmente asociados con hipercalcemia en pacientes hospitalizados.</data>
      <data key="d10">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d11">688a1af1ca6249b39c6d3f3128771c9d</data>
      <data key="d12">6332</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE RI&#209;&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de ri&#241;&#243;n puede causar hipercalcemia a trav&#233;s de mecanismos tumorales y es una de las causas comunes en pacientes hospitalizados.</data>
      <data key="d10">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d11">27a7412dbbba4278bcf37aec6aa98d68</data>
      <data key="d12">6333</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n es un tipo de c&#225;ncer que puede estar asociado con hipercalcemia, especialmente en etapas avanzadas de la enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d10">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d11">48c78179e8b24dae8a0186e2197349b9</data>
      <data key="d12">6334</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="MIELOMA M&#218;LTIPLE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El mieloma m&#250;ltiple es un tipo de c&#225;ncer que puede causar hipercalcemia debido a la destrucci&#243;n &#243;sea asociada con la enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d10">ba0a1fee09e488cf2628102b72a52435</data>
      <data key="d11">1df885f231404bc2ab9a51d0325db271</data>
      <data key="d12">6335</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="OBESITY">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obesity is a significant determinant of cancer risk and mortality, particularly in the United States. It is recognized as a major risk factor for the development of various types of cancer. The relationship between obesity and cancer underscores the importance of addressing obesity as a public health concern to reduce cancer incidence and improve overall health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">b110392fc91bc3d7875124ec3fa07c46,ea79efb65695c260a301f5c42237e2cb</data>
      <data key="d11">866e8c1dc98b4e02bf793fa1aabed06c</data>
      <data key="d12">6336</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="CANCER PREVENTION-II">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer Prevention-II study investigates the mortality rates associated with cancer and obesity</data>
