    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="PANCREATIC CANCER">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pancreatic cancer is a specific type of cancer that presents unique challenges and risks for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">bd3162e408d0d1ddd770ea833aad5ff3</data>
      <data key="d11">688e18f5f6cd4baf9af8b17d81d41a76</data>
      <data key="d12">6346</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="ADENOCARCINOMA DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El adenocarcinoma de p&#225;ncreas es una forma espec&#237;fica de c&#225;ncer</data>
      <data key="d10">5f4610a3d5efde69d7f34ec14c4bed0b</data>
      <data key="d11">b2405ad29a9a4f1da9aabf3cd545cd40</data>
      <data key="d12">6347</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="ACS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Cancer Society (ACS) focuses on cancer prevention and research, making it directly related to the event of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a</data>
      <data key="d11">89515b52e4cc46b694437ff2287668df</data>
      <data key="d12">6348</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="NUTRITION">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer and nutrition are intricately linked, with nutrition playing a crucial role in both the prevention and management of cancer. Research indicates that nutrition can influence the risk of developing certain types of cancer, highlighting the importance of dietary choices in cancer prevention. Furthermore, for individuals diagnosed with cancer, nutrition becomes a critical aspect of their care, significantly impacting their treatment outcomes and recovery process. Overall, there is a clear relationship between nutrition and cancer, underscoring the need for attention to dietary factors in both preventive and therapeutic contexts.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b361c0a9b5d08df1a67476a3ae3b968,67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,70e4538100be270d06e7a3cdc254ba28</data>
      <data key="d11">365dbbbc5bed4fa8b289bd32982a8ae6</data>
      <data key="d12">6349</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dietotherapy is used as a treatment approach for cancer, establishing a direct relationship with the event of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a</data>
      <data key="d11">04320f28597d4d43be1b2646cad4b514</data>
      <data key="d12">6350</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="PREDIMED">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PREDIMED study shows a reduction in cancer incidence associated with adherence to the Mediterranean diet</data>
      <data key="d10">c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670</data>
      <data key="d11">d38bb0576a7d4fd1a2fb3f648c3f2503</data>
      <data key="d12">6351</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="BLOQUE DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BLOQUE DIETOTERAPIA's dietary therapy initiatives are designed to lower cancer risk through improved nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">1566fcfef74295869c46405aaca05b32</data>
      <data key="d11">130fb7601c054b8583c7865b0251804b</data>
      <data key="d12">6352</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="NETHERLANDS COHORT STUDY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Netherlands Cohort Study investigates dietary factors that may influence the risk of developing cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766</data>
      <data key="d11">aae241e6b3094d40abbbbf46e90d244a</data>
      <data key="d12">6353</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER" target="DASH DIET">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The DASH diet is associated with reduced risk factors for cardiovascular diseases, which may also relate to cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766</data>
      <data key="d11">6b0969ec46f74a9486862a9022180204</data>
      <data key="d12">6354</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
