      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Resource Support Plus is a product used in nutritional support for patients, particularly in oncology.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">b287f0484fde455189cd2e867623463e</data>
      <data key="d12">6782</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="RESOURCE SUPPORT INSTANT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Resource Support Instant is utilized in nutritional support for patients who require dietary assistance.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">cc2931fbdf09437ca635eadb5b8098ce</data>
      <data key="d12">6783</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PROSURE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Prosure is a nutritional drink that supports patients needing enhanced dietary intake, especially in oncology.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">5fabdf8cb6fd4234a443f790dbae343d</data>
      <data key="d12">6784</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="SUPPORTAN DRINK">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Supportan Drink is designed to provide nutritional support for patients with increased energy and protein needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">b6f73f83f315452183b7fe406802dda3</data>
      <data key="d12">6785</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="FORTICARE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Forticare is a nutritional product aimed at patients requiring additional energy and protein, fitting into the category of nutritional support.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">1d288f577da94c88a5326ef57069e07b</data>
      <data key="d12">6786</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="MACROGOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Macrogol is often included in nutritional support regimens for patients experiencing constipation.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">88e6c7f224d74a21a1a48421a84a4755</data>
      <data key="d12">6787</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PLANTAGO OVATA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Plantago ovata is recommended in nutritional support for patients with chronic constipation to improve bowel regularity.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">85dc4b2ffdf940d0b5b198cfb8b5a852</data>
      <data key="d12">6788</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="BISACODILO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bisacodilo is used in nutritional support for patients to alleviate constipation, especially in those receiving opioids.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">8a08b1b552b14855835df68be3be2864</data>
      <data key="d12">6789</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PREDNISONA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Prednisona may be included in treatment regimens for patients requiring nutritional support due to its anti-inflammatory properties.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">48f17e7fd88645ecb9b9e762fc78b55a</data>
      <data key="d12">6790</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ONDANSETR&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ondansetron is often used in conjunction with nutritional support to manage nausea in patients undergoing cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">81959483de7a4c359c01ee420930e405</data>
      <data key="d12">6791</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="NISTATINA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nistatina may be prescribed alongside nutritional support for patients with fungal infections affecting their ability to eat.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">ef45f5189b73412aaf4ecf003bef88a4</data>
      <data key="d12">6792</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ACICLOVIR">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aciclovir can be part of the treatment plan for patients receiving nutritional support who have viral infections.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">8d59f9f4829941f58178f92468d5741a</data>
      <data key="d12">6793</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="FLUCONAZOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fluconazole may be used in patients receiving nutritional support who are suffering from systemic fungal infections.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">21a45f36ef7646a48f71238f0cb23676</data>
      <data key="d12">6794</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ITRACONAZOL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Itraconazole can be included in the treatment of patients receiving nutritional support who have fungal infections.</data>
      <data key="d10">dc8d12d9f32208671f6067b0bb64a645</data>
      <data key="d11">5a85eb2fe4e2495d9583225556cec782</data>
      <data key="d12">6795</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="BIBL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BIBL refers to literature that discusses artificial nutrition and its implications</data>
      <data key="d10">beaa66c30582232126ce2c762a9c6bdb</data>
      <data key="d11">7bd264fde92449f09f4b83faaf5a909b</data>
      <data key="d12">6796</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI LA FE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospital Universitari La Fe is involved in practices related to artificial nutrition for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">d2f4a90f3a3df7c568cd82d019bb5edd</data>
      <data key="d11">59f80c6da0fa44ebb922355414aaddf1</data>
      <data key="d12">6797</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PACIENTES CEL&#205;ACOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Artificial nutrition may be necessary for patients with celiac disease to address nutritional deficiencies before starting a gluten-free diet.</data>
      <data key="d10">8a7b2d5e0440750e36603c8d3f93a68a</data>
      <data key="d11">b658adb19caf4602831d4e12e3477cee</data>
      <data key="d12">6798</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PACIENTES CON DM">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with diabetes require artificial nutrition to manage their condition effectively</data>
      <data key="d10">8d1eb00b23450a2f2cb1243ea32aa36f</data>
      <data key="d11">fbad12f75f18438cb622bb7037185744</data>
      <data key="d12">6799</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ENFERMEDADES INFLAMATORIAS INTESTINALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La nutrici&#243;n artificial es un tratamiento importante para evitar la desnutrici&#243;n en pacientes con enfermedades inflamatorias intestinales.</data>
      <data key="d10">b4580c82418cd4df97f400e183702858</data>
      <data key="d11">5a1b3c47c09d4bf0a2f23562f3850140</data>
      <data key="d12">6800</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PACIENTE QUEMADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Burn patients often require artificial nutrition due to their inability to meet nutritional needs orally</data>
      <data key="d10">916d4d35de887923f4ea5b05928f13e3</data>
      <data key="d11">f9d007f799ff4667be78235661fdb41e</data>
      <data key="d12">6801</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="FLUIDOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fluid therapy is often initiated alongside artificial nutrition to ensure comprehensive care for burn patients</data>
      <data key="d10">916d4d35de887923f4ea5b05928f13e3</data>
      <data key="d11">86b96029fe644be78e3ce18674bf6f15</data>
      <data key="d12">6802</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="DIETISTA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The dietitian is involved in planning and managing artificial nutrition for patients unable to eat orally</data>
      <data key="d10">99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec</data>
      <data key="d11">027382018df441628229b24dad751429</data>
      <data key="d12">6803</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support is often necessary for patients with head and neck tumors post-surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">99900c6d95f85a5b4b88fcfed6775cec</data>
      <data key="d11">9bcd9d06a0774959a6009d38997e40f1</data>
      <data key="d12">6804</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="MUCOSITIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL and MUCOSITIS are closely related in the context of patient care. Mucositis, a condition characterized by inflammation and ulceration of the mucous membranes, can significantly impair a patient's ability to eat. As a result, individuals suffering from mucositis may require nutritional support through artificial means. Nutritional artificial is often initiated in these patients when oral intake becomes impossible, ensuring that they receive the necessary nutrients despite their difficulties with eating.</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1,eae8ddef005974a2ffe71cf7c61b0634</data>
      <data key="d11">b26817d4d55d407895dc8376962cd869</data>
      <data key="d12">6805</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="TUMORES S&#211;LIDOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with solid tumors may require nutritional support due to the risk of malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">dbca64eee8c24f8685023d92c49fc44b</data>
      <data key="d12">6806</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ALOG&#201;NICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alog&#233;nic bone marrow transplants often require more intensive nutritional support</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">825e2d738caf41f4ba675db0c6c54da5</data>
      <data key="d12">6807</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="AUT&#211;LOGO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Autologous transplants may also require nutritional support, though typically less than allogeneic</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">e3cf1b9591284119b1310a29eba0546d</data>
      <data key="d12">6808</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="ENFERMEDAD VENOCULOSIVA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatic veno-occlusive disease can complicate nutritional intake, necessitating artificial support</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">5f58f0d445964a9a94120a30dcad0b8c</data>
      <data key="d12">6809</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PACIENTE CR&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Critical patients may require artificial nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake</data>
      <data key="d10">428ea9c156fe3f0571b20d5d81648868</data>
      <data key="d11">c9b73d5c93f245fa89b5ffee6020abf9</data>
      <data key="d12">6810</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="FORMULAS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional formulas are often used in artificial nutrition to provide essential nutrients</data>
      <data key="d10">428ea9c156fe3f0571b20d5d81648868</data>
      <data key="d11">dfdb88fea0ec48608c67cafb67ea08d4</data>
      <data key="d12">6811</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="YEYUNOSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Yeyunostomy is another method of providing artificial nutrition when access through the stomach is not possible</data>
      <data key="d10">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9</data>
      <data key="d11">9617d6b2648f45a09cbd1904d3165e33</data>
      <data key="d12">6812</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="NE">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL is a form of nutritional support commonly administered to NE patients who experience difficulties with swallowing as a result of neurological conditions. This support is typically delivered through enteral means, which is utilized when the digestive tract remains functional.</data>
      <data key="d10">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">200cf0e414794fcfa631f103a9f5dd5c</data>
      <data key="d12">6813</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="SONDA ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enteral tubes are commonly used for providing artificial nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9</data>
      <data key="d11">571d43e52e5248c4a9962d4c19839f41</data>
      <data key="d12">6814</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="SONDA POSTPIL&#211;RICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Post-pyloric tubes are used for enteral nutrition in patients at risk of aspiration</data>
      <data key="d10">0b3eea4ed6da979f796aeba1ff2ee8d9</data>
      <data key="d11">46a63f11b15c48dd83a61714fb04383e</data>
      <data key="d12">6815</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL and HIPONATREMIA are closely related in the context of patient care, particularly for those receiving artificial nutrition. Hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, is frequently observed in patients undergoing artificial nutrition. This condition can arise due to fluid overload and impaired sodium regulation, as well as imbalances in electrolytes that may occur during the administration of artificial nutrition. 

In some cases, hyponatremia may necessitate the use of artificial nutrition for management, especially in patients who are unable to maintain adequate sodium levels through a regular diet. Effective management of hyponatremia in these patients often requires careful adjustments to their artificial nutrition regimen to prevent complications. The diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia in patients receiving artificial nutrition are critical areas of focus, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing electrolyte intake to ensure patient safety and health.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec,3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4</data>
      <data key="d11">9978c4ad67c24898ac07b6375ab506ba</data>
      <data key="d12">6816</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="NP">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NP patients may require NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL post-surgery due to complications like nausea and vomiting</data>
      <data key="d10">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">5a56d5e485db405aafb17af33d1cee0c</data>
      <data key="d12">6817</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="SIADH">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients receiving artificial nutrition may develop SIADH due to fluid imbalance</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">0e6bbdf4ce3a418aa0660836feadbe75</data>
      <data key="d12">6818</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="HIPONATREMIA EUVOL&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiponatremia euvol&#233;mica puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici&#243;n artificial debido a la regulaci&#243;n del agua y sodio.</data>
      <data key="d10">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d11">2c2414e67b64496e8c859cbd072c8f32</data>
      <data key="d12">6819</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="HIPOANTREMIA">
