    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS DE CADENA MEDIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los triglic&#233;ridos de cadena media se recomiendan para pacientes con esteatorrea asociada a enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d11">978451599c3b4caba8db85ce1c513497</data>
      <data key="d12">6988</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="OLESTRA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Olestra se utiliza como sustituto de grasa en productos alimenticios para pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d11">eb78ed1ead76496eab6f0d51c2ede945</data>
      <data key="d12">6989</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="COLLESTERAMINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La colesteramina puede afectar la absorci&#243;n de nutrientes en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d11">ce797087019a4eab9bd1e1ae20e81bd5</data>
      <data key="d12">6990</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="FIBRA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fibra puede afectar la salud intestinal y se recomienda su consumo moderado en pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">609140cabbcd0c7297a7029f5365d186</data>
      <data key="d11">f15e57c094314a31acb1eada5f395c98</data>
      <data key="d12">6991</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions can lead to severe malnutrition in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf</data>
      <data key="d11">b68323b7eaee42809f78fc55b00e2cd6</data>
      <data key="d12">6992</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="PATOLOG&#205;A M&#201;DICA INFECCIOSA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions can cause severe malabsorption and malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf</data>
      <data key="d11">d540dd61e5a1477cbba4c38ecc9a917e</data>
      <data key="d12">6993</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions can lead to malnutrition due to digestive issues</data>
      <data key="d10">298e79737894aa157da136b1996578bf</data>
      <data key="d11">7f53c24dbc444921a41f7d9554fca013</data>
      <data key="d12">6994</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL" target="PACIENTES CON C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer patients may also experience complications related to inflammatory bowel disease, affecting their treatment and quality of life</data>
      <data key="d10">29c2dd6ce196c0166033a861582e9721</data>
      <data key="d11">e5b3cd01bd394663bb2eff12e1897bd0</data>
      <data key="d12">6995</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="TUMOR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;ncer is characterized by the presence of tumors, which can lead to various symptoms including weight loss.</data>
      <data key="d10">b26b998479da515c234ce46b1bfa73db</data>
      <data key="d11">0d1485ea0afd4575b6d5760ff4298219</data>
      <data key="d12">6996</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer and malnutrition are closely interconnected, with malnutrition being a prevalent issue among cancer patients. This condition arises due to various factors associated with the disease, including metabolic changes, treatment side effects, and reduced food intake. Malnutrition not only complicates the treatment and recovery of cancer patients but also significantly impacts patient outcomes and the overall efficacy of cancer therapies. Furthermore, malnutrition can serve as a risk factor in the development of cancer, highlighting the importance of addressing nutritional needs in cancer care to improve patient health and treatment success.</data>
      <data key="d10">24e49b0b93b2307e2c4e7ac34f4d7f4b,5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c,ce62d279f86b3364fed4e121ad2d5e1f</data>
      <data key="d11">f3682e9ab51e4fa4a787df0876884cff</data>
      <data key="d12">6997</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="DHA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Research indicates that DHA may play a role in suppressing cancer development</data>
      <data key="d10">bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d11">2bbef24e542049d685e51407df2e1c2d</data>
      <data key="d12">6998</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="EPA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER and EPA are interconnected in the context of health and nutrition. The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) plays a crucial role in assessing the impact of nutrition on health, particularly concerning diseases such as cancer. Research indicates that EPA may have beneficial effects that could aid in the prevention of cancer, highlighting the importance of understanding the relationship between environmental factors, nutrition, and cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">2ab0f03a87bdf418c83a614b2183332f,bfe7b32b596449644b274ed7486a507a</data>
      <data key="d11">1d2c04e2e0c34f1d8df2424558dc12de</data>
      <data key="d12">6999</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="SONDA DE GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La sonda de gastrostom&#237;a se utiliza en pacientes con c&#225;ncer que tienen dificultades para mantener un estado nutricional adecuado</data>
      <data key="d10">5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833</data>
      <data key="d11">707c7f5583154cf2a57520ac6262a5f4</data>
      <data key="d12">7000</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El tratamiento del c&#225;ncer puede incluir intervenciones que afectan el estado nutricional del paciente</data>
      <data key="d10">5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833</data>
      <data key="d11">28c24eb68a7a44d99ed4875e250ddca1</data>
      <data key="d12">7001</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CAQUEXIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cachexia is a condition frequently associated with cancer, resulting in significant weight loss and malnutrition among affected patients. It is a serious complication that contributes to the overall decline in health and quality of life for individuals suffering from cancer. In Spanish, it is noted that "la caquexia es una condici&#243;n que se presenta en pacientes con c&#225;ncer y contribuye a la malnutrici&#243;n," emphasizing its role in exacerbating malnutrition in these patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">5549895a3a7f54651e6c54f5a5d7d833,ce62d279f86b3364fed4e121ad2d5e1f</data>
      <data key="d11">87767ca5b21042cda1de24920145d1c2</data>
      <data key="d12">7002</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER, classified as a chronic disease, is influenced by various dietary and lifestyle factors. Certain types of cancer fall under the category of chronic diseases and can be significantly affected by an individual's dietary habits. This highlights the importance of nutrition and lifestyle choices in the management and prevention of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074,ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">a11c151fbc86485db3018bb4cec04d8a</data>
      <data key="d12">7003</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="FRUTAS Y VERDURAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de frutas y verduras se ha asociado con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de c&#225;ncer en diversas localizaciones.</data>
      <data key="d10">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d11">0c8a8681475241b4b3d65e5b0f218575</data>
      <data key="d12">7004</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de alcohol ha demostrado ser un factor de riesgo para el desarrollo de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d10">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d11">14c00ae25b254d28aff379a066c91a08</data>
      <data key="d12">7005</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="FIBRA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER and FIBRA are interconnected through the impact of dietary fiber on health outcomes. Research indicates that an increase in fiber intake is associated with a decrease in cardiovascular mortality and may also influence cancer risk. Specifically, high fiber consumption has been linked to a reduced risk of certain types of cancer. This suggests that incorporating more fiber into the diet could be beneficial for both cardiovascular health and cancer prevention.</data>
      <data key="d10">7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3,ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507</data>
      <data key="d11">d881cf8983b84a578a934a49869a22fa</data>
      <data key="d12">7006</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="ACTIVIDAD F&#205;SICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER y ACTIVIDAD F&#205;SICA est&#225;n interrelacionados en el contexto de la salud y el bienestar. La actividad f&#237;sica regular se ha asociado con una reducci&#243;n en el riesgo de varios tipos de c&#225;ncer, lo que sugiere que un estilo de vida activo puede ser un factor protector contra el desarrollo de esta enfermedad. Adem&#225;s, se recomienda aumentar la actividad f&#237;sica en pacientes con c&#225;ncer, ya que esto puede ayudar a mantener la masa muscular y la funcionalidad durante el tratamiento y la recuperaci&#243;n. En conjunto, estas evidencias destacan la importancia de la actividad f&#237;sica tanto en la prevenci&#243;n como en el manejo del c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d10">ca3fd82e042bcc480e80a1ae56b34507,f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af</data>
      <data key="d11">2c53cbe411a946409167299b0e0bdd0e</data>
      <data key="d12">7007</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="VERDURAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de verduras se asocia con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de c&#225;ncer en diversas localizaciones</data>
      <data key="d10">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b</data>
      <data key="d11">1e1adcb0d09f4ff1acbc8e5c3f11c90a</data>
      <data key="d12">7008</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CRUC&#205;FERAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de verduras cruc&#237;feras se ha relacionado con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de ciertos tipos de c&#225;ncer</data>
      <data key="d10">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b</data>
      <data key="d11">152e3ec492e84e8a90f718fed1915144</data>
      <data key="d12">7009</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="DIETA RICA EN FRUTAS Y VERDURAS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Una dieta rica en frutas y verduras se asocia con una reducci&#243;n del riesgo de c&#225;ncer</data>
      <data key="d10">240ded3c69bd7ae82bed4089517ffb6b</data>
      <data key="d11">2643245ab1ae4aad8a420a6681ee4561</data>
      <data key="d12">7010</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CARNE ROJA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de carne roja se asocia con un aumento del riesgo de varios tipos de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">7db2dd628a734e17b834659847cfed42</data>
      <data key="d12">7011</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CARNE PROCESADA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de carne procesada incrementa el riesgo de c&#225;ncer colorrectal y otros tipos de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">3438fe8ef12543b3ab6bc27c69a139f5</data>
      <data key="d12">7012</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="NITRITOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los nitritos en la carne est&#225;n relacionados con un mayor riesgo de c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico y de vejiga.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">2f06fb31eee244a9a7fb5b064c71acd0</data>
      <data key="d12">7013</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER ESOF&#193;GICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer esof&#225;gico es un tipo de c&#225;ncer que se asocia con el consumo de carne roja y procesada.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">845d74b283924d4092a2264dab42acc7</data>
      <data key="d12">7014</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER G&#193;STRICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer g&#225;strico se relaciona con el alto consumo de nitritos de la carne roja o procesada.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">c5b27fd0ce2242b9a191dc4523e2a9a3</data>
      <data key="d12">7015</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER COLORRECTAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer colorrectal se ha vinculado con el consumo de carne roja y procesada, aumentando el riesgo de adenomas.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">c978c126234e4c2d8c454f30939eab39</data>
      <data key="d12">7016</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER HEP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de carne blanca puede reducir el riesgo de c&#225;ncer hep&#225;tico.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">bc02a19bae64401c8e73d223f767582d</data>
      <data key="d12">7017</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de p&#225;ncreas tiene una asociaci&#243;n positiva con el consumo de carne procesada.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">aaeb1c2993bf4e549a5cbd6712d9ddc8</data>
      <data key="d12">7018</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n se ve afectado por el consumo de carne roja y aves de corral.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">23084e03258a4d9ea91d6563c549be7f</data>
      <data key="d12">7019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de mama se relaciona con el consumo de carne roja y procesada, aunque algunos estudios no son concluyentes.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">e2593b1fd19244d2b80f92bd7984598d</data>
      <data key="d12">7020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE OVARIO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de ovario no muestra asociaci&#243;n con el consumo de carne roja o procesada, pero los nitritos parecen incrementar el riesgo.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">2951cc49ae76475c92b6ebb6bd1b14a5</data>
      <data key="d12">7021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE VEJIGA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de vejiga se asocia con el consumo de carne roja y procesada, as&#237; como con los nitritos.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">d5fa93f8011d465598bac3135c1ebb3e</data>
      <data key="d12">7022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de pr&#243;stata ha mostrado una relaci&#243;n d&#233;bilmente positiva con el consumo de carnes procesadas.</data>
      <data key="d10">fa42f07df0762860c72a58c869627aec</data>
      <data key="d11">372bd58a8a8644f193dd122b4a580dcd</data>
      <data key="d12">7023</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="SUPLEMENTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La suplementaci&#243;n con &#225;cidos grasos omega-3 se ha estudiado en relaci&#243;n con varios tipos de c&#225;ncer, mostrando efectos variados en la prevenci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d11">9b501c3581514611a309a5e28e6da641</data>
      <data key="d12">7024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="PERSONAS DE MEDIANA EDAD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las personas de mediana edad pueden experimentar una reducci&#243;n en la mortalidad por ictus y cardiopat&#237;a isqu&#233;mica, lo que sugiere una relaci&#243;n entre la salud cardiovascular y la edad</data>
      <data key="d10">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d11">ab3e473d379d4dbcacb67d86d392a0a0</data>
      <data key="d12">7025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N EN MUJERES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de pulm&#243;n en mujeres puede estar relacionado con la ingesta de &#225;cidos grasos omega-3, sugiriendo un posible beneficio en la prevenci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d11">b45497e1cc3945c484a58f4a67873633</data>
      <data key="d12">7026</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA EN MUJERES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer de mama en mujeres puede ser influenciado por la suplementaci&#243;n con &#225;cidos grasos omega-3, indicando un posible efecto protector</data>
      <data key="d10">5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d11">22645d39830c486fa791d8dd97a6f085</data>
      <data key="d12">7027</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="PRODUCTOS L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dairy products have been associated with a reduced risk of various cancers, including colorectal and breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1</data>
      <data key="d11">63105532207742d4a4f71cf1f4498b44</data>
      <data key="d12">7028</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium from dietary sources, particularly dairy, is inversely associated with digestive cancers.</data>
      <data key="d10">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1</data>
      <data key="d11">41d397d796a04a2685d77ae093af7187</data>
      <data key="d12">7029</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="CASE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Casein has anticancer properties that may help reduce the risk of certain cancers.</data>
      <data key="d10">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1</data>
      <data key="d11">f752601852ce46cdbe904f2be143b5d1</data>
      <data key="d12">7030</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="LACTOFERRINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactoferrin's properties may inhibit cancer cell proliferation, contributing to cancer prevention.</data>
      <data key="d10">a0ef28095dacaada520d8e6fbaf518f1</data>
      <data key="d11">b0789c7ee1cd458d8393564ceb7ddfc7</data>
      <data key="d12">7031</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="AZ&#218;CARES LIBRES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High intake of free sugars may contribute to the risk of developing cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">7ba4c7b49d445c147394ac626d055ef3</data>
      <data key="d11">013afcc7f60543fd8bd863c2af74f065</data>
      <data key="d12">7032</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="VLCD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El c&#225;ncer es una contraindicaci&#243;n para el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">31c01e02f53148ea966c0914f2b08865</data>
      <data key="d12">7033</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta mediterr&#225;nea se asocia con una disminuci&#243;n del riesgo de varios tipos de c&#225;ncer.</data>
      <data key="d10">4e6568999eba5abd852eedecc5fc580f</data>
      <data key="d11">24121bdffddf49a9870ca399a2219e7b</data>
      <data key="d12">7034</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="DIETAS VEGETARIANAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Certain vegetarian diets may be linked to a reduced risk of developing certain types of cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8</data>
      <data key="d11">37c01cf4f0e74d69b2dd53105e345cd8</data>
      <data key="d12">7035</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N RELACIONADA CON EL C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer often leads to malnutrition, requiring targeted nutritional interventions</data>
      <data key="d10">5e934738b2a8cb03468f4ebf4eec0cd2</data>
      <data key="d11">44db36f642e541798a44881800545b6e</data>
      <data key="d12">7036</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="GRUPO ERAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El grupo ERAS proporciona recomendaciones espec&#237;ficas para la recuperaci&#243;n de pacientes con c&#225;ncer, especialmente aquellos con tumores digestivos</data>
      <data key="d10">f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af</data>
      <data key="d11">fbbfbf27911b403bbe01869fefc04fa3</data>
      <data key="d12">7037</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ingesta adecuada de prote&#237;nas es crucial para pacientes con c&#225;ncer para mantener un balance nitrogenado positivo</data>
      <data key="d10">f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af</data>
      <data key="d11">6cddde476efe4593b10974796ca6fdbb</data>
      <data key="d12">7038</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="MICRONUTRIENTES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los micronutrientes son necesarios en la dieta de pacientes con c&#225;ncer y su ingesta debe ser controlada</data>
      <data key="d10">f7871bbaa57d50bb5f5675cd580cb0af</data>
      <data key="d11">86f60d0c51704c7da01a2da0d7fdb2d8</data>
      <data key="d12">7039</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="INMUNONUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La inmunonutrici&#243;n enteral se utiliza para tratar a pacientes con c&#225;ncer, mejorando su respuesta inmune y recuperaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">95ec74fd93c18ac23c08eb70137bc8db</data>
      <data key="d11">228c8f21b7b04c8a8bc1abca3cde06c6</data>
      <data key="d12">7040</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="NUPAC">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The NUPAC study investigates the nutritional status of cancer patients, providing insights into the prevalence of malnutrition in this group.</data>
      <data key="d10">ce62d279f86b3364fed4e121ad2d5e1f</data>
      <data key="d11">aec96bb2c1c44d34be511ee946216872</data>
      <data key="d12">7041</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="PACIENTE NEOPL&#193;SICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El paciente neopl&#225;sico es quien padece c&#225;ncer y requiere tratamientos que afectan su nutrici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">9c3716c3860855ce045a1e5d9d30b9d1</data>
      <data key="d11">1ac59ecb687241228f97036bd60c6d5a</data>
      <data key="d12">7042</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER refers to a group of diseases characterized by the uncontrolled growth and spread of abnormal cells. PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS are individuals diagnosed with C&#193;NCER and require specific nutritional attention to support their health and treatment. These patients often face unique challenges related to their condition, necessitating tailored nutritional care to enhance their overall well-being during their cancer journey.</data>
      <data key="d10">5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732,a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c</data>
      <data key="d11">a16de1d8770d49f8b6761bb010cd72e1</data>
      <data key="d12">7043</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER" target="RETICS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The cancer thematic network is one of the specific research areas under the RETICS initiative.</data>
      <data key="d10">5173ac9bd92d5f238acade41f8c65ebf</data>
      <data key="d11">583d8db410374fbba0d29a92f8e1e525</data>
      <data key="d12">7044</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUEMADOS" target="DIETA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with burns require a hospital diet that meets their increased nutritional needs</data>
      <data key="d10">c6406ac5c0c7b03d4ee61ca311fd783f</data>
      <data key="d11">7a8727faf1994139ab9129fe75c56672</data>
      <data key="d12">7045</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUEMADOS" target="FACTOR DE MULTIPLICACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The multiplication factor for burn victims is used to adjust energy expenditure</data>
      <data key="d10">8d7280a9f9085fe677f5993b12910ea2</data>
      <data key="d11">1251745ea0bc444d8874ba85e9f9eaaf</data>
      <data key="d12">7046</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El soporte nutricional es fundamental para los pacientes que se someten a un trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas para asegurar una recuperaci&#243;n adecuada</data>
      <data key="d10">af40d7a664dbfc9c14307a26f52b9bff</data>
      <data key="d11">6c678b0d6a384613880b693738a94ad0</data>
      <data key="d12">7047</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="ENFERMEDAD DE INJERTO CONTRA HU&#201;SPED">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La EICH es una complicaci&#243;n que puede surgir espec&#237;ficamente del trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas, afectando la salud del receptor.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972</data>
      <data key="d11">465ce0f67bb24f399724298ff15f7722</data>
      <data key="d12">7048</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="EICH AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La EICH aguda ocurre como una complicaci&#243;n del trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas, afectando la salud del paciente en las primeras semanas.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972</data>
      <data key="d11">ae564c1b8e434e22b91b7f412b49ab85</data>
      <data key="d12">7049</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="EICH CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La EICH cr&#243;nica tambi&#233;n se relaciona con el trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas, pero se presenta mucho despu&#233;s del procedimiento.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972</data>
      <data key="d11">5a1d8b1fdaa14b598994b12f0b345742</data>
      <data key="d12">7050</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="ENFERMEDAD VENOCLUSIVA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas puede dar lugar a diversas complicaciones, entre las cuales se encuentra la enfermedad venoclusiva hep&#225;tica. Esta condici&#243;n afecta la funci&#243;n hep&#225;tica y puede surgir como una complicaci&#243;n postoperatoria tras el procedimiento de trasplante.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b26dc0fdf0ff94c225f96626b785972,84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">a23354367b85453eb6b8a34a4e2f8668</data>
      <data key="d12">7051</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="CORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los corticoides pueden afectar el metabolismo de los carbohidratos en pacientes que han recibido un trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas</data>
      <data key="d10">84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">1e30105312bb4f789882753ea32d20dc</data>
      <data key="d12">7052</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="CICLOSPORINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ciclosporina es utilizada en el tratamiento de complicaciones postrasplante, afectando el metabolismo lip&#237;dico</data>
      <data key="d10">84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">88b9a35293974ce4abe2b4b72dc69c32</data>
      <data key="d12">7053</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="EICH">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La EICH es una complicaci&#243;n que puede ocurrir en pacientes que han recibido un trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas</data>
      <data key="d10">84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">d12c033921df425bb9b36c038c7939be</data>
      <data key="d12">7054</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPOY&#201;TICAS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A focuses on the nutritional management of patients undergoing the trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas</data>
      <data key="d10">08d8220e35364eb95bacafae7dd2953b</data>
      <data key="d11">e16d2410697c4305b20938ecaee85b9c</data>
      <data key="d12">7055</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="CFRD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CFRD is a common complication that arises in patients with Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica, affecting their overall health and management</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">044eab39ff064ebcbd513e8b6b46fbc5</data>
      <data key="d12">7056</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="K. GARC&#205;A MALPARTIDA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">K. Garc&#237;a Malpartida is an author discussing the implications of Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica on nutrition and diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">f1a5d74e7ab64fec9c6d8b23002475a6</data>
      <data key="d12">7057</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="A. RAMOS PROL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A. Ramos Prol contributes to the discussion on the nutritional aspects of managing Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">d0dc6feb1025492498c472bf86ccd0c3</data>
      <data key="d12">7058</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="M. ARGENTE PLA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M. Argente Pla is involved in the analysis of nutritional management in patients with Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">384b74029194491dbf79ab1ae220c7c3</data>
      <data key="d12">7059</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="TRATAMIENTO ENZIM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enzymatic treatment is relevant in the context of managing nutritional needs in patients with Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">933fb36687d94342be124dd2a9cede3d</data>
      <data key="d12">7060</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="ANTIBI&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Antibiotics are often prescribed to cystic fibrosis patients during respiratory infections, impacting their overall health and nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">8247f93b1c8a431fbba4f44a51e1c97e</data>
      <data key="d12">7061</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="VITAMINA E">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with cystic fibrosis may experience malabsorption of vitamin E, affecting their health.</data>
      <data key="d10">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d11">59c42e1f6b004810ba160fb99e077995</data>
      <data key="d12">7062</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="VITAMINA A">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis (Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica) can lead to malabsorption of vitamin A, which may result in deficiencies of this essential nutrient. To address this issue, vitamin A supplementation is considered an important aspect of the management of cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4</data>
      <data key="d11">841e8d58f198428f9193fc7a4e9ee600</data>
      <data key="d12">7063</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIABETES NEONATAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis, known as "fibrosis qu&#237;stica" in Spanish, can result in diabetes due to damage to the pancreas. This pancreatic damage may lead to the development of neonatal diabetes in some cases. The conditions associated with cystic fibrosis can overlap with those of neonatal diabetes, indicating a connection between the two entities.</data>
      <data key="d10">ac89fcaa7dcce835c0d5b9ed9ce94cea,b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b</data>
      <data key="d11">1bbae0b0231445fdb24aae72d3ba569f</data>
      <data key="d12">7064</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with cystic fibrosis may require insulin therapy due to diabetes resulting from pancreatic damage</data>
      <data key="d10">ac89fcaa7dcce835c0d5b9ed9ce94cea</data>
      <data key="d11">700200b20ef149e08e55ba3c787d6dd7</data>
      <data key="d12">7065</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="HEMOCROMATOSIS HEREDITARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions are related to diabetes and have significant implications for patient management</data>
      <data key="d10">4885c129837f58f091d24d2cbc8aae66</data>
      <data key="d11">18abc98fad234bb7b7b967c040c3954f</data>
      <data key="d12">7066</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="F508DEL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has been diagnosed with cystic fibrosis due to the F508del mutation</data>
      <data key="d10">84e91b50850bfa0ad0122cdebf477a1d</data>
      <data key="d11">04b8cbf68e024c539f542f3b56679de6</data>
      <data key="d12">7067</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="CFTR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis is caused by mutations in the CFTR gene, which is crucial for the disease's pathology.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">3d7fc3dc9bd44744ab3304bb8f331831</data>
      <data key="d12">7068</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes related to cystic fibrosis is a common complication arising from the disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">f57f8160f4c94b8c87506eaddb92470f</data>
      <data key="d12">7069</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA EXOCRINA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis (FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA) is a genetic disorder that often leads to various complications, one of which is exocrine pancreatic insufficiency (INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA EXOCRINA). This condition is prevalent among patients with cystic fibrosis and significantly impacts their digestive processes. Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency arises as a complication of cystic fibrosis, affecting the pancreas and hindering its ability to produce the necessary enzymes for proper digestion.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab,ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d11">5bfb0a56136c485d81e22f13a9c88bb6</data>
      <data key="d12">7070</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE&#193;TICA ENDOCRINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Endocrine pancreatic insufficiency is another complication of cystic fibrosis that can lead to diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">6e36c343a4bd45ca923a2e18d3804329</data>
      <data key="d12">7071</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="EUROPA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis has a specific incidence and prevalence in Europe, highlighting its impact in the region.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">dbc597803b2946d9907aa9097d721dc1</data>
      <data key="d12">7072</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="MUTACI&#211;N F508DEL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The F508del mutation is the most frequent mutation associated with cystic fibrosis, affecting its clinical expression.</data>
      <data key="d10">7f4fe49df6d472c0b2e39db535bd01ab</data>
      <data key="d11">8577a14f2729489d93578c5c20e1dcf4</data>
      <data key="d12">7073</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DRFQ">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Desnutrici&#243;n relacionada con la fibrosis qu&#237;stica is a complication that affects the prognosis of patients with cystic fibrosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">3f295222427803a7fc92b83386e5ec56</data>
      <data key="d11">f7896248714b42189993e1809a05bc97</data>
      <data key="d12">7074</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="MEMBREZ">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Membrez's research includes the effects of antibiotics on weight gain in patients with fibrosis qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">15ac197b57d904b3bf72905c4d946c0d</data>
      <data key="d11">f263237e02774e8b940b0fe5690b5d63</data>
      <data key="d12">7075</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="PANCREATITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis is a common cause of chronic pancreatitis in children, establishing a relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">803363886f385b089938bf122246dfa2</data>
      <data key="d11">b05a070b1fb74d0ca64a15437871c119</data>
      <data key="d12">7076</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="PANCREATITIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis can lead to pancreatitis and associated nutritional issues</data>
      <data key="d10">32642463df83d3626d7a9c5acf121825</data>
      <data key="d11">a8c3c819ec77484b86fc83704e4c3257</data>
      <data key="d12">7077</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="HOSPITAL REGIONAL UNIVERSITARIO DE M&#193;LAGA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Hospital Regional Universitario de M&#225;laga provides treatment and management for patients with fibrosis qu&#237;stica.</data>
      <data key="d10">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d11">92d25f710ba0437384d1a00dfb22d71e</data>
      <data key="d12">7078</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dietoterapia is an important aspect of managing patients with fibrosis qu&#237;stica to ensure proper nutrition and health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d11">bb95127cfc944799937872e6881c66f8</data>
      <data key="d12">7079</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR OBSTRUCTIVA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fibrosis qu&#237;stica can lead to complications such as enfermedad pulmonar obstructiva cr&#243;nica due to chronic lung infections and inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d10">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d11">ba23568c37f7474f98e09ab02f9356bb</data>
      <data key="d12">7080</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="BRONQUIECTASIAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bronquiectasias can occur as a complication of fibrosis qu&#237;stica, resulting from chronic lung damage and infection.</data>
      <data key="d10">0bf272be187cbf9ec33184c8052e19c6</data>
      <data key="d11">57116e4b2a27498e93e71c9cc3914f60</data>
      <data key="d12">7081</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="MUTATION CLASSIFICATION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutation classification is relevant to understanding genetic disorders like cystic fibrosis, which can affect lung health</data>
      <data key="d10">6dd2bf3e3132697b855c16e624c56ed0</data>
      <data key="d11">4908834261da4fe49dd488b1fdd03a7f</data>
      <data key="d12">7082</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic Fibrosis (Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica) and Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (EPOC) are both pulmonary diseases that present significant respiratory and nutritional challenges. Cystic Fibrosis can lead to respiratory complications that may manifest as EPOC in some patients, highlighting the interconnected nature of these two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">7db0f975ca8148e68d225474c41766ca</data>
      <data key="d12">7083</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="CIRROSIS BILIAR FOCAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Focal biliary cirrhosis can develop as a liver complication in patients suffering from cystic fibrosis</data>
      <data key="d10">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d11">241da0b35dda4d54ba4ab6fd82fafffc</data>
      <data key="d12">7084</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="ESTEATOSIS HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatic steatosis is often associated with cystic fibrosis, particularly in cases of severe malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d11">24bb8efa337645699dcf8c36c7ac918b</data>
      <data key="d12">7085</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="S&#205;NDROME DE OBSTRUCCI&#211;N INTESTINAL DISTAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fibrosis qu&#237;stica, also known as cystic fibrosis, is a genetic disorder that affects various organs, particularly the lungs and digestive system. One of the complications associated with this condition is the s&#237;ndrome de obstrucci&#243;n intestinal distal, which frequently occurs in patients with fibrosis qu&#237;stica. This syndrome is characterized by the obstruction of the intestines, often resulting from thickened intestinal contents that are a consequence of the underlying cystic fibrosis. Thus, there is a clear link between fibrosis qu&#237;stica and s&#237;ndrome de obstrucci&#243;n intestinal distal, as the latter is a common complication arising from the former.</data>
      <data key="d10">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d11">f8b42c3de859474b88c09d561248203a</data>
      <data key="d12">7086</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="DIABETES RELACIONADA CON LA FQ">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis is associated with an increased prevalence of diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d11">7e030611f0c54e4f89b46c9a07b8f60f</data>
      <data key="d12">7087</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="ALTERACIONES DEL METABOLISMO HIDROCARBONADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cystic fibrosis leads to alterations in carbohydrate metabolism, affecting patients' health</data>
      <data key="d10">ad6c1f4ea2a6b80d32100cf5c2808cdc</data>
      <data key="d11">d2bde011d6b247a3a16020b9dbf14633</data>
      <data key="d12">7088</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="S&#205;NDROME DE DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Malnutrition syndrome is often observed in patients with cystic fibrosis due to the disease's impact on nutrient absorption</data>
      <data key="d10">b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d11">a2315e71a0c8477e9723aca8cce88d89</data>
      <data key="d12">7089</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS QU&#205;STICA" target="ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alfa-1-antitripsina deficiency is a known cause of complications in patients with fibrosis qu&#237;stica, linking the protein to the event</data>
      <data key="d10">d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d11">b7cf568a4d4f443dabcf12b633eae651</data>
      <data key="d12">7090</data>
