    <edge source="MNA" target="NRS 2002">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA and NRS 2002 are both tools utilized for assessing the nutritional status of individuals, with a particular focus on the elderly population. While MNA is a widely recognized method for this purpose, NRS 2002 serves as an alternative screening tool that is recommended for use when MNA is not applicable. Together, these tools provide valuable resources for healthcare professionals in evaluating and addressing the nutritional needs of older adults.</data>
      <data key="d10">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
      <data key="d11">5e2cec1a96304a9cb1c5cc19983ba7ac</data>
      <data key="d12">7196</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA is particularly relevant for assessing the nutritional status of frail elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4</data>
      <data key="d11">b1a31cf1504a4ab8bdb273562835444b</data>
      <data key="d12">7197</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="TABLA 1">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Table 1 provides the criteria and scoring for the MNA tool</data>
      <data key="d10">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4</data>
      <data key="d11">b9711a440ab346a6bdda85b1eedbcf95</data>
      <data key="d12">7198</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="MORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA can be used to predict mortality rates in elderly patients based on their nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4</data>
      <data key="d11">eb68576f686b461a8117e5d9627e0c96</data>
      <data key="d12">7199</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="COMPLICACIONES">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA does not provide evidence for predicting complications in patients</data>
