      <data key="d10">8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d11">e28fb813532247e0b7a2714ef07636ce</data>
      <data key="d12">7202</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="MNA-SF">
      <data key="d8">35.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA and MNA-SF are both tools used for nutritional assessment, particularly in the elderly population. MNA-SF, which stands for Mini Nutritional Assessment - Short Form, is a shortened and simplified version of the original MNA. It is specifically designed to streamline the assessment process while maintaining its effectiveness in evaluating nutritional status. Both MNA and MNA-SF serve similar purposes in assessing nutritional needs, with MNA-SF allowing for quicker assessments without compromising the quality of the evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04,e596bbb9231cc72bade554b3d67804b8,ef8194ca70c613876b927087bf7554f5</data>
      <data key="d11">47fa6c3a06bf4625bd852217e3ab5c13</data>
      <data key="d12">7203</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="NUFFE">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA and NUFFE are both tools specifically designed for assessing the nutritional status and evaluating the nutritional needs of elderly patients. These tools aim to ensure that the dietary requirements of older individuals are adequately met, promoting better health and well-being in this demographic.</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d11">d207324f15ce4ebfa2f37e6402169fdf</data>
      <data key="d12">7204</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MNA" target="NUTRICION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MNA is a tool used in the nutritional assessment of frail elderly patients</data>
