      <data key="d12">7332</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MARCADORES NUTRICIONALES" target="BALANCE NITROGENADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Balance Nitrogenado se relaciona con la evaluaci&#243;n del estado nutricional y el metabolismo proteico</data>
      <data key="d10">c69834419bc4c69bcafd7a81ed8535d4</data>
      <data key="d11">dce9a872aea14f9782d8fe457c1d7e56</data>
      <data key="d12">7333</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="SOLUCIONES DE FLUIDOS INTRAVENOSOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is a key component in intravenous fluid solutions used for patient hydration and energy</data>
      <data key="d10">056067ecde43f31b356fc39e056221ee</data>
      <data key="d11">58640ae7d6994239a9f24f5b691fb3a6</data>
      <data key="d12">7334</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="PACIENTE S&#201;PTICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glucosa es un componente clave en la nutrici&#243;n de pacientes s&#233;pticos para evitar la degradaci&#243;n de otros sustratos</data>
      <data key="d10">422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">440d73ed2ff64d0da55a21eac1760a7e</data>
      <data key="d12">7335</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="CFRD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Monitoring glucose levels is crucial for managing Cystic Fibrosis Related Diabetes (CFRD)</data>
      <data key="d10">00de48c582cca92f1a59df5fceb07bfb</data>
      <data key="d11">5a6c3396544c422ab5fca1ce7dcf7a65</data>
      <data key="d12">7336</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="SOLUTION FORMULATIONS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is a key ingredient in solution formulations, providing energy and caloric content</data>
      <data key="d10">622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817</data>
      <data key="d11">40ddb123c0e54f0794feb7b89270be7e</data>
      <data key="d12">7337</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="AMINOVEN INFANT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aminoven Infant and glucose are both critical components of nutritional support for infants, particularly in managing energy needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
      <data key="d11">3f9d929fdb134454a268a386750642a0</data>
      <data key="d12">7338</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="RNPT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is particularly important for RNPT to prevent hypoglycemia due to their high energy needs and low fat reserves.</data>
      <data key="d10">e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
      <data key="d11">6dd6341ba80646f8b2a7458af1cf808e</data>
      <data key="d12">7339</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="RNT">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose requirements differ between RNPT and RNT, highlighting the need for tailored nutritional strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
      <data key="d11">c4beb3fd52404d30a545631ae4d1a9bf</data>
      <data key="d12">7340</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="RN PRET&#201;RMINO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">RN Pret&#233;rmino infants require specific glucose intake to prevent hypoglycemia due to their high energy needs and low fat reserves.</data>
      <data key="d10">e41a9b2827462263a11ef60ce74c160b</data>
      <data key="d11">8bc5551fd17d48b387bf2796872b366f</data>
      <data key="d12">7341</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GLUT2">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GLUCOSA and GLUT2 are closely related entities in the context of glucose metabolism. GLUT2 is a transporter that facilitates the entry of glucose into cells, which is essential for energy production. Additionally, glucosa, or glucose, is absorbed through the GLUT2 transporter in the intestines, highlighting the critical role of GLUT2 in both the absorption of glucose from the diet and its subsequent utilization by cells for energy.</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,9baa05f21f51764ac1d0537294bdc7db</data>
      <data key="d11">f736f63236514ff58f49eadf684ed156</data>
      <data key="d12">7342</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="KREBS CYCLE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is metabolized through glycolysis to produce pyruvate, which enters the Krebs cycle for further energy production</data>
      <data key="d10">9baa05f21f51764ac1d0537294bdc7db</data>
      <data key="d11">9a8b24f7330441b0a43596898872ce41</data>
      <data key="d12">7343</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GLUCOSA and HIPOGLUCEMIA are closely related in the context of metabolic health. Glucose is a critical treatment for hypoglycemia, particularly in patients suffering from metabolic disorders such as fructosa-1,6-bifosfatas deficiency. Hypoglycemia is characterized by low glucose levels, which are the primary cause of this condition, making immediate intervention essential to restore normal glucose levels and prevent further complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51,8bcf09481326ab5017cc3b45317538a3</data>
      <data key="d11">bee53f22394b4588b9bda76318ba2861</data>
      <data key="d12">7344</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="FETO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El feto utiliza la glucosa como su principal fuente de energ&#237;a durante el embarazo</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d11">45187776b4404165ad018fa848fa821b</data>
      <data key="d12">7345</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="DRFQ">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is used in oral overload tests to diagnose and manage DRFQ</data>
      <data key="d10">dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
      <data key="d11">64f945a1ac9a49df9e06612c15b184dc</data>
      <data key="d12">7346</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GALLETA MARIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galleta Maria contains Glucosa, which adds sweetness and energy to the product</data>
      <data key="d10">0a0bea4b9792f715e9d625450c4cd25c</data>
      <data key="d11">a302baa3203f4e88bf929dba250352bc</data>
      <data key="d12">7347</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="DIETAS BAJAS EN HIDRATOS DE CARBONO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Low-carbohydrate diets aim to lower glucose levels in the body by reducing carbohydrate intake</data>
      <data key="d10">880102f905a34cd6b5e2638ce7bad162</data>
      <data key="d11">fe28a1a7251243be9ea38ded0bca9824</data>
      <data key="d12">7348</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GLUC&#211;GENO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glucosa es el precursor del gluc&#243;geno, que se forma a partir de ella durante la glucogenog&#233;nesis</data>
      <data key="d10">439efa4d64a3de0b12975ea727c939f4</data>
      <data key="d11">d02bddcb4624432a843a7d437cabf6aa</data>
      <data key="d12">7349</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa-6-fosfatasa converts glucose-6-phosphate into glucosa, allowing it to enter the bloodstream</data>
      <data key="d10">f0bfe278aa9f43f4bc9d056de67a5b96</data>
      <data key="d11">124c0831badd40a08f8b3f45af872703</data>
      <data key="d12">7350</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="TORRENTE SANGU&#205;NEO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is transported through the torrente sangu&#237;neo to provide energy to cells</data>
      <data key="d10">f0bfe278aa9f43f4bc9d056de67a5b96</data>
      <data key="d11">343ef24ab62443ca9447c14788386ac5</data>
      <data key="d12">7351</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GLUCOGEN&#211;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gluconeogenesis produces glucosa from non-carbohydrate sources, contributing to blood glucose levels</data>
      <data key="d10">f0bfe278aa9f43f4bc9d056de67a5b96</data>
      <data key="d11">e8558f1bcb49426bbfad4fca1cd8d9d0</data>
      <data key="d12">7352</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GSDI">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose management is critical for individuals with GSDI to prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e</data>
      <data key="d11">4f31bf6dd559421fb5c18a6135c0369c</data>
      <data key="d12">7353</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose is converted into glucose through the Leloir pathway, which is essential for carbohydrate metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">db2574c60b9a4642b854f8830b577e11</data>
      <data key="d12">7354</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="GLUCOPROTE&#205;NAS Y GLUCOL&#205;PIDOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is a building block for glycoproteins and glycolipids, establishing a biochemical relationship between them.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">a2c2080d7d6b47a9b265e4934761da54</data>
      <data key="d12">7355</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="LACTASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactase converts lactose into glucose, which is a primary energy source for the body, establishing a strong relationship.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">d0bb85bb57184cc28d57d7418dc63fc3</data>
      <data key="d12">7356</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="HIGADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is metabolized in the liver after being absorbed into the bloodstream</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d11">3856b87824414521af508cfba0de6f72</data>
      <data key="d12">7357</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="MALTOSA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GLUCOSA and MALTOSA are closely related entities in the context of carbohydrate chemistry. MALTOSA, a disaccharide, is composed of two glucose units. It undergoes hydrolysis, a chemical process that breaks it down into its constituent monosaccharides, specifically glucosa (glucose), through the action of the enzyme maltase. Thus, maltosa is effectively converted into glucosa, highlighting the direct biochemical relationship between these two entities.</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">db37a471a1df4b788cf0e2a968d7562f</data>
      <data key="d12">7358</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="ISOMALTOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Isomaltosa is also broken down into glucose during digestion</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d11">4dc9608b5e724f3bb6a12c716063faef</data>
      <data key="d12">7359</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="SGLT1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is absorbed in the intestines through the SGLT1 transporter</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d11">dce5b05ac9904349bfc3acddde72c389</data>
      <data key="d12">7360</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL NOCTURNA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional therapy often involves the administration of glucose to support patients</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d11">f57f470ebe6c4dec8f7c6875ced968e1</data>
      <data key="d12">7361</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="VENA PORTA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose absorbed in the intestines enters the bloodstream and is transported to the liver via the portal vein</data>
      <data key="d10">638e8fa7af82ec833d23c7df72ee9b1f</data>
      <data key="d11">b957488c1c0249efbaa388fc1b0347b4</data>
      <data key="d12">7362</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="MALTODEXTRINAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Maltodextrinas are hydrolyzed to produce glucosa, which is then absorbed</data>
      <data key="d10">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">2f7d8d1dc93f42728fc0c4b91ac94933</data>
      <data key="d12">7363</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="CITOPLASMA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucosa is utilized in the citoplasma for energy production</data>
      <data key="d10">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">6a975c0b4cbf4667904bb20f19cd1840</data>
      <data key="d12">7364</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="MALABSORCI&#211;N DE FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The transformation of glucosa into fructosa in food products can contribute to malabsorci&#243;n de fructosa</data>
      <data key="d10">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e</data>
      <data key="d11">bfeab4ffcf46443583b690e333a5135d</data>
      <data key="d12">7365</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="FRUCTANOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is well absorbed and can be consumed without symptoms, contrasting with the malabsorption of fructans</data>
      <data key="d10">79168ac744819ae83bdd5ad50140fead</data>
      <data key="d11">8a664b06977c4ad995c4ec5e53927300</data>
      <data key="d12">7366</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin regulates glucose levels in the body, making it essential for managing blood sugar during and after surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae</data>
      <data key="d11">36f0dc231b4e46daad306f819f41388d</data>
      <data key="d12">7367</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="HIDRATOS DE CARBONO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbohydrates are broken down into glucose, which is critical for energy metabolism, especially in the context of surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">d42b833940d845abc98aa8e8ea05d6ae</data>
      <data key="d11">bfcab3cc0afe46cda7e99e8c775a4858</data>
      <data key="d12">7368</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose administration is critical in managing the nutritional needs of critically ill patients to prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">01704aec4089b2f0f24dd0f0841b5ecf</data>
      <data key="d11">1f4a1af4effb45e08206930435a2df10</data>
      <data key="d12">7369</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="PACIENTES QUEMADOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La administraci&#243;n de glucosa debe ser controlada en pacientes quemados para evitar complicaciones</data>
      <data key="d10">111edb0e21c873322871e35619a1ebf5</data>
      <data key="d11">f2f4ef31fd1c475e859fc8e324e9c749</data>
      <data key="d12">7370</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="PACIENTES CON C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is a critical energy source for cancer patients, potentially affecting their treatment outcomes</data>
      <data key="d10">202e4fa915a698c9d9164c3fcc61534e</data>
      <data key="d11">d5634920c3bd4ea1a3e7e68af07ade01</data>
      <data key="d12">7371</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fructosa y la glucosa son az&#250;cares que se absorben en el intestino, y la presencia de fructosa puede interferir con la absorci&#243;n de glucosa</data>
      <data key="d10">7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f</data>
      <data key="d11">7d68f1fba59a4d2ba3688c7fcc8013b3</data>
      <data key="d12">7372</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="RADIOTRAZADOR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glucosa puede interferir con la captaci&#243;n del radiotrazador durante las pruebas m&#233;dicas</data>
      <data key="d10">e82ce4aa73097ca70936be74cdafc12b</data>
      <data key="d11">42896dab753a475c9343f5db67c17317</data>
      <data key="d12">7373</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="M&#218;SCULOS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glucosa es utilizada por los m&#250;sculos como fuente de energ&#237;a durante el ejercicio prolongado</data>
      <data key="d10">490f5e3c6dbf3754eee50c52154da09a</data>
      <data key="d11">a6dfdb50c75b4d6a9dea0400a20bcfa6</data>
      <data key="d12">7374</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucose is essential in pediatric nutrition for energy provision and managing dietary needs</data>
      <data key="d10">507eeea555c496a467930836fc4c1a39</data>
      <data key="d11">9e3e6ebc15e44eba9e8eb03a690c2ea5</data>
      <data key="d12">7375</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOSA" target="D-GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">D-glucosa is a form of glucose used in medical nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">507eeea555c496a467930836fc4c1a39</data>
      <data key="d11">34a647d501d04346800ddcf48e00ee2e</data>
      <data key="d12">7376</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="PACIENTE S&#201;PTICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los l&#237;pidos son esenciales en la nutrici&#243;n de pacientes s&#233;pticos, proporcionando energ&#237;a y evitando d&#233;ficits</data>
      <data key="d10">422dbd193843eb5098307e57ba002ced</data>
      <data key="d11">7b1f65c00afa4bd5a9784bd576476c9f</data>
      <data key="d12">7377</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="PACIENTE ANCIANO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los l&#237;pidos en la dieta del paciente anciano deben ser controlados para asegurar un aporte saludable de energ&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d10">2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9</data>
      <data key="d11">85c6dfdb53fd47c2941eee83043dbf0c</data>
      <data key="d12">7378</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="CALORIC COMPONENTS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are included as caloric components in dietary formulations for energy</data>
      <data key="d10">622b4827c8894dba02debfade4a9f817</data>
      <data key="d11">e1733974532b45dea7a395b98fc8fac8</data>
      <data key="d12">7379</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are essential for health, and potassium helps control blood pressure, which is related to cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">8e8bb558f66f4e1284a7cf62703aaf53</data>
      <data key="d12">7380</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos play a role in health, and magnesium is studied for its effects on blood pressure regulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">7e004a03e3024b3f8471bb03362df7b9</data>
      <data key="d12">7381</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are important for health, and calcium's role in cardiovascular prevention is a topic of discussion.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">4ecd6169569441239c0b632061f18b8a</data>
      <data key="d12">7382</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="VITAMINA E">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are essential nutrients, and vitamin E is an antioxidant that protects cells, linking them to cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">849df3e7ff1d48e0b8c3eafab0791038</data>
      <data key="d12">7383</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="CAROTENOS">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are important for health, and carotenoids have antioxidant properties that may influence health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">03ddc27141f64cc5bdeed24b2505aa69</data>
      <data key="d12">7384</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="VITAMINA C">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are essential nutrients, and vitamin C is known for its antioxidant properties, linking them to health benefits.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">f649db04243941eba6909267784d4cec</data>
      <data key="d12">7385</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="AJO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are essential nutrients, and garlic has health benefits that may influence lipid metabolism, linking them.</data>
      <data key="d10">eff56271e184ab2f11877bfab7f715c4</data>
      <data key="d11">b2450d253dbd4b8399c7802412243ae4</data>
      <data key="d12">7386</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El an&#225;lisis de l&#237;pidos es fundamental para confirmar el diagn&#243;stico de quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">06bccb5505ad4c468bb7132b45909865</data>
      <data key="d12">7387</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos are a primary source of calories in the ketogenic diet, making up a significant portion of its macronutrient composition</data>
      <data key="d10">0ebd0c517a3d578a6823dc39797e4da1</data>
      <data key="d11">9264c8060dcd4da8887a42d8026a5ff6</data>
      <data key="d12">7388</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="INTESTINO DELGADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El intestino delgado es el lugar donde se absorben los l&#237;pidos en el sistema digestivo.</data>
      <data key="d10">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9</data>
      <data key="d11">f8e7f94b74f14431ac811ee3c83372ff</data>
      <data key="d12">7389</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="EJERCICIO F&#205;SICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">During physical exercise, particularly in endurance activities, lipids serve as a crucial energy source. This is especially evident during prolonged physical exercise when the intensity decreases, leading to an increased reliance on lipids for energy.</data>
      <data key="d10">39da0855b83941d97766254aa36ed2fd,638446780cdd61df83a06944c4e15c15</data>
      <data key="d11">724bd9b9b6b34b378926d3085acd78f0</data>
      <data key="d12">7390</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="DEPORTISTA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Athletes need to manage their lipid intake to ensure they have adequate energy sources without compromising performance.</data>
      <data key="d10">39da0855b83941d97766254aa36ed2fd</data>
      <data key="d11">d69a4919b89e471091f59622f890e56f</data>
      <data key="d12">7391</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L&#205;PIDOS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L&#237;pidos play a crucial role in NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA, as they are included in pediatric nutrition to enhance energy density and supply essential fatty acids. The emphasis on l&#237;pidos in the diet is vital for ensuring proper growth and development in children, highlighting their importance in a balanced nutritional approach for young individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">507eeea555c496a467930836fc4c1a39,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5</data>
      <data key="d11">b6b9af8e44cd4c92a059d57671f9d175</data>
      <data key="d12">7392</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="SURGICAL PATIENT">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumina levels are used to evaluate the nutritional status of surgical patients</data>
      <data key="d10">d23c564df025cf16e37f2ef2be83ec34</data>
      <data key="d11">2a4d405a2e7e41f6a1767bee2ab0bcae</data>
      <data key="d12">7393</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="NUTRICION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alb&#250;mina is a biochemical parameter used to assess the nutritional status of patients</data>
      <data key="d10">6458fe5a14762d5f8c1561f80acb844a</data>
      <data key="d11">1960c69a91174cca875409d950abed68</data>
      <data key="d12">7394</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="MAASTRICHT INDEX">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumin is one of the parameters used in the Maastricht Index for nutritional assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">0597a142067272f25431b8b42cb5288f</data>
      <data key="d11">28548b3c3ee34c338d05e2adab161e45</data>
      <data key="d12">7395</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Variations in albumina levels can affect calcium concentration, which is relevant in glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis</data>
      <data key="d10">9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d11">cd4098b751ef42d18bcb63e3d8bfee76</data>
      <data key="d12">7396</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="LAPAROTOM&#205;A EXPLORADORA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumin levels were monitored as part of the evaluation leading to the exploratory laparotomy</data>
      <data key="d10">cba5d81f1acff7cbf84e85ef35420521</data>
      <data key="d11">8995323813da4ec8a29aabc1f5e71829</data>
      <data key="d12">7397</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles bajos de alb&#250;mina son un indicador de malnutrici&#243;n en pacientes con insuficiencia renal cr&#243;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">61564a330848cb173088bd08e1a9a181</data>
      <data key="d11">b57f8a7efbe743ec965edc94a92fb3dc</data>
      <data key="d12">7398</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="DOPPS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DOPPS confirms the prognostic value of albumin levels in assessing the risk of mortality in dialysis patients</data>
      <data key="d10">541c13a95526e4d68903f0901042f292</data>
      <data key="d11">6bcd746a8e22491bba9bfdde87343bcd</data>
      <data key="d12">7399</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="S&#205;NDROME NEFR&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumina levels are critical in diagnosing and managing s&#237;ndrome nefr&#243;tico, as low levels indicate kidney dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d10">d1e7cd9fdc3093bc5902030d654d0763</data>
      <data key="d11">687b69b2b02d49cd9d38b0e11344f242</data>
      <data key="d12">7400</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="SISTEMA LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La alb&#250;mina se encuentra en el quilo y es transportada a trav&#233;s del sistema linf&#225;tico.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7</data>
      <data key="d11">5b146592e6f243bb8a81b2702487f145</data>
      <data key="d12">7401</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Low levels of albumin can contribute to the development of quilot&#243;rax due to its role in maintaining fluid balance in the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">1e3832db97fc4bc19c4d95ebb35f8839</data>
      <data key="d12">7402</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="TCM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCM can be transported in the bloodstream bound to albumina</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">835ccfd5b4d1484fa9e67dcb6836a937</data>
      <data key="d12">7403</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="PACIENTES EN DI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients in dialysis need to monitor their albumin levels as part of their nutritional management</data>
      <data key="d10">d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9</data>
      <data key="d11">15792f9310a24bd28e88454397b18dfa</data>
      <data key="d12">7404</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="HIPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoalbuminemia puede causar una falsa hipocalcemia, afectando la medici&#243;n de calcio en el suero.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">c2227aa9bede4a44b5029187eab3c7f4</data>
      <data key="d12">7405</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALBUMINA" target="HIPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fijaci&#243;n del calcio a la alb&#250;mina puede influir en los niveles de calcio ionizado, afectando la hipercalcemia.</data>
