      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROTE&#205;NAS" target="DIETA CONTROLADA EN HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In a controlled iron diet, protein sources are recommended to ensure adequate nutrition while managing iron levels</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">0c6dc7f5960342f3bcdd91d0503ef249</data>
      <data key="d12">7448</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROTE&#205;NAS" target="NEFROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High protein intake can lead to an increased risk of kidney stones due to its effects on urinary composition</data>
      <data key="d10">e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
      <data key="d11">c91610591b0e4868ae131be20762fec1</data>
      <data key="d12">7449</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROTE&#205;NAS" target="CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High protein diets can affect calcium metabolism and excretion, influencing kidney stone risk</data>
      <data key="d10">e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
      <data key="d11">53a899c6715b4e228334f102211778a6</data>
      <data key="d12">7450</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROTE&#205;NAS" target="OXALATO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dietary oxalate and protein intake can both influence the risk of developing kidney stones</data>
      <data key="d10">e67ea94c6cdb27cf6bb6715598cfe224</data>
