    <edge source="PROTE&#205;NAS" target="LEUCINA">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PROTE&#205;NAS and LEUCINA are closely related, as leucina is a key amino acid that plays a crucial role in the structure and function of proteins. It is a vital component that stimulates protein synthesis, thereby influencing the effectiveness of protein intake in promoting muscle protein synthesis. This highlights the importance of leucina in the context of nutrition and muscle health, as it directly impacts the body's ability to build and repair proteins.</data>
      <data key="d10">78d3252445aa1a02df4627450218fb59,dcb97f7ffdb0aea3051bdf53e04bcc29</data>
      <data key="d11">fe601e2dd48d4c3d9e54f6bfa1aaf088</data>
