    <edge source="ARGININA" target="PROTEINAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginine is an amino acid that is related to protein intake and metabolism, particularly in specific patient groups.</data>
      <data key="d10">33815f13a51d2a716356eaca97176390</data>
      <data key="d11">39610804416040bc93991ce78b8611f9</data>
      <data key="d12">7754</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="MELAS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginina is an amino acid that plays a significant role in the production of nitric oxide, a compound that is essential in addressing the vascular pathology associated with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). It is utilized as a therapeutic agent with the potential to alleviate symptoms of MELAS by enhancing the availability of nitric oxide, thereby contributing to improved vascular function and overall management of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bcc5beeb4b20475f24131743313fb30,c6d3d43de4b87527989dd0a7d9bda8e0</data>
      <data key="d11">5f7167d0ae5b49a88495f7f441ce996a</data>
      <data key="d12">7755</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginina is highlighted as a beneficial nutrient in the context of post-surgical recovery for oncology patients</data>
      <data key="d10">7c43869fff0960219e47d176597b35b8</data>
      <data key="d11">035199f96d1949429ca4ea7f85b7cb45</data>
      <data key="d12">7756</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="DEPORTISTAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Athletes may use arginine to improve their performance</data>
      <data key="d10">3e8ab018917854d76a0137102e0392bd</data>
      <data key="d11">8a025648e62549bf87ccf1975dd4744a</data>
      <data key="d12">7757</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="CAFE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambas sustancias son utilizadas para mejorar la recuperaci&#243;n y el rendimiento deportivo.</data>
      <data key="d10">fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d11">7e26befbfa574561a9b31dea8a10fc1f</data>
      <data key="d12">7758</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="GLUTAMINA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginina and Glutamina are both significant immunonutrients that play a crucial role in enhancing immune response. They are frequently studied together in the field of immunonutrition due to their importance in supporting immune function. Both Arginina and Glutamina are often discussed in the context of nutritional support, highlighting their complementary roles in promoting overall health and immune resilience.</data>
      <data key="d10">d2f16314e7098030a6780411d2e03023</data>
      <data key="d11">f9d4dd1408e44c8e82cd630bdd6ac250</data>
      <data key="d12">7759</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="&#211;XIDO N&#205;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginina is the sole precursor of nitric oxide, which plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and vascular function.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">304fcea029b541c69ffdcb1629650243</data>
      <data key="d12">7760</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGININA" target="CICATRIZACI&#211;N DE HERIDAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginina enhances wound healing processes, making it important in recovery from injuries.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">8d1bad572e9e477596f3781413dbaa70</data>
      <data key="d12">7761</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="HIPERGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine supplementation can help manage hyperglycemia and improve insulin sensitivity</data>
      <data key="d10">c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">e314c391376a4755a876f6fc99ad54fb</data>
      <data key="d12">7762</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="PROTEINAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine is an amino acid that plays a role in protein metabolism and is discussed in the context of protein intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">33815f13a51d2a716356eaca97176390</data>
      <data key="d11">04aa97bcec3b41368cc8373ca1a538fc</data>
      <data key="d12">7763</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NUTRICION ENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine may enhance the effectiveness of enteral nutrition by improving absorption</data>
      <data key="d10">d147df5b06fa62d87b7edd3f20dcd246</data>
      <data key="d11">9632572aa287459d9845c004745d42f7</data>
      <data key="d12">7764</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="GH">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both glutamine and growth hormone are considered in nutritional support but lack sufficient evidence for their effectiveness</data>
      <data key="d10">896ddfd9f06dc3ec8b1cfb986fae97fe</data>
      <data key="d11">c0f4a2d9335c44d28f9fa34a8d36bd91</data>
      <data key="d12">7765</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine is an amino acid that is relevant in the context of patients in critical condition. It can be administered to these patients in specific situations, although it is not included in standard solutions. The use of glutamine for critically ill patients highlights its potential benefits in supporting their recovery and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d10">7b34ed1eb4b09b2e0762c7e917f8a516,a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855</data>
      <data key="d11">f91012c7527a449380ff68dd8a52adff</data>
      <data key="d12">7766</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="PACIENTE QUEMADO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine supplementation is recommended for burn patients to prevent muscle loss and support immune function</data>
      <data key="d10">916d4d35de887923f4ea5b05928f13e3</data>
      <data key="d11">b2b0f0700afe4bbc9d64f1595d723cee</data>
      <data key="d12">7767</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN PACIENTES QUEMADOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine supplementation is considered in the nutritional therapy for burn patients</data>
      <data key="d10">125acd19edb76fa23986de56fc2517e8</data>
      <data key="d11">16a6e59e95e54d26896afecd756e77af</data>
      <data key="d12">7768</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN CIRUG&#205;A DE TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine is used in nutritional management to support patients undergoing surgery for head and neck tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">2bbe847617971cacfe15b2c970de2d21</data>
      <data key="d11">cf3b34c7cb4a4e239236a72c43f79ee1</data>
      <data key="d12">7769</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamina is recommended as a preventive treatment in nutritional support for oncology patients</data>
      <data key="d10">eae8ddef005974a2ffe71cf7c61b0634</data>
      <data key="d11">8b855b9e6f094c0e948ca3bb2ea94307</data>
      <data key="d12">7770</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="PACIENTES CON C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine supplementation may benefit cancer patients undergoing parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">202e4fa915a698c9d9164c3fcc61534e</data>
      <data key="d11">b123d5a4d041438db2d1e19748587761</data>
      <data key="d12">7771</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="MUCOSITIS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GLUTAMINA has been studied as a treatment to alleviate the symptoms of MUCOSITIS in patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Research indicates that the oral administration of glutamine can reduce both the duration and severity of mucositis, making it a potentially beneficial intervention for affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6,f333e5a9af59dd8504607b2559ac35dd</data>
      <data key="d11">468374ca5b174a85bccf4f89ff7a70cc</data>
      <data key="d12">7772</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="ENFERMEDAD VENOCLUSIVA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glutamina se ha recomendado para mejorar los s&#237;ntomas de la enfermedad venoclusiva hep&#225;tica en pacientes trasplantados</data>
      <data key="d10">84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">9d2f8634eaae4e40b2bb97951f5fa432</data>
      <data key="d12">7773</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="C&#201;LULAS HEMATOPI&#201;TICAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glutamina se ha utilizado para mejorar la recuperaci&#243;n y el bienestar de los pacientes trasplantados de c&#233;lulas hematopoy&#233;ticas.</data>
      <data key="d10">86a4647fb1fa580f7b72aa4833965ecb</data>
      <data key="d11">e771485c17e84d87b3af29d322d71efb</data>
      <data key="d12">7774</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="METOTREXATO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamina interacts with metotrexato, potentially affecting its clearance and increasing its tumoricidal effects</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">13cd29fff714450e975632b7b8dd0b17</data>
      <data key="d12">7775</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="PACIENTES CON TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients undergoing hematological cell transplants may receive glutamina for its potential benefits</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">e6a00bc1975b4678a35957feb7beb400</data>
      <data key="d12">7776</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="ALANINA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alanina is used in conjunction with glutamina to support its production from &#945;-ketoglutarate</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">10c431c81e8449d8ad805461350cd1dc</data>
      <data key="d12">7777</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="VALINA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Valina provides nitrogen that aids in the production of glutamina</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">3a9a5e17b45648aea5b690e6db28af49</data>
      <data key="d12">7778</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="ESTUDIOS EN RATAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Studies in rats provide evidence for the benefits of glutamina supplementation</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">d1711a29f02e441e9520293e7b4a7b3f</data>
      <data key="d12">7779</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="ADMINISTRACI&#211;N INTRAVENOSA DE AMINO&#193;CIDOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Intravenous administration of amino acids includes glutamina to prevent muscle loss</data>
      <data key="d10">546d2f3d8a308b461c44f6b0e1351ee6</data>
      <data key="d11">05500bdfa5ff4eda800398c5c8b442c7</data>
      <data key="d12">7780</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="TRASPLANTE DE C&#201;LULAS HEMATOL&#211;GICAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glutamina se ha estudiado en el contexto de su efecto sobre la mortalidad y recuperaci&#243;n en pacientes que han recibido un trasplante de c&#233;lulas hematol&#243;gicas.</data>
      <data key="d10">3e6ae05671fed21e332ee155332df21e</data>
      <data key="d11">1c995b000686456d8b6ed6e4a072b8ac</data>
      <data key="d12">7781</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="EQUINACEA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambas son utilizadas para mejorar la recuperaci&#243;n y el rendimiento en deportistas.</data>
      <data key="d10">fae6538f87888794da1ff0aaf0d842fe</data>
      <data key="d11">98ca5f60313e4323988fd8b546bd07d5</data>
      <data key="d12">7782</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NUCLE&#211;TIDOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamine and Nucleotides are both crucial for improving T lymphocyte function and are part of the discussion on immunonutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">d2f16314e7098030a6780411d2e03023</data>
      <data key="d11">5ddd869b3d5d48de86533d0917e737bd</data>
      <data key="d12">7783</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="GLUTATI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamina is a precursor in the synthesis of glutathione, which is crucial for antioxidant defense in cells.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">59a48fb25bac483e8dfe85a598a01f84</data>
      <data key="d12">7784</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="CICATRIZACI&#211;N DE HERIDAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamina supports the immune system and energy supply during stress, which is vital for effective wound healing.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">3cae5e004eb54b9a968113f62f1d1806</data>
      <data key="d12">7785</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="M&#218;SCULO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Muscle releases glutamine during stress, which is essential for various bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">3b608a692197463381699016a24d3527</data>
      <data key="d12">7786</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="INTESTINO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Intestine is the primary recipient of glutamine, utilizing it for energy and immune support.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">bc963c415d6b45e6803edce7e5b50e90</data>
      <data key="d12">7787</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="RI&#209;&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kidney acts as a donor of glutamine during stress, increasing its release into the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">11a4bed4306942b1989eae5f0052fed2</data>
      <data key="d12">7788</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Liver receives glutamine during stress, which is important for metabolic functions.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">e79e7f0e8686420bb09fc4722db8fae4</data>
      <data key="d12">7789</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTAMINA" target="NFKB/IKB">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NFkB/IkB complex is influenced by glutamine levels, which can affect inflammation regulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">194ecedd60f53d4157bd44eac52cbcd8</data>
      <data key="d11">2ac11ac274c24ff9a503a40f94683667</data>
      <data key="d12">7790</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACEITES VEGETALES" target="F&#211;RMULAS PEDI&#193;TRICAS">
