      <data key="d12">7816</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERGUCEMIA" target="GSD0">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Some patients with GSD0 may experience hyperglycemia as a metabolic complication</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">7b9662cc36c54c2da131edd48c4d6268</data>
      <data key="d12">7817</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="HIPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambas condiciones son alteraciones en los niveles de minerales en el cuerpo, donde la hipercalcemia se refiere a un exceso de calcio y la hipofosfatemia a una deficiencia de f&#243;sforo.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">de7a7411d54447089716343e2d7c202b</data>
      <data key="d12">7818</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="FGF-23">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El FGF-23 tiene un efecto directo en la regulaci&#243;n de los niveles de f&#243;sforo, y su actividad puede contribuir a la hipofosfatemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">58a620f1e59c44d1a2f8addd4e13475d</data>
      <data key="d12">7819</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="F&#211;SFORO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipofosfatemia se define por niveles bajos de f&#243;sforo en la sangre, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n directa entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">e1eaa9e4e4f742c7ab214bbf01a4af6e</data>
      <data key="d12">7820</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="HOSPITALIZADOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes hospitalizados tienen una incidencia de hipofosfatemia del 5%, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">9e09a2e37aac4870b7b14e5ea924e0f2</data>
      <data key="d12">7821</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipofosfatemia can occur as a complication in patients with chronic kidney disease due to impaired kidney function</data>
      <data key="d10">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d11">75f2e3d8fdef438888e8b342b2a4da70</data>
      <data key="d12">7822</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFOSFATEMIA" target="PACIENTE PEDI&#193;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pediatric patients on parenteral nutrition may experience hypophosphatemia due to nutrient imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d11">277157a2f2c440d2a80f7cbd6f3a6194</data>
      <data key="d12">7823</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="SUERO HIPERT&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertonic saline is administered to treat severe hyponatremia by increasing sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">5b84651340244c398b549a2b8ac0fe93</data>
      <data key="d12">7824</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="NATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">35.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia and natremia are closely related concepts in the context of sodium levels in the blood. Hyponatremia is defined by abnormal natremia levels, specifically when sodium concentrations are low. Natremia serves as a critical measurement for diagnosing and managing hyponatremia, as it directly indicates the presence of low sodium levels in the bloodstream. Therefore, natremia levels are essential for both the diagnosis and management of hyponatremia, highlighting the importance of monitoring sodium concentration in the blood for effective medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec,94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">d046995c32984a21b843461b7622e336</data>
      <data key="d12">7825</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiponatremia puede ser un hallazgo en pacientes con insuficiencia suprarrenal, lo que indica una relaci&#243;n entre la condici&#243;n y el desequilibrio electrol&#237;tico.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0</data>
      <data key="d11">b88e2b03972d471299ef3f141b42a218</data>
      <data key="d12">7826</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes insipidus can lead to hyponatremia due to excessive fluid loss and electrolyte imbalance</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">7e47885946f64a8c8967c07a3d4dccdc</data>
      <data key="d12">7827</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="OXITOCINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oxytocin can cause hyponatremia due to its antidiuretic effects, leading to water retention</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">2c79749327b84ab09ed7471338a9a8f0</data>
      <data key="d12">7828</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="&#201;XTASIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ecstasy use is associated with acute hyponatremia due to increased water retention and inappropriate vasopressin release</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">399c537a41384ec3853c96f4b905ef3b</data>
      <data key="d12">7829</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="METANFETAMINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Methamphetamine can lead to severe acute hyponatremia through similar mechanisms as ecstasy</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">423895239cf54f299a097bfa26f064d3</data>
      <data key="d12">7830</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPOGLICEMIA AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acute hypoglycemia can lead to hyponatremia due to the body's response to low blood sugar levels</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">e4bcc9eb7766459db34f2c1b797c73e8</data>
      <data key="d12">7831</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPOGLICEMIA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic hypoglycemia can also contribute to hyponatremia over time due to ongoing electrolyte imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">773a1daa539dd85e562a59e09f434af1</data>
      <data key="d11">b8f8d262ac13475b9a6dc8382a21c8ba</data>
      <data key="d12">7832</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiponatremia is a condition that has been reported in patients undergoing dietary treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141</data>
      <data key="d11">b235be70e7ae45dd8f79da12428d1c01</data>
      <data key="d12">7833</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA ESTRICTA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiponatremia es un posible efecto adverso de seguir una dieta hipos&#243;dica estricta</data>
      <data key="d10">1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108</data>
      <data key="d11">925c020c5b1a467a9d0244e760042b2c</data>
      <data key="d12">7834</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta hipos&#243;dica puede causar hiponatremia en pacientes con alteraciones renales o en tratamiento con diur&#233;ticos</data>
      <data key="d10">9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b</data>
      <data key="d11">9436a2b3a2c74617827d4d368194f79a</data>
      <data key="d12">7835</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="FISIOPATOLOG&#205;A DE LA HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pathophysiology of hyponatremia is directly related to the condition itself</data>
      <data key="d10">8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9</data>
      <data key="d11">c6cfc95d5a4940a6b8570032c7297968</data>
      <data key="d12">7836</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="MANIFESTACIONES CL&#205;NICAS DE LA HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clinical manifestations are a key aspect of understanding and diagnosing hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9</data>
      <data key="d11">b84cb90e08ed4b098a28930297ff547a</data>
      <data key="d12">7837</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIAGN&#211;STICO Y ETIOLOG&#205;A DE LA HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diagnosis and etiology are critical for understanding and treating hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9</data>
      <data key="d11">711bd4a0de0542179768e13f6cf892f8</data>
      <data key="d12">7838</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="TRATAMIENTO DE LA HIPONATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Treatment strategies are essential for managing hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">8ff1cad741bacfef19d53bb8941b5ca9</data>
      <data key="d11">2eb3b10af6fc43189de849df5d7db2b0</data>
      <data key="d12">7839</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="ADH">
      <data key="d8">36.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, and it is significantly influenced by the hormone Antidiuretic Hormone (ADH). ADH plays a crucial role in regulating water balance within the body, which directly impacts the occurrence of hyponatremia. Elevated levels of ADH can lead to excessive water retention, thereby diluting sodium levels and contributing to the development of hyponatremia. This condition is particularly common in hospitalized patients, where fluid balance can be disrupted. Additionally, the secretion of ADH is influenced by the body's fluid balance, further linking it to the onset of hyponatremia. Overall, ADH is a key hormone in the pathophysiology of hyponatremia, as its excessive secretion can result in significant alterations in sodium concentration due to increased water retention.</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9,94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,e4b62c2ae5857a5dd11f609286271bb4,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">fed55b5330b245a1be70ea1240250e7c</data>
      <data key="d12">7840</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="SIADH">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, and it is often a result of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). SIADH is a condition that leads to increased levels of antidiuretic hormone (ADH), which causes the body to retain excess water. This inappropriate secretion of ADH is a frequent cause of hyponatremia, as it results in water retention that dilutes sodium levels in the bloodstream. Thus, SIADH plays a significant role in the development of hyponatremia by promoting water retention and disrupting the balance of electrolytes.</data>
      <data key="d10">94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">31a194bdb3cb436a8e5f558d1033181d</data>
      <data key="d12">7841</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="NE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia, a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, may be associated with nutritional enteral (NE) methods. Although specific studies exploring this relationship are lacking, it is noted that enteral nutrition is linked to a lower incidence of hyponatremia when compared to parenteral nutrition. This suggests that there are different risks associated with these two nutritional approaches, highlighting the importance of understanding the implications of each method on sodium levels in patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">db6c7f1a2a8c44d68937f1add3c769a9</data>
      <data key="d12">7842</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="MORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, and it has been linked to higher mortality rates in hospitalized patients. The presence of hyponatremia is significant in a clinical context, as it is associated with an increased risk of mortality among patients. This relationship underscores the importance of monitoring and managing sodium levels in order to improve patient outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">94df5002f2221058a9bb77f456a50e61,e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">f2b871cfa4804b9a9426c7a6c1f5193e</data>
      <data key="d12">7843</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="NP">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia was studied in NP patients, showing a correlation with their hospital stay</data>
      <data key="d10">e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">5c8bbe55801e4a458fb24056cc5b7083</data>
      <data key="d12">7844</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="TRATAMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Effective treatment of hyponatremia can reduce mortality rates</data>
      <data key="d10">e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">0930a8fe09624ce0a2582c69394a5201</data>
      <data key="d12">7845</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia can lead to longer hospital stays for patients</data>
      <data key="d10">e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">23ee52d484fa4e468ef9f665e1b2e447</data>
      <data key="d12">7846</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="GABA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GABA is involved in the defense mechanisms activated during episodes of hyponatremia to reduce cerebral edema</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">7803a2fdb9d645de969b454bee4ed283</data>
      <data key="d12">7847</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="GLUTAMATO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glutamato plays a role in the body's response to cerebral edema during hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">4b5bebab77f3481e9ef9cfc97a5183ee</data>
      <data key="d12">7848</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="INOSITOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Inositol is involved in the mechanisms that help reduce cerebral edema during hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">3109eeaf2bf447cb90e0e5df1802eda6</data>
      <data key="d12">7849</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPERGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia can be secondary to hyperglycemia, complicating its diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">2a4afdd928eb4e3e92ceaf755767fa0e</data>
      <data key="d12">7850</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia can also be influenced by hypoglycemia, affecting sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">fa8a809041494c3da0b96ffbe40d1a09</data>
      <data key="d12">7851</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia can be misdiagnosed in patients with hypertriglyceridemia due to pseudohyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">1ae392d1a1bd421194b7d80ebe63d717</data>
      <data key="d12">7852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="OSMOLALIDAD PLASM&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Plasma osmolality is a key factor in diagnosing the type of hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">d4d13e8b6431480e8fae2eb0ab64de01</data>
      <data key="d12">7853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="PROTE&#205;NAS TOTALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Total protein levels can affect sodium measurements and the diagnosis of hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">c73e5e558cab6ae4736ce1619142c0a4</data>
      <data key="d11">0b66b3f953014ca68fd864dfa68b1ab5</data>
      <data key="d12">7854</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPOPROTEINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoproteinemia puede contribuir a la aparici&#243;n de hiponatremia en los pacientes</data>
      <data key="d10">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d11">04978a1fe18545dfb74af80d63f23fed</data>
      <data key="d12">7855</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="EDEMA PULMONAR">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El edema pulmonar puede ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado a la hiponatremia hipervol&#233;mica</data>
      <data key="d10">94481f05649e1ec83f8cc2e4a70b660b</data>
      <data key="d11">bdb585b0321646aa9b3d6ccd5ff314e9</data>
      <data key="d12">7856</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, which can be caused by insuficiencia cardiaca (heart failure). In patients with insuficiencia cardiaca, fluid retention and altered sodium levels contribute to the development of hiponatremia. This condition often arises as a complication in these patients, primarily due to fluid imbalance resulting from the heart's inability to pump effectively. Thus, there is a clear relationship between hiponatremia and insuficiencia cardiaca, where the latter can lead to the former through mechanisms of fluid retention and sodium dysregulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9</data>
      <data key="d11">55c2290837724358a97fa83305a3d235</data>
      <data key="d12">7857</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="CIRROSIS HEPATICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiponatremia can occur in patients with cirrosis hep&#225;tica due to fluid overload and altered sodium balance</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d11">97eb3b344b8548bea30bd7c80a685d36</data>
      <data key="d12">7858</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIUR&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a condition characterized by low sodium levels in the blood, and diuretics are medications commonly used to manage fluid retention associated with this condition. However, it is important to note that diuretics can also lead to hyponatremia, as they promote the loss of sodium and water from the body. Thus, while diuretics can be beneficial in managing fluid retention in patients with hyponatremia, they also carry the risk of exacerbating the condition by causing further sodium depletion.</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">e83fe321c69a40dba5c7e039096809f8</data>
      <data key="d12">7859</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="SODIO">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is characterized by low levels of sodium (sodio) in the body. Sodium levels are crucial for both the diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing sodium levels in individuals affected by this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,500e56f18da6e8b6ed0e1eed4af927e9</data>
      <data key="d11">ad870eb2e0544f6e9532aedc4659c548</data>
      <data key="d12">7860</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio levels can be affected in patients with hiponatremia, influencing overall electrolyte balance</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d11">1a4bb80af18c4cab80dbc51948b05f05</data>
      <data key="d12">7861</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HIPOALDOSTERONISMO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipoaldosteronismo is a condition characterized by insufficient levels of aldosterone, a hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating sodium retention in the body. This deficiency can lead to hiponatremia, which is a condition marked by low sodium levels in the blood. The impaired sodium retention caused by hipoaldosteronismo results in the development of hiponatremia, highlighting the interconnectedness of these two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791,fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">8f8deaa053f642f596e96b039cd64699</data>
      <data key="d12">7862</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol levels can influence the diagnosis of hiponatremia, as low cortisol may mimic the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d11">d8d64ab1dc0a4d87ba5574f69e713d7f</data>
      <data key="d12">7863</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HORMONAS TIROIDEAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hormonas tiroideas can affect sodium levels and contribute to the development of hiponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">3733abb85045220c8e373e316f858791</data>
      <data key="d11">88ae021ef93f4259be2024d3a7f1fc1f</data>
      <data key="d12">7864</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="DIUR&#201;TICOS DEL GRUPO TIAZIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diur&#233;ticos del grupo tiazida are a common cause of hiponatremia in patients, as they can lead to electrolyte imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">549f2de3e06c48fb9b11b087e565debc</data>
      <data key="d12">7865</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria can lead to hyponatremia due to inadequate production of aldosterone, which regulates sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">bda6a9e09c0e47e084ea16586f95f7fc</data>
      <data key="d12">7866</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="ACIDOSIS METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acidosis metab&#243;lica can occur alongside hyponatremia, indicating a complex interplay of electrolyte imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">2165fcd7a365480e9c5fa0dd2816a0d3</data>
      <data key="d12">7867</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="HYPERKALEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperkalemia can be associated with hyponatremia, particularly in cases of hipoaldosteronismo</data>
      <data key="d10">fee4d9611c98c81859bccdb4ded03622</data>
      <data key="d11">261ba418a32a467dacea7e76dc22455c</data>
      <data key="d12">7868</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="EDEMA CEREBRAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cerebral edema can be a consequence of severe hyponatremia, necessitating urgent treatment to alleviate swelling.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec</data>
      <data key="d11">1bf37cfa393e4b6685eea7adb4908fda</data>
      <data key="d12">7869</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="SOLUCI&#211;N SALINA HIPERT&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertonic saline solution is a treatment specifically used to correct severe hyponatremia and reduce associated cerebral edema.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec</data>
      <data key="d11">9521dd528f124ddda63b7dcca26eb5c3</data>
      <data key="d12">7870</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="S&#205;NDROME DE DESMIELINIZACI&#211;N OSM&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osmotic demyelination syndrome can occur as a complication of the rapid correction of chronic hyponatremia, highlighting the need for careful management.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec</data>
      <data key="d11">e10a5f40864f4ccbba44cbc92ef8fdb3</data>
      <data key="d12">7871</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="TRATAMIENTO ADECUADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adequate treatment is necessary for effectively managing hyponatremia and preventing complications such as cerebral edema.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a2506becec805cd1374d73de9a9fec</data>
      <data key="d11">d31c75368e4e45cda5eaf04ce0f3bb26</data>
      <data key="d12">7872</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPONATREMIA" target="SUERO GLUCOSADO">
