    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#211;SFORO and CALCIO are two essential minerals that play a critical role in bone metabolism. Both minerals are often monitored together, particularly in newborns, to ensure proper development and health. It is important to note that excessive intake of phosphorus can negatively affect calcium absorption, which in turn can impact overall bone health. This relationship highlights the need for a balanced intake of both minerals, as an excess of phosphorus may lead to decreased calcium absorption, further emphasizing the interconnectedness of F&#211;SFORO and CALCIO in maintaining healthy bones.</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d11">862ca74a5c16465885365d2d71fb8dd2</data>
      <data key="d12">8011</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#243;sforo and Magnesio are essential minerals that require careful monitoring in the diets of patients. Both minerals play significant roles in bone health, indicating their importance, particularly for newborns. Their relationship underscores the necessity of ensuring adequate intake of these minerals to support overall health and development.</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,cb892163c42e6e5ec9dede2d66693978</data>
      <data key="d11">a68d05b41c434514a904d8318b641c7b</data>
      <data key="d12">8012</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="HIPOFOSFOREMIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipofosfatemia is directly related to phosphorus levels in newborns, indicating a strong relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07</data>
      <data key="d11">f5b630b42da948d4a0691a1727b6427e</data>
      <data key="d12">8013</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="CETOACIDOSIS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Phosphorus levels can be affected during the treatment of cetoacidosis, and its replacement may be considered in certain cases</data>
      <data key="d10">afe0f4f37815c175f0faff06eb24a256</data>
      <data key="d11">45fe46f305d2495eba94952d62016a65</data>
      <data key="d12">8014</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#211;SFORO and VITAMINA D are closely related in the context of bone health and mineralization. The deficiency of vitamina D leads to hipofosfatemia, which is characterized by low levels of phosphorus in the blood. This condition arises due to a decreased absorption of phosphorus in the intestines. Conversely, vitamina D plays a crucial role in facilitating the absorption of phosphorus in the intestines, making it essential for proper bone mineralization. Thus, adequate levels of vitamina D are vital for maintaining healthy phosphorus levels, which in turn supports overall bone health.</data>
      <data key="d10">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d11">673430b6727e4cddba5d46af8070b1b2</data>
      <data key="d12">8015</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#211;SFORO es un mineral que puede presentar deficiencias en la DIETA CETOG&#201;NICA, lo que ha llevado a la recomendaci&#243;n de su suplementaci&#243;n de manera independiente. Se sugiere que la suplementaci&#243;n de f&#243;sforo se considere por separado para optimizar la mineralizaci&#243;n &#243;sea en pacientes que siguen esta dieta.</data>
      <data key="d10">1592143354d1ef792f8618ec03a32a16,4d84210c815fb41f2fa44f3e01aafa02</data>
      <data key="d11">a8af70c2037e498f8ee658e68a6e26e7</data>
      <data key="d12">8016</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="PACIENTES EN DI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients in dialysis need to limit phosphorus intake to avoid complications</data>
      <data key="d10">d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9</data>
      <data key="d11">ecae046e04d743418dc19cdff6e654d2</data>
      <data key="d12">8017</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hormona paratiroidea tambi&#233;n afecta los niveles de f&#243;sforo en la sangre, favoreciendo su reabsorci&#243;n renal y disminuyendo su concentraci&#243;n plasm&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d10">dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d11">e308308fe9614a4ab2ef094ffe5c37e0</data>
      <data key="d12">8018</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="CALCITONINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La calcitonina tambi&#233;n promueve la excreci&#243;n urinaria de f&#243;sforo, ayudando a regular sus niveles en el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d10">dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d11">872387f9445a48f1b43c63c735b3f8dc</data>
      <data key="d12">8019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#211;SFORO and ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA are closely related, particularly in the context of managing chronic kidney disease (CKD). High phosphorus levels are a significant complication associated with CKD, necessitating careful monitoring of phosphorus intake. To prevent health complications, individuals with chronic kidney disease must regulate their phosphorus consumption effectively. This management is crucial for maintaining overall health and mitigating the risks associated with elevated phosphorus levels in the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d11">a3b2dfad993b4d33b27f653536a21cbf</data>
      <data key="d12">8020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="HEMODI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated phosphorus levels in the blood are a concern for patients undergoing hemodialysis</data>
      <data key="d10">d59a9ea18d433acb64d60dbe17f5ae9b</data>
      <data key="d11">eb8f719aefc340d6acc6be479bfefd8d</data>
      <data key="d12">8021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="ALIMENTOS PROTEICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los alimentos proteicos son una fuente significativa de f&#243;sforo que debe ser controlada en la dieta de pacientes con enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d11">5a01ec989927440b8fb9484964a1b1eb</data>
      <data key="d12">8022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="&#193;CIDO F&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El &#225;cido f&#237;tico es una forma de f&#243;sforo que se encuentra en alimentos vegetales y afecta la absorci&#243;n de f&#243;sforo en el cuerpo</data>
      <data key="d10">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d11">6783db34c6cd45d5a7f5cb98215e2420</data>
      <data key="d12">8023</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="ADITIVOS ALIMENTARIOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los aditivos alimentarios pueden contener f&#243;sforo inorg&#225;nico, lo que complica el control de la ingesta de f&#243;sforo en la dieta</data>
      <data key="d10">7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824</data>
      <data key="d11">9dc26966b60e448b883abd3c41f1d503</data>
      <data key="d12">8024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="F&#211;SFORO" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#211;SFORO is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in the dietary recommendations for NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA. NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA includes specific guidelines for phosphorus intake to ensure proper bone development in pediatric patients, highlighting the importance of this mineral in supporting healthy growth and development during childhood.</data>
      <data key="d10">b789dfd7a5aa36fac33c5c881a1a4981,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5</data>
      <data key="d11">7432396d64f84914accfaaf159eb8db4</data>
      <data key="d12">8025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMINO ACIDS" target="NITROGEN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
