    <edge source="OBESITY" target="MICROBIOTA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The relationship between obesity and microbiota is significant, as the composition of the microbiota can influence the development of obesity through various metabolic changes. Research indicates that specific bacterial populations within the microbiota are linked to obesity, affecting weight gain and overall metabolic health. This connection highlights the role of microbiota in the regulation of body weight and the potential for targeting microbial communities in obesity management.</data>
      <data key="d10">2582e3a8c599c599624ee99e7754a7e0,2689c33de87eab465f004fff5f0530b8</data>
      <data key="d11">f2d634e478fe4014af15f594297ae7b0</data>
      <data key="d12">8125</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
