      <data key="d11">0ab99d27eb2549798a352f80eefc3a49</data>
      <data key="d12">8217</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El potasio puede tener efectos beneficiosos sobre la salud cardiovascular, sugiriendo una relaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">bc32b4a0e8544398bc90cb49e3b6ef20</data>
      <data key="d12">8218</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio intake is important for managing hipertensi&#243;n arterial through dietary control</data>
      <data key="d10">66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de</data>
      <data key="d11">1fa15a213754436592423490f28268b1</data>
      <data key="d12">8219</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="NEFROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nefrolitiasis can be influenced by dietary potassium levels, which are controlled in certain diets</data>
      <data key="d10">66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de</data>
      <data key="d11">aa382ae563434cd5869486cd1b56508f</data>
      <data key="d12">8220</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="SODIO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">POTASIO y SODIO son dos elementos qu&#237;micos que desempe&#241;an roles importantes en la salud humana, especialmente en relaci&#243;n con la presi&#243;n arterial. El potasio se utiliza en sales modificadas que combinan sodio y potasio, lo que ayuda a reducir la ingesta de sodio. Adem&#225;s, se ha demostrado que la ingesta adecuada de potasio puede contrarrestar los efectos del sodio en la presi&#243;n arterial, sugiriendo que un equilibrio entre estos dos minerales es crucial para mantener una presi&#243;n arterial saludable.</data>
      <data key="d10">5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb,66b7c4d336056f832579dc20ffb92992</data>
      <data key="d11">90af813702d04454887498fd7db25ac9</data>
      <data key="d12">8221</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA MODERADA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta hipos&#243;dica moderada puede requerir control del potasio en algunos casos</data>
      <data key="d10">1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108</data>
      <data key="d11">26f02296059a46368c1f2a496801df19</data>
      <data key="d12">8222</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="DIETA HIPOS&#211;DICA ESTRICTA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta hipos&#243;dica estricta requiere un control riguroso del potasio</data>
      <data key="d10">1d959525e9a5fe22094271d67d0b9108</data>
      <data key="d11">2f5f33bace4844c1a6ce7b5e140e854e</data>
      <data key="d12">8223</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="DIETA CONTROLADA EN POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta controlada en potasio regula la ingesta de potasio, esencial para la salud y el equilibrio electrol&#237;tico</data>
      <data key="d10">9de04e5aa72249acf96899ca74c17e0b</data>
      <data key="d11">a0858db3bfd64550a315b357cc3a3b68</data>
      <data key="d12">8224</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="CHINA">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">China has an average potassium intake of 1.8 g/day, which is relevant to dietary discussions about potassium levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">31b61ae47905168ef430433c9eb5237a</data>
      <data key="d11">d5d5284084604cb896c436a25677a0d4</data>
      <data key="d12">8225</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="PACIENTES EN DI&#193;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients in dialysis must control their potassium intake to prevent hyperkalemia</data>
      <data key="d10">d87b6185e9826c5338c079056e2019a9</data>
      <data key="d11">8c3dbf5ba66f4a8b809a38a05d8caef7</data>
      <data key="d12">8226</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="HTA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potassium is known to help lower blood pressure and is often recommended for individuals with hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a</data>
      <data key="d11">772c4ed52e7f4deda6720491560d8709</data>
      <data key="d12">8227</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="DIARREA SECRETORA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diarrea secretora puede resultar en p&#233;rdidas significativas de potasio, un mineral esencial.</data>
      <data key="d10">86a4647fb1fa580f7b72aa4833965ecb</data>
      <data key="d11">9d7fbc1a5ba14515a3c4622c71aa8742</data>
      <data key="d12">8228</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="BEBIDAS DEPORTIVAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potassium is often added to sports drinks in small amounts to assist with hydration.</data>
      <data key="d10">cfe1de28f01fa6428be1486b6af8f0a2</data>
      <data key="d11">bc20dbf0f5204f138c30014641a11063</data>
      <data key="d12">8229</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio is a required electrolyte in advanced nutritional support</data>
      <data key="d10">d1d2d307f9b3ceb8f8a21846f314b260</data>
      <data key="d11">22076006c16646cea8ec371df093da0d</data>
      <data key="d12">8230</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio is essential in the dietary plans outlined in NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA for maintaining heart and muscle function in children</data>
      <data key="d10">e5b3805730df59cb36030c92aa33c194</data>
      <data key="d11">2dd3bf37ae984364a65e2f26f96a374e</data>
      <data key="d12">8231</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="LACTANCIA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">POTASIO (potassium) is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions, including maintaining fluid balance and supporting muscle and nerve function. LACTANCIA (lactation) provides dietary reference intake guidelines for potassium tailored to different age groups, emphasizing the importance of adequate potassium levels during this critical period. Specifically, it highlights that infants have specific recommended intake levels for potassium during lactation, ensuring their nutritional needs are met for healthy growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d10">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d11">d0ed1d7b85714d8cb5b438b809512c70</data>
      <data key="d12">8232</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="DRI 971">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio is one of the minerals with recommended daily intake levels outlined in DRI 971</data>
      <data key="d10">565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be</data>
      <data key="d11">c2252af5ed584c4d9d2500356e146721</data>
      <data key="d12">8233</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="NUTRICION PARENTERAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Potasio is included in parenteral nutrition solutions to support muscle and heart function</data>
      <data key="d10">cd2b394eb36bf2bba5fba6e1145cdda2</data>
      <data key="d11">04c92f11c432410687d118295c149371</data>
      <data key="d12">8234</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="SMOFKABIVEN CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SmofKabiven Central contains potassium as an essential electrolyte for parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">d6abfd0fdff414c8f98db6dc3c239723</data>
      <data key="d11">d49be203053945128e11b3c10c8eec6e</data>
      <data key="d12">8235</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POTASIO" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesio and Potasio are both types of mineral supplements used to address deficiencies in magnesium and potassium, respectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">b1d4c144806ac7875725e152251868f3</data>
      <data key="d11">04ba17d0634d4b2d9c9abf4876ddc499</data>
      <data key="d12">8236</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="MAGNESIO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium and magnesium are both essential minerals that play crucial roles in maintaining bone health and supporting metabolism. They work together in various bodily functions, highlighting their interdependent relationship in nutrition. Their combined presence is vital for overall health, as they contribute to numerous physiological processes within the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07,9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6</data>
      <data key="d11">fc29b7f7905e48ae80524cfe2e3d62b9</data>
      <data key="d12">8237</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El calcio es un suplemento recomendado para pacientes en tratamiento con nutrici&#243;n artificial para prevenir complicaciones &#243;seas</data>
      <data key="d10">d66daca6ec5ffce0fc73bce55a3c0ff0</data>
      <data key="d11">eb4b00f4c2d84f6a80f7bbe9a581f95c</data>
      <data key="d12">8238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">73.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and VITAMINA D are both essential nutrients that play a critical role in maintaining bone health and preventing diseases such as osteoporosis. They are recommended to be taken together, as calcium supplementation should be paired with vitamin D to enhance absorption and overall effectiveness. Vitamin D significantly improves the bioavailability of calcium, which is particularly crucial for the bone health of elderly patients. A deficiency in vitamin D can lead to decreased intestinal absorption of calcium, highlighting its necessity for proper calcium absorption in the body. Furthermore, vitamin D supplementation is vital to ensure adequate calcium absorption, especially in individuals with lactose intolerance. In addition to its role in bone health, vitamin D also contributes to improving muscle function when combined with calcium. Overall, the synergistic relationship between CALCIO and VITAMINA D is essential for optimal metabolic processes and bone formation.</data>
      <data key="d10">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6,2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9,6ff2742793c37a38db1c11c14d2a6629,7925a5f252f3bfc107f8199401edf824,94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c,a25b0f84bc321cad942a2e33f681a5e4,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66,b68dc7398a80c0b67d28b1d9f73ff885,c947e3441a061fe1807f7aaf29becdce,dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d11">2c18c6ac661e44c5a361d081a3b5bdf4</data>
      <data key="d12">8239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="PACIENTE ANCIANO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Calcio es esencial para la salud &#243;sea del paciente anciano, y su d&#233;ficit puede llevar a osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9</data>
      <data key="d11">75924bea498145bdb74ef40772393cfb</data>
      <data key="d12">8240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="HIPOCALEMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and HIPOCALEMIA are closely related entities, particularly in the context of medical treatment. Calcium supplementation is often necessary in the treatment of HIPOCALEMIA, which is a condition characterized by low calcium levels in the body. This condition is especially significant in newborns, as HIPOCALEMIA is directly related to calcium levels in this population, indicating a strong relationship between calcium levels and the health of newborns. Thus, maintaining adequate CALCIO levels is crucial for preventing and managing HIPOCALEMIA.</data>
      <data key="d10">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3,44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07</data>
      <data key="d11">43fe412b363548318ebabe56d610a5e8</data>
      <data key="d12">8241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="DIETA IDEAL PARA LOS MAYORES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ideal diet for older adults emphasizes the importance of calcium to prevent bone density loss.</data>
      <data key="d10">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d11">e256bb48ff534d91bb245f4a99925239</data>
      <data key="d12">8242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="PERSONAS MAYORES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium is a critical micronutrient for older adults to prevent osteoporosis and fractures, making it essential for their health.</data>
      <data key="d10">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d11">d4cafc9e165548d9a9fc86410cfe8599</data>
      <data key="d12">8243</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and OSTEOPOROSIS are closely related, as calcium intake is critical for both preventing and treating osteoporosis. Insufficient calcium can lead to the development of osteoporosis, particularly in young athletes who may be at higher risk due to their physical demands. Therefore, maintaining adequate calcium levels is essential to support bone health and prevent the onset of osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">700a4472a23342b891a5685b622437d2,9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d11">85a88584c3084287908c4974d45964db</data>
      <data key="d12">8244</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="MOTHER">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La madre aumenta la absorci&#243;n de calcio para facilitar el desarrollo esquel&#233;tico del feto</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d11">fa5a0678ad344e5eaee06e269d91c5e4</data>
      <data key="d12">8245</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH)">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PTH regulates calcium levels in the blood, promoting calcium release from bones and increasing calcium reabsorption in the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">5c4daeb505f14a47a03fe1b5e3ea3324</data>
      <data key="d12">8246</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcio absorption is decreased by glucocorticoids, contributing to glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis</data>
      <data key="d10">9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d11">6714d5e1ddde462cbca82138f72fd564</data>
      <data key="d12">8247</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="OSTEOMALACIA ONCOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de calcio puede contribuir a la osteomalacia, que es un s&#237;ntoma de la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">3602b017a0b54c48bf7674258de2d3e6</data>
      <data key="d12">8248</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="RAQUITISMO">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcio, or calcium, is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in the mineralization of bones. A deficiency in calcium can lead to raquitismo, known as rickets, which is characterized by the inadequate mineralization of bones, resulting in weakened and deformed skeletal structures. Additionally, raquitismo can also be caused by the malabsorption of calcium, particularly in patients with celiac disease, where the body's ability to absorb this vital mineral is compromised. Thus, maintaining adequate levels of calcium is essential to prevent raquitismo and ensure proper bone health.</data>
      <data key="d10">4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">017ea3c935f04aaf9815ca4fe2812a04</data>
      <data key="d12">8249</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de calcio se ha asociado con una menor incidencia de s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico, indicando una relaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">daefd5c8b762491abe4cc996107a314d</data>
      <data key="d12">8250</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="YODO">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos nutrientes son esenciales en la dieta y se discuten en el contexto de la salud p&#250;blica y la nutrici&#243;n en Espa&#241;a.</data>
      <data key="d10">b68dc7398a80c0b67d28b1d9f73ff885</data>
      <data key="d11">b09f49ae971149d0860c3d3b3332fd05</data>
      <data key="d12">8251</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="PRODUCTOS L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and PRODUCTOS L&#193;CTEOS are closely related, as dairy products are recognized as a primary source of calcium, which is essential for bone health, particularly in children. This highlights the importance of incorporating dairy products into the diet to ensure adequate calcium intake for maintaining strong bones.</data>
      <data key="d10">62bb1dedc96b7530649f4c9762faab9d,b68dc7398a80c0b67d28b1d9f73ff885</data>
      <data key="d11">eff3e079497f46f1a48f18387e038af1</data>
      <data key="d12">8252</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium and dietary fiber are both nutrients studied for their roles in weight management and body composition.</data>
      <data key="d10">51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d</data>
      <data key="d11">f421f9e7acd94a5f8937e5887bfeedf9</data>
      <data key="d12">8253</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium deficiency is another common micronutrient deficiency that can occur after bariatric surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2</data>
      <data key="d11">6c648358c45f4db584d2f38c1469a066</data>
      <data key="d12">8254</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="DIETAS VEGETARIANAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium is an important nutrient that may require special attention in vegetarian diets to ensure adequate intake</data>
      <data key="d10">62afbb83c3f69bd45bf24467ac5b47b8</data>
      <data key="d11">e2361dff81fc4790aa27ae901cd4243d</data>
      <data key="d12">8255</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="GALACTOSEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcium is necessary for individuals with galactosemia, especially during lactation, and is provided through soy formulas.</data>
      <data key="d10">743649231e27012822c870ff5878263c</data>
      <data key="d11">7ce543e7f3474792952fa68cb40e7f33</data>
      <data key="d12">8256</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="RDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Recommended Dietary Allowances (RDA) include calcium as an essential nutrient for children.</data>
      <data key="d10">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d11">7b94ee60275e4e2b8a68cad6add6b2db</data>
      <data key="d12">8257</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="YOGUR">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and YOGUR are closely related, particularly in the context of dietary recommendations. Yogur, commonly known as yogurt, is frequently recommended as a beneficial source of calcium, especially for individuals who are lactose intolerant. It is recognized for its high calcium content and is advised for daily consumption to help meet nutritional needs. Thus, YOGUR serves as an important dietary option for those seeking to increase their calcium intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">6ff2742793c37a38db1c11c14d2a6629,ae2bf939fd143e4d8d998722ad86ba66</data>
      <data key="d11">6070b20ed2254cdf92363505cf729e34</data>
      <data key="d12">8258</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El calcio es esencial para los pacientes en di&#225;lisis, quienes necesitan suplementos debido a la falta de vitamina D</data>
      <data key="d10">9f77fc213da2123b013166c181a60323</data>
      <data key="d11">dcfc4124d23241a196a74c535f6fd5f7</data>
      <data key="d12">8259</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="PACIENTES CELIACOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Se recomienda la suplementaci&#243;n de calcio para pacientes celiacos para mejorar la salud &#243;sea</data>
      <data key="d10">9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30</data>
      <data key="d11">92efb869ecc84c5fb2bd99e8e974b303</data>
      <data key="d12">8260</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
