    <edge source="CALCIO" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in the dietary recommendations for NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA. NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA includes specific guidelines regarding the intake of CALCIO for children, emphasizing its importance for supporting bone health. These nutritional guidelines provide comprehensive recommendations for calcium intake, ensuring that children receive adequate amounts to promote healthy growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d10">06f547bc6311ffa370bc1a65dc7184d2,62bb1dedc96b7530649f4c9762faab9d,b789dfd7a5aa36fac33c5c881a1a4981,df73c75d84a055e0a67bc7f14d35e9d5</data>
      <data key="d11">cd816d31e59941d69966eab9f522fd4b</data>
      <data key="d12">8291</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCIO" target="NI&#209;OS">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CALCIO and NI&#209;OS are closely related in the context of calcium requirements. Calcium is essential for children, as their needs are specifically tailored to support proper growth and bone development. Adequate calcium intake during childhood is crucial to ensure healthy skeletal development and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d10">b2bdb1e00976001800583298f8dddc7a,efbbfb33c127e16f4f9013683aff2c5f</data>
      <data key="d11">4882b9747add412e87d5e6688f98e9ea</data>
      <data key="d12">8292</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
