      <data key="d9">Bicarbonato is often used in conjunction with Magnesio to help regulate pH levels in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">9200477669cf2a6e6f67f912c729ddc6</data>
      <data key="d11">4e5d50120b4c46e28195a737ff357869</data>
      <data key="d12">8304</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="PACIENTE ANCIANO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Magnesio es importante para la salud del paciente anciano, ya que su d&#233;ficit puede influir negativamente en enfermedades cr&#243;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d10">2f548ddee569586dbe82ca124f2695e9</data>
      <data key="d11">cd906569b5064f2099ea30e386e7dd39</data>
      <data key="d12">8305</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="PRETERM INFANTS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesium can lead to hypermagnesemia in preterm infants if their mothers were treated with it</data>
      <data key="d10">fa356397bc52582bdbbd1868639feec9</data>
      <data key="d11">540aeaf2d11d46b6a16fcc272c12af05</data>
      <data key="d12">8306</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both are essential minerals with recommended daily intakes that support various bodily functions</data>
      <data key="d10">5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5</data>
      <data key="d11">e7dda32559644d0ba865168157c19f2e</data>
      <data key="d12">8307</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesium deficiency is common in patients with chronic liver disease, which can be related to eating disorders</data>
      <data key="d10">8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25</data>
      <data key="d11">e007c613ad4b4c548245a97db2ece00a</data>
      <data key="d12">8308</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Severe magnesium deficiency can lead to hypocalcemia, which may mimic or exacerbate conditions like Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">c2e6b5916ce04299a40f2d1085fecfca</data>
      <data key="d12">8309</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="PTH">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipomagnesemia puede llevar a una secreci&#243;n inapropiadamente normal de PTH a pesar de la hipocalcemia</data>
      <data key="d10">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6</data>
      <data key="d11">fb27fa3fb8b047aaa3c2fd824f729815</data>
      <data key="d12">8310</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El magnesio puede tener efectos beneficiosos sobre la salud cardiovascular, sugiriendo una relaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">b6482dd0e207436db69ea6d2c692020f</data>
      <data key="d12">8311</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesium deficiency can occur in patients with significant diarrhea, which may follow bariatric surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">bd26f1257d0d7f3e1de6624b3b4a3cc2</data>
      <data key="d11">706a62324fed434ab95084038fb3ffef</data>
      <data key="d12">8312</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="ZINC">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MAGNESIO and ZINC are both essential micronutrients that play significant roles in various bodily functions. They are crucial for maintaining health and are included in dietary guidelines. However, deficiencies in these minerals can occur, particularly in patients undergoing specific surgical procedures. It is important to ensure adequate intake of magnesium and zinc to support overall health and recovery during such medical interventions.</data>
      <data key="d10">3bd46addca98ca875c66aab3827bbf5f,91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d11">5ddbf3bcca624c07b15cae540563ee58</data>
      <data key="d12">8313</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="PACIENTES CIRR&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesium levels are often reduced in cirrhotic patients, contributing to their nutritional deficiencies</data>
      <data key="d10">4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92</data>
      <data key="d11">3b8bcb6bf3a34dc7be01fee69b8feb4d</data>
      <data key="d12">8314</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="HTA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Magnesium is noted for its vasodilatory properties and has been studied for its effects on hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d10">29b354fe9b007cadb55ce27555391d5a</data>
      <data key="d11">acb2eac663d749bf8295fb2ba5e45f82</data>
      <data key="d12">8315</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="HIPOMAGNESEMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypomagnesemia is a condition characterized by low levels of magnesium in the plasma</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">b142630411a643d6b7367c8a6988d933</data>
      <data key="d12">8316</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="CALCITRIOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcitriol enhances the absorption of magnesium in the intestines</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">103b79107ca54b1c88b0b545a1881b10</data>
      <data key="d12">8317</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Growth hormone increases magnesium absorption in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">f9c3e3c48ff64d1885f5720de0469641</data>
      <data key="d12">8318</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="DIUR&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diuretics can affect the renal reabsorption of magnesium, impacting overall magnesium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">8a1848c016bd423b83a697dd4f208412</data>
      <data key="d12">8319</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="HUESO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone serves as a major reservoir for magnesium, containing a significant portion of the body's total magnesium</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">0b34d5d3fb1f41858326e544a95c8af7</data>
      <data key="d12">8320</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="M&#218;SCULO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Muscle tissue is another important site for magnesium, contributing to various physiological processes</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c</data>
      <data key="d11">2eaa6dd83eac416f9ad8f11f9a08f406</data>
      <data key="d12">8321</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAGNESIO" target="SEVELAMER">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sevelamer is used to control hyperphosphatemia, which can affect magnesium levels in patients with kidney disease</data>
