    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="ANTIOXIDANTE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin A has antioxidant properties that protect against cancer and atherosclerosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">c879b2e3799c9353091ac931a92a99e8</data>
      <data key="d11">94092131833149249334b96d3d7470b8</data>
      <data key="d12">8351</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="VITAMINA K">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both vitamins are essential for maintaining health, with Vitamin A affecting vision and Vitamin K involved in blood coagulation</data>
      <data key="d10">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d11">ebb9910182cc47a6a87978917a618dee</data>
      <data key="d12">8352</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="ALCOHOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alcoholism can lead to a deficiency in vitamin A, affecting vision and overall health</data>
      <data key="d10">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d11">0c0a180268d544a7bcf7bf9619200f8b</data>
      <data key="d12">8353</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="XEROFTALMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Xerophthalmia is a direct consequence of vitamin A deficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d11">0d98c87ed23346f384246e35bbe46ef8</data>
      <data key="d12">8354</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="RECOMENDACIONES DIARIAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Daily recommendations for vitamin A are essential for maintaining health</data>
      <data key="d10">bead99df88cb929a33cc2799a84da77e</data>
      <data key="d11">a169d8aea7b840d084e656818806b78e</data>
      <data key="d12">8355</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="NUTRICI&#211;N DURANTE LA GESTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ingesta de vitamina A debe ser controlada durante la gestaci&#243;n para evitar efectos teratog&#233;nicos</data>
      <data key="d10">135d72a9407315b8bbf5b1ac13d72abf</data>
      <data key="d11">0256219818e84fd6b7c115f011e7f82f</data>
      <data key="d12">8356</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="VITAMINA E">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamins A and E deficiencies can occur after malabsorptive surgeries, indicating a need for monitoring and supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d10">91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d11">ef3a8bd1c4e04f0e89a34e51114f67d4</data>
      <data key="d12">8357</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="DBP">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DBP techniques can lead to vitamin A deficiency, highlighting their interrelation.</data>
      <data key="d10">91f7ece6ed9226a98b3f59f46000ebf6</data>
      <data key="d11">156e6635cfd945628d06e8fcd4e545ec</data>
      <data key="d12">8358</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin A levels need to be monitored in patients with acute renal failure to prevent toxicity</data>
      <data key="d10">532561f62a972376f3f898b265623fc0</data>
      <data key="d11">61f70d2376c44b389a2f410baf52ce31</data>
      <data key="d12">8359</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="EUROPEAN CONSENSUS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Consensus includes recommendations for Vitamin A supplementation in the management of Fibrosis Qu&#237;stica</data>
      <data key="d10">f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4</data>
      <data key="d11">c2f2687e954b49c2ba8dbf6af2ec8396</data>
      <data key="d12">8360</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="VITAMINA D">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both Vitamin D and Vitamin A are essential nutrients discussed in the context of supplementation and health recommendations</data>
      <data key="d10">a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233</data>
      <data key="d11">bea2aa4bfa5a45669a18b61093ae7edc</data>
      <data key="d12">8361</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="BETACAROTENOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Beta-carotene is a safer alternative to retinol for Vitamin A supplementation, particularly in certain health conditions</data>
      <data key="d10">a4886f74d848ccd61cefcaab3103f233</data>
      <data key="d11">fb193ca7e30c41ecbe4ee789cafc8a2e</data>
      <data key="d12">8362</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="PACIENTE ONCOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de vitamina A en altas dosis no se recomienda para pacientes oncol&#243;gicos debido a sus efectos adversos</data>
      <data key="d10">d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56</data>
      <data key="d11">b4f9cb1307694b56a2f32244106f05a8</data>
      <data key="d12">8363</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VITAMINA A is an essential vitamin that plays a crucial role in the growth and development of children. It is included in the dietary recommendations for NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA, highlighting its importance in ensuring the health and well-being of pediatric populations.</data>
      <data key="d10">b789dfd7a5aa36fac33c5c881a1a4981,e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728</data>
      <data key="d11">ad9bf10055b744f88c05dd508e52096a</data>
      <data key="d12">8364</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="VITAMINA B1">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both vitamins are essential nutrients that play critical roles in maintaining health and are often included in dietary supplements</data>
      <data key="d10">3202b451a4ece0fc376bd2899a412bef</data>
      <data key="d11">400bcf5dc7644e929799c2d7afcf4a1b</data>
      <data key="d12">8365</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA A" target="AUXINA A MASIVA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Auxina A Masiva is a product that contains Vitamin A, thus directly related to its function and benefits</data>
      <data key="d10">3202b451a4ece0fc376bd2899a412bef</data>
      <data key="d11">4ab21bb763df446d81224e88069b5b41</data>
      <data key="d12">8366</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N EN C&#193;NCER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is recommended for cancer patients to support overall health and combat malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">bf234f719a608fc6858d9a1749463539</data>
      <data key="d11">d838df6c031344309a08e18dae565251</data>
      <data key="d12">8367</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="COMIT&#201; DE NUTRICI&#211;N DE LA AEP">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Committee recommends a daily supplement of vitamin D for infants to prevent deficiency, especially for those exclusively breastfed.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d11">2d012acac4cc48308ba5cda94db00c94</data>
      <data key="d12">8368</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="PRETERM INFANTS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is crucial for calcium absorption and bone health in preterm infants</data>
      <data key="d10">d0f40e5a802daab3992f9e1746a82467</data>
      <data key="d11">f9676c3b2876450d8c26fa9b779ef72f</data>
      <data key="d12">8369</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="INFUVITE PEDI&#193;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Infuvite Pedi&#225;trico contains Vitamin D as part of its composition for pediatric nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd</data>
      <data key="d11">1da1e0e1a5974ac1a63ab21781d3bcd0</data>
      <data key="d12">8370</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="SARCOPEMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D deficiency is linked to muscle weakness and sarcopenia, highlighting its importance in elderly health.</data>
      <data key="d10">caab2e12a2bce3c947d663cf8b71cb67</data>
      <data key="d11">c8f7e73f8af14a0e945240137e2369a2</data>
      <data key="d12">8371</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="FRAILTY">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D deficiency is an independent factor contributing to frailty in the elderly</data>
      <data key="d10">1052683f23a0c9825af9c5c1d39ceb2c</data>
      <data key="d11">7183a24aedfc41c8ba935e00da584f1b</data>
      <data key="d12">8372</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D supplementation is recommended to improve strength and prevent falls in frail elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">beca26663a8b4b3bb5afca45b937b0cc</data>
      <data key="d12">8373</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="DIETA IDEAL PARA LOS MAYORES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ideal diet for older adults should include vitamin D to support calcium absorption and bone health.</data>
      <data key="d10">368804d3e1f8a58c4e6c3a8210f08a35</data>
      <data key="d11">b71458943ab14764bbbc975c7b4e0785</data>
      <data key="d12">8374</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="PERSONAS MAYORES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is crucial for older adults to maintain bone health and prevent osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">aa44a32ccc29ae80ddbbc4a77b33a297</data>
      <data key="d11">30c0710e62b64ef4acdd93c382c39689</data>
      <data key="d12">8375</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="INSTITUTO DE MEDICINA NORTEAMERICANO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Institute of Medicine provides recommendations for serum levels of vitamin D, indicating its importance in health guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d11">7134d77fe8cb4dc8af955f3380cc84b3</data>
      <data key="d12">8376</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="BISCHOFF-FERRARI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bischoff-Ferrari's meta-analysis suggests that vitamin D supplementation can significantly reduce non-vertebral fractures.</data>
      <data key="d10">fe2e0137e7ca501d13c9a8fa4d800377</data>
      <data key="d11">a7b3a8edebce4a63bc4f5a211b997b52</data>
      <data key="d12">8377</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">24.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VITAMINA D and OSTEOPOROSIS are closely related, as the deficiency of vitamin D can significantly contribute to the development of osteoporosis. Vitamin D plays a crucial role in bone health by facilitating the absorption of calcium, which is vital for maintaining strong bones. Consequently, a lack of vitamin D is recognized as a significant risk factor for the onset of osteoporosis. To mitigate this risk, vitamin D is often supplemented in patients diagnosed with osteoporosis, highlighting its importance in the management and prevention of this bone condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,e945adb09eb8d9984302b72f9a2a68cb,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d11">92853b16c3984b819ae547d5af8bc425</data>
      <data key="d12">8378</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="COLESTIRAMINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cholestyramine can lead to malabsorption of fat-soluble vitamins, including vitamin D</data>
      <data key="d10">8bcd338de10fbee8f3c808cc30b69b25</data>
      <data key="d11">0a9f81e9a5ca4171ab044d7e2e607b87</data>
      <data key="d12">8379</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D deficiency may contribute to the symptoms seen in Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism, affecting calcium absorption.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">34f5c56def43426ca9744145e1da308f</data>
      <data key="d12">8380</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="PTH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de vitamina D puede causar un aumento en los niveles de PTH debido a la hipocalcemia</data>
      <data key="d10">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6</data>
      <data key="d11">22094a0b88594d59843b1f923658cb0c</data>
      <data key="d12">8381</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypoparathyroidism can lead to low levels of vitamin D, affecting calcium metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">1fe696b5fc264a13894d0a18d7dc16d8</data>
      <data key="d12">8382</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="OSTEOMALACIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D deficiency can lead to osteomalacia, a condition characterized by softening of the bones</data>
      <data key="d10">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">3c480d340a0140f6b10059c99f9fcfc1</data>
      <data key="d12">8383</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="RAQUITISMO">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VITAMINA D and RAQUITISMO are closely related, particularly in the context of health conditions such as celiac disease. Rickets, a condition characterized by weak and soft bones, is primarily caused by a deficiency in vitamin D. In patients with celiac disease, the malabsorption of vitamin D can contribute to the development of rickets. Therefore, ensuring adequate levels of vitamin D is crucial in preventing rickets, especially in individuals who may have absorption issues due to gastrointestinal disorders.</data>
      <data key="d10">4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f,6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">5dc555b634264837bb8859f1d45acbfe</data>
      <data key="d12">8384</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="25(OH)D">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">25-hydroxyvitamin D is a marker used to assess vitamin D levels in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">ec1181b130584bf186c2ca8d533977da</data>
      <data key="d12">8385</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="1,25(OH)&#8322;D&#8323;">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 is the active form of vitamin D that regulates calcium and phosphate metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">f8a3458d8bf548979bec44da280e954c</data>
      <data key="d12">8386</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="HIPOCALEMIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is crucial for preventing and treating hypocalcemia by facilitating calcium absorption</data>
      <data key="d10">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3</data>
      <data key="d11">d3a9171163224cdf93989130bc3e2956</data>
      <data key="d12">8387</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="1&#913;-HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">1&#945;-hidroxilasa is essential for the activation of vitamin D, which is crucial for calcium and phosphate metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">96bb0a8e59424f13b36fe5ff9a01dfeb</data>
      <data key="d12">8388</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de vitamina D puede aumentar el riesgo de c&#225;ncer de pr&#243;stata, sugiriendo una relaci&#243;n entre ambos</data>
      <data key="d10">a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">5788b6a1f5384580a44553d8a5c40b77</data>
      <data key="d12">8389</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="C&#193;NCER DE OVARIO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de vitamina D puede aumentar el riesgo de c&#225;ncer de ovario, sugiriendo una relaci&#243;n entre ambos</data>
      <data key="d10">a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">9a1539bf3f6946078afe41dd9ddaf7a6</data>
      <data key="d12">8390</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La vitamina D y el s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico est&#225;n interrelacionados, ya que la hipovitaminosis D se asocia con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico. Adem&#225;s, se sugiere que la vitamina D puede tener un efecto protector sobre esta condici&#243;n, lo que indica una relaci&#243;n significativa entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">cc66685a470d4548a825b6129955a577</data>
      <data key="d12">8391</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La vitamina D se asocia con la mejora de la salud cardiovascular y la regulaci&#243;n de la glucosa, lo que puede influir en la aparici&#243;n de enfermedades cardiovasculares. Adem&#225;s, se ha observado que niveles adecuados de vitamina D est&#225;n relacionados con un menor riesgo de desarrollar estas enfermedades, indicando una conexi&#243;n significativa entre la vitamina D y la salud cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d10">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704,a45daf363c832c36bc8ece57f5887f53</data>
      <data key="d11">745dd6fa3da046b88c5bf80f5da7d2da</data>
      <data key="d12">8392</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La vitamina D mejora la secreci&#243;n de insulina, lo que puede influir en la tolerancia a la glucosa</data>
      <data key="d10">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704</data>
      <data key="d11">d37edc359dbe4cccb803b40f36dbe4a5</data>
      <data key="d12">8393</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMINA D" target="FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D and dietary fiber are both important nutrients that have been researched for their effects on health and weight management.</data>
      <data key="d10">51729d1c2f83f752895eaca1969e2c0d</data>
      <data key="d11">6b687831086f4b1aa3b8abf76f8d4df1</data>
      <data key="d12">8394</data>
