      <data key="d12">8631</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="NUTRICIONES COMERCIALIZADAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Iodine may be present in commercial nutrition formulations, essential for thyroid function</data>
      <data key="d10">12ceae17f5df9d7a1a40ebc43156a35e</data>
      <data key="d11">a7b589ff8e5d41cda6336974ab00bb09</data>
      <data key="d12">8632</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="HORMONAS TIROIDEAS">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">YODO, or iodine, is a crucial element necessary for the synthesis of hormonas tiroideas, or thyroid hormones. A deficiency in iodine can hinder the proper production of these hormones, potentially leading to conditions such as hipotiroidismo, or hypothyroidism. Iodine plays a vital role in regulating metabolism through its influence on thyroid hormone production.</data>
      <data key="d10">89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d,f43e3958f11ed24b0a02f60a2993309a,f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
      <data key="d11">0126f6f3b69640eb8d7224f3aa07242d</data>
      <data key="d12">8633</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="BICIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de yodo puede causar bocio, afectando la salud de la tiroides.</data>
      <data key="d10">89fc75473a09f83406bce1f9e3a15a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">fd14b6d87e50412196ba68586de66bb0</data>
      <data key="d12">8634</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both are essential nutrients with recommended daily intakes that support metabolic processes</data>
      <data key="d10">5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5</data>
      <data key="d11">eb4e3c627acc42169f561192c07080eb</data>
      <data key="d12">8635</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="AMIODARONA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La amiodarona puede inducir hipotiroidismo, especialmente en &#225;reas con baja ingesta de yodo, lo que afecta la producci&#243;n de hormonas tiroideas.</data>
      <data key="d10">f701d832b0dc8b95c2cb09997d543897</data>
      <data key="d11">a40bcae829ea4132ad8e9b679b142929</data>
      <data key="d12">8636</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YODO" target="MUJERES EMBARAZADAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las mujeres embarazadas necesitan un consumo adecuado de yodo para el desarrollo saludable del feto.</data>
      <data key="d10">b68dc7398a80c0b67d28b1d9f73ff885</data>
      <data key="d11">b403cdeffe3f4d80802e7ab00ab8c35f</data>
      <data key="d12">8637</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
