    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE CARDIOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Heart Association provides dietary guidelines to help prevent chronic diseases, particularly cardiovascular diseases.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">5c171bf859084c2f9c4ae7eaaf5c45d3</data>
      <data key="d12">8685</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Diabetes Association offers dietary recommendations to prevent and manage chronic diseases, especially diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">9f541a24f52a453cb1340c765cef58e1</data>
      <data key="d12">8686</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Society of Clinical Oncology provides dietary guidelines aimed at reducing the risk of cancer, a significant chronic disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">35d388aaa9d047b2909e088e30d58c13</data>
      <data key="d12">8687</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="ALIMENTACI&#211;N SALUDABLE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Healthy eating is linked to a lower risk of developing chronic diseases, including cancer and cardiovascular diseases.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">c680ebaa094b409a8173644b6d94cd7c</data>
      <data key="d12">8688</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="H&#193;BITOS ALIMENTARIOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Eating habits are a major factor in the development and prevention of chronic diseases.</data>
      <data key="d10">ea5b0e748b16db9640ab70c394ca1a4c</data>
      <data key="d11">6d7b45ab2aa94f5b84d635bb010e6813</data>
      <data key="d12">8689</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="CONSUMO ALIMENTARIO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic diseases are linked to dietary habits and consumption patterns</data>
      <data key="d10">b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074</data>
      <data key="d11">c50ae87854504bf5ac567a9e483f3c3c</data>
      <data key="d12">8690</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cardiovascular diseases are a category of chronic diseases that can be affected by nutrition and lifestyle</data>
      <data key="d10">b003f8a156374bb4430475f4ffe8e074</data>
      <data key="d11">2c4dde1875a244c087e6726afa3eef0e</data>
      <data key="d12">8691</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS and NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA are closely interconnected, particularly in the context of children's health. Chronic diseases in children often necessitate tailored nutritional interventions to manage their conditions effectively. NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA plays a crucial role in this regard, as it aims to prevent the development of ENFERMEDADES CR&#211;NICAS through proper dietary management. By focusing on appropriate nutrition, healthcare providers can help mitigate the risk of chronic diseases in pediatric populations, ensuring better health outcomes for children.</data>
      <data key="d10">b6c8d5ff1536806d6512fb9d1af1e6db,e55003dbf85cc1fb81cac90716ce0e87</data>
      <data key="d11">7b178e585b624a379e2dc5c6e6a813ef</data>
      <data key="d12">8692</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO" target="CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El alcoholismo puede causar un aumento en los niveles de cortisol, llevando a un estado de hipercortisolismo</data>
      <data key="d10">e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d11">ae85d0b3fff5439398be4f85afa9a9bc</data>
      <data key="d12">8693</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO" target="VLCD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El alcoholismo es una contraindicaci&#243;n para el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">60f3ec1b48214310916a4df5d8c890a7</data>
      <data key="d12">8694</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El alcoholismo es una de las principales causas de cirrosis, afectando la salud hep&#225;tica de los individuos.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503</data>
      <data key="d11">97675d47677d43b580f91207e78393cf</data>
      <data key="d12">8695</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALCOHOLISMO" target="HIPOMAGNESEMIA">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alcoholism is a condition that can significantly impact nutritional health, particularly leading to hypomagnesemia, which is characterized by low levels of magnesium in the body. This relationship is primarily due to two factors: decreased magnesium absorption and inadequate nutritional intake. Individuals suffering from alcoholism may experience malabsorption of essential nutrients, including magnesium, which further exacerbates the risk of developing hypomagnesemia. Thus, the interplay between alcoholism and hypomagnesemia highlights the importance of addressing nutritional deficiencies in individuals with alcohol use disorders.</data>
      <data key="d10">863198ceabd6e1c11a0d0944c676737c,ed9dfe1b1e334597565187840983df05</data>
      <data key="d11">99c6bc3bbeaa424db7a9ce4003b41603</data>
      <data key="d12">8696</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osteoporosis is a common complication in patients with anorexia nervosa due to low body weight and nutrient deficiencies</data>
      <data key="d10">9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68</data>
      <data key="d11">007d9aaf7d0045c19e3c4bb072c8b55d</data>
      <data key="d12">8697</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="DSM-IV">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The DSM-IV provides diagnostic criteria for anorexia nerviosa, outlining the symptoms and behaviors associated with the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239</data>
      <data key="d11">80a6a7e5931d4a22998d907a645ce4ae</data>
      <data key="d12">8698</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="DSM-5">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia nervosa is a complex eating disorder characterized by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image, leading to self-imposed starvation and excessive weight loss. The DSM-5, or the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition, provides comprehensive diagnostic criteria for anorexia nervosa, outlining its symptoms and classifications. The DSM-5 also reflects updates in the understanding of the disorder, incorporating new insights and research findings to enhance the accuracy and relevance of its diagnostic criteria.</data>
      <data key="d10">8029c950c540c731bb9334bd90348239,9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210</data>
      <data key="d11">1eee707e715c44c992204972f8d6fb5b</data>
      <data key="d12">8699</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia nerviosa is a specific type of eating disorder within the broader category of trastornos de la conducta alimentaria</data>
      <data key="d10">9c65bcd67b717641c8d9d94ef9cfb210</data>
      <data key="d11">97d60b555f2c47ba923a265a387ae3d3</data>
      <data key="d12">8700</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia Nervosa is a complex eating disorder that can be associated with various physiological changes, including alterations in cortisol levels. Elevated cortisol levels in patients with Anorexia Nervosa can contribute to the development of osteopenia, a condition characterized by lower than normal bone density. This relationship highlights the potential impact of stress hormones on bone health in individuals suffering from this disorder. Additionally, Anorexia Nervosa may be linked to disruptions in cortisol levels, further emphasizing the intricate connection between this eating disorder and hormonal imbalances.</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359,e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d11">d68bd8d97aff46da898c1db88dcace68</data>
      <data key="d12">8701</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="AMENORREA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia nervosa can lead to hormonal changes that result in primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">f610cf4b8da4445ea93f0a30da7d67cf</data>
      <data key="d12">8702</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 may develop Anorexia Nervosa due to the pressures of managing their weight and insulin intake</data>
      <data key="d10">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d11">cdd41c8d7a1241749f9447e0a2e54cad</data>
      <data key="d12">8703</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TRASTORNO DEL COMPORTAMIENTO ALIMENTARIO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia Nervosa is classified as an eating disorder under the broader category of Eating Disorders (TCA)</data>
      <data key="d10">bbb0b98043e40738bce354afe3de265c</data>
      <data key="d11">8979af32692c4790a30f5172c17028a8</data>
      <data key="d12">8704</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO GREGORIO MARA&#209;&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hospital provides treatment and support for patients suffering from anorexia nervosa</data>
      <data key="d10">ecf27310ce7cbfc335117dafa5d4eefb</data>
      <data key="d11">a8ceac7206ca4b3cbff9ee8df80a819b</data>
      <data key="d12">8705</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="MUJERES ADOLESCENTES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las mujeres adolescentes tienen una prevalencia del 1% para la anorexia nerviosa, lo que indica una relaci&#243;n directa entre este grupo y el trastorno.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">2f064e60dd01462eb73f4c9d77ffca00</data>
      <data key="d12">8706</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="VARONES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aunque los datos son limitados, se estima que los varones tambi&#233;n pueden desarrollar anorexia nerviosa, aunque en menor proporci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">c6ffe95550574fabaedc397d1130353f</data>
      <data key="d12">8707</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="MODELOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los modelos son un grupo profesional que parece estar m&#225;s afectado por la anorexia nerviosa debido a la presi&#243;n para mantener un peso bajo.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">7e28d2ef22d34ec38915f9d735e3b669</data>
      <data key="d12">8708</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="GIMNASTAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los gimnastas son un grupo profesional que se encuentra en riesgo elevado de desarrollar anorexia nerviosa por la presi&#243;n de la imagen corporal.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">0a62be78da4849a0a921529ff996bcd7</data>
      <data key="d12">8709</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TCA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La anorexia nerviosa es una de las categor&#237;as dentro de los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria (TCA).</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">0822be6fded343c0a853a8f3ccc1af81</data>
      <data key="d12">8710</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="MORTALIDAD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mortalidad asociada a la anorexia nerviosa es un indicador de la gravedad de este trastorno dentro de los TCA.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">bfe22f8c0af04a87be64a421e87b7dd2</data>
      <data key="d12">8711</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="FACTORES DE MAL PRON&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los factores de mal pron&#243;stico, como los v&#243;mitos y las conductas purgativas, son relevantes en la evoluci&#243;n de la anorexia nerviosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">c7875293883e4870aba57a82db4b122e</data>
      <data key="d12">8712</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="FACTORES DE BUEN PRON&#211;STICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los factores de buen pron&#243;stico, como el inicio en adolescentes j&#243;venes, son importantes para la recuperaci&#243;n de la anorexia nerviosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">04221ccceb5e95933ff349645c328457</data>
      <data key="d11">631f8ff7a30841d9a0701cd58247dacc</data>
      <data key="d12">8713</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="BULIMIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia nervosa and bulimia nervosa are both classified as eating disorders that significantly impact patients' mental and physical health. These disorders are characterized by unhealthy eating behaviors and body image issues, which can lead to a range of complications. Additionally, anorexia nervosa and bulimia nervosa may exhibit overlapping symptoms, further complicating their diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48,7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe,e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d11">4d2e8a207fee438cacfe366f7e81d1d1</data>
      <data key="d12">8714</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TRASTORNO POR ATRAC&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anorexia nerviosa and trastorno por atrac&#243;n both involve episodes of binge eating but differ in compensatory behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d10">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d11">b73057ee02b34ac48733a4491b6887ca</data>
      <data key="d12">8715</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="GASTROPARESIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gastroparesis is a common complication that arises when significant weight loss occurs in patients with anorexia nerviosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">7cc3d3c5826ce81977ed8ad725e1ddbe</data>
      <data key="d11">33f397718af74c21856623f56b83d2d7</data>
      <data key="d12">8716</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TC">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tomograf&#237;a Computarizada is often used to assess the physical health of patients with Anorexia Nervosa</data>
      <data key="d10">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d11">974f67400a824097acfa7095a3888089</data>
      <data key="d12">8717</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="RM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Resonancia Magn&#233;tica is utilized to evaluate neurological changes in patients suffering from Anorexia Nervosa</data>
      <data key="d10">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d11">c952466faa4e45468bcdcb9b10d8e294</data>
      <data key="d12">8718</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Educational institutions may provide resources and support for individuals recovering from Anorexia Nervosa</data>
      <data key="d10">e165a1c74230c4f9f29f883df45e4c8c</data>
      <data key="d11">93f62b6819f647a6b8a9568b3d718694</data>
      <data key="d12">8719</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="GHRELIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ghrelin levels are elevated in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, indicating a negative energy balance</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">f415e7d35e1e42228bbc80bcda8ace44</data>
      <data key="d12">8720</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="LEPTIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Leptin levels are low in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, correlating with body weight</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">2724fb89a56f4d7aa7e977d1726ac0fa</data>
      <data key="d12">8721</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="GROWTH HORMONE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Growth Hormone levels are elevated in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, but IGF-1 levels are low due to resistance</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">12f866818653442085cbe937e868867c</data>
      <data key="d12">8722</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="INSULIN">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin levels are low in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa, indicating metabolic changes</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">1718c6d940ca4ae490f161e3cfdb0f3b</data>
      <data key="d12">8723</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="HYPOTHALAMUS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hypothalamus is responsible for the dysregulation leading to amenorrhea in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">39f7b9ad82734e6da98c45c1049f527c</data>
      <data key="d12">8724</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="ESTROGENS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Estrogen production decreases in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa due to weight loss</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">033179f5fec14c1caf1374ad63dfe881</data>
      <data key="d12">8725</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="MENSTRUATION">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Recovery of menstruation is a key indicator of healing in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">9c2f7a5d72b34bd0a4fa9bebe4c9a9f3</data>
      <data key="d12">8726</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="OSTEOPENIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osteopenia can develop in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa due to hormonal changes and malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">691d01dd78ea4db3b182e5bc5be8d31e</data>
      <data key="d12">8727</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="AMENORREA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amenorrhea is a common hormonal manifestation in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">06b6212bec7c442d9b494c964114338f</data>
      <data key="d12">8728</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="DIABETES TIPO 1">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">There is a noted higher prevalence of eating disorders like Anorexia Nerviosa among patients with Type 1 Diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">a0addfbcde1e45cea9429e32accd1186</data>
      <data key="d12">8729</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="T4">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Low-normal levels of T4 are a consequence of malnutrition in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">2603ef26b12d4422b51380e95addd7df</data>
      <data key="d12">8730</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="TSH">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Low TSH levels are indicative of thyroid axis alterations in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">35261a8daa0a4031a444b74c35b9c259</data>
      <data key="d12">8731</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="T3">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Low T3 levels are a metabolic consequence of Anorexia Nerviosa</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">1e68561f709f480aa09f46eda4c24118</data>
      <data key="d12">8732</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="RT3">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated rT3 levels in patients with Anorexia Nerviosa indicate metabolic adaptation to malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">1f9d0f4850dde2dbd335969b016fc359</data>
      <data key="d11">f8e6f9f358ed4bf6ba049ddbb48eeef8</data>
      <data key="d12">8733</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="AUTONOM&#205;A DEL PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The treatment of anorexia nerviosa often involves complex considerations of patient autonomy and the right to make decisions about one's health</data>
      <data key="d10">bf941c97b0ce9caab6cfbab0a4832c27</data>
      <data key="d11">8f8a8c8569f7469c841232df71761880</data>
      <data key="d12">8734</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOREXIA NERVIOSA" target="SENTENCIA 120/1990">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sentencia 120/1990 includes considerations regarding the treatment of individuals with anorexia nerviosa in the context of prisoners' rights</data>
      <data key="d10">1f8ce52208981fd781dcf23f690f6c3c</data>
      <data key="d11">1051d418b6c145babc706791c264c50b</data>
      <data key="d12">8735</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DENSITOMETR&#205;A &#211;SEA" target="HIPOGONADISMO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone densitometry is important for assessing bone health in males with hypogonadism</data>
      <data key="d10">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d11">c6dff6e314df46ec8389f1dbbaa86ca5</data>
      <data key="d12">8736</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEGUIMIENTO" target="PRODUCTO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Seguimiento is conducted to assess the product's performance and quality during and after production</data>
      <data key="d10">4196233cbb95a9ab194177cc11875e7a</data>
      <data key="d11">9219185f66d24824a469b0a0193a0bfd</data>
      <data key="d12">8737</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI I POLIT&#200;CNIC" target="NUTRICIONES PARENTERALES ADULTOS PROTOCOLIZADAS EN EL HOSPITAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
