      <data key="d9">Infuvite Pedi&#225;trico contains Pyridoxine as part of its composition for pediatric nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">49e05b04f80c53d5f20f7d97f970f5dd</data>
      <data key="d11">09670d924db7448f92013d1dc3ac2846</data>
      <data key="d12">8753</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PIRIDOXINA" target="DEMENTIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Piridoxina is discussed in the context of dementia, but studies show limited benefits for cognitive health</data>
      <data key="d10">b3f35283251afbd3276cf40d7be382c0</data>
      <data key="d11">6c01bdd97b8941d680de737a9bc0be61</data>
      <data key="d12">8754</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HICKMAN" target="CVC">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hickman is a type of CVC used for long-term access</data>
      <data key="d10">781bee94bdbc4f6a3cf4186d6ae0daff</data>
      <data key="d11">db2df7d142ae4d08acf9db0c5e338194</data>
      <data key="d12">8755</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HICKMAN" target="CENTRAL VENOUS CATHETERS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hickman is a type of central venous catheter used for venous access</data>
      <data key="d10">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826</data>
      <data key="d11">f835c2bb30734d5eafc02a79b01f8bbc</data>
      <data key="d12">8756</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PORT-A-CATH" target="CVC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Port-a-Cath is another specific type of central venous catheter used in medical practice.</data>
      <data key="d10">20a97c2641138578710a84f5040c86ef</data>
      <data key="d11">6049d7a2a8ab42f6a5e5cd760b4ed466</data>
      <data key="d12">8757</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VENAS" target="CATAETERES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Catheters are inserted into veins for various medical treatments, including parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">c1ae9c48e1f64748b0cf6ffe04a8fd55</data>
      <data key="d12">8758</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTACI&#211;N PARENTERAL" target="PACIENTE PEDI&#193;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes pedi&#225;tricos pueden necesitar alimentaci&#243;n parenteral cuando no pueden recibir nutrici&#243;n por v&#237;a oral o enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">69de439cf1f8310eaa37927a74d94c6b</data>
      <data key="d11">bd38a0ea112845eb80188182af814495</data>
      <data key="d12">8759</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CATAETERES" target="NEUMOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The insertion of catheters can lead to complications such as pneumothorax</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">54952eebcc164d93a5576c2d4ed1198e</data>
      <data key="d12">8760</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CATAETERES" target="HEMOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The insertion of catheters can lead to complications such as hemothorax</data>
      <data key="d10">9ee81e7e8558eff462947643e3a64588</data>
      <data key="d11">10d5ee6ecba94bf1a11f973f89300d46</data>
      <data key="d12">8761</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUMOT&#211;RAX" target="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pneumothorax is a complication that critically ill patients may face with central nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">a687eee1e8bfd2d98ce40a14628dd855</data>
      <data key="d11">5a73b29fe7bb4725b8bd0bf99e64c077</data>
      <data key="d12">8762</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUMOT&#211;RAX" target="VENOUS ACCESS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neumot&#243;rax can complicate the placement of venous access devices</data>
      <data key="d10">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826</data>
      <data key="d11">09242ecdc4c7442a9ad82175b37b2c1d</data>
      <data key="d12">8763</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUMOT&#211;RAX" target="CAT&#201;TER CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pneumothorax is a potential complication associated with the use of central catheters</data>
      <data key="d10">67344d72dff60fcb903b258fbca95de5</data>
      <data key="d11">57d0f5da55534a938b8d2180ec8d7bc5</data>
      <data key="d12">8764</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUMOT&#211;RAX" target="CAT&#201;TER VENOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El neumot&#243;rax es una complicaci&#243;n que puede surgir de la inserci&#243;n incorrecta de un cat&#233;ter venoso central.</data>
      <data key="d10">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728</data>
      <data key="d11">646f500ccdb64d81a4a3a8cdb860503a</data>
      <data key="d12">8765</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOT&#211;RAX" target="CAT&#201;TER VENOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El hemot&#243;rax puede ser una complicaci&#243;n de la inserci&#243;n de un cat&#233;ter venoso central si se punciona una arteria.</data>
      <data key="d10">21bd0c4198fa2be0aa931387bd631728</data>
      <data key="d11">5fd766ea89cb4c4abd807158a57d3fd7</data>
      <data key="d12">8766</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="ETANOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ETANOL is used in home parenteral nutrition to prevent catheter-related infections</data>
      <data key="d10">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445</data>
      <data key="d11">71e6462ec2ea4d67a031a0767cf6a5d0</data>
      <data key="d12">8767</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="TAUROLIDINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TAUROLIDINA is also used in home parenteral nutrition to prevent infections</data>
      <data key="d10">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445</data>
      <data key="d11">d0d0ebeaf7a54690a0854c48b32dc86a</data>
      <data key="d12">8768</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="HEPATOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HEPATOPAT&#205;A is a complication that can arise from home parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">7ad48347b2499729451a184bae719445</data>
      <data key="d11">7a403aa33c294634b81bafa22bfee6dc</data>
      <data key="d12">8769</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="SIC">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA, also known as home parenteral nutrition, is a medical intervention frequently utilized to manage patients suffering from Short Bowel Syndrome (SBS). This condition often necessitates the use of home parenteral nutrition for patients to maintain their nutritional needs and overall survival. The approach is critical for individuals with SBS, as it provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the digestive system, which may be compromised in these patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">9f38649a548112c415a1c33a8aa72d68,a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc</data>
      <data key="d11">ad64079609cc45e5bc5ab7a8914cd7a5</data>
      <data key="d12">8770</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="OSTEOMALACIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Home parenteral nutrition can lead to conditions such as osteomalacia due to nutrient deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">8ac39b8f1fad40b589c9317df68148c6</data>
      <data key="d12">8771</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="OSTEOPENIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Home parenteral nutrition can result in osteopenia due to inadequate nutrient absorption.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">c2d8ea109eee4baa9d1c32ab684355bf</data>
      <data key="d12">8772</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients on home parenteral nutrition are at risk of developing osteoporosis due to nutrient deficiencies.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">8534848cb39d4a7fa8dad3907fe26620</data>
      <data key="d12">8773</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="VALORACI&#211;N GLOBAL SUBJETIVA GENERADA POR EL PACIENTE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The VGS-GP is used to assess the nutritional status of patients receiving home parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">f438b4eef6df4a3ba61e4d07c6b4ee5a</data>
      <data key="d12">8774</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="MINI-NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MNA can be used to assess the nutritional status of patients on home parenteral nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ccd7ff955c5b8a333f23f41e34c563a</data>
      <data key="d11">6a62df7290e54d7b92166cc22c215c1b</data>
      <data key="d12">8775</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="POIC">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La POIC a menudo requiere nutrici&#243;n parenteral domiciliaria debido a la incapacidad de los pacientes para alimentarse adecuadamente por v&#237;a oral</data>
      <data key="d10">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d11">0ff71cfb2ac347dc930880d4652b5d8d</data>
      <data key="d12">8776</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La NPD puede incluir la NPP como parte del tratamiento nutricional para pacientes que requieren soporte en casa.</data>
      <data key="d10">40fbc53467b8460d1d2d6bcd0d6dbf2a</data>
      <data key="d11">b13721e39e7341169b2e502a421ad9df</data>
      <data key="d12">8777</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO 12 DE OCTUBRE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre offers home parenteral nutrition services</data>
      <data key="d10">57a5157c4312ac09073e72ad7789ad7c</data>
      <data key="d11">60f97c1ab4e1419eb9aa4129397b0e1b</data>
      <data key="d12">8778</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="FAMILIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The family must be trained to manage home parenteral nutrition effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">0dab18980ece5562db9bbd4a3bb9f9ac</data>
      <data key="d11">60f828729fc54578b7f8de3aaeb630f0</data>
      <data key="d12">8779</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL HOSPITALARIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NPH and NPD are compared in cost-effectiveness studies to determine the most efficient method of providing nutrition to patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">c1fce1d059978d0a9ee9e63f75c8ca98</data>
      <data key="d11">0a44d43a7a3949159db3078bd33283ab</data>
      <data key="d12">8780</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA, also known as NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA, refers to a specific type of nutritional therapy administered at home. This form of nutrition is utilized when ordinary feeding methods are insufficient to meet a patient's dietary needs. It represents a significant advancement in the care of patients requiring nutritional support, particularly in cases where parenteral nutrition (NPD) is necessary. Overall, nutritional therapy provided at home encompasses various methods, with parenteral nutrition being a key component for those who cannot rely on traditional food intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">123ef22fb42b6ade4fa2dda096df8490,4e86ca77481672995a03989d321652bc,efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608</data>
      <data key="d11">702af91388d445eaaab26bced440e22d</data>
      <data key="d12">8781</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="EUROPE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The prevalence of NPD in Europe varied significantly, indicating a regional focus on this treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608</data>
      <data key="d11">ee3bf7d79eb543079540d975a5bf0c0d</data>
      <data key="d12">8782</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="USA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The USA has a history of tracking NPD patients through registries like OASIS and Sustain</data>
      <data key="d10">efc0b55f4e91f02e4708b7cc43c64608</data>
      <data key="d11">1acdb09f6a5a4c8683b29e62f2df30e6</data>
      <data key="d12">8783</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="EUROS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The costs of parenteral nutritional support are similarly evaluated in euros</data>
      <data key="d10">0d083c309fb6f4d0d16c0e2b23ea5c8b</data>
      <data key="d11">56ec4fe4c04642c3ba767980855e8756</data>
      <data key="d12">8784</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="QALY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support through parenteral feeding is also evaluated using QALY</data>
      <data key="d10">0d083c309fb6f4d0d16c0e2b23ea5c8b</data>
      <data key="d11">99d1fec6310849e088408f445d49f7e4</data>
      <data key="d12">8785</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="NADYA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NADYA is responsible for the registration and reporting of home parenteral nutrition data in Spain</data>
      <data key="d10">4cf0c8d0f4e711be85d16ee71317aa4e</data>
      <data key="d11">79a51c59393447cdaf601a8a563da05b</data>
      <data key="d12">8786</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA" target="GRUPO NADYA-SENPE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Grupo NADYA-SENPE is responsible for the registration and reporting of home parenteral nutrition data in Spain</data>
      <data key="d10">4cf0c8d0f4e711be85d16ee71317aa4e</data>
      <data key="d11">df31e05f411544e18fc738ef8a82c09d</data>
      <data key="d12">8787</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STAPHYLOCOCCUS" target="BATERIEMIA 0">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Bacteriemia 0 protocol aims to prevent infections caused by Staphylococcus during catheter procedures</data>
      <data key="d10">c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">a672efe2ad90482983df0aa08066d771</data>
      <data key="d12">8788</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLEBSIELLA" target="BATERIEMIA 0">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Bacteriemia 0 protocol aims to prevent infections caused by Klebsiella during catheter procedures</data>
      <data key="d10">c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">aa5a1420aea048b9b4a84b699d50dec0</data>
      <data key="d12">8789</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLEBSIELLA" target="INFECTION">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Klebsiella can lead to infections in patients with invasive devices like catheters</data>
      <data key="d10">be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a</data>
      <data key="d11">6d9c8f488ff440f0b2f28b6b74b6dd0c</data>
      <data key="d12">8790</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANDIDA ALBICANS" target="BATERIEMIA 0">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Bacteriemia 0 protocol aims to prevent infections caused by Candida albicans during catheter procedures</data>
      <data key="d10">c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">70dd9753871644f396baae5df2680da2</data>
      <data key="d12">8791</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANDIDA ALBICANS" target="INFECTION">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Candida albicans can cause infections in immunocompromised patients, particularly those with catheters</data>
      <data key="d10">be901905a9eef428a784ea179931028a</data>
      <data key="d11">11e07acf5d034b709696f00b411e39c8</data>
      <data key="d12">8792</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANDIDA ALBICANS" target="CVC">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Candida albicans can cause infections in patients with CVCs</data>
      <data key="d10">fe3ebcedac0857680bcc85bb58dcb3e1</data>
      <data key="d11">7ffcbcaddf0f4920839e86b252f70950</data>
      <data key="d12">8793</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYNDROME DE REALIMENTACION" target="HIPERGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The syndrome of realimentation can lead to hyperglycemia in malnourished patients</data>
      <data key="d10">c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">134671dda21841ddbfac5268f10f2d77</data>
      <data key="d12">8794</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINA" target="HIPERGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin is a vital hormone used to manage hyperglycemia, particularly in patients receiving nutritional support. It plays a crucial role in controlling elevated blood sugar levels, which can be a significant issue for patients suffering from conditions such as pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d10">88dcf64f61e33adc3702b1ec401e2d4e,c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">3d24dfec21c6449983c12222f45ec301</data>
      <data key="d12">8795</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINA" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin management is crucial for preventing hypoglycemia in patients. Proper management of insulin treatment is essential, as it can lead to hypoglycemia if not monitored effectively. Therefore, careful monitoring of insulin levels is necessary to ensure patient safety and avoid the risks associated with low blood sugar levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">ac2955cad85e541f3b61de2f4df0a3a9,c58712e2ee5757b5175054fcc54f4dd6</data>
      <data key="d11">60e6c0a6aebd47ddae9ba0f8d921829b</data>
      <data key="d12">8796</data>
