    <edge source="COPD" target="CYSTIC FIBROSIS">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) and Cystic Fibrosis are two respiratory conditions that are often studied in relation to one another due to their overlapping respiratory issues. Cystic Fibrosis can lead to complications that may result in the development of COPD, primarily due to chronic lung infections and inflammation associated with the disease. This connection highlights the importance of understanding the interplay between these two conditions in the context of respiratory health.</data>
