      <data key="d9">Brown RO's research is published in the Cochrane Database, contributing to evidence-based healthcare</data>
      <data key="d10">d6a596828c4ca22ce0a49c5ba26b33e8</data>
      <data key="d11">6568d73e8e77416d8659f3d3812c9ad7</data>
      <data key="d12">9203</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICION ARTIFICIAL EN PANCREATITIS AGUDA" target="M. HIG&#211;N BALLESTER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M. Hig&#243;n Ballester co-authored a chapter discussing artificial nutrition in acute pancreatitis.</data>
      <data key="d10">00467cf9f31ccb0046bfd36ff48c4448</data>
      <data key="d11">ded26a3696874c28a2bbbf8c377a9cba</data>
      <data key="d12">9204</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DI&#193;LISIS PERITONEAL" target="ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La di&#225;lisis peritoneal es un tratamiento para la enfermedad renal cr&#243;nica que implica el uso del abdomen para filtrar la sangre</data>
      <data key="d10">169eceabd2bd24183f24faccb2c00088</data>
      <data key="d11">8c0c364862e24d2095fddcf6a426cac6</data>
      <data key="d12">9205</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENZIMAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS" target="PANCREATITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enzimas pancre&#225;ticas may need to be supplemented in patients with pancreatitis cr&#243;nica to aid in digestion</data>
      <data key="d10">67106be274787fd7f400ce3023c33a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">cc0e69965bcb4c4aa6ce5a35047312a0</data>
      <data key="d12">9206</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENZIMAS PANCRE&#193;TICAS" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with EPOC may require pancreatic enzymes if they experience malabsorption, impacting their nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
      <data key="d11">6d40551d485e41b1b07bf9511ae35103</data>
      <data key="d12">9207</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIETA ABSOLUTA" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Absolute diet is often implemented in patients with suspected lymphatic injuries to prevent further complications like quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">ed38755c35ea441fb6fbb5039eadbc09</data>
      <data key="d12">9208</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIETA L&#205;QUIDA" target="DIETA SEMIL&#205;QUIDA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DIETA L&#205;QUIDA and DIETA SEMIL&#205;QUIDA are two stages in a dietary progression. DIETA L&#205;QUIDA serves as the initial phase, typically lasting between 24 to 72 hours, during which individuals consume only liquid foods. Following this phase, DIETA SEMIL&#205;QUIDA is introduced, which incorporates foods with a greater consistency than those allowed in the liquid diet. This progression allows for a gradual transition to more solid foods, facilitating the adaptation of the digestive system.</data>
      <data key="d10">4b19145e0977ee48b7132c9915d8c284,4d74cee5793710b781c0b83db2f27209</data>
      <data key="d11">45824230ad844c4e92b422acd2006640</data>
      <data key="d12">9209</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HIPERPROLACTINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cirrosis hep&#225;tica puede disminuir el aclaramiento de prolactina, contribuyendo a la hiperprolactinemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b6e6d589cd4e83086e44c77205b3740</data>
      <data key="d11">05e11b609e6f420a88cd28cc3101b0d3</data>
      <data key="d12">9210</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="SONDA DE GASTROSTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis can complicate the placement of a gastrostomy tube, leading to potential risks</data>
      <data key="d10">f7b4cba3bbdeec64513c036fd4166835</data>
      <data key="d11">7a7e27f7389a49cba5aaeceaf762d4fb</data>
      <data key="d12">9211</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic liver disease can lead to hepatic cirrhosis as a severe complication.</data>
      <data key="d10">9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f</data>
      <data key="d11">9c33098327784eb09bb2f6344ae48848</data>
      <data key="d12">9212</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HIPERTENSI&#211;N PORTAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA and HIPERTENSI&#211;N PORTAL are closely related medical conditions. Cirrhosis of the liver can lead to the development of portal hypertension, which is a complication that affects blood flow and pressure in the portal vein. This condition contributes to the accumulation of fluids in the body, a common issue associated with cirrhosis. Thus, portal hypertension serves as a significant factor in the progression and complications of cirrhosis hep&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d10">84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4,9426220ccd162a5796b1bb2cb373e29f</data>
      <data key="d11">aac1b5b1c719459e8b963dacab811539</data>
      <data key="d12">9213</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS B (VHB)">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatitis B virus is a significant cause of cirrhosis, establishing a direct relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">738149d63846496ca9d2bd9e40e2295f</data>
      <data key="d12">9214</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS C (VHC)">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatitis C virus is another major cause of cirrhosis, indicating a strong connection</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">3925e2373fad4038b44e90b85197a010</data>
      <data key="d12">9215</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Wilson's disease can lead to cirrhosis, establishing a connection between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">8794316c97704265903ca3e037c35d35</data>
      <data key="d12">9216</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HEMOCRMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis can also lead to cirrhosis, indicating a relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">71dd228326087dc7aaa0d310d49b6f42</data>
      <data key="d11">d639607bbcc2440299055b462a192aa5</data>
      <data key="d12">9217</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis can result in ascitis quilosa due to liver dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">5e206838ac3e4f7b97d503a79260ddc9</data>
      <data key="d12">9218</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="INSUFICIENCIA CARDIACA CONGESTIVA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambas condiciones requieren una restricci&#243;n diet&#233;tica de sodio para su manejo</data>
      <data key="d10">84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4</data>
      <data key="d11">05d3f8c0721a4aeba2c35e20c89c4f83</data>
      <data key="d12">9219</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ENFERMEDAD RENAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambas condiciones requieren una restricci&#243;n de sal para manejar la acumulaci&#243;n de l&#237;quidos</data>
      <data key="d10">84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4</data>
      <data key="d11">ef0745cdc581404f9b290731b92e3db8</data>
      <data key="d12">9220</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HIPOALBUMINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoalbuminemia es un factor que contribuye a la acumulaci&#243;n de l&#237;quidos en la cirrosis hep&#225;tica</data>
      <data key="d10">84b542fb745825398f17e4f8f4756cb4</data>
      <data key="d11">e91a159eba7644b0822013c9c33b39be</data>
      <data key="d12">9221</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ELASTOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elastography is used to evaluate liver fibrosis, which can be a consequence of untreated hereditary hemochromatosis leading to cirrhosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d11">4d292de074734d33b30a5ff7eba496d4</data>
      <data key="d12">9222</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="FLEBOTOM&#205;AS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Phlebotomies are critical in preventing the progression to liver cirrhosis in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d11">d43c3bae28e944dc89061ce654347c2f</data>
      <data key="d12">9223</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="CARCINOMA HEPATOCELULAR">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis of the liver increases the risk of developing hepatocellular carcinoma in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">9610fe47fea8bd5de48277db4233764c</data>
      <data key="d11">df7f5c1fd0884f0a9bc92decfaa2cec2</data>
      <data key="d12">9224</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HEMOCROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis can lead to cirrhosis due to the accumulation of excess iron in the liver over time</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">a3ee0eb795804380b881e28d5274a705</data>
      <data key="d12">9225</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="ALFA-FETOPROTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alfa-fetoprote&#237;na levels are monitored in patients with cirrhosis to assess the risk of hepatocarcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">3cb5bf81a6454554bef47900a1f8db6e</data>
      <data key="d12">9226</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS B">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatitis B virus infection can lead to cirrhosis of the liver</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">304268b088bd418bae0e1ace8be82c5d</data>
      <data key="d12">9227</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="VIRUS DE HEPATITIS C">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatitis C virus infection is a major cause of cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">0be1872c12ba4627a8319829bb348b42</data>
      <data key="d12">9228</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="HIPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Wilson's disease can lead to parathyroid dysfunction, contributing to hypocalcemia</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">087ba2b1615d472ba88e0aab4c159fa3</data>
      <data key="d12">9229</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="HEMOCROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad de Wilson and hemochromatosis both involve dietary restrictions related to minerals</data>
      <data key="d10">66bc37c9c52956b468bccf2ef89662de</data>
      <data key="d11">9f72b7f33648495db7ad197176ed4692</data>
      <data key="d12">9230</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="MUTACI&#211;N DEL GEN ATP7B">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutaci&#243;n del gen ATP7B is directly associated with the development of Enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">4216916ebab948061d2dca4afe7e1e84</data>
      <data key="d11">5ec478b848154b4c8e03e3c04d108bbe</data>
      <data key="d12">9231</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="MUTACI&#211;N DEL GEN ATP7A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutaci&#243;n del gen ATP7A is related to genetic disorders affecting copper metabolism, including Enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">4216916ebab948061d2dca4afe7e1e84</data>
      <data key="d11">e1baee4bbc4141319ee99bac7e9bd56a</data>
      <data key="d12">9232</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="COPPER">
      <data key="d8">20.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad de Wilson is a disorder characterized by the abnormal accumulation of copper in the body. Copper metabolism plays a crucial role in this condition, as excess copper accumulation is the primary cause of Wilson's disease. The disorder arises due to the body's inability to properly regulate copper levels, leading to toxic buildup, which can result in various health complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">4216916ebab948061d2dca4afe7e1e84,d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849,d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550</data>
      <data key="d11">183542e81522498389e22345c46b709c</data>
      <data key="d12">9233</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="ATP7B">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Wilson's disease is a genetic disorder caused by mutations in the ATP7B gene. These mutations result in the body's inability to properly regulate copper, leading to its accumulation. This excessive copper buildup can cause various health issues, affecting multiple organs and systems.</data>
      <data key="d10">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d11">f7d7d3a6099f44519c697c2acc5bbaa8</data>
      <data key="d12">9234</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="INSTITUTO DE MEDICINA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Instituto de Medicina proporciona recomendaciones sobre la ingesta de cobre, que es relevante para la enfermedad de Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d10">d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849</data>
      <data key="d11">7c05063ef920452d999a9783bb3e6624</data>
      <data key="d12">9235</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CERULOPLASMINA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad de Wilson es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica caracterizada por la acumulaci&#243;n excesiva de cobre en el organismo. Un componente clave en el diagn&#243;stico y manejo de esta enfermedad es la ceruloplasmina, que act&#250;a como un reactante afectado por la enfermedad. Los niveles de ceruloplasmina son cruciales para el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad de Wilson, ya que suelen estar bajos en los pacientes que padecen esta condici&#243;n. Adem&#225;s, la ceruloplasmina sirve como un indicador de los dep&#243;sitos de cobre en el cuerpo, lo que la convierte en un elemento esencial para evaluar la gravedad y el progreso de la enfermedad.</data>
      <data key="d10">d6bd9fbceb166872651dd2deade92849,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">4c7df880cb7846c285f05fc157064ebf</data>
      <data key="d12">9236</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CUPROPLASMINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad de Wilson se relaciona con niveles bajos de ceruloplasmina, afectando el metabolismo del cobre</data>
      <data key="d10">232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903</data>
      <data key="d11">db443c170efb489a832481b48ad1457c</data>
      <data key="d12">9237</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cirrosis puede ser una complicaci&#243;n de la enfermedad de Wilson debido a la acumulaci&#243;n de cobre</data>
      <data key="d10">232591ff32b33e56e95717d4582a5903</data>
      <data key="d11">2fc4a4de9f404f81b04ac46d40340b8c</data>
      <data key="d12">9238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="ATP7A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ATP7A is related to copper metabolism disorders, which can also be involved in Wilson's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d11">3124a8a8ea134a33a8d399b38646c45d</data>
      <data key="d12">9239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Wilson's disease, also known as Enfermedad de Wilson, is a genetic disorder characterized by the abnormal accumulation of copper in the body, particularly in the liver (h&#237;gado). The liver serves as a primary site for this copper accumulation, which leads to significant damage and dysfunction of the organ. As a result, individuals with Wilson's disease may experience severe liver-related health issues due to the toxic effects of excess copper.</data>
      <data key="d10">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">ef0f108bdfef41e9ba2aff9d0b550ebc</data>
      <data key="d12">9240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="C&#211;RNEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The cornea is affected in Wilson's disease due to copper deposits</data>
      <data key="d10">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d11">c856c2e6e8fb4f1ca701f18a5a005867</data>
      <data key="d12">9241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="RI&#209;ONES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The kidneys are impacted by Wilson's disease due to copper accumulation</data>
      <data key="d10">071b24f95071bec88fffa3ee7cbcde41</data>
      <data key="d11">01de8084428f4248b66dc2a14ffc8f01</data>
      <data key="d12">9242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="AASLD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La AASLD emite recomendaciones para el diagn&#243;stico y tratamiento de la Enfermedad de Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d10">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d11">36f2e04073b64b88a122927df85d979c</data>
      <data key="d12">9243</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="EASL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La EASL proporciona directrices para el manejo de la Enfermedad de Wilson.</data>
      <data key="d10">5310010ed05fb1b56f667b44eb14106d</data>
      <data key="d11">ad87b285a20a462ba67742fdaf0b2068</data>
      <data key="d12">9244</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="D-PENICILAMINA">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "Enfermedad de Wilson" is a genetic disorder that leads to excessive accumulation of copper in the body, which can cause serious health issues. "D-Penicilamina" is the first-line medication used to treat this condition. It functions by removing the excess copper from the body, thereby helping to manage the symptoms and complications associated with Wilson's disease. D-Penicilamina is recognized as a key treatment for effectively handling this disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550,ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">3292899b930b46438712baa83ea372a1</data>
      <data key="d12">9245</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="KAYSER-FLEISCHER RING">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El anillo de Kayser-Fleischer es un signo cl&#237;nico importante en el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">0219cc4bf72b4074bb9e93fef8952f33</data>
      <data key="d12">9246</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="HEPATOMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hepatomegalia es un s&#237;ntoma com&#250;n en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">b47fc9d5405e4e4289f1e165fcf94fca</data>
      <data key="d12">9247</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="OSTEOMALACIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La osteomalacia puede ser una complicaci&#243;n de la enfermedad de Wilson debido a la alteraci&#243;n en el metabolismo del cobre</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">497f14d964b54cf796945fbd472ac70a</data>
      <data key="d12">9248</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="RAQUITISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El raquitismo puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson, afectando el desarrollo &#243;seo</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">389dffc53735441c8eab66feb85d1543</data>
      <data key="d12">9249</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La osteoporosis es una complicaci&#243;n que puede surgir en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">e0b5142b14e04949834cc87a79470b16</data>
      <data key="d12">9250</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="POLIARTRITIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La poliartritis puede ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado a la enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">314400928bc74a5b8be34f2b52ee901c</data>
      <data key="d12">9251</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="FRACTURAS ESPONT&#193;NEAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las fracturas espont&#225;neas pueden ocurrir en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson debido a la debilidad &#243;sea</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">b58909dc78c6452fb18b439712ad94bd</data>
      <data key="d12">9252</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CALCIFICACIONES ARTICULARES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las calcificaciones articulares pueden ser una manifestaci&#243;n de la enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">764a379642b44058b3d359c6f809da82</data>
      <data key="d12">9253</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CUPREMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles de cupremia son fundamentales para el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad de Wilson, ya que indican la acumulaci&#243;n de cobre en el cuerpo</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">31b378597a814789b3bedfe2eade2bba</data>
      <data key="d12">9254</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="CUCURRIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cupruria se utiliza para evaluar la eliminaci&#243;n de cobre en pacientes con enfermedad de Wilson, siendo un indicador clave</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">34ee27907cb6462babf40bb2b8f2bc94</data>
      <data key="d12">9255</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="BIOPSIA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La biopsia hep&#225;tica puede confirmar la presencia de dep&#243;sitos de cobre en el h&#237;gado, lo que es crucial para el diagn&#243;stico de la enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">ea816809115cc37c571bd36191042123</data>
      <data key="d11">ebf8568a357f4e4cb3f29691e223c7c0</data>
      <data key="d12">9256</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="SYPRINE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Syprine es un medicamento utilizado como tratamiento alternativo para la enfermedad de Wilson</data>
      <data key="d10">d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550</data>
      <data key="d11">cc9e5e0354f9441087c4f85c961ea108</data>
      <data key="d12">9257</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="TRIENTINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Enfermedad de Wilson, also known as Wilson's disease, is a genetic disorder that leads to excessive accumulation of copper in the body, causing various health issues. Trientina, or trientine, is utilized as an alternative treatment for patients suffering from Wilson's disease, particularly for those who are unable to tolerate D-penicillamine, a more commonly used medication. Trientine serves as a viable treatment option for managing Wilson's disease, providing an important alternative for patients with specific sensitivities to other therapies.</data>
      <data key="d10">d750228cb05d1651c8df327308bdc550,ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">733bab940cb34311a30e885eb8e5d5f8</data>
      <data key="d12">9258</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="ASOCIACI&#211;N ESPA&#209;OLA DE FAMILIARES Y ENFERMOS DE WILSON">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The association provides support and resources for those affected by Wilson's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">e0843ef22a05468d93c9f42a665f4808</data>
      <data key="d12">9259</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="ACETATO DE ZINC">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acetato de zinc is utilized in the treatment of Wilson's disease to manage copper levels</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">d6d6d6b194944c75a7ee8b2edddb91a0</data>
      <data key="d12">9260</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="S&#205;NDROME DE HEMOL&#205;TICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemolytic syndrome can develop as a result of the complications associated with Wilson's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">5d0c0dadc80e4594bd54893bbb36f0e9</data>
      <data key="d12">9261</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="METALOTIONE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Metallothioneins are involved in the body's response to excess copper in Wilson's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">b554a6ed3f0d4893b2ddef3bca349afe</data>
      <data key="d12">9262</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="QUINOLONAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Quinolones may interact with treatments for Wilson's disease, affecting copper absorption</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">9b8a7352d3a140eeacc185b1295d21b0</data>
      <data key="d12">9263</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE WILSON" target="TETRACICLINAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tetracyclines can interact with Wilson's disease treatments, impacting copper metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">ed4179754d9e9ed3a2971c762ec54390</data>
      <data key="d11">c299bfccfa264e1dbc346ec4f46ff9ca</data>
      <data key="d12">9264</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="COPPER">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Copper and hemochromatosis are related as both involve trace element metabolism and can lead to health complications</data>
      <data key="d10">5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5</data>
      <data key="d11">3270581517ab41389484743062687bbe</data>
      <data key="d12">9265</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="NUTRITIONAL NEEDS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional needs must be carefully managed in individuals with hemochromatosis to prevent iron overload</data>
      <data key="d10">5cab61b11d03ef705141159d100ae7c5</data>
      <data key="d11">9a1594d04bc54a7fa21a5b443899d048</data>
      <data key="d12">9266</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis can lead to endocrine dysfunction, which may affect calcium metabolism and mimic symptoms of Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">14b38d1337b542fcae35d0dd55c33895</data>
      <data key="d12">9267</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="PTH">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hemocromatosis puede causar destrucci&#243;n de las gl&#225;ndulas paratiroides, resultando en niveles bajos de PTH</data>
      <data key="d10">1d2e960cc2c2980890a657d98fab39b6</data>
      <data key="d11">f7c2c9a7c43444f691a7e7b7c3336feb</data>
      <data key="d12">9268</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis can lead to dysfunction of the parathyroid glands, causing hypoparathyroidism</data>
      <data key="d10">18f04b0302d49a339210d54d9cc55cd3</data>
      <data key="d11">289fe9dd33984e70b5a7951875c6e538</data>
      <data key="d12">9269</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="DEFICIENCIA DE HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos eventos est&#225;n relacionados con problemas de absorci&#243;n de hierro en el organismo, aunque la deficiencia de hierro es m&#225;s com&#250;n y la hemocromatosis es una acumulaci&#243;n patol&#243;gica</data>
      <data key="d10">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d11">9ca5348f12194f6c97c44ac8f26bb015</data>
      <data key="d12">9270</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="GEN HFE">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis is a hereditary condition primarily caused by mutations in the HFE gene. The HFE gene plays a crucial role in the regulation of iron absorption in the body, and its mutations lead to the development of hereditary hemochromatosis. This genetic disorder results in excessive iron accumulation, which can cause various health complications if left untreated.</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d11">9dafe73801bf4bc385ac3f0ec4223da3</data>
      <data key="d12">9271</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="MUTACI&#211;N C282Y">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mutaci&#243;n C282Y en el gen HFE es la causa m&#225;s frecuente de hemocromatosis tipo 1</data>
      <data key="d10">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d11">6689968cc7e84603a1ee6eba5b55644c</data>
      <data key="d12">9272</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="MUTACI&#211;N H63D">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mutaci&#243;n H63D puede contribuir a la hemocromatosis cuando se presenta junto con la mutaci&#243;n C282Y</data>
      <data key="d10">49058309baf3bb1fadf8956dd9ed0e89</data>
      <data key="d11">7e74d0fe594a47159506a143c5c12c4e</data>
      <data key="d12">9273</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="HEPCIDINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepcidin regulates iron absorption and is involved in the pathophysiology of hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">f023ab0fb1e8401b9c6bb8e87996ad8f</data>
      <data key="d12">9274</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="DMT1">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DMT1 is responsible for the absorption of iron, which is increased in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">d181c4520b5c4e3bbc43985dc9217f9f</data>
      <data key="d12">9275</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="FERRITINA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ferritin stores excess iron in the body, which is relevant in the context of hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">157dfb44a32a440d9f1a5b115bb7247a</data>
      <data key="d12">9276</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="FERROPORTINA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ferroportin is involved in the release of iron into the bloodstream, which is affected in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">f1b0f3d822014560a35a514ec1010223</data>
      <data key="d12">9277</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="HFE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in HFE are linked to hereditary hemochromatosis, affecting iron regulation</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">e7ebdecbe86846b395c4678b332c863c</data>
      <data key="d12">9278</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="MACR&#211;FAGOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Macrophages play a role in iron metabolism and are involved in the pathology of hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">79524f18828a4a53a43612f03864ba1f</data>
      <data key="d12">9279</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis is a condition characterized by excessive iron accumulation in the body, with the liver being a primary site for iron deposition. The liver is the primary organ affected by hemochromatosis, as it experiences significant iron accumulation, leading to potential damage and dysfunction.</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a,45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">e0019fed375947db9083c7920c5381a5</data>
      <data key="d12">9280</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="P&#193;NCREAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pancreas can be affected by iron overload in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">d7567468ba944d75b163dd093efb2ec8</data>
      <data key="d12">9281</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="CORAZ&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The heart can suffer from complications due to iron accumulation in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">47d002d1d70d4777b6a003a6d37e5c0c</data>
      <data key="d12">9282</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="ARTICULACIONES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Joints can be impacted by iron overload in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">4b03def047dc4442b49dc1c437afe5e3</data>
      <data key="d12">9283</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="HIP&#211;FISIS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pituitary gland may be affected by iron accumulation in hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">bcb01c96d5704766997f2c836e0901c6</data>
      <data key="d12">9284</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="C282Y">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The C282Y mutation is a genetic factor that contributes to the development of hereditary hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">8bd6782cfbd84085a626ed439f4c74b8</data>
      <data key="d12">9285</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="S65C">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The S65C mutation is associated with increased iron absorption and can exacerbate conditions of hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">45921035725d6b94d451399b0dac4079</data>
      <data key="d11">2982d53f0d3d4256b55a0d615c5df136</data>
      <data key="d12">9286</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="DIETA CONTROLADA EN HIERRO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A controlled iron diet is recommended for managing hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">3789d2bbf53646e6bf98cb2aa7057cb5</data>
      <data key="d12">9287</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="FLEBOTOM&#205;AS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Phlebotomy is a primary treatment for reducing excess iron in patients with hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">2eeab2238556165bbea897f24c5b1c7a</data>
      <data key="d11">dbb90f1f9a1243da96548659b6917f0a</data>
      <data key="d12">9288</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEMOCROMATOSIS" target="WILSON'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemochromatosis and Wilson's disease are both genetic disorders that affect metal metabolism in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">41a33a13610bbae73208f0d201781724</data>
      <data key="d11">ea6f3024841842a996983d09ab84c37d</data>
      <data key="d12">9289</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="HIPERLIPIDEMIA FAMILIAR COMBINADA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiperlipidemia familiar combinada est&#225; relacionada con la sobreproducci&#243;n de lipoprote&#237;nas en el h&#237;gado</data>
      <data key="d10">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d11">32cde39affa14854a45ce7593c748e61</data>
      <data key="d12">9290</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="LIPOPROTE&#205;NAS DE MUY BAJA DENSIDAD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El h&#237;gado produce lipoprote&#237;nas de muy baja densidad (VLDL) que transportan triglic&#233;ridos en la sangre</data>
      <data key="d10">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d11">8f6f8a2644ab4669a7a577ef914a7b99</data>
      <data key="d12">9291</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="VLDL">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The h&#237;gado, or liver, plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism by synthesizing Very Low-Density Lipoprotein (VLDL). VLDL is responsible for transporting triglycerides and cholesterol to various tissues throughout the body, facilitating the distribution of these essential lipids.</data>
      <data key="d10">8938669dda86a6eafe0882ea036408c1,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
      <data key="d11">32ca26335b2b4c8e83ab4d854b2b0b36</data>
      <data key="d12">9292</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El tama&#241;o del h&#237;gado se eval&#250;a y puede reducirse significativamente con una dieta antes de la cirug&#237;a bari&#225;trica</data>
      <data key="d10">de5f304890ba39f7c9e3d5c0201bc247</data>
      <data key="d11">3dc84d77932d48f7a3b07a6dcc57e532</data>
      <data key="d12">9293</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GLUC&#211;GENO">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El h&#237;gado es un &#243;rgano vital que desempe&#241;a un papel crucial en el metabolismo de los carbohidratos. Almacena gluc&#243;geno, que es una forma de energ&#237;a, y lo convierte en glucosa para mantener los niveles de energ&#237;a durante el ejercicio. Adem&#225;s, el h&#237;gado regula los niveles de glucosa en sangre, liberando glucosa cuando es necesario para asegurar un suministro constante de energ&#237;a al cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d10">439efa4d64a3de0b12975ea727c939f4,490f5e3c6dbf3754eee50c52154da09a</data>
      <data key="d11">865cc42abcf94442aac8c601fcbf9237</data>
      <data key="d12">9294</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GLUC&#211;GENO STORAGE DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver is primarily affected in Glycogen Storage Disease due to its role in glycogen storage and metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">f0bfe278aa9f43f4bc9d056de67a5b96</data>
      <data key="d11">4039a4542c904feda3394e5d1e272946</data>
      <data key="d12">9295</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactosa is primarily metabolized in the h&#237;gado, where it is converted into glucose</data>
      <data key="d10">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d</data>
      <data key="d11">483cce030179450d87bf42e241e068de</data>
      <data key="d12">9296</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GALACTOSEMIA CL&#193;SICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El h&#237;gado es el &#243;rgano donde se observa la actividad enzim&#225;tica relacionada con la galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d10">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d11">b250da42956842f2b183617ef834e77a</data>
      <data key="d12">9297</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GALACTOSEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver is a key organ involved in the metabolism of galactose, and its GALT activity is crucial for diagnosing galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">689aa4939b33472087ac5cd75111891c</data>
      <data key="d12">9298</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GALK1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The GALK1 gene is expressed in the liver, which is crucial for galactose metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad</data>
      <data key="d11">29aa115f10144d1bae7136276669cd45</data>
      <data key="d12">9299</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="CIRROSIS">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis is a condition that severely affects the liver's function and structure, leading to irreversible damage. It directly impacts the liver's ability to perform its essential functions, resulting in significant health complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,ea1d430dfc773b669eec18759441b31a</data>
      <data key="d11">24bb30ce25ce4f0e9095cae41e4a1ecb</data>
      <data key="d12">9300</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="PACIENTE CIRR&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El paciente cirr&#243;tico padece una enfermedad del h&#237;gado que afecta su estado nutricional</data>
      <data key="d10">c51fc76876398ca4252c2585fb1dbb6b</data>
      <data key="d11">048e190a2f3e4c139dcc0331811540a1</data>
      <data key="d12">9301</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="PACIENTES CIRR&#211;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver's function is critical in the health and nutritional status of cirrhotic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">4296623c2da263830137344ead99ba92</data>
      <data key="d11">5e9f033329b347cbb4677813b57093a6</data>
      <data key="d12">9302</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver is the main organ affected by glucogenosis de tipo I, where glycogen accumulates</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d11">f57ebca452004760841a8639a4827322</data>
      <data key="d12">9303</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="ENFERMEDAD DE VON GIERKE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver is primarily involved in enfermedad de Von Gierke, showing glycogen storage issues</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d11">e266ed0140064aee860464ec5f5e21d9</data>
      <data key="d12">9304</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="VON GIERKE TYPE IA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver is the primary organ affected in Von Gierke Type Ia, which may lead to severe metabolic complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d11">955bc792a2ce4c34baac9515999a1b42</data>
      <data key="d12">9305</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="TCM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCM are rapidly oxidized in the liver, producing acetyl-CoA</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">58d42d5a7b24492abc94c4c5ab2f03c1</data>
      <data key="d12">9306</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="TCL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCL are metabolized in the liver, which plays a key role in fat metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">053f42abfa7c45c9826ce1ee68255c3c</data>
      <data key="d12">9307</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="CUPROENZIMAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cuproenzyme activity in the liver is essential for copper metabolism and detoxification processes</data>
      <data key="d10">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">9dae1aa0468b4e939875c45e7d947d75</data>
      <data key="d12">9308</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="ATP7B">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ATP7B is involved in the transport of copper in the liver, regulating its levels</data>
      <data key="d10">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d11">9da81d67d1034717ac00701854313424</data>
      <data key="d12">9309</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="SUPER&#211;XIDO DISMUTASA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Superoxide dismutase is present in the liver and plays a role in protecting liver cells from oxidative damage</data>
      <data key="d10">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d11">1b34efbef84e4af6af8dcdf19246e2d5</data>
      <data key="d12">9310</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="METALOTIONEINAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Metallothioneins in the liver help in the storage and detoxification of excess copper</data>
      <data key="d10">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36</data>
      <data key="d11">affe739723dc42fb83ed77a1643db657</data>
      <data key="d12">9311</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El h&#237;gado es el principal &#243;rgano donde se produce el &#225;cido &#250;rico a partir del metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">5aad373899774d418581be752bc59959</data>
      <data key="d12">9312</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="ENFERMEDAD VENOCLUSIVA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad venoclusiva hep&#225;tica afecta al h&#237;gado, causando s&#237;ntomas como ictericia y hepatomegalia</data>
      <data key="d10">84aebe8ee79b67a8fe16d40b6c07331d</data>
      <data key="d11">9b770c5e96fa42338694cd1666f42fb3</data>
      <data key="d12">9313</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="C-REACTIVA PROTE&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The liver synthesizes C-reactive protein, which is a key marker of inflammation</data>
      <data key="d10">d0fb942f9036630b4cf0727dea808fd2</data>
      <data key="d11">1cce9d8fa08c4bf6b36e43b1ab54f557</data>
      <data key="d12">9314</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="H&#205;GADO" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">H&#237;gado is a rich source of iron and vitamins, making it beneficial in pediatric nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">e742c891694171ad455b038f416b7728</data>
      <data key="d11">56054aef874b44deace3ae255174409c</data>
      <data key="d12">9315</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="CREATININA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Creatinine levels can indicate kidney function, which may be compromised in patients with cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d11">e8f09d8ca2554a1ea1ac20d22b2d4313</data>
      <data key="d12">9316</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis is a severe form of liver disease that significantly impacts nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">ecc0b96af9066f424f1c114102063682</data>
      <data key="d11">981f372b003c436c8cb6dcaa50a20c4c</data>
      <data key="d12">9317</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="CHILD-PUGH CLASSIFICATION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Child-Pugh classification is used to assess the prognosis of patients with cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">63cf08481b614b78a962d5d0b7aafb9a</data>
      <data key="d12">9318</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="MELD SCORE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MELD score is utilized to prioritize patients with cirrhosis for liver transplantation</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">5523b17a1e7e436f99d5e47863594907</data>
      <data key="d12">9319</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis is a severe form of liver damage that can develop as a complication of chronic liver disease (enfermedad hep&#225;tica cr&#243;nica). This condition signifies a significant deterioration in liver function, highlighting the serious implications of chronic liver disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503,1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">1e0262df6b2142ffafe58f95bdddca9d</data>
      <data key="d12">9320</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="HEPATOPULMONAR SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatopulmonary syndrome can occur in patients with advanced cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">82145cc0b9fc472faaf99503f7082028</data>
      <data key="d12">9321</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="MIOCARDIOPAT&#205;A CIRR&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhotic cardiomyopathy is associated with liver cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">fcf30db7c7e64c65a2f8eff8bb185f0b</data>
      <data key="d12">9322</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="S&#205;NDROME HEPATORRENAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatorenal syndrome is a serious complication that can arise from cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">95dd8ce5db13400e9e0c6ac937f2a2b4</data>
      <data key="d12">9323</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="ALTERACIONES DE COAGULACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Coagulation disorders are common in patients with cirrhosis due to liver dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">8ed905908a984b7aa0cc2df404e6dff2</data>
      <data key="d12">9324</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ENFERMEDAD HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional support is essential for managing complications associated with cirrhosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1911ce26c118381473eccb438875b29c</data>
      <data key="d11">5e4a5779f00c4e8b9eecd2f5dfbd091d</data>
      <data key="d12">9325</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="TRASPLANTE DE H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cirrosis puede llevar a la necesidad de un trasplante de h&#237;gado debido a la severidad de la enfermedad</data>
      <data key="d10">b4b789f8b1484fea88d0b5c58dfde854</data>
      <data key="d11">8ff8e8d671644da38a5813e16afadb96</data>
      <data key="d12">9326</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="MALABSORCI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cirrosis puede causar malabsorci&#243;n de nutrientes debido a la disfunci&#243;n hep&#225;tica.</data>
      <data key="d10">1290ddd67bed33472ff31398d8699503</data>
      <data key="d11">bbd083dcbd9c4462bfae1802bdf6fdc8</data>
      <data key="d12">9327</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="EHCA">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cirrhosis is a medical condition characterized by the progressive scarring of the liver, which can lead to various complications, including the event known as EHCA (Extrahepatic Cholestasis and Ascites). This condition significantly impacts the nutritional status of individuals, as the liver plays a crucial role in metabolism and nutrient processing. Conversely, EHCA can also arise as a consequence of the progression of cirrhosis, further exacerbating metabolic and nutritional issues. Thus, there is a reciprocal relationship between cirrhosis and EHCA, where each condition can influence the severity and management of the other.</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1,f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d11">bdb6170a6e1c4355a5ca8627dc007edd</data>
      <data key="d12">9328</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional intervention is crucial for managing cirrhosis and improving patient outcomes</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d11">2ac6ed4cc15d4813ab43e1be0b6a1f32</data>
      <data key="d12">9329</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="NEOGLUCONEOGENESIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neoglucogenesis is affected in cirrhosis, as the liver's ability to produce glucose is compromised</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d11">aa85b3e4d14b4d7ca15c27676c166c2e</data>
      <data key="d12">9330</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="HYPERMETABOLISM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypermetabolism is often observed in cirrhosis patients, leading to increased energy expenditure and muscle loss</data>
      <data key="d10">5341a1454aa3fed0eab02f9ce7fea5d1</data>
      <data key="d11">93bcc5f80b2c412bb7d8e6442ca13a9b</data>
      <data key="d12">9331</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="ALBUMIN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumin levels are affected by cirrhosis and are important for assessing nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d11">44a27b4ece084fe4812c02610e2c7b4a</data>
      <data key="d12">9332</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CIRROSIS" target="MUSCLE STRENGTH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Muscle strength is an important prognostic factor in patients with cirrhosis and is assessed to determine nutritional status</data>
      <data key="d10">f7b74dc42fea9d33e4675a41e15975ab</data>
      <data key="d11">334dc59d5a1f4963af27a7f45d178409</data>
