    <edge source="COLON" target="FLORA BACTERIANA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The colon hosts flora bacteriana that ferment undigested carbohydrates, producing beneficial short-chain fatty acids</data>
      <data key="d10">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">a16b0ab1e69e4f448ea5aca3c9dc367a</data>
      <data key="d12">9473</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COLON" target="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota resides in the colon and is essential for metabolic functions</data>
      <data key="d10">235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3</data>
      <data key="d11">8aab8fae311044808e5c42d0b604fbf4</data>
      <data key="d12">9474</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COLON" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The colon plays a crucial role in the absorption of short-chain fatty acids, which are produced through the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates and dietary residues. This process highlights the importance of the colon in the digestive system, as it not only facilitates the absorption of these beneficial fatty acids but also contributes to overall gut health.</data>
      <data key="d10">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9,235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3</data>
      <data key="d11">66eefc5c829241f3bf967cf244ee6c61</data>
      <data key="d12">9475</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COLON" target="INTESTINO DELGADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El colon y el intestino delgado est&#225;n interconectados en el proceso de absorci&#243;n y digesti&#243;n de nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9</data>
      <data key="d11">010ea922522745499014251197a1bf93</data>
      <data key="d12">9476</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COLON" target="V&#193;LVULA ILEOCECAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La v&#225;lvula ileocecal regula el paso de contenido del intestino delgado al colon.</data>
      <data key="d10">06ffde2dc989dcf66c55a8058f4f51d9</data>
      <data key="d11">f8c945f82d2d49998e48aa224db2b9b1</data>
      <data key="d12">9477</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COLON" target="SECRECIONES GASTROINTESTINALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
