      <data key="d11">fc358918f0654712a9e68427eb974bf5</data>
      <data key="d12">9630</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HISTORIA DIET&#201;TICA" target="M&#201;TODOS DE EVALUACI&#211;N DE LA INGESTA DE ALIMENTOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Historia Diet&#233;tica is one of the methods discussed for evaluating food intake</data>
      <data key="d10">0c83fbbd4b26fbfe03a1df6d36025796</data>
      <data key="d11">0094e85a2eea40c4b7e86a9ee85c824e</data>
      <data key="d12">9631</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HISTORIA DIET&#201;TICA" target="DIETOTERAPIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Historia diet&#233;tica is a method used in dietotherapy to gather detailed dietary information for nutritional assessments.</data>
      <data key="d10">f14ec70726a24a574ae5d437903fddb8</data>
      <data key="d11">e201e7bd37384f2aa1dbfa54cb5271a9</data>
      <data key="d12">9632</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HISTORIA DIET&#201;TICA" target="DIETA ESPECIAL/NO CODIFICADA/PERSONALIZADA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Historia Diet&#233;tica is essential for creating a personalized diet plan, as it assesses the patient's usual intake and dietary restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d10">4681d149c863ed06c99b19443f841abd</data>
      <data key="d11">65023edb5eb2485d8cf18cd516481bf8</data>
      <data key="d12">9633</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GASTO ENERG&#201;TICO EN REPOSO" target="PACIENTE ONCOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El gasto energ&#233;tico en reposo puede estar alterado en pacientes oncol&#243;gicos, afectando su nutrici&#243;n y tratamiento</data>
      <data key="d10">d667e6abc204bbfa6aba210705db6d56</data>
      <data key="d11">272d26f7412b4fa7a75e3d4d818bbb58</data>
      <data key="d12">9634</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANTIOXIDANTS" target="NUTRITIONAL GUIDELINES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The role of antioxidants is included in nutritional guidelines as part of dietary recommendations for cardiovascular health</data>
      <data key="d10">a826c03dcc41919d172b2e1ae8eeceb2</data>
      <data key="d11">06ec609b720d4d548eba23967faec7dd</data>
      <data key="d12">9635</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="VITAMINS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ provides guidelines on the administration of vitamins for patients with cystic fibrosis</data>
      <data key="d10">f6135205f57ce2216ab62038ac34a2bb</data>
      <data key="d11">dcbda79ea89a4ba1808d190c189ca87c</data>
      <data key="d12">9636</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="ESSENTIAL FATTY ACIDS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ highlights the deficiency of essential fatty acids in patients with cystic fibrosis and the need for dietary supplementation</data>
      <data key="d10">f6135205f57ce2216ab62038ac34a2bb</data>
      <data key="d11">7cfc20c1e21e419082919f10a175201f</data>
      <data key="d12">9637</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="SAMUEL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Samuel is a patient suffering from FQ, which complicates his nutritional status and diabetes management</data>
      <data key="d10">dc7539b4d637d6dd09963c2564f4f084</data>
      <data key="d11">3eddc732be0541e281c64f50267b3e54</data>
      <data key="d12">9638</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">28.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ and EPOC are both chronic respiratory diseases characterized by inflammation and impaired lung function. These conditions can lead to nutritional deficiencies, significantly impacting the quality of life for affected individuals. Due to their chronic nature, FQ and EPOC necessitate similar monitoring and treatment approaches, including dietary assessments and evaluations of muscle function. Overall, both diseases share commonalities in their management and the challenges they present to patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f,9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d11">f7eaa572fe854d99b32ae8a3f7e927e3</data>
      <data key="d12">9639</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="OLVEIRA C ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Olveira C et al. researched the impact of nutritional status on patients with FQ</data>
      <data key="d10">8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f</data>
      <data key="d11">6efb30aea430401cb72b528b697b0073</data>
      <data key="d12">9640</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="BQ">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ and BQ are both conditions that affect lung function and may require similar diagnostic and treatment strategies. Additionally, they necessitate dietary evaluations and monitoring of muscle function.</data>
      <data key="d10">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">7b17f643ce1a4ce6a22c407221896df4</data>
      <data key="d12">9641</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="EUROPEAN CONSENSUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Consensus provides guidelines for managing patients with FQ</data>
      <data key="d10">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27</data>
      <data key="d11">2c37d492c1b643f0ad1178af308b5c94</data>
      <data key="d12">9642</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="ALBUMIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Albumin levels are monitored in patients with FQ to assess their nutritional status and predict morbidity</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">b265bb8af5324d97a89310925a9d3397</data>
      <data key="d12">9643</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="SELENIUM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Selenium levels may be evaluated in patients with FQ due to its role in metabolism and immune function</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">ddfcc18098d04a2f9da8044bec7ce458</data>
      <data key="d12">9644</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="COPPER">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Copper levels may be assessed in patients with FQ as part of their nutritional evaluation</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">601914c31eea419e85f289240e98fb2f</data>
      <data key="d12">9645</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="HEMOGLOBIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemoglobin levels are monitored in patients with FQ as they can indicate overall health and survival rates</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">0560d686e5c949f69fb6b75d0fb24c70</data>
      <data key="d12">9646</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="VITAMIN K">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ refers to a group of patients whose Vitamin K levels are closely monitored to evaluate their nutritional status and assess their risk of bleeding. In cases where these patients have specific conditions that affect the absorption of Vitamin K, supplementation is recommended to ensure adequate levels of this essential nutrient.</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d11">ba41a5168bff456e91559e9a73fc8b6e</data>
      <data key="d12">9647</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="VITAMIN D">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FQ patients are closely monitored for Vitamin D levels due to the high prevalence of deficiency observed in this group. To address this issue, Vitamin D supplementation is recommended for FQ patients, particularly for those who have low exposure to sunlight, which can further contribute to their deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,d76cb2d50e736da37be7fe2a415a7281</data>
      <data key="d11">c81d4cc1905c4cc7a233aadaa6255c69</data>
      <data key="d12">9648</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="PROTEIN-INDUCED DEFICIT OF VITAMIN K">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PIDVK is used to assess vitamin K status in patients with FQ</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">d3a807151e7c4c5a8afcc64dc1ac49c6</data>
      <data key="d12">9649</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FQ" target="OSTEOCALCIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
