    <edge source="LACTANTES" target="LACTANCIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactancia provides dietary guidelines specifically for lactantes, which refers to infants who are being breastfed. Lactantes are directly related to lactancia, as they represent the group of infants that benefit from these breastfeeding practices and nutritional recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d10">4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d11">3eabf05d05ba4c76b8f2c94797bbce0f</data>
      <data key="d12">10012</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="LIPOFUNDINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglycerides levels need to be monitored in patients receiving LIPOFUNDINA, indicating a relationship in patient care</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07</data>
      <data key="d11">f71649d7169b44ae95d95368081694b4</data>
      <data key="d12">10013</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="SMOFLIPID">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglycerides levels need to be monitored in patients receiving SMOFlipid, indicating a relationship in patient care</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07</data>
      <data key="d11">b28e13964d3541aab533d16428518376</data>
      <data key="d12">10014</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="LIPOPLUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglycerides levels need to be monitored in patients receiving LIPOPLUS, indicating a relationship in patient care</data>
      <data key="d10">44bcef3c5453091f304bd39882ae1a07</data>
      <data key="d11">a98970d4becd47e4ac47beca0f8f5a70</data>
      <data key="d12">10015</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="LIPOPROTE&#205;NAS DE MUY BAJA DENSIDAD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las lipoprote&#237;nas de muy baja densidad (VLDL) son ricas en triglic&#233;ridos y son transportadas en la sangre</data>
      <data key="d10">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d11">e417439c77bc44a99291f83541151374</data>
      <data key="d12">10016</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="LIP&#211;LISIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La lip&#243;lisis es el proceso que descompone los triglic&#233;ridos en &#225;cidos grasos libres, afectando los niveles de l&#237;pidos en el cuerpo</data>
      <data key="d10">e57266facd7498d191a9107e090446e2</data>
      <data key="d11">76e0d6707b374fe3962d3697be90d86c</data>
      <data key="d12">10017</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Familial hypercholesterolemia is associated with normal or low triglyceride levels despite high LDL cholesterol</data>
      <data key="d10">916ad020bd9c528e55001071b4d9530b</data>
      <data key="d11">076b3bac291e43a69a772d26b3cb703c</data>
      <data key="d12">10018</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="QUILOMICRONES">
      <data key="d8">32.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS and QUILOMICRONES are closely related entities in the context of lipid transport within the body. Chylomicrons, also known as quilomicrones, play a crucial role in transporting triglycerides from the intestines to the bloodstream. This process occurs after dietary intake, allowing the quilomicrones to carry triglycerides not only to the bloodstream but also to various tissues throughout the body. Thus, the relationship between TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS and QUILOMICRONES is characterized by the latter's function in facilitating the movement of triglycerides from the digestive system into the circulatory system and subsequently to other bodily tissues.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7,5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10,8938669dda86a6eafe0882ea036408c1,e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
      <data key="d11">25f23a74c326468590a3a0e37248cc86</data>
      <data key="d12">10019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="VLDL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglic&#233;ridos are a major component of VLDL, which transports them from the liver</data>
      <data key="d10">e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
      <data key="d11">f98ec55263a147a0be1ef736528e1752</data>
      <data key="d12">10020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="TEJIDO ADIPOSO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglic&#233;ridos are stored in adipose tissue as energy reserves</data>
      <data key="d10">e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
      <data key="d11">74c0dd49050e40d7b85c15dbdf47a6fb</data>
      <data key="d12">10021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="LIPASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lipase enzymes hydrolyze triglycerides into free fatty acids and glycerol</data>
      <data key="d10">e55f521d442f8ba50012b67d7051d39f</data>
      <data key="d11">37bf9fc6f51f48b7990e857a1e3f40db</data>
      <data key="d12">10022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alcohol consumption can lead to increased triglyceride levels in the blood, indicating a negative relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">5f7420a865ebf111326e5fc746c66c10</data>
      <data key="d11">3101e8cbed08499288a0b72b7dc5b4ef</data>
      <data key="d12">10023</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="CARDIOVASCULAR SALUD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triglic&#233;ridos levels should be monitored for better cardiovascular health</data>
      <data key="d10">c78125c02ea4d5afdf5cb5ac4baeeb27</data>
      <data key="d11">2639781cbfa747cbb3adb317a92d40fc</data>
      <data key="d12">10024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="HIPERLIPIDEMIA FAMILIAR COMBINADA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiperlipidemia familiar combinada se caracteriza por niveles elevados de triglic&#233;ridos en la sangre, lo que contribuye al riesgo cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d10">ed97532e0b848baf08ee24448e340f98</data>
      <data key="d11">2f3472051fa54addaf7621710e00629b</data>
      <data key="d12">10025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles de triglic&#233;ridos est&#225;n relacionados con el riesgo de desarrollar s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico</data>
      <data key="d10">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704</data>
      <data key="d11">32f465d356d846f298fcdd3441e98003</data>
      <data key="d12">10026</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mediterranean diet is associated with lower triglyceride levels, which is beneficial for cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d10">72d0be9d03c79097f867a8af2e3e89e4</data>
      <data key="d11">63d0a0f320af4a4894fb091e87966d9a</data>
      <data key="d12">10027</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="F&#211;RMULAS RICAS EN GRASA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dietary changes in fat-rich formulas can lead to decreased triglyceride levels in diabetic patients</data>
      <data key="d10">8d1eb00b23450a2f2cb1243ea32aa36f</data>
      <data key="d11">f380ece22c304078a644053ceddbbd3c</data>
      <data key="d12">10028</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="GSDI">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Monitoring triglyceride levels is important for managing health in GSDI patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e</data>
      <data key="d11">a7e6176847404539bc17ab77339dd455</data>
      <data key="d12">10029</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="FRUCTOSE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fructose can be converted into triglycerides when metabolic pathways are saturated</data>
      <data key="d10">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d11">a665d05e92d44cce99cf7f6342d83a57</data>
      <data key="d12">10030</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="AGP-&#937;3">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AGP-&#969;3 has been shown to reduce triglic&#233;ridos levels in the blood</data>
      <data key="d10">41d7db510fc74d3763959481cc15ea20</data>
      <data key="d11">71c418e7de344efbabf4a140c98ddb60</data>
      <data key="d12">10031</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="TCM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCM are a specific type of triglycerides that have unique metabolic properties</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">ee9691d68c704f38ad673ef1f5b5f9a8</data>
      <data key="d12">10032</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="TCL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCL are another type of triglycerides that differ from TCM in their absorption and metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">38ca9be509414d178137ca869c23809d</data>
      <data key="d12">10033</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIGLIC&#201;RIDOS" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Management of EPOC may involve monitoring triglyceride levels as part of overall health and dietary considerations</data>
      <data key="d10">cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
      <data key="d11">6b59f1de51a14a62b82a612c58296a27</data>
      <data key="d12">10034</data>
