    <edge source="CVC" target="TROMBOSIS VENOSA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CVCs, or central venous catheters, are medical devices that can lead to the development of venous thrombosis, particularly in patients who require long-term use, such as children. The presence of a CVC can complicate the condition of venous thrombosis, potentially resulting in further medical issues. Therefore, the use of CVCs is associated with an increased risk of thrombosis venosa, highlighting the need for careful monitoring and management in patients with these devices.</data>
      <data key="d10">1c3eeb30a49c70f750b79e7bc1dfef52,20a97c2641138578710a84f5040c86ef</data>
      <data key="d11">7556e486c0ba4ddfafac68962620fed1</data>
      <data key="d12">10112</data>
