    <edge source="CVC" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CVC, or central venous catheters, are commonly utilized in pediatric nutrition, particularly for administering parenteral nutrition in acute situations. Nutritional therapy in pediatric patients frequently necessitates the use of CVCs for intravenous feeding, highlighting their critical role in ensuring that children receive the necessary nutrients when oral intake is not feasible.</data>
      <data key="d10">222519e556047fafecd61c2964aaaeed,e5313f692c0a8259c93be803a704413c</data>
      <data key="d11">cd47e99918444d1a9840657aedec1dca</data>
      <data key="d12">10124</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CVC" target="UNIDADES DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS">
