    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CEL&#205;ACA" target="MNGIE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad cel&#237;aca must be differentiated from MNGIE</data>
      <data key="d10">b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d11">221737c963e64e5b80d37121b63b793d</data>
      <data key="d12">10194</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CEL&#205;ACA" target="ANEMIA FERROP&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Celiac disease can lead to malabsorption of iron, which can result in iron deficiency anemia</data>
      <data key="d10">6595cec039fe5a2c290eea9ab7e3b2fc</data>
      <data key="d11">bd13175250e944a3879bb6d3d304fb5e</data>
      <data key="d12">10195</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CEL&#205;ACA" target="NEFROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad cel&#237;aca can lead to malabsorption and is associated with an increased risk of kidney stones</data>
      <data key="d10">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d11">c2f5c0da143446e4a0103a2ec1a0b430</data>
      <data key="d12">10196</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CEL&#205;ACA" target="ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alergias alimentarias and enfermedad cel&#237;aca are both related to adverse reactions to food, but they involve different immune responses</data>
      <data key="d10">9d84c9c66c832dd17e7247a6966c2ea1</data>
      <data key="d11">39bc8a9576c44198bebd2c551cf6ac8d</data>
      <data key="d12">10197</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CEL&#205;ACA" target="ALERGIA ALIMENTARIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad cel&#237;aca es considerada una forma de alergia alimentaria que se desencadena por la ingesta de gliadina.</data>
      <data key="d10">693b5721c7fc52c8165c48b580777840</data>
      <data key="d11">335987eb9bb748c488b552e99a857066</data>
      <data key="d12">10198</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="HIPERALDOSTERONISMO FAMILIAR TIPO 3">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El hiperaldosteronismo familiar tipo 3 se asocia con hipertensi&#243;n grave y resistente al tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d10">261db9bb173f461ca4f26fd087d3da2a</data>
      <data key="d11">ef6c0e6fb1274105875012da28b07a14</data>
      <data key="d12">10199</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="SEUDOHIPOALDOSTERONISMO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El seudohipoaldosteronismo puede provocar hipertensi&#243;n debido a la resistencia a la acci&#243;n de los mineralocorticoides.</data>
      <data key="d10">261db9bb173f461ca4f26fd087d3da2a</data>
      <data key="d11">e0f8ee472e13499cb50c71e52fe5ee1c</data>
      <data key="d12">10200</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="HYPERALDOSTERONISM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a common consequence of hyperaldosteronism due to excess aldosterone causing sodium retention and increased blood volume.</data>
      <data key="d10">1cdfccda20ac47427fc4c103ddd87cf3</data>
      <data key="d11">bd77a3f69f9c4529bb57be75e3064ea7</data>
      <data key="d12">10201</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="FEOCROMOCITOMA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIPERTENSI&#211;N and FEOCROMOCITOMA are closely related, as pheochromocytomas can lead to hypertension. This condition arises from the excessive secretion of catecholamines, which are hormones produced by the adrenal glands. Both descriptions highlight that pheochromocytomas are responsible for causing episodes of hypertension due to this overproduction of catecholamines.</data>
      <data key="d10">8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3,c77f2833180015d5264f465f51c441f3</data>
      <data key="d11">ca5502ce36ef4263a753d9ea50ea3353</data>
      <data key="d12">10202</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="NEFROANGIOESCLEROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nefroangioesclerosis can be a consequence of long-term uncontrolled hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">8f5500c9a9e74d855b17365c80375df3</data>
      <data key="d11">2dc54207a175410b88abc2f86801538a</data>
      <data key="d12">10203</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="VAR&#211;N DE 56 A&#209;OS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The 56-year-old male patient has a history of hypertension, which is relevant to his overall health status</data>
      <data key="d10">319591d16b552cff77a5cd56e69c1ca2</data>
      <data key="d11">71c72617c55f4209b3bc6f533229b18d</data>
      <data key="d12">10204</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="DISLIPEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The patient has dislipemia and hypertension, which are often related conditions affecting cardiovascular health</data>
      <data key="d10">3a1d1c4eb34995d440bd72c4b64e3c8d</data>
      <data key="d11">f33f4904d6b84256b34f6511b215cece</data>
      <data key="d12">10205</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's disease can lead to secondary hypertension, necessitating dietary management.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">4ae1238ea6f04d698cacd4bae7990421</data>
      <data key="d12">10206</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipertensi&#243;n puede estar asociada con la litiasis renal y otros trastornos de salud</data>
      <data key="d10">b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb</data>
      <data key="d11">131a7b853ef84ce0905478572f822b94</data>
      <data key="d12">10207</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="NEFROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipertensi&#243;n is linked to metabolic syndrome, which increases the risk of kidney stones</data>
      <data key="d10">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d11">74f241b553cf4d99bade80978a6ba2ee</data>
      <data key="d12">10208</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N" target="TUMORES CARCINOIDES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tumores carcinoides can lead to various syndromes, including those that may affect blood pressure regulation, linking them to hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">47ba8105b81c59f81a9038446898d200</data>
      <data key="d11">83dfc555405d4697955d516de7c1533a</data>
      <data key="d12">10209</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="LACTANCIA MATERNA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breastfeeding can decrease the risk of developing cardiovascular diseases in mothers</data>
