    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="ACEITE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El aceite de oliva virgen extra se asocia con beneficios para la salud cardiovascular, lo que puede reducir el riesgo de enfermedad cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">b92a108dd7694f70aca661f3fcbda917</data>
      <data key="d12">10235</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="CARNES PROCESADAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de carnes procesadas se ha relacionado con un mayor riesgo de enfermedad cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">a79d587d1a8c42869899f91223346b69</data>
      <data key="d12">10236</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="CARNES MAGRAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las carnes magras se consideran neutras en su efecto sobre el riesgo cardiovascular, lo que sugiere que su consumo no incrementa el riesgo.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">5b4a85837748481c9f40862bfd5487b7</data>
      <data key="d12">10237</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="LACTEOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los l&#225;cteos no parecen incrementar el riesgo cardiovascular, lo que sugiere un efecto neutro en la salud del coraz&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">612e4269dec14d3786cd52b7f994e8ae</data>
      <data key="d12">10238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="CAF&#201;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo moderado de caf&#233; se ha asociado con un menor riesgo cardiovascular, aunque el efecto puede variar con el consumo excesivo.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">8146c3113bf9475ebb93334a5285c298</data>
      <data key="d12">10239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="T&#201;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El t&#233; muestra una relaci&#243;n no lineal con el riesgo cardiovascular, donde un consumo moderado puede ser beneficioso.</data>
      <data key="d10">e04d44fa9d8f83cab42b04dd086695fc</data>
      <data key="d11">23736f09b2ea43d6a2076c5c6adf7a7a</data>
      <data key="d12">10240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad cardiovascular is often associated with conditions that lead to kidney stones, indicating a relationship between these health issues. Additionally, it can be related to litiasis renal and other metabolic disorders, highlighting the interconnectedness of cardiovascular health and renal conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb</data>
      <data key="d11">06792daa7b98466984bd4e475e2b57f2</data>
      <data key="d12">10241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="HIPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperuricemia is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases (enfermedad cardiovascular). This condition has been particularly linked to a heightened risk of cardiovascular issues in patients who already have high-risk conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">b16f5918f6a94bc6af43a7ef08528d3b</data>
      <data key="d12">10242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles elevados de &#225;cido &#250;rico se han asociado con un mayor riesgo de enfermedad cardiovascular.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9</data>
      <data key="d11">9101e12d63354a94a345692467147238</data>
      <data key="d12">10243</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR" target="NEFROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enfermedad cardiovascular is often related to metabolic syndrome, which can increase the risk of kidney stones</data>
      <data key="d10">a29197a0d36ee2c688c9c959435e999f</data>
      <data key="d11">f7063cb3150945b0a768b41923efe4b7</data>
      <data key="d12">10244</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="HYPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#225;ncer de mama is often linked to hypercalcemia in advanced cases</data>
      <data key="d10">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d11">fe12f210fc96491fa5790b4e7467133e</data>
      <data key="d12">10245</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="MEN1">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Women with MEN1 have a higher risk of developing breast cancer at younger ages compared to the general population</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">3012a7fa426143cf9cc18f067893a99e</data>
      <data key="d12">10246</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="C&#193;NCER DE PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both lung cancer and breast cancer risks are influenced by dietary habits, particularly the consumption of fruits and vegetables</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d11">2726c824b5144f189e8c1f1ecbe868fe</data>
      <data key="d12">10247</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER DE MAMA and C&#193;NCER DE PR&#211;STATA are both types of cancer that have been studied in relation to various dietary factors. Research indicates that the risks associated with both breast cancer and prostate cancer are linked to the consumption of fruits and vegetables. Additionally, both cancers have also been examined concerning the intake of processed meats, suggesting that dietary choices may play a significant role in the risk factors for these diseases.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198,a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
      <data key="d11">b92c5bb577d644dba47cc58a700e4068</data>
      <data key="d12">10248</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="C&#193;NCER OV&#193;RICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breast cancer (C&#193;NCER DE MAMA) and ovarian cancer (C&#193;NCER OV&#193;RICO) are two types of cancer that may have their risks influenced by dietary factors, specifically the consumption of cruciferous vegetables. Research suggests that incorporating these vegetables into one's diet could potentially impact the likelihood of developing both breast and ovarian cancers.</data>
      <data key="d10">4ff95b497607c33ba3da4182ac19d198</data>
      <data key="d11">cf337a8bc97f473b99574c1b569eca03</data>
      <data key="d12">10249</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="CEREALES INTEGRALES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ingesta de cereales integrales puede reducir el riesgo de c&#225;ncer de mama al disminuir los niveles de estr&#243;genos circulantes.</data>
      <data key="d10">8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692</data>
      <data key="d11">883f8728fbb34280a74264e62e1f3e5a</data>
      <data key="d12">10250</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="FIBRA DIET&#201;TICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La fibra diet&#233;tica puede reducir el riesgo de c&#225;ncer de mama al disminuir los niveles de estr&#243;genos circulantes.</data>
      <data key="d10">8f4f0fffa52482a1b5a520849d10c692</data>
      <data key="d11">7e698aa2fb1247fcbac6423ed9751cbf</data>
      <data key="d12">10251</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE MAMA" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS OMEGA-3">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">C&#193;NCER DE MAMA and &#193;CIDOS GRASOS OMEGA-3 are interconnected through research suggesting that the supplementation of omega-3 fatty acids is associated with a decreased risk of breast cancer. This indicates a potential benefit of omega-3 fatty acids in the prevention of this type of cancer. Both descriptions highlight the role of omega-3 fatty acids in potentially reducing the risk of developing breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">11c3cb37b1a2c111ceb227aefa8d9e1a,5075c65bfc020ec93f9bf14d3fe764c3</data>
      <data key="d11">d693593a6c4b41c78b4e2b774a94643b</data>
      <data key="d12">10252</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C&#193;NCER DE OVARIO" target="C&#193;NCER DE H&#205;GADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both cancers have associations with dietary habits, particularly the consumption of certain meats</data>
      <data key="d10">a6ba6423064bccccefee095de7435164</data>
      <data key="d11">04146ffff7524feaae31d88205124797</data>
      <data key="d12">10253</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IHAN" target="UNICEF">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IHAN works with UNICEF to support breastfeeding initiatives for children's health</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">e28dc9b934204e079ea3b7f19a22d04a</data>
      <data key="d12">10254</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IHAN" target="LACTANCIA MATERNA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IHAN promotes breastfeeding as a key health intervention for mothers and infants</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">492d4a20bec648e4ae6731020b200cf0</data>
      <data key="d12">10255</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IHAN" target="GRUPOS DE APOYO A LA LACTANCIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IHAN encourages the establishment of breastfeeding support groups to assist mothers</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">41f15c5c3e074c42969b84cf1e6cf9fd</data>
      <data key="d12">10256</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="GALACTOSEMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactosemia is a contraindication for breastfeeding, requiring special formulas</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">041cc3fc01ca4a1d824a580b1209a0a9</data>
      <data key="d12">10257</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="HIV">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIV positive mothers in developed countries may face challenges in breastfeeding</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">aededbc33299495e911ca19492d1835f</data>
      <data key="d12">10258</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="BRUCELLOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Untreated brucellosis can contraindicate breastfeeding</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">03f11c9a99cc435c97ad7c144f389a6f</data>
      <data key="d12">10259</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="TUBERCULOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Active tuberculosis can temporarily prevent a mother from breastfeeding</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">e83526d1e876462ab60be7cdc846e63b</data>
      <data key="d12">10260</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="CES&#193;REA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mothers who have undergone a cesarean section may need additional support to initiate breastfeeding</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">d4e25c0655e14843b8523de7b8301226</data>
      <data key="d12">10261</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="LECHE MATERNA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breast milk is the primary focus of breastfeeding practices promoted by IHAN</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">fba806cc226e4a9abafc4398b934ead1</data>
      <data key="d12">10262</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="DIABETES TIPO II">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breastfeeding may lower the risk of developing Type II diabetes in mothers</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">80d6431516e44186857efbe943b2680c</data>
      <data key="d12">10263</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="ARTRITIS REUMATOIDE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breastfeeding has been associated with a reduced incidence of rheumatoid arthritis</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">c5666f1a3ed0423c9e5245acb864efb4</data>
      <data key="d12">10264</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="V&#205;NCULO AFECTIVO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breastfeeding promotes the establishment of a strong emotional bond between mother and child</data>
      <data key="d10">cf034f02916ec46dcba7e0f8d8e24c0c</data>
      <data key="d11">94f7c704d438489895c6c1d18ebea1b8</data>
      <data key="d12">10265</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="LACTANCIA ARTIFICIAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Breastfeeding is the preferred method of feeding, while artificial lactation is used when breastfeeding is not possible.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a1b909c98067bf7fc270d6f30199f96</data>
      <data key="d11">85c5df0ad66241b7b433d27e440fb076</data>
      <data key="d12">10266</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA MATERNA" target="ALMID&#211;N DE MA&#205;Z">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La lactancia materna es recomendada para lactantes, y el almid&#243;n de ma&#237;z puede ser introducido posteriormente si es bien tolerado.</data>
      <data key="d10">658ee56030a35ceeeec05d15cfa49842</data>
      <data key="d11">b97284f816d6438eb67c77b4a5d79e2f</data>
      <data key="d12">10267</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="AFROAMERICANS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Afroamericans are frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, which is linked to a specific genetic mutation.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">6ec40d4b03174dfc93ae0472b4af2f96</data>
      <data key="d12">10268</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="AFRICANS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Africans, particularly those native to South Africa, are frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, sharing the same genetic mutation as Afroamericans.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">5a521899e77a49f691fe22df4da82547</data>
      <data key="d12">10269</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="DUARTE VARIANT">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Duarte variant is a specific biochemical variant of galactosemia that presents with milder symptoms compared to classical galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">0be3294f8a724c2cb598395ebb8b14c6</data>
      <data key="d12">10270</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="NEONATAL SCREENING">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neonatal screening is a method used to diagnose galactosemia early in newborns by measuring galactose levels and GALT activity.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">48b58e359a1f4838bef9c895e20efeb0</data>
      <data key="d12">10271</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="GALT">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GALT is the enzyme whose activity is crucial for diagnosing galactosemia and its variants, making it directly related to the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">3addc470b96445d1b08841e58ab12456</data>
      <data key="d12">10272</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="GALACTOSE">
      <data key="d8">33.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose is a key substrate in the metabolic disorder known as galactosemia. In individuals with galactosemia, there is an inability to metabolize galactose properly, which leads to the accumulation of this sugar in the body. As a result, those affected by galactosemia must adhere to dietary restrictions to manage their condition and prevent complications associated with the excess galactose. Overall, galactosemia is characterized by the body's inability to process galactose, resulting in significant health implications for those diagnosed with the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa,ce9cd0d993ab8b3995c1a78e9306bcad,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d11">779709945a1d4835b0bcd71af1789b0d</data>
      <data key="d12">10273</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="ERITROCITOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Erythrocytes are used to measure GALT activity and galactose levels, which are essential for diagnosing galactosemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">655ec6e226b847feb33bae6a222acb97</data>
      <data key="d12">10274</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="AL&#201;LO DUARTE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Duarte allele is associated with a milder form of galactosemia, affecting the severity of the disease in individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">c4056d00ff7cbd7d7e3464150ea3d5aa</data>
      <data key="d11">b05fff90e1334e60b9a0bec52980c87e</data>
      <data key="d12">10275</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="NEONATO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neonates are screened for galactosemia to identify those who may require dietary intervention to avoid complications</data>
      <data key="d10">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc</data>
      <data key="d11">e4ddde1fcde74350bd53d525f9947466</data>
      <data key="d12">10276</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="GAL-1-P">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactosemia is a genetic disorder that affects the body's ability to metabolize galactose, a sugar found in milk and other dairy products. A key metabolite associated with this condition is Gal-1-P (galactose-1-phosphate), which plays a crucial role in the screening and diagnosis of galactosemia. Monitoring Gal-1-P levels in patients diagnosed with galactosemia is essential to ensure proper dietary compliance and management of the disorder. This monitoring helps healthcare providers assess the effectiveness of dietary restrictions and make necessary adjustments to the patient's treatment plan.</data>
      <data key="d10">0765b6a482d8348e9746183291e9e9bc,f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d11">bdd7587b46dc4153b6c5e2b647d02f99</data>
      <data key="d12">10277</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSEMIA" target="GALACTITOL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
