      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUBERCULOSIS" target="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tuberculosis is a significant health concern that can lead to primary adrenal insufficiency, also known as insuficiencia suprarrenal. This condition arises when tuberculosis causes destruction of the adrenal glands, establishing a direct relationship between the two entities. Furthermore, tuberculosis is recognized as a common cause of adrenal insufficiency, particularly in low-income countries, highlighting its impact on public health in these regions.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,c925b6205ea7a28ba24640c28ec558da</data>
      <data key="d11">8e374576a4bc4546b23ef2799f5a5c2f</data>
      <data key="d12">10298</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUBERCULOSIS" target="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tuberculosis can lead to ascitis quilosa as a complication of the disease</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">db4118256d7a4df2b58929873533f49b</data>
      <data key="d12">10299</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CES&#193;REA" target="RECI&#201;N NACIDO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
