    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="PREMATURIDAD">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Premature infants are at a higher risk of vitamin D deficiency, necessitating supplementation</data>
      <data key="d10">919ff63f7f48a238e717f60361d8dbd1</data>
      <data key="d11">c4d0dff2a19143ddaa8e7627dbd9e336</data>
      <data key="d12">10461</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="FRAILTY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insufficient levels of vitamin D have been linked to a higher risk of frailty in older populations</data>
      <data key="d10">6d6fc66abf6c858e5c5e9e47eb1ff6d2</data>
      <data key="d11">5d6a7a56cd734eea8c3b6a411a8df7bf</data>
      <data key="d12">10462</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="FRAILTY SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D supplementation has been shown to help prevent frailty and falls in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">3ec3efbe130c20d623681e00e3d784f7</data>
      <data key="d11">fcd2f00323ca44e0a17727e34024c15e</data>
      <data key="d12">10463</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="HYPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is essential for calcium absorption, and its deficiency can lead to hypocalcemia</data>
      <data key="d10">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d11">b113544a180b4116a082d2fc9920710f</data>
      <data key="d12">10464</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="MALABSORPTION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Malabsorption can lead to vitamin D deficiency as it affects the absorption of this fat-soluble vitamin</data>
      <data key="d10">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d11">1b3797d7b4d740f1b651fe641bc2eaa8</data>
      <data key="d12">10465</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="ANTIEPILEPTIC MEDICATION">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Antiepileptic medications can increase the metabolism of vitamin D, leading to lower levels in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d11">0d3711fbb28c487ea8f49af828ea245c</data>
      <data key="d12">10466</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="TUBERCULOSTATIC MEDICATION">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tuberculostatic medications can also affect vitamin D metabolism, contributing to deficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d11">751fc07dadb44d25af3a75578a803bdf</data>
      <data key="d12">10467</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="BREAST CANCER">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Research indicates that vitamin D may play a role in reducing the risk of breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
      <data key="d11">1ba7bc035bac4c09bb884ce712ff1dc3</data>
      <data key="d12">10468</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="METABOLIC SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is thought to influence metabolic syndrome outcomes, potentially mediating susceptibility.</data>
      <data key="d10">e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
      <data key="d11">fd8f4d7c59c943808b0e13fed6189674</data>
      <data key="d12">10469</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="COLON CANCER">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D levels have been linked to cancer risk, including colon cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">ea920d08266b329db73fb7b804bbb9ce</data>
      <data key="d11">c74be398ce90428f95a8e2f0b05464dc</data>
      <data key="d12">10470</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="ANOREXIA NERVOSA">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D deficiency is commonly observed in patients with anorexia nervosa, which significantly impacts their bone health. To address this deficiency, vitamin D is often supplemented in individuals with anorexia nervosa. This supplementation plays a crucial role in aiding calcium absorption and supporting overall bone health, thereby helping to mitigate some of the adverse effects associated with the disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543,bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d11">8fb57ca237f1443b92fcf15375935151</data>
      <data key="d12">10471</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="CALCIUM">
      <data key="d8">33.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D and calcium are closely related nutrients that play a vital role in maintaining bone health. They are often recommended to be supplemented together to reduce the risk of osteoporosis. Vitamin D is essential for the absorption of calcium, which is crucial not only for the bone health of infants but also for overall bone metabolism. The presence of vitamin D is necessary for effective calcium absorption, making it indispensable for managing bone health and preventing osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">08bc4a83d18482b48f5bbef4fbf316f3,08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c,1f8cd198519be7b535a3f5be8181931c,9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">1460370c012e4631b73cf1d98fedf1f1</data>
      <data key="d12">10472</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="IRON">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D supplementation is recommended alongside iron to meet dietary needs in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">eebd73221cd04707a94b31cdd5f9c1f4</data>
      <data key="d12">10473</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VITAMIN D" target="HEMODIALYSIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vitamin D is recommended for patients undergoing hemodialysis to maintain appropriate levels</data>
      <data key="d10">9da930839072b524410f2345ab1df8b1</data>
      <data key="d11">9a3da58752d140bc8a7c6556c3f480a5</data>
      <data key="d12">10474</data>
