    <edge source="COPPER" target="LACTANCIA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Copper plays a crucial role in the dietary needs of infants during lactation, with specific recommended intake levels established to ensure their health and development. Lactancia, which provides dietary reference intake guidelines, outlines the necessary copper intake for various age groups, emphasizing the importance of this mineral in the diets of nursing infants. Together, these insights highlight the significance of copper in lactation and the need for adherence to established dietary guidelines to support optimal growth in infants.</data>
