      <data key="d9">Las herramientas de identificaci&#243;n son necesarias para detectar a los pacientes fr&#225;giles y facilitar su intervenci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d11">68f5e5f1862d48acbb89060e7f8892c2</data>
      <data key="d12">10915</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HERRAMIENTAS DE IDENTIFICACI&#211;N" target="GROENINGEN FRAILTY INDEX">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Groningen Frailty Index es una de las herramientas de identificaci&#243;n utilizadas para detectar la fragilidad en pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d11">a6606ed55ec847cf920187596e8af05b</data>
      <data key="d12">10916</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HERRAMIENTAS DE IDENTIFICACI&#211;N" target="VULNERABLE ELDERS' SURVEY-12">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Vulnerable Elders' Survey-12 es otra herramienta de identificaci&#243;n que ayuda a detectar la fragilidad en ancianos.</data>
      <data key="d10">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d11">80ad327a3ac744ed916bc227b1637af5</data>
      <data key="d12">10917</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HERRAMIENTAS DE IDENTIFICACI&#211;N" target="TILLBURG">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tillburg es una herramienta que se utiliza para identificar pacientes fr&#225;giles en la evaluaci&#243;n geri&#225;trica.</data>
      <data key="d10">28606a3b4799e394f7600d47c4f5a223</data>
      <data key="d11">d8414ebfc6514d748d94d0aa79aa9dab</data>
      <data key="d12">10918</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VULNERABLE ELDERS' SURVEY-12" target="GROENING FRAILTY INDEX">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both the Groningen Frailty Index and the Vulnerable Elders' Survey-12 are tools used to assess frailty and vulnerability in elderly populations</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">e403d3cd76b549b0a838cbc73eca0e3e</data>
      <data key="d12">10919</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="REVISI&#211;N SISTEM&#193;TICA" target="EVIDENCIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Systematic reviews compile and evaluate evidence from various studies</data>
      <data key="d10">4261c82c43dac1a06d46f91f46f6d510</data>
      <data key="d11">39b5953071784d62aa03f4e872db2a0c</data>
      <data key="d12">10920</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS" target="MALNUTRICI&#211;N RELACIONADA CON LA ENFERMEDAD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oncological patients are at high risk for disease-related malnutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">45c3281fd6beffb0e9ac61ae5700af3d</data>
      <data key="d11">e868545d7c9b48b784007cd0b959e042</data>
      <data key="d12">10921</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS" target="HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cancer patients may also benefit from a high-protein diet to support their nutritional needs during treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">c6406ac5c0c7b03d4ee61ca311fd783f</data>
      <data key="d11">262a0bf0e35b4851bcda06f07132bcca</data>
      <data key="d12">10922</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS" target="AGENTES FARMACOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los agentes farmacol&#243;gicos son utilizados en pacientes oncol&#243;gicos para mejorar su estado nutricional y apetito</data>
      <data key="d10">a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c</data>
      <data key="d11">5ac5492d57ca47aea9a20e30d6d47f2b</data>
      <data key="d12">10923</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS" target="PROFESIONAL NUTRICIONAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El profesional nutricional asesora a los pacientes oncol&#243;gicos sobre su ingesta alimentaria y h&#225;bitos nutricionales</data>
      <data key="d10">a96b8f4fe52b5b963b28242c3352aa7c</data>
      <data key="d11">0ac6be53b0434f76944f327d5a27f863</data>
      <data key="d12">10924</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NUTRICI&#211;N EN ONCOLOG&#205;A focuses on the nutritional needs and interventions for PACIENTES ONCOL&#211;GICOS</data>
      <data key="d10">5277ea34ef65b7d029950f2c905c6732</data>
      <data key="d11">5b95f80be01e456ab6960bce5c376b23</data>
      <data key="d12">10925</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VALORACI&#211;N GERI&#193;TRICA INTEGRAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE FRAGILIDAD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Comprehensive geriatric assessment is essential for diagnosing and managing the frailty syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">6656dd3bdc79720504c3e4245f935d32</data>
      <data key="d11">012599e1207f41a1a6a79c22a20ef8ec</data>
      <data key="d12">10926</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INTERNATIONAL ACADEMY ON NUTRITION AND AGEING" target="GRONINGEN FRAILTY INDICATOR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The International Academy on Nutrition and Ageing utilizes the Groningen Frailty Indicator as part of its assessment tools for elderly nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">ed1a29a5a4ad4013b9df6717a3a0b533</data>
      <data key="d12">10927</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL OF LEICESTER" target="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The University Hospital of Leicester employs the Edmonton Frailty Scale to evaluate frailty in elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">da7f83e6532d4ff3ae02752f3c191a57</data>
      <data key="d12">10928</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GRONINGEN FRAILTY INDICATOR" target="TILBURG FRAILTY INDICATOR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both the Groningen and Tilburg Frailty Indicators are tools used to assess frailty in elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">027c81150f75415682bbb482cab1ce0d</data>
      <data key="d12">10929</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE" target="FRAIL SCALE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Edmonton Frailty Scale and FRAIL Scale are both assessment tools aimed at identifying frailty in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">3862d66020e84862a06bfb6b9265e03f</data>
      <data key="d12">10930</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE" target="MORLEY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Morley discusses the Edmonton Frailty Scale as part of the assessment tools for identifying frailty in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">12e65d9804494767b87d9d021d5b0ce9</data>
      <data key="d12">10931</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE" target="TWO-STEP OLDER PERSONS SCREENING">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both the Edmonton Frailty Scale and the Two-step Older Persons Screening are tools used to assess frailty in elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">47ead85c9d6f4f72ac876dbf3b96745e</data>
      <data key="d12">10932</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EDMONTON FRAILTY SCALE" target="SHORT PHYSICAL PERFORMANCE BATTERY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Short Physical Performance Battery is included in the Edmonton Frailty Scale as a measure of physical performance</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">a4ed781f21904bafa5e242373197226a</data>
      <data key="d12">10933</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="NRS 2002">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NRS 2002 is used to screen frail elderly individuals for nutritional risk</data>
      <data key="d10">79b6030cb061514423118a8c4214b5e4</data>
      <data key="d11">682b02ee394d497bb7c0c00258e393d5</data>
      <data key="d12">10934</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="CONSENSO MULTIDISCIPLINAR SOBRE EL ABORDAJE DE LA DESNUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consenso proporciona pautas espec&#237;ficas para la intervenci&#243;n nutricional en ancianos fr&#225;giles</data>
      <data key="d10">cc6ee3d7bc9bfaf4a06f3f02c4907eb0</data>
      <data key="d11">bc4c2deb70134a40b342779b5f630bd4</data>
      <data key="d12">10935</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="PROT-AGE STUDY GROUP">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PROT-AGE Study Group provides guidelines for protein intake specifically for the frail elderly population</data>
      <data key="d10">b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">83af484e96774e37ac2c9ec85defc831</data>
      <data key="d12">10936</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="DIETA MEDITERR&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mediterranean diet is suggested as a beneficial dietary pattern for preventing frailty in elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">8b98b9a8548742ba9702a5a10f5806aa</data>
      <data key="d12">10937</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="CREATINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Creatine is suggested as a promising nutritional intervention for muscle regeneration in frail elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">380968d2d94b4ae980a0ae8ebfe0a8e9</data>
      <data key="d12">10938</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANCIANO FR&#193;GIL" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS OMEGA-3">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Omega-3 fatty acids are associated with improved muscle response in frail elderly individuals when combined with amino acids</data>
      <data key="d10">b36323a01af9698c9ac089dd8d37213d</data>
      <data key="d11">741a1decf25a438493a26843bfb7ca23</data>
      <data key="d12">10939</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ABBREVIATED COMPREHENSIVE GERIATRIC ASSESSMENT" target="GERIATRIC 8">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Abbreviated Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment and Geriatric 8 are both methods used to evaluate the health status of elderly individuals</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">18409cf94ab741fea4575f807d303122</data>
      <data key="d12">10940</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GERIATRIC 8" target="TRIAGE RISK SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Triage Risk Screening Tool and Geriatric 8 are both utilized to assess risks and frailty in older adults</data>
      <data key="d10">f87b3e7660657fc2ac8535a3b283e4e7</data>
      <data key="d11">260c544b54b04a03b25015fe496c8131</data>
      <data key="d12">10941</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TWO-STEP OLDER PERSONS SCREENING" target="GERONTOPOLE FRAILTY SCREENING TOOL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Gerontopole Frailty Screening Tool was designed alongside the Two-step Older Persons Screening to provide effective screening for frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">02766c99c5c54212b72549bb43fd0d3a</data>
      <data key="d12">10942</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRAILTY TRAIT SCALE" target="MORLEY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Morley proposed the Frailty Trait Scale as a new tool to identify dimensions of frailty</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">7dd913bc8f0f4cada0b078c05ecf39d2</data>
      <data key="d12">10943</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRAILTY TRAIT SCALE" target="PHYSICAL ACTIVITY SCALE FOR THE ELDERLY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Physical Activity Scale for the Elderly is one of the dimensions assessed by the Frailty Trait Scale</data>
      <data key="d10">d99a6175f2d81fae9bf733be64a65dd4</data>
      <data key="d11">f910e50224234030a01755d3e752b7b4</data>
      <data key="d12">10944</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DEPRESSION" target="BN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BN is contraindicated in patients with severe depression</data>
      <data key="d10">f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
      <data key="d11">dcc463fb739545ae92426faba83a6bbd</data>
      <data key="d12">10945</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARTHRITIS" target="HEMATOCHROMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arthritis can develop in patients with hereditary hemochromatosis due to iron accumulation in the joints.</data>
      <data key="d10">83d2bb17e643e047bb3ad2ecc88d8271</data>
      <data key="d11">2015e202d8fa4cf5bdbfd27b915d998d</data>
      <data key="d12">10946</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EMPHYSEMA" target="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at increased risk for emphysema</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">238fa77bfae449cca3cd3b61c4d16d9c</data>
      <data key="d12">10947</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DIABETIC NEPHROPATHY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a major factor in the progression of diabetic nephropathy, necessitating aggressive treatment to protect kidney function.</data>
      <data key="d10">8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d11">ebc11b56ae6447839fa99b646f2ff16e</data>
      <data key="d12">10948</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="CHRONIC KIDNEY DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a common comorbidity that can exacerbate chronic kidney disease and is critical to manage in affected patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">8886631425cf090457592f633ee8cae8</data>
      <data key="d11">062db1debdbc47aa8dbf3b3059c3c23f</data>
      <data key="d12">10949</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a common comorbidity in patients with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1</data>
      <data key="d10">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d11">915ae59d492249e9a6fcb6e545aa7391</data>
      <data key="d12">10950</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 2">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is frequently observed in patients with Diabetes Mellitus Type 2</data>
      <data key="d10">aa9279dacd764b478618ae36af93ad83</data>
      <data key="d11">fcc61ce2828541249413a8c79c037e74</data>
      <data key="d12">10951</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease, establishing a direct relationship between the two. This condition is particularly concerning as it is associated with an increased risk of developing cardiovascular disease, especially in individuals with diabetes.</data>
      <data key="d10">67d484d5c0c84fff32782bd773c0fd7a,fe5f390fb67fd3b1ad222db3500574b9</data>
      <data key="d11">31cfbf3a1e2942a0b7f2caace519c715</data>
      <data key="d12">10952</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="TYPE II DIABETES MELLITUS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is often associated with type II diabetes, complicating management and treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">265fcc321b2c0bbf0bf8200d0489e1a1</data>
      <data key="d11">bb36d6214f7e4629b28bb940a2982c2e</data>
      <data key="d12">10953</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DOCA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Excess levels of DOCA can lead to the development of hypertension due to its mineralocorticoid effects.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c</data>
      <data key="d11">7e1ba650fbae4a0b9c77eb6a198379cc</data>
      <data key="d12">10954</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension can be a consequence of metabolic syndrome in individuals with Klinefelter syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">465b35e2234340dfa2d548be748a8905</data>
      <data key="d12">10955</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="SODIUM">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERTENSION is closely linked to SODIUM, as excessive sodium intake is a well-known risk factor for developing hypertension. Numerous studies have established a clear relationship between high sodium consumption and the onset of hypertension, indicating that excessive sodium intake significantly contributes to the development of this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,6c509f5e704c690cfa39b3f7b19eb766,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7</data>
      <data key="d11">427df5112b7f47499fee18e83c48a340</data>
      <data key="d12">10956</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="BN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BN is contraindicated in patients with uncontrolled hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">f44811ae5b3e9dab0f295efe8842767a</data>
      <data key="d11">9ac0e673046748a88caf57bd0b33951b</data>
      <data key="d12">10957</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="GSDIB">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension can develop as a secondary condition in patients with GSDIb due to renal impairment.</data>
      <data key="d10">a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98</data>
      <data key="d11">304828bcfd4a488787de81928516bacd</data>
      <data key="d12">10958</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="POST-LIVER TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension may develop in patients after liver transplantation, requiring ongoing monitoring</data>
      <data key="d10">df284534230932ffa363470a1a101b29</data>
      <data key="d11">26ff9f956b5148b69869ddbdeb2bb43a</data>
      <data key="d12">10959</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="PREDIMED TRIAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PREDIMED trial findings on blood pressure were published in Hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">63593ac5546e44eaddb37a2f257bfa80</data>
      <data key="d11">f8793afe17b84314a670b1008d979970</data>
      <data key="d12">10960</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="FRAMINGHAM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Framingham study provides data on the prevalence of hypertension and its risk factors, establishing a direct link between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">04b9cfc4e62a43c8964e67d5bd339f30</data>
      <data key="d12">10961</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="PATHS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PATHS study investigates the impact of alcohol reduction on hypertension, showing a relationship between alcohol consumption and blood pressure</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">1ea394e431c54eb9a7345a8336041373</data>
      <data key="d12">10962</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="NATIONAL HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE EDUCATION PROGRAM">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The National High Blood Pressure Education Program is dedicated to educating the public about hypertension, focusing on both its prevention and management. The program aims to raise awareness regarding the importance of understanding hypertension and provides information on effective treatment options. Through its initiatives, the program seeks to empower individuals with knowledge to help prevent and manage high blood pressure effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,b49f181ca7099fc110f35ccc27e7fafc</data>
      <data key="d11">9daa8cd4c5064e729bcc64adce6aae70</data>
      <data key="d12">10963</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="NATIONAL HEART, LUNG AND BLOOD INSTITUTE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The NHLBI conducts research and provides guidelines for the prevention and treatment of hypertension</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">3a87e1c5b6394de094d49aa8ecd4616b</data>
      <data key="d12">10964</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DASH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The DASH diet is specifically designed to prevent and manage hypertension through dietary changes</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">20d09da979b34c80bbffe42627c164df</data>
      <data key="d12">10965</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="ALCOHOL">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HYPERTENSION is associated with alcohol consumption, as excessive intake of alcohol can contribute to elevated blood pressure levels. To effectively manage hypertension, it is recommended that individuals reduce their alcohol consumption. Limiting alcohol intake is advised as a key strategy in controlling and managing hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa,e40d5e26456fbd223dc887d7d6d0eeb7</data>
      <data key="d11">059a898c4ab54925bde89ca0aaca0e37</data>
      <data key="d12">10966</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="EXERCISE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Regular exercise is recommended as a preventive measure against hypertension, showing a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">b5031fd21497489cac1780798663aa38</data>
      <data key="d12">10967</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="SOBREPESO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sobrepeso significantly increases the risk of developing hypertension, establishing a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">a5da5f3cb8b14a799506580560cfc902</data>
      <data key="d12">10968</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="PA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PA is the primary measure used to diagnose and monitor hypertension, indicating a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">5eab0fab994f4e96b12f7b89a2a97692</data>
      <data key="d12">10969</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="EJERCICIO F&#205;SICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Regular physical exercise is essential for managing hypertension and improving overall cardiovascular health</data>
      <data key="d10">3fab4e796fd2145b2d0f62ffa60775aa</data>
      <data key="d11">e45e3e50fcc94185b468430108e9e725</data>
      <data key="d12">10970</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERTENSION" target="DASH DIET">
