    <edge source="MEDITERRANEAN DIET" target="PREDIMED">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mediterranean Diet is a dietary pattern that emphasizes the consumption of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, legumes, nuts, and healthy fats, particularly olive oil, while being low in red meat and processed foods. The PREDIMED study, which stands for "Prevenci&#243;n con Dieta Mediterr&#225;nea," evaluates adherence to this diet through comprehensive dietary assessments. It specifically investigates the effects of the Mediterranean diet on various health outcomes, including diabetes and cardiovascular disease. The study focuses on understanding how adherence to the Mediterranean diet influences cardiovascular health and overall well-being. Through its research, PREDIMED aims to provide insights into the health benefits associated with following the Mediterranean dietary pattern.</data>
      <data key="d10">1388342730ee9177144f78f9e9d7816e,52bc63fdc8f15b328d9033bca7021363,a739523b87def5cdfa8fe97cdf423fe7,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,f41688eecb31d8e55fc70e993e99c3e9</data>
      <data key="d11">2bf3bffdc8584c4e846b83faac41a48c</data>
      <data key="d12">11196</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDITERRANEAN DIET" target="NURSES' HEALTH STUDY">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mediterranean diet is a focal point of research within the Nurses' Health Study, which investigates its effects on women's health. This extensive study provides valuable evidence regarding the benefits of the Mediterranean diet, highlighting its positive impact on various health outcomes for women.</data>
      <data key="d10">c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,eb275fa50517d86a71589fd318784a5b</data>
      <data key="d11">76114a2b76e54a569f0ce9fbac749823</data>
      <data key="d12">11197</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDITERRANEAN DIET" target="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Mediterranean diet is recognized for its protective effects against cardiovascular disease. Research indicates that adherence to this diet is associated with a lower risk of developing cardiovascular conditions. This beneficial relationship is attributed to the diet's nutrient composition, which includes a variety of healthy fats, fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and lean proteins. Overall, the Mediterranean diet is linked to a reduced risk of cardiovascular disease, highlighting its importance in promoting heart health.</data>
      <data key="d10">35a49a079daea350a5552c8fd96d7967,c9a02c0d93ca431827b63d51ae564670,f2b8b21255397ebbaf2b5d66ff6bde88</data>
      <data key="d11">307f6cb9730548999982e68935ed3dfd</data>
      <data key="d12">11198</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
