    <edge source="HOMOCYSTEINE" target="VITAMIN B12">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HOMOCYSTEINE and VITAMIN B12 are closely related in the context of metabolic health. Vitamin B12 is administered to improve metabolic control and is known to effectively lower homocysteine levels. Elevated homocysteine levels are associated with various health issues, including cognitive decline. Therefore, by reducing homocysteine levels, Vitamin B12 may play a significant role in mitigating the risk of cognitive decline.</data>
      <data key="d10">7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1,b3760fcb9c0421b66d37c20b1dc68577</data>
      <data key="d11">44c1fd12e73243a38fe672214dc4e6a4</data>
      <data key="d12">11342</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HOMOCYSTEINE" target="FOLATE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Folate is necessary for the metabolism of homocysteine and is often given alongside vitamin B6</data>
      <data key="d10">7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1</data>
      <data key="d11">6f97a4cc2904490895909c74bbd8f585</data>
      <data key="d12">11343</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HOMOCYSTEINE" target="BETAINE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Betaine helps to lower homocysteine levels by converting it to methionine</data>
      <data key="d10">7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1</data>
      <data key="d11">9220844d96bb464b8ba448b0e86e817a</data>
      <data key="d12">11344</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HOMOCYSTEINE" target="UREA CYCLE DISORDERS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Urea cycle disorders can lead to elevated homocysteine levels due to impaired metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1</data>
      <data key="d11">20bcb50a3fe046feb0332e121f6701c0</data>
      <data key="d12">11345</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HOMOCYSTEINE" target="CYSTEINE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cysteine is synthesized from homocysteine, linking these two amino acids in metabolic pathways</data>
      <data key="d10">7754f367b453475179218cac4bc24de1</data>
