    <edge source="VITAMINA B" target="EUROPA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de suplementos de vitaminas B ha aumentado en Europa, especialmente entre personas con problemas cognitivos.</data>
      <data key="d10">fd3d9ab95227ef9290fe59028df2cda3</data>
      <data key="d11">f093292240cc4a6c82fedea441883cfe</data>
      <data key="d12">11367</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EUROPA" target="FENILCETONURIA">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EUROPA is associated with FENILCETONURIA, a genetic disorder characterized by the inability to metabolize phenylalanine, an amino acid found in many protein-containing foods. The IVS10 mutation, which is prevalent in Southern Europe, is linked to this condition. In terms of its prevalence, phenylketonuria is estimated to occur in approximately 1 in every 800 newborns across Europe, highlighting its significance as a public health concern in the region.</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">860ce75db0434ebc9c07c9a2fe64ba10</data>
      <data key="d12">11368</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EUROPA" target="GASTO SANITARIO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
