      <data key="d11">0449216c52c14089bfafcc21fd0e94bc</data>
      <data key="d12">11422</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL RISK INDEX" target="CHANDRA NUTRITION SCREEN">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Nutritional Risk Index (NRI) and the Chandra Nutrition Screen are both tools designed to assess nutritional risk, particularly in elderly patients. The Chandra Nutrition Screen serves a similar purpose to the NRI, focusing on evaluating the nutritional status and potential risks associated with malnutrition in this demographic. Both assessment methods are interconnected, as they aim to identify individuals at risk of nutritional deficiencies and guide appropriate interventions.</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822,8e8a6418528a5c33a9ddf7eb94066a04</data>
      <data key="d11">a9853bd6a3be425bacf4c346d51cdffe</data>
      <data key="d12">11423</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRITIONAL RISK INDEX" target="MEONF-II">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEONF-II and NRI are both focused on assessing the nutritional status of elderly patients</data>
      <data key="d10">07b1884f11a85f8feb424b7cc369f822</data>
      <data key="d11">8febaffe623549ecb207a11d75b6e9b2</data>
      <data key="d12">11424</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
