    <edge source="SNAQ" target="CNAQ">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CNAQ and SNAQ are both questionnaires designed to assess appetite in elderly patients. CNAQ, which stands for the "Council on Nutrition and Aging Questionnaire," is the original version, while SNAQ, or the "Simplified Nutritional Appetite Questionnaire," serves as a more straightforward adaptation intended specifically for institutionalized elderly individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">17f48ff2bbbb22ecd24983f41739c88b,1bad878c6efa9d3f5719546bb51bccb6</data>
      <data key="d11">123d378120e34cfe81e4d52520f273ab</data>
      <data key="d12">11453</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SNAQ" target="NUTRITIONAL SCREENING TOOLS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The SNAQ is one of the nutritional screening tools used to assess appetite and risk of malnutrition</data>
