    <edge source="AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION" target="AMERICAN COLLEGE OF CARDIOLOGY">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The American Heart Association (AHA) and the American College of Cardiology (ACC) are two prominent organizations that work together to enhance cardiovascular health. They collaborate on developing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of cardiovascular diseases, including those associated with diabetes. Their joint efforts focus on reducing cardiovascular risk and promoting heart health through various strategies, including lifestyle changes. By providing these guidelines, the AHA and ACC aim to improve patient outcomes and support healthcare professionals in delivering effective cardiovascular care.</data>
      <data key="d10">5b7201af7da852101713ee9f11864f50,844d065cac5f5304fffed35b5da90416,e032cf926bee7048e207a0e28604f60e,fe8c41d0de4d4e277554bb9256255f30</data>
      <data key="d11">dcbca87ea38b4d6ea328ca1d808232eb</data>
      <data key="d12">11627</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION" target="NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
