    <edge source="OSTEOPENIA" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osteopenia is a condition that poses a significant risk to patients with EPOC (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease). These patients are often underdiagnosed for osteopenia, which can lead to serious health complications. The increased risk of osteopenia in EPOC patients is primarily attributed to factors such as malnutrition and low muscle mass, which are common in this population. Therefore, it is crucial for healthcare providers to be vigilant in screening and managing osteopenia in individuals with EPOC to improve their overall health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf,f3d21fef234a5c6fed6ef3fb2c8da1f4</data>
      <data key="d11">3cac43a1d7034a509e822e21ac77411d</data>
      <data key="d12">11692</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
