    </edge>
    <edge source="FEOCROMOCITOMA" target="HYPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Feocromocitoma can produce excess PTHrP, leading to hypercalcemia</data>
      <data key="d10">74c9662af46dca03f3941e133df2e783</data>
      <data key="d11">605fbae86da14fb097d34ffdd75d5c6e</data>
      <data key="d12">11971</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="ADENOMA">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Incidentalomas suprarrenales, commonly referred to as adrenal incidentalomas, are often discovered during imaging studies of the adrenal glands. These incidental findings are frequently benign adenomas, which are a type of tumor that arises from glandular tissue. The majority of adrenal incidentalomas identified in such studies are indeed benign adenomas, indicating that while they may be detected unexpectedly, they typically do not pose significant health risks.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">d8dc7c5dcc844a60b371922c975a18aa</data>
      <data key="d12">11972</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The term "incidentaloma suprarrenal" refers to an adrenal incidentaloma, which is an adrenal mass that is discovered incidentally during imaging studies conducted for unrelated reasons. In some cases, these incidentalomas may raise suspicion for adrenal carcinoma, particularly if certain characteristics are present. It is important to note that incidentalomas suprarrenales can sometimes be diagnosed as carcinoma suprarrenal, indicating that while many incidentalomas are benign, there is a potential for them to be malignant. Therefore, careful evaluation and monitoring are essential in cases where adrenal incidentalomas are identified, as they may represent underlying adrenal carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">da182699d0c04c13b8d6dd659c86fba0</data>
      <data key="d12">11973</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="MET&#193;STASIS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Incidentalomas suprarrenales may also represent metastatic disease</data>
      <data key="d10">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">df53cb185d344c5184aeafd0f1ac0b9f</data>
      <data key="d12">11974</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="MIELOLIPOMA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Incidentalomas suprarrenales can include mielolipomas as a type of benign tumor</data>
      <data key="d10">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">c34b002372854688b94b169ef5572011</data>
      <data key="d12">11975</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="QUISTES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Incidentalomas suprarrenales may also be identified as quistes</data>
      <data key="d10">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">4c949787977048e99a7303b1c0743cf3</data>
      <data key="d12">11976</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="HYPERCORTISOLISM">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Incidentalomas can be associated with hypercortisolism, necessitating further evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d10">8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7</data>
      <data key="d11">a93559c4298c4050abb3be4e96b919a6</data>
      <data key="d12">11977</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE CUSHING SUBCL&#205;NICO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Cushing subcl&#237;nico puede ser una condici&#243;n asociada a la evaluaci&#243;n de un incidentaloma suprarrenal</data>
      <data key="d10">a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">452bca1fb1e943ec881dba40a038286e</data>
      <data key="d12">11978</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="DHEA-S">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DHEA-S is a marker that is evaluated in the context of studying an incidentaloma suprarrenal (adrenal incidentaloma). Its use as a marker in this field is somewhat controversial, indicating that while it is commonly assessed, there may be differing opinions regarding its effectiveness or relevance in the evaluation of adrenal incidentalomas.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">78eb87d86875448fa73ab141600df6c3</data>
      <data key="d12">11979</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" refers to an adrenal incidentaloma, which is an unexpected mass found on the adrenal gland during imaging studies conducted for other reasons. In the evaluation of patients with adrenal incidentalomas, "HORMONAS SEXUALES" or sex hormones play a significant role. These hormones are assessed particularly in cases where there is a suspicion of malignancy associated with the adrenal incidentaloma. It is important to note that adrenal tumors may secrete sex hormones, which necessitates their evaluation in the context of adrenal incidentalomas to determine the nature of the tumor and guide further management.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">d234c098fad34c51bcbcc7696d11aea8</data>
      <data key="d12">11980</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="FASSNACHT M">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fa&#223;nacht M es autor de una gu&#237;a que aborda la gesti&#243;n del incidentaloma adrenal</data>
      <data key="d10">a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">f492e8d58a5d41f29b1daac1c02c2e41</data>
      <data key="d12">11981</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="YOUNG WF, JR">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Young WF, Jr es autor de un art&#237;culo que proporciona informaci&#243;n sobre el incidentaloma adrenal</data>
      <data key="d10">a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">ec38c69a47674d579420422b827c3f1f</data>
      <data key="d12">11982</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Society of Endocrinology offers comprehensive clinical guidelines for the management of adrenal incidentalomas, also known as incidentaloma suprarrenal. These guidelines are designed to assist healthcare professionals in effectively diagnosing and treating patients with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">6d4297de208c45d39376a90f7c56c41b</data>
      <data key="d12">11983</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="UPTODATE">
      <data key="d8">2.0</data>
      <data key="d9">UpToDate provides current literature and guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas, known in Spanish as "incidentaloma suprarrenal." The platform offers updated information to assist healthcare professionals in effectively managing this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,a9f15831bf090502bcde79d58544ea8b</data>
      <data key="d11">676e752a992749929fec67ed6fabf336</data>
      <data key="d12">11984</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="TAC">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TAC is a preferred imaging test for evaluating adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">4ab50e694dcf463683d5f7a7c380b3d5</data>
      <data key="d12">11985</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="RMN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">RMN is used to better define the characteristics of adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">80bae66ecf5e469394b547b9e1bafaed</data>
      <data key="d12">11986</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="ALD/ARP">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The aldosterone/renin plasma activity ratio is relevant in assessing adrenal function in incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">05ab0c58e143495285262569cb26a0d4</data>
      <data key="d12">11987</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The textbook provides information on adrenal disorders, including incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">53fd633bfc1c4ed1a696e0f91e217727</data>
      <data key="d12">11988</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="GUIAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Guidelines provide recommendations for the management of adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">f90fbdb5575b4e8e9de295d3b33e9a12</data>
      <data key="d12">11989</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="DHEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DHEA levels are evaluated in the context of adrenal incidentalomas to assess hormonal activity</data>
      <data key="d10">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">f2ba941bb3cf4df09deaf60ff7589b06</data>
      <data key="d12">11990</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="DEXAMETASONA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dexamethasone suppression tests are used to evaluate the possibility of autonomous cortisol secretion in adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">8619af1820ac45008dc0e433bf9c5877</data>
      <data key="d12">11991</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="ACTH">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH levels are measured to assess adrenal function in patients with incidental adrenal masses</data>
      <data key="d10">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">b76385020e9c4a9f900112ab036d9d2b</data>
      <data key="d12">11992</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="HIPERCORTISOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercortisolism is a condition that may be associated with adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">1ba8f4e7c2514f07bb9b39c1bf5a6f3b</data>
      <data key="d12">11993</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INCIDENTALOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="METANEFRINAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Metanephrines are assessed to rule out pheochromocytoma in patients with adrenal incidentalomas</data>
      <data key="d10">6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">524edd64c4d24523a5adca92dd53ed3d</data>
      <data key="d12">11994</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="SECRECI&#211;N DE HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The secretion of sex hormones is rare in benign adenomas but may occur in adrenal carcinomas</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0</data>
      <data key="d11">53c5590d530e43ad8aab928f5548d115</data>
      <data key="d12">11995</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="MITOTANO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mitotano is indicated for the treatment of advanced adrenal carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d</data>
      <data key="d11">696a3eb076cf479bb976a0731105843e</data>
      <data key="d12">11996</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL" target="HIDROXIPROGESTERONA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">17-hidroxiprogesterona is relevant in the context of ruling out congenital adrenal hyperplasia in cases of adrenal carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d</data>
      <data key="d11">b28dabb478ab4ae6aa097cc54c38a691</data>
      <data key="d12">11997</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita can be associated with autoimmune conditions, including s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">4408d5ecdfe64e2f8c69dc5d6a80246b</data>
      <data key="d12">11998</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="GLUCOCORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los glucocorticoides son el tratamiento recomendado para controlar la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe</data>
      <data key="d11">1e072943668b430abf1152de7149923f</data>
      <data key="d12">11999</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="21-HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La deficiencia de 21-hidroxilasa es la causa principal de la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe</data>
      <data key="d11">56fb30f2a64e4f04aae4a3a94bbd7173</data>
      <data key="d12">12000</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="ACTH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita es una condici&#243;n m&#233;dica que se diagnostica mediante la estimulaci&#243;n con la hormona adrenocorticotr&#243;pica (ACTH). Esta hormona se utiliza en pruebas espec&#237;ficas para confirmar la presencia de esta enfermedad. La estimulaci&#243;n con ACTH es un m&#233;todo clave en el diagn&#243;stico de la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita, ayudando a los m&#233;dicos a evaluar la funci&#243;n adrenal y determinar si hay una producci&#243;n anormal de hormonas.</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe</data>
      <data key="d11">6b30c9e6d35b41edab55ae2ab42eb431</data>
      <data key="d12">12001</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="MANUAL DE ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A Y NUTRICI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n incluye informaci&#243;n sobre la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899,1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe</data>
      <data key="d11">c1e1901d593a40238d5ad941558078bb</data>
      <data key="d12">12002</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="ENDOCRINE SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La Endocrine Society proporciona gu&#237;as de pr&#225;ctica cl&#237;nica sobre la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe</data>
      <data key="d11">5a2632d714fb4dc8a62830bbbe12a36d</data>
      <data key="d12">12003</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="CYP21A2">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El gen CYP21A2 es responsable de la producci&#243;n de la enzima cuya deficiencia causa hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">eaef57d6b426483aa018029200591abe</data>
      <data key="d12">12004</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="ARLT W.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arlt W. ha escrito sobre trastornos de la corteza suprarrenal, incluyendo la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">83a5d64e03944beebe730021267fad00</data>
      <data key="d12">12005</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="UPTODATE INC.">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">UpToDate Inc. proporciona informaci&#243;n sobre el tratamiento de la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">555354e8b82340179ab4fc50cf9134b1</data>
      <data key="d12">12006</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="KASPER DL.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kasper DL. ha contribuido a la literatura m&#233;dica sobre la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">de8ef779c74342cc9c15aa774d8796d2</data>
      <data key="d12">12007</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="SPEISER PW.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Speiser PW. ha escrito gu&#237;as sobre la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">0b823901c2d4476785f3ddb261906b64</data>
      <data key="d12">12008</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="WILLIAMS TEXTBOOK OF ENDOCRINOLOGY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Williams Textbook of Endocrinology cubre temas relacionados con la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">4b0139a6604e48c28f8a613c5dd4c9fb</data>
      <data key="d12">12009</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="GENOTIPO-FENOTIPO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El genotipo-fenotipo se relaciona con la expresi&#243;n cl&#237;nica de la hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">273e5bdb43ad4634a730e289da533eb1</data>
      <data key="d12">12010</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="HETEROCIGOTOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Un alto porcentaje de pacientes con hiperplasia suprarrenal cong&#233;nita son heterocigotos compuestos para mutaciones en CYP21A2</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">cc51fc965f4d4f59a53b673242c16da7</data>
      <data key="d12">12011</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONG&#201;NITA" target="HIPERANDROGENISMO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Congenital adrenal hyperplasia leads to increased androgen production, causing hyperandrogenism.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">9ec147949e0048ae9a1b3190b35167dc</data>
      <data key="d12">12012</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="METABOLISMO FOSFOC&#193;LCICO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">S&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune can affect metabolic processes, including metabolismo fosfoc&#225;lcico</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">9e4d12fee85147c08c6cfdf0ba268cc1</data>
      <data key="d12">12013</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="ENFERMEDAD DE ADDISON">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune puede incluir enfermedad de Addison como una de sus manifestaciones cl&#237;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">45eefa901c9a4538b7aa6fd93b9ee9b1</data>
      <data key="d12">12014</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="GEN AIRE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1 est&#225; originado por mutaciones en el gen AIRE.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">26695f03c12d4bd09be71c9de7a5ddbf</data>
      <data key="d12">12015</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El hipoparatiroidismo es una de las condiciones que pueden asociarse con el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">75c4ad8f44a1439ba4e28b9a0bfeebe5</data>
      <data key="d12">12016</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="CANDIDIASIS MUCOCUT&#193;NEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La candidiasis mucocut&#225;nea es una manifestaci&#243;n com&#250;n en el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">79dd6fb6c72946d5be871eb4d10563b6</data>
      <data key="d12">12017</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="DIABETES DE TIPO 1">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes de tipo 1 puede presentarse en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">a84752fb04da47ae897299e436a89b8f</data>
      <data key="d12">12018</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="TIROIDITIS AUTOINMUNE CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La tiroiditis autoinmune cr&#243;nica puede asociarse con el s&#237;ndrome poliglandular autoinmune.</data>
      <data key="d10">6c905aeacb0ae6ac9dfa4418c8bf29f7</data>
      <data key="d11">b2c4ec3c4030439a9381df83e701a1fe</data>
      <data key="d12">12019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="POEMS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Autoimmune polyglandular syndrome is related to the endocrine disorders discussed in the context of POEMS syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">77fb6e19a2882617993d1d283afcb86a</data>
      <data key="d11">3d8883b0b2d84e558a69750359e74bc4</data>
      <data key="d12">12020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE" target="HIPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The autoimmune polyglandular syndrome type 1 can lead to hypocalcemia due to parathyroid gland destruction</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">431f9439df154a829477a951998fde42</data>
      <data key="d12">12021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METABOLISMO FOSFOC&#193;LCICO" target="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alterations in metabolismo fosfoc&#225;lcico can influence the behavior of tumores neuroendocrinos</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">db95ee83235d4c8f94b2cc46a1ebfdea</data>
      <data key="d12">12022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="MEN">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tumores neuroendocrinos are often part of the conditions seen in MEN syndromes</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">0f9a39e0d7fa489186785134ffdd02c6</data>
