      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="NURIA VALDES GALLEGO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nuria Valdes Gallego's research focuses on neuroendocrine tumors, particularly paragangliomas and pheochromocytomas</data>
      <data key="d10">cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d11">f95c112a27bb4f77b6ff6ad2e2d04321</data>
      <data key="d12">12024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="HIPERCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercalcemia is a condition that can be related to neuroendocrine tumors and their effects on parathyroid hormone levels</data>
      <data key="d10">cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d11">903ba8635c554d60aabcfc9601809e6e</data>
      <data key="d12">12025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="HYPERCALCEMIA DE MALIGNIDAD">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores neuroendocrinos pueden causar hipercalcemia de malignidad</data>
      <data key="d10">6ba1a5e8454a503171991c13d33cf5e2</data>
      <data key="d11">78d4e51919614718b26561a9f73b382b</data>
      <data key="d12">12026</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulinoma is a specific type of neuroendocrine tumor, establishing a direct relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">c43dc71ed40643379f942628625c524f</data>
      <data key="d12">12027</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="MEN1">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS, or neuroendocrine tumors, are closely associated with MEN1 syndrome. MEN1 is a genetic condition that predisposes individuals to the development of various tumors, including gastrinomas, which are a specific type of neuroendocrine tumor. These tumors are significant in the context of MEN1, as they represent one of the primary causes of mortality among affected patients. Thus, the relationship between MEN1 and neuroendocrine tumors is critical, highlighting the importance of monitoring and managing these tumors in individuals with MEN1 syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc,9851218c3244d6f4279055a04d219044</data>
      <data key="d11">d15867072b3c40c8ae967bb546233de3</data>
      <data key="d12">12028</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS" target="DIARREA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores neuroendocrinos pueden causar s&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales, incluyendo diarrea cr&#243;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">449c8567a3aa59b49fbe65b7a3a26d46</data>
      <data key="d11">4450f3377a79488d84fc12bea718edd3</data>
      <data key="d12">12029</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN" target="WOMEN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both groups are referenced in dietary guidelines with specific nutritional recommendations</data>
      <data key="d10">e173daca5490a19b057aecb1ee4edca2</data>
      <data key="d11">93a937dd302b42d2954cfb5f8fcbf305</data>
      <data key="d12">12030</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">G&#243;nadas play a crucial role in the onset of pubertad precoz by producing sex hormones</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">8749f034cb33442fafbf0e71b85efd22</data>
      <data key="d12">12031</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="GL&#193;NDULA PINEAL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La pubertad precoz puede asociarse con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal, aunque no es la manifestaci&#243;n m&#225;s frecuente.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">6ababac9ad084f66835ec1056a018836</data>
      <data key="d12">12032</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="TRIPTORELINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Triptorelin is used as a treatment for conditions related to precocious puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">2c81359287c249f59332cf33018f3b53</data>
      <data key="d12">12033</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="LEURPORELINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Leuprolide is also used in the management of precocious puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">7f2a2c20ec1546afb54188450703cd66</data>
      <data key="d12">12034</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="SAMUEL NAMARA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Samuel Namara is diagnosed with precocious puberty, showing signs of early sexual maturation</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">b76cf3ecb11444fbad21df3b391c1378</data>
      <data key="d12">12035</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="LUFORAN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Luforan is used in testing for precocious puberty to evaluate gonadotropin response</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">ed09bc1d6d154bbf82912fe6edb37094</data>
      <data key="d12">12036</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Central precocious puberty is a subtype of precocious puberty characterized by early activation of the reproductive hormone axis</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">973f2ed3c11147439ba2ad4330b55fda</data>
      <data key="d12">12037</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="PUBERTAD PRECOZ PERIF&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Peripheral precocious puberty is another subtype of precocious puberty that occurs due to factors outside the central hormonal axis</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">af1ba226c91c4566895c4a92230d3911</data>
      <data key="d12">12038</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="TESTOTOCICOSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La testotoxicosis es una forma de pubertad precoz, ya que causa un desarrollo sexual temprano debido a la producci&#243;n excesiva de testosterona</data>
      <data key="d10">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d11">28673ddb6b364ba69ff463b7ab1a0d8d</data>
      <data key="d12">12039</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ" target="MCUNE-ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de McCune-Albright se relaciona con la pubertad precoz, ya que muchas mujeres con este s&#237;ndrome experimentan desarrollo sexual temprano</data>
      <data key="d10">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d11">f1222c29ae1f4f638e4094c1a1c79399</data>
      <data key="d12">12040</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RETRASO PUBERAL" target="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">G&#243;nadas are involved in the hormonal regulation that can lead to retraso puberal</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">c490c4b0c5fe4d45b8d8e7e38664fe57</data>
      <data key="d12">12041</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMOS" target="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipogonadismos directly affect the function of g&#243;nadas, leading to insufficient hormone production</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">caeaa2bd145446349f3b8445ee1675bd</data>
      <data key="d12">12042</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMOS" target="HIRSUTISMO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hirsutismo can be a symptom of hipogonadismos due to hormonal imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">b7a9ed32a8ae45d1ad6998d79d72cfc8</data>
      <data key="d12">12043</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASTORNOS DE LA DIFERENCIACI&#211;N SEXUAL" target="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Trastornos de la diferenciaci&#243;n sexual can arise from abnormalities in g&#243;nadas</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">cedbc4085e5c4c94a60ae7e1efab9762</data>
      <data key="d12">12044</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIRSUTISMO" target="CUSHING'S SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hirsutism can be a symptom of Cushing's syndrome due to elevated androgen levels</data>
      <data key="d10">88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f</data>
      <data key="d11">cb0a68a411714d0899401da628a8657c</data>
      <data key="d12">12045</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIRSUTISMO" target="HIPERANDROGENISMO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hirsutismo is a common manifestation of hyperandrogenism, indicating a direct relationship between the two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">f98cdf6260234a2595ef3528ec1f8951</data>
      <data key="d12">12046</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIRSUTISMO" target="S&#205;NDROME DE OVARIO POLIQU&#205;STICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de ovario poliqu&#237;stico es una de las causas m&#225;s comunes de hirsutismo en mujeres debido a la producci&#243;n elevada de andr&#243;genos.</data>
      <data key="d10">401a6af689562ae0b9d7fe627eb56d0f</data>
      <data key="d11">bfcffa6b88ab4570999c7d8daca87a27</data>
      <data key="d12">12047</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRANSEXUALES" target="G&#211;NADAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Transexuales may seek medical intervention related to g&#243;nadas as part of their transition process</data>
      <data key="d10">bcb4f7ab0760e548b520c667b305722a</data>
      <data key="d11">f8383c2619594a8597e86efad01859c7</data>
      <data key="d12">12048</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="G&#211;NADAS" target="HORMONAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gonads produce sex hormones that are crucial for reproductive functions</data>
      <data key="d10">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d11">e4e6a9e92f924421989a6d8b0665465d</data>
      <data key="d12">12049</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="HIPOCALCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipercalcemia and hipocalcemia are both conditions related to abnormal calcium levels in the blood, representing opposite ends of the calcium balance spectrum.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">57e81d5919224305acaa995ac0503ee5</data>
      <data key="d12">12050</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="TRASTORNOS ELECTROLITICOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipercalcemia is another specific type of electrolyte disorder, indicating a direct relationship between the two entities.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">059b363786a94f818a040d9064720412</data>
      <data key="d12">12051</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="MAR&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercalcemia could be a differential diagnosis for Mar&#237;a's symptoms, as it can affect kidney function</data>
      <data key="d10">d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d11">3b8b0f2e87e1403b8ed553447e34c48e</data>
      <data key="d12">12052</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="CALCITONINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcitonin is used to treat hypercalcemia by inhibiting osteoclastic activity and promoting renal calcium excretion</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">1de7601d619240e69c40744aa6759645</data>
      <data key="d12">12053</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="PAMIDRONATO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pamidronate is used to treat hypercalcemia by inhibiting bone resorption</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">fc842d4a09d3486a892d8a3af0e6c42c</data>
      <data key="d12">12054</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="FUROSEMIDA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Furosemide can be used in the management of hypercalcemia to promote renal excretion of calcium</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">ae821093f36542fd9d6fde64fbc38f4d</data>
      <data key="d12">12055</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="SUERO SALINO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Saline solution is used in the treatment of hypercalcemia to help hydrate and manage calcium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">5b17d64092ad4d44b013a0720cb43a66</data>
      <data key="d12">12056</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipercalcemia, characterized by elevated levels of calcium in the blood, can lead to the formation of kidney stones, known as litiasis renal. This condition arises when excess calcium is excreted in the urine, contributing to the development of stones within the kidneys. Therefore, litiasis renal can occur as a direct consequence of hypercalcemia, highlighting the relationship between these two medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d11">7a73a8c89b6b41e79d6776f9e491f3e5</data>
      <data key="d12">12057</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="PTH">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIPERCALCEMIA is a condition characterized by elevated levels of calcium in the blood. Parathyroid hormone (PTH) plays a crucial role in regulating calcium levels within the body. Its activity is significant in maintaining calcium homeostasis, and an excess of PTH can lead to an increase in calcium levels, thereby contributing to the development of hipercalcemia. Thus, the regulation of calcium by PTH is essential, and any imbalance in PTH levels can influence the occurrence of hipercalcemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">0e8d90c22b3a48b79329e0465638543c</data>
      <data key="d12">12058</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="CALCIO PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipercalcemia se caracteriza por un aumento del calcio plasm&#225;tico por encima de 10,5 mg/dl.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">0a90390a696040eda71d9adf3279ad0f</data>
      <data key="d12">12059</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="DIETA CONTROLADA EN CALCIO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Una dieta controlada en calcio se recomienda para manejar la hipercalcemia, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">3c07075c64ac41d391afbd50ece85d70</data>
      <data key="d12">12060</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="ALUMINIO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La intoxicaci&#243;n por aluminio puede ser una de las causas de hipercalcemia, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">22bff1173fec4946b89ad56a8ece4a9a</data>
      <data key="d12">12061</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="TIAZIDAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de f&#225;rmacos como las tiazidas puede influir en los niveles de calcio, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">f7eeffc776bd4ceb8ca438d6aa59ca9a</data>
      <data key="d12">12062</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="LITIO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El litio es un f&#225;rmaco que puede causar hipercalcemia, lo que establece una relaci&#243;n entre ambos.</data>
      <data key="d10">8824d8c01c7332dd9fd487d1ece0f7e5</data>
      <data key="d11">04014937ff7247cab4dab80cc66a2ef9</data>
      <data key="d12">12063</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="HIPERPARATIROIDISMO PRIMARIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipercalcemia is commonly caused by hyperparathyroidism, where excess parathyroid hormone leads to increased calcium levels in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d10">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d11">01289619becb456b9af2178e08c12285</data>
      <data key="d12">12064</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERCALCEMIA" target="HIPOCAUCALCEMIA IDIOP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipercalcemia can be associated with idiopathic hypercalciuria, which is characterized by abnormal calcium levels in urine.</data>
      <data key="d10">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d11">f603d723faa9461eaa823201e8fa1f84</data>
      <data key="d12">12065</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="TRASTORNOS ELECTROLITICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipocalcemia is a specific type of electrolyte disorder, indicating a direct relationship between the two entities.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">8afdbc5eab7143a7b0eca458d0ce67b9</data>
      <data key="d12">12066</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="MAR&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypocalcemia may also be considered in the context of her overall health and symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d11">fb5d0e5b82234fb49b17cbeef0beee30</data>
      <data key="d12">12067</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="PTH">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIPOCALCEMIA, or hypocalcemia, is a condition characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood. Parathyroid hormone (PTH) plays a crucial role in regulating calcium levels within the body. A deficiency or dysfunction of PTH can lead to hypocalcemia, as it is responsible for maintaining appropriate calcium concentrations. In cases of hypocalcemia, PTH levels are typically low due to parathyroid dysfunction, which is a significant contributing factor to the development of this condition. Thus, the relationship between PTH and hypocalcemia is critical, with PTH being essential for calcium homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4,85df619f6d535bbe5c0485f540242903</data>
      <data key="d11">69f2bd7ec3214d81875b9f5c08e42d64</data>
      <data key="d12">12068</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipoparatiroidismo leads to chronic hypocalcemia due to insufficient parathyroid hormone production</data>
      <data key="d10">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d11">d2b0835e3b1540c9a1b8487632ed0c8a</data>
      <data key="d12">12069</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="CALCIO PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipocalcemia se define por un descenso del calcio plasm&#225;tico total por debajo de 8,5 mg/dl.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">52a3547a420a4d9bbf93c50448d0c4a6</data>
      <data key="d12">12070</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="HIPOALBUMINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoalbuminemia puede causar una falsa hipocalcemia, afectando la medici&#243;n del calcio en el suero.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">26f84f26d09b4c1cba3d696f1d20ee21</data>
      <data key="d12">12071</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="ALCALOSIS RESPIRATORIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La alcalosis respiratoria puede causar un aumento en la fijaci&#243;n del calcio a la alb&#250;mina, afectando los niveles de calcio ionizado.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">e213f8fdd248412c91ae657f24691077</data>
      <data key="d12">12072</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="ALCALOSIS METAB&#211;LICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La alcalosis metab&#243;lica puede causar un aumento en la fijaci&#243;n del calcio a la alb&#250;mina, afectando los niveles de calcio ionizado.</data>
      <data key="d10">30676865841b1573426895ff17c40ab4</data>
      <data key="d11">543d9f46bcc747e3b94f6148d1ffc6ba</data>
      <data key="d12">12073</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOCALCEMIA" target="PACIENTE PEDI&#193;TRICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pediatric patients receiving parenteral nutrition may develop hypocalcemia if calcium levels are not monitored</data>
      <data key="d10">c06e5bcd7933ed338cd1257d11c709cf</data>
      <data key="d11">0e2bc9e8ec274e9ea5d38ea2beeb60c5</data>
      <data key="d12">12074</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASTORNOS ELECTROLITICOS" target="CASOS CLINICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Trastornos electrol&#237;ticos are frequently examined in clinical cases to highlight their effects on patient health and treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">79d722fcf8c140fb80d7d157425a61cf</data>
      <data key="d12">12075</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASTORNOS ELECTROLITICOS" target="M&#211;DULO 8">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M&#243;dulo 8 covers electrolyte disorders, discussing their relevance to obesity and lipid metabolism in health contexts.</data>
      <data key="d10">7c6e51fbc38204b42b4d619b271037c3</data>
      <data key="d11">8c9aa33311ee47d0b05157662964c77b</data>
      <data key="d12">12076</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
