    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="PROLACTINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La prolactina es una hormona producida por la adenohip&#243;fisis que regula la lactancia</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">4c6caf0d01e94d7eaf8a75770cd177b7</data>
      <data key="d12">12138</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="TSH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La TSH es una hormona producida por la adenohip&#243;fisis que regula la funci&#243;n tiroidea</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">5bdb4aae46f646159825a348a7449126</data>
      <data key="d12">12139</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="GH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La GH es una hormona secretada por la adenohip&#243;fisis que es crucial para el crecimiento y desarrollo</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">b9fc6ae48b7c41a6bde2ad6815e09118</data>
      <data key="d12">12140</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="FSH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La FSH es una gonadotropina producida por la adenohip&#243;fisis que regula el desarrollo de los fol&#237;culos ov&#225;ricos</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">652c9ac3d9c34bbc84a80d54f1146000</data>
      <data key="d12">12141</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="LH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La LH es otra gonadotropina producida por la adenohip&#243;fisis que regula el ciclo menstrual y la ovulaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">78558e36354d4031a98cc8e5d1d4cab6</data>
      <data key="d12">12142</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="BOLSA DE RATHKE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La adenohip&#243;fisis se origina de la bolsa de Rathke durante el desarrollo embrionario</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">a017ea275aef45ef8a49be2bbad796c4</data>
      <data key="d12">12143</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="HIPOTALAMO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El hipot&#225;lamo regula la secreci&#243;n de hormonas de la adenohip&#243;fisis a trav&#233;s de hormonas adenohipofisotropas</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">36ed44db644b42c7802e31457f879faf</data>
      <data key="d12">12144</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="CITOCINAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las citocinas pueden influir en la secreci&#243;n de hormonas de la adenohip&#243;fisis</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">0be699b56d6d453cab13364b4a548459</data>
      <data key="d12">12145</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="FACTORES SOLUBLES DE CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los factores solubles de crecimiento pueden influir en la regulaci&#243;n de la secreci&#243;n de hormonas en la adenohip&#243;fisis</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">57da382e548149f59e6e0a23a23bc310</data>
      <data key="d12">12146</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="RETROALIMENTACI&#211;N NEGATIVA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La retroalimentaci&#243;n negativa regula la secreci&#243;n de hormonas hipofisarias a trav&#233;s de hormonas perif&#233;ricas</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">944a410aa588494aa4a1a2be736fd783</data>
      <data key="d12">12147</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="DOPAMINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dopamina act&#250;a como un inhibidor de la secreci&#243;n de prolactina en la adenohip&#243;fisis</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">50e7808a14c54d799cdf1c587cbee5aa</data>
      <data key="d12">12148</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOHIP&#211;FISIS" target="HORMONAS HIPOFISARIAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The adenohypophysis is responsible for producing pituitary hormones, which are affected by transcription factor mutations.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">5ea4bb4592424f5a86521f340c5355e8</data>
      <data key="d12">12149</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROHIP&#211;FISIS" target="OXITOCINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La oxitocina es una hormona que se libera desde la neurohip&#243;fisis y est&#225; involucrada en el parto y la lactancia</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">b9353fbee772438f8b969ffbc2bc52c8</data>
      <data key="d12">12150</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROHIP&#211;FISIS" target="VASOPRESINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La vasopresina es una hormona que se libera desde la neurohip&#243;fisis y regula la retenci&#243;n de agua en los ri&#241;ones</data>
      <data key="d10">78b093da6669fb9ed3258ed62a73260e</data>
      <data key="d11">0347932f91e1415795efbeaaf4d3853d</data>
      <data key="d12">12151</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROHIP&#211;FISIS" target="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetes ins&#237;pida is often caused by dysfunction of the neurohip&#243;fisis</data>
      <data key="d10">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d11">aad6a20774144ce79008872ace135aec</data>
      <data key="d12">12152</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROHIP&#211;FISIS" target="ADH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The neurohypophysis is responsible for the secretion of ADH into the bloodstream</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">29d1d3e4141a41b3a27333e1297edc60</data>
      <data key="d12">12153</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROHIP&#211;FISIS" target="N. SUPRA&#211;PTICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The supraoptic nucleus sends signals to the neurohypophysis to release ADH</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">71f5bfb077b24438ba171fcaf871ee31</data>
      <data key="d12">12154</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROLACTINA" target="DOPAMINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dopamina inhibe la secreci&#243;n de prolactina en el cuerpo humano</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198</data>
      <data key="d11">813de5d867454f748de0b83798ea7d3a</data>
      <data key="d12">12155</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="GNRH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GnRH stimulates the secretion of TSH from the pituitary gland</data>
      <data key="d10">68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c</data>
      <data key="d11">d9d4d30f4d00411aaa7d2cb38c03a3f4</data>
      <data key="d12">12156</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="TRH">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TRH (Thyrotropin-Releasing Hormone) plays a crucial role in the regulation of thyroid function by stimulating the secretion of TSH (Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone) from the pituitary gland. The release of TSH, in turn, prompts the thyroid gland to produce thyroid hormones, which are essential for various metabolic processes in the body. Thus, TRH is integral to the hormonal cascade that regulates thyroid activity through its stimulation of TSH release.</data>
      <data key="d10">68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">ef3f74f835b04d3ca53b056b4567bbfe</data>
      <data key="d12">12157</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="GLUCOCORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TSH levels are important for adjusting glucocorticoid treatment in patients with hypothyroidism</data>
      <data key="d10">55a9e6e8ff365dac34555c938dd3c244</data>
      <data key="d11">5121524043e248f2b508ba5bcf63fb91</data>
      <data key="d12">12158</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="TUMORES HIPOFISARIOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores hipofisarios pueden ser productores de TSH, afectando la regulaci&#243;n de la tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626</data>
      <data key="d11">92ad76e7080d49b9915eeefc98483e71</data>
      <data key="d12">12159</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipofisitis es una condici&#243;n que puede provocar d&#233;ficits de TSH (hormona estimulante de la tiroides), lo que a su vez afecta la funci&#243;n tiroidea. Esta relaci&#243;n indica que la hipofisitis tiene un impacto significativo en la regulaci&#243;n hormonal y puede llevar a alteraciones en el funcionamiento de la tiroides debido a la disminuci&#243;n de TSH.</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d11">f8aa5d5d62524f8c9f522af8f87bba25</data>
      <data key="d12">12160</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="AMIODARONA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amiodarone can induce thyroid dysfunction, which may require monitoring of TSH levels in affected patients</data>
      <data key="d10">be2de576112f22070e8ef8a5cb9e1017</data>
      <data key="d11">b22f81a0f0f44ea29ea188c963b29580</data>
      <data key="d12">12161</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="CARBAMACEPINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbamazepine affects the metabolism of thyroid hormones, necessitating TSH level monitoring in hypothyroid patients</data>
      <data key="d10">be2de576112f22070e8ef8a5cb9e1017</data>
      <data key="d11">3d950287ac0b462791e94a73412e9406</data>
      <data key="d12">12162</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="HCG">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HCG influences TSH levels during pregnancy, affecting thyroid function and management</data>
      <data key="d10">92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2</data>
      <data key="d11">96b076c871fc4e80a878be60e6f553f8</data>
      <data key="d12">12163</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="T4L">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">T4L and TSH levels are both critical for assessing thyroid function, especially in pregnant women</data>
      <data key="d10">92e235fe76b5046c18c1cb2c782e1ac2</data>
      <data key="d11">f2447242b75a4f189590200087fd3f60</data>
      <data key="d12">12164</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="BOCIO DIFUSO NO T&#211;XICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La TSH media la hiperplasia tiroidea en respuesta a factores que dificultan la s&#237;ntesis de hormonas tiroideas, como el bocio difuso no t&#243;xico.</data>
      <data key="d10">14299e85574ef5c76c7164e2c4d20a53</data>
      <data key="d11">9ea6c1adcb3a4c778bffa62f952c723b</data>
      <data key="d12">12165</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="TBG">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TSH levels can influence the production of TBG, affecting thyroid hormone transport</data>
      <data key="d10">bbe700b5b290ea119e511c94a6f0c67f</data>
      <data key="d11">d3c40cfd70fa488a8fbeea5d456853d0</data>
      <data key="d12">12166</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TSH levels are critical in diagnosing and managing medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">a7471638fcdb48a9b74a664323fdd05c</data>
      <data key="d12">12167</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="FEMALE PATIENT">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TSH levels may be evaluated to rule out thyroid-related causes of delayed puberty in the female patient</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">6a9a99a19e824c0789b01f87aea28f32</data>
      <data key="d12">12168</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La TSH se eval&#250;a para descartar problemas tiroideos que pueden afectar el desarrollo puberal</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">6a65842bf3cf4e17aa199214c51c7764</data>
      <data key="d12">12169</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TSH" target="THYROID HORMONES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TSH stimulates the thyroid gland to produce thyroid hormones, which regulate metabolism</data>
      <data key="d10">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">2fcc822dcfeb4a0ea606b2c287b66910</data>
      <data key="d12">12170</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="SOMATOSTATINA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin is a peptide hormone that plays a crucial role in regulating various physiological processes. It is known to inhibit the secretion of growth hormone (GH) from the pituitary gland. This inhibitory effect on GH secretion is significant in maintaining hormonal balance within the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c</data>
      <data key="d11">4c1d8fa855b449faad768f2bbd827e2c</data>
      <data key="d12">12171</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="IGF-1">
      <data key="d8">22.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Growth Hormone (GH) and Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 (IGF-1) are closely related entities in the context of growth and development. GH stimulates the production of IGF-1, which plays a crucial role in promoting growth and development in various tissues. Conversely, IGF-1 acts as a suppressor of GH secretion, regulating its activity and ensuring a balanced hormonal environment. This interplay highlights the regulatory relationship between GH and IGF-1, where GH promotes IGF-1 production, while IGF-1, in turn, modulates the secretion of GH.</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c,adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa</data>
      <data key="d11">36138973a7474941858224fb286ce9ad</data>
      <data key="d12">12172</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="SUE&#209;O PROFUNDO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Deep sleep stimulates the secretion of growth hormone</data>
      <data key="d10">68be432b2dd3e64676989cd544f23d8c</data>
      <data key="d11">d35618ec5c1e41a68fe6868923c6bf90</data>
      <data key="d12">12173</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="IGFBP3">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IGFBP3 levels are dependent on GH levels, increasing when GH levels rise</data>
      <data key="d10">adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa</data>
      <data key="d11">8da14ddecb2a4d8ca1c052fb2bc3cf3c</data>
      <data key="d12">12174</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="HYP&#211;FISIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hypophysis (pituitary gland) produces GH, which is crucial for growth</data>
      <data key="d10">adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa</data>
      <data key="d11">4557e88d39424e3692402e19d36e2142</data>
      <data key="d12">12175</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">En hipofisitis, la reserva de GH puede ser normal, a pesar de los d&#233;ficits de otras hormonas</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d11">e41d351142af434b8e514290bd90ec60</data>
      <data key="d12">12176</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acromegalia is a condition caused by the hypersecretion of growth hormone (GH). This excessive production of GH leads to abnormal growth and enlargement of various body parts. The condition is characterized by noticeable changes in physical appearance, including enlarged hands, feet, and facial features.</data>
      <data key="d10">9b9d487a35d8197bfe9d1aa0fce19c32,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">59b92ff1400e4803873d26ad70820afa</data>
      <data key="d12">12177</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="ACROMEGALY">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Excess growth hormone (GH) is a primary cause of acromegaly</data>
      <data key="d10">2261671ccad439da1ed9ea5a27857dc8</data>
      <data key="d11">65b08c88e132424993f34a593a3c0b4c</data>
      <data key="d12">12178</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="FEMALE PATIENT">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Growth hormone levels may be assessed in the context of delayed puberty in the female patient</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">998b677c8b644ad7ad6eefff577d250e</data>
      <data key="d12">12179</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GH" target="GHRH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GHRH stimulates the release of growth hormone from the pituitary gland, promoting growth</data>
      <data key="d10">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">7129008dcfd143c495a9626ecc10a8ce</data>
      <data key="d12">12180</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="LH">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FSH (Hormona Fol&#237;culo Estimulante) y LH (Hormona Luteinizante) son gonadotropinas que desempe&#241;an un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n de las funciones reproductivas. Ambas hormonas son secretadas por la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria y est&#225;n interrelacionadas en su secreci&#243;n, lo que les permite trabajar de manera sin&#233;rgica para regular el desarrollo sexual y la reproducci&#243;n. FSH y LH son fundamentales en procesos como la pubertad, y su liberaci&#243;n est&#225; controlada por la GnRH (Hormona Liberadora de Gonadotropinas). En conjunto, estas hormonas son esenciales para el funcionamiento adecuado del sistema reproductivo.</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">7a069862a6e14811ac0181eddd48b69e</data>
      <data key="d12">12181</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FSH (Hormone Follicle-Stimulating) and HIPOFISITIS (Hypophysitis) are interconnected in the context of hormonal regulation and diagnosis. In cases of hipofisitis, it is noted that the levels of FSH may remain normal despite the presence of hormonal deficits. This phenomenon can complicate the clinical picture, as normal FSH levels can mislead healthcare providers during diagnosis. Therefore, the presence of normal FSH levels in hipofisitis can serve as a significant indicator, highlighting the need for careful evaluation when diagnosing this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d11">b0b81368d93e424b89efa5946d68126c</data>
      <data key="d12">12182</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="GONADOTROFINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La FSH es otra gonadotropina que se secreta durante la pubertad y que estimula la funci&#243;n gonadal</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">0da42f71dfed43f492d934c503334d3e</data>
      <data key="d12">12183</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="SAMUEL NAMARA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Samuel Namara's FSH levels are measured to assess his reproductive health in the context of precocious puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">4932f99e60aa4f15912b39ad77a60fdd</data>
      <data key="d12">12184</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="AMENORREA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FSH levels are evaluated to understand the reproductive hormone balance in cases of primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">b341b5d7fe67446cae849745151add55</data>
      <data key="d12">12185</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La FSH es una de las hormonas sexuales que se eval&#250;an para determinar el estado del eje gonadal</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">63c3cdc5f1954c01ba76950e3478df3e</data>
      <data key="d12">12186</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="HORMONAL STUDY">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FSH levels were measured as part of the hormonal study to evaluate the patient's endocrine function.</data>
      <data key="d10">592d424edaa447a54ab4489d82495db6</data>
      <data key="d11">f090ca4f072e4065bac97d6534704a0f</data>
      <data key="d12">12187</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FSH" target="C&#201;LULAS DE SERTOLI">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La FSH estimula las c&#233;lulas de Sertoli para la producci&#243;n de esperma, crucial para la fertilidad masculina</data>
      <data key="d10">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99</data>
      <data key="d11">20a9364f98bf41729108dc437e245323</data>
      <data key="d12">12188</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="GHRH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GHRH estimula la liberaci&#243;n de LH y FSH en la hip&#243;fisis</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198</data>
      <data key="d11">a98db15a5d9b42d09a9f25bdeb0867ec</data>
      <data key="d12">12189</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LH (Luteinizing Hormone) is a hormone that can exhibit normal levels in cases of hipofisitis, a condition characterized by inflammation of the pituitary gland. In hipofisitis, despite the presence of hormonal deficits, the levels of LH may remain within the normal range. This phenomenon can serve as a significant indicator during the diagnostic process for hipofisitis, highlighting the complexity of hormonal interactions and the importance of comprehensive evaluation in understanding the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d11">f7745b64084c42d8bb68c91e51f331c4</data>
      <data key="d12">12190</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="GONADOTROFINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La LH es una de las gonadotrofinas que se secretan durante la pubertad y que estimulan la funci&#243;n gonadal</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">a84280df71b94726992ef6c9525c0d42</data>
      <data key="d12">12191</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="SAMUEL NAMARA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Samuel Namara's LH levels are evaluated to understand his hormonal status related to precocious puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">9a92d2ad7423e6f4566f67259abc86b2</data>
      <data key="d11">5198c074653f4b8d9f0689777f1660c7</data>
      <data key="d12">12192</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">McCune-Albright syndrome is associated with precocious puberty, which involves the regulation of LH levels</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">539c9f1a75dc48bda21623864dd16cdc</data>
      <data key="d12">12193</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="GNRH">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LH (Luteinizing Hormone) and GnRH (Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone) are closely related entities in the endocrine system. GnRH stimulates the release of LH from the pituitary gland, playing a vital role in the process of ovulation. Additionally, LH is released in response to GnRH, which is essential for the onset of puberty. Together, these hormones are critical for regulating reproductive functions in the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">4413d3abc5a3469789b9684630f51490</data>
      <data key="d12">12194</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="AMENORREA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LH levels are measured to assess the hormonal status in cases of primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">ecaaf3603faf489cb20d94bb1ab7bfd4</data>
      <data key="d12">12195</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="HORMONAS SEXUALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La LH es otra hormona sexual que se eval&#250;a junto con la FSH para entender el desarrollo puberal</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">13065b8f15454c30bad707262b319065</data>
      <data key="d12">12196</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="HORMONAL STUDY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LH levels were also measured in the hormonal study to assess the patient's hormonal balance.</data>
      <data key="d10">592d424edaa447a54ab4489d82495db6</data>
      <data key="d11">a916885509264c51ac55baf19091b79e</data>
      <data key="d12">12197</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LH" target="C&#201;LULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La LH estimula las c&#233;lulas de Leydig para producir testosterona, esencial para la funci&#243;n testicular</data>
      <data key="d10">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99</data>
      <data key="d11">7e7d655f90a84e61bae972a69efd82c4</data>
      <data key="d12">12198</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DOPAMINA" target="CUPROENZIMAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dopamine metabolism is influenced by cuproenzyme activity in the brain</data>
      <data key="d10">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">13904ad11412440282dcb6a882ae97e2</data>
      <data key="d12">12199</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DOPAMINA" target="NOREPINEFRINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Norepinephrine is synthesized from dopamine in the brain</data>
      <data key="d10">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">e0130f28bab74ad0bf0c849f0ca6d061</data>
      <data key="d12">12200</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VASOPRESINA" target="ACTH">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La vasopresina est&#225; implicada en la regulaci&#243;n de la secreci&#243;n de ACTH</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198</data>
      <data key="d11">7fb6458a322c441195d4c70a99668225</data>
      <data key="d12">12201</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GHRH" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In less than 5% of acromegalia cases, the cause is excess GHRH due to a hypothalamic or neuroendocrine tumor</data>
      <data key="d10">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">fbf949eff29f4262a87a49661038bc68</data>
      <data key="d12">12202</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="TUMORES HIPOFISARIOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores hipofisarios productores de TSH utilizan an&#225;logos de somatostatina como parte de su tratamiento</data>
      <data key="d10">b18ef5c018c100e1582224fe82f03626</data>
      <data key="d11">02c67800bab94dbaaf08483a1bca563f</data>
      <data key="d12">12203</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin analogs are used to treat acromegaly by inhibiting growth hormone secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">82a508cead564659ac62b999ee47fd87</data>
      <data key="d12">12204</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="DEHISCENCIA DE ANASTOMOSIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La somatostatina se utiliza como tratamiento conservador en casos de dehiscencia de anastomosis tras la cirug&#237;a</data>
      <data key="d10">3ee948dc4ddfdc75daa8fe7db9bb471e</data>
      <data key="d11">a15d6593eb00421b962816290ebe811f</data>
      <data key="d12">12205</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="OCTREOTIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Octreotide is an analog of somatostatin and is used in conjunction with it to enhance treatment efficacy for lymphatic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">064e2cf3b0324c7197c570947ea36c30</data>
      <data key="d12">12206</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin is utilized in the conservative treatment of quilot&#243;rax, especially in instances where there is significant fluid loss. It functions by reducing lymphatic flow, which aids in the resolution of chylothorax. This dual role highlights somatostatin's importance in managing conditions associated with lymphatic fluid accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">7da3aa2063fb43aca85c1f91a88af4f4</data>
      <data key="d12">12207</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="FLUJO LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin is known to reduce lymphatic flow, which is beneficial in treating conditions like chylothorax.</data>
      <data key="d10">b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">46a806675fac40ba9edefff05126c6e9</data>
      <data key="d12">12208</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SOMATOSTATINA" target="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin is part of the conservative treatment for ascitis quilosa, especially in cases with significant fluid loss</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">a73573f1b92349018d178666efe308b4</data>
      <data key="d12">12209</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">33.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH (hormona adrenocorticotr&#243;pica) regula la secreci&#243;n de cortisol en respuesta a factores como el estr&#233;s. Esta hormona estimula las gl&#225;ndulas suprarrenales para producir cortisol, estableciendo una relaci&#243;n directa entre ambas hormonas. La producci&#243;n de cortisol es fundamental para la respuesta al estr&#233;s, lo que resalta la importancia de ACTH en la regulaci&#243;n de las funciones del cuerpo relacionadas con el manejo del estr&#233;s.</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,6083387b51909347a13ed5aa1c92bb26,c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">d082a4daa15c457b80147c3f82dbdbb3</data>
      <data key="d12">12210</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="CRH">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Corticotropin-releasing hormone (CRH) plays a vital role in the body's stress response by stimulating the release of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) from the pituitary gland. This process is essential for the regulation of cortisol levels, which are critical for managing stress. Through its action on the pituitary gland, CRH initiates a cascade of hormonal responses that help the body respond effectively to stressors.</data>
      <data key="d10">08a470f7ca590eb337a66093ccb5c198,88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">f9e2091d096a40ce922b5b4c45d86c2f</data>
      <data key="d12">12211</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="GLUCOCORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH levels are monitored to adjust glucocorticoid treatment in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">55a9e6e8ff365dac34555c938dd3c244</data>
      <data key="d11">0dc6a3ec292f4edeabcfac282699bc1b</data>
      <data key="d12">12212</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="HIPOFISITIS">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH (Hormona Adrenocorticotr&#243;pica) y la hipofisitis est&#225;n interrelacionados, ya que la hipofisitis puede causar d&#233;ficits de ACTH, lo que a su vez afecta la funci&#243;n adrenal. Esta condici&#243;n implica una inflamaci&#243;n de la gl&#225;ndula pituitaria, que puede resultar en una disminuci&#243;n en la producci&#243;n de ACTH, llevando a disfunciones en la respuesta adrenal del organismo.</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1,e5bb316d81c54ddbb3d8c7d9c2f9fc14</data>
      <data key="d11">36883e154ad74caca7104540d566c3a5</data>
      <data key="d12">12213</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH, o hormona adrenocorticotr&#243;pica, es la hormona cuya producci&#243;n anormal est&#225; asociada con la enfermedad de Cushing. Esta hormona juega un papel crucial en la regulaci&#243;n del cortisol, ya que estimula su producci&#243;n en las gl&#225;ndulas suprarrenales. En el contexto de la enfermedad de Cushing, los niveles elevados de ACTH pueden contribuir a la sobreproducci&#243;n de cortisol, lo que lleva a los s&#237;ntomas caracter&#237;sticos de esta condici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f,dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb</data>
      <data key="d11">c4ccb8bbbdd644fb99267e2c9d390d64</data>
      <data key="d12">12214</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="CUSHING'S SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">43.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH, or adrenocorticotropic hormone, is a key hormone that plays a crucial role in the development and management of Cushing's syndrome. It stimulates the production of cortisol, a hormone that is often found in elevated levels in individuals with Cushing's syndrome. This condition is frequently caused by excessive levels of ACTH, which leads to increased cortisol production. Consequently, elevated ACTH levels are commonly observed in patients suffering from Cushing's syndrome. The relationship between ACTH and cortisol is significant, as it is essential for both the diagnosis and management of this syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,85eef7ed9c9b92d86939a6687ea2acfd,88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0,bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257</data>
      <data key="d11">d3f3da732c1a4959a265788944a21bbd</data>
      <data key="d12">12215</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="COLLESTEROL DESMOLASE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH stimulates cholesterol desmolase to enhance steroid hormone production, which is relevant in Cushing's syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">85eef7ed9c9b92d86939a6687ea2acfd</data>
      <data key="d11">680917a4c33143eeb77d86195e7f7569</data>
      <data key="d12">12216</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="HYPOTHALAMUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hypothalamus regulates the secretion of ACTH from the pituitary gland, which in turn stimulates cortisol production in the adrenal cortex</data>
      <data key="d10">b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0</data>
      <data key="d11">c73898edc07343b78b16268a8d33e78f</data>
      <data key="d12">12217</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="ENFERMEDAD DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad de McCune-Albright est&#225; relacionada con mutaciones que afectan la regulaci&#243;n de ACTH</data>
      <data key="d10">62abcb4e755766817e948341a56b196b</data>
      <data key="d11">635e3ea2f5f24900a683429d99030c57</data>
      <data key="d12">12218</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="HYPERALDOSTERONISM FAMILIAR TIPO 1">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH signaling can influence aldosterone production in familial hyperaldosteronism type 1</data>
      <data key="d10">7f3df1437755b60344fdffd2ef3b8a9e</data>
      <data key="d11">d02f161dead24e8d9265603784ffbc62</data>
      <data key="d12">12219</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="ALDOSTERONE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH regulates the production of aldosterone, especially in conditions involving the chimeric gene.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c</data>
      <data key="d11">9c7c47dde2c74175b82f85d8e95a1f78</data>
      <data key="d12">12220</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="HIPERPLASIA SUPRARRENAL CONGENITA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Congenital adrenal hyperplasia leads to increased levels of ACTH due to cortisol deficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">8eb2b7021402eb440fe88889b78c2785</data>
      <data key="d11">09a31c5d3c00490b9339d75ac9e4ce44</data>
      <data key="d12">12221</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="TETRACOSACTIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La tetracosactida es un an&#225;logo sint&#233;tico de ACTH utilizado en pruebas de estimulaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">095d265c06452e52ccbfbc871a19a899</data>
      <data key="d11">d54dee5f95da44428c535099716c2133</data>
      <data key="d12">12222</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH levels are measured to diagnose acute adrenal insufficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
      <data key="d11">ea075585e25b49dcafd30097dfdf4810</data>
      <data key="d12">12223</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="ADH">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH influences the secretion of ADH, which can impact water balance and sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">e5a3c206a42a0c2ba4df914b54591a3b</data>
      <data key="d11">20c000f215c14cd1b351e5afcaa253b5</data>
      <data key="d12">12224</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACTH" target="HIPONATREMIA EUVOL&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Un d&#233;ficit de ACTH puede contribuir a la hiponatremia, ya que afecta la producci&#243;n de cortisol y la regulaci&#243;n de l&#237;quidos.</data>
      <data key="d10">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d11">753814a48b0943f5b6b49d45047838f9</data>
      <data key="d12">12225</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="INSULIN">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol affects insulin sensitivity and glucose metabolism, particularly during pregnancy, impacting how insulin functions in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">7b084f7afc5f3c66a528475ae4fa76b1</data>
      <data key="d11">bb046ac8b34f43c1a444a1395c5a4af4</data>
      <data key="d12">12226</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="DIABETES 2">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol levels can increase in response to stress, contributing to insulin resistance and hyperglycemia in diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582</data>
      <data key="d11">eb3a4b3d6d9445f79df7bb5d4aaf8f51</data>
      <data key="d12">12227</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="CUSHING'S SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol is a crucial hormone in the diagnosis and management of Cushing's syndrome, a condition characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body. Elevated cortisol levels are a key indicator of this syndrome, highlighting the importance of monitoring and understanding cortisol's role in this disorder.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257</data>
      <data key="d11">eb95e438da2f431189f509b51434e4f1</data>
      <data key="d12">12228</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="RESISTENCIA TISULAR A GLUCOCORTICOIDES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In tissue resistance to glucocorticoids, cortisol levels may be elevated but the tissues do not respond appropriately</data>
      <data key="d10">bcbca87f5ebf2c5d260810cf83a70257</data>
      <data key="d11">a8eb926d1337455e957dc06fe07c1380</data>
      <data key="d12">12229</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE BARTTER">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Bartter puede estar relacionado con alteraciones en los niveles de cortisol en el cuerpo</data>
      <data key="d10">e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d11">69629378732e480a9bc8df583bda0ded</data>
      <data key="d12">12230</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="DIABETES MAL CONTROLADA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes mal controlada puede influir en los niveles de cortisol en el cuerpo</data>
      <data key="d10">e5103e718912067f1a2766544cf1b4db</data>
      <data key="d11">21ae33e3bae04e0aa930eaaf54c422c2</data>
      <data key="d12">12231</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="HIPERALDOSTERONISMO PRIMARIO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">In primary hyperaldosteronism, cortisol levels may be elevated, affecting the regulation of aldosterone.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c</data>
      <data key="d11">21995988fd384695a9e26e428f36c07d</data>
      <data key="d12">12232</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="RESISTENCIA PRIMARIA AL CORTISOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Primary cortisol resistance is characterized by increased cortisol levels without the typical clinical signs of hypercortisolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcbf695abeb609e2cdbff56c1bde675c</data>
      <data key="d11">d1b246a2f29249a996e1492b90142443</data>
      <data key="d12">12233</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="HIPERCORTISOLISMO">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol is a hormone whose levels are evaluated to diagnose hypercortisolism, a condition characterized by excessive cortisol production. This diagnosis is particularly relevant in patients with adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal masses during imaging studies. The measurement of cortisol levels is a critical step in identifying hypercortisolism and understanding its implications for patient health.</data>
      <data key="d10">151237aa6e4e4aaa2d1115a10ab09be0,6ebb5385c8eda09a187e6d0595812bbf</data>
      <data key="d11">7e47ed3f787c4c1da047d82d1b41c045</data>
      <data key="d12">12234</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="MITOTANO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mitotano affects cortisol metabolism, potentially leading to adrenal insufficiency and requiring higher doses of glucocorticoid replacement.</data>
      <data key="d10">209bcca22090a109f52e26657bf3c999</data>
      <data key="d11">11b48cc5bfa64588a7f31a370c204445</data>
      <data key="d12">12235</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="GLANDULA SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol is produced by the adrenal gland, which is essential for various bodily functions</data>
      <data key="d10">8eb2b7021402eb440fe88889b78c2785</data>
      <data key="d11">5741ea102a004b938473cfa52041d436</data>
      <data key="d12">12236</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AGUDA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol levels are assessed to confirm the diagnosis of acute adrenal insufficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">fec130428af4ee62996a9b72494212dc</data>
      <data key="d11">4a352a40e8b5440d9d2739b4ad7229d5</data>
      <data key="d12">12237</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="ALDOSTERONE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol and aldosterone are both steroid hormones produced by the adrenal glands</data>
      <data key="d10">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">82dc7fd341f2458cacd541004ba3ce2e</data>
      <data key="d12">12238</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="ALDOSTERONA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol and aldosterone both interact with mineralocorticoid receptors, influencing sodium retention and fluid balance</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d11">35418b6f852b4fa5bb86cc96cef44fca</data>
      <data key="d12">12239</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="CYTOCHROME CYP3A4">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol metabolism is influenced by the activity of cytochrome CYP3A4, which can alter the required dosage in adrenal insufficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">84ebd4f784ceacfe0744f6bb9cd9a5a3</data>
      <data key="d11">3f8119d979b74feb9e16cc0d10d14b5c</data>
      <data key="d12">12240</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="IPILIMUMAB">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ipilimumab can lead to autoimmune conditions that may result in secondary adrenal insufficiency, affecting cortisol levels</data>
      <data key="d10">84ebd4f784ceacfe0744f6bb9cd9a5a3</data>
      <data key="d11">1ae38339fd0b4678ada2ba68d42b170d</data>
      <data key="d12">12241</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="CYP3A4">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CYP3A4 is responsible for the metabolism of cortisol, which may require dosage adjustments in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">40253f8b49d61452dbc56454cd1a07e0</data>
      <data key="d11">22617b6b087b4c1ba4298f0eeac31e6d</data>
      <data key="d12">12242</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTISOL" target="HIPO-NATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cortisol levels can affect sodium retention and thus influence the occurrence of hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215</data>
      <data key="d11">2ad54ac82c67463e8ed75e674c236fc6</data>
      <data key="d12">12243</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IGF-1" target="IGFBP3">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IGFBP3 binds to IGF-1, controlling its availability and activity in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">adab3c750c469ba13dd6c020d2b53aaa</data>
      <data key="d11">aeb81016565e405f94c5e387e92389de</data>
      <data key="d12">12244</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IGF-1" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acromegalia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 (IGF-1), which is directly linked to the severity of clinical changes observed in patients. Monitoring IGF-1 levels is essential for assessing the control of acromegaly, as these levels provide critical insights into the progression and management of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608,e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">1bf42976efb6444b8089b5c3728a0291</data>
      <data key="d12">12245</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IGF-1" target="ACROMEGALY">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated levels of IGF-1 are often found in patients with acromegaly, indicating growth hormone activity</data>
      <data key="d10">2261671ccad439da1ed9ea5a27857dc8</data>
      <data key="d11">4cf22a59e4ba47ed9684537f2f5125db</data>
      <data key="d12">12246</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IGF-1" target="FETO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IGF-1 is crucial for fetal growth and development during pregnancy</data>
      <data key="d10">ebfccc35cef320c7240cf36dd52e847a</data>
      <data key="d11">2fdeca0d19f14733841a7210ab8c4ce6</data>
      <data key="d12">12247</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="IGF-1" target="ANOREXIA NERVOSA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IGF-1 levels are affected by the nutritional status of patients with Anorexia Nervosa, impacting their bone health</data>
      <data key="d10">bb6a2caec3fa27e00fc1044b17147ccb</data>
      <data key="d11">9193cc07f86f4ef69eabc676e9ab839b</data>
      <data key="d12">12248</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRH" target="CUSHING'S SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome can be influenced by CRH, which stimulates the release of ACTH</data>
      <data key="d10">7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b</data>
      <data key="d11">b9a2a181fe65423f83234620f172588e</data>
      <data key="d12">12249</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRH" target="HORMONA ADRENOCORTICOTROPA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ACTH is released in response to CRH from the hypothalamus, playing a role in the stress response</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">5553551432d74e849dc7b7c815ae70e1</data>
      <data key="d12">12250</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
