      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PIT-1" target="HIPOPITUITARISMO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PIT-1 is necessary for the differentiation of cells that produce hormones, and its mutation can contribute to hypopituitarism.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">79f6d52296c14529b3b50ac9b6fe25c8</data>
      <data key="d12">12345</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="T-PIT" target="HIPOPITUITARISMO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">T-PIT is essential for the differentiation of corticotropic cells, and its mutation can lead to hormonal deficiencies seen in hypopituitarism.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea2863d43f4c93ae3681a0faf1a0a3d</data>
      <data key="d11">296cb31009b94647bdd2eccd3638fb76</data>
      <data key="d12">12346</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="T-PIT" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
