    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="KETOCONAZOL">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome is a condition characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body. Ketoconazole is a medication commonly used to treat Cushing's syndrome by inhibiting steroidogenesis, specifically by blocking cortisol production and synthesis. This makes ketoconazole an effective treatment option for managing the symptoms associated with elevated cortisol levels in patients with Cushing's syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">88a8ebb15abeea8eaded56ef3d2df73f,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0,dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb</data>
