    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="HARRISON PRINCIPLES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome is a condition characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body, and it is thoroughly covered in the "Harrison Principles of Internal Medicine." This authoritative medical text includes detailed information on the diagnosis of Cushing's syndrome, as well as comprehensive insights into its pathophysiology, clinical features, and management. The "Harrison Principles of Internal Medicine" serves as a valuable resource for understanding this syndrome and its implications in internal medicine.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0</data>
      <data key="d11">2d4d58cd32484098b3c28e2699276f62</data>
      <data key="d12">12526</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="ADRENAL CORTEX">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome is a medical condition characterized by excessive production of cortisol, which is primarily produced by the adrenal cortex. The adrenal cortex plays a crucial role in the synthesis of cortisol, and its overactivity is central to the pathology of Cushing's syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0</data>
      <data key="d11">9a4528b5cf034bf28c60dc513f38f25c</data>
      <data key="d12">12527</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="ENDOCRINE SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">32.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome is a condition characterized by excessive levels of cortisol in the body, which can lead to various health issues. The Endocrine Society plays a significant role in addressing this condition by providing comprehensive clinical practice guidelines for its diagnosis and treatment. These guidelines are essential resources for healthcare professionals, ensuring that patients with Cushing's syndrome receive appropriate and effective care. The Endocrine Society's commitment to publishing these guidelines underscores its dedication to improving the understanding and management of Cushing's syndrome within the medical community.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,7082a5d31b18dd81d4c4a0e8ed02623b,7f3df1437755b60344fdffd2ef3b8a9e,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de,b2ca509109e853875e707e29a98391e0</data>
      <data key="d11">4cd0bf7b9ebf47caa329aeedd1964085</data>
      <data key="d12">12528</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="SOMATOSTATIN ANALOGS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin analogs are used to treat Cushing's syndrome by normalizing cortisol levels</data>
      <data key="d10">9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de</data>
      <data key="d11">6223452342574c7380a283304de0abc3</data>
      <data key="d12">12529</data>
