    <edge source="CUSHING'S SYNDROME" target="HYPERCORTISOLISM">
      <data key="d8">19.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cushing's syndrome is a condition characterized by hypercortisolism, which is defined as an excess of cortisol in the body. Hypercortisolism is not only a defining characteristic of Cushing's syndrome but also a key factor in its development. This relationship highlights the central role that elevated cortisol levels play in the manifestation and progression of Cushing's syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c034422eb6302c32e0d5fdce5b3046d,9ff14a3c49bd56b2fb12b3fd8ed246de</data>
      <data key="d11">fa0d4fa3d8fc410b9e20d8b1634287dd</data>
      <data key="d12">12532</data>
