    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES INSIPIDA" target="LACTANTE DE 6 MESES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The 6-month-old infant may be experiencing diabetes insipida due to severe dehydration and hypernatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">a1b16c80a55fd88d0b1efb78addf3853</data>
      <data key="d11">cb6f475a6451405a9e8eb5981575f797</data>
      <data key="d12">12566</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="RMN HIPOFISARIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La RMN hipofisaria se utiliza para diagnosticar la enfermedad de Cushing al detectar adenomas corticotropos.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">8f489d66d8a045608b8f574115008f67</data>
      <data key="d12">12567</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="TAC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La TAC es una t&#233;cnica de imagen que se utiliza para detectar la enfermedad de Cushing, aunque es menos efectiva que la RMN hipofisaria.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">bf7fbc834ac34188b368c74716ff4c29</data>
      <data key="d12">12568</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="CATETERISMO DE SENOS PETROSOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El cateterismo de senos petrosos se realiza para confirmar la hipersecreci&#243;n de ACTH en pacientes con enfermedad de Cushing cuando la RMN no es concluyente.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">250d942f38ca4480809b06a469c6564e</data>
      <data key="d12">12569</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="KETOCONAZOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El ketoconazol se utiliza para tratar la enfermedad de Cushing al inhibir la producci&#243;n de cortisol.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">f47c383f69d34a729d28e0fb19dce532</data>
      <data key="d12">12570</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="METIRAPONA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La metirapona se utiliza en el tratamiento del s&#237;ndrome de Cushing al inhibir la producci&#243;n de cortisol.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">1fc021ed605340da8eee856fcc5c65ae</data>
      <data key="d12">12571</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="PASIRE&#211;TIDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El pasire&#243;tida se utiliza para tratar la enfermedad de Cushing al actuar sobre la secreci&#243;n de ACTH.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">c400e9f974b04923ab820f4ecae88124</data>
      <data key="d12">12572</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="MIFEPRISTONA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mifepristona se utiliza en el tratamiento del s&#237;ndrome de Cushing como antagonista de los receptores de glucocorticoides.</data>
      <data key="d10">6d1d33d516f4ff2c0edf5bf266205c1f</data>
      <data key="d11">478e50b85d35477385613e9083c9cc59</data>
      <data key="d12">12573</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENFERMEDAD DE CUSHING" target="HORMONAS ESTEROIDES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las hormonas esteroides, como el cortisol, est&#225;n implicadas en la enfermedad de Cushing, que se caracteriza por su exceso.</data>
      <data key="d10">dbe034ccd694ae06cf72d347d7dbdacb</data>
      <data key="d11">43f2f8a8e6bf42e2b0afddc58df04346</data>
      <data key="d12">12574</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="HISTIOCITOSIS X">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Histiocytosis X can affect the pineal gland, leading to complications</data>
      <data key="d10">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51</data>
      <data key="d11">ee825b1902044ef3b31336dd9b63e461</data>
      <data key="d12">12575</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="ENFERMEDAD DE ERDHEIM-CHESTER">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Erdheim-Chester disease can involve the pineal gland and cause various symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51</data>
      <data key="d11">46c72b37f1ec455aadcade5f4f81f16e</data>
      <data key="d12">12576</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="GL&#193;NDULA PINEAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores pineales afectan a la gl&#225;ndula pineal, causando diversas manifestaciones cl&#237;nicas.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">74495d9d1f8c4d9f80e4976b65106a5a</data>
      <data key="d12">12577</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="LIQUIDO CEFALORRAQU&#205;DEO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores pineales pueden provocar un aumento en el l&#237;quido cefalorraqu&#237;deo debido a la producci&#243;n de oncoprote&#237;nas.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">d347b06657454273a056201062dd8c2f</data>
      <data key="d12">12578</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="ONCOPROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las oncoprote&#237;nas son producidas por tumores pineales, como los germinomas, y est&#225;n relacionadas con el l&#237;quido cefalorraqu&#237;deo.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">dc63dcd340ac4bbdbfb6d4dbe13fcac8</data>
      <data key="d12">12579</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="ALTERACIONES VISUALES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las alteraciones visuales son un s&#237;ntoma que puede aparecer en pacientes con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">736e6f68f4444e8e855f7456c64a89b7</data>
      <data key="d12">12580</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="CEFALEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La cefalea es un s&#237;ntoma com&#250;n en pacientes con tumores pineales, apareciendo en el 73% de los casos.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">90537e12677f4ca5b1d3e6195a2eee25</data>
      <data key="d12">12581</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="NAUSEAS Y V&#211;MITOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las n&#225;useas y v&#243;mitos son s&#237;ntomas que pueden presentarse en pacientes con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">40ce1cc8a59f40e093aa6a2362d540d4</data>
      <data key="d12">12582</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="ALTERACIONES EN LA DEAMBULACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las alteraciones en la deambulaci&#243;n son un s&#237;ntoma que puede aparecer en pacientes con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">219ee62ca3e9468da70074a6396415bc</data>
      <data key="d12">12583</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="AFECTACI&#211;N SUPRASELAR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La afectaci&#243;n supraselar puede causar endocrinopat&#237;as en pacientes con tumores pineales.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">c2d738cd557842309f95a5c4cb716a7c</data>
      <data key="d12">12584</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="RITMO CIRCADIANO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El ritmo circadiano puede verse alterado en pacientes con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">e21680ba6cf9412ba24e3f5c5819228f</data>
      <data key="d12">12585</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="HIDROCEFALIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hidrocefalia puede resultar de la obstrucci&#243;n del flujo del l&#237;quido cefalorraqu&#237;deo debido a tumores pineales.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">a846d11372d245ab976d93bcd8c95b96</data>
      <data key="d12">12586</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES PINEALES" target="ALTERACIONES EN LA REGULACI&#211;N DEL APETITO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las alteraciones en la regulaci&#243;n del apetito pueden ser consecuencia de la afectaci&#243;n hipotal&#225;mica por tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">bb58e4dbfc8b43a2a0cf7c08c5133b5e</data>
      <data key="d12">12587</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LOPES MB" target="METE O">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mete O and Lopes MB co-authored the overview of the 2017 WHO Classification of Pituitary Tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51</data>
      <data key="d11">1178ca47f60d472ba44e277abfcb4b4e</data>
      <data key="d12">12588</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AND&#218;JAR P" target="JACOBSEN E">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Jacobsen E and And&#250;jar P have both contributed to the literature on Erdheim-Chester disease and pituitary pathology</data>
      <data key="d10">4faa9b46acd7540904fc5b0772bb7c51</data>
      <data key="d11">6ade012ca9824c4a98f4733e4395b0f8</data>
      <data key="d12">12589</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GL&#193;NDULA PINEAL" target="GERMINOMAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los germinomas son los tumores m&#225;s frecuentes que afectan a la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">d03a585deb9944d4a95cc2c000d87c9e</data>
      <data key="d12">12590</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GL&#193;NDULA PINEAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE PARINAUD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Parinaud es un conjunto de s&#237;ntomas neurol&#243;gicos que puede aparecer en pacientes con tumores de la gl&#225;ndula pineal.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">b9ba7f6c754d4f9aaf5c1e7fb7672c9d</data>
      <data key="d12">12591</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GL&#193;NDULA PINEAL" target="MELATONINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La melatonina es una hormona producida por la gl&#225;ndula pineal que regula el sue&#241;o y puede verse afectada por tumores en esta gl&#225;ndula.</data>
      <data key="d10">309cfad754049a78b0459a3e71f496ef</data>
      <data key="d11">65dbfbbdb1d54fc39e0abcecd127d82b</data>
      <data key="d12">12592</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE PARINAUD" target="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Parinaud puede presentarse en pacientes con adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d11">6f91bee088734865a3e0342af157b82a</data>
      <data key="d12">12593</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HCG" target="HIPERTIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La HCG puede causar hipertiroidismo secundario al interactuar con el receptor de TSH en la tiroides.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c18507e3d98242cdbcddd1a1997b92f</data>
      <data key="d11">c9aaa9aead1f4c1890199b275cd7f394</data>
      <data key="d12">12594</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HCG" target="HMG">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HCG and HMG are both used in the hormonal treatment of cryptorchidism to enhance testicular descent</data>
      <data key="d10">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d11">e02cfacb1b6247299c90036444fac376</data>
      <data key="d12">12595</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AIP" target="CRANEOPARINGIOMAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las mutaciones inactivadoras de AIP est&#225;n relacionadas con algunos casos de adenomas hipofisarios, que pueden incluir craneofaringiomas</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d11">123be41846c544a2ad02e3e377781704</data>
      <data key="d12">12596</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AIP" target="CASTA&#209;O I ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Casta&#241;o I ha investigado el impacto cl&#237;nico de las mutaciones en el gen AIP en adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">640676d4cf19e18530a974c0bac4cfb1</data>
      <data key="d11">4e395ab3f65d4442813117c2172616fd</data>
      <data key="d12">12597</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="OSTEOMALACIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN1 syndrome can be associated with various endocrine tumors, including those affecting bone health</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">43e9dfa3976a4240996a03598f9ad30f</data>
      <data key="d12">12598</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN1, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1, is a genetic syndrome characterized by the occurrence of multiple endocrine tumors. One of the tumors that can be associated with MEN1 is insulinoma, a type of pancreatic tumor that secretes insulin. The relationship between insulinoma and MEN1 syndrome is significant, as insulinomas can occur in a percentage of individuals with MEN1, highlighting the connection between these two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166,8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">b7e7444b3ff04226a7e9a3b05ab84691</data>
      <data key="d12">12599</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="WHO CLASSIFICATION OF TUMOURS OF ENDOCRINE ORGANS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The WHO Classification provides guidelines that include information on MEN1 and its associated tumors like gastrinomas and vipomas</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">890847eb84b84cbc978101ccf2e36637</data>
      <data key="d12">12600</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="GASTRINOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gastrinomas are often associated with MEN1, with a significant percentage of gastrinomas being duodenal in patients with this syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">4afb0d0220964b45b340a8374c142b73</data>
      <data key="d12">12601</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="VIPOMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vipomas can occur as part of MEN1 syndrome, indicating a relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">b8ebacf289e943acbd3a79febfdb968c</data>
      <data key="d12">12602</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="GLUCAGONOMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucagonoma can also be associated with MEN1, highlighting the connection between this syndrome and various neuroendocrine tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">c59f14e0fcfa4ae98d108ae314e0b92d</data>
      <data key="d12">12603</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="SOMATOSTATINOMA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatinomas, while rare, can also be linked to MEN1, showing the broader implications of this syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">0b3bcbebf3b9454485f523dd4ee030ec</data>
      <data key="d12">12604</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="MEN4">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN4 is a clinical entity related to MEN1, sharing similar phenotypes and genetic mutations</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">32c3f391e2fc41ecbcbcf9c48191b109</data>
      <data key="d12">12605</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="MEN2">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN1 and MEN2 are both syndromes characterized by the presence of multiple endocrine tumors, but they are associated with different types of tumors. MEN1, also known as Wermer's syndrome, typically involves tumors of the parathyroid glands, pancreatic islet cells, and the pituitary gland. In contrast, MEN2, which is related to MEN1 through the concept of hereditary endocrine tumors, primarily involves medullary thyroid carcinoma, pheochromocytoma, and primary hyperparathyroidism. Both syndromes highlight the genetic predisposition to endocrine neoplasia, but they manifest through distinct tumor types and clinical features.</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526,fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d11">6626a63de1ef486884f33a30a9ef2d04</data>
      <data key="d12">12606</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="SDHB">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in SDHB can lead to tumor development in patients with phenotypes similar to MEN1</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">e061c11dc95d4cc5aab555e2b21baa95</data>
      <data key="d12">12607</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="AIRE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AIRE is involved in autoimmune conditions that can overlap with endocrine disorders seen in MEN1</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">1d5663cd47d34aa1b1a47d6aece19c9d</data>
      <data key="d12">12608</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="ARNOLD A.">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arnold A. has written extensively about MEN1, contributing to its definition and understanding</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">d56e58c61a704c8687977b1950150882</data>
      <data key="d12">12609</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="DREZNER MK">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Drezner MK is an editor of a medical resource that discusses MEN1 and its implications</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">0c5ef44a75154cf3a053ee929af7549a</data>
      <data key="d12">12610</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="MELMED S.">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Melmed S. is a key author in the field of endocrinology, providing insights into MEN1</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">bfdf269dba02478386da77602a2e1fe3</data>
      <data key="d12">12611</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="VALD&#201;S GALLEGO N.">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vald&#233;s Gallego N. has authored a manual that includes information on MEN1 and its clinical aspects</data>
      <data key="d10">02b8a693303f9f8603c740fefc53d526</data>
      <data key="d11">dbe210cfe48a48649c68461634a9ba16</data>
      <data key="d12">12612</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="D">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">D is a patient suspected of having MEN1 based on her medical history and symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d11">1fbdf4ba43054af7b810ff20586dfd35</data>
      <data key="d12">12613</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="PROTOONCOGEN RET">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The study of protooncogen RET is important for understanding MEN2, which is related to MEN1</data>
      <data key="d10">fbba0b43850ff5e50b710069959c2416</data>
      <data key="d11">8fc724b112424ca68f41542f4832d6cc</data>
      <data key="d12">12614</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="ENETS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ENETS provides guidelines for the management of patients with MEN1 syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">5193cd33645548488f464bcfbcd2bac2</data>
      <data key="d12">12615</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="NANETS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">NANETS also provides guidelines for the management of patients with MEN1 syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">c22c77e7c2384bd7aa9184f4f3c7ef4b</data>
      <data key="d12">12616</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="C&#193;NCER DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with MEN1 may develop thyroid cancer, although the relationship with the MEN1 gene is not well established</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">f6c8d927a48842e79ff212c0ab3d2bdd</data>
      <data key="d12">12617</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="MELANOMA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Melanoma is a potential risk for patients with MEN1, but its connection to the MEN1 gene is not documented</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">7d955aaddb324430af1221a9244ed617</data>
      <data key="d12">12618</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="CARCINOMA DE COLON">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Colon carcinoma is a risk for patients with MEN1, but no link to the MEN1 gene has been established</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">cf326290929c489abe95dbf85edf1872</data>
      <data key="d12">12619</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="GU&#205;A CL&#205;NICA DE 2012">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Clinical Guidelines of 2012 provide recommendations for the management of patients with MEN1</data>
      <data key="d10">7e4e3e944e1b58b8d92e93ee4a9f33cc</data>
      <data key="d11">77be9f7f2cf64f78abf8bca0eeca2a11</data>
      <data key="d12">12620</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="ZOLLINGER-ELLISON SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN1 is associated with the development of gastrinomas, which cause Zollinger-Ellison syndrome due to excessive gastrin production.</data>
      <data key="d10">9851218c3244d6f4279055a04d219044</data>
      <data key="d11">082a1a489163432bad0cc6a11c2222dd</data>
      <data key="d12">12621</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN1" target="DREIJERINK KM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dreijerink KM conducted research related to breast-cancer predisposition in MEN1, linking the genetic syndrome to cancer risks.</data>
      <data key="d10">9851218c3244d6f4279055a04d219044</data>
      <data key="d11">a9d81be6dd074486a2b6d5d8d62e49aa</data>
      <data key="d12">12622</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS" target="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutaciones en el gen GNAS pueden encontrarse en adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">755475a08c9b594dacee6386b782065f</data>
      <data key="d11">381f5cc159f1494f9567e9e80f18d117</data>
      <data key="d12">12623</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS" target="ACROMEGALIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the GNAS gene are linked to the development of acromegaly by causing overproduction of growth hormone.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">bef28c9f3c7a413ab3d6b35b0436a30c</data>
      <data key="d12">12624</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="PEGVISOMANT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pegvisomant is used as a treatment for acromegaly by blocking the action of growth hormone</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">f472d3b03ec84905b709e97c2e19bdde</data>
      <data key="d12">12625</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="CABERGOLINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cabergoline can be used to treat mild cases of acromegaly by inhibiting growth hormone secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">b51efe7d935643b584ef0597f0163cce</data>
      <data key="d12">12626</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="KATZNELSON L">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Katznelson L has authored works on the treatment of acromegaly, contributing to its medical understanding</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">0ca8fd918a2141d3b20a3bd9f846e168</data>
      <data key="d12">12627</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypersecretion of growth hormone causes acromegaly</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">c3ccbfac1bdf4ca0b94b12f2df906d1c</data>
      <data key="d12">12628</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="AN&#193;LOGOS DE SOMATOSTATINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatin analogs are used to treat acromegaly by inhibiting growth hormone secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">200447233341122a47f0010251600608</data>
      <data key="d11">1d8b2623fad64cbc9e49151d4aa88277</data>
      <data key="d12">12629</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="HO PJ ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ho PJ et al. studied the regulation of growth hormone secretion in relation to acromegaly</data>
      <data key="d10">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">fff9eccfb9c24eb8ad82c1c0edd4a05d</data>
      <data key="d12">12630</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="KATZNELSON L ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Katznelson L et al. provided clinical guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of acromegaly</data>
      <data key="d10">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">7093422119934660bd91655eaf2955a8</data>
      <data key="d12">12631</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO SOMATOTROPO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acromegalia is commonly associated with adenoma hipofisario somatotropo, which causes excessive growth hormone secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">f9ffeb383c47400e940daa501aa146b4</data>
      <data key="d12">12632</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="X-LAG">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">X-LAG is a genetic condition that can lead to gigantism, which is related to the pathophysiology of acromegaly</data>
      <data key="d10">e717441e0bce4da41df774553a5ddcaf</data>
      <data key="d11">d87039722f7046a3a286ef9ab2f54c39</data>
      <data key="d12">12633</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with acromegaly often experience increased cardiovascular disease, which is a significant cause of mortality associated with the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">866e6b06106b451a81f2e3cbf465cd47</data>
      <data key="d12">12634</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="HORMONAL DISORDERS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acromegalia is classified as a hormonal disorder due to its association with excess growth hormone production.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">a505572425d14a1cb5cf33123d25413d</data>
      <data key="d12">12635</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="MACROADENOMAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Macroadenomas are a common cause of acromegaly due to their role in the overproduction of growth hormone.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">0a6c7178c87f403583f0fffc1c7873e4</data>
      <data key="d12">12636</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="HIPERPLASIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperplasia can contribute to the development of acromegaly by causing an increase in hormone production from the pituitary gland.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">f2798f5e85c94880977d0fdfbb7ced25</data>
      <data key="d12">12637</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="S&#205;NDROME DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">McCune-Albright syndrome can present with symptoms similar to acromegaly due to hormonal dysregulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">2e73034a100b1adb0a00561c08416bda</data>
      <data key="d11">94b6b9ee42af45ab98fc07f640476c3b</data>
      <data key="d12">12638</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACROMEGALIA" target="SHBG">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Acromegalia can affect SHBG levels due to hormonal imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">4beab004731d7baff10fd2796a523b55</data>
      <data key="d11">a6bddf59aaee45998806a61bc6bdbeef</data>
      <data key="d12">12639</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CORTICOTROPINOMA SILENTE" target="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El corticotropinoma silente es un tipo espec&#237;fico de adenoma hipofisario que se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci&#243;n de la OMS</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">6f2ff2019ac247b5b4ce3f92af4dcb6f</data>
      <data key="d12">12640</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="ADENOMA SOMATOTROPO ESCASAMENTE GRANULADO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El adenoma somatotropo escasamente granulado es una categor&#237;a de adenoma hipofisario reconocida por su agresividad cl&#237;nica</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">56e5f8642a344be88fca26ac5d635b24</data>
      <data key="d12">12641</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="MACROADENOMA LACTOTROPO EN VARONES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El macroadenoma lactotropo en varones es un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se clasifica seg&#250;n su tama&#241;o y caracter&#237;sticas cl&#237;nicas</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">c4d168790e2d444cbae8f543bc69a0b5</data>
      <data key="d12">12642</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="ADENOMA DE C&#201;LULAS DE CROOKE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El adenoma de c&#233;lulas de Crooke es otro tipo de adenoma hipofisario que se clasifica en la nueva actualizaci&#243;n de la OMS</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">726d334f9f864500b86e691ea962ca28</data>
      <data key="d12">12643</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="ADENOMA PLURIHORMONAL PIT-1 POSITIVO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El adenoma plurihormonal Pit-1 positivo es un tipo de adenoma hipofisario que produce m&#250;ltiples hormonas</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">02835926319c4b569095a2eae4674e14</data>
      <data key="d12">12644</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="PITUICITOMAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pituicitomas son neoplasias que pueden ser confundidas con adenomas hipofisarios, pero tienen un origen diferente</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">a2448911a07f425f8138bd11feff4e94</data>
      <data key="d12">12645</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="CRANEOPARINGIOMAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los craneofaringiomas son tumores que pueden aparecer en la misma regi&#243;n que los adenomas hipofisarios y tienen caracter&#237;sticas cl&#237;nicas distintas</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">5c022d2789664058bf8ae9b2f6c8e994</data>
      <data key="d12">12646</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="QUISTE DE RATHKE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El quiste de Rathke puede encontrarse en la regi&#243;n selar, donde tambi&#233;n se localizan los adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">b344c7542352481c947a532550d4cfca</data>
      <data key="d12">12647</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="ANEURISMAS CAROT&#205;DEOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los aneurismas carot&#237;deos pueden tener implicaciones en la regi&#243;n selar, donde se encuentran los adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">bffc7543297144558095aa2defd59214</data>
      <data key="d12">12648</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="F&#205;STULAS CAROT&#205;DEAS ARTERIOVENOSAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las f&#237;stulas carot&#237;deas arteriovenosas pueden afectar la regi&#243;n selar, donde se localizan los adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">04f30b8c59b3463ead8307b66e23432e</data>
      <data key="d12">12649</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="HORMONAS ADENOHIPOFISARIAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los adenomas hipofisarios pueden afectar la producci&#243;n de hormonas adenohipofisarias, alterando su funci&#243;n endocrina</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">6162541883504c4fb16e1dc07c0123bd</data>
      <data key="d12">12650</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="FACTORES DE TRANSCRIPCI&#211;N HIPOFISARIOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los factores de transcripci&#243;n hipofisarios son importantes en la regulaci&#243;n de la expresi&#243;n gen&#233;tica en adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">4c0352c2779642e2b469bf463309e64c</data>
      <data key="d12">12651</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="&#205;NDICE KI67">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El &#237;ndice Ki67 se utiliza para evaluar la proliferaci&#243;n en adenomas hipofisarios, ayudando a determinar su agresividad</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">eba939e85a3e4b2e893e2bc7a9fc4832</data>
      <data key="d12">12652</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO" target="RECUENTO DE MITOSIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El recuento de mitosis es una t&#233;cnica utilizada para evaluar la actividad proliferativa de los adenomas hipofisarios</data>
      <data key="d10">8ceedaeea54ca164b32a166116187b29</data>
      <data key="d11">ab34b94d154a4a92ac572021113f7228</data>
