    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="NAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The NAS outlines energy requirements during lactation in its guidelines</data>
      <data key="d10">bd31c6face847551241359e37e4baa2e</data>
      <data key="d11">06ea2226ab044986bcfaa116d4182ad6</data>
      <data key="d12">12737</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="DIETARY REFERENCE INTAKES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactancia is a specific population group for whom dietary reference intakes are provided</data>
      <data key="d10">b46fefa9f55d92c74acad101fc4f812e</data>
      <data key="d11">98acc2ccbac94e028af10caa4496b987</data>
      <data key="d12">12738</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="EMBARAZO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactancia and Embarazo are interconnected events that play a crucial role in maternal and infant health, each with specific dietary recommendations to support the health of both mothers and their children. Embarazo, or pregnancy, serves as a precursor to Lactancia, which is the breastfeeding phase. During Lactancia, the nutritional needs of mothers are particularly important, as they must ensure adequate nourishment to support both their own health and the health of their breastfeeding infants. Together, these stages highlight the importance of proper nutrition and care during the maternal journey from pregnancy to breastfeeding.</data>
      <data key="d10">4d3437a0370e3fe7789ba3908d445576,4fe098dece0637a1082d6a439757620a,565aef05382a327b4bdefb2ab3d3b4be</data>
      <data key="d11">76679a8183e94d9dbcb5327c4fe299b0</data>
      <data key="d12">12739</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="INSTITUTE OF MEDICINE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Institute of Medicine provides dietary recommendations for lactation and other life stages</data>
      <data key="d10">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445</data>
      <data key="d11">205cbad2135744a99945cc074dd325dd</data>
      <data key="d12">12740</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="FLUOR">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactancia provides dietary reference intake guidelines for fluoride (fl&#250;or) for different age groups, emphasizing the importance of specific recommended intake levels for infants during lactation. These guidelines ensure that infants receive appropriate amounts of fluoride to support their health while breastfeeding.</data>
      <data key="d10">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d11">9f6e0c6c49da49cc85c838642f39c3c0</data>
      <data key="d12">12741</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTANCIA" target="IODINE">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LACTANCIA and IODINE are interconnected in the context of dietary recommendations for infants. Iodine has specific recommended intake levels that are crucial for infants during the lactation period. Additionally, Lactancia offers dietary reference intake guidelines for iodine, tailored for various age groups, ensuring that nutritional needs are met effectively. This highlights the importance of adequate iodine intake during lactation for the health and development of infants.</data>
      <data key="d10">74a9c62d0f932e27419151241f7db445,acf7f978dbec397c60ed463f4eb2fcf6</data>
      <data key="d11">1c75be7fa8e1495d979935e37c773503</data>
      <data key="d12">12742</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
