    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERINSULINISM" target="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperinsulinism is a key feature of insulinoma, indicating a direct relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">b373d98c5b1c494e86a3cdc868d45a8e</data>
      <data key="d12">12935</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERCALCIURIA" target="NEPHROLITHIASIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercalciuria is a significant risk factor for the development of nephrolithiasis, which is the formation of kidney stones. The condition of nephrolithiasis is often associated with hypercalciuria, as excessive levels of calcium in the urine can lead to the formation of these stones. Thus, hypercalciuria plays a crucial role in the pathophysiology of nephrolithiasis, highlighting the interconnectedness of these two entities.</data>
      <data key="d10">550574bce077f34348bd11c78dc814a1,f757219e84dba985f7c8d66ac951b9f2</data>
      <data key="d11">63a9aa8ad8ce46d49cca9851f0017273</data>
      <data key="d12">12936</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERCALCIURIA" target="LOW-SALT DIET">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A low-salt diet has been researched for its effects on managing hypercalciuria in patients prone to kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d10">f757219e84dba985f7c8d66ac951b9f2</data>
      <data key="d11">c947b3dfcc824e18adb9189e0cdaa613</data>
      <data key="d12">12937</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERPHOSPHATEMIA" target="HYPOKALEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperphosphatemia and hypokalemia are conditions that can occur in preterm infants receiving parenteral nutrition</data>
      <data key="d10">9ef354c0ee5ac877ce8fba79fcc7e2b3</data>
      <data key="d11">3ac11e79f22c492eb79b6f7f1661f54a</data>
      <data key="d12">12938</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MURAD MH" target="PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA AND PARAGANGLIOMA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Murad MH is involved in the clinical practice guidelines for pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma</data>
      <data key="d10">97afc23d7c06c09383611da00b084017</data>
      <data key="d11">6159383bdb7046f29a94dc1d5dab8da4</data>
      <data key="d12">12939</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MURAD MH" target="ENDOCRINE SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Murad MH is an author who has contributed to the clinical practice guidelines published by the Endocrine Society. Specifically, Murad MH is involved in the development of guidelines concerning the treatment of gender-dysphoric individuals, reflecting a commitment to advancing clinical practices in this area.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c5004508264971bc2e63c88d19f480,1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b</data>
      <data key="d11">f7c3ab22881b4a4b8a6349ac627f2ccc</data>
      <data key="d12">12940</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DESMOPRESINA" target="TOLVAPT&#193;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Desmopresina is used in conjunction with tolvapt&#225;n to manage sodium levels when they rise too quickly</data>
      <data key="d10">85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e</data>
      <data key="d11">c799f744c06a44c6ba5c0c766bfdf80d</data>
      <data key="d12">12941</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HORMONA ANTIDIUR&#201;TICA" target="SIADH">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH is a key factor in the pathophysiology of SIADH, as its inappropriate secretion leads to hyponatremia</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">e4d8c3e058c04e3fbca7963caff0b0ff</data>
      <data key="d12">12942</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLIURIA" target="DIABETES 2">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polyuria is a common symptom of uncontrolled diabetes due to high blood sugar levels</data>
      <data key="d10">bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582</data>
      <data key="d11">0ba6fe26f8f540f4a738ad7119be6f43</data>
      <data key="d12">12943</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLIURIA" target="MAR&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mar&#237;a's condition includes symptoms of polyuria, which is often associated with diabetes and kidney issues</data>
      <data key="d10">d77ee7b5259ebdf92e8375c5f2d322e6</data>
      <data key="d11">7a2857ea255746258d9acbbf3d9e2e10</data>
      <data key="d12">12944</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLIDIPSIA" target="DIABETES 2">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polydipsia often accompanies polyuria in diabetes as the body seeks to rehydrate due to fluid loss</data>
      <data key="d10">bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582</data>
      <data key="d11">7e1a1b31f13f4091a45e00c6b81b533a</data>
      <data key="d12">12945</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLIDIPSIA PRIMARIA" target="HIPONATREMIA EUVOL&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La polidipsia primaria puede ser una causa de hiponatremia euvol&#233;mica al provocar una ingesta excesiva de agua.</data>
      <data key="d10">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d11">a80774eb1ef6429abe6582fe4cbdef2f</data>
      <data key="d12">12946</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA CENTRAL" target="ADH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes ins&#237;pida central se caracteriza por la falta de producci&#243;n de ADH, lo que resulta en una incapacidad para concentrar la orina.</data>
      <data key="d10">67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37</data>
      <data key="d11">0df735ca5417412189a4e5cd053ce646</data>
      <data key="d12">12947</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES INS&#205;PIDA NEFROG&#201;NICA" target="ADH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La diabetes ins&#237;pida nefrog&#233;nica se produce cuando los ri&#241;ones no responden a la ADH, lo que lleva a la incapacidad de concentrar la orina.</data>
      <data key="d10">67fc85f14d95a9a24054c2a3ec125e37</data>
      <data key="d11">e1c826edf98f4f269a95cc8b3f7ec291</data>
      <data key="d12">12948</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="KIDNEYS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH regulates water balance by controlling the amount of water reabsorbed by the kidneys</data>
      <data key="d10">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">eb6cacd4fed544fe920e10b3252b3482</data>
      <data key="d12">12949</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="SRAA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH secretion is influenced by the activation of the SRAA in response to low blood volume</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">7c10e8633a2a4b1da60e60a6f9e2d36d</data>
      <data key="d12">12950</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="SIADH">
      <data key="d8">25.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH, or antidiuretic hormone, is a hormone whose inappropriate secretion is responsible for the condition known as SIADH, or Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion. SIADH is characterized by the excessive release of ADH, which results in water retention in the body. This condition can lead to hyponatremia, a potentially serious electrolyte imbalance caused by low sodium levels in the blood. Thus, the relationship between ADH and SIADH is crucial, as the dysregulation of ADH secretion directly contributes to the symptoms and complications associated with SIADH.</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591,62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">4266d0b60e0544d3b1f451230a90df16</data>
      <data key="d12">12951</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="H2O">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH regulates the reabsorption of water in the kidneys, affecting overall water balance</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">5c4efefb00b84d2fbd4aa3ca79fb33b7</data>
      <data key="d12">12952</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="ACUAPORINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH increases the expression of aquaporins in the kidney, enhancing water reabsorption</data>
      <data key="d10">4f92e69f74f9c3ceabd5aa23ddc2b591</data>
      <data key="d11">c34be6bd98d04a4aa916cb49a08fb0b8</data>
      <data key="d12">12953</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADH" target="NEUROHYPOPHYSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ADH is produced and secreted by the neurohypophysis, which is essential for regulating water balance</data>
      <data key="d10">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d11">45b1528404354ce3a57e8291e6a3b95b</data>
      <data key="d12">12954</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFISITIS IGG4" target="ENFERMEDAD RELACIONADA CON LA IGG4">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipofisitis IgG4 is a specific manifestation of the broader enfermedad relacionada con la IgG4</data>
      <data key="d10">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d11">99a9a329388a4ab38691afe53cdef82a</data>
      <data key="d12">12955</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFISITIS IGG4" target="SIADH">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SIADH can be a complication following surgery related to conditions like hipofisitis IGG4</data>
      <data key="d10">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d11">55c53d77896c4900aeea173665a3d652</data>
      <data key="d12">12956</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOFISITIS IGG4" target="PITUITARIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipofisitis IgG4 affects the pituitaria, leading to various hormonal imbalances</data>
      <data key="d10">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d11">dca835a2815f499797c15a826a8fa68b</data>
      <data key="d12">12957</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGLICEMIA" target="VAR&#211;N DE 77 A&#209;OS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The 77-year-old man may experience hypoglycemia due to his diabetes management and medication regimen.</data>
      <data key="d10">2f91f92c99da813a8d1be2f6ac0fa552</data>
      <data key="d11">7eadf55e6247490389e11c7d4e7c2bc6</data>
      <data key="d12">12958</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="F&#211;RMULA DE FURST">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">F&#243;rmula de Furst is used to guide fluid restriction in patients with SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">c6994d09848639470e57b0ab0b7166cf</data>
      <data key="d11">b81c4e963a344150bfdb3866ee32e797</data>
      <data key="d12">12959</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="VILLABONA C.">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Villabona C. discusses SIADH in the Manual de Endocrinolog&#237;a y Nutrici&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd</data>
      <data key="d11">72d11e393e07497098255877ef0fe48a</data>
      <data key="d12">12960</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="TOLVAPT&#193;N">
      <data key="d8">48.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tolvapt&#225;n is a medication indicated for the treatment of hyponatremia associated with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). It is specifically utilized to manage sodium levels in patients suffering from SIADH, particularly after the failure of fluid restriction measures. The drug functions by promoting the excretion of free water, thereby alleviating the symptoms of SIADH and effectively treating the hyponatremia caused by this condition. Overall, Tolvapt&#225;n serves as a crucial therapeutic option for patients with SIADH, helping to restore normal sodium levels and improve their clinical status.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b390802e6a6df561cafb9593e97d6bd,69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,85cfae7019d0efa6f0c87f5cd5b9ce8e,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013,a56fad7f6dac4a75bd4748b247aa9215,fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">5a67902edfe24e949e170f1a1a96f32f</data>
      <data key="d12">12961</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FLUOXETINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fluoxetina is known to be associated with the development of SIADH, especially in older patients</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">eca21b08b4d8410c909afd9189b44021</data>
      <data key="d12">12962</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="CLORPROPAMIDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clorpropamida is recognized as a medication that can induce SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">562f8545c2f845b182a192c284f49418</data>
      <data key="d12">12963</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="CARBAMACEPINA">
      <data key="d8">11.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbamazepine is a medication that can induce the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), which may impact the duration of treatment. This association arises from Carbamazepine's effects on the release of vasopressin, a hormone that regulates water balance in the body. As a result, patients taking Carbamazepine may experience alterations in fluid retention and electrolyte balance due to the development of SIADH.</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966,a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">7ae10a9ef2274c0595b47918f45a26a9</data>
      <data key="d12">12964</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="C&#193;NCER PULMONAR DE C&#201;LULAS PEQUE&#209;AS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Small cell lung cancer can lead to SIADH through ectopic vasopressin production</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">3bf32e49b0af4d8d826d953b46b36cf5</data>
      <data key="d12">12965</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR OBSTRUCTIVA CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease can be a contributing factor to the development of SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">4c2eea615e3c4f9d97eb36a462e670de</data>
      <data key="d12">12966</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="HIPOFLISIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hypophysis plays a role in the regulation of antidiuretic hormone, which is involved in SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">a2bc3ecb4c946bf6d4905a8d4fe7d013</data>
      <data key="d11">681c13590bca4eb7b223ded4209d3bfd</data>
      <data key="d12">12967</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ANTIEPILEPTICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los antiepil&#233;pticos son medicamentos que pueden inducir el SIADH, afectando la regulaci&#243;n de la vasopresina.</data>
      <data key="d10">c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d11">184045433f214e31ad0c612ca2c60060</data>
      <data key="d12">12968</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="QUIMIOTERAPICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los quimioter&#225;picos pueden causar SIADH, afectando la funci&#243;n hormonal del cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d10">c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d11">166a49798b2741c0ab728b4cadb99a5d</data>
      <data key="d12">12969</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ANTIDIABETICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Algunos antidiab&#233;ticos est&#225;n relacionados con la aparici&#243;n del SIADH, afectando la regulaci&#243;n de la vasopresina.</data>
      <data key="d10">c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d11">50fd7485b1eb4abcb0a9cd6f99bd2782</data>
      <data key="d12">12970</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ANALOGOS DE VASOPRESINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los an&#225;logos de vasopresina pueden inducir el SIADH al imitar la acci&#243;n de la vasopresina natural.</data>
      <data key="d10">c5ebf416dfb2be58a226e15fb9771c86</data>
      <data key="d11">58a5471906944271b8c60ec262238bf1</data>
      <data key="d12">12971</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="BLOQUE: SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL AVANZADO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The block discusses advanced nutritional support in the context of managing conditions like SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d11">102eadd4fd324e32b74cd67cbfcb4776</data>
      <data key="d12">12972</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="CEREBRAL EDEMA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SIADH can lead to conditions that cause cerebral edema due to water retention and electrolyte imbalance</data>
      <data key="d10">62accad551112bfbff64638bfce78a73</data>
      <data key="d11">62a7e0f9275a478bbd9e1a233dd2e041</data>
      <data key="d12">12973</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ELLISON DH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ellison DH's research contributed to the understanding and diagnosis of SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">91379effbbfc4bec979afd3338f85730</data>
      <data key="d12">12974</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="VERBALIS ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Verbalis et al. provided insights into the causes of SIADH, enhancing the understanding of the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">6dc6d3721d184b6c9bac5725c9a9af75</data>
      <data key="d12">12975</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="HIPOANTREMIA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyponatremia is a key clinical feature of SIADH, resulting from inappropriate ADH secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">13f8e791817f4682a1945a192008ce74</data>
      <data key="d12">12976</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="SISTEMA NERVIOSO CENTRAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Disorders of the central nervous system can lead to the development of SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">81342f3414ee41d9b42497c5d6b0801f</data>
      <data key="d12">12977</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FARMACOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Certain medications can induce SIADH by enhancing ADH secretion</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">5a5e769de44444e99a7af7ed2e4c1c7c</data>
      <data key="d12">12978</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="DIUR&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The use of diuretics can complicate the diagnosis of SIADH due to their effect on sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">addd6db95fafa3464a6f085f8d0041ce</data>
      <data key="d11">c3e0f5deaa084c4697d8fb4bb985974d</data>
      <data key="d12">12979</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="HIPONATREMIA EUVOL&#201;MICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El SIADH es una de las causas m&#225;s frecuentes de hiponatremia euvol&#233;mica en pacientes con nutrici&#243;n artificial.</data>
      <data key="d10">d8ad55d79ba614f2c8906babacf0e9f6</data>
      <data key="d11">59fc4161a9704f3e98071208385e9196</data>
      <data key="d12">12980</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FURSEMIDE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Furosemide is used to treat patients with SIADH by promoting the elimination of free water</data>
      <data key="d10">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7</data>
      <data key="d11">263d341680294238bf15dfca9d612612</data>
      <data key="d12">12981</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FURST FORMULA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Furst formula is utilized to assess renal function in patients with SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">22769156746e1c11980b01e7fffbcac7</data>
      <data key="d11">0f219abf2327477b94664a11d9d43979</data>
      <data key="d12">12982</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="CONIVAPT&#193;N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Conivapt&#225;n is used to treat hyponatremia caused by SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">84dc80044acb4e8680e8dea2b33434c3</data>
      <data key="d12">12983</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EPOC can lead to the development of SIADH, affecting treatment duration</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">39a721bdc6f04f258bfd5366c9b11284</data>
      <data key="d12">12984</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="VIH">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIV can induce SIADH, impacting treatment response</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">d0ece96f9c384e6c9a2fd0ec776a63c9</data>
      <data key="d12">12985</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FUROSEMIDA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Furosemide is often used in the treatment of SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">9f6698b8d6494e3483af73fc4c290eb1</data>
      <data key="d12">12986</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="ALGORITMO MULTIDISCIPLINAR">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The multidisciplinary algorithm provides guidelines for managing SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">6ecbff0a64af42d5adbd75dc4f5c4701</data>
      <data key="d12">12987</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="TABAQUISMO">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tabaquismo can lead to respiratory issues that may complicate SIADH treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">2b0666b9bae8437d86f309f4aa8ea1ce</data>
      <data key="d12">12988</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="HEMORRAGIA SUBARACNOIDEA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemorragia subaracnoidea can induce SIADH, with a specific treatment duration of 1-4 weeks</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">42e8475ad9814560b5d686f9e829bdf8</data>
      <data key="d12">12989</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="MASAS CEREBRALES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Masas cerebrales can cause SIADH, with treatment duration determined by the evolution of the underlying disease</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">865a91008e0148358d21cf4d0666d914</data>
      <data key="d12">12990</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEF&#193;LICO">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Traumatismo craneoencef&#225;lico can lead to SIADH, with treatment duration ranging from 2-7 days to indefinite</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">840fe9bc1dd64b8fa90fa6a5e4f2167b</data>
      <data key="d12">12991</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="LESIONES CEREBRALES INFLAMATORIAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lesiones cerebrales inflamatorias can induce SIADH, with treatment duration depending on the response</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">c892cd6ba7864299927c0dd1ee061b7d</data>
      <data key="d12">12992</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="IDIOP&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Idiop&#225;tico cases of SIADH have an indefinite treatment duration</data>
      <data key="d10">69844236241841a2f03d6419e0916966</data>
      <data key="d11">b82e67fd65fe4c388b596c21add9b948</data>
      <data key="d12">12993</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FLUDROCORTISONA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fludrocortisona may be used in cases of isolated aldosterone deficiency related to SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">8c5a8f66c40543faab91b5088552f5a1</data>
      <data key="d12">12994</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="HIDROCORTISONA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hidrocortisona is administered in primary adrenal insufficiency which can be related to SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">6df1214c85aa44879cf1fcfe23acd756</data>
      <data key="d12">12995</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="SFS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SFS is used for rehydration in the treatment of SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">73c35ba8d1504b55b29e80984451ced0</data>
      <data key="d12">12996</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="FURSEMIDA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Furosemida is used to manage fluid retention in patients with SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">b9927966adb7425e93e6b6d24cab475a</data>
      <data key="d12">12997</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="SRAA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The SRAA system is involved in the management of fluid balance in SIADH</data>
      <data key="d10">fa0165b0420f4c761829a08a3ab08508</data>
      <data key="d11">1eb65912f19846f2bad2685ca1cccc7a</data>
      <data key="d12">12998</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="CONIVAPTAN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Conivaptan is used to treat hyponatremia associated with the syndrome of inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone (SIADH).</data>
      <data key="d10">1ceaa92ed88d3f829122e1554f2e7277</data>
      <data key="d11">bafc2a6840d74f0e90ee4f8cfddfd6fe</data>
      <data key="d12">12999</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIADH" target="TOLVAPTAN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tolvaptan is used to treat hyponatremia caused by the syndrome of inappropriate secretion of antidiuretic hormone (SIADH).</data>
