    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="COMPLICACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension is a risk factor that contributes to the development of cardiovascular complications, which the Mediterranean diet aims to mitigate.</data>
      <data key="d10">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d11">c62a621566824c3fbd8ac8d4a1361603</data>
      <data key="d12">13116</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="GSDIB">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertension can develop as a secondary condition in patients with GSDIb due to renal issues.</data>
      <data key="d10">a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98</data>
      <data key="d11">a19cc04f3cd440258b9b5e3dd2cccf48</data>
      <data key="d12">13117</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="DIETA CONTROLADA EN SODIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta controlada en sodio es esencial para el control de la hipertensi&#243;n arterial.</data>
      <data key="d10">5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb</data>
      <data key="d11">50f0438a7f0c4bf88680cc27dd02c542</data>
      <data key="d12">13118</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="INTERSALT">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El estudio INTERSALT demuestra la relaci&#243;n entre el consumo de sodio y la hipertensi&#243;n arterial.</data>
      <data key="d10">5f2499e1d1e1a498084eb95bdfe634fb</data>
      <data key="d11">697ef44318b244caa92a1cdb3bf5c2c4</data>
      <data key="d12">13119</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="DIETA RICA EN POTASIO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A diet rich in potassium is used to manage and prevent hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">0722201044be4bed85160d46aad167b4</data>
      <data key="d12">13120</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="AFROAMERICANOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Afroamericans are known to develop hypertension more frequently and at an earlier age.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">f171e986ea174910aff2f6eeca17dc02</data>
      <data key="d12">13121</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="SISTEMA SCORE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The SCORE system is used to assess cardiovascular risk, which includes hypertension as a factor.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">42cb7e63344f4fcb9866ff76ba5035ba</data>
      <data key="d12">13122</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="ESTUDIO FRAMINGHAM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Framingham study found a higher prevalence of hypertension in obese individuals, linking weight to hypertension risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">64b852479a464960a611e613c2d221b6</data>
      <data key="d12">13123</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="DASH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The DASH diet is specifically designed to help control hypertension.</data>
      <data key="d10">92ae465a11b49807321be06ec9f5bc5a</data>
      <data key="d11">88ff5ee881fc4f06a88387e281bea76d</data>
      <data key="d12">13124</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERTENSI&#211;N ARTERIAL" target="TRASTORNOS NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipertensi&#243;n arterial can be a consequence of poor nutrition and is addressed in pediatric dietary management.</data>
      <data key="d10">b6c8d5ff1536806d6512fb9d1af1e6db</data>
      <data key="d11">9776fa06e56a464a9a92415eb15cb324</data>
      <data key="d12">13125</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA FAMILIAR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipercolesterolemia familiar es un tipo de dislipidemia que contribuye al riesgo cardiovascular</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">1c785965547548419e937bac93fa4198</data>
      <data key="d12">13126</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="HIPERCOLESTEROLEMIA POLIG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipercolesterolemia polig&#233;nica es una forma de dislipidemia que afecta los niveles de colesterol</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">935723d2d4c04462b890617e1b7b65b2</data>
      <data key="d12">13127</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE APOPROTE&#205;NA B-100">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El d&#233;ficit familiar de apolipoprote&#237;na B-100 es un trastorno que se manifiesta como dislipidemia</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">4447a45409c54d9f90661bdd0f46cf1e</data>
      <data key="d12">13128</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="ESTATINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las estatinas son utilizadas para tratar la dislipidemia y controlar los niveles de colesterol LDL</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">4cad30aebe7d44c48a8253d7c529eb3c</data>
      <data key="d12">13129</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="EZETIMIBA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ezetimiba is a medication used to treat dyslipidemia, a condition characterized by abnormal lipid levels in the blood. It works by inhibiting the absorption of cholesterol in the intestines, which helps to lower levels of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol. This action aids patients in reaching their LDL cholesterol goals, thereby contributing to better overall cardiovascular health.</data>
      <data key="d10">64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63,a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">cb49097a937040449d55346f2f7e41c3</data>
      <data key="d12">13130</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="INHIBIDORES DE PCSK9">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los inhibidores de PCSK9 son utilizados para tratar la dislipidemia en pacientes que no responden a las estatinas</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">11d27a57e88c4bd59e0e029879f37de9</data>
      <data key="d12">13131</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="CARDIOVASCULAR ENFERMEDAD">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dislipidemia es un factor de riesgo importante para el desarrollo de enfermedades cardiovasculares</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">ebe7160864e44be28b2a2c19acbd608d</data>
      <data key="d12">13132</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="SENSIBILIDAD A LA INSULINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dislipidemia aterog&#233;nica est&#225; estrechamente relacionada con la resistencia a la insulina</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">0924940645d24ae88908f839328de95a</data>
      <data key="d12">13133</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dislipidemia es un componente del s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico, que aumenta el riesgo cardiovascular</data>
      <data key="d10">a284cea0d1f3969e0df5f78d3b9189c6</data>
      <data key="d11">0053281ab0404acb900b197268280541</data>
      <data key="d12">13134</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="&#193;CIDO NICOT&#205;NICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido nicot&#237;nico is used to treat dyslipidemia by decreasing VLDL production</data>
      <data key="d10">64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63</data>
      <data key="d11">f970f61e6d8a450eb77661d9e7522945</data>
      <data key="d12">13135</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="FIBRATOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fibratos are used to treat dyslipidemia, particularly hypertriglyceridemia</data>
      <data key="d10">64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63</data>
      <data key="d11">0fb58a9c595f46e7b4b1cd82da58fdb9</data>
      <data key="d12">13136</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="AACE/ACE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">AACE/ACE provides guidelines for the management of dyslipidemia and prevention of cardiovascular disease</data>
      <data key="d10">64476b3e50fca7a5cbcb70822bd1be63</data>
      <data key="d11">8e2ea0b440b84edb9c114cb7710f6ca2</data>
      <data key="d12">13137</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTIONS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional interventions are important for managing dyslipidemia through dietary modifications</data>
      <data key="d10">55aabc274c460459322072406f17d52c</data>
      <data key="d11">6799d19fc41d4f0cb2d6e10b623b4ab2</data>
      <data key="d12">13138</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="GSDIII">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dislipidemia, particularly hypertriglyceridemia, is a complication associated with GSDIII</data>
      <data key="d10">b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">0b1ad89e45a3401382aae1326bc824a0</data>
      <data key="d12">13139</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="GSD0">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mild dyslipidemia can be observed in patients with GSD0</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">957835dd43e148c6bce95b7e09fcb8bc</data>
      <data key="d12">13140</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DISLIPIDEMIA" target="DC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dislipidemia is a common occurrence in patients undergoing dietary treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141</data>
      <data key="d11">c9b7960285684728acc8464699522e03</data>
      <data key="d12">13141</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEDENTARISMO" target="COMPLICACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sedentarismo contributes to the risk of cardiovascular complications, highlighting the importance of physical activity.</data>
      <data key="d10">c0b1584b66f6fc74e457e1281d64cd49</data>
      <data key="d11">01054f32acad4e97bf6245b7019c5336</data>
      <data key="d12">13142</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AFROAMERICANOS" target="HEREDITARY FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The prevalence of hereditary fructose intolerance in Afroamericans is estimated to be 1 in 200,000</data>
      <data key="d10">ada55dc10a07d6ad1d50199d5cb5f950</data>
      <data key="d11">d46ded4f94eb4d8f875f499f98009af4</data>
      <data key="d12">13143</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MODY" target="HNF-4&#913;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HNF-4&#945; is a gene mutation associated with MODY type 1, which affects insulin secretion and diabetes management.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">a1f356b1bb664101a6e7f78c59de2681</data>
      <data key="d12">13144</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MODY" target="GLUCOKINASE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucokinase is a gene mutation associated with MODY type 2, which is characterized by mild hyperglycemia and often does not require treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">e6b386b6ca2b473380a3ca973db6c406</data>
      <data key="d12">13145</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MODY" target="HNF-1&#914;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HNF-1&#946; is a gene mutation associated with MODY type 5, which can lead to renal complications and requires specific treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">389c0cbc287c4b2b8f80f856cbb1c0c8</data>
      <data key="d12">13146</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MODY" target="HNF-1&#913;">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HNF-1&#945; is a gene mutation associated with MODY type 3, which is linked to microvascular complications and insulin sensitivity.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">d6a2eb4ea1c449ad8990b4ddb6a46212</data>
      <data key="d12">13147</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MODY" target="IPF-1">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">IPF-1 is a gene mutation associated with MODY type 4, which can lead to pancreatic agenesis and requires careful management.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">665d41e7856a4e06b03826e0de1bf91c</data>
      <data key="d12">13148</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HAPO" target="DIABETES GESTACIONAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The HAPO study established diagnostic criteria for gestational diabetes based on blood glucose levels during pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">15b2acf811a14248ba1558b15ca158bb</data>
      <data key="d12">13149</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SULFONILUREAS" target="DIABETES NEONATAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sulfonylureas can be an appropriate treatment for many cases of neonatal diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">ac89fcaa7dcce835c0d5b9ed9ce94cea</data>
      <data key="d11">da3059352f7a40b7a2707b2798f2b3ed</data>
      <data key="d12">13150</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CURVA CON 75 G DE GLUCEMIA" target="DIABETES GESTACIONAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The 75g glucose curve test is used to diagnose gestational diabetes by measuring blood glucose levels after glucose intake.</data>
      <data key="d10">f1bd89f4a1fcc385a19f5c5323ee2f89</data>
      <data key="d11">306daea7683e41d48199fd49896992e5</data>
      <data key="d12">13151</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES GESTACIONAL" target="MAR&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mar&#237;a was diagnosed with diabetes gestacional during her pregnancy</data>
      <data key="d10">6a2d5ced0ad16871fec539845797e0ac</data>
      <data key="d11">4a7f88c360d54599b09ab19472400a2f</data>
      <data key="d12">13152</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES GESTACIONAL" target="TEST DE TOLERANCIA ORAL A LA GLUCOSA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El Test de Tolerancia Oral a la Glucosa es recomendado para el cribado de diabetes gestacional en mujeres embarazadas</data>
      <data key="d10">48e690b80c196e397d9ab9527b38c3d4</data>
      <data key="d11">9fbd71aca5fb468f8adc35ed2b06372e</data>
      <data key="d12">13153</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES GESTACIONAL" target="TTOG">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The TTOG is specifically used to diagnose diabetes gestacional by measuring glucose levels in pregnant women.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c37affdd97e7772d1ea27aee34533b8</data>
      <data key="d11">91e24dcacf42465dbd71ba0ed7971ea2</data>
      <data key="d12">13154</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES GESTACIONAL" target="O'SULLIVAN TEST">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The O'Sullivan test is a preliminary screening method for diagnosing diabetes gestacional.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c37affdd97e7772d1ea27aee34533b8</data>
      <data key="d11">f4e6577d78db4cedbcbc71064f23f7d2</data>
      <data key="d12">13155</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES GESTACIONAL" target="GLUC&#211;METRO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A gluc&#243;metro is used for monitoring blood glucose levels in patients diagnosed with diabetes gestacional.</data>
      <data key="d10">4c37affdd97e7772d1ea27aee34533b8</data>
      <data key="d11">dc05da3c55c343e7a7cdd297484ee1ca</data>
      <data key="d12">13156</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCOKINASE" target="GLUCONEOGENESIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glucokinase is involved in glucose metabolism, which is essential for gluconeogenesis, linking these two processes.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb8d31ef68f83e6b01f6fc8548f36d0c</data>
      <data key="d11">c98a59060428420db8f1f491bc725d08</data>
      <data key="d12">13157</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HNF-1&#914;" target="DIABETES TIPO MODY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HNF-1&#946; mutations are a cause of MODY 5 diabetes, a subtype of diabetes tipo MODY</data>
      <data key="d10">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b</data>
      <data key="d11">35e95a3cc83c4cefb86ce90a0778729c</data>
      <data key="d12">13158</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HNF-1&#914;" target="DIABETES NEONATAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HNF-1&#946; mutations can contribute to neonatal diabetes, particularly in specific genetic contexts</data>
      <data key="d10">b29ba49771904108b9b729f30a6f672b</data>
      <data key="d11">9e0efc1918e44ac58c6050d2b757a0c2</data>
      <data key="d12">13159</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES TIPO 2" target="BUPROPION-NALTREXONE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bupropion-naltrexone can be indicated for patients with obesity and type 2 diabetes</data>
      <data key="d10">7eea8ed505de441028811dbb848d0fa0</data>
      <data key="d11">a3cb97c4ecb540ad83c5db9449f28a6b</data>
      <data key="d12">13160</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES TIPO 2" target="FEDERACI&#211;N ESPA&#209;OLA DE DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FEDE provides resources and support for individuals with Type 2 diabetes in Spain</data>
