    <edge source="INSULIN" target="HYPOGLYCEMIA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin is a key hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of blood sugar levels in the body. It is particularly important for individuals with diabetes, as they often require insulin therapy to manage their condition. However, the administration of insulin can lead to hypoglycemia, a condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels, if not properly managed. This risk is especially pronounced in diabetic patients who may not adequately monitor their insulin doses or dietary intake. Therefore, careful management of insulin therapy is essential to prevent hypoglycemia and ensure the safety and well-being of individuals relying on this treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">06fe3811ad957d6841997b2a0e9be50f,5b487245068b8e8b87ffcc04970aaff4</data>
      <data key="d11">ef627286b6bd452fa95fabc1863ee333</data>
      <data key="d12">13187</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULIN" target="CAD">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulin deficiency is a key factor in the development of CAD</data>
      <data key="d10">bcded135629c889cb0a10ae968743582</data>
      <data key="d11">c14eb5dc404e41229d62be8a2893e3bc</data>
      <data key="d12">13188</data>
