    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2" target="ESTATINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The relationship between statins and Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is characterized by a notable association. Research indicates that the use of statins has been linked to an increased risk of developing Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2. Specifically, there is a potential heightened risk of developing this type of diabetes associated with the use of statins. This suggests that while statins are commonly prescribed for managing cholesterol levels and reducing cardiovascular risks, they may also contribute to the onset of type 2 diabetes in some individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">2729f43dc666433fb3fabad498b99f91,9312fdfba5d3f79b95c5e6af38ced009</data>
      <data key="d11">1bc4d445de0644749dbde781c16335c4</data>
