      <data key="d12">13396</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1" target="SUPLEMENTOS VITAM&#205;NICOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Suplementos vitam&#237;nicos are often considered by individuals with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 to potentially enhance performance, despite limited evidence of their effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d10">043ed163c427b880fe39884076cae7ea</data>
      <data key="d11">aea623cb7ec140e2a64669154c3cc764</data>
      <data key="d12">13397</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1" target="SUPLEMENTOS DE AMINO&#193;CIDOS Y PROTE&#205;NAS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Athletes with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 may consider amino acid and protein supplements, but the necessity is debated by experts.</data>
      <data key="d10">043ed163c427b880fe39884076cae7ea</data>
      <data key="d11">bf0921feae7a4d06b43f5e02740d7183</data>
      <data key="d12">13398</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1" target="ALIMENTOS ERGOG&#201;NICOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alimentos ergog&#233;nicos may be considered by athletes with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 to potentially enhance performance, but their effects are not well established.</data>
