    <edge source="LIVER TRANSPLANTATION" target="CIRRHOSIS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Liver transplantation is a critical procedure for patients suffering from end-stage cirrhosis, a severe liver condition characterized by the progressive replacement of healthy liver tissue with scar tissue. It is frequently considered a necessary treatment option for individuals with advanced cirrhosis, as their liver function deteriorates significantly. Consequently, patients with cirrhosis may require liver transplantation to restore liver function and improve their quality of life.</data>
