    <edge source="COWDEN SYNDROME" target="PTEN">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cowden syndrome is caused by mutations in the PTEN gene, which is critical for understanding the syndrome's pathology.</data>
      <data key="d10">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d11">c4d8abdafa784091adaf1d7bb238e5aa</data>
      <data key="d12">13956</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COWDEN SYNDROME" target="MEN2B">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both Cowden syndrome and MEN2B are genetic conditions that increase the risk of thyroid cancer and require specific management strategies.</data>
      <data key="d10">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d11">4cded4b253454c36bdf7e4eac8cef8c7</data>
      <data key="d12">13957</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Medullary thyroid carcinoma is often associated with MEN2B, necessitating specific management and treatment protocols.</data>
      <data key="d10">0c7db743733d35ca867a97cda57322ce</data>
      <data key="d11">2ea1a42999bc40008de68fb88f49afa1</data>
      <data key="d12">13958</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="MEN2A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2B and MEN2A are both genetic conditions caused by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene</data>
      <data key="d10">2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c</data>
      <data key="d11">49271005effc42808514e01f6c2e5061</data>
      <data key="d12">13959</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="MULLIGAN LM">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mulligan LM studied point mutations in the RET proto-oncogene related to MEN2B</data>
      <data key="d10">2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c</data>
      <data key="d11">321564331f364cff9c5e64191c31005c</data>
      <data key="d12">13960</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2B est&#225; relacionado con carcinomas medulares de tiroides y requiere intervenci&#243;n quir&#250;rgica temprana.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140</data>
      <data key="d11">4aa9d9a7a04c46dba7a955cb90a0bb4e</data>
      <data key="d12">13961</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="PROTOONCOG&#201;N RET">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las mutaciones en el protooncog&#233;n RET son responsables del desarrollo de MEN2B, que est&#225; asociado con carcinomas medulares.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140</data>
      <data key="d11">dfe016b7874c44d59b9126c8f1968746</data>
      <data key="d12">13962</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="CMT">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2B is characterized by a high risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma (CMT), often requiring early surgical treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">13253681c114423890a8ddbafc781d61</data>
      <data key="d12">13963</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="RET">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the RET proto-oncogene are linked to MEN2B, which increases the risk of medullary thyroid carcinoma and other tumors.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">fd37cd510b4949cc986a0ba9cc4d42d2</data>
      <data key="d12">13964</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="FEO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pheochromocytoma (FEO) is a common manifestation of MEN2B, necessitating monitoring and management.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">0bfb6d7768ee49e9bfda68c53abf8f8c</data>
      <data key="d12">13965</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="MEN2">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2B is a subtype of MEN2 that is more aggressive and has distinct clinical features compared to MEN2A</data>
      <data key="d10">2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f</data>
      <data key="d11">a70917708beb46be9122e21509d2350c</data>
      <data key="d12">13966</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2B" target="HYPERPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2B syndrome does not typically associate with hyperparathyroidism, distinguishing it from MEN2A</data>
      <data key="d10">2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f</data>
      <data key="d11">162a59d0f7f1409eaa4b311f2ea7ab60</data>
      <data key="d12">13967</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PTEN" target="S&#205;NDROME DE COWDEN">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Cowden est&#225; asociado a mutaciones en el gen PTEN, el cual es crucial para su desarrollo. La mutaci&#243;n en el gen PTEN es imprescindible para el diagn&#243;stico del s&#237;ndrome de Cowden, siendo un factor clave en su identificaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">aa7c3342c84b44918bd8677aded0ed34</data>
      <data key="d12">13968</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="CALCITONIN">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a type of thyroid cancer characterized by the abnormal growth of parafollicular C cells, which produce the hormone calcitonin. Calcitonin levels are crucial in the context of medullary thyroid carcinoma, as they are monitored to predict the evolution of patients with this condition. These levels serve as a significant marker for both diagnosing and monitoring the disease, with their concentrations being directly related to the presence and extent of the carcinoma. Therefore, elevated calcitonin levels can indicate the presence of medullary thyroid carcinoma and help assess its progression over time.</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec,de6e1d8ac9f422acb17fd26b77b485da</data>
      <data key="d11">d449b6fd3a1f4326b2245dcb7f2af1c0</data>
      <data key="d12">13969</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="SALTIKI ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Saltiki et al. studied the evolution of medullary thyroid carcinoma in their series</data>
      <data key="d10">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d11">4fe603a5a7f64c529bf1f53d7fcd4b1f</data>
      <data key="d12">13970</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="CERVICAL ULTRASOUND">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a type of thyroid cancer that requires careful monitoring and evaluation, particularly concerning lymph node involvement. Cervical ultrasound is a crucial diagnostic tool in this context, as it is recommended for assessing lymph node metastases in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. Additionally, cervical ultrasound is also employed to evaluate surgical outcomes in these patients, providing valuable information on the effectiveness of treatment and any potential complications. Thus, cervical ultrasound plays a significant role in both the diagnosis and post-surgical assessment of medullary thyroid carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d11">295a7b3ccc8f4da2aee098ccb306f8a0</data>
      <data key="d12">13971</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="MRI">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MRI is used to detect bone metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d11">7b59c1eed81347549a78375688a03f02</data>
      <data key="d12">13972</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="BONE SCINTIGRAPHY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone scintigraphy is also used to detect bone metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d11">f8cc06733bfa423e95c13d59ea54f453</data>
      <data key="d12">13973</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="PET 18F-FDG">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PET 18F-FDG is used to assess metabolic activity in tumors, but has low sensitivity for detecting medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">72b937574e8e90d19c9549a10b75057c</data>
      <data key="d11">d09c5c0e96304a2a8fdca34495c0af61</data>
      <data key="d12">13974</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="ATA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ATA provides guidelines for the management of medullary thyroid carcinoma, influencing treatment decisions</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1</data>
      <data key="d11">31957d0fa0664b39809835575ffd32b5</data>
      <data key="d12">13975</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="PELLEGRITI ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pellegriti et al. studied the outcomes of patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma, providing insights into its management</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1</data>
      <data key="d11">cd4b5314ad694f738e752c9ead8f2bb2</data>
      <data key="d12">13976</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="BARBET ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Barbet et al. researched the prognostic factors related to medullary thyroid carcinoma, focusing on calcitonin levels</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1</data>
      <data key="d11">b3710c3f4fd3415c8f4ee507db56da97</data>
      <data key="d12">13977</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="VANDETANIB">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vandetanib is used as a treatment option for patients with advanced medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1</data>
      <data key="d11">8a0e942f6c7d44ea99dbaa1d194295d2</data>
