      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="CABOZANTINIB">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cabozantinib is another treatment option for patients with progressive medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1</data>
      <data key="d11">e709d6da85dc4fc792d9ba29d429aa4b</data>
      <data key="d12">13979</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a type of thyroid cancer characterized by the presence of specific tumor markers, one of which is carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA). CEA levels are frequently elevated in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma, making it a valuable tool for monitoring the disease. In clinical practice, the assessment of carcinoembryonic antigen levels is typically conducted alongside calcitonin measurements to evaluate the prognosis of patients with this type of cancer. This dual assessment aids in understanding the progression of the disease and guiding treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d10">53eefebd95b547fa56967d97b31beec1,a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">3a4805e100374195b71582dfe6cff753</data>
      <data key="d12">13980</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="BRITISH JOURNAL OF CANCER">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The journal features research articles on the long-term outcomes of patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">dc48577f4dca4f518d5ad2b21b3ed2da</data>
      <data key="d12">13981</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="PHASE III TRIAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The phase III trial evaluates the effectiveness of Vandetanib in treating medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">d8576e670b624298a1328f8540ba3d2a</data>
      <data key="d12">13982</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="HYPERTIROXINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperthyroxinemia can be a differential diagnosis when evaluating patients for medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">66f26e0d2aac4bef9f3af560640c8250</data>
      <data key="d12">13983</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA" target="RESISTANCE TO HORMONES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Resistance to hormones can affect the clinical presentation and management of medullary thyroid carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d10">a2303199b7587142ad661841870790ec</data>
      <data key="d11">820186fa98ef4c1ba12ff81b842cd6ac</data>
      <data key="d12">13984</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE COWDEN" target="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La tiroidectom&#237;a es un tratamiento recomendado para pacientes con s&#237;ndrome de Cowden que presentan riesgo de carcinoma medular de tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">5e29e42f1c924c9b983473a13e7fdfd4</data>
      <data key="d12">13985</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE COWDEN" target="S&#205;NDROME DE DENYS-DRASH">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos s&#237;ndromes son raros y est&#225;n asociados a mutaciones gen&#233;ticas que afectan la salud de los pacientes</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">75b730fffd004c069b0b9885cb9230c1</data>
      <data key="d12">13986</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE COWDEN" target="S&#205;NDROME DE SMITH-LEMLI-OPITZ">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos s&#237;ndromes presentan caracter&#237;sticas fenot&#237;picas variadas y est&#225;n relacionados con mutaciones gen&#233;ticas</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">35c01831dd4846f3ba73ea6fcc015503</data>
      <data key="d12">13987</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A" target="LINFADENECTOM&#205;A CERVICAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La linfadenectom&#237;a cervical se realiza junto con la tiroidectom&#237;a total en el tratamiento del carcinoma medular de tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">782a4b9523114201871c3a6c44f1c367</data>
      <data key="d12">13988</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A" target="M918T MEN2B">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mutaci&#243;n M918T MEN2B requiere tiroidectom&#237;a profil&#225;ctica antes del primer a&#241;o de vida para prevenir el carcinoma medular de tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">f7a423e5a50c49faa9ea50d67e505d92</data>
      <data key="d12">13989</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A" target="GU&#205;A DE CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES DE LA ATA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La Gu&#237;a de carcinoma medular de tiroides de la ATA establece criterios para la realizaci&#243;n de tiroidectom&#237;as en funci&#243;n de las mutaciones detectadas</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">00ca4ed5025942b5b5b3d6333e2c8bc0</data>
      <data key="d12">13990</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A" target="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tiroidectom&#237;a, which refers to the surgical removal of the thyroid gland, can lead to complications such as hipoparatiroidismo, or hypoparathyroidism. This condition may arise as a result of total thyroidectomy performed on patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. The procedure can cause either transient or permanent hypoparathyroidism due to potential damage to the parathyroid glands, which are responsible for regulating calcium levels in the body. Thus, there is a significant relationship between tiroidectom&#237;a and the risk of developing hipoparatiroidismo as a postoperative complication.</data>
      <data key="d10">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4,c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">0e34a41b212f4dd6802563741045d694</data>
      <data key="d12">13991</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="M918T MEN2B" target="GU&#205;A DE CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES DE LA ATA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La Gu&#237;a de carcinoma medular de tiroides de la ATA menciona la mutaci&#243;n M918T MEN2B y su relaci&#243;n con la cirug&#237;a profil&#225;ctica</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">8037668a78f749a494baf7b8c8fff76a</data>
      <data key="d12">13992</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="M918T MEN2B" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La mutaci&#243;n M918T MEN2B est&#225; asociada con un alto riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma medular de tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">0702eb1ee9634a1d90c788b28a577e2a</data>
      <data key="d12">13993</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HAMPARTOMAS" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los hamartomas pueden ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado en pacientes con carcinoma medular de tiroides y s&#237;ndrome de Cowden</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">ee147a3153d044ed82a67c02a884494d</data>
      <data key="d12">13994</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCITONINA" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles de calcitonina son utilizados para evaluar la presencia y el seguimiento del carcinoma medular de tiroides</data>
      <data key="d10">c4c0b3b2e4f4d6cad02aa1bbd92fd558</data>
      <data key="d11">feb3d3d8719645b6a4f746ab790049f0</data>
      <data key="d12">13995</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCITONINA" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles de calcitonina son utilizados como un marcador para evaluar la evoluci&#243;n del carcinoma medular de tiroides.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140</data>
      <data key="d11">2a5aec387e01403499d198b8248f1eba</data>
      <data key="d12">13996</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCITONINA" target="CMT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Calcitonina is used as a marker for monitoring medullary thyroid carcinoma (CMT) in patients with RET mutations.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">33e8999793034dff9557e2c74c133f9b</data>
      <data key="d12">13997</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CALCITONINA" target="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hormona paratiroidea y la calcitonina regulan los niveles de calcio en el cuerpo, actuando de manera opuesta en el hueso y el ri&#241;&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">dd8d59465dd2648ee8f73d8d2c95fe56</data>
      <data key="d11">374f5171ef804d9780435479e496f3e6</data>
      <data key="d12">13998</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOPARATIROIDISMO" target="DISECCI&#211;N CERVICAL">
