      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="CARCINOMA MEDULAR">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2A, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2A, is a genetic condition that significantly increases the risk of developing medullary carcinoma, particularly medullary thyroid carcinoma. This type of carcinoma is a common manifestation of MEN2A and is often diagnosed in patients who have this syndrome. Due to the heightened risk associated with MEN2A, individuals diagnosed with this condition require careful monitoring and appropriate treatment to manage the potential development of medullary carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d10">2c745fa0855caf0a3316554b5a46752c,8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140</data>
      <data key="d11">46bbdb4e209f47cbb846cf5b704f9d3c</data>
      <data key="d12">14019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="PROTOONCOG&#201;N RET">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las mutaciones en el protooncog&#233;n RET son responsables del desarrollo de MEN2A, que est&#225; asociado con carcinomas medulares.</data>
      <data key="d10">8ef1954ebfc3ede96038ff1db145e140</data>
      <data key="d11">390dcaf8810d4b2881d01757f807c46c</data>
      <data key="d12">14020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="CMT">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2A is associated with an increased risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma (CMT), necessitating monitoring and potential surgical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">c7ffb771b25b497b987fa617c6b15d37</data>
      <data key="d12">14021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="RET">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the RET proto-oncogene are responsible for the development of MEN2A, influencing the risk of associated tumors.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">ae732ffd71354a89a5c0cc3b91984f8c</data>
      <data key="d12">14022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="HYPERPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">MEN2A, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2A, is a genetic syndrome that is associated with several endocrine disorders, one of which is hyperparathyroidism. Hyperparathyroidism can occur in patients with MEN2A, making it essential for healthcare providers to monitor and manage this condition as part of the overall syndrome. Thus, hyperparathyroidism is recognized as one of the key conditions linked to MEN2A syndrome, highlighting the importance of comprehensive care for affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">2415ccd829f700cbe1975f4bca87245f,931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">52723a7141924b40aaa112a0a161bd01</data>
      <data key="d12">14023</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="FEO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pheochromocytoma (FEO) is one of the tumors associated with MEN2A, requiring surveillance and potential surgical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">703270b25eb940dfbe7d79c7501f2c99</data>
      <data key="d12">14024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="M918T">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">M918T is a mutation that significantly increases the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma in patients with MEN2A.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">7a4c622af969460d9f199ac34ae5c6ae</data>
      <data key="d12">14025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="E805K">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">E805K is a mutation that is part of the risk assessment for patients with MEN2A, influencing management decisions.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">211d1d58a9de4d36a586d270741eba75</data>
      <data key="d12">14026</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="Y806C">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Y806C is a mutation associated with MEN2A, affecting the clinical approach to monitoring and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">a334a2c232a7481fb22a2368c889da15</data>
      <data key="d12">14027</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="S904C">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">S904C is a mutation in the RET gene that is relevant for the risk stratification of patients with MEN2A.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">39f7623920e446538fefcda5751576fc</data>
      <data key="d12">14028</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="NIVELES DE RIESGO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Niveles de riesgo is a classification system used to stratify patients with MEN2A based on their RET mutations and associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">639e219028cc4e7388ca59b0062a127f</data>
      <data key="d12">14029</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEN2A" target="TIROIDECTOM&#205;A TOTAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tiroidectom&#237;a total is recommended for patients with MEN2A to prevent the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma based on their genetic risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">931560e7015f30adee5741819cdd0fab</data>
      <data key="d11">f5cd995d28954241b7ef5ed6715b106f</data>
      <data key="d12">14030</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
