    <edge source="NEFROLITIASIS" target="HYPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nefrolitiasis, commonly known as kidney stones, can be influenced by hyperuricemia, a condition characterized by elevated uric acid levels in the blood. High levels of uric acid can contribute to the formation of kidney stones, indicating a direct relationship between hyperuricemia and the development of nefrolitiasis.</data>
      <data key="d10">393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc,a0162312192878417ef2c4ef8f9cffba</data>
