      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="SOBREPESO GRADO II">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El sobrepeso grado II es una condici&#243;n que puede ser tratada con dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">166ecd6b0fa8498a95185863864b8517</data>
      <data key="d12">14420</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="APNEA DEL SUE&#209;O">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La apnea del sue&#241;o es una comorbilidad que se considera en el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">978a1d787c724045ad20ed4b299f360d</data>
      <data key="d12">14421</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="ENFERMEDADES CARD&#205;ACAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las enfermedades card&#237;acas son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">f3eddb118da74bf4af745bc367626718</data>
      <data key="d12">14422</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="TRASTORNOS PSIQUI&#193;TRICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los trastornos psiqui&#225;tricos son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">9b18b2e0e2ca483397bb151a3a885d67</data>
      <data key="d12">14423</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="ANOREXIA/BULIMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La anorexia y la bulimia son contraindicaciones para el uso de dietas VLCD</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">fadd2f6b5488433c9ac363e2be665263</data>
      <data key="d12">14424</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="PRODUCTOS COMERCIALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los productos comerciales son utilizados en las dietas VLCD para proporcionar nutrientes necesarios</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">a8817f3ea0804a3dac6cb7e0a4c4b4b6</data>
      <data key="d12">14425</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="MOTIVOS DE SALUD">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los motivos de salud pueden justificar la prescripci&#243;n de dietas VLCD para la p&#233;rdida de peso</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">f3ada865cbd54beca72d3195157525c5</data>
      <data key="d12">14426</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="PER&#205;ODOS SUPERIORES A 16 SEMANAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">No se recomienda el uso de dietas VLCD por per&#237;odos superiores a 16 semanas</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">4da98dc8219046d0b83f3f8f257b8b4d</data>
      <data key="d12">14427</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="DURACI&#211;N DE USO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La duraci&#243;n de uso de las dietas VLCD est&#225; regulada y no debe exceder 16 semanas</data>
      <data key="d10">3926ed628d3d5919b8a65e44fffbc3b9</data>
      <data key="d11">f50a4194fc104baaafd9ee69ccefa741</data>
      <data key="d12">14428</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="DIABETES TYPE 1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VLCD is not recommended for individuals with Diabetes Type 1 due to the risk of ketosis and hypoglycemia</data>
      <data key="d10">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6</data>
      <data key="d11">66bf37238ae041b29273db358432c7ef</data>
      <data key="d12">14429</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="GASTROINTESTINAL DISCOMFORT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The use of VLCD can lead to gastrointestinal discomfort, which includes symptoms like nausea and constipation</data>
      <data key="d10">032fc2148da74e586c8fd91e073c2be6</data>
      <data key="d11">15219568d4564fa281243bdb3567aece</data>
      <data key="d12">14430</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="CIRUG&#205;A BARI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VLCDs are recommended for patients before undergoing bariatric surgery to aid in weight loss</data>
      <data key="d10">64347a9be918a67f786cbdf9f9db9c8a</data>
      <data key="d11">3c7cb59b86fb4ae588657ffc9b201bf5</data>
      <data key="d12">14431</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VLCD" target="PACIENTE OBESO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Obese patients may follow VLCDs as part of their pre-surgery weight loss program</data>
      <data key="d10">64347a9be918a67f786cbdf9f9db9c8a</data>
      <data key="d11">d33c20d48fd149ff9d95fff7f4998a57</data>
      <data key="d12">14432</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEH-LELHA" target="FENILCETONURIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SEH-LELHA provides guidelines for managing phenylketonuria through dietary recommendations</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d11">f5a07eeab795467c9e347b4d074283e3</data>
      <data key="d12">14433</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEH-LELHA" target="UNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both organizations provide resources for nutritional information and dietary analysis, with USDA offering comprehensive databases and SEH-LELHA providing online tools for dietary calculations.</data>
      <data key="d10">91ec0cc70cd70254acbbebc425f84163</data>
      <data key="d11">1af0e44cb961497bbd299eb52a3f7e5e</data>
      <data key="d12">14434</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEH-LELHA" target="IENVA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both organizations provide access to nutritional information and tools for dietary analysis, enhancing public access to dietary resources.</data>
      <data key="d10">91ec0cc70cd70254acbbebc425f84163</data>
      <data key="d11">a0c6bd9e7c3943379e72eea66810a375</data>
      <data key="d12">14435</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEH-LELHA" target="DIETSTAT">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DIETSTAT and SEH-LELHA both provide tools for dietary analysis and nutritional assessment</data>
      <data key="d10">6da89a24c60015649c1d669e4e23fb2d</data>
      <data key="d11">2ee9f6b428244653a5327c97ca32ab42</data>
      <data key="d12">14436</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FENILCETONURIA, also known as phenylketonuria, is a metabolic disorder characterized by the inability to properly metabolize phenylalanine, an amino acid. TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA, or tetrahydrobiopterin, is utilized as a treatment option for this condition, particularly in cases of mild phenylketonuria. It aids in regulating the levels of phenylalanine in the body, thereby helping to manage the disorder effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d11">1ab5f175c2114419892f870dea0f92f4</data>
      <data key="d12">14437</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FENILALANINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Foods high in phenylalanine must be restricted in the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d11">bebe2a76375a4651b8ae052ed6404209</data>
      <data key="d12">14438</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota interacts with dietary fiber, which is relevant for managing phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d11">de7ea5f7d4dc4e26bc8f215c60252f10</data>
      <data key="d12">14439</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="HYPERPHENYLALANINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FENILCETONURIA, also known as phenylketonuria (PKU), is a specific condition that falls under the broader category of HYPERPHENYLALANINEMIA. Hyperphenylalaninemia encompasses various clinical phenotypes associated with phenylketonuria, indicating that it includes PKU as one of its manifestations. Thus, while phenylketonuria represents a particular disorder characterized by the inability to metabolize phenylalanine, hyperphenylalaninemia refers to a wider spectrum of conditions related to elevated levels of phenylalanine in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">88e3d76fef8b4c3da194f474707819fc</data>
      <data key="d12">14440</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="AMINO&#193;CIDOS EXENTOS DE FENILALANINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amino acids free of phenylalanine are used to supplement the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3</data>
      <data key="d11">b488bf271e06413f872c50dabf64591a</data>
      <data key="d12">14441</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="SAPROPTERINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sapropterin is indicated for the treatment of mild phenylketonuria, helping to manage phenylalanine levels in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d11">8f27d498ff9140559d00a40c9733cebb</data>
      <data key="d12">14442</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO P&#201;REZ">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Luis Miguel Luengo P&#233;rez is involved in the treatment and management of phenylketonuria as part of his clinical nutrition work</data>
      <data key="d10">0148b1abded087a7c25eda89c8014f38</data>
      <data key="d11">a22c1e31e2504edeafcbc2846f7940de</data>
      <data key="d12">14443</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="PAH">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Phenylketonuria is caused by a deficiency in the enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH)</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">a901fa272169460ca972e679f645abab</data>
      <data key="d12">14444</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="BH4">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4) is a cofactor necessary for the function of phenylalanine hydroxylase, thus linking it to phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">39305d653355441b89334bc0d7ab43c7</data>
      <data key="d12">14445</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="DHPR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dihydropteridine reductase (DHPR) is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine and is related to the treatment of phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">3e896bd078ba40229f9f75ed6c363a1b</data>
      <data key="d12">14446</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="PKU">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a specific type of hyperphenylalaninemia, indicating a direct relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">55a8bac680d544a0adca777b2349434d</data>
      <data key="d12">14447</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="HPA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperphenylalaninemia benign (HPA) is a milder form of phenylketonuria, showing a relationship between the two conditions</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">d8fa30c6ff8c4bd39086d05b05a2d67d</data>
      <data key="d12">14448</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="DIAGNOSTICO BIOQUIMICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Biochemical diagnosis is crucial for identifying phenylketonuria in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">b58f6fa51f9619cf6fde245bc7d36be5</data>
      <data key="d11">a23f4a61142a42368d2ec1e07814dfc5</data>
      <data key="d12">14449</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="L-TIROSINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">L-tirosina may be necessary to supplement the diet of individuals with phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">b3118ec88eef403482ade4f373a754c7</data>
      <data key="d12">14450</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="ALIMENTOS RESTRINGIDOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with phenylketonuria must restrict foods high in phenylalanine</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">bc77da6c495b461aaaf05572a67aa0d5</data>
      <data key="d12">14451</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="ALIMENTOS LIBRES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with phenylketonuria can consume foods that are low in phenylalanine freely</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">e13983cba468467aad645a99b0b3c9b6</data>
      <data key="d12">14452</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="TABLA 3">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tabla 3 provides information on phenylalanine content in foods, which is crucial for managing phenylketonuria</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">c22bbfa088274e1fba9a84e955392d1c</data>
      <data key="d12">14453</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="CARNE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with phenylketonuria must restrict the consumption of meat due to its high phenylalanine content</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">7cdd9d79a90f485ebb731d2e68d1134b</data>
      <data key="d12">14454</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="PESCADO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with phenylketonuria must avoid fish and seafood due to their high phenylalanine levels</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">67441a3fda6548d281619547d916a35f</data>
      <data key="d12">14455</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="QUESOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with phenylketonuria need to limit cheese intake due to varying levels of phenylalanine</data>
      <data key="d10">5f1b707b42d6235a666179f880d1d98a</data>
      <data key="d11">1ba44805cb954daf9349e77136a52526</data>
      <data key="d12">14456</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FENILCETONURIA" target="GLUCOGENOSIS">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both glucogenosis and phenylketonuria are metabolic disorders that involve enzyme deficiencies leading to toxic accumulations in the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">76287e9b94faab94755c56fead3541d7</data>
      <data key="d11">558da45ff031419590cbb40936b28257</data>
      <data key="d12">14457</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="ACIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota plays a crucial role in the fermentation of dietary fiber, leading to the production of short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs). These SCFAs significantly influence energy metabolism and inflammation within the body. Through this fermentation process, the intestinal microbiota not only contributes to the generation of SCFAs but also impacts overall health by modulating metabolic and inflammatory responses.</data>
      <data key="d10">5896bac781a5373225377824d7901ce3,9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">0d01fd4095b14a26afbdf17db78f7088</data>
      <data key="d12">14458</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="DIETA HIPERPROTEICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las dietas hiperproteicas pueden alterar la microbiota intestinal, lo que puede tener efectos negativos en la salud.</data>
      <data key="d10">0fba67c4e6cffbde6f31d895bedc4bf7</data>
      <data key="d11">31db4e096edd4e4394fb9debd491a479</data>
      <data key="d12">14459</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La microbiota intestinal reside en el tracto gastrointestinal y es esencial para la digesti&#243;n y la salud del hu&#233;sped.</data>
      <data key="d10">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d11">d2202691eb5045a09f7ec20436e74cb8</data>
      <data key="d12">14460</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="INTESTINO GRUESO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El intestino grueso alberga la mayor parte de la microbiota intestinal, que juega un papel crucial en la fermentaci&#243;n y absorci&#243;n de nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d11">5e6ae7c232a54535a2977850d6a8428a</data>
      <data key="d12">14461</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="ELDERMET">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ELDERMET studies the characteristics of the intestinal microbiota in the elderly, highlighting differences from younger adults</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">0a29d4b798b64147add6cb9ab41a334f</data>
      <data key="d12">14462</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="FILO: FIRMICUTES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Filo: Firmicutes includes various bacteria that are part of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">5e21c1f3f8b94ad0a82c3f6e61d3ba6d</data>
      <data key="d12">14463</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="FILO: BACTEROIDETES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Filo: Bacteroidetes includes important bacteria that contribute to the composition of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">12a2f171866448258b971de25352dfcf</data>
      <data key="d12">14464</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="BACTEROIDES">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota, particularly in children, exhibits significant variations based on dietary habits, with the genus Bacteroides playing a crucial role. Bacteroides is a prominent genus within the Bacteroidetes phylum and is commonly found in the intestinal microbiota. Notably, studies indicate that the intestinal microbiota of African children shows an increase in Bacteroides compared to their European counterparts, highlighting the influence of diet on microbial composition.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314,b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">f0368292feee476da3b0eef8b2c13b91</data>
      <data key="d12">14465</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="LACTOBACILLUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactobacillus is a significant genus in the intestinal microbiota, contributing to gut health</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">6d6053491a50409a933af83d1428f4e4</data>
      <data key="d12">14466</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="STREPTOCOCCUS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Streptococcus is a prevalent genus in the intestinal microbiota, impacting human health</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">43b3d76eb9274c328d352b60850f8034</data>
      <data key="d12">14467</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="CLOSTRIDIUM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Clostridium is a genus that plays a role in the intestinal microbiota and can affect gut health</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">4658823063e3454eabd57841b2b89ce0</data>
      <data key="d12">14468</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="ENTEROBACTERIACEAE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enterobacteriaceae is a family of bacteria that is part of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">40da55735aaa48739b5e115ac07a1be6</data>
      <data key="d12">14469</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="ENTEROCOCCUS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Enterococcus is a genus that contributes to the composition of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">51acb6d692904f25b0742049506e33b2</data>
      <data key="d12">14470</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="VEILLONELLA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Veillonella is a genus that is part of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">e8bb1c242a024901a8fb03e91a3b9674</data>
      <data key="d12">14471</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="EUBACTERIUM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Eubacterium is a genus that plays a role in maintaining gut health within the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">225c25abf0564404a45da45544b89465</data>
      <data key="d12">14472</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="FUSOBACTERIUM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fusobacterium can be part of the intestinal microbiota and is associated with certain health conditions</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">c4a3798ccaa943aba38e6e2874380c73</data>
      <data key="d12">14473</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="PEPTOSTREPTOCOCCUS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Peptostreptococcus is a genus that contributes to the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">e0ecebf6b1774caf990e01114f666438</data>
      <data key="d12">14474</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="RUMINOCOCCUS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ruminococcus is a genus that plays a role in the fermentation processes in the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">cefe28027c4a4724913c7c1797de2551</data>
      <data key="d12">14475</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="BIFIDOBACTERIUM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bifidobacterium is a beneficial genus in the intestinal microbiota, often found in probiotics</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">347f10ba6dc54cc184a2532247e26e11</data>
      <data key="d12">14476</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="PROTEOBACTERIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Proteobacteria includes various bacteria that can influence the composition of the intestinal microbiota</data>
      <data key="d10">b36b8846f109ee75806c6ea03015e5d5</data>
      <data key="d11">15be92d0d3b94ae1b4627548637fc19e</data>
      <data key="d12">14477</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="NI&#209;OS AFRICANOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los ni&#241;os africanos presentan una microbiota intestinal rica en Bacteroidetes, lo que refleja su dieta alta en fibra vegetal.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">4d2735975a114cca9e0ab2d0b6737065</data>
      <data key="d12">14478</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="NI&#209;OS EUROPEOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los ni&#241;os europeos tienen una microbiota intestinal caracterizada por una mayor proporci&#243;n de Firmicutes, asociada a su dieta alta en grasas y prote&#237;nas animales.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">3c8d5d1a66684d4584e0db961936bba8</data>
      <data key="d12">14479</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="FIRMICUTES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La microbiota intestinal de los ni&#241;os europeos muestra un aumento en Firmicutes en comparaci&#243;n con los ni&#241;os africanos, reflejando diferencias diet&#233;ticas.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">58cac4f47e6843c9beb86598025a41fd</data>
      <data key="d12">14480</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="DIETA ALTA EN GRASAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta alta en grasas est&#225; asociada con un aumento en Firmicutes y una disminuci&#243;n en Bacteroidetes en la microbiota intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">705d41e25b4c45619276c1ec77c246fc</data>
      <data key="d12">14481</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="DIETA ALTA EN FIBRA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dieta alta en fibra est&#225; asociada con un aumento en Bacteroidetes y una disminuci&#243;n en Firmicutes en la microbiota intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">220ba54277164eeebca9eb1927df2045</data>
      <data key="d12">14482</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="PATRONES DIET&#201;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los patrones diet&#233;ticos influyen en la composici&#243;n de la microbiota intestinal, mostrando diferencias entre grupos con h&#225;bitos diet&#233;ticos diferentes.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">9064d0e0496b46caa8c58f223eb98515</data>
      <data key="d12">14483</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES OCCIDENTALES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La microbiota de comunidades occidentales muestra una composici&#243;n diferente en comparaci&#243;n con la de comunidades orientales, influenciada por la dieta.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">aae94fde6410438daf42e6a4519f4cb7</data>
      <data key="d12">14484</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES ORIENTALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La microbiota de comunidades orientales muestra una composici&#243;n diferente en comparaci&#243;n con la de comunidades occidentales, influenciada por la dieta.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">4bb4814c1d9f49d2a7c3724502621308</data>
      <data key="d12">14485</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="TEJIDO ADIPOSO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota influences the function and metabolism of adipose tissue, affecting energy homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">0facfe73de564cb68152b10d41a8cd10</data>
      <data key="d12">14486</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="FIAF">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota can decrease FIAF production, affecting lipoprotein lipase activity and fat storage.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">9754b9cef1734c58b49471d56224bbea</data>
      <data key="d12">14487</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="BUTIRATO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Butyrate is produced by the fermentation of dietary fiber by the intestinal microbiota, influencing energy metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">49f5e77aee9d402aac075135d6a0e2fe</data>
      <data key="d12">14488</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="SEROTONINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Serotonin levels can be influenced by the gut microbiota, affecting intestinal permeability and satiety.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">4a338a5898d54835bfee1c070bcb4569</data>
      <data key="d12">14489</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="ACIDOS BILIARES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The gut microbiota transforms primary bile acids into secondary bile acids, impacting metabolism and energy expenditure.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">20ac8100fe8d4119b1244444d67446e8</data>
      <data key="d12">14490</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="RECEPTOR TOLL-LIKE 4">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TLR4 is activated by lipopolysaccharides from the microbiota, leading to inflammatory responses that can affect metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">19de7163986b4771998c6e6cab4158d8</data>
      <data key="d12">14491</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="PROBIOTICOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Probiotics can modulate the composition of the gut microbiota, enhancing butyrate production and influencing metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d10">9538d3f95062fd16213d9c718bb42872</data>
      <data key="d11">006086ea2ed74190b37186332de77eb8</data>
      <data key="d12">14492</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="POLISAC&#193;RIDOS INDIGERIBLES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota is essential for the digestion of indigestible polysaccharides, converting them into energy, indicating a strong relationship.</data>
      <data key="d10">ffdc08ec09899ab7dfa255af4cecac1c</data>
      <data key="d11">46c84ac2655d40e4aa8e414a9648ba31</data>
      <data key="d12">14493</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL" target="SISTEMA INMUNE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The intestinal microbiota plays a crucial role in the development and maintenance of the immune system</data>
      <data key="d10">235520bdfb411a2997762c99ac421bf3</data>
      <data key="d11">a8cc289f1307410696d565c13e0cab6d</data>
      <data key="d12">14494</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N EN CROHN'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional management is crucial for patients experiencing intestinal failure, particularly those with Crohn's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">f7d56bac9cc29e47690669e812094c99</data>
      <data key="d11">4f9330a85bef40f4a7d33bf0d2ea1558</data>
      <data key="d12">14495</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="FEC">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La falla intestinal cr&#243;nica es una complicaci&#243;n del fallo intestinal que puede requerir nutrici&#243;n parenteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">a2c6ccdc966e72b4675d71b4c072e1dc</data>
      <data key="d11">4fc0718083704dcc8400bb4950df76e3</data>
      <data key="d12">14496</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="LIQUIDOS HIPERTONICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertonic liquids can exacerbate the condition of intestinal failure by increasing digestive losses</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">8c44cf6a541d4e2882904216431b6646</data>
      <data key="d12">14497</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="LIQUIDOS HIPOTONICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypotonic liquids can also worsen the condition of intestinal failure by increasing digestive losses</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">e9ae8f33088246a0b15fac475f791e62</data>
      <data key="d12">14498</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="DIETA BAJA EN LACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A low-lactose diet is recommended for patients with intestinal failure to help manage symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">9ea2656604c7467098a5b05e0bae83f7</data>
      <data key="d12">14499</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="POIC">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La POIC puede llevar a un fallo intestinal debido a la reducci&#243;n de la funci&#243;n intestinal y la necesidad de soporte nutricional.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d11">abdf3bc48ac240f7994d297d8d0d9415</data>
      <data key="d12">14500</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="TRASPLANTE INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El trasplante intestinal es una opci&#243;n de tratamiento en casos severos de fallo intestinal que amenazan la vida.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d11">ac575c270fdc49ab97381953d67a7a71</data>
      <data key="d12">14501</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL" target="HIPOMOTILIDAD INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipomotilidad intestinal es una de las causas del fallo intestinal, afectando la absorci&#243;n de nutrientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">0cdbb308e3359fd3ddbb1d828d12dc04</data>
      <data key="d11">fac8f58b66e9472d94ff54cd8a9fc1b5</data>
      <data key="d12">14502</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OSTEOMALACIA" target="FOSFATASA ALCALINA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated alkaline phosphatase levels are often associated with osteomalacia</data>
      <data key="d10">6aa8928e063b4107007dc14cc1b301bd</data>
      <data key="d11">f0b057dbdd7c49cebfe03c0b84407d75</data>
      <data key="d12">14503</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OSTEOMALACIA" target="RAQUITISMO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both raquitismo and osteomalacia are conditions related to poor mineralization of bones</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">d7b302358ab34c43b169fccc462ee1c5</data>
      <data key="d12">14504</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
