    <edge source="ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA" target="GEN X-ALD">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleucodystrophy (ALD) is a genetic disorder caused by mutations in the X-ALD gene. This gene plays a crucial role in fatty acid metabolism, and its dysfunction directly leads to the development of the disease. The relationship between adrenoleucodystrophy and the X-ALD gene is therefore established, highlighting the importance of this gene in the pathology of ALD.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ac394c08f6c4bdfbee5440e56a97dd0,4eb5a5cd6147917dd1380d49c613a78b</data>
      <data key="d11">610178c70b1b44ef985872e40c426130</data>
      <data key="d12">14527</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA" target="MNGIE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleucodistrofia must be differentiated from MNGIE</data>
      <data key="d10">b8db8cc3349b8ac0cce45497da6244fc</data>
      <data key="d11">e31ef5b9fd6e40959a98180ff471ffe0</data>
      <data key="d12">14528</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
