      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA" target="KASPER DL">
      <data key="d8">31.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kasper DL is a prominent editor of "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine," a comprehensive medical textbook that serves as a key resource in the field of internal medicine. The book includes extensive information on various medical conditions, including congenital adrenal hyperplasia. As one of the editors, Kasper DL has significantly contributed to the content and overall quality of this essential medical reference.</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,28bca03cd2152cf2562d7aa16d7ced1d,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf</data>
      <data key="d11">7c682267469f480e9c5b7cb4669b3994</data>
      <data key="d12">14591</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA" target="HAUSER SL">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine is a comprehensive medical textbook that serves as a key resource in the field of internal medicine. Hauser SL is one of the editors of this influential work, contributing significantly to its content. The book includes various topics, such as congenital adrenal hyperplasia, which is specifically mentioned in the descriptions related to Hauser SL's contributions. Through his editorial role, Hauser SL has played a vital part in shaping the information presented in Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine, ensuring it remains a valuable reference for medical professionals.</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf</data>
      <data key="d11">b981cf3980fd43ac916577e197b0d3c9</data>
      <data key="d12">14592</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HARRISON PRINCIPIOS DE MEDICINA INTERNA" target="JAMESON JL">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine is a comprehensive medical textbook that includes contributions from various authors and editors, including Jameson JL. Jameson JL is recognized as one of the editors of this influential work, playing a significant role in shaping its content. The book covers a wide range of medical topics, including congenital adrenal hyperplasia, which is specifically mentioned in the context of its content. Through his editorial contributions, Jameson JL has helped ensure that Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine remains a vital resource for medical professionals and students alike.</data>
      <data key="d10">1400aceda067bb7180ca90f0a5335bfe,8fe4d0101ea7a6ddaefd71c963d9ecc7,b7b162b783ea688c5fe9b7f531b46aaf</data>
