    </edge>
    <edge source="PARAGANGLIOMA" target="SUCCINATE DEHYDROGENASE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the succinate dehydrogenase genes are also linked to the development of paraganglioma</data>
      <data key="d10">973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9</data>
      <data key="d11">3e33a70f304f44a2a88775a770b4cf28</data>
      <data key="d12">14709</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PARAGANGLIOMA" target="VHL GENE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The VHL gene is also associated with the development of paraganglioma in patients with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">973f9100fbfeb9ef31038f51312620a9</data>
      <data key="d11">6c1ea1a6342945769a00dd1a4c777cf2</data>
      <data key="d12">14710</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PARAGANGLIOMA" target="SUPRARRENAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Paragangliomas can also be associated with the adrenal glands, similar to feocromocitomas</data>
      <data key="d10">94ef3a3488643695a99523d5c9d1f606</data>
      <data key="d11">0583ed95570b4b09a213433552c667b7</data>
      <data key="d12">14711</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PARAGANGLIOMA" target="GEN VHL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Paraganglioma can also be associated with mutations in the VHL gene, highlighting its role in tumorigenesis</data>
      <data key="d10">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d11">bc0b328ae79e418ea38f519977c6da2f</data>
      <data key="d12">14712</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SDHB" target="VHL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the VHL gene can lead to the development of tumors associated with the SDHB gene in hereditary pheochromocytomas</data>
      <data key="d10">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d11">3655031f50f94cf69b97a7b6eab751d1</data>
