    <edge source="VHL" target="NF1">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The NF1 gene is associated with neurofibromatosis type 1, which can also lead to pheochromocytomas, similar to the conditions seen in Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d11">54611184c27c443e860af61c8c99ed98</data>
      <data key="d12">14769</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VHL" target="MAX">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MAX gene is involved in the regulation of cell growth and is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas, which can occur in patients with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d11">e4174d63b91745b3b3bb5ee0b4ac0bc3</data>
      <data key="d12">14770</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VHL" target="TMEM127">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The TMEM127 gene is associated with hereditary pheochromocytomas, which can be present in patients with Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">c3d752ff301355241e1420e398f0e6a4</data>
      <data key="d11">bba17a2d6d3b4467bf0de279d66af05f</data>
      <data key="d12">14771</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANFETAMINAS" target="G&#211;MEZ ENTERR&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">G&#243;mez Enterr&#237;a provides information about the effects of Anfetaminas on the central nervous system</data>
      <data key="d10">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e</data>
      <data key="d11">c14c64f937e24dd5b05b5eb063540b34</data>
      <data key="d12">14772</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANFETAMINAS" target="G&#211;ME(&quot;ENTITY&quot;">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d10">04f886244ff7d736eb270f175d6b120e</data>
      <data key="d11">cf93ff903e7443dbb7b6f500c12fa7c8</data>
      <data key="d12">14773</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RET" target="FEOCHROMOCITOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the RET proto-oncogene are linked to the occurrence of pheochromocytoma</data>
      <data key="d10">92d73407a11da797ae160c4ac13a6efe</data>
      <data key="d11">5aecc4dfa07f43c0a447ec727c65abc3</data>
      <data key="d12">14774</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MART&#205;N L&#211;PEZ DE LA TORRE CASARES" target="UNIVERSIDAD DE BOLONIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mart&#237;n L&#243;pez de la Torre Casares obtained his Doctorate in Medicine from the University of Bologna</data>
      <data key="d10">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d11">25dcd021ca4c46b2940c114b359943ef</data>
      <data key="d12">14775</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MART&#205;N L&#211;PEZ DE LA TORRE CASARES" target="UNIVERSIDAD INTERNACIONAL MEN&#201;NDEZ PELAYO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mart&#237;n L&#243;pez de la Torre Casares completed his Master's in Clinical Management of Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Universidad Internacional Men&#233;ndez Pelayo</data>
      <data key="d10">0ec21b45b9a154289761f46105b364f2</data>
      <data key="d11">18d0832a72d44d88b91ca4396ed0ff95</data>
      <data key="d12">14776</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL" target="AN&#193;LOGOS DE LA GNRH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los an&#225;logos de la GnRH son el tratamiento de elecci&#243;n para estabilizar la progresi&#243;n de la pubertad precoz central</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">012a1a1774dc403aa8a063188363a2f8</data>
      <data key="d12">14777</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL" target="EJE HIPOT&#193;LAMO-HIP&#211;FISO-GONADAL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La pubertad precoz central implica la activaci&#243;n temprana del eje hipot&#225;lamo-hip&#243;fiso-gonadal</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">5bd4f98ad41d4d25992fda777050c6e5</data>
      <data key="d12">14778</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PUBERTAD PRECOZ CENTRAL" target="EDAD &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La edad &#243;sea se eval&#250;a para determinar si un ni&#241;o presenta pubertad precoz central, ya que suele ser mayor que la edad cronol&#243;gica</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">f4d5756b34cc49d9b3bddcb5f755bcb4</data>
      <data key="d12">14779</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AN&#193;LOGOS DE LA GNRH" target="TRIPTORELINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La triptorelina es un tipo de an&#225;logo de la GnRH utilizado para tratar la pubertad precoz central</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">bb4ec689683c431d89d4a3429ac2d289</data>
      <data key="d12">14780</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AN&#193;LOGOS DE LA GNRH" target="LEURPORELINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La leurporelina es un tipo de an&#225;logo de la GnRH utilizado para tratar la pubertad precoz central</data>
      <data key="d10">5359b474e1b8ddab593222dd705128df</data>
      <data key="d11">18d06054187b4b6eb295c56ffff729b4</data>
      <data key="d12">14781</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GONADOTROFINAS" target="C&#201;LULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las gonadotrofinas, como la LH, estimulan las c&#233;lulas de Leydig para producir testosterona</data>
      <data key="d10">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99</data>
      <data key="d11">4a252e03ba4146ef8ef35fa413e4596f</data>
      <data key="d12">14782</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GONADOTROFINAS" target="C&#201;LULAS DE SERTOLI">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las gonadotrofinas, como la FSH, estimulan las c&#233;lulas de Sertoli para la producci&#243;n de esperma</data>
      <data key="d10">4accb4afaddfdc671690221252ff1b99</data>
      <data key="d11">0414a55f198747b5ba7381923f717cf5</data>
      <data key="d12">14783</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TESTOTOCICOSIS" target="CELULAS DE LEYDIG">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las c&#233;lulas de Leydig son responsables de la producci&#243;n de testosterona, que est&#225; aumentada en casos de testotoxicosis</data>
      <data key="d10">1436fed20a28649406ac34dcfb553734</data>
      <data key="d11">b4f429c1b6474d05af7aa4a28f180446</data>
      <data key="d12">14784</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RNM CEREBRAL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE KALLMAN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La RNM cerebral puede mostrar la ausencia del bulbo olfatorio, un hallazgo en el s&#237;ndrome de Kallman</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">620dfb81cd244002a8bfba56c1a09220</data>
      <data key="d12">14785</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="17-OH-PROGESTERONA" target="AMENORREA PRIMARIA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">17-OH-Progesterone levels can help diagnose conditions related to primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">e006462e08ed49b38d3e4fcbd1c32ce1</data>
      <data key="d12">14786</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT SYNDROME" target="FIBROUS DYSPLASIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fibrous dysplasia is a characteristic feature of McCune-Albright syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">b3316095dd6a408a95a5f1b1b06d9e4f</data>
      <data key="d12">14787</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT SYNDROME" target="PRECOCIOUS PUBERTY">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Precocious puberty is a common manifestation of McCune-Albright syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">fb2a4dc54f6844d980f7c88425d3c2cf</data>
      <data key="d12">14788</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENARQUIA" target="HYPERANDROGENISM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenarche can lead to hyperandrogenism, which may cause early signs of puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">a23011de98224e78b7dcc9e3e0854be5</data>
      <data key="d12">14789</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="CLITOROMEGALY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperandrogenism can result in clitoromegaly as a sign of virilization</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">7a4f3874e25046b9b5330a8c26377899</data>
      <data key="d12">14790</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="FERRIMAN-GALLWEY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Ferriman-Gallwey scale is used to evaluate hyperandrogenism in women, indicating a direct relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">bb07d662fd7a4de494d77f73e61634c2</data>
      <data key="d12">14791</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="OVARIES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ovaries can be a source of androgens, contributing to hyperandrogenism in women</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">7455d5db1127426da12312836676f44d</data>
      <data key="d12">14792</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="MENARCHE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The onset of menarche can be associated with the development of hyperandrogenism, particularly if symptoms appear shortly after</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">05c55ace286b46f1ae5170c71eb8e8e8</data>
      <data key="d12">14793</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="HIRSUTISM">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hirsutism is a clinical manifestation of hyperandrogenism, indicating a strong relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">66edac90eb19476b9900cd3140222fca</data>
      <data key="d12">14794</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="VIRILIZATION">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Virilization is a severe form of hyperandrogenism, showing a direct link between elevated androgen levels and the development of male characteristics</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">c44977b9f53844d9b979c41ea935629c</data>
      <data key="d12">14795</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="ANDROGENS">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperandrogenism is a condition characterized by elevated levels of androgens, which are male hormones that are present in both men and women. The primary cause of hyperandrogenism is these elevated androgen levels, establishing a foundational relationship between the two entities. This direct relationship indicates that hyperandrogenism is fundamentally defined by the presence of increased androgens in the body.</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1,dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d11">b8558084926d41f19ed707a9ef5e2d2e</data>
      <data key="d12">14796</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="FAMILY HISTORY">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A family history of conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia can indicate a genetic predisposition to hyperandrogenism</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">f68fef606ebb4b6e931cdbc56852f45b</data>
      <data key="d12">14797</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="TESTOSTERONE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Testosterone levels are often evaluated to diagnose hyperandrogenism, which is a key factor in conditions like Polycystic Ovary Syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d10">70bc9625e649f5e478fdef15e27dda58</data>
      <data key="d11">96c70ef59fd24397bc323959dd6b32f9</data>
      <data key="d12">14798</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERANDROGENISM" target="POLYCYSTIC OVARY SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome is often associated with hyperandrogenism, as it is a common hormonal imbalance in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">dda58e50ce4bb9fa40e3c61e40e1b9c7</data>
      <data key="d11">78ac3b9a3361495a9e6c4fdabc394ea3</data>
      <data key="d12">14799</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PRECOCIOUS PUBERTY" target="FEMALE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Females are more commonly affected by precocious puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">bd40327c00434b539b6cba957e34fdcc</data>
      <data key="d12">14800</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PRECOCIOUS PUBERTY" target="MALE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Males can also experience precocious puberty, though it is less common than in females</data>
      <data key="d10">4c65e91aa4dbec2d2ad859d07fbcb2cd</data>
      <data key="d11">0125af524f0a4ddf9dd289ae09892843</data>
      <data key="d12">14801</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMENORREA PRIMARIA" target="HAMARTOMA HIPOTAL&#193;MICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypothalamic hamartoma can lead to hormonal disruptions that result in primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">314e4c44c1d54f1bb3bd13b09a91eddf</data>
      <data key="d12">14802</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMENORREA PRIMARIA" target="ESTRADIOL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Estradiol levels are important indicators in diagnosing the causes of primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">e5d952f41bd34babbc361dcd376f7e83</data>
      <data key="d12">14803</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMENORREA PRIMARIA" target="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism can lead to primary amenorrhea due to insufficient hormone production</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">561189c84a24405899f15df770104949</data>
      <data key="d12">14804</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMENORREA PRIMARIA" target="RETRASO CONSTITUCIONAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Constitutional delay can be a reason for primary amenorrhea, as it affects the timing of puberty</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">febcf9905e5a4fcd9aea58259af7a1b4</data>
      <data key="d12">14805</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AMENORREA PRIMARIA" target="CARIOTIPO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Karyotyping can identify chromosomal abnormalities that may cause primary amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d10">31ce1e681d5daab6e4f4071ed09a0266</data>
      <data key="d11">a258b703d136400b9455df8fe2c6bade</data>
      <data key="d12">14806</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESTRADIOL" target="AROMATASE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Estradiol levels are regulated by aromatase, and deficiency can lead to low estradiol levels in affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">9403e1facb0d4be7a026ed26e4120805</data>
      <data key="d12">14807</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ESTRADIOL" target="PROGESTERONE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Estradiol and progesterone work together to regulate the menstrual cycle and prepare the uterus for pregnancy</data>
      <data key="d10">d4fb31e0ff471ed415f98bc11ca26d1d</data>
      <data key="d11">a83447dcfd0e4ca9addfdf704125a12d</data>
      <data key="d12">14808</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="S&#205;NDROME DE KLINEFELTER">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Klinefelter es una de las causas m&#225;s comunes de hipogonadismo primario en varones, lo que implica una relaci&#243;n directa entre ambas condiciones.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">eea1beb996874103940a1adbba761722</data>
      <data key="d12">14809</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="S&#205;NDROME DE MAESTRE DE SAN JUAN-KALLMAN">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo puede estar asociado con el s&#237;ndrome de Maestre de San Juan-Kallman, que incluye defectos olfativos y problemas hormonales.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">40bf5e0f18984007974cc8ca47267b0b</data>
      <data key="d12">14810</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="INHIBINA B">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los niveles de inhibina B se encuentran disminuidos en el hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, lo que ayuda en su diagn&#243;stico.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">c50024a2fb804eaabd6b565d45d6aa6d</data>
      <data key="d12">14811</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="HORMONA ANTIM&#220;LLERIANA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hormona antim&#252;lleriana se utiliza en el diagn&#243;stico diferencial del hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, ya que sus niveles son diferentes en esta condici&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">5766f69854dc45a6a02450abcfaf1ff4</data>
      <data key="d12">14812</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="RETARDO CONSTITUCIONAL DEL CRECIMIENTO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Es importante diferenciar el hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo del retraso constitucional del crecimiento para un pron&#243;stico adecuado y tratamiento.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">3345ec26861547218e38003d00d6795a</data>
      <data key="d12">14813</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="PALADAR HENDIDO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El paladar hendido puede ser un problema fenot&#237;pico asociado a pacientes con hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">f62e5444fb274a92a0e9aa101ebde633</data>
      <data key="d12">14814</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGONADISMO HIPOGONADOTROPO" target="SORDERA NEUROL&#211;GICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La sordera neurol&#243;gica puede aparecer en pacientes con hipogonadismo hipogonadotropo, indicando una relaci&#243;n entre ambas condiciones.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">468de4dcec6d4877b4ceffd2b9cc32e9</data>
      <data key="d12">14815</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE KALLMAN" target="ANOSMIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La anosmia es un s&#237;ntoma caracter&#237;stico del s&#237;ndrome de Kallman, que afecta la percepci&#243;n del olfato</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">8b4df620f940491e8a9637a283b458dc</data>
      <data key="d12">14816</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE KALLMAN" target="RETARDO PUBERAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Kallman puede causar retraso puberal debido a la falta de hormonas sexuales</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">69b61f78070c4e26bafc9c6e2f3b8f66</data>
      <data key="d12">14817</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE KLINEFELTER" target="RETARDO PUBERAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Klinefelter puede causar retraso puberal debido a la disfunci&#243;n testicular</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">5d436c9069824d7d95f62ad299ceb86c</data>
      <data key="d12">14818</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE KLINEFELTER" target="GEN SRY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The SRY gene is involved in male sexual differentiation, and its abnormalities can lead to Klinefelter syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">0cf04c95a8e6bbdf9201bf3fff9103f6</data>
      <data key="d11">a6916dd6c7414289af37eb2665b0c91f</data>
      <data key="d12">14819</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CRIPTORQUIDIA" target="ORQUIDOPEXIA">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CRIPTORQUIDIA, commonly known as cryptorchidism, is a condition that often necessitates surgical intervention. The standard treatment for this condition is ORQUIDOPEXIA, which is a surgical procedure aimed at correcting the position of undescended testicles. The primary goal of orquidopexia is to place the undescended testicle into the scrotum, thereby addressing the complications associated with cryptorchidism.</data>
      <data key="d10">1776df2694e83680f59e035be5ffb00b,b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621,df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">cf05716c113f4aafb64df1ebd56574f0</data>
      <data key="d12">14820</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RETARDO PUBERAL" target="DISGENESIA GONADAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La disgenesia gonadal puede resultar en retraso puberal y amenorrea primaria debido a la falta de desarrollo adecuado de los ovarios</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">d18214f7aa8c4068824b33b419be9dfc</data>
      <data key="d12">14821</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RETARDO PUBERAL" target="ANOMAL&#205;AS M&#220;LLERIANAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las anomal&#237;as m&#252;llerianas pueden causar retraso en el desarrollo puberal y amenorrea primaria</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">4ae6af88ff60452793f3ea7099ae7652</data>
      <data key="d12">14822</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RETARDO PUBERAL" target="P&#201;RDIDA DE PESO/ANOREXIA NERVIOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La p&#233;rdida de peso o anorexia nerviosa puede causar retraso puberal y amenorrea primaria</data>
      <data key="d10">b972e75c5d62cc5cd76d9fc308265621</data>
      <data key="d11">d93dc530c9e3472ba671fd80b3663e67</data>
      <data key="d12">14823</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE MAESTRE DE SAN JUAN-KALLMAN" target="RNM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La RNM se utiliza para confirmar el diagn&#243;stico del s&#237;ndrome de Maestre de San Juan-Kallman al mostrar alteraciones en el desarrollo del bulbo olfatorio.</data>
      <data key="d10">df1d5ee8cb182840589e630b67691942</data>
      <data key="d11">627ec11a79384fff9981bbb26d2c26f2</data>
      <data key="d12">14824</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="ADDISON'S DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with Klinefelter syndrome are predisposed to autoimmune disorders, including Addison's disease</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">ca9e4938ded04d7cbd45bf4a2cc25fd8</data>
      <data key="d12">14825</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="TROMBOEMBOLISM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Klinefelter syndrome is associated with an increased risk of thromboembolic events due to thrombophilia</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">3dd62b9358ba48a2ad4b53b7738ab5d4</data>
      <data key="d12">14826</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="CANCER OF THE BREAST">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Klinefelter syndrome have a higher risk of developing breast cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">ad1af178bce74677b4c9a5a292b8e05e</data>
      <data key="d12">14827</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="CANCER OF THE PROSTATE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Klinefelter syndrome have a higher risk of developing prostate cancer</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">200dfc96ffdd4e2bb1d7674a198856d7</data>
      <data key="d12">14828</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="BRONCHITIS CHRONIC">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Klinefelter syndrome are at increased risk for chronic bronchitis</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">7ec6f437e0684cb2851f80e2b94ea012</data>
      <data key="d12">14829</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="BRONCHIECTASIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with Klinefelter syndrome may be predisposed to bronchiectasis</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">eb62cced4188450aadc97cdfdc030489</data>
      <data key="d12">14830</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="METABOLIC SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with Klinefelter syndrome often exhibit features of metabolic syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">ae982d15084c4277ac36f80c1400b467</data>
      <data key="d12">14831</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="DYSPLIPIDEMIA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Dyslipidemia is often observed in patients with Klinefelter syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">5509bb6959e4faa5989289c1ddbcc96b</data>
      <data key="d11">c33aa86eb11b421997a4e1dd91908de6</data>
      <data key="d12">14832</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KLINEFELTER SYNDROME" target="TURNER SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Klinefelter Syndrome and Turner Syndrome are both chromosomal disorders that impact sexual development. These genetic disorders are characterized by abnormalities in the sex chromosomes, leading to various developmental and reproductive challenges.</data>
      <data key="d10">766fec9f74738cf0af53aee77d58dc78,bc241ef500af250c0f0e0253bf5ae0f2</data>
      <data key="d11">0ab3eb88f33f43579b21742f16e358f6</data>
      <data key="d12">14833</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="CHRONIC OBSTRUCTIVE PULMONARY DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bronchiectasis can be a complication of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, leading to increased morbidity</data>
      <data key="d10">cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
      <data key="d11">07e280de3e8044a4bdb95cce51f041e0</data>
      <data key="d12">14834</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="CYSTIC FIBROSIS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bronchiectasis is a condition that can arise as a complication of cystic fibrosis, significantly impacting lung function. It is commonly observed in patients with cystic fibrosis, primarily due to the chronic lung infections that characterize this genetic disorder. The relationship between bronchiectasis and cystic fibrosis highlights the challenges faced by individuals with cystic fibrosis in maintaining respiratory health.</data>
      <data key="d10">4eb41f33f9aba3b8ecd3906de91a1345,cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
      <data key="d11">026ef1a694cc4e2f9e14025f63f5097c</data>
      <data key="d12">14835</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="EXACERBATIONS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Exacerbations in bronchiectasis can lead to increased hospitalizations and healthcare costs</data>
      <data key="d10">cb63c034c676fa9dbbd8e5a07dd8c279</data>
      <data key="d11">af7c780c59dc41c49bed14da432dedc7</data>
      <data key="d12">14836</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="NUTRITIONAL DEPLETION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with bronchiectasis may experience nutritional depletion due to chronic infections and inflammation</data>
      <data key="d10">6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68</data>
      <data key="d11">8eb9e6bf4edc479d91aae08bb1a09815</data>
      <data key="d12">14837</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="ONEN ZP">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Onen ZP's research analyzes mortality factors in bronchiectasis patients</data>
      <data key="d10">6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68</data>
      <data key="d11">cbde726fd98d44dab73b8cb1acd63c60</data>
      <data key="d12">14838</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="MAIZ L">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Maiz L's study focuses on nontuberculous mycobacteria in bronchiectasis</data>
      <data key="d10">6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68</data>
      <data key="d11">9ee09a65550c49e59d9a76ee911f3471</data>
      <data key="d12">14839</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="OLVEIRA G">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Olveira G's research investigates the relationship between fat-free mass depletion and bronchiectasis</data>
      <data key="d10">6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68</data>
      <data key="d11">0d07e7773a9b49c1ae54cc1f323778fd</data>
      <data key="d12">14840</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRONCHIECTASIS" target="DIEHL N">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diehl N's work focuses on osteopenia and osteoporosis in bronchiectasis patients</data>
      <data key="d10">6d15ecf6cc2367b96e3ff917060f7f68</data>
      <data key="d11">3ba8e5005e244a10b4c79ae54aeba01e</data>
      <data key="d12">14841</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METABOLIC SYNDROME" target="BREAST CANCER">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Studies suggest a link between metabolic syndrome and increased breast cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
      <data key="d11">81367465b0714e49acf09ea0c1e4ab08</data>
      <data key="d12">14842</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METABOLIC SYNDROME" target="WORLD JOURNAL OF DIABETES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The journal discusses the role of dietary factors, including vitamin D, in metabolic syndrome outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">e757275b1935a42dabd03a0b528649a3</data>
      <data key="d11">d8fb2bb7c08e4d16921f1cd62dd86a5b</data>
      <data key="d12">14843</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METABOLIC SYNDROME" target="BURCELIN R">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Burcelin R's research on immuno-microbiota interactions is relevant to understanding metabolic syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">b602544ec2048878e40226cd2c0b29d4</data>
      <data key="d11">a6c1060f34b4422e94caf9e5ac6df9df</data>
      <data key="d12">14844</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CANCER OF THE BREAST" target="HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The risk of breast cancer is increased with hormone replacement therapy, particularly when progestogens are included</data>
      <data key="d10">f979a07da5d7c814ccf957629ab91cc5</data>
      <data key="d11">f2515faccfeb4b458f47c60a09b5ab07</data>
      <data key="d12">14845</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="HIPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico incluye la hiperuricemia como uno de sus componentes, lo que sugiere una relaci&#243;n directa entre ambos. Adem&#225;s, la hiperuricemia se asocia con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico. Sin embargo, aunque existe esta asociaci&#243;n, no se ha demostrado una relaci&#243;n causal directa entre la hiperuricemia y el s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico. En resumen, mientras que la hiperuricemia es un factor que puede estar presente en el s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico y se relaciona con un mayor riesgo de su desarrollo, la naturaleza de esta relaci&#243;n no ha sido completamente establecida.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9,3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">13f75e6cdb804320952eb8f250f79881</data>
      <data key="d12">14846</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de bebidas azucaradas se ha relacionado con una mayor incidencia de s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d11">d6aa264bc63f47c099393dc843e9fcae</data>
      <data key="d12">14847</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="GRASAS TRANS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El consumo de grasas trans se ha asociado con un aumento de la insulinorresistencia y el s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d11">e06c9e540c53426f83faaabf6fcbe41e</data>
      <data key="d12">14848</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="CITOCINAS PROINFLAMATORIAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El incremento de citocinas proinflamatorias en pacientes con sobrepeso se ha relacionado con un mayor riesgo de s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico.</data>
      <data key="d10">dcb29ef57f2b65cd420e728a3e29102d</data>
      <data key="d11">63f4d59e59fe4086b86f506eb0d874e1</data>
      <data key="d12">14849</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="GLUCOSA PLASM&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La glucosa plasm&#225;tica elevada es un indicador del s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico</data>
      <data key="d10">05ad4e8782ea0fc2d2347d73a0b5c704</data>
      <data key="d11">d151e041e18a438f9b2704325538fdb9</data>
      <data key="d12">14850</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="DIETAS HIPOPROTEICAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las dietas son fundamentales en el tratamiento del s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico</data>
      <data key="d10">5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448</data>
      <data key="d11">a6f79c5cefc04a7ea5f0b2fb012688fd</data>
      <data key="d12">14851</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="SOCIETAD ESPA&#209;OLA DE ARTERIOSCLEROSIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La SEA proporciona recomendaciones diet&#233;ticas para el manejo del s&#237;ndrome metab&#243;lico</data>
      <data key="d10">5b88c6556b90149ce0c0cea0bead7448</data>
      <data key="d11">e860aa9b8a914bc5bfa256352dae3c3e</data>
      <data key="d12">14852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME METAB&#211;LICO" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The entity "S&#237;ndrome Metab&#243;lico" is associated with an increased risk of "Litiasis Renal" (kidney stones). This relationship indicates that metabolic disorders can contribute to the development of kidney stones, highlighting a connection between the two health conditions. Additionally, the syndrome is linked to various other health issues, further emphasizing its significance in overall health management.</data>
      <data key="d10">9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb</data>
      <data key="d11">65a3cfcc73cf40e79f7f6a6cad5609fc</data>
      <data key="d12">14853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GEFFNER ME" target="DAVIS SM">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Davis SM y Geffner ME son coautores de un estudio sobre la salud cardiometab&#243;lica en el s&#237;ndrome de Turner.</data>
