    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE DENYS-DRASH" target="S&#205;NDROME DE ANTLEY-BIXLER">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos s&#237;ndromes est&#225;n relacionados con trastornos de la diferenciaci&#243;n sexual y mutaciones en genes espec&#237;ficos</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">4c03da787caa4faba25a6a90f2429bbd</data>
      <data key="d12">14899</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE DENYS-DRASH" target="WT1">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Denys-Drash se debe a mutaciones en el gen WT1, que son fundamentales para su manifestaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">92bf2031f2bc4ea9a2f85994f61d3f32</data>
      <data key="d12">14900</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE SMITH-LEMLI-OPITZ" target="S&#205;NDROME DE ANTLEY-BIXLER">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ambos s&#237;ndromes presentan anomal&#237;as fenot&#237;picas y est&#225;n relacionados con problemas en la s&#237;ntesis de esteroides</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">2362966679db433085df60f44ebb7813</data>
      <data key="d12">14901</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE SMITH-LEMLI-OPITZ" target="CYP19A1">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Smith-Lemli-Opitz est&#225; relacionado con mutaciones en el gen CYP19A1, que afectan la s&#237;ntesis de esteroides</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">f77ec9c7b4dc41b6995753d55f0fe5a0</data>
      <data key="d12">14902</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME DE ANTLEY-BIXLER" target="CYP51A1">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome de Antley-Bixler est&#225; asociado a mutaciones en el gen CYP51A1, que afectan la esteroidog&#233;nesis</data>
      <data key="d10">6aec863f7ec32f8ad87cf6713faf74ab</data>
      <data key="d11">da62e3ff4074464485275e80c2b8a970</data>
      <data key="d12">14903</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CYP19A1" target="AROMATASE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CYP19A1 encodes the aromatase enzyme, which is responsible for the conversion of androgens to estrogens.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">d0450a9334484a6d9ad434894a0b0dc6</data>
      <data key="d12">14904</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AROMATASE" target="FETOPLACENTARY UNIT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aromatase plays a crucial role in the fetoplacental unit by regulating androgen levels to protect the fetus.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">2b128aa6dd5b4bb2af5c3cb6e2fe17f9</data>
      <data key="d12">14905</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="46,XX" target="HYPERGONADOTROPIC HYPOGONADISM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with 46,XX genotype may develop hypergonadotropic hypogonadism due to aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">4c860d380b5445e0a290c5d7c1819be9</data>
      <data key="d12">14906</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="46,XY" target="HYPERGONADOTROPIC HYPOGONADISM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with 46,XY genotype may also experience hypergonadotropic hypogonadism related to aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">399a609f8ea04b63807da9d507bc5deb</data>
      <data key="d12">14907</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERGONADOTROPIC HYPOGONADISM" target="HYPOSPADIAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism can lead to developmental issues such as hypospadias in affected males.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">3deb3d53955e4716b5ca8d3ea3e6514f</data>
      <data key="d12">14908</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIRSUTISM" target="ACNE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hirsutism and acne are both symptoms that can arise from hormonal imbalances associated with aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">6b7fb6fce7ee43438f12f457ad3395f1</data>
      <data key="d12">14909</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MIEDLICH SU" target="BONE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Miedlich SU authored a case report published in the Bone journal regarding aromatase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">88e88db2c25e4b16fdf9464354512152</data>
      <data key="d11">32341263b13a48bfaee7599b13cf4d92</data>
      <data key="d12">14910</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERANDROGENISMO" target="S&#205;NDROME DE OVARIOS POLIQU&#205;STICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polycystic Ovary Syndrome is a leading cause of hyperandrogenism in women, linking the two conditions closely.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">49d17c29def3458c97e98ef17ad6292a</data>
      <data key="d12">14911</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERANDROGENISMO" target="TUMOR OV&#193;RICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ovarian tumors can produce androgens, contributing to hyperandrogenism and its symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">cf23b20c0bf54b4c8bd539c25f7c6926</data>
      <data key="d12">14912</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERANDROGENISMO" target="CARCINOMA DE SUPRARENAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenal carcinoma can lead to hyperandrogenism due to androgen secretion, linking the two.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">e6be49edb1d349cfb460856a7c5a5c62</data>
      <data key="d12">14913</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERANDROGENISMO" target="D&#201;FICIT DE 21-HIDROXILASA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">21-Hydroxylase deficiency results in increased androgen production, causing hyperandrogenism.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">f4461bb2e073495a80ccabfa73ad2095</data>
      <data key="d12">14914</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERANDROGENISMO" target="ESTEROIDES ANABOLIZANTES">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anabolic steroids can increase androgen levels, contributing to hyperandrogenism and related symptoms like hirsutism.</data>
      <data key="d10">b30c94def1763c77fe1fc302cc896d6c</data>
      <data key="d11">e81c5ff82afa428bb1b447d484840601</data>
      <data key="d12">14915</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="17-OH-PROGESTERONE" target="HYPERPLASIA SUPRARENAL CONG&#201;NITA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated levels of 17-OH-Progesterone are indicative of congenital adrenal hyperplasia, establishing a diagnostic relationship</data>
      <data key="d10">05a6995cef9c8d0279b9f026da1ffed1</data>
      <data key="d11">efc59afe355f4f2bb813efb268e8208b</data>
      <data key="d12">14916</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
