    </edge>
    <edge source="LYSODREN" target="MITOTANE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lysodren contains mitotane as its active ingredient</data>
      <data key="d10">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d11">3f53e0004ac64a4cb87be6546bc81947</data>
      <data key="d12">14989</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE TYPE I">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperuricemia is a complication associated with Glycogen Storage Disease Type I</data>
      <data key="d10">704cfd179507a977ecc0691a5bd2861e</data>
      <data key="d11">4735f28db8994694aeaf005c88270f79</data>
      <data key="d12">14990</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="DC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperuricemia is a condition that can frequently appear in patients undergoing dietary treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">214cb2b8ddec52ff69849d87feb8e141</data>
      <data key="d11">25551f352d9045d79d4706a71224b4d1</data>
      <data key="d12">14991</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="ASOCIACI&#211;N EUROPEA DE UROLOG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Association of Urology provides dietary guidelines for managing hyperuricemia and related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">c3fb2cdb71724deaa94f0d7d8f50b9ca</data>
      <data key="d12">14992</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperuricemia can lead to the formation of uric acid stones, a type of kidney stone.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">5a425cd05ae142dcafc06c6f2fe4adce</data>
      <data key="d12">14993</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="PURINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High intake of purines can lead to elevated uric acid levels, contributing to hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">566a1bc96b1c4cc0958a6e9497bf6ed4</data>
      <data key="d12">14994</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="ALIMENTOS RICOS EN PURINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Foods rich in purines can increase uric acid levels, which is a key factor in hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">6869e457b204461d8c6af7ccabc4bc2f</data>
      <data key="d12">14995</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="DIETA MUY BAJA EN PURINAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A very low purine diet is recommended to help lower uric acid levels in patients with hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">ebb7844c7c304d6e953375f927e8c612</data>
      <data key="d12">14996</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="ACIDO URICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elevated levels of uric acid are the defining characteristic of hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">57d928013f61475d356dcec181cc0c6c</data>
      <data key="d11">f2df76482bb9413f861ffc7cb36058b7</data>
      <data key="d12">14997</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fructosa consumption is associated with increased levels of hyperuricemia due to its effect on uric acid metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc</data>
      <data key="d11">e4ef0dee9a204bbe81beb724b7fc8f8b</data>
      <data key="d12">14998</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="CARNES ROJAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Red meats contribute to hyperuricemia by providing a significant source of purines that elevate uric acid levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc</data>
      <data key="d11">e536a24ff1044606a778e4c576a2b9c8</data>
      <data key="d12">14999</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="REFRESCOS EDULCORADOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sweetened soft drinks are linked to hyperuricemia due to their high fructose content, which affects uric acid metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">393fd6c0f1d43f0413a5b82d1dc0c2fc</data>
      <data key="d11">edecfbc481244579b2e9e461625436a1</data>
      <data key="d12">15000</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPERURICEMIA" target="GOUT">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperuricemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of uric acid in the blood, which is a significant risk factor for the development of gout. This excess uric acid can lead to the formation of urate crystals in the joints, ultimately resulting in the painful inflammatory condition known as gout. Therefore, hyperuricemia plays a crucial role in the onset of gout, as the accumulation of uric acid is directly linked to the disease's progression.</data>
      <data key="d10">6533cbcb76873caf6fd68eb95d313d24,a0162312192878417ef2c4ef8f9cffba</data>
      <data key="d11">3c3a9824343c4eb98889a5e8e6b193c7</data>
      <data key="d12">15001</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALTERACI&#211;N" target="INMUNIDAD">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alterations in immunity can lead to various health issues, including autoimmune diseases</data>
      <data key="d10">af95ffa2f3eaddc28a86d59cd2d89415</data>
      <data key="d11">d28854a4b2474b83a5299dab2de59f67</data>
      <data key="d12">15002</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INMUNIDAD" target="TRATAMIENTO ORAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La inmunidad se ve afectada por el tratamiento oral que induce tolerancia a los al&#233;rgenos</data>
      <data key="d10">0f0303399f29734dede9db544e1dda9e</data>
      <data key="d11">ef038a71bfbf4e718573c46a5481a676</data>
      <data key="d12">15003</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INMUNIDAD" target="TRATAMIENTO NASAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La inmunidad se ve afectada por el tratamiento nasal que induce tolerancia a los al&#233;rgenos</data>
      <data key="d10">0f0303399f29734dede9db544e1dda9e</data>
      <data key="d11">d78b74234ad84cc795196650032a0b64</data>
      <data key="d12">15004</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="HIPERURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">26.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido &#250;rico and hiperuricemia are closely related entities in the context of metabolic processes in the body. Hiperuricemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of &#225;cido &#250;rico, which can occur due to an increase in its production or a decrease in its elimination from the body. The accumulation of &#225;cido &#250;rico is the primary factor that defines hiperuricemia, making it a direct consequence of imbalances in the metabolism of this substance. Thus, the relationship between &#225;cido &#250;rico and hiperuricemia is fundamental, as the excess of &#225;cido &#250;rico leads to the development of this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290</data>
      <data key="d11">907a19f565db470b9d5fe094ee01c21a</data>
      <data key="d12">15005</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="XANTINA OXIDASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La xantina oxidasa cataliza la conversi&#243;n de hipoxantina y guanina en &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">2dcd29ff37aa4bb19d7fd6b75fbd3434</data>
      <data key="d12">15006</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="FEBUXOSTAT">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El febuxostat es un inhibidor que se utiliza para tratar la hiperuricemia, afectando la producci&#243;n de &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">9853e96349514a63bd14c21cf0c8b347</data>
      <data key="d12">15007</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="XANTINA">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido &#250;rico is a waste product that is formed during the metabolism of purines. Xantina, a compound in this metabolic pathway, is further degraded into &#225;cido &#250;rico. Thus, the relationship between xantina and &#225;cido &#250;rico is that xantina is converted into &#225;cido &#250;rico as part of the purine metabolism process.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">668964e4351949a79bd300681ab8e5cf</data>
      <data key="d12">15008</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="ALANTO&#205;NA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El &#225;cido &#250;rico se transforma en alanto&#237;na en los mam&#237;feros.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">267acbb636434a81b868474474f82b29</data>
      <data key="d12">15009</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="PURINAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las purinas son metabolizadas para producir &#225;cido &#250;rico.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">80b7cf28c9124ef7bdf86d1896cd7dde</data>
      <data key="d12">15010</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="URATO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El &#225;cido &#250;rico se ioniza a urato en condiciones fisiol&#243;gicas, siendo la forma predominante en el cuerpo.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">9577e03aeaa040f89b54467dfa576441</data>
      <data key="d12">15011</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="C&#193;LCULOS DE &#193;CIDO &#218;RICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los c&#225;lculos de &#225;cido &#250;rico se forman debido a la baja solubilidad del &#225;cido &#250;rico en la orina.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">1c037a5bd17a4384b09bbd5fac121473</data>
      <data key="d12">15012</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="URICASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Uricasa converts &#225;cido &#250;rico into allantoin, facilitating its excretion</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">e1384256314f40bd8c147e94985cc57c</data>
      <data key="d12">15013</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="ALANTOINA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido &#250;rico is converted into alanto&#237;na by the enzyme uricasa, facilitating its excretion</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">8cff60c002e649b3853c8c3ebd25f6b8</data>
      <data key="d12">15014</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&#193;CIDO &#218;RICO" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido &#250;rico is associated with the formation of uric acid stones, which are a type of kidney stone.</data>
      <data key="d10">634b74df7b9403e4c578f3fc84fe3335</data>
      <data key="d11">592f69b609ed441890666720ddcaaf33</data>
      <data key="d12">15015</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="ARTRITIS GOTOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiperuricemia puede predisponer a las personas a desarrollar artritis gotosa debido a la acumulaci&#243;n de cristales de urato en las articulaciones.</data>
      <data key="d10">3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483</data>
      <data key="d11">72996c14d97741108ccf34adce82e209</data>
      <data key="d12">15016</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="UROLITIASIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiperuricemia puede causar la formaci&#243;n de c&#225;lculos renales, lo que se conoce como urolitiasis, debido a la acumulaci&#243;n de &#225;cido &#250;rico en el tracto urinario.</data>
      <data key="d10">3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483</data>
      <data key="d11">0f276314e8b54c18a6bd4f83594cf328</data>
      <data key="d12">15017</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="ENFERMEDAD NEFR&#211;PATA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hiperuricemia puede llevar a la enfermedad nefr&#243;pata, afectando la funci&#243;n renal y causando da&#241;o a los ri&#241;ones.</data>
      <data key="d10">3ea911f4fe93a5403638aacc9085b483</data>
      <data key="d11">ebb24cd5af3e4e5d999e71e4253d3fe7</data>
      <data key="d12">15018</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="GSDIB">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hyperuricemia is a common metabolic disturbance in patients with GSDIb, leading to potential gout.</data>
      <data key="d10">a81765e6d24ccef0c86801f71673de98</data>
      <data key="d11">07cce9698cec42dc829032c99dbfc21b</data>
      <data key="d12">15019</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="LITIASIS RENAL">
      <data key="d8">23.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperuricemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of uric acid in the blood, and it is recognized as a contributing factor to the development of kidney stones, also known as litiasis renal. There is a direct relationship between hiperuricemia and the formation of kidney stones, particularly those composed of uric acid. This association highlights the importance of managing uric acid levels to prevent the occurrence of kidney stones.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d,9ea70909c43b9b7923a0fa217c0e7290,b703f173982cf68d36653cc0d9cc1fcb</data>
      <data key="d11">6643e7bba81448049be8124df2bfea6e</data>
      <data key="d12">15020</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="GOTA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hiperuricemia can lead to the development of gota due to the deposition of urate crystals</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">8efcda153cf6491989801c7db9513bda</data>
      <data key="d12">15021</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="ANEMIA HEMOL&#205;TICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anemia hemol&#237;tica can lead to hiperuricemia due to increased breakdown of red blood cells</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">43bf001dcedc4e66a3c1bbfc76c6b542</data>
      <data key="d12">15022</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="TRASTORNOS MIELOPROLIFERATIVOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Trastornos mieloproliferativos can cause hiperuricemia due to high cell turnover</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">c6251c112512479b9c52dd87d1a287ef</data>
      <data key="d12">15023</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="TRASTORNOS LINFOPROLIFERATIVOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Trastornos linfoproliferativos can lead to hiperuricemia due to increased lymphocyte production</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">6934289f26184d22a5e4c1f5648297a2</data>
      <data key="d12">15024</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="SORIASIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sor&#237;asis can contribute to hiperuricemia due to metabolic changes</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">a858f8109c454ccaa31beedd7d92f482</data>
      <data key="d12">15025</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="DEFICIT DE VITAMINA B12">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Deficit de vitamina B12 can lead to hiperuricemia due to metabolic alterations</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">ac1021f50bcb48bd83426bc12e06489a</data>
      <data key="d12">15026</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="DIUR&#201;TICOS TIAZ&#205;DICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diur&#233;ticos tiaz&#237;dicos can lead to hiperuricemia by decreasing renal elimination of &#225;cido &#250;rico</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">379bc619b912408b8cb05b3daae4bfac</data>
      <data key="d12">15027</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="SALICILATOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Salicilatos at low doses can contribute to hiperuricemia by reducing the elimination of &#225;cido &#250;rico</data>
      <data key="d10">ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">e153590eaf954109a1c45b68cdb21e25</data>
      <data key="d12">15028</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="ENFERMEDAD VASCULAR MANIFIESTA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad vascular manifiesta puede estar asociada con niveles elevados de &#225;cido &#250;rico, lo que sugiere una relaci&#243;n entre ambas condiciones.</data>
      <data key="d10">12c1878563254283012703d4f20ff4a9</data>
      <data key="d11">7fe9c0229930481b893c898aa9c0237f</data>
      <data key="d12">15029</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="PURINAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased intake of purinas can elevate uric acid levels, contributing to the development of hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">0131e43d67aa4b6ba9901e13187a584c</data>
      <data key="d12">15030</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Consumption of low-fat dairy products may help lower uric acid levels and reduce the risk of hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">346484c4dae04867ba178265310538c9</data>
      <data key="d12">15031</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="VERDURAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A diet rich in verduras is associated with lower serum uric acid levels, potentially reducing hyperuricemia risk.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">97ca012a77f246c1aaf1fa5e737e5ade</data>
      <data key="d12">15032</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPERURICEMIA" target="&#193;CIDO OR&#211;TICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">&#193;cido or&#243;tico may help in the excretion of uric acid, potentially lowering the risk of hyperuricemia.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ad59ffc3e39719e331a017fe64cd07d</data>
      <data key="d11">0cf19081151e4be1b058d81609f500c2</data>
      <data key="d12">15033</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NURIA VALDES GALLEGO" target="HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE CABUE&#209;ES">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nuria Valdes Gallego is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the University Hospital of Cabue&#241;es</data>
      <data key="d10">cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d11">d7fc7795d3e04084b4ab6be6958542a3</data>
      <data key="d12">15034</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NURIA VALDES GALLEGO" target="UNIVERSIDAD DE OVIEDO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nuria Valdes Gallego is an associate professor at the University of Oviedo</data>
      <data key="d10">cc9543ac7abe58ae289e1fbd5353e219</data>
      <data key="d11">d4e4c0a3877c465e9d44bf86ce2dbe13</data>
      <data key="d12">15035</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NURIA VALDES GALLEGO" target="SOCIEDAD ASTURIANA DE DIABETES, ENDOCRINOLOG&#205;A, NUTRICI&#211;N Y OBESIDAD">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
