    <edge source="GOLTZMAN D" target="PSEUDOHYPOPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Goltzman D discusses the etiology and diagnostic approach to pseudohypoparathyroidism</data>
      <data key="d10">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d11">9caa552a40e34ef089c425a6cd05e32a</data>
      <data key="d12">15112</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PSEUDOHYPOPARATHYROIDISM" target="OSTEODISTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osteodistrofia hereditaria de Albright is a condition that can be associated with pseudohypoparathyroidism due to genetic factors affecting hormone resistance</data>
      <data key="d10">85ee651c191c3b0c5fe786fe2e0718a4</data>
      <data key="d11">b9c23a5c57744a17a0fd8bdb034cc233</data>
      <data key="d12">15113</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="OSTEODYSTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in GNAS1 are responsible for the development of osteodystrophy, leading to the symptoms associated with this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">86a8297d29df4067962a42595b97010e</data>
      <data key="d12">15114</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="PSEUDOPSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pseudopseudohypoparathyroidism is linked to mutations in GNAS1, resulting in a phenotype similar to osteodystrophy without the biochemical abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">af5a51bc387a41dea6b23e82563055e0</data>
      <data key="d12">15115</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1A">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 1a pseudohypoparathyroidism is caused by mutations in GNAS1, leading to resistance to multiple hormones.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">68ca16ca4cf54089b40961f3774d091c</data>
      <data key="d12">15116</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1B">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 1b pseudohypoparathyroidism is associated with maternal mutations in GNAS1, leading to specific renal resistance to PTH.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">525ddcc309874d3d9682bc5ad89d4522</data>
      <data key="d12">15117</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1C">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 1c pseudohypoparathyroidism involves mutations in GNAS1 that affect its coupling to the PTH receptor, leading to hormone resistance.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">f01e014bbe1345d39c68c31e460a0bab</data>
      <data key="d12">15118</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GNAS1" target="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism is thought to involve defects in signaling pathways related to GNAS1, affecting calcium metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">6c2ccbc2112b4e8197f78585fc274c90</data>
      <data key="d12">15119</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2" target="DIAG&#201;ORGE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DiGeorge syndrome can present with hypoparathyroidism, leading to similar calcium metabolism issues as seen in Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">de965187adef4941bd18ae7a01fd5d3a</data>
      <data key="d12">15120</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH)" target="RECEPTOR PTH/PTHRP">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PTH binds to the PTH/PTHrP receptor to exert its effects on calcium and phosphate metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">b241988eddbf4bf7a981f9de3169dfa1</data>
      <data key="d12">15121</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH)" target="ADENIL-CICLASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">PTH activates adenyl cyclase, leading to increased levels of cyclic AMP, which mediates its physiological effects.</data>
      <data key="d10">764b89f13f6ebf12ba0d0ec4a73d2c68</data>
      <data key="d11">8ad6df6e80f64ea5bfbd9e8c00d05399</data>
      <data key="d12">15122</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RAQUITISMO" target="OSTEOMALACIA ONCOG&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El raquitismo y la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica comparten caracter&#237;sticas similares en cuanto a la mineralizaci&#243;n &#243;sea deficiente.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">6777b0dad48c4569907aace3d82ae809</data>
      <data key="d12">15123</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RAQUITISMO" target="ENFERMEDAD CELIACA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad cel&#237;aca puede llevar al raquitismo por malabsorci&#243;n de calcio y vitamina D</data>
      <data key="d10">4335489f570bb14684484e76cd6c196f</data>
      <data key="d11">9d75d870352542028391d258d045b10b</data>
      <data key="d12">15124</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPOCALCEMIA" target="HYPOPARATHYROIDISM">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypocalcemia is a common consequence of hypoparathyroidism due to insufficient parathyroid hormone levels</data>
      <data key="d10">313611d83ceda2a812387fbcffbedad6</data>
      <data key="d11">9f7cc481af124079b7ae1d3cbe25afdd</data>
      <data key="d12">15125</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYPOCALCEMIA" target="PA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypocalcemia is frequently observed in patients with pancreatitis and is related to the severity of the disease</data>
      <data key="d10">46bc44144e19709e2d7f9838c9c54ccf</data>
      <data key="d11">a09c03ca2250453d86447834512ac20b</data>
      <data key="d12">15126</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DENOSUMAB" target="OSTEOCLASTO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Denosumab inhibits the formation of osteoclasts, thereby reducing bone resorption</data>
      <data key="d10">43b6763c37598cae7a26ed8a26b45f54</data>
      <data key="d11">705e42e390544481a0b356afadebe1e2</data>
      <data key="d12">15127</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DENOSUMAB" target="ANOREXIA NERVOSA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Denosumab has been used in patients with anorexia nervosa to address osteoporosis.</data>
      <data key="d10">203ff7a2671a44d48a1a326f469c5543</data>
      <data key="d11">62b57aad091840c9baf5a0bad5baba53</data>
      <data key="d12">15128</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ROSEN CJ" target="GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Rosen CJ has written about glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis in UpToDate</data>
      <data key="d10">9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d11">c199e47a649a46ccbb1c5df23f256dde</data>
      <data key="d12">15129</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TAMOXIFENO" target="SULPIRIDA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sulpirida and Tamoxifeno can interact in the treatment of mental health and cancer conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ff94f3fcc6eff16c2fdae5eb9b3aefa</data>
      <data key="d11">778bb2d4b85e42fd8ae2b3573755de9b</data>
      <data key="d12">15130</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BISFOSFONATOS" target="PACIENTES CELIACOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los bisfosfonatos son utilizados como tratamiento en pacientes celiacos para prevenir la p&#233;rdida de densidad mineral &#243;sea</data>
      <data key="d10">9d5e76e37794965024f4b16e7e163d30</data>
      <data key="d11">8da718f43f8347af8b30d44444e498fa</data>
      <data key="d12">15131</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DMO VERTEBRAL" target="GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">DMO vertebral is a sensitive indicator of bone loss in patients with glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis</data>
      <data key="d10">9944c8e8d3d7769c5297f8dfb9b6f664</data>
      <data key="d11">a17a01577fd541e8ae17697ed504ff6b</data>
      <data key="d12">15132</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OSTEOMALACIA ONCOG&#201;NICA" target="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos son responsables de causar osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica al secretar FGF23 y otras prote&#237;nas que afectan la mineralizaci&#243;n &#243;sea.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">72de390ee4f44236aab2b83371a309b0</data>
      <data key="d12">15133</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FGF23" target="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FGF23 es secretado por tumores mesenquimatosos y est&#225; relacionado con la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">3a1e3c792e804cc896e93950688520f6</data>
      <data key="d12">15134</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS" target="HUESOS LARGOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos pueden encontrarse en los huesos largos, contribuyendo a la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">78b8e856d5d44b2c800059f8b3c23da0</data>
      <data key="d12">15135</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS" target="EXTREMIDADES DISTALES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos pueden encontrarse en las extremidades distales, contribuyendo a la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">643775f174d44fc1991750f6efa2cc75</data>
      <data key="d12">15136</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS" target="NASOFARINGE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos pueden localizarse en la nasofaringe, contribuyendo a la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">0e8fc536363944eca04a57e0f1d17bfd</data>
      <data key="d12">15137</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS" target="SENOS NASALES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos pueden encontrarse en los senos nasales, contribuyendo a la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">8460fc8a6d5c4c208ec4ad13f4311e42</data>
      <data key="d12">15138</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS" target="INGLE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores mesenquimatosos pueden localizarse en la ingle, contribuyendo a la osteomalacia oncog&#233;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">bbd5823476958a6df68c50c99779656c</data>
      <data key="d11">dbc753a24ba942b5b17f4132a567bc98</data>
      <data key="d12">15139</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1&#913;-HIDROXILASA" target="CYP27B1">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the CYP27B1 gene affect the production of 1&#945;-hidroxilasa, leading to vitamin D deficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">697cab4ee38241e887f0414179763e2c</data>
      <data key="d12">15140</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NTOMAS NEUROGLUCOP&#201;NICOS" target="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with insulinoma often experience neuroglucopenic symptoms during hypoglycemic episodes</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">5b863fd7626948119dfc5c85919d4e82</data>
      <data key="d12">15141</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NTOMAS SIMP&#193;TICOS ADRENALES" target="INSULINOMA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulinoma can lead to sympathetic adrenal symptoms during episodes of hypoglycemia</data>
      <data key="d10">8f51c67fbf44368dcfc2d7c767e2cef6</data>
      <data key="d11">3f2f174357d44f2e86896f55cb5aac60</data>
      <data key="d12">15142</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINOMA" target="CRYER PE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cryer PE has authored guidelines that include information on insulinoma, establishing a connection between the author and the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">e3ac1ed8fcbc4e5495c05c6de28e7409</data>
      <data key="d12">15143</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINOMA" target="AXELROD L">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Axelrod L's contributions to the guidelines include insights on insulinoma, linking the author to the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">0a3cafbf9c3f45d48bae70b2fc4c1125</data>
      <data key="d12">15144</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINOMA" target="GROSSMAN AB">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Grossman AB's work on clinical practice guidelines encompasses insulinoma, creating a relationship between the author and the condition</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">7a6e6c759e6842b58128393aa9fba847</data>
      <data key="d12">15145</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INSULINOMA" target="PANCREAS">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Insulinomas develop in the pancreas, indicating a strong relationship between the organ and the tumor</data>
      <data key="d10">2a73a65aa862d055c1e417cc50a42166</data>
      <data key="d11">fd876ff396f549a6956c3e67c34fb682</data>
      <data key="d12">15146</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PANCREAS" target="SOMATOSTATINOMAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Somatostatinomas are tumors that develop in the pancreas</data>
      <data key="d10">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d11">30eb9b17fef84992bf5a264d2dc7b410</data>
      <data key="d12">15147</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PANCREAS" target="MEN1 SYNDROME">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors can be part of MEN1 syndrome</data>
      <data key="d10">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d11">5be5ce7f826d49d8aafc94e51342f584</data>
      <data key="d12">15148</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PANCREAS" target="VIPOMA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">VIPomas are primarily located in the pancreas</data>
      <data key="d10">3e0612d31ede59ef0f89172aca549f87</data>
      <data key="d11">d5ac1cf6060f4fb39f34ee9e853ad568</data>
      <data key="d12">15149</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEPATOCARCINOMA" target="GSDIII">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hepatocarcinoma, specifically hepatocellular carcinoma, is a rare complication associated with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII). It occurs in less than 10% of patients with GSDIII, highlighting that while the risk is present, it is not common. This condition represents a potential outcome for individuals diagnosed with GSDIII, emphasizing the importance of monitoring for such complications in this patient population.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">400833530b4942dd891641517218b6a9</data>
      <data key="d12">15150</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="TRIPT&#211;FANO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome carcinoide est&#225; relacionado con el metabolismo alterado del tript&#243;fano, que se convierte en serotonina en exceso en estos pacientes.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">003e75c9c24f4b468fa4e6c4ee6fb3b3</data>
      <data key="d12">15151</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="SEROTONINA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome carcinoide se caracteriza por la liberaci&#243;n excesiva de serotonina en la circulaci&#243;n sist&#233;mica.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">5da40bbe55ab4f0cb04d37eb7b0e5fec</data>
      <data key="d12">15152</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="ECOCARDIOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ecocardiograf&#237;a se utiliza para detectar lesiones card&#237;acas en pacientes con s&#237;ndrome carcinoide.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">e732fe1f5c69479a9013888997609299</data>
      <data key="d12">15153</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="TUMORES CARCINOIDES">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los tumores carcinoides pueden causar el s&#237;ndrome carcinoide al liberar sustancias vasoactivas en la circulaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">e271daaecbc14cdd924be85be9e70a22</data>
      <data key="d12">15154</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="MASA TUMORAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La masa tumoral est&#225; relacionada con la aparici&#243;n del s&#237;ndrome carcinoide, ya que su tama&#241;o y localizaci&#243;n afectan la liberaci&#243;n de sustancias vasoactivas.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">cfb47d4dc56341bb8edb79089673dc06</data>
      <data key="d12">15155</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME CARCINOIDE" target="D&#201;FICIT DE NIACINA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El d&#233;ficit de niacina puede contribuir a los s&#237;ntomas del s&#237;ndrome carcinoide, como las lesiones cut&#225;neas.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8099d0ade1b1539ca9f357d155574b</data>
      <data key="d11">54d1f39fd805426c9fb254cdbecd9db2</data>
      <data key="d12">15156</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRIPT&#211;FANO" target="L&#193;CTEOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tript&#243;fano found in l&#225;cteos complements the protein quality when combined with cereals</data>
      <data key="d10">ccac97d61bc412a8574fd71aa26dad79</data>
      <data key="d11">835eeaa24654475faade93915f88ec2a</data>
      <data key="d12">15157</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEROTONINA" target="ANSIEDAD">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Changes in serotonin levels can also contribute to anxiety disorders in patients with eating disorders</data>
      <data key="d10">3bc554a0031c436483a977c2b9e57b48</data>
      <data key="d11">001f5658a55e42a5927d223590ecb0f5</data>
      <data key="d12">15158</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEROTONINA" target="TUMORES CARCINOIDES">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Serotonina and tumores carcinoides are closely linked through the secretion of serotonin by carcinoid tumors. These tumors are known to produce serotonin, which plays a significant role in their diagnosis. The relationship between serotonin and carcinoid tumors highlights the importance of serotonin in understanding the behavior and identification of these neoplasms.</data>
      <data key="d10">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7,7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a</data>
      <data key="d11">edbedd2210ff43359bfd2e3db7b3347e</data>
      <data key="d12">15159</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SEROTONINA" target="5-HIA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">5-HIA is a metabolite of serotonin, indicating its presence and activity in the body</data>
      <data key="d10">7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a</data>
      <data key="d11">fd27237670104f6c93e78428fed14087</data>
      <data key="d12">15160</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES CARCINOIDES" target="ACIDO 5-HIDROXIINDOLACETICO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carcinoid tumors secrete serotonin, which is metabolized to 5-HIA and eliminated in urine.</data>
      <data key="d10">029a82f84eb8dfda723f9feabe2384d7</data>
      <data key="d11">265be15bc87742879ec181eac4d795ca</data>
      <data key="d12">15161</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TUMORES CARCINOIDES" target="PULM&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carcinoid tumors can appear in the lung, indicating a relationship between the two</data>
      <data key="d10">7d4d879207b235ab3018772eea448b2a</data>
      <data key="d11">094b38f8d6fd422bbd2e4d48a55ab744</data>
      <data key="d12">15162</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GASTRINOMA" target="PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gastrinomas are a functional type of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor that secretes gastrin</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">244b2e27ae7b40ea9aaea3b7b5f68a97</data>
      <data key="d12">15163</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="VIPOMA" target="PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Vipomas are another functional type of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide</data>
      <data key="d10">2ad120e12741c91b54f0eee4e16a3022</data>
      <data key="d11">bc5bac2d1e6e4eadb4431d283cc7b418</data>
      <data key="d12">15164</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUCAGONOMA" target="PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS">
