    <edge source="AVP" target="DIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginine-vasopressin (AVP) is involved in the regulation of water retention, and its dysfunction leads to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.</data>
      <data key="d10">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f</data>
      <data key="d11">02803b46c8274b65a12baa3537d54d85</data>
      <data key="d12">15558</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIN" target="HYPERNATREMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypernatremia can occur as a result of nephrogenic diabetes insipidus due to excessive urination and loss of water.</data>
      <data key="d10">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f</data>
      <data key="d11">3e22f50e33d84365b7a1c04e6e8ef001</data>
      <data key="d12">15559</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIN" target="CIDOFOVIR">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cidofovir is a medication that can cause nephrogenic diabetes insipidus as a side effect.</data>
      <data key="d10">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f</data>
      <data key="d11">9643683710114c43b313c3da09f07309</data>
      <data key="d12">15560</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIN" target="FOSCARNET">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Foscarnet can lead to nephrogenic diabetes insipidus in some patients as a side effect.</data>
      <data key="d10">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f</data>
      <data key="d11">7ef91316b70e4293b352e6d9aa132a5d</data>
      <data key="d12">15561</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIN" target="ANFOTERICINA B">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amphotericin B can cause nephrogenic diabetes insipidus as a side effect.</data>
      <data key="d10">1fb4c8ba1bc908ea3a3c7717a073fa4f</data>
      <data key="d11">173674b0b6e8450b86d5fcacb0bfdba6</data>
