    <edge source="NATIONAL INSTITUTES OF HEALTH" target="NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES">
      <data key="d8">12.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The National Institutes of Health (NIH) and the National Academy of Sciences (NAS) are two prominent organizations that play significant roles in the fields of scientific research and health policy. Both entities contribute to advancing knowledge and informing health-related initiatives. The NAS specifically provides expert advice that helps shape the research priorities of the NIH, ensuring that the NIH's efforts are aligned with the latest scientific insights and societal needs. Together, they collaborate to enhance the understanding of health issues and promote effective health policies.</data>
