      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CEL&#205;ACOS" target="GLUTEN">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El gluten es la sustancia que causa problemas de salud en las personas cel&#237;acas</data>
      <data key="d10">e4edae03f8089b7bc1c46e697e658e3c</data>
      <data key="d11">0554f01f7a4c4bf5b342fdc9c2714b26</data>
      <data key="d12">16894</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="ENFERMEDAD CELIACA">
      <data key="d8">20.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gluten is the primary trigger for celiac disease, causing inflammation and damage in the small intestine. It is the cause of this autoimmune condition, and individuals diagnosed with celiac disease must avoid gluten in their diet to prevent adverse health effects.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9,41babae4bb4b80271c9bfd9da1528392,a3d1ea55509c69a04f3268ea20a33ba4</data>
      <data key="d11">dfebeb9977014863a6ab2233eb466a4d</data>
      <data key="d12">16895</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="SENSIBILIDAD AL GLUTEN NO CELIACA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Non-celiac gluten sensitivity involves symptoms triggered by gluten consumption, similar to celiac disease but without the autoimmune response.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d11">5bf3140a151849398319fb32557ff69e</data>
      <data key="d12">16896</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="BARLEY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Barley contains gluten, which can trigger symptoms in individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d11">4b87f359c88240d6859f428ecb7e3b0a</data>
      <data key="d12">16897</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="CENTENO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Rye contains gluten and is associated with celiac disease, causing adverse reactions in sensitive individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d11">ab038519f038425f957cae2e64d5df0e</data>
      <data key="d12">16898</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="AVENA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oats can be safe for individuals with celiac disease if they are processed correctly to avoid gluten contamination.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d11">f6ab1701d9a64cc5a67ef80872c5bc2c</data>
      <data key="d12">16899</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GLUTEN" target="CORN">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Corn is a gluten-free grain, making it safe for individuals with celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">281c46dd2bcde6e6fbb1505ed667b0e9</data>
      <data key="d11">1e1bd7e945b142e69f6ea28fda8f7153</data>
