    <edge source="AOECS" target="GLUTEN-FREE SYMBOL">
      <data key="d8">16.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The gluten-free symbol is a certification mark that is granted and regulated by AOECS (the Association of European Coeliac Societies). AOECS is responsible for ensuring that products bearing this symbol meet established gluten-free standards. The organization oversees the use and certification of the gluten-free symbol, ensuring that consumers can trust that the products labeled with it are safe for individuals with gluten intolerance or celiac disease.</data>
      <data key="d10">d3ffabc46da9b238994a7769ffc8f6b7,dfb6e1826ded0b8ca7cf3304d1b75d1a</data>
      <data key="d11">57ca1de7eb97489ebb64208da77339c9</data>
      <data key="d12">16907</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AOECS" target="SPIGA BARRADA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Spiga barrada is the symbol for gluten-free products, which AOECS oversees for compliance</data>
