    </edge>
    <edge source="SAND&#205;A" target="TEMA 14">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Tema 14 discusses nutritional support which may include fruits like Sand&#237;a for their health benefits</data>
      <data key="d10">5f60e39bc965632761d15273062b91fe</data>
      <data key="d11">f262a0906df74414a41183e3a79d4d69</data>
      <data key="d12">17080</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HUESOS" target="CUPROENZIMAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cuproenzyme activity is important for the development and maintenance of bones</data>
      <data key="d10">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">67106c8c643d4f57857e62db4301225b</data>
      <data key="d12">17081</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MERIENDA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Merienda, which refers to the afternoon snack, is an important component of NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA guidelines aimed at ensuring balanced nutrition for children throughout the day. It is recommended that the afternoon snack should contribute approximately 10-15% of the total caloric content in children's diets. This inclusion emphasizes the significance of merienda in promoting healthy eating habits and maintaining adequate energy levels for children.</data>
      <data key="d10">61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,f96dd2fbe3cd9aa6516522de8ed33145</data>
      <data key="d11">226bddfe31a24dd6bdc1ee8758402502</data>
      <data key="d12">17082</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="COMIDA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Comida is emphasized in the NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA guidelines as the most important meal of the day</data>
      <data key="d10">f96dd2fbe3cd9aa6516522de8ed33145</data>
      <data key="d11">0969d27ea4154b31a515de6d1eb4bac4</data>
      <data key="d12">17083</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CENA" target="NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CENA is an integral component of the NUTRICI&#211;N PEDI&#193;TRICA guidelines, which aim to ensure that children receive adequate nutrition in the evening. According to these guidelines, dinner should account for 25% of the total energy value of a child's diet, highlighting the importance of a balanced evening meal in promoting overall health and well-being in pediatric nutrition.</data>
      <data key="d10">61b84039de5ac2d9e25890c3b8f4f87a,f96dd2fbe3cd9aa6516522de8ed33145</data>
      <data key="d11">efc30dd3dca34e9e9979f938914617ba</data>
      <data key="d12">17084</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ALIMENTACI&#211;N CON NUTRICI&#211;N ARTIFICIAL" target="PACIENTES CON QUEMADURAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with severe burns may require artificial nutrition to meet their dietary needs</data>
      <data key="d10">c6406ac5c0c7b03d4ee61ca311fd783f</data>
      <data key="d11">e7744a887cfe47b49fe6ceda8e58740d</data>
      <data key="d12">17085</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DIETAS HIPOPROTEICAS" target="HEPATOPAT&#205;A CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las modificaciones diet&#233;ticas son esenciales en el tratamiento de la hepatopat&#237;a cr&#243;nica</data>
