    </edge>
    <edge source="FIRMICUTES" target="BACTEROIDETES">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Firmicutes and Bacteroidetes are phyla of bacteria that coexist in the human gut and are essential for digestive health. The balance between these two groups in the gut microbiota is linked to body weight and obesity phenotypes. Research indicates that the ratio of Firmicutes to Bacteroidetes is often higher in obese individuals, suggesting a relationship between these two phyla in the context of energy absorption. This interplay highlights the importance of Firmicutes and Bacteroidetes in maintaining a healthy gut microbiome and their potential influence on metabolic health.</data>
      <data key="d10">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021,e189588f51b4bb84b3621a1f846d07bc,ffdc08ec09899ab7dfa255af4cecac1c</data>
      <data key="d11">5c72e08953a04ce4bfd57116daba3551</data>
      <data key="d12">17362</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIRMICUTES" target="ACTINOBACTERIAS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Firmicutes y Actinobacterias son filos de bacterias que forman parte de la microbiota intestinal y tienen funciones metab&#243;licas importantes.</data>
      <data key="d10">90ec2b7e4fe7ed5c84bafaaba8834021</data>
      <data key="d11">59954cd8502d42b4a5b9a1a0014e804f</data>
      <data key="d12">17363</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIRMICUTES" target="NI&#209;OS EUROPEOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La microbiota intestinal de los ni&#241;os europeos est&#225; dominada por el filo Firmicutes, que se asocia con su dieta alta en grasas y prote&#237;nas.</data>
      <data key="d10">1ea9b98ae148853da00e395690177314</data>
      <data key="d11">dc03cc937a704fbe93858e784aa3a7cc</data>
      <data key="d12">17364</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIRMICUTES" target="ROEDORES">
