    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDI" target="JARABE DE MA&#205;Z RICO EN FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">High fructose corn syrup is not recommended for children with GSDI as it can lead to glucose management issues.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e</data>
      <data key="d11">fda4ed63feff4da3b8ccc693291d920d</data>
      <data key="d12">17675</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDI" target="LACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intake should be limited in older children with GSDI to manage their dietary needs.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e</data>
      <data key="d11">a372dc840bbb439c862c90eb016c26a4</data>
      <data key="d12">17676</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDI" target="GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose should be restricted in the diet of children with GSDI to maintain stable glucose levels.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae68887594ec21900691a1100f61b43e</data>
      <data key="d11">2b98b14d1efd455a8b966f1bd9850aab</data>
      <data key="d12">17677</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDI" target="GSDIII">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GSDI and GSDIII are both types of glycogen storage diseases (GSDs) that involve the abnormal storage and metabolism of glycogen in the body. While they share some similarities, such as overlapping dietary management strategies, they also exhibit distinct differences. GSDI typically presents with more severe symptoms compared to GSDIII. Additionally, GSDIII and GSDI have different dietary management strategies tailored to their specific metabolic needs. Overall, both conditions require careful dietary planning to manage their respective symptoms and complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1,a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">8a2ef9322d1349c88cb65f31cae710c7</data>
      <data key="d12">17678</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDI" target="FRUCTOSA-1,6-BIFOSFATASA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Symptoms of fructosa-1,6-bifosfatas deficiency are similar to those of GSDI, indicating a relationship between the two conditions.</data>
      <data key="d10">449046c83c1432d2b8cc6cacb5eadf51</data>
      <data key="d11">9fd9923cb66a4e8da3dd594950050cfc</data>
      <data key="d12">17679</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MAICENA" target="GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Maicena is used in the dietary management of glucogenosis tipo I to maintain stable blood glucose levels</data>
      <data key="d10">28633689bf0b9bc990e61fb26722ce16</data>
      <data key="d11">0d43571e21644405a5f8dfc2cfe89b82</data>
      <data key="d12">17680</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="HEREDITARY FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sorbitol is another sugar that individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance need to avoid</data>
      <data key="d10">cdc634d994ef64b248220c990c844160</data>
      <data key="d11">ed14f2e2164a488cada93a061c56d1ca</data>
      <data key="d12">17681</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="POLIOLES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sorbitol is a type of poliol that is absorbed in the intestine</data>
      <data key="d10">fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">47d61050cf93476080b619f61a00d416</data>
      <data key="d12">17682</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="FRUCTOSE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sorbitol and fructose are often consumed together in foods, leading to increased symptoms of intolerance in individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">b5cb8dd1fb2d4b22b7106cbd3e9e5d32</data>
      <data key="d12">17683</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="SII">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with SII often experience heightened symptoms when consuming sorbitol.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">aaa979ec73a94c9fa1a95eca8d1655d9</data>
      <data key="d12">17684</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="ALIMENTARY PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alimentary products may contain sorbitol, which can lead to malabsorption issues in sensitive individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">472abfb81ed8438f87bdb2fbb2e2e74e</data>
      <data key="d12">17685</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="DIABETIC PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diabetic products may contain sorbitol, which can lead to malabsorption issues in sensitive individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">6d33d16c64744dd9bdc0a63b3fc9fc41</data>
      <data key="d12">17686</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="S&#205;NDROME DE INTESTINO IRRITABLE">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El sorbitol puede causar s&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales que se asemejan a los del s&#237;ndrome de intestino irritable</data>
      <data key="d10">7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f</data>
      <data key="d11">f01383776e364e49ac4e4931bcf07d32</data>
      <data key="d12">17687</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SORBITOL" target="DIARREA OSM&#211;TICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El sorbitol puede causar diarrea osm&#243;tica cuando se ingiere en grandes cantidades, lo que provoca s&#237;ntomas gastrointestinales</data>
      <data key="d10">7dcfce8c5d823846c83fa7ff807da54f</data>
      <data key="d11">01d2a4fa9b2f44f7bf6cd4dbe2af1b79</data>
      <data key="d12">17688</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="GALACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactosa, commonly known as lactose, is a sugar found in milk that plays a crucial role in mammalian diets. It is composed of two monosaccharides: glucose and galactosa. Galactosa, one of the components of lactosa, is essential for various biological functions. When lactose is consumed, it is hydrolyzed by the enzyme lactase into its constituent sugars, glucose and galactosa, highlighting the direct relationship between these two sugars.</data>
      <data key="d10">160d4259ba08a1bfcdc877b63a4c799d,2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,fd661ab8e042d0fed76b34b7ceff6631</data>
      <data key="d11">cd94c100be4b4d77b385fc0409648484</data>
      <data key="d12">17689</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="LACTASA">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LACTOSA and LACTASA are closely related entities in the context of lactose metabolism. LACTASA, also known as lactase, is the enzyme responsible for breaking down LACTOSA, which is a sugar found in milk and dairy products. This enzymatic action converts LACTOSA into glucose and galactose, two simpler sugars that can be easily absorbed by the body. The relevance of LACTASA is particularly significant for individuals with lactose intolerance, a condition where the body lacks sufficient lactase to properly digest lactose, leading to various digestive issues. Thus, LACTASA plays a crucial role in the digestion of LACTOSA, highlighting the importance of this enzyme in maintaining digestive health for those who consume dairy products.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838,527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">a35f34ffe4454218860cdd41abb80f4e</data>
      <data key="d12">17690</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The measurement of enzymatic activity is essential for diagnosing issues related to lactose consumption.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5</data>
      <data key="d11">dee6e7e69bfc41c4822de1f644bf0397</data>
      <data key="d12">17691</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="MALABSORCI&#211;N DE FRUCTOSA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactosa may need to be managed in the diet of individuals with malabsorci&#243;n de fructosa</data>
      <data key="d10">033a22e7215395479d0775d6a1a2563e</data>
      <data key="d11">7bdaa68f536347e9b32e6e2d79ea6a64</data>
      <data key="d12">17692</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="EII">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose can exacerbate symptoms in patients with EII, making its restriction important in their diet</data>
      <data key="d10">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c</data>
      <data key="d11">c179ee4dfed64cea8af6f1f1074938d7</data>
      <data key="d12">17693</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="FLORA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alterations in intestinal flora can impact the digestion of lactose in patients with EII</data>
      <data key="d10">94afd4bf40b661992e66cf7963ef236c</data>
      <data key="d11">50b5d1a74041430ea33780f03a295b90</data>
      <data key="d12">17694</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="INTOLERANCIAS ALIMENTARIAS">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LACTOSA is a specific type of food intolerance that affects many individuals, particularly adults who have difficulty absorbing this sugar. This condition, known as lactose intolerance, is a common form of food intolerance that can lead to various digestive issues when lactose-containing foods are consumed.</data>
      <data key="d10">39a7166ca777be46a1613c54a746e2b8,9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd</data>
      <data key="d11">6571e8e4f0e54b3a8d5e952a09a32413</data>
      <data key="d12">17695</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="TEST DE HIDR&#211;GENO ESPIRADO">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El test de hidr&#243;geno espirado se utiliza para diagnosticar la intolerancia a la lactosa, midiendo la producci&#243;n de hidr&#243;geno tras la ingesti&#243;n de lactosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd</data>
      <data key="d11">1f1ad01c59924a94abcc214e74b861ea</data>
      <data key="d12">17696</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="TEST DE TOLERANCIA A LA LACTOSA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El test de tolerancia a la lactosa se utiliza para evaluar la capacidad del cuerpo para procesar lactosa, ayudando a diagnosticar la intolerancia.</data>
      <data key="d10">9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd</data>
      <data key="d11">e8bfd5b051e54031976afa79ef53ee85</data>
      <data key="d12">17697</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="BIOPSIA DE INTESTINO DELGADO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La biopsia de intestino delgado puede confirmar la intolerancia a la lactosa tras un test positivo, aunque es un m&#233;todo invasivo.</data>
      <data key="d10">9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd</data>
      <data key="d11">6732296bc2b64f469132737184f25bff</data>
      <data key="d12">17698</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="PCR DEL GEN DE LA LACTASA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La PCR del gen de la lactasa puede ayudar a diferenciar entre tipos de hipolactasia, aunque no es com&#250;nmente utilizada en la pr&#225;ctica cl&#237;nica.</data>
      <data key="d10">9d1d9a50a4a29ae7660c32b749e46dbd</data>
      <data key="d11">98318442b9b14b928bf23d7d9cbfffb6</data>
      <data key="d12">17699</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="ALERGIAS ALIMENTARIAS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance is a type of food allergy that can cause severe reactions in some individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">a562e90891c11da0293bc7de511acc8f</data>
      <data key="d11">bfbdc30a9f9c4575a0369086265376ec</data>
      <data key="d12">17700</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSA" target="FODMAP">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La lactosa es un tipo de FODMAP que puede causar s&#237;ntomas en personas con intolerancia a este carbohidrato.</data>
      <data key="d10">527c3c962d22018377b32c52e984d4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">e72ca8cbe90b4f07807479d07c0eed0e</data>
      <data key="d12">17701</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose is a substrate for the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, which converts it into uridine diphosphate galactose.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">c8f1bb5d0a134a6185498bed2f6f0da0</data>
      <data key="d12">17702</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="GALACTITOL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose can be converted into galactitol through the action of aldose reductase, which is an alternative metabolic pathway.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">e7e414af4a0044319a61ba9d8bf4a9f1</data>
      <data key="d12">17703</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="&#193;CIDO GALACT&#211;NICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose is metabolized to galactonic acid via the action of galactose dehydrogenase, which is part of its metabolic pathway.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">741c62cd93b04638b7b1a6860848bfe9</data>
      <data key="d12">17704</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="GALACTOKINASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactokinase phosphorylates galactose to initiate its metabolism, establishing a direct relationship.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">16bfa8d454f24970afcbf1cf9abdfc71</data>
      <data key="d12">17705</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="V&#205;A LELOIR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The Leloir pathway is the metabolic route through which galactose is converted into glucose, establishing a strong relationship.</data>
      <data key="d10">2b4d246337cb56a96ab80fec81181838</data>
      <data key="d11">7c3d0e0e8bb54421bf11173fbf33a872</data>
      <data key="d12">17706</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="GALACTOSEMIA CL&#193;SICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ingesta de galactosa causa complicaciones en pacientes con galactosemia cl&#225;sica.</data>
      <data key="d10">f2f8594bddb0ab77444cdcd2a7799d59</data>
      <data key="d11">bb48dcabb7e44a23aca45b0ac2aa49b8</data>
      <data key="d12">17707</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSA" target="GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactosa does not improve hypoglycemia in glucogenosis de tipo I and may worsen acidosis</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8877823f796fc9a02f5103dc4650cc</data>
      <data key="d11">be898a43ad7f4697bad582f6e67e3373</data>
      <data key="d12">17708</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CITRATE" target="NEPHROLITHIASIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Citrate is used to prevent nephrolithiasis by alkalinizing urine</data>
      <data key="d10">9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">10f631c5100a4af29c0f4b68a9c9135f</data>
      <data key="d12">17709</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CITRATE" target="NEFROCALCINOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Citrate is used to manage nefrocalcinosis by alkalinizing urine</data>
      <data key="d10">9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">ef4a8bddf3034a0181bc45e7ada23b77</data>
      <data key="d12">17710</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BICARBONATE" target="NEPHROLITHIASIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bicarbonate can also be used to prevent nephrolithiasis by alkalinizing urine</data>
      <data key="d10">9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">3320ebbc2b314914bc8788b5977ac71a</data>
      <data key="d12">17711</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BICARBONATE" target="NEFROCALCINOSIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bicarbonate can also be used to manage nefrocalcinosis by alkalinizing urine</data>
      <data key="d10">9a0227d0ea548fa46814e6403be885ce</data>
      <data key="d11">d6495bf7ef8c42ceb2477cd66657c401</data>
      <data key="d12">17712</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="AMILO-1,6-GLUCOSIDASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GSDIII is caused by a deficiency of the enzyme amilo-1,6-glucosidasa</data>
      <data key="d10">b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">fe9557a7f30049cc8a2089d429910606</data>
      <data key="d12">17713</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="GEN AGL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mutations in the AGL gene lead to the development of GSDIII</data>
      <data key="d10">b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">fa8924ccaca3432ab181304b4f4c3bbd</data>
      <data key="d12">17714</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="FIBROSIS HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII) is a metabolic disorder that can lead to various complications, one of which is fibrosis hep&#225;tica, or liver fibrosis. While it is uncommon for patients with GSDIII to progress to cirrhosis, liver fibrosis can still develop as a complication in these individuals. Thus, while the occurrence of liver fibrosis in GSDIII patients is noted, the progression to more severe liver conditions like cirrhosis remains rare.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35,b5e899a3def3da339630eb0d2bfe4af8</data>
      <data key="d11">34383c5fedb54b9db2507752c2593acb</data>
      <data key="d12">17715</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="MIKARDIOPAT&#205;A HIPERTR&#211;FICA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy is a common cardiac manifestation in patients with GSDIII.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35</data>
      <data key="d11">73e10c86b5514143847ff9a72c4618bd</data>
      <data key="d12">17716</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL NOCTURNA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nighttime enteral nutrition is a strategy used to help maintain glucose levels in GSDIII patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35</data>
      <data key="d11">21110e2e74c84395bbc3f0c67740cc8e</data>
      <data key="d12">17717</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="HIPERTON&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Increased muscle tone (hipertonia) is a symptom that can be associated with GSDIII.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35</data>
      <data key="d11">6fce06d2b1b142e8bade5a0dcb311fe1</data>
      <data key="d12">17718</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="HIPOURICEMIA">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypouricemia can be an infrequent complication in patients with GSDIII.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35</data>
      <data key="d11">9a694e64943c49e49f558b393e26ebd2</data>
      <data key="d12">17719</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="AFECTACI&#211;N RENAL">
      <data key="d8">3.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Renal involvement is a potential but infrequent complication in GSDIII patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">a3fd8bf0a5229c36813682803cd15e35</data>
      <data key="d11">17b037414c8a4b0681ccba91acac5a95</data>
      <data key="d12">17720</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="FRUCTOSE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fructose is allowed in the diets of patients with GSDIII, which helps manage their condition</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">725ab07f10ad4a049639c109000bccf2</data>
      <data key="d12">17721</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSDIII" target="GALACTOSE">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Galactose is permitted in the diets of patients with GSDIII, aiding in their dietary management</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">1fea75b02711402a826f4d1e11009e0e</data>
      <data key="d12">17722</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FIBROSIS HEP&#193;TICA" target="HH">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fibrosis hep&#225;tica can occur due to chronic iron overload in hereditary hemochromatosis</data>
      <data key="d10">a3d834f1d854ecde12e808ae924b8eb0</data>
      <data key="d11">6ee41d063af84d8eae28e4eba902cf8e</data>
      <data key="d12">17723</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NUTRICI&#211;N ENTERAL NOCTURNA" target="ENFERMEDAD DE MCARDLE">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Most patients with McArdle disease do not require nocturnal enteral nutrition due to their dietary management</data>
      <data key="d10">4464b0da291e94ba7b7f5b51134b4a75</data>
      <data key="d11">71c2425bb4394a849e7398b074cd0b9d</data>
      <data key="d12">17724</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSD0" target="GLYCOGEN SYNTHASE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GSD0 is caused by a deficiency in glycogen synthase, which is critical for glycogen synthesis</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">9ec219f1edb541a3adb7034236eb901c</data>
      <data key="d12">17725</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSD0" target="HIPOALANINEMIA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hipoalaninemia can occur in patients with GSD0 due to increased gluconeogenesis</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">c0c6be0b52a44458bd76d220b8041c2d</data>
      <data key="d12">17726</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSD0" target="BIOPSIA HEP&#193;TICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A liver biopsy may be performed to confirm the diagnosis of GSD0</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">5b435c999bb64ad49c2cb28759990bac</data>
      <data key="d12">17727</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GSD0" target="ESTUDIO GEN&#201;TICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Genetic studies are used to confirm the diagnosis of GSD0</data>
      <data key="d10">9f5a8d86160d5d097bca174e2e2496c1</data>
      <data key="d11">00be76ccd0d14a269e85de4094593d96</data>
      <data key="d12">17728</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="ALDOB">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The ALDOB gene encodes an enzyme that is crucial for the metabolism of fructose</data>
      <data key="d10">f290b280f5c5a9e2e8326fec68b6016f</data>
      <data key="d11">59508438ca8d459a9cf1b882bace6519</data>
      <data key="d12">17729</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="SII">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Individuals with SII often experience heightened symptoms when consuming fructose.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">17428a0d60684542bd7b6e799a585518</data>
      <data key="d12">17730</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="ALIMENTARY PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alimentary products may contain fructose, which can lead to malabsorption issues in sensitive individuals.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">1ea093e485ce4c579a8d38058a2a67d0</data>
      <data key="d12">17731</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="CARAMELOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Caramelos often contain high levels of fructose, which can exacerbate symptoms in individuals with intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">b2e9986d5032454e8f3c9e07183bf7d0</data>
      <data key="d12">17732</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="LIGHT PRODUCTS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Light products may contain fructose, which can exacerbate symptoms in individuals with intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">763ef3a3c5454cb78d834aca522a5761</data>
      <data key="d12">17733</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FRUCTOSE" target="FRUIT JUICES">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fruit juices often contain high levels of fructose, which can exacerbate symptoms in individuals with intolerances.</data>
      <data key="d10">fb0fe813a0b63d3b7f4a1bccaf15d291</data>
      <data key="d11">d8ce65048a944b609bdea1ae66e97e4e</data>
      <data key="d12">17734</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GALACTOSE" target="GALACTOKINASA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
