      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance can develop in patients with celiac disease, particularly at the time of diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d10">e6153f0024d75c281071b521b08ed53a</data>
      <data key="d11">87e8f6ce9efe48eeb932787c5b3c4cd8</data>
      <data key="d12">17885</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FINLAND" target="LACTASE DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Most cases of congenital lactase deficiency have been reported in the Finnish population.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">e25396fa22ec4ee78d906c8d692a3f2e</data>
      <data key="d12">17886</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="LACTASE DEFICIENCY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance is a condition that arises from lactase deficiency.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">2dc8658a10a7424e891f8a68119d42e4</data>
      <data key="d12">17887</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="CELIAC DISEASE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Celiac disease can cause secondary lactose intolerance due to damage to the intestinal mucosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">e349b1f1a4ed4f2d8a08ba584af02da1</data>
      <data key="d12">17888</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="DIARRHEA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Diarrhea is a common symptom experienced by individuals with lactose intolerance after consuming lactose.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">2df842531e1148a79fb47f0351d3080c</data>
      <data key="d12">17889</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="ABDOMINAL PAIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Abdominal pain is frequently reported by individuals suffering from lactose intolerance after lactose consumption.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">de492d625d804a9da007024fcc9285dd</data>
      <data key="d12">17890</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="METEORISM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Meteorism is a symptom that often accompanies lactose intolerance due to the fermentation of undigested lactose in the gut.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">6b65f1bda749471c94d1a0855075e8a6</data>
      <data key="d12">17891</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="LACTOSE ELIMINATION DIET">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The lactose elimination diet is a diagnostic approach to confirm lactose intolerance by observing symptom changes.</data>
      <data key="d10">c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">535460a37803419ca4b9bd8902dfdd63</data>
      <data key="d12">17892</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="HYDROGEN BREATH TEST">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance is a condition characterized by the inability to properly digest lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. The hydrogen breath test is a common diagnostic tool used to identify and confirm the presence of lactose intolerance. This test measures the levels of hydrogen in the breath after the ingestion of lactose. Elevated breath hydrogen levels indicate that lactose is not being adequately digested, thus confirming lactose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5,c43f12d9be878da7ceb2074808ca7922</data>
      <data key="d11">811bb5a5d3e4434aa03ccccc987dfce4</data>
      <data key="d12">17893</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="BIOPSY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A biopsy is performed to confirm the diagnosis of lactose intolerance by assessing the presence of lactase activity.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5</data>
      <data key="d11">3bf58bb8f112460f9960616ddc3ab6f7</data>
      <data key="d12">17894</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="DIET WITHOUT LACTOSE">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A diet without lactose is essential for managing symptoms of lactose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5</data>
      <data key="d11">f918465f0dc64113a67ffd0be366ef11</data>
      <data key="d12">17895</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="LACTASE">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactase deficiency is the primary cause of lactose intolerance, as it prevents the digestion of lactose.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b7850cb85e0e94111aee2530619ffc5</data>
      <data key="d11">4011957f4d6b404299b9973b79db60f9</data>
      <data key="d12">17896</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="GARCIA-PERIS P">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Garcia-Peris P has authored recommendations related to nutrition for individuals with lactose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d10">e3203d9f5bd82749de9eee35c52c67ce</data>
      <data key="d11">caccf580cc074ab49fbeeb9483314a20</data>
      <data key="d12">17897</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="MART&#205;NEZ AUGUST&#205;N">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Mart&#237;nez August&#237;n has contributed to the understanding of carbohydrate metabolism, which is relevant to lactose intolerance.</data>
      <data key="d10">e3203d9f5bd82749de9eee35c52c67ce</data>
      <data key="d11">b25ebb552e0a43fba1ab0eb4b09f990e</data>
      <data key="d12">17898</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="ALLERGIES">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance is a specific type of food allergy that affects a portion of the population</data>
      <data key="d10">fa4851ce095f27e98350dcb826e5b09c</data>
      <data key="d11">a62cadd71e61415f83788ed3f6944fa2</data>
      <data key="d12">17899</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LACTOSE INTOLERANCE" target="FOOD ALLERGY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lactose intolerance and food allergy are both conditions that can cause gastrointestinal symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">bfb5dadab0c08f9f5f549ddd4b5db30c</data>
      <data key="d11">3a725499f310409a8e48f46511b5539d</data>
      <data key="d12">17900</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CELIAC DISEASE" target="ARETAEUS DE CAPADOCIA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
