      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PAH" target="TERAPIA G&#201;NICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The PAH gene is the target of gene therapy for patients with PKU, aiming to restore the function of the deficient enzyme.</data>
      <data key="d10">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027</data>
      <data key="d11">20994bd360184da5a0ff7ac88bd258c1</data>
      <data key="d12">18343</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PAH" target="HIDROXILACI&#211;N DE PHE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The hydroxylation of phenylalanine is catalyzed by the PAH enzyme, which is deficient in PKU patients.</data>
      <data key="d10">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027</data>
      <data key="d11">08252d9ca5054d089a7512e87a7e7ac3</data>
      <data key="d12">18344</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PKU" target="LNAA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">LNAA is a therapeutic option for managing PKU, particularly for patients with poor dietary adherence.</data>
      <data key="d10">06b374fc6a6ebf2091ac0a00329bd027</data>
      <data key="d11">c75d1d17e71b4a109e30906b30d9e884</data>
