    <edge source="BCAA" target="MSUD">
      <data key="d8">17.0</data>
      <data key="d9">BCAA, or branched-chain amino acids, are essential in the dietary management of patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD). This condition is characterized by the poor metabolism of these specific amino acids, which include leucine, isoleucine, and valine. Therefore, understanding the relationship between BCAA and MSUD is crucial, as the effective management of MSUD relies on addressing the metabolic challenges associated with these amino acids.</data>
