    <edge source="N-ACETILGLUTAMATO SINTETASA" target="CARBAMILFOSFATO SINTETASA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">N-acetilglutamato sintetasa (NAGS) is involved in the regulation of carbamilfosfato sintetasa (CPS) activity in the urea cycle</data>
      <data key="d10">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a</data>
      <data key="d11">a7c6e9826dbe4d42931424d0feb17d0a</data>
      <data key="d12">18411</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARBAMILFOSFATO SINTETASA" target="ORNIT&#205;N TRANSACARBAMILASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Carbamilfosfato sintetasa (CPS) produces carbamoyl phosphate, which is a substrate for ornit&#237;n transcarbamilasa (OTS) in the urea cycle</data>
      <data key="d10">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a</data>
      <data key="d11">6043b08de0b349cdb2ce690a56f52366</data>
      <data key="d12">18412</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ORNIT&#205;N TRANSACARBAMILASA" target="ARGINOSUCCINATO SINTETASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ornit&#237;n transcarbamilasa (OTS) produces citrulline, which is then used by arginosuccinato sintetasa (ASS) in the urea cycle</data>
      <data key="d10">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a</data>
      <data key="d11">b0a8004ee4b749f7a1a9b377eca38f46</data>
      <data key="d12">18413</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGINOSUCCINATO SINTETASA" target="ARGINOSUCCINATO LIASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginosuccinato sintetasa (ASS) produces argininosuccinate, which is then converted to arginine by arginosuccinato liasa (ASL)</data>
      <data key="d10">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a</data>
      <data key="d11">9d6314713fbf41808fe1e212ba21b121</data>
      <data key="d12">18414</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARGINOSUCCINATO LIASA" target="ARGINASA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Arginosuccinato liasa (ASL) produces arginine, which is then hydrolyzed by arginasa (ASA) to produce urea</data>
      <data key="d10">0487e1a4525547575a1d284297280f9a</data>
      <data key="d11">a4109e3ed0664bbf9be507f8f2086da6</data>
      <data key="d12">18415</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
