    <edge source="ACEITE DE LORENZO" target="ADRENOLEUCOMIELOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo no detiene la progresi&#243;n de la adrenoleucomielopat&#237;a en estados avanzados</data>
      <data key="d10">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d11">6b84d14aba0d4309b4c00589a63f4dd9</data>
      <data key="d12">18544</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACEITE DE LORENZO" target="PACIENTES ASINTOM&#193;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes asintom&#225;ticos pueden beneficiarse del tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo</data>
      <data key="d10">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d11">e1e26055180a4540a33b1fbd0ebbc1d4</data>
      <data key="d12">18545</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACEITE DE LORENZO" target="PACIENTES CON DISFUNCI&#211;N ADRENAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes con disfunci&#243;n adrenal pueden no ver mejoras con el tratamiento de aceite de Lorenzo</data>
      <data key="d10">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d11">ed1b1b69ce9d42c2aaeec76cdee95812</data>
      <data key="d12">18546</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACEITE DE LORENZO" target="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Aceite de Lorenzo is used as a treatment for Adrenoleukodystrophy to manage fatty acid levels</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">309d52acd69446b989bd2436229ea131</data>
      <data key="d12">18547</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="C26:0" target="NIVEL PLASM&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Plasma levels of C26:0 are monitored to assess the effectiveness of treatments for ALD</data>
      <data key="d10">015189b6c6e12a45665ac4c614da79c9</data>
      <data key="d11">e2595b781f73419b846f0be6923128b9</data>
      <data key="d12">18548</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUCOMIELOPAT&#205;A" target="TRASPLANTE DE M&#201;DULA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El trasplante de m&#233;dula &#243;sea se ha realizado en algunos casos de adrenoleucomielopat&#237;a, aunque su eficacia es cuestionable</data>
      <data key="d10">9aa00ebb9b33b958c9956b7859eb11d8</data>
      <data key="d11">e2475e90cdcd4b1eb624534dae68e6e0</data>
      <data key="d12">18549</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TRASPLANTE DE M&#201;DULA &#211;SEA" target="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone marrow transplant is a treatment considered for patients with neurological involvement in Adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">8268efc893f744fdb7b99c6132964d4f</data>
      <data key="d12">18550</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INMUNOGLOBULINAS" target="SISTEMA LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las inmunoglobulinas se encuentran en el quilo y son transportadas por el sistema linf&#225;tico.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7</data>
      <data key="d11">6d38ca5042b049df91dea2be6026f4a0</data>
      <data key="d12">18551</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="INMUNOGLOBULINAS" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Immunoglobulin levels may be altered in patients with quilot&#243;rax, affecting their immune response and susceptibility to infections.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">3f2c0de4835e4c4789a180192b8fda92</data>
      <data key="d12">18552</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S&#205;NDROME REYE-LIKE" target="AGCL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El s&#237;ndrome Reye-like puede ser causado por alteraciones en la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n de los &#225;cidos grasos de cadena larga (AGCL)</data>
      <data key="d10">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079</data>
      <data key="d11">31a3b461c1d74d07a17d882804aaff52</data>
      <data key="d12">18553</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOGLOCEMIA" target="TRASTORNOS METAB&#211;LICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoglucemia puede ser un s&#237;ntoma de trastornos metab&#243;licos, especialmente en aquellos relacionados con la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079</data>
      <data key="d11">ff1b1febba964038a4a84ce2b65a3728</data>
      <data key="d12">18554</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROPAT&#205;A" target="TRASTORNOS METAB&#211;LICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La neuropat&#237;a puede ser un s&#237;ntoma de trastornos metab&#243;licos, incluyendo alteraciones en la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079</data>
      <data key="d11">e9751a91347b4f3c9941314ec1451148</data>
      <data key="d12">18555</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEUROPAT&#205;A" target="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Neuropathy can occur as a result of Adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">c58e1f8b7d464deaa095ec3d40a48826</data>
      <data key="d12">18556</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARRITMIAS CARD&#205;ACAS" target="TRASTORNOS METAB&#211;LICOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las arritmias card&#237;acas pueden ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado a trastornos metab&#243;licos que afectan la &#946;-oxidaci&#243;n</data>
      <data key="d10">2f96bbc5eafd39b659620da7282a2079</data>
      <data key="d11">e5b82ae1b6b949a0ad131f7e2f186277</data>
      <data key="d12">18557</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ARRITMIAS CARD&#205;ACAS" target="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleukodystrophy may lead to cardiac arrhythmias as a symptom</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">704ea452c1aa43c084bd694ee53b01d2</data>
      <data key="d12">18558</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TCM" target="TCL">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCM and TCL are both types of triglycerides that differ in their chain length and metabolic properties. TCM, or medium-chain triglycerides, are utilized by TCL in its dietary modifications and nutritional supplementation programs. This indicates that TCL incorporates TCM to enhance its nutritional strategies, leveraging the unique characteristics of medium-chain triglycerides for improved dietary outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375,3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">5be976f6f2a347d0954a68b270f1ac74</data>
      <data key="d12">18559</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TCM" target="DIETA MODIFICADA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The modified diet incorporates TCM as a suitable supplement for reducing dietary fat</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">a3aa60a24716459a876362257c81c14b</data>
      <data key="d12">18560</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TCM" target="TCL INTRALIPID">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCM is introduced in lipid emulsions to reduce the intake of omega-6 fatty acids, which are present in TCL Intralipid</data>
      <data key="d10">87da0f3b46604498629565db45667b3b</data>
      <data key="d11">7d5336c577504de7a1d41765a0908e12</data>
      <data key="d12">18561</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TCL" target="DIETA MODIFICADA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The modified diet restricts the intake of TCL to manage fat consumption</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02</data>
      <data key="d11">89865c5c2ca14c34b42399df6f7efaf1</data>
      <data key="d12">18562</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TCL" target="ALIMENTARY SUPPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">TCL promotes nutritional supplementation with TCM as part of its dietary strategies</data>
      <data key="d10">347e3d175ef7f30e3dcad731f84fb375</data>
      <data key="d11">f013730ca09d444e9d170c18940916f8</data>
      <data key="d12">18563</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="&#193;CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA MUY LARGA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleukodystrophy involves the accumulation of very long-chain fatty acids, which are restricted in the diet</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">8606e5ce445344b6b2b50bb000cdedf6</data>
      <data key="d12">18564</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="TRASTORNOS DE LA &#914;-OXIDACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleukodystrophy is classified under disorders of &#946;-oxidation of fatty acids</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">c2e0d7da1f5c4165be43412b66648390</data>
      <data key="d12">18565</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="HIPOGLUCEMIA NO CET&#211;SICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleukodystrophy can lead to symptoms such as hypoglycemia non-ketotic</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">ff2603c9f37b4033b3d3c2b0d6dd843d</data>
      <data key="d12">18566</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="MIOTOPAT&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenoleukodystrophy may present with myopathy as a symptom</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">f72f1be825124c0fa5e57d79940d423f</data>
      <data key="d12">18567</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="AGENTES ANTIINFLAMATORIOS">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Anti-inflammatory agents have been explored for their potential role in treating Adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">c4abdcd9f1628aa02ca6ed662b795fd6</data>
      <data key="d11">94bcff8bc77f46d1b4d181215aeccc04</data>
      <data key="d12">18568</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="ADRENOMYELONEUROPATHY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Adrenomyeloneuropathy is a condition that is often associated with adrenoleukodystrophy, sharing similar pathophysiological features</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">40e123c8f9bc43e68daf89db9c8df019</data>
      <data key="d12">18569</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="LORENZO'S OIL">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lorenzo's Oil is a treatment specifically designed for managing adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">23aefbd3628944cdbc15b692aeb7b36a</data>
      <data key="d12">18570</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="MOSER HW">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Moser HW has conducted significant research on adrenoleukodystrophy, contributing to its understanding and treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">46222d71f23c4ce1a55abf9b47d5887d</data>
      <data key="d12">18571</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="RIZZO WB">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Rizzo WB has published research related to the fatty acid abnormalities in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">18fcafc8104745ddb07f0cc2d1207221</data>
      <data key="d12">18572</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="JOHN HOPKINS MEDICAL JOURNAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">John Hopkins Med J publishes research articles that include studies on adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">78cbc1e5465d4ea0bfca6c2d1acf16fb</data>
      <data key="d12">18573</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="FATTY ACID ABNORMALITY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fatty acid abnormality is a key characteristic of adrenoleukodystrophy, indicating the disorder's metabolic impact</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">a41ea7df37494f6a9de595eab38cf9a0</data>
      <data key="d12">18574</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone marrow transplantation is considered an effective treatment for central nervous system disease in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">d3ebe7cad7a1416ea3ca50e3b4bda9e8</data>
      <data key="d12">18575</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="KISHIMOTO Y">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kishimoto Y has researched fatty acid abnormalities specifically in the context of adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">99c8365266c841a7aa524f76f6632c26</data>
      <data key="d12">18576</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADRENOLEUKODYSTROPHY" target="VAN DUYN MA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Van Duyn MA has conducted research on dietary therapies aimed at treating adrenoleukodystrophy</data>
      <data key="d10">05d06d6f7343640e80cb10fe00c9353f</data>
      <data key="d11">6d018b65f5384d348bbe8577b69af53d</data>
      <data key="d12">18577</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION" target="TUMORES HEMATOL&#211;GICOS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone marrow transplantation is often used as a treatment for hematological tumors</data>
      <data key="d10">c7577b8eccf83ced48f5ecf36717b4e1</data>
      <data key="d11">d9a030638ebd48619463aaeb2be2a863</data>
      <data key="d12">18578</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION" target="HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANTATION">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone Marrow Transplantation journal publishes research specifically related to hematopoietic stem cell transplantation</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd686507e25374444e2e7525a5aacf4</data>
      <data key="d11">dfbe2bf0084741ed8516cd51c0521e87</data>
      <data key="d12">18579</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BONE MARROW TRANSPLANTATION" target="HAEMATOLOGICAL MALIGNANCIES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone marrow transplantation is a common treatment for patients with hematological malignancies.</data>
      <data key="d10">6efaddddefe1cf5ab78825e1d8c53cab</data>
      <data key="d11">29f45fb01f38451b86a100bb52d6fe8d</data>
      <data key="d12">18580</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="ASCITIS QUILOSA">
      <data key="d8">30.0</data>
      <data key="d9">QUILOT&#211;RAX and ASCITIS QUILOSA are medical conditions that involve the accumulation of chyle, a type of lymphatic fluid, in different body cavities. Both conditions are related to the lymphatic system and can arise from similar underlying issues. Specifically, quilot&#243;rax refers to the accumulation of this fluid in the pleural cavity, while ascitis quilosa involves its accumulation in the abdominal cavity. These conditions often require similar treatment approaches due to their related nature and the underlying mechanisms that lead to the accumulation of lymphatic fluid.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,ba4a819ecea2015fc907ed907767f6c5,c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">1a90b7f9e33647f49476a36893856fca</data>
      <data key="d12">18581</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="CONDUCTO TOR&#193;CICO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El quilot&#243;rax puede ser causado por la lesi&#243;n del conducto tor&#225;cico, resultando en la acumulaci&#243;n de quilo en la cavidad pleural.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7</data>
      <data key="d11">e4d0738cb6864408a97e3ff5cadf2cf0</data>
      <data key="d12">18582</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="TORACOCENTESIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La toracocentesis es un procedimiento utilizado para diagnosticar y tratar el quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">2b633a954bb44ec9ac2a7e71a3be2ab0</data>
      <data key="d12">18583</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="DERRAME PLEURAL">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">El derrame pleural puede ser un s&#237;ntoma asociado al quilot&#243;rax, ya que ambos involucran la acumulaci&#243;n de l&#237;quido en cavidades corporales.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">bbcefcb614f2459f918667e98ccbd757</data>
      <data key="d12">18584</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="T&#201;CNICAS DE IMAGEN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Las t&#233;cnicas de imagen son utilizadas para diagnosticar y localizar el quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">2564a67e3da74530be5e2ee6fdc47a7d</data>
      <data key="d12">18585</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="LINFOGRAF&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La linfograf&#237;a puede ser utilizada para evaluar el sistema linf&#225;tico en casos de quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">ee92503decd144b3bcb67227d1398db2</data>
      <data key="d12">18586</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="SISTEMA LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The lymphatic system is directly involved in the development of quilot&#243;rax, as it is the system from which the fluid accumulates in the pleural cavity.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">88dad3f3e63849ad807a5ff2d6e9c346</data>
      <data key="d12">18587</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="LINFOCITOS T">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The presence of T lymphocytes is crucial for the immune response in patients with quilot&#243;rax, as they help mediate cellular immunity.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">bc3942a7d76341fcb161cf25e7b0c9d6</data>
      <data key="d12">18588</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="LINFOCITOS B">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">B lymphocytes play a role in the immune response in patients with quilot&#243;rax, producing antibodies to fight infections.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">1a4b7d84140d4028a489dd67bdd934aa</data>
      <data key="d12">18589</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR">
      <data key="d8">20.0</data>
      <data key="d9">QUILOT&#211;RAX, also known as chylothorax, is a condition that can be effectively managed through TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR, or conservative treatment. This approach is typically the first line of management for quilot&#243;rax, aiming to achieve resolution without the need for surgical intervention. The conservative treatment strategy focuses on reducing lymphatic flow and managing symptoms, which may include dietary changes and various medical therapies. By implementing these measures, healthcare providers seek to alleviate the condition while minimizing the risks associated with more invasive procedures.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">dd06f615fb5f4bef81072ddbeb7c8f5d</data>
      <data key="d12">18590</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="TRATAMIENTO FARMACOL&#211;GICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pharmacological treatment is used to manage symptoms and complications associated with quilot&#243;rax, helping to control fluid accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">b79f0d588f514e7c8a2cf0a497b73ddf</data>
      <data key="d12">18591</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX ASOCIADO A TUMOR">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Quilot&#243;rax associated with a tumor indicates a specific type of quilot&#243;rax that has implications for prognosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">bc19fe8d0bda40efb855708f7cda6dcb</data>
      <data key="d12">18592</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="DIETA MODIFICADA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">QUILOT&#211;RAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural space. As part of the conservative treatment for quilot&#243;rax, a modified diet is recommended to help manage this fluid accumulation. This modified diet focuses on regulating fat intake, which may assist in managing the condition effectively. By adhering to this dietary approach, patients may experience improved outcomes in the management of quilot&#243;rax.</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">d8e8a6895e834fa78de46c899637a46a</data>
      <data key="d12">18593</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="OCTREOTIDA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">QUILOT&#211;RAX, also known as chylothorax, is a condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural space. OCTREOTIDA, or octreotide, is a medication that is administered in conjunction with dietary modifications to manage quilot&#243;rax effectively. It plays a crucial role in improving clinical outcomes for patients by reducing lymphatic flow, thereby contributing to the resolution of the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">c689f3a2f42a4d3797de1b8f0147669c</data>
      <data key="d12">18594</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="ETILNEFRINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Etilnefrina is used to reduce lymphatic flow in the thoracic duct, which can be beneficial in managing chylothorax.</data>
      <data key="d10">b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">2f9fc6e4d8c7464289022f47cb3647fa</data>
      <data key="d12">18595</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="TRATAMIENTO QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Surgical treatment is indicated for patients with chylothorax who do not respond to conservative management.</data>
      <data key="d10">b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">6374aa43c6c34b3b8bfc3fe8c527c786</data>
      <data key="d12">18596</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="EMBOLIZACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Embolization is a treatment method that can be applied to quilot&#243;rax, showing high success rates in traumatic cases</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">701d6a029e144f0bbc3c656095de680e</data>
      <data key="d12">18597</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="QUILOT&#211;RAX" target="F&#205;STULAS QUILOSAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Quilot&#243;rax can lead to the development of f&#237;stulas quilosas, which may complicate the condition and require additional treatment</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">819951b7510e4e669d4fcdad9e0aca55</data>
      <data key="d12">18598</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="CONDUCTO TOR&#193;CICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La ascitis quilosa puede resultar de la ruptura u obstrucci&#243;n de los conductos linf&#225;ticos abdominales, que incluye el conducto tor&#225;cico.</data>
      <data key="d10">0f2aa9d202fbabe2b0f310000e6987e7</data>
      <data key="d11">5dd1250583d349e5927ecc8a4e0a6281</data>
      <data key="d12">18599</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="CARCINOMATOSIS PERITONEAL">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Peritoneal carcinomatosis can lead to ascitis quilosa as a complication</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">593fd9c24d3f41739f30076122cc5d78</data>
      <data key="d12">18600</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="QUILOT&#211;RAX CONG&#201;NITO">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Congenital chylothorax and ascitis quilosa are both conditions involving the accumulation of chyle</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">c79ec7fc93b945909dbb86122c3f4794</data>
      <data key="d12">18601</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="SARCOMA DE KAPOSI">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Kaposi's sarcoma can lead to ascitis quilosa as a complication of the disease</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">9cda8d1a529447cd9e7f583f6979f594</data>
      <data key="d12">18602</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="AMILOIDOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Amyloidosis can result in ascitis quilosa due to organ dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">560d3205dba64169b0694331d748d8f7</data>
      <data key="d12">18603</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="LINFANGIOLEIOMATOSIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Lymphangioleiomyomatosis can lead to complications that may result in ascitis quilosa</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">a408379c5cd64102a6c7ac97be1d783d</data>
      <data key="d12">18604</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="TROMBOSIS VENA SUBCLAVIA IZQUIERDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Thrombosis of the left subclavian vein can affect lymphatic drainage, potentially leading to ascitis quilosa</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">e273d0b96e52453dafb4f3eae9687e1c</data>
      <data key="d12">18605</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="BOCIO ENDOTOR&#193;CICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Endothoracic goiter can obstruct lymphatic flow, contributing to ascitis quilosa</data>
      <data key="d10">c77caafffd9b5d42c51cb2359ad9cc6d</data>
      <data key="d11">b1a132669df94aabb5a8f22bd7796d8c</data>
      <data key="d12">18606</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="PARACENTESIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La paracentesis es un procedimiento utilizado para diagnosticar y tratar la ascitis quilosa.</data>
      <data key="d10">8d4057f6ab3a5d00b2ae7609742cdf86</data>
      <data key="d11">db5b5b75f27447ab95308633c58b17b1</data>
      <data key="d12">18607</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="SISTEMA LINF&#193;TICO">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The lymphatic system is directly involved in the development of ascitis quilosa, as it is the system from which the fluid accumulates in the abdominal cavity.</data>
      <data key="d10">6bbb4df989ed7353f621a7d44dbc7972</data>
      <data key="d11">310ba6b7a7f44edc9d950e09ed703902</data>
      <data key="d12">18608</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="DIETA MODIFICADA">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">ASCITIS QUILOSA is a condition that can be managed conservatively through the implementation of a modified diet, referred to as DIETA MODIFICADA. This diet is specifically designed to reduce fat intake, which is crucial for controlling dietary fat absorption. By adhering to this modified diet, individuals with ascitis quilosa can effectively support their nutritional needs while also addressing the condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">3c2bb3d9d6534668e58f571710c9bb02,ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">dba497ca54e34b6198e3224c6e709e1c</data>
      <data key="d12">18609</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ascitis quilosa, also known as chylous ascites, is a condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the abdominal cavity. The management of ascitis quilosa primarily involves conservative treatment strategies. This approach emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies aimed at resolving the condition without the need for invasive procedures. By focusing on these non-invasive methods, conservative treatment seeks to effectively manage chylous ascites and promote recovery.</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16,b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">1aff72536a5a4a05ac65af973e16199e</data>
      <data key="d12">18610</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="TRATAMIENTO QUIR&#218;RGICO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Surgical treatment may be necessary for refractory cases of chylous ascites when conservative measures fail.</data>
      <data key="d10">b55a8ca77c67f4c18eea7abe52c3d2f9</data>
      <data key="d11">b3ba1e6bcbf94278b2a020042fa0ec39</data>
      <data key="d12">18611</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="OCTREOTIDA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Octreotide is used in the treatment of ascitis quilosa, often in combination with dietary modifications</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">f07dca5ed3fc45f2a4ff0700349be5fd</data>
      <data key="d12">18612</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ASCITIS QUILOSA" target="F&#205;STULAS QUILOSAS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ascitis quilosa can also result in the formation of f&#237;stulas quilosas, necessitating further medical intervention</data>
      <data key="d10">ae05ce71cf124553fea10e6c602f8d16</data>
      <data key="d11">c1455ff54dd3441986bc261a33d185f0</data>
      <data key="d12">18613</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
