    </edge>
    <edge source="CUPROENZIMAS" target="SUPER&#211;XIDO DISMUTASA">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">CUPROENZIMAS refers to a group of enzymes that include SUPER&#211;XIDO DISMUTASA, which is a specific type of cuproenzyme. The activity of cuproenzyme is essential for the proper functioning of superoxide dismutase, which plays a vital role in protecting cells from oxidative stress. Superoxide dismutase, as a cuproenzyme, helps mitigate the damaging effects of reactive oxygen species, thereby contributing to cellular health and stability.</data>
      <data key="d10">78482a90281ee54a4aac11bb36bd6e36,d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">c733cb944cf940359f4e7b18ba9564db</data>
      <data key="d12">18852</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CUPROENZIMAS" target="NEUROTRANSMISORES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cuproenzyme activity influences the metabolism of neurotransmitters in the nervous system</data>
      <data key="d10">d2916698f201a31d6bb74619a3fa064b</data>
      <data key="d11">80983ca668e64266a6bcb778883b80c2</data>
      <data key="d12">18853</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CUPROENZIMAS" target="DIAMINOOXIDASA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
