    <edge source="HIPOXANTINA" target="XANTINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La hipoxantina se convierte en xantina durante el metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">c69dd5fd5daf4eaea811031171039632</data>
      <data key="d12">18910</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOXANTINA" target="GUANINA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">HIPOXANTINA and GUANINA are closely related entities involved in purine metabolism. HIPOXANTINA converts guanosine into GUANINA, highlighting its crucial role in this metabolic pathway. Additionally, it is noted that HIPOXANTINA is transformed into GUANINA during the process of purine metabolism. This relationship underscores the importance of HIPOXANTINA in the synthesis and regulation of purine nucleotides.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">1ef7553b0a2043a48c7d7828dcd23e91</data>
      <data key="d12">18911</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOXANTINA" target="ADENOSINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La adenosina se desamina para formar inosina, que se convierte en hipoxantina durante el metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">a674cae9106a416bae88d386739294d0</data>
      <data key="d12">18912</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIPOXANTINA" target="NUCLE&#211;SIDO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los nucle&#243;sidos como la adenosina y guanosina se convierten en hipoxantina durante el metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">1f2e0ac2abcf4ed2834a339e080c63ca</data>
      <data key="d12">18913</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUANINA" target="XANTINA">
      <data key="d8">14.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Guanina is a purine nucleotide that is degraded into xantina as part of the purine degradation pathway. This process is an essential aspect of purine metabolism, where guanina is converted into xantina.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6,ab93481c5db482b6da2462b4687e4313</data>
      <data key="d11">3b5ab8749c304e588a7915e6314d1744</data>
      <data key="d12">18914</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUANINA" target="GUANOSINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La guanosina se convierte en guanina durante el metabolismo de las purinas.</data>
      <data key="d10">869a4bbc356ac84d0b4ed76c5f7a64b6</data>
      <data key="d11">4372696013b3400cbb8e816aadbd5b0e</data>
      <data key="d12">18915</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
