    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="INGLATERRA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Inglaterra tiene una incidencia anual de fallo intestinal tipo II, lo que indica la relevancia de esta condici&#243;n en la poblaci&#243;n.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">3f1b5a1f6b8741078eb1b6325af51a80</data>
      <data key="d12">19140</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="DEHISCENCIA DE SUTURAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dehiscencia de suturas puede resultar en la aparici&#243;n de f&#237;stulas, contribuyendo al fallo intestinal tipo II.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">273ee7882f1a4d48b10198670bcc9442</data>
      <data key="d12">19141</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="TRAUMATISMOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los traumatismos pueden causar fallo intestinal tipo II al requerir resecciones intestinales extensas.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">660a2de2cb09463087a3883b6219cbd9</data>
      <data key="d12">19142</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="ISQUEMIA INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La isquemia intestinal es una de las causas que puede llevar al fallo intestinal tipo II.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">100b66b368d5428baf0989d427d8946b</data>
      <data key="d12">19143</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="F&#205;STULA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La aparici&#243;n de f&#237;stulas puede ser una complicaci&#243;n del fallo intestinal tipo II.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">48396e2aede0435f80e1af16b135fe0a</data>
      <data key="d12">19144</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="OBSTRUCCI&#211;N MEC&#193;NICA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La obstrucci&#243;n mec&#225;nica puede contribuir al desarrollo de fallo intestinal tipo II.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">e6681d7be2214461ab777d08d853b14e</data>
      <data key="d12">19145</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="ENFERMEDAD EXTENSA DE LA MUCOSA">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad extensa de la mucosa puede ser un factor que contribuya al fallo intestinal tipo II.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">e3081c1043e44152b57f9553fce08c7d</data>
      <data key="d12">19146</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FALLO INTESTINAL TIPO II" target="DISMOTILIDAD INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dismotilidad intestinal puede ser una causa del fallo intestinal tipo II, afectando la funci&#243;n intestinal.</data>
      <data key="d10">998342e0e27f4902274d51c0658d2f17</data>
      <data key="d11">84ca89504bb743dfb887767cc4444385</data>
      <data key="d12">19147</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ISQUEMIA INTESTINAL" target="PACIENTES CR&#205;TICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los pacientes cr&#237;ticos pueden experimentar isquemia intestinal como una complicaci&#243;n de la nutrici&#243;n enteral.</data>
      <data key="d10">4bf9e20e18b101e95ebd6a9ca591fc54</data>
      <data key="d11">b062670b230443e1a63ac39c4b8aed55</data>
      <data key="d12">19148</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POIC" target="ENFERMEDAD DE HIRSCHSPRUNG">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La enfermedad de Hirschsprung puede llevar a complicaciones que resultan en la necesidad de tratamientos como la nutrici&#243;n parenteral, similar a lo que ocurre en la POIC</data>
      <data key="d10">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d11">4df2b289bd1049a2a16444726671f198</data>
      <data key="d12">19149</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POIC" target="VIRUS NEUROTROPOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Los virus neurotropos han sido implicados en la etiolog&#237;a de la POIC, sugiriendo una relaci&#243;n entre estas condiciones</data>
      <data key="d10">4dff41ef8e80b9381bc674195671c430</data>
      <data key="d11">3325d34659794eaf8ec54f3bad11bcd5</data>
      <data key="d12">19150</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POIC" target="CINE-RM">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cine-RM is a new diagnostic technique being explored for use in diagnosing POIC</data>
      <data key="d10">3d03390859575cc2ead8aa5f917d0066</data>
      <data key="d11">e81a0a6410ab4c75841f1cff7f1e352c</data>
      <data key="d12">19151</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POIC" target="FEC">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Both conditions require careful nutritional management and may involve similar treatment approaches</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">3f51e6e2aaeb444587bfc61957189f33</data>
      <data key="d12">19152</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POIC" target="DILATACI&#211;N INTESTINAL">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">La dilataci&#243;n intestinal es una complicaci&#243;n que puede presentarse en pacientes con POIC.</data>
      <data key="d10">eb8fe6b54f7eab9cbe7b90c53e7007ed</data>
      <data key="d11">b3482e0a4b3543da848551341415e366</data>
      <data key="d12">19153</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ADAPTATION" target="CHILDREN">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Children also exhibit a notable capacity for intestinal adaptation, which is important for their growth and health post-surgery</data>
      <data key="d10">4ada21f24df8df18dbc05f5619c0a368</data>
      <data key="d11">f3b920d95f6b4e0b97b9148ef5a18e15</data>
      <data key="d12">19154</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANATOMY" target="VENOUS ACCESS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Understanding anatomy is crucial for successful venous access procedures</data>
      <data key="d10">3d5e0a3ef45c7ba15063791545dc4826</data>
      <data key="d11">283513e5232d4f2883bf313a917a6ceb</data>
      <data key="d12">19155</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="SUSRUTA">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Susruta's historical contributions to the treatment of FEC highlight the long-standing medical practices in managing this condition.</data>
      <data key="d10">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d11">0dd004a5d8894818b3f539f97a63c949</data>
      <data key="d12">19156</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="DRENAJES">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Drainage management is essential in the treatment of patients with FEC to monitor fluid loss and prevent complications.</data>
      <data key="d10">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d11">e5a2fc49642c44ada7643bab37bfa1f3</data>
      <data key="d12">19157</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="ALTERACIONES NUTRICIONALES">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Nutritional alterations are prevalent in patients with FEC and significantly impact their health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d10">c031cb3bc7513b4a3f8e4f264c00a675</data>
      <data key="d11">65b245b480414445957fe9ff0d186b2e</data>
      <data key="d12">19158</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="SUCRALFATO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sucralfate is used in the treatment regimen for patients with FEC</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">b469574d848a402c9b68e4c913451962</data>
      <data key="d12">19159</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="OCTRE&#211;TIDO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Octreotide is used in the management of high-output fistulas in patients with FEC</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">f020e1c7314943de8ebd3cf183cc441d</data>
      <data key="d12">19160</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="D&#201;BITO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The output from a fistula (d&#233;bito) is a critical factor in managing FEC</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">3318d556dff443f2b2812f9a759eb512</data>
      <data key="d12">19161</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="DIETA POBRE EN RESIDUOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">A low-residue diet is recommended for patients with FEC when the output is less than 1.5 l/day</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">d5b3e05eb9fb4d39855e699317dc5456</data>
      <data key="d12">19162</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="SOLUCI&#211;N DE REHIDRATACI&#211;N ORAL ISOT&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Oral rehydration solutions are recommended for patients with high output from fistulas</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">d302cec0093c4b0795e8063752aff9b6</data>
      <data key="d12">19163</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FEC" target="FISTULACLISIS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Fistulaclisis is a technique used to manage nutritional needs in patients with FEC</data>
      <data key="d10">e5838e52fbc5d3d18fc0533b71148201</data>
      <data key="d11">110b215251af495fb5a0af4634decedc</data>
      <data key="d12">19164</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GATORADE" target="SUERORAL">
      <data key="d8">4.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Gatorade is often compared to Sueroral in discussions about hydration solutions</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">1ccf95cbd9c34654aca946319500f661</data>
      <data key="d12">19165</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUERORAL" target="SUERORAL HIPOS&#211;DICO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Sueroral hipos&#243;dico is a variation of Sueroral with lower sodium content</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">b9529269e7354314884ee5032f5fe11f</data>
      <data key="d12">19166</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CAPSULA DE CLORURO SODICO" target="LIQUIDOS ISOTONICOS">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The sodium chloride capsule is recommended to be taken with isotonic liquids to help manage sodium levels</data>
      <data key="d10">d9948a6c321263db8a8d220a4d079379</data>
      <data key="d11">c8f5a5555e4c4682ae1db65c925654f2</data>
      <data key="d12">19167</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES CON FALLA INTESTINAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N HYPERF&#193;GICA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercaloric diets are often recommended for patients with intestinal failure to meet their energy needs</data>
      <data key="d10">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d11">4eebed2b8ecb468596e1a32801a244b4</data>
      <data key="d12">19168</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES CON FALLA INTESTINAL" target="NUTRICI&#211;N POLIM&#201;RICA">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Polymeric nutrition is used for patients with some digestive capacity to help meet their nutritional requirements</data>
      <data key="d10">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d11">636d7d3bbb7347de9bd25a187bddaf81</data>
      <data key="d12">19169</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PACIENTES CON FALLA INTESTINAL" target="DIETA ELEMENTAL">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Elemental diets may be considered for patients with severe malabsorption to facilitate nutrient absorption</data>
      <data key="d10">f5a758425c5e471b0421d16558001d59</data>
      <data key="d11">1dae3b62e23f44229acd97135f03208a</data>
      <data key="d12">19170</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DANIEL DRUCKER" target="TEDUGLUTIDA">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Daniel Drucker is the scientist who discovered and characterized GLP-2, which is the basis for the drug teduglutida</data>
      <data key="d10">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d11">ee7f9e2d77f2426283684fd674e5e91e</data>
      <data key="d12">19171</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TEDUGLUTIDA" target="OCTREOTIDO">
      <data key="d8">5.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Octreotide is used in conjunction with teduglutida for managing high output in patients with jejunostomy</data>
      <data key="d10">e0196a8a0ead0a27b38ddfb16a5c5772</data>
      <data key="d11">4865fac1eb4a4c54a42ea3762c353b91</data>
      <data key="d12">19172</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TEDUGLUTIDA" target="ADENOMAS DE COLON">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
