    <edge source="BRONQUIECTASIAS" target="EPOC">
      <data key="d8">15.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bronchiectasis and Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (EPOC) are both respiratory conditions that significantly impact lung function and necessitate dietary management for affected patients. There is a causal relationship between the two, as EPOC can lead to the development of bronchiectasis. Furthermore, it has been observed that more than 50% of patients with moderate to severe EPOC also present with associated bronchiectasis. This highlights the interconnectedness of these conditions and the importance of comprehensive management strategies for individuals suffering from them.</data>
      <data key="d10">bede549235c80e5de32a793f3c456a22,cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf,d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d11">6765c9dce0ac4c28b55cf22a350e9d1c</data>
      <data key="d12">19308</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RTFQ" target="INSUFICIENCIA PANCREATICA">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Pancreatic insufficiency is often a result of mutations in the RTFQ gene</data>
      <data key="d10">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2</data>
      <data key="d11">c8fc8aeca48d4be6b86545b3eef7ff36</data>
      <data key="d12">19309</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="IBERPOC">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The IBERPOC study focuses on identifying and understanding the characteristics of EPOC in the population</data>
      <data key="d10">0219c6252728c139c780352d4c593bb2</data>
      <data key="d11">ed121e03961f4a11acb54e07f7c29716</data>
      <data key="d12">19310</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="PACIENTE FUMADOR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The smoker patient is at risk of developing EPOC due to their smoking history, which is a major contributing factor to the disease</data>
      <data key="d10">b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d11">e6b94565024543039c620241ba7496b8</data>
      <data key="d12">19311</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="ALFA-1-ANTITRIPSINA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency can lead to the development of EPOC, making it a significant factor in the disease's etiology</data>
      <data key="d10">b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d11">4ea54e75cbc1406fa20c948c42c2f5f8</data>
      <data key="d12">19312</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="BRONQUIECTASIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EPOC can lead to the development of bronchiectasis due to chronic inflammation and infection in the lungs</data>
      <data key="d10">b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d11">30f8f720d8b64d2c850f360e58d1963a</data>
      <data key="d12">19313</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="S&#205;NTOMAS RESPIRATORIOS">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Respiratory symptoms are key indicators of EPOC, as patients typically present with these symptoms during diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d10">b62146237c90c7a018b9a3d2c060c722</data>
      <data key="d11">fd754eb071604357bbabb2450683d18b</data>
      <data key="d12">19314</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="SEPAR-ALAT">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">SEPAR-ALAT provides clinical guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of EPOC, indicating a direct relationship between the organization and the event</data>
      <data key="d10">d22c91140c11f7344e9aeebb21454cee</data>
      <data key="d11">6f89e1f78e384137950a3c43ede7c403</data>
      <data key="d12">19315</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="EUROPEAN RESPIRATORY SOCIETY">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The European Respiratory Society provides guidelines and research on the management of EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f</data>
      <data key="d11">a879c50e114c459186c890629da5a6c8</data>
      <data key="d12">19316</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="SOLER ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Soler et al. investigated the prevalence of malnutrition in EPOC patients</data>
      <data key="d10">8efd8d610de6aced043032198b436f3f</data>
      <data key="d11">cdc577849e254b7bb29e223389623ff1</data>
      <data key="d12">19317</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="BRONQUITIS CR&#211;NICA">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Chronic Bronchitis is a common condition that falls under the umbrella of EPOC, contributing to its symptoms</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">4b8c0ec690e447e9862712d4f28d3aa7</data>
      <data key="d12">19318</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="SOPLADOR ROSADO">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "Soplador Rosado" phenotype is a specific classification within EPOC, indicating a particular body type and respiratory condition</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">6b695651d6944a648c77741826d22645</data>
      <data key="d12">19319</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="OBESO AZULADO">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The "Obeso Azulado" phenotype is another classification within EPOC, indicating a different body type and respiratory condition</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">3fb2848a8f84409ba1774e54e7226ac6</data>
      <data key="d12">19320</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="DEFECTO CELULAR">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cellular defects can contribute to the pathophysiology of EPOC and its complications</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">2e0f6446840d476fac74dbea479054d1</data>
      <data key="d12">19321</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="D&#201;FICIT DE ENERG&#205;A">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Energy deficit is often observed in EPOC patients due to increased energy expenditure and poor nutritional intake</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">98ea41ab22344625b51fcb89b3498862</data>
      <data key="d12">19322</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="ALTERACI&#211;N DE M&#218;SCULOS RESPIRATORIOS">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alteration of respiratory muscles can lead to decreased lung function in EPOC patients</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">73953f2c06cf45e3b24fc8bb37b34fd7</data>
      <data key="d12">19323</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="ALTERACI&#211;N PAR&#201;NQUIMA PULMONAR">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Alteration of pulmonary parenchyma is a hallmark of EPOC, affecting respiratory efficiency</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">696395b779904220ad72bffd2ffd043a</data>
      <data key="d12">19324</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="DISFUNCI&#211;N INMUNE">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Immune dysfunction can exacerbate the symptoms and complications of EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">e41bdd4c80ca47999d5749cb6e583c82</data>
      <data key="d12">19325</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="INFECCI&#211;N PULMONAR">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Patients with EPOC are at higher risk for pulmonary infections due to compromised lung function</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">eb234404d9b247d8a4e73f851feff116</data>
      <data key="d12">19326</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="MIOFIBRILLAS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Changes in myofibrils can affect muscle function in EPOC patients, contributing to overall weakness</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">bb38a29f55d94a998c44c4a149f7dcb1</data>
      <data key="d12">19327</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="MASA &#211;SEA">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Bone mass can be affected in EPOC patients, increasing the risk of osteoporosis</data>
      <data key="d10">ddd48beea3c882bf1a651cb25283ba91</data>
      <data key="d11">8788bdf7eeed45a6b536a54100d8a59e</data>
      <data key="d12">19328</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="BODE INDEX">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The BODE index is specifically designed to assess the severity and predict mortality in patients with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">42755d8b752442c38c78f547215b24bc</data>
      <data key="d12">19329</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="FEV1">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">FEV1 is a critical measure used to evaluate lung function in patients diagnosed with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">bf109a2654dc4269b39d76cafa90cb5f</data>
      <data key="d12">19330</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="MRC">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The MRC dyspnea scale is utilized to assess the level of breathlessness experienced by patients with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">4698812d7a6f4c5f9a7d39494e594d5d</data>
      <data key="d12">19331</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="GOLD STAGE">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The GOLD stage classification is used to determine the severity of EPOC in patients</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">7c961f878d6c4ef99a0a1f0741e16fcc</data>
      <data key="d12">19332</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="CIRCUMFERENCE OF ARM">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The circumference of the arm is used to predict mortality in EPOC patients, highlighting the importance of muscle mass</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">765b53e45d064ed79861dacf4ab9fc74</data>
      <data key="d12">19333</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="OBESITY PARADOX">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">The obesity paradox may influence the outcomes of patients with EPOC, as body composition can affect disease progression</data>
      <data key="d10">cc406ffdbe4f62a6f2d9763ee4888fdf</data>
      <data key="d11">8f5822a91f324a1d94a64a58fc7dffff</data>
      <data key="d12">19334</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="BQ">
      <data key="d8">21.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EPOC and BQ are both chronic lung diseases that can lead to similar symptoms and complications. BQ has been associated with improvements in exercise capacity and quality of life in patients with EPOC. Additionally, both EPOC and BQ require similar dietary assessments and monitoring to manage the conditions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d10">9704c66c0d725d94e3dbd8f09440ed27,add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a,c2b3f93bb7fcffe1bc023ab4148e600c</data>
      <data key="d11">a1d30cee2a644518b50671258c18f45b</data>
      <data key="d12">19335</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="HEMOGLOBIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hemoglobin levels are important in assessing the health of patients with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">09ac9fd8d77e4c9fa095a8e7635a0d3a</data>
      <data key="d12">19336</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="OSTEOCALCIN">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Osteocalcin is relevant in evaluating bone metabolism in patients with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">add3641ae46ac521317bb4c12922895a</data>
      <data key="d11">642070272d7243e3b35649f0e946e019</data>
      <data key="d12">19337</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="FERREIRA ET AL.">
      <data key="d8">1.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Ferreira et al. conducted a review on the effects of nutritional supplementation in patients with EPOC</data>
      <data key="d10">cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
      <data key="d11">d1b8ab8443c842aeaf54f5a0e2cd203e</data>
      <data key="d12">19338</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="EPOC" target="ALIMENTOS HIPERCAL&#211;RICOS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hypercaloric foods are recommended for EPOC patients to help maintain or improve caloric intake</data>
      <data key="d10">cbadd445efd24c3f7ab682a373e416cf</data>
      <data key="d11">422d12b48d524cc189abd3e36eea0308</data>
      <data key="d12">19339</data>
