    </edge>
    <edge source="APLV" target="HYDROLYZED FORMULAS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Hydrolyzed formulas are recommended for infants suffering from APLV to provide necessary nutrition without triggering allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d10">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c</data>
      <data key="d11">185b0a3e2205448db89044bb85bcfeb0</data>
      <data key="d12">20177</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="APLV" target="COW'S MILK PROTEIN">
      <data key="d8">9.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Cow's milk protein is the primary allergen involved in APLV, leading to allergic reactions in susceptible infants.</data>
      <data key="d10">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c</data>
      <data key="d11">8feec36e85f5435fa2d34a29fcbb3d5a</data>
      <data key="d12">20178</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="APLV" target="PROCTOCOLITIS">
      <data key="d8">6.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Proctocolitis is another condition that can arise in infants with APLV, causing inflammation and discomfort.</data>
      <data key="d10">08d66dc8414668a3ec627a1e164cfa6c</data>
      <data key="d11">bc3a77ee89ed4a31a61fda1ed9fc3ed4</data>
