    <edge source="GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA" target="MACROGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">7.0</data>
      <data key="d9">Macrogesti&#243;n is a component of gesti&#243;n sanitaria that focuses on health policy and state intervention</data>
      <data key="d10">f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d11">8a8e7ea1bd4a4564baa602f39efae268</data>
      <data key="d12">20343</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA" target="MESOGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA and MESOGESTI&#211;N are interconnected concepts within the realm of healthcare management. MESOGESTI&#211;N, specifically, refers to a level of gesti&#243;n sanitaria that is dedicated to coordinating the operations of health centers. It plays a crucial role in the administration of healthcare facilities, ensuring that they function effectively and efficiently. Meso-management, as a component of healthcare management, emphasizes the importance of overseeing these healthcare centers, highlighting the significance of structured management practices in delivering quality health services. Together, these concepts underscore the vital role of effective management in the healthcare sector.</data>
      <data key="d10">26765fd0d663c8708d7bd6a545de3e2c,f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d11">4d1c26d1b3544c48965ac77ad135f937</data>
      <data key="d12">20344</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA" target="MICROGESTI&#211;N">
      <data key="d8">13.0</data>
      <data key="d9">GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA and MICROGESTI&#211;N are interconnected concepts within the realm of healthcare management. Microgesti&#243;n, or micro-management, is a strategic approach that focuses on enhancing efficiency at the individual professional level. This method is crucial for the effective functioning of gesti&#243;n sanitaria, as it emphasizes the importance of clinician decision-making. By integrating microgesti&#243;n into healthcare practices, organizations can improve overall performance and ensure that healthcare professionals operate at their highest potential.</data>
      <data key="d10">26765fd0d663c8708d7bd6a545de3e2c,f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d11">74ee26a3df104ae7936092e4be8ca98d</data>
      <data key="d12">20345</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GESTI&#211;N SANITARIA" target="EEIS">
      <data key="d8">8.0</data>
      <data key="d9">EEIS is a critical tool within gesti&#243;n sanitaria for evaluating the cost-effectiveness of health interventions</data>
      <data key="d10">f70e5dee3fad44cd9576113c0bb941d5</data>
      <data key="d11">7b3a14866e974c0397b442d4f1d7b80c</data>
      <data key="d12">20346</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
